inl note_of_spiral_independent_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 2u32, "2026-10-15T04:00Z", "lane-b", "00:00 lane B: step 3 Kino part LANDED (uncommitted): polyglot_root option/app env/SPIRAL_KINO_POLYGLOT_ROOT alias removed (kino.ex, notebook.ex option list, kino_test, notebook_test, README), toolchain.ex default_package_dir is spiral's own deps clone only (the ../polyglot candidate never matched in any CI layout: in dice the spiral root is deps/polyglot/deps/spiral), spi/domain_compiler.ex the same; no consumer in spiral/dice/alphabet/polyglot/eoie used the alias (git grep); left: notebook.ex @lib_rels deps/polyglot/deps/spiral entries (dice still reaches spiral that way, step 2), env.ps1:129-130")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: Kino's polyglot fallbacks and the polyglot_root alias are removed (lane B, uncommitted). Next grain: list remaining polyglot references in spiral (scripts and docs).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 4u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: step 1 staged and reviewed: pack-a/namespace-spiral.ps1 renames namespace Polyglot to Spiral in core, host, 3 refs, both fsproj RootNamespace, compat PolyglotCommon.fs, profile scripts and formatter fsx (15 files). The 3 Polyglot stack-frame filters on gpt5parallel-only sides stay (pair-drift rejects one-sided edits; they filter nothing after the rename). Pack: night pack 10-17 (scripts %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\packs\\night-1017, each with -DryRun; final review single-flight-20261017-053315 on the exact pack: 6,906 rows, DISAGREE 0, residual-only Zig 457 and Rust 415, 3 intended Rust exit cells (shown as 2 NATIVE-DIFF rows); builds in single-flight, hopacsota and gpt5parallel; hopacsota inline and random:23 equal single-flight on every compile and residual cell; corpus 144 of 144; Zig at C speed on the bench).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 5u32, "2026-10-19T12:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:33 lap 1 grain: step 1 shipped: the compiler file declares namespace Spiral (0 namespace Polyglot left), from the 10-17 night pack-a rename; remaining polyglot coupling to measure: who still resolves through deps/polyglot (dice and alphabet build.ps1 dot-source ../deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib) Next: grep every repo's scripts for deps/polyglot paths and list which could point at spiral directly")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 6u32, "2026-10-19T12:50Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:50 lap 2 grain: deps/polyglot references in tracked scripts/yml/spiproj: dice 25 in 14 files, alphabet 12 in 8, spiral 1 (env.ps1:135, a package-dir fallback to polyglot's The-Spiral-Language clone), x/blog/dir-tree-html/eoie/i574n.github 0; dice's reduce to two patterns: polyglot's own scripts/core.ps1 (11x) and spiral reached through polyglot/deps/spiral (lib.ps1 5x, dir-tree-html.ps1, publish-tree.ps1) Next: diff the function sets of polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and spiral/scripts/core.ps1; if spiral's covers dice's calls, dice and alphabet can clone spiral directly")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 7u32, "2026-10-19T12:50Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:50 follow-up: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 defines no functions; it is a forwarder that finds spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (deps/spiral or a sibling clone, else clones it) and dot-sources it. So every dice and alphabet dependency on polyglot is really on spiral: the switch is dice/alphabet init cloning spiral into deps/spiral and rewriting 25 + 12 paths (deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 -> deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1, deps/polyglot/deps/spiral -> deps/spiral), mirrored in both repos (alphabet mirrors dice)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 8u32, "2026-10-19T13:26Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:26 lap 2 grain: prepared lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/rewrite-deps.ps1 (dry run by default, -Apply writes) for dice and alphabet together (alphabet mirrors dice). Rules: deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/ -> deps/spiral/ and deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 -> deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1 over tracked .ps1/.spiproj/.yml/.toml/.json, plus EnsureSymbolicLink ../deps/spiral -> ../../spiral in scripts/init.ps1 where missing (dice lacks it; alphabet has it since earlier), inserted after polyglot's init call so the sibling spiral clone exists. Equivalence checked: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is a 13-line forwarder that dot-sources spiral's scripts/core.ps1 (or clones spiral beside polyglot), polyglot/deps/spiral is a link to the sibling C:\\home\\git\\spiral, and every rewritten target exists in spiral (scripts/core.ps1, lib/spiral/lib.ps1, apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1, scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1, scripts/publish-tree.ps1, apps/spiral/build.ps1). Dry run: 22 files change (dice 14, alphabet 8). 4 deps/polyglot references stay on purpose because they name polyglot-owned files: dice lib/fsharp/build.ps1:24 (polyglot lib/fsharp/Common.fs), both init.ps1 polyglot links, alphabet init.ps1:28 (polyglot apps/parser build). Not applied: it changes CI wiring in two repos, so it goes with a user push; decision recorded: apply in one step for both repos, then run both repos' build.ps1 (heavy) before the push. Next: decide whether Common.fs and apps/parser can move to spiral (the last two polyglot needs of dice/alphabet)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 9u32, "2026-10-19T14:04Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:04 lap 3 grain: decided the two polyglot-owned leftovers. (1) polyglot/apps/parser (F# JsonParser/Parser exported from .livemd) is built by both inits (dice scripts/init.ps1, alphabet scripts/init.ps1:28) but nothing in dice or alphabet reads its output (grep for JsonParser, Parser.fs, apps/parser/Parser: 0 files in either repo), so the build step is dead work: rewrite-deps.ps1 now drops it from both inits. (2) polyglot/lib/fsharp/Common.fs (50 lines) stays for now: its only dice consumer is lib/fsharp/build.ps1 (the F# runtime modules of the dice lib), which retires with the F# lane (bold native goals), so moving it into spiral would only move dead weight. Also added rule ../../polyglot/deps/spiral/ -> ../../spiral/ (dice init still built spiral apps and dir-tree-html through polyglot's link to the sibling spiral). Dry run: 22 files; dice init now links deps/spiral, drops the parser build, and builds apps/spiral, apps/wasm and dir-tree-html from ../../spiral directly. Left deps/polyglot references: Common.fs and the two polyglot links (needed only for Common.fs and polyglot's own init). Next: after the F# lib of dice is retired or moved, drop polyglot from dice/alphabet entirely; apply rewrite-deps.ps1 -Apply with a user push")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 10u32, "2026-10-19T15:19Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:19 lap 5 grain on step (1) naming: the namespace rename is done (spiral_compiler.fs has namespace Spiral, no namespace Polyglot left), but the two stack-trace filters the 10-12 inventory listed still keep only frames containing Polyglot (spiral_compiler.fs:127534 debugTraceAt, :185367 the FatalError path for NullReference/InvalidOperation/... exceptions). Since the rename they match nothing, so an internal compiler exception reports only its message and the debug term trace has no frames: a silent regression from the rename. Staged lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/stack-frames.py (both filters -> Spiral.; dry run 2 anchors match) to ride pack 7; matrix.psd1 has no pin naming those exception types, so no pin changes expected. Step (3) leftovers in Cells: notebook.ex @lib_rels lines 30 and 33 (deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral, polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral) stay until dice/alphabet drop polyglot (rewrite-deps.ps1); fsi_session.ex:7 is a doc mention only.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 11u32, "2026-10-19T15:36Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:36 lap 6 grain, step (3) inventory and the first cut. Polyglot mentions left in spiral code: Cells notebook.ex @lib_rels (2, waiting on rewrite-deps), fsi_session.ex (doc only), lib file_system.spi:761 (a test that also accepts a source dir named polyglot, harmless until vendoring ends), and apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/env.ps1:135-136, Get-SpiralPackageDir's two polyglot fallbacks. The env.ps1 pair is dead: the first candidate, spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language, exists locally and is cloned by scripts/init-app-build.ps1 in CI. Staged lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py (dry run: the anchor matches once), queued for main after the switch accept, because the switch may rewrite how core- resolves. Also today: spiral scripts/core.ps1 now resolves the Cells dir through ResolveLink, so the polyglot/deps/spiral route no longer runs mix from a second path (WORKFLOW-END-TO-END note).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 12u32, "2026-10-19T15:56Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:56 lap 7 grain: rewrite-deps.ps1 rechecked against today's trees (dry run, still 22 files) and taught to keep its own TODO block true. After the rewrite, dice/scripts/init.ps1's SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT block (which says dice still reaches spiral through polyglot) would be false, so the script now replaces it with: dice keeps deps/polyglot only for lib/fsharp/build.ps1's Common.fs (polyglot/lib/fsharp); drop this link and the polyglot init once the F# lib of dice retires or Common.fs moves (each line at most 120 columns). The dry-run diff shows the swap; the harvest will then point at the remaining tie only.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 13u32, "2026-10-19T16:33Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:33 lap 8 grain: post-switch census of spiral's remaining code ties to polyglot (apps/cells/lib + compiler scripts, case-insensitive): env.ps1:135-136 (the two VS Code Plugin core fallbacks; drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py dry run still matches its anchor after the switch) and cells notebook.ex:30 and :33 (lib_rels for deps/polyglot/deps/spiral, the route dice and alphabet use until rewrite-deps lands). The older step-3 ties (domain_compiler.ex, toolchain.ex, kino polyglot_root option) no longer exist; fsi_session.ex:7 is a history mention. So step 3 is 2 staged lines now plus 2 lib_rels lines that wait on step 2")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_14 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 14u32, "2026-10-19T16:39Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 12:39 stack-frames.py taken out of pack 7: both of its filters live on gpt5parallel-only sides (PartEval at 127534, SignalRSupervisor at 185367), so the Release build's pair-drift check stopped the build (changed only on the gpt5parallel side), exactly as the 10-17 note predicted; reverted in the tree (pair-drift clean). The dead Polyglot filters can only go with gpt5parallel's retirement (HOPACSOTA-P6) or with a mirrored single-flight change.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_15 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 15u32, "2026-10-19T17:00Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:00 lap 9 grain: dry run of rewrite-deps.ps1 rechecked against what it leaves behind: (1) alphabet's EnsureSymbolicLink deps/polyglot (init.ps1:25) becomes dead after the rewrite, because alphabet has no lib/fsharp (so no Common.fs), its parser build line is dropped and every deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is mapped to deps/spiral; the link should go in the same rewrite, unlike dice's, which Common.fs still needs. (2) The rewrite covers only deps/polyglot paths; sibling-path uses of polyglot stay: alphabet scripts/build.ps1:8, init.ps1:20 and :23, apps/hangul/build.ps1:8, and dice scripts/init.ps1:20 and :26 (core.ps1 dot-source and the polyglot init). These are the last ties to plan for, with the same core.ps1 mapping to ../../spiral/scripts/core.ps1")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_16 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 16u32, "2026-10-19T17:34Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:34 lap 10 grain: rewrite-deps.ps1 extended for lap 9's gap, dry run 24 files (was 22), parse 0 errors. Found first why a plain path map was unsafe: dice init.ps1 sources ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 BEFORE polyglot's init clones spiral, and that core.ps1 is only a shim that clones spiral itself when missing; so mapping it to ../../spiral/scripts/core.ps1 alone breaks a fresh runner. The script now (1) adds a spiral clone (Set-Location .., git clone spiral.git, git pull) to the single polyglot clone block of each init.ps1, keeping its indentation, (2) maps ../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 to ../spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (dice init, alphabet init, alphabet scripts/build.ps1, apps/hangul/build.ps1, which already sources ../../../spiral/lib), (3) drops alphabet's dead deps/polyglot link. After it, alphabet has 0 deps/polyglot references; dice keeps only Common.fs + its link. Caveat: alphabet -fast on a never-initialized tree no longer self-clones spiral (fast assumes an initialized tree). Next: user/main go for --Apply in dice + alphabet together (alphabet mirrors dice), then their workflow.ps1 runs")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_17 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 17u32, "2026-10-19T17:52Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:52 lap 11 grain: rewrite-deps.ps1 now parse-checks every rewritten .ps1 in memory (PowerShell Parser.ParseInput) and refuses the whole run if one would not parse, so --Apply cannot write a broken init.ps1; dry run: all 24 rewritten files parse (files changed: 24, no parse refusal). Next: go for -Apply in dice + alphabet together, then their workflow.ps1 runs")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_18 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 18u32, "2026-10-19T17:52Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:52 follow-up: made the refusal claim true for -Apply too: writes are collected and done only after every file was rewritten and parsed (before, files earlier in the loop were written before a later refusal); dry run unchanged (24 files), dice tree untouched (12 dirty paths before and after)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_19 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 19u32, "2026-10-19T18:19Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 14:19 lap 12: dice keeps deps/polyglot only for lib/fsharp Common.fs, and dice_fsharp.fs uses it in exactly one place (line 95, trace Debug (...) _locals). Common.trace only maps its own TraceLevel onto SpiralTrace.TraceLevel, so dice_fsharp.livemd can call SpiralTrace.trace SpiralTrace.TraceLevel.Debug directly and drop the Common.fs import and the open Polyglot/Common lines (livemd 37, 41, 45) plus build.ps1:24's module, which removes the last polyglot link")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_20 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 20u32, "2026-10-19T22:48Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 18:48 lap 19 grain: rechecked the three staged applies after main's core-v1 migration of dice, alphabet and polyglot (18:3x, 163 rule edits): dry runs still clean, dice-drop-common.py 5 edits in 3 files (Common.fs import and the one trace call), drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py its 1 env.ps1 anchor, rewrite-deps.ps1 24 files that all parse; the migration touched none of their anchors. Next: main's go for the three applies (dice and alphabet together)")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_21 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 21u32, "2026-10-19T23:20Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 19:20 lap 21 grain: stack-frames.py (debugTraceAt and the FatalError path keep only frames containing Polyglot, but the namespace is Spiral now, so both filters drop every frame) did not land with pack 7: its 2 anchors still match today's spiral_compiler.fs. The script now reads newline-preserving (it used read_text, which would normalize line endings) and refuses a file that already filters on Spiral.; checked on a scratch copy (apply, then a second apply refuses). Queue row 67 is still the one to take with the next pack")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_22 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 22u32, "2026-10-19T23:59Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 19:59 main's decision on stack-frames.py: it stays out of every pack until gpt5parallel retires, because both filters it edits sit on the gpt5parallel side of the PartEval section pair, so pair-drift.ps1 stops the build on a one-sided change (that is why pack 7 dropped it). Removed from lab/CALYX-BACKEND/stack-candidate.ps1; queue row 67 is parked on gpt5parallel's retirement")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_23 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 23u32, "2026-10-20T02:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 22:33 user 2026-10-19 21:4x: check again whether polyglot is really isolated now: no repo depends on it for anything, spiral standalone.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_24 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 24u32, "2026-10-20T02:44Z", "review-lane", "2026-10-19 22:44 review-lane recheck of polyglot isolation (git grep -i polyglot over tracked + untracked files of 16 repos, top-level deps links, CI ymls, spiproj packageDir census, the 3 lab dry runs). Verdict: spiral itself is standalone in CI (its scripts, workflow and gh-pages.yml never reach polyglot; it clones its own deps/The-Spiral-Language in init-app-build.ps1), but polyglot is NOT isolated: 4 repos still depend on it live. (1) i574n.github, the reference run, not covered by any lab script: init.ps1:29 clones polyglot, :32 and build/outdated/publish/workflow.ps1 dot-source ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1, workflow.livemd:4 sources polyglot/scripts/nbs_header.ps1 (exists only in polyglot), build.ps1:15 and outdated.ps1:12 run polyglot's own build/outdated; plus 2 code-workspace files. (2) dice, live beyond rewrite-deps: init.ps1:15-26 clones and inits polyglot, and polyglot init is the only thing that clones hyperui (dep_hyperui.ps1), which ui/index.html:8 links as ../deps/polyglot/deps/hyperui/public/component.css for trunk (an .html file, outside rewrite-deps' ps1/spiproj/yml/toml/json filter); lib/fsharp/dice_fsharp.livemd:5 imports polyglot/lib/fsharp/Notebooks.livemd (which imports polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral/spiral_runtime.fs), a line dice-drop-common.py does not touch; Common.fs (build.ps1:24, livemd:37) is covered. (3) alphabet: after rewrite-deps it has 0 deps/polyglot paths but init.ps1:16-20 still clones polyglot and runs its init. (4) tibia (other lane, report only): init.ps1:16-25 clones polyglot to get spiral cloned and dot-sources its core.ps1, build/publish/workflow and apps/arena/build.ps1 use deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1; CI runs that init. Local-only/backup: vault (scripts reach polyglot and a gone apps/dir-tree-html: dead), fc1943s.github (dump repo), singularity (data/playground: dead). x, blog, dir-tree-html, eoie: 0 references (eoie only a prose mention in spec/one-call.md).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_25 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 25u32, "2026-10-20T02:44Z", "review-lane", "2026-10-19 22:44 review-lane, spiral's own leftovers and what is left on this epic. Spiral: (a) cells notebook.ex:30 and :33 @lib_rels are live, not only for dice: find_spiral_lib walks ancestors and tries deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral first, and C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\deps\\polyglot is a stale local symlink to polyglot (created 2025-01-05, untracked, gitignored, nothing creates it any more), so every notebook under the spiral tree resolves lib through spiral -> polyglot -> spiral (same files, second path; the 10-19 two-path mix relink was this class); tibia\\deps\\polyglot does the same. Removing the stale link (user's call, local only) and then the two lib_rels lines plus notebook_test.exs:309 (the lib-mounted-once test builds deps/polyglot/deps/spiral) closes it; :272 only names a temp dir polyglot. (b) env.ps1:135-136 dead fallbacks, covered by drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py (dry run: 1 anchor matches). (c) three dead Polyglot frame strings, all on gpt5parallel sides: spiral_compiler.fs:127597 and :185606 (stack-frames.py, parked on gpt5parallel retirement) and :137232 Replace of at Polyglot.spiral_compiler (not in stack-frames.py; a no-op strip, goes with the same retirement). (d) stale docs: apps/compiler/AGENTS.md:16 (names a build.ps1 that does not exist and a polyglot builder), tmp/AGENTS.md:254 and samples/README.md:14 (core- through deps/polyglot), NEXT.md:249, tmp/README.md:96 and scripts/upstream.py:13 (the fork lives at polyglot/deps/The-Spiral-Language; spiral has its own deps clone now). (e) lab NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS run.ps1:10 and contract-run.ps1:7 hardcode dice\\deps\\polyglot\\deps\\spiral and break after rewrite-deps. Lab dry runs today: rewrite-deps.ps1 24 files, all parse, leaves dice Common.fs + its link; dice-drop-common.py 5 edits in 3 files; drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py 1 anchor. Left for full isolation, in order: apply the 3 staged scripts (dice + alphabet together); extend rewrite-deps (or a sibling script) to drop the polyglot clone/init from dice and alphabet inits in favour of pwsh ../../spiral/scripts/init.ps1, move the hyperui clone into dice (or spiral init) and rewrite ui/index.html:8 to deps/hyperui, and replace the livemd:5 Notebooks.livemd import with a direct ../../deps/spiral/lib/spiral/spiral_runtime.fs import or drop it; then cells lib_rels + test; then i574n.github drops polyglot from init/build/outdated/workflow and gets nbs_header from spiral (or inlines it); tibia's lane does the same mapping; finally archive polyglot (user decision 10-12).")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_26 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 26u32, "2026-10-20T02:47Z", "review-lane", "2026-10-19 22:47 review-lane follow-up: what dice and alphabet lose if their inits call pwsh ../../spiral/scripts/init.ps1 instead of cloning and initing polyglot. polyglot init.ps1 + init.livemd do: rustup toolchains, cargo-binstall, sccache, trunk 0.21.14, playwright 1.44 browsers, patched cargo-outdated, PowerShellGet, bun install at the polyglot root, dep_spiral(_extension), Linux apt packages via init.sh, gleam from source on Linux, hyperui clone, apps/spiral build, and spiral's own init. spiral/scripts/init.ps1 already does the toolchains, binstall, sccache (:78), trunk (:71), playwright (:91), cargo-outdated (:82) and the near nightly-2024-07-14 (:34); dice init builds apps/spiral itself; CI installs Gleam/OTP via setup-beam and runners ship build-essential, unzip and pwsh; wasm-pack has no user in dice, alphabet, tibia or i574n.github. The only real loss is the hyperui clone (polyglot dep_hyperui.ps1, a depth-1 clone of markmead/hyperui), which only dice/ui needs (index.html:8). So the init swap is safe once dice gets its own hyperui clone (dice init or a dice dep script, linked as deps/hyperui) and index.html:8 points there. With that, the livemd:5 import swap (to ../../deps/spiral/lib/spiral/spiral_runtime.fs, which dice-drop-common's direct SpiralTrace call needs in the notebook path; deleting the line would break the notebook run) and the 3 staged scripts, dice and alphabet need nothing from polyglot.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_27 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 27u32, "2026-10-24T02:25Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:2x main grooming: Paused by rule (Active, no note since 2026-10-20T02:47Z, no child item noted in 3 days). Resume when picked; progress kept at 60%.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_28 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 28u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 4 10:32 (subagent2): waiting: rewrite-deps.ps1 -Apply rides a user push (TODO block placed in dice init this lap) -> next: apply with push | lap 13 14:37 (subagent2): staged lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/dice-drop-common.py (dry run 5 edits in 3 files): dice_fsharp.livemd + .fs drop the Common.fs import and open Polyglot/Common, the one trace call goes to SpiralTrace.trace (Lib from spiral_runtime.fs), build.ps1:24 drops the Common.fs module; refuses if Common is still named after the edits -> next: after rewrite-deps' go: apply, then dice lib/fsharp build.ps1 (heavy); livemd line 5 Notebooks.livemd import is interactive-only (bold-native drops it) | lap 14 15:03 (subagent2): staged set complete for dice (rewrite-deps + dice-drop-common + drop-polyglot-fallbacks); waiting -> next: main's go for rewrite-deps -Apply | lap 16 15:50 (subagent2): the remaining polyglot mention in dice_fsharp.livemd (line 5, #!import of polyglot Notebooks.livemd) never reaches the build: the committed dice_fsharp.fs has no import or polyglot text except the open Polyglot that dice-drop-common.py removes, so after that script the dice F# build has no polyglot input (the line only matters for interactive sessions, which bold-native drops) -> next: main's go: rewrite-deps -Apply, dice-drop-common --apply, then dice lib/fsharp build.ps1 | lap 16b 15:51 (subagent2): mirror check (alphabet rule): alphabet hangul has no Common.fs tie (only build.ps1:8 polyglot core.ps1, which rewrite-deps already moves; rewrite-deps covers dice + alphabet); after rewrite-deps + dice-drop-common the rewritten dice init.ps1 TODO (keeps deps/polyglot only for Common.fs) and its deps/polyglot EnsureSymbolicLink become stale: a third small step removes both -> next: stage that step once rewrite-deps' output is in the tree (anchors are its output) | lap 17 16:43 (subagent2): unchanged -> next: main's go | lap 22 19:59 (subagent2): per main: stack-frames.py parked until gpt5parallel retires (pair-drift); dropped from stack-candidate.ps1; OpenQasm sim patch has its own queue row -> next: gpt5parallel retirement")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_29 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 29u32, "2026-10-30T14:12Z", "main", "10-30 10:12 main, BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030 R1: the only blocker is rewrite-deps.ps1 -Apply rides the user's push. Now assignee=user + user-batch; grooms stop re-verifying it, and it moves when the user acts.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_30 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 30u32, "2026-10-31T03:21Z", "main", "10-30 23:21 main: lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT is ARCHIVED (user, 10-30 22:5x: the lab dir didn't work and drifted; drafts don't live outside the repo). Archive 20261030-232045 under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive. Restore this folder with: pwsh i574n.github/scripts/scratch-archive.ps1 -Root C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab -Restore '%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045\\manifest.tsv' -Only 'SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT\\*' -RestoreTo C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab. Its 4 migration scripts now live in i574n.github/scripts/spiral-independent/ (dice scripts/init.ps1 comment updated). Resume this item's work in its real place in the repo, not in lab.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_31 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 31u32, "2026-10-31T21:03Z", "main", "10-31 17:02 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK): stays PAUSED. Reason: the remaining step is running the migration (i574n.github/scripts/spiral-independent/rewrite-deps.ps1) in dice, alphabet, mechahaze-album1 and tapas2, a user-batch decision (it also gates POLYGLOT-RETIRE's apps/parser). Resume when: the user approves the migration run.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_32 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 32u32, "2026-11-01T04:51Z", "main", "main 00:5x LAB CODE IS SAFE (user 11-01 00:2x: 'check for all lab references in history... make sure we didn't lose that code... to repurpose them or groom their tasks'). This item's lab/SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT folder (4 files: dice-drop-common.py, drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py, rewrite-deps.ps1, stack-frames.py) is archived in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045 (blob-verified). Restore it into its proper repo place with: pwsh C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\scripts\\scratch-archive.ps1 -Restore '%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045\\manifest.tsv' -RestoreTo <repo dir> -Only 'SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT/*'. Next step for the owner at its next pull: restore the useful files in place as incomplete drafts (Cells heals them in place), or record why it starts over.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_33 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 33u32, "2026-11-01T13:55Z", "main", "main 09:5x: the migration's helper scripts in i574n.github/scripts/spiral-independent/ include three untracked .py files (dice-drop-common.py, drop-polyglot-fallbacks.py, stack-frames.py; written 10-19 by helper-lane-2, moved out of lab/ by main 10-30). New .py tools are drift by the user's rule (spiral-first-tooling), so they are NOT to be committed. Before the migration runs (the user-batch step), port them to Spiral run through KIT-RUN-SPI, or fold their logic into rewrite-deps.ps1's Spiral replacement; archive the .py after. Listed in commit-suggestion.md as don't-commit.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_34 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 34u32, "2026-11-02T14:03Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByTest. QUESTION: Remove the stale untracked symlinks spiral\\deps\\polyglot and tibia\\deps\\polyglot (n25 calls it the user's call), then the two notebook.ex lib_rels lines? RULE (written before acting): Record each link's target, then remove the links. KEEP REMOVED iff (a) the Cells lib-resolution test (notebook_test.exs lib-mounted-once, updated to build spiral/lib directly) passes, (b) 'lib_gate.ps1 -File async.spi' is green, and (c) a spiral notebook and a tibia notebook resolve lib to C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral with no 'polyglot' in the resolved path. If any fails, restore the links and keep the lib_rels lines. The multi-repo step (2) (dice cloning spiral directly) follows the n12-era plan by default: mirror dice -> alphabet, with changes unstaged. BACKUP/UNDO: Before removal, write both link targets (C:\\home\\git\\polyglot) into a kit state-backup. Undo = New-Item -ItemType SymbolicLink -Path <link> -Target C:\\home\\git\\polyglot. Code edits are left unstaged. OWNER: main. NEXT: Run the rule on the box, then drop the lab-held tag (spiral/lab no longer exists, per SPIRAL-TO-YAML n27) and set the assignee to agent. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_35 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 35u32, "2026-11-02T15:45Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:45 x: DANGLING CHECK for n34's removal (user rule relayed 11-02: agents run removals themselves, unstaged; never a user step). Both spiral\\deps\\polyglot and tibia\\deps\\polyglot are untracked SymbolicLinks to C:\\home\\git\\polyglot. Four sites still resolve through deps/polyglot, all fallbacks: apps/compiler/scripts/env.ps1:141 (VS Code Plugin bundle path), apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1:15 (lib-root candidates), apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/notebook.ex:30 (lib_rels) and apps/compiler/tmp/samples/README.md:14 (docs). So the removal is a code change plus test, not a plain delete. Drop those 4 fallbacks, record both link targets in a kit state-backup, remove the links, then n34's KEEP-REMOVED tests decide. Owner main; nothing here is the user's.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_36 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 36u32, "2026-11-02T17:16Z", "main", "main 11-02 13:1x n34 RULE RUN: spiral\\deps\\polyglot REMOVED and KEPT REMOVED. (a) the Cells notebook tests: Result 13 passed; (b) lib_gate.ps1 -File async.spi: 3 of 3 passed, 0 type errors; (c) lib resolution through Spiral.Cells.Notebook.find_spiral_lib: spiral resolves to c:/home/git/spiral/lib/spiral and tibia to c:/home/git/tibia/deps/spiral/lib/spiral (tibia's deps\\spiral links to C:\\home\\git\\spiral), no polyglot in either path. The chain's first run reported (c) as failing only because `mix run -e` through mix.bat mangled the quotes (memory bat-args-parens), and its restore step then failed on its own bug (target read after Delete), so the link stayed removed; (c) re-run as an .exs file passes. Backup + undo: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\backups\\spiral-independent-links-*.json (target C:\\home\\git\\polyglot). The 4 fallback sites are dropped (unstaged: env.ps1, lib_gate.ps1, notebook.ex, samples README). KEPT: tibia\\deps\\polyglot, because tibia build/publish/workflow dot-source deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and init.ps1 recreates the link (x's dangling check missed tibia). tibia must replace that core.ps1 dependency first.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_37 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 37u32, "2026-11-02T17:34Z", "main", "main 11-02 13:3x tibia\\deps\\polyglot REMOVED too. tibia moved its 6 dot-sources to deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1 and dropped the init.ps1 EnsureSymbolicLink line (unstaged; node proof tibia-polyglot-free green, table_rows 1/1, typed_network 5/5). main's dangling check: 0 tracked tibia files reference deps/polyglot. Lib resolution after removal: tibia resolves to c:/home/git/tibia/deps/spiral/lib/spiral, no polyglot. Backup + undo: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\backups\\spiral-independent-links-tibia-20261102-133110.json. Both local polyglot links are gone. REMAINING: tibia's init.ps1 still CLONES polyglot and runs its init/core.ps1 from ../../polyglot, the CI route to spiral. Switch it to clone spiral directly as regex's init does (init-app-build.ps1); then no repo needs polyglot and POLYGLOT-RETIRE can proceed.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_38 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 38u32, "2026-11-02T18:23Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia: tibia NO LONGER NEEDS POLYGLOT (unstaged). scripts/init.ps1 now clones spiral directly into ../../spiral (when absent), dot-sources ../../spiral/scripts/core.ps1, links deps/spiral and runs deps/spiral/scripts/init-app-build.ps1, regex's shape; the polyglot clone and its init.ps1/core.ps1 calls are gone. scripts/build.ps1 now fetches Cells' mix deps itself (mix local.hex, local.rebar, deps.get when deps/kino is missing) before mix spiral.cell_budget. run_notebook.ps1 already did that, but the cell-budget step runs first, so a fresh clone failed with \"Can't continue due to errors on dependencies\"; polyglot's init used to hide it. PROOF, a CI-like fresh run on the node in a clean dir (C:\\home\\remote-stage\\fresh-1102: the tibia tree without deps/target, origin set to github i574n/tibia): init exit 0 in 12 min (spiral cloned, deps/spiral junction, WGSL runner built, no polyglot dir); then build.ps1 -Files table_rows exit 0 (deps fetched, cell budget 26 non-blocking findings, table_rows 1/1). Jobs tibia-fresh-init and tibia-fresh-build.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_39 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 39u32, "2026-11-02T21:42Z", "main", "main 11-02 17:4x RE-DECIDED Paused -> Active (90%). The 'user batch' pause is over: the user's 11-02 rule says lanes do the removals themselves. State: spiral + tibia are free of polyglot (n36-38). Tonight's work, proven on the node: dice + alphabet rewritten onto deps/spiral (contract 7/7 + NEAR sandbox; alphabet apps compile); vault, mechahaze-album1 and tapas2 ported (POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT, Done); i574n.github scripts now take spiral's core.ps1. The last dice links are in proof on the node: lib/fsharp now imports spiral_runtime.fs directly instead of polyglot's Common.fs and Notebooks.livemd; ui/index.html takes hyperui from dice's own deps/hyperui; scripts/init.ps1 runs spiral's init instead of polyglot's and clones hyperui. Once that proof is green, dice has 0 polyglot references and this epic closes; the polyglot repo itself retires under POLYGLOT-RETIRE.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_40 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 40u32, "2026-11-02T22:26Z", "main", "main 11-02 18:3x dice lib/fsharp PROVEN off polyglot: an in-job A/B on the node's checkout. A = the git-index version (polyglot Common.fs + Notebooks.livemd): the notebook step fails with 'input.fsx(12,13): Unexpected character'. B = the new version (spiral_runtime.fs import, SpiralTrace.trace, modules = GetFsharpRuntimePaths only) with -SkipNotebook: 'FSHARP-OK dice/lib/fsharp / result 16211931'. The notebook-step red is the node's code page (CELLS-FSI-STDIN-UTF8, filed, fix in proof), the same in A and B. dice ui: the trunk build is RUST-OK with hyperui from dice's own deps/hyperui (wasm 1,985,068 B). Its e2e step failed only on the node's old bun 1.2.5 (a frozen lockfile written by 1.4.4); main upgraded node bun to 1.4.4, and the ui re-run comes next.")
inl note_of_spiral_independent_41 () = Note ("SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT", 41u32, "2026-11-02T22:47Z", "main", "main 11-02 18:5x DONE. Every i574n consumer is off polyglot, and the user committed tonight's dice/alphabet/spiral work at 17:57-17:58 (dice 84acdd5, alphabet e3f4266, spiral 91bd70dc). CI: dice run 41538911884 SUCCESS, which proves on GitHub's runners that dice's new init.ps1 (spiral's own init + its own hyperui clone, no polyglot clone/link/init) and the ui e2e work; alphabet gh-pages SUCCESS. git grep polyglot in dice = 0. Readers left are not consumers: vault/mechahaze-album1/tapas2 (ported, unstaged; POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT Done), i574n.github's umbrella clone/build/outdated lines and docs prose. Those, and the 'split what remains of polyglot' half of this title, continue under POLYGLOT-RETIRE.")
