inl note_of_self_checking_samples_5 () = Note ("SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES", 5u32, "2026-10-19T18:17Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:17 lap 4 grain: the harness --test-blocks step named in the lap 1 note does not exist: no script in apps/compiler/tmp/scripts mentions test blocks, so the matrix cannot read a test-block sample yet; the lab slice (lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS/ebpf_family.spi) passes 3/3 through Cells since the mounts fix; design for the missing step: a matrix row kind Cells whose job runs the .spi through spiral cells --gate --metrics and turns each (test, target) pass/fail into one row (backend = target, exit 0 or 1, stdout = the test name), so test blocks get oracle columns like samples Next: write the row-kind as a lab patch for test.ps1 (pack material), proven on the ebpf slice; SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS consumes it")
inl note_of_self_checking_samples_6 () = Note ("SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES", 6u32, "2026-10-23T18:03Z", "main", "2026-10-23 14:03 main: the matrix row kind for test blocks exists now, as its own script rather than inside test.ps1 (1,143 lines, already past the 1k limit; and test.ps1's native code is the native-memo key): apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/test-blocks.ps1 [-Lib <package dir> -Files <spi...>] [-Reports <*.tests.tsv>] [-Out <run dir>]. It runs Cells lib_gate per file (or takes existing reports) and writes a results.tsv in the matrix schema: id testblocks/<file>/<test>, backend = target, suite testblocks, exit 0/1, oracle agree / DISAGREE against the test's inline expectation, not-run-<status> otherwise; exit 1 on any DISAGREE. Dry-proven on 4 existing family reports (80 rows, agree 80), and compare-runs.ps1 reads two such run dirs: a flipped test shows as exit + oracle cells and 'DISAGREE rows on right: 1'. The real -Lib run over the 11 lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS family files is queued at the chain end (job-1792778604345, after the float wiring gate).")
inl note_of_self_checking_samples_7 () = Note ("SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES", 7u32, "2026-10-26T09:36Z", "main", "10-26 05:36 main: the real -Lib run of test-blocks.ps1 over the 11 lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS family files (job-1792778604345, 10-23) never ran: a hold stopped it while it waited on the float-wire gate, and nothing requeued it (the same loss as main-dir-tree-repo-build-2; my pause tooling now snapshots and requeues waiting jobs, which is the fix). Requeued as main-test-blocks-families (%TEMP%\\test-blocks-families\\run.ps1, same files and arguments). Pass rule unchanged from n.14:03: exit 0, every row oracle agree, 0 DISAGREE, in a results.tsv compare-runs.ps1 can read.")
inl note_of_self_checking_samples_8 () = Note ("SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES", 8u32, "2026-10-26T14:34Z", "main", "10-26 10:34 main: n.05:36's pass rule is met: main-test-blocks-families (job-1793007377286) exited 0 with 150 rows, agree 150, DISAGREE 0, not run 0, in a matrix-schema results.tsv (spiral-bin\\runs\\testblocks-20261026-074135, readable by compare-runs.ps1). The result is recorded once, on SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS n26.")
inl note_of_self_checking_samples_9 () = Note ("SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES", 9u32, "2026-10-27T23:41Z", "main", "10-27 19:41 main: Groom 10-27 19:3x: not stale. The 10-26 pass (150 test-block rows, agree 150, DISAGREE 0) was a milestone, not the end state in the title. The epic advances through SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS, whose sample migration resumes only when the Cells test-block path costs at most 2x the matrix's CPU (rule n27). Today's E1 measured 9.89x (private compiler daemon, down from 22.28x); the next lever is E2 (compile each family file once), with the compiler lane after packs 5n and 5o. Dependency recorded: SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS. The assignee stays the user: the design choices (promote-run semantics, oracle per file or cell) come from the user's 10-12 session.")
inl note_of_self_checking_samples_10 () = Note ("SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES", 10u32, "2026-10-30T23:42Z", "main", "10-30 19:4x main R3 groom (BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030): advances only through SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS (its E2 bench, owner main, is the next step); no separate action.")
