inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_5 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:32 lap 2 grain: unblock condition made exact. The grammar side is done and pushed: extension.toml pins rev 3c76d3ed on github-i574n/main with no grammar change since, runnables.scm tags test_header as spiral-test, spiral/.zed/tasks.json runs apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1 for the cursor test, the tagged test and the file. Lib holds 402 test headers today, all matched by the runnable query (TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL note). The only open step is the user's: in Zed, install the dev extension from apps/zed, open e.g. lib/spiral/sm'.spi, and confirm a run button on each test line and that one runs. Nothing for agents")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_6 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 6u32, "2026-10-19T15:22Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:22 lap 5 grain: re-verified the task half against today's tree: test-at-row.ps1 resolves apps/cells/spi/run_notebook.ps1 (exists; the old apps/kino path is gone), and -DryRun gives the right --test for rows inside lib testing.spi tests (assert_approx_eq, _2, _3) and, for a definition row in tibia src/coins.spi, the 5 of 6 tests that reach it. Gap found: the tagged spiral-test task lives only in spiral/.zed/tasks.json and calls ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, so in every other worktree (tibia, eoie, x, dice, alphabet, blog, polyglot: none has .zed/tasks.json) the gutter button has no task to run. Proposed fix (not applied; check in Zed with the user's step): ship the tasks with the extension as apps/zed/languages/spiral/tasks.json (Zed loads language tasks from extensions) and resolve the script through the sibling layout (ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/../spiral/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, as Cells finds lib), or a repo-local .zed/tasks.json per consumer repo. User check unchanged: install the dev extension, confirm the gutter button in spiral and in tibia.")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_7 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 7u32, "2026-10-19T15:40Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:40 lap 6 grain, closed the worktree gap from lap 5 in the tree: Zed loads an extension language's tasks.json (zed crates/extension_host/src/extension_host.rs:2364-2376, load_plugin_language reads language_path/tasks.json, TaskTemplates::FILE_NAME = tasks.json, into a ContextProviderWithTasks), so apps/zed/languages/spiral/tasks.json now ships the tagged spiral-test task and the file-tests task with the extension. The script path goes through the sibling layout, ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT/../spiral/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1, which resolves from tibia, eoie and spiral itself (checked). The gutter button therefore gets a task in every repo beside spiral. The spiral worktree may now list the tagged task twice (the extension's copy and spiral/.zed/tasks.json); drop the .zed copy once the user's check confirms the extension one. User check unchanged: dev-install apps/zed, then a run button on a test line in spiral and in tibia.")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_8 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 8u32, "2026-10-19T16:01Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:01 lap 7: real-dialect files work as well. test-at-row.ps1 -DryRun on lib sm'_real.spir resolves rows to their test blocks (test sm static, symbol_to_string), and config.toml's path_suffixes include spir, so the gutter task covers .spir files with no extra work. (The dry run asks the compiler for --source-blocks, so it is a short compiler process, not text-only.)")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_9 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 9u32, "2026-10-19T16:37Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:37 lap 8 grain: apps/zed/languages/spiral/tasks.json now also carries the untagged spiral: run test at cursor task (the keybinding target), with the sibling-layout script path, so every repo beside spiral gets it. The language file is now a superset of the tracked spiral/.zed/tasks.json: all 3 .zed tasks duplicate it (same labels, same script, only the path spelling differs), so in the spiral worktree each would show twice. Valid JSON, LF. For the user after the Zed check: remove .zed/tasks.json (tracked; left in place by me)")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_10 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 10u32, "2026-10-19T17:12Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:13 lap 9 grain: the sibling-layout path of the language tasks.json checked from a non-spiral worktree: with ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT=C:\\home\\git\\dice the script path dice/../spiral/apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1 exists, and -DryRun on dice/lib/dice.spi row 3 resolves the enclosing block (run_notebook --test dice_dice). So the language tasks work in sibling repos without a per-repo .zed. Next: user's Zed check (gutter button + keybinding), then the user drops spiral/.zed/tasks.json")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_11 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 11u32, "2026-10-19T17:36Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:36 lap 10 grain: checked what Zed actually loads: extension.toml pins grammar rev 3c76d3ed on i574n/spiral (path apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral), that commit is on github-i574n/main, and the worktree grammar has no diff against it, so the user's Zed check exercises the committed grammar; the new language tasks.json is untracked (?? in git status) and runnables.scm +3 lines vs the rev, so the user's check needs those two staged with the Zed dev-extension reload. Next: user's Zed check, then the user drops spiral/.zed/tasks.json")
inl note_of_zed_test_runnables_12 () = Note ("ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES", 12u32, "2026-10-19T17:54Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:54 lap 11 grain: validated the language tasks.json against Zed's task docs (zed.dev/docs/tasks): every key it uses (label, command, args, use_new_terminal, allow_concurrent_runs, reveal = always, tags) is a documented task key, and the docs give runnable-tag precedence as workspace tasks.json, then global, then language-provided bindings; so while spiral/.zed/tasks.json exists, its tagged task overrides the language one inside the spiral worktree, which is one more reason the user drops it after the check (other repos get the language task). Next: user's Zed check, then git rm .zed/tasks.json (user)")
