inl eoie_regen_drift () = Task ("EOIE-REGEN-DRIFT", "eoie follow-ups from the 2026-10-12 dogfood lane: the current compiler renames generated items and adds impl Default, so every regenerated .rs churns (a full regeneration touched 94 files and left eoie_cli at exactly the 1000-line gate); split eoie_cli before the next regeneration; regression tests for the new receipts (eoie_contracts is at 999 lines); move the remaining rust_global receipt call sites to granular Spiral; 2026-10-12: `agile check <root>` without --compiler stops with \"state drift requires build-time Spiral attestation\" instead of finding the deployed compiler (spiral-bin single-flight SpiralCompiler.dll); with --compiler it passes; default to the deployed compiler or name it in the error; 2026-10-12 eoie lane: not started (gate waits 40-68 min); measured eoie_cli regenerates to eoie.rs 921 lines (+5); crates near the 1000-line gate: agile_task_listing ~956, agile_planning_migration ~988, eoie_contracts 999 (no room: new tests went to agile_planning_rollup/tests); 2026-10-13 17:37 Kino lane: (1) agile check without --compiler now finds the deployed compiler: compiler discovery order is argument, EOIE_SPIRAL_COMPILE, config, PATH, then deployed (SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL, else <SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR or LOCALAPPDATA/spiral-bin or ~/.cache/spiral-bin>/bin/single-flight/SpiralCompiler/Release/net11.0/SpiralCompiler.dll); the build-time attestation error names that path; verified on a copy of this backlog: agile check ok source=deployed build_attested=2 in 7 s; agile_cache contract tests isolate it (SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR=fixture) and assert the error names the deployed path; (2) regeneration workspaces leaked: 99 staged copies, 15.8 GB under spiral-bin/eoie-regeneration; test-regeneration.ps1 now removes its workspace after a successful run (-KeepStaged keeps it; test-dev-workflow passes it) and prunes workspaces older than 2 days at start (failed runs stay for diagnosis until then); first run freed 13 GB (99 -> 34 dirs); test-dev-workflow contracts pass; (3) the gate splits (eoie_cli 528, eoie_contracts 587, eoie_agile_state 510) leave room before the next full regeneration; the generated-name churn itself is compiler-side (bootstrap_policy.rs regenerates with a changed allow list and wasm32 main); 2026-10-14 01:17 receipt regression tests (uncommitted): src/eoie_contracts/tests/proxy_receipts.rs, 5 tests that run the CLI (EOIE_BIN_UNDER_TEST or target eoie) in a temp root with a space and a non-ASCII character and compare whole receipt lines exactly, with only elapsed_ms/serial_ms/parallel_ms/workers normalized to N and the root to <root>: fs-read, fs-list, fs-write (create and --create-or-replace), fs-copy, fs-remove, fs-remove-tree, text-replace check/apply/--all and the --expect mismatch (exit 2, quoted corrected command), fs-search, parallel-search (hits, truncated=true found_at_least), fs-slice, fs-context, hash and hash-tree (digest on stdout, receipt apart), parallel-manifest, command-output ok and child-failed (child exit propagated); cargo test -p eoie-contracts --test proxy_receipts: 5 passed against eoie.exe; still open: the agile set receipt is covered only by planning_cli show; the receipt call sites are still whole Rust functions inside rust_global blobs (parallel_search_contract/search_terminal.spi 20, proxy_file_receipt users, legacy_operations_entry), which needs a rewrite (EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE), not a move; new test files may need census/evidence renewal (compiler-contracts/renew-strict-evidence.ps1); 2026-10-14 02:34 drift measured without touching the tree (job scratch eoie-lane/regen-drift.ps1: compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1 -KeepStaged, never -Publish, outputs compared byte for byte with git show HEAD:<target>, staged work removed): compiler snapshot 555BB9B47239 (spiral-bin single-flight SpiralCompiler.dll), 128/128 owners emitted (median 2.7 s, slowest 5.7 s), 44 same as HEAD and 84 differ (3 of them have dirty sources from the other lane: eoie_proxy_edit_contracts, proxy_failure_classification); the 84 diffs add 3,573 and remove 3,446 lines; 14 owners gain 42 impl Default blocks and drop 681 lines naming numbered variants (US0_0 style), and the rest are other generated-name or layout changes (largest: agile_task_creation +198/-153, handoff_state_projection_domain +189/-190, canonical_plan_ir_domain +188/-189, state_receipt_codec_core +155/-156); a second run for determinism is running; 2026-10-14 02:57 regeneration is deterministic: a second staged run with the same compiler snapshot (555BB9B47239) produced byte-identical outputs for all 128 owners (0 of 128 SHA-256 differ), again 84 differ from HEAD and 44 match; a diff sample (handoff_state_projection_domain) shows only intentional codegen changes: methodN functions get readable names (method4 -> starts_with_loop_4, method1 -> codec_empty_1), empty Rc<str> literals become thread_local cached clones, the allow list drops unreachable_patterns, and a stale comment line goes; so the churn is one-time, not ongoing: the fix is one published regeneration, committed, after the main thread's codegen cleanup lands (pwsh compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1 -Test -Publish, then a second test-regeneration.ps1 run must report 0 changed owners); 2026-10-14 03:12 the regenerated staged workspace compiles: cargo check --workspace --all-targets --locked -j 4 (scratch target dir, through the heavy gate) exit 0 in 161 s with no errors; staged copies and the scratch target removed; source-topology on the live tree with the new test file: topology_limits_ok=true (crate max 995 lines, rust_global_site_count 261); left: publish+commit the one-time regeneration after main's codegen cleanup (and with the other lane's eoie_proxy_edit_contracts/proxy_failure_classification edits settled), confirm a follow-up regeneration changes 0 owners; the agile set receipt still lacks a CLI test (needs the agile_cache fixture with package.spiproj and a fixture compiler); moving receipt call sites out of rust_global is a rewrite of whole Rust functions (EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE), not part of this item; 2026-10-14 03:39 agile set receipt covered too (uncommitted): src/eoie_contracts/tests/agile_receipts.rs builds a backlog with agile init + agile add in a temp root (space and non-ASCII), asserts the whole set receipt line (eoie agile set ok id=ID-A progress=40 status=Active validation=runtime-attested compiler=not-required, byte counts and elapsed normalized), that show reflects it, and that progress 140, status Sleeping and an unknown id are rejected with their messages while state/agile.spi stays byte-identical; cargo test -p eoie-contracts --test agile_receipts --test proxy_receipts: 6 passed; source-topology still topology_limits_ok=true; 2026-10-14 03:44 correction to the 02:5x conclusion: determinism was shown for one compiler snapshot only, and every Rust codegen change in the compiler produces another wave like this one, so the churn is per compiler change, not one-time: regenerate and commit eoie whenever the compiler's Rust output changes (a step after each compiler bless), then confirm a second regeneration changes 0 owners; the receipt tests were checked against the deployed eoie.exe, not a build of the current tree, so rerun them with build.ps1 -Test once the other lane's edits land; its pending change only lets '~' stay unquoted after the first character in corrected commands (proxy_failure_classification proxy_words), which does not touch the pinned lines (the pinned root is quoted for its space either way); 2026-10-14 04:26 review fix: proxy_receipts.rs and agile_receipts.rs set EOIE_LEASE_POLICY=renewing and EOIE_CONFIG_HOME=<fixture root> on every command, so a machine without the renewing lease-policy file (CI) cannot lease-block the mutations; 6/6 pass with the shell's EOIE_LEASE_POLICY unset; 2026-10-14 06:01 the drift found in eoie_contracts is also a source drift: contracts.rs had been hand-patched (a743a92) with lease-test isolation its source contracts_entry/harness.spi lacked, so regeneration silently removed it; now in the source, regenerated, dev.ps1 passes", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "eoie,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_regen_drift () = Planning ("EOIE-REGEN-DRIFT", Minutes 300u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl spiral3_editions () = Task ("SPIRAL3-EDITIONS", "Spiral 3 as an edition of the fork, both editions in one compiler (user 2026-10-12: mrakgr has not touched the language for over a year): edition per package in package.spiproj (Rust-edition style, mixed-edition imports allowed), lexical only: the tokenizer var table (spiral_compiler.fs ~43072, words -> TokKeyword Spec*) gets an edition-3 table mapping symbol keywords to the same Spec tokens and the operator lexer consults it first, so parser/typecheck/peval/backends stay shared; start from geandra_v0_4.py FORWARD (inl :=, let :~, rec ^, union :|, match ?=, nominal :!, prototype :?, instance :+, fun \\, if ?, else |:, ...) and audit collisions per edition (=> already a match arm); keep dot record access, 2-space indent as the edition-3 formatter default (parser is column based, verify); test blocks need an edition-3 spelling; gate: spiral convert --edition 3|2 round-trips every sample and lib .spi byte for byte and both editions compile to identical residuals; 2026-10-12 first collision audit (regex lexer over 1,739 .spi in spiral lib + samples, dice/lib, eoie/src; script tmp/edition3/collisions.py): 25 of the 29 FORWARD symbols never occur as operators today (free: !+ !- &= -| :! :+ :< := :== :? :| :~ ;; ?& ?: ?= \\* \\? \\| ^ |: |? ~> ~~ ~~>); => occurs 10,932 times as the match/lambda arrow (reusing it for then/with is a parser-context question, not a lexer clash); a real clash: & is pattern conjunction (`{ level } & trace_state`, 4 uses) so `and` needs another symbol in edition 3; the ? (60) and \\ (41) hits look like $'...' macro-string escapes the regex does not model, so redo the audit with the compiler tokenizer (SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY) before deciding; 2026-10-12 18:25 main, lexical-only check (reference converter tmp/edition3/lexical.py: Spiral-style tokens = words / maximal punctuation runs / strings+comments skipped; forward = keyword words -> symbols, reverse = symbol runs -> words; exact round trip per file over apps/compiler/tmp/samples + lib/spiral, 1,269 files): with the geandra_v0_4 FORWARD table 665/1,269 round-trip; drift is dominated by => (already the match-arm/lambda arrow in 602 files, and it also stands for both then and with, so reversing needs parser context, not lexing) and & for and (pattern conjunction, plus && glue); proposed table change: then -> ?>, with -> ?|, and -> :& (all three never appear as operators in the corpus) gives 1,262/1,269; the last 7 involve fun -> \\ next to the existing !\\ inline-code operator and $'...' strings with escaped quotes that the reference converter does not skip, to be settled by the real lexer; the geandra prototype itself only round-trips 26/820 samples (whole-program parser subset: rejects nominal/union and operators like +. =. $ !!!!), so its 116 tests are frontend acceptance cases, not a converter; correction: the note above is from 18:06, not 18:25; decided by the user 2026-10-12 18:44: table changes accepted (then ?>, with ?|, and :&) and edition-3 symbols lexed in every file (edition3_symbol_token, both cores, one shared Tokenize section); a per-package edition flag only when a real conflict needs it (upstream '#' escape); 18:45 first real-compiler check (single-flight Debug, 820-sample corpus, each sample compiled as written and converted to edition 3): 590 compared before the Debug batch hit a stack overflow; 249 ok in both with byte-identical C, 340 failed identically in both (C-backend contract rejections, intended type errors), 1 difference: closure_pair_bool, where !-, glued the comma into the run '!-,'; fixed in the shared Tokenize section (a run that is a symbol followed only by commas gives the commas back); rebuild + recheck queued; 19:00 recheck with the comma fix (single-flight Debug 18:47): 590 of 820 samples compared, 250 byte-identical C in both editions (closure_pair_bool included), 340 failed identically, 0 status or text differences; the Debug batch again died with a stack overflow (0xC00000FD) around sample 591, so the last 230 need a Release build run; check script tmp/edition3/build-and-check.ps1 + check.ps1, corpus tmp/edition3/corpus; user direction 2026-10-12 19:14: edition 3 prioritizes X compatibility (a source must survive being posted to X unchanged); '#': edition 2 = upstream (literal '#' in macro strings), edition 3 never uses '#' before a letter (no hashtags), so it needs its own escape spelling; this is the first real reason for the per-package edition flag; 20:03 edition-3 lexing verified harmless for edition 2 by single-flight-20261012-193841 (-Suite all -Native, Release built 19:36 from the source with the unified Tokenize section, edition-3 symbols + comma fix, WGSL nullary unions and the FOR-D offside fix): 3,799 jobs, baseline parity 3,793 / new 6 / missing+regressed 0 / residual-differs 0, native 2,775 ran, 11 build-fail, oracle agree 2,307, DISAGREE 0, 23 min: every existing row is byte-identical to the accepted oracle; 22:46 edition-3 lexing Release check (single-flight 22:26 DLL): 743 of 820 corpus samples: 363 identical C, 379 fail identically in both editions, 0 C text differences; the batch died at runaway_inline_match_recursion (e2 timeout, exit 3); the remaining 155 jobs (tmp/edition3/corpus/jobs-remaining.tsv) rerun after the InlineDepth guard; 00:07 edition-3 lexing check COMPLETE on Release: all 820 corpus samples: 438 identical C, 381 fail identically in both editions, 0 C text differences; the only status difference is runaway_inline_match_recursion (e2 timed out on the old 22:26 DLL, e3 stopped with EJP0011 on the 00:04 DLL with the InlineDepth guard), a DLL difference, not lexing; 2026-10-13 12:35 main: concrete first use: upstream programs (Spiral-s-ML-Library head) need prefix * = RawLayoutIndex (var or parenthesised term), while the fork's lib needs * = user ~* over the application chain; the parser plumbing (RawLayoutIndex through Infer/Prepass, ETY-ExpectedLayout) is in both cores, only the surface case needs the edition switch; Kino already reads edition: 3 from package.spiproj for X-compat; 2026-10-13 18:05 main: first switch landed and accepted (pack 3): DefaultEnv.edition (SpiralEdition = UpstreamEdition2 | ForkEdition3), --edition 2|3 on the host / SPIRAL_EDITION, default 3; edition 2 parses prefix * as upstream's layout index; lib/spiral unaffected (lib smoke green both cores); next candidates for the switch: '#' inside macro strings, edition3_symbol_token keywords", Epic, P0, D7, 35u32, Planned, "SOURCE-BOUNDARY-AUTHORITY", "compiler,edition,syntax,main,team:compiler", "current", "current")
