inl note_of_ml_labs_11 () = Note ("ML-LABS", 11u32, "2026-11-02T11:12Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia lane, CORRECTED 11-02 after the user pointed at the history. My first version said no older tibia plan survives. That was wrong: TIBIA-AGENT (Done, 53 notes) IS the plan. Its title: \"Agent from mrakgr's graph code upgraded with the mega-sample patterns\".\nHistory, all from backlog notes:\n- 10-12: the tibia lane probed the ML library and filed UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC.\n- 10-13: TIBIA-POLICY-FEATURES built src/network.spi (Q8 8-6-3) as \"groundwork without the ML library (whose entry points are bound to its CUDA/Python host stack)\".\n- 10-22, TIBIA-AGENT rule A1 (n9): porting means re-hosting the primitives on C and WGSL, not copying. Milestones, one novelty each: M1 = dense layer + staged-graph memory plan + CEM (ml/cem.spi) on C; M2 = typed per-agent view (the pickler idea, n6); M3 = sizes as type indices + raw/planned/frozen typestate.\n- Results: the M1 CEM port failed twice (14.76 vs network.evolve's 13.47 potions; n35, n47). M2e (the 25-input typed view under network.evolve) failed at 47.60 (n52). Stop note n53. M3 was drafted green (6/6 Cells; bit-exact against network.decide, 3 compile-fail pins; n49) but never ran or landed, because milestones are judged in sequence.\nDrafts survive at tibia/target/predict/agent-m1 (search.spi evolve_cem), agent-m2e (views.sighted, wide_features) and agent-m3 (src/typed_network.spi).\nAnswers, revised:\n(1) What tibia took was the ideas, not the code: CEM, the memory plan, the typestate graph and the typed view. The integer-only rule (standards.spi) is deliberate, for C/WGSL bit-exactness. It is not drift. The open reuse is M3's typed_network, which is unlanded.\n(2) Backends: C, Rust, WGSL, Lua. corebase arrays still rule out direct use.\n(3) A transformer lab owns its package. A shared typed-graph core in lib (sizes as indices, plan/freeze typestate, a generic element type) is where tibia's M3 and the lab would meet.")
inl note_of_ml_labs_12 () = Note ("ML-LABS", 12u32, "2026-11-02T11:15Z", "regex", "regex 07:2x LINK: TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB (filed 11-02 for the user) depends on this item; tibia's n11 answer is folded into it (a lib shape/dimension core with C/Rust/WGSL arms is the shared piece tibia would consume).")
inl note_of_ml_labs_13 () = Note ("ML-LABS", 13u32, "2026-11-02T14:07Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia: the Tensor Lab half of this epic is now carried by the lib items filed under TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB (LIB-TYPE-SHAPES, LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS, LIB-ARENA-PLANNER, LIB-OP-GRAPH, LIB-ROW-OPS, LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES). The Leduc Lab's learning machinery (CEM ensembles, CFR+/VR-MCCFR, LSH tables, the game-node state machine) is carried by TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS. Full per-file inventory: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md. Library lessons, inventory section 6: neural CFR/CEM never learned NL Hold'em, and the Hebbian/K-means dictionaries were abandoned. Proposal: close this epic as superseded once those items are Active; the call belongs to main (the epic is tagged main).")
inl package_registry_design () = Task ("PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN", "Package manager design: exact caller-pinned locks (the prototype's plan format), declared capabilities checked at install, index separate from blob storage (crates.io model: index + object storage/CDN; Cloudflare R2 candidate), signatures; social platforms (X/Bluesky/Mastodon) only as optional mirrors and discovery, never the source of truth; 2026-10-14 02:20 lane 3 typed model (not compiled; C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\registry\\model.spi, 290 lines of Spiral nominals/unions/records + operation types), built from the prototype's planner (geandra_v0_4.py validate_lock/plan_install: schema, caller-pinned root, digest-keyed nodes, iterative DFS order, cycle/unreachable rejection, grants vs declared capabilities, offline/budget): exact locks (exact_version, exact_requirement carries the dependency's package_id, RootDiffersFromCallerPin), declared capabilities as a union (files by path scope, network host, process, env, foreign library per backend, GPU, clock) checked against granted ones at install (CapabilitiesNotGranted lists package*capability), index separate from blobs (signed append-only index_checkpoint chain of Released/Yanked entries vs content-addressed blob_origin ObjectStore bucket/key e.g. R2, social platforms only as MirrorOnly with a required authoritative digest), detached Ed25519 signatures for releases and checkpoints; PACKAGE-JUNCTIONS: ModuleDirectory packages live as immutable directories in a content-addressed store and are linked into the workspace by DirectoryJunction (files by hard link or copy; errors JunctionTargetNotDirectory, StoreEntryMutable); editions and default numerics are per release (edition UpstreamEdition2|ForkEdition3, numeric_defaults) and travel to the compiler as one compile_unit per package, which needs the compiler to hold DefaultEnv per package instead of per process; correction: model.spi is 284 lines, not 290", Story, P1, D5, 75u32, Planned, "", "packages,registry,team:main,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_package_registry_design () = Planning ("PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN", Minutes 600u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
