inl note_of_mega_samples_together_1 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:29Z", "main-thread", "08:29 finding: negative_forge_constructive_minimality_witness compiles once its unbound names are fixed (root_* aliases) and returns true. A 1-state minimality witness for ends_with_zero type-checks because indexed_dfa_minimality_witness is a public constructor and nothing at the type level ties the rows to the representative count. The sample's encoding has a gap; the compiler is not at fault. Restored to HEAD (old unbound-name parity row); root-names copy is in the job tmp/rotation. Fix: make the witness constructible only through a sealed checker (prototype/opaque) and give the negative a type-level count mismatch.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_2 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:56Z", "lane-a", "08:56 lane-a: oracle matrix: all 252 negatives error as intended; native rows only for the roots (brz 4 pkgs, others 1); ERP has no Lua/Wasm row. Shared gaps across all 5: forgeable witnesses (SPIRAL-PRIVATE-CONSTRUCTORS design) and record update base (lane-A patch).")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_3 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:49Z", "main-thread", "06:49 groom: the 5 mega roots (brzozowski, lean_cic, omniledger, spiral_proves_spiral, zeta) compile ok in every full suite tonight (mega suite 5/5). Lane A's formatter G3 found mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency sensitive to type layout, a useful canary for this item.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_4 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 4u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: the Lean CIC mega sample stays frozen as a compiler oracle; the kernel continues as notebooks in LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_5 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 5u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night status from the pack review: brzozowski 115 rows (48 native, 44 agree with C), lean_cic 56 (13, 12), omniledger 57 (10, 9), spiral_proves_spiral 106 (13, 12), zeta 63 (13, 12); every mega compile error is a contract row (deliberate), so all five compile on every listed backend.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_6 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 6u32, "2026-10-17T18:24Z", "bundle-wisdom", "14:24 from brzozowski alpha54 + samples alpha705 agile_eoie.md (2026-09-19/26). Modeling idioms that worked (verify against today's compiler): capture prototype-driven ops (regex_equal, symbol_compare, normalize) as nominal alphabet-indexed capabilities BEFORE a GADT match, because implicit dictionary recovery after the match fails; keep the strongest structural witness authoritative and project weaker views from it (positioned regex derived from the position tree); 'nominal succ n = ()' let a 3-slot vector inhabit a 2-slot type, and '= length' fixed it, so pin it as a regression; refinement is lost after an existential unpack into a generic helper, so certify inside the refinement branch. Compiler sentinels from that lane: emitted union box/unbox tags must come from the emitted case order after specialization (tag-compaction bug, US1_5 vs US1_0); degenerate-union failure continuations specialized per remaining case removed FS0025 without wildcards; an assert inside the residual plus fsi --exec replaces stdout parsing; differential probes bind source hash + expected outcome (one 'compiler blocker' was a probe bug). Not carried into today's repo: the ERP strict burn-in gate (10 s ceiling, active_calls=12, persistent fsi-multi-verifier) and proof-export\\ (see LEAN-BACKEND).")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_7 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 7u32, "2026-10-19T06:40Z", "claude", "2026-10-19 02:40 x lane (git-2c) read all five mega samples for modeling ideas (user 2026-10-19: see if their modeling can inspire x, tibia or eoie). Matrix finding for the main lane, no action asked now: the samples' negative fixture folders are weak oracles. apps/compiler/tmp/tests/matrix.psd1 ExpectedErrors (from line 218) pins expected error text for brzozowski only, so a negative in the other four passes on any compile error; examples: zeta negative_legacy_completion_refusal_arbitrary_text uses a constructor main.spi no longer defines, and two omniledger negatives fail with Unbound variable (sample README:203-207). In-file 'test x fails ETY-TermError <message>' blocks (tibia style) would pin the reason. None of the five uses union private, so every *_authority/certificate constructor is forgeable; the sound techniques are the evidence-carrying decision unions (zeta order/search decisions, lean typed meta identity, omniledger duplicate/collision outcomes), the phase typestate (brzozowski bit_matcher_state, omniledger chain of custody), erased nominal handles (runtime_interned) and the linear merge with no Used/Used case (spiral_proves S:555-583). Gleam codegen of GADT-indexed unions was fixed only in pack-1x, so the sim port keeps indices shallow")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_8 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 8u32, "2026-10-19T12:35Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:35 lap 1 grain: sized the x lane's ExpectedErrors finding from today's review results (no compile needed): negatives per mega 31 brzozowski (28 pinned), lean_cic 40, omniledger 44, spiral_proves 90, zeta 47, the last four with 0 pinned texts; their 221 F# rows all fail compile, by code: ETY-TermError 208, ETY-UnboundVariable 11 (stale names such as erp_p2p_unit_event_from_plan, CertifiedIntervalPositivePositionalLegacyCompletionRefused: these test nothing), ETY-UnionsCannotBeApplied 1, existential dyn 1; table at spiral/lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/negatives.tsv Next: pin the 208 TermError texts as ExpectedErrors entries (generated from the table), and fix the 13 stale negatives so each fails for its intended reason")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_9 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 9u32, "2026-10-19T13:35Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:35 lap 2 grain: pinned the 208 TermError negatives. lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/pin-term-errors.py reads today's review (single-flight-20261019-072348 results.tsv), takes each compile-error row of the 4 unpinned families whose FIRST error code is ETY-TermError (rows that start with UnboundVariable are the stale ones and are left out), and writes Contains = ETY-TermError: Unification failure. Got: <the got type> Expected: (the got side names what each negative breaks; 3 contain the type variable 'a, quote-escaped). Applied to tests/matrix.psd1 ExpectedErrors: 43 -> 251 entries (lean_cic 40, omniledger 41, spiral_proves 88, zeta 39 = 208); the file loads with Import-PowerShellDataFile -SkipLimitCheck, and replaying test.ps1's check (detail.Contains per compile-error row, lines 1036-1039) over today's rows gives 0 WRONG-ERROR across the 296 covered error rows. From the next review on, a negative that starts failing for another reason shows as WRONG-ERROR instead of passing silently. Left: the 13 stale negatives (11 ETY-UnboundVariable on renamed definitions such as erp_p2p_unit_event_from_plan, 1 UnionsCannotBeApplied, 1 existential dyn): each needs its source fixed so it fails for its intended reason, then a pin. Next: list the 13 with their unbound names and the current names they should use (grep the family sources)")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_10 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 10u32, "2026-10-19T14:12Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:12 lap 3 grain: the 13 stale negatives traced and decided. 11 fail on names that do not exist in their family root at all (omniledger erp_p2p_unit_event_from_plan, erp_p2p_three_owner_physical_takeover_authority; spiral_proves impossible_inhabited_bool_empty_match; zeta CertifiedIntervalPositivePositional{CompletionBlocked, LegacyCompletionRefused, LegacyCompletionRefusalDescentUnavailable}, certified_interval_positive_positional_legacy_completion_refusal, two certified_arithmetic_rooted_ordered_prime_power_nf_uniqueness_mixed_second_prime_* obligations): git log -S on main shows they arrived with the 09-27 import (1eb2ecfd) already pointing at surfaces the roots had retired (the roots' own comments, stripped on 10-08 in 98492a63, said Retired ... source quarantined); the zeta root's proof strings still name LegacyCompletionRefused elimination as the open goal. Plus 1 UnionsCannotBeApplied (omniledger recorded_hash_primary_caller_membership) and 1 Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var. (spiral_proves beta_strengthening_target_without_index_transport). Decision: pin all 13 with their current first error rather than rewrite them, because their intent (the retired constructor cannot be used to forge a refusal) holds exactly while the name stays absent, and a pin turns a reintroduction into WRONG-ERROR; rewriting them against today's GADT surfaces is real mega work that belongs with the zeta/omniledger proof goals. lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/pin-stale.py (dry run lists the 13 entries; --apply appends them to ExpectedErrors). Not applied: matrix inputs change only between main's runs (main's rule 10-19). HEAVY QUEUE row (apply between runs, no run needed beyond the next review). With it every negative of the 4 families is pinned (208 + 13 = 221). Next: per family, list what each root cannot express today (the item's goal), starting with zeta's LegacyCompletionRefused elimination")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_11 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 11u32, "2026-10-19T14:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:32 lap 4 grain, the item's per-root question (what each root cannot express today) answered from the roots' own statements: their proof strings end in while ... remain open, so mining while-<goals>-remain-open over each root main.spi lists the open goals mechanically. zeta (10 statements): arbitrary (factorization) tree uniqueness 7x, accessibility over arbitrary strict predecessors with quotient descent, factorization-specific and flattened quotient composition with transitive candidate descent (the retired LegacyCompletionRefused elimination is part of these). omniledger (19): physical durability 4x (real fsync, atomic rename, CAS, process-kill evidence), field-complete byte-only tree reconstruction 3x, type-level open identity (families) 3x, arbitrary field decoding, true multiprocess linearizability. lean_cic (2): general renaming/lifting, substitution, a generic total structural defeq engine. spiral_proves (8): substitution 4x, general recursive term renaming under lambda 2x, universal term coverage 2x, all-used closure, arbitrary beta, composite term renaming. brzozowski: none stated. Shared shape across 3 roots: substitution plus renaming under binders (lean_cic, spiral_proves, zeta's quotient descent), i.e. what needs type-level recursion over indexed terms; that is the candidate compiler capability that would advance several roots at once, per the user's 10-06 idea. Next: write the smallest Spiral sample of type-level renaming under a binder (de Bruijn shift over a GADT term) and see where the compiler stops")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_12 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 12u32, "2026-10-19T14:36Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:36 drive slice: the shared blocker is found and filed. Static renaming under binders works (de Bruijn term GADT, inl rec rename/lift: compiles, correct result), but the runtime form the roots need (a let rec join point over a runtime term whose recursion goes term n -> term (succ n)) hangs the compiler; a runtime join point with a fixed index compiles. Filed as GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (P1, compiler lane) with three repros in spiral/lab/GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX, and made it a dep of this item: substitution/renaming over arbitrary (runtime) terms in lean_cic and spiral_proves, and quotient descent in zeta, are this shape")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_13 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 13u32, "2026-10-19T15:24Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:24 lap 5 grain: re-ran pin-stale.py read-only on today's matrix: still exactly 13 stale negatives. Classified their current first errors: 11 of 13 fail on an UNBOUND name of a retired surface (ETY-UnboundVariable for erp_p2p_unit_event_from_plan, erp_p2p_three_owner_physical_takeover_authority, impossible_inhabited_bool_empty_match, and 8 zeta CertifiedIntervalPositivePositional... / certified_arithmetic_rooted_... names). A pin on an unbound name proves nothing (any typo would fail the same way), so pinning those 11 hides that they no longer test their property. Only 2 fail for a reason tied to the property: negative_recorded_hash_primary_caller_membership (ETY-UnionsCannotBeApplied) and negative_beta_strengthening_target_without_index_transport (Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var). Decision proposed for main (sample inputs are main's): pin those 2 as today's row says, and retire or rewrite the 11 against the live surface instead of pinning them; until then they stay unpinned and visible as stale. Still blocked for the runtime rewrite on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_14 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 14u32, "2026-10-19T15:41Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:41 lap 6 grain: the user-side workaround (option a, phantom-index erasure, done in sample code instead of the compiler) is drafted as lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/erased_runtime_rename.spi. The de Bruijn term GADT stays static, so binders are still checked by the type system. A static inl rec erase maps term n to an index-free runtime union erased (EVar i32 / ELam / EApp), and the runtime work runs as let rec on that union: shifted (cutoff, by) and free_sum. A let rec over a fixed type never grows an index, so it avoids the hang. Expected result worked by hand: 42 (free occurrences 2 before the shift, 4 after: 4*10+2). Queued a 1-minute try.ps1 row after the switch window. If it compiles, lean_cic and spiral_proves can do runtime substitution this way today, and the compiler fix stays a nicety.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_15 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 15u32, "2026-10-19T16:01Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:01 lap 7 grain, the port target for the erased-index workaround in lean_cic: samples/mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel/main.spi 4290 lift_corrected_cic_term_by_extension. It is a static inl rec that weakens a corrected_cic_term across a context-extension plan, and its terminal (4335) says that general renaming under binders, Pi and substitution remain open. Port plan once the queued try row returns 42: an index-free runtime union for corrected_cic_term (variable index, Pi, lambda, application, sorts), a static erase over the GADT, and let rec shift/substitute on the erased form, plus one new terminal that checks a runtime renaming under a binder. The GADT stays the static proof of well-sortedness. Sample inputs are main's, so the port will be staged as a lab patch with expected new pins.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_16 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 16u32, "2026-10-19T16:42Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:42 lap 8 grain: drafted the lean_cic half of the port as lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/lean_cic_erased.spi: an index-free runtime union erased_cic_term (sort, var index, constant, definition, lambda, Pi, dependent lambda, dependent application, application, let), a static inl rec erase_corrected_cic_term over all 12 corrected_cic_term cases (main.spi 201-248; existentials opened with inl exists like apply_cic_corrected_substitution; CorrectedBoundThere becomes a runtime shift of the erased outer term, the de Bruijn weakening), and let rec shift and free-index-sum over the erased form, so runtime renaming under binders never grows a GADT index. Also rechecked the queued erased_runtime_rename.spi for core v1 (+, >= live in core.spi) and re-derived its expected exit 42 by hand. Next: after that try row returns 42, append this fragment to a scratch copy of the sample with one terminal that renames under a Pi binder")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_17 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 17u32, "2026-10-19T17:18Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:18 lap 9 grain: the lean_cic port is now a runnable probe package instead of a loose fragment: lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/rename_probe/ = package.spiproj (packageDir to the samples, packages core- and mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel-), erased_kernel.spi (the erased fragment + open main; replaces lean_cic_erased.spi) and main.spi, one renaming terminal over the kernel's own identity_binder: identity lambda, CorrectedBoundHere and CorrectedBoundThere erased statically, then the runtime let rec shift; expected exit 221 traced by hand. Queue row added (after the 42 try row). Next: run it; if it compiles, append the fragment into lean_cic main.spi as a sample candidate for main")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_18 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 18u32, "2026-10-19T17:41Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:41 lap 10 grain: static clash check of the rename probe against the 9,296-line kernel: none of the fragment's names (erased_cic_term, its 10 Erased cases, shifted_/erase_/free_index_sum_ functions) occur in the kernel; identity_binder (used by the terminal) is the kernel's own (11 uses); the kernel ends with inl main () : string = cic_root_contract () (line 9296), which the probe's own later main () : i32 shadows after open main, and the kernel defines no operators, so +, >=, - and * in erased_kernel come from core- alone. Next: the queued probe compile (expect 221)")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_19 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 19u32, "2026-10-19T17:56Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:56 lap 11 grain: post-accept recheck of the two pin scripts: pin-term-errors.py finds 0 new ExpectedErrors entries in all 4 mega families (its pins are in the matrix), and pin-stale.py still proposes exactly 13 stale-negative pins with the same texts (e.g. zeta negative_recursive_divisor_refusal_wrong_child pinned on its unbound type variable), none of them present in matrix.psd1 yet; so pack 7 changed none of the mega negatives' first errors. The queued 42 try row and the 221 rename probe are still unrun (no runs/try entries for them). Next: main runs pin-stale.py --apply between runs, then the two try rows")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_20 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 20u32, "2026-10-19T17:57Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:57 correction to the 13:56 note: pin-stale.py read a fixed 08:05 run, so that note's pack-7 claim was not yet shown; pin-stale.py now takes --run <name> (default unchanged), and run against the pack 7 accept single-flight-20261019-125623 it prints the identical 13 pins (output byte-equal to the 08:05 run), which now does show pack 7 left the mega negatives' first errors unchanged. Main can apply with --run single-flight-20261019-125623 --apply")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_21 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 21u32, "2026-10-19T18:29Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 14:29 lap 12: the erased-index workaround for GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX works on the installed pack 7 compiler: lab erased_runtime_rename.spi (GADT term static, static inl rec erase to an index-free runtime union, let rec shift/count on that) compiles to C and exits 42 as the probe expects. Next: the rename_probe row against the real lean_cic kernel package (180 s budget, stays in the queue)")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_22 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 22u32, "2026-10-19T22:56Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 18:56 lap 19 grain: pin-stale.py --run single-flight-20261019-161549 (pack 9 accept) prints output identical to its pack 7 run (0 differing lines, the same 13 pins), so packs 8b and 9 left the mega negatives' first errors unchanged; main can apply with that run name between runs. Next: the rename_probe row")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_23 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 23u32, "2026-10-22T07:09Z", "main", "03:09 main: pin-stale.py --run single-flight-20261021-190054 (tonight's night-pack review) prints the same 13 pins as the 10-19 runs, so packs 7 through the night pack left the mega negatives' first errors unchanged. NOT applied, deliberately: 12 of the 13 now fail on an unbound name (a renamed or removed definition) and 1 on 'Cannot dyn an existential', so they are stale negatives that no longer reach the rejection they were written for. Pinning their current text would turn each into a permanently passing row that tests nothing. The item's fix is to repair each negative so it reaches its intended rejection (or delete it when the API it tested is gone), then pin the real error. The 13 ids are listed by the script. Kept in lab for that work.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_24 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 24u32, "2026-10-22T09:53Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:53 main: deciding the 13 stale negatives myself (memory decide-autonomously). Rule fixed before looking: for each negative, take the unbound name it now fails on and grep the family's non-negative sources (its package files, excluding negative_* folders). (R1) The exact name is defined: the negative's own text is broken, so repair it there. (R2) A definition shares the name's distinctive stem (the name minus generic words such as certified, interval, positive, positional, legacy): repair by switching to that definition, if it is the same concept (same case or type role). (R3) No such definition: the API the negative tested is gone, so delete the negative folder by rule (worktree only, the user commits). The two non-unbound ones (UnionsCannotBeApplied; Cannot dyn an existential) are read by hand and repaired if their intended rejection is still expressible. Every repair is verified after tibia's block by compiling that negative and checking that it reaches a TermError-class rejection rather than an unbound name; then its message is pinned with pin-term-errors.py.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_25 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 25u32, "2026-10-22T09:55Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:55 main: applied the 05:53 rule. None of the 9 unbound names is defined in its family's non-negative sources (R1 none). The stem greps found no same-concept definition for 10 negatives: zeta's LegacyCompletionRefused survives only inside prose strings (main.spi 2875, 4058), and the takeover-authority and inhabited-empty-match stems hit nothing. So R3 applies to 10: 8 zeta, 1 spiral_proves, 1 omniledger. DELETED now (worktree only, clean and unstaged): zeta negative_completion_blocked_raw_payload, negative_legacy_completion_refusal_arbitrary_text, negative_recursive_child_refusal_without_child_witness; spiral_proves negative_quantified_no_closed_false_inhabited_empty_match, plus its row in lanes/formatter/allowlist.tsv (rows pin files by sha256, so the row would have dangled). HELD, not deleted: 6 R3 folders whose main.spi the user has staged (index M): zeta negative_descent_unavailable_divisor_wrong_child, negative_legacy_completion_raw_classification, negative_mixed_contradiction_obligation_not_rejection, negative_mixed_rejected_obstruction_not_found_consistency (allowlist row 26 goes with it), negative_recursive_divisor_refusal_wrong_child; omniledger negative_three_owner_physical_takeover_authority_wrong_endpoint. Resume condition: once git status shows a folder clean (the user committed), delete it by the same rule with no new check needed. Left for hand repair (verify after tibia's block): omniledger negative_recursive_payload_outbox_version_mismatch (erp_p2p_unit_event_from_plan is gone, but union erp_p2p_unit_event still exists at main.spi:6002, so it may be repairable through its constructor), omniledger negative_recorded_hash_primary_caller_membership (UnionsCannotBeApplied), spiral_proves negative_beta_strengthening_target_without_index_transport (Cannot dyn an existential).")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_26 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 26u32, "2026-10-22T09:57Z", "main", "2026-10-22 05:57 main: hand cases. (1) omniledger negative_recursive_payload_outbox_version_mismatch REPAIRED: erp_p2p_unit_event_from_plan (X_plan ()) became erp_p2p_unit_event_from_op (X_op ()) for reserve_budget, collect_approvals and issue_purchase_order. All 10 names it uses are defined (main.spi 275-9265), and its intended rejection, a four-event store against a three-event outbox, is untouched. A compile probe (job-1792663022675-main-negative-probe, single-flight C) is queued behind tibia's block; pass = a TermError-class rejection with no unbound name, then pin it with pin-term-errors.py. (2) omniledger negative_recorded_hash_primary_caller_membership DELETED by R3: case TypedFxHashedStatementClosedRecordedHashPrimary is nullary now (main.spi 3771), so applying it to a membership is UnionsCannotBeApplied, and the membership type typed_fx_hashed_statement_history_contains no longer exists, so the caller-supplied-membership API it guarded is gone; no references outside the folder. (3) spiral_proves negative_beta_strengthening_target_without_index_transport HELD: the user has staged it. Tally of the 13: 1 repaired, 5 deleted, 7 held as staged (resume = clean git status).")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_27 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 27u32, "2026-10-22T10:11Z", "main", "2026-10-22 06:11 main: the repaired omniledger negative_recursive_payload_outbox_version_mismatch probe ran in the gap between tibia's live windows (single-flight C, 4.7 s): exit 5, 'FatalError: File main has a type error somewhere in its path', a type error rather than an unbound-name failure at parse. That is the intended class of rejection. The exact ETY message comes from the next matrix run's detail column, which pin-term-errors.py pins.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_28 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 28u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap drive5 10:36 (subagent2): shared blocker found: let rec join point over a runtime GADT with a growing index hangs the compiler (static version works); filed GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX with 3 repros, dep added -> next: after the compiler fix: rewrite one lean_cic substitution as runtime code | lap 13 14:41 (subagent2): waiting: rename_probe needs ~180 s (over the 2-min bounded slot), pin-stale --apply is main's matrix edit -> next: main's queue: rename_probe row, pin-stale apply | lap 14 15:03 (subagent2): waiting: rename_probe (~180 s) and pin-stale apply -> next: main's queue | lap 16 16:06 (subagent2): waiting: rename_probe (~180 s) + pin-stale apply -> next: main's queue | lap 17 16:43 (subagent2): unchanged -> next: main's queue | lap 21 19:21 (subagent2): pin-stale.py: a second --apply found 0 entries and would still have inserted a blank line into ExpectedErrors; it now refuses an empty apply and takes --matrix <copy>; checked on a matrix copy: first apply +13 lines (psd1 parses), second refuses -> next: main applies pin-stale --run single-flight-20261019-161549 --apply between runs")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_29 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 29u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_30 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 30u32, "2026-10-31T03:21Z", "main", "10-30 23:21 main: lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER is ARCHIVED (user, 10-30 22:5x: the lab dir didn't work and drifted; drafts don't live outside the repo). Archive 20261030-232045 under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive. Restore this folder with: pwsh i574n.github/scripts/scratch-archive.ps1 -Root C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab -Restore '%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045\\manifest.tsv' -Only 'MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER\\*' -RestoreTo C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab. Resume this item's work in its real place in the repo, not in lab.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_31 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 31u32, "2026-10-31T20:29Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:29 compiler, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK): Paused -> PLANNED, back in agile next. It was paused by the 3-day silence rule, not by a decision; the 5 mega samples are the closest stand-in for a self-hosted compiler-sized Spiral program (compile speed and codegen on big inputs), a SELF-HOSTED-SPIRAL concern.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_32 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 32u32, "2026-11-01T04:50Z", "main", "main 00:5x LAB CODE IS SAFE (user 11-01 00:2x: 'check for all lab references in history... make sure we didn't lose that code... to repurpose them or groom their tasks'). This item's lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER folder (7 files: erased_runtime_rename.spi, negatives.tsv, pin-stale.py, pin-term-errors.py, rename_probe\\erased_kernel.spi, rename_probe\\main.spi) is archived in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045 (blob-verified). Restore it into its proper repo place with: pwsh C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\scripts\\scratch-archive.ps1 -Restore '%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045\\manifest.tsv' -RestoreTo <repo dir> -Only 'MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/*'. Next step for the owner at its next pull: restore the useful files in place as incomplete drafts (Cells heals them in place), or record why it starts over.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_33 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 33u32, "2026-11-01T12:04Z", "main", "main 08:1x: DIRECTION-1031's research picked brzozowski as the first public product (BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT, M0-M9 with gates against rust/regex on rebar). That doesn't undo this item's 'advance all five together' for compiler fixes; the product track takes brzozowski further while the other four keep pulling compiler gaps.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_34 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 34u32, "2026-11-02T12:27Z", "regex", "regex 08:3x RETIREMENT MAP of all five mega samples (user 11-02: rewrite each in its real home, then archive): brzozowski -> regex (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB, gate REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION n2); lean_cic -> spiral/apps/cic (LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS children CIC-*, archive CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE); zeta -> lib/spiral/zeta (ZETA-FINAL, archive ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE); omniledger ERP -> fiscal generic layer (FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC, archive OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE); spiral_proves_spiral -> notebooks (SPS-NOTEBOOKS, purpose SPS-PURPOSE, archive SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE). Every archive keeps one minimal compiler regression sample per guarded bug and swaps this item's canary to the new home's CI; archive, never delete; user go each time.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_35 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 35u32, "2026-11-02T14:36Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MIGRATION DONE RULE (user 11-02: \"make sure all these mega sample migrations have a definition of done so they don't spin forever again, and so we remove their code from the repo asap so we keep only latest code following the new style with test cells etc ... gotta transfer all the goodies before though, different than what regex did, only implemented a sliver then called it done\"). APPLIES TO all five: brzozowski (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB / REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION), lean_cic (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB / CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE), zeta (ZETA-TYPED-ARITH + ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE / ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE), omniledger (FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP / OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE), spiral_proves_spiral (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT + SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS / SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE). (1) A migration is DONE only when the old sample is ARCHIVED out of the repo; a new home that works (regex published, CI green) is NOT done while absorption rows remain (the regex lesson: 9 of 71 legacy items absorbed at \"publishable\"). (2) Before the archive, every absorption-map row is resolved: (a) absorbed = a passing test in the new home in CI on both OSes, citing the legacy line; (b) lib = landed with lib tests; (c) compiler = a minimal regression sample with a matrix row; (d) dropped = a reason the map states. No row is left \"partial\". (3) ANTI-SPIN: the map is written first (one item, <= 4 h), then every (a)/(b) row is worked in priority order with the row count reported on the parent each groom round (absorbed / total); a week with no row closed raises the parent to P0 for the next round; a row blocked only by a compiler bug becomes its (c) regression sample plus a compiler item, and the archive may proceed with that row recorded as blocked-in-compiler (the goodie survives as the repro, in the new style). (4) The archive step runs in the SAME groom round the last row closes (scratch-archive.ps1, hash-verified, restore command in a note, dangling check by stem, user go), and MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER swaps its canary to the new home. (5) The parent item is set Done only after the archive note exists.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_together_36 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER", 36u32, "2026-11-02T14:59Z", "main", "main 11-02 DECIDED, no longer a user decision: the 'go' to archive a legacy mega sample is the migration-done rule (n35), not a separate user approval. RULE (fixed before looking, per the user via fiscal 11-02: \"those things can be decided autonomously\"; technical calls are ours, decided by a pre-stated rule with rule and outcome recorded). Rule: archive in the same groom round its last absorption row closes, with a hash-verified archive and a restore command (archive-never-delete). The user said 'it'll be a long road until deleting that lab mega sample', so the gate is the absorb rows, not a date.")
inl compiler_namespace_collisions () = Task ("COMPILER-NAMESPACE-COLLISIONS", "Fix name collisions in the compiler instead of moving code around (user 2026-10-06 18:04 'are you sure moving code was the best call? can't we fix the compiler so everything gets working without namespace collisions?'): reproduce the collisions that forced code moves (lib/apps during the fable-to-native migration), make module/package scoping resolve them, then move the code back where it belongs", TaskKind, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,modules,main,lab-held", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_namespace_collisions () = Planning ("COMPILER-NAMESPACE-COLLISIONS", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl default_backend_decision () = Task ("DEFAULT-BACKEND-DECISION", "Pick Spiral's default backend (user 2026-10-06 23:49 'shouldn't rust (or lua) be the default spiral backend? since fsharp have the dotnet boot up time, and not even mrakgr uses it anymore'; ratings were given that night): decide, then change the CLI/Kino default and the docs, keeping F# reachable by flag; decided by the user 2026-10-12 18:44: Zig becomes the default once it runs at C speed (ZIG-HUB-SPEED); F# stays the default until then; 2026-10-13 23:41 user decision: the final default needs CROSS-BACKEND-BENCHMARK with every backend at state of the art; until then the default is the fastest backend that beats F#, preferably not C (C tooling), picked by measurement (compile + run time on the same programs)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "CROSS-BACKEND-BENCHMARK", "compiler,backends,decision", "current", "current")
