inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_3 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 3u32, "2026-10-18T23:35Z", "claude", "Runner lab/EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC/one-call-runner.ps1 on build 1 (19:15): 12/34 green, exactly the target set 1 2 3 7 8 9 10 11 13 14 25 26. Next slice in build 3: crate eoie_do_facts (682 generated lines; sha2, regex, serde_json; globs via a new eoie_do_read_matching export) for hash (28), env + exists (19), nearest (18), json get (20), lines count by (22), files count by extension (17); fact union + grammar tests; eoie_do decode routes any fact verb to FactProgram; facts and read queries cannot share one program yet. Still red after it: run/stop/errors (6 15 16 24 33), git (12 23 31 32), dirs (4), diff (5), append (21), table (27), copy (29), job (30), lab audit (34).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_4 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 4u32, "2026-10-18T23:57Z", "claude", "Build 3 (19:50): runner 17/34 green, adding 17 18 19 20 28 (facts crate). 22 was red because the program tokenizer dropped the backslash of unknown escapes (\\w became w); build 4 keeps \\x unless x is a quote or backslash (regression test regex_escapes_survive_the_tokenizer). Build 4 also adds crate eoie_do_process (823 lines; sysinfo, regex; per-run job object so stops take the tree; clears NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath so cmd /c finds root scripts) for run/until/background/stop, tail output, search in output, errors in output by, processes where command ~; a scratch probe matched cases 6 15 16 33 byte for byte (15 depends on 5-digit pids: its header pads pid to the widest pid). table count by (27) joined the facts crate, probe matches. Left after build 4: 4 dirs, 5 diff, 12 23 31 32 git (need a setup grammar: git init/commit at/write/append line), 21 append, 24 edit+run in one program, 29 copy, 30 job in do, 34 lab audit.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_5 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 5u32, "2026-10-19T00:33Z", "claude", "Builds 4-6 (20:32): runner 24/34 green. Build 4: process crate live (6 15 16 33), table count by (27), tokenizer escape fix (22). Build 5b: pid column fixed at width 7 so the processes table no longer depends on pid length (spec case 15 header updated to it); runner rule: the spaces after a placeholder cell are flexible, since <HH:mm> and <pid> are padded at placeholder width in the spec; quoted run words keep their quotes. Build 6: edits then runs in one program (24): eoie_do validates and commits edits, then eoie_do_process_rejection (checked before any write) and eoie_do_process_after_edits (report, counts, failed) give one combined receipt; a failed edit runs nothing. eoie_do sits at 991 generated lines after part_at/printed became let; the next eoie_do feature needs a split. Still red: 4 dirs, 5 diff, 12 23 31 32 git (setup grammar), 21 append, 29 copy, 30 job, 34 lab audit.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_6 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 6u32, "2026-10-19T01:01Z", "claude", "Build 8b (21:01): runner 25/34 green; case 4 dirs/tag/count by landed in the facts crate (930 generated lines). A dirs line owns the tag and count lines below it; tag expressions combine <file> ~ \"re\" with and, or, not (or of ands). Build 7 had a panic: real program records carry empty fields, which the hand-encoded probe never had (lesson: probe with trailing empty fields). The test that nested a nullary constructor in a pattern (FactParsed DirsDetail) failed to parse; it now asserts through rejection_at. Still red (9): 5 diff, 12 23 31 32 git (setup grammar), 21 append, 29 copy, 30 job in do, 34 lab audit.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_7 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 7u32, "2026-10-19T01:05Z", "claude", "Case 5 diff (21:20) deferred to its own crate: written into eoie_do_facts it pushed the crate to 1,047 generated lines (gate 1,000). Profile: outcome_merged 160 and receipt_counts 92 lines, because each { state with ... } arm rebuilds a 30-field tally. A typed counter union over an Rc<RefCell<[u64; 30]>> barely helped (1,052): per-arm payload rebinding and one let per literal argument eat the savings, and inl->let on small helpers made it worse (1,065). Facts sources restored to the build 8b set (regenerates byte-identical). Plan: eoie_do_tables crate (diff by keys on columns; maybe absorb table count by) routed like facts. The primitive and grammar draft were tested to compile; the spec case 5 key column is one space wider than the spec's own widest-cell rule and needs the same whitespace correction as case 1.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_8 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 8u32, "2026-10-19T01:07Z", "claude", "Case 5 draft parked at lab/EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC/eoie_do_tables (crate eoie-do-tables, 330 generated lines, no extra deps; diff grammar test; scratch probe 21:07 printed the case 5 table and receipt rows a 3  b 4  changed 2  added 1  removed 0). To land: move it to src, add the workspace member and eoie_do dep, add diff to the program verbs and a TableProgram route in eoie_do decode/run (eoie_do is at 991 lines, so trim first, e.g. fold the per-crate *_run wrappers into one export call), refresh Cargo.lock offline, add the grammar notebook to the registry, and fix the spec case 5 key column (width 7, widest-cell rule).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_9 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 9u32, "2026-10-19T01:18Z", "claude", "Build 9 (21:18): diff landed as crate eoie_do_tables (330 lines), promoted from the lab draft (lab folder removed). Facts delegates any program containing diff to it, so eoie_do stays at 991 lines (one routing word added). Spec case 5 key column corrected to the widest-cell rule. Runner 26/34 green; read 5/5, ps 5/5, inherit-pipe PASS, timeout-tree 2/2. Red (8): 12 23 31 32 git (need a setup grammar), 21 append, 29 copy, 30 job in do, 34 lab audit. The next eoie_do-routed family must trim eoie_do first.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_10 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 10u32, "2026-10-19T07:31Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 03:31 eoie lane: 34/34 on a probe build of the regenerated eoie_do chain (was 26). New families, each its own crate under 1000 lines: eoie_do_write 684 (append with {clock:FMT}, copy <glob> to <dir> except ...; reads after writes go through new eoie_do_read rejection/report exports), eoie_do_git 880 (init, commit all at <iso>, history, status group by state, log count by day) plus search ... with git status in eoie_do_read, eoie_do_jobs 727 (job start/wait on real supervised eoie jobs through new eoie_jobs exports; wait resolves the newest job by label), eoie_do_lab 538 (lab audit against a backlog via agile list --json). eoie_do became a router (991 -> 270 lines) over a program_family union, with the edit engine moved to eoie_do_edit (862). The runner now runs setup blocks (eoie do programs grouped by family, or plain CLI lines); setups 12, 23 and 31 use append instead of the missing write/append-line verbs; cases 29 and 34 had one extra pad space against the +2 column convention of every other table, fixed in the spec. Release build with these is job eoie-release-install-4.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_11 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 11u32, "2026-10-19T09:40Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 05:40 eoie lane: 34/34 confirmed on the real debug build and the installed release eoie.exe (05:39). The spec cases now all run their setups through the runner. Next for the families: stale = last note older than 14 days (EOIE-LAB-AUDIT wording), gitignored files present in lab (not done yet), job notify beyond the printed line (not done yet).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_12 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 12u32, "2026-10-19T10:09Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 06:09 eoie lane: eoie.exe 06:08 has 34/34 on the installed binary. Fixed a clock-dependent bug the 06:00 release exposed: git log since <date> passed a bare date to git, which reads it as that date at the current time of day, so after 06:00 local a 10:00Z commit on the since day dropped out (case 31). A bare date now means midnight.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_13 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 13u32, "2026-10-21T10:00Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 06:00 eoie team: the one-call runner's case 30 (a job with a wall-clock timeout, cmd /c slow.cmd) starts job 'j1' in the user's real jobs home (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\jobs), so every runner pass leaves one: 40 j1 directories since 10-19, and every lane's job-change watcher reports them. Fix after the r26c release (the runner is one of its steps): the runner sets EOIE_JOBS_HOME to the case's temp directory, then the old j1 directories are deleted (they are runner fixtures by label, argv slow.cmd and cwd eoie-one-call-*).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_14 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 14u32, "2026-10-21T20:59Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 16:59 eoie team, progress review: 34 cases written, all green against every release today (the release gate requires >= 34); left: cases for the r30-r34 verbs (patch hunks, pattern rules, except, move, resume, views), written from real runs once those binaries exist, and the zed and grok habit shapes.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_15 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 15u32, "2026-10-21T22:35Z", "eoie-lane", "18:35 eoie team, decision on the 'zed and grok habit shapes' remainder: measured the client stores' newest writes: Zed (AppData\\Local\\Zed, 1.7 GB) 10-12 17:43, Grok (~\\.grok, 1.1 GB) 10-12 15:19, Gemini 10-11, OpenCode 10-12; Codex has no sessions in 14 days. Only Claude Code is in use (56 transcript files in 14 days). Mining dormant clients' shapes would tune the guide for nobody, so that part is deferred until a client is active again (the adoption verb in r35 reports per client and will show it). Left: tutorial cases for the r30-r34 verbs (patch hunks, pattern rules, except, move, resume, views), written from real runs after the r30-r33 install tonight (r34's after its release).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_16 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 16u32, "2026-10-22T18:27Z", "eoie", "2026-10-22 14:27 the runner (lab/EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC/one-call-runner.ps1) also accepts direct-verb commands: when a command is not the do form, Get-DirectArguments tokenizes 'eoie <tokens>' with single- and double-quote groups. Setup parsing is unchanged. New TDD cases 38 (table sequences latency across two log files) and 39 (mirror check, an in-step file plus a left-only file; avoids timestamp-dependent results) are red until release I installs. Installed binary: 35/39 green (36 and 37 were already red on it). Incident while adding them: a PowerShell one-liner reused the names $t and $T (PowerShell names are case-insensitive) and wrote spec/one-call.md as 54 lines; it was restored byte-exact from release F's regen staging copy (the spec had not changed since 04:01), and the cases were re-appended with structure checks before writing. eoie-snapshot.ps1 now also covers spec, standards, compiler-contracts, docs and .github.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_17 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 17u32, "2026-10-22T20:29Z", "eoie-lane", "16:29 case 40 drafted (scratch one-call/apply-spec-case-40.ps1, applied after F's lease; dry run on copies: spec +20 lines, 0 removed, case count 39 -> 40). It is mined from today's habit: sync-lab, drain-after-F and the hook each hand-roll the lease check (list tree-leases, parse pid=, Get-Process, compare roots); the one call is 'eoie window claim <path>', with a setup 'window request tree-read 5 --label repo'. The same slice fixes a runner leak found while writing the case: the runner isolated EOIE_JOBS_HOME per case but not EOIE_WINDOWS_HOME, so any window case would have written the machine's shared window store (where every session's admissions live). It now sets EOIE_WINDOWS_HOME=<case>-windows and adds a <ms> placeholder for window ids. Green needs F's binary (tree-read class + window claim).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_18 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 18u32, "2026-10-22T21:17Z", "eoie-lane", "17:17 applied: spec case 40 (window claim) appended (39 -> 40 cases, additions only), and the runner isolates EOIE_WINDOWS_HOME per case and knows <ms>. Green after F installs.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_19 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 19u32, "2026-10-22T22:45Z", "eoie-lane", "18:45 case 40 does not run yet: its setup line starts with eoie (like commands do), but the runner passes setup tokens to eoie verbatim, so eoie sees the verb 'eoie'. The fix is drafted (one-call/apply-runner-setup-prefix.ps1: drop a leading eoie in setup statements) and applied after F2's lease. Dry run: the setup then reaches eoie, and the installed 10-21 binary answers 'unknown class tree-read', which F2's binary adds. Today's runner baseline on the installed binary: 35/40 green (36-37 wait for the new binary, 38-39 for release I, 40 for this fix plus F2). F2's runner gate needs 34.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_20 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 20u32, "2026-10-23T05:44Z", "eoie", "01:44 eoie: case 30 (job start slow.cmd as j1 timeout 2s notify; job wait j1) is load-flaky. It was red in F7's full runner pass at 00:00 under release load (Quiet mode keeps only the first output line, which matched), but green alone through the runner on the debug candidate at 01:44, and the installed binary's output matched the expected block line for line by hand. The other F7 reds are real gaps: 36 (do edit grammar), 38 (table query usage), 39 (mirror verb, release I), 40 (runner setup prefix, fixed in post-F). The release gate is greens >= 34, so one flake fits. Quiet mode should keep the first differing line instead of the first line, so a red under load says why.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_21 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 21u32, "2026-10-23T09:11Z", "eoie-lane", "05:11 install probe (spec case 40 claim): PASS. 40 green  | one-call spec: 1/1 green")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_22 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 22u32, "2026-10-23T12:50Z", "eoie", "08:50 red cases on the installed binary: 36, 38, 39 (37/40). 38 (table sequences) and 39 (mirror) are features in release I and turn green when it installs. 36 was the runner, not eoie: its setup 'do . '...'' (no eoie prefix, a quoted program spanning two lines) missed the grouped path that requires a leading 'eoie ', so it split at the line and sent an unterminated program. Fix drafted as scratch one-call/apply-runner-setup-do.ps1 (normalizes the eoie prefix before matching); on a copy of the runner and spec, 36 turns green (38/40). Applies to lab/ after HP-tail's tree lease ends.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_23 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 23u32, "2026-10-23T17:52Z", "eoie", "13:52 eoie: cases 41 and 42 added (spec/one-call.md). 41: a saved agile view (existing verbs; green on the installed binary). 42: 'job chain -- one ... -- two ...' from main's re-chaining habit (7-8 re-chains on 10-23), with expected receipts using <ms>/<pid> placeholders; red until release M installs job chain (TDD target). Not written as cases: ci parity and job doctor, whose output depends on this machine's toolchains and live processes; their acceptance lives in after-install-M instead. Runner: 39/42 (38 and 39 land with L and I, 42 with M).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_24 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 24u32, "2026-10-23T18:08Z", "eoie", "14:08 eoie: case 43 added, 'crate gate . --enforce --limit 4' over a fixture with two Spiral crates (3 and 5 generated lines): rows 'gate / tool tool.rs 3 lines ok' and 'gate / big big.rs 5 lines OVER 4', then the refused receipt. Row order traced through eoie_crate_gate's walker: dir_names reverses, the worklist fold reverses again, the final listm.rev gives tool then big. Red until L installs crate gate (TDD target). Runner: 39/43 (38 I+L, 39 I, 42 M, 43 L).")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_25 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 25u32, "2026-10-23T21:00Z", "eoie", "17:00 eoie: case 47 drafted (scratch spec41/write-case47.ps1): 'eoie help env' must print env's own usage line. Today it answers with the do grammar, whose 'env <A,B>' fragment matches first, and help mirror has no line. Release O's direct-verb-lines slice makes it green. The spec can't be written now, because GE2's release holds a tree lease (since 15:47) and a repo write mid-run would block its publish. launch-O therefore appends case 47 itself, after its gates and before its snapshot, which is the one moment no release holds the tree; the case and its fix arrive together.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_26 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 26u32, "2026-10-24T01:46Z", "main", "2026-10-23 21:46 main: user direction 2026-10-23 21:4x: eoie gaps are 'reported for immediate fixes, then propagating the new usage with detailed tutorials'. So every landed eoie gap fix also adds a case here (provenance, the habit it replaces, fixture, command, exact expected output). That case is the tutorial the other lanes read, plus a one-line note to them that names it.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_27 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 27u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:2x main: consolidated pendencies covered here (EOIE-CONSOLIDATED-INTAKE, class a): EDIT-10 (plan grammar and a minimal example in help), CLI-6 (every parse error with usage, valid values and a corrected example), CLI-4 (compact summary, full receipt). Tutorials for each new consolidated verb land here.. Spec text: Downloads/eoie-consolidated/agile_eoie.md.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_28 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 28u32, "2026-10-24T23:43Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 195m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D5 at 60%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_29 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 29u32, "2026-10-28T10:29Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_eoie_one_call_spec_30 () = Note ("EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC", 30u32, "2026-10-31T21:26Z", "kit", "10-31 17:2x kit (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK repair): Paused -> Planned. The 10-28 pause was for silence only ('Last note 2026-10-24, nothing queued'), the pattern the user rejected today: a pause needs a reason AND a resume condition. Its recorded next step still stands: check whether the remaining milestone shipped (now against the installed E14F1F0B, not TRAIN2c), close it with that evidence if so, otherwise size the remaining slice. Back in 'agile next' as ready work.")
inl hopacsota () = Task ("HOPACSOTA", "hopacsota: parallel core restarted from single-flight's evaluator, the Hopac way (fill-once cells, server-owned tables, local scheduler), determinism by construction, no record/replay; contract = spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (decisions D1-D15, gates G1-G6, phases 0-7, scoreboard, decision-change log); gpt5parallel stays reference until Phase 6; user decision 2026-10-13 22:47, plan 2026-10-13 23:15", Epic, P0, D8, 25u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,hopacsota,parallel,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_hopacsota () = Planning ("HOPACSOTA", Minutes 2400u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_hopacsota_1 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 1u32, "2026-10-14T10:39Z", "user", "2026-10-14 06:39 user decision: gpt5parallel no longer gates blesses (rungs dropped; build only to keep it compiling); pack 2 (Bend small ints + A4) waits for hopacsota")
inl note_of_hopacsota_2 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 2u32, "2026-10-14T11:38Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:38 touch: Phase 0 runs today (R3 instrumented build queued in the night cache; R4 after); gpt5parallel no longer gates blesses")
inl note_of_hopacsota_3 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: phase 0 nearly done (HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH 90%: R3 measured, R4 orders proven byte-identical with the keyed D6 merge). Phase 1 (HOPACSOTA-P1) is next once the phase-1 design note is written.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_4 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:56Z", "main-thread", "06:56 groom: status corrected from Planned 0% to Active 15%: phase 0 (HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH) is at 90% with R3 and R4 measured and D6 proven; phases 1-7 not started.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_5 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 5u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: user 21:05: hopacsota is carried until F# is gone; HOPAC-DOCS-REREAD (later) rereads the full Hopac docs against the plan.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_6 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 6u32, "2026-10-17T18:24Z", "bundle-wisdom", "14:24 from the gpt5parallel-era bootstrap (Downloads\\files\\code\\bootstrap_llm_compiler_v60..v101.00.md, 2026-01-03..05), as lessons, not designs to copy: (1) join-point waits that blocked (ManualResetEventSlim.Wait) starved the workers that should signal them; v101 made every wait a helping wait (the waiter runs queued work) and stopped the soft-abort that switched parallelism off; Hopac jobs avoid this by construction, so a phase gate could assert that no blocking OS wait sits on the evaluator path. (2) Rerunning a failed build deterministically was used only to tell a race (passes serially) from a real error, as a diagnostic, never as a fallback. (3) Default DOP = ProcessorCount, eager worker start, and draining workers at the end of peval avoided leaking spinning threads between builds. (4) Depth guards gave false positives on finite long stdlib loops (listm); limits sized to the stack regime (BigStack floors) plus re-entry guards keyed by reference identity, not hash, separated cycles from long recursions.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_7 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 7u32, "2026-10-19T12:17Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:17 lap 1 grain: epic state from PLAN.md scoreboard: Phase 0 (R1-R4) and Phase 1 (Gate 1, seams, 0 cells on 6,758 rows) done, Phase 2 Active at 30%, Phases 3-7 Planned; research child closed this lap; progress 15 -> 25 Next: read HOPACSOTA-P2's last gate attempt and name its next measurable step")
inl note_of_hopacsota_8 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 8u32, "2026-10-19T13:08Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 09:08 lap 2 grain: epic step named: P2's next measurable step is the engine slice (BodyContext + body-thread bridge in a new PartEvalEngineHopacsota section, 350-500 lines est.) gated by hopacsota-g3.ps1 against today's accepted pack 5 run single-flight-20261019-080524 at 1 worker; research and LF children closed this morning Next: -")
inl note_of_hopacsota_9 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 9u32, "2026-10-19T18:41Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:41 lap 4 grain: epic state: research and LF scheduling Done; P2 (engine slice) is the critical path, P3 (scheduling policy) and P4/P6 wait on it; the gpt5parallel pairs that P6 retires are PartEval, SignalRSupervisor and GraphIdentity (the 4 adapters are hooks and vanish with them) Next: P2 engine slice as a candidate pack (pair-drift -Tracked plus a private Debug build make it safe to iterate)")
inl note_of_hopacsota_10 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 10u32, "2026-10-20T03:25Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 23:25 user 2026-10-19 23:1x: full hopac SOTA right after XSD; the whole critical path is P0 now (P2 engine, P3 scheduling, P4 diagnostics, P6 promotion, HOPAC-DEPTH real Hopac API); P5 HUD and P7 engine interface stay P1.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_11 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 11u32, "2026-10-24T03:08Z", "main", "2026-10-23 23:08 main grooming: umbrella: last note was 10-20, but work moved on its parts (HOPACSOTA-P2, P3, P6 noted 10-22 and 10-23), and main-hopacsota-promotion is running now (chain B, behind rustls-check, am-any-gate and curried-main-probe).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_12 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 12u32, "2026-10-27T23:04Z", "main", "10-27 19:04 main: Groom 10-27 18:5x, the critical path to hopacsota SOTA, re-read from its parts: the single-threaded side is done and proven (P6: 7,352 rows match single-flight, apps/spiral byte-identical under inline, dfs, bfs and two random schedules). The open blocker is parallel determinism: the 10-25 waits census (finished, unread until now) shows policy=parallel gives a different output per run at 2, 4 and 8 workers (HOPACSOTA-P2 note). Order from here: (1) P2 determinism gate (1 hash per worker count, equal to single-flight), (2) localise and fix the order dependence, (3) speed (w4 is 0.68x of w1 today; w8 regresses on wait contention), (4) P6 promotion re-gated with the parallel policy included, then the user's call on deleting gpt5parallel. P3 (granularity cutoff) and P4 (diagnostics) don't gate promotion. The census sat unread for 2 days because nothing watched it after it was queued behind the quiet gate; lesson for this epic: every queued measurement gets a watcher that posts its reading.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_13 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 13u32, "2026-10-30T23:42Z", "main", "10-30 19:4x main R3 groom (BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030): owner compiler (hopacsota is the compiler team's critical path: parallel determinism, per the 10-25 waits census in the 10-27 groom). main keeps only the install step after compiler's proofs.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_14 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 14u32, "2026-11-01T03:36Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 23:34 compiler, cadence groom (user 23:33: drift/stall check; no Active item silent >12 h): stays Active, progress today: P3's deferred validation measured twice on the node, the second with A/A (P3 n60, n62): waits cut 98-99%, wall inside the A/A spread, so NOT ADOPTED on speed; the w8 cost is claim transport, not waits. gpt5parallel fully retired (PACK-10 + PACK-11), so single-flight is the only reference. Next concrete step: HOPACSOTA-HOPAC-DEPTH's design decision (below).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_15 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 15u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:38 compiler, R5 MEASURABLE ANSWER PLAN (user: is upstream single-flight close to SOTA before the Rust/Gleam rewrite?). Metrics, all on installed single-flight, Normal priority, node, with an in-job A/A arm: (M1) phase split of the 7,413-row matrix compile and the 5 mega samples (lex/parse/infer/peval/codegen) via dotnet-trace; (M2) GC share of wall time (dotnet-counters time-in-gc); (M3) size scaling exponent per phase on agile.spi slices (shared with COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE); (M4) join-point memo hit rate and duplicate specializations; (M5) critical-path bound for parallel speedup (the P3 granularity data). VERDICT RULE written now: near-SOTA = GC < 15% of wall AND every phase exponent <= 1.1 AND no identified algorithmic fix worth >= 2x on any phase; otherwise the fixes are listed and done in F# BEFORE the rewrite so the rewrite ports the fast algorithm. External reference: fsc and ocamlopt check time per kloc on comparable code, reported for context only (different languages, not a gate). NEXT STEP: M2 + M1 on the 5 mega samples, one node job, after CHAR-ORDERING.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_16 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA", 16u32, "2026-11-03T07:30Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (41 h). Next: the R5 measurement plan M1-M3 (phase split, GC share, size exponent) on installed pack23, on the node with an in-job A/A arm.")
inl hopacsota_research () = Task ("HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", "hopacsota Phase 0 (no core code): R1 rest of Bend 2 (BendTT 6+, term_check/term_infer, emit_match/emit_task); R2 shared-state inventory with every access line; R3 per-specialization work/span from an instrumented single-flight copy on the mega roots + a scaling corpus (apps/spiral, all lib/spiral, generated N=10/100/1000 modules) -> the chains that make the span long and the D16 technique for each (parallel evaluation is required, R3 never decides whether); R4 Deferred DFS/BFS/random-seed worklist on single-flight, -Suite all residual hashes identical; gate numbers into spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md scoreboard; 2026-10-14 00:58 R1 done (BendTT pp. 7-10, 12 bend2 functions + checker bench: D12 +12 applied, 5 not applied) and R2 done (31 inventory rows, 0 without a line, 3/3 R2-decides resolved, 34/34 PartEval write lines covered, 5 proposed decision changes P1-P5 in PLAN.md); R3, R4 open; 2026-10-14 01:50 P1-P5 folded into the PLAN.md decision text (technical core facts 3-4, D3, D4, D5, D6, D7, D16; the Decision changes log kept as history); every PLAN.md line now <= 120 columns (inventory turned into a list); 2026-10-14 02:58 lane 3 R3/R4 patch scripts (not built; anchors checked once each against the current spiral_compiler.fs into scratch copies): C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\hopacsota-p0\\r3_instrument.ps1 (-Target copy; SPIRAL_R3_DUMP=<path> TSV per specialization: run, id, kind, annotated, awaited, parent, offset_us, self_us, inclusive_us, outcome, note; awaited cache hits too), r3_simulate.py (W, S, greedy list scheduling at 1/2/4/8 workers, critical path, top 10 awaited chains with a D16 technique each; checked on a synthetic dump), r4_deferred.ps1 (SPIRAL_R4_POLICY=dfs|bfs|random:<seed>: closures and annotated methods go through a worklist, dfs runs them at once in the caller's context = single-flight, bfs/random drain after the root with D3 relative context unless SPIRAL_R4_CONTEXT=canonical; SPIRAL_R4_REPORT=<path> counts inline-depth and dynamic-if restarts, validating callers, relative-trace bodies, stack/inline/if stops)", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "HOPACSOTA", "compiler,hopacsota,research", "current", "current")
inl eoie_agile_rename_id () = Task ("EOIE-AGILE-RENAME-ID", "eoie agile has no way to rename a task id (edit fields: title, kind, priority, difficulty, deps, tags, estimate, load, assignee); needed for the hopac -> gpt5parallel rename of HOPAC-* items; one call: rename <root> <old-id> <new-id> updating deps that point at it; 2026-10-13 22:47; 2026-10-14 03:58 lane 3 design: rename <old> to <new> as a typed agile do statement (Rename :: rename_request -> agile_statement agile_mutate rename_receipt): one write renames the Task id and inl name, its Planning and Note items, and every deps entry naming it (deps_rewritten listed), counting titles that mention the old id; fails with RenameTargetTaken or UnknownTask and then writes nothing; 2026-10-14 04:56 lane 2 done (uncommitted, eoie repo): eoie agile rename <root> <old-id> <new-id> in granular Spiral: crate agile_rename_rewrite (701 lines, line-wise rewrite of the Task line and inl name, the Planning row and planning_of_ name, each Note row and note_of_<id>_<seq> name, and every other task's deps entry equal to the old id; titles that mention it are counted and listed, not changed) and crate agile_task_rename (360, validation: the old id exists, the new id is upper-case letters, digits and - and not taken, not equal; one guarded write that refuses when state/agile.spi changed since it was read); receipt: eoie agile rename ok old= new= items= deps_rewritten= deps_in= titles_mentioning_old= titles_in= bytes_before= bytes_after= elapsed_ms=; proof on a copy of this backlog: EOIE-ONE-CALL -> EOIE-ONE-SHOT rewrote the task, its planning and a note plus deps in 11 tasks (EOIE-AGILE-BODY, EOIE-ONE-CALL-SPEC, ...), counted 1 title mention (PS1-TO-SPIRAL), 534 ms on the 504 KB file; taken, malformed and unknown ids rejected with nothing written; agile check build_attested=2 on the copy afterwards; tests in agile_note_receipts.rs: rename receipt and every rewritten item, plus a concurrent-writer test (EOIE_AGILE_TEST_PAUSE_MS pauses after the read; an outside write during the pause wins and the rename exits 2 writing nothing); not used on the real backlog (rename is proven on the copy only, as asked); 2026-10-14 05:20 review round: rename also refuses a new id whose inl name is already declared anywhere (e.g. MAIN collides with inl main) or that starts with a digit (2FA-LOGIN would give inl 2fa_login, not an identifier; agile add still accepts such ids, which is a separate gap), both tested with the state byte-identical; an expired lease blocks rename like every other mutation (tested); the concurrent-writer test waits for the pause marker; agile_note_receipts 5/5 against the new build; dev.ps1 staged run: see EOIE-AGILE-BODY note 4 (one eoie-contracts lib test fails only in the staged workflow, passes in the tree with the same binaries); left: deploy the new eoie.exe, renew owner growth and strict evidence, commit; 2026-10-14 05:55 final round: agile add now also rejects an id starting with a digit (agile add 2FA-LOGIN rejected: the id must start with a letter, so its inl name is a valid identifier; FA2-LOGIN still accepted), receipt test in agile_note_receipts.rs; the staged-only lease failure is fixed at its source: contracts.rs had been hand-patched (a743a92) with EOIE_LEASE_POLICY/EOIE_CONFIG_HOME isolation that contracts_entry/harness.spi never got, so every regeneration dropped it; harness.spi now carries env_remove EOIE_LEASE_POLICY + env_remove EOIE_LEASE_ROOT + EOIE_CONFIG_HOME=<root> on the 4 lease-sensitive commands and contracts.rs is regenerated from it; eoie dev.ps1 -Package (11 packages incl. agile-task-creation and eoie-contracts) -Publish passed end to end in 719 s: 11/11 owners emitted, cargo check ok, every package test ok: eoie-contracts lib 8/8 (7 ignored) incl. expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface, agile_note_receipts 6/6, agile_receipts 1/1, proxy_receipts 5/5, batch_completion 2/2; Published 0 changed owners, 11 unchanged (the tree already held the regenerated outputs); 2026-10-14 06:01 deployed in eoie.exe 44897B5C8234 (eoie build.ps1, release, published=True); rename still not used on the real backlog; left: commit, then renew-strict-evidence.ps1", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "eoie,agile,one-call", "current", "current")
inl hopacsota_p1 () = Task ("HOPACSOTA-P1", "hopacsota Phase 1: -Mode hopacsota + SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA, D10 seam hooks (single-flight code moved unchanged, projection-hash equal), hopacsota-lint.ps1 G1 size + G2 banned, Deferred worklist with D3 tables/D6 merge/D8 types, 4 frontier_hopacsota_* fixtures first; gate: -Suite all 0 diffs on Inline + Deferred DFS/BFS/3 seeds, Inline <=1.05x single-flight (spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md); 2026-10-14 02:15 lane 3 drafted 7 frontier fixtures in scratch (C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\hopacsota-fixtures, README with expected single-flight outcomes derived from PartEval line by line, not yet compiled): recursion_unannotated (Recursive join points must be annotated, 163000), mutual_pending (exit 0, annotated pending key returns its type, 162999), globals_order (main.c lines m1 a1 c1 a2 b1 m2), two_errors (type error 'first body fails'), if_depth_across_fork (P1: EJP0040 only via the caller's depth 600 + leaf's 600), validation_global (P2: '// nested validation global' between g1 and g2, added once through the validation cache), pending_type_join_point (P3: recursive union read by ty_is_uninhabited, exit 0); the main thread compiles them after the bless", Story, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", "compiler,hopacsota", "current", "current")
