inl note_of_x_client_15 () = Note ("X-CLIENT", 15u32, "2026-10-27T12:57Z", "x", "2026-10-27 08:57 x: CI read (gh, read-only). ci on main failed for the user's last 3 pushes, including today's 9b90151 'tests' (run 40488607167). (1) xc-windows: \"couldn't find file apps\\client\\domains\\domains.rs\". The commit carried the WIP crates' .spi and Cargo.toml (domains, requests), but generated .rs were never put in the tree; I had wrongly left generated outputs to the verify. Fix in progress: x/scripts/verify.ps1 -Part regen (job-1793105792101 via i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1) regenerates every client crate on the current tree with the pinned compiler, and the .rs that the WIP changes or adds (new crates; changed ones by the same-compiler base comparison) land in the tree unstaged. (2) build (ubuntu-24.04): the gate passed (28 crates), then e2e threw \"the Mastodon stub did not write its port\", because apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py is UNTRACKED: e2e.ps1 (committed) starts it, but the commit did not include it. Untracked files a commit needs today: apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py, apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.txt (untracked since 10-25 and compared by the sim build), apps/client/e2e/links.txt (new tutorial input), scripts/verify.ps1, plus the new crates' .rs once landed. Also added __pycache__/ to x/.gitignore (the Python stubs write it under e2e/). Only the user commits; this note is the list for that.")
