inl note_of_pipelines_green_1 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 1u32, "2026-10-16T02:24Z", "main-thread", "22:24 main: state 10-15: every repo of ours runs one gh-pages.yml through scripts/workflow.ps1 (spiral, eoie after today's change, polyglot, dice, alphabet, i574n.github); no push since 10-14 21:31, so none of today's packs ran in CI yet. Children: CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION, CI-COMPILER-FULL-SUITE, WORKFLOW-END-TO-END, CI-SINGLE-PIPELINE, CI-NIX, CI-K3S, SUITE-MAP, NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE, PS1-TO-SPIRAL.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_2 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 2u32, "2026-10-16T15:48Z", "main-thread", "11:48 main: CI state read with gh (i574n remotes): green on the last push for spiral (build windows+ubuntu), eoie, polyglot, alphabet, i574n.github, x. Red: (1) spiral's nightly scheduled compiler job (run 38893948663): No .NET 11 SDK found (workflow.ps1 -Compiler never installed it) and upload-artifact refused SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR=github.workspace/../spiral-bin (relative '..'); fixed in scripts/workflow.ps1 (install-dotnet.ps1 when Resolve-SpiralDotnet finds none) and gh-pages.yml (runner.temp/spiral-bin). (2) dice Windows job failing since 10-09 (every run): contract/build.ps1 runs dice_contract test cells whose NEAR wasm runner goes through invoke-block -Linux and workspace/target/release/spiral_wasm, which a Windows runner does not have (NEAR sandbox is Linux-only, decision NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE); fixed in dice scripts/build.ps1: the two contract steps run where nearSandboxRunsHere = IsLinux (the ubuntu job still builds and tests the contract). Playwright 1.44 chromium download 400s in those logs are non-fatal. Both need the user's push to verify.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_3 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 3u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: 6 of 7 repos green on their last push; spiral blocked only by the workflow-file error fixed in the tree; the scheduled compiler job also needed the .NET resolve fix (CI-COMPILER-FULL-SUITE).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_4 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 4u32, "2026-10-18T11:46Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 07:46 main-thread triage of the red runs: spiral compiler job (run 39121783429 on adffe65a, which already has the macro lookahead fix) reached the native tier on Linux, then test.ps1 called kernel32 SetErrorMode (Value cannot be null, path1); fixed in the tree: the WerFault guard runs only when IsWindows (needs the user's push; the other native-tier paths already branch on IsWindows). dice windows job 39106582938: workflow step without a conclusion and no log blob (lost runner; ubuntu passed); rerun --failed at 07:46. x: e2e tutorial steps xc --help and --per-account expect the old usage without the xc thread line; the X lane's uncommitted README already adds it, so it clears with that commit. eoie: own source-topology gate (rust_file_max=982 over its limit), eoie lane. i574n.github: same run ids as x (shared workflow), recheck after x.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_5 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 5u32, "2026-10-18T11:47Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 07:47 main-thread correction to the previous note: i574n.github's repo is i574n/.github; its red run 39103223121 (06:12Z) failed apps/spiral compile on spiral main 1723e220 (the first macro fix), which adffe65a fixed; rerun --failed at 07:47. The x and i574n.github ids in the earlier note were a listing bug (one repo's JSON reused for the next).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_6 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 6u32, "2026-10-18T13:22Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 09:22 main-thread: dice run 39106582938 rerun --failed is success (the windows failure was a lost runner); spiral push 39127751148 (e1eef3bc) ubuntu success, windows running; i574n/.github 39103223121 rerun --failed again at 09:21 now that spiral main has the Gleam warm-slot fix (its 07:47 rerun cloned the old main and failed on the same stale-Gleam symptom). Still red: x (the X lane's README tutorial update is uncommitted) and eoie (its topology gate, eoie lane).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_7 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 7u32, "2026-10-18T13:32Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 09:32 main-thread: push run 39129835185 on 80b16019 (user commit 09:02) failed: build ubuntu, apps/spiral compile, lib/spiral/rust/near.spi:44:19 Expected: } (git-0e's 08:54 block-form conversion put ') : () -> ()' after an indented block closer inside a record, which the installed parser also rejects). Isolated (a lib copy with only near.spi reverted compiles) and reverted by git-0e at 09:31 to its e1eef3bc content; a lib-backed probe compiles again. Needs the user's next commit; the other 11 converted lib files compile. My bless now aborts first if a lib-backed sample does not compile.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_8 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 8u32, "2026-10-18T13:42Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 09:42 main-thread: spiral push 39127751148 on e1eef3bc is fully green (build ubuntu + windows, push to gh-pages): the first green spiral push of the day, carrying the macro lookahead fix, the cells warm-slot fix and today's backend work. i574n/.github rerun 39103223121 failed again, as expected: it cloned spiral main at 80b16019 (broken near.spi); goes green after the user commits git-0e's near.spi revert, then one more rerun.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_9 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 9u32, "2026-10-19T12:16Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:16 lap 1 grain: diagnosed the 06:48 push runs: spiral, dice, polyglot fail on Linux only, rustix 0.37.27/0.37.28 (near-workspaces 0.11 -> cargo-near -> near-cli-rs -> keyring -> zbus 3 -> async-io 1) uses rustc_layout_scalar_valid_range attributes that nightly-2026-10-18 rejects (the Windows nightly verification never compiles rustix); alphabet fails in dir-tree-html exit 3 (UTF-8 slice of its Korean README); x fails in apps/client/protocol.spi:80 and eoie in eoie-do-edit (their lanes); dice/polyglot/alphabet also lose html at mix spiral.html before mix deps.get Next: check the next push runs of spiral, dice, polyglot, alphabet after the user commits the fixes")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_10 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 10u32, "2026-10-19T13:53Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 09:53 lap 2 grain: push checklist (uncommitted fixes the user's next push must carry, git status at 09:5x): spiral 30 modified + 18 new (gh-pages.yml nightly pin, scripts/core.ps1 mix deps.get, workspace/.cargo/config.toml rustix cfg, scripts/publish-tree.ps1 failed-render guard from helper 2, test.ps1 per-backend native keys, sm'.spi fixes, Cells edits); dice 6 + 3 (gh-pages.yml, .cargo/ rustix cfg); polyglot 3 + 3 (gh-pages.yml, apps/chat/.cargo/); alphabet 3 + 2 (gh-pages.yml); dir-tree-html 3 (gh-pages.yml, dir_tree_html.spi UTF-8 runs + README test); blog 6 + 4; x 24 + 2 (ci.yml, protocol.spi fix); eoie 32 + 8 (gh-pages.yml nightly, missing generated crates per the eoie lane); i574n.github 3 Next: after the user pushes, read each repo's run; the first new failure per repo becomes this item's next grain")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_11 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 11u32, "2026-10-19T18:13Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:13 lap 4 grain: push checklist refreshed at 14:1x: uncommitted spiral 229 (22 new; includes the core v1 consumer migration, pack 7 compiler, 147 regenerated sample outputs from the accepted reviews), dice 12, alphabet 5, polyglot 6, dir-tree-html 3, i574n.github 4, plus the fork clone deps/The-Spiral-Language (core v1); the 10-17/10-18 gh-pages runs were green in dice, alphabet, polyglot and spiral, so the 06:48 reds are only the causes already fixed in these trees Next: after the user pushes: watch spiral, dice, alphabet, polyglot, then i574n.github (push-only workflow, last) with ci-runs.ps1")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_12 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 12u32, "2026-10-19T20:14Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 16:14 lap 5 grain: compiler install race fixed in build.ps1: other lanes compile continuously with the shared Release DLL (a Rust compile from another session started mid-build at 16:08), so the Release copy step failed twice with MSB3021/MSB3027 (FParsecCS.dll and others locked by .NET Host); Unlock-SpiralOutputs already ran before the 3-minute compile, which left the window open; now a build that fails only on locked-file copies (no error FS) unlocks again and reruns the incremental build up to 3 times, so the copy follows the unlock within seconds; the pack 9 install then succeeded and hashes equal the candidate Next: none; watch the next installs for the retry line")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_13 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 13u32, "2026-10-19T20:14Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 16:14 correction to note 12: the pack 9 install at 16:10 built in 67 s without contention, so the new unlock-and-recopy retry did not fire; it is parsed and in place but not yet exercised by a real lock race.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_14 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 14u32, "2026-10-20T00:45Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 20:45 lap 6 grain: second face of the shared-DLL lock race: the pack 12 install (20:33) built fine, but Invoke-SpiralReadyToRun could not swap 5 DLLs (FSharp.Core, FSharpx.Collections, Hopac.Core, Hopac.Platform, the host SpiralCompiler.dll: Move access denied while other lanes ran compilers), so they stay IL; same code, slower startup, and the host no longer hash-equals the R2R candidate (the core DLL does); the unlock-and-recopy retry covers only the msbuild copy Next: make the ReadyToRun swap use the same move-aside trick (rename the locked IL dll to .r2r-old-<stamp>, then move the R2R one in), so a busy machine still gets precompiled outputs")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_15 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 15u32, "2026-10-20T00:46Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 20:46 main: R2R swap fixed in build.ps1 (Invoke-SpiralReadyToRun): when Move(r2r, dll, overwrite) is refused because a running compiler holds the dll, it renames the IL dll to .r2r-old-<stamp> (Unlock-SpiralOutputs already deletes those later) and moves the R2R image in, moving the IL file back if that fails; proven with a simulated open-with-delete-share handle (overwrite refused, aside + move-in works); parse clean; first real exercise is the next Release build.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_16 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 16u32, "2026-10-21T22:17Z", "main", "18:17 CI survey (gh run list on each repo's i574n remote; the first remote of spiral, polyglot, dice and alphabet is the fc1943s backup, whose runs are from 2025): green: polyglot, dice, tibia; red: spiral gh-pages 10-21 07:49, alphabet gh-pages 10-20 00:04, x ci 10-20 00:04 (x lane), eoie gh-pages 10-19 22:10 (eoie lane), i574n/.github gh-pages 10-19 22:09. spiral's only failure was DISAGREE 1: samples/zig_exit_wide F# 'exit 305 (warm)' vs C 49 and every other backend 49. Linux truncates exit codes to 8 bits, but the warm F# tier reads the code from fsi output, and its 8-bit mask in test.ps1 (line 787) never ran: warm.ps1 returns Exit as [string], so '-isnot [int]' was always true. Fixed: the mask now applies to any numeric string off Windows (305 -> 49, -1 -> 255, 'timeout' and '' unchanged); unit-checked, parse clean. Windows was never affected (32-bit exit codes).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_17 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 17u32, "2026-10-21T22:20Z", "main", "18:20 alphabet gh-pages (run 39367599510, HEAD 01da480): apps/hangul/hangul.livemd's two Cells tests (hanja, hanjaconvert) fail on the Zig target only: hanja.spi:2:5 ETY-TermError, Unification failure, Got array (i32 * i32), Expected array_base (i32 * i32), in hanja_to_hangul_table. hanja.spi declares '() : array_base (i32 * i32) = ;[ ... ]'. The parser turns ';[' into an application of the term named array to the RawArray (compiler line 45226), and core base.spi:24 has 'nominal array t = array_base t', so the literal is the nominal array; other targets pass, so a backend-dependent path resolves array differently (not found by reading: no 'inl array' in core or lib). Next: one probe compile of the hanja cell for Zig and Rust when a compile window is free. Also removed 2 stray files of mine from alphabet/apps/hangul (hanja.spi.err/.out from the 08:21 format-timings job).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_18 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 18u32, "2026-10-21T22:22Z", "main", "18:22 i574n/.github gh-pages (run 39357416239): lib/spiral/parsing.spi test pipe2 failed on Zig only, at 1343:86 (got array, expected string) and 1343:92 (got array_base, expected unit). Cause: commit 002c71f6 (10-19 22:09) rewrote the test lambda 'fun a, b => a () ++# b ()' to 'fun a, b => array () ++# b ()', apparently a rename sweep that caught the parameter a; array () then means core's nominal constructor applied to unit. The other targets passed only through the CI memo (memo_hits 37), and Zig was the one target compiled fresh. Fixed back to a () ++# b () (test block only, so builds and other lanes are unaffected). That commit's lib diff contains no other such rewrite. Gate: Cells --gate on parsing.spi when a slot is free, after the night-pack review. Open question for CELLS: memo replays can keep a broken test green on old targets; the alphabet hanja case below may be the same.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_19 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 19u32, "2026-10-21T22:24Z", "x", "2026-10-21 18:24 x: x ci status for this survey. Red on HEAD 61b8fff only from the windows-2025 CLIXML e2e failure (run 39367603402); ubuntu passed in 9.5 min against a 120-min timeout. The uncommitted tree fixes it, and it is green locally on CI's own scripts/build.ps1 (10-20 precommit; 10-21 x-split-fix3 for the post_id slice and the sim fixes). Precondition for x going green: x CI clones i574n/spiral's default branch, and pushed 33ee6412 lacks the postability profile reader, the 'x-compat report' line x's client build parses, and today's lib Gleam fixes, so spiral must be pushed with x (the user has always pushed both together; X-DONE note 8).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_20 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 20u32, "2026-10-21T22:24Z", "main", "18:24 correction to note 18, from x's memo analysis: Cells' memo key (memo.ex key/2) hashes the test program itself plus the package blocks it reaches, and pipe2's own text changed, so on the non-Zig targets pipe2 most likely ran fresh and passed. That makes the 'masked by the memo' explanation unlikely: array () genuinely type-checks on the other targets and fails only on Zig, the same Zig-only pattern as alphabet's hanja array_base literal. Both point at one question: what the term array resolves to when Cells compiles for Zig versus the other targets (a different package or prelude set for the Zig builder?). The pipe2 fix back to a () stands either way (the lambda's a was otherwise unused). Probe planned: compile the hanja and pipe2 cells for Zig and Rust with SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 once a compile window is free.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_21 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 21u32, "2026-10-21T23:24Z", "main", "19:24 alphabet cause found by probe (installed compiler, a tiny package with core- and spiral-, 4 backends each): a let annotated : array_base (i32 * i32) whose body is a ;[ ... ] literal fails on EVERY backend (Rust, Zig, C, F#: ETY-TermError at 2:5), because ;[ is core's nominal array; annotated : array it compiles everywhere. So hanja.spi's annotation was always wrong, and the 'Zig only' CI failure means the other targets never compiled it fresh in that run (a memo replay or another path; not the compiler). The hangul test cell expects array_base (it wraps with fun x => array x), so the fix keeps the annotation and unwraps in place: hanja.spi now ends with '    |> fun (array x) => x' (1 line; probe: compiles on all 4 backends). Verifying on the real 465 KB table now (job main-hanja-probe). The same probe also re-reads parsing.spi's pipe2: array () is core's nominal constructor there too, so the a () fix was right on every backend.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_22 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 22u32, "2026-10-21T23:25Z", "main", "19:25 alphabet fix verified on the real 465 KB table (job main-hanja-probe, 57 s): hanja.spi with the in-place unwrap plus a main that wraps it like the hangul test cell (fun x => array x : array _ |> am'.length) compiles on Rust, Zig, C and F#. alphabet apps/hangul/hanja.spi is changed for the user to commit (+1 line); its gh-pages turns green on the next push if nothing else breaks.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_23 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 23u32, "2026-10-22T04:13Z", "main", "00:13 lab drain: fsharp-warm-exit.py landed in refined form: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/test.ps1 computes processExit (the Linux 8-bit mask of the warm F# exit; tonight's version also guards non-numeric exits), so the script's anchor is gone. Removed spiral/lab/PIPELINES-GREEN (1 file); the item stays open for its remaining work.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_24 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 24u32, "2026-10-22T07:28Z", "main", "03:28 main: why the spiral and alphabet pages are stale since 10-18 (read-only: gh run view --log-failed; ties to TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO note 25). spiral: the last push run (39367586923, 10-20 04:04, HEAD 33ee6412) fails in build (ubuntu) at lib/spiral/build.ps1. 346 of 347 lib tests pass; parsing.spi test pipe2 on zig hits ETY-TermError at 1343:86, 'Got array _ Expected string'. HEAD's line 1343 reads 'fun a, b => array () ++# b ()', a parameter 'a' rewritten to 'array' by a rename (the only such line in HEAD's lib). The working tree already has 'a () ++# b ()' (inside an uncommitted 38+/30- parsing.spi change), so committing tree lib unblocks it. (The scheduled 10-21 run fails in the compiler suite job, a separate track.) alphabet: run 39367599510 fails in apps/hangul. hanja.spi:2:5 hanja_to_hangul_table declares array_base (i32 * i32), but the ;[ ... ] literal is 'array', the core-v1 split. The user already STAGED the fix ('|> fun (array x) => x' after the literal). dice and polyglot last deployed 10-20 (green). So both red pages turn green with the user's next commits; no code change is needed from main.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_25 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 25u32, "2026-10-22T07:30Z", "main", "03:30 main: the scheduled spiral compiler-suite job (run 39594781370, 10-21) fails on one row: samples/zig_exit_wide [Fsharp] DISAGREE on the Linux runner (exit 305 while C, Rust, Zig, Python, Gleam and OpenQasm exit 49 = 305 mod 256). Cause: the warm F# native runner returns the program's int without a real process exit, and HEAD's test.ps1 masked it to 8 bits off Windows only when '\\.Exit -isnot [int]' was false. The warm result is not a .NET int, so it was never masked. The STAGED test.ps1 already fixes it: parse the exit as a number, then '-band 255' when not on Windows. So all three red signals (spiral build, alphabet build, spiral compiler suite) have fixes waiting in the user's next commits.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_26 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 26u32, "2026-10-22T07:31Z", "main", "03:31 main: the rest of the CI picture (read only, last runs). i574n/.github gh-pages (39357416239) fails the same way as spiral: it clones spiral and builds its lib, and dies on 'notebooks failed: parsing' (the pipe2 line), so its push job finds no gh-pages artifact. It is fixed by the same spiral commit. Green: tibia, blog, dir-tree-html (and dice and polyglot, 10-20). Red, owned by other lanes: x ci (10-20 04:04) and eoie gh-pages (10-20 02:10); not diagnosed here.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_27 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 27u32, "2026-10-22T19:37Z", "x", "2026-10-22 15:37 x: x ci status update (details in X-DONE notes 41-51, not repeated here). The red on HEAD 61b8fff (windows-2025 e2e '#< CLIXML') now has a fix verified locally: '-OutputFormat Text' in e2e's step launcher, e2e 31+5 green on 10-22 15:00. CI parity: zig 0.17.0 checked (prelude passed, exsss smoke 5/5 incl. rust+gleam); rust was already pinned by Cells via the rustup proxy. The full notebook rerun on CI's zig is due ~17:50-18:55. Preconditions for green are unchanged: the user commits x's whole working tree and pushes spiral with it (still 33ee6412).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_28 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 28u32, "2026-10-23T11:53Z", "main", "2026-10-23 07:53 main: CI survey (gh run list on the i574n remotes). No push since 10-20 04:14 in any repo. Green on the last run: dice, polyglot, x (dynamic), eoie (dynamic), tibia, blog, dir-tree-html. Red: alphabet push 39367599510 (hanja fix staged by the user), i574n/.github push 39357416239 (parsing.spi pipe2, fixed in the tree), and spiral's scheduled compiler job 39773873815 (10-22 11:52, HEAD 33ee6412) with DISAGREE 1, samples/zig_exit_wide [Fsharp]: the Linux 8-bit warm F# exit mask fixed in the tree on 10-21 (note 17). Spiral's 10-23 11:39 schedule is running on the same HEAD and will show the same row. All three reds clear with the user's next commits; nothing new to fix in code.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_29 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 29u32, "2026-10-24T03:11Z", "main", "2026-10-23 23:11 main grooming estimate, corrected 03:00: the 07:53 survey already showed nothing left to fix in code. All 3 reds (spiral's schedule on HEAD 33ee6412, alphabet, i574n/.github) are fixed in the tree and clear with the user's next commits; the '240 m, reproduce and fix each red' reading was wrong. Agent estimate 0; blocked on the user's commits and pushes.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_30 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 30u32, "2026-10-24T07:00Z", "main", "2026-10-24 03:00 main: survey refreshed with gh run list: unchanged since 07:53. No push in any repo since 10-20 04:14; red: spiral schedule run 39947580678 (10-23 11:39, HEAD 33ee6412), alphabet 39367599510, i574n/.github 39357416239; the other 7 green. Status Active -> Blocked: every red is fixed in the tree and waits on the user's commits.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_31 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 31u32, "2026-10-25T08:29Z", "main", "10-25 04:29 main: spiral CI red cause found (run 40161876207 on HEAD 47d1e562, build ubuntu-24.04, workflow.ps1): RUST-FAILED apps/spiral, 'ETY-UnboundVariable: Unbound term variable: rust_type' in the lua/lua_function/lua_error/lua_value/lua_multi_value nominals (each body is rust.rust_type applied at type level). The CI compiler is built from HEAD's apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, which is 1,136+/153- lines behind the working tree (the uncommitted 5i/5j/5k pack layer, plus Program.fs 13 lines), while HEAD's lib and apps are edition 3 (lib rust.spi: ':= rust_type \\* fs rs. ...'). Locally the installed tree compiler builds apps/spiral, so the commit pairs new sources with the old compiler. Fix: the user commits apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs + tmp/compiler/host/Program.fs with the next commit (the 5k install lands in the tree first: job-1792916161438). Pages: spiral and alphabet still serve renders without the README section, so they refresh on the first green run. kit (eoie renamed) is served at i574n.github.io/kit/; pages-sweep.ps1 now lists kit instead of eoie.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_32 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 32u32, "2026-10-29T07:04Z", "main", "10-29 03:1x main: why spiral's pages have not refreshed since 10-18 (gh-pages dff26794, deploy of 10-18T19:00Z): scheduled runs skip build and push by design (gh-pages.yml:18 'if: github.event_name != schedule'), so only push runs deploy, and every push run since fails. The latest, 40677661106 (push, cec8840c, 10-28 11:08Z), fails in build (ubuntu-24.04) at apps/spiral/build.ps1:127 'RUST-FAILED apps/spiral / run check': 'mix spiral.render_cells exit 1: Unchecked dependencies for environment dev: kino (Hex package) the dependency is not available, run mix deps.get'. On a fresh runner nothing has fetched apps/cells' Hex deps by the time apps/spiral's run check calls into Cells; core.ps1:379-383 and run_notebook.ps1:114-120 guard their own Cells calls with 'if deps/kino/mix.exs is missing: local.hex, local.rebar, deps.get', and build.ps1:61-63 had no such guard. FIXED (unstaged, parse-clean): apps/spiral/build.ps1 runs the same three mix tasks inside the existing try before spiral.render_cells when deps/kino/mix.exs is missing; a failure there still surfaces through the render's own failure row. Locally deps/kino exists, so the guard is a no-op here, and the next push run is the proof. The same stale shape (200, no readme section, gh-pages from 10-18) holds for alphabet (cdd28acb), whose push failures were not read tonight.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_33 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 33u32, "2026-10-29T07:08Z", "main", "10-29 03:1x main: alphabet's pages are stale for a different reason (gh-pages cdd28acb, deploy 10-18T16:49Z). Every alphabet push run since 10-20 fails; the latest, 40483234158 (10-27 09:45Z), has build (ubuntu-24.04) success and build (windows-2025) failure, so push is skipped. The Windows log shows Playwright's browser downloads failing (playwright.azureedge.net chromium/firefox/webkit win64 zips: HTTP 400 GatewayExceptionResponse), then Invoke-Block exit 1 in polyglot/apps/parser, alphabet/scripts and alphabet/apps/documents (retry 1/3). Not read deeper tonight. Next: the first failing step's own error in apps/documents (the F# step removed tonight under FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER n9 predates nothing here; the failure is from 10-27), and whether the Windows job needs Playwright at all.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_34 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 34u32, "2026-10-29T07:09Z", "main", "10-29 03:2x main: alphabet Windows push failure, one step deeper (run 40483234158, job 122118500594): apps/documents' build runs the spiral CLI (target\\spiral\\spiral\\target\\debug\\spiral_<hash>.exe, built from spiral's apps/spiral), which panics at D:\\a\\alphabet\\spiral\\apps\\spiral\\spiral.rs:16776:42: 'called Result::unwrap() on an Err value: Os { code: 3, kind: NotFound, message: The system cannot find the path specified. }', on all 3 retries. So a filesystem call in the spiral CLI unwraps a missing Windows path on the runner. The Playwright 400s earlier in the log are a separate, non-fatal setup noise. The local spiral.rs (3f1b7588) does not line up with CI's generated file at 16776, so mapping the panic to Spiral source needs CI's spiral.rs (or a local Windows run of alphabet/apps/documents/build.ps1 on a clean checkout).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_35 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 35u32, "2026-10-29T08:13Z", "main", "10-29 04:1x main: ROOT CAUSE of the Windows push failures of alphabet (40483234158) and .github (40677888927): both die in polyglot/apps/parser's notebook run, where Cells calls the spiral CLI 'export <TEMP>/spiral_cells_fs_<n>/JsonParser.cells fs'. The CLI's own trace shows the path given as C:\\Users\\RUNNER~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp/... and then written and parsed as D:\\Users\\RUNNER~1\\..., so it panics at spiral.rs:16776 ('Os { code: 3, NotFound }'). GitHub's Windows runners keep the workspace on D: (D:\\a\\...) and TEMP on C:. lib/spiral/file_system.spi:1247-1248, get_full_path's Rust arm, rebuilds a path's drive segment from the CURRENT DIRECTORY's first letter (sm'.(++#) (current_dir |> sm'.slice 0i32 0i32) \":\") instead of the segment's own letter, so any absolute path on another drive is re-rooted onto the current drive. Locally everything is on C:, so it never shows. (The Playwright 1.44 'playwright.azureedge.net ... 400' errors are non-fatal noise: spiral/scripts/init.ps1:91 only prints a message. That CDN host is retired, so the pin wants a bump.) .github's page 404 is separate and older: its gh-pages (1afcd1a5, 10-18T23:32Z) has 16 root entries and no index.html, and Pages is enabled and built from gh-pages, so it is a deploy without a render; the next green push run fixes it. FIX drafted and being proven on lib copies (lib-drive applier in main's session scratchpad): line 1248 takes x's own letter, upper-cased (x |> sm'.slice 0i32 0i32 |> sm'.to_upper), plus test get_full_path_keeps_the_drive_of_an_absolute_path (Windows only: a path on a drive the cwd is not on must keep its drive; it fails on the current code by the bug's own path).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_36 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 36u32, "2026-10-29T08:23Z", "main", "10-29 04:2x main: the drive fix is PROVEN on lib copies (lib_gate -File file_system.spi -Test get_full_path_keeps_the_drive_of_an_absolute_path,get_full_path_2,get_full_path_3, each arm with its own MIX_BUILD_PATH). The first run was VOID: sccache was missing, so the known-good control tests failed too; it was reinstalled, see PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY. CONTROL (new test only, old code): get_full_path_2 and _3 pass, and the new drive test FAILS, which reproduces CI's C-to-D re-rooting locally. A first fix (always upper-case the segment's own letter) broke get_full_path_2: Cells cells run with a lower-case cwd drive (c:/...), and the old code deliberately kept the cwd's letter case for same-drive paths. FINAL fix, file_system.spi:1247-1248: when the segment's letter equals the cwd's drive letter (case-insensitively), use current_dir's letter exactly as before; otherwise use the segment's own letter, upper-cased. Same-drive results are byte-identical by construction. FIXED arm: all 3 pass (3/3, type errors 0). It lands in the live lib after main's lib sweep finishes (the sweep is a live lib reader), followed by a full file_system.spi gate on the live lib. Then the next Windows push run of alphabet or .github is the CI proof.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_37 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 37u32, "2026-10-29T09:26Z", "main", "10-29 05:2x main: drive fix LANDED in the live lib (unstaged; the original is saved in main's session scratchpad as lib-drive/file_system.spi.before). It landed after the lib sweep finished and with 0 Cells readers running, and the live file's sha256 (C46D38D8A5A717A6) equals the proven fixed copy's. Full gate on the live lib: lib_gate -File file_system.spi gives 29 of 29 passed, type errors 0, including the new get_full_path_keeps_the_drive_of_an_absolute_path. Every Rust consumer of file_system.get_full_path regenerates with it, including the spiral CLI that alphabet's and .github's Windows CI build from source. The next Windows push run of either repo is the CI proof, after the user's commit.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_38 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 38u32, "2026-10-29T10:46Z", "main", "10-29 06:4x main: the Playwright step, made concrete (npm registry, read-only): @playwright/test and playwright are at 1.64.1 latest. 1.44.0 is pinned in 4 places: spiral scripts/init.ps1:91 (bunx --bun playwright@1.44.0 install), spiral lib/spiral/near/wallet/package.json, dice ui/e2e/package.json and polyglot apps/spiral/temp/extension/package.json. 1.44's browser host playwright.azureedge.net now answers HTTP 400 (CI logs of alphabet and .github). Bump all 4 together (the browsers must match the test library), then prove it with 'bunx --bun playwright@1.64.1 install' plus the dice ui and near wallet e2e runs. Not done tonight: the browser download is several hundred MB, and the e2e proof did not fit before 07:00.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_39 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 39u32, "2026-10-29T11:42Z", "main", "10-29 07:3x main: Playwright bumped from 1.44.0 to 1.64.1 at 7 sites (all unstaged):\n- spiral: scripts/init.ps1:91, lib/spiral/near/wallet/package.json.\n- dice: ui/e2e/package.json, plus bun.lockb regenerated.\n- currency_converter: test/e2e/package.json, plus bun.lockb, and scripts/init.ps1:9. Its working copy was CRLF against LF in HEAD, so it was normalized to LF.\n- polyglot: apps/spiral/temp/extension/package.json, plus bun.lockb, and scripts/init.livemd:67.\nConsumer path: 'bunx --bun playwright@1.64.1 install' exits 0 and downloads from cdn.playwright.dev (chromium-1248, chromium_headless_shell-1248, firefox-1555, webkit-2370, ffmpeg, winldd), so the retired azureedge host's 400 is gone. dice ui e2e on 1.64.1 passes 1 of 1 in 25s against the 10-26 dist, through the config's own ssl-serve webServer. Also healed: ~/.bun/bin/bun.exe and bunx.exe, which were lost in the wipe; dice's webServer command and currency_converter's run.ps1 and init.ps1 call them by path. They are copies of scoop bun 1.4.4. Left: currency_converter e2e, which needs the Phoenix app up (its run.ps1), and CI after the user's push.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_40 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 40u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit: naming/slimness of every own repo's workflow is now CI-WORKFLOW-NAMES (census: 12 conforming, 5 name deviations, 12 without actions.lock). Green status stays here.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_41 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 41u32, "2026-11-01T20:57Z", "main", "main 16:5x CI CENSUS (gh run list, latest run per repo): GREEN spiral 3464d8e, kit e575f7c, x a2d3318, tibia f6a4309, fiscal 1ab6fcd, dice 2f41f4c, dir-tree-html e2f2623, polyglot 69ecfaf, blog 3ff83fc, i574n.github.io. RED: only alphabet 09b0df2, and only its windows-2025 job. Ubuntu passed, and the two runs before it (78e8731, aa79372) passed. The Windows 'pwsh scripts/workflow.ps1' step ran exactly 60 min (16:33-17:33 UTC), hit the job limit, and its log blob is gone (HTTP 404 BlobNotFound). Suspect: the Windows compile-server main-thread stack overflow (COMPILER-WIN-STACK-OVERFLOW) showing as a hang. pack15a's Program.fs fix reaches CI only once the user pushes spiral. Main re-ran the failed job at 16:5x to get a readable log. Status Blocked -> Active: nothing blocks this epic now except that push and alphabet's rerun verdict.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_42 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 42u32, "2026-11-01T23:58Z", "main", "main 20:0x spiral b3fd292b (user push 18:51): CI run 41359205750 GREEN on ubuntu-24.04 and windows-2025. It is the first green run with the edition-3 :: lib respell, pack15a's Program.fs (1 GB compile thread), the Cells profile-loader removal, lib_gate's exit-on-failure and the Linux-portable Cells scripts. Remaining reds: kit (test-attestation.ps1:53 'Plan payload changed', kit is on it), alphabet windows (60-min timeout; rerun in progress), and fiscal windows until its next run picks up the spiral fix.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_43 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 43u32, "2026-11-01T23:59Z", "main", "main 20:0x alphabet 09b0df2: main's re-run of the failed windows-2025 job (run 41326953157) is GREEN on both OSes and pushed Pages, so the 60-min timeout was a runner flake, not the code. Open reds now: kit (test-attestation 'Plan payload changed') and fiscal windows pending its run on the fixed spiral.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_44 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 44u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_45 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 45u32, "2026-11-02T17:21Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 13:3x KIT gh-pages RED diagnosis (main's sweep: run 41463936725 @7830da93, both OSes, \"Native Spiral developer workflow failed (exit 101)\"). History: kit's gh-pages has been red on every push since 10-18 (last green dd48d2a6, 10-18 17:48); 56c32ef6 died earlier on a Chocolatey rsync fetch, so 6037c1dd/7830da93 are the first runs to reach these tests. TWO CAUSES in kit_contracts (cargo test -p kit-contracts --lib, under build.ps1 -Test -CompilerContracts): (1) LINUX ONLY, 3 tests (family_contract_semantic_drift_is_rejected, flat_bundle_roundtrip_is_self_verified, public_rejections_and_bundle_drift_fail_closed): \"ColdProofV4 renewal rolled back: regular file exceeds limit: .../kit bytes=313561064 limit=134217728\": the Linux debug kit binary is 313 MB (DWARF inside the ELF; the Windows debug exe is 51 MB with a separate PDB, release 23 MB), over the bundle's 128 MiB per-file cap. Fix candidates, to measure: CI-only CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=line-tables-only (or 0) in the workflow env, which keeps local debugging, vs raising the bundle cap for the kit binary only. (2) BOTH OSes, patch_and_agile_failures_preserve_authority: `agile begin` fails \"KIT failed: Missing check input: <tmp>/state/prompt.spi\" from the compiler host (Program.fs:752 runCheck) during agile_attest_known_mutation, although begin's agile_atomic_write wrote that file just before. NOT REPRODUCIBLE locally: the same fixture + KIT_SPIRAL_COMPILE=<single-flight DLL> passes on the box with installed kit (TRAIN10) and with TRAIN11's candidate D29D6E40, and on the node with both the installed and compiler's linked2 DLL (host 94891444; host source 01:29 < installed host 02:39, so CI's host is the same). So the cause is CI-environment-specific (parallel tests in one process? TEMP layout? runner FS). Next step: download the run's artifacts / rerun with RUST_TEST_THREADS=1 to split parallelism from environment. CI is the user's push domain; the workflow env edit stays unstaged for them.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_46 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 46u32, "2026-11-02T19:49Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 15:5x CAUSE (1) FIXED, MEASURED on vultr (TRAIN11 tree, Linux, debug kit-cli). Full debug: 336,416,784 B; CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=line-tables-only: 154,908,040 B (STILL over the 134,217,728 cap, so that candidate is out); CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=0: 86,895,256 B (fits, 1m35s build). Edit (unstaged, for the user to commit and push): .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml job env gains `CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG: \"0\"`. It's env-only, so actions.lock needs no regeneration. Local builds keep full debug info. CAUSE (2), \"Missing check input: state/prompt.spi\": a Linux repro of `cargo test -p kit-contracts --lib` is running on vultr now. The earlier non-repros were both Windows (box, node), while CI fails on ubuntu too.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_47 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 47u32, "2026-11-02T20:03Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 16:0x CAUSE (2) ROOT-CAUSED AND FIXED; both causes now proven green on Linux (vultr, live tree with the fixes, CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=0): `cargo test -p kit-contracts --lib -- --include-ignored` gave 15 passed, 0 failed. ROOT CAUSE: the Spiral compiler emits byte-identical `global \"\"\"...\"\"\"` blocks ONCE. contracts_entry/cli_driver.spi splits each Rust test across several global blocks, and patch_and_agile_failures_preserve_authority's \"write state/prompt.spi + agile begin\" block was byte-identical to patch_and_agile_mutation_are_transactional's. The regenerated contracts.rs therefore lacked those two lines in the failures test, which then ran `agile check` on a state package without prompt.spi (\"Missing check input\"). Found by bisection: every replay outside the test passed (environment, cwd, stdin, tight timing, cargo env), the failing test's leftover fixture had no prompt.spi, and the generated body showed the missing lines. Windows box/node \"passed\" only because the committed contracts.rs predated the dedupe. FIX (unstaged): merge that block into its unique predecessor (cli_driver.spi) and regenerate contracts.rs (copied into the box tree; 3 begin sites now). A scan found no other duplicate global blocks in any kit package. With the gh-pages.yml `CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG: \"0\"` env, kit CI should be green once the user commits and pushes. Memory: spiral-identical-globals-dedupe.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_48 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 48u32, "2026-11-03T01:35Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:4x SWEEP (latest non-Pages run per i574n repo). GREEN: spiral 698bc3da, x 60d8c798, dice 84acdd55 (proves the polyglot-free init), alphabet e3f4266d, blog, i574n.github.io. RED, each with its owner and cause:\n- regex d7aa16be: nullable.spi 'Pattern miss'. pack17's GADT erasure wrongly erased the closed-index evidence family. compiler has a proven fix (GADT-ERASE-ONLY-GROWING) shipping with pack20, after pack19 (queued behind kit's TRAIN13c heavy window).\n- dir-tree-html 71c801f (user commit 19:16): 'module does not have the key: try_write_all_text'. LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS's dir-tree-html half was committed before its lib function landed. main lands lib/spiral/file_system.spi once TRAIN13c stops reading the live lib; then a spiral push + re-run.\n- html 05162bda: COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS Step B, which ships in pack19.\n- kit ba3d2100 and tibia 355726ca (23:16Z): those lanes' own reds, not triaged by main.\n- fiscal: in progress.\n- vault (08-10) and dotfiles: stale runs, no recent push.\n- tapas2: no runs yet (its first push carries tonight's port).\n- i574n.github: Actions API 404.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_49 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 49u32, "2026-11-03T13:33Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:3x CI sweep (latest runs per org repo): green = alphabet, blog, dice, fiscal, regex, spiral, x (+ pages deploys). RED: html (1000-line gate; fixed by the unstaged 8-crate split, awaits the user's push), .github (polyglot core.ps1 + pins drift; fixed unstaged in i574n.github, awaits push), kit 1266f9df run 41602520066 NEW: test-regeneration's notebook batch passes 119 paths on one Windows command line -> 'The command line is too long.' -> 'spiral notebooks failed (119)' (src/kit_dev_spiral_tests main.spi:32); ubuntu fails in the same step. Reported to kit (owner).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_50 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 50u32, "2026-11-03T13:37Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:3x addendum: tibia gh-pages RED too (bfd1641c, 07:42): deps/spiral/scripts/init-wgsl-run.ps1:35 LunarG 'latest' = 1.4.363.1 has no Windows runtime (404). Fixed by the unstaged spiral init-wgsl-run.ps1 fallback (published versions newest first -> 1.4.363.0); turns green when the user pushes spiral. So 4 reds: 3 await pushes (html, .github, spiral->tibia), 1 is kit's (reported).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_51 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 51u32, "2026-11-04T12:18Z", "resilience", "11-04 ~08:2x resilience CI RED-LIST AUDIT across 15 active i574n repos (additive data, no claim). RESULT: 13/15 green; 2 RED on the Rust/Spiral tests workflow on main = .github and html. x ci(tests) is GREEN; the doc-only repos (spiral/kit/fiscal/dice/tibia/alphabet/regex/blog/hangulize/The-Spiral-Language/i574n.github.io/dotfiles) have only gh-pages + pages-build-deployment (no test CI), all green. ROOT CAUSE (html run 41598172732, CONFIRMED from log-failed): NOT a test failure - spiral-tests all pass (37 passed, 0 failed, 8 unsupported, 7 files). The build fails at build.ps1 line 36 because ReadyToRun crossgen codegen FAILS on Hopac.dll (message: ReadyToRun Hopac.dll stays IL; Code generation failed for method Hopac.EmbeddedJob generic GetHashCode over __Canon) then exit 1, fail-fast cancels the windows sibling, push job fails/skips. .github (run 41598261461) fails at the SAME build.ps1 step on ubuntu - very likely the SAME Hopac R2R issue (same build.ps1; not log-confirmed). So both reds share ONE root cause: build.ps1 ReadyToRun cannot compile a Hopac generic method. FIX is build-logic (exclude Hopac from R2R, or tolerate stays-IL, or fix the crossgen path) - owner call, likely tied to HOPACSOTA-P6. Side note: cargo-quickinstall warehouse-clerk endpoint returns 402 Payment Required (non-fatal WARN). Diagnosis only - build scripts are not resilience autonomous remit.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_52 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 52u32, "2026-11-04T12:19Z", "resilience", "11-04 ~08:2x CONFIRMED: .github (run 41598261461 ubuntu) is the IDENTICAL root cause as html - ReadyToRun Hopac.dll stays IL, ILCompiler.CodeGenerationFailedException: Code generation failed for method Hopac.EmbeddedJob generic GetHashCode over __Canon, then exit 1. So BOTH reds are the SAME Hopac R2R crossgen failure (exception class ILCompiler.CodeGenerationFailedException). Tests pass; only the R2R precompile step fails (the run also logs 22 dlls precompiled in 15s, so R2R continues past Hopac but the captured error exits 1). Handing to the owner - build-logic fix (exclude Hopac from R2R, or tolerate CodeGenerationFailedException for Hopac.dll). resilience CI-audit contribution complete: 2/15 repos red, one shared root cause, actionable.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_53 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 53u32, "2026-11-04T14:40Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main CI CENSUS (gh run list, latest run per repo): GREEN kit, x, fiscal, tibia, regex, dice, alphabet, blog (pages builds 11-02..11-03); spiral IN PROGRESS (98e51d3, started 14:32Z); RED html (05a1a43 \"tests\", 11-03) and dir-tree-html (71c801f, 11-02); i574n.github and polyglot show no runs. html's red is ONLY the 1000-line gate (markdown/entry.rs 2339 lines in the committed single-crate layout; all 37 executed tests pass). The unstaged html tree (crate split + 11-04 cell-budget and viewer work) is HTML-OK on vultr with 49/49 and largest generated 994 lines, so html heals with the user's next commit, with no CI change needed. dir-tree-html: not checked (html is replacing it).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_54 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 54u32, "2026-11-04T14:41Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main dir-tree-html RED CAUSE (run on 71c801f, 11-02): RUST-FAILED dir-tree-html/inline, ETY-ModuleIndexFailed \"The module does not have the key: try_write_all_text In the definition: write_text\": dir-tree-html calls a lib file_system export that lib no longer has. html replaces dir-tree-html (its retirement is planned), so no patch here; the retirement itself is the user's call and isn't done by a lane.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_55 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 55u32, "2026-11-05T05:17Z", "main", "11-05 01:17 main SURVEY after the user's 11-04 23:18 push (gh run list, every active i574n repo): 9 of 11 red, ALL ONE ROOT CAUSE: spiral, fiscal, kit, .github, blog, regex, x, alphabet, dice each fail at spiral's scripts/init-app-build.ps1 CLI build with \"could not execute process `sccache ... rustc -vV`\" (2-6 hits per log), because main's 11-03 init-app-build step (ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT n7) builds and run-checks the CLI before init.ps1 installs sccache; fiscal additionally hits the deps/spiral get_workspace_root panic. Green: tibia, html (plus static-pages repos). FIX in the tree, unstaged (ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT n8/n9): init-app-build installs binstall+sccache first and sets SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT; the get_workspace_root deps fallback is in its node proof now. PENDING the user's next spiral push; any red left after it is a separate cause, to be re-surveyed then.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_56 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 56u32, "2026-11-05T06:50Z", "main", "11-05 02:50 main FRESH-RUNNER PROOF of the init fix (before the user's push): codespace miniature-meme-x7jqqp6pp3v957 (Ubuntu 24.04, 4 cores, no Rust, no sccache, no cargo-binstall), spiral HEAD faf422c9 cloned with the box's fixed scripts/init-app-build.ps1 (886B46344C30) and init.ps1 dropped in; rustup + nightly-2026-10-18 minimal installed first, as setup-rust does in CI. init.ps1 -> init-app-build: cargo-binstall --self-install, then \"cargo binstall sccache\" (sccache v0.19.0 -> ~/.cargo/bin, 2.7 s), THEN apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1: run check rust exit 0 \"spiral-check-rust 42\" (the CI red case), cuda/lua/gleam 42, protocol cases as expected, no FAILED / RUST-FAILED line; init continued (trunk via binstall). So the sccache-ordering red is fixed for every repo whose CI runs spiral init. The deps/spiral panic fix is the file_system.spi land (n10). PENDING: CI on the user's next push.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_57 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 57u32, "2026-11-05T20:19Z", "main", "main 11-05 16:2x CI SURVEY: spiral's scheduled run 42046993944 (14:38, HEAD faf422c9) is red in compiler and cells-gate for the SAME known cause as push run 41960731928 (03:18): apps/spiral/build.ps1 run check -> 'could not execute process sccache ... rustc -vV (never executed)' (CLI built before sccache is installed). The fix (init-app-build.ps1/init.ps1 install order) is unstaged and was proven on a fresh codespace at 02:58 (CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS n12). Last green: 41848519924 on 98e51d32 (11-04; compiler 18 min, cells-gate 54 min). Because CI stops at init, nothing after it has run against the unstaged tree: a full pre-push rehearsal of both jobs on a codespace is running now (CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS n13). Still waits on the user's push.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_58 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 58u32, "2026-11-05T22:35Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:4x PRE-PUSH REHEARSAL RESULT (codespace, HEAD faf422c9 + the box's whole unstaged spiral tree, CI's two jobs as written): compiler job GREEN (exit 0, 1162 s; native 3556 ran, 8 build-fail tolerated, oracle agree 2797, DISAGREE 0). cells-gate job exited 0, BUT its table holds 3 FAILED of 938 executed: ci_gate.ps1 only threw on 0 executed and never on failed tests, so cells-gate has been green with failures. The 11-04 green CI artifact (run 41848519924) shows 2 of 717 failed there too. FIXED (unstaged, spiral apps/cells/spi/ci_gate.ps1): the summary line counts failures, and any failed test prints file: test=targets and throws 'cells gate is RED'; tested on 3 summaries (rehearsal tsv -> RED 3 of 938, all-pass -> green, empty -> VOID). So after the push, cells-gate turns RED on 3 real failures until they are fixed: (1) NEW vs 11-04: lib/spiral/json_schema.spi json_schemas_map_onto_the_xsd_model_and_generate (rust; failed after 44 s). The file and its :< imports are unchanged; it consumes xsd_emit (+1162/-770 unstaged, fiscal's lands). Routed to fiscal. (2) PRE-EXISTING: process.spi:981 a_program_past_its_deadline_is_killed (rust) runs 'ping -n 30 127.0.0.1'; -n is Windows' count flag, so on Linux ping exits at once and is never killed; needs a per-OS long program (sleep 30 on Linux). (3) PRE-EXISTING: reactors.spi:311 physical_micros_reads_a_real_clock_that_moves_forward (c) asserts > 1.7e15 us since epoch; the C backend likely returns a monotonic clock.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_59 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 59u32, "2026-11-05T22:37Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:5x ROUTING the 3 reds behind the ci_gate fix: (1) json_schema (rust, new) -> fiscal (xsd_emit owner), with repro 'run_notebook --gate --path lib/spiral/json_schema.spi'. (2) process.spi:981 ping -n on Linux -> DRAFT written: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\PIPELINES-GREEN\\process.spi, base 9DD18D6D3EF1, a 2-line change: ':= program, args = ? platform::is_windows () ?> \"ping\", [-n 30 127.0.0.1] |: \"sleep\", [\"30\"]' (the idiom of exit_four_shell at :708). NOT yet proven or landed: the node is saturated by TRAIN32 until ~23:00 and the land needs the node -PrivateLib proof + box -ProvenLog (LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX); lands through lib_land_window -Draft lib/spiral/process.spi=<draft> -BaseHash 9DD18D6D3EF1 (pending). (3) reactors.spi:311 C clock (epoch bound fails; likely a monotonic clock id) -> compiler.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_60 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 60u32, "2026-11-05T22:53Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:5x CORRECTION to n58/n59 red (3), from compiler: reactors.spi:311 on C is NOT a monotonic-clock bug (the code already uses CLOCK_REALTIME). It's a BUILD failure, gcc 'error: CLOCK_REALTIME undeclared' (visible in run 41848519924's gate.log). Cells compiles C in strict -std mode, where glibc hides clock_gettime without POSIX feature macros. compiler's fix: the POSIX branch calls C11 timespec_get(&ts, TIME_UTC), which builds under c11/c17/gnu11 and returns epoch micros; proven on vultr gcc 15.2; draft drafts\\spiral\\REACTORS-C-CLOCK\\1-timespec-get.kitdo, landing via lib_land_window now. Remaining push reds: json_schema (fiscal) and process ping -n (main's draft, pending a node proof).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_61 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 61u32, "2026-11-05T22:53Z", "main", "main 11-05 18:5x EVIDENCE for red (2), process.spi ping: the 11-04 CI gate.log shows '__assert_eq { actual = 2; expected = -1 }' after 2169 ms on rust. So Linux ping exited 2 at once (-n is not a count there, and '30' is read as a host) instead of being killed at the 400 ms deadline. The draft's per-OS program (sleep 30 on Linux) is the right fix; still to be proven and landed.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_62 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 62u32, "2026-11-05T22:59Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:0x RED (1) json_schema FIXED by fiscal: cause was a stale expectation, not xsd_emit breakage. Nominal records arrived in faf422c9, so the root object is now emitted as 'nominal x_invoice =', not 'type x_invoice'. The assertion was updated; proven on vultr (8/8, and a mutant expecting x_no_such_root fails on the same assertion); landed via lib_land_window fiscal-json-schema-1105, json_schema.spi B6139AD7 -> F7564185, closed green, undo 20261105-185110, unstaged. Note the 11-04 CI was on 98e51d32, before faf422c9, which is why it passed there. STATE of the 3 push reds: json_schema fixed+landed (fiscal); reactors C clock fix landing (compiler, timespec_get); process ping draft under a Linux proof on vultr (main, control+draft run).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_63 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 63u32, "2026-11-05T23:03Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:0x red (2) process ping: the vultr proof is VOID. Scratch lib copy outside the mirror (base 9dd18d6d3ef1), process.spi gate under systemd MemoryMax=1500M with a private MIX_BUILD_PATH. CONTROL (base) failed 11 of 15, where CI fails exactly 1, and the draft failed 10, with different sets (split_command vs split_args): an environment failure, not a result. Causes: 'ld terminated with signal 7 [Bus error]' while linking a Rust cell under the cap on the 2-CPU host, and vultr has no 'python' (only python3), which several process tests invoke. Scratch removed. Lesson: vultr can't host process.spi's gate (link memory + python name). The draft (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\PIPELINES-GREEN\\process.spi, base 9DD18D6D3EF1) still needs a Linux proof: a codespace (python present, 16 GB) or the next CI after a land. Not landed.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_64 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 64u32, "2026-11-05T23:09Z", "compiler", "11-05 19:0x compiler: the 2 cells-gate test failures that turn RED once ci_gate.ps1 fails on failed tests (main, 11-05), both from run 41848519924 (i574n/spiral, cells-gate artifact): (1) reactors physical_micros_reads_a_real_clock_that_moves_forward on C: a BUILD failure, gcc 'CLOCK_REALTIME undeclared' (Cells compiles C in a strict standard mode, where glibc hides clock_gettime without POSIX feature macros). Vultr Ubuntu gcc 15.2: under -std=c11/c17 clock_gettime fails with 2 errors and builds only under gnu11, while C11 timespec_get(&ts, TIME_UTC) builds in every mode, returns epoch micros and passes the predicate. LANDED (unstaged): the POSIX branch calls timespec_get; the Windows branch is unchanged. Box gate c/rust/zig 1/1; lib_land_window GREEN (document_test 26, type_probe PASS, 0 drift); live reactors.spi 5114A20318F7 -> 8B2A746DD533, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-185656. (2) process a_program_past_its_deadline_is_killed on rust: the test ran 'ping -n 30 127.0.0.1' (Windows syntax); on Linux, -n is numeric output, so ping exits 2 at once (vultr: exit 2) and the test saw 2, not -1. Fix: a portable 'python -c import time; time.sleep(30)' (python is on the CI runner, since a_started_program_reports_its_exit passes there). Box gate rust+gleam 1/1; lib_land_window running.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_65 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 65u32, "2026-11-05T23:16Z", "compiler", "11-05 19:1x compiler: (2) process a_program_past_its_deadline_is_killed LANDED too (unstaged): lib_land_window GREEN, 2 consumer signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26, type_probe PASS (18 typed), 0 drift. Live process.spi 9DD18D6D3EF1 -> B68E3B9F02E5, lib digest FBD04FD38F7EFF1F, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-190655. Both of run 41848519924's cells-gate failures are now fixed in the tree; confirmation is the next CI run on Linux after the user's push (box gates prove the Windows path and the Linux C behaviour was proven on vultr; the Linux Rust cell itself is CI's to show).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_66 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 66u32, "2026-11-05T23:17Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:1x ALL THREE push reds now have landed fixes (unstaged): json_schema (fiscal, F7564185), reactors C clock (compiler, timespec_get, 8B2A746D), process deadline (compiler, 'python -c import time; time.sleep(30)', process.spi 9DD18D6D -> B68E3B9F, landed 19:09). main's per-OS sleep draft is superseded and deleted. A codespace run (started 19:05, so before compiler's land; its tree has the original ping test) is checking on Linux (a) that the fixed ci_gate goes RED on the original test and (b) that a non-ping long program passes. The real confirmation is the next Linux CI after the user's push.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_67 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 67u32, "2026-11-05T23:32Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:3x FLEET CI (latest run per own repo): RED at init from the SAME root, spiral's CLI-before-sccache order inherited through init.ps1: kit 0f6dd8f, x f9c95a5, dice 09c27e2, alphabet 082f8f2, blog 7f35d12 ('could not execute process sccache' in each), fiscal bb1ebad (fails inside the init.ps1 step), regex 53b31ae, i574n/.github f509c4f, plus spiral faf422c itself. GREEN: html 68ccb00, tibia eb5900b (pages), dotfiles, i574n.github.io. So one user push of spiral (with the unstaged init-order fix) unblocks 9 repos; after that the next push or schedule of each is the real gate, and cells-gate turns honest via the ci_gate fix (3 known reds now fixed and landed).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_68 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 68u32, "2026-11-05T23:40Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:4x LINUX PROOF (fresh codespace, HEAD faf422c9 + the box's unstaged tree as of 19:06, after workflow.ps1 -Compiler exit 0): (a) the FIXED ci_gate.ps1 on the ORIGINAL process.spi (9dd18d6d3ef1): exit 1, 'cells gate is RED: 1 of 18 executed tests failed', failed_tests = [a_program_past_its_deadline_is_killed] only. So the gate now fails honestly on Linux, and the ping -n bug reproduces exactly as in CI. (b) the same file with a per-OS long program (sleep 30 on Linux) passes: 18/18, exit 0, 95 s. compiler's LANDED variant (python -c time.sleep(30); python is present on the codespace and the runner) is the same approach but was not itself run here; the next Linux CI confirms it. Codespace deleted.")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_69 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 69u32, "2026-11-06T00:03Z", "main", "main 11-05 20:0x CONSUMER PRE-PUSH PROOF: regex's full workflow at 53b31ae, run against the box's unstaged spiral tree on a fresh codespace, is GREEN (init passes with the order fix; 93/93 tests). So the user's spiral push is expected to turn regex's red (run 41960786290, sccache at init) green, and by the same root very likely kit, x, fiscal, dice, alphabet, blog and .github too (not individually rehearsed).")
inl note_of_pipelines_green_70 () = Note ("PIPELINES-GREEN", 70u32, "2026-11-06T00:34Z", "main", "main 11-05 20:3x CONSUMER REHEARSALS (codespace, each repo's own workflow.ps1 beside the box's unstaged spiral tree): blog 7f35d12 GREEN (exit 0, 214 s, every notebook passed, 'BLOG-OK'); regex 53b31ae GREEN (93/93, earlier). VOID, not a verdict: dice 09c27e2 hit my 840 s per-repo bound (exit 124; its workflow is longer); alphabet 082f8f2 exit 1 because 'cargo install tectonic' built from source and failed on the missing graphite2 system libs, while real CI provides tectonic/pandoc/fonts via wtfjoke/setup-tectonic + cache-apt-pkgs-action, which a bare codespace doesn't replicate. Both regex and blog passed spiral's init with the order fix, which is the step all 9 red repos die at today.")
