inl gadt_growing_index_hang () = Task ("GADT-GROWING-INDEX-HANG", "Compiler hang (both builds tested: candidate single-flight DLL of pack night-1017): a value of a recursive GADT whose case FIELD mentions the type at a grown index never finishes compiling (CPU-bound, ~230 MB, killed after 45-250 s). 8-line repro: nominal zero = (); nominal succ n = (); union rec transcript pending = | Done :: transcript zero | Call :: forall n. i32 * transcript (succ n) -> transcript n; inl main () : i32 = (inl t : transcript zero = Done) then 7i32. Same union defined but unused: compiles. Index kept the same (chain n -> chain n) or a non-recursive index change (box (succ n)): compile and run. Wrong programs over the full Call/Result transcript are rejected fast and correctly (Got transcript (succ zero) / Expected transcript zero), so type checking is fine; the suspect is the representation/reachable-cases closure of a GADT-indexed union (pack-1x: 'a GADT-indexed union holds only its reachable cases'), which expands transcript zero -> transcript (succ zero) -> ... without bound. Fix: compute reachable cases over the index modulo the case's quantified variables (a case whose field index grows is reachable for every instance, no expansion), or bound the closure and fall back to all cases; add the repro as the regression sample. Found while prototyping CONVO-IN-SPIRAL's type-level tool-call protocol (unanswered Call = type error).", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,gadt,bug", "current", "current")
inl lab_in_repo () = Task ("LAB-IN-REPO", "Experiments live in the repo, not in job tmp (user 2026-10-17: tmp overuse is drift; it also blocks continuing on another machine or in a cloud agent). Convention started in spiral/lab: one directory per backlog item named by its id lowercased (lab/convo-in-spiral, lab/lib-reactors, lab/hopacsota-hopac-depth, lab/hopacsota-lf-scheduling, lab/gadt-growing-index-hang), git-tracked sources only, one shared bounded runner lab/try.ps1 (60 s kill, shared DLL or SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL), run outputs in git-ignored lab/.runs; portable references only (nuget refs, repo-relative paths, no user-profile paths). Lifecycle: when the item is Done, its lab dir is promoted (lib/, apps/, samples/) or deleted in the same change; an item Paused/Planned keeps it. Measured drift it replaces: this job's tmp holds ~850 scripts in ~120 topic folders (packs, lanes, probes, benches) plus spiral-bin\\packs, all lost with the job and invisible to other machines; the heavy gate itself (tmp/shared/heavy.ps1 with the run ledger) lives there. Next: (1) EOIE-LAB-AUDIT; (2) move the reusable main-lane tools (heavy gate + ledger, compare-runs, kino-suite runner, pack scripts) into repo homes (apps/compiler/tmp/scripts or lab/<item>); (3) per-repo lab/ in eoie, i574n.github, polyglot as they need it.", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "process,lab,drift,main,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lab_in_repo () = Planning ("LAB-IN-REPO", Minutes 135u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lab_in_repo_1 () = Note ("LAB-IN-REPO", 1u32, "2026-10-17T14:47Z", "main-thread", "10:47 main-thread fork: first main-lane tools moved into the repo: (1) apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/heavy.ps1 = the heavy gate + run ledger, comment-free and split into named functions (Wait-HeavySlot, Get-HeavyTicketPrefix, Wait-WslReady, Stop-IdleWsl); the FIFO queue moved from the job tmp to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\heavy-queue (machine state, outlives jobs); exclusion still comes from the machine-global mutexes, so the job-tmp copy and this one exclude each other (smoke: repo copy took slot 2 while the parent held slot 1; both ledger rows written); until every lane sources the repo copy, FIFO order between the two queue dirs is not shared. (2) apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/compare-runs.ps1 = cell-by-cell diff of two harness runs (run name or dir), DISAGREE count; verified on bless 081502 vs reuse run 084050 (0 cells). Next: lanes switch to . apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/heavy.ps1, then the Kino suite runner and the pack scripts (spiral-bin\\packs) get repo homes.")
inl note_of_lab_in_repo_2 () = Note ("LAB-IN-REPO", 2u32, "2026-10-17T15:01Z", "main-thread", "11:01 main-thread fork: (3) apps/kino/spi/run_suite.ps1 = the Kino suite runner from the job-tmp lane-b script merged with the targeted-tests runner (-Label, -Tests a,b, -Dll, -Port, -TimeoutMin): repo-relative paths, MIX_BUILD_PATH and logs under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin (kino-builds/<label>, kino-suite/<label>.log), retires its daemon by TCP afterwards, and defers while a live Tibia client/server process runs (the old lane-specific arena flag file is gone). Smoke through the repo heavy gate: cell_test 12 tests, 0 failures. Moved so far: heavy.ps1, compare-runs.ps1, run_suite.ps1; still in job tmp: the pack scripts (spiral-bin\\packs), after-bless / determinism scripts, kino-tests.ps1 (superseded by run_suite -Tests).")
inl note_of_lab_in_repo_3 () = Note ("LAB-IN-REPO", 3u32, "2026-10-17T15:11Z", "main-thread", "11:11 main-thread fork: HANDOFF (lane paused): lab convention live in spiral/lab (7 item dirs, runner lab/try.ps1); main-lane tools moved: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/heavy.ps1 + compare-runs.ps1, apps/kino/spi/run_suite.ps1. Next: lanes source the repo heavy.ps1 (shared FIFO queue), move the pack scripts, per-repo lab/ elsewhere.")
inl note_of_lab_in_repo_4 () = Note ("LAB-IN-REPO", 4u32, "2026-10-17T15:30Z", "main-thread", "11:30 main-thread: reconciled with the study lane. Canonical tools are apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/heavy.ps1 (gate + run ledger), scripts/compare-runs.ps1 and apps/kino/spi/run_suite.ps1, and the job-tmp heavy.ps1 is a one-line forwarder to scripts/heavy.ps1. I removed my duplicates from lab/harness-run-only-useful; it keeps only the experiment probes (rebuild/cross-folder determinism, bindiff.py, fsharp-resources, kino-tests). Patches live in lab/zig-hub-speed and lab/gadt-growing-index-hang.")
inl note_of_lab_in_repo_5 () = Note ("LAB-IN-REPO", 5u32, "2026-10-19T12:29Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:29 lap 1 grain: today's moves out of job tmp into spiral/lab: HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH (9 R3/R4 scripts), WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (toolchain.spi), SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS (ebpf_family.spi), UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC (upstream_let_rec_annotation draft), LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS (CIC kernel + neg package); each rewritten LF with repo-relative packageDir; job tmp outputs (ipynb, html, logs) stay behind Next: count what job tmp still holds that a backlog item cites, and move the next batch")
inl note_of_lab_in_repo_6 () = Note ("LAB-IN-REPO", 6u32, "2026-10-19T13:03Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 09:03 lap 2 grain: backlog notes cite 47 distinct job-tmp paths; the most cited, sweep/ (intent-report.txt 8x, intents.py), serves eoie-lane items (EOIE-ZED-SWEEP and others) and holds a copy of the opencode database, so it must never be moved into a git-tracked lab (credential tables, possible provider keys); rotation/* (CORE-PAIR-UNIFICATION 7 notes) are applied one-shot patches, which the lab lifecycle deletes rather than promotes; night/civil, night/ebpf-blocks, night/cic and hopacsota-p0 were moved into spiral/lab this morning; 9 cited paths no longer exist (into, todo-source, caches, outputs, ...), mostly prose words matched after 'job tmp' Next: rule for the move: only source files (spi, spiproj, ps1, py, fsx) of main-lane items, never databases or logs; next batch: night/bend64 and rotation/coverage-probe if any open item still needs them")
inl note_of_lab_in_repo_7 () = Note ("LAB-IN-REPO", 7u32, "2026-10-19T18:35Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:35 lap 4 grain: resolved Done folders: of 99 spiral lab folders, 18 belong to Done items; 10 were removed after a zip into the session scratchpad (CELLS-ACCEPT-TUPLES, DIR-TREE-README, FSHARP-UTF8-STRINGS, FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER, MATRIX-RUN-ONLY-USEFUL, MATRIX-TOOLCHAIN-IDENTITY, TEST-FAILS-SPECIFIC, UPSTREAM-SYNTAX-SYNC, WGSL-RUN-WGPU-30, SPIRAL-MACRO-FIELD-SPLICE: none tracked, nothing written in the last 2 h, references only in ledger and finished queue rows); kept: CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE (probe-lib.ps1 is the live lab gate tool, to be promoted), HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH (P3 inputs), CELLS-GATE + CELLS-REPIN (cross-referenced scripts), SPIRAL-CORE-NEQ (after-freeze probes), ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE and SPIRAL-DIAGNOSTIC-LOCATIONS (touched within 2 h) Next: promote probe-lib.ps1 into a tracked gate script (it hardcodes scratchpad MIX_BUILD_PATH, which must become a parameter), then resolve the remaining 8")
