inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 1u32, "2026-10-20T03:24Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 23:24 user 2026-10-19 23:1x: finish xsd first (start, after the 10-17 research go-gate); slice from SEFAZ-XSD-APP notes 1-10.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 2u32, "2026-10-21T23:13Z", "main", "19:13 slice-5 plan, written while compiles are blocked (no code run yet). Local inventory: fpc (scoop) is present and is what the matrix's Delphi rows use; the DFe.NET sparse clone under .claude/jobs/5a6e53fb/tmp/xsd-data holds the XSDs and AppTeste folders but 0 .cs sources (a sparse checkout), and no ACBr checkout exists. Plan in gated steps: (1) compile ONE generated module (generated_nfe_v4_00.spi, 1 example) with --backend Delphi and build it with fpc; gate: it compiles, and the example document validates with 0 messages and round-trips byte-identical, like the 13 .NET examples (needs a compile window, after the night install). (2) all 13 modules on Delphi, same gate. (3) benchmarks: widen the DFe.NET checkout to its NFe sources (a git sparse-checkout add, local), and fetch ACBr's NFe units (ProjetoACBr, the GitHub mirror), each into its own new folder per the untrusted-download rule. Compare parse, validate and serialize of the same 13 documents: results must agree; speed reported per document. Rule for 'done': steps 1-2 green and step 3 numbers recorded; a fetch failure or a license problem keeps step 3 open, not the item. Order: after PACK-AFTER-NIGHT, since SEFAZ variant 3 changes the generated modules first.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 3u32, "2026-10-21T23:15Z", "main", "19:15 step-1 blocker found by reading and staged: the lab's xml.spi has Rust-only arms (plus one Zig) for code_point_at, code_point_width, code_point_count, code_point_string and is_file; every other backend failwiths, so the generated modules could not run on Delphi at all. lab/SEFAZ-XSD-XML-READER/delphi-arms.ps1 (4 anchors, dry run matches each once) adds byte_at with a Delphi arm (UInt32(Ord(s[i + 1])); codegenDelphi indexes strings by byte, 1-based, and Length counts bytes), a Spiral UTF-8 decoder on top of it (utf8_width_of, utf8_decode_at), Delphi arms for code_point_at / width / count, and is_file via FileExists. Not covered: code_point_string (it builds a string from a code point, needed only for numeric entities) stays failwith on Delphi; find_from already has a generic fallback. The lib never converts char to a number, so a fully portable byte reader would need compiler support; one Delphi macro is the smallest step. Verified only by step 1's compile and run (after the night install).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 4u32, "2026-10-25T00:54Z", "main", "2026-10-24 20:54 main groom: P1 -> P0 by the priority-order rule. It's a FISCAL-APP dep and the last slice of the user's XSD order (memory priority-order).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 5u32, "2026-10-25T06:49Z", "fiscal", "02:49 fiscal: scripts/delphi-arms.ps1 deleted from fiscal under FISCAL-COMMIT-HYGIENE rule D6 (note 10): it was a parked patch adding Delphi arms to lib xml.spi, written in the pre-edition-3 lib, never landed (lib had 0 of its arms; main n4). This slice needs those arms; they get drafted fresh against the current edition-3 xml.spi when it starts. The old text is in the 02:31 snapshot (session scratchpad fiscal-snapshot-20261025-023152\\scripts\\delphi-arms.ps1).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 6u32, "2026-10-25T07:30Z", "fiscal", "03:30 fiscal: step-1 blocker re-drafted against the current edition-3 lib (no lib module has a | Delphi => arm yet). Landing form: session scratchpad xml-delphi-arms\\apply.py <path to xml.spi> [--apply], anchored, base xml.spi 9980B7ACD658A591, format --check clean, macro splice scan clean. delphi_byte_at is the only host call (Ord(s[i]) with the 1-based index computed in Spiral, granular rule); utf8_width_of and delphi_code_point_at decode UTF-8 in plain Spiral; Delphi arms for code_point_at, code_point_width and is_file (FileExists). code_point_string stays without a Delphi arm (numeric entities only). Unverified until step 1 compiles one generated module with --backend Delphi and builds it with fpc: whether the Delphi output already uses SysUtils for FileExists, and whether codegenDelphi strings are byte-indexed UTF-8 as main n3 read them. Land with that compile, not before (lib readers: fiscal gate job-1792912920241 and main pack reviews).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 7u32, "2026-10-25T07:34Z", "fiscal", "03:34 fiscal: step-3 source research (no download yet). DFe.NET: LGPL-2.1, last push 2026-09-24 (gh api); the benchmark side needs NFe.Classes and DFe.Classes (serialization model) beside the 4 schema folders init.ps1 already sparse-checks out, so the fetch is one git sparse-checkout add in a NEW folder (untrusted-download rule), never in deps/corpus. ACBr: the canonical source is SourceForge SVN svn://svn.code.sf.net/p/acbr/code/trunk2; the largest GitHub copy, frones/ACBr, is a git-svn mirror last pushed 2025-08-03 (stale, 183 stars); the Projeto-ACBr-Oficial GitHub org holds only SDKs (acbrapi-sdk-*), n8n, TEF and FPDF-Pascal, not the core. The ACBrNFe units pull ACBrComum, ACBrDFe and the OpenSSL bindings, so the fetch is an svn export of those folders into its own folder; no svn client on this machine (scoop install svn first). Order unchanged: steps 1-2 (Delphi compile of the generated modules) before any fetch.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 8u32, "2026-10-25T07:44Z", "fiscal", "03:44 fiscal: svn client installed (scoop main/sliksvn 1.14.5, the current 1.14 LTS line). ACBr trunk2 mapped with svn list only (no code fetched): svn://svn.code.sf.net/p/acbr/code/trunk2/Fontes holds ACBrDFe (ACBrNFe, ACBrCTe, ACBrMDFe, ACBrBPe, ACBrDCe, ... plus the shared ACBrDFe*.pas units and the reform units ACBrDFe.RTC.Classes/XmlReader/XmlWriter for IBS/CBS), next to ACBrComum, PCNComum, ACBrOpenSSL, ACBrLibXML2, ACBrTCP and Terceiros. Step-3 export set: Fontes/ACBrDFe/{ACBrNFe,ACBrCTe,ACBrMDFe} + Fontes/ACBrDFe/*.pas + Fontes/{ACBrComum,PCNComum,ACBrOpenSSL,ACBrLibXML2}, svn export into its own new folder (untrusted-download rule), never compiled from inside it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 9u32, "2026-10-25T16:33Z", "main", "10-25 12:33 main: n8's two unverified points, answered by reading codegenDelphi (no compile). (1) Every Delphi program has 'uses SysUtils, Math;' (spiral_compiler.fs:165652), so FileExists resolves. (2) string = AnsiString (:165196), StringLength = Length(s), bytes (:165475), StringIndex emits s[i + 1] (:165493), i.e. 0-based in Spiral and +1 in the output; fiscal's delphi_byte_at adds the 1 once in Spiral, which is consistent. Remaining risk for step 1: FPC {H+} with no {codepage} keeps bytes raw, so step 1's round-trip gate compares bytes. Sent to fiscal.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 10u32, "2026-10-25T16:34Z", "fiscal", "12:4x fiscal: step-1 reach survey, static (no compile). (1) The n6 open questions are answered from codegenDelphi, and main confirmed them independently: every program has uses SysUtils, Math (spiral_compiler.fs:165652), strings are AnsiString under {$H+} (:165196) and byte-indexed (StringSlice :165255). The xml-delphi-arms draft still dry-runs on xml.spi 9980B7ACD658A591. (2) A generated module calls only xml.*, listm, sm'.length, env.get_environment_variable and file_system.{write_all_text, get_current_directory, find_parent} (census over generated_ksef_fa_3). Scanning those lib run_target blocks (session scratchpad delphi-survey/arms.py) finds more Delphi gaps than xml. Silent ones: write_all_text's _ arm is () and read_all_text/get_current_directory return null, so on Delphi the example document would not be written and .NET validation would have nothing to check. Hard ones: env.get_environment_variable has no Delphi arm; sm'.substring's fallback is .NET text (!str.Substring), and xml.find_from goes through it; find_parent's error message is an F# interpolation macro ($'$\"...{!name}...\"'), which only the Python codegen rewrites (:177895). (3) Drafted as lib slice delphi-arms/apply.py (bases sm' 2E259892F464E82A, env 8A982F53CB26F7F8, file_system 7DB84A4BBD4E158C; base-hash pinned, all-or-nothing, dry run ok):\n- Copy(str, start+1, len), GetEnvironmentVariable, GetCurrentDir(), DirectoryExists, FileExists;\n- directory_get_parent via ExtractFileDir(ExcludeTrailingPathDelimiter), mirroring the TypeScript arm;\n- write/read through one global helper each, using an untyped File + BlockWrite/BlockRead, so bytes stay raw (no TextFile codepage conversion; main's point: compare the round trip as bytes);\n- find_parent's message built with ++# (same text, portable to every backend).\nRule for step 1, fixed now: land xml-delphi-arms + delphi-arms together only after one generated module (generated_mdfe_v1_00, the smallest) compiles with --backend Delphi, builds with fpc, writes its example, and that example (a) is byte-identical to the Rust run's example and (b) validates with 0 .NET messages. Any compile error in a lib arm is fixed in the slice first. Step 1 needs a compile slot, so it queues after the XSD-SLICES land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 11u32, "2026-10-25T16:41Z", "fiscal", "12:5x fiscal: delphi-arms reshaped per main's granular-style review (GRANULAR-HEAL: a global Pascal helper with a body is the rust_global pattern). write_all_text's Delphi arm is now single host calls sequenced in Spiral: FileCreate(path) -> handle : i64; failwith on -1; length via sm'.length; FileWrite(handle, text[first], length) with first = 1 computed in Spiral and a short-write failwith; FileClose(handle). That is the SysUtils handle API, not AssignFile/BlockWrite, because an untyped File value cannot be created by codegen's v := expr (file types are not assignable in Pascal) and AssignFile/Rewrite take it as var. The bytes stay raw. read_all_text has no Delphi arm now: FileRead needs a by-reference buffer, filed as DELPHI-FILE-READ-BUFFER; generated modules never read files. The slice has 0 global; format --check on a patched copy shows only the 3 over-120 lines the tree already has (file_system 286, 299, 793 -> 801).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 12u32, "2026-10-25T16:44Z", "fiscal", "12:5x fiscal: step-1 probe staged as session scratchpad delphi-step1.ps1 [-Module generated_mdfe_v1_00 -Schema MDFe.AppTeste/Schemas/mdfe_v1.00.xsd]. It copies the tree lib to <work>\\lib and applies xml-delphi-arms + delphi-arms there, then positive-controls that the 4 patched files carry their Delphi arms. It places the module under <work>\\fiscal\\generated\\<m> (deps holds only a corpus junction, and it refuses if deps\\spiral exists, so Cells' ancestor walk resolves the patched lib), retargets the module's single ///> rust test header to ///> delphi (Cells builds it with scoop fpc), and runs it with FISCAL_ROOT=<work>\\fiscal. Then it byte-compares the written example with fiscal/samples' Rust example and validates it with scripts/validate-example.ps1 against the official XSD. Queue condition: after the XSD-SLICES land and the full fiscal run, which regenerates generated/<m> (today only generated_ksef_fa_3 is on disk) and a fresh Rust example.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 13u32, "2026-10-25T17:28Z", "fiscal", "13:3x fiscal: step-1 reach made exact (still static, no compile). The first survey read only run_target blocks; backend_switch blocks matter too, because a non-unit backend_switch with no Delphi key emits the identifier backend_switch_has_no_Delphi_arm_in_lib_spiral (lib backend.spi:46), which fpc rejects, and a unit one emits '' (silently nothing). New tool, session scratchpad delphi-survey/reach.py <generated .spi> <lib dir>: a call-graph BFS from the module's calls over lib definitions that follows only what Delphi specializes (the Delphi arm, else _, of a run_target; the Delphi key of a backend_switch). On generated_ksef_fa_3 it found 3 more gaps: unicode.code_point_count (xml.code_point_count, 54 calls; Gleam/Rust/Zig only); sm'.index_of (xml.local_name <- with_namespace); sm'.replace (xml.escape_text_xml <- write_node). It also found 4 optionm' functions, all through find_parent: option' is a host-boxed option whose option'_switch has no Delphi type. Also fixed in my own draft: its directory_get_parent Delphi arm built option' via optionm'.box and would have failed. Slice changes:\n- xml-delphi-arms: code_point_count gains run_target Delphi -> delphi_code_points_from (counts lead bytes in Spiral with the draft's utf8_width_of);\n- delphi-arms: index_of Delphi = conv (portable_index_of search s), the C arm's pure-Spiral path over the StringLength/StringIndex builtins; replace Delphi = StringReplace(!s, !old, !new, [rfReplaceAll]), one call;\n- new file_system.directory_parent (path) : option string (Delphi: ExtractFileDir in Spiral option; _: directory_get_parent |> optionm'.unbox), used by find_parent, so option' never reaches Delphi; the directory_get_parent arm is dropped.\nResult on a patched lib model: 45 definitions reached, 0 without a Delphi path; positive control on the tree lib: 14. Not seen statically: the |core- package (listm) and codegen intrinsics, which the step-1 compile covers. The smoke notebook in delphi-step1.ps1 now also checks index_of on UTF-8 bytes and a miss, replace on every occurrence, and local_name.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 14u32, "2026-10-25T18:12Z", "fiscal", "14:2x fiscal: step-3 benchmark design, written before any fetch or measurement (rules fixed now).\nCorpus: the 13 BR example documents that fiscal's build writes to samples/ (NF-e 2.00/3.10/4.00, CT-e 2.00/3.00/4.00, CT-e OS 3.00/4.00, CT-e Simp 4.00, GTV-e 3.00/4.00, MDF-e 1.00/3.00). Each library is measured only on the layouts it supports, and a row says 'unsupported' instead of being dropped.\nOperations per document: parse (XML text -> the library's model), validate, serialize (model -> XML text).\nReferee: .NET XmlSchemaSet over the OFFICIAL XSDs in deps/corpus (scripts/validate-example.ps1), not any library's own validator. ACBr ships modified schemas (its tiposBasico was changed to work with OpenSSL, per the ACBr forum), and its Validar expects a signed NF-e.\nAgreement rules: (A1) every library parses every supported document; (A2) each library's serialize(parse(doc)) is canonically equal to doc (C14N, whitespace-insensitive), else the differing paths are listed; (A3) each validator's verdict equals the referee's, and a validator that refuses unsigned documents is reported as such, not as a disagreement.\nSpeed rule: per document and operation, 5 warm-up runs, then the median of 31, single thread, in one test-suite window on this machine, reported for ours on Rust, ours on Delphi (fpc), ACBr (fpc, the same toolchain as ours) and DFe.NET (.NET release build). No winner claim without A1-A3 holding for that row.\nHarness language: ours is Spiral. ACBr's is Spiral compiled to Delphi calling ACBr through one-call macros, which needs DELPHI-USES-UNITS (filed); until then, a thin Pascal program, recorded as a stopgap. DFe.NET's API (deserialize/serialize entry points; FuncoesXml in DFe.Utils is the expected home) is read from the source after the fetch; a web search did not confirm it.\nSources: ACBr forum threads on LoadFromString, Validar (signature, schemas folder) and GerarXml: https://www.projetoacbr.com.br/forum/topic/17751-validar-assinar-e-gerarnfe/ , https://www.projetoacbr.com.br/forum/tags/loadstring/ , https://www.projetoacbr.com.br/forum/topic/36956-erro-ao-enviar-xml-para-homologa%C3%A7%C3%A3o/")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 15u32, "2026-10-25T18:15Z", "fiscal", "14:2x fiscal: rule revision, recorded before acting. Note 03:34's 'steps 1-2 before any fetch' rested on main's 10-21 reason (SEFAZ variant 3 changes the generated modules first). That reason is gone: the generated modules' shape has no bearing on ACBr's or DFe.NET's API, and the step-3 design (n14) needs their real entry points. New rule: exploration fetches are allowed now, read-only. Each goes into its own new folder under the session scratchpad (untrusted-download rule); nothing from them is built or executed; only .pas/.cs text is read. Scope: ACBr trunk2 Fontes/ACBrDFe/ACBrNFe via svn export; DFe.NET's DFe.Utils + NFe.Classes via a blobless sparse git clone. The reproducible fetch into deps/ (an init.ps1 step, with CI cost considered) is decided after step 1, as before.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 16u32, "2026-10-25T18:17Z", "fiscal", "14:3x fiscal: step-3 APIs read from source (exploration fetches, read-only, nothing built or run).\nDFe.NET (commit 08743cd, 2026-09-24; blobless sparse clone at session scratchpad fetch-dfe-net-141515):\n- parse: DFe.Utils FuncoesXml.XmlStringParaClasse<T>(string xml, bool ignorarOrdenacaoElementos = false), an XmlSerializer cached per type, so the first call per type pays the build and the warm-up runs absorb it. T = NFe.Classes.NFe, whose [XmlRoot(Namespace = \"http://www.portalfiscal.inf.br/nfe\")] matches our examples' root.\n- serialize: FuncoesXml.ClasseParaXmlString<T>(T), which serializes, reloads through XElement, strips xsd/xsi attributes and re-parses; that double parse is timed as-is.\n- validate: NFe.Utils.Validacao.Validador.Valida(ServicoNFe, VersaoServico, string xml, bool validarLote, string pathSchema) : string[]. It builds a new XmlSchemaSet and loads the schema file on every call, and it suppresses two known official-schema defects (hashTentativaEntrega length; tcOrgaoIBGE declared twice), so a verdict that differs from the raw-XSD referee only there is an A3 exception, not a disagreement.\nACBr (trunk2 r48801, last changed 2026-10-23; svn export of Fontes/ACBrDFe/ACBrNFe, 60 units, at fetch-acbr-141640):\n- parse: TNotasFiscais.LoadFromString(const AXMLString: String; AGerarNFe: Boolean = False): Boolean.\n- serialize: NotaFiscal.GerarXML: String.\n- validate: NotaFiscal.Validar, a procedure that raises EACBrNFeException on failure. It validates the signed XML or else XMLOriginal, so unsigned documents ARE validated (corrects n14's 'expects a signed NF-e', which came from a forum flow), through SSL.Validar(xml, GerarNomeArqSchema(layout, version), Erro), i.e. the configured XML library, libxml2 under FPC.\n- extra: ValidarRegrasdeNegocios(out Erros): Boolean, SEFAZ business rules beyond the XSD, which no other library here has (reported as its own row, never compared).\nRule refinement for n14: both libraries get their schema folder pointed at the official XSDs in deps/corpus (ACBr Configuracoes.Arquivos.PathSchemas; DFe.NET pathSchema), so each validator is compared on the same schemas as the referee. ACBr also needs libxml2 (and the OpenSSL DLLs its SSL layer loads), recorded as a step-3 toolchain prerequisite.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 17u32, "2026-10-25T18:21Z", "fiscal", "14:4x fiscal: ACBr build closure for step 3, static (session scratchpad delphi-survey/uses_closure.py <tree> <root unit>: uses-clause BFS from a root unit, comments stripped; {$IFDEF} branches are NOT evaluated, so every conditional branch counts and the external list over-approximates). From ACBrNFe over Fontes/ACBrDFe/ACBrNFe alone: 28 of 60 units reached; the 60 also hold DANFE/report units (Fortes RL*, FastReport frx*, LazReport LR_*, Qt, FMX) that the root never reaches, so the benchmark compiles no printing code. A second read-only export (47 s) added Fontes/{ACBrComum, PCNComum, ACBrIntegrador, ACBrOpenSSL, ACBrLibXML2, ACBrDFe top-level files + Comum + small DF-e folders, Terceiros/synalist, Terceiros/LibXmlSec}: 270 units, 107 reached. Still outside, ACBr/third-party: ACBrValidador, ACBrIBGE, ACBrMail and ACBrWin{HTTP,INet}ReqResp/ACBrWinReqRespClass (expected in ACBrDiversos/ACBrTCP); ACBr_WinCrypt/BCrypt/NCrypt, ACBrCAPICOM_TLB, ACBrMSXML2_TLB (Windows crypto/COM, expected in ACBrCapicom, used by the non-OpenSSL SSL back ends); Terceiros ZLibExGZ/GZIPUtils, JsonDataObjects (JsonDataObjects_ACBr), json4delphi (Jsons), FastStringReplace (StrUtilsEx). The rest is platform-conditional (Posix.*, Libc, FMX.*, System.Net.*, System.Generics.* for Delphi; FPC's own Registry, WinInet, Dos, LConvEncoding, ctypes). Next, when step 3 builds: export ACBrDiversos, ACBrTCP, ACBrCapicom and those 5 Terceiros folders, then let fpc -vu name what is really missing under {$mode delphi} on win64. The static list is only the starting set.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 18u32, "2026-10-25T22:07Z", "fiscal", "19:0x fiscal: first real Delphi build of the lib arms, on the remote kit worker node (FPC 3.3.1-21298, core guard ok). The Spiral side went through: type check, partial evaluation and Delphi codegen of the smoke with xml-delphi-arms + delphi-arms applied. fpc then rejected one line: a COMPILER codegen gap (StringIndex on a one-character literal emits 'z'[i]; Pascal treats a one-char literal as Char), not a lib-arm bug. It is filed with a fix draft as DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX. The literal comes from the smoke's own sm'.index_of \"z\" ..., inlined through portable_index_of. A first hypothesis (parenthesized indexing (s)[i] in my macros) was tested with fpc and FALSIFIED (it compiles and runs); the real line was captured during a rerun by a watcher, because Cells deletes its temp folder. Next: re-run the smoke once the fix is packed and installed, or now with a variable search argument in place of the literal to get past this line and find the next gap.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 19u32, "2026-10-25T22:20Z", "fiscal", "19:1x fiscal: Delphi probing on the node, 3 more rounds (FPC 3.3.1-21298; each failing main.pas line captured by a watcher during the run).\n(1) With the smoke's 1-char literal made runtime (:= ~needle = \"z\"), the next failure was the SAME gap inside lib: xml.local_name's sm'.index_of \":\" name emits ':'[v1 + 1]. Every generated module reaches it through with_namespace, so DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX is a hard prerequisite for any generated module on Delphi; main has it staged for pack 5n.\n(2) With local_name dropped from the probe copy only, the next failure was backend_switch_has_no_Delphi_arm_in_lib_spiral in file_system's (</>) path join: sm'.ends_with (for \"/\" and \"\\\") had no Delphi key, and EOIE-BACKEND-REACH's prototype missed it because it does not resolve operator definitions like (</>). Fixed in the delphi-arms slice: sm'.ends_with / starts_with gain Delphi arms through new portable_ends_with / portable_starts_with, which the C arms now share (inline, so C output stays identical); dry run ok, format-clean.\n(3) Probing further is gated: (</>) indexes the literal \"/\", which is the literal-index gap again, and lib indexes one-char literals on many paths. Rule, fixed now: resume the smoke when pack 5n (DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX) is installed, then run the full generated_mdfe_v1_00 module (delphi-step1.ps1); every new gap is fixed in the slice and re-run.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 20u32, "2026-10-25T23:32Z", "fiscal", "ACBr step-3 build closure completed statically (2026-10-25 19:32, ACBr svn r48801, session scratchpad fetch-acbr-141640 + delphi-survey/uses_closure.py). Note 18's remaining folders (ACBrDiversos, ACBrTCP, ACBrCapicom, Terceiros ZLibExGZ/GZIPUtils/JsonDataObjects/json4delphi/FastStringReplace) were already exported; the 6 Windows crypto/COM units were not in ACBrCapicom but in Terceiros/Ole (ACBrCAPICOM_TLB, ACBrMSXML2_TLB) and Terceiros/CodeGear (ACBr_WinCrypt, ACBr_BCrypt, ACBr_NCrypt, ACBr_WinHttp), now exported. From ACBrNFe: 137 of 351 local units reached; ZERO ACBr or Terceiros units remain outside the export. What is left outside is only platform/toolchain units (Posix.*, FMX.*, Libc, QDialogs, System.Generics.*/System.Net.* for Delphi; Dos, Registry, WinInet, Sockets, ctypes, UnixUtil for FPC). New prerequisite found: under {$IfDef FPC} the core ACBrUtil.* units (Base, Strings, FilesIO, DateTime, Math, Compatibilidade, ACBrUtil) unconditionally use LazUTF8, LConvEncoding and LCLType, which are Lazarus units (LazUtils + LCL), not FPC; the closure script's RTL filter hid LazUTF8/LCLType, so this was invisible in note 18. Plain FPC 3.3.1 has 0 of them and no Lazarus is installed, so step 3 needs Lazarus sources (lazutils + lcl/lcltype) on the fpc unit path, or a Lazarus install, as a toolchain prerequisite next to libxml2/OpenSSL. Next for step 3, still CPU-light: fetch Lazarus sources matching FPC 3.3.1 (trunk) and check whether lcltype compiles standalone without the rest of the LCL.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 21u32, "2026-10-25T23:36Z", "fiscal", "Lazarus prerequisite sized (2026-10-25 19:36): it is 7 units, not a Lazarus install. Sparse clone of gitlab.com/freepascal.org/lazarus/lazarus at ebadd0b (2026-10-24), components/lazutils + lcl only (673 units, 72 s; session scratchpad fetch-lazarus-193304). uses_closure.py now indexes .pp as well as .pas (Lazarus names units .pp; ACBrNFe closure unchanged at 137, a positive control). Closures: LCLType -> lcltype + wsreferences (its UTF8BIDI use is under {$IFDEF USE_UTF8BIDI_LCL}, off by default); LazUTF8 -> lazutf8 + fpcadds; LConvEncoding -> lconvencoding + lazutf8 + fpcadds + codepagesasian + codepagescommon. Everything else they reference is FPC itself (Classes, SysUtils, StrUtils, Windows, dos, System.UITypes) or Unix-only and platform-conditional (cwstring, iconvenc). So step 3's ACBr build on FPC 3.3.1 win64 = ACBr r48801 export (137 units reached from ACBrNFe) + these 7 Lazarus units via -Fu/-Fi on lazutils and lcl, + libxml2 and OpenSSL DLLs at run time. Still static: fpc -vu on the real build decides; no compile run here.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 22u32, "2026-10-25T23:42Z", "fiscal", "DFe.NET step-3 harness drafted, unbuilt (2026-10-25 19:42; session scratchpad bench-dfe-net/{Bench.csproj,Program.cs}). Build closure read from the csproj files (sparse cone widened, read-only, still commit 08743cd): NFe.Utils -> NFe.Classes -> DFe.Utils -> DFe.Classes, all net462;netstandard2.0;net6.0, one package System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 6.0.1; the harness targets net11.0 and pins the references to their net6.0 build. Types: DFe.Utils.FuncoesXml, NFe.Classes.NFe, NFe.Classes.Servicos.Tipos.ServicoNFe, DFe.Classes.Flags.VersaoServico (Versao100/200/300/310/400), NFe.Utils.Validacao.Validador. Harness: Bench <official schema folder> <out.tsv> <documents...>; per document parse (XmlStringParaClasse<NFe>), serialize (ClasseParaXmlString) and validate (Valida(NFeAutorizacao, version, xml, validarLote: false, schemas)), each 5 warm-ups + median of 31 single-threaded Stopwatch runs (n14's speed rule); A2 verdict = XNode.DeepEquals after dropping namespace declarations and trimming text (prefix placement differs by serializer); version from infNFe/@versao. Validador maps only 3.10/4.00 to a schema file (any other version falls back to nfe_v3.10.xsd), so v2.00 validation is reported 'unsupported', never measured against the wrong schema (n14: rows say unsupported instead of being dropped). Not built: n13 forbids building/executing fetched code before the deps/ fetch decision after step 1. CT-e/MDF-e rows need CTe.Classes/MDFe.Classes + Utils in the cone (same pattern). Next draft: the ACBr stopgap Pascal harness (LoadFromString / GerarXML / Validar) on the same TSV shape.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 23u32, "2026-10-25T23:48Z", "fiscal", "ACBr stopgap harness drafted + one shared A2 comparer, proven on controls (2026-10-25 19:48). (1) session scratchpad bench-acbr/bench_acbr.lpr (n14's stopgap until DELPHI-USES-UNITS lets Spiral drive ACBr): FPC {$mode delphi} + modeswitches functionreferences/anonymousfunctions (FPC 3.3); names read from the r48801 export: TACBrNFe.Create(nil); Configuracoes.Geral.SSLLib := libOpenSSL and SSLXmlSignLib := xsLibXml2 set EXPLICITLY, because libOpenSSL defaults to xsXmlSec unless DFE_SEM_XMLSEC (ACBrDFeConfiguracoes.pas:630-640), so n15's 'libxml2 under FPC' only holds when set; Configuracoes.Arquivos.PathSchemas := the official XSD folder (n15 rule); Configuracoes.Geral.VersaoDF from infNFe/@versao (TpcnVersaoDF = ve200/ve300/ve310/ve400, so ACBr covers 2.00 where DFe.NET's validator does not); parse = NotasFiscais.Clear + LoadFromString, serialize = NotasFiscais[0].GerarXML, validate = NotasFiscais[0].Validar with EACBrNFeException -> invalid; QueryPerformanceCounter, 5 warm-ups + median of 31; same TSV columns as the DFe.NET harness. Not built (n13). (2) A2 is ONE method for every library (one record per fact): both harnesses write their serialized output as <library>-<document> next to the TSV, and bench-compare/compare-roundtrip.ps1 -Documents -Written -Out compares each to its source after dropping namespace declarations and trimming text, reporting the first differing path; the DFe.NET harness's inline comparison was removed. Controls on samples/generated_nfe_v3_10_example.xml: identical copy -> roundtrip-equal; cNF changed -> roundtrip-differs at /NFe/infNFe/ide/cNF: text '00000000' vs '99999999'. Two PowerShell traps hit and fixed on the way: '-split, 2' comma precedence, and a foreach variable $written shadowing the [string] parameter $Written (case-insensitive names coerce each FileInfo to a string).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 24u32, "2026-10-26T16:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:07 fiscal: DFe.NET harness extended from NF-e only to all 13 BR documents (session scratchpad bench-dfe-net/{Program.cs,Bench.csproj}; still unbuilt per n13). Sparse cone widened read-only (still commit 08743cd): CTe.Classes (274 .cs), CTe.Utils (27), MDFe.Classes (124), MDFe.Utils (4), DFe.Wsdl (28). The build closure is complete inside the cone: CTe.Utils -> CTe.Classes -> DFe.Classes/DFe.Utils; MDFe.Classes -> MDFe.Utils -> DFe.Classes/DFe.Utils/DFe.Wsdl (System.Net.Http 4.3.4)/NFe.Utils; all net462;netstandard2.0;net6.0. Dispatch is on the root element; the version comes from the first inf* element with @versao (checked on all 13 samples). Roots: NFe -> NFe.Classes.NFe; CTe -> CTe.Classes.CTe; CTeOS -> CTe.CTeOSClasses.CTeOS; CTeSimp -> CTe.Classes.Simplificado.cteSimp (XmlRoot 'CTeSimp'); MDFe -> MDFe.Classes.Informacoes.MDFe. GTVe has no DFe.NET class, so its rows read 'unsupported:GTVe' for all three operations (n14: rows say unsupported). Validators: CT-e and MDF-e are 'Valida(string xml, string schemaFile, config)', which returns void and THROWS on the first ValidationEventArgs, warnings included. So their A3 verdict is 'no exception' plus the last message line, and a warning-only throw is an A3 exception class, not a disagreement. The CT-e config is new ConfiguracaoServico { DiretorioSchemas, VersaoLayout = versao.ve200/ve300/ve400 }; the MDF-e config is new MDFeConfiguracao { CaminhoSchemas }. Schema files follow family-gates' names (cte_v*, cteOS_v*, cteSimp_v4.00, mdfe_v*), under each family's own official folder; the first argument is now the deps/corpus root (NFe.AppTeste/Schemas, CTe.AppTeste/schemas, MDFe.AppTeste/Schemas). Trap found by reading: MDFeIde formats from the GLOBAL MDFeConfiguracao.Instancia.VersaoWebService.VersaoLayout unless given a version, so the harness sets it per document (1.00 / 3.00) before parse and serialize are timed. CT-e classes have no global-version hooks (0 Instancia.Versao uses). The three Validador classes share a name, so they are fully qualified. Coverage: parse + serialize for 11 of 13 documents; validate for 10 (NF-e 2.00 is unsupported in DFe.NET's validator; GTV-e x2 is unsupported).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 25u32, "2026-10-26T16:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:12 fiscal: ACBr stopgap harness extended from NF-e only to all 13 BR documents (session scratchpad bench-acbr/bench_acbr.lpr; unbuilt per n13). New read-only svn export at r48801 (same revision as ACBrNFe): Fontes/ACBrDFe/ACBrCTe (39 units) + ACBrMDFe (37) in the session scratchpad fetch-acbr-ctemdfe-120817. APIs read from source: TACBrCTe.Conhecimentos (LoadFromString / Items[0].GerarXML / Validar), TModeloCTe = (moCTe, moGTVe, moCTeOS, moCTeSimp), TVersaoCTe = (ve200, ve300, ve400); TACBrMDFe.Manifestos (same three calls), TVersaoMDFe = (ve100, ve300). Coverage beats DFe.NET: ACBr models GTV-e (modelo 64), so ACBr has 13 of 13 documents for parse / serialize / validate, against DFe.NET's 11 / 11 / 10. Traps read in the source: (a) CT-e GerarXML writes with the CONFIGURED Geral.VersaoDF (ACBrCTeConhecimentos.pas:742), while Validar picks its schema from the document (infCTe.Versao); so the harness sets VersaoDF AND ModeloDF per document before timing; (b) MDF-e's writer takes VersaoDF from the document itself (pmdfeMDFeW.pas:187), but it is set anyway for symmetry; (c) LoadFromString detects the model by the closing tag ('</CTeOS>', '</GTVe>', '</CTeSimp>', else CTe), and the harness dispatches the same way (longer tags first); (d) ve200 / ve300 / ve400 exist in several units, so values are type-qualified (TVersaoCTe.ve200), and TVersaoCTe / TModeloCTe are declared twice (ACBrCTe.Conversao, new, and pcteConversaoCTe, old PCN), so which one Configuracoes.Geral uses is settled at the first build. Each family's component gets the same explicit SSLLib libOpenSSL + SSLXmlSignLib xsLibXml2 and its own official schema folder (the first argument is now the deps/corpus root, matching the DFe.NET harness). The A2 comparer (bench-compare) is unchanged: it already takes any <library>-<document> output.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 26u32, "2026-10-26T16:52Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:52 fiscal: 'ours' row of step 3, designed from the generated API (read on generated_cfdi_v4_0, unbuilt). A generated module has no whole-document validator: its reader x_<root>_of_xml turns constrained strings into validated nominals through the per-type x_<t>_is_valid checks, and its writer is x_<root>_attributes / x_<root>_children -> xml.element -> xml.write_node (the same path its own *_writes_its_example test uses). So for ours, parse = xml.read_xml + x_<root>_of_xml; serialize = the writer path; 'validate' = the reader's verdict. It is reported as 'reader-checked (facets + structure the reader enforces)', NOT as an XSD validator, so A3 compares it to the referee only where those checks reach (no false claim of full content-model validation). Shape: one bench driver per family under fiscal bench/ (a separate package importing one generated module), so the generated modules and their identity gates stay unchanged; the same TSV columns; A2 through bench-compare like the other libraries. Timing gap found in lib: benchmark.run' uses am'.parallel_map (breaks n14's single-thread rule) and millisecond resolution (sub-ms parses would read 0), and date_time has only stopwatch_elapsed_milliseconds. Drafted the lib fix (session scratchpad bench-ours/micros_transform.py -> draft date_time.spi EF51C8C9 over 6D530E6A): stopwatch_elapsed_microseconds, Rust as_secs + subsec_micros with arithmetic in Spiral (granular), fallback Elapsed.Ticks / 10 (TimeSpan 100 ns ticks, not the frequency-dependent ElapsedTicks); test stopwatch_microseconds_agree_with_milliseconds (non-negative, monotone, the floor-ms reading never ahead of a later us reading); 0 shadow clashes. The Delphi row also needs a stopwatch Delphi arm (stopwatch has no Delphi key, so backend_switch would emit the no-Delphi-arm identifier), which goes into the delphi-arms slice when step 1 resumes. Proof: date_time suite on the node when a slot frees.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 27u32, "2026-10-26T16:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 12:54 fiscal: ours-row driver shape refined after reading the entry points (generated_cfdi_v4_0: 'x_comprobante_of_xml (c : xml.xml_node) : x_comprobante' and 'x_comprobante_to_xml (name : string) (x : x_comprobante) : xml.xml_node'; each generated module is its own single-file package, '///- --package . --timeout 1200000'). A separate bench package would have to import a single-file package, so the driver instead takes a scratch COPY of generated_<family>.spi and appends one '///> rust' bench test (read the sample with file_system.read_all_text; parse = xml.read_xml + x_<root>_of_xml; serialize = xml.write_node (x_<root>_to_xml '<Root>' parsed); 5 warm-ups + median of 31 via stopwatch_elapsed_microseconds; TSV rows on stdout). The repo's generated output stays byte-identical and Cells compiles the copy as usual. The reader fails hard on invalid input (on Rust, failwith panics, which Spiral cannot catch), so the 'reader-checked' verdict is measured only on documents expected valid, which all 13 corpus samples are; that limit is reported in the row. The block needs compile iterations, so it is drafted when a slot frees, together with the microseconds lib proof.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 28u32, "2026-10-26T18:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 14:26 fiscal: step-1 readiness re-checked against TODAY's lib, so the Delphi slices are ready when pack 5n installs. (1) Pins: sm' 2E259892 and env 8A982F53 unchanged; xml.spi 9980B7AC unchanged; file_system MOVED 7DB84A4B -> ACF6BC84. A per-anchor check (fiscal session scratchpad delphi-arms/anchor_check.py) shows every slice anchor, including all 6 in file_system, still matches exactly once, so the move is outside the slice's edit sites. Pin updated in delphi-arms/apply.py; its dry run is ok on 3 files. (2) Both slices applied to a temp lib copy and TYPE-CHECKED in seconds with the installed compiler ('SpiralCompiler.dll fsharp <m>.spi'; it checks every definition, including unreached arms, per the date_time control): xml exit 0, sm' exit 0, file_system exit 0. env has no entry expression (the live baseline also says 'Cannot find main'), but file_system references env. 3x and type-checked with the patched env in the same copy, so env is covered via its dependent. The slices' Spiral-side code (UTF-8 decoders, portable_index_of / starts_with / ends_with, directory_parent, find_parent's ++# message) therefore type-checks on today's lib; the Delphi arms themselves are only proven by step 1's fpc build. (3) Main's pending Nil batch on xml.spi: the xml slice has 0 anchors containing 'Nil', so it survives that landing; its remaining guard is the CRLF check. Step 1 remains: delphi-step1.ps1 after pack 5n (DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 29u32, "2026-10-26T22:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 18:12 fiscal: ours-row driver BUILT and TYPE-CHECKED without a compile slot. Generic appender (session scratchpad bench-ours/append_bench.py <generated.spi> <family> <root type> <root element> <out>) adds a top-level inl <family>_bench () plus a one-line rust test calling it, in the generated module's own dialect (inl / let rec / match, sm'.(++#) concat): read the family sample via sample_path; per iteration xml.read_xml + x_<root>_of_xml (parse) then xml.write_node (x_<root>_to_xml) (serialize), timed with date_time.stopwatch_elapsed_microseconds; 5 dyn warm-ups then 31 runs, insertion-sorted, median = element 15; serialized bytes summed into the row so neither phase is dead code; one TSV row (family, parse_us, write_us, runs, bytes) on stdout. As an ordinary definition it is checked by the fast fsharp check: appended to the 6966-line generated_cfdi_v4_0 in a lib copy carrying every landing (incl. the microsecond stopwatch), exit 0 with 0 errors after one fix (sm'.length is dim-polymorphic, so it yields i64 directly; a conv around it left a metavar, ETY-ValueRestriction). Node run queued: job-1793052770934-fiscal-bench-ours-cfdi after the UBL proof; runner bench-ours/run-bench.ps1 -Family <f> (memo off; installs the transformed date_time into the integ mirror only for the run and restores it hash-verified in finally; bench package at fiscal/bench/<f>, which build.ps1 never discovers, removed after). The date_time transform applies to the mirror's older base (2E011521) as well as live; its one over-120 line is a pre-existing Zig string on both bases.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 30u32, "2026-10-26T23:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 19:16 fiscal: FIRST OURS ROW MEASURED (job-1793052770934, node, memo off, 3/3 tests): generated_cfdi_v4_0 parse_us 416, write_us 328 (medians of 31 after 5 warm-ups, Rust, microsecond stopwatch), 17391 bytes over 31 writes = 561 bytes per document vs the 597-byte sample (the sample test adds the xmldsig namespace via xml.with_namespace; the round-trip writer writes the plain root, so compare documents namespace-normalized in A3). Mirror date_time restored hash-verified. Root map for the other 15 families derived from the generated modules themselves (reader whose underscore-free name equals x + lowercased root_type; one hit each): session scratchpad bench-ours/families.tsv (e.g. GTVe -> x_tgt_ve, FatturaElettronica -> x_fattura_elettronica_type, Invoice -> x_invoice_type). UBL's row waits on XSD-RECURSIVE-TYPE-GROUPS (its module does not compile).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 31u32, "2026-10-27T00:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 20:14 fiscal: ours rows for the other 14 families staged and queued: append_bench.py derived every one from the integ mirror's generated modules with its families.tsv root (no refusals: every family has its <root>_of_xml / _to_xml / sample_path anchors; 349 KB FatturaPA to 1.5 MB CT-e v4), pushed with run-bench-all.ps1 (one serial runner looping run-bench.ps1, memo off, date_time swapped and restored per family) as job-1793060123777-fiscal-bench-ours-all on the node after the recursive-groups proof. UBL waits on XSD-RECURSIVE-TYPE-GROUPS. Output: one TSV row per family (parse_us, write_us, runs, bytes) for the A2/A3 comparison against ACBr and DFe.NET.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 32u32, "2026-10-27T00:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-26 20:44 fiscal: Delphi step-1 blocker re-checked at the source: DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX's verified fix (note 3; anchored apply script delivered in note 4) is NOT yet in the compiler: spiral/apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs:165463 still reads the old form | StringIndex, [a;b] -> {tup a}[{tup b} + 1], exactly the line note 4 predicted; installed SpiralCompiler.dll is from 10-26 08:19. So delphi-step1.ps1 still waits on pack 5n landing that one line and installing; the ours rows (15 families, node job fiscal-bench-ours-all2) do not depend on it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 33u32, "2026-10-27T04:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 00:19 fiscal: OURS ROWS for 12 of 15 families (node job-1793060915958, Rust, memo off, medians of 31 after 5 warm-ups, microsecond stopwatch). parse_us / write_us: CFDI 4.0 344/264; CT-e v2 1634/1325, v3 1675/1330, v4 1487/1167; CT-e OS v3 1381/1117, v4 1379/1071; GTVe v3 1831/1610, v4 629/596; MDF-e v1 827/641, v3 919/698; FatturaPA 1070/804; KSeF FA(3) 1368/989. Round-trip (namespace-normalized against each family's own sample): equal for 7 (CFDI, CT-e OS v3/v4, FatturaPA, GTVe v3/v4, KSeF); 5 lose infModal/modal (CT-e v2-v4, MDF-e v1/v3) -> XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER. Not measured, 3: NF-e v2.00, v3.10 and CT-e Simp v4.00 cannot read their own examples (a choice whose alternatives can all be empty) -> XSD-CHOICE-EMPTIABLE-READER (fix drafted); UBL waits on XSD-RECURSIVE-TYPE-GROUPS. Note GTVe v4 measured much faster than v3 over the same bytes; it is a single run, so re-measure before reading anything into it. INCIDENT in my own runner, now fixed: run-bench.ps1 reused the variable name saved for the saved XML document, which overwrote the path of the date_time backup, so each family's finally 'restored' its example XML into the mirror's lib/spiral/date_time.spi (every restore line said MISMATCH). Measurements are valid (the correct date_time was installed before each run), but the mirror lib was broken from the 4th family on, which also voided the root-fallback check and rg-proof2. Repaired: mirror date_time back to 2E011521 from the copy fetched earlier, rg-proof2 stopped and its own restore run by hand from its work backup (xsd_emit C9734987, 64 generated, 16 samples), poisoned backup removed; run-bench.ps1 now names it dateTimeBackup and refuses to restore anything that is not a date_time module (control: refuses XML, accepts the real file).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 34u32, "2026-10-27T07:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 03:30 fiscal: estimate set to 390m remaining, from the open milestones in these notes: Delphi step 1 (delphi-step1.ps1 once pack 5n installs DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX, plus the fallout of the first fpc build) 120m; ACBr harness bench_acbr.lpr build + run over the 13 documents (traps in note 23: VersaoDF/ModeloDF per document, model by closing tag) 120m; DFe.NET harness Bench.csproj build + run (11 docs) 60m; ours rows re-measured after XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER lands (15 of 16 families measure today; UBL waits on XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS) 30m; A2/A3 cross-library comparison through bench-compare and the report 60m.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 35u32, "2026-10-27T07:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 03:55 fiscal: work in progress moved into the repo, unstaged, per the user's practice correction (WIP lives in its proper repo location from the start; scratch is only for throwaway proof copies). Now in fiscal/bench/ (untracked): acbr/bench_acbr.lpr (ACBr harness, 13 documents), dfe-net/Program.cs + Bench.csproj (DFe.NET harness), compare-roundtrip.ps1 (namespace-normalized round-trip comparator), ours-families.tsv (each family's generated root reader and element). Checked first: no absolute or scratch paths in any of them; moved hash-verified and removed from scratch. Kept in scratch on purpose: run-bench.ps1 / run-bench-all.ps1 (proof runners hard-wired to the node mirror). NOT moved, recorded instead: append_bench.py (adds the ours-bench function to a generated module). fiscal removed Python on purpose (FISCAL-COMMIT-HYGIENE strand 2), so the right home is the generator itself: generator.spi emits <family>_bench () into each generated module next to its example test, which also removes the per-run append step. That port is the next bench task.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 36u32, "2026-10-27T08:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:30 fiscal: append_bench.py PORTED into the generator, in the tree unstaged (fiscal/src/generator.spi; backup in the session scratchpad backups/generator-bench-20261027-0424). The generator now emits a test <module>_bench_runs into every generated module whose family has no known defect: 5 warm-up + 31 timed parse/write rounds over its own example, prints '<module> parse_us N write_us N runs 31 bytes N' (median, space-separated so no backslash escape is needed in generator strings), then writes the re-serialized document to target/bench/ours-<module>_example.xml (creating the folder) for bench/compare-roundtrip.ps1. The example test and the bench share two new helpers, example_document family value and signed_text expression, so the example test's emitted text is unchanged by construction. Checked: generator + probe type-check 0 errors on the combined lib (emptiable + xs:any + namespace drafts), no new over-120 lines, installed formatter no-op. Next: the regeneration proof shows the example tests byte-identical and every bench row present; then run-bench.ps1 / append_bench.py retire.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 37u32, "2026-10-27T09:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 05:04 fiscal: the Delphi backend arms (step-1 lib slices) are IN THE TREE, unstaged, per the user's WIP-in-repo practice: lib/spiral/sm'.spi EB31A33E, env.spi 368F9BAE, file_system.spi 749056BD. Before landing: all three slice bases had moved since 10-26 (sm' 2E259892 -> 9459C71F, env 8A982F53 -> ACFFB30C, file_system ACF6BC84 -> 9FA37D04), so the per-anchor check ran again: all 14 anchors still match exactly once. Re-pinned, applied to a fresh lib copy and type-checked with the installed compiler: sm', file_system, xml, xsd_emit, date_time 0 errors; env 0 located errors (its exit 5 is the live baseline's 'no entry expression'). No Cells reader was live (0 erl processes); backup + spiral's git diff --cached in the session scratchpad backups/delphi-arms-20261027-0503; staged diff verified unchanged; installed formatter no-op on all three. Step 1's remaining precondition is unchanged: the first fpc build of the Delphi output needs pack 5n (DELPHI-STRING-LITERAL-INDEX, still 70%, not installed: compiler of 10-26 08:19).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 38u32, "2026-10-27T09:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 05:45 fiscal: DFe.NET HARNESS MILESTONE DONE (A2/A3 rows for DFe.NET). Harness made buildable and run in the tree (fiscal/bench/dfe-net, unstaged): (1) its dependency moved out of the session scratchpad: DFe.NET library sources now live at fiscal/deps/bench/DFe.NET (ignored, like every deps/), a sparse clone PINNED at 08743cd5f5b82769a26ad9ae0093b1b0ae60c74f so bench numbers stay reproducible, and scripts/init.ps1 fetches exactly that (new deps/bench/DFe.NET block); Bench.csproj's default DfeNetRoot points there (the old default was a scratch-relative path that my 03:55 absolute-path check missed); (2) .gitignore ignores /bench/*/bin/ and /bench/*/obj/; (3) three compile fixes: ImplicitUsings, MDFe's own VersaoServico enum (alias MdfeVersion; DFe.Classes.Flags has a same-named enum), and per-document failure verdicts (parse/serialize exceptions become 'failed:<innermost message>' rows instead of killing the run). Run on this box over the 11 BR samples, 5 warm-ups + 31 timed runs, medians in us (parse / serialize / validate): CT-e OS v3 354/1026/95315; CT-e OS v4 525/1419/146971; CT-e Simp v4 200/415/144299; CT-e v2 417/1346/35220; CT-e v3 355/1193/42049; CT-e v4 341/1081/63404; MDF-e v1 205/829/11293; MDF-e v3 193/899/16363; NF-e v2 496/1492/(validation unsupported by DFe.NET); NF-e v3.10 489/1236/41541; NF-e v4 (nfe_v4_example.xml) REFUSED at parse: \"Instance validation error: '00' is not a valid value for FormaPagamento\" although the sample validates against the schema with 0 messages, so DFe.NET's enum is narrower than the XSD. ROUND TRIP (bench/compare-roundtrip.ps1, target/bench/dfe-net-roundtrip.tsv): 0 of 10 equal. Defects found: (a) CT-e v2/v3/v4 and MDF-e v1 write dhEmi '2088-02-29T20:00:00' as '2088-02-29T20:00:29': the SECONDS become the day of month (a 'dd' where 'ss' belongs), a real data change; (b) CT-e OS v3/v4 and MDF-e v3 rewrite '+00:00' to the machine's local offset ('16:00:00-04:00'): same instant, different text, so a signed document's bytes change; (c) NF-e v2/v3.10 write cMunFG '0000000' as '0' (leading zeros lost); (d) CT-e Simp v4 drops infCte's Id and versao attributes. Ours on the same documents: NF-e v2/v3.10 round-trip EQUAL; CT-e/MDF-e differ only by infModal/modal (XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER, proof queued on the node). TIMING CAVEAT: ours rows were measured on the worker node and these on the review box, so the speed comparison is not valid until both run on one box (next: run ours' generated bench tests on this box, or this harness on the node).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 39u32, "2026-10-27T09:48Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 05:50 fiscal: estimate 390m -> 330m remaining (the DFe.NET harness milestone, 60m, is done: note 38). Same-box timing queued locally as job-1793094391561-fiscal-local-bench (one serial runner, memo off): regenerate with the tree generator (its new <module>_bench_runs tests), build the 10 NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e units so ours prints its rows, then run the DFe.NET harness over the same samples IMMEDIATELY AFTER in the same job, so both libraries are measured on one box under the same load (note 38's DFe.NET numbers and the earlier ours rows came from two machines and are not comparable). It waits for a local heavy slot (both held: kit's release, main's proof). Remaining milestones: Delphi step 1 after pack 5n 120m; ACBr harness build + run 120m; the A2/A3 comparison report 60m; ours rows re-measured after xs:any lands 30m.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 40u32, "2026-10-27T10:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 06:36 fiscal: ACBr HARNESS MILESTONE DONE: built and run for the first time. (1) Sources moved out of the session scratchpad into fiscal/deps/bench (ignored): ACBr/Fontes at trunk2 r48801 (svn layout; CT-e and MDF-e exports merged under Fontes/ACBrDFe; the duplicate top-level ACBrNFe export dropped after a byte-identity check), lazarus at ebadd0b458c6 (lazutils + lcl); scripts/init.ps1 fetches both, pinned (svn export of exactly the 27 folders on disk, checked 27/27, plus the ACBrDFe root units; a sparse git checkout for Lazarus); every scratch fetch was verified file by file in deps and deleted. (2) bench/acbr/build.ps1 (new, unstaged): fpc 3.3.1 cross to win64 (-Px86_64 -Twin64: the scoop host compiler is i386 and the first build was 32-bit), -Mdelphi -O2 -dNOGUI (ACBr.inc's text-mode switch: without it the link pulled LCL widget units and failed on WSRegister* symbols, which the 10-25 static closure of 7 Lazarus units did not show), every ACBr source folder except the DANFE/DACTE/DAMDFE rendering-engine subfolders (their base report units stay, ACBrNFe needs ACBrDFeDANFeReport); output target/bench/acbr/bench_acbr.exe (3.9 MB), 96 s from clean. (3) Harness fixes: r48801 keeps TWO copies of each enum (ACBrNFe.Conversao vs pcnConversaoNFe, ACBrCTe.Conversao vs pcteConversaoCTe) and the components still take the legacy pcn/pcte ones, so the harness uses those, plus the ACBrDFe unit. Run on the review box over all 13 BR samples (GTV-e included, which DFe.NET cannot model), runtime DLLs from PATH (libxml2-2.dll from emacs 30.2 bin, OpenSSL 3 from calibre's bin; a pinned runtime folder is a follow-up): 39 rows, 55 s, medians us parse / serialize: CT-e OS v3 1060/834, v4 853/826; CT-e Simp 1581/1426; CT-e v2 1312/917, v3 1205/965, v4 1284/1137; GTV-e v3 1312/1341, v4 1511/1228; MDF-e v1 645/708, v3 688/731; NF-e v2 1604/1307, v3.10 1512/1683, v4 1567/1953. Validate: GTV-e v3/v4 valid, the other 11 invalid, with messages like NroRegEstadual '' failing [0-9]{25} although our samples validate with 0 messages: ACBr validates its OWN re-serialized document, not the input. Round trip: 0 of 13 equal, all first differing at infX/@Id, because ACBr RECOMPUTES the access key from ide fields while our synthetic examples carry an all-zeros key; that is ACBr's design, not a defect, and it masks later differences (the comparator stops at the first). Follow-ups for the A2 report: give examples a key consistent with their ide fields, or let compare-roundtrip report every difference; also pin the runtime DLLs. Same-box timing caveat (n38) applies.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 41u32, "2026-10-27T11:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:40 fiscal: the generator's bench test is PROVEN on the node (ns-proof, XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS note of this time): 15 of 16 families print '<module> parse_us N write_us N runs 31 bytes N' from their own generated test and round-trip equal; UBL waits on its compile time. append_bench.py and the scratch run-bench runners are now superseded.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 42u32, "2026-10-27T21:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:32 fiscal: from main (nil gate job-1793105884062): lib sm' show_floats and show_floats_in_python_repr_layout disagree on the Delphi target only, on the unchanged tree; flagged to the compiler lane. Relevance here: fiscal's generated codecs keep decimals as text, so they print no floats; the bench's timing output might. Check when Delphi step 1 resumes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 43u32, "2026-10-27T21:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:55 fiscal: CORRECTION to note 42: the Delphi 'show_floats' disagreement is not a float bug. The compiler lane found FPC trunk printing its banner to stdout, which Cells folded into cell output; fixed with -l- -v0w in apps/cells targets.ex:321, pending a Cells run. No impact on fiscal's generated Delphi.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_44 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 44u32, "2026-10-27T21:55Z", "main", "10-27 17:55 main: Delphi rows build 32-bit, and the 64-bit fix needs no install. The compiler lane found the cause of the 2 'delphi disagrees' sm' reds (FPC trunk printing its banner to stdout, which the Cells delphi runner captured as program output) and fixed it in apps/cells targets.ex:321 (fpc args gain -l- -v0w; build failures are still detected). The banner also said 'for i386': scoop freepascal has only bin\\i386-win32, so every Delphi row so far has been a 32-bit program. Probe (main, 17:5x): that bin also ships ppcrossx64.exe, and units\\x86_64-win64 (with rtl) is installed, so 'fpc -Px86_64 -l- -v0w p.pas' builds a 64-bit exe that prints SizeOf(Pointer)*8 = 64. So x86_64 needs only -Px86_64 in the delphi target args (Cells targets.ex) and the matrix's Delphi native step, no new install. NOT applied: it changes every Delphi row's native result (pointer width, int sizes in layouts), so it waits for accept-6 (the oracle accept now running) and for kit's 'TRAIN window closed' (no apps/cells edits until then). Then it gets its own review run (Delphi rows vs C oracle) before any accept.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_45 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 45u32, "2026-10-28T00:07Z", "main", "10-27 20:07 main: Delphi 64-bit, step 1 of 2 (Cells). apps/cells targets.ex:321 now passes -Px86_64 to fpc, so the flags are -O2 -Mdelphi -Px86_64 -l- -v0w. Proof on a scratch hello.pas printing SizeOf(Pointer), with scoop FPC's i386 driver, which uses ppcrossx64.exe and units/x86_64-win64: without the flag the PE machine is 014C and it prints 4; with it, 8664 and 8. Both builds print nothing on stdout, so the banner fix holds. targets_test.exs:43 had still expected the pre-banner-fix list [\"-O2\", \"-Mdelphi\"] and was stale. It now asserts the full list. The file's mix run is being repeated to attribute 3 failures (19/22) to before or after this edit. Step 2 is the matrix: test.ps1:754 builds Delphi rows with -O2 -Mdelphi (32-bit), so Cells and the matrix now differ in bitness. It waits on the CCMR land, which rewrites test.ps1 and must not see an edit between its two A/B runs. Then a Delphi review run against the oracle, and the apps/cells README:223 sentence ('the way the matrix builds its Delphi rows') is true again. Then the Delphi-vs-C bench on equal 64-bit footing.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_46 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 46u32, "2026-10-28T13:18Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:18 fiscal: UNBLOCKED by the compiler lane: DELPHI-64BIT is an FPC 3.3.1 x86_64 -O2 register-variable miscompile (loop_9's loop-carried state dropped across the back-edge), not Spiral; -O2 -OoNOREGVAR -Px86_64 is correct on the real main.pas (32 -O2 ref = 0, 64 -O2 = 1 bug, 64 -O2 -OoNOREGVAR = 0). Held: scratchpad recgroups\\delphi64-noregvar-apply.ps1, dry run 4/4 anchors (cells targets.ex:321 + targets_test.exs:43, matrix test.ps1, Cells README; -OoNOREGVAR on both arms). Apply after kit TRAIN3 publishes (~13:10), then rerun the 64-bit rows.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_47 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 47u32, "2026-10-28T13:22Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:22 fiscal: PLAN REVISED per main: the permanent fix is in-source (CodegenPascal prelude emits {$IFDEF CPUX86_64}{$OPTIMIZATION NOREGVAR}{$ENDIF}; 64 -O2 exits 0 with it, 1 without), riding the compiler install ~16:00. Shared configs get -Px86_64 ONLY (no -OoNOREGVAR). fiscal owns the Cells consumers: held scratchpad recgroups\\delphi64-cells-apply.ps1 (targets.ex:321, targets_test.exs:43, README:223; dry run 3/3), applied AFTER that install; the compiler lane owns test.ps1:754. Bench numbers that count are post-install; -OoNOREGVAR only in my own interim builds.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_48 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 48u32, "2026-10-29T16:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 12:30 fiscal: UNBLOCKED by pack 6b (NOREGVAR prelude installed, DELPHI-64BIT-DFA-DISAGREE n8). Cells consumer half REBUILT after the wipe as fiscal/lib-programs/cells-delphi-x64.kit (apps/cells: targets.ex:321 fpc args gain -Px86_64, targets_test.exs:43 asserts it, README:223 says it; exact one-line anchors, so other lanes' unstaged hunks in targets.ex are untouched; rehearsed). Local proof: the installed FPC trunk with Cells' exact flags plus -Px86_64 builds a PE32+ (machine 0x8664) program that runs and reports 8-byte pointers. Consumer-path proof queued: fiscal-cells-delphi64 (job-1793291482758) runs a ///> delphi test cell through lib_gate on mirror cells1029 holding the three changed files. Land through lib-guarded-do -Lib apps/cells (Cells is read by every run) once it holds. Then: the step-1 probe and the bench folders (n12-n14), still redo.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_49 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 49u32, "2026-10-29T17:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 13:26 fiscal: Cells consumer proof HOLDS: fiscal-cells-delphi64 (job-1793291482758, mirror cells1029 with the 3 changed Cells files): the ///> delphi probe cell builds with -Px86_64 and passes, 0 type errors. Land requested from main (kit's TRAIN4 window holds the slot).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_50 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 50u32, "2026-10-29T18:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 14:14 fiscal: re-proven on PACK 6b (node stage spiral-bin-1029-6b, host 9895730DAE80, core 31CC96520D6B7269), mirrors freshly synced: fiscal-6b-cells-delphi64 (mirror cells1029 + cells-delphi-x64.kit's 3 files): the ///> delphi probe cell builds -Px86_64 and passes, 0 type errors. Lands first in kit's post-TRAIN4 window (main's order: xsd_emit, schematron, then these Cells edits).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_51 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 51u32, "2026-10-29T19:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 15:28 fiscal: Cells -Px86_64 LANDED 15:19:06 (cells-delphi-x64.kit re-cut onto the current README: targets.ex ACED40C9 -> 8AC48681, test/spiral/cells/targets_test.exs F6520DFF -> 50B45E26, README.md FC6B7F7B -> 0CBDBD20), via lib-guarded-do in the 15:18 gap (no exemptions), hash equal to the pack-6b-proven copy (node stage spiral-bin-1029-6b, core 31CC96520D6B7269); main's closing document_test 22/22 over all gap lands. Byte-exact undo copies: C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\land-1029\\{m7,sch2,mod,cells64b}\\base (not git HEAD: other lanes' unstaged lib hunks). Cells now builds Delphi cells 64-bit; with pack 6b's NOREGVAR prelude the DFA miscompile is covered. Next: the step-1 probe and the bench folders (redo).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_52 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 52u32, "2026-10-30T15:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:03 fiscal: ENV PIN (tibia via main, PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n42, memory scoop-reset-flips-fpc): scoop's freepascal\\current is 3.2.2 again since the 10-30 06:2x scoop reset sweep. Any Delphi verdict for this row must pin SPIRAL_FPC to the trunk scoop\\apps\\freepascal\\3.3.1-20261025\\bin\\i386-win32\\fpc.exe, and record that path in the proof note. [UPDATE 11:04, main: the compiler lane flipped freepascal\\current back to trunk 3.3.1 (fpc -iV 3.3.1, fpc.exe 116,736 B), so unpinned runs are fine again; keep the SPIRAL_FPC pin only as a guard.]")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_53 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 53u32, "2026-10-30T22:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:45 fiscal: GROOM, redo state verified against the live lib (for step 1, n12-n13). Both 10-25 lib drafts the step-1 probe applied (xml-delphi-arms, delphi-arms) and the reach survey tool (delphi-survey/reach.py) were lost in the 10-28 wipe, and none of their content is in the lib: xml.spi has 0 Delphi arms (code_point_at/rust_first_char are Rust-only), unicode.code_point_count has Gleam/Rust/Zig only, sm'.index_of and sm'.replace have no Delphi key (Fsharp/Rust...), and optionm' has 0 Delphi mentions (the option'/find_parent path, n13). Only the Cells half survived and is LANDED (-Px86_64, 10-29 15:19). Redo order, sized by milestones: (1) re-derive the reach set for one module (generated_mdfe_v1_00) as a Spiral/PowerShell survey over Delphi-specialized arms, 60m; (2) Delphi arms for each reached gap (code_point_count, index_of, replace, code_point_at, the xml read path, option'), as a lib draft with a ///> delphi test per function, 120m; (3) the step-1 probe itself (copy the lib, retarget the module's ///> rust test to ///> delphi, byte-compare with the Rust example, validate against the official XSD), 60m. Then step 3 (bench, design n14). Not started today: the remaining window is better spent landing and verifying DIAN; next fiscal session starts at (1).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_54 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 54u32, "2026-10-30T22:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:57 fiscal: MILESTONE 1, FIRST CUT (upper bound). New survey C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\delphi\\reach.ps1 (replaces the lost reach.py): indexes every lib definition, then BFS from generated_mdfe_v1_00.spi's module.function calls and each body's calls (unqualified names resolved through the module and its :< imports), flagging any reached run_target/backend_switch with no Delphi key and no non-failing _ arm. Result: 179 reached definitions, 25 flagged: xml.code_point_at and code_point_width (Rust-only, _ fails), unicode.code_point_count and unicode_types, optionm' (map, none', default_value', of_obj, option'_types), sm'.slice / obj_to_string / from_std_string, convert.u8/u16/f32/f64/unbox, am'.to_vec, resultm.from_try, date_time.* and env.* . It is a SUPERSET: unlike n13's tool it follows calls inside every backend's arm, so date_time.to_calendar_gleam / env.os_environ are likely reached only through other backends' arms. Next refinement (the rest of milestone 1): when a body has run_target/backend_switch, follow only its Delphi arm (else _). Then milestone 2 drafts Delphi arms for the true set; the xml.code_point_* and option' gaps are certain (they match n13).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_55 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 55u32, "2026-10-30T22:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:57 fiscal: MILESTONE 1 DONE (refined): reach.ps1 now follows only the Delphi arm (else _ when there is no Delphi arm) of every run_target / backend_switch, like n13's tool. generated_mdfe_v1_00 reaches 84 lib definitions, with 13 Delphi gaps = the milestone-2 scope: xml.code_point_at, xml.code_point_width (run_target, _ fails), unicode.code_point_count, unicode.unicode_types (the XML read path; matches n13), optionm'.map, optionm'.of_obj (the option' path; matches n13), sm'.slice, sm'.obj_to_string, date_time.seconds / stopwatch / time_span (most likely the bench cell's timing), env.environ_get / os_environ (most likely fiscal_paths' FISCAL_ROOT lookup). n13's sm'.index_of / sm'.replace are no longer reached on this module. Tool: C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\delphi\\reach.ps1 -Module <generated .spi>. 60 -> 65 by the n53 milestones (60 of 240 minutes). Next: milestone 2, Delphi arms for these 13 as a lib draft with a ///> delphi test each.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_56 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 56u32, "2026-10-30T22:59Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:59 fiscal: MILESTONE 2 SCOPE CLASSIFIED (arms per gap read from the lib). Mirrorable from an existing C arm (cheap): sm'.slice (C = sm.slice s { from to }, if core sm.slice has a Delphi lowering) and sm'.obj_to_string (C = obj_to_string_c, C-specific, likely needs a Delphi formatter). Need a real Delphi design, each with a ///> delphi test: unicode.code_point_count + xml.code_point_at / code_point_width (UTF-8 stepping over the FPC string's bytes; only Rust/Zig arms today), optionm'.map / of_obj (host-boxed option' has no Delphi type, n13), date_time.seconds / stopwatch / time_span (FPC Now / GetTickCount64 or SysUtils), env.environ_get / os_environ (FPC GetEnvironmentVariable). Next session: draft these 13 arms on a lib copy, prove each with a ///> delphi cell (box FPC trunk 3.3.1), then the step-1 probe (milestone 3).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_57 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 57u32, "2026-10-30T23:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:03 fiscal: MILESTONE 1 CORRECTED, 9 true gaps (not 13). reach.ps1's arm filter missed run_target arms with a binding (| Gleam _ =>, | Cuda _ =>) and the lowercase catch-all (| target =>), so env.environ_get / os_environ (reached only through get_environment_variable's Cuda arm; that function HAS a Delphi arm, GetEnvironmentVariable) and optionm'.map / of_obj (through Fsharp/Cuda arms) were false reach. Fixed, and the survey now prints each gap's call chain. 78 reached definitions, 9 gaps, every chain on a real Delphi path: date_time.stopwatch / seconds / time_span (the bench cell's stopwatch_elapsed_microseconds), sm'.slice (sm'.trim <- xml.read_nodes <- read_xml), sm'.obj_to_string (direct), unicode.code_point_count / unicode_types (xml.code_point_count), xml.code_point_at / code_point_width (direct, run_target _ fails).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_58 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 58u32, "2026-10-30T23:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:05 fiscal: MILESTONE 2 STARTED, first 2 of 9 arms drafted: C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\delphi\\lib-draft\\sm'.spi (base A683500F -> 8113E287, 3 lines). sm'.slice gets Delphi = sm.slice s { from to } (the core primitive every other backend calls), sm'.obj_to_string gets Delphi = obj_to_string_c x (the C dispatcher over PrimToString, so integers, bools and chars, like C), and test slice_2 gains ///> delphi so FPC proves the slice arm. Proof queued after the windows clear: round trip + fiscal-box5-delphi-slice (lib_gate -Test slice_2 on scratch boxgate5, all the test's backends incl. delphi). Left: date_time.stopwatch / seconds / time_span, unicode.code_point_count / unicode_types, xml.code_point_at / code_point_width.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_59 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 59u32, "2026-10-30T23:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:33 fiscal: MILESTONE 2 ALL ARMS DRAFTED, survey at 0 gaps (C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\delphi\\lib-draft, bases = live): sm' A683500F->8113E287, unicode C9F0A794->F3E7BE24 (delphi_code_point_count_from + unicode_types gets Delphi = () like Rust, since code_point_count calls it on every backend), xml 58CA22E1->D540BC09 (delphi_code_point_at / width + test code_points_step_through_utf8), date_time 21D9AE92->BD5014E7. date_time: the backend is FPC {$mode delphi}, and FPC trunk 3.3.1 ships vcl-compat System.Diagnostics (3.2.2 does not; CI runs no Delphi). stopwatch_switch Delphi : TStopwatch; stopwatch () Delphi = global \"uses System.Diagnostics\" (spiral_compiler.fs:165800 lifts uses-globals into the uses clause) + TStopwatch.StartNew. The existing non-Rust elapsed arms (.ElapsedMilliseconds, .Elapsed.Ticks div 10) are already valid Delphi, and stopwatch_start's .Start is a no-op on a running watch. FPC probes (scratchpad fpcwatch): value-copy reads agree (467461 us vs 467 ms, IsHighResolution TRUE); Start after StartNew keeps the original start (66929 us after Sleep 50). stopwatch_microseconds_agree_with_milliseconds gains ///> delphi. seconds/time_span were survey false positives: reach.ps1 now skips locally bound names (:= x, params) except in type position; control on the live lib still lists all real gaps. Proofs: fiscal-box5-delphi-slice was VOID, not red (cell cap 300 s hit during fsharp: gleam 151 + lua 53 + fsharp 106 s; delphi not_run); run-gate.ps1 now shows 'timed out' lines. Re-proof with gate-only header --timeout 1800000 queued as fiscal-box5-delphi-r2 (slice_2 + stopwatch) after fiscal-box5-delphi-codepoints (running). Formatter: date_time draft 0 diffs.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_60 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 60u32, "2026-10-30T23:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:51 fiscal: r2 on the box (pack 8): slice_2 GREEN on every target incl delphi (gleam 286 s, lua 35, fsharp 41, cuda 51, delphi 35; gate copy B66F1FAF = draft 8113E287 + --timeout header), so sm'.slice's Delphi arm is proven and the earlier slice VOID is replaced. code_points_step_through_utf8 GREEN on rust + delphi (221 s; gate 693692F8 = draft D540BC09 + header). stopwatch_microseconds_agree_with_milliseconds: rust passed, DELPHI RED: fpc 'main.pas(26,6) Error: Invalid assignment, procedures return no value'. The applied macro $'!stopwatch.Start' () is emitted as an expression bound to a variable, and TStopwatch.Start is a procedure. Fix (date_time draft 468359D2, formatter-clean, round trip true): stopwatch_start becomes run_target with Rust and Delphi arms that do nothing (both clocks start at creation: Instant::now / TStopwatch.StartNew) and _ keeping the old .Start line, so every other backend is unchanged (is_rust was true only on Rust). Re-gate queued (fiscal-box5-delphi-stopwatch2) behind main's tree-write window.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_61 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 61u32, "2026-10-31T00:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:05 fiscal: MILESTONE 2 COMPLETE, every drafted Delphi arm proven by a ///> delphi cell on FPC trunk 3.3.1 (box, pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A; gate copies = draft + a line-1 --timeout header): slice_2 all 5 targets; code_points_step_through_utf8 rust + delphi; stopwatch_microseconds_agree_with_milliseconds rust + delphi (fiscal-box5-delphi-stopwatch2, gate C97A2307 = date_time 468359D2 + header). Drafts, all with bases = live: sm' 8113E287, unicode F3E7BE24, xml D540BC09, date_time 468359D2; all formatter-clean, all round trip true. Reach survey on the CURRENT generated unit (fetched from node mirror e3lv; the tree's generated/ copy is the stale 10-27 edition-2 output): 83 definitions, 0 Delphi gaps. 65 -> 75. MILESTONE 3 (step-1 probe) QUEUED: fiscal-box6-delphi-step1-probe runs generated_mdfe_v1_00_writes_its_example retargeted to ///> delphi (scratch boxgate6\\fiscal: lib = live + the 4 drafts) and the untouched ///> rust twin (boxgate6\\fiscal-rust); then I byte-compare the two example and parse-then-write files and validate the Delphi one against the official MDF-e 1.00 XSD. run-gate.ps1 gained -FiscalRoot. Before the land: full-module gates of xml, unicode, sm' and date_time on the drafts (only targeted tests have run so far), then lib-guarded-do.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_62 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 62u32, "2026-10-31T00:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:09 fiscal: LAND PROGRAMS BUILT and rehearsed on fresh copies of the live lib. C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\delphi\\delphi-arms.kit (4 files, 13 hunks) gives sm' 8113E287, unicode F3E7BE24, xml D540BC09, date_time 468359D2, each hash-equal to its draft. C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\xml-fidelity\\xml-xpath-fidelity.kit (2 files, 8 hunks; bases xml 58CA22E1, xpath_eval 3BCD928E = live) applies cleanly ON TOP of the Delphi program: xpath_eval CC078F4B (= draft), and the combined xml.spi is D20A5A18. Both drafts change xml.spi from the same base, so D20A5A18 (Delphi + fidelity) is the file that would actually land, and it has not been gated yet: before landing both, gate xml.spi D20A5A18 as a whole module (rust, zig, delphi rows), plus round trip and formatter.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_63 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 63u32, "2026-10-31T00:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:10 fiscal: HASH UPDATE (supersedes D540BC09 / D20A5A18 above). The formatter re-lays delphi_sequence_width (one line over 120 columns) as a two-line body; adopted, so the Delphi xml draft is E8614181 (layout only; the code-points proof ran on D540BC09). Programs rebuilt and re-rehearsed on fresh live copies: delphi-arms.kit -> xml E8614181 (= draft); then xml-xpath-fidelity.kit -> xml E8F8E8F3, xpath_eval CC078F4B. The combined xml E8F8E8F3 shows only the formatter diffs live already has (2), and its round trip on the pre-relayout combination was true. The full-module gate before landing runs on E8F8E8F3.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_64 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 64u32, "2026-10-31T00:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:50 fiscal: STEP-1 PROBE, first run (fiscal-box6-delphi-step1-probe): the Rust twin passes and writes a 952-byte example (B813E064D2E7) whose only XSD finding is the required ds:Signature (expected: the example is the Unsigned stage since XSD-SIGNING-STAGES; the 10-25 copy was 1691 B and signed). The Delphi run FAILED at compile time: 'PrimToString with 1 args not supported in the Delphi backend', reached from the bench row's sm'.obj_to_string on an i64. My milestone-2 Delphi arm (obj_to_string_c) was wrong: it lowers to the compiler primitive !!!!PrimToString, which only C implements, and the reach survey cannot see primitives (it reads backend switches). Fix (sm' draft D699E8D2, formatter-clean, round trip true, names clash with nothing): obj_to_string_delphi = IntToStr for every integer width, else obj_to_string_delphi_bool = LowerCase(BoolToStr(x, True)), else a compile-time failwith, as C does; new test obj_to_string_on_delphi_prints_ints_and_bools (42, -7, u64 max, false). Queued: fiscal-box6-delphi-step1-probe2 (that test, then the Delphi probe again, then byte-compare against B813E064 and XSD-validate). Survey follow-up: also flag !!!!Prim* uses on Delphi paths.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_65 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 65u32, "2026-10-31T02:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 22:11 fiscal: STEP-1 PROBE, runs 2-3. probe2: obj_to_string_on_delphi_prints_ints_and_bools GREEN on delphi (gate B0249838 = sm' D699E8D2 + header). The MDF-e probe then compiled through parse, write and all 31 bench runs, and stopped on the generated test's 'file_system.create_dir_all folder |> resultm.unbox' (target/bench output): create_dir_all emits Rust unconditionally (!\\\\(path, std::fs::create_dir_all)), and its result' is host-boxed (resultm.unbox's backend_switch has no Delphi key). A third gap class the survey could not see (no switch at all). Fix, the directory_parent pattern: file_system.directory_create_all (path) : result () string, Delphi = ForceDirectories, _ = create_dir_all |> map_error' sm'.format |> unbox (the live precedent, 3 uses); test directory_create_all_makes_nested_directories (rust + delphi). probe3 caught my own type error in it (format' returns std_string, not string); fixed, draft file_system E1FD77AC (base 91738A22 = live), formatter: 0 diffs of mine (24 = live's own). The probe module copy calls directory_create_all; the GENERATOR needs the same one-line change in its emitted bench test (filed for after the edition-3 commit, with the budget fix). Survey extended: it now also lists !!!!Prim* uses and Rust emit macros (!\\\\( / !\\() reached on Delphi paths, and the 'type position' check no longer treats the |: else-operator as a type colon. Positive controls: the old sm' draft lists PrimToString in obj_to_string_c; the original module lists file_system.create_dir_all; the live lib still lists all 7 real gaps. With the drafts: 0 switch gaps, 0 primitives, 0 Rust emits on 81 reached definitions. probe4 (dir test + MDF-e probe) is queued behind m4, gated on free memory >= 3 GB (box at 1.2 GB beside kit's train5).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_66 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 66u32, "2026-10-31T02:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 22:30 fiscal: generator follow-up DRAFTED in the post-edition-3 layer C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live-budget\\src\\generator.spi (now 62FDA504; base 59AD5447 = the edition-3 draft generator): its emitted bench test writes 'match file_system.directory_create_all folder with' instead of 'file_system.create_dir_all folder |> resultm.unbox', so every generated unit's bench path compiles on Delphi; the generator's own create_dir_all call (line 26, Rust-run) stays. Same layer as FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE's budget change (header 3600000, factor 48). ORDER: the Delphi lib program lands first (delphi-arms.kit adds file_system.directory_create_all), then the user's edition-3 commit, then this layer, then regeneration (the generated/ drift guard then expects the new text in all 74 units).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_67 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 67u32, "2026-10-31T04:59Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 00:59 fiscal: (1) TOOL IN THE REPO (work-in-the-repo rule): the Delphi reach survey is now fiscal/scripts/delphi-reach.ps1 (unstaged; default -Lib = the repo's deps/spiral/lib/spiral), with the primitive and Rust-emit checks and the shadowing fix; smoke on generated_mdfe_v1_00 against the live lib: 7 gaps + create_dir_all, as expected. The drafts-folder copy and a restored roundtrip-one.exs went to the archive store (scratch-archive 20261031-005850). Round trips now use the committed i574n.github/scripts/slice-roundtrip-sweep.ps1 -Files (checks the _real.spir pair too). (2) healing's recovered pre-wipe model (scratchpad delphi-lib-model, 10-25) had one arm today's lib lacks: xml.is_file Delphi = FileExists. Restored in the xml draft (D8F5F3BD) with test is_file_is_false_for_a_missing_path (rust + delphi). xml.code_point_count's old Delphi arm is superseded by unicode.code_point_count's. (3) Sweep of every pending draft (sm' D699E8D2, unicode 50D83509, xml D8F5F3BD, date_time 468359D2, file_system E1FD77AC, the combined xml BA1B4166): all ok, except sm' whose _real.spir pair differs at line 5 ('/// ## rust'). The LIVE pair fails at the same line (sm'.spi A683500F + sm'_real.spir, unchanged since 12:55 and committed 22:33), so the difference predates this work; land check = the first difference stays that one. (4) delphi-arms.kit rebuilt: 5 files, 20 replacements, each file hash-equal to its draft on a fresh live copy.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_68 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 68u32, "2026-10-31T05:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 01:14 fiscal: probe4 (Normal priority): directory_create_all_makes_nested_directories GREEN on rust + delphi (gate 16324605 = file_system E1FD77AC + header). The MDF-e probe now compiles through the WHOLE Spiral stage on Delphi and reaches FPC; one error left: 'Identifier not found backend_switch_has_no_Delphi_arm_in_cells_console' from the bench row's console.write_line. Cause: Cells mounts its own apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/console.spi for test runs, whose show_some_value / write_line have PLACEHOLDER Delphi arms (the lib's console.spi already has Writeln). apps/cells is a live shared tree in main's Cells windows, so: anchored program C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\cells-console\\cells-console-delphi.kit (2 hunks, Writeln(!value) / Writeln(!text); base A70EDFA2 = live -> 4BC11C0F, rehearsed hash-exact), sent to main to apply in its next Cells window. Survey (fiscal/scripts/delphi-reach.ps1) now reads the Cells mounts (-Mounts, default deps/spiral/apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells, overriding same-named lib modules) and reports placeholder Delphi arms ('has_no_Delphi_arm') as gaps; !!!!BackendSwitch is no longer counted as a primitive. Control: the probe module + drafts lists console.write_line as the placeholder gap; with the cells draft mounted, 0 gaps. Next: probe5 after main's apply.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_69 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 69u32, "2026-10-31T08:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 04:57 fiscal: MILESTONE 3 GREEN, first generated SEFAZ unit end to end on Delphi (job-1793436771002-fiscal-box6-delphi-step1-probe5, compiler EEBCBFF8, FPC trunk; scratch root boxgate6 = live lib + the Delphi lib drafts (sm' D699E8D2, unicode 50D83509, xml D8F5F3BD, date_time 468359D2, file_system E1FD77AC) + live Cells console.spi 4BC11C0F (main's window 6 apply8)): generated_mdfe_v1_00 retargeted ///> delphi, generated_mdfe_v1_00_writes_its_example passes, 0 type errors. The Delphi example is BYTE-EQUAL to the Rust twin's (952 B, B813E064D2E7), and so is the bench's parse+write re-emission (952 B, B813E064D2E7). XSD (validate-example.ps1, mdfe_v1.00.xsd): exactly 1 message, the missing ds:Signature, which is the Unsigned stage's expected shape and the same single finding as the Rust reference. Delphi bench row: parse_us 720 write_us 183 (median of 31, 28148 bytes), on a saturated box (100% CPU, other lanes' heavy jobs), so a provisional number. Next: the lib drafts land after the full-module gates (fiscal-box9-delphi-modules running), then a same-load Rust/Delphi bench pair on the landed lib.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_70 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 70u32, "2026-10-31T10:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 06:33 fiscal: FULL-MODULE GATES, 4 of 6 read (fiscal-box9-delphi-modules, job-1793431082691, box, compiler EEBCBFF8; scratch root boxgate9 = live lib + delphi-arms.kit + xml-xpath-fidelity.kit re-rehearsed on today's live, hash-equal to last night's targets: sm' D699E8D2, unicode 50D83509, xml BA1B4166, date_time 468359D2, file_system E1FD77AC, xpath_eval CC078F4B; gate headers --timeout 3600000). sm' 73/73 and unicode 9/9, 0 type errors. date_time 42/44... wait-free count: 43 of 44 pass, 1 red: new_guid_from_timestamp fsharp (assert actual -1 expected 0, in GUID/timestamp code the draft does not touch; the draft only adds the stopwatch Delphi arms). file_system 33/36: find_parent fsharp, find_parent_2 rust, trace_file fsharp, all VOID BY LOCATION (they walk up for a 'workspace' dir / README.md or write under get_workspace_root, absent above a scratch copy: 'No parent for dir workspace at ...boxgate9\\\\lib\\\\spiral'); the draft's directory_create_all test passes. xml and xpath_eval are running. Before the land: a control on a live-copy root at the same depth for new_guid_from_timestamp (expected to fail identically, i.e. pre-existing), then lib-guarded-do with delphi-arms.kit then xml-xpath-fidelity.kit; the guard refuses until kit's train5e heavy-build window ends (~10:40).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_71 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 71u32, "2026-10-31T10:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 06:33 fiscal: CORRECTION to n70's date_time count: the gate printed 'tests: passed 42 failed 1 of 44', so 42 passed, 1 failed (new_guid_from_timestamp fsharp) and 1 was neither (not run or skipped; to be read from date_time.txt.tests.tsv before the land), not '43 of 44 pass'.")
