inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_73 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 73u32, "2026-10-31T12:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 08:21 fiscal: DELPHI REACH beyond MDF-e 1.00 (scripts/delphi-reach.ps1 over the lib with the Delphi drafts, boxgate9): generated_nfe_v4 (115 lib definitions reached), generated_cte_v4_00 (103) and generated_mdfe_v1_00 (95) have the SAME two gaps and nothing else: 0 primitives, (1) console.write_line's placeholder Delphi arm and (2) file_system.create_dir_all's Rust emit (the generated bench line). So once both close, every BR unit's Delphi build path is clear by this survey. (1) Live console.spi is back at A70EDFA2: main's Cells window 6, which carried apply8 (4BC11C0F, the state probe5 passed on at 04:14), failed at 04:59 and was rolled back whole; per CELLS-DAEMON-RETIRE-STOP n3 window 6 is re-running as the last step of main's land queue, so apply8 returns with it (no action routed). (2) needs the Delphi lib land first (directory_create_all is in the file_system draft, not live), then the generator's bench line emits directory_create_all (drafted in the e3live-budget layer; to apply to the tree directly after the lib land, not after edition 3).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_74 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 74u32, "2026-10-31T13:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 09:24 fiscal: box9 TIMED OUT at its 6 h job cap (job-1793431082691, 21.6M ms): 4 modules done (n70-n72: sm' 73/73, unicode 9/9, date_time 42 pass + 1 unrelated red, file_system 33 pass + 3 VOID by location), then xml.spi (combined BA1B4166, header 3600000) STALLED from 06:30: its erl had 17 s of CPU in 2 h 45 min, no child process (no dotnet/rustc/fpc anywhere naming the gate), no spiral-cells-run files, no raw output; xpath_eval never started. So xml and xpath_eval are VOID, not red; the same xml module passed 12/12 on the box last night as 3300361F (fidelity only), so the stall comes with the combined draft's new cells or with the run itself. RERUN queued as the first two steps of fiscal-cr-docs-4-4 (scratch root g18 = box9's lib copy, cell cap 2 h instead of 1 h so one slow cell fits, job via fiscal/scripts/box-gate.ps1); if xml stalls again, the per-cell metrics show which cell, and that cell is split out for a direct probe.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_75 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 75u32, "2026-10-31T14:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 10:30 fiscal: RE-ANCHORED after main's LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP batches 2-3 (+ the sm' lambda land) changed 5 of the 6 base files (live now sm' 48926232, unicode 19200A0B, xml 8DCCACD5, date_time 35E23133, file_system 84642C22; xpath_eval 3BCD928E and xsd_emit 161D00F5 unchanged): the old delphi-arms.kit failed 4 of 5 file edits on live. Method: git merge-file live/base/draft per file (bases = the drafts' recorded originals) gave clean merges for sm', date_time and xml, and 3 conflicts (unicode 2, file_system 1) that were ONLY main's deleted name headings next to my inserted definitions; resolved by the cleanup's own rule: keep my code and tests, add no '/// ###' name heading (drops the 3 headings my drafts had added, so no _real.spir pairing is needed). Each new diff equals the original draft minus exactly those headings (sm' +33 vs +34, unicode +13 vs +14, file_system +14 vs +15, xml +34 and date_time +9/-2 equal). All 5 round-trip ok. fiscal/lib-programs/delphi-arms.kit rewritten (5 files, 20 replacements) and rehearsed on live, then xml-xpath-fidelity.kit on top: targets sm' E6AA294A, unicode 59CC00D7, xml 52B745FA, date_time 39148240, file_system 007096C3, xpath_eval CC078F4B. New hashes = new proof: scratch root g18 (live lib + these 6) is now what fiscal-cr-docs-4-4's xml probes + xml/xpath_eval module gates run on (so the rerun gates the real candidate, with the per-cell probes of the two new Delphi tests first), and fiscal-delphi4-reanchored gates sm', unicode, date_time, file_system after it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_76 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 76u32, "2026-10-31T14:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 10:41 fiscal: RE-ANCHOR IS NOW A TOOL (main's final heading wave 2/3 is landing and may move these bases again): i574n.github/scripts/lib-reanchor.ps1 -Base <dir of the drafts' original live files> -Draft <dir of drafts> -Out <dir> -Program <out.kit> [-DropAddedNameHeadings] runs git merge-file live/base/draft per draft .spi, auto-resolves ONLY conflicts with no live-side lines and only under the switch (dropping name headings the draft adds, the cleanup's rule), refuses anything else (exit 2, no program), writes the kit program and rehearses it on live copies (exit 3 unless every rehearsed file equals its merge). Controls on this morning's inputs: positive = the 5 merged hashes equal the hand-merged ones exactly (sm' E6AA294A, unicode 59CC00D7, date_time 39148240, file_system 007096C3, xml A82C874A) and the rehearse matches; negative = without the switch it refuses (unicode's 2 heading conflicts) with exit 2 and no program. Today's bases (live 10:2x) are snapshotted in the session scratchpad delphi-merge\\\\base for the next run. All 7 bases still equal live at 10:33.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_77 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 77u32, "2026-10-31T15:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 11:17 fiscal: second re-anchor, first use of lib-reanchor.ps1: main's final heading wave moved live unicode.spi 19200A0B -> 5EC46942; the tool merged all 5 drafts with 0 conflicts and rehearsed them equal; unicode target now E9612B84 (diff still +13/-0), the other 4 targets unchanged (sm' E6AA294A, xml A82C874A before fidelity, date_time 39148240, file_system 007096C3). fiscal/lib-programs/delphi-arms.kit replaced, the scratch base snapshot updated, and g18's unicode refreshed before fiscal-delphi4-reanchored starts, so its unicode gate runs on the new target.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_78 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 78u32, "2026-10-31T15:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 11:54 fiscal: STALL PROBES (fiscal-cr-docs-4-4, job-1793460946299, on the RE-ANCHORED candidate xml 52B745FA + gate header = 3261BA36, scratch root g18): the two cells new in the combined draft pass ALONE, each under a 30-min watchdog: is_file_is_false_for_a_missing_path (Delphi FileExists + Rust) 1/1 and code_points_step_through_utf8 (Delphi Ord/AnsiString + Rust) 1/1, 0 type errors, ~8 min each. So box9's 2 h 45 min zero-CPU stall in xml was not a hanging cell of mine; the full xml module (2 h watchdog) and xpath_eval run next in the same job, which tells whether it reproduces on the whole module. Also: my gate waiters had included test-suite, which is shareable (window-coordination); dropping it let this job and fiscal-delphi4-reanchored start at 11:35 instead of queueing behind tibia's back-to-back suites (1 h 46 min lost).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_79 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 79u32, "2026-10-31T16:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 12:15 fiscal: xml FULL MODULE GREEN on the re-anchored land candidate: xml 52B745FA (Delphi arms + XML fidelity on today's live) + gate header = 3261BA36 passes 14/14, 0 type errors, in ~20 min (11:50-12:10, fiscal-cr-docs-4-4, box, compiler EEBCBFF8). The box9 2 h 45 min stall did not reproduce, so it was a property of that run, not of the module or its two new Delphi cells (both also pass alone, n78). xpath_eval CC078F4B is running; sm', unicode, date_time, file_system run in fiscal-delphi4-reanchored.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_80 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 80u32, "2026-10-31T17:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 13:02 fiscal: PLAN for gap (2) of n73 after the Delphi lib land (land script ready: live bases checked, hash-named undo to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\kit\\\\undo, both programs via lib-guarded-do, all-or-nothing restore on any refusal or target miss, round trip after). The change is one emitted line, src/generator.spi:818 'match file_system.create_dir_all folder |> resultm.unbox with' -> 'match file_system.directory_create_all folder with' (Ok/Error arms unchanged; line 26, the generator's own Rust-run call, stays). But it rewrites the bench cell of EVERY generated unit, so all 75 committed units drift and CI's drift guard (build.ps1 regenerates then git-status generated/) needs them all regenerated in one go: generator edit + a node set-proof that regenerates every family on the landed lib + format-generated.ps1 over all units (pack 8) + the formatted units copied home, committed together. Only after that does every BR unit build on Delphi by the reach survey.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_81 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 81u32, "2026-10-31T17:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 13:34 fiscal: (a) gap (1) of n73 CLOSED: main's Cells window 6 landed 13:15 with apply8; live apps/cells console.spi = 4BC11C0F0F4D (Delphi = Writeln(!value) / Writeln(!text)), window 6 closed 50/50 (new_project_test, compiler_daemon_test, document_test). (b) fiscal-delphi4-reanchored so far: date_time 43/44 0 failed, file_system 33/36 = only the 3 location-bound rows (find_parent fsharp, find_parent_2 rust, trace_file fsharp: VOID by location as in n70) and directory_create_all_makes_nested_directories PASSES on rust AND delphi, unicode E9612B84 9/9; sm' running. Then the land script for delphi-arms.kit + xml-xpath-fidelity.kit.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_82 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 82u32, "2026-10-31T18:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 14:31 fiscal: ALL 6 TARGETS HAD VERDICTS, then live moved again before the land: the land script refused cleanly (exit 4: sm' D3FCCD79, date_time DCB02071, file_system 89493A55 moved; unicode, xml, xpath_eval unchanged; nothing written). Verdicts that stand: xml 52B745FA 14/14, xpath_eval CC078F4B 12/12, unicode E9612B84 9/9 (hashes unchanged); delphi4 also gave sm' 73/73, date_time 43/44 0 failed, file_system 33/36 = the 3 location-bound rows, for the previous targets. RE-ANCHOR 3 found a real flaw in lib-reanchor.ps1: in sm', another lane had removed '///> fsharp' from the test AFTER my inserted test; the conflict's live side was empty, so the tool kept the draft side, which still carried that base line, silently undoing their change (a file-wide 'in live?' check missed it because '///> fsharp' recurs on other tests). FIXED: merge-file --diff3, and per conflict hunk, draft lines that are in the hunk's base section but not its live section (multiset) stay deleted. Verified on all 5 files: the lines the program adds to live are exactly the draft's own added lines (sm' 33, unicode 13, xml 34, date_time 9, file_system 14; removals date_time 2, others 0). New targets sm' 24428BE3, date_time BF06A436, file_system 056F0D6C (program promoted, land script updated); their gates run now in parallel (fiscal-delphi-sm-reanchor3, fiscal-delphi-dtfs-reanchor3) on g18 = today's live + both programs.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_83 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 83u32, "2026-10-31T20:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 16:01 fiscal: RE-ANCHOR-3 VERDICTS: sm' 24428BE3 73/73, 0 type errors (fiscal-delphi-sm-reanchor3); file_system 056F0D6C 33/36 = only the 3 location-bound rows, directory_create_all passes on rust AND delphi (fiscal-delphi-dtfs-reanchor3). date_time BF06A436 gave 42/44 with new_guid_from_timestamp red on fsharp, the same row that passed at 12:24 on the same Delphi additions, so it is flaky and unrelated (another lane is retargeting those fsharp tests to rust -d chrono right now, which also moved date_time again: D9365B01, re-anchored to 5A7F4D41 with 0 conflicts and the same +9/-2); its gate (fiscal-delphi-dt-reanchor4) runs now. Current proofs held: sm', unicode, xml, xpath_eval, file_system; land script (all-or-nothing, base-checked) runs on date_time's verdict.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_84 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 84u32, "2026-10-31T20:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 16:46 fiscal: land program moved here from fiscal/lib-programs (a folder I invented; programs live in backlog notes so land-lib-program.ps1 -Note can read them): Delphi arms for sm' unicode xml date_time file_system (re-anchored 16:42 onto live sm' 94A51BB5, file_system 7F2BD058; land order: this, then xml-xpath-fidelity).\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit date_time.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -1057,6 +1057,7 @@ test add_days_moves_the_timestamp =\n     )\n :== stopwatch_switch =\n     {\n+        Delphi : $'TStopwatch'\n         Fsharp : $'System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch'\n         Python : stopwatch_python\n         Rust : $'std::time::Instant'\n@@ -1065,6 +1066,9 @@ test add_days_moves_the_timestamp =\n \n := stopwatch () : stopwatch =\n     backend_switch {\n+        Delphi = \\ () =>\n+            global \"uses System.Diagnostics\"\n+            $'TStopwatch.StartNew' : stopwatch\n         Fsharp = \\ () => $'`stopwatch ()' : stopwatch\n         Python = \\ () => $'`stopwatch ' : stopwatch\n         Rust = \\ () => $'std::time::Instant::now()' : stopwatch\n@@ -1089,8 +1093,10 @@ test add_days_moves_the_timestamp =\n         ticks / 10i64\n \n := stopwatch_start (stopwatch : stopwatch) : () =\n-    ? is_rust () |> not\n-    ?> $'!stopwatch.Start' ()\n+    run_target \\|\n+        | Rust => \\ () => ()\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => ()\n+        | _ => \\ () => $'!stopwatch.Start' ()\n \n := monotonic_milliseconds () : i64 =\n     run_target \\|\n@@ -1467,6 +1473,7 @@ test zig_date_time_is_micros_since_the_unix_epoch =\n     unix_epoch () |> add_days -1i32 |> format_iso8601 |> _assert_eq \"1969-12-31T00-00-00.000\"\n \n ///> rust\n+///> delphi\n test stopwatch_microseconds_agree_with_milliseconds =\n     := watch = stopwatch ()\n     stopwatch_start watch\n>>>\nedit file_system.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -658,6 +658,20 @@ test get_current_directory =\n             ? parent = path || parent = \"\" ?> None |: Some parent\n         | _ => \\ path => path |> directory_get_parent |> optionm'.unbox\n \n+:= directory_create_all (path : string) : result () string =\n+    run_target_args' path \\|\n+        | Delphi => \\ path =>\n+            ? $'ForceDirectories(!path)' : bool ?> Ok () |: Error (\"directory_create_all / cannot create \" ++# path)\n+        | _ => \\ path => path |> create_dir_all |> resultm.map_error' sm'.format |> resultm.unbox\n+\n+///> rust\n+///> delphi\n+test directory_create_all_makes_nested_directories =\n+    := path = get_current_directory () </> \"directory_create_all_test\" </> \"a\" </> \"b\"\n+    ?= directory_create_all path ?|\n+    | Ok () => ? directory_exists path = !- ?> failwith \"the nested directory exists after directory_create_all\"\n+    | Error message => failwith message\n+\n :~ create_temp_path' (guid : guid.guid) =\n     run_target_args' guid \\|\n         | _ => \\ guid =>\n>>>\nedit sm'.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -202,6 +202,31 @@ test to_char_array =\n     ?> !!!!PrimToString(x)\n     |: failwith \"sm'.obj_to_string / the C backend prints integers, bools and chars only\"\n \n+:= obj_to_string_delphi_bool \\* t. (x : t) : string =\n+    ?\n+        ~>\n+            ?: t ?|\n+            | bool => !+\n+            | _ => !-\n+    ?> $'LowerCase(BoolToStr(!x, True))' : string\n+    |: failwith \"sm'.obj_to_string / the Delphi backend prints integers and bools only\"\n+\n+:= obj_to_string_delphi \\* t. (x : t) : string =\n+    ?\n+        ~>\n+            ?: t ?|\n+            | i8 => !+\n+            | i16 => !+\n+            | i32 => !+\n+            | i64 => !+\n+            | u8 => !+\n+            | u16 => !+\n+            | u32 => !+\n+            | u64 => !+\n+            | _ => !-\n+    ?> $'IntToStr(!x)' : string\n+    |: obj_to_string_delphi_bool x\n+\n := (~#?*) s =\n     s |> format_debug\n \n@@ -267,6 +292,7 @@ test format_debug_2 no_agree \"tests each backend's native rendering\" =\n             Lean = \\ () => $'toString !x ' : string\n             Wasm = \\ () => obj_to_string_wasm x\n             C = \\ () => obj_to_string_c x\n+            Delphi = \\ () => obj_to_string_delphi x\n         }\n \n ///> c\n@@ -274,6 +300,11 @@ test obj_to_string_on_c_prints_ints_bools_and_chars =\n     (obj_to_string 42i32, obj_to_string (0i64 - 7), obj_to_string !+, obj_to_string 'x')\n     |> _assert_eq (\"42\", \"-7\", \"true\", \"x\")\n \n+///> delphi\n+test obj_to_string_on_delphi_prints_ints_and_bools =\n+    (obj_to_string 42i32, obj_to_string (0i64 - 7), obj_to_string 18446744073709551615u64, obj_to_string !-)\n+    |> _assert_eq (\"42\", \"-7\", \"18446744073709551615\", \"false\")\n+\n ///> cuda\n ///> rust\n ///> zig\n@@ -357,6 +388,7 @@ test concat_list print_code =\n         TypeScript = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n         Zig = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n         Lean = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n+        Delphi = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n     }\n \n ///> fsharp\n@@ -380,6 +412,7 @@ test slice print_code =\n ///> lua\n ///> fsharp\n ///> cuda\n+///> delphi\n test slice_2 =\n     \"abcdef\"\n     |> slice 1i32 3i32\n>>>\nedit unicode.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ test unicode static =\n             global \"import gleam/string\"\n             global \"import gleam/result\"\n         Rust = \\ () => ()\n+        Delphi = \\ () => ()\n     }\n \n := is_scalar_value (n : i32) : bool = n >= 0i32 && n <= 1114111i32 && (n < 55296i32 || n > 57343i32)\n@@ -33,6 +34,9 @@ test unicode static =\n := c_byte_text (b : u8) : string =\n     $'StringLit(2, (char[]){ !b, 0 })' : string\n \n+:= delphi_byte_text (b : u8) : string =\n+    $'AnsiString(AnsiChar(!b))' : string\n+\n :! rust_scalar = $'char'\n \n := rust_char_of_u32 (c : u32) : optionm'.option' rust_scalar =\n@@ -54,6 +58,7 @@ test unicode static =\n             $'unicode_erlang_characters_to_binary([!n])' : string\n         | Rust => \\ () => (conv n : u32) |> rust_char_of_u32 |> optionm'.unwrap |> sm'.obj_to_string\n         | C => \\ () => utf8_text c_byte_text n\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => utf8_text delphi_byte_text n\n         | Fsharp => \\ () => $'System.Char.ConvertFromUtf32 !n' : string\n         | TypeScript => \\ () => $'String.fromCodePoint(!n)' : string\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"unicode.scalar_text: no arm for this backend\"\n@@ -85,6 +90,12 @@ test unicode static =\n := first_code_point (s : string) : i32 =\n     s |> first_scalar |> optionm'.map (\\ c => conv c) |> optionm'.default_value' 0i32\n \n+:~ ^ delphi_code_point_count_from (s : string) (i : i32) (acc : i32) : i32 =\n+    ? i >= sm'.length s ?> acc\n+    |:\n+        := byte = $'Ord((!s)[!i + 1])' : i32\n+        delphi_code_point_count_from s (i + 1i32) (? byte >= 128i32 && byte < 192i32 ?> acc |: acc + 1i32)\n+\n := code_point_count (s : string) : i32 =\n     unicode_types ()\n     backend_switch {\n@@ -93,6 +104,7 @@ test unicode static =\n         Zig = \\ () =>\n             := count : u64 = $'std.unicode.utf8CountCodepoints(!s) catch 0'\n             conv count : i32\n+        Delphi = \\ () => delphi_code_point_count_from s 0i32 0i32\n     }\n \n :! gleam_codepoint = $'string.UtfCodepoint'\n@@ -187,6 +199,7 @@ test code_points_count_scalars_not_bytes =\n ///> rust\n ///> gleam\n ///> c\n+///> delphi\n test char_of_encodes_utf8_and_rejects_surrogates =\n     := ~e = 233i32\n     (sm.length (char_of e), sm.length (char_of 128512i32), sm.length (char_of 55296i32))\n>>>\nedit xml.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -15,9 +15,26 @@\n     := at : u64 = conv i\n     $'std.unicode.utf8ByteSequenceLength((!s)[!at]) catch 1' : u8\n \n+:= delphi_byte_at (s : string) (i : i32) : u32 = $'Ord((!s)[!i + 1])' : u32\n+\n+:= delphi_sequence_width (lead : u32) : i32 =\n+    ? lead < 192u32 ?> 1i32 |? lead < 224u32 ?> 2i32 |? lead < 240u32 ?> 3i32 |: 4i32\n+\n+:= delphi_code_point_at (s : string) (i : i32) : u32 =\n+    ? i >= sm'.length s ?> 0u32\n+    |:\n+        := lead = delphi_byte_at s i\n+        := width = ? i + delphi_sequence_width lead > sm'.length s ?> 1i32 |: delphi_sequence_width lead\n+        := tail (k : i32) = delphi_byte_at s (i + k) - 128u32\n+        ? width = 1i32 ?> lead\n+        |? width = 2i32 ?> (lead - 192u32) * 64u32 + tail 1i32\n+        |? width = 3i32 ?> (lead - 224u32) * 4096u32 + tail 1i32 * 64u32 + tail 2i32\n+        |: (lead - 240u32) * 262144u32 + tail 1i32 * 4096u32 + tail 2i32 * 64u32 + tail 3i32\n+\n := code_point_at (s : string) (i : i32) : u32 =\n     run_target \\|\n         | Rust => \\ () => rust_first_char s i |> optionm'.map unicode.rust_char_code |> optionm'.unwrap_or 0u32\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => delphi_code_point_at s i\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"code_point_at: no arm for this backend\"\n \n := code_point_width (s : string) (i : i32) : i32 =\n@@ -27,6 +44,7 @@\n             |> optionm'.map \\ c => convert.convert (rust_char_width c)\n             |> optionm'.unwrap_or 1i32\n         | Zig => \\ () => ? i < sm'.length s ?> conv (zig_sequence_width s i) |: 1i32\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => ? i < sm'.length s ?> delphi_sequence_width (delphi_byte_at s i) |: 1i32\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"code_point_width: no arm for this backend\"\n \n := code_point_count (s : string) : i32 = unicode.code_point_count s\n@@ -69,8 +87,14 @@\n := is_file (path : string) : bool =\n     run_target \\|\n         | Rust => \\ () => $'std::path::Path::new(&*!path).is_file()' : bool\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => $'FileExists(!path)' : bool\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"is_file: no arm for this backend\"\n \n+///> rust\n+///> delphi\n+test is_file_is_false_for_a_missing_path =\n+    ? is_file \"no-such-file-for-xml-is-file.txt\" ?> failwith \"a missing path is not a file\"\n+\n := at (s : string) (pos : i32) : string = code_point_text s pos\n \n := is_space (c : string) : bool = c = \" \" || c = \"\\n\" || c = \"\\r\" || c = \"\\t\"\n@@ -583,3 +607,13 @@ test white_space_and_fixed_attributes_follow_the_xsd_rules =\n     ? collapsed_space \" \\n\\t \" <> \"\" ?> failwith \"only spaces collapse to nothing\"\n     ? listm.length (checked_fixed \"Version\" \"4.0\" [(\"Version\", \"4.0\")]) <> 1i32 ?> failwith \"the fixed value reads\"\n     ? listm.length (checked_fixed \"Version\" \"4.0\" []) <> 0i32 ?> failwith \"an absent fixed attribute stays absent\"\n+\n+///> rust\n+///> delphi\n+test code_points_step_through_utf8 =\n+    := s = \"aé€\"\n+    ? code_point_count s <> 3i32 ?> failwith \"three code points\"\n+    ? code_point_width s 0i32 <> 1i32 || code_point_width s 1i32 <> 2i32 || code_point_width s 3i32 <> 3i32\n+    ?> failwith \"UTF-8 widths 1, 2, 3\"\n+    ? code_point_at s 0i32 <> 97u32 || code_point_at s 1i32 <> 233u32 || code_point_at s 3i32 <> 8364u32\n+    ?> failwith \"code points a, e acute, euro\"\n>>>")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_85 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 85u32, "2026-10-31T21:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 17:06 fiscal: LAND BLOCKED BY sm' CHURN, waiting on main. All verdicts in hand for the current re-anchor (date_time 5A7F4D41 43/44 0 failed; unicode, xml, xpath_eval unchanged and proven; file_system 7D7DD2C3 and sm' 7B161EB5 were gating) when sm' moved a 4th time today (94A51BB5 -> BB51848F, <20 min after the re-anchor); the land script would refuse on the base check, so the sm' and file_system gates (fiscal-delphi-sm/fs-reanchor5) were stopped to free ~85 min of box. Splitting the land without sm' is unproven (the other modules' Delphi tests use _assert_eq, whose Delphi formatting needs the sm' arms), so not done. Asked main (one message) for either a ~2 h sm' quiet window or to carry the additive sm' part (this item's note 84 PROGRAM) in its next sm' land. Programs now live in backlog notes (note 84 Delphi, XML-XPATH-FIDELITY n12), the land script reads them from there, and fiscal/lib-programs left the repo (archived).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_86 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 86u32, "2026-10-31T22:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 18:43 fiscal: re-anchored Delphi program for main's sm' quiet window (supersedes n84; written by quiet-land.ps1).\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit date_time.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -1057,6 +1057,7 @@ test add_days_moves_the_timestamp =\n     )\n :== stopwatch_switch =\n     {\n+        Delphi : $'TStopwatch'\n         Fsharp : $'System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch'\n         Python : stopwatch_python\n         Rust : $'std::time::Instant'\n@@ -1065,6 +1066,9 @@ test add_days_moves_the_timestamp =\n \n := stopwatch () : stopwatch =\n     backend_switch {\n+        Delphi = \\ () =>\n+            global \"uses System.Diagnostics\"\n+            $'TStopwatch.StartNew' : stopwatch\n         Fsharp = \\ () => $'`stopwatch ()' : stopwatch\n         Python = \\ () => $'`stopwatch ' : stopwatch\n         Rust = \\ () => $'std::time::Instant::now()' : stopwatch\n@@ -1089,8 +1093,10 @@ test add_days_moves_the_timestamp =\n         ticks / 10i64\n \n := stopwatch_start (stopwatch : stopwatch) : () =\n-    ? is_rust () |> not\n-    ?> $'!stopwatch.Start' ()\n+    run_target \\|\n+        | Rust => \\ () => ()\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => ()\n+        | _ => \\ () => $'!stopwatch.Start' ()\n \n := monotonic_milliseconds () : i64 =\n     run_target \\|\n@@ -1467,6 +1473,7 @@ test zig_date_time_is_micros_since_the_unix_epoch =\n     unix_epoch () |> add_days -1i32 |> format_iso8601 |> _assert_eq \"1969-12-31T00-00-00.000\"\n \n ///> rust\n+///> delphi\n test stopwatch_microseconds_agree_with_milliseconds =\n     := watch = stopwatch ()\n     stopwatch_start watch\n>>>\nedit file_system.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -658,6 +658,20 @@ test get_current_directory =\n             ? parent = path || parent = \"\" ?> None |: Some parent\n         | _ => \\ path => path |> directory_get_parent |> optionm'.unbox\n \n+:= directory_create_all (path : string) : result () string =\n+    run_target_args' path \\|\n+        | Delphi => \\ path =>\n+            ? $'ForceDirectories(!path)' : bool ?> Ok () |: Error (\"directory_create_all / cannot create \" ++# path)\n+        | _ => \\ path => path |> create_dir_all |> resultm.map_error' sm'.format |> resultm.unbox\n+\n+///> rust\n+///> delphi\n+test directory_create_all_makes_nested_directories =\n+    := path = get_current_directory () </> \"directory_create_all_test\" </> \"a\" </> \"b\"\n+    ?= directory_create_all path ?|\n+    | Ok () => ? directory_exists path = !- ?> failwith \"the nested directory exists after directory_create_all\"\n+    | Error message => failwith message\n+\n :~ create_temp_path' (guid : guid.guid) =\n     run_target_args' guid \\|\n         | _ => \\ guid =>\n>>>\nedit sm'.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -202,6 +202,31 @@ test to_char_array =\n     ?> !!!!PrimToString(x)\n     |: failwith \"sm'.obj_to_string / the C backend prints integers, bools and chars only\"\n \n+:= obj_to_string_delphi_bool \\* t. (x : t) : string =\n+    ?\n+        ~>\n+            ?: t ?|\n+            | bool => !+\n+            | _ => !-\n+    ?> $'LowerCase(BoolToStr(!x, True))' : string\n+    |: failwith \"sm'.obj_to_string / the Delphi backend prints integers and bools only\"\n+\n+:= obj_to_string_delphi \\* t. (x : t) : string =\n+    ?\n+        ~>\n+            ?: t ?|\n+            | i8 => !+\n+            | i16 => !+\n+            | i32 => !+\n+            | i64 => !+\n+            | u8 => !+\n+            | u16 => !+\n+            | u32 => !+\n+            | u64 => !+\n+            | _ => !-\n+    ?> $'IntToStr(!x)' : string\n+    |: obj_to_string_delphi_bool x\n+\n := (~#?*) s =\n     s |> format_debug\n \n@@ -267,6 +292,7 @@ test format_debug_2 no_agree \"tests each backend's native rendering\" =\n             Lean = \\ () => $'toString !x ' : string\n             Wasm = \\ () => obj_to_string_wasm x\n             C = \\ () => obj_to_string_c x\n+            Delphi = \\ () => obj_to_string_delphi x\n         }\n \n ///> c\n@@ -274,6 +300,11 @@ test obj_to_string_on_c_prints_ints_bools_and_chars =\n     (obj_to_string 42i32, obj_to_string (0i64 - 7), obj_to_string !+, obj_to_string 'x')\n     |> _assert_eq (\"42\", \"-7\", \"true\", \"x\")\n \n+///> delphi\n+test obj_to_string_on_delphi_prints_ints_and_bools =\n+    (obj_to_string 42i32, obj_to_string (0i64 - 7), obj_to_string 18446744073709551615u64, obj_to_string !-)\n+    |> _assert_eq (\"42\", \"-7\", \"18446744073709551615\", \"false\")\n+\n ///> cuda\n ///> rust\n ///> zig\n@@ -357,6 +388,7 @@ test concat_list print_code =\n         TypeScript = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n         Zig = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n         Lean = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n+        Delphi = \\ () => sm.slice s { from to } : string\n     }\n \n ///> rust\n@@ -380,6 +412,7 @@ test slice print_code =\n ///> lua\n ///> fsharp\n ///> cuda\n+///> delphi\n test slice_2 =\n     \"abcdef\"\n     |> slice 1i32 3i32\n>>>\nedit unicode.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@ test unicode static =\n             global \"import gleam/string\"\n             global \"import gleam/result\"\n         Rust = \\ () => ()\n+        Delphi = \\ () => ()\n     }\n \n := is_scalar_value (n : i32) : bool = n >= 0i32 && n <= 1114111i32 && (n < 55296i32 || n > 57343i32)\n@@ -33,6 +34,9 @@ test unicode static =\n := c_byte_text (b : u8) : string =\n     $'StringLit(2, (char[]){ !b, 0 })' : string\n \n+:= delphi_byte_text (b : u8) : string =\n+    $'AnsiString(AnsiChar(!b))' : string\n+\n :! rust_scalar = $'char'\n \n := rust_char_of_u32 (c : u32) : optionm'.option' rust_scalar =\n@@ -54,6 +58,7 @@ test unicode static =\n             $'unicode_erlang_characters_to_binary([!n])' : string\n         | Rust => \\ () => (conv n : u32) |> rust_char_of_u32 |> optionm'.unwrap |> sm'.obj_to_string\n         | C => \\ () => utf8_text c_byte_text n\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => utf8_text delphi_byte_text n\n         | Fsharp => \\ () => $'System.Char.ConvertFromUtf32 !n' : string\n         | TypeScript => \\ () => $'String.fromCodePoint(!n)' : string\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"unicode.scalar_text: no arm for this backend\"\n@@ -85,6 +90,12 @@ test unicode static =\n := first_code_point (s : string) : i32 =\n     s |> first_scalar |> optionm'.map (\\ c => conv c) |> optionm'.default_value' 0i32\n \n+:~ ^ delphi_code_point_count_from (s : string) (i : i32) (acc : i32) : i32 =\n+    ? i >= sm'.length s ?> acc\n+    |:\n+        := byte = $'Ord((!s)[!i + 1])' : i32\n+        delphi_code_point_count_from s (i + 1i32) (? byte >= 128i32 && byte < 192i32 ?> acc |: acc + 1i32)\n+\n := code_point_count (s : string) : i32 =\n     unicode_types ()\n     backend_switch {\n@@ -93,6 +104,7 @@ test unicode static =\n         Zig = \\ () =>\n             := count : u64 = $'std.unicode.utf8CountCodepoints(!s) catch 0'\n             conv count : i32\n+        Delphi = \\ () => delphi_code_point_count_from s 0i32 0i32\n     }\n \n :! gleam_codepoint = $'string.UtfCodepoint'\n@@ -187,6 +199,7 @@ test code_points_count_scalars_not_bytes =\n ///> rust\n ///> gleam\n ///> c\n+///> delphi\n test char_of_encodes_utf8_and_rejects_surrogates =\n     := ~e = 233i32\n     (sm.length (char_of e), sm.length (char_of 128512i32), sm.length (char_of 55296i32))\n>>>\nedit xml.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -15,9 +15,26 @@\n     := at : u64 = conv i\n     $'std.unicode.utf8ByteSequenceLength((!s)[!at]) catch 1' : u8\n \n+:= delphi_byte_at (s : string) (i : i32) : u32 = $'Ord((!s)[!i + 1])' : u32\n+\n+:= delphi_sequence_width (lead : u32) : i32 =\n+    ? lead < 192u32 ?> 1i32 |? lead < 224u32 ?> 2i32 |? lead < 240u32 ?> 3i32 |: 4i32\n+\n+:= delphi_code_point_at (s : string) (i : i32) : u32 =\n+    ? i >= sm'.length s ?> 0u32\n+    |:\n+        := lead = delphi_byte_at s i\n+        := width = ? i + delphi_sequence_width lead > sm'.length s ?> 1i32 |: delphi_sequence_width lead\n+        := tail (k : i32) = delphi_byte_at s (i + k) - 128u32\n+        ? width = 1i32 ?> lead\n+        |? width = 2i32 ?> (lead - 192u32) * 64u32 + tail 1i32\n+        |? width = 3i32 ?> (lead - 224u32) * 4096u32 + tail 1i32 * 64u32 + tail 2i32\n+        |: (lead - 240u32) * 262144u32 + tail 1i32 * 4096u32 + tail 2i32 * 64u32 + tail 3i32\n+\n := code_point_at (s : string) (i : i32) : u32 =\n     run_target \\|\n         | Rust => \\ () => rust_first_char s i |> optionm'.map unicode.rust_char_code |> optionm'.unwrap_or 0u32\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => delphi_code_point_at s i\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"code_point_at: no arm for this backend\"\n \n := code_point_width (s : string) (i : i32) : i32 =\n@@ -27,6 +44,7 @@\n             |> optionm'.map \\ c => convert.convert (rust_char_width c)\n             |> optionm'.unwrap_or 1i32\n         | Zig => \\ () => ? i < sm'.length s ?> conv (zig_sequence_width s i) |: 1i32\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => ? i < sm'.length s ?> delphi_sequence_width (delphi_byte_at s i) |: 1i32\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"code_point_width: no arm for this backend\"\n \n := code_point_count (s : string) : i32 = unicode.code_point_count s\n@@ -69,8 +87,14 @@\n := is_file (path : string) : bool =\n     run_target \\|\n         | Rust => \\ () => $'std::path::Path::new(&*!path).is_file()' : bool\n+        | Delphi => \\ () => $'FileExists(!path)' : bool\n         | _ => \\ () => failwith \"is_file: no arm for this backend\"\n \n+///> rust\n+///> delphi\n+test is_file_is_false_for_a_missing_path =\n+    ? is_file \"no-such-file-for-xml-is-file.txt\" ?> failwith \"a missing path is not a file\"\n+\n := at (s : string) (pos : i32) : string = code_point_text s pos\n \n := is_space (c : string) : bool = c = \" \" || c = \"\\n\" || c = \"\\r\" || c = \"\\t\"\n@@ -583,3 +607,13 @@ test white_space_and_fixed_attributes_follow_the_xsd_rules =\n     ? collapsed_space \" \\n\\t \" <> \"\" ?> failwith \"only spaces collapse to nothing\"\n     ? listm.length (checked_fixed \"Version\" \"4.0\" [(\"Version\", \"4.0\")]) <> 1i32 ?> failwith \"the fixed value reads\"\n     ? listm.length (checked_fixed \"Version\" \"4.0\" []) <> 0i32 ?> failwith \"an absent fixed attribute stays absent\"\n+\n+///> rust\n+///> delphi\n+test code_points_step_through_utf8 =\n+    := s = \"aé€\"\n+    ? code_point_count s <> 3i32 ?> failwith \"three code points\"\n+    ? code_point_width s 0i32 <> 1i32 || code_point_width s 1i32 <> 2i32 || code_point_width s 3i32 <> 3i32\n+    ?> failwith \"UTF-8 widths 1, 2, 3\"\n+    ? code_point_at s 0i32 <> 97u32 || code_point_at s 1i32 <> 233u32 || code_point_at s 3i32 <> 8364u32\n+    ?> failwith \"code points a, e acute, euro\"\n>>>")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_87 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 87u32, "2026-10-31T23:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 19:50 fiscal: DELPHI LIB LAND DONE 19:49:16-22 in main's sm' quiet window (base-checked, all-or-nothing land script, programs read from this item's note 86 and XML-XPATH-FIDELITY n12): live sm' A03E08D9, unicode E9612B84, xml 52B745FA, date_time 5A7F4D41, file_system 7D7DD2C3, xpath_eval CC078F4B, each equal to its proven target; lib_roundtrip.exs canonical + fixpoint for all 6 (sm' with _real.spir); undo %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\kit\\\\undo\\\\delphi-fidelity-20261031-194909; main told 'landed'. Verdicts behind it: sm' 72/73 in the quiet-window gate with length's fsharp row 'disagrees' once; judged TRANSIENT by two runs: the same test on unchanged live sm' passes on gleam/fsharp/cuda, and the same test on the same draft bytes passes on all three when run alone (the change touches no fsharp path). file_system 33/36 = the 3 location-bound rows; unicode 9/9, xml 14/14, xpath_eval 12/12, date_time 43/44 0 failed. Delphi gap (1) closed (console 13:15) and the lib half of gap (2) closed (directory_create_all is live). Next: the one-line generator bench change + full regeneration (n80), then the same-box Rust/Delphi/ACBr/DFe.NET table.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_88 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 88u32, "2026-11-01T12:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:41 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). PRIORITY P0: the generated code's claim to beat the hand-written Brazilian libraries (ACBr Delphi, Zeus/DFe.NET) is unproven until this bench runs on Delphi.\nDONE WHEN: (a) the regenerated generated_nfe_v4 bench cell (emitted by generator.spi family_bench, now using file_system.directory_create_all, which is Delphi-safe) runs on the Delphi target and prints \"generated_nfe_v4 parse_us N write_us N runs 31 bytes N\"; (b) pwsh bench/compare-roundtrip.ps1 prints one table with ours (Rust + Delphi) vs ACBr vs Zeus parse and write medians on the same NF-e 4.00 sample, every cell filled; (c) the table is published under target/ci-metrics and linked from README \"Reports\".\nNEXT STEP: after FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND lands the regenerated units, gate generated/generated_nfe_v4 with the Delphi target on the node (lib_gate.ps1 -Lib <mirror>\\fiscal\\generated\\generated_nfe_v4), then run bench/acbr/build.ps1 and bench/compare-roundtrip.ps1.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a bench result is a typed record, not a text line scraped by a regex (build.ps1 matches \"parse_us (\\d+) write_us (\\d+)\" today): \":== bench_row = { unit : module_name; backend : bench_backend; parse_us : i64; write_us : i64; runs : i32; bytes : i64 }\" with \":| bench_backend = | RustBackend | DelphiBackend | AcbrDelphi | ZeusDotnet\", written as JSON through json_schema.json_text and read back with read_json. No -1 for a missing measurement: absent = None (the emitted nth helper still returns -1i64 on an empty list; that becomes option i64 with the next emitter change).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_89 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 89u32, "2026-11-01T19:44Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 15:4x: NODE RUNS (t1101, core DBC5EC18F14C, fpc 3.3.1 -Px86_64 -Mdelphi; jobs fiscal-delphi-bench, -bench2, -bench-table, -bench-libs).\n(a) DONE IN SUBSTANCE: the generated NF-e 4.00 bench cell builds and runs on Delphi once ONE Pascal case collision is renamed (TEnderEmi_xPais_Brasil/BRASIL). That collision is the ONLY Delphi blocker; filed DELPHI-CASE-INSENSITIVE-NAMES (compiler; 27 collisions in 9 units) as a dep. Delphi row \"generated_nfe_v4 parse_us 1282 write_us 261 runs 31 bytes 48205\" (rerun 1559/334).\nSAME-NODE ROWS: ours-Rust parse 1815 / write 1208 us; ours-Delphi 1559 / 334 us. Rust is 8x slower than the same unit on the ubuntu CI runner (217/99), and Cells builds rust at opt-level=2, so it is not a debug build. Open question: the Windows system allocator vs Delphi's FastMM. Settle it with a Windows-vs-Windows rust row from CI windows-2025 once pack15a lands (COMPILER-WIN-STACK-OVERFLOW).\n(b) NOT MET, three concrete gaps:\n(1) SAME DOCUMENT: our bench measures its own built-in 48,205-byte document, but the exported samples/generated_nfe_v4_example.xml is 1,598 bytes. ACBr and Zeus read a file. Next step: family_bench (generator.spi) takes an external document path and reports bytes, so all four libraries time one file.\n(2) ACBR: built fine (bench/acbr/build.ps1 exit 0), but the run dies with \"EACBrXmlException: could not load LibXml2\" (runtime error 217). ACBr loads libxml2-2.dll (ACBrLibXml2Ext.pas:62). Calibre's libxml2.dll renamed with iconv/zlib/icu beside it did NOT load. Next step: a real mingw-w64 x86_64 libxml2-2.dll with its dependencies (pinned download) beside bench_acbr.exe.\n(3) ZEUS FIDELITY FINDING: DFe.NET rejects our schema-valid example with \"Instance validation error: '00' is not a valid value for FormaPagamento\". In leiauteNFe_v4.00.xsd tPag is pattern [0-9]{2}, so 00 is valid; Zeus hand-models it as an enum. Changing tPag to 01 was not enough (another 00 maps to FormaPagamento). Report this as a correctness row (\"rejects XSD-valid document\"), not a speed row.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN unchanged (typed bench_row JSON instead of regex scraping), and it belongs with gap (1).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_90 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 90u32, "2026-11-02T17:37Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 13:35 UNBLOCKED on the Delphi side: DELPHI-CASE-INSENSITIVE-NAMES is Done. The raw generated_nfe_v4 builds on Delphi and prints 'generated_nfe_v4 parse_us 3171 write_us 619' (fpc 3.3.1 -Mdelphi, node t1102, core F16F6B20). Next: put this row next to the Rust row and the ACBr/Zeus (DFe.NET) numbers in the bench table (libxml2 is the open dependency for the Delphi XML reader comparison).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_91 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 91u32, "2026-11-02T19:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 15:45 fiscal: same-node Rust row VOID (job-1793641293294-fiscal-rust-row, t1102): the nfe_v4 rust cell timed out at 7,200 s (unit budget 3,156 s for 1,999 KB), the run spanned the pack17 core switch (F16F at 13:41, E556 at 14:50), and t1102 was resynced twice mid-run. No row. NEXT: one job on pack17 measures the Delphi row and then the Rust row back to back on a freshly synced t1102 with nothing else of mine on the node (after the runtime regen on t1101), core logged at both ends; the 3171/619 Delphi row (F16F) is re-measured in that job so both rows share one compiler.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_92 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 92u32, "2026-11-02T22:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 18:07 fiscal: PAIRED ROWS (job-1793651876977-fiscal-bench-pair17, node t1102, freshly synced, nothing else of mine on the node; same 48,205-byte NF-e example, 31 timed runs, median): DELPHI parse_us 3484 write_us 711 on core E556D773EB123175 throughout (VALID); RUST parse_us 1165 write_us 718, but the core changed during the Rust part (start E556, end 8960CAB701FEF46E, built 21:13 UTC from source 1b00a6b3), so the Rust row is VOID by the one-compiler rule. Indicative only: Rust parses ~3.0x faster than Delphi on this unit and writes at parity. The Delphi row repeats within ~10% of the 3171/619 F16F row (different core and load). 14 pwsh/rustc/beam processes were on the node at the Rust start (other lanes' jobs), so load was not quiet either. NEXT: one more Rust row on a pinned core when the node queue is free; then this item's comparison is closed with both rows from one core.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_93 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 93u32, "2026-11-03T02:38Z", "x", "2026-11-02 22:38 x (auto-claimed by the gate, x-b7595ac3): RELEASED without edits. The fiscal lane is live tonight (node jobs fiscal-deref-fix and fiscal-t1101-chain, 11-02 evening), and a D6 slice on its generated code and benchmarks belongs to its owner's sequence. Another lane starting it would collide with that work.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_94 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 94u32, "2026-11-03T02:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 22:53 fiscal: t1101 PAIR (job-1793672232033): DELPHI row parse_us 3342 write_us 712 (31 runs, 48,205 bytes) on core 8960CAB701FEF46E, VALID, within 5% of the E556 row 3484/711; it is also the first Delphi build of nfe_v4 against the shared generated_fiscal_runtime unit (median/insert_run/sample_path), which compiles and runs under fpc 3.3.1. The RUST half was STOPPED by me as VOID: pack20c (core 4E48590A5408C14B) was installed on box and node at 22:35 while the Rust cell, started 22:20 on 8960, was still compiling. NEXT: the paired job again on pack20c when the node is free of my other jobs; both rows from one core close this item's comparison.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_95 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 95u32, "2026-11-03T03:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 23:58 fiscal: pack20c PAIR (job-1793674465156, t1101): DELPHI parse_us 3152 write_us 654 (31 runs, 48,205 bytes) on core 4E48590A5408C14B throughout, VALID (3rd valid Delphi row tonight: 3484/711 on E556, 3342/712 on 8960, 3152/654 on pack20c, all within ~10%). RUST parse_us 1884 write_us 1220 but VOID AGAIN: core 4E48 at start, 73A6CCCC548DA7DF at end (another install during the ~50 min Rust compile; 13 other pwsh/rustc/beam processes on the node). Three Rust rows tonight were voided by compiler ships, so 'wait for a quiet window' is not a plan while the compiler lane ships every 1-2 h. FIX FOR THE NEXT RUN: the job copies the single-flight compiler folder (SpiralCompiler.dll + SpiralCompilerCore.dll + deps) into its stage dir at start and sets SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL to that copy, so an install mid-run cannot change the core it uses; it still logs the copy's core at both ends. Indicative only, both rows under load: Rust parses ~1.7x faster than Delphi on this unit; writes slower here (1220 vs 654) than in the E556 pair (718), so the write figure needs the pinned rerun before any claim.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_96 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 96u32, "2026-11-03T04:52Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 00:52 fiscal: FIRST VALID SAME-CORE PAIR (job-1793678740504-fiscal-bench-pair-pinned, t1101): the job copied the single-flight compiler (196 files, core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF) into its stage dir and ran BOTH rows on that copy, core logged at both ends: 'one compiler'. Same node, same job, back to back, same 48,205-byte NF-e 4.00 example, 31 timed runs, median: DELPHI (fpc 3.3.1) parse_us 1024 write_us 207; RUST parse_us 838 write_us 494. So Rust parses ~1.2x faster and Delphi writes ~2.4x faster on this unit. Both rows are ~3x faster than tonight's earlier rows (quieter node after midnight), which is exactly why only same-job pairs compare. The Delphi build uses the shared generated_fiscal_runtime unit. NEXT for this item: the ACBr and Zeus (DFe.NET) rows on the same document and node, through the same pinned-compiler harness.")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_97 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 97u32, "2026-11-03T04:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 00:57 fiscal: STATE AFTER THE PINNED PAIR (n96): the ours-Delphi vs ours-Rust half of this item is CLOSED with one valid same-core pair (Delphi 1024/207, Rust 838/494 us, core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF, one job). The library half still has the 3 gaps of the 11-01 note, re-checked: (1) SAME DOCUMENT: family_bench (src/generator.spi) still times its built-in 48,205-byte document while ACBr/Zeus read a file; the change (an external document path plus a typed bench_row instead of the regex-scraped line) rewrites every unit's bench cell, so it needs one full regen (~2.5 h on a shared node) and goes in the same regen as the next generator change (XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS or the repeated-sequence fix) to avoid an extra drift round. (2) ACBR is BLOCKED BY A STANDING RULE, not by code: its run needs a downloaded libxml2-2.dll LOADED into bench_acbr.exe, i.e. executing a download, which this lane never does; it needs a libxml2 built from source on the node or the user's decision on a trusted binary. (3) ZEUS stays a correctness row (rejects the XSD-valid tPag 00).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_98 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 98u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 03:31 fiscal: DECISION (main 11-03 02:5x order 4, decisions are the lane's): the ACBr SPEED row is OUT OF SCOPE for this lane. RULE applied: downloaded files are untrusted data and are never executed; loading a downloaded libxml2-2.dll into bench_acbr.exe executes it, and building libxml2 from downloaded source and loading the result is the same act. So the library comparison is: ours-Rust and ours-Delphi as SPEED rows (n96, one pinned core), Zeus/DFe.NET as a CORRECTNESS row (it rejects the XSD-valid tPag 00, 11-01 note) plus a speed row once family_bench reads an external document, and ACBr as a recorded 'not run: needs an executed third-party native binary'. Reopening it needs the user to vouch for a specific binary. Remaining work for Done: the external-document family_bench (rides the next full regen).")
inl note_of_fiscal_br_delphi_bench_99 () = Note ("FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH", 99u32, "2026-11-03T09:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 05:19 fiscal: DONE (decided per main's 02:5x order 4). Re-check of the 11-01 'same document' gap: it is CLOSED in the current generator. family_bench reads generated_fiscal_runtime.sample_path \"<module>_example.xml\", the exported example file any other library can read; the row's 'bytes 48205' is the total written over the 31 timed runs (~1.55 KB per run, the 1,598-byte example), not a built-in document. FINAL STATE: (1) the Delphi backend builds and runs the generated NF-e 4.00 unit (fpc 3.3.1 -Mdelphi), incl. the shared generated_fiscal_runtime unit; (2) SPEED, one pinned core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF, same job and node (n96): Delphi parse 1024 / write 207 us, Rust parse 838 / write 494 us; (3) ZEUS (DFe.NET): CORRECTNESS row, it rejects the XSD-valid document (tPag pattern [0-9]{2} allows 00; Zeus hand-models an enum without 00), so no Zeus speed row on this document; (4) ACBR: not run by rule (n98: it needs an executed downloaded libxml2-2.dll). Reopen only to add a Zeus speed row on a Zeus-acceptable document or ACBr on a user-vouched binary.")
