inl note_of_ci_actions_latest_7 () = Note ("CI-ACTIONS-LATEST", 7u32, "2026-10-29T23:30Z", "main", "10-29 19:30 main, re-check: the 10-24 hold cleared that same morning (the user committed the staged workflows at 05:02), and the bumps themselves LANDED on 10-26 under SPIRAL-TO-YAML n12. Main bumped alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, i574n.github, polyglot and spiral and regenerated each actions.lock; x, kit/eoie and tibia bumped their own. Verified today in all 8 repos' workflows: checkout v7.0.1, download-artifact v8.0.2, upload-artifact v7.0.2, setup-python v7.1.0, setup-dotnet v6.0.0, setup-go v7.0.0, setup-tectonic v4.0.6, all committed with no workflow diffs. The item was left Blocked by oversight; progress 60 -> 90. LEFT: (1) alphabet's awalsh128/cache-apt-pkgs-action@master -> v1.6.3 (latest, 2026-06-30, read via gh api today). The pins tool skips it because it has no pin, and its actions.lock records @master. BLOCKED NOW by a different cause: the gh actions-lock extension was lost in the wipe (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY), and reinstalling it is the user's call. (2) x's python-version 3.12.10 -> 3.15 (n3) belongs to x's repo, team x. The %TEMP%\\ci-actions-latest\\apply.ps1 script was lost in the wipe; it's not needed, since the remaining edit is one line. CORRECTION (10-29 20:19, sweep 9): the extension's source is github/gh-actions-lock v0.2.0 (archive/done-notes.spi, CI-ACTIONS-LOCKFILE n1/n6/n7); reinstall with 'gh extension install github/gh-actions-lock' on the user's yes.")
