inl note_of_ci_actions_latest_10 () = Note ("CI-ACTIONS-LATEST", 10u32, "2026-11-02T14:07Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
inl eoie_heavy_one_limit () = Task ("EOIE-HEAVY-ONE-LIMIT", "heavy jobs have two limits: eoie's timeout and Invoke-Heavy's 240-minute watchdog (heavy_wrapper drops the timeout)", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN", "eoie,jobs,process", "current", "current")
