inl x_emoji_weight () = Task ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", "x: emoji sequences weigh 2 as one entity, as twitter-text v3 counts them (x counts per code point: thumbs-up with skin tone = 4, a ZWJ family = 11)", Story, P3, D3, 100u32, Done, "X-WIP-VERIFY", "x,glyphs,weights", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_emoji_weight () = Planning ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_1 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 1u32, "2026-10-23T04:25Z", "x", "2026-10-23 00:25 x: found while measuring X-E2E-NON-ASCII's draft texts. twitter-text's config/v3.json has emojiParsingEnabled: true and defaultWeight 200 (scale 100), and js/src/parseTweet.js:37-53 extracts emoji entities with twemoji-parser, adds defaultWeight ONCE per entity and skips its length. So a skin-tone thumbs-up and a 4-person ZWJ family each weigh 2. x's weight (glyphs.spi, per code point by v3 ranges) gives 4 and 11 (measured with xc post-thread --dry-run), and glyphs.spi's weights_follow_x asserts thumb = 4. No backlog note shows a live X measurement behind that 4. Effect: safe but not exact. x over-counts emoji, so posts split early (never over 280), and x-compat's one-post-per-definition check can flag emoji-rich definitions that X would accept. Fix: x already segments graphemes (unicode-segmentation, gleam string graphemes), so a grapheme cluster that contains an emoji code point weighs 2 in total. The tests become thumb = 2 and the ZWJ family = 2, and keep U+2014 + U+200B = 2. Before changing, check twemoji-parser's entity rules against grapheme clusters for flags (regional-indicator pairs) and keycaps, and ideally confirm one value against X's live counter when the user allows a write.")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_2 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 2u32, "2026-10-23T04:26Z", "x", "2026-10-23 00:26 x: scope beyond x's glyphs.spi. The same per-code-point model lives in spiral/apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/x_compat.ex:112-113 (weight = sum of code_point_weight over the charlist, ranges from the profile) and in the compiler's XCompat overweight check (spiral_compiler.fs:183089: 'CJK and emoji weigh 2'). The profile x/postability/x.json describes weights only as code_point_weight ranges, so it cannot express 'an emoji entity weighs default_weight once'. Fix order: add an emoji-entity rule to the profile schema (e.g. post.emoji_entity_weight: 2, segmented by extended grapheme clusters), then x's glyphs.spi, Cells' x_compat.ex and the compiler read it. The Cells and compiler parts are main's (told 2026-10-23).")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_3 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 3u32, "2026-10-23T04:48Z", "x", "2026-10-23 00:48 x: a design draft (steps, edge cases, tests; no code yet) is at C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\x-precommit-next\\drafts\\X-THREAD-RESUME-and-X-EMOJI-WEIGHT.md.")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_4 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 4u32, "2026-10-23T12:49Z", "x", "2026-10-23 08:52 x: RULE, written before the code. A grapheme cluster is an emoji entity (weight 2 in total) when it has more than one code point and ONE of these holds: (a) its first code point is >= U+1F000 (pictographs, regional-indicator flag pairs, tag flags, ZWJ sequences, skin tones); (b) it contains U+FE0F and its first code point is in U+2000..U+2BFF or is U+00A9, U+00AE, U+3030, U+303D, U+3297 or U+3299 (text-default symbols made emoji by VS16); (c) it contains U+20E3 and starts with 0-9, # or * (keycaps). Every other cluster keeps the per-code-point weight, so the change can only LOWER a weight, and only for multi-code-point emoji clusters. Deliberately unchanged: a lone (c) or (R) without VS16 stays 1, and a letter + U+FE0F stays 3, because twemoji does not parse those as emoji and lowering them could produce a 281-weight post. Code shape: glyph_weight g = if emoji_entity g then 2 else plain_weight g, with two one-expression primitives (first_code_point, code_point_count) on both backends. VS16/keycap checks use sm'.index_of. splitter's posted_unit and budget_for switch to glyph_weight. Expected tests: thumb + skin tone 4 -> 2, the ZWJ family 11 -> 2, heart + VS16 4 -> 2, keycap 1 5 -> 2, JP flag 4 -> 2. Unchanged: decomposed e 2, a + VS16 3, CJK 2, U+2014 + ZWSP 2. Cells' x_compat.ex and the compiler's XCompat stay main's (note 2).")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_5 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 5u32, "2026-10-23T13:27Z", "x", "2026-10-23 09:27 x: the glyphs half PASSES. Cells on scratch copy C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\x-emoji\\client (x tree + apply_emoji_weight.ps1): glyphs.spi 8/8 on rust + gleam, including emoji_entities_weigh_two (thumb + skin tone, ZWJ family, heart + VS16, keycap 1, JP flag all = 2) and other_clusters_keep_code_point_weights (decomposed e 2, a + VS16 3, CJK 2, lone (c) 1, a 1). first_code_point and code_point_count agree on both backends. splitter.spi (units use glyph_weight) is running. Landing still waits for main's x_compat.ex / XC005 side (note 2), so the checkers agree with x.")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_6 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 6u32, "2026-10-23T13:29Z", "x", "2026-10-23 09:29 x: splitter.spi with glyph_weight units PASSES 7/7 (rust + gleam) on the same scratch copy, so the whole x-side draft is green. Emoji-free sources keep their weights by construction (glyph_weight only differs for multi-code-point emoji clusters), and no existing splitter test changed.")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_7 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 7u32, "2026-10-23T14:19Z", "x", "2026-10-23 10:19 x: open question from note 4 CLOSED against twemoji-parser's source (src/lib/regex.js, read-only). Bare (c), (R) and TM are NOT entities: their only branch is '(?:[(c)(R)\\u2122\\u265f]\\ufe0f)', where FE0F is mandatory. Keycaps match with or without FE0F ('[#*0-9]\\ufe0f?\\u20e3'), which rule (c) already covers: it only needs U+20E3 in the cluster. Safety argument completed: the only emoji in x's weight-1 ranges (0-4351, 8192-8205, 8208-8223, 8242-8247) are (c) and (R), and those need FE0F, which rule (b) weighs 2. (Double-exclamation U+203C and U+2049 are 8252 and 8265, already weight 2.) So no lone code point weighs more on X than in x, and the draft can only remove over-counting, never cause a 281-weight post.")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_8 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 8u32, "2026-10-24T07:24Z", "x", "10-24 03:24 x: LANDED in C:\\home\\git\\x's working tree (unstaged layer over the user's staged commit; X-DONE n74). Left: run8 on the real tree after tibia's block (N8), then the user commits.")
inl note_of_x_emoji_weight_9 () = Note ("X-EMOJI-WEIGHT", 9u32, "2026-10-24T11:19Z", "x", "10-24 07:19 x: in HEAD 6ef9c48 (user commit 05:20). x-verify-landing2 (07:08) compiled all 16 crates and passed the line gate, then failed only on x-compat. The 3 findings came from my prelude step 1 and the heal: autolinks listm.map/resultm.map in prelude.spi, and wire.spi replied_to_in at weight 290 > 271. All 3 were fixed unstaged at 07:05, and x-compat now finds 0 in 36 files. Done = job-1792840102746-x-verify-landing3 exits 0 (regen, gate, x-compat, release build, e2e -Accept, scripts/build.ps1).")
