inl eoie_agile_root_flag () = Task ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", "agile verbs refuse a flag in the root slot and name the flag with the verb's usage", Story, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,agile,friction,team:kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_agile_root_flag () = Planning ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", Minutes 20u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_1 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 1u32, "2026-10-23T08:16Z", "eoie", "04:16 friction measured on myself: eoie agile next --team eoie (and --prefix EOIE) answered 'unexpected argument eoie' three times, because --team filled the <root> slot and its VALUE was reported; the usage list even names eoie as valid. Fix drafted in scratch agile-root-flag/apply-agile-root-flag.ps1 (src frozen until F9): agile_subcommand_domain gets root_place (RootLeads, RootAfterMode for migrate-tags and notes) and root_operand (RootNamed, RootFlagged via lib sm'.starts_with); agile_entry refuses RootFlagged with 'agile next takes <root> before any flag, got --team; usage: agile next <shape>' and takes the state lock on the RootNamed value, which also fixes migrate-tags and notes locking argument 1 (a mode word) instead of their root. Rule: ships only if agile_mutation.rs stays under 1000 lines (981 today, headroom 19) and next_cli plus the new domain test pass; over 1000 -> move the refusal into agile_subcommand_domain behind an export crate instead of trimming.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_2 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 2u32, "2026-10-23T08:26Z", "eoie", "04:26 slice dry-run clean on a copy of the 3 packages (idempotent, LF kept) and chained into apply-rJ.ps1 after note-filter (agile-words only inserts --words after --prefix, so the usage prefix the test pins still holds); J's regen filter gains eoie_agile_mutation. Full-chain prelaunch (G, E2, 5 job-env slices, H, J, K with the GE2 and HIJK release scripts) clean at 04:26. next_cli is already an HIJK candidate. Left: the 1000-line rule check in HIJK's preview.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_3 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 3u32, "2026-10-23T12:04Z", "eoie", "08:04 fixed before shipping: the slice's test block called expect, which subcommand.spi does not define, so it would have failed J's typecheck; the slice now adds the local expect helper. Verified: subcommand.spi passes on a post-GE2 tree with I and J applied.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_4 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 4u32, "2026-10-23T12:36Z", "x", "2026-10-23 08:36 x: a second case of the same friction, from x: 'agile note docs/backlog X-E2E-NON-ASCII --as x <text>' answered only 'usage: agile note <root> <id> <text> [--as <author>]'. --as filled the <text> slot, and the error didn't name the flag. Moving --as to the end worked. Suggestion for the same slice: accept --as at any position after <id>, or refuse with 'agile note takes <text> before --as'.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_5 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 5u32, "2026-10-23T19:08Z", "eoie", "15:08 eoie: x's second case drafted as scratch note-as-first/apply-note-as-first.ps1. agile note takes --as on either side of the text: <root> <id> <text> --as <a> and <root> <id> --as <a> <text> both record the note. A note_request record (body, author choice) replaces the position-bound author_choice, and the arity router's 4|6 is unchanged. The empty-text check (now also for --as a with empty text) and the rule that an agent must name the author are unchanged, and the usage text is unchanged, so existing tests still pin it. A notes_cli test covers both orders plus the empty text. Dry run on the post-L copy is clean and idempotent. Queued for the release after N, next to the root-flag slice already in J.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_6 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 6u32, "2026-10-28T10:30Z", "eoie", "10-28 groom (user via main): Paused. Last note 2026-10-23, nothing queued. Next step: check whether its remaining milestone shipped in TRAIN2c (installed kit.exe A5B55974, 10-28 05:25). If it did, close it with that evidence; if not, size the remaining slice from its last milestone note and resume it through agile next.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_7 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 7u32, "2026-10-31T23:49Z", "kit", "10-31 19:5x kit, pause re-decision (main pre-night groom; R3 is now \"never auto-pause for silence\"): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the 10-28 silence groom (\"nothing queued\"), not by a blocker, and no note names an external condition. Back in agile next at its priority; its first step stays the one in the 10-28 note: check whether the remaining milestone shipped in a later train (installed kit 4983F9C0, TRAIN6) and close it with that evidence, else do the next milestone.")
inl note_of_eoie_agile_root_flag_8 () = Note ("EOIE-AGILE-ROOT-FLAG", 8u32, "2026-11-04T20:03Z", "kit", "11-04 20:3x kit: DONE, verified on the INSTALLED kit (TRAIN14c): `kit agile <verb> --open` for list, next, show, note and set each exits with \"kit error: agile <verb> takes <root> before any flag, got --open; usage: agile <verb> <root> ...\", i.e. it refuses the flag in the root slot, names it and prints the verb's usage (agile_subcommand_domain root_place + the shared message, test in agile_task_next/next_cli.spi). The verbs added since (lint, gate, cadence) use the default RootFirst place, so the same guard covers them once TRAIN23 installs; sprint is RootAfterMode by design (`agile sprint start <root>`). While here, the usage shapes the guard prints for lint and cadence were stale and now list --team / --since / --round (unstaged, vultr --check ok).")
