inl note_of_eoie_notebook_progress_3 () = Note ("EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS", 3u32, "2026-10-23T10:46Z", "eoie", "06:46 full package typechecks against the live lib (model + progress.spi with file_system.last_write_ms; notebook check livelib). Found on the way: the scratch model tree's src/spiral was a copy of lib from 10-20, so every scratch model check since then ran on a 3-day-old lib (the new last_write_ms was invisible); it is now a junction to C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib\\spiral, and notebook progress, accept-review and adoption-habits models all pass against the live lib.")
inl note_of_eoie_notebook_progress_4 () = Note ("EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS", 4u32, "2026-10-24T02:23Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:2x main: consolidated pendencies covered here (EOIE-CONSOLIDATED-INTAKE, class a): JOB-5 (typed progress counts instead of sleep loops). Spec text: Downloads/eoie-consolidated/agile_eoie.md.")
inl note_of_eoie_notebook_progress_5 () = Note ("EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS", 5u32, "2026-10-31T09:19Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 05:2x kit: RECORD WAS STALE. Since the wipe this item said 0% Planned, yet src/kit_notebook_progress (model.spi with 3 tests, progress.spi, export kit_notebook_batch_line) landed on 10-25. kit_machine_watch/run.spi calls it for every process row and prints '== notebook batches:'. The 10-23 notes still pointed at scratch drafts in f5/; nobody updated the item after the landing. GAP FIXED NOW (unstaged): release trains were invisible to it, because each train notebook runs alone with --output-path, not as a --output-dir batch. model.spi gains train_verdict (Pending/Passed/TimedOut/Failed) and train_progress, read from the train's own logs. progress.spi's train_line handles any '...\\scripts\\release-train.ps1 -Name <n>' process: it reads <root>/.cache/release-train/<n>/notebooks.txt and each notebook's log and prints 'release train <n>: D of T notebooks done, P pass, X timed out (a starved run, retried), F failed'. That replaces the hand loops lanes ran tonight to count train5e's .ipynb files. Two new test blocks (command parsing, verdict sorting with a timeout counted apart from a failure). Notebook and in-place regen are running.")
