inl note_of_eoie_notebook_progress_9 () = Note ("EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS", 9u32, "2026-11-01T19:35Z", "kit", "11-01 15:35 kit ACCEPTANCE on the INSTALLED TRAIN7 binary (kit.exe A25B8FBD): a Cells batch-mode run (run_notebook.ps1 --path x3 --output-dir, kit job job-1793561524824-kit-accept-batch) plus \"kit machine watch\" printed \"== notebook batches:\" and \"pid 29308 notebook batch: 0 of 3 written (3 share a report name, not counted), none yet after 2 min\". The three modules are all named model.spi, so their reports collide on model.spi.ipynb and are correctly not counted. One line per running batch, as specified. DONE. GAP found (not this item's scope): kit/scripts/notebook-batch.ps1 calls the runner once per module with --output-path, so its batches are never detected (the watch shows only the job line). It is fixed by construction when KIT-RUN-SPI replaces notebook-batch.ps1 (noted there).")
