inl note_of_lib_gleam_os_arms_30 () = Note ("LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS", 30u32, "2026-10-29T15:47Z", "x", "2026-10-29 11:5x x: fs-heal-4 REDONE after the wipe (its 10-24 copy was in TEMP) as x/lib-programs/fs-heal-4.kit (file_system.spi, 4 replacements, proven byte-exact on a copy, 0 new lines over 120; base 9C90242EE8514168 -> target F1495496B0021AED). (1) directory_create_symbolic_link and file_create_symbolic_link: the Rust arms no longer carry '#[cfg] ... .unwrap()' in macro text. Each declares cfg-gated helper fns of one name and signature in a global (windows symlink_dir/symlink_file, unix symlink; each body is one call + is_ok; closing triple quote aligned to the content, per memory rust-global-closing-quote) and keeps the panic semantics through Spiral failwith when the call fails. (2) new_file_uri: the F# interpolation 'file:///{!path}' becomes the Spiral concatenation 'file:///' ++# path. (3) trace_file's file_name: an F# interpolation becomes assembly_name ++# '_' ++# sm'.obj_to_string guid ++# '.txt'. Left as n26 said: read_link's mixed-type messages and trace_file's %A. OVERLAP: none with tibia's LIB-FS-HEAL-P (junction, read-only), main's DELETE-ROOT-GUARD (directory_delete, remove_dir_all) or kit's merged-lib (adds read_text_or_empty); main confirmed from tibia's rescued stage. But kit's insert lands inside hunk 1's leading context, so the program is regenerated on the post-land text (scratch fs4/gen-fs-heal-4.ps1). GATE (not yet run; after verify29 frees the node): whole-file A/B, base vs candidate, verdict = identical failure sets (n27's baseline already failed find_parent, find_parent_2, trace_file), plus a NEG arm ('file://' in new_file_uri, whose two Rust tests must go red).")
inl note_of_lib_gleam_os_arms_31 () = Note ("LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS", 31u32, "2026-10-29T18:47Z", "x", "2026-10-29 15:0x x: the A/B on base B5339FEF is VOID, not red. Arms: base 30/34 passed, candidate 33/34, NEG 29/34. NEG failed new_file_uri and new_file_uri_2 on the assertion, as designed (the control works). But every other failure in every arm was 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s' (slowest cell: base 545 s, candidate 323 s) on a node running 7+ jobs: base failed main's 4 delete-guard Rust tests, the candidate failed file_exists_on_gleam, NEG failed 3 Gleam tests, so the sets differ only by which cell hit the budget. Rule kept (identical failure sets) and not loosened. The rerun gives ALL arms the same gate-only header '///- --timeout 900000' (iggy.spi's precedent), and runs ONCE, on main's post-TRAIN4 file_system land (it replaces the delete_target_is_protected block, which fs-heal-4 does not touch), via the launcher that regenerates the candidate from the live file.")
inl note_of_lib_gleam_os_arms_32 () = Note ("LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS", 32u32, "2026-10-29T19:45Z", "x", "2026-10-29 15:5x x groom (WIPE-REDO-LEDGER n41): blockers for fs-heal-4, which are not backlog items, so no deps entry: (a) the node A/B gate on the rebased base 633EE8887B75 (base/cand/neg, all arms with the 900 s cell budget; launched 15:2x, results pending), then (b) the next lib window after TRAIN4c publishes. Verdict rule unchanged: identical failure sets for base and candidate, NEG fails new_file_uri/new_file_uri_2 on the assertion.")
inl note_of_lib_gleam_os_arms_33 () = Note ("LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS", 33u32, "2026-10-29T19:58Z", "x", "2026-10-29 16:2x x: fs-heal-4 GATED GREEN on base 633EE8887B75 (main's post-gap file_system), pack-6b, every arm with the gate-only 900 s cell budget. Base job-1793301920545 passed 34/34; candidate job-1793302026852 passed 34/34, so the failure sets are identical (both empty); NEG job-1793302359479 fails exactly new_file_uri and new_file_uri_2 (Rust, assertion path), 32/34. The earlier void A/B is resolved: the 300 s budget, not the change, caused those failures. Program x/lib-programs/fs-heal-4.kit regenerated on the live file by the launcher's derivation guard: base 633EE8887B75923A -> target 1F37E39FF3595D80. LAND by hand in the next lib window (after TRAIN4c publishes): pwsh -File x/lib-programs/land-lib-program.ps1 -Program x/lib-programs/fs-heal-4.kit -File file_system.spi -Base 633EE8887B75923A -Target 1F37E39FF3595D80 (re-run gen-fs-heal-4.ps1 first if file_system moved again).")
inl note_of_lib_gleam_os_arms_34 () = Note ("LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS", 34u32, "2026-10-29T21:32Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:4x x: FOLLOW-UP registered from main's review of fs-heal-4.kit (non-blocking; it lands as gated). (1) wasm32 and other non-windows/non-unix targets: the new cfg'd helper globals leave spiral_fs_symlink_dir/_file UNDEFINED there, where the old cfg'd macro expressions compiled away, so a wasm build that reaches directory_/file_create_symbolic_link would fail. Add '#[cfg(not(any(windows, unix)))] fn ...(target: &str, path: &str) -> bool { false }' (only reachable code is emitted; no wasm consumer calls these today). (2) Diagnostics: is_ok() + failwith(path) drops the io::Error text that unwrap() printed; return the error string (empty on success) and put it in the failwith message. Both go through their own gate (A/B + NEG), as a separate program after fs-heal-4 lands.")
inl note_of_lib_gleam_os_arms_35 () = Note ("LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS", 35u32, "2026-10-29T21:34Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:34 x: fs-heal-4 LANDED 17:34:27 in main's lib window (after main's 'main lands done'), one guarded try, no exemptions: file_system.spi 633EE8887B75923A -> 1F37E39FF3595D80, exactly the gated target (A/B base 34/34 = candidate 34/34, NEG fails new_file_uri x2). Undo: C:\\home\\data\\undo\\fs-heal-4. Main's closing document_test (the lib round-trip gate) follows. Open: the fs-heal-4b follow-up (x/lib-programs/fs-heal-4b-other-targets.kit, base 1F37E39F -> 0577F852336BCC6A, the cfg(not(any(windows, unix))) fallback helpers; drafted and proven on a copy, gate next) and the io::Error-text follow-up (design pending, one-call host rule).")
inl note_of_lib_gleam_os_arms_36 () = Note ("LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS", 36u32, "2026-10-29T21:40Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:3x x: fs-heal-4b (other-target fallback) PROVEN THROUGH THE BUG'S OWN PATH: a 3-line Spiral probe calling file_system::directory_create_symbolic_link, BuildSpiral -> Rust on pack-6b, then cargo check (pinned nightly). With live lib (fs-heal-4, 1F37E39F): windows exit 0, wasm32-unknown-unknown exit 101 'E0425 cannot find function spiral_fs_symlink_dir' (main's review concern reproduced). With fs-heal-4b applied (0577F852336BCC6A): windows exit 0, wasm32 exit 0 (3 cfg'd helpers per name). Windows regression gate (the whole file_system notebook, 900 s budget) on the node next; base 34/34 is known from the fs-heal-4 A/B. Lands in the next lib window after TRAIN4d.")
