inl lib_format_automation () = Task ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", "Unformatted code still lands in lib: automate formatting at land time (gate kit and lib_land run the formatter on touched files) and measure its cost so it does not clog the queue (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D3, 80u32, Planned, "", "formatter,lib,tooling,main,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_format_automation () = Planning ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_1 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 1u32, "2026-10-24T12:55Z", "main", "2026-10-24 08:55 main: measured: the installed formatter checks all of lib in 22 s on 2 threads (SPIRAL_FORMAT_PARALLEL=2), so it cannot clog the queue. Today 18 files would change, and 86 over-120 lines are strings and macros the formatter leaves alone (sm'_real 51, benchmark 12, trace 5). Automation: the gate kit's land.ps1 now hashes every lib file before the apply and formats exactly the files the apply touched, with the installed formatter, which is token-neutral by its own corpus gate. Every land therefore leaves its files formatted, and no file outside the slice is reflowed under another team's pending anchors. The files no pending slice edits (csv, conversation, cursor_walk, date_time, float_text, lustre, parsing, near_wallet) are formatted by a guarded land now (main-serial-format-idle). The other 10 (env, file_system, json_schema, oauth, otp_actor, otp_supervisor, resultm, sm', xpath_eval, xsd_emit) get formatted by their pending lands. oauth and otp_* are x drafts, so they wait for x.")
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_2 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 2u32, "2026-10-28T01:33Z", "main", "10-27 21:33 main: Groom 10-27 21:2x (WIP rule, set before applying). main's Active items with no note since 10-24 were classed by the evidence in the tree, not by age alone. (1) SHIPPED -> Done: the item's pass is in the installed tree core (apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs, core 8660C34A11F33259, the installed 5m' core), found by its own identifier or anchor, and an accept has passed on that core since (accept-6, run single-flight-20261027-173417, 0 blocking cells). (2) COLD -> Paused: no lane is driving it this week and nothing is queued. Its last note keeps the next step, and it resumes when a lane picks it or its condition fires. (3) KEPT Active: a lane is on it this week, or demand is waiting on it. (4) Blocked: only the user's commit or push unblocks it.\n Verdict for this item: (2) COLD, so Active -> Paused. The next step is the one in its latest note above.")
