inl spiral_notebook_files () = Task ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", "Spiral files as large subject notebooks: one file per subject organized by sections, tests next to the code they test (never all at the end), merge needlessly split lib/product files; check every repo for distanced tests and fix them; the 1k split stays only for compiled crates. Try first on the XSD files (one file instead of many underscored ones), spread destructively only if it works (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D5, 15u32, Planned, "", "lib,structure,tests,main,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_notebook_files () = Planning ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", Minutes 960u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:30Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:30 main: test placement census (scratch test-placement-census.ps1: share of test blocks after a file's last definition, i.e. clustered at the end). lib: 46 files with tests, 450 tests, 17% at the end; 9 files fully clustered (process, xsd, erlang_process, unicode, ...). The user's interleaving habit holds in most of lib, and the clustered files are agent-era. eoie: 68 files, 266 tests, 77% at the end, 27 files fully clustered (model.spi 10/10, notes_cli 9/9, window_model 8/8, program 7/7): the main offender. x: 34% (cli.spi 20/20 at the end), tibia: 50% (lua.spi, block_plan), fiscal: 27%. Rule from here: a test block sits right after the definition it tests; the lint (GRANULAR-LINT verb) reports files above 50%. Healing order: my lib files first (xsd, unicode, erlang_process; process is tibia's replace), then eoie by team (EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION slices move tests while touching each file), x cli.spi with X-GRANULAR-HEAL. The one-file-per-subject trial (XSD modules into one file organized by sections) goes after the XSD heal slices land, so their anchors are not broken mid-queue.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 2u32, "2026-10-25T13:57Z", "main", "10-25 09:57 main: applied to new code before it lands: lib cli_args.spi (CLI-ARGS-STYLE) now carries its tests next to the functions they test instead of at the end; the reorder kept the sorted line multiset identical and the livemd round trip ok. Rule for my new lib files from here: a test goes right after the definition it tests, and a fixture type goes right before its first test.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 3u32, "2026-10-25T14:02Z", "main", "10-25 10:02 main: lib census redone today: 51 files with 2+ tests, 482 tests, 87 after the file's last definition (18%). 17 files are fully clustered. Excluded: the XSD set (xsd, xsd_regex, xsd_resolve, xpath, xpath_eval; the fiscal team's pending slices) and process/unicode (under LIB-LIST-SUGAR-REST's anchors; process is tibia's). The other 10 go in one slice: %TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1 moves each trailing test right after the last top-level definition its body references, and throws if a file's sorted line multiset changes. Dry run: 26 tests moved, 0 left trailing. Gate + land job-1792936954610 (after the list-sugar chain).")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 4u32, "2026-10-25T14:06Z", "fiscal", "10:06 fiscal (XSD set, at main's 10:0x handoff): the lib slices now end with main's interleaver (%TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1 -Files xsd.spi,xsd_resolve.spi,xsd_emit.spi -Apply) plus a formatter pass, inside lib-gate-xsd.ps1. Dry run on the patched copies: xsd 6, xsd_resolve 3 (the new namespace test included) and xsd_emit 1 trailing tests move right after the last definition they use, 0 stay, exact line multiset kept. xsd_regex, xpath and xpath_eval are untouched by these slices and keep their trailing tests until the fiscal team next edits them.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 5u32, "2026-10-25T15:32Z", "fiscal", "11:3x fiscal: lib-test-interleave (%TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1) Defined-Names did not read ':& :~ name' lines, so a test that uses a member of a recursive group (xsd_resolve references_in) was placed after the group's predecessor and failed with ETY-UnboundVariable. Fixed in place: the name regex takes an optional ':& ' prefix; chunking is unchanged (':& ' lines still extend their group's chunk), so a test now lands after the whole group. Found by lib gate 1 of XSD-NAMESPACE-NAMES.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 6u32, "2026-10-26T00:51Z", "main", "10-25 20:51 main: lib-wide distanced-test census (dry run of %TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1 per file over all 108 lib/spiral .spi, nothing written): 47 files still hold trailing tests that would move (86 tests), 0 stay, 0 errors. 10 of them are the held main-serial-test-interleave chain (erlang_term, decimal, json_schema, otp_actor, lustre, json_scan, cursor_walk, csv, oauth, benchmark). The other 37, largest first: process 6, physics 5, unicode 5, base 4, xpath 3, listm' 3, xpath_eval 2, file_system 2, sm' 2, then 28 files with 1 (xsd_emit, xsd_regex, routes, schematron_run, schematron, step_runtime, resultm, util, xsd_constraints, testing, reflection, array_dim, xsd_resolve, parsing, otp_supervisor, optionm', ...). Rule, written before batching: a file with a slice pending against it gets its interleave inside that slice, as fiscal's XSD slices do, so no anchor ever clashes. That covers process (tibia's process heal), unicode (x's code-points patch), xsd*/xpath*/schematron* (fiscal's XSD set), listm' (main's list-sugar-rest), file_system (main's fs-link-length) and json_scan (in the held chain). Every other file goes into ONE batch-2 interleave slice, composed after the held chain lands, gated like batch 1 (exact line multiset kept; Cells tests of each touched file; a test after a recursive group's last member, the 15:32 fix). The pending set is re-read from the gate-kit work folders and the job list at compose time, not from this note.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 7u32, "2026-10-26T00:52Z", "main", "10-25 20:52 main: product-repo half of the census (the same per-file dry run; spiral/apps without the compiler, dice, alphabet, polyglot, dir-tree-html; 9 .spi files hold tests). Clean: dice (2 files), alphabet (1), dir-tree-html (0). Distanced: (1) apps/cells/priv/new_project/src/PROJECT_NAME.spi, 4 trailing tests: the spiral.new template, so every new project starts with tests at the end; it matters most and goes first. Cells reads it live (mix spiral.new), and CELLS-NEW-PROJECT's tests may pin the template text, so it is a Cells slice gated on those tests, not a tree edit. (2) polyglot apps/scheduler/Tasks.spi, 1 test: polyglot is the user's repo, so interleave and leave it unstaged for the user's commit. (3) apps/cells/tmp/Spiral.Cells.NotebookTargetsTest/.../bare.spi: a fixture a Cells test run wrote under tmp, not source; no change.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 8u32, "2026-10-26T00:53Z", "main", "10-25 20:53 main: CORRECTION to n6/n7's counts. The interleaver's 'N trailing tests moved' counts every trailing test that has a target, including tests whose target is already the file's LAST definition, where they already sit (the spiral.new template's 4 'moves' were 1 trivial reorder). Recounted with scratchpad distanced-tests.ps1, which loads the interleaver's own Split-Chunks/Defined-Names/Is-Test, so the chunking is identical: a test counts as distanced only when its last-referenced definition precedes the file's final definition; distance = lines between that definition and the final one. Result over 108 lib files plus the 2 product hits: 19 files, 40 tests, 3,937 lines of distance in all, concentrated in physics 4 tests/900 lines, listm' 2/802, sm' 1/524, date_time 1/475, json_scan 2/244, xpath_eval 1/208, json_schema 2/175, process 4/154, base 2/142, unicode 4/134, xpath 2/87, then 8 files at 22 lines or fewer. spiral.new template: 3 tests 6 lines away (trivial, low value). polyglot Tasks.spi: 0, nothing to do. So batch 2's value sits in physics, date_time, base and sm' (no pending slice on those except sm'), and the n6 rule still applies to the rest. The interleaver should print the corrected metric; that fix rides batch 2.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 9u32, "2026-10-26T00:55Z", "main", "10-25 20:55 main: the interleaver's count fixed in place (%TEMP%\\lib-test-interleave\\apply.ps1): 'moved' now counts only tests whose target definition precedes the file's last one, so it reports real relocations. The reorder itself is unchanged, and so is the message text (no script under %TEMP% parses it; checked). It now agrees with distanced-tests.ps1 on 3 probes: spiral.new template 3, physics 4, polyglot Tasks 0. Parse 0 errors. n8's 'fix rides batch 2' is done.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 10u32, "2026-10-30T02:00Z", "main", "10-29 22:00 main, groom (WIP rule, 3 days with no note): Active -> Paused, progress kept at 15%. Last note 2026-10-26, before the 10-28 profile wipe interrupted every lane, and no live job. Resume when picked; it is not abandoned, and it keeps its priority P1.")
inl note_of_spiral_notebook_files_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES", 11u32, "2026-10-31T20:58Z", "main", "10-31 16:53 main, pause re-decision (KIT-PAUSE-RULE-REWORK; rule R3 is now 'never auto-pause for silence'): Paused -> PLANNED. It was paused by the old silence/WIP rule, not by a blocker: its notes name no external condition (a 10-30 lab-archive note blocks nothing: restore the draft from the archive into the repo when picked). Back in agile next at its priority; deps, if any, gate it as usual.")
inl bang_macro_cleanup () = Task ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", "Code relying on !!!! intrinsics is ugly: inventory !!!! uses in lib and products, replace them with upstream core aliases (reuse upstream's names) or lib wrappers (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P0, D4, 70u32, Planned, "EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN", "lib,core,macros,granular,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_bang_macro_cleanup () = Planning ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_1 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:18Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:18 main: inventory of !!!! uses outside core (lib, eoie src, x, tibia, fiscal; lab and deps excluded), with the core alias each one has. Export 596: no core alias; eoie's crate exports. Proposal: one lib `export` wrapper (named, typed), then a mechanical rewrite in eoie (eoie team). Global 107: core base `global (x : string)` exists, so rewrite to `global`, mechanical. StaticStringConcat 18: the `^^` operator form, decided by CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's rule. Array intrinsics ArrayCreate 10, ArrayIndex 5, ArrayIndexSet 6, ArrayLength 6: core base has the prototype instances create/index/set/length on `array`, so rewrite to those (this is also the prototype usage TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCE wants). Conv 5: core `conv`. StringLength 4: core `sm.length`. LTE 6, Sub 3, Add 2: the operators `<=`, `-`, `+`. Without a core alias (keep as primitives until core grows one): Indent 6, NominalCreate 4, UnionToRecord 4, SymbolToString 3, RecordTypeFoldBack 2, Unbox 2. Order: Global (107) and the arithmetic/array/string ones (about 47) are mechanical rewrites, then the Export wrapper with the eoie team, and the rest wait for core aliases (upstream fork, UPSTREAM-FORK-START).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_2 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 2u32, "2026-10-26T00:41Z", "main", "10-25 20:41 main: re-census (tracked .spi; deps, target, _build, .cache and lab excluded; apps/compiler excluded because its samples exercise the intrinsics on purpose). lib: json_scan 27 (StaticStringConcat 8 at :32/128/130/133/268-271, array intrinsics 19 over raw array_base), array_dim 4 (its own create/index/set/length over the intrinsics: a wrapper, which is the target shape), base 2 (Add/Sub are the operator definitions themselves, so they stay), float_text 1 (has a land pending; untouched), rust/testing 1 ((++) = StaticStringConcat, used inside global (...)). apps: cells StaticStringConcat 5. eoie src: Global 107 (eoie team, frozen until KIT-RENAME). x Conv 5, tibia arrays 23 (their teams), polyglot Conv 4. Order: StaticStringConcat (lib 9, cells 5) waits on CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's fold probe (queued), since its target form (++# or ^^) is that rule's output. json_scan's array intrinsics are not mechanical: core's create/index/set/length are prototype instances over the array nominal, and json_scan's API passes raw array_base i32, so moving it changes types. That goes as a typed slice through the gate kit after the probe. Next: after the probe, one lib slice for json_scan (concat form plus arrays through the array nominal, gated with its tests).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_3 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 3u32, "2026-10-26T05:19Z", "main", "10-26 01:19 main: CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN decided (DOES-NOT-FOLD): the target form for !!!!StaticStringConcat is ^^, the compile-time concat. Sites: lib json_scan.spi 8 (:32, 128, 130, 133, 268-271), rust/testing.spi 1 (the (++) used inside global (...), where only ^^ keeps the literal global accepts), cells 5. Note json_scan's :128-133 concat run-time values (prefix, text_between results), where StaticStringConcat behaves as a plain concat; those become ++#, and only literal-only sites become ^^. Next: one lib slice over json_scan and rust/testing, classifying each site by literal-only (^^) or run-time operand (++#), gated on json_scan's tests.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_4 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 4u32, "2026-10-26T05:48Z", "main", "10-26 01:48 main: lib concat slice drafted per CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's verdict: %TEMP%\\lib-static-concat\\apply.ps1 (10 anchored edits, each exactly once, 0 lines over 120, no StaticStringConcat left in either file). json_scan.spi: all 8 sites have a run-time operand (key, prefix, the text_between results, piece, and the test's unicode.char_of values), so they become ++#, and json_scan gains ':< sm'_operators' (json_schema opens it the same way; package order allows it). rust/testing.spi's (++) builds global (...) text, where only a compile-time literal works, so it becomes 'a ^^ b'. Queued main-serial-static-concat after the test-interleave chain, because json_scan.spi is one of that chain's files (the interleave moves tests without changing lines, so these line anchors stay unique). Gate on json_scan.spi and rust\\testing.spi; every lib test runs through testing, so the ^^ change gets exercised. Remaining: cells 5 StaticStringConcat, then the array intrinsics as the typed array-nominal refactor.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_5 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 5u32, "2026-10-26T07:21Z", "eoie", "03:21 eoie: eoie's Global part drafted, with one coupling found. Census on the renamed tree: !!!! intrinsics 768 (Export 604, Global 107, StaticStringConcat 11, the rest single digits). All 100 Global wrappers are the same copy-pasted line ':= rust_global (x : string) : () = !!!!Global(x)', duplicating core base's 'inl global (x : string) : () = !!!!Global(x)' (base.spi:22); x and tibia already call bare global. Converter: kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\global-wrapper.ps1, string and macro aware. Dry run on a tree copy: 110 files, 100 local definitions removed, 256 call sites renamed to core global, and no string or macro body touched (a tests.spi string holding 'rust_global (' as rewriter input stays). Left by design: 7 direct !!!!Global(triple-quote) test calls, and the variant wrapper rust_global_transport (1 definition, 3 calls), which should fold in too. COUPLING, blocking a plain rename: eoie's drift tools key on the token rust_global: the style census token (kit style model.spi:135, probes.spi:87 RustGlobal), the ratchet rule 'a new package carries rust_global' (census.spi:183), and the authority census counting 'rust_global (quote)' sites inside host code (terminal.spi:118/155). Renamed call sites would make all of them blind to host blocks, and the ratchet would pass new drift written as global. So the class lands as one change: the rename, plus those detectors counting a global macro call as the same host-block marker, plus their fixtures updated. Gate: every regenerated product crate byte-identical (inl wrapper to inl wrapper), and the census numbers unchanged before and after on the same tree.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_6 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 6u32, "2026-10-26T07:32Z", "eoie", "03:32 eoie: the census coupling, measured. Probe counts over eoie src (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\probe-delta.ps1), before the Global cleanup and after it (dry-run tree copy). Old RustGlobal probe (the bare token rust_global): 381 before, 25 after. The rename alone would report a 93% drop in host-code drift while migrating nothing. Drafted probe (clean\\list-sugar\\census-probes.do, kit_style_census/probes.spi): a host-block call in either spelling, (?<![\\w.])(rust_)?global\\s*( paren or quote ), gives 363 before and 263 after, exactly the 100 removed definitions, and no longer counts Rust identifiers such as stats.rust_global_sites. Gate for the class, written now: with the new probe, RustGlobal falls by exactly the number of removed wrapper definitions, every other probe is unchanged on the same tree, and every regenerated crate is byte-identical. The probe change lands first (or in the same change); the authority census counter (kit_source_topology_core terminal.spi, counting 'rust_global (quote)' inside host code) and the ratchet's 'a new package carries rust_global' rule need the same either-spelling form.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_7 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 7u32, "2026-10-26T07:34Z", "main", "10-26 03:34 main: tibia is landing am'.create_base n (!!!!ArrayCreate) and am'.set_base ar i v (!!!!ArrayIndexSet) beside index_base (tibia-serial-heals, for terrain.spi's 23 raw array ops; probed on Rust and C). Follow-up for main once it lands: json_scan.spi's raw ArrayIndexSet sites (:162, :211) move to set_base, as a separate slice after main-serial-static-concat lands (same file), with no second wrapper. Rule for every lane: a raw !!!! whose lib wrapper exists is replaced by the wrapper. A missing wrapper is added once in lib, beside its siblings.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_8 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 8u32, "2026-10-26T08:01Z", "main", "10-26 04:01 main: raw !!!! in main's small repos (tracked .spi): dir-tree-html 8 (7 Export, 1 LT in shared.spi's char (<.)), dice 4 (all Export, contract/dice_contract.spi), polyglot 15 (6 Export in chat_contract.spi, plus apps/spiral/temp/cube/cube.spi: Sin, Cos, 2 Conv, 4 Printf), blog 0, alphabet 0. Plan, with order rules: (1) Export (17 sites) waits for x's base.export (job-1792997503468-x-serial-lib-export: ':= export \\* t. (name : string) (f : t) : () = !!!!Export(name, f)', which x proved byte-identical on Rust), then reuses x's generic %TEMP%\\x-simland-0214\\export_migrate.ps1 -Root per repo. No second tool. Per-repo proof: dir-tree-html's build with .rs byte-identical; dice and polyglot contract wasm export lists identical. Ordering: chat_contract.spi after the alias heal (job-1793000241647); dir-tree-html's tree.spi after the tree heal (main-serial-reland-fs). (2) cube.spi's Sin/Cos/Conv wrappers become core sin/cos/conv (core.spi:96-100 already wraps them); Printf has no lib or core wrapper, so it stays until BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP adds one beside console.write. (3) dir-tree-html's (<.) on char: core '<' is {number}-only, so a lib char comparison would be the home; low value, last.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_9 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 9u32, "2026-10-26T08:46Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:52 x: first wrapper, Export. lib/spiral/base.spi gets ':= export \\* t. (name : string) (f : t) : () = !!!!Export(name, f)' next to emit (base- is included unprefixed, so consumers call it bare: export \"xc_refs\" ((\\ x => refs_of x) : refs_args -> refs_reply)). Proof on the node (job-1792992991779-x-export-proof): all 51 x sites in 23 entries rewritten by export_migrate.ps1 (multi-line sites keep their authored breaks), and every entry compiles to byte-identical output, 22 Rust + simframes Gleam, 0 differ. Queued as job-1792997503468-x-serial-lib-export: lib gate on base.spi, land.ps1 (GREEN verdict + reader guard), then the x migration (refuses unless the live lib has export, rolls back on failure). eoie's 604 sites can use the same wrapper; x is now free of !!!! (exsss.spi moved to ^^^/&&&/|||/<<</>>>/conv, posts.spi to (~!) p).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_10 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 10u32, "2026-10-26T09:24Z", "main", "10-26 05:24 main: LIB-STATIC-CONCAT landed 05:21 (main-serial-static-concat, gate GREEN then a land through the mutex-held kit): json_scan.spi 9C2DBF8E3FCE19D3 (8 StaticStringConcat -> ++# plus ':< sm''_operators') and rust\\testing.spi A33B2BEF370CE01C ((++) = a ^^ b, compile-time concat for global). Neither file has a !!!!StaticStringConcat left. The json_scan follow-up (ArrayIndexSet at :162/:211 -> am'.set_base) waits only on tibia's create_base/set_base land now, since this one is in.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_11 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 11u32, "2026-10-26T09:25Z", "main", "10-26 05:25 main: json_scan.spi has 19 raw array intrinsics, not 2: ArrayLength x5, ArrayIndex x4, ArrayIndexSet x4, ArrayCreate x6 (lines 163-245 after the static-concat land). am' has index_base and init_base; tibia's pending slice adds create_base and set_base beside index_base; there's no length_base. Plan: after tibia's land, one gate-kit slice adds am'.length_base beside the landed wrappers (anchored on their landed text, so the two lands can't collide) and moves all 19 sites onto length_base, index_base, set_base and create_base. Rule for the gate: Rust and Gleam outputs of json_scan's tests stay identical in behavior, with 0 candidate-only reds.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_12 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 12u32, "2026-10-26T11:50Z", "x", "2026-10-26 07:50 x: the lib export gate waited 4.9 h for a local heavy slot (05:36-10:3x) without starting, so it moved to the node: local chain job-1792997503468 stopped while still waiting (gate.ps1 never ran, no writes), node gate job-1793015478185 runs the node lib-gate-kit against a fresh spiral mirror (xgate). On GREEN, the verdict is copied into the local kit and a local serial job runs only land.ps1 (stage + reader guard + mutex) and x-migrate.ps1 (manifest serial-x-lib-land.json); both are non-heavy and write live trees, so they stay local.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_13 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 13u32, "2026-10-26T12:03Z", "main", "10-26 08:03 main: json_scan array slice drafted and proven on a lib copy: %TEMP%\\lib-json-scan-arrays\\apply.ps1 -Lib <lib\\spiral> [-Apply]. am'.spi gets length_base (`ar |> array |> length`, the same form as index_base) right after tibia's set_base, plus a ///> rust test, base_wrappers_round_trip (create_base 3, set_base, then [length; index] = [3; 7]). json_scan.spi moves all 19 raw sites, each pattern at its exact expected count: 4 ArrayLength -> am'.length_base, 7 ArrayCreate -> am'.create_base (the element type comes from each site's annotation or return type), 4 ArrayIndexSet -> am'.set_base, 3 ArrayIndex -> am'.index_base. 0 raw array intrinsics left; 0 lines over 120. Type check first: the wrappers take `int`, and a --check probe shows int is i32 (`(x : i32) : int = x` accepted; the negative twin `(x : i64) : int = x` rejected), so json_scan's i32 counts need no conv. Proof (proof-check.ps1): a robocopy of lib, tibia's exact LIB-ARRAY-BASE text simulated from their apply script (their script itself not run), then this slice, then --check of a probe that calls json_scan.parse_i32_array and both wrappers: exit 0. Negative control: a string planted as index_base's index in the copy is rejected (exit 5), so the check reads the copy, not the live lib. The slice refuses until am'.spi carries tibia's set_base line, since it anchors on that landed text. Next: when LIB-ARRAY-BASE lands (tibia's 'gaps' part), run the gate kit on am' and json_scan (Cells tests on both backends, 0 candidate-only reds), then land.ps1.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_14 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 14u32, "2026-10-26T13:49Z", "x", "2026-10-26 09:49 x: GREEN at last on the node (attempt 3, job-1793016941188), using tibia's node gate (-Tree/-Gate against the mirror's lib_gate.ps1, mix deps.get first, EOIE_EXE set). Attempts 1-2 were VOID because the plain gate ran no test rows in a fresh mirror. Verdict GREEN 20261026-0817: baseline red 39, 10 candidate-only reds (join_body_unit_3/gleam, from_pair*) all passed when rerun alone (5 of 5), 0 type errors. Gated base.spi hash 4E28EB421DBB5F8F equals live, so the verdict was copied into the local kit; local land+migrate job-1793021989909-x-serial-lib-land runs land.ps1 (stage, reader guard, mutex) then x-migrate.ps1.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_15 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 15u32, "2026-10-26T13:55Z", "x", "2026-10-26 09:55 x: LANDED. lib base.spi gained export (land.ps1 09:53, base.spi 8C92D23BA51E50A5, waited 11 min for a Cells run to clear). Then x-migrate rewrote 51 sites in 23 files under x/apps to call lib export (backup %TEMP%\\x-lib-export\\x-backup-20261026-095402). x .spi files now hold 0 '!!!!' sites. Compile proof of the migrated x tree rides on the next full x verify.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_16 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 16u32, "2026-10-26T14:36Z", "main", "10-26 10:36 main: apps/cells' 5 StaticStringConcat sites, looked at 10:3x: each of cell.spi, directives.spi, document.spi, notebook.spi and text.spi opens with its own ':= (++) (left : string) (right : string) : string = !!!!StaticStringConcat(left, right)', applied to run-time strings. By CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN's verdict (run-time operands: ++#, literal-only: ^^) the target is lib's ++#. The 5 local copies go, replaced by one shared operator rather than 5 renamed aliases. Ordering rule, written now: this slice starts only after install-5n has run, because install-5n.ps1 hash-guards directives.spi (FFE782851366145F) and applies x's structural-names apply_host_cells.ps1 to Cells inside the install window, so an earlier edit would make the P0 install refuse. The slice is drafted after 5n lands, anchored on the post-install text, with the Cells mix tests as its gate.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_17 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 17u32, "2026-10-26T14:36Z", "main", "10-26 10:36 main: correction to the previous note: apps/cells/spi/package.spiproj lists only |core- (no spiral-), so lib's ++# (sm'_operators) is not reachable from Cells, which is likely why each module keeps a local (++). The slice's choice, by the same post-5n rule: either core's own run-time string concat, if core has one (check core before drafting), or one shared Cells module (text.spi is first in the package order) holding the single definition that the other 4 open. Adding spiral- to the Cells package is out of scope, since Cells must build before lib.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_18 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 18u32, "2026-10-26T19:37Z", "main", "10-26 15:37 main: 10-26 15:3x main: the Cells StaticStringConcat slice's open check (n17) is resolved by reading, and its shape is decided. (1) Core has NO run-time string concat: the fork core's sm.spi defines only index, length and slice; its concat functions are arraym.concat and listm.concat (arrays and lists). So the core-alias option is out. (2) apps/cells/spi/package.spiproj order is text, cell, directives, document, notebook, targets, main (|core- only). Each of the 5 modules defines its own '(++) ... = !!!!StaticStringConcat(left, right)' on line 1 and opens nothing.\nShape, by lib's existing idiom (sm'_operators, rust.rust_operators): a new operators-only module apps/cells/spi/text_operators.spi, first in the package, holds the single (++); all 5 modules replace their line-1 definition with ':< text_operators'. Rejected alternative: ':< text' from the other 4 would open every text definition unqualified (notebook calls text.replace and text.next_line by qualified name), risking shadowing, whereas an operators-only module exposes just the operator.\nResult: 5 !!!! sites become 1 (the operator's own body, an irreducible intrinsic with no core alias); 0 renamed aliases. Ordering unchanged: draft after install-5n (it guards directives.spi) and after fiscal's fidelity and keep_docs lands (document.spi, directives.spi). Gate: Cells mix test, failures equal to the 3-known baseline, plus a corpus notebook run.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_19 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 19u32, "2026-10-26T19:40Z", "main", "10-26 15:40 main: 10-26 15:4x main: lib census re-run by intrinsic: 40 '!!!!' sites in 6 files, down from the 10-24 inventory. Classified, by n1's rule (core alias, else lib wrapper, else irreducible): base.spi 6 (Add/Sub/Mult/Div/Do/Export) ARE the lib wrappers, the irreducible single definitions everyone else calls; backend.spi 8 (BackendSwitch x2, Indent x6) is the dispatch machinery itself; array_dim.spi 4 are the array primitive wrappers; console.spi 2 (Printf in write_line_bend, the Bend backend's only output route) have no core alias (the fork core has no printf), and a lib wrapper would only move them one level down, so irreducible; float_text.spi 1 (StaticStringConcat) sits in fiscal's pending LIB-TARGET-GAP landing, re-checked after it lands; json_scan.spi 19 (array intrinsics) wait on tibia's LIB-ARRAY-BASE, as recorded. So lib has 0 sites left that main can heal today; the remaining reducible ones are float_text (fiscal, after its land), json_scan (tibia's array base), and the Cells 5 to 1 slice (n18, after 5n).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_20 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 20u32, "2026-10-26T19:46Z", "main", "10-26 15:46 main: 10-26 15:5x main: product census of '!!!!' in main's repos: dice contract 4 Export; polyglot apps/chat/contract 6 Export, plus apps/spiral/temp/cube Conv/Cos/Sin/Printf (cube-core-math's own heal); dir-tree-html 7 Export (tree 3, inline 2, markdown 1, selftest 1) plus shared.spi's '(<.)' over !!!!LT; alphabet 0; blog 0. The LT is irreducible for now: Spiral char has no ordering, so lib would need a char comparison first.\nThe 17 Export sites move to lib base.spi's export (x landed it 09:53; x migrated its own 51 sites) through x's converter (TEMP x-simland-0214/export_migrate.ps1: balanced parens, string-aware). Dry run on copies of all 6 files: 17 sites, 0 left. Single-line '!!!!Export(\"n\", f)' becomes 'export \"n\" f'; multi-line forms become 'export' with the name and lambda indented on the following lines (offside application).\nRunner TEMP main-export-migrate/run.ps1, one generic tool for all three repos: lib guard (base.spi has export), backup plus hashes, conversion on a staged copy first (nothing written if the converter fails), then the repo's own consumer build. Rule, written before the runs: GREEN iff that build exits 0 AND 0 '!!!!Export(' is left; otherwise restore every file, verified by hash. Builds: dice/contract/build.ps1 (full, incl. notebook tests and export check); polyglot apps/chat/contract/build.ps1; dir-tree-html via repo-build.ps1 (build + --self-test + 1k units).\nOrdering: the dir-tree migration is step 2 of the repo-build-3 serial manifest, so the two dir-tree builds never share the live tree concurrently; dice and polyglot-chat are standalone requeue extras. All three are queued after kit's rename finalize.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_21 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 21u32, "2026-10-26T23:15Z", "main", "10-26 19:15 main: 10-26 19:15 main: json_scan.spi's 19 array intrinsics are unblocked: tibia landed LIB-ARRAY-BASE (am'.create_base, set_base, index_base; gated GREEN ~17:5x). The 08:00 slice (TEMP lib-json-scan-arrays/apply.ps1: am'.length_base + a round-trip test, and json_scan's 19 sites through am') now dry-runs clean on live lib, its set_base anchor present once, 0 raw intrinsics left, 0 lines over 120. proof-check.ps1 updated to skip its LIB-ARRAY-BASE simulation when lib already has create_base; on a fresh lib copy, --check exit 0 (TYPECHECKS) through parse_i32_array -> item_positions -> record_start. The real gate (json_scan's rust/gleam/c test blocks and am''s new test) is queued as requeue extra main-serial-json-scan-arrays (gate -> land, kit gate-kit), AFTER job-1793030605331-main-serial-am-try-item, because both edit am'.spi and each gate must gate the bytes it lands on (pause-requeue.ps1 gained an optional After field for this). When it lands, lib's '!!!!' count drops 40 -> 21, all classified irreducible or held (n19).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_22 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 22u32, "2026-10-26T23:16Z", "main", "10-26 19:16 main: 10-26 19:16 main: CORRECTION to n21's count, measured on live lib now: lib has 43 '!!!!' sites in 8 files, not 40. Since the 15:40 census (n19): am'.spi +2 (tibia's create_base and set_base bodies, the array wrappers themselves) and sm'.spi +1 (PrimToString in obj_to_string_c, the C backend's only primitive-to-string route). Both are irreducible single definitions by n1's rule, like base.spi's 6. So the json_scan slice takes lib 43 -> 24: backend 8, base 6, array_dim 4, am' 2, console 2, sm' 1 (all wrappers or dispatch machinery) and float_text 1 (held for fiscal's LIB-TARGET-GAP).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_23 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 23u32, "2026-10-27T06:41Z", "main", "10-27 02:41 main: 10-27 02:41 main: the polyglot apps/chat/contract export migration (job-1793062387257, 20:54-00:14) went RED, but not because of the migration. Its build failed one test, generate_cid on rust, and tibia's fresh baseline on the restored, untouched tree fails it the same way: chat_contract.spi:74:8 ETY-TermError, where the test pipes ;[] straight into am'.to_vec, which takes array_base (red since about 10-24 23:19). The migration's runner restored its file by hash. tibia fixes the test (tibia-polyglot-cid-test-fix: ;[] |> am'.base |> am'.to_vec, the crypto.spi idiom) and then reruns its generate_cid heal (cid-land7, --after-ok). The polyglot export migration requeues AFTER cid-land7, on a copy of the tree rather than in place, because the in-place run overlapped tibia's baseline build for ~3 h. The dice export migration is unaffected.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_24 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 24u32, "2026-10-27T06:41Z", "main", "10-27 02:41 main: 10-27 02:41 main: dice's export migration LANDED (unstaged). job-1793062386837 went GREEN: 1 file in dice/contract migrated from !!!!Export to lib export, dice/contract build.ps1 exit 0, contract tests all passed, NEAR sandbox tests passed on dist/dice.wasm (backup in TEMP main-export-migrate). Of n19's 17 product Export sites, dice's are done; polyglot chat waits on tibia's cid-land7 (n23), and dir-tree-html's are in main-serial-dir-tree-repo-build-3.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_25 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 25u32, "2026-10-27T06:44Z", "main", "10-27 02:44 main: 10-27 02:43 main: polyglot chat's export migration is UNBLOCKED, not yet run. tibia landed the generate_cid test fix (6/6) and its heal (cid-land7: rebuild exit 0, notebook tests 6/6, all 9 exports identical) as an unstaged layer in polyglot, so the baseline is green now. Next run, in this order: (1) change TEMP main-export-migrate/run.ps1 so the convert-then-build proof runs on a copy of the repo (cargo workspace and deps links included), and only a GREEN verdict writes the live tree, as promised to tibia after the 3 h overlap. (2) Run it on polyglot apps/chat/contract, anchored on tibia's new chat_contract.spi bytes. The pass rule is unchanged: build exit 0 AND 0 sites left; otherwise nothing is written. Deferred tonight because main's standing run ended at 21:00 and the runner change is real work.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_26 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 26u32, "2026-10-27T07:21Z", "main", "10-27 03:21 main: 10-27 03:21 main: json_scan's 19 array intrinsics LANDED (json-scan-arrays chain, re-chained behind the new am-try-item; gate and land exit 0). lib's '!!!!' count should now be 24 (n22's projection); re-measure next run. With dice's export migration (n24), the open product sites are polyglot chat's (n25, deferred) and dir-tree-html's (migrated in repo-build-3, GREEN).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_27 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 27u32, "2026-10-27T09:45Z", "main", "10-27 05:45 main: 10-27 05:45 main: lib re-measured, 24 '!!!!' sites in 7 files, n26's projection exactly. ALL 24 are inside lib wrapper definitions, so lib is at its floor. am' create_base/set_base and array_dim create/index/set/length are the array primitives. base.spi has export, do and the arithmetic operators (+ - * /). float_text has concat. backend.spi holds backend_switch itself (2) and its 6 Indent helpers. console.spi:57-58 is write_line_bend, the Bend arm of console printing. sm'.spi:226 is obj_to_string's C path. Each wraps exactly one intrinsic, and callers use the wrapper. The item's open work is products only: polyglot apps/chat/contract's export sites (unblocked since cid-land7; runner change next) and dir-tree-html's (migrated in repo-build-3, GREEN). Then a product census for the other intrinsics.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_28 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 28u32, "2026-10-27T10:26Z", "main", "10-27 06:26 main: polyglot chat's export migration is QUEUED (job-1793096715870), with the runner change promised to tibia on 10-27 02:44 done. TEMP main-export-migrate/run-copy.ps1 copies apps/chat plus scripts and lib into a work folder, recreates deps links, and re-points every absolute link that pointed back into the live repo into the copy (apps/chat/contract/lib -> C:\\home\\git\\polyglot\\lib was one). It refuses (VOID) if any link in the copy still points into the live repo, then converts and builds apps/chat/build.ps1 (the contract, then its tests) inside the copy, with cargo's target in a main-owned cache. It writes the live tree only on GREEN, and only if every site file still has the hash read at the start (else VOID: nothing written). The copy stage was tested alone with -CopyOnly: 394 MB, 1 link re-pointed, 0 escaping, then removed links-first with the live lib and spiral intact. The pass rule is unchanged from n24: build exit 0 AND 0 sites left. The old in-place run.ps1 is kept for reference and no longer used.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_29 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 29u32, "2026-10-27T12:00Z", "main", "10-27 08:00 main: polyglot chat migration (job-1793096715870) is RED by its rule, and the live tree is untouched as designed: the copy, the link re-point and the conversion all worked (6 sites in 1 file, 0 left). The build failed for ENVIRONMENTAL reasons, not the migration. (1) The contract step runs spiral_wasm through WSL, which failed with Wsl/Service/ERROR_TIMEOUT under the box's 100% load. (2) chat_contract.spi's 6 rust test cells all exceeded Cells' 300 s timeout (slowest 624 s, headroom 2.08). The runner had no control, so it couldn't tell the two failure kinds apart. Fix before the next run: run-copy.ps1 also builds an UNCONVERTED copy (the control). Converted GREEN is GREEN; converted RED with control GREEN is RED (the migration broke it); both RED is VOID (environment), with the failing step of each named.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_30 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 30u32, "2026-10-27T15:53Z", "main", "10-27 11:53 main: chat-2 (job-1793103260833) VOID, and the cause was my harness, not the migration. Both the converted and the unconverted control copy failed the same 6 chat contract tests the same way (the failure lines differ only by a thread id): the WSL spiral_wasm binary panicked on 'No such file or directory' reading target/spiral/spiral_contract/target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/spiral_<hash>.wasm. Cargo had built all 6 artifacts fine (exit 0; a failed build prints 'cargo error', not 'wasm error'), but into the per-side CARGO_TARGET_DIR that run-copy.ps1 set (LOCALAPPDATA main-cargo-target/export-migrate-<side>, where all 6 top-level .wasm files sit). apps/spiral/spiral.spi:327 hard-codes the wasm path under the workspace's own target/, so it never finds output redirected by CARGO_TARGET_DIR. A race between parallel test steps was ruled out: there are 6 distinct hashes, one per test. Both sides generate identical hashes, so the isolation bought nothing. run-copy.ps1 now sets CARGO_TARGET_DIR only when -CargoTarget is passed (default off). Re-queued as chat-3: job-1793116323641 (heavy, 8 h cap counting the queue). Product defect for later, owner whoever next needs wasm runs under a redirected target: spiral rust's wasm_path (spiral.spi:327) and its cleanup paths (spiral.spi:392) should resolve against CARGO_TARGET_DIR when it is set, so a caller's redirection doesn't break the run.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_31 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 31u32, "2026-10-27T20:18Z", "main", "10-27 16:18 main: Inventory of main's other products (blog, dice, alphabet, dir-tree-html; grep !!!!\\w+ over their .spi): exactly 1 site outside chat, dir-tree-html/shared.spi:4 ':= (<.) (left : char) (right : char) : bool = !!!!LT(left, right)', used once at tree/tree.spi:58 (left_ch <. right_ch) to order tree entries. It's a lib gap, not a shortcut: lib has no char ordering (no char compared with < anywhere in lib/spiral), and the compiler docs note that char 'only supports equality' where it isn't a number (the eBPF profile). Fix: a lib slice adding char ordering in the char/sm' operators, written over the existing code-point conversion so no host text is needed, with test blocks per backend; then dir-tree-html drops its local (<.) and uses it. After TRAIN publishes, per kit's lib cut-off. Chat's 6 Export sites stay with chat-3 (job-1793116323641, running). The blog (55 Cons/Nil sites converted to list sugar 16:0x, node proof running), dice and alphabet have 0 Cons/Nil and 0 !!!! sites.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_32 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 32u32, "2026-10-28T00:07Z", "main", "10-27 20:07 main: dir-tree-html's last !!!!LT drafted, TEMP dir-tree-char-less/apply.ps1 (dry run clean on the live repo). It drops shared.spi:4's (<.) operator, which wraps !!!!LT, and replaces its only use, tree.spi:58 in cmp_at, with (conv left_ch : u32) < (conv right_ch : u32). That's the lib idiom at xsd_regex.spi:911. Rust orders char by scalar value, which is the u32 order, so the render must be byte-identical. Proof: proof.ps1, the dir-tree-heal harness. It builds reference and healed copies with their --self-test and requires HTML byte equality over spiral/scripts, x/scripts and dir-tree-html, no unit over 1,000 lines, and 0 host macros in tree.spi. Queued as job-1793145529520 and stopped at 20:1x before it built, to give the box to the CCMR A/B. It requeues on 'CCMR landed'. Other !!!!LT sites seen in the scan are in kit (another team), the archived backlog and the Spiral-s-ML-Library/VS Code plugin cores (older eras).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_33 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 33u32, "2026-10-28T11:19Z", "main", "10-28 07:19 main: Inventory (main, 10-28 07:1x, Grep over the live trees, excluding deps and target). lib/spiral: 55 uses in 10 files. 31 are in .spir real-dialect modules (sm'_real 19, routes_real 7, json_real 5), where intrinsics are the dialect's primitives (out of scope). The 24 in plain .spi are each a single named wrapper, the target shape: am' create_base and set_base; base Export, Do, Add, Sub, Mult, Div; array_dim create, index, set, length; backend BackendSwitch dispatch (2) and Indent (6); console Printf (2, in a typecase); float_text concat (StaticStringConcat; could become sm' ++#, a one-line follow-up); sm' PrimToString in show's fallback. So lib is healed. Products: x 0, fiscal 0, dice 0, blog 0; dir-tree-html's last !!!!LT has its slice drafted (dir-tree-char-less, proof pending a slot); tibia 4 (terrain 3 and hunting_pack 1), already scheduled in TIBIA-EDITION3-ROUND onto am'.create_base, index_base and set_base. kit/src holds the bulk: 683 uses in 226 files, of which !!!!Export is 622 (91%), then StaticStringConcat 11, Global 7, LTE 6, NominalCreate 4, StringLength 4, UnionToRecord 4, SymbolToString 3, and a small tail. lib already wraps Export once (base.spi:17), so kit's 622 raw Export sites are one mechanical rewrite to that wrapper (kit's code, so kit's team: a kit-side slice, verified by byte-identical regen), and the remaining 61 are a small hand pass. Remaining scope: kit Export rewrite (kit), dir-tree char proof (main), tibia's 4 (tibia), float_text concat (main, trivial).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_34 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 34u32, "2026-10-28T11:51Z", "eoie", "07:5x kit: the kit/src slice is drafted. scratchpad clean\\bang-export\\rewrite-exports.ps1 rewrites every single-line !!!!Export(name, f) into lib's wrapper, export name (f) (base.spi:17, the form x already uses), with a paren- and string-aware argument split. It also adds spiral- to the package.spiproj of any touched package that lacks it, since export comes from lib's base-. On a tree copy: 578 sites in 200 files, 64 packages linked; the 47 multi-line or non-literal sites are left for a second pass. Byte-identity regen-compare on the node: job (kit-bang-export-regen), 205 crates, P2 DLL pinned. If it's 205/205 identical, it rides the release after TRAIN4.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_35 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 35u32, "2026-10-28T12:01Z", "eoie", "08:0x kit: the rewriter also handles the stacked multi-line form now: export, then the name on its own line, then the parenthesized body, all at the original indentation. That makes 623 of 625 kit sites in 215 files (2 non-literal sites left) and 64 packages given spiral-. The 578-site compare was stopped and replaced by job-1793188973244 (214 crates, P2 DLL pinned).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_36 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 36u32, "2026-10-28T13:43Z", "main", "10-28 09:43 main: dir-tree-html part DONE (10-28 09:3x-09:43). Proof GREEN (job-1793194605722, TEMP dir-tree-char-less proof.ps1): reference and healed copies both build and pass --self-test; HTML byte-identical on 3 trees (spiral/scripts 52CD6D8E, x/scripts EE3FFFD5, dir-tree-html B3226587); no Rust unit over 1,000 lines (largest inline.rs 912); 0 host macros in tree.spi. First attempt RED (job-1793194267634): '(conv left_ch : u32)' has no char instance (tree.spi:58 ETY-ConstraintError); the heal now uses lib sm'.char_code (a backend_switch, Rust arm u32::from), equivalent to the old char '<' because Rust orders char by code point. Landed into C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html at 09:43 (unstaged): shared.spi drops ':= (<.) ... = !!!!LT(left, right)', tree/tree.spi:58 becomes '|? sm'.char_code left_ch < sm'.char_code right_ch ?> -1i32'; both files byte-identical to the proven healed copies (6754BC0C, 3DEEF7ED). dir-tree-html now holds 0 '!!!!' sites (7 .spi files searched per folder, positive control sm'.char_code found 1). Remaining for the item: kit's !!!!Export regen and tibia's 4 sites. Also fixed: proof.ps1's Rust line census no longer recurses over the whole repo copy (source folders only).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_37 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 37u32, "2026-10-29T06:08Z", "main", "10-29 02:2x main: post-wipe census (git grep -F --untracked '!!!!' over *.spi per repo; compiler samples/tests, deps, backlog and target excluded; positive control: a scratch repo with one untracked !!!!Probe reports 1). First pass without --untracked read the control as 0, so every 'tracked-only' count misses lab and scratch files; counts below include untracked files. kit 688 sites in 232 files (Export 636, Global 7, StaticStringConcat 7, LT 5, UnionToRecord 4, EQ 4): the n34-n35 Export rewriter (623 of 625 sites) lived in kit's TEMP scratchpad and was LOST in the wipe (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY), as was its regen-compare job state; it must be rebuilt from n34-n35 (paren- and string-aware split, stacked multi-line form, spiral- added to touched spiprojs). tibia 4 (ArrayCreate, ArrayIndex, ArrayIndexSet, BackendSwitch; tibia team). polyglot 15 in 2 files (Export 6, Printf 5, Conv 2, Sin, Cos). spiral 404, of which 336 are untracked lab copies (SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS 320, mostly LayoutToHeap/LayoutIndex in copied mega families; they drain with their items), and the tracked rest is apps/compiler 36, lib/spiral 24 (lib is where wrappers legitimately hold the intrinsic) and apps/cells 8. 0 in x, dice, alphabet, dir-tree-html, fiscal, blog and i574n.github. Product work left: kit (rebuild the rewriter, then the 214-crate byte-identity regen), tibia 4, polyglot 15, cells 8, and the compiler's own .spi 36 after a per-site read (some may be the compiler's own intrinsic tests).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_38 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 38u32, "2026-10-29T06:16Z", "main", "10-29 02:2x main: the kit-slice Export rewriter, lost with kit's TEMP, is REBUILT as a generic org codemod (committable home, since it applies to any repo): i574n.github/scripts/bang-export-rewrite.ps1 -Root <repo or copy> [-Apply] (untracked). It rebuilds n34-n35's design. A paren-, bracket-, string-, char- and comment-aware scan finds each !!!!Export( call and splits it at the first top-level comma. Single-line calls become export \"name\" <f> (f kept as is when it is already one parenthesized group, so the output is x's exact form, e.g. export \"iggy_job_started\" ((\\ ...) : T)). The stacked form (!!!!Export( / name line with comma / body / closing-paren line) becomes export / name line / body at the original indentation, with the closing line dropped. Code after the closing paren, a non-literal name, and any file that defines export itself (lib base.spi, cells main.spi) are skipped and reported. Packages without spiral- get it inserted right after |core-, so every later, more specific package still shadows lib names as before; the 151 src packages that already list spiral- resolve lib the same way, with no packageDir. Dry run on the real kit: 218 files, 634 sites rewritten (261 single-line, 373 stacked) in 217 files, 64 packages given spiral-, 2 skipped (src/typed_predicate/model.spi:64 and :67, non-literal item.name). That matches n35's 64 packages and its 2 non-literal sites exactly. Applied to a scratch copy (1,319 .spi/.spiproj files): 281 files change (217 .spi, 64 .spiproj), only those 2 sites remain, 0 files gain CRLF, and the diffs are the forms above. NOT yet proven: a parse check (SpiralCompiler format --check on the copy, after main's oracle run, to keep its timeouts clean) and n35's byte-identity regen of every touched crate with the P2 DLL pinned (heavy: kit team or the node, which is still blocked on the key). Nothing written to kit.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_39 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 39u32, "2026-10-29T06:44Z", "main", "10-29 02:4x main: the codemod now also rewrites the 2 'non-literal' sites (src/typed_predicate/model.spi:64 and :67, !!!!Export(item.name, ...)). A name that is an identifier path is accepted, because export is an inline definition (lib base.spi), so the macro sees the same term, and the same module already passes a field path as a plain argument (line 70: inspected item.name). Dry run on the real kit: 636 of 636 sites in 218 files (263 single-line, 373 stacked), 65 packages given spiral- (typed_predicate is the 65th), 0 skipped. Still to prove, after main's oracle runs: the parse check (format --check, before and after) and the byte-identity regen.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_40 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 40u32, "2026-10-29T08:00Z", "main", "10-29 04:0x main: two product slices LANDED (unstaged), each proven byte-identical first. (1) apps/cells/spi: the 5 local '(++) ... = !!!!StaticStringConcat(left, right)' wrappers (cell, directives, document, notebook, text) become 'left ^^ right' (CARET-OPERATOR-ORIGIN: ^^ is the parser's StaticStringConcat). Copies compiled with --backend Gleam give the same domain.gleam before and after (7A2CC6E9E03AC97C, also the live file's hash), and after landing mix's spiral_domain compiler regenerated domain.gleam at 03:59 to the same hash. cells spi has 1 '!!!!' left: main.spi's local export wrapper (the package lists only |core-, no lib). (2) polyglot apps/chat/contract/chat_contract.spi: 6 stacked !!!!Export sites go through i574n.github/scripts/bang-export-rewrite.ps1; copies compiled with --backend Rust give the same chat_contract.rs (EE7B10970DD4B2CE, 1,387 lines); polyglot now has 0 !!!!Export (cube.spi's Sin/Cos/Conv/Printf stay: a deliberately intrinsic-only benchmark). CORRECTION to n39's plan: SpiralCompiler format --check is NOT a parse gate. A deliberately broken .spi gives exit 0 and no 'format error' (the formatter keeps unparsable blocks as written), so the kit copy's '0 format errors before and after' is VOID. kit's only proof is n35's byte-identity regen (kit team, or the node once the key works).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_41 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 41u32, "2026-10-29T12:51Z", "kit", "10-29 08:5x kit: the byte-identity proof for the kit slice is running on the node: job-1793277020393-kit-bang-identity. The rewrite was applied to a copy of the live kit/src: 624 sites in 215 files (252 single-line, 372 stacked), 65 spiprojs given spiral-, 0 skipped. draft-regen-bundle.ps1 reached 214 crates plus the agile_note_listing control; bundle sha256 1BC33285E8B4; P2 DLL A4E480202BD4, equal to the box's installed compiler. Scope, reconciled with main's 636/218 (02:4x, whole kit root): today the root has 635 sites in 217 files. The 11 sites in 2 files outside src are infra/a/iggy-client/codec/encode.spi (10) and decode.spi (1); they're outside the shipped crates and need their own identity check (their own build, or a second bundle root) before the rewrite touches them. The remaining 1 site and 1 file is kit_job_env/env_adopt.spi, already moved to lib export by the env guard. Plan (agreed with main): if the compare is identical, the rewrite rides TRAIN4 as a phase that re-applies it to the TRAIN4 tree and re-proves identity in that train's full regen; the iggy codec pair waits for its own check.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_42 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 42u32, "2026-10-29T14:09Z", "kit", "10-29 10:0x kit: PROVEN byte-identical on the node (job-1793277020393, 99 min, finished exit 0; compiler pinned explicitly: spiral-bin-p2 core 05E94769A86A9B9C / host A4E480202BD40D80, the box's install, so unaffected by the node's stale default compiler). bang-export-rewrite.ps1 -Apply on a copy of live kit/src: 624 sites in 215 files, 65 spiprojs given spiral-. Result: 215 of 215 crates identical=True (214 reached plus the agile_note_listing control), 0 candidate crates over 1000 lines. The one compile failure is path_tag_contract, which fails identically on base and cand ('ParserErrors' at model.spi:15, 'Expected one of: inl, let, union ...'), the same pre-existing failure GRANULAR-HEAL n87 recorded; it needs its own look. Plan (agreed with main): TRAIN4 gets a phase that re-applies the rewrite to the TRAIN4 tree, and that train's full regen re-proves identity. The 11 iggy codec sites (infra/a/iggy-client/codec) still need their own check.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_43 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 43u32, "2026-10-29T14:32Z", "kit", "10-29 10:3x kit: the iggy codec pair is PROVEN identical too, which completes the kit slice's proof: all 635 sites in 217 files (src's 624/215 in n42, plus these 11/2). infra/a/iggy-client/codec was copied base/cand (packageDir pointed identically at the node mirror kit-depstest's lib, because the node's own C:\\home\\git\\spiral checkout has no iggy.spi; the first attempt, job-1793284170409, was VOID with 'Unbound module iggy' on both sides). The rewrite took 11 sites (10 single-line, 1 stacked) in 2 files, 0 spiprojs. Node job job-1793284289184 (-RequireCore 05E94769A86A9B9C, P2 DLL A4E480202BD4): encode 348 lines and decode 916 lines, identical=True for both. Side finding: the node's own spiral checkout is stale (no iggy.spi), so node jobs must use a synced mirror's lib, never C:\\home\\git\\spiral there. Plan unchanged: the rewrite lands as a TRAIN4 phase on the TRAIN4 tree, re-proven in that train's full regen; the codec files are re-applied together with it.")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_44 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 44u32, "2026-10-29T19:49Z", "kit", "2026-10-29T19:49 kit: re-proof at pack-6b started on the TRAIN4c tree. bang-export-rewrite.ps1 -Apply on a .spi/.spiproj/Cargo.toml copy of live kit/src: 636 sites in 221 files (257 single-line, 379 stacked), spiral- added to 64 spiprojs, 0 skipped; 285 changed files reach 220 crates plus the agile_note_listing control (bundle FA0F9B557EBC). Node job job-1793303438170-kit-bang-identity-6b runs under -RequireCore 31CC96520D6B7269 (L6 guard ok) and resolves the node's installed compiler, replacing the 10:09 proof on the P2 DLL. Done = every crate identical=True; then it applies as its own TRAIN after TRAIN5 (it touches 221 files, so it gets its own train).")
inl note_of_bang_macro_cleanup_45 () = Note ("BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP", 45u32, "2026-10-29T20:56Z", "kit", "2026-10-29T20:56 kit: RE-PROVEN at pack-6b. job-1793303438170-kit-bang-identity-6b (core 31CC96520D6B7269, the node's installed compiler, L6 guard ok), finished exit 0: 221 of 221 rows identical=True (220 reached crates plus the agile_note_listing control), 0 compile failures, 0 missing backend arms. Two crates are over 1000 lines on BOTH base and cand (kit_standards 1024, kit_machine_windows 1009), so the rewrite didn't cause them; they're TRAIN4 growth, filed as KIT-CRATE-GATE-TRAIN4. The rewrite applies as its own train after TRAIN5 (221 files).")
