inl note_of_mega_samples_as_models_1 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-AS-MODELS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T16:17Z", "main", "10-31 12:17 main, RESEARCH DONE (read-only survey of the 5 mega samples vs lib/spiral; counts measured by regex scripts). IDIOMS (paths under apps/compiler/tmp/samples): typestate via unit nominals indexing ops by from/to state with existential middle states (omniledger main.spi:3-11, :117-171); branded string nominals as type indexes (:13-33, :92-94); type-level naturals from nominals, binary positional in zeta :12-23 with addition as a relation GADT :50-78, Peano meta_zero/meta_succ in spiral_proves :1-16, length-indexed vectors that need no fallback arm (brzozowski :75-97); proof-carrying Accepted cert | Rejected reason decisions instead of bool (cic :53-118); existentials \\? pack/unpack; prototypes+instances for comparison returning an ordering union (brzozowski :7-24); nominal-over-tuple data, 0 record fields; 98-100% annotated signatures; runtime code fenced to mega_runtime_fail and i64 wrappers; positive checks as *_terminal () : string claims aggregated in all_terminals, negative checks as negative_* sub-packages that must fail to type-check (no test blocks at all). brzozowski is the weakest model (18% GADT cases, bool predicates with '| _ => !-'). LIB SLOP, cited: stringly dispatch json_schema.spi:170-182, xpath.spi:58-69, xsd.spi:134-140, xpath_eval.spi:26-28; -1 sentinels sm'.spi:825/830/845/881, json_scan.spi:12/49/58, xpath_eval.spi:33-34/424; bool flags xpath_eval.spi:387/408/473, convert.spi:216; sign ints xpath_eval.spi:397-402; silent catch-all listm'.spi:28 (map4 truncates unequal lists); mutation am'.spi:477-479/586-591; untyped point-free listm'.spi:20/23/46/93/101. METRICS (strip test blocks, comments and macro text first; mega vs lib): M1 return-annotation coverage 98-100% vs listm' 45%; M2 bare-parameter defs 0% vs listm' 52%; M3 GADT case share 86-100% vs date_time 0; M4 indexed-union share 54-88% vs 0-33%; M5 existentials per 1k lines 9-61 vs ~0; M6 wildcard-arm ratio 1-6% vs 12-30%; M7 stringly dispatch per 1k 0 vs xpath 124; M8 sentinel ints per 1k 0-0.4 vs ~11; M9 bool/option in signatures per def 0 vs convert 1.36; M10 mutation per 1k 0 vs listm' 31.7; M11 type defs per 100 fns 24-41 vs 2-4. Score FFI-binding modules (base, convert, file_system: 115-254 macros/1k lines) separately. ML LIBRARY is not in lib/spiral: C:\\home\\git\\Spiral-s-ML-Library (old dialect; graph GADT ml\\layers.spi:24-55, type-level int literals corebase\\type_arith.spir:3-7). NEXT: the metrics as a repo tool (apps/cells/spi), report per lib file, then pick the worst files (xpath*, json_schema, listm') for modeling rewrites.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_as_models_2 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-AS-MODELS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T16:34Z", "main", "10-31 12:34 main: METRICS TOOL in the repo: apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1 -Path <files or dirs, comma list> [-Tsv out]. Strips test blocks (header + indented body), // and /// lines and macro text before counting; M1-M11 per file plus Kind = ffi when macros+intrinsics exceed 100 per 1k lines (score those separately). Validated against the survey: omniledger main.spi M1 98 / M2 0 / M3 86 / M5 14.5, zeta 99 / 0 / 90 / 60.9, listm' 45 / 52, base 83 / 15: identical. Whole lib: 110 files, 56 model + 54 ffi, saved %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\model-metrics-lib-20261031.tsv. Worst model files by a first combined score (100-M1 + M2 + M6 + M7 + 5*M8 + 10*M9): float_text 552, json_scan 441, decimal 210, sm'_operators 200, testing 190, json_schema 184, stream 167, xsd_regex 153, xpath 146, xsd 144. CAVEAT: M8 (sentinels) over-counts index-bound checks in parsers (float_text, json_scan: 'i >= 0i32'), so tighten it to -1 returns before ranking by it; M7 (stringly dispatch) agrees with the survey's reading (xpath 136, json_schema 101, xsd 81 per 1k). NEXT: tighten M8, then pick the first modeling rewrite (likely xpath/xsd dispatch on name strings -> a union).")
inl note_of_mega_samples_as_models_3 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-AS-MODELS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T16:38Z", "main", "10-31 12:38 main: M8 tightened to -1i32/-1i64 literals only (index-bound comparisons no longer count). Re-ranked model files: sm'_operators 200 (operator aliases: bare signatures are the norm there, read it per kind), json_scan 190 (its real -1 returns, the survey's :12/:49/:58), testing 190, stream 167, xpath 146 (M7 135.5), physics 127, xsd 122 (M7 81.3), json_schema 118 (M7 101.1). First rewrite candidates: xpath/xsd/json_schema name-string dispatch -> unions, json_scan -1 -> option.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_as_models_4 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-AS-MODELS", 4u32, "2026-11-01T03:40Z", "main", "main 23:4x WIP groom (user 23:3x: drift/stall, too much waiting): Active -> Planned. metrics ranked (n3); feeds TYPEFEATURESET work when code is touched; no separate step running.")
inl note_of_mega_samples_as_models_5 () = Note ("MEGA-SAMPLES-AS-MODELS", 5u32, "2026-11-01T14:35Z", "main", "main 10:3x (user 11-01: 'the mega samples shouldn't be a sota measure yet because they don't use prototypes, that means all of that code could've been modeled even better while leveraging peak gadts/existentials/hkts/reflection ... the projects will compete with cognitive cannibalism'). So the scoreboard (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT) must not treat the mega samples as the ceiling: prototypes become a scored dimension, and the reference model is a per-concept best example from any repo, not the mega samples as a set.")
