inl note_of_x_edition3_respell_10 () = Note ("X-EDITION3-RESPELL", 10u32, "2026-10-28T11:38Z", "x", "2026-10-28 07:38 x: 10-26 round APPLIED (tree, unstaged), the first run on the installed compiler after the compiler team confirmed the edition-3 features ship in it (DLL A4E480202BD4). i574n.github/scripts/respell-repo.ps1 -Name x -Root C:\\home\\git\\x -Compiler <installed DLL>: 67 files, 59 respelled, 337 test headers kept as written, 0 errors, words round trip byte-identical for every file, and the installed formatter normalizes 21 on top (net +50 lines: splits only, no joins; 0 lines over 120). Member and module access is now :: (sm'::replace, e::base; 62 files). Before applying, x-compat on the respelled COPY found 3 cells pushed over one post by the added ':' (wire post_json 283 > 271, sim memory_watch grown 276 > 273, scenario_checks frame_edit_shape 273 > 272). Fixed in the tree first with behaviour-neutral helpers (post_named, complete_after, framed_edit_count), then the respell re-run: x-compat 0 in 43 client + 24 sim files on the respelled copy, and on the tree after applying. checks.spi is not respelled, so the e2e resume fixture in world.json (hand-made from its text on 10-25) stays valid. Originals: %TEMP%\\x-respell-originals-1028 (67 files). Proof: verify28 (job-1793187520986, installed compiler, mirror xv28); its e2e and sim accepts regenerate the README thread/dry-run outputs and the sim fixtures that quote respelled sources. Left in this round's scope: the 51 raw !!!! exports to lib wrappers, then X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY.")
