inl spiral_zwsp_transparent () = Task ("SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT", "Lexer drops U+200B everywhere (code, string literals, macro text), so a post the x poster defused compiles byte-identically when pasted back; an intended zero-width space is written as an escape. Today 'st<U+200B>.head' is a TokenizerError and 'st.<U+200B>head' a ParserError (10-26 probe); 0 raw U+200B in any .spi/.spir (10-26 scan), so no program changes. Tests: st<U+200B>::head lexes as st + symbol; a string literal holding main<U+200B>.rs equals main.rs; macro text keeps its bytes minus U+200B", Story, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX", "team:compiler,lexer,x-compat,edition3,migration", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_zwsp_transparent () = Planning ("SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT", Minutes 90u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_zwsp_transparent_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:35Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: layer L3 of the X-compliance compromise (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX note 11): foreign text that X would link or tag (about 700 sites: file names main.rs, Gleam @external, C #include, PowerShell $env) stays as written and the poster defuses only those sites (X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY).")
inl note_of_spiral_zwsp_transparent_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT", 2u32, "2026-10-28T10:59Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-28 DONE: U+200B fully transparent in the installed core 9FF1B708 -- spiral_compiler.fs:43376 (let zwsp = char 0x200b; strip + position remap in tokenize_line, both anchors). Composed into 5n via lexer-zwsp-apply.ps1 + blessed. Functional re-run delegated to consuming lanes vs installed; reopen on red.")
inl spiral_macro_sigil_escapes () = Task ("SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES", "Macro text writes a literal '@' as '@@' and a literal '#' as '##' (today '\\@' and '\\#'; '\\@intCast' is an X mention and '\\#app_' a hashtag, while '@@intCast' and '##include' match no X entity); the macro lexer (Tokenize.fs p_text/p_expr ~396-409 and its spiral_compiler.fs copy) accepts both spellings during the transition, respell maps '\\@' <-> '@@' and '\\#' <-> '##', and the 83 entity-shaped escape sites migrate in the round. Optional '$$' for a literal '$' (2 existing '$$' sequences to check first). Regression sample: Zig '@@intCast(@@as(i32, !x))', Rust '##[cfg(windows)]'", Story, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX", "team:compiler,lexer,macros,x-compat,edition3,migration", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_macro_sigil_escapes () = Planning ("SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES", Minutes 150u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
