inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 30u32, "2026-11-01T03:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 23:41 fiscal: PAUSED (groom 10-31 night; it sat at the top of the light queue while not workable, which is how a window wait turns into idling). REASON: the round is held on EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL (main's, 95%, compiler pack 9); its drafts were also archived as stale against today's generator. RESUME CONDITION: EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL reaches Done; then resume as Active and re-derive the edition-3 respell from the current tree with format --spelling symbols, proving generated output byte-identical as on 10-29.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 31u32, "2026-11-01T03:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 23:58 fiscal: RESUMED (re-decided on main's word that EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL is Done: pack 10, Cells manifest.ex landed). The round needs only fiscal's own manifest (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML, Done), not lib's spiral.toml, so it does NOT wait on LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION. The held Cells spiral.toml program (n of 16:46) is RETIRED, replaced by main's manifest.ex; never land it. NEXT (CPU-light): re-derive the respell from the current tree (generator.spi now includes the bench-line edit, directory_create_all) with format --spelling symbols, and draft it on a scratch copy. Then (node): ONE regeneration proving generated output byte-identical to the edition-2 tree plus the bench-line change, shared with FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE n15.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 32u32, "2026-11-01T04:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 00:40 fiscal: RESPELL RE-DERIVED from the current tree (incl. tonight's generator edits and the DIAN/RO port). respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 (excluding generated/deps/bench) is GREEN on copies: 5 files, 4 respelled, 0 errors, words round trip differs 0; the installed formatter (pack 10 DFC86B91968D) re-lays 2. Extra check: the concatenated string-literal content is identical in all 5 files, so the respell cannot change emitted unit text and generated/ stays byte-identical by construction. Draft at scratchpad e3-src: 5 .spi, package.spiproj with edition: 3 as its first line, and spiral.toml from format --manifest toml (edition = 3). SCOPE: src only. The 32 generated units' package.spiproj are generator output (module_package) and stay edition 2, which their text is; converting them is a FOLLOW-UP generator change. PROOF: node mirror t1101 (synced from the tree), draft overlaid, then node-e3-regen.ps1: the generator cell at edition 3, format-generated, a check that generated/ changes only by the bench + samples-folder lines, then corpus/lifecycle/corpus_checks gates. Queued after the t1031 set-all job.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 33u32, "2026-11-01T04:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 00:55 fiscal: overlay refreshed before the regen job started: the respell was re-derived with the new pint_rules_read_fully test (still GREEN, 5 files, 0 errors, round trip 0, literals identical); t1101 src/corpus_checks.spi = DF6D8854.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 34u32, "2026-11-01T05:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 03:35 fiscal: overlay refreshed again before the job started: t1101 generator 367522F1 (respell of the tree, which now has the CL EnvioDTE prefix fix; literals identical to the tree's) and corpus_checks A5F2E6D3 (EN16931 981 pin). node-e3-regen.ps1 now runs pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write before the src gates (the mirror has no gitignored pattern files). EXPECTED unexpected-change list: generated_cl_envio_dte_v10 only (xmlns:SiiDte on the root). Lib route checked: each notebook resolves the mirror's fiscal\\deps\\spiral junction (process.spi BE258A03), not the node's stale C:\\home\\git\\spiral.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 35u32, "2026-11-01T05:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 03:45 fiscal: RESPELL TRAP SWEEP (main's warning: keyword-anchored source regexes match nothing after --spelling symbols, so gates count 0 and pass). fiscal scripts: build.ps1:44 already accepts ^(test|:#); delphi-reach.ps1:13 already accepts := and inl; delphi-reach.ps1:16 ^(test |///) -> ^(test |:# |///) (unstaged; this round keeps test headers as written, but a later -SymbolTestHeaders run would have broken it silently). sefaz/scripts/candidate-gate.ps1:29 ^inl xsd_table_ -> ^(inl|:=) xsd_table_. No other script anchors on test/inl/let/open/type/union. The src tests' \"inl ...\" checks read generated units, which this round keeps in edition-2 spelling; they must be revisited when the emitter itself moves to edition 3 (the follow-up on generated manifests).")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 36u32, "2026-11-01T12:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:40 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). PRIORITY P0: every later emitter change (cluster B, 9 items in deps) waits on it.\nDONE WHEN: node job-1793506463392 prints (a) \"generator.spi / ... failed 0\" with the 14,400,000 ms cap, (b) \"changed beyond the bench + samples-folder lines\" = generated_cl_envio_dte_v10 + the CR units only, (c) \"corpus.spi / lifecycle.spi / corpus_checks.spi ... failed 0\"; then the tree''s src/*.spi equal the t1101 overlay hashes (respell-repo -Apply), src/package.spiproj starts \"edition: 3\" and src/spiral.toml exists (format --manifest toml), and CI is green on the push that carries them.\nNEXT STEP: read the job''s \"e3-regen /\" lines when it finishes; then pwsh i574n.github/scripts/respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 -Root C:\\home\\git\\fiscal -Exclude ''generated/*,deps/*,bench/*'' -Compiler <pack 10> -Apply, and copy package.spiproj + spiral.toml from the scratchpad e3-src.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: none by design. The respell is mechanical and must not change emitted text (checked: the concatenated string-literal content of all 5 files is identical before and after). Model changes ride the cluster-B items after it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 37u32, "2026-11-01T12:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:40 fiscal: PROOF PROGRESS: job-1793506463392 (t1101) gated the edition-3 respelled generator at 08:04: 23/23 passed, 0 failed, under the 14,400,000 ms cap (the set-all run lost this gate to the 1,400 s cap). It is now in format-generated / src gates. Its 4 node dotnet processes (17084/21816/13564 from 07:00, 10908 from 08:19) are idle compiler servers in its own tree: left for the job's end-of-tree reaping, checked after it ends.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 38u32, "2026-11-01T12:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:41 fiscal: CORRECTION to n37. The 3 node dotnet processes 17084/21816/13564 were NOT this job's: x proved them its own (command lines name spiral-cells-19304-, erl 19304 = x-verify46's client notebooks, the only node job at 07:00) and stopped them. I had attributed them by start time and a broken parent chain without reading the full command line. 10908 (under 18792, 08:19) is unattributed. At this job's end, check survivors by command line (spiral-cells-<erlpid> naming its job), never by a pid from a log. Idle orphans like these come from the CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT leak main is fixing.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 39u32, "2026-11-01T13:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:31 fiscal: PROOF RESULT (job-1793506463392 finished): generator 23/23 under edition 3 (cap 14,400,000 ms); format-generated 81/81; regeneration changed 44 files, and after normalising the size-derived timeout header + the bench/samples-folder lines only the predicted 7 remain (cl_envio xmlns:SiiDte + 6 CR units Canton/Distrito 00 -> 01); corpus 1/1, lifecycle 4/4; corpus_checks 23/26: (a) resolves_the_nfe_tree + resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet fail in rustc ONLY under edition 3 (E0425 undeclared st; filed EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN for the compiler lane, P0; same tests pass in edition 2 on CI and t1031u), (b) en16931_rules_parse_completely: a THIRD stale 1.3.17 pin, \"23 code-list tests become member tests\" (XML count of padded contains/concat member tests in 1.3.17: 24), fixed in the tree to 24 with the actual count in the message. DECISION: the respell is NOT applied to the tree until EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN is fixed; the regenerated units (edition-2 emitter output, identical text) ARE brought home now because CI needs them. Mirror t1101 kept as the compiler repro.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 40u32, "2026-11-01T13:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:41 fiscal: UNBLOCKED: EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN is fixed (pack14a) and verified by a box rerun of both resolves tests in edition 3 (2/2). All parts of the proof are now green or fixed: generator 23/23, corpus 1/1, lifecycle 4/4, corpus_checks resolves 2/2 (box), en16931 member pin fixed to 24 (counted from the XML; engine confirmation on the next CI run, whose message now prints the actual). ORDERING DECISION: the respell is NOT applied to the tree yet. The user's next commit is the CI-green one (44 regenerated units + pins + Windows retry, edition 2), and CI compiles with spiral main from GitHub, which must contain pack14a before an edition-3 src can pass there. NEXT: after that commit's CI is green AND pack14a is in spiral main, run respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 -Root C:\\home\\git\\fiscal -Exclude 'generated/*,deps/*,bench/*' -Compiler <installed> -Apply, copy src/package.spiproj (edition: 3) and src/spiral.toml from the scratchpad e3-src, and leave it unstaged for the user.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 41u32, "2026-11-01T13:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:50 fiscal: CONDITION (b) IS A USER STEP (main): pack14a's source is the live, unstaged spiral apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs (sha256 prefix F6F6879566C5A830, checked on the box); it reaches CI only when the user commits and pushes spiral (CI clones https://github.com/i574n/spiral.git main, per fiscal init.ps1). WATCHER armed (fiscal session background bh3hoy321): every 10 min it reads i574n/spiral main's head and, when it moves, downloads apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs at that commit and compares the hash; it prints \"PACK14A IN SPIRAL MAIN\" on a match. Then (and after the CI-green commit) apply the respell.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 42u32, "2026-11-01T13:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:58 fiscal: RESPELL APPLIED to the fiscal tree (unstaged). Trigger: the watcher saw pack14a in i574n/spiral main at 7a4c960e (09:52; apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs F6F6879566C5A830), so CI compiles with the fixed backend. Condition (a) (a separate CI-green commit first) is DROPPED on purpose: its only purpose was to keep an edition-3 src away from a CI without pack14a, and that risk is gone, so one commit saves a 2.5 h CI cycle. Applied with respell-repo.ps1 -Name fiscal-e3 -Apply (4 files respelled + formatted; restore: robocopy %TEMP%\\respell-repo\\fiscal-e3\\original C:\\home\\git\\fiscal /E) plus src/package.spiproj (\"edition: 3\") and new src/spiral.toml. The tree src is now byte-identical to the gated e3-src: corpus_checks 8CE3E213, corpus 54066D22, fiscal_paths D1AAA4C5, generator E187DAD2, lifecycle ABB9021B, package.spiproj C98B264E, spiral.toml A2445EBD (generator 23/23, corpus 1/1, lifecycle 4/4 on node; corpus_checks resolves 2/2 on box pack14a). DONE WHEN: CI on the user's next push (which carries this + the 44 regenerated units + the 283/24 pins + the Windows retry) concludes success on both OSes; the watcher is armed.")
inl note_of_fiscal_edition3_round_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", 43u32, "2026-11-01T18:46Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 14:4x: DONE. All three gates are met on CI run 41314140694 (push f6abb23, the edition-3 commit). (1) Generated code: \"generated / matches the committed copy\" on both OSes. (2) Fiscal tests: every src unit green on ubuntu AND windows-2025: generator 23/23, corpus_checks 26/26, lifecycle 4/4, corpus 1/1. (3) x-compat: 0 findings in each unit's output, plus 0 on the new src/canon.spi (node gate 11-01 14:44). Remaining windows red = 7 generated units crashing the compiler (COMPILER-WIN-STACK-OVERFLOW, fixed by the compiler lane, ships as pack15a). That failure predates edition 3 (every push since 10-25) and is tracked under FISCAL-CI-WORKFLOW.")
inl eoie_edition3_round () = Task ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", "eoie: run the 10-26 edition-3 round on the eoie repo in one review: spiral.toml for its 435 package.spiproj, member access .x -> ::x, word keywords (3,112 line-start, 3,319 if/match), 113 Cons ( -> :: sugar, macro sigils @@/##, 803 raw !!!! -> lib wrappers, formatter (2,354 lines > 120, 29 comment lines), 280-weight split; gates: every crate byte-identical per class (the rsIntended gate), regen manifest, x-compat 0 findings", Story, P0, D5, 0u32, Planned, "SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX,SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES,SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT", "team:eoie,edition3,migration,x-compat,kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_edition3_round () = Planning ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", Minutes 480u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_1 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 1u32, "2026-10-26T06:36Z", "x", "2026-10-26 02:35 x: round scope EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION note 32; X-compliance layers SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX notes 10-11. Classes in order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), lexer respells (keywords, ::, Cons sugar, macro sigils), macro wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP lib helpers), formatter, 280 split (EDITION3-280-SPLIT); one identical-output gate per class.")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_2 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-10-26T06:55Z", "eoie", "02:55 eoie: inventory remeasured on the working tree (the KIT-RENAME release already applied the edition-3 respell to 843 files tonight; the round's counts came from git HEAD at 01:52). Scripts: kit scratch clean\\respell\\edition3-left.ps1, keyword-sample.ps1, keyword-sample2.ps1.\n- Line-start keywords: 3,112 by the round's regex, but 2,927 of them are Rust 'let' inside multi-line host macro blocks, not Spiral and out of scope for a respell (they leave with GRANULAR-HEAL host-block migration). Of the 185 real inl/union/type lines: 85 are fixture text inside triple-quoted strings (they mimic agile state rows; leave them); about 100 are real Spiral the respell skipped: every one is a binding whose right side opens a triple-quoted string (inl kinds = triple-quote, inl emit_runtime () : () = rust_global triple-quote). A respell gap, reported on SPIRAL-FORMATTER.\n- Flow keywords: 2,662 by a rough regex, likely inflated the same way (Rust if/match in host blocks); recount with macro text excluded before planning.\n- Cons ( : 119. Raw !!!! : 767. Lines over 120: 2,332. Comment lines: 5. package.spiproj: 431, spiral.toml: 0.\nSequencing: all classes start after KIT-RENAME publishes (eoie feature freeze; the tree is under the release lease now). Order: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter), the ~100 respell-gap sites once the respell handles them, Cons sugar, !!!! wrappers (BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP), formatter; each class through the identical-output gate (rsIntended plus the regen manifest, proven on the worker node first).")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_3 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-10-26T07:05Z", "eoie", "03:05 eoie: Cons class ready. The existing converter (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar.ps1, balanced-paren aware, rewrites Cons (a, b) as a :: b) dry-ran on a copy of the renamed and respelled tree: 113 sites in 19 files across 15 packages (kit_repo_affected 36, kit_log_sequences 21, kit_mirror 17, kit_env_pins 9, kit_do_verbs 8, ...), 0 skipped, 0 left, 0 doubled parens. Gate: list sugar is syntax for the same constructor, so every touched crate must regenerate byte-identical. Node proof script ready (clean\\respell\\node-sugar.ps1: convert on a mirror, regen the touched crates, compare every .rs hash before and after; verdict 'codegen-neutral' only at 0 changed). It runs when the node's strict notebook chain finishes (node at 100% CPU now), and the class lands right after KIT-RENAME publishes.")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_4 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-10-26T07:08Z", "eoie", "03:08 eoie: keyword class recounted with macro bodies, triple-quoted strings and plain strings stripped (kit scratch clean\\respell\\keyword-recount.ps1): line-start word keywords 106 (the respell-gap bindings, SPIRAL-FORMATTER note 85), flow keywords 9 (then 3, if 3, with 3). So eoie's real keyword work is about 115 sites, not the round inventory's 3,112 plus 3,319; the rest was Rust inside host macros and string fixtures. The class waits only on the respell handling bindings whose right side opens a triple-quoted string.")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_5 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 5u32, "2026-10-26T07:28Z", "eoie", "03:28 eoie: the Cons class's node proof caught a converter bug: 13 of 14 touched crates regenerated, but kit_crate_gate/gate.spi:44 did not type-check (Got: list string, Expected: string). 'Cons (dir </> name, acc)' had become 'dir </> name :: acc', which parses as dir </> (name :: acc) because the custom operator binds looser than ::. Fixed: the converter parenthesizes a head with any top-level infix operator, and a tail with any operator other than :: (right-associative, so chains stay bare). Test 9/9 (kit scratch clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar-test.ps1: the path operator, ++#, ++ in the tail, a negative literal, a comma in a string, glued member access, a pattern). Proof rerunning on the node (job kit-sugar-proof-3).")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_6 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 6u32, "2026-10-26T07:33Z", "eoie", "03:33 eoie: Cons class PROVEN codegen-neutral on the worker node. With the precedence-fixed converter (heads with a top-level infix operator and tails with an operator other than :: get parens; test 9/9), all 113 Cons ( sites in 19 files were converted on a mirror of the renamed tree, the 14 touched crates regenerated (ok), and 0 of 260 generated .rs changed. The class is ready to land right after KIT-RENAME publishes: run clean\\list-sugar\\cons-to-sugar.ps1 -Root src -Apply, then the identical-manifest check.")
inl note_of_eoie_edition3_round_7 () = Note ("EOIE-EDITION3-ROUND", 7u32, "2026-10-26T08:21Z", "eoie", "04:21 eoie: status of the two waiting classes. The compiler lane's edition-3 lexer core (9E1F72AB) built clean on the worker node at about 04:1x (single-flight Debug, 0 errors): the :: member access, the macro sigil respell (@@ and ##) and the ZWSP strip/remap all compile; behavioral probes are next on their side. When their respell pairs land (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT), eoie's '.x to ::x' and sigil classes run through the same identical-output gate as the Cons class: convert on a node mirror, regenerate the touched crates, require 0 changed generated .rs. Ready now (after KIT-RENAME lands): Cons (proven), the Global wrapper cleanup with its census probe (drafted, gate written), stop_cli and harness fixes (node proof running). Waiting: manifests (EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML converter, main), the ~106 keyword sites (SPIRAL-FORMATTER note 85 respell gap).")
inl lib_edition3_round () = Task ("LIB-EDITION3-ROUND", "spiral repo (lib/spiral, apps, samples) plus dice, alphabet, polyglot, blog, dir-tree-html: run the 10-26 edition-3 round in one review: spiral.toml for 1,251 + 9 package.spiproj (the upstream core keeps package.spiproj), member access .x -> ::x, word keywords (28,318 line-start, 14,427 if/match in spiral), Cons ( -> :: sugar (spiral 230, blog 55), macro sigils @@/##, raw !!!! -> lib wrappers (spiral 3,580, polyglot 15, dir-tree-html 8, dice 4), formatter (136 lines > 120, 75 trailing-space lines), 280-weight split; gates: Cells --gate, matrix, generated code identical per class, x-compat 0 findings", Story, P0, D5, 0u32, Planned, "SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX,SPIRAL-MACRO-SIGIL-ESCAPES,SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT", "team:main,lib,edition3,migration,x-compat,main", "current", "current")
