inl xsd_any_content_reader () = Task ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", "xsd_emit: generated readers keep xs:any content instead of reading it as Nil (CT-e/MDF-e lose their whole modal section)", Story, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "FISCAL-TYPEFEATURE-DRIFT", "team:fiscal,xsd,xsd_emit,reader,correctness,data-loss", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_any_content_reader () = Planning ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_1 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 1u32, "2026-10-27T04:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 00:19 fiscal: FOUND by the ours bench's round-trip check (compare-roundtrip.ps1, namespace-normalized, node job-1793060915958): parsing each family's own example with its generated reader and writing it back LOSES DATA in 5 of 12 families: CT-e v2.00/v3.00/v4.00 ('/CTe/infCte/infCTeNorm/infModal: missing modal') and MDF-e v1.00/v3.00 ('/MDFe/infMDFe/infModal: missing modal'). Those schemas put the transport-mode payload (road, air, rail, water, pipeline) under an xs:any inside infModal. Cause: xsd_emit's reading stage hard-codes 'any_part reading = any = Nil', so every generated reader silently discards wildcard content, while the writer writes x.any and the example puts a modal element there. For CT-e and MDF-e this drops the whole modal section of a real document without any error. Fix direction: the reader captures the children that no named element of the record claims (in document order) into the any field, instead of Nil: any_part reading needs the list of the record's own element names (from the walked parts) to filter children. Gate: the bench round-trip reports roundtrip-equal for CT-e and MDF-e; acyclic families without xs:any keep their bytes; regression test: a record with a wildcard reads back an unknown child unchanged.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_2 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 2u32, "2026-10-27T07:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 03:34 fiscal: DRAFTED and TYPE-CHECKED on the live tree: session scratchpad recgroups/any_content_transform.py edits two lib files. xml.spi gains named_in and unclaimed_children (claimed names -> list xml_node -> the child elements whose local name no named element claims, in document order; test unclaimed_children_keep_only_unknown_elements). xsd_emit.spi gains claimed_names (every element tag of a record's content particle tree) and with_any_claims, applied at the single record_texts call site in record_walk: it rewrites only the reader's '        any = Nil' line to 'any = xml.unclaimed_children [<the record's element names>] children' (the exampling stage writes [xml.element ...] and the writer x.any, so neither matches); test a_wildcard_reads_the_children_no_named_element_claims. Checks: xml, xsd_emit, both test probes and json_schema 0 errors; no new over-120 lines. Node proof queued: job-1793086574129-fiscal-ac-proof after the full build. PASS rule (pre-written): transform applies; true baseline then fixed regeneration; generator 0 failed, 0 memo hits; every moved module reads its wildcard through xml.unclaimed_children; CT-e v2/v3/v4, CT-e Simp v4 and MDF-e v1/v3 each read their own example AND round-trip EQUAL (modal preserved).")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_3 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 3u32, "2026-10-27T08:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:21 fiscal: IN THE TREE, unstaged (per the user's WIP-in-repo practice; backup + both repos' git diff --cached in the session scratchpad backups/wip-drafts-20261027-0419, staged diffs verified unchanged). lib/spiral/xml.spi 321990D4F9120C50 and xsd_emit.spi 9EF79DB949E83D96 now hold this draft together with XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS (same two files; the combination with the emptiable readers type-checks: xml, xsd_emit, probe_xml, probe_xsd_emit, json_schema, fiscal generator + probe all 0 errors, installed formatter applied). One revision since note 2: named_in compares LOCAL names, so a prefixed claim (ds:Signature, cbc:ID) still claims its element. The node proof (job-1793086574129, queued after the full build) now applies the emptiable readers first, since CT-e Simp reads its example only with them; its pass rule is unchanged.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_4 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 4u32, "2026-10-27T10:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 05:57 fiscal: PROOF PASSED (job-1793086574129-fiscal-ac-proof, node, exit 0, 0 broken claims, mirror restored hash-verified). Every pre-written claim HOLDS: the emptiable readers applied first (baseline = post-landing emitter); true baseline regeneration exits 0; the transform applies; the fixed regeneration exits 0 with every generator test run and passed (0 memo hits); it moved 12 modules and EVERY moved one reads its wildcard through xml.unclaimed_children; CT-e v2/v3/v4, CT-e Simp v4 and MDF-e v1/v3 each read their own example and measure a row; and each of them now ROUND-TRIPS EQUAL (modal preserved). Whole round-trip table for ours: 15 of 15 measured families roundtrip-equal (CFDI, CT-e OS v3/v4, CT-e Simp v4, CT-e v2/v3/v4, FatturaPA, GTV-e v3/v4, KSeF, MDF-e v1/v3, NF-e v2.00/v3.10). Rows (node, us parse / serialize): CT-e v2 580/446, v3 834/648, v4 776/615, CT-e Simp 1993/1673, MDF-e v1 841/665, v3 1194/915. For contrast, DFe.NET on the same documents round-trips 0 of 10 equal (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n38). The code is already in the tree unstaged (xml.spi 321990D4, xsd_emit.spi C6282D52). 90%, not Done: the local same-box bench (job-1793094391561-fiscal-local-bench) regenerates from the TREE copy itself; it closes this item when its CT-e/MDF-e rows and round trips match.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_content_reader_5 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", 5u32, "2026-10-28T10:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:31 fiscal: DONE: in the live lib since 10-27 04:21, proof job-1793086574129 0 broken claims; node set-proof 10-27/28, compiler 4FD712E9E357: xml lib gate 14/14 incl claimed_children_keep_the_named_elements_in_order; CT-e/MDF-e units green (job-1793152028390).")
inl xsd_imported_namespace_elements () = Task ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", "xsd_emit: write elements in the namespace of the schema that declares them (UBL cbc:/cac:), so multi-namespace documents validate", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "XSD-RECURSIVE-TYPE-GROUPS", "team:fiscal,xsd,xsd_emit,ubl,namespaces,correctness", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements () = Planning ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_1 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T05:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 01:54 fiscal: FOUND once UBL main compiled (XSD-RECURSIVE-TYPE-GROUPS proof job-1793077378367). The generated UBL example is <Invoice xmlns=...Invoice-2><ID>1</ID><IssueDate>..</IssueDate><AccountingSupplierParty/>...: every element is written in the Invoice namespace, but UBL 2.1 takes its vocabulary from imported schemas, so ID/IssueDate must be cbc: (urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:schema:xsd:CommonBasicComponents-2) and AccountingSupplierParty etc. cac: (CommonAggregateComponents-2). Validation (with the validator fix below): 'The element Invoice ... has invalid child element ID in namespace ...Invoice-2'. Single-namespace families (NF-e, CT-e, MDF-e, CFDI, FatturaPA, KSeF) never needed this, which is why it is invisible elsewhere. Fix direction: carry each element's target namespace (from the schema that declares it, honoring elementFormDefault and element refs into imported schemas) into the writer, emit a prefix per namespace on the root (xmlns:cbc / xmlns:cac) and the reader matches on local name + namespace. Also visible in the example: required aggregates written empty (<AccountingSupplierParty/> needs Party), a second, example-side gap. Gate: family-gates reports 0 validation messages for generated_ubl_invoice_2_1_example.xml; the other 16 samples stay at 0. VALIDATOR FIX landed unstaged in fiscal/scripts the same night: UBL's xmldsig-core schema carries a DTD, which .NET prohibits by default, so the UBL schema set never compiled ('xmldsig#:Signature is not declared') and family-gates reported a 'fatal: null-valued expression' instead of validating; validate-example.ps1 now loads preloaded schemas with DTDs ignored, gained -Resolve (keep the resolver alongside preloads), and reports a fatal's script line; family-gates preloads UBL's xmldsig with -Resolve. Regression: all 16 node samples still 0 messages through the new scripts.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_2 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T07:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 03:38 fiscal: DESIGN from a code read (no compile yet). Where the namespace is lost: xsd.spi takes an element's name from name= or ref= (line 229), so a UBL reference starts as 'cbc:ID' / 'cac:AccountingSupplierParty'; xsd_resolve.merge keeps ONE target_namespace for the merged schema; and xsd_emit's dereference pass replaces a ref-only element by the global element it names ('Element { root ?| occurs = e.occurs }'), whose name is the unprefixed 'ID'. So the prefix exists in the model and is dropped at dereference. Plan, four small changes: (1) dereference keeps the referencing element's (prefixed) name: Element { root ?| occurs = e.occurs; name = e.name }, so the writer emits cbc:ID; (2) xml.children_named compares local names on BOTH sides (today local_name name = target), so readers keep matching prefixed targets; a generic, safe lib change; (3) the root element declares every prefix the document uses (xmlns:cbc, xmlns:cac, ...), taken from the root schema's declared namespaces (xsd_resolve.declared_namespaces), the same way the generator already adds xmlns and with_namespace adds xmldsig; (4) field names use the local name (field_name (local_name ...)), so record fields stay prefix-free and acyclic families keep their bytes. Single-namespace families never use refs with prefixes into another namespace, so they should stay byte-identical (to verify with the true-baseline regeneration used for the emptiable proof). Also visible in the UBL example and separate: required aggregates written empty (<AccountingSupplierParty/> needs cac:Party), an example-side gap to look at once the namespaces are right.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_3 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T08:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:21 fiscal: DESIGN REVISED after a census, and IN THE TREE unstaged (xml.spi 321990D4, xsd_emit.spi 9EF79DB9, fiscal src/generator.spi 80043D5F; type-checked with the emptiable and xs:any drafts; the backup is in the session scratchpad backups/wip-drafts-20261027-0419). Census of prefixed refs: cbc 1360 + cac 881 (UBL), but ALSO ds: in NF-e (77), CT-e (31+18), MDF-e (9), FatturaPA (3), UBL (33). Keeping the prefix at dereference alone would write <ds:Signature xmlns=...xmldsig#> with ds undeclared, which is invalid XML in four families that are green today. So the draft is five changes: (1) dereference keeps the ref's prefixed name; (2) xml.children_named / count_named compare local names on both sides; (3) xml.with_namespace renames the element to its LOCAL name when it adds the default xmlns (the prefix is redundant there and may be undeclared), so BR Signature output stays as today; (4) field_name snake-cases the local name, and the two 'choice_' ++# first compositions take xml.local_name first, so BR field names do not churn; (5) generator.spi declares on the example root every xmlns:<p> of the root schema other than the target, XSD and xmldsig namespaces (prefix_declarations). New tests: a_prefixed_target_matches_the_same_local_element, a_default_namespace_drops_the_element_prefix. Known limit: prefixes declared only by an imported schema (sac/sbc/sig, inside UBL extension content) are not declared on the root. Next: node proof = true-baseline regen, BR modules byte-identical or Signature-only moves, then the UBL example validates (validate-example -Resolve) with 0 messages.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_4 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 4u32, "2026-10-27T08:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:47 fiscal: node proof QUEUED: job-1793090714004-fiscal-ns-proof (after the xs:any proof). It also proves the generator's new bench test (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n36). Inputs are staged hash-verified: base = the pre-draft tree (xml D55BBB83, xsd_emit DD404B4E, generator 9BA3862A) plus the emptiable and xs:any transforms; candidate = the tree now (xml 321990D4, xsd_emit C6282D52 as landed, generator 2B17149C). PASS rule (pre-written): both regenerations exit 0 with every generator test run and passed (0 memo hits); with each module's new <module>_bench_runs block set aside, ONLY generated_ubl_* modules move (every BR, CFDI, FatturaPA and KSeF module byte-identical, so the ds:Signature handling and the field names are unchanged); every listed family's module carries its bench test, and all 16 print a bench row 'parse_us N write_us N runs 31 bytes N' (UBL included: it reads its own example once the namespaces are right); family-gates exits 0 (every sample validates with 0 messages, the UBL example included); mirror restored hash-verified. Round-trip rows are reported, not gated (UBL's empty required aggregates are a known example-side gap).")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_5 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 5u32, "2026-10-27T08:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 04:50 fiscal: PASS RULE CORRECTED before the run (ns-proof still queued; node copy hash-verified 2C348373). Two defects in note 4's sample claim, found by reading family-gates.ps1: (1) it never sets an exit code from validation results, so 'family-gates exits 0' checked nothing; (2) 'the UBL example validates with 0 messages' also needs the empty required aggregates fixed, a separate example-side gap, not what this item claims. Replaced by: every non-UBL '== <sample>' section reports 'validation messages 0'; and the UBL example, validated directly with every message shown (-Show 2000), has NO message naming a child element in the Invoice namespace (the wrong-namespace symptom). The regex was controlled both ways: it matches the real wrong-namespace message shape and does not match an 'incomplete content' message. The other claims are unchanged.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_6 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 6u32, "2026-10-27T10:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 06:48 fiscal: ns-proof (job-1793090714004) claim BROKEN, by the rule as written: with each module's bench block set aside, 17 modules moved, not only generated_ubl_*. Every move is explained from the candidate output (the local same-box bench regenerated the same tree, so its generated/ is this candidate): (a) 14 BR families + FatturaPA now emit the ref's qualified name in lookups, e.g. cte_v4 line 16125 'xml.required_child \"ds:Signature\" children' (cte_v4 14 such lines, nfe 4, mdfe_v1 2): same element, since readers now compare local names; behavior evidence: generated_cte_os_v3_00 (12 such lines) passed 3 of 3 tests including its bench test, which reads its own example; (b) CFDI's example root now declares xmlns:catCFDI and xmlns:tdCFDI, prefixes cfdv40.xsd uses only in type= references, never in element names: dead declarations, a real flaw in prefix_declarations. Note 3 of this item had anticipated 'Signature-only moves'; note 4's stricter rule omitted them, so the rule was miscalibrated, not the behavior. NEXT, rule pre-written before the rerun: (1) fix: prefix_declarations declares a prefix only when the root schema text contains ref=\"<prefix>: (UBL's Invoice schema refs cbc:/cac:/ext:, CFDI refs none, so CFDI's root returns to its old bytes); (2) rerun claim: after setting the bench block aside AND normalizing every '\"ds:' to '\"' in both texts, ONLY generated_ubl_* modules differ; plus all the other claims of note 4/5 unchanged. The rest of this run's claims (bench rows, sample gates, UBL namespace messages) are still reported when it ends.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_7 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 7u32, "2026-10-27T11:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:50 fiscal: ns-proof FINISHED (job-1793090714004, exit 1). HOLDS: both regenerations exit 0 with 0 failed / 0 memo hits; every listed family carries its bench test; 15 of 16 families measure a bench row through the generator's new <module>_bench_runs test (node, us parse/write: NF-e v2 1033/773, v3.10 2357/1720, CT-e v2 609/450, v3 717/536, v4 1267/853, CT-e OS v3 753/545, v4 1570/1210, CT-e Simp 1806/1528, GTV-e v3 1432/1081, v4 1483/1102, MDF-e v1 662/526, v3 608/471, CFDI 237/165, FatturaPA 617/465, KSeF 583/391), so the append_bench port is proven; all 15 measured families round-trip EQUAL; every non-UBL sample validates with 0 messages (16 sections). BROKEN: (1) the module-move claim, already explained in note 6 (Signature-only lookups + CFDI's dead prefix declarations; the CFDI fix is in the tree since 06:5x); (2) UBL: its unit timed out again at the 1,200 s cell budget (units build exit 1), so it wrote no sample, so neither its bench row nor the namespace check could run. UBL's compile time is now the blocker for this item and for the seven UBL-based country items (Peppol, ZATCA, MyInvois, SUNAT, DIAN, RO_CIUS, UBL-TR). Next: measure the UBL rust cell alone on the node with a raised budget (phases: target vs compile), then decide between a higher budget and a smaller module (XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS / FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES shrink every module).")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_8 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 8u32, "2026-10-27T12:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:51 fiscal: the UBL blocker is resolved by budget, not by code: UBL's unit passes in 2,852 s (rustc 92%), and the generator now scales each module's cell budget with its size (FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE note of this time). The next regeneration proof (with the CFDI prefix fix) can now check UBL's bench row and its namespace messages.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_9 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 9u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. xml's a_prefixed_target_matches_the_same_local_element and a_default_namespace_drops_the_element_prefix pass.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_10 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 10u32, "2026-10-30T02:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:02 fiscal: GROOM, END-TO-END EVIDENCE: fiscal-6b-set-ublj2 (pack 6b, mirror ublj6b, 10-29 16:21-20:26) HOLDS 'the UBL Invoice example has no child element in the wrong (Invoice) namespace (0 such messages)' for regenerated generated_ubl_invoice_2_1. That is this story's correctness claim on a real regeneration, not only the 10-27 lib tests. Not closed: the same run's json round trip fails on all 22 UBL-JSON documents (FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS n16-18), which may or may not be namespace-related. Its 7 dependents (Peppol, ZATCA, UBL-TR, MyInvois, SUNAT, DIAN, RO_CIUS) can't close before this one; decide next session whether the JSON size drift belongs here or to MyInvois.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_11 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 11u32, "2026-10-30T15:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:25 fiscal: the namespace claim on the regenerated UBL Invoice is still VOID: fiscal-p7-set-ublj2 timed out in generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 at its 85-min cell budget under node load (details FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS, this time). Rerun fiscal-p7-set-ublj3 (job-1793373950641-fiscal-p7-set-ublj3) gets a mirror-only 3x budget; the 10-29 pack-6b HOLDS (n of 10-29 22:02) stands as the latest real evidence.")
inl note_of_xsd_imported_namespace_elements_12 () = Note ("XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", 12u32, "2026-10-30T22:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:52 fiscal: CLOSED. fiscal-p7-set-ublj3 (job-1793373950641, mirror p7ublj2, live lib, pack 7, mirror-only cell budget x3 so the unit could finish): 'HOLDS / the UBL Invoice example has no child element in the wrong (Invoice) namespace (0 such messages)', the same claim as 10-29 pack 6b, now on the live lib. The 10-29 open question is DECIDED: the UBL-JSON drift belongs to FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS. The diagnostic shows the typed JSON path ADDING nodes (408 -> 430 at ID//ExtensionURI), only in the 22 UBL-JSON documents, so it is not a namespace fault; the XML documents read back fine. Dependents unblocked: Peppol, ZATCA, UBL-TR, MyInvois, SUNAT, DIAN, RO_CIUS.")
inl kit_wip_todo_markers () = Task ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", "In-tree WIP as typed TODO markers shown beside backlog items: register harvest roots, read every comment prefix, typed marker fields, one merged list/next view", Story, P1, D4, 80u32, Active, "", "kit,todo,wip,agile,wipe-redo,team:kit,kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_wip_todo_markers () = Planning ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_1 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T08:16Z", "kit", "04:1x kit, groomed with the compiler lane (user 2026-10-27 03:2x: WIP files live in their proper repo place unstaged from the start, never in temp; refinement: in-tree WIP tasks must be typed enough to show ALONGSIDE backlog items in one merged view, not a separate todos list). Rule: an unstaged file plus one TODO: <ID> marker per incomplete site (TODO-AS-SOURCE grammar), and agile todos --id X is the WIP inventory for X across repos. Milestones (estimate by them): M1 roots: agile roots on the backlog returns roots=0 (compiler lane 04:0x), so todos harvests nothing; register spiral, i574n.github, eoie, x, fiscal, tibia. M2 prefixes: confirm or add # (ps1) and // in .fs (the scan's sibling logic is .spi-shaped). M3 marker schema: ID + what is left + typed fields (kind, load, estimate, assignee) parsed from the marker, so a TODO renders as a task row. M4 merged view: agile list/next show TODO rows beside items (a source column: backlog or file:line), filters apply to both. Accept: list on the backlog shows the compiler lane's two LIB-IGGY-CLIENT markers in lib/spiral/iggy.spi as rows.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_2 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T08:21Z", "kit", "04:2x kit: M1 done, M2 measured. M1: agile roots add registered C:/home/git/{spiral,i574n.github,eoie,x,fiscal,tibia} (roots 0 -> 6). M2 probe (throwaway folder, kit.exe installed 10-26): '# TODO: ID' in .ps1 and '// TODO: ID' in .fs harvest (todos=2, scanned=2). Two gaps: (a) a .fs/.ps1 whose same-stem .spi sits beside it is skipped as generated (probe.fs + probe.spi: skipped generated:2), right for Spiral outputs but it also hides a hand-written twin; (b) an F# block marker '(* TODO: ID ... *)' on one line did not harvest. The compiler lane's iggy.spi markers (lines 121, 189) both harvest; 189 is flagged wide (over 120 columns). Next: M2 fix for (b) and a precise generated rule for (a) (generated only when the file carries the compiler's output header, not by sibling alone), after kit-release-SLICES frees the tree.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_3 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T09:06Z", "kit", "05:2x kit, M3/M4 design written before building. Marker grammar stays TODO-AS-SOURCE compatible: '<leader> TODO: <ID> [field=value ...] <what is left>', where optional typed fields come right after the ID and before the prose. Fields reuse the backlog's own field words and value sets (kind=Story|TaskKind|..., load=light|medium|heavy, est=<minutes>m, who=agent|pair|user, prio=P0..P5); an unknown field or value is a finding (like wide), never silently dropped. Every marker without fields still parses (all 12 harvested today stay valid). Row model: a todo_row union (BacklogRow item | MarkerRow site) where site = { id; file; line; fields; text }. A marker inherits unspecified fields from its item, so a bare marker renders as a task row with its parent's planning fields and its own what-is-left title. M4 view: agile list/next take --with-markers (later the default once it is measured) and print marker rows directly under their item, indented, with a file:line source column; filters (--team, --load, --ready) apply to the inherited and the overridden fields alike; next can return a marker row as the next unit of work. Acceptance: the compiler lane's iggy.spi marker shows under LIB-IGGY-CLIENT in list --with-markers with load and estimate inherited, and a marker with est=30m overrides the estimate. Harvest cost: a full harvest over 6 roots took 147 s (13,778 files), so list caches harvested rows by file mtime under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit and rescans only changed files (target: list --with-markers under 3 s warm).")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_4 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 4u32, "2026-10-27T10:30Z", "kit", "06:3x kit: M2 gap (b) fixed in a draft and proven. Cause: .fs/.fsx/.fsi were classified CFamily (leaders //|/*), so the F# block leader (* never opened a comment. Draft clean/kit-rename/fsharp-todo-family.do (agile_todo_model/model.spi, 9 replacements): a new FsharpFamily case appended last (leaders //|(*), so existing path-verdict codes, which are case indices, stay stable; fs|fsx|fsi move to fsharp_family_extensions; syntax_label 'fsharp'; tests for the path label, the block-closer strip and the case code 12. Proven on a full src copy: applies 9/9, todo_lines and todo_paths compile. Behavior check: the generated todo_lines.rs, run directly on a two-marker F# text, finds 1 marker as syntax 1 (old CFamily) and 2 as syntax 12 ((* TODO: ... *) with the closer stripped, plus // TODO). Gate note: todo_lines.rs grows from 983 to 997 lines, 3 under the 1000 limit, so the next leader family must come with a :~ cut there. Lands after kit-release-SLICES drops its lease. Gap (a), a hand-written .fs/.ps1 beside a same-stem .spi being skipped as generated, is still open: the rule should look for the compiler's output header rather than the sibling alone.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_5 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 5u32, "2026-10-27T11:48Z", "kit", "07:5x kit: landed in the kit tree (unstaged) at 06:38 and 07:48: the F# family fix, plus a size cut that gives M3 room. todo_lines.rs was 997/1000 with the F# family; todo_in_line alone was 272 generated lines, because comment_leaders (a 12-arm := lambda), comment_text, directive_line and outside_quotes were each inlined twice. With all four as :~ (program clean/kit-rename/todo-lines-cut.do, 4 replacements): 898 lines (-99). The behavior check re-ran on the cut build: same results (CFamily 1 marker, FsharpFamily 2). Both ride kit-release-SLICES (agile_todo_model's crates are in its regen list). Next: M3 typed marker fields in agile_todo_model (marker_fields parsed after the ID, inherited from the item, unknown field reported like wide).")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_6 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 6u32, "2026-10-27T12:12Z", "kit", "08:1x kit: M3 typed fields built and proven, staged to land after kit-release-SLICES. (1) agile_todo_model/marker_fields.spi, a granular module that is lib-first (sm', convert.try_convert, am'): typed union marker_field (KindField, LoadField planning_load, EstimateMinutes, AssigneeField, PriorityField, UnknownField); words after the ID parse as key=value until the first plain word; a bad key or value becomes UnknownField, never a silent drop; fields_json, unknown_count, tail_after. agile_todo_model now references the lib (spiral- was missing, against the AGENTS contract). (2) finding_json is migrated off concat5 to ++# and emits a typed fields object for markers with an ID. Test block: typed_marker_fields_parse_before_the_prose. (3) Size: inlining the parser put todo_lines at 1,286 lines, so it is a hand-split build unit, the new crate agile_todo_fields (393 lines) exporting kit_agile_todo_fields(id, comment), which todo_lines calls through one macro (907 lines). Behavior, run on the generated Rust (todo_lines plus the fields crate as a path dependency): a three-marker F# text gives fields {est:30, load:light, who:pair}; {unknown:load=huge, kind:Story}; {} for a bare marker. Landing: clean/kit-rename/m3-fields-apply.ps1 (staged files plus a guarded apply; it refuses while a release is queued, when model.spi moved from its staged base, or on any other drift). Next: M4, the merged list/next view with inherited fields.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_7 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 7u32, "2026-10-27T18:56Z", "kit", "kit 14:5x, M4 design written before building (base: the post-TRAIN tree, M3 included). (1) A new crate, agile_todo_merge, because agile_task_listing is at 978/1000. It exports kit_agile_todo_columns(root), which returns typed parallel columns (ids: array string, counts: array i32, untracked: i32) across the Export boundary, never joined-string rows: the census ratchet refuses those. (2) Cache: harvesting every registered root on each list is too slow, so findings are cached per file, keyed by (path, size, mtime_ms), in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\todo-cache\\<root sha8>.spi as typed Spiral data written by kit, never in the backlog repo (git noise). Only changed or new files rescan; deleted files drop out. (3) Views: 'agile list --todos' adds a wip=<n> column per item (markers whose ID names the item), and a trailing 'untracked wip: <n> markers without an ID' line. 'agile next' is unchanged in M4; ranking by markers waits for a measured need. (4) Done check, rule first: on the six registered roots, list --todos equals a recount from 'agile todos --json' (same per-ID counts), and a second run with no file changes reads the cache only (0 files rescanned, from the receipt) and takes under 25% of the first run's time. Starts after TRAIN installs; M3 rides TRAIN.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_8 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 8u32, "2026-10-27T20:28Z", "kit", "kit 16:2x, M4 baseline measured (the installed kit, the shared backlog's 6 registered roots, the box under release load): one full 'agile todos' harvest takes 99.4 s, listing 13,241 files, scanning 4,148 and skipping 6,124 generated and 2,965 by syntax; it finds 10 markers (1 stale). So an uncached merged view is not usable inside agile list. The cache from note 7 is required, not an optimization. Its rule stands: a no-change rerun must take under 25% of this. Building blocks for the new crate, read from the post-train tree: agile_todo_sources.kit_agile_todo_sources(path) gives the listing; agile_todo_paths.kit_agile_todo_path_verdict(relative, spiral_sibling) gives the per-file verdict; agile_todo_lines.kit_agile_todo_findings(code, only, backlog, text, display, json) gives the findings (JSON objects carry an id field); agile_todo_lines.kit_agile_todo_id(backlog, comment) gives the item id. agile_todo_scan (993/1000) cannot grow, so the merged view stays out of it.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_9 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 9u32, "2026-10-27T20:33Z", "kit", "kit 16:3x, M4 cache format decided. It was open after note 8: the lib writes TSV via csv.tsv_line but has no parser, and hand-split tab rows are what the census refuses. The cache reuses the backlog's own typed record codec. Each scanned file gets one row, inl c_<n> () = Cached (\"<relative path>\", <size>u64, <mtime_ms>u64, \"<ID> <ID> ...\", <untracked>u32), written with the agile record writer's quoting (spi_quoted) and read back with agile_task_text's tuple_field walk, the same parser agile list and census use on state/agile.spi. That gives no TSV, no new parser and no census flag, and the cache is a readable Spiral file. Location: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\todo-cache\\<sha8 of the backlog root>.spi. Next: the agile_todo_merge crate (walk via kit_agile_todo_sources and kit_agile_todo_path_verdict; a cache hit skips the read; a miss calls kit_agile_todo_findings), then agile wip <root>, then list --todos.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_10 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 10u32, "2026-10-27T20:55Z", "kit", "kit 16:5x, M4 built and run on the node. A new crate, agile_todo_merge (scratch clean/wip-merge: merge.spi, package.spiproj, Cargo.toml; merge.rs is 834 generated lines), has a test block covering finding ids, the cache row round trip and an mtime change counting as a miss. Four new boundary primitives in rust_std_fs: file_byte_size, file_modified_ms, spiral_sibling_of and scan_text_of (fs-scan-primitives.do). Routing for 'agile wip <root>' is wip-routing.do: AgileWip is a non-mutating route, kit_agile_mutation goes to 802, and it composes with the seal routing. The walk reuses kit_agile_todo_sources, kit_agile_todo_path_verdict and kit_agile_todo_findings; the cache is typed Cached rows (note 9) in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\todo-cache. Node run, debug build of a probe binary that calls kit_agile_wip_run on a copy of the shared backlog (6 roots): the cold run scans 2,787 files; the warm run takes all 2,787 from the cache and rescans 0, with item lines byte-identical between the runs. Counts agree with 'agile todos' (9 markers): 3 on open items (KINO-WITHOUT-ELIXIR, KINO-HOT-PATHS, DIB-MODERNIZE), 5 untracked, and 1 stale (an ID of a Done item, not printed yet). Found while proving it: a probe binary must run its entry on a 1 GiB stack thread, as Spiral's generated mains do; the default 1 MB stack overflowed on the 11k-entry listing recursion. Timing against the note-7 rule (a warm run under 25% of cold): FAILED. Run 1: cold 42.9 s, warm 23.8 s (0.56). With a moving cache cursor (to rule out the cache scan): cold 43.9 s, warm 27.0 s (0.63). So the lookup was never the cost: with 0 files read, the warm time is the 11k-entry listing (kit_agile_todo_sources per root), the per-file verdicts and 3 metadata calls per scanned file. For scale, the existing 'agile todos' took 53.8 s and 109.7 s on the same busy node, so the cold wip run is already faster than it. Next experiment, rule first: time the listing alone; if it is over half of the warm time, cache each root's listing keyed by the root's git index mtime (or skip unchanged directories by their mtime), and rerun the same pair. Debug build, probe binary on the node; agile wip is not routed into kit yet (wip-routing.do, staged).")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_11 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 11u32, "2026-10-27T21:06Z", "kit", "kit 17:0x, M4 timing continued (node, probe binary, same backlog copy). Listing alone, all 6 roots: 3.6 s and 5.0 s (spiral is 10,652 of 11,065 entries; the node's kit root is a junction, so the lister skips it). Release build: cold 37.7 s, warm 11.3 s (0.30), a second warm run 16.1 s. With the sibling stat deferred until a path is a non-.spi scan candidate: cold 49.7 s, warm 23.2 s (0.47), a second warm run 17.3 s. The run-to-run spread on the busy node (warm 11.3 to 23.2 s) is larger than either change, so one pair per arm cannot decide; the deferral showed no gain and cost +65 generated lines (861 -> 926), so it is reverted. The rule is still unmet (best warm/cold 0.30 vs < 0.25). Next measurement, rule written now: 5 alternating cold/warm pairs per arm on a quiet node (no release or gate running), compared by median. If the median warm is still over 25% of cold, the next cut is caching each root's listing keyed by its directory mtimes.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_12 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 12u32, "2026-10-28T12:24Z", "eoie", "08:2x kit (corrected after reading agile_todo_sources): why the warm/cold rule can't be met by the per-file cache alone, and the design that can. Inside a git work tree, the source list comes from 'git ls-files -co --exclude-standard -z' (todo_sources.spi:58-62), so build folders are already excluded by .gitignore; only non-git roots are walked by hand (vendor folders skipped). The 3.6-5.0 s listing cost in note 11 is therefore that git call plus the per-entry path verdict and size/mtime stat over 10,652 spiral entries. A warm run still stats every listed file to validate its Cached row, so its floor is that per-entry work. Design, M5 (git-delta cache): store each git root's HEAD commit and the dirty set from its last scan beside the Cached rows. On a warm run, if HEAD is unchanged, only the paths in 'git status --porcelain=v1 -z' now or at the last scan are re-checked; if HEAD moved, add 'git diff --name-only <cached HEAD> HEAD'. Every other cached row is reused without a stat. Non-git roots keep the per-file stat. Rule, written before measuring: build M5, then measure 5 alternating cold/warm pairs on the node as it is (no waiting for quiet, per the standing direction), compared by median. Adopt if the median warm/cold ratio is under 0.25 on the full root set; if not, record the numbers and park M5 with the per-root breakdown. Measured on the node after TRAIN4 (needs a fresh probe build).")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_13 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 13u32, "2026-10-28T12:29Z", "eoie", "08:3x kit: M5 (git-delta cache) drafted, not yet compiled. (1) agile_todo_sources gains git_head (rev-parse HEAD) and git_changed_since: a NUL-separated list from 'git diff --name-only --relative -z <commit>' plus 'git ls-files -o --exclude-standard -z', relative to the root like ls-files. Exported as kit_agile_todo_git_head and kit_agile_todo_git_changed (scratchpad clean\\wip-merge\\git-delta-sources.do). (2) merge.spi (M4 kept as merge.spi.m4-backup): per git root the cache stores RootHead (root, HEAD, dirty paths of that run). On the next run, changed = diff since the cached HEAD + current dirty + the last run's dirty set; the last set covers a file that was dirty and has since been reverted. A listed path outside changed reuses its Cached row found by path alone (cached_row_of), with no verdict, no stat and no read. Anything else goes through the M4 path (file_scanned). Non-git roots and git failures fall back to M4 entirely. The test block now also covers lookup by path and the head-plus-dirty round trip. Next: node compile plus probe, then the 5-pair measurement under the note-12 rule.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_14 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 14u32, "2026-10-28T12:50Z", "eoie", "kit 08:4x, M5 self-review before the first compile found one cost bug and one correctness gap, both fixed in the draft (scratch clean/wip-merge/merge.spi). Cost: in trusted mode every unchanged listed path looked up its row by path, but only scanned files had rows. The ~7,800 entries skipped by path verdict or size (10,652 listed, 2,787 scanned) each missed and searched the whole cache text twice, which would have made the warm run slower than M4. Every listed path now leaves a row: Cached (...) for a scanned file, Skipped (\"path\") for a path the verdict or the size cap skips. The cache follows the git listing order, so each lookup lands just past the cursor. Correctness: a path's verdict depends on whether a .spi sibling exists (spiral_sibling_of, Rust with_extension). A path now counts as changed when it or its sibling (spiral_sibling_relative, with dotfile and double-extension cases tested) is in the changed set, so a new x.spi turns x.rs generated on the next warm run. Also: when the cached HEAD equals HEAD, the second git diff is skipped (moved = dirty). New test rows: a skipped row is found as skipped, a cached row after a skipped one, an unseen path is a miss, the sibling cases, and whole-path matching in the changed set. Proof scripts, written before any run: wip-m5-revert.ps1 builds a scratch git repo plus a one-root backlog and expects 7 (untracked, scanned) pairs: cold 1/1, dirty edit 2/1, revert 1/1 (from the last dirty set), unchanged 1/0, commit moving HEAD 2/1, committed Rust file 3/1, new Spiral sibling 2/1. wip-m5-pairs.ps1 runs 5 cold/warm pairs and applies the note-12 rule (median warm/cold under 0.25 means adopt). apply-wip.ps1 now also applies git-delta-sources.do. Next: compile and both proofs on the node once the box is free.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_15 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 15u32, "2026-10-28T14:43Z", "eoie", "10:3x kit: the first node regen of M5 (job-1793193076004) put agile_todo_merge at 1322 generated lines, over the 1000 gate (M4 was 834). The ranked generated functions show the cache text format is the bulk: cached_row_of 104, cached_head_of 55, the old size-and-mtime cached 54, head_row 44, row_key and cache_row 30 each, ids_in 31. Split by hand into a new crate, agile_todo_cache (scratch clean/wip-merge/cache/cache.spi): ids_in, cache_row, skipped_row, number_between, row_of, head_row and head_of, exported with plain types. row_of returns (kind 0 miss / 1 skipped / 2 cached, size, mtime, ids, untracked, tail). merge.spi keeps the walk and calls them through one-expression cross-crate wrappers, rebuilding row_lookup from the tuple. The old size-and-mtime 'cached' lookup is gone: file_scanned uses the by-path lookup and compares size and mtime itself, so one search per file instead of two. The round-trip tests moved with the format (cache_rows_round_trip_by_path_and_by_root: ids, row by path, skipped, cached and unseen rows, head and dirty set round trip, unknown root); merge keeps words, siblings and changed paths. Both modules carry '///> _' above main. Wiring: agile-todo-cache dependency, workspace member, apply-wip copies the crate. The same run's other failures (clip, first_line, split_nth unbound in base and candidate) were my bundle: the TRAIN4 base needs the land-window lib. The rerun (job-1793198615614) uses the gated lib copy on both sides, with every pending draft applied together (13 programs, all clean, 91 crates).")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_16 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 16u32, "2026-10-29T22:42Z", "kit", "2026-10-29T22:40 kit: shipped in TRAIN4c (installed kit C528BE4D). kit agile wip lists in-tree markers next to backlog items (closeout PASS: items=4 markers=4 untracked=5). It took 130 s with 4367 of 4381 files cached, during the notebook run; re-time it on a quiet machine before calling the view done.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_17 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 17u32, "2026-10-31T13:07Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 09:0x kit: PERF BUG FOUND, fix in the tree (unstaged). Every 'agile set <id> <p> Done' costs about 2.5 MINUTES for every lane, because agile_done_route (kit_agile_routes) first runs agile_todo_scan::kit_agile_todo_sites(root, id) over all 6 harvest roots (spiral, i574n.github, x, fiscal, tibia, kit) to refuse the close while a TODO names the item. MEASURED on the installed E14F1F0B: 'agile todos <backlog>' listed 13,653 files, read 4,382, elapsed_ms=126,544 (about 29 ms per file read). On a copy of the live backlog, a Done set printed elapsed_ms=1011 but ran 149 s wall, 0.6 cores of pure CPU, no child processes. Active->Active on the same copy took 1.6 s. Tonight's 10-item close batch took about 2 min per item for this reason; it isn't new in E14F1F0B, since the guard predates it. FIX: in read_and_scanned, when an id filter is set (state.only) and the file text doesn't contain the id (byte_find_from < 0), count the file as scanned content with 0 todos and skip crate_findings' comment parse. A marker always names its id literally ('TODO: LIB-IGGY-CLIENT M3 ...'), so no match can be lost, and the roots_cli fixture (set A-1 Done refused while a TODO names A-1) guards that. Census ratchet ok. Ships in TRAIN7 (after main's gap for Cells window 6 and pack 10); acceptance = a Done set on the live backlog under 10 s wall, plus the roots_cli refusal still firing.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_18 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 18u32, "2026-11-01T01:06Z", "kit", "10-31 21:1x kit: REGRESSION in the n17 prefilter, caught before TRAIN7 and fixed. The prefilter skipped a file unread when it lacked state.only, but --tagged sets only=\"*\" (meaning any tagged marker, not literal text), so a tagged scan skipped every file without a literal * and reported todos=0. The node TRAIN7 preview (candidate 923AAF5A) failed todo_cli.spi todos_flag_blocks_whose_item_is_done_or_missing (\"missing /b.spi:1 // TODO: WORD declared\", todos=0). TRAIN6 (4983F9C0) never had the prefilter, and the train5e/6 todo_cli passes were reused from an older run's log, so nothing earlier could catch it. FIX (domain first): agile_todo_model gains text_may_hold (filter : todo_filter) (text) = only TodosOf wanted needs the id in the text, AllTodos and TaggedTodos always read; todo_scan calls negated (text_may_hold (todo_filter_of state.only) text), so the \"*\" meaning stays in todo_filter_of alone. Test only_an_id_filter_lets_a_file_be_skipped_unread. PROOF: node job-1793492637691-kit-node-todo-lint2, candidate FB34FD11 (30 owners regenerated): agile_todo_model/model.spi 12/12, todo_cli.spi 4/4. Ships with TRAIN7.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_19 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 19u32, "2026-11-02T14:38Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is TODO-AS-SOURCE; recorded here instead of as a dep (sole dep on an unfinished parent epic hid it from 'agile next'; AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT).")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_20 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 20u32, "2026-11-02T18:40Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 14:45 GATE from main's TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH n2, measured on the node with TRAIN11. Writes: source markers take 1-2 ms vs agile.spi notes at 1.5 s for 1 writer and 4.3 s p50 / 10 s p95 for 4-8 writers; agile.spi lost 0 of 72 concurrent writes. Query: `agile todos` over 925 files took 17.4 s, SLOWER than `agile list` at 8.4 s, and that is the one adoption blocker under the pre-registered rule. TODO (kit): (1) make todos answer within list's time, with a changed-file prefilter (mtime/hash index over the registered roots) or a cached index. agile_todo_cache exists; check why it isn't serving the scan. (2) Double count: todos reported 80 BENCH markers where 40 were written. Suspect overlapping registered roots or one file reached through two roots/junctions; dedupe by canonical path before counting. Re-run main's bench after both.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_21 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 21u32, "2026-11-02T22:55Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 18:5x DOUBLE COUNT root-caused and fixed (main's bench: 80 markers found where 40 were written). Reproduced with the installed kit on a scratch backlog: one TODO file is counted 2x when the same root is registered in another spelling (C:/x and C:/X/; roots add only refused a byte-identical path), and 3x when a nested root (C:/x/src) is added too, because each root is walked on its own. Junctions are NOT the cause: the walker skips them (links:1). FIX (unstaged, ships next train): agile_todo_model.roots.root_added refuses a root whose key equals, sits inside, or contains an existing root. The key is slash-normalized and lower-cased for drive-letter paths; POSIX paths keep their case, and a sibling like C:/work/repository vs C:/work/repo is still allowed. Model test a_root_in_another_spelling_or_tree_is_refused passes 3/3 on vultr; agile_todo_roots regenerates to 609 lines. The live registry's 6 roots are already disjoint. The query speed half of the gate (todos 17.4 s vs list 8.4 s) is still open.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_22 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 22u32, "2026-11-02T23:08Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 19:0x QUERY SPEED profiled on the live registry (box, sharing with TRAIN13c): gile todos = 437 s for roots=6 files=14031 scanned=4675 (skipped: generated 6238, syntax 3115, vendor 3). That's ~31 ms per listed path, far beyond main's 17 s on a 925-file copy. Cause (todo_scan.spi scanned_file): EVERY listed path pays entry_kind_of (stat) plus spiral_sibling_present (stat) before the path-only verdict, then file_size (stat) and a full read for candidates, and nothing is cached: agile_todo_cache (path+size+mtime keyed, used by gile wip) is not consulted by gile todos. PLAN: (1) compute crate_path_verdict on the relative path first and stat/read only ScanPath candidates (saves ~9.3k of 14k path visits); (2) consult agile_todo_cache per candidate and re-read only changed files; (3) gate: warm todos <= agile list time on the same registry, cold todos measured and recorded. todo_scan.rs is 937 lines, so the cache reader likely goes in its own crate.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_23 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 23u32, "2026-11-02T23:28Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 19:3x STEP (1) DONE (unstaged): todo_scan classifies each listed path by its relative path first and touches the disk (entry kind, Spiral sibling, size, read) only for scan candidates; the sibling check still decides generated .rs. Proof on vultr: todo_cli 4/4, roots_cli 3/3, record_cli 1/1, todo_scan.rs unchanged at 937 lines; old vs new binary on the same 13,260-file registry give identical results (scanned=4087 todos=9). Linux wall time is 3-7 s either way (stats are cheap there), so the 437 s is a Windows file-access cost; the box A/B runs after TRAIN13c releases the heavy slot. Step (2), the cache, follows if the box still misses the list-time gate.")
inl note_of_kit_wip_todo_markers_24 () = Note ("KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", 24u32, "2026-11-04T20:59Z", "kit", "11-04 22:4x kit groom: still waiting on an INSTALL, not idle. Step (1) (path-first classification in todo_scan, proven on vultr 11-02) never reached the box: trains 15-22 all failed or timed out, so the installed kit is still TRAIN14c. TRAIN23 (running on the node since 15:56, every crate sized under 1000 first) carries it. NEXT: once TRAIN23 installs, the box A/B (`kit agile todos` old vs new on the live registry; the 11-02 baseline was 114 s / 94 s vs `agile list` 2.5 s) decides whether step (2), the cache, is needed. Side finding today: a note on this item contains a raw BEL (0x07) from a \"\\agile\" escape, which makes `agile show --json` invalid (filed as a repro on LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE).")
inl kit_scratch_watch () = Task ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", "Daily deterministic workspace watcher: place deliverables parked in scratch into their repos or archive the experiment, never delete, with periodic backups of every repo unstaged layer on both boxes", Story, P2, D4, 50u32, Planned, "", "kit,backup,drift,upkeep,team:kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_scratch_watch () = Planning ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_1 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 1u32, "2026-10-27T08:16Z", "kit", "04:1x kit (user 2026-10-27 via the compiler lane: a daily deterministic watcher that prunes tmp/scratchpad workspaces across lanes and mines each lane's drift into a generic workflow; 'we should have periodic code backups, they're cheap'). Example drift #1: WIP deliverables parked in session scratchpads instead of their repo (fixed 03:2x). Shape: a kit job on a daily schedule. (1) Inventory each session scratchpad and %TEMP% kit/lib-gate copies: size, age, owner session (alive or not), and files that look like deliverables (.spi/.ps1/.do outside a proof copy). (2) Report deliverable-looking files to their lane as a move list (never moves them itself). (3) Prune only throwaway copies of dead sessions older than N days, by rule, after a backup. (4) Backups: zip every repo's unstaged layer (git diff + untracked, minus target/.cache) to a dated store on both boxes, keep 14 days. Milestones: M1 inventory report (read-only), M2 backup job + restore check, M3 prune by rule with a dry run first, M4 drift classes mined into memory/backlog rows.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_2 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 2u32, "2026-10-27T08:28Z", "kit", "04:2x kit, user correction (relayed by the compiler lane 04:2x): not prune/delete. The watcher PLACES deliverables into their repos, or pivots/ARCHIVES an experiment (moves it to a dated archive store), and never risks losing code or backups. 'Keep going forward as destructive as we can' is safe only because backups and archives exist. Deletion is allowed only for provably redundant throwaways (byte-identical to a repo file or an archived copy), and only after a backup. Milestones replace note 1's M3: M3 = place-or-archive by rule, dry run first, with each move logged (from, to, sha256) so it can be reversed; there is no prune milestone.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_3 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 3u32, "2026-10-27T09:07Z", "kit", "05:2x kit, drift example #2 (my own lane), measured: the kit lane's scratchpad holds 574 top-level .ps1 plus about 260 scripts under clean\\ (respell 81, kit-rename 45, list-sugar 27, slate 11, ...). Most are finished experiments (archive candidates). The live tools have no repo home yet: the release drivers (release-build-job-*, make-*/launch-* per release, release-go, compose-slices, land-post-rename, mark-proven, heavy-cap-align, job-script-check, eoie-snapshot, notebook-check, byte-identity, release-wait-check, handoff-parity-release); node tooling (node-candidate, node-neutral, node-serial-runner, prune-mirrors, node-push, node-watch); and the pending list-sugar converters (arith-literals, casts, int-text, print). Move list, to apply when kit-release-SLICES frees the kit tree: release drivers into kit scripts/release/ (one parameterized make/launch pair instead of per-label copies, which is itself a kit verb candidate per generic-tools-not-per-experiment); generic node tooling into i574n.github/scripts beside remote.ps1; pending converters into kit scripts/migrations/ with a TODO: EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION marker each. Everything else goes to a dated archive (never deleted). Iggy client done 04:4x (kit infra/a/iggy-client).")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_4 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 4u32, "2026-10-27T09:22Z", "kit", "05:2x kit: M2 backup half built and run once. i574n.github/scripts/unstaged-backup.ps1 zips each C:/home/git repo's unstaged patch (git diff --binary), staged patch (diff --cached), untracked files (ls-files --others --exclude-standard, files over 20 MB skipped and listed) and a backup.txt (head, stamp) into %LOCALAPPDATA%/kit/backups/unstaged/<stamp>/<repo>.zip. It skips junctions and never deletes old runs; it only lists those past 14 days for the archive rule. -Verify re-hashes every archived untracked file against its source. First run 20261027-050846: 25 repos with a layer, 22.4 MB total (kit 10.05 MB: 234,056 unstaged and 19,106 staged patch lines, 808 untracked), verify mismatches 0 on every repo. Next: a daily schedule (a kit job), a second copy on the node, and a restore drill (apply the patches to a fresh worktree at backup.txt's head, compare tree hashes).")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_5 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 5u32, "2026-10-27T10:46Z", "kit", "06:4x kit: M1 inventory and M3 archive built and run once. (M1) i574n.github/scripts/scratch-inventory.ps1, read-only: per session scratchpad its team (from standing.txt), alive (transcript touched in the last 6 h), GB and files outside copy folders, deliverable-looking files (source and script extensions), newest. First run 06:37: 21 scratchpads, 5.8 GB outside copy folders, 6 alive, 227,154 deliverable-looking files. Top rows (session team alive lastturn GB files): fc1568a6 eoie True 10-27 05:24 2.62 | ac4b4e98 tibia True 10-27 04:48 1.97 | 84b53718 fiscal True 10-27 04:46 0.41 | 5a6e53fb main True 10-27 04:43 0.40 | b7595ac3 x True 10-27 05:22 0.26 | 88a146f8 compiler True 10-27 04:48 0.14. (M3) i574n.github/scripts/scratch-archive.ps1: a content-addressed archive (unique files as sha256-named blobs in blobs.zip, plus manifest.tsv with path, hash, size, mtime), every blob re-hashed, originals removed only with -Apply after a clean verify; -Restore rebuilds any folder. Drill: 4,786 files restored byte-identical. Run on my own scratchpad (474 folders older than 10-26, minus any folder a live script references): 345,711 files, 5.27 GB -> unique 0.52 GB -> blobs.zip 0.067 GB, verify failures 0. Plus 5.4 GB of idle cargo target dirs freed directly (build output). %TEMP%/eoie-parked-train is being archived the same way. C: went from 36 GB to 46 GB free so far. Remaining: the daily schedule, place-don't-archive for live deliverables (my move list, note 3), and the node copy of each archive.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_6 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 6u32, "2026-10-27T14:43Z", "kit", "10:4x kit: gap found in my 05:45 archive pass. Its exclusion rule spared folders that live scripts reference, but not folders that backlog notes cite: 68 of the 474 archived folders are cited in agile.spi notes (job-env 7, f1-owner 6, memory-features 5, next-train 4, lib-gaps-3 4, ...). Nothing is lost: the first real restore (EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT's four lib drafts from lib-gaps-3) was byte-identical through the new -Only filter. Mitigation: a redirect file, the kit lane scratchpad's ARCHIVED-FOLDERS.txt, with the restore command and the 68 cited names. Rule for M3 from now on: before archiving, grep each folder name in agile.spi notes (and memories); cited folders get a redirect entry at minimum, and preferably their deliverables are placed in a repo instead of archived.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_7 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 7u32, "2026-10-27T23:12Z", "main", "10-27 19:12 main: Demand data from main's 10-27 groom (the side review found parked drafts to be the main remaining drift source). Proven deliverables sitting in TEMP only, each waiting on a window: cli-args-usage (cli_args help slice, GREEN on node proof-7; after TRAIN), lib-gate-retention (land.ps1 work-folder retention, controls GREEN; after the last land of the cycle), cells-lib-snapshot (SPIRAL_CELLS_LIB resolution, 5/5 tests on node; needs a window with no Cells jobs), blog-list-sugar (already applied live; its TEMP copy is only the revert patch), rmd-wildcard (measurement scripts for RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION; reference data), matrix-bundle (accept/compare-accept harness; in use), pack-next5n (the 5n install; after accept-6, TRAIN and CCMR), lib-nil-literal (spent; nil batch 2 landed 17:39). What a watcher would catch: a draft whose window has opened but nothing triggered its land. Today that happened twice in reverse (a land and a job released by a stopped train, see memory train-guard-gap), so the watcher should key on the window owner's 'window closed' message, not only on process state.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_8 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 8u32, "2026-10-30T02:00Z", "kit", "2026-10-30T02:00 kit groom: the 10-28 wipe proved this item's premise: TEMP-only proven drafts were lost (ledger WIPE-REDO-LEDGER). Two inputs now exist. (1) The daily trigger: 'kit schedule due <name> <minutes>' / 'ran <name>' ships in installed kit C528BE4D (closeout PASS: due 0, ran, due 1), so the watcher can run as 'kit schedule due scratch-watch 1440 && <watch> && kit schedule ran scratch-watch' from any hook or job, without a live session. (2) A manual instance today: kit moved its TEMP-only helpers (watch-train, lane-notes, user-env, bang-prep, gaps-bundle, iggy-bang-prep, libland-gates, do-landed, tail-visible) to C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\tools and re-pointed every launcher. Progress stays 50: the automated daily pass and both-box backups of unstaged layers are still to build.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_9 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 9u32, "2026-10-31T07:36Z", "kit", "10-31 03:2x kit: VISIBLE-WINDOW FIX. The user asked \"why kit.exe started being spawned out of nowhere without being hidden?\". Cause: the M2 Task Scheduler task kit-unstaged-backup (daily 03:10, Interactive logon) ran C:\\home\\git\\kit\\kit.exe directly. A console program started by an Interactive task gets a visible window, and this one stayed open about 90 s while it waited for the job host. Fix: the action is now C:\\Windows\\System32\\conhost.exe --headless \"%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe\" job start ..., which also points it at the installed binary instead of the repo copy. The pre-fix XML is in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\backups\\scheduled-tasks. The registration is now in the repo: i574n.github/scripts/register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 (idempotent, --DryRun reports 'unchanged' against the live task). A test run was watched by a process-chain probe: no window, and the job started under the job host. SEPARATE FINDING: tonight's 03:10 job job-1793430684160 reports \"the supervisor stopped beating ... its job tree ended with it\", but its supervisor (pid 6324) and pwsh (16960) are alive and still backing up repos. That is a false verdict under box load; it goes to job doctor.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_10 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 10u32, "2026-10-31T10:45Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 06:4x kit: n9's 'supervisor stopped beating' verdict was FALSE. The 03:10 job job-1793430684160 finished with exit 0: 22 repos with a layer, 12.6 MB, in backups\\unstaged\\20261031-031152. 21 rows verified clean. i574n.github had VerifyMismatch=1, most likely the backlog state being written by lanes while the zip was read (it is the busiest file on the box). It is unproven, so a fresh run started at 06:44 through the fixed task (headless, priority 5): job-1793443449403. If i574n.github mismatches again, the verify step needs to retry a changed file instead of reporting it. Follow-up for job doctor: a supervisor that is alive (pid 6324 at 03:2x) yet reported 'stopped beating' on a saturated box means the heartbeat threshold doesn't allow for starvation.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_11 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 11u32, "2026-10-31T10:49Z", "kit", "10-31 06:49 kit: the fresh run is CLEAN. job-1793443449403 exited 0: backups\\unstaged\\20261031-064413, 22 repos, 13 MB, VerifyMismatch 0 on every row, including i574n.github. So the 03:10 mismatch was a file changing mid-read, not corruption. It ran in 283 s through the fixed task (conhost --headless, priority 5), against about 26 min for the 03:10 run at the default BelowNormal (7) on the same saturated box.")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_12 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 12u32, "2026-10-31T12:38Z", "kit", "10-31 08:4x kit: dangling-citation census over backlog notes: 53 distinct C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts paths are cited and 48 no longer exist, across 34 items (most of them kit's). They were archived, not lost: kit-drafts was emptied through scratch-archive.ps1 on 10-30 (runs %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-225704 .. -233632), and each manifest.tsv maps the path relative to kit-drafts to its blob hash; -Restore brings any file back. Most of those drafts landed, so the tree is the current record. Rule from here (work-in-the-repo, enforced by the kit-work-in-repo hook): new notes cite repo paths or carry the content inline, as EOIE-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE n3 now does for its table. The lookup recipe is in the archive-never-delete memory. Census script: the session scratchpad's drafts-citation-census.ps1 (one-shot; it can become 'kit agile check --dangling-paths' if this recurs).")
inl note_of_kit_scratch_watch_13 () = Note ("KIT-SCRATCH-WATCH", 13u32, "2026-11-01T03:36Z", "kit", "10-31 23:4x kit groom (main 23:33, user: cadence/drift): Active -> PLANNED. No note in over 12 h, so nobody is working it this week; Planned keeps it in agile next at its priority (never auto-Paused, R3). First step when picked = the next step in its latest note.")
inl polyglot_retire () = Task ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", "Move everything useful from polyglot into i574n.github and retire polyglot from the org; i574n.github (already the agile home) may become the examples lab, with a drift guard against duplicate scripts", Epic, P1, D6, 70u32, Planned, "", "org,polyglot,i574n.github,migration,examples,drift,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_polyglot_retire () = Planning ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", Minutes 1230u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_1 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:15Z", "main", "user 2026-10-27 06:0x: \"move everything useful from polyglot to i574n.github so we remove polyglot from the org. also check if there's something in the spiral repo or in the others that could also be moved to i574n.github, that one since already holds agile could also become the examples lab etc. gotta care for drift though, we already dumped a lot of scripts into it recently.\"\nCENSUS 10-27 06:1x (main). polyglot holds:\n- apps: chat (12 files, the NEAR chat contract and its tests, last commit 10-27, live), spiral (37, 10-25), parser 5, ipfs 4, perf 2, scheduler 2, builder 0 (empty, all 10-07 or later)\n- lib: fsharp 18, math 9, rust 97, typescript 121\n- scripts: 17, incl. core.ps1, which most consumer builds dot-source\n- examples 1, .github/workflows 2\n- deps: mostly third-party checkouts (Fable, dotnet-interactive, Paket, The-Spiral-Language, mpmath, hyperui), plus deps/spiral -> C:\\home\\git\\spiral\nCONSUMERS: 662 references to polyglot in 118 script/config files:\n- dice: scripts/init.ps1 x11, publish, build, contract and lib builds, and ui/package.spiproj, whose packageDir resolves lib through deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib\n- alphabet: init x7, apps/hangul and apps/documents spiproj and builds\n- vault and tibia: init, workflow, publish, app builds\n- i574n.github's own scripts: workflow, publish, init, build, outdated, pins, remote, pages-sweep\n- dotfiles: dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1\n- spiral: lab scripts, and compiler tmp scripts env.ps1, parser-corpus-gate, lib-usage-census\n- also an absolute link apps/chat/contract/lib -> C:\\home\\git\\polyglot\\lib\nPLAN (phase rules fixed before any move):\n(1) Inventory every polyglot path into exactly one class: MOVE (unique and useful), ELSEWHERE (an equal or newer copy exists, proven by hash or a diff of the content), THIRD-PARTY (re-fetchable dependency), DROP (empty or history-only). Record it in this item's notes, not a new doc.\n(2) Drift guard before anything lands in i574n.github: grep each moved file's stem across i574n.github/scripts (44 files, incl. the 8 job-runner tools main moved there on 10-26/27), spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/scripts and polyglot/scripts. A second copy is merged into the existing one or dropped, never added beside it (one record per fact).\n(3) Shared build scripts (core.ps1 and what it dot-sources) move first, as i574n.github/scripts/<name>, with the consumer path unchanged until (5).\n(4) Apps and libs: polyglot lib rust/typescript/fsharp/math go to spiral lib where they are Spiral-generated lib code (lib-first), otherwise to i574n.github. chat moves as one unit with its contract tests; its build proof is the existing build.ps1 exit 0 plus the contract tests on a copy.\n(5) Consumers repoint one repo at a time (dice, alphabet, vault, tibia, dotfiles, i574n.github, spiral), each proven by that repo's own build GREEN on a copy. Each repo's team gets its edit.\n(6) Done when grep finds 0 polyglot references outside fc1943s backups and history. Then the repo is ARCHIVED on GitHub by the user (deleting or archiving an org repo is the user's call). fc1943s keeps the dump.\nEXAMPLES LAB (the user's suggestion: i574n.github as the examples lab). Candidates to census next:\n- spiral/lab (107 folders, 1,506 files; LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL): drafts land in their home repo by rule, so only true examples move, never WIP\n- polyglot apps parser/ipfs/perf/scheduler/examples\n- standalone sample apps in other repos that are demos rather than products\nThe compiler's regression fixtures stay in spiral (apps/compiler/tmp/tests and samples: they are the matrix's oracle input). The examples/ top-level folder is a structure decision: the user proposed it here, and its exact name and layout are confirmed with the user before the first move.\nRelated: SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (spiral's own polyglot references), COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE, LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_2 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-10-27T10:18Z", "main", "10-27 06:18 main: planning fields, set by note because kit has no verb for them after add (agile set takes only progress and status; agile add accepts --estimate/--deps only at intake, a gap for EOIE-AGILE-FIELD-COMPLETENESS). ESTIMATE 1,230m, from the plan's milestones: (1) inventory 120m, (2) drift census by stem across the three script homes 60m, (3) shared scripts 120m, (4) apps and libs 480m (chat with its contract tests is most of it), (5) consumer repoints 7 repos x 60m = 420m, (6) final grep 30m. DEPS: SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (Paused; spiral's own polyglot references, now a sub-goal of this epic's phase 5), soft COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE and LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL (both decide what of spiral is an example, which this epic's examples-lab half needs). LOAD light (it's file moves and builds on copies), ASSIGNEE agent, TEAM main (repoint edits go to each repo's team).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_3 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-10-27T10:28Z", "main", "10-27 06:28 main: phase-5 input from tibia (ack 10-27 06:2x). tibia's polyglot consumers are scripts/build.ps1, init.ps1, workflow.ps1 and publish.ps1, plus apps/arena/build.ps1 and apps/canary/build.ps1. apps/arena/build.ps1 dot-sources deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and runs first in every tibia gate, so its repoint needs a full tibia gate on a copy; tibia proves each repoint itself when it's due. Also from the 06:2x census: polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is already a shim that dot-sources deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (spiral's shared helpers). So phase 3 for core.ps1 is a repoint to spiral's scripts/core.ps1 (or a one-line i574n.github shim), not a move of code.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_4 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-10-27T10:32Z", "main", "10-27 06:32 main: phase 2 drift census (by file stem and by function definition, PowerShell AST) over the four script homes: i574n.github/scripts 21 scripts, spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/scripts 43, polyglot/scripts 15, spiral/scripts 13. STEMS in more than one home: only the per-repo standard entry points build, init, outdated, publish and workflow (every repo has one by the sibling convention, and all differ), plus core (polyglot's 13-line shim over spiral's 423-line scripts/core.ps1). No script was copied between homes, so tonight's job-runner tools (serial-runner, queue-serial, job-stop, watch-ids and the rest) have no second copy anywhere. FUNCTIONS (123 definitions): CheckToml is byte-identical in polyglot/scripts/outdated.ps1 and spiral/scripts/outdated.ps1, and the polyglot copy goes with polyglot. Get-FileSha256 has two different bodies in compiler-tmp env.ps1 and test.ps1, and Resolve-Results two in ci-classify.ps1 and compare-runs.ps1; both are compiler-internal duplication, flagged to COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE. Verdict: moving polyglot's scripts into i574n.github adds no duplicate as long as each standard entry point merges into i574n.github's own and core.ps1 becomes a repoint to spiral's.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_5 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-10-27T12:00Z", "main", "10-27 08:00 main: phase 1, first pass (identity test): 302 polyglot files outside deps and generated folders (target, node_modules, dist, bin, obj, .history), each hashed against byte-identical copies in spiral, dice, alphabet, i574n.github, vault, tibia, kit, blog, dir-tree-html, x and fiscal. Only 9 are ELSEWHERE by identity, all repo config (.editorconfig, .gitattributes, .markdownlint.json, LICENSE, requirements.txt, rust-toolchain.toml, plus one file each in apps/chat and apps/spiral). Everything substantive is unique to polyglot: lib/rust 81, lib/typescript 90, lib/fsharp 18, lib/math 5; apps chat 12, spiral 37, parser 5, ipfs 4, perf 2, scheduler 2; scripts 17 (incl. build.livemd, core.ps1 the shim, dep_hyperui.ps1); workflows 2, devcontainer 2, flake 2. So no substantive file is an exact duplicate; the next pass classifies by content and use (MOVE or DROP), starting with lib/rust and lib/typescript, the two largest. Table: TEMP polyglot-inventory.tsv (Top, Path, Twin).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_6 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-10-27T12:53Z", "main", "10-27 08:53 main: phase 1, second pass (content and use), the two largest folders. lib/rust (81 files: 48 .rs, 20 .fsx) and lib/typescript (90: 54 .ts, 24 .fsx) each hold only a fable/ subfolder: vendored Fable runtime libraries (fable_modules/fable-library-rust and its TS twin) plus generated .fsx. lib/fsharp is 18 files (8 .livemd, 6 .fsx, 3 .rs); lib/math is 9 files, with built .dll/.exe/.pdb under dist/ (generated output). The org dropped Fable, so these classify as DROP once no consumer is left. But two consumers still build against lib/rust's Fable library through a Cargo path dependency: tapas2 (i574n, Cargo.toml:16 fable_library_rust = { path = \"deps/polyglot/lib/rust/fable/fable_modules/fable-library-rust\" }, and its contract/build.ps1 dot-sources deps/polyglot/scripts/core.ps1) and mechahaze album1 (an outside org, apps/album1/Cargo.toml:9, the same path dependency). Both are outside the census's repo list, which covered only i574n's main repos. So (a) phase 5's consumer list gains tapas2 and album1, and (b) lib/rust is blocked on their Fable exit: each either drops Fable (no-Fable direction) or vendors fable-library-rust itself, and that is their teams' call, not a move into i574n.github. The grep found no consumer of lib/typescript's Fable library outside polyglot/deps/Fable itself. Next pass: apps/spiral (37), apps/chat (12), scripts (17).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_7 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 7u32, "2026-10-27T12:56Z", "main", "10-27 08:56 main: phase 1, third pass: apps and scripts. PROPOSED classes; the examples-lab layout in i574n.github is the user's call before anything moves. apps/chat (12 files, live; last commit 10-27): MOVE as one unit (contract, contract tests, Cargo workspace, .cargo config); its home is the open question (i574n.github examples, or a repo of its own like dice). apps/perf (Perf.spi) and apps/scheduler (Tasks.spi), 2 files each: small Spiral programs, examples-lab candidates. apps/spiral (37 files): all under temp/, experiments (cube in C, .fsx, Lua and Python with a build.ps1; a Blender build.py). The spiral matrix's native_cube_* samples already cover the cube on every backend, so this is ELSEWHERE for the cube and examples or DROP for the rest. apps/parser (5: JsonParser.fs and Parser.fs with their .livemd, last 10-07): F# from the Fable era, DROP under the no-Fable direction unless a consumer appears. apps/ipfs (4: a Bun index.ts with package.json): examples or DROP after a consumer check. scripts (17: build/init in .ps1 and .livemd, core.ps1 = the shim over spiral's core.ps1, dep_hyperui, dep_spiral, dep_spiral_extension and the rest): each standard entry point merges into i574n.github's own (drift census n4), and core.ps1 becomes a repoint. Open user decisions, asked together when phase 3 starts: the examples/ layout, and chat's home.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_8 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 8u32, "2026-10-27T13:22Z", "main", "10-27 09:22 main: examples-lab census, spiral side (the user's 06:0x ask: anything in spiral or other repos that could also move to i574n.github). spiral top level: apps (10,627 files), lib (1,146), lab (289 in 50 folders after tonight's drains), scripts (16), plus config folders. Inside apps: cells, compiler, spiral and zed are products. plot and wasm are referenced by spiral's own CI/scripts, so they stay (CI builds them). lisp (6 files: a Lisp written in Spiral as 3 .spl plus livemd, a Python helper and build.ps1; last 10-19; no CI or script reference) is an examples-lab CANDIDATE. apps/cells-nightpack is an EMPTY folder (0 entries, untracked, named by no script in spiral or i574n.github); it's checked for live owners before removal. lab: drafts land in their home repo by rule, so only folders that are genuinely examples (not WIP) are candidates; LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL judges each one, and none has been classified as an example yet. Compiler fixtures (apps/compiler/tmp/samples and tests) stay: they're the matrix's oracle input. Shortlist so far for the lab, pending the user's layout decision: polyglot apps/perf, apps/scheduler, maybe apps/ipfs (n7), and spiral apps/lisp.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_9 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 9u32, "2026-10-30T22:51Z", "main", "10-30 18:51 main, R4 DECIDED (placement is answered by rules, not left as a user call; BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030): the examples lab is i574n.github/examples/<name>/, one self-contained folder per example (its .spi + build.ps1). build.ps1 reaches the sibling spiral checkout through ../../../spiral (the same relative pattern as i574n.github/scripts/pins), so no deps/ copy. polyglot keeps its copies until the retire step archives the repo (archive, never delete). FIRST SLICE moved (unstaged): examples/perf (Perf.spi 23,420 B, edition 3, byte-identical to polyglot apps/perf) and examples/scheduler (Tasks.spi 5,969 B, edition 3), each with build.ps1 repointed (core.ps1 and run_notebook.ps1 from ../../../spiral; both paths resolve). PROOF next: run each build.ps1 (a Cells notebook run) after main's Cells window 3; pass = notebook exits 0. Still open: apps/chat (a NEAR contract with a Cargo workspace; it stays in polyglot until NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES decides its home); apps/spiral temp/ experiments (drop or elsewhere, per n-1); apps/parser F# (drop under the no-Fable direction).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_10 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 10u32, "2026-10-30T23:38Z", "main", "10-30 19:3x main: examples/perf from its new home: the notebook ran (Perf.spi.ipynb written 19:25) but exit 1 after 993 s: cell 22 (binary_search_tests, count = 10,000,000) hit the 300 s Cells cell timeout while the box was at 100% CPU (three main proofs plus fiscal and kit runs). It is a timing workload, so this is a load red, not a move regression; rerun it alone on a quiet box (or inside a short bench window). examples/scheduler passed 4/4 earlier.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_11 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 11u32, "2026-10-31T15:39Z", "main", "10-31 11:39 main, the two open decisions, from the tree (dangling check by stem across C:\\home\\git): (1) apps/parser (F#: Parser.fs, JsonParser.fs, their .livemd, build.ps1) can NOT be dropped yet: dice/scripts/init.ps1:28, alphabet/scripts/init.ps1:28, mechahaze-album1/scripts/init.ps1:29 and tapas2/scripts/init.ps1:22 still build it, and tapas2/contract/build.ps1:18 runs its DibParser to turn the .dib into .spi. i574n.github/scripts/spiral-independent/rewrite-deps.ps1:26 already strips that build line, but the migration hasn't been run in those repos. DECIDED: parser retires right after SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT's rewrite runs in those 4 repos (tapas2's .dib->spi step needs its .spi committed first). (2) apps/spiral/temp: cube (13 files) is referenced only by polyglot itself (scripts/symlinks.ps1:9, README.md:112) and blender (2) and extension (269 files, 25 MB, mostly untracked) by nothing: all three go with the polyglot archive, nothing to move. Still open: examples/perf's timing rerun on a quiet box (after kit's train6).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_12 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 12u32, "2026-11-01T03:40Z", "main", "main 23:4x WIP groom (user 23:3x: drift/stall, too much waiting): Active -> Planned. apps/parser stays until dice/alphabet/mechahaze init.ps1 stop using it (n11); blocked by SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (Paused, user batch).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_13 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 13u32, "2026-11-01T14:35Z", "main", "main 10:3x (user 11-01: 'gotta check for the old tasks checking what's left to retire polyglot'). State: n11 found apps/parser still used by dice/alphabet/mechahaze init.ps1, and the migration waits on SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (user batch). Also wanted from polyglot before retiring: its Nov-2025 state for CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT and ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH (the dib plotting/export reference), the Blender experiment (BLENDER-SAMPLE) and the Perf notebooks (PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY). NEXT STEP: a full census of polyglot's tracked folders by: still used (by whom) / moved / to move (target) / drop, written on this item.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_14 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 14u32, "2026-11-02T19:01Z", "main", "main 11-02 14:5x CENSUS of polyglot's tracked folders, with readers in sibling repos (git grep \"polyglot/<folder>\"; forks excluded). SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT is DONE for spiral and tibia (both deps\\polyglot links removed, tibia's init clones spiral directly; n36/n37), so these are the remaining readers:\n- STILL USED, migrate the reader first:\n  - scripts/ (17 files): build/init dot-sources in alphabet (apps/documents, apps/hangul build.ps1), dice (contract/build.ps1, contract/tests/build.ps1), dotfiles (dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1), fc1943s.github, mechahaze-album1, tapas2, vault (init/publish), i574n.github (scripts/build.ps1). Fix = point each at deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1, as tibia and regex do.\n  - apps/parser (5): init.ps1 of alphabet, dice, mechahaze-album1, tapas2; tapas2 contract/build.ps1 (DibParser). Retires once those init.ps1 stop building it (rewrite-deps.ps1 already strips the line).\n  - apps/spiral (36): dotfiles appdata build, mechahaze-album1 (apps/album1 build + init), tapas2 (contract build + init), vault (data/spiral/spiral.md docs).\n  - lib/fsharp (18): dice lib/fsharp (build.ps1 + .livemd), singularity Tidal.dib, tapas2 contract .rs.\n  - lib/math (5): only README mentions (fc1943s, i574n.github profile); its pyo3/mpmath harness is the zeta porting oracle, so it MOVES to lib/spiral/zeta with ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE.\n- ONLY THE BACKLOG MENTIONS IT (move or drop on decision): apps/chat (12), apps/perf (2; PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY), apps/scheduler (2).\n- NO READERS (drop at retire): apps/ipfs (4), examples (1), .devcontainer, .github, root files (16), workspace (2; only the .code-workspace files list it).\nORDER: (1) repoint the scripts/core.ps1 dot-sources in dice, alphabet, dotfiles, mechahaze-album1, tapas2, vault, i574n.github (alphabet mirrors dice); (2) their init.ps1 stop building apps/parser; (3) lib/math moves with zeta; (4) archive the rest. fc1943s.* repos are the dump (fc1943s-dump-i574n-destructive): leave them.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_15 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 15u32, "2026-11-02T19:02Z", "main", "main 11-02 15:0x STEP 1 started. polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 is a pure forwarder to spiral/scripts/core.ps1 (SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT n7), so repointing each dot-source at spiral is behaviour-preserving. DONE: dotfiles dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1 (absolute path -> c:/home/git/spiral/scripts/core.ps1; parse ok; 0 polyglot sites left; unstaged). REMAINING sites (git grep polyglot/scripts/core.ps1): dice 12, alphabet 8 (mirror dice), mechahaze-album1 6, tapas2 6, vault 3 (one reaches it through deps/alphabet/deps/polyglot). Repos WITHOUT a deps/spiral link today: dice, tapas2, vault (alphabet and mechahaze-album1 have one). So each also needs its init.ps1 to clone or link spiral as deps/spiral, the way regex and tibia now do, and a local deps/spiral link for local builds. Prove each with its own build (dice/alphabet on the node). Next heartbeats: dice + alphabet as a pair, then mechahaze-album1, tapas2, vault.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_16 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 16u32, "2026-11-02T21:07Z", "main", "main 11-02 17:1x STEP 1 alphabet PROVEN on the node's real checkout (synced -Force, digest 57736BEE7E55D702, deps/spiral linked): apps/documents compiles (cargo Finished) and runs through the new paths; its one test row fails only because the node lacks crowbook (test.hangul.md + test.md.html come back Ok after main copied the box's hangulize.exe over; before that hangulize.exe was missing too, the node has no Go). apps/hangul: spiral-tests 2/2 passed; its livemd F# cell 'AssertAreEqual(국어, hanjaConvert 國語)' fails, and an in-job A/B with HEAD's build.ps1 + package.spiproj (the polyglot paths) fails IDENTICALLY, so it predates the rewrite (filed as a note here; the hanja table lookup misses, likely an encoding read of the cell source). vault repointed (POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT n2). mechahaze-album1 + tapas2 need a port, not a repoint: POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_17 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 17u32, "2026-11-02T21:15Z", "main", "main 11-02 17:2x STEP 1 dice PROVEN on the node's real checkout (deps/spiral junction, the rewritten tree): contract build exit 0, spiral-tests 7/7 passed, 'RUST-OK dice/contract / the NEAR sandbox tests passed on dist/dice.wasm'. So dice + alphabet are done for step 1 (dice keeps deps/polyglot only for lib/fsharp Common.fs). Side fix in dice contract/build.ps1: ClearCargoTarget '../..' -> '..' (from contract/, '../..' is the folder above the repo, so the CI cleanup never reached dice's workspace target). Readers left after tonight: tapas2 (port in proof, POLYGLOT-READERS-PORT), dice lib/fsharp Common.fs, the docs-only mentions, i574n.github scripts/build.ps1.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_18 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 18u32, "2026-11-02T23:27Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:2x NO CONSUMER CLONES POLYGLOT ANY MORE (unstaged). (1) alphabet scripts/init.ps1: polyglot clone + 'pwsh ../../polyglot/scripts/init.ps1' replaced by spiral's own 'pwsh ../../spiral/scripts/init.ps1', the exact change dice's CI proved green tonight (run 41538911884); git grep polyglot in alphabet = 0. (2) i574n.github umbrella: scripts/build.ps1 no longer runs polyglot's build, outdated.ps1 no longer runs polyglot's outdated, and init.ps1 no longer clones polyglot (all parse; 0 polyglot refs in those 3 + the workflows). Readers left: vault/mechahaze-album1/tapas2 ported (unstaged), docs prose, and the inventory scripts that LIST polyglot as an org repo (pins.ps1, pages-sweep.ps1, recovered-drafts-census.ps1, remote.ps1's route check). Those stay while the repo exists. NEXT (step 3/4): lib/math moves with ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE; then archive polyglot's remaining folders (CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT reference, Blender, Perf notebooks noted in n13). Archiving the GitHub repo is the user's call (n1).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_19 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 19u32, "2026-11-03T08:49Z", "main", "main 11-03 04:1x ORG EXIT DONE BY THE USER (11-03): polyglot left the i574n org and is now fc1943s/polyglot, with no redirect. The local C:\\home\\git\\polyglot stays as the SOURCE until every folder below is absorbed or ruled out; it is then deleted after a proper check (11-03 rule: hash/tree comparison against the new homes). CI and link fallout is ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT. ABSORPTION MAP (tracked files per folder, then owner):\napps/chat (12; the NEAR chat contract .spi + generated .rs) -> NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES / NEAR-MOCKED-UNIT-TESTS, destination i574n.github/apps/chat (this item's examples lab).\nlib/math (5) -> ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE (spiral lib), then ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE.\nlib/fsharp (18; Common.fs and friends, F#-era helpers) -> FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER decides per file: whatever a live fixture needs (Cells' document_test reads dice's own lib/fsharp, not polyglot's) is copied to its consumer, everything else is ruled out.\napps/perf (2) -> PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY (read as a reference, then ruled out).\napps/parser (5; FParsec era) -> FPARSEC-RETIRE / parsing lib, reference only.\napps/spiral (36; the Supervisor / old CLI) -> superseded by spiral's apps; rule out after a stem grep.\napps/ipfs (4), apps/scheduler (2), examples/elixir (1) -> UNOWNED, a triage step: keep as an i574n.github example if it still builds or teaches something, otherwise rule it out.\nscripts (17) -> superseded by spiral/scripts (core.ps1, init, publish); diff for any function that exists only here, then rule out.\nAlso referenced as a source: CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT (old plots), BLENDER-SAMPLE (Blender experiment), DIB-MODERNIZE (.dib remnants), all read from the local copy.\nNEXT: the triage step for ipfs/scheduler/elixir, then the ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT sweep.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_20 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 20u32, "2026-11-03T09:03Z", "tibia", "11-03 05:0x tibia: tibia's polyglot dependency census = NONE in sources. grep over tibia (deps/ excluded) finds polyglot only in README.md:256, which said init.ps1 'clones polyglot (which brings spiral) ... links both under deps/'. scripts/init.ps1 actually clones spiral only and links deps/spiral (plus Lua 5.1 and, via spiral's init-wgsl-run.ps1, Mesa Vulkan on Ubuntu). README fixed to match (unstaged). The local tibia/deps/polyglot link is unused by tibia's build and tests; only the node's consumer3 gate runner links it for spiral's process.spi route check, so tibia is not a blocker for retiring polyglot.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_21 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 21u32, "2026-11-03T09:36Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:4x TRIAGE of the 3 unowned folders. RULE, written first: keep what is Spiral or teaches something no kept repo has; rule out copies of third-party material and code for dead external services. (1) apps/ipfs (index.ts 15 lines + package.json, bun.lockb, build.ps1; last 10-07): a TypeScript uploader to nft.storage, whose classic upload API was sunset in 2024. Not Spiral; the NEAR chat contract computes its own CID (generate_cid). RULED OUT. (2) apps/scheduler (Tasks.spi 214 lines, last 10-25; build.ps1): a typed task-scheduling model (task_id/task_name nominals, recurrency_offset/fixed_recurrency unions over date_time). Typefeatureset-shaped domain code with no equivalent elsewhere. KEEP -> i574n.github/apps/scheduler, respelled to edition 3 with test blocks, proven by a gate, then the polyglot copy is ruled out. (3) examples/elixir/exercism.livemd (433 lines, last 10-07): Exercism's exercise text copied into the retired livemd format. RULED OUT. NEXT: move scheduler, then the per-folder rule-outs for lib/fsharp, apps/perf, apps/parser, apps/spiral and scripts (diff for unique functions first).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_22 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 22u32, "2026-11-03T09:38Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:5x RULE-OUTS, checked. (a) scripts (17 files): function diff against spiral/scripts + lib/spiral (24 functions). Only 5 exist solely in polyglot: UpdateToml/UpdateJson (update.ps1: thin wrappers over 'cargo update' / 'bun update'), CheckJson (outdated.ps1, the JSON twin of spiral's CheckToml), and Resolve-PolyglotSpiralBundle / Ensure-SpiralRustCompiler (spiral-bundle.ps1, polyglot's own obsolete bundle). Nothing unique worth moving: RULED OUT. (b) lib/fsharp (18): no live reader in any i574n repo (the 11-03 full-repo grep: dice no longer references polyglot; the only hits are the fc1943s dump repos and singularity's playground data), so RULED OUT; FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER keeps dice's own lib/fsharp. (c) apps/spiral (36; Supervisor, old CLI): superseded by spiral's apps (cells, compiler, spiral) and referenced only in history comments: RULED OUT. STILL READ FROM THE LOCAL COPY, so the local C:\\home\\git\\polyglot is deleted only after these close: ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE (lib/math), NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES (apps/chat), SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE (apps/scheduler), PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY (apps/perf, reference), FPARSEC-RETIRE (apps/parser, reference), compiler's extract-corpus 'user' corpus (polyglot@bb856d13), CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT (old plot reference). Progress 60 -> 70.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_23 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 23u32, "2026-11-03T11:37Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:5x compiler: the extract-corpus 'user' corpus no longer reads the local C:\\home\\git\\polyglot (done 05:4x, ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT n3). tmp/formatter/extract-corpus.ps1 clones https://github.com/fc1943s/polyglot bare with --filter=blob:none into LOCALAPPDATA/spiral-bin/corpus-src/polyglot.git on first use, at the same pinned bb856d13 (on fc1943s/main). End-to-end run: 86 files, 577,482 bytes, 0 content mismatches against the local copy, 1 MB clone. Strike it from the list of local-copy readers.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_24 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 24u32, "2026-11-03T12:42Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:5x PATH CORRECTION: the examples lab is i574n.github/examples/<name>/ (R4, 10-30; examples/perf and examples/scheduler already live there), not i574n.github/apps/. n21 and the apps/chat line said apps/; that wording produced a duplicate apps/scheduler, now folded into examples/scheduler (SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE n3). So apps/chat's destination is i574n.github/examples/chat when NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES moves it (X-ON-NEAR is deferred by the user, so it stays in the local polyglot copy until then). SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE is closed: strike it from the local-copy readers.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_25 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 25u32, "2026-11-03T13:42Z", "tibia", "11-03 09:2x tibia, CORRECTION to n20 (tibia has no polyglot dependency): its SOURCES do not use polyglot, but tibia CI did bootstrap through polyglot until d4ad52ad (11-02 21:59), and the switch to spiral's init-app-build.ps1 is exactly where tibia's Ubuntu CI went red: 4 unchanged Lua-only test files now report unsupported and a Zig main fails (TIBIA-1-0-DOD n4). So retiring polyglot from tibia is not done until spiral's bootstrap provides what polyglot's did for these targets.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_26 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 26u32, "2026-11-03T13:58Z", "tibia", "11-03 09:5x tibia, follow-up to n25: the gap is exact. Polyglot init.ps1 built the Spiral CLI (deps/spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1, line 151); spiral scripts/init-app-build.ps1 does not, so every app that switched to it loses its lua target on CI (cells runs lua via spiral lua). Tibia now builds the CLI itself in scripts/init.ps1 (unstaged). Other apps that moved to init-app-build need the same, or init-app-build should build the CLI (spiral-owned script, main lane decision).")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_27 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 27u32, "2026-11-03T14:03Z", "main", "main 11-03 10:0x FIXED IN ONE PLACE (unstaged, spiral): scripts/init-app-build.ps1 now builds the Spiral CLI when workspace/target/release/spiral[.exe] is missing, via apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1 (the canonical release-unwind + mimalloc build; spiral's own workflow.ps1 runs the same call green on ubuntu-24.04 and windows-2025). This restores what polyglot init.ps1:151 did, so every init-app-build app (tibia, fiscal, blog, kit, x, html, regex) gets its lua/cuda cell targets back on CI (tibia n26 root cause). tibia's per-app copy stays harmless (same missing-exe guard). Turns green on the user's spiral push.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_28 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 28u32, "2026-11-03T18:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:4x LOCAL COPY CHECKED: C:\\home\\git\\polyglot is an exact mirror of https://github.com/fc1943s/polyglot branch main-i574n (HEAD 2fbb9ee2, 0 ahead / 0 behind after fetch, clean, 0 untracked non-ignored files). So nothing in it is unique: every 'reads the local copy' item can clone fc1943s instead (compiler's corpus already does). Deletion stays gated by n22's owners (ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE, NEAR-CONTRACT-CRATES, PERF-FRAMEWORK-STUDY, FPARSEC-RETIRE, CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT) for workflow continuity, not data loss. DANGER for whoever deletes it: polyglot\\deps\\spiral is a LINK to the live spiral tree (it measures 40 GB if followed) and apps/chat/contract/lib links back into polyglot/lib; never run 'git clean -X' or a following recursive delete there: remove the links first (pwsh 7.6 Remove-Item deletes a junction without following, verified on the box 11-03), then the folder. Disk isn't a reason to hurry: C: has 228 GB free.")
inl note_of_polyglot_retire_29 () = Note ("POLYGLOT-RETIRE", 29u32, "2026-11-05T19:17Z", "main", "main 11-05 15:2x ORPHAN SWEEP: the deletion gate is WIDER than n22's five main items (all still Planned p=0..10). Live references outside polyglot: fc1943s.github/scripts/{build,init,publish,outdated,workflow}.ps1 + workflow.dib dot-source ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 (publish.ps1:80 also runs polyglot/apps/dir-tree-html/dist/DirTreeHtml), fc1943s.code-workspace + fc1943s-deps.code-workspace open ../polyglot/{workspace,deps/*}, and The-Spiral-Language 2.fsproj:56 falls back to ../../polyglot/spiral/clr/clr.fsx. fc1943s.github is the user's dump repo (no destructive edits there), so deleting the local copy breaks the user's own fc1943s build. NEXT before any delete: either the user retires fc1943s.github's tooling or its core.ps1/nbs_header.ps1/dir-tree-html move into i574n.github. Active untouched 54 h -> Planned at 70.")
inl kit_pending_dangling () = Task ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", "replace_file_checked leaves <path>.<pid>.pending forever when a writer dies between write and rename: use one fixed <path>.pending the next write consumes", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,agile,heal,files", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_pending_dangling () = Planning ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_1 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:24Z", "kit", "06:2x kit, from main's heal request (user 10-27 06:0x: 'check those pending files dangling, heal what's generating it'). Generator: workspace_primitives/files.spi replace_file_checked wrote <path>.<pid>.pending and then renamed it, so a writer killed between the two (job timeout, tree kill) left a file no later writer ever looked for (every writer has a new pid). Main archived and removed the two found (agile.spi.115112.pending, agile.spi.78508.pending; superseded, verified). Fix, decided against main's suggested sweep of dead-pid siblings, because the lib has no Rust directory listing or process liveness: the temporary becomes the fixed <path>.pending (pending_path). A killed writer now leaves at most one copy per file, and the next replacement overwrites and renames it, so nothing accumulates. It also removes a host macro (std::process::id). Two concurrent writers of one file now meet on the same temporary, and the existing readback check reports ReadbackMismatch; before, both renames succeeded and one update was silently lost. Draft: kit scratch clean/kit-rename/pending-fixed-name.do (files.spi + a test in toolchain.spi: every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy). Proven on a full src copy: applies 2/2; agile_todo_roots compiles, 422 lines against 425 live, process::id references 1 -> 0. workspace_primitives is inlined, so the next release regenerates every crate reaching it. Lands after kit-release-SLICES drops its lease. No .gitignore entry: a dangling copy should stay visible.")
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_2 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 2u32, "2026-10-27T14:33Z", "kit", "10:3x kit: a bug in my own landed test, caught by the literal-set node run: toolchain.spi's every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy is ETY-UnboundVariable 'files' (a test block cannot reach a sibling module by its bare name; --backend builds skip tests, so only a notebook catches it). Fix staged as clean/kit-rename/pending-test-fix.do: the test moves into files.spi beside pending_path, with a plain failwith check (dry-run 2/2 on the probe). It applies after the SLICES2 rerun, because touching workspace_primitives now would void that rerun's regen-skip freshness proof. toolchain.spi is not in its notebook set.")
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_3 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 3u32, "2026-10-29T12:53Z", "kit", "10-29 08:5x kit, wipe check: the lost pending-test-fix.do needs no redo, because both halves are in the live tree. workspace_primitives/files.spi:26 has pending_path (the fixed <path>.pending), and replace_file_checked uses it (:33); the test every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy sits beside it in files.spi:29 with a plain failwith check, and toolchain.spi no longer has it. No dangling *.pending files under the backlog or %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit (checked now). Closes once TRAIN3 (job-1793275863025, a full regen of every owner) installs and workspace_primitives/files.spi passes as its own notebook run after the install. Correction 09:0x: it is NOT in TRAIN3's candidate set, which holds only packages with uncommitted changes.")
inl note_of_kit_pending_dangling_4 () = Note ("KIT-PENDING-DANGLING", 4u32, "2026-10-29T15:41Z", "kit", "10-29 11:4x kit: closed. Installed in TRAIN3 (kit.exe CD2F0D1A, 11:35; the full regen republished every crate reaching workspace_primitives). workspace_primitives/files.spi ran as its own notebook (job-1793288400504): 1/1 pass, every_writer_of_one_file_shares_one_pending_copy included. No dangling *.pending under the backlog, before or after today's agile writes (TRAIN3 closeout row). Done.")
inl x_wip_verify () = Task ("X-WIP-VERIFY", "x: full verify of the unstaged WIP tree (apps/client and apps/sim build.ps1 on a node mirror, compiler pinned, syncs gated on REMOTE-SYNC-OK), reviewed sim/e2e accepts, then land the generated .rs and fixtures the WIP changed (land_outputs.ps1: new vs base regen)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "x,build,verify,wipe-redo", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_wip_verify () = Planning ("X-WIP-VERIFY", Minutes 60u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_1 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: the one heavy step the 85% client items wait on. verify15 (job-1793096804459) is running on the tree with the split, Bluesky A/B'/D/S1/R1, defuse wire v3, the perf fix and today's test fixes.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_2 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 2u32, "2026-10-27T12:34Z", "x", "2026-10-27 08:32 x: verify16b sim part (job-1793101238694, x/scripts/verify.ps1 -Part sim -Accept, pinned compiler): the Gleam frames built (11,469 lines -> 15 modules, largest 957), x-compat on the sim 0, and every sim fixture was re-accepted from the fixed split_cell (sim-small/stress/lost/gap world+expected, thread-oauth1, prelude events/final/parity; review pending). mix test 42/45, the same on both passes. Two tests timed out at 60 s (spiral_test 'a corpus run and the scenario facade draw the same deliveries', xsim_test 'evicting withdrawn results...'), and the known load-sensitive 'results assigned to whoever asked ... surface stale revisions' (an 80 ms executor against a 100 ms harvest window) passed where it should flag. The node was saturated (main: 9 jobs, 100% CPU), and verify15 passed 45/45 with the same split_cell code on a quieter node, so contention is the first suspect, per the retry rule. Open question to measure, not assume: the timeout stacks sit in the new defusing path (defused_dots_by -> pieces_from -> run_glyph -> ascii_of inside split_cell, which now posts before splitting), so the sim does more work per cell than before the split. Next: rerun only the sim part when the node is below about 70% CPU; if the timeouts repeat, time Frames.split per cell before and after posting.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_3 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 3u32, "2026-10-27T12:38Z", "x", "2026-10-27 08:38 x: reviewed verify16b's accepted sim fixtures against the tree. Every change comes from links-only defusing: the zero-width spaces are gone (sim-small 6 -> 0, lost 4 -> 0, gap 8 -> 0, stress 518 -> 0, prelude events 17 -> 0; none of the inputs has a known-TLD dot or a sigil), cut points move because posts weigh less (prelude events: '\\n    listm.foldBack' now fits in post 1), and stress world ids shift by one with fewer frames. The shape is OK, but NOT landed: the mirror was synced at 07:37, before prelude.spi step 2 changed spread's text, which these fixtures quote. The next verify re-accepts from the current tree, and those fixtures land after the same review.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_4 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 4u32, "2026-10-27T13:21Z", "x", "2026-10-27 09:20 x: generated outputs LANDED in the tree (unstaged), fixing the CI xc-windows 'couldn't find domains.rs'. x/scripts/verify.ps1 -Part regen (job-1793105792101, first real use of i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1: both syncs REMOTE-SYNC-OK, compiler pinned 4FD712E9E357) regenerated all 28 client crates with 0 failures. Compared with the same-compiler base (proof 7's split tree): api is unchanged and keeps its file; 25 crates CHANGED (the WIP touches prelude, wire and glyphs, which most crates open) and 2 are NEW (domains 334, requests 794); all 27 copied into apps/client/<crate>/<crate>.rs. Sizes: write 875 (the Bluesky with_site fix added about 160; R1's bound is 900), posted 899 (at the bound), xc 969, digest 954; 0 over 1000. Cargo.lock gains only xc_requests and xc_domains (+15 lines, through cargo metadata --offline; no version moved; old lock backed up in x-backup-1027-0355). Note verify16b client's first pass failed on infrastructure, not code: Cells stopped on 'Getting kino (Hex package)' (node network flaky today, like the gh TLS timeouts); its second pass is running. Next: one full verify of exactly this tree when the node frees.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_5 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 5u32, "2026-10-27T14:55Z", "x", "2026-10-27 10:55 x: verify17 verdict (job-1793108152156; the tree as of 09:28, pinned compiler). GREEN parts: client gate (28 crates, 0 over 1000) and x-compat 0 on both passes; e2e 153 requests; sim ExUnit 45/45 on both sim passes (so the 42/45 in verify16b was node load); corpus commute ok (699 s, 350 s per schedule); the real-Cells executor run passed; sim x-compat 0. RED, three causes, none in xc: (1) my e2e check read stdout (.Raw) for an stderr message (fixed in the tree after the sync); (2) verify.ps1 accepted the e2e tutorial BEFORE the sim accept regenerated the sim world fixtures that the tutorial's 'xc thread 3000001' step reads, so the plain pass found that step DIFFERENT (fixed: the sim accept now runs first); (3) apps/sim/build.ps1's tampered-thread negative control silently stopped working when oauth1.spi lost its string asserts in the 10-25 lib move (only '_assert_eq 40i32' is left), so replacing '_assert_eq \"' changed nothing and the tampered thread passed. Fixed: the tamper now appends a test that must fail (1i32 |> _assert_eq 2i32), so thread_run must reject it whatever the file asserts. Nothing landed from verify17's outputs (its README accept preceded its sim accept, and the tree has moved since); verify18 runs on the current tree with the fixed order and lands one consistent set.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_6 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 6u32, "2026-10-27T16:06Z", "x", "2026-10-27 12:06 x: closure rule for the 18 dependents, written before verify19 (job-1793116068742) finishes. GREEN means all of: verify exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, commute ok, thread_run pass, and the tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate with every crate <= 1000; x-compat 0 on both packages; every client notebook total with failed 0; e2e with no FAILED line and no DIFFERENT step on the plain pass. On GREEN, (a) land verify19's outputs with node-proof -Land x-verify19 -From C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xv19-out -Repo x: review the report, then -Apply; any CONFLICT is resolved by hand first. (b) Close at 100: SIM-WORLD-SPIRAL, SIM-RUNNER-CORE-SPIRAL, X-GENERIC-TO-LIB, X-PER-ACCOUNT-MIN-1, X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO, X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT, X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS (only if defuse, tlds and splitter appear among the notebook totals), X-LIB-FIRST-PRELUDE, X-COMPAT-VS-POSTABLE (then tell main: unblocks tibia), X-STRING-SLICE-SITES, X-SIM-ANYDOT-SWEEP, X-README-WIP-SYNC, X-REQUESTS-REVIEW (with write.rs landed), X-SITE-E2E-REVIEW, X-STUB-WEIGHTED-LIMIT, X-SPLIT-ON-NO-ARRAY, X-E2E-SAYS-HELPER and ORG-NODE-PROOF-LAND (after its first real -Apply). (c) X-TUTORIAL-DEFUSE-STEP closes only after a hand review of the accepted links.txt step: a ZWSP before .com and after @, none in listm.foldBack or x.io. (d) X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY stays open on its other deps (SPIRAL-PATH-SYNTAX, SPIRAL-ZWSP-TRANSPARENT). (e) XSIM-GLEAM-SPLIT-BENCH closes once its generated Gleam lands. NOT GREEN: nothing closes; fix the cause, then a new verify.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_7 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 7u32, "2026-10-27T20:56Z", "x", "2026-10-27 16:56 x: verify20 (job-1793123162251) NOT GREEN: (1) token/token's renewal test failed with memo_hits 0 (verify20 synced before the token fix; this refutes my stale-memo guess, which I retracted to main), and (2) it hit its 3 h cap (exit 124) in the final sim pass on a loaded node. Root cause of the failures surfacing one per verify: Invoke-SpiralTests stopped at the first failing notebook, so later ones were neither passed nor failed (token sits after defuse). Fixed at main's suggestion: every notebook runs, each prints passed/FAILED, and the run throws at the end naming all failures. verify21b (job-1793134676549, 6 h cap, manifest x-verify21b) carries the defuse and token fixes plus the run-all gate; closure follows note 6's rule.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_8 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 8u32, "2026-10-27T23:50Z", "x", "2026-10-27 19:50 x: verify21b (job-1793134676549) NOT GREEN, stopped: the client x-compat found one cell over weight (token.spi:153, 284 > 272), my token test edit, which I hadn't run the real x-compat on. That check precedes the notebooks, so they did not run. Everything else it reached was green: sim accept 45/45, gate 28 crates 0 over, e2e accept 2 of 37, the tampered thread rejected on same_cells. Fixed by moving the CR rendering into a shown_cr helper outside the cell; the real x-compat run locally (same DLL 4FD712E9E357) now reports 0 findings in 42 client and 24 sim files. verify22 (job-1793145082977, 6 h cap, manifest x-verify22) carries everything; closure follows note 6's rule, landing via node-proof -Land x-verify22 -From C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xv22-out -Repo x.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_9 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 9u32, "2026-10-28T00:15Z", "x", "2026-10-27 20:15 x: ADDENDUM to note 6's closure rule, before any verify22 result. Seven more rows close at 100 on the same GREEN: X-INVARIANTS-ROW-KIND, X-SIM-RUNNER-CRASHES, X-PAGING-GUARD, X-TOKEN-REFRESH-SAFE, X-LOOKUP-LIMITS and X-READ-BUDGET (their 'Done =' named 10-24 verify jobs that never went green; deps re-pointed from X-DONE, the epic they roll into, to X-WIP-VERIFY), plus X-READ-BUDGET's own condition: review the README answers that the e2e accept rewrote. X-GRANULAR-HEAL closes only after a verify that includes tonight's wire.spi reply_record heal (verify22 synced before it) and a wire.rs regen. X-SIM-FRAMES-GLEAM-IMPORTS was closed tonight on the existing evidence (frames compiles; sim 45/45 in every run today).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_10 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 10u32, "2026-10-28T01:50Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:50 x: verify22 (job-1793145082977) STOPPED at 21:4x before its verdict: it synced before tonight's wire reply_record heal, the CJK/emoji and RT:@ sigil-defuse fixes, and the 900 s cell budgets that the bench showed rust+gleam notebooks need under this load (its splitter/reading/defuse cells would time out at 300 s). verify23 (job-1793152313075, 8 h cap, manifest x-verify23) carries all of it. The closure rule (notes 6 and 9) now applies to verify23, and X-GRANULAR-HEAL and X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS close on it too, since it carries their changes.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_11 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 11u32, "2026-10-28T06:02Z", "x", "2026-10-28 02:02 x: verify23 (job-1793152313075, 14615 s) NOT GREEN on one cause: client gate 'posted 1034 lines OVER 1000' (tonight's sigil-defuse fixes grew it from 899), and the gate runs before the client notebooks, so those did not run. Everything else it reached was green: sim accept 45/45, the e2e accept (2 of 37 tutorial outputs rewritten), plain sim build exit 0 with all 23 sim notebooks passed and the per-module lines working, and the tampered thread rejected on same_cells=false. Fix: X-POSTED-MARGIN's planned split into a new xc_entities crate (note 3 there); regen measuring as job-1793167383150, then verify24 carries it. New untracked folder for the user's commit: apps/client/entities/.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_12 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 12u32, "2026-10-28T08:07Z", "x", "2026-10-28 04:07 x: verify24 (job-1793167893768, 6798 s) NOT GREEN on one notebook: the new entities/entities.spi test used zero_width_space without opening glyphs (Unbound), now fixed. Everything else was green: gate 29 crates 0 over (posted 555 after the X-POSTED-MARGIN split), the e2e accept, 16 client notebooks before entities passed, sim build exit 0 with all 23 sim notebooks passed, and the tamper rejection. It also exposed a second hole in MY run-all gate: the client loop STOPPED at entities, with no FAILED line and no later notebooks run. Spiral's Invoke-Block calls 'exit' (core.ps1 line 100) on a failure when OnError is Stop in a non-interactive host, and no try/catch can catch an exit; my 16:5x stub test modelled the failure as a throw, so it never went through that path. Fixed: Invoke-SpiralTests now runs the notebook runner directly and reads $LASTEXITCODE. Re-proven through the REAL path: a real child pwsh with a stub run_notebook.ps1 that exits 1 for module b ran all of a,b,c,d, marked b FAILED, and threw '1 of 4 notebooks failed: b'. Real x-compat 0 in 43 files. verify25 (job-1793174907446, manifest x-verify25) carries both fixes; closure per notes 6, 9 and 10.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_13 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 13u32, "2026-10-28T10:31Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:31 x groom: ADDENDUM to the closure rule (notes 6, 9, 10), written before verify25 reports. Also close at 100 on the same GREEN: X-E2E-NON-ASCII, X-EMOJI-WEIGHT and X-THREAD-RESUME (re-pointed from X-DONE today; their e2e steps run in every verify), X-POSTED-MARGIN, and X-E2E-SAYS-HELPER. After the reviewed node-proof -Land x-verify25 -Apply: ORG-NODE-PROOF-LAND (first real apply), XSIM-GLEAM-SPLIT-BENCH (generated Gleam landed), then SIM-GLEAM-PACKAGES. X-GRANULAR-HEAL closes on the verify after verify25 (its 4 lint heals came after verify25's sync).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_14 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 14u32, "2026-10-28T11:09Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:50 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_15 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 15u32, "2026-10-28T11:38Z", "x", "2026-10-28 07:38 x: ADDENDUM before verify27/28 report. verify27 (job-1793185923019; installed compiler A4E480202BD4, pre-respell tree with the lint heals) closes X-GRANULAR-HEAL if GREEN by note 6's clauses and confirms the compiler's three edition-3 features functionally (reported to the compiler team). verify28 (job-1793187520986; the same compiler on the respelled tree) closes X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY if GREEN; its outputs land three-way through node-proof -Land x-verify28 (report, review, -Apply). If verify28 is green, verify27's outputs are NOT landed: verify28's are the same compiler on the newer tree.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_16 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 16u32, "2026-10-29T11:44Z", "x", "2026-10-29 07:41 x: verify27/28 (10-28) both hit their 8h cap (exit 124) from NODE OVERLOAD, not a defect. On 10-28 the node carried both verifies plus tibia lib gates (4.6h each) and fiscal jobs. verify28's sim corpus was still running at the cap (verify25 did its 2 schedules in 577 s), and the 42/45 and 38/45 sim accepts were ExUnit 60s timeouts; the later plain mix test passed 45/45, all 42 client notebooks passed, and the e2e accepted 1 of 37 ('xc thread 3000001'). verify29 (node job-1793273389666, mirror xv29, compiler A4E480202BD4, 8h cap) replaces both. It was synced at 07:27 with the respell, the xc :~ headroom edit, and main's cells/dictm fixes. Per main (10-29), X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY closes with it. Closure rule = n6/n9/n10/n13/n15 applied to verify29: GREEN closes X-GRANULAR-HEAL, X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY; outputs land three-way via node-proof -Land x-verify29 -From C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xv29-out -Repo x. The manifest was rewritten at 07:28 after a node-proof -LandRepos comma bug, now fixed in i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_17 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 17u32, "2026-10-29T14:14Z", "x", "2026-10-29 10:4x x: ADDENDUM to the closure rule, written BEFORE verify29 reports (pre-registered). Context: verify29 (job-1793273389666) passed sim accept 45/45, the client gate (29 crates, 0 over), x-compat, the e2e accept (1 README answer rewritten: the respell's '.'->'::' inside the prelude-text fixture, benign, reviewed 08:3x) and the plain e2e (153 stub requests, 0 FAILED). It is now in the client notebooks (7 of 42 passed, 0 failed at 2h42m), on a node at 100% CPU with 6 other jobs, while verify25 needed 2.5h end to end. If verify29 hits its 8h cap: the phases it reported green STAND. A follow-up job on the SAME mirror xv29, with the tree unchanged (a re-sync must print the same digest, or the follow-up is void), runs exactly the not-yet-reported clauses: the remaining client notebooks via verify.ps1 -Notebooks <unrun list>, then the plain sim build (ExUnit, corpus commute, sim notebooks) and -Out for the three-way landing. Together they close per n6/n9/n10/n13/n15. A notebook that FAILED in verify29 is not rerun into green: it is a RED, diagnosed first. Asked fiscal (5 of 7 node jobs) to cap at 2 until verify29 reports.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_18 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 18u32, "2026-10-29T16:31Z", "x", "2026-10-29 12:3x x: COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE follow-up (main applied it 12:3x: apps/compiler/tmp/scripts -> apps/compiler/scripts, with forwarding stubs that write a notice to stderr). x had 3 callers of the old env.ps1; all now dot-source apps/compiler/scripts/env.ps1, keeping SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT = apps/compiler/tmp (the bundle root did not move): scripts/gate.ps1:14 (the client crate gate), apps/sim/build.ps1 (toolchain block) and scripts/sim-shell.ps1. Why not leave the stubs: a stderr line inside 2>&1 pipelines under ErrorActionPreference Stop can turn into a terminating error. Checked: the new path resolves the same package dir and the installed DLL with no stderr; a full scan of x's *.ps1/*.yml (19 files) shows 0 old callers. None of these is a verify output, so verify29's three-way land is unaffected; the NEXT verify runs all three on the real path.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_19 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 19u32, "2026-10-29T17:16Z", "x", "2026-10-29 13:1x x: verify29 GREEN (see X-EDITION3-RESPELL's closing note for every clause); it closed X-GRANULAR-HEAL, X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY, and its 20 outputs landed with 0 conflicts. Applied AFTER the land, as pre-registered: LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER's x half (net.spi 48466BA9 -> 4D3AB954) and CELLS-EVERYWHERE's fields.spi program. Both, plus the COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE path updates (n18), are proven by the next x verify, which runs on the installed pack-6b compiler once the node has it.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_20 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 20u32, "2026-10-29T18:38Z", "x", "2026-10-29 14:5x x: verify30 (job-1793295825981, pack-6b 9895730DAE80) RED on two causes, both fixed, neither from the counter or the respell. (1) MINE: the fields.spi test cell I added for CELLS-EVERYWHERE weighed 287 > 272 (one post minus the k/n header), and I had not run x-compat on the draft (the n8 lesson again). Split into two tests (a_payload_keeps_the_blank_defaults, empty_external_text_is_none); the real x-compat on pack-6b now reads 0 findings in 43 files (local, 5 s). Rule for myself from now on: run the installed compiler's --x-compat on apps/client and apps/sim/spi before launching any verify. (2) LOAD: sim accept 43/45, both failures ExUnit.TimeoutError at the 60 s default (XsimTest's correct-runner and eviction tests, async beside 16 cases on a node at 100%), the same as verify27/28. By SIM-IN-SPIRAL n64's rule (a deadline bounding an expected completion is raised; one whose expiry is the asserted outcome stays short), XsimTest gets @moduletag timeout: 300_000; its sleeps simulate slow executors and assert no timing. Everything else verify30 reached was green: 29 crates 0 over, 162 files 0 over. verify31 (job-1793299160741, pack-6b, 8h cap, mirror xv30 re-synced) carries both fixes; closure per n6/n9/n10/n13/n15/n17.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_21 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 21u32, "2026-10-29T19:57Z", "x", "2026-10-29 16:1x x: verify31 (job-1793299160741, pack-6b) went red on a COMPILER defect, not on x: xc_net failed with rustc E0599 (RequestBuilder has no clone). Root cause by the compiler lane (RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY): ureq's RequestBuilder was missing from codegen's move-only host types, and the clone-stripping post-pass bailed out of exchange because the compiler's own literal cache line (for the new 'xc_requests' argument of process_counter_add) looks like a closure. Reproduced locally from the exact source (evidence: C:\\home\\data\\x-evidence\\verify31-net-clone). Workaround in x (tree, unstaged): posted's branches now return the http_reply instead of a builder (post_builder_for removed), giving 0 non-Clone branch clones on 6b (scan positive-controlled). x-compat 0 on client (43 files) and sim (29). The compiler fix is verified on x's real failing source with the candidate (2 clones -> 0) and rides pack 8. Earlier in verify31: sim accept 45/45 (the ExUnit deadline fix works), x-compat 0, gate 29 crates 0 over. verify32 (job-1793303169424, 6b, re-synced after main's lib gap) carries the workaround; closure per n6..n17, and it is also the pack-6b re-proof of the three items closed on verify29.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_22 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 22u32, "2026-10-29T23:38Z", "x", "2026-10-29 19:38 x: verify32 (job-1793303169424, running for 3h50m) logged '** (Mix) .../apps/client/posts.spi: Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed', after both release builds finished (5m48s and 5m02s) on a node at 100% CPU. Cause class: LOAD. posts.spi had no budget in its header, so it ran at Cells' 300 s default, while 7 client notebooks (defuse, glyphs, paging, protocol, reading, splitter, tlds) carry --timeout 900000. By SIM-IN-SPIRAL n64 (a deadline bounding an expected completion is raised), posts.spi's header is now '///- --package . --timeout 900000' (unstaged). verify32's final verdict is still pending; if this is its only red, it is a load VOID for posts, not a code finding. verify33 carries the budget, thin16 and the entities dependency cleanup. Because main's pack-7 review rule forbids box compiles, x-compat runs as verify33's FIRST node step instead of locally (rule n20), and its result gates the rest of the job.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_23 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 23u32, "2026-10-30T00:52Z", "x", "2026-10-29 20:52 x: verify33 note: the live posts.spi header (--timeout 900000) changes the sim-stress fixtures (apps/client/e2e/sim-stress.world.json / .expected.json come from posts.spi). verify33 runs verify.ps1 -Accept, so it regenerates them and they land three-way with its outputs. Until then, a non-Accept sim build on the live tree fails Confirm-Fixture for sim-stress, which is expected and not a regression.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_24 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 24u32, "2026-10-30T01:58Z", "x", "2026-10-30T02:00Z groom: reopened Done 100 -> Active 80. The state was stale: verify30-33 (n20-n23) have run on this item since it was marked Done, and none is green yet. Remaining: verify32 (job-1793303169424, live in xv30, in its final sim build at 21:51) and verify33 (launch-x-verify33.ps1 into xv30, -Accept so the sim-stress fixture regenerates). Closes on verify33 green with its outputs landed three-way. LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER (dep) and X-CARGO-BUILD-PROFILE wait on the same run.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_25 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 25u32, "2026-10-30T02:04Z", "x", "2026-10-29 22:04 x: caught before launch: launch-x-verify33.ps1's x-compat gate matched '\\b0 findings\\b', but the installed compiler prints 'x-compat report: 0 finding(s) in N file(s)', so the gate could never pass and verify33 would have refused to start every time. Fixed to '^x-compat report: 0 finding\\(s\\) in [1-9]\\d* file\\(s\\)$'. Controls: clean report TRUE; '29 unchecked without a profile' FALSE; 5 findings FALSE; 0 files FALSE.")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_26 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 26u32, "2026-10-30T02:41Z", "x", "2026-10-29 22:3x x: verify32 (job-1793303169424) STOPPED by me at 22:34 after 6.8 h, with kit job stop (exit 143; 0 xv30/xv32 processes left). Verdict RED, cause LOAD (already known): apps/client/posts.spi failed 4 tests (zig targets, slowest 365 s against the 300 s cell budget; verify32 was synced before posts.spi got --timeout 900000). The other 56 notebooks it reached all passed. Stopping freed xv30 about 70 min early for the real proof: verify33 (job-1793328097444, pack 7 core 9C899B30495F7DC5, fixed x-compat gate, -Accept, LandRepos x,spiral) started 22:3x. It writes only to the xv30 mirror (re-synced by digest) and remote-stage\\xv32-out (partial, not landed).")
inl note_of_x_wip_verify_27 () = Note ("X-WIP-VERIFY", 27u32, "2026-10-30T10:26Z", "x", "2026-10-30 06:2x x groom: CLOSED with evidence. verify33 (job-1793328097444, pack 7 core 9C899B30495F7DC5, -Accept, LandRepos x,spiral) finished exit 0: client build, sim build, e2e accept and sim accept all exit 0; 66 notebooks passed.")
inl x_proof_scripts_in_repo () = Task ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", "x: the node proof scripts live in x/scripts, not %TEMP%: one parameterized verify (pinned compiler, OK-gated mirror syncs, client+sim, optional accepts, saved outputs), the base-vs-new output lander, and a crate-size measure", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "X-WIP-VERIFY", "x,build,verify,tooling", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo () = Planning ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_1 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: per the user's 10-27 03:2x rule (deliverables live in their proper repo place from the start). Today's verify11..15, base_regen, land_outputs and measure_* scripts are copies with one changed mirror name each. Fold them into x/scripts/node-verify.ps1 and friends, writing only under their -Out path.")
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_2 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:02Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:02 x: x/scripts/verify.ps1 in the tree (unstaged): -Accept (client build, e2e -Accept with the xc binary, sim -Accept), then client and sim build.ps1 plain, -Out saves .rs/.json/.jsonl/.txt/README.md and Cargo.lock, -Notebooks a,b runs only those notebooks through Assert-SpiralTotals; it prints the SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL hash when one is pinned. It also fixes the E2E-ACCEPT 'no xc binary' skip of verify12-15 (they never dot-sourced core.ps1, so _exe was undefined). Left: the node launcher (mirror sync gated on REMOTE-SYNC-OK, scp, job start, waiter) is cross-repo, so it belongs in i574n.github/scripts next to remote.ps1; land_outputs.ps1 (base-vs-new) goes in as x/scripts/land-outputs.ps1 after its first real use on verify15.")
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_3 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 3u32, "2026-10-27T11:46Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:46 x: the cross-repo half landed unstaged in i574n.github/scripts/node-proof.ps1 (org tooling, next to remote.ps1). -MirrorName -Label -Command ['{mirror}' expands to C:\\home\\remote\\<MirrorName>] [-Repos spiral,x] [-CompilerDll <node path>]. It writes a job script with the pinned compiler and the erlang/elixir PATH, parse-checks it, scps it to remote-stage\\<MirrorName>\\run.ps1 and checks the hash, syncs each repo to the mirror and throws unless every sync printed REMOTE-SYNC-OK, then starts the job. The command sits inside the staged script, so remote.ps1 never sees -Mirror/-Out-like arguments. Also fixed today in x/scripts/verify.ps1: -Part selected nothing (comma precedence) and exited 0; it now throws when nothing is selected. First real use: the next verify.")
inl note_of_x_proof_scripts_in_repo_4 () = Note ("X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:44Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:39 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
inl x_notebook_assert () = Task ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", "x: every scripted notebook check asserts on the spiral-tests total JSON (failed 0, passed = executed, unsupported 0) instead of trusting that Invoke-SpiralTests did not throw", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "X-WIP-VERIFY", "x,verify,tooling", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_notebook_assert () = Planning ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", Minutes 20u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_1 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: my B'/S1/R1 measure scripts printed NOTEBOOK ok over a test that does not parse (SOCIAL-PROFILES-LOCAL note 23). A small helper used by X-PROOF-SCRIPTS-IN-REPO.")
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_2 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:02Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:02 x: in the tree (unstaged): x/scripts/common.ps1 Assert-SpiralTotals throws unless every spiral-tests total line has failed 0, unsupported 0, not_run 0, passed = executed, and executed > 0 when tests were discovered, and throws when no total line exists. Checked against the real data: a good total passes, verify14b's failing wire.spi total throws, an output with no total throws. Root cause of the false NOTEBOOK ok lines: my measure scripts set ErrorActionPreference Continue, so Invoke-Block's failure was non-terminating and the catch never ran.")
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_3 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 3u32, "2026-10-27T17:23Z", "x", "2026-10-27 13:23 x: bug in my own Assert-SpiralTotals, found by its first real caller (node job-1793120236416, verify.ps1 -Notebooks defuse, 1004 s of notebook work then 'Cannot bind argument to parameter Lines because it is an empty string'). Its [string[]] parameter had [AllowEmptyCollection()] but not [AllowEmptyString()], and real notebook output always carries blank lines; the build.ps1 path never hit it, but both new verify.ps1 paths (-Notebooks and -ParallelNotebooks) would have thrown every time. My earlier controls passed because they used tidy arrays with no blank line, which is not the real data's shape. Fixed (both attributes) and re-proven locally: blank lines with a good total pass, blank lines with a failing total throw, no total throws. -Notebooks also printed nothing on success or failure; it now echoes the spiral-tests and type-error lines. The stopped bench (job-1793120714727) would have hit the same throw after its first arm; restarted as job-1793121820362, and defuse is rechecked as job-1793121647959.")
inl note_of_x_notebook_assert_4 () = Note ("X-NOTEBOOK-ASSERT", 4u32, "2026-10-28T10:45Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:39 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it).")
inl x_defuse_edge_tests () = Task ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", "x: tests pin the defuse edges: link dot and @/#/$ sigil at text start, at a chunk start, after an emoji or CJK glyph, and splitter split_cell defusing (the sim's contract)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "X-WIP-VERIFY", "x,splitter,defuse,tests", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_defuse_edge_tests () = Planning ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", Minutes 40u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_1 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T10:51Z", "x", "2026-10-27 06:51 x: two bugs today lived exactly there: ascii_of \"\" counted text start as non-ASCII, so a leading link stayed live, and the frames split dropped defusing from split_cell, which the sim calls. Draft the tests in the tree, unstaged; X-WIP-VERIFY runs them.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_2 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T11:02Z", "x", "2026-10-27 07:02 x: drafted in the tree (unstaged): defuse.spi a_link_and_a_mention_at_the_start_are_defused (cell.app and @bob at text start, the ascii_of empty-string bug) and a_link_right_after_a_wide_glyph_stays_plain (documents the blocks_domain rule), and splitter.spi split_cell_posts_before_splitting (the sim's contract). Every cell <= 272 and every line <= 120. They run in the next X-WIP-VERIFY (defuse and tlds are in build.ps1's notebook list now).")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_3 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T17:31Z", "x", "2026-10-27 13:31 x: PRODUCT BUG found by this item's new tests, the first time defuse.spi ran as a notebook (verify19, then node job-1793121647959): a mention at the very START of a post was never defused. mention_quiet asked sm'.contains prev \"!#$%&*@\", and lib's signature is contains (value) (s), so this tests whether the set contains prev; at the start prev is \"\", and every string contains \"\". So \"@bob hi\" posted with a live mention (expected '@<ZWSP>bob hi', got '@bob hi'; both failing tests start with @). Same class as this morning's ascii_of \"\" fix for dots. Fixed with glyphs.spi's existing one_of \"!#$%&*@\" prev, which requires a single glyph; hashtag_after and cash_quiet compare with =, so \"\" cannot match there, and no other sm'.contains <glyph> \"<set>\" call exists in x/apps. Also moved a_link_and_a_mention_at_the_start_are_defused below defused_entities (it ran before the definition: Unbound). Recheck: node job-1793122349993.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_4 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 4u32, "2026-10-28T00:25Z", "x", "2026-10-27 20:25 x: LEAK found while writing the 'after an emoji or CJK glyph' edge test: the mention and hashtag rules were SUBSETS of X's, against this item's own superset principle (an undefused token corrupts the post for good; an extra ZWSP costs 1 weight). Source, twitter-text master: js/src/regexp/validMentionPrecedingChars.js = (?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_!#$%&*@＠]|(?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_+~.-])(?:rt|RT|rT|Rt):?), so ANY non-ASCII glyph (CJK or emoji) before @ allows a live mention; js/src/regexp/hashtagBoundary.js = (?:^|︎|️|$|(?!hashtagAlphaNumeric|&)codePoint), so letters, marks and digits of every script block a hashtag but an emoji does not. x's defuse.spi blocked both on wide_letter (any non-ASCII), so '日本@bob' and '🙂@bob' posted live mentions and '🙂#tag' a live hashtag. Fixed (tree, unstaged): mention_quiet blocks only on ASCII word glyphs, !#$%&*@ and fullwidth ＠; hashtag_after only on ASCII word glyphs, & and # (so CJK before # gets an extra, harmless ZWSP: a superset). Cashtags already were a superset (X needs whitespace before $). New test sigils_after_wide_glyphs_are_defused. Known gap, not fixed: X's 'RT:@name' form allows a mention right after RT/rt letters, which needs more than one preceding glyph; recorded here for a follow-up. Real x-compat 0 in 42 files. Proof: node job-1793147170243 (defuse notebook), then the next full verify, whose accept may regenerate fixtures holding such texts. Sources: https://github.com/twitter/twitter-text/blob/master/js/src/regexp/validMentionPrecedingChars.js and https://github.com/twitter/twitter-text/blob/master/js/src/regexp/hashtagBoundary.js")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_5 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 5u32, "2026-10-28T01:05Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:05 x: defuse-nb4 (job-1793147170243): 2/8 passed, and all 6 failures are cell timeouts (300 s budget; one cell took 230 s on rust plus 120 s on gleam; node at 100% cpu), with no assertion failure and no type error. Per the user's no-quiet-machine rule the budget is the fix: defuse.spi's header now carries --timeout 900000, the lib's convention for files whose cells build both rust and gleam. Rerun: job-1793149356415.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_6 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 6u32, "2026-10-28T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:39 x: defuse proven under load (job-1793149356415, 2295 s): 8/8, including sigils_after_wide_glyphs_are_defused (a mention after CJK and a hashtag after an emoji now get their ZWSP). Slowest cell 525 s against the new 900 s budget (headroom 0.58); the old 300 s would have failed it, so the budget, not the code, caused nb4's 6 failures. What remains: the full verify that carries the fix (after verify22), where the e2e and sim accepts may regenerate fixtures, and the RT:@name gap from note 4.")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_7 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 7u32, "2026-10-28T01:50Z", "x", "2026-10-27 21:50 x: note 4's RT gap closed in the tree. twitter-text also accepts a mention after (?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9_+~.-])(?:rt|RT|rT|Rt):?, so 'RT@bob' and 'rt:@bob' are live on X. defuse.spi: rt_before looks back through entities_from's accumulated glyphs (an optional ':' then t/T, r/R) and rt_boundary requires nothing from [a-zA-Z0-9_+~.-] or the text start before them; mention_after takes 'mention_quiet prev || rt_before before'. Test a_mention_right_after_rt_is_defused: RT@bob and rt:@bob defused, art@bob plain (as on X). Real x-compat 0 in 42 files. Proof: verify23 (job-1793152313075).")
inl note_of_x_defuse_edge_tests_8 () = Note ("X-DEFUSE-EDGE-TESTS", 8u32, "2026-10-28T10:47Z", "x", "2026-10-28 06:39 x: CLOSED by X-WIP-VERIFY's pre-registered rule. verify25 (node job-1793174907446, pinned compiler 4FD712E9E357) GREEN on every clause of X-WIP-VERIFY note 6: exit 0; sim accept and plain sim build exit 0 (ExUnit 45/45, corpus commute ok, thread_run pass, tamper rejected with same_cells=false); client gate 29 crates 0 over 1000; x-compat 0 in 43 client and 24 sim files; all 42 client and 23 sim notebooks passed, 0 failing totals; plain-pass e2e 37 of 37 tutorial steps same, 0 FAILED, 153 stub requests. Outputs landed three-way (node-proof -Land x-verify25: 21 files plus 19 Gleam modules, 0 conflicts; net.rs held back because its source changed after the sync, so verify26 lands it). Its condition holds: defuse, tlds and splitter are among the 42 client notebooks that passed.")
