inl xsd_facet_types () = Task ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", "xsd_emit: XSD builtins become real types (decimal.decimal, i64, bool, date nominals); facet-free restrictions alias their parent; totalDigits/fractionDigits/min/max facets validated", Story, P0, D5, 65u32, Active, "FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", "team:fiscal,fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_facet_types () = Planning ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_1 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 1u32, "2026-10-27T12:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:35 fiscal: STEP 1 IN THE TREE, unstaged (lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi EDE98016): a NAMED facet-free restriction of a named type that this module emits now ALIASES its parent instead of becoming '= string' (the review's TServ restricts the pattern-checked TString and lost the pattern, nfe_v3_10:734; 53 such aliases in generated_cte_v4_00). Done at module assembly, not in emit_named_type, so inline anonymous restrictions are untouched: simple_aliases (named, no enumeration, not constrained, non-builtin base, parent emitted here), inherited_kinds (an alias takes its parent's kind through chains, bounded at 64 against cycles), aliased_items (the item's text becomes 'type ty = parent' with ty_example/ty_example_text delegating, plus ty_of_string/ty_to_string delegating when the resolved kind is enum or validated, so readers call the parent's validator and writers use the parent's to_text instance: no second instance). Test a_facet_free_restriction_aliases_its_parent. Type-checked: xsd_emit + probe + json_schema 0 errors; formatter no-op. Remaining steps of this item: builtins to real types (decimal.decimal, i64, bool, date nominals), totalDigits/fractionDigits/min/max facets validated, dead 'true &&' conjuncts. Proof: full regeneration + every unit compiled, queued on a reused node mirror after cj-proof (node disk is tight).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_2 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 2u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. This item's a_facet_free_restriction_aliases_its_parent passes (step 1 proven at the emitter level; units and samples follow in the same run).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_3 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 3u32, "2026-10-27T18:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 14:31 fiscal: constraint for 'builtins as real types': xs:integer is UNBOUNDED; real signed documents carry 39-digit X509SerialNumber (MyInvois samples), which .NET's decimal-backed validator rejects. Today our readers keep unrestricted builtins as text, so they are correct; a numeric type for xs:integer must be arbitrary precision (or stay text), never i64/decimal.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_4 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 4u32, "2026-10-30T15:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:37 fiscal: GROOM R3 (2.9 d): Active -> Paused, progress kept (step 1, facet-free aliases, proven 10-27; the xs:integer constraint of 10-27 14:31 stands: arbitrary precision or text, never i64/decimal). The remaining steps change lib xsd_emit's output. The edition-3 round's gate compares generated units from two trees on ONE lib (p7cl vs e3lv, 74 units), so emitter changes wait until that round closes. Dep FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND; resume when it lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_5 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 5u32, "2026-10-31T21:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 17:09 fiscal: RE-DECIDED: stays Paused. REASON (still true today): its remaining steps change xsd_emit/generator output, and FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (95%, held behind EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL, 95%, compiler pack 9) will respell that text; writing against the pre-respell tree would stale every anchor (rule anchors-stale-across-respell). RESUME CONDITION: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND reaches Done (the dep is recorded), then resume as Planned and re-anchor on the respelled tree.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_6 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 6u32, "2026-11-01T12:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:38 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). PRIORITY P0 (Paused on FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, in deps): generated fields typed as string where the XSD says decimal/integer/boolean/date are the main remaining \"stringly\" output of the lane.\nDONE WHEN: (a) a node gate of xsd_emit.spi with 0 failed, including new tests builtins_become_carrier_types (xs:decimal -> decimal.decimal, xs:integer family -> i64 with range, xs:boolean -> bool, xs:date -> date nominal) and facets_build_only_through_validators; (b) regenerated generated_nfe_v4: every xs:decimal-based field (e.g. TDec_1302 values) has a decimal carrier, and its round-trip tests stay green; (c) model_metrics.ps1 over lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi: M7 string dispatch below 40 per 1k lines (81 in model-metrics-lib-20261031.tsv); (d) 0 generated drift other than the intended type changes, reviewed per family.\nNEXT STEP: after the e3 round lands, draft on a scratch lib: replace builtin_example / prefers_builtin_example / is_calendar_builtin (xsd_emit.spi :836-851, string compares on xml.local_name) with one classification function returning the GADT below; move positive_example (:853, added 11-01) onto it.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a GADT indexed by the Spiral carrier type: \":| ^ builtin carrier = | DecimalBuiltin :: builtin decimal | IntegerBuiltin :: { min : option i64; max : option i64 } -> builtin i64 | BoolBuiltin :: builtin bool | DateBuiltin :: builtin date | TextBuiltin :: builtin string\". classify (reference) : exists carrier. builtin carrier (an existential) is the ONLY place a builtin's local name is read. Example values, readers (of_text) and writers (to_text) are prototype instances over the carrier (\":+ example_of builtin\", \":+ parse_of builtin\"), so adding a builtin is a GADT case plus instances, never another string branch. Facets wrap a carrier in a validated nominal built only by its smart constructor (of_string : string -> option t); raw strings where a validated value is expected stay a type error (the item FISCAL-APP lists as a known limit). No -1 or \"\" sentinels: bounds are option i64. MODEL: xsd.spi''s GADT \"xsd sort form\" (:48-80); the mega sample mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel for indexed families.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_7 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 7u32, "2026-11-02T21:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 17:20 fiscal: RE-DECIDED (stop-gate groom): Paused -> Planned. The recorded resume condition is MET: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND is Done since 11-01 14:4x (CI run 41314140694, both OSes), and lib xsd_emit.spi is in edition 3, so new work anchors on the respelled tree. ORDER (from the specs): XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES first (it is the base of XSD-FACET-TYPES' parse/example instances and XSD-DECODE-RESULT's of_xml returning result), then XSD-DECODE-RESULT, then XSD-FACET-TYPES. Each changes every generated unit, so each lands with one full node regen; the first starts after the 90-file shared-runtime regen and the typed family-roots regen are placed in fiscal/generated, so drifts don't compound.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_8 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T12:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:07 fiscal: NEXT STEP (n? spec) DRAFTED, output-neutral, inside the GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT draft (drafts\\spiral\\GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi, layered on the decode draft): builtin_example / is_calendar_builtin / prefers_builtin_example / positive_example no longer string-compare xml::local_name in four places; one classifier builtin_kind_of returns ':| builtin_kind = Base64Builtin | UriBuiltin | IdBuiltin | DateTimeBuiltin | DateBuiltin | BooleanBuiltin | PositiveIntegerBuiltin | OtherBuiltin', and the four functions match on it (semantics kept exactly: builtin_example classifies by local name alone, the calendar/positive checks keep their is_builtin_reference guards; is_positive_integer_builtin is shared). vultr pack27: --check exit 0, format clean; output-identity run queued with the split steps. The carrier-indexed GADT (':| builtin carrier = DecimalBuiltin :: builtin decimal | ...') is the type-changing step that follows XSD-DECODE-RESULT's land, per the ORDER (codec -> decode -> facet types).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_9 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 9u32, "2026-11-05T04:34Z", "fiscal", "DESIGN DECISION (grounded), 11-05 00:5x local: builtin carriers must keep their lexical text. Corpus facts (fiscal deps/corpus, 319 xml, all 6846 cbc *Amount/*Quantity/*Percent/*Rate/*Numeric values): 4478 (65%) end in a trailing zero after the point (100.00); 8 have leading zeros (ZATCA zero tax 00.00 / 00.0, in 5 documents); 1 has a trailing space (UBL-TR TicariFaturaOrnegi 786.90 ); 1 is not a number (LHDN my/samples/1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency-Sample.xml PayableAmount = abc); 0 plus signs. Lib decimal.parse NORMALIZES (+007.500 prints back as 7.5, 2.50 as 2.5), so a plain decimal.decimal field would break 65% of real-document read-backs, and a scale-keeping decimal would still break ZATCA and TR. DECISION: one generic carrier \":== lexical t = { value : t; text : string }\" (value = typed, validated, used for arithmetic; text = the raw lexical form the writer prints). Built from a value through a canonical printer (decimal.text, i64 / bool printers), and read through parse-or-Invalid, so the decode result carries Invalid (path, text) for abc. Fields: xs:decimal -> lexical decimal.decimal; integer family -> lexical i64 (range facets checked); xs:boolean -> lexical bool (1/0/true/false all parse; text keeps the spelling); date/dateTime stay text until a date nominal exists. This updates DoD (a)/(b): \"every builtin-typed field has a lexical carrier, and its round-trip tests stay green\". Expected intended drift: LHDN 1.1 ForeignCurrency becomes a decode failure (a true sample defect), to be recorded as that family's known_defect, not hidden. Draft order: a new lib draft layered on GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT (AB4B0165) plus xml_codec readers; proof after XSD-DECODE-RESULT lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_10 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 10u32, "2026-11-05T04:54Z", "fiscal", "DRAFTED + emitter-PROVEN, 11-05 01:0x local: drafts\\spiral\\XSD-FACET-TYPES\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi 4E831159 (formatter output), base xsd_emit.base-AB4B0165 = the GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT draft, layered on the decode draft. 220 changed lines. Design (n9) implemented through the EXISTING codec path, not a new kind: builtin decimal/integer-family/boolean references map to carrier aliases with kind KindValidated, so reader (read_value <t>_of_string), writer (text_node / to_text), attributes (attribute_parsed), simpleContent base (parsed_text / to_text x.base), examples (<t>_example) and fixed values (required_value) all work unchanged. Pieces: builtin_kind gains DecimalBuiltin / IntegerBuiltin (integer long int short byte) / NonNegativeIntegerBuiltin (nonNegativeInteger unsignedInt/Short/Byte; unsignedLong stays text because it overflows i64); builtin_kind_of is now one data table plus a lookup instead of a 9-arm string chain (M7 -9); a carriers () data table {kind; name; value_type; parse; example} is the single source for kind_carrier and the prelude; carrier_prelude body emits \"nominal lexical t = { value : t; text : string }\", \"instance to_text lexical t = fun x => x.text\", lexical_of, whole_of / whole_at_least / boolean_of, and per USED carrier \"type xsd_decimal = lexical decimal.decimal\" plus _of_string / _example / _example_text, in main units and in the family core (versions open the core). Text-only units get NO carrier text. PROOF vultr pack27, base-decode (xml_codec 5694B36A): --check module + bodies exit 0; negative control (reference_type returns 1i32) gives ETY-TermError exit 5. New tests builtins_become_lexical_carriers and text_only_schemas_declare_no_carrier run in Rust: run exit 0. Mutant (\"decimal\" mapped to OtherBuiltin) FAILS with \"xs:decimal is carried as xsd_decimal\". Round trip canonical/fixpoint true (pre-format 7003D2B1; formatted copy recheck pending). NEXT: generated-unit --check probe (queued on vultr, load-gated; vultr at load 11-38 from main's file_system gate and k3s), then a full regen diff vs gen-decode2 plus node gates after the decode land.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_11 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 11u32, "2026-11-05T05:06Z", "fiscal", "GENERATED-CODE PROVEN, 11-05 01:1x local, vultr pack27 over base-decode. (1) The facet emitter 4E831159, compiled to Rust, wrote a unit for a probe schema (decimal / positiveInteger / repeated nonNegativeInteger / optional boolean elements, a required xs:int attribute, an optional xs:decimal attribute, a simpleContent xs:decimal base). It shows fields total : xsd_decimal, count : list (xsd_non_negative_integer), paid : option (xsd_boolean), seq : xsd_integer, base : xsd_decimal, readers read_value <carrier>_of_string, and attribute_parsed xsd_integer_of_string. The unit --check passes with exit 0 and 0 diagnostics. Controls: d.unitz inside whole_of gives ETY-RecordIndexFailed (23:52) and x.textz inside the to_text lexical instance gives ETY-RecordIndexFailed (16:39), so the prelude bodies are really checked. (2) BEHAVIOUR in native Rust, 14 checks on the corpus forms all pass: ZATCA 00.00 parses with value 0 and prints back 00.00; UBL 100.00 prints back 100.00; UBL-TR \"786.90 \" prints back with its trailing space; LHDN abc does not parse; integer 1.0 does not parse; positive 0 does not parse; non-negative 0 parses and -1 does not; boolean 1 prints back 1; boolean 0 and \" false \" read as false; boolean yes does not parse. Mutant (positive accepts 0) FAILS with \"positive 0 parses but must not\". Round trip of the formatted 4E831159: canonical/fixpoint true. PENDING (vultr, load-gated): full regen with the facet emitter in its own tree facet-gen, diffed unit by unit against dec-gen (same generator, decode lib), plus --check of every changed unit (log facet-regen-1793855140.log).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_12 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 12u32, "2026-11-05T05:17Z", "fiscal", "FULL REGEN with the facet emitter, 11-05 01:1x local, vultr pack27, own tree facet-gen (dec-gen's generator DA6BE426 + decode lib, with xsd_emit replaced by 4E831159; log facet-regen-1793855140.log): compile 21 s, rustc 196 s, run \"exit 36\" = main's return value, write_family_modules counting 36 families (69 units), not an error. Against dec-gen (same generator, pre-facet emitter): 49 units BYTE-IDENTICAL (every NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e/GTV-e/event/CFDI/KSeF/UBL-applicationresponse etc.: no direct numeric or boolean builtins), 20 CHANGED, 0 missing. Each changed unit gets only the carriers it uses: cii_d16b decimal+boolean; cl_dte / cl_envio decimal+integer+positive; the 9 CR hacienda units integer only (42 lines each); es_facturae and es_verifactu integer; fatturapa integer; gr_mydata decimal+integer+boolean (336 lines); hu_nav boolean; pt_saft non_negative_integer (232 lines); ubl_invoice / ubl_creditnote decimal+integer+boolean (132 lines). All 20 changed units --check exit 0 with 0 diagnostics. LEFT for the DoD: (b) node Cells gates of the 20 changed units after the decode land, where real-document read-backs exercise the lexical round trip, with the LHDN abc sample expected to report Invalid and become ubl_invoice's recorded defect; (c) model_metrics M7 on xsd_emit; (d) per-family drift review (the 20 above).")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_13 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 13u32, "2026-11-05T05:23Z", "fiscal", "DoD (c) MET, 11-05 01:2x local, spiral apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1 on the code lines (tests excluded): xsd_emit M7 string dispatch 6.3 /kl on the split base AB4B0165 (3498 lines, 423 defs) -> 4.2 /kl on the facet draft 4E831159 (3612 lines, 437 defs); M8 sentinels 0 -> 0. The DoD asked for below 40 (it was 81 on 10-31). The drop comes from builtin_kind_of becoming a data table plus a lookup. Status: (a) emitter tests proven in Rust; (b) PENDING the node Cells gates of the 20 changed units after the decode land; (c) met; (d) the drift list is in n12.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_14 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 14u32, "2026-11-05T06:06Z", "fiscal", "FACET LAND COMPANIONS DRAFTED + PROVEN, 11-05 02:0x local (drafts\\spiral\\XSD-FACET-TYPES\\fiscal\\src). The facet types make one official sample fail by design (LHDN my/samples/1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency-Sample.xml, PayableAmount abc), so per-document defects are now MODELED, not hidden. families.spi 8472AD8B (base F1CF3DDF): \":| family_extra\" gains \"DocumentDefect : string * string\" (path, expected message) and document_defects extras, so the other 20 family literals are untouched; ubl_invoice_2_1 extras = [ DocumentDefect (\"deps/corpus/my/samples/1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency-Sample.xml\", \"PayableAmount: abc\") ]. The message text comes from xml_codec error_text (\"invalid <path>: <text>\"). generator.spi CE32E90E (base .next7 D6F663A7): document_checks drops recorded defects from the read-back list at generation time and emits defect_check, which asserts each one FAILS and that its first failure contains the expected text (\"a recorded defect now reads back\" / \"fails differently: ...\"). New test a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back. PROOF vultr pack27, lib = sentinel D00BE390: generator --check + bodies exit 0 (the package includes the families draft); the defect test and ubl_json_documents_read_through_the_transcoder run in Rust with exit 0 (FISCAL_ROOT set for the binary; run-rust.sh sets it only for the compile). MUTANT (the DocumentDefect removed from ubl_invoice) FAILS \"a recorded defect leaves the read-back list\". LAND ORDER: decode -> split -> (.next6 + families F1CF3DDF) -> facet lib 4E831159 + sentinel lib D00BE390 + this families 8472AD8B + generator CE32E90E in ONE window.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_15 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 15u32, "2026-11-05T06:15Z", "fiscal", "Validity note on n12's regen (11-05 02:1x local): the facet-gen scratch tree copied dec-gen's absolute lib symlink, so its deps write went THROUGH to dec-gen/lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi (memory scratch-tree-copies-keep-symlinks). The n12 verdict STANDS: the generator compile used facet-gen's real lib copy (4E831159), the 20 unit checks resolved the same facet xsd_emit through the link, and the dec-gen baseline units it was diffed against were generated at 11-04 21:27Z, before any of this. dec-gen is restored to the decode 5B274B48 and checked by hash.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_16 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 16u32, "2026-11-05T12:08Z", "fiscal", "FACET COMPANIONS REBASED onto live fiscal src (after the 08:0x generator/families land), 11-05 08:1x local: drafts\\spiral\\XSD-FACET-TYPES\\fiscal\\src2\\ families.spi 889D2546 (base 99A8339B: DocumentDefect + document_defects, ubl_invoice_2_1 extras record the LHDN 1.1 ForeignCurrency sample) and generator.spi 96302219 (base 40DE71DF: write_certificates_unit takes option string; document_checks drops recorded defects through documents_of plus kept_documents, then emits defect_check; new test a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back). The src\\ drafts (on .next7 / F1CF3DDF) are superseded. PROOF vultr pack27 over the sentinel lib D00BE390 (facet + sentinel): generator --check + bodies exit 0; the defect and transcoder tests run in Rust with exit 0; MUTANT (DocumentDefect removed) FAILS 'a recorded defect leaves the read-back list'; reference 5B274B48 held. GRANULAR (vultr counter): families 4 code defs over, generator 0 of 98. THE FACET WINDOW is then: lib xsd_emit D00BE390 (facet 4E831159 + sentinel, on live AB4B0165) + fiscal families 889D2546 + generator 96302219 + the 20 changed units. PENDING before it: DoD (b), node Cells gates of the 20 changed units.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_17 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 17u32, "2026-11-05T12:14Z", "fiscal", "DoD (b) STARTED, 11-05 08:2x local: node job-1793880841250-fiscal-facet-gate (cap 36000000 ms from start; script node-facet-gate.ps1 6D57D24F; inputs hash-verified). It builds a scratch tree: core; the mirror lib with xml B6EED09B, xml_codec 5694B36A and the sentinel xsd_emit D00BE390 (facet + sentinel); live fiscal src with the rebased companions families 889D2546 / generator 96302219 and the harness main; the corpus as a read-only junction. It regenerates every unit, then Cells-gates (lib_gate, pinned compiler) each unit that declares \"nominal lexical t\" (the carrier units, about 20), with caps raised x3 IN THE SCRATCH TREE ONLY, so a kill leaves no shared-mirror state. Guards: corpus file count and mirror xsd_emit hash compared start vs end; junctions removed as links before any delete. Expected intended drift: ubl_invoice's real-document test now asserts the LHDN abc sample as a recorded defect. PENDING.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_18 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 18u32, "2026-11-05T15:40Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:4x local fiscal: FACET-WINDOW COMPANION TESTS BODY-PROVEN on VULTR, ahead of the land (the node facet gate covers the generated units, not these src tests). Stage = box core + box lib with the sentinel xsd_emit D00BE390 + live fiscal src with src2 families 8F72669F and generator 6ADC38CB over it; pinned vultr compiler core dc49ffdc170199df. eff-fam1793893052: families' 2 bodies (every_family_has_its_own_module_name, every_regime_lists_its_own_families) compile, rustc, run exit 0. eff-gen1793893052: generator a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back compile, rustc, run exit 0. Neither compile printed ParserErrors, so no test block was silently dropped. MUTANT eff-genm1793893148 (the recorded defect's message 'PayableAmount: abc' -> 'xyz' in families): run exit 1 with exactly 'the LHDN sample must fail with its recorded message'. Window pre-checks also done (bases AB4B0165 / E6AC72B3 / 03111A90 live, drafts at their recorded hashes). Waiting only on the node facet gate (15/20 green at 11:29) and the regen-and-zip job.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_19 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 19u32, "2026-11-05T15:43Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:4x local fiscal (follow-up): the other LIGHT src2 generator tests are body-proven on vultr too, same facet stage (sentinel lib D00BE390, src2 generator 6ADC38CB, families 8F72669F, plus the it/fatturapa, pl/ksef and DFe.NET tiposBasico schemas they read): eff-gl1793893349 generates_the_uf_code_union, ubl_json_documents_read_through_the_transcoder, unqualified_schemas_prefix_the_example_root -- compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors. With a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back that is 4 of the generator's 25 tests; the other 21 regenerate whole families (write_family_modules / generates_*) and are covered by the node regen + facet unit gates, not repeated on the 2-CPU vultr.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_20 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 20u32, "2026-11-05T16:20Z", "fiscal", "11-05 12:2x local fiscal: the queued regen-and-zip job (job-1793883003188, not started yet) now FORMATS the regenerated units before zipping (script D4120E4D runs fiscal scripts/format-generated.ps1 0C8D80B8 -Jobs 4 with the node's pinned compiler, core 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3 like the box), because the live generated/ units are committed formatted: an unformatted zip would show every unit as changed. Placement prepared: scratch facet-place-units.ps1 (dry run lists changed / unchanged / new / missing units against fiscal/generated; -Apply backs up each replaced unit, then places). Expected after the window: the 20 carrier units changed, the other 62 byte-identical.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_21 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 21u32, "2026-11-05T16:23Z", "fiscal", "11-05 12:2x local fiscal: GAP FOUND AND CLOSED before the window. The facet harness main (used by the identity regens and the facet gate's own regen) named only 13 families + family_roots / hacienda_documents / nfe_events, so 9 families never regenerated under the facet emitter: nfe_v4_00, cfdi_tfd_1_1, cfdi_pagos_2_0, cfdi_v4_0, ksef_fa_3 and ubl_business_documents_2_1 (DebitNote, ApplicationResponse, DespatchAdvice, ReceiptAdvice; 0 carriers in their live units today, decimals that a facet emitter would carry). Landing the window without them would leave those units on the pre-facet generator and CI's regen drift check (scripts/build.ps1: 'generated: N files differ from the committed copy') would go red. FIX in the still-queued regen job-1793883003188: harness-main.spi 491D7AB1 now writes every family the generator tests write (CFDI in the test's order tfd, pagos, cfdi), and node-facet-regen.ps1 4403B67A, after formatting and zipping, GATES every carrier unit that is not among the facet gate's 20 (same x3 scratch cap), so the window's unit set is proven complete before it lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_22 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 22u32, "2026-11-05T19:00Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:0x local fiscal: NODE CONTENTION, status of the last facet unit: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's gate started 12:49; its rustc (pid 21888, started 12:55) is still compiling at 15:00 with 4,699 CPU-seconds, i.e. about 40% of a core, because the node runs at 100% with another lane's dotnet / erl jobs started 14:58 (not mine, not touched). Its scratch cell cap is 5 h (to about 17:49) and the gate job's own cap 10 h (to about 18:20). PROJECTION: invoice verdict in about an hour, then the regen (compile + rustc + run + format 82 + gates of the 9 newly included families' carrier units) another 3-4 h under this load, so the window can land around 20:00 at best; the src Cells confirmation and the MyInvois twin job queued after it will most likely still be pending at 21:00 (both already body-proven on vultr). If the invoice gate hits its cap the verdict is VOID, not red, and the unit is re-gated alone.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_23 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 23u32, "2026-11-05T19:24Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:2x local fiscal: FACET GATE GREEN on the NODE, job-1793880841250 (t1101 scratch tree: base lib + decode xml / xml_codec + the sentinel xsd_emit D00BE390 + src2 families 8F72669F / generator 6ADC38CB + harness; pinned compiler copy): all 20 carrier units passed -- cii_d16b, cl_dte_v10, cl_envio_dte_v10, the 9 Costa Rica 4.4 units, es_facturae_3_2_2, es_verifactu, fatturapa_1_2_3, gr_mydata_2_0_2, hu_nav_3_0, pt_saft_1_04_01 (2/2 each), ubl_creditnote_2_1 and ubl_invoice_2_1 (1/1 each: their single writes_its_example test carries every document read-back; invoice finished 15:22 after a contended 2.5 h rustc). Corpus 1290 files start and end, mirror xsd_emit 738935CD unchanged, tree dropped. NEXT on the node, now running: the regen-and-zip job-1793883003188 (full harness, format pass, gates of the newly included families' carrier units); the window lands once that is green.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_24 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 24u32, "2026-11-05T20:04Z", "fiscal", "11-05 16:0x local fiscal: REGEN DONE on the NODE (job-1793883003188, exit 0): compile 38 s, rustc 1495 s, run 449 s, 45 families -> 83 units (the full harness; the unit set equals fiscal/generated exactly), zip C:\\home\\remote-stage\\fiscal-facet-regen-units.zip 6DD036E2 (4781 KB), corpus 1290 start / end, mirror untouched. TWO CORRECTIONS to my 12:2x notes: (a) the job runs C:\\home\\remote-stage\\node-facet-regen.ps1 (its argv), not the copy I patched in fiscal-facet-in, so the format pass and the extra gates did NOT run; only the full harness (read from the inputs folder) took effect. (b) The facet gate and this regen used the node's input copies generator 96302219 / families 889D2546; formatted with the box compiler they are byte-identical to src2 6ADC38CB / 8F72669F, so the gated code IS the window's code. CARRIER UNITS in the zip: 25; the 20 already green plus 5 never gated: generated_ksef_fa_3 (815 KB) and the four UBL business units applicationresponse / debitnote / despatchadvice / receiptadvice (about 3.6 MB each, the invoice unit's size class, whose rustc peaked at 6.4 GB). NF-e and the CFDI trio gained no carriers. DECISION: the window does NOT land today. Landing 78 proven units with 5 unproven would leave those 5 on the old emitter and turn CI's generated-drift check red, and the 4 big units cannot run on vultr (3.3 GB) or the box (3.7 GB free) and take 1-2.5 h each on the contended node. QUEUED: node job-1793908968483-fiscal-facet-extra (script 2F5DA04A, after the MyInvois twin job, 12 h cap): the same scratch tree as the facet gate, all 83 regenerated units unpacked from the zip, the 5 gated (x3 scratch cap). It will run overnight; the window (lib xsd_emit D00BE390 on base AB4B0165 + src2 families / generator + the 25 formatted units) follows its verdict.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_25 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 25u32, "2026-11-05T23:38Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:3x local fiscal: FACET WINDOW LANDED, unstaged. Gate: node job-1793908968483-fiscal-facet-extra finished exit 0, all 5 remaining carrier units green in Cells (ksef_fa_3 2/2, ubl applicationresponse / debitnote / despatchadvice / receiptadvice 1/1 each; guards: corpus 1290 files and mirror xsd_emit 738935CD unchanged start to end), on top of the earlier facet gate's units. Pre-land consumer check (lesson from main's json_schema red): json_schema F7564185, the only lib caller of xsd_emit, ran 8/8 bodies green on vultr against the draft. (1) lib: lib_land_window label fiscal-facet-1105, xsd_emit.spi AB4B0165 -> D00BE390 (facet + sentinel): signatures unchanged, apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (36 tests typed), 0 respell drift, lib digest D63B5E3ED272FCFB, undo 20261105-193122. (2) fiscal src: families E6AC72B3 -> 8F72669F and generator 03111A90 -> 6ADC38CB (the src2 companions; format-only over the 889D2546 / 96302219 text the node gated); package --check exit 0. Backups families/generator.before-facet-* in the session scratchpad. (3) generated/: 25 of 83 units replaced by the pin-a688-formatted regen (58 byte-identical); re-run dry run: 0 changed. Backup generated.before-facet-20261105-193742 in the session scratchpad. PENDING: a box regen identity check with the live generator, and CI at the user's next push.")
inl note_of_xsd_facet_types_26 () = Note ("XSD-FACET-TYPES", 26u32, "2026-11-06T00:28Z", "fiscal", "11-05 20:2x local fiscal: REGEN IDENTITY PROVEN on the box (scratch trees, pinned compiler a688, today's live box lib with xsd_emit D00BE390, full box corpus, 1292 files unchanged start to end): the whole-family regen harness run with the generator the node gated (96302219 + families 889D2546) and with the live formatted pair (6ADC38CB + 8F72669F) wrote the same 83 units: 166 files each, 0 differing, 0 on one side only (each run exit 45 = family count). So the format pass that produced the live companions changed no generated text. Remaining for this item: CI at the user's next push.")
inl xsd_decode_result () = Task ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", "generated readers return result t decode_error (Missing/Invalid/Unexpected with element path) instead of failwith; failwith only at the test boundary", Story, P0, D5, 98u32, Active, "FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", "team:fiscal,fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_decode_result () = Planning ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_1 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 1u32, "2026-10-27T13:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:00 fiscal: DESIGN (no code yet). Rejected: a result per field with a match on each (nests every record reader; rustc is already 92% of UBL's 2,852 s cell, FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE n7). Rejected: a mutable decode context, because lib's ref is an F#-only macro (base.spi:573, \\$'\\\t ref') and generated tests run on Rust. CHOSEN: pure state-passing, linear: every reader takes the path and the error list and returns its value with the extended list: '_of_children (path : list string) (attributes) (children) (errors : list decode_error) : t * list decode_error'; a record body becomes 'inl a, e1 = <read a> e0 ... inl z, eN = <read z> eN-1' then '{ a = a; ... }, eN'; a missing or invalid required value records Missing (path, name) / Invalid (path, name, text) and yields the type's existing '_example 0i32' as a placeholder, so decoding goes on and reports EVERY problem, not just the first; unclaimed children (xml.unclaimed_children) can feed Unexpected. Entry: 'x_root_decode (c) : result x_root (list decode_error)' = Ok when the list is empty, else Error (reverse). xml.spi gains the decode_error union and required_value_or / required_child_or helpers; failwith stays only in tests. ORDER: implemented after the joint regeneration proof of the four emitter changes already in the tree (namespace, repeated choice, facet aliases, validator), so a failure stays attributable.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_2 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 2u32, "2026-10-30T15:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:09 fiscal: GROOM R3 (silent >= 3 d): Active -> Paused, progress kept. The design stands, but its code changes the generator/emitter, whose text the edition-3 respell is about to change (FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, draft proving on e3lv). Rule anchors-stale-across-respell: land the respell first, then write against the respelled tree. Dep added: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND; resume (Active) when that lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_3 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 3u32, "2026-10-31T21:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 17:09 fiscal: RE-DECIDED: stays Paused. REASON (still true today): its remaining steps change xsd_emit/generator output, and FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (95%, held behind EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL, 95%, compiler pack 9) will respell that text; writing against the pre-respell tree would stale every anchor (rule anchors-stale-across-respell). RESUME CONDITION: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND reaches Done (the dep is recorded), then resume as Planned and re-anchor on the respelled tree.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_4 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 4u32, "2026-11-01T12:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:42 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). PRIORITY P0 (Paused on FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, in deps): today a generated reader failwith-s or drops data, so a bad document cannot be reported precisely; three other specs (PT-SAFT assertions, PINT findings, XSD-FACET-TYPES validators) rely on a typed error.\nDONE WHEN: (a) every generated of_xml returns \"result t decode_error\"; a node gate of xsd_emit.spi passes new tests a_missing_required_element_is_reported_with_its_path and an_invalid_facet_value_is_reported_with_its_path; (b) regenerated units: every existing round-trip test still green, and a deliberately broken NF-e (one required element removed) yields Missing with path \"NFe/infNFe/ide/cUF\" instead of a crash; (c) 0 failwith left in generated reader code (grep count reported).\nNEXT STEP: after the e3 round, find the reader emitters in xsd_emit.spi (element_part reading :1743, occurs_expression :1445 required_child) and draft the error type plus a result-threading emitter on a scratch lib.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: \":| decode_error = | Missing : decode_path | Invalid : decode_path * string | Unexpected : decode_path * string\" with \":! decode_path = list string\" built only by a push helper (no \"/\"-joined strings until display). Readers become prototype instances (\":+ of_xml t : xml_node -> result t decode_error\") with a monadic bind, so an emitter cannot forget to propagate. A GADT indexed by occurrence (\":| ^ occurs_read t = | Required :: occurs_read t | Optional :: occurs_read (option t) | Many :: occurs_read (list t)\") gives the reader of each field the right result shape by type, replacing today''s per-occurrence text templates. No -1, no \"\" defaults standing in for absence.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_5 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 5u32, "2026-11-02T21:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 17:20 fiscal: RE-DECIDED (stop-gate groom): Paused -> Planned. The recorded resume condition is MET: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND is Done since 11-01 14:4x (CI run 41314140694, both OSes), and lib xsd_emit.spi is in edition 3, so new work anchors on the respelled tree. ORDER (from the specs): XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES first (it is the base of XSD-FACET-TYPES' parse/example instances and XSD-DECODE-RESULT's of_xml returning result), then XSD-DECODE-RESULT, then XSD-FACET-TYPES. Each changes every generated unit, so each lands with one full node regen; the first starts after the 90-file shared-runtime regen and the typed family-roots regen are placed in fiscal/generated, so drifts don't compound.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_6 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 6u32, "2026-11-02T23:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 19:19 fiscal: READER SHAPE DECIDED BY MEASUREMENT (pack17-era core 8960CAB701FEF46E, lib-free edition-2 probes, one 60-field record reader read from a runtime lookup, compiled to Rust; generated-UBL records reach ~60 fields): failwith reader (today's shape) 50,236 bytes / 996 lines; NESTED result (one match per field, Error e => Error e) 439,398 bytes / 1,688 lines (8.7x, longest line 849 chars, nearly all indentation from 60 nesting levels; rustc is already 92% of the UBL unit's time, measured in FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE on 10-27); FLAT ACCUMULATING result ('inl v_i, errors = field \"f_i\" lookup errors' per field, one 'match errors with [] => Ok {...} | _ => Error errors' at the end) 69,490 bytes / 1,413 lines (1.4x). Both result shapes type-check; 60 same-indent nested matches parse. DECISION: generated readers use the flat shape, returning result t (list decode_error), which also reports EVERY missing/invalid field of a document instead of the first. decode_error = | Missing : path | Invalid : path * text | Unexpected : path; the path is built per walker level. Updates DONE WHEN (a): a missing required element is reported with its path AND a document with two problems reports both. Probes in the session scratchpad (decode-result-probe, decode-flat-probe, decode-failwith-probe).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_7 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 7u32, "2026-11-03T20:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:21 fiscal: ANCHORS ON THE CURRENT BASE (the rebased codec draft drafts\\spiral\\XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.on-325E10F1.spi D5B290F3, i.e. group_part 325E10F1 + nominal + codec; 3,702 lines). Reader emitters to convert to the flat accumulating shape: occurs_expression :1482 (Required -> xml.required_child, the main failwith source at run time), record reader head :1757 ('and let <ty>_of_xml (c : xml.xml_node) : <ty> ='), element_part reading instance :1784, the choice reader's 'if false then failwith ... else failwith' tail :1811-1813, staged reader head :1841 and its field :1853-1855, the no-first-alternative failwith :2043, the versioned reader :2950-2958, and the codec instances :2665-2674 (of_xml must become 'xml_node -> result t (list decode_error)', so the instance text changes with it). NOT STARTED TODAY on purpose: it changes every reader emitter and every generated unit, and two xsd_emit drafts (nominal, codec) are still waiting for their node regen proofs; a third layer before those land would compound drifts (the ORDER in n?: codec first, then this). Start right after XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_8 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 8u32, "2026-11-04T05:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:37 fiscal: STARTED (codec landed, so the resume condition is met). STEP 1 DRAFTED + PROVEN, additive only: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\XSD-DECODE-RESULT\\lib\\spiral\\xml_codec.spi (DD2A7758; base xml_codec.base-D3348061.spi). Adds ':! decode_path = list string' (root first, built only by at_root/pushed), ':| decode_error = Missing : decode_path | Invalid : decode_path * string | Unexpected : decode_path * string', within (a child's errors get the parent element name), decoded errors value (Ok, or Error in document order), and the flat-shape field readers read_required (takes a fallback thunk), read_optional, read_repeated (keep what decodes, report the rest), leaf readers read_text/read_value parse, and attribute_required/attribute_parsed/fixed_checked (attribute paths '@key'), error_text/error_texts for display. The of_xml prototype is NOT changed yet: that breaks every unit's instance and must ship with the emitter change + regen. PLACEHOLDER DESIGN: a failed required read binds '<ty>_example 0i32' (every generated type already has one), so the flat accumulation needs neither option-wrapping nor a partial unwrap; any error makes the result Error, so a placeholder never escapes, and 0 failwith remains in reader code (DoD c). PROOF on vultr pack27: --check and bodies exit 0; format --check --respell-drift exit 0; all 5 xml_codec tests to Rust exit 0, incl. the DoD wording a_missing_required_element_is_reported_with_its_path ('missing Header/ID') and a_document_with_two_problems_reports_both_in_order (['missing Header/ID'; 'invalid Total: x12']); MUTATION (within dropped from prepended) fails 'a missing child is named by its path...' as predicted. NEXT, step 2 (emitter): reading instances emit 'inl f, errors = xml_codec.read_* ... errors' per part instead of record field lines, record_body ends 'xml_codec.decoded errors (ty {...})', choice readers return Error [Unexpected] instead of failwith, node_expression -> read_text / read_value <ty>_of_string, attributes -> attribute_required/attribute_parsed/fixed_checked; staged and versioned readers likewise; then of_xml becomes 'xml_node -> result t (list decode_error)' and one full node regen proves it (layered on the FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE fold draft D24E724E, whose node proof is queued).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_9 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 9u32, "2026-11-04T05:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:49 fiscal: DESIGN REVISED (supersedes n8's placeholder plan): staged examples are typed '<ty> unsigned' (test staged_examples_are_unsigned), so '<ty>_example 0i32' cannot stand in for a required field of type '<ty> s'. Now uniform OPTION accumulation, no placeholders: read_required / taken / attribute_parsed return 'option t * errors' (None + a recorded error on failure); the record is built by 'xml_codec.decoded_by errors (fun () => ty { f = xml_codec.present v_f; g = v_g; ... })' -- the thunk runs only when no error was recorded, and every None records one, so present's single 'unreachable' failwith lives in lib and generated reader code keeps 0 failwith (DoD c); no coupling to example constructors. Lib helpers also gained read_child / mapped / pair_decoded (choice arms: Required via read_child; Optional and Repeated via read_optional/read_repeated wrapped by pair_decoded, so an emptiable choice's else-branch still reads 'absent' as None, not Missing), taken / optional_taken / all_taken (nested choice and group results, no path push), attribute_optional_parsed, no_alternative (replaces both choice failwiths). Draft xml_codec F5A0A53x: vultr pack27 format clean, check + bodies exit 0, 6 tests to Rust exit 0. STAGED: generated prelude gets 'staged_read witness (fun errors => <flat read>) errors' (Unsigned binds Pending WITHOUT reading, keeping laziness). Emitter layer next: drafts\\spiral\\XSD-DECODE-RESULT\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi (copied from the fold draft D24E724E, base copy kept).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_10 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 10u32, "2026-11-04T06:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:01 fiscal: STEP 2 DRAFTED (all reader sites), drafts\\spiral\\XSD-DECODE-RESULT: lib\\spiral\\xml_codec.spi A06FA0A8 (of_xml prototype now 'xml_node -> result t (list decode_error)'; round_trip_difference reports decode errors; + parsed_text, decoded_or, as_some, read_back_difference, expect_decoded; joined takes a separator), lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi D727C2F3 (on the fold draft D24E724E: reader_of/read_call/arm_read/binding/option_binding/field_binding/decoded_body/decode_result; record, element, attribute (attribute_binding; fixed values -> fixed_checked line), derived base, any (with_any_claims), choice part/group part (taken/optional_taken/all_taken), choice arms (mapped + read_child / pair_decoded), choice text and with_empty_fallback (no_alternative; 0 failwith), staged (prelude staged_read keeps Unsigned lazy; staged-typed fields read '(T_of_xml witness)'), versioned (mapped), complements (decoded_or ... (Unknown node): lax = keep whole), recursive Record_ constructor inside the decoded_by thunk; node_expression/occurs_expression removed), fiscal\\src\\generator.spi 97B3E15E (on the CII draft 7C315FDB: 7 test-boundary reads -> xml_codec.expect_decoded, the real-documents check -> xml_codec.read_back_difference, so a broken document is reported with its decode path instead of aborting). vultr pack27: xml_codec + xsd_emit type-check jointly (exit 0); all xsd_emit bodies to Rust RUNNING (old-text assertions expected to need updates).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_11 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 11u32, "2026-11-04T06:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:35 fiscal: FIRST GENERATED-CODE PROOF (vultr pack27, tree dec-gen = live lib/fiscal + the decode drafts + families F1CF3DDF, fiscal's deps/spiral/lib link re-pointed to the draft lib -- the copied link pointed at the live lib, which would have proven nothing): the generator (decode draft, main writing only facturae_3_2_2) compiled to Rust (36 s), rustc 180 s, ran exit 0 and wrote generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 (8,556 lines). Its readers are the flat shape ('inl v_any, errors = any_content_of (xml.unclaimed_children [] children), errors' ... 'xml_codec.decoded_by errors (fun () => x_object_type { any = v_any; ... })'; ds:Object keeps its content via the fold), 0 failwith in reader code (the unit's 5 are 1 choice example + 4 in tests = DoD c). The unit TYPE-CHECKS: --check exit 0 in 18 s. RUNNING: its writes_its_example body as a Rust main with the 10 real Facturae documents (fold + decode together); also queued: all xsd_emit bodies with the updated assertions (the first run stopped at the stale versioned-reader assertion, as expected).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_12 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 12u32, "2026-11-04T06:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:44 fiscal: (a)+(c) PROVEN ON GENERATED CODE, (b) prepared: the Facturae unit generated by the decode drafts type-checks and its read-back test body passes in Rust with all 10 real documents (see FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE). Lib xml_codec 5694B36A adds pruned name node (drops every descendant with that local name -- 'without' is a reserved word) and reports text r, test a_document_broken_on_purpose_reports_the_removed_element ('missing Header/ID' and nothing else); 8 xml_codec tests to Rust exit 0, format clean. Next: the NF-e DoD (b) generated test (x_tn_fe example, prune cUF, read with Unsigned, expect 'missing infNFe/ide/cUF'), then the node regen of every unit.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_13 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 13u32, "2026-11-04T07:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:35 fiscal: DoD (b) MET ON NF-e (vultr pack27, tree dec-gen with the decode drafts + NF-e schemas): the generator (decode draft incl. the new NfeModelChecks test) wrote generated_nfe_v4 (2,036,533 bytes); the unit compiled to Rust in 912 s and rustc 402 s -- the largest family type-checks under the flat decode readers -- and both bodies ran exit 0: generated_nfe_reports_a_missing_element_with_its_path (example written, cUF pruned, read with Unsigned -> the result reports exactly 'missing infNFe/ide/cUF', no raise) and generated_nfe_v4_writes_its_example (round trip with the decode readers; bench parse 283 us, write 152 us, 48,205 bytes). With Facturae's 10 real documents (n12) and the unit type checks, DoD (a) is met on generated code and (c) holds (0 failwith in reader code). REMAINING: the xsd_emit test suite (last stale assertion fixed; box + vultr reruns running), then one full node regen of every unit (Cells) and the land of lib xml_codec + xsd_emit and fiscal generator together.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_14 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 14u32, "2026-11-04T08:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 04:03 fiscal: xsd_emit TEST SUITE GREEN under the decode emitter (vultr pack27): all 33 xsd_emit bodies to Rust, rustc 747 s, run exit 0, after updating the assertions that pinned old reader text (versioned mapped, any binding, attribute_required + fixed_checked, staged_read single + repeated, choice no_alternative else-line for both emptiable and required choices, complement decoded_or, the VeriFactu choice field -- whose real type name keeps the prefix, x_registro_factura_type_choice_sf_registro_alta -- and the staged container '(T_of_xml witness)'). Two old assertions would have passed vacuously (matched example text instead of reader text); both now pin the reader. Formatter: xml_codec 0 diffs, xsd_emit 1 wrap applied. Drafts now: xml_codec 5694B36A, xsd_emit E8F660ED, generator 3564751D. The node decode regen (job-1793777894379-fiscal-decode) carries the same code (only assertion text and the wrap differ from its inbox). Next: its verdict, then the joint land.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_15 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 15u32, "2026-11-04T08:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 04:45 fiscal: EVERY FAMILY TYPE-CHECKS UNDER THE DECODE READERS (vultr pack27, tree dec-gen with every family's schemas staged): the generator (decode draft) compiled 43 s + rustc 150 s and wrote 34 families (the process exit code is the written count, 34) in 13 s; then --check on each generated unit: 68 units (mains + certificates), 0 failing -- incl. CFDI's complements (decoded_or Unknown fallback), the versioned families (mapped per version), UBL's large choices, CII D16B, NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e staged signatures (staged_read), Facturae, VeriFactu, FatturaPA, KSeF, Chile, myDATA, NAV, GST, SAF-T, Costa Rica. Runtime proof so far: Facturae 10 real docs + NF-e missing-cUF (vultr Rust). The node's Cells regen of all units (job-1793777894379-fiscal-decode) remains the final gate before the land. NB this run's log had interleaved writers (a restart overlapped the first run, my error); every unit line was counted once (68 distinct).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_16 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 16u32, "2026-11-04T09:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 05:04 fiscal: CII D16B under the decode readers (vultr pack27): generated_cii_d16b's writes_its_example body as a Rust main, run exit 0 -- the example and the 15 pinned CEN CII examples read back with result-returning readers. UBL credit note running next.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_17 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 17u32, "2026-11-04T09:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 05:16 fiscal: UBL CreditNote 2.1 under the decode readers (vultr pack27): writes_its_example body as a Rust main (rustc 1,506 s), run exit 0 -- every credit note in ubl-creditnote-documents.txt (incl. SUNAT's 15 homologation credit notes) reads back unchanged; bench parse 76 us, write 92 us. Runtime read-back proofs under decode so far: Facturae (10 real), NF-e (example + missing-cUF), CII D16B (15 CEN), UBL CreditNote (manifest); VeriFactu and CR Factura 4.4 queued on vultr.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_18 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 18u32, "2026-11-04T09:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 05:19 fiscal: VeriFactu (parse 124 us, write 61 us, 47,678 bytes) and Costa Rica Factura 4.4 (68 us / 45 us, 29,078 bytes) read back under the decode readers (vultr pack27, writes_its_example bodies run exit 0); both are fold-changed W3C-xmldsig families, so this also exercises ds:Object as any_content under decode. FatturaPA was not in the generate-all main (missed like UBL Invoice); it is covered by the node's full decode regen. Runtime read-back proofs under decode: Facturae, NF-e, CII D16B, UBL CreditNote, VeriFactu, CR Factura 4.4 -- 6 families, 0 failures.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_19 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 19u32, "2026-11-04T10:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 06:03 fiscal: FatturaPA 1.2.3 reads back under the decode readers (vultr pack27, generated by the decode draft, writes_its_example body run exit 0; parse 119 us, write 82 us, 46,407 bytes) -- 7 families with runtime read-back under decode, 0 failures. UBL Invoice 2.1: first run VOID (NotFound: its manifest also lists co/my/pe/ro/sa/tr documents, which were not staged in that tree -- an environment gap, not a verdict); folders staged, rebuilt under its own binary name and rerunning (rustc ~35 min).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_20 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 20u32, "2026-11-04T10:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 06:42 fiscal: UBL Invoice 2.1 reads back under the decode readers (vultr pack27, rerun after staging the co/my/pe/ro/sa/tr corpus folders; compile 62 s, rustc 2,319 s, writes_its_example body run exit 0; parse 106 us, write 126 us). Its body reads every document of ubl-invoice-documents.txt (PEPPOL, CEN, MyInvois, SUNAT, Turkey, Saudi Arabia, Colombia, Romania) -- the largest real set. RUNTIME READ-BACK UNDER DECODE, 8 families, 0 failures: Facturae (10 real), NF-e (example + missing-cUF), CII D16B (15 CEN), UBL CreditNote, UBL Invoice, VeriFactu, FatturaPA, CR Factura 4.4; plus all 68 units type-check. Remaining: the node's Cells regen of every unit (queued), then the joint land (lib xml_codec + xsd_emit via lib_land_window, fiscal generator).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_21 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 21u32, "2026-11-04T12:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:16 fiscal: DEAD CODE REMOVED from the decode draft (now 5B274B48): the staging prelude's 'staged_of' (thunk-based staging) has no caller left under the decode readers -- in every unit the decode draft generated (vultr gen-decode tree), 'staged_of' appears only as its own definition -- so its 4 template lines are gone. vultr pack27 --check exit 0; staged_read intact. The queued node regen job-1793777894379-fiscal-decode got the new xsd_emit in its inbox while still queued (inbox hash = draft hash 5B274B48), so its Cells verdict covers the removal. The GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT draft carries the same removal (base copy refreshed to 5B274B48).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_22 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 22u32, "2026-11-04T14:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:51 fiscal: JOINT LAND PLAN checked against live (no change made). LIB via lib_land_window: xml_codec live D3348061 = decode base -> 5694B36A; xsd_emit live 5E485076 = fold base -> 5B274B48 (decode draft, built on the fold D24E724E, so fold + decode land together; or the split draft 7FDA3007 on top, proven identical); document_syntax NEW (FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS, 6B55B078). FISCAL SRC in place: generator live 5DB916E8 = CII draft 7C315FDB minus 4 added lines -> decode generator 3564751D (or GRANULAR-GENERATOR 28372016, proven identical); families live B59F8A10 -> F1CF3DDF (intended diff: the W3C xmldsig mapping replacing the SEFAZ restricted copy, Facturae's 10 real documents, the CII family). Then place the regenerated units from the node decode stage. TRIGGER: the node decode regen job-1793777894379-fiscal-decode (running; xml_codec gate 7/7 so far) reporting green, with UBL Invoice under the raised mirror cap.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_23 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 23u32, "2026-11-04T14:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:55 fiscal: TIMING (pending, not a forecast of the verdict): the node decode regen job-1793777894379-fiscal-decode gates EVERY generated unit under Cells (the decode change touches every reader), one unit at a time; at the es-object pace (14 units in ~5 h, UBL units 45-90 min) the full set runs past 21:00 into 11-05. The joint land waits for it. Considered and DROPPED: gating half the units in reverse order on the half-idle box -- the land-window guard treats any command line containing lib_gate.ps1 as a live lib reader, so hours of box gates would refuse every lane's lib land windows, not only mine (scratch tree built then removed unused; live untouched). vultr Rust read-back proofs of the decode readers stand as recorded; the Cells verdict is the land gate.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_24 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 24u32, "2026-11-04T16:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 12:14 fiscal: node decode job progress (job-1793777894379-fiscal-decode, pinned core 0758BAF4): xml_codec gate 7/7 GREEN (10:30). xsd_emit gate (11:46): discovered 33, passed 31, 'failed' 2 = a_required_signature_list_is_staged_as_one_slot and a_family_with_required_signatures_generates_staged_units, listed in the SAME second as 'timed out after 900s; the process tree was killed' -- the module's own cap (///- --timeout 900000) killed the run, so those 2 are VOID pending proof, not red. vultr pack27 Rust run of ALL decode xsd_emit test bodies (base with the decode xml_codec 5694B36A) queued to settle them. The node job continues with the generator regen and the unit gates. If the 2 are just slow, the fix is the module's emitted cap (mirror-only raise for the gate, as for UBL Invoice), not code.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_25 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 25u32, "2026-11-04T16:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 12:38 fiscal: the node's 2 'failed' xsd_emit tests (a_required_signature_list_is_staged_as_one_slot, a_family_with_required_signatures_generates_staged_units) are CONFIRMED timeout VOIDs, not red: vultr pack27 ran ALL 33 decode xsd_emit (5B274B48, with the decode xml_codec 5694B36A) test bodies in Rust -- check + bodies exit 0, compile exit 0, rustc exit 0 (804 s for the module's test binary), run exit 0. The node's Cells cell hit the module's own 900 s cap ('timed out after 900s; the process tree was killed') while those two heaviest tests ran. For the joint land, the xsd_emit Cells gate needs the module cap raised (the emitted ///- --timeout 900000 header of xsd_emit.spi itself) -- a one-line header change in the land draft, or a mirror-only raise for the gate, as for UBL Invoice.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_26 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 26u32, "2026-11-04T16:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 12:47 fiscal: COMBINED LAND SET PROVEN on vultr pack27: the land xsd_emit (GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT AB4B0165) + the GRANULAR-GENERATOR generator (28372016 + the harness main) regenerate all 69 units with 0 differing files vs the decode reference (compile / rustc / generate as every prior run; harness restored after: xsd_emit 5B274B48, generator DA6BE426). So the joint land can carry decode + both granular drafts at once without changing a generated byte relative to the decode verdict the node gate is producing. Still pending: the node decode regen's unit gates (UBL Invoice under the raised mirror cap).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_27 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 27u32, "2026-11-04T17:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 13:53 fiscal: node decode gate, generator stage: 24 discovered, 23 passed, 1 'failed' = generates_every_family_version, logged in the same second as 'timed out after 1400s; the process tree was killed' -> a timeout VOID, not red (that test writes all 12 family roots; the same regen ran natively on vultr today with 69 units, 0 differing vs the decode reference, several times). Since CI runs it under the same 1400 s header, the decode's extra read code would trip CI too after the land, so the HEAL is in the land drafts, not mirror-only: generator.spi header '///- --timeout 1400000' -> '3600000' (corpus_checks already uses 3600000) in both drafts: decode generator 3564751D -> B03BC358, GRANULAR-GENERATOR 28372016 -> FC53C8CA (diff = that one header line each; compile + 69-unit identity proofs unchanged). Joint land set now: xml_codec 5694B36A, xsd_emit 5B274B48 (then split AB4B0165), document_syntax 6B55B078, generator B03BC358 (or FC53C8CA), families F1CF3DDF. Gate continues into the unit stages.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_28 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 28u32, "2026-11-04T17:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 13:57 fiscal: generates_every_family_version CONFIRMED PASS natively: on vultr pack27 the capped decode generator (B03BC35x) + a main running exactly the test's assertion (write_family_modules (family_roots ()) = 12) -> compile 0, rustc 0, run returned 12 (assertion held) in 7 s, units 0 differing vs the decode reference; harness restored (DA6BE426). So the node's 1400 s timeout is Cells' cost for this test on a loaded node (7 s native vs > 1400 s in Cells), not a decode fault; the 3600 s header in the land drafts covers it. Decode gate so far: xml_codec 7/7, xsd_emit 33/33 (2 timeouts confirmed in Rust), generator 24/24 (1 timeout confirmed natively); unit stages pending.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_29 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 29u32, "2026-11-04T18:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 14:04 fiscal: SCOPE of my vultr identity proofs, corrected: '69 units, 0 differing' covers exactly the 69 unit files the regen main writes (family_roots + hacienda_documents + nfe_events + 24 more roots). fiscal/generated on the box has 14 MORE files that main never writes: cfdi_pagos_2_0, cfdi_tfd_1_1, cfdi_v4_0 (+ certificates), ksef_fa_3 (+ certificates), nfe_v4 (+ certificates), ubl_applicationresponse/debitnote/despatchadvice/receiptadvice_2_1 -- written by individual generator TESTS (e.g. generates_nfe_v4_with_a_staged_signature). Those 14 are NOT covered by any vultr proof; their only evidence is the node decode gate, whose generator stage (24/24 incl. the native-confirmed timeout) regenerated them in the mirror, and whose unit stages are checking them now. For the joint land: the land must carry the regenerated forms of these 14 as well (from the gate's output), not only the 69. Also: generated_cii_d16b is written by the decode set but is not in the live tree yet (new unit).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_30 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 30u32, "2026-11-04T18:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 14:29 fiscal: node decode gate progress: format-generated 83 units: 83 formatted, 0 from cache, 0 failed (2864 s) -- the full set (the 69 regen-main units + the 14 test-written ones, see note 29); now 'units to gate: 83' (each unit's own Cells tests; likely runs past 21:00). Library + generator stages already settled: xml_codec 7/7, xsd_emit 33/33, generator 24/24 (all 3 timeouts confirmed natively).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_31 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 31u32, "2026-11-04T21:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 17:41 fiscal: node decode job ENDED exit 1 at 17:32 -- NODE DISK FULL ('There is not enough space on the disk'), not a decode verdict. Units gated before it: 20 of 83, ALL passed (cfdi x6, cl_dte x4, cr_* hacienda units ...); the last 4 (cte_os_v4_00 (+cert), cte_simp_v4_00 (+cert)) are NO TOTAL (kino deps could not compile / ebin write failed for lack of space) = VOID; 59 never ran. INCIDENT, mine, fixed: the script's finally-restore ran under ErrorActionPreference Stop, so the first failed copy (lib package.spiproj, disk full) aborted the rest and left the SHARED t1101 mirror with my decode drafts in lib (xsd_emit 5B274B48, xml_codec 5694B36A) and fiscal (families F1CF3DDF) and NO lib package.spiproj, from 17:32 to ~17:40. Restored by hand from the stage keep copies and verified by hash: lib xml C2F46E8A, xsd_emit 738935CD, package.spiproj 16C663F9, xml_codec removed (the mirror had none); fiscal generator A12D3E7E, families 0AB7E110, package.spiproj E87DACB9, spiral.toml FC0E762E. Freed my two stale compiler pins (1.4 GB); node free 14.3 GB. Any node job that read t1101 lib between 17:32 and 17:40 saw a missing package.spiproj. Next: the restore becomes per-file (each copy tried, all failures reported), and the 63 remaining units re-gate.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_32 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 32u32, "2026-11-05T00:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 20:19 fiscal: units-only decode gate (node job-1793829209251-fiscal-decode-units, script node-decode-units.ps1 A39C5538: places only lib xml B6EED09B + xml_codec 5694B36A, restores each file in its own try with hash check) at 20:17: 31 (first run) + 19 = 50 of 83 gated; 49 PASS. 1 VOID: generated_gtve_v4_00 'failed 2/2' because its build produced nothing -- raw output ends '** (Mix) ...generated_gtve_v4_00.spi: BuildFile returned no code and no diagnostic arrived' (a silent compiler-process failure under 100% node load; no ETY, no assertion; its _certificates unit passed 1/1). It needs one re-run before the land. The job continues past 21:00 (about 33 units left, incl. ubl_invoice under its mirror-only 18000000 ms cap); it restores the mirror itself when it ends.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_33 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 33u32, "2026-11-05T01:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 21:28 fiscal: DECODE GATE RED (blocks the joint land). Unit gate at 21:27 (raw outputs, both runs): 65 of 83 units PASS; 3 not: generated_gtve_v4_00 0/2 = VOID (build returned no code, silent compiler failure; one-unit re-gate job-1793838041480 queued after the units job); generated_mdfe_v1_00 1/2 = REAL: ETY-InstanceNotFound 'The higher order type instance list does not have the prototype stage_of. In the definition: of_xml x_tmd_fe.'; generated_mdfe_v3_00 0/2 = REAL: ETY-TermError 'Unification failure' (x3) in writes_its_example. Suspect: MDF-e's staged root (TMDFe) reaches a stage_of use with no instance emitted under the decode set -- check against the decode xsd_emit 5B274B48 (which dropped staged_of as dead) and its emission for signed families whose root is staged; CTe/NF-e/GTVe v3 pass, so it is MDF-e-shaped. My vultr identity proofs could not catch it: they compare decode output with the decode reference (same MDF-e text); only compiling the units does. ~15 units still to gate; the job restores the t1101 mirror per file when it ends.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_34 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 34u32, "2026-11-05T03:54Z", "fiscal", "11-05 00:0x local. The two MDF-e \"REAL reds\" in n33 were STALE INPUTS, not decode defects. Six node mirror units (t1101 fiscal/generated: gtve_v4_00, mdfe_v1_00, mdfe_v3_00 and their _certificates) still held the 11-03 committed text. mdfe_v1_00 3201A7F5 and mdfe_v3_00 4948B2D1 are byte-equal to the box HEAD units; they have the old staged_of and plain-returning decoders. The 11-04 node regen rewrote only the other 77, so the gate checked the new lib xml_codec (of_xml : xml_node -> result t (list decode_error)) against old units. That produced ETY-InstanceNotFound stage_of and the plain-vs-result unification failures. Evidence, vultr pack27 dll 21E08222, --check against the decode lib xsd_emit 5B274B48 / xml_codec 5694B36A (log ~/remote-stage/fiscal-check/stale-check-1793850402.log): the gen-decode2 units mdfe_v1_00 F6833126, mdfe_v3_00 D9986CD5 and gtve_v4_00 A2B28BA9, plus their certificates and the control nfe_evento_canc_v1_00, check with 0 diagnostics. Negative control: the stale 3201A7F5 / 4948B2D1 reproduce the node's exact ETY-InstanceNotFound (of_xml x_tmd_fe, x_t_envi_md_fe) plus 45 / 69 unification failures. gtve_v4_00's \"BuildFile returned no code\" VOID is in the same stale set. nfe_v4 timed out at its own text-size cap of 3258112 ms (generator cell_budget_ms = len/10*16): VOID, not red. The decode build costs more than the text-size cap predicts. PENDING (node): job-1793838041480-fiscal-decode-one, queued after the units job. It places the gen-decode2 versions, checks hashes, then gates all 6 plus nfe_v4 under a mirror-only 10800000 cap that is restored per file. Land consequence: the land must regenerate every unit, the 14 generator-test-written ones included; any placement keyed off a unit list must be diffed against the full 83.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_35 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 35u32, "2026-11-05T04:29Z", "fiscal", "LAND PREP, 11-05 00:4x local. The user commits of 11-04 23:18 moved every base, so the land is re-planned on live: (1) lib xsd_emit: live 5E485076 = the draft base D24E724E minus FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE's unlanded sequence-wildcard rule (wildcard_choice on Sequence plus test a_sequence_of_only_wildcards_is_any_content). The Facturae draft F8AA22F5 on base 5E485076 equals D24E724E except one test-string line split. So the decode xsd_emit 5B274B48 lands JOINTLY on -BaseHash 5E485076 and carries the Facturae rule its proof already included; FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE closes with that land. (2) lib xml.spi: the proof used B6EED09B, live is 3D9AC927 (faf422c: tibia's :< unsupported and no_arm respell of three failwith arms, 7 lines, no API change). The decode drafts do not touch xml.spi. (3) lib xml_codec.spi 5694B36A: a new file. (4) fiscal src generator: land copy drafts\\spiral\\XSD-DECODE-RESULT\\fiscal\\src\\generator.land.spi 385DD926 = proven B03BC358 minus test generates_cii_d16b, matching live 5DB916E8, where it was dropped because live families has no cii_d16b. Its change lines vs live are byte-equal to the proven change vs 7C315FDB (44 lines), with max 1 blank line at the cut. Round trips: xml_codec and xsd_emit canonical/fixpoint true (n of 00:2x). Gate still PENDING on the node: job-1793838041480 re-gates the 6 fresh units plus nfe_v4.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_36 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 36u32, "2026-11-05T05:24Z", "fiscal", "LAND SEQUENCE (ready, gated on node job-1793838041480 green): (1) lib: pwsh spiral/apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft \"xsd_emit.spi=%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\XSD-DECODE-RESULT\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi,xml_codec.spi=%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\XSD-DECODE-RESULT\\lib\\spiral\\xml_codec.spi\" -BaseHash \"5E485076,new\" -Label fiscal-decode-1105 -Apply *> log (never through a pipe). xml_codec is a new file, so it takes \"new\"; lib is toml-derived, so no manifest edit is needed. FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE's wildcard rule lands inside this xsd_emit. (2) fiscal src in place (backup first): generator.spi = drafts\\spiral\\XSD-DECODE-RESULT\\fiscal\\src\\generator.land.spi 385DD926, guard live 5DB916E8. (3) fiscal/generated: the 69 regen units = vultr gen-decode2 (the .next6 identity proof shows the same bytes), plus the 14 generator-test-written units from the node gate (t1101 fiscal/generated, regenerated 11-04 13-14h with the same drafts), then the gtve/mdfe fresh six. Format all with scripts/format-generated.ps1 (units are kept formatted), and diff by multiset against the node copies before leaving them unstaged for the user. (4) after the land: document_test once over the landed lib files; then GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT (AB4B0165 on base 5B274B48, i.e. the landed decode xsd_emit), then XSD-FACET-TYPES 4E831159 on AB4B0165, then MyInvois document_syntax 6B55B078 (new file).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_37 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 37u32, "2026-11-05T06:06Z", "fiscal", "Compiler note, 11-05 02:0x local: main swaps the NODE compiler pack38 -> pack40 around 02:0x (the live lib needs pack39's UnionCaseName). The running units job keeps its own pinned copy. The queued re-gate job-1793838041480 copies the installed compiler at START, so it will most likely gate on pack40. I patched its queued script (FD8685BB, hash-verified on the node) to pin only a STABLE tree: the installed tree hash must match before and after the copy and equal the pin, retrying every 60 s, and it exits VOID after 20 tries. Its log names the pinned tree hash. So the 7 re-gated units and the earlier 65 may span two compilers; the verdict will say so.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_38 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 38u32, "2026-11-05T06:38Z", "fiscal", "NODE TALLY, 11-05 02:3x local: units job-1793829209251 finished exit 0 after 8.7 h; lib restored and verified by hash; ONE compiler throughout (core 21F39A40A549E6E6). Over both stage dirs (raw outputs, not the tail): 83 units with a verdict, 79 PASS. The 4 not passing are exactly the explained ones: gtve_v4_00 (2/2 fail), mdfe_v1_00 (1/2) and mdfe_v3_00 (2/2) were gated on the stale 11-03 text (n34), and nfe_v4 (2/4) hit its own text-size cap, so it is VOID. ubl_invoice_2_1 passed after 1 h 46 min under the raised mirror cap. PENDING (node): re-gate job-1793838041480, started 02:35. Pinned on try 1, tree 23436174C91809FD, core DDCA78971B4EAB36: a DIFFERENT compiler from the 79, because main swapped the node to pack40. It placed the fresh gen-decode2 units (gtve_v4_00 A2B28BA9 confirmed) and gates 7: gtve_v4_00 + certificates, mdfe_v1_00 / v3_00 + certificates, nfe_v4 at a mirror-only 3 h cap.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_39 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 39u32, "2026-11-05T06:54Z", "fiscal", "RE-GATE RESULT for the 6 fresh units (node job-1793838041480, core DDCA78971B4EAB36, 11-05 02:35-02:47 local), each placed from gen-decode2 with its hash checked: gtve_v4_00 A2B28BA9 2/2 PASS, gtve_v4_00_certificates E341BDB9 1/1 PASS, mdfe_v1_00 F6833126 2/2 PASS, mdfe_v1_00_certificates 74615AE7 1/1 PASS, mdfe_v3_00 D9986CD5 2/2 PASS, mdfe_v3_00_certificates DC83D4EC 1/1 PASS. This confirms n34: the MDF-e \"REAL reds\" and gtve_v4_00's VOID were stale 11-03 inputs. Decode gate now 82/83 units green (79 on core 21F39A40A549E6E6, plus these 6 replacing their stale runs on DDCA78971B4EAB36). The LAST unit, nfe_v4, is PENDING on the node under a mirror-only 10800000 ms cap (started 02:47 local). When it is green the land sequence in n36 runs.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_40 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 40u32, "2026-11-05T08:42Z", "fiscal", "nfe_v4 VOID + MIRROR RESTORED, 11-05 04:4x local. Re-gate job-1793838041480 was STOPPED by the kit job host (state=timed-out, exit 124, \"wall-clock timeout; process tree stopped\"). It had been started with a 7200000 ms cap sized for gtve alone; I widened its queued script to 6 units plus nfe_v4 at a 3 h cell cap without kit job amend --timeout. Started 02:35, killed about 04:35 inside nfe_v4: no nfe_v4 verdict, and the finally restore never ran. The t1101 mirror was left with the decode xml.spi B6EED09B, xml_codec.spi, lib package.spiproj 3A089C8E and the nfe_v4 unit cap 10800000. RESTORED by hand per file from the stage keep copies, each hash-verified: xml.spi C2F46E8A, package.spiproj 16C663F9, generated_nfe_v4.spi 12FCE333, xml_codec.spi removed. No orphan of mine (the one erl running is the x lane's xqueue3 sim). The 6 fresh gtve/mdfe units stay placed (the decode regen, like the other 77). Memory: widen-queued-job-amend-timeout. RERUN PENDING (node): job-1793868130086-fiscal-decode-nfe, nfe_v4 alone, job cap 14400000 ms over the 3 h cell cap, own stage and pin (fiscal-decode-nfe), the same stable-pin guard and per-file restore.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_41 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 41u32, "2026-11-05T10:41Z", "fiscal", "DECODE GATE GREEN: 83/83 units, 11-05 06:40 local, node. nfe_v4 (job-1793868130086, alone, mirror-only cap 10800000) discovered 4 executed 4 passed 4 failed 0 in 1 h 58 min, against the 54 min its text-size cap allowed. That confirms the n34 VOID was the cap, and that generator cell_budget_ms under-sizes decode units (filed for the generator). Lib restored and hash-verified, one compiler (core 887F89D1821E70AA). The full set spans three compilers because main swapped the node install overnight: 79 units on 21F39A40A549E6E6, the 6 fresh units on DDCA78971B4EAB36, nfe_v4 on 887F89D1821E70AA; all green. With xml_codec 7/7, xsd_emit 33/33 and generator 24/24 from 11-04, XSD-DECODE-RESULT's proof is complete. NEXT: the land sequence of n36.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_42 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 42u32, "2026-11-05T10:53Z", "fiscal", "LANDED, 11-05 06:5x local. (1) lib through lib_land_window, label fiscal-decode-1105, CLOSED GREEN: xsd_emit 5B274B48 (base 5E485076) and xml_codec 5694B36A (base D3348061; it already existed from XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES, so n36's \"new file\" was wrong, the base is the recorded D3348061). Round trip ok; 0 consumer-used signatures changed; apps/spiral compiles; document_test 26 passed; type_probe xsd_emit 33 typed and xml_codec 7 typed, both PASS, controls ok; respell_drift 0; lib digest 6799DAEB324F44DF; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-064517. No other module uses xml_codec / of_xml (checked: lib, apps, fiscal, sibling repos). FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE's wildcard rule landed inside this xsd_emit. (2) fiscal src/generator.spi in place: 5DB916E8 -> 385DD926 (the proven decode change minus generates_cii_d16b, 44 lines; backup generator.before-decode-land-5DB916E8.spi in the scratchpad). Both unstaged. (3) PENDING: placing the 83 regenerated units (staging from the node mirror in progress) and formatting them with the box compiler; CI re-generates and diffs, so any formatter drift will show as \"generated drift\" after the push.")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_43 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 43u32, "2026-11-05T10:58Z", "fiscal", "Step (3), 11-05 07:0x local: 82 decode units copied from the node mirror (zip 5.1 MB, 83 dirs) into fiscal/generated, in place and unstaged. generated_cii_d16b is left out: it belongs to the unlanded FISCAL-CII-PROFILES families (live families has no cii_d16b). Only 47 files differ from HEAD; 35 units were already decode text in bb1ebad. The box format pass (scripts/format-generated.ps1 with the installed compiler, Jobs 2) is PENDING; CI regenerates and diffs, so any formatter drift between this compiler and the one CI builds from spiral main will show as \"generated drift\". WATCH ITEM, not a blocker: the decode units are slower. nfe_v4 took 1 h 58 min on the node against its 54 min text-size cap. In the last green CI (41598162815, pre-decode) nfe_v4 took 765 s ubuntu / 429 s windows. At the node:CI ratio of about 3:1 (ubl units 16 min vs 5-6 min), CI should land near 40 min, inside the cap but with thin margin. If the first decode CI times out on a unit, the fix is generator cell_budget_ms (filed).")
inl note_of_xsd_decode_result_44 () = Note ("XSD-DECODE-RESULT", 44u32, "2026-11-05T11:31Z", "fiscal", "Step (3) DONE, 11-05 07:3x local: fiscal/generated holds the 82 decode units, formatted with the box compiler (core 657DA4B173F9D3D3): format-generated.ps1 reports 82 formatted, 0 failed, in 1776 s. 44 files differ from HEAD (after formatting, 3 of the 47 matched the committed bytes again). The whole decode land is now in place and UNSTAGED for the user: spiral lib xsd_emit 5B274B48 -> split AB4B0165 and xml_codec 5694B36A (both landed green); fiscal src/generator.spi 385DD926; fiscal generated/ 44 files. AFTER the user commits and pushes, fiscal CI regenerates and diffs. Two things to watch there: (a) \"generated drift\" if the CI-built compiler formats differently from the box install (then commit CI's bytes); (b) nfe_v4 / ubl unit time against their text-size caps (see n43). Neither is expected to fail, but the push is the proof.")
