inl xsd_codec_prototypes () = Task ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", "generated code exposes of_text/of_xml/to_xml/example prototypes with one instance per type, so lib round trips and the generator tests are generic instead of string-glued names", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND,XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS", "team:fiscal,fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_codec_prototypes () = Planning ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", Minutes 360u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_1 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 1u32, "2026-10-27T13:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:57 fiscal: DESIGN (no code; emitter frozen until the joint regeneration proof). Today the emitter declares one prototype (codec_prelude: to_text) with 321 instances in generated_cte_v4_00, and every other codec is reached by gluing names as strings (generator.spi: t ++ '_of_xml', '_to_xml', '_example', '_of_string'). PLAN: the prelude declares four more single-method prototypes, of_text t : string -> option t (scalars: enums, nominals, aliases resolve to their parent's instance, no duplicates), of_xml t : xml.xml_node -> t, to_xml t : string -> t -> xml.xml_node, example t : i32 -> t; the emitter adds one instance line per emitted type and prototype, delegating to the existing functions (no logic moves). Payoff: lib-level generics such as 'inl round_trip forall t {of_xml; to_xml}. (name) (c : xml.xml_node) : xml.xml_node = to_xml name (of_xml c : t)' replace the generator's string-built test bodies (example check, bench, real documents); the KindText/KindEnum/KindValidated branches in node_expression/value_node collapse to one prototype call; XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS builds on it. COST RULE (pre-registered, because rustc is 92% of UBL's cell, FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE n7): Spiral is staged, so instances should emit Rust only where used; measure on generated_cte_v4_00 before and after (Cells phases_ms rustc of the example cell, same box, memo off): adopt if rustc grows <= 5%; if more, emit instances only for types reached from the root's codec, or keep the string path for readers and use prototypes only in lib generics.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_2 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 2u32, "2026-10-30T15:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:09 fiscal: GROOM R3 (silent >= 3 d): Active -> Paused, progress kept. The design stands, but its code changes the generator/emitter, whose text the edition-3 respell is about to change (FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, draft proving on e3lv). Rule anchors-stale-across-respell: land the respell first, then write against the respelled tree. Dep added: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND; resume (Active) when that lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_3 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 3u32, "2026-10-31T21:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 17:09 fiscal: RE-DECIDED: stays Paused. REASON (still true today): its remaining steps change xsd_emit/generator output, and FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (95%, held behind EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL, 95%, compiler pack 9) will respell that text; writing against the pre-respell tree would stale every anchor (rule anchors-stale-across-respell). RESUME CONDITION: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND reaches Done (the dep is recorded), then resume as Planned and re-anchor on the respelled tree.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_4 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 4u32, "2026-11-01T12:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:43 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). DONE WHEN: generated units expose of_text / to_text / of_xml / to_xml / example as prototype instances, one per generated type (not free functions named t_of_xml ...); a node gate of xsd_emit.spi passes a new test every_generated_type_has_its_codec_instances; generic code over \"a type with a codec\" compiles once (a round-trip test written against the prototype, not per type), and model_metrics on a regenerated unit shows prototype instances replacing the per-type function family.\nNEXT STEP: after the e3 round; it is the base of XSD-FACET-TYPES (parse/example instances over the builtin GADT) and XSD-DECODE-RESULT (of_xml returning result), so land it first among cluster B.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: prototypes \":+ codec t\" with of_text/to_text and \":+ xml_codec t\" with of_xml/to_xml/example; instances emitted per generated type through the existing walker-prototype machinery (\":+ ... exampling/reading/writing\" in xsd_emit). The unit''s round-trip and bench tests become one generic function over xml_codec (removes the per-family string templates json_round_trip / family_bench emit today). HKT where the container varies: occurs-shaped readers (option/list) through the occurs GADT of XSD-DECODE-RESULT. MODEL: lib prototypes already used by the walkers; mega samples for prototype-polymorphic tests.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_5 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 5u32, "2026-11-02T21:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 17:20 fiscal: RE-DECIDED (stop-gate groom): Paused -> Planned. The recorded resume condition is MET: FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND is Done since 11-01 14:4x (CI run 41314140694, both OSes), and lib xsd_emit.spi is in edition 3, so new work anchors on the respelled tree. ORDER (from the specs): XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES first (it is the base of XSD-FACET-TYPES' parse/example instances and XSD-DECODE-RESULT's of_xml returning result), then XSD-DECODE-RESULT, then XSD-FACET-TYPES. Each changes every generated unit, so each lands with one full node regen; the first starts after the 90-file shared-runtime regen and the typed family-roots regen are placed in fiscal/generated, so drifts don't compound.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_6 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 6u32, "2026-11-02T21:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 18:05 fiscal: DESIGN PROBED ON PACK17 (scratch probe, edition 2 like generated units, SpiralCompiler --check + --backend Rust): codec prototypes work as THIN INSTANCES over the existing recursive group, so the emitter's 'and let ty_of_xml / ty_to_xml / ty_example' functions stay (recursion lives in join points) and each type gains 'instance of_xml ty = ty_of_xml' etc. Proven: (1) a prototype whose type variable is only in the RESULT (of_text t : string -> t) dispatches when generic code fixes t through its own signature: inl reparse forall t {of_text; to_text}. (x : t) : t = of_text (to_text x) type-checks and compiles to Rust (1,381 bytes); (2) NEGATIVE: the same generic call on a type with no instances fails 'ETY-InstanceNotFound: ... uncoded does not have the prototype to_text' (and of_text), so a generic round-trip test cannot pass vacuously over an uncoded type. Constraint found: a forall whose t appears in no parameter or result is rejected (ETY-UnusedTypeVariable), and backtick type arguments do not parse, so generic tests take a VALUE (e.g. each type's example) and round-trip it. DESIGN: (a) the prototypes are declared ONCE in lib (a new xml_codec module: of_xml t : xml.xml_node -> t, to_xml t : string -> t -> xml.xml_node, example t : i32 -> t), not per unit like today's 'prototype to_text t' preamble (xsd_emit.spi:165), so cross-unit generic code sees one prototype; (b) xsd_emit emits 3 instance lines per type after its group; (c) lib gets one generic test, round_trip forall t {of_xml; to_xml; example}, and every generated unit's example test calls it instead of string-glued names. OPEN: staged types (ty_of_xml forall s. (witness : stage s)) need an instance over the higher-kinded 'ty s' (the error text names 'higher order type instance', so the instance form exists); probe that before emitting. Unit size grows by 3 lines per type (UBL Invoice ~ +2k lines); measure on the first regen.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_7 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 7u32, "2026-11-02T22:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 18:01 fiscal: OPEN QUESTION CLOSED: staged (higher-kinded) types take ONE instance per type constructor. Probe on pack17: nominal doc s = string with phantom stages unsigned/signed, 'let rec doc_of_text forall s. (x : string) : doc s', 'instance of_text doc s = doc_of_text' and 'instance to_text doc s = doc_to_text' (the edition-2 form of lib's ':+ append array t'); the generic keeps_its_text round-trips both doc unsigned and doc signed; --check exit 0, Rust 1,387 bytes. So xsd_emit emits 'instance of_xml ty s = ty_of_xml' for staged types (the witness argument stays inside the function) and plain 'instance of_xml ty = ty_of_xml' otherwise. This is also fiscal's first HKT use (scoreboard HKT 0 vs lib 1.3/kloc). Design complete; implementation starts after the two pending fiscal regens are placed (see this item's n5 order).")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_8 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 8u32, "2026-11-02T22:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 18:01 fiscal: CORRECTION to n7: the HKT instance FORM is proven, but 'instance of_xml ty s = ty_of_xml' is wrong for staged types: their reader takes a witness first (ty_of_xml forall s. (witness : stage s) (c : xml.xml_node) : ty s), so it has type stage s -> xml_node -> ty s, not the prototype's xml_node -> t, and my probe had no witness parameter. STILL OPEN: where the instance gets the stage witness from its type. Candidates: (a) a second prototype 'stage_of s : () -> stage s' with one instance per stage nominal, so 'instance of_xml ty s = fun c => ty_of_xml (stage_of ()) c' under a {stage_of} constraint; (b) the codec prototype itself takes the witness (of_xml t : stage s -> xml_node -> t s), which keeps the GADT honest but makes non-staged types carry a dummy stage. NEXT: probe (a) first; it keeps one prototype shape for every generated type.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_9 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 9u32, "2026-11-02T22:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 18:09 fiscal: STAGE WITNESS SOLVED (candidate (a) from n8), probed with the real staging prelude shape (union stage s = | Unsigned :: stage unsigned | Signed :: stage signed, reader doc_of_text forall s. (witness : stage s) (x : string) : doc s that matches on the witness). Two pieces: 'prototype stage_of s : () -> stage s' with 'instance stage_of unsigned = fun () => Unsigned' and 'instance stage_of signed = fun () => Signed', and a CONSTRAINED HKT instance 'instance of_text doc s {stage_of} = fun x => doc_of_text (stage_of ()) x' (forall_var accepts a {constraints} block after the var, spiral_compiler.fs:2733). Without {stage_of} the instance is rejected with ETY-ForallVarConstraintError ('Got {stage_of} Expected {}'). Results: generic 'stable forall t {of_text; to_text}' round-trips both doc unsigned and doc signed; --check exit 0, Rust 2,143 bytes. NEGATIVE: a doc draft with no stage_of instance fails 'ETY-InstanceNotFound: ... draft does not have the prototype stage_of'. So the emitter shape is: the staging prelude gains stage_of and its 2 instances (lib, once), staged types get 'instance of_xml ty s {stage_of} = fun c => ty_of_xml (stage_of ()) c', plain types 'instance of_xml ty = ty_of_xml'. Probes kept in the session scratchpad (codec-proto-probe/-neg/-hkt/-stage/-stage-neg). Progress 10 -> 25 (design proven, nothing emitted yet).")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_10 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 10u32, "2026-11-02T22:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 18:14 fiscal: CROSS-PACKAGE PROVEN: prototypes declared once in package a (prototype of_text/to_text + generic 'stable') and instances in package b ('open codec' then 'instance of_text amount = amount_of_text') type-check and compile to Rust (1,041 bytes); b calls codec.stable on its own type. So a lib xml_codec module can own of_xml/to_xml/example, and every generated unit opens it and adds instances (generated split units already emit 'open <module>', xsd_emit.spi:2740). LIMIT FOUND IN THE EMITTER: staged examples are fixed to the unsigned stage ('and let ty_example (k : i32) : ty unsigned', xsd_emit.spi:2027), so staged types get of_xml/to_xml instances over 'ty s' but their example stays a function (an instance on 'ty unsigned' alone is not the HKT shape). PLAN for the draft, in order: (1) lib/spiral/xml_codec.spi: the 3 prototypes plus 'round_trips' (to_xml, of_xml, to_xml again, then xml.first_difference = None) and its own test on a hand-written nominal; (2) xsd_emit: units_of_parts appends an instances block after functions_group, one line per type whose 'and let <ty>_of_xml' exists (the has_function_key idiom at :2774), with the staged form under {stage_of}; the staging prelude gains stage_of and its 2 instances; (3) a new xsd_emit test every_generated_type_has_its_codec_instances; (4) the generator's example test calls xml_codec.round_trips instead of string-glued names. Gates: xsd_emit node gate, then a full fiscal regen. Draft goes to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES until the pending fiscal regens are placed.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_11 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 11u32, "2026-11-02T22:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-02 18:33 fiscal: BLOCKER FOUND FOR THE THIN-INSTANCE PLAN (n10): instances cannot attach to structural type aliases. Probe on pack17: 'type x_record = { amount : string }' + 'instance of_text x_record = ...' fails 'ETY-ExpectedHigherOrder: Expected a higher order type. Got: {amount : string}'. And generated records ARE aliases: across fiscal/generated, 9,607 'type x_... =' record declarations vs 25 nominal records and 6,056 unions (cfdi_tfd: 'type x_timbre_fiscal_digital =' at line 3547). So codec instances need records emitted as NOMINALS first ('nominal x_foo = { ... }'), which changes every record construction (x_foo { ... }) and every field read (unwrap or a pattern) in the reader, writer and example walkers. That is a type-safety win on its own: today two XSD types with the same fields are the SAME Spiral type, so one type's reader accepts the other's value; as nominals they are distinct. RE-PLANNED: step 0 = XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS (emitter: records become nominals; generated units regenerate; every round trip stays green; prediction: generated line count roughly unchanged, construction sites gain the constructor name), then the instance block from n10. Unions (6,056) can take instances today, so a partial first slice over unions alone is possible but leaves records, the main codec carriers, out; not worth a regen by itself. Estimate up: this item now needs 2 full fiscal regens (nominal records, then instances), not 1. Progress stays 25 (design proven; the record shape blocks emission).")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_12 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 12u32, "2026-11-03T09:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 05:17 fiscal: EMITTER LAYER DRAFTED, proof queued. %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES\\lib\\spiral\\ (xsd_emit.spi A90D8A59 on top of XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS A10404BA; xml_codec.spi; package.spiproj registering xml_codec after xml). xsd_emit: codec_prelude opens xml_codec; the staging prelude gains 'prototype stage_of s : () -> stage s' with its unsigned/signed instances; units_of_parts appends codec_instances, built from the unit's own function keys ('and let X_of_xml' + 'and let X_to_xml' -> 'instance of_xml X = X_of_xml' / 'instance to_xml X = X_to_xml'; the 'forall s.' pair -> 'instance of_xml X s {stage_of} = fun c => X_of_xml (stage_of ()) c' and 'instance to_xml X s = X_to_xml'); types still emitted as 'type' aliases get none (ETY-ExpectedHigherOrder, n11); versioned split families get none yet. New test generated_types_have_codec_instances. QUEUED: job-1793697385566-fiscal-codec-layer (t1101, after the nominal-records job; one Cells run per node; pinned compiler): mutation, xml_codec 1/1, xsd_emit 32/32, generator 23/23, then cfdi_tfd (plain instances) and nfe_evento_canc (staged instances) unit gates. Generic round-trip use in the generator's tests comes after this layer lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_13 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 13u32, "2026-11-03T09:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 05:46 fiscal: The repeated-sequence fold beneath this layer was refuted (FISCAL-PT-SAFT n22), so the draft is REBASED in place onto spiral HEAD's xsd_emit (738935CD) by removing that arm and its test : XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES draft now D5103118 (31 tests). The queued job (job-1793697385566) runs on the pre-rebase copy (expects 32/32 there); landing uses D5103118 after XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS lands.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_14 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 14u32, "2026-11-03T11:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 07:52 fiscal: TYPE-CHECKED ON IDLE VULTR (pack24 compiler, lib = spiral HEAD 98e51d32 + this draft, SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR = the shipped core; mutation-proven: an appended ill-typed definition exits 5 / ETY-TermError): the REBASED draft D5103118 xsd_emit.spi exit 0 in 4 s and xml_codec.spi (registered after xml) exit 0 in 4 s.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_15 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 15u32, "2026-11-03T12:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 08:37 fiscal: PARTIAL VERDICT (job-1793697385566, still running its xsd_emit/regen steps): mutation FAILS on the live lib as predicted. xml_codec's own test FAILED at runtime with '/Amount: text 12.50 vs (empty)': the sample instance read the value with xml.node_text, which returns text only for a text node and the empty string for an element. FIX in the draft (xml_codec D3348061): 'of_xml amount_text = \\ node => amount_text (text_in (element_children node))', the same form generated readers use (xml.text_in (xml.element_children c)). Type-checks on vultr (exit 0); its Cells re-run rides the codec landing gate. The emitter's instance texts are unaffected (they delegate to the generated ty_of_xml / ty_to_xml).")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_16 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 16u32, "2026-11-03T13:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 09:40 fiscal: xsd_emit GATE (job-1793697385566, pre-rebase draft): 31/32. The new test generated_types_have_codec_instances PASSES. The 1 failure, coded_types_share_the_text_prototype, asserted that a generated module STARTS WITH 'prototype to_text t : t -> string', and the layer now prepends 'open xml_codec'; that is the intended change, so the assertion follows: it now requires the module to start with the open line and then the to_text prototype, before any instance. Updated in the rebased draft, now 9F2CA353, type-checked on vultr (exit 0). The job's regen and its plain/staged unit gates are still running.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_17 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 17u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 11:28 fiscal: CODEC LAYER PROVEN IN GENERATED UNITS (job-1793697385566, t1101, pinned core 21D5992EDB80D270, one compiler; pre-rebase copy on the nominal-records base): regen gives 44 units that open xml_codec and 20,908 codec instance lines; the PLAIN-instance unit generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1 passes 2/2 and the STAGED unit generated_nfe_evento_canc_v1_00 (constrained 'instance of_xml ty s {stage_of}' over its signed types) passes 2/2, so the HKT + {stage_of} design compiles and runs in real generated code; generator 21/23 (the same 2 'type' assertions as XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS n6). Earlier steps: mutation FAILS on the live lib; xsd_emit 31/32 (the prelude assertion, updated in 9F2CA353); xml_codec 0/1 (the sample instance's node_text, fixed in D3348061). All test bodies of the rebased drafts parse and type-check on vultr. LANDING: after XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS lands, D5103118->9F2CA353 xsd_emit + xml_codec D3348061 + lib package.spiproj registration, with one regen.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_18 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 18u32, "2026-11-03T18:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 14:26 fiscal: REBASE NEEDED: lib xsd_emit.spi moved 738935CD -> 325E10F1 (FISCAL-PT-SAFT group_part landed unstaged). This draft was rebased onto 738935CD, so it must be re-applied onto 325E10F1 and re-proven (output-exact regen) before landing.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_19 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 19u32, "2026-11-03T19:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:02 fiscal: REBASED onto group_part 325E10F1 the same way (it already contains the nominal change): draft D5B290F3 (scratch rebase\\codec.resolved.spi) = nominal + 76/-4 codec lines. PROVEN on vultr with xml_codec D3348061 registered after xml: xsd_emit and xml_codec --check exit 0 with bodies; ALL 32 xsd_emit test bodies run exit 0 as Rust. Lands after XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS' node proof; then one regen.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_20 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 20u32, "2026-11-04T00:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 20:31 fiscal: PROVEN ON NOMINAL (node job-1793743680574-fiscal-codec, core 2ABF22D79E6B6943, one compiler; it finished at 19:48, before the 19:50 box BSOD, and the node was unaffected): MUTATION generated_types_have_codec_instances alone on the nominal lib FAILS; generator 23/23; format 82 units 0 failed; 44 units changed vs the nominal units; pt_saft 2/2. CLASSIFIED on the box (line multisets per unit, ///- headers excluded): 0 lines lost in any of the 44 units; added = 10,455 'instance of_xml', 10,455 'instance to_xml', 54 'instance stage_of', 44 'open xml_codec', 'prototype stage_of' in staged units, and the formatter's wrapped continuations of long instance lines -- purely additive, as designed (a plain line diff showed 140 'removed' lines in the UBL invoice unit: a test block moved below the new instances, not changed). Pre-proven landing bytes on vultr pack27: xsd_emit 5E485076 (formatted; 4 over-width lines vs 21 live) all 32 bodies as Rust exit 0; xml_codec D3348061 body exit 0; respell 0. LANDING through lib_land_window now (label fiscal-codec-prototypes): xsd_emit + xml_codec (new) + package.spiproj; then the 44 units into fiscal.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_21 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 21u32, "2026-11-04T00:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 20:39 fiscal: LANDED. spiral lib through lib_land_window (label fiscal-codec-prototypes, closed green: signatures 0 changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22, type_probe xsd_emit 32 + xml_codec 1 tests typed, respell 0; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261103-203122): xsd_emit.spi 5E485076 (nominal + codec, formatted), NEW xml_codec.spi D3348061, package.spiproj registers xml_codec after xml. fiscal (unstaged): the 44 units from job-1793743680574 placed (generator unchanged, 5DB916E8). Every generated record now has 'instance of_xml' / 'instance to_xml' (10,455 each) and staged units 'instance stage_of' -- the base for XSD-DECODE-RESULT, XSD-FACET-TYPES and the ERP adapters. COMMIT spiral + fiscal TOGETHER.")
inl note_of_xsd_codec_prototypes_22 () = Note ("XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES", 22u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 00:13 fiscal: DONE (groom 11-04): landed via lib_land_window (xsd_emit 5E485076 + new xml_codec D3348061, closed green: signatures 0 changed, document_test 22/22, type_probe 2/2, respell 0); 44 units regenerated with 10,455 of_xml + 10,455 to_xml instances, 0 lines lost (multiset check); joint pack27 type check of both live trees 22/22. Unstaged by the user's choice.")
inl xsd_field_descriptors () = Task ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS", "field GADT indexed by owner and value with field_meta and a fields prototype, so writer, example, diff and path rules are one lib walk", Story, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES,FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", "team:fiscal,fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
