inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_1 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T12:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:06 fiscal: GROOM (pre-merge inventory): this item had no notes. STATE: Planned, not started; its title is the spec. GATE: it changes xsd_emit/generator output, so it waits for FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND to land (the same reason as the Paused XSD-FACET-TYPES / XSD-DECODE-RESULT / XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES), then one regeneration per change. NEXT: write a design note against the edition-3 emitter before any code.")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_2 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:51 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (round 5). DONE WHEN: every generated record exposes \"fields : list (exists v. field owner v)\"; a node gate of xsd_emit.spi passes a new test a_generic_diff_uses_only_field_descriptors (one diff/printer over any generated record, written once); the canon coverage table (FISCAL-CANON-MODEL) is computed from descriptors, not grepped paths. NEXT STEP: after XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES (in deps), emit descriptors from the same record walk that emits the codec instances (xsd_emit record_walk). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a GADT indexed by owner and value, \":| ^ field owner value = | Field :: { name : tag_name; get : owner -> value; meta : field_meta } -> field owner value\", collected existentially per record; \":== field_meta = { occurs : occurs; facets : list xsd_facet; namespace : option namespace_uri }\"; a \"fields\" prototype per type. This is the reflection layer that XSD-TYPED-RULES and the canon bindings consume, so neither ever indexes a record by a field-name string.")
inl note_of_xsd_field_descriptors_3 () = Note ("XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:15Z", "fiscal", "groom 11-01 19:1x SPLIT (720 min is over the 4 h bar), each step about 4 h with its own gate: S1: the field GADT (owner x value) for record fields only in xsd_emit, plus a test that a record's field list is typed by its owner (gate xsd_emit on the node). S2: existential field lists (\"exists v. field owner v\") replace the string-keyed part walk in record_texts for the reading and writing instances; gate xsd_emit + regenerate 2 families per-family (FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL), 0 diff. S3: choice and attribute parts move to descriptors, and the exampling instance uses them (this is where XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES' attribute_view owner field folds in). DONE per step = its gate green + its regeneration diff 0.")
inl fiscal_versioned_families () = Task ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES", "fiscal adopts generate_versioned_family: one module per schema closure, payload-free nominal version tags, a reader dispatching on @versao to exists v. version_witness v", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", "team:fiscal,fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_versioned_families () = Planning ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES", Minutes 390u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES", 1u32, "2026-10-30T17:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 13:04 fiscal: GROOM (fill-all-fields: no estimate, no notes until now). State: lib already has xsd_emit.generate_versioned_family (xsd_emit.spi:2858; union version_witness v with one payload-carrying tag per version, a reader _of_xml forall v. (witness : version_witness v); demo test at :2948 over generated_demo_v1/v2 -> generated_demo_core). fiscal does not call it. Versioned groups in fiscal/generated today: nfe x3, cte x3, cte_os x2, gtve x2, mdfe x2 (SAF-T PT publishes 4 versions, only 1.04_01 generated: a later candidate). Estimate from milestones, 390m: M1 120m, MDF-e (the smallest group, v1.00 + v3.00) onto generate_versioned_family, then regenerate, diff the generated text, set-proof the units and their real documents. M2 180m, the other 4 groups the same way. M3 90m, the reader dispatching on @versao proven with one real document per version. Load medium (regeneration + unit compiles on the node). Dep FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND: the change is in src/generator.spi, which the edition-3 respell rewrites (anchors-stale-across-respell).")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES", 2u32, "2026-10-31T12:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 08:14 fiscal: MEASURED DUPLICATION in the committed generated/ (74 units): generated_cte_v4_00, generated_cte_os_v4_00, generated_cte_simp_v4_00 and generated_gtve_v4_00 are each 33,518 lines and each holds the WHOLE CT-e 4.00 closure (type x_tc_te s, x_tc_te_os s, x_tc_te_simp s all appear in every unit); cte_v4_00 vs gtve_v4_00 differ in 38 lines only (the --timeout header and the root-specific writes_its_example / bench test). So ~100k of the four units' 134k lines are the same model compiled four times (each unit is its own rustc/Delphi build), which is the case this item's 'one module per schema closure' fixes: one closure package + four thin root packages. Size before/after is the measurable outcome to pin when this starts.")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES", 3u32, "2026-11-01T14:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:42 fiscal: TREE-WIDE MEASUREMENT (child of FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE): across the 44 committed generated units (954k lines), about 453,000 lines (48%) are top-level definitions repeated byte for byte in 5+ units. Largest: DFA pattern functions shared by many schemas (xsd_pattern_f653e85e_247 206 lines x 14 units, xsd_pattern_f009c066_169 145 x 16, xsd_pattern_ad0d4073_128 112 x 16 ...), the UBL common records (x_consignment_type_children 385 x 6, x_transport_equipment_type_children 220 x 6) and CT-e enums (x_tc_list_serv_of_string 197 x 9). DONE WHEN repeated lines < 5% (same counter: identical top-level def bodies in >= 5 units), with the shared parts as closure/pattern modules imported through module_package dependencies, and every unit gate green. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a shared pattern function is identified by its pattern's content hash (it already is: xsd_pattern_<hash>), emitted once into a patterns module; a shared record type lives in its closure module and units refer to it by its qualified name, never by re-emitting it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_versioned_families_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T04:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 00:16 fiscal: GROOM 11-04 (last note 11-01): owner fiscal, still Planned. It is the module-per-schema-closure step that FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE's shared patterns module rides on (anchors re-derived 11-03 on xsd_emit 5E485076). NEXT: start after the patterns change lands, together with it in one regen proof on the node.")
