inl note_of_xsd_typed_rules_1 () = Note ("XSD-TYPED-RULES", 1u32, "2026-11-01T12:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:06 fiscal: GROOM (pre-merge inventory): this item had no notes. STATE: Planned, not started; its title is the spec. GATE: it changes xsd_emit/generator output, so it waits for FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND to land (the same reason as the Paused XSD-FACET-TYPES / XSD-DECODE-RESULT / XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES), then one regeneration per change. NEXT: write a design note against the edition-3 emitter before any code.")
inl note_of_xsd_typed_rules_2 () = Note ("XSD-TYPED-RULES", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:51 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (round 5). DONE WHEN: the EN 16931 UBL rules (104 rules, 981 asserts, validation-1.3.17) compile to typed predicates over the generated UBL Invoice type, and on the 5 CEN examples plus the mutated invoices of corpus_checks cen_rules_catch_mutated_invoices their verdicts equal the schematron engine's (0 disagreements), with the count of rules not yet compilable reported per reason. NEXT STEP: after XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS, pick the 10 simplest BR-* rules (single-path existence/equality) and compile them through the field descriptors; diff the verdicts with schematron_run on the CEN examples. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: \":| ^ rule doc = | Rule :: { id : rule_id; flag : rule_flag; check : doc -> verdict } -> rule doc\" indexed by the generated document type, so a UBL rule cannot be applied to a CII document; \":! rule_id = string\" from the rule's id attribute; \":| verdict = | Holds | Fails : list decode_path\"; \":| rule_flag = | Fatal | Warning\". XPath text is parsed once at generation time (lib xpath) into the predicate; no XPath strings are evaluated at run time. key/unique constraints become the same rule type.")
inl xsd_any_complements () = Task ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", "xs:any content typed as a closed complement union with an Unknown case (generate_complements), not list xml_node", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "XSD-ANY-CONTENT-READER", "fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,codegen,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_any_complements () = Planning ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_1 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T22:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:12 fiscal: PLAN (pre-registered). Exists: xsd_emit.generate_complements builds union complement + complement_of_xml (namespace dispatch, Unknown case). Missing: wiring. (1) family_root gains complements : list (case, namespace, schema path); (2) the any_part reader/writer of a module with complements types the field list complement via listm.map complement_of_xml over xml.unclaimed_children; (3) CFDI first: init pins SAT TimbreFiscalDigitalv11.xsd + Pagos20.xsd. PASS: CFDI regenerates; a stamped CFDI's Complemento reads as TimbreFiscalDigital, round-trip equal; an unknown complement reads as Unknown with its XML kept.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_2 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T22:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:13 fiscal: plan step 3 IN THE TREE: init fetches SAT TimbreFiscalDigitalv11.xsd (sha FB3D061F) and Pagos20.xsd (sha F37DD303) pinned into corpus/mx/complements; both reachable from scripts (unlike SUNAT). Steps 1-2 (family_root.complements, any_part wiring) touch xsd_emit + generator: next after the lib hold.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_3 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T22:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:15 fiscal: plan refinement: generate_complements emits only a READER (complement_of_xml); there is no complement_to_xml. Typing any as list complement breaks the writer and round trips until a writer dispatch exists (per case: member.T_children / element wrapper; Unknown writes its kept nodes). Add that as step 1b before wiring.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_4 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 4u32, "2026-10-28T11:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 07:40 fiscal: step 1b REFINED by reading the emitter: complement_of_xml's fallback is 'Unknown (local, xml.element_children node)', which DROPS the element's attributes, prefix and namespace, so no writer could reproduce an unknown complement and the plan's own PASS ('unknown complement keeps its XML') fails. Change: Unknown : xml.xml_node (keep the whole element); complement_to_xml = per case module.T_to_xml '<element>' v with the schema namespace prepended via xml.element + element_attributes, and Unknown node -> node. Also: fiscal's mx corpus has 0 CFDI documents, so a stamped CFDI must be sourced first (candidate: CfdiUtils test fixtures with SAT's test taxpayer EKU9003173C9; check license/provenance).")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_5 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 5u32, "2026-10-28T11:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 07:53 fiscal: stamped CFDI SOURCED (in the tree, unstaged): init pins CfdiUtils@f2a03dc2 tests/assets/cfdi40-valid.xml (MIT; sha 66056C12) to corpus/mx/stamped; issuer is SAT test taxpayer EKU9003173C9, Complemento = tfd:TimbreFiscalDigital only. .NET referee vs cfdv40 + TFD 1.1: 0 messages; positive control (TFD Version 9.9) gives 1 error on the TFD, so lax xs:any is really checked. New manifest mx-cfdi-comprobante (1 doc) + validate-manifests row. Next: step 1b on top of xsd-emit-list-sugar.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_6 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 6u32, "2026-10-28T12:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 08:32 fiscal: step 1b DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-any-complements-writer.kit (3 hunks in the complements region, +34/-5, stacks on xsd-emit-list-sugar; draft %TEMP%\\tc-cx-draft). Unknown : xml.xml_node (whole element); complement_to_xml per case = complement_in <ns> (module.T_to_xml <element> v), complement_in adds a default xmlns (right for SAT TFD/Pagos: elementFormDefault qualified; unqualified forms not modelled); Unknown node => node. Test renamed complements_read_and_write_typed_cases_and_keep_unknown_elements_whole. Proof job-1793190814819 fiscal-fix-cx (A4E48020).")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_7 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 7u32, "2026-10-28T13:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:26 fiscal: step 1b HOLDS on the node (job-1793190814819 fiscal-fix-cx, A4E48020, mirror lib + draft xsd_emit 841B97D2 = list sugar + 1b): complements_read_and_write_typed_cases_and_keep_unknown_elements_whole passed on rust in 343 s; xsd_emit type errors 0. Program xsd-any-complements-writer.kit is ready to land after xsd-emit-list-sugar (same file, non-overlapping hunks). Next: step 2 wiring (family_root.complements + any_part typed via complement_of_xml) in xsd_emit + generator, then CFDI regen with the stamped fixture.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_8 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 8u32, "2026-10-28T13:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:28 fiscal: step 2 PLAN (pre-registered): one indirection, emitter stays family-agnostic. The 5 any sites (field type 844, claim 1228, writer 1622, example 1682, witness 1666) emit any : any_content, any_content_of (unclaimed nodes), any_content_to x.any. Unit prelude default: any_content = list xml.xml_node, both identity. A family with complements (generator: family_root.complements, TFD 1.1 + Pagos 2.0 as their own generated units) gets list complement + listm.map complement_of_xml / complement_to_xml. PASS: non-CFDI units regenerate identical except the 5 sites; the stamped CFDI reads TimbreFiscalDigital and round-trips (first_difference).")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_9 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 9u32, "2026-10-28T13:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:42 fiscal: step 2 lib half DRAFTED, held as lib-programs/xsd-any-content-indirection.kit (10 hunks +44/-12, stacks on xsd-any-complements-writer; draft %TEMP%\\tc-ac-draft). The 5 any sites emit any_content/any_content_of/any_content_to; generated_units_with (any_content prelude) + generated_units = untyped default (signature unchanged for fiscal + json_schema); the prelude is emitted only when a unit uses any_content (no-any units stay byte-identical); versioned cores carry it when core or a version uses it; complement_any_content () is the override. Tests updated + 1 added. Full-file gate job-1793195005528 fiscal-fix-ac.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_10 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 10u32, "2026-10-28T13:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:46 fiscal: step 2 generator half DRAFTED (scratchpad complements/src/generator.spi, held until writer + indirection land): cfdi_tfd_1_1 family (TFD imports only tdCFDI, local); complement_source + complements_of lookup (no new family_root field, so the UBL-JSON draft still merges); module_package/write_generated_module_with take dependency units (CFDI package lists ../generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1-); write_family_modules passes generate_complements + complement_any_content, else untyped_any_content; CFDI documents = mx-cfdi-comprobante manifest. Pagos 2.0 deferred: it imports catPagos.xsd, not yet pinned. Proof after fix-ac: set-proof, units generated_cfdi.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_11 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 11u32, "2026-10-28T13:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:58 fiscal: Pagos 2.0 UNBLOCKED: init.ps1 pins SAT catPagos.xsd (sha 72DBAA6E, own file guard since the complements folder already exists); .NET compiles Pagos20 with its 3 imports (4 schemas, root Pagos). Held generator draft now has cfdi_pagos_2_0 (catalog catCFDI/tdCFDI/catPagos to local copies) and complements_of CFDI = [TimbreFiscalDigital11; Pagos20]; its test writes 3 units.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_12 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 12u32, "2026-10-29T11:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 07:47 fiscal: step 1b writer LANDED 07:28:50 (xsd-any-complements-writer.kit, xsd_emit 1FC1425B -> 841B97D2 = the hash fix-cx proved). Step 2 lib proof fix-ac (job-1793195005528) was VOID, not red: 11 of 17 tests hit the 900 s cell cap under node load (headroom 1.03), 0 type errors. Requeued as fiscal-fix-ac2 (job-1793274140547, after the emit gate) on mirror ac re-synced to the live tree + xsd-any-content-indirection.kit (841B97D2 -> CF7BBF4D, rehearsed on a scratch copy), header --timeout 5400000 in the mirror only. The generator half draft (cfdi_tfd_1_1 + cfdi_pagos_2_0) was lost with the scratchpad: rebuild from n10/n11.")
inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_13 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 13u32, "2026-10-29T12:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 08:06 fiscal: step 2 generator half REBUILT after the wipe, held IN THE REPO as fiscal/lib-programs/generator-complements.kit (4 hunks on fiscal/src/generator.spi; rehearsed on a scratch copy: tree 28099567 -> 3E7BCC48). Content: cfdi_tfd_1_1 + cfdi_pagos_2_0 families (local tdCFDI/catCFDI/catPagos catalogs), complements_of CFDI = [TimbreFiscalDigital11; Pagos20], members via family_schema -> generate_complements ++# complement_any_content () into generated_units_with, CFDI package lists ../generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1- and ../generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0- (module_package now takes a dependency list; empty list = byte-identical packages, already in the tree), CFDI documents = mx-cfdi-comprobante manifest, test writes 3 units and checks 'type any_content = list complement' + the package lines. Apply after the indirection lands (fix-ac2), then set-proof units generated_cfdi.")
