inl note_of_xsd_any_complements_18 () = Note ("XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS", 18u32, "2026-10-29T16:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 12:30 fiscal: set-cfdi3 (job-1793281272369) finished exit 1 with one REAL lib bug: init, generator, generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1 (+certificates) and generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0 (+certificates) HOLD and 3 files declare private nominals; generated_cfdi_v4_0 fails to type-check: 'Unbound term variable: ++#' in complement_namespace, because generate_complements emits a bare ++# while generated units spell the operator sm'.(++#) (they don't open sm'_operators). It's an old line, but this is the first real unit with complements. Fix held as fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-complement-namespace-operator.kit (live xsd_emit F49F611A -> 5606F4B4; rehearsed); the complements test now pins the spelling; proof fiscal-m7-complements (job-1793291208588) queued. After it lands, rerun set-proof units generated_cfdi.")
