inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 38u32, "2026-10-29T19:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 15:28 fiscal: xpath-mod-and-long-integers LANDED 15:19:10 (decimal 99EB6B29 -> B9AC478A, xpath_eval 1AB4EE5A -> BB243652), via lib-guarded-do in the 15:18 gap (no exemptions), hash equal to the pack-6b-proven copy (node stage spiral-bin-1029-6b, core 31CC96520D6B7269); main's closing document_test 22/22 over all gap lands. Byte-exact undo copies: C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\land-1029\\{m7,sch2,mod,cells64b}\\base (not git HEAD: other lanes' unstaged lib hunks). XPath mod works, decimal.parse no longer overflows on long digit strings, and DE-R-019/020's IBAN check evaluates (test on DE89370400440532013000 = 1). Next: a full Peppol evaluation run over its samples.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 39u32, "2026-10-29T22:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 18:07 fiscal: PEPPOL ROOT CAUSE (fiscal-6b-eval2-peppol_exa, rule ids now in the failure text): the only Peppol failure left is CEN BR-CO-17 on examples/vat-category-O.xml (peppol rules: none). The category-O disjunct not(exists(cac:TaxCategory[..]/xs:decimal(cbc:Percent))) fails because xpath_eval.mapped_each kept a step's empty result as a nested VSequence [VSequence []], which is_empty_value does not see as empty. Fix drafted as held program fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-path-step-flattens.kit (xpath_eval BB243652 -> 38FCB953: flatten step values via sequence_items, VNodes when nothing remains; 2 regression lines in evaluates_en16931_style_rules), rehearsed hash-equal, proving as fiscal-6b-seqflat-proof. Next: land, then rerun peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules.")
inl note_of_fiscal_peppol_bis3_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-PEPPOL-BIS3", 40u32, "2026-10-29T23:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 19:05 fiscal: PEPPOL EVALUATION GREEN on the combined lib drafts (fiscal-6b-zfn2-peppol, mirror zfn6b = live lib + schematron-pattern-lets-shared + xpath-path-step-flattens + xpath-floor-pictures-errors, pack 6b): peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules HOLDS (329.6 s, memo_hits 0). Every Peppol BIS 3.0.20 example passes the Peppol and CEN EN16931 UBL schematrons with zero fatal findings, and the and/or error propagation surfaced no hidden failure. The test turns green in the tree once these programs land (next session's first window, per main).")
