inl fiscal_in_gst_einvoice () = Task ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", "India GST e-invoice (IRP INV-01, JSON Schema 1.1) as fiscal's first JSON Schema family", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "FISCAL-GENERIC", "fiscal,generic,country,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice () = Planning ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source: the JSON Schema (draft-07) is embedded in https://einv-apisandbox.nic.in/version1.03/generate-irn.html#JSONSchema, verified only through a Wayback snapshot (web.archive.org/web/20241005055248/...); from the review box einvoice1.gst.gov.in does not resolve and the sandbox times out, so 1.1 being current is UNVERIFIED. Plan: init.ps1 extracts the schema from the page (or the snapshot), pinned by hash; generator family source JsonSchema (source union landed 10-27, generator.spi family_schema); example and round trip through json_schema.json_document / json_document_text (writer landed 10-27).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 2u32, "2026-10-27T12:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 08:56 fiscal: IN THE TREE, unstaged (fiscal generator.spi E3FD312C, scripts/init.ps1). (1) Schema source: init.ps1 fetches the NIC sandbox page through the Wayback snapshot of 2024-10-05 (reachable from here; the live NIC hosts are not), extracts the JSON Schema from its <pre> block, and REFUSES unless its sha256 starts 2F53D00F2F754722. The published schema is NOT standard draft-07: its 15 sections sit at the root (no properties/type), the key 'AddlDocDtls ' and an inner 'type ' carry trailing spaces, and ItemList/AddlDocDtls are written as one-element arrays holding the item schema. init keeps the raw copy (deps/corpus/in/gst/inv01_published.json) and writes a standard one (inv01_1.1.json) by three recorded rules: root sections under properties with type object; every key trimmed; a one-schema array inside properties becomes type array + items. Checked: root object, 15 properties, 7 required, ItemList an array of objects with 30 properties, 0 keys with spaces. (2) Generator: family gst_inv01_1_1 (module generated_in_gst_inv01_1_1, root GstInvoice, source JsonSchema) with test generates_gst_inv01_1_1; a JSON family's example test writes <module>_example.json through json_schema.json_document_text (schema read at run time by its repo-relative path) and then ROUND-TRIPS it: json_document -> typed _of_xml -> _to_xml -> json text, failing unless identical; the XML-only bench is skipped for JSON families. Type-checked (generator + probe 0 errors), formatter no-op. Next: node proof (regeneration + the unit's example test).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 3u32, "2026-10-27T14:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 10:54 fiscal: an independent JSON referee FOUND THREE MORE DEFECTS in NIC's published schema, each silently corrupting our generated model: PowerShell's Test-Json (a strict draft-07 validator) refused to even parse the normalized schema, and each refusal led to one: (a) type VALUES with stray spaces ('string ' x2, ' number' x1, 'object ' x1): our front end compares type names exactly, so ' number' became a string field and 'object ' would have flattened a whole section into one string; (b) 'String' with a capital S (the two Ph fields); (c) RefDtls carries a 'required': [InvNo, InvDt] list INSIDE its properties, which our front end would have generated as a bogus field named 'required'. init.ps1's normalization now has 5 recorded rules (sections under properties; keys trimmed; type values trimmed and lowercased; a misplaced required list moved up to its object; one-schema arrays as type array + items); refetched; Test-Json now parses it and correctly rejects a partial document for its 6 missing required sections. family-gates.ps1 now judges India's JSON example with Test-Json against this schema (a '== ...json' section with 'validation messages N', so proofs read it like every XML sample). Known gap, recorded not fixed: 6 of 91 GST patterns use ECMA-262 lookaround ('^(?!0+\\$)...') which XSD's regex dialect lacks; our front end passes JSON patterns into XSD pattern facets, so those 6 need an ECMA->XSD translation or a validated-in-code fallback (next step for this item).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 4u32, "2026-10-27T15:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:01 fiscal: the regex-dialect gap is CLOSED at the boundary: every GST pattern is now XSD-expressible (0 patterns with '(?' left), by two more recorded normalization rules in init.ps1 (7 in all), each exact and each refusing what it cannot translate exactly: rule 6, the not-all-zeros idiom '^(?!0+\\$)(<digit runs>)\\$' (Stcd x4, Pos, HsnCd) becomes the union of '0{k}[1-9][0-9]{n-k-1}' over each run length, proven by brute force against .NET's regex: 0 disagreements over 711,134 strings for both shapes ('[0-9]{1,2}' and '[0-9]{4}|[0-9]{6}|[0-9]{8}'); rule 7, a '(?i)' case-insensitive word list (SupTyp, Typ) drops the flag and expands each letter to [xX] (0 disagreements on 14 probes incl. mixed case and near misses); a lookaround or (?i) pattern of any other shape now THROWS in init (that guard caught the (?i) ones on its first run, and the partial-fetch trap removed the half-written folder). Test-Json still parses the result and rejects partial documents. The all-proof running now used the schema from before these fixes; the next proof regenerates India from this one.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 5u32, "2026-10-27T15:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 11:24 fiscal: LIB TESTS PASS on the node (all-proof job-1793112172864, Cells lib_gate per module, process compiler, memo off, full logs kept): xsd 8/8, xsd_resolve 4/4, xsd_emit 17/17, json_schema 5/5, xml 10/10 (13 rows), every one of today's new tests present and green. json_schema's element_trees_write_back_to_the_json_their_schema_describes (the JSON writer) and number_bounds_become_the_xsd_range_facets pass.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 6u32, "2026-10-27T18:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 14:41 fiscal: all-proof GST unit FAILED (writes_its_example panicked: not a valid seller Stcd). Cause: the node's in/gst came via the corpus zip, and init normalized only inside the fetch guard, so the node generated from the raw lookahead schema. FIX IN THE TREE: init guards only the fetch (inv01_published.json), then re-checks the pin and derives inv01_1.1.json every run. Verified: unchanged bytes on a normal run; control (raw file in place) is rewritten to the exact normalized bytes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 7u32, "2026-10-27T22:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:28 fiscal: IN THE TREE: (1) the official NIC sample request was INVALID against our normalized schema, exposing 2 normalization bugs: a stray required list went to the enclosing object (RefDtls) instead of the sibling whose items hold the names (PrecDocDtls), and names inside required lists were not trimmed (' InvStDt '). Fixed in init; all 13 required lists checked, controls rejected. (2) init derives the sample (pinned AB5BC97C, nulls dropped) to in/gst/examples; the family lists it; the generator emits a JSON document cell (json_document_checks) comparing schema-ordered text. Generator type-checks.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 8u32, "2026-10-28T03:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 23:45 fiscal: RUNTIME: node set-proof setb (job-1793152028390, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357): fiscal's generator HOLDS, 21/21 tests, 0 failed, 0 memo hits, including the new json_document_checks cell for the GST sample request; the generated units build next (59 in this group).")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 9u32, "2026-10-28T03:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 23:45 fiscal: CORRECTION to the previous note: the generator's 21 tests EMIT the json_document_checks cell into the generated GST unit; the round trip itself runs only when setb builds that unit, so it is not proven yet.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 10u32, "2026-10-28T06:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 02:57 fiscal: RUNTIME: the GST unit with json_document_checks is GREEN on the node (setc, job-1793162726520): the official NIC sample request round-trips unchanged through the generated JSON reader/writer. First JSON-family real-document proof.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 11u32, "2026-10-30T16:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 12:14 fiscal: GROOM R3 status (2.3 d): the remaining step is a re-proof. This row's runtime evidence (setc 10-28, compiler 4FD712E9E357) predates pack 6b (stale-pin restamp, FISCAL-GENERIC n of 10-29 15:18), so the official NIC sample request (JSON) must round-trip again on the current lib and compiler. Queued: fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-hugst (job-1793376840350-fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-hugst), units generated_in_gst_inv01_1_1 (+ its partner), on e3lv = live lib + the edition-3 draft + the box corpus, pack 7 staged, after fiscal-p7-set-ublj3, so it runs serially with fiscal's other jobs. Closes at 100 on HOLDS for its documents claim.")
inl note_of_fiscal_in_gst_einvoice_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-IN-GST-EINVOICE", 12u32, "2026-10-31T00:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:12 fiscal: RE-PROVEN, CLOSING. fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-hugst (node job-1793376840350, mirror e3lv = live lib + edition-3 draft + box corpus, pack 7 F2F6F4CB5A18) finished exit 0 with 0 broken claims: the generator 22/22 (0 memo hits), the regenerated units declare their validated nominals private, and generated_in_gst_inv01_1_1 passes every test (2/2), including the json_document_checks round trip of the official NIC sample request, so the documents claim HOLDS on the current lib and compiler. 70 -> 100, Done.")
