inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 9u32, "2026-10-28T10:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:31 fiscal: BLOCKED on user download: an official Facturae 3.2.2 sample invoice (facturae.gob.es Ejemplos or FACe); scripted sourcing found only templates (Odoo fixtures with ___ignore___) and vendor pages.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 10u32, "2026-10-30T14:18Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:18 fiscal: GROOM R1: user-batch. The only blocker is a download: an official Facturae 3.2.2 sample invoice from facturae.gob.es (Ejemplos) or FACe. Scripted sourcing found only templates (n: Odoo fixtures with ___ignore___ placeholders), and the Claude in Chrome extension was not connected on 10-30, so there was no assisted fetch either. The dep FISCAL-GENERIC is its umbrella, not a prerequisite. Once a sample is in deps/corpus/es, the round trip is agent work (generator facturae 3.2.2 already generates).")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 11u32, "2026-11-01T12:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:06 fiscal: UNBLOCKED (groom). The only blocker was a user download (an official Facturae 3.2.2 sample from facturae.gob.es), and the user lifted the download gate on 10-31 ~18:00 (\"stop asking for my oks for things like downloads\"). Agent work again: Blocked -> Planned, assignee agent. NEXT: fetch the official sample into deps/corpus/es/facturae/samples via init.ps1 (pinned by SHA-256), add it to the family's documents, regenerate, and gate the round trip. VeriFactu (generated_es_verifactu) waits on XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES fix (2) for its sf:-qualified children.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 12u32, "2026-11-01T14:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:57 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 5). DONE WHEN: (1) an official Facturae 3.2.2 sample invoice (facturae.gob.es, pinned by sha256 in init.ps1 under deps/corpus/es/facturae/samples) reads back through generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 with 0 drift (no \"real documents do not read back\"); (2) its signed form keeps ds:Signature as the staged slot (the XSD-SIGNING-STAGES model) and the example still validates (validate-example \"validation messages 0\", it is in family-gates since 11-01); (3) VeriFactu (generated_es_verifactu) validates once XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES fix 2 lands (its sf:-qualified children), and its row joins family-gates.\nNEXT STEP: fetch the sample (downloads are standing-OK), add it to src/generator.spi facturae_3_2_2 documents (after the e3 commit), regenerate the unit, gate it on the node.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: Facturae''s invoice issuer type (Individual vs LegalEntity) and tax kinds are XSD choices, so they must stay generated unions (no string discriminators); amounts use the decimal carrier of XSD-FACET-TYPES; the VeriFactu record chain (RegistroAlta with Encadenamiento: PrimerRegistro or RegistroAnterior) is a union whose \"previous record\" case carries the typed hash of the previous record, and the hash is a nominal built by its computing function, never a raw string.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 13u32, "2026-11-02T15:06Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 11:01 DONE WHEN (3) MET: generated_es_verifactu_example.xml validates with 0 messages on both OSes (CI run 41427219939, after the XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES lib push). Remaining: (1) the official Facturae 3.2.2 sample round trip, (2) the staged ds:Signature slot. Status Planned -> Active (70% with work done is not Planned).")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 14u32, "2026-11-03T20:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:43 fiscal: DoD (1) SOURCE RESOLVED: facturae.gob.es publishes NO example invoice for 3.2.2 (it serves only the XSD; the version-3-2-2 page answers 404). Real documents instead: the 10 signed Facturae 3.2.2 invoices in invopop/gobl.facturae test/data/convert/out (Apache-2.0, an active open-source Facturae implementation), pinned by commit b702b599 and per-file sha256 in fiscal scripts/init.ps1 (new block -> deps/corpus/es/facturae/samples; unstaged; block run in isolation fetched all 10 with matching pins; copied into the box corpus). VERIFIED against the corpus XSD with .NET, schema provably loaded (2 schemas: Facturae + xmldsig, 25 global elements): all 10 validate with 0 messages; a control with InvoiceNumber renamed gives 1 message. Every one carries a ds:Signature, so they also exercise DoD (2), the staged signature slot. NEXT: families.spi es_facturae documents = the 10 paths, which changes generated_es_facturae_3_2_2, so it lands only with a regen (queue after the nominal/codec chain); predicted verdict: read back with 0 drift, or the first difference names the staged-signature gap.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 15u32, "2026-11-03T22:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:12 fiscal: NEXT STEP STAGED: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE\\src\\families.spi 010A7436 = the live families.spi with es_facturae documents = the 10 pinned samples (multi-line list); vultr --check with bodies exit 0. It changes generated_es_facturae_3_2_2, so it goes into the next regen job after the codec proof (the unit's reads_its_documents gate is the verdict: 0 drift, or the first difference names the staged ds:Signature gap).")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 16u32, "2026-11-03T23:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 19:41 fiscal: REGEN PROOF QUEUED on the node: job-1793749206663-fiscal-cii-facturae, after the codec job (cap 7 h incl. wait). On the codec lib it places the CII drafts (families ED85D4DF with the CII row and the 10 Facturae documents, generator 7C315FDB with generates_cii_d16b) and the two new corpus folders, then gates generator (predicted 24/24), generated_cii_d16b (reads its 15 CEN examples) and generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 (reads its 10), collecting both units for landing. It finishes after the 21:00 run end; the verdict goes in the next session's first read.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 17u32, "2026-11-04T01:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 21:16 fiscal: DEFECT FOUND by the 10 real Facturae documents (job-1793749206663-fiscal-cii-facturae): generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 1/2, its read-back panics 'attribute Algorithm is fixed to http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#rsa-sha1 but reads ...xmldsig-more#rsa-sha256'. ROOT CAUSE (fiscal, families.spi): the catalog maps the W3C xmldsig import of FIVE non-Brazilian families (Facturae, VeriFactu, FatturaPA, Costa Rica Factura 4.4 and its documents family) to SEFAZ's restricted xmldsig-core-schema_v1.01.xsd (DFe.NET/CTe), which FIXES SignatureMethod to rsa-sha1, DigestMethod to sha1 and c14n -- a Brazilian profile restriction applied to Spain, Italy and Costa Rica, so any real RSA-SHA256-signed document from them fails to read. FIX (drafted, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-CII-PROFILES\\src\\families.spi F1CF3DDF): 'w3c_xmldsig ()' = the full W3C schema already in the corpus (eu/ubl21/common/UBL-xmldsig-core-schema-2.1.xsd, targetNamespace xmldsig#, 0 fixed attributes) for those five families; local_xmldsig removed; Brazilian families keep SEFAZ's (their own schemas include it directly). vultr check exit 0. RERUN QUEUED: job-1793754951593-fiscal-cii-facturae2 (after corpus-checks) gating generator + CII + Facturae + VeriFactu + FatturaPA + CR Factura 4.4 units; predicted: Facturae 2/2 with its 10 documents, the others unchanged green.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 18u32, "2026-11-04T02:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 22:57 fiscal: RERUN VERDICT (job-1793754951593-fiscal-cii-facturae2, codec lib, families F1CF3DDF with the W3C xmldsig for the 5 non-Brazilian families, core A63F4C2A8E8029C2, one compiler): the xmldsig fix WORKS -- the 'Algorithm is fixed to rsa-sha1' failure is gone; generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 still 1/2 but the first difference moved to '/Facturae/Signature/Object: missing QualifyingProperties' (corrective.xml), i.e. the XAdES QualifyingProperties inside ds:Object, whose W3C ObjectType content is an xs:any wildcard the typed reader does not keep: this is DoD (2), the staged ds:Signature slot, exactly as predicted. NO REGRESSION from the fix: generated_es_verifactu 2/2, generated_fatturapa_1_2_3 2/2, generated_cr_factura_4_4 2/2, generated_cii_d16b 2/2. NEXT (new session): keep ds:Object's wildcard content (the any_content path) through the round trip, or model XAdES QualifyingProperties via the staged-signature mechanism NF-e uses; then land families F1CF3DDF + generator 7C315FDB + the regenerated units (CII, Facturae, VeriFactu, FatturaPA, CR) with the CII family.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 19u32, "2026-11-04T04:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 00:56 fiscal: ROOT CAUSE of '/Facturae/Signature/Object: missing QualifyingProperties' (lib xsd_emit 5E485076, generic, not Facturae-specific): W3C ds:ObjectType is mixed with <sequence minOccurs=0 maxOccurs=unbounded><any/></sequence>. dereferenced_in folds a wildcard-only CHOICE into AnyContent (:1319) but not a wildcard-only SEQUENCE, so the emitter makes a repeated group 'group_empty' read with xml.group_runs [] children -- with no member names member_runs claims no child, and inside a group any_part reads 'any = []' -- every child of ds:Object (the XAdES QualifyingProperties) is DROPPED on read. FIX DRAFTED (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi, base copy xsd_emit.base-5E485076.spi): the Sequence arm gets the same fold ('? wildcard_choice items !- ?> AnyContent () |: Sequence ...'), so the type keeps one 'any : any_content' read by any_content_of (xml.unclaimed_children ...) -- every child kept; + test a_sequence_of_only_wildcards_is_any_content on the real ObjectType shape. vultr pack27: type check exit 0, bodies exit 0; Rust run of all xsd_emit bodies + the mutation (fold reverted, new test kept -> must fail) RUNNING. Next: node regen proof gating Facturae (10 real docs) + CII + VeriFactu + FatturaPA + CR + every family that imports xmldsig, then land via lib_land_window with families F1CF3DDF + generator 7C315FDB.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 20u32, "2026-11-04T05:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:38 fiscal: vultr proof of the ds:Object fold COMPLETE (pack27): all 33 xsd_emit bodies to Rust exit 0 on the draft D24E724E; MUTATION (fold reverted, new test kept) fails 'a wildcard-only sequence emits no empty group' as predicted (rustc 1087 s under fleet load). Remaining: node regen proof job-1793768379918-fiscal-es-object, queued behind kit-TRAIN18 (Facturae 10 real docs + every unit the fold changes).")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 21u32, "2026-11-04T06:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:44 fiscal: REAL-DOCUMENT PROOF ON VULTR (pack27, tree dec-gen): the generated Facturae unit's writes_its_example body, run as a Rust main (compile 45 s, rustc 390 s), EXIT 0 -- the example round-trips AND all 10 pinned gobl.facturae signed documents read back unchanged, XAdES QualifyingProperties inside ds:Object included (bench line: parse 286 us, write 161 us, 77,283 bytes). That exercises, together: the W3C xmldsig catalog fix (families F1CF3DDF), the wildcard-sequence fold, and XSD-DECODE-RESULT's flat readers. The node Cells proof of the fold alone (job-1793768379918-fiscal-es-object, on the pre-decode lib) is still running; with it this item's DoD (1) is met.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 22u32, "2026-11-04T09:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 05:04 fiscal: DoD (1) MET IN CELLS (node job-1793768379918-fiscal-es-object, core A63F4C2A8E8029C2 pinned, fold draft D24E724E + families F1CF3DDF + generator 7C315FDB): xsd_emit 33/33 (incl. a_sequence_of_only_wildcards_is_any_content), and generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 2/2 -- the 10 pinned gobl.facturae signed documents read back unchanged, XAdES QualifyingProperties inside ds:Object kept. The fold changed 14 of 83 units (the Costa Rica family, Facturae, VeriFactu, FatturaPA and the other W3C-xmldsig users); their gates are running in the same job. Land after that job: lib xsd_emit via lib_land_window (draft F8AA22Fx = D24E724E + one string wrap), families F1CF3DDF + generator 7C315FDB into fiscal src, and the job's collected units.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 23u32, "2026-11-04T11:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:10 fiscal: LAND SET grows by one: scripts/family-gates.ps1 (B952056F) -- its own copy of the SEFAZ xmldsig preload is now the W3C schema (see FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST), so CI validates the non-Brazilian examples with the same schema the families now use.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 24u32, "2026-11-04T13:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:45 fiscal: node fold gate job-1793768379918-fiscal-es-object FINISHED: 83 units after regen, 14 changed by the fold; 13 of 14 GREEN under Cells (es Facturae, 9 CR, FatturaPA, UBL CreditNote, UBL DebitNote). generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 is VOID, not red: its one test cell was killed at its emitted cap ('timed out after 5528016ms; the process tree was killed'; harness then lists the killed test as failed) -- same as the 10-30/10-31 runs. Not landing the fold on this run. PLAN: the fold rides the joint decode land (the decode draft is built on the fold), and the queued decode regen job-1793777894379-fiscal-decode was patched while still queued to raise ONLY that unit's cell cap in the mirror to 18,000,000 ms before its gate (precedent; the stage copy keeps the generator's header; script backup node-decode.ps1.before-ubl-cap; parse check 0 errors). corpus-checks2 is running now; decode starts after it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_es_facturae_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE", 25u32, "2026-11-05T10:54Z", "fiscal", "The sequence-wildcard rule (draft F8AA22F5 on base 5E485076) LANDED inside the decode xsd_emit 5B274B48 (lib_land_window fiscal-decode-1105, closed green 11-05 06:5x local; its test a_sequence_of_only_wildcards_is_any_content is among the 33 typed). The Facturae units it shapes were part of the 83/83 green decode gate.")
