inl fiscal_my_myinvois () = Task ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", "Malaysia LHDN MyInvois 1.0/1.1: stock UBL 2.1 in XML and OASIS UBL-2.1-JSON", Story, P2, D4, 96u32, Active, "XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", "team:fiscal,fiscal,generic,country,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_my_myinvois () = Planning ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified samples): https://sdk.myinvois.hasil.gov.my/files/sdksamples/1.1-Invoice-Sample.xml and .json (Credit/Debit/Refund/Self-Billed same pattern). No custom XSD: XML is stock UBL 2.1; the JSON uses OASIS UBL-2.1-JSON v1.0 _D/_A/_B keys, schemas https://docs.oasis-open.org/ubl/UBL-2.1-JSON/v1.0/cnd02/json-schema/maindoc/ (that LHDN uses exactly these is an inference). A double test of the two front ends on one model.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T13:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:50 fiscal: corpus IN THE TREE (fetch block in scripts/init.ps1, unstaged): deps/corpus/my/myinvois: 1.1-Invoice-Sample.xml (CA703B48) and .json (60CC77C5); the XML is stock UBL 2.1. init.ps1 fetches it through Save-Pinned (sha256-pinned, refuses changed content, 3 in-memory attempts for flaky hosts) and Expand-Pinned. Its Invoice documents join generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's real documents through the new manifest deps/corpus/ubl-invoice-documents.txt, which init rewrites every run from every corpus .xml whose PARSED root is Invoice in urn:oasis:...:Invoice-2 (87 today: DIAN 33, UBL-TR 35, CEN 10, Peppol 7, ANAF 1, LHDN 1; Turkish StandardBusinessDocument envelopes are excluded by the root check); the generator reads the manifest (manifest_documents) and UBL's example cell round-trips each through the typed reader/writer with xml.first_difference.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T18:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 14:31 fiscal: all 42 other official LHDN SDK samples IN THE TREE (init: corpus/my/samples, pinned per file; list read from sdk.myinvois.hasil.gov.my/sample/). 22 XML, all stock UBL Invoice roots (types 01-04, 11-14): Invoice manifest 87 -> 108. 12/22 .NET-valid; 9 'fail' only on a 39-digit xmldsig X509SerialNumber (xs:integer is unbounded, .NET caps at decimal: referee limit), 1 is truly invalid upstream (PayableAmount 'abc'). 22 UBL-JSON kept for the JSON reader.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 4u32, "2026-10-27T23:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:41 fiscal: VERIFIED (was an inference): the 21 LHDN JSON samples follow OASIS UBL-2.1-JSON exactly. Pairwise structure check vs the XML twin: prefixes _D/_A/_B, every element an array of objects (0 scalar entries), text in '_', attributes as sibling keys, local names unchanged. 124 path differences: 110 in the signature block (each form signed separately), 14 optional elements present in one twin only; 0 rule violations. So the JSON front end is a mechanical codec over the same XSD model; no JSON Schema needed.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 5u32, "2026-10-28T08:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 04:16 fiscal: RUNTIME: its real UBL documents are among the 155 invoices that read back unchanged through the generated UBL Invoice reader/writer on the node (set-proof setc, job-1793162726520, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357, generator with the count-type fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 6u32, "2026-10-28T11:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 07:17 fiscal: DESIGN (no code), UBL-JSON front end: generated readers match children by LOCAL name (xml.children_named compares local_name), so ONE lib transcoder ubl_json_to_xml (root key = element; arrays = repeated elements; '_' = text; sibling keys = attributes; _D/_A/_B = xmlns) feeds every existing UBL reader unchanged: no per-type code. Lossless: json_schema's json_value keeps JsonNumber as its lexeme (98 sample numbers carry trailing zeros like 436.50; 697 of 2553 '_' values are numbers/booleans). Check = JSON -> xml -> T -> xml, first_difference against the transcoded input. Writer back to UBL-JSON needs the XSD type per element (number/bool/string): a second, generated step.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 7u32, "2026-10-28T12:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 08:50 fiscal: TRANSCODER DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/ubl-json-transcoder.kit (lib json_schema.spi; draft %TEMP%\\tc-uj-draft): ubl_json_document text -> list xml_node beside json_document. Array = repeated elements; object = one element ('_' scalar = text, scalar keys = attributes, arrays/objects = children); root '_D' -> xmlns, '_X' -> xmlns:X (bijective, no backend-partial helper); JsonNumber lexeme kept. Test ubl_json_becomes_the_xml_its_readers_take. Node --check hit the 30 s attestation cap on live AND draft: inconclusive, rerun via --backend.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 8u32, "2026-10-28T13:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:06 fiscal: transcoder TYPE-CHECKS: fsharp on a node copy of the live-synced cx lib (json_schema 7B51A3E9, xsd 1D437DBF = box live), A4E48020: live 0 errors (control), draft 0 errors. (A first try on the integ mirror's lib gave a false error at the xsd_schema literal: integ's lib is stale, json_schema 9AAFF1C4.) Next: run its test cell on the node, then the 21 LHDN JSON samples through the UBL Invoice reader (JSON -> xml -> T -> xml, first_difference).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 9u32, "2026-10-28T13:23Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:23 fiscal: FISCAL SIDE. In the tree (unstaged, inert): init.ps1 writes ubl-<kind>-json-documents.txt by matching {_D}rootKey to the XML manifests' qualified root: invoice 22 (all LHDN JSON, credit/debit/refund/self-billed are Invoice roots), other kinds 0. HELD until the transcoder lands (scratchpad ubljson/src/generator.spi): family_root.ubl_json_documents on all 17 literals; document_checks takes the reader (xml.read_xml | json_schema.ubl_json_document), same first_difference round trip. Proof after fix-uj: set-proof on UBL Invoice, 155 XML + 22 JSON.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 10u32, "2026-10-28T13:52Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 09:52 fiscal: cell proof job-1793193481614 BROKEN in the TEST only: '| node :: [], wanted :: [] =>' parses as node :: (([], wanted) :: []) since ',' binds tighter than '::' (3 unification errors in spiral_cells_test; the module itself type-checks). Fixed to '| (node :: []), (wanted :: []) =>'; program rebuilt (+84); rerun job-1793195601588 fiscal-fix-uj2 on mirror uj (draft 306976C3).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 11u32, "2026-10-28T14:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 10:08 fiscal: transcoder HOLDS on the node (job-1793195601588 fiscal-fix-uj2, A4E48020, live-synced lib + draft json_schema 306976C3): ubl_json_becomes_the_xml_its_readers_take passed on rust in 280 s, 0 type errors. lib-programs/ubl-json-transcoder.kit is land-ready for the 20:00 window (after list sugar + complements writer, per main). Then: apply the held generator draft (ubl_json_documents) and run the UBL Invoice unit on 155 XML + 22 JSON.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 12u32, "2026-10-29T11:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 07:47 fiscal: transcoder HOLDS 7/7 incl ubl_json_keeps_every_top_level_member (uj3, job-1793199492259, json_schema 54CFD0B2 = with the silent-drop fix, A4E48020, headroom 0.93) and is LANDED 07:28:51 (ubl-json-transcoder.kit, json_schema 7B51A3E9 -> 54CFD0B2, equal to the proven copy). Lib gate queued: job-1793273720127-fiscal-land-gate-json2. Next: rebuild the lost ubl_json_documents generator draft (n9), run the UBL Invoice unit on 155 XML + 22 JSON.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 13u32, "2026-10-29T12:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 08:06 fiscal: ubl_json_documents generator draft REBUILT in the fiscal tree (unstaged): family_root.ubl_json_documents on all 17 literals (UBL Invoice/CreditNote/business kinds read ubl-<kind>-json-documents.txt, others []), document_round_trip shared by check (xml.read_xml) and check_json (json_schema.ubl_json_document); a family with no JSON documents emits exactly the old text. New test ubl_json_documents_read_through_the_transcoder. PROOF RUNNING: fiscal-set-ublj job-1793275326126 (land1029 mirror = live lib incl. transcoder + this generator 3AF581CC, init re-ran OK, generator budget raised in the mirror only): generator tests + unit generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 on 155 XML + 22 JSON.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 14u32, "2026-10-29T14:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 10:41 fiscal: set-ublj (job-1793275326126, mirror land1029 = live lib incl. the landed transcoder + fiscal tree with the ubl_json_documents draft, A4E48020): init HOLDS; the generator HOLDS 22/22 tests, 0 failed, 0 memo hits (incl. the new ubl_json_documents_read_through_the_transcoder); all business-document units are generated. Now running the unit generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 over 155 XML + 22 JSON documents.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 15u32, "2026-10-29T20:20Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 16:20 fiscal: fiscal-6b-set-ublj (pack 6b, core 31CC96520D6B7269, mirror ublj6b) RED with a syntax bug in the new JSON check: json_round_trip emitted '    and xml_sizes', but Spiral's recursive groups need 'and let' (generated unit line 56235: 'Expected one of: inl, let'; the block was left out, so generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 failed). Generator 22/22 and every business-document unit HOLD. Fixed in the tree (generator 84A609E1 -> A5BA4532, one line: '    and let xml_sizes'); rerun fiscal-6b-set-ublj2 (job-1793305287354). The 'private nominals (0 files)' claim is the set-proof script's artifact for a one-unit group without constrained strings.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 16u32, "2026-10-30T00:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 20:32 fiscal: UBL-JSON SET-PROOF VERDICT (fiscal-6b-set-ublj2, mirror ublj6b, pre-window-4 lib, 16:21-20:26): generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 BROKEN: '22 real documents do not read back unchanged; first: deps/corpus/my/myinvois/1.1-Invoice-Sample.json: the typed reader does not keep every element, text and attribute' (json_round_trip's element/text/attribute count check). The UBL Invoice example holds (687 bytes, 0 validation messages, no child element in the wrong namespace); 'validated nominals private' reports 0 files. Next: diff the element/text/attribute counts of 1.1-Invoice-Sample.json before and after the typed round trip to name the dropped part (likely the UBL-JSON array-of-objects wrapping for repeated scalars or attributes).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 17u32, "2026-10-30T00:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 20:43 fiscal: NARROWING the UBL-JSON size mismatch (note 16): json_round_trip passes stability (first_difference None) and fails only on xml_size (elements + text nodes + data attributes), node vs once. Empty-string values are NOT the common cause: 13 of the 22 UBL-JSON documents contain one ('_':'' x4-x8, Type, URI), but the 9 without (1.0-Credit-Note, 1.0-Debit-Note, 1.0-Invoice-ForeignCurrency, 1.0-Invoice, 1.0-Refund-Note, 1.0-Self-Billed-{Credit,Debit,Invoice,Refund}) fail too. Something all 22 share drops or adds nodes: candidates are the UBLExtensions/ExtensionContent xs:any slot and the _A/_B/_D namespace keys on the root. Next (generator.spi, CPU-light): make the failure print both sizes plus the first child whose subtree size differs (a size-diff walk over node/once), then rerun set-ublj on a post-land mirror.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 18u32, "2026-10-30T00:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 20:47 fiscal: DIAGNOSTIC DRAFTED in the tree (src/generator.spi -> 414BE185, uncommitted, NOT yet compiled): json_round_trip's emitted check now reports 'N -> M at <path>'. A generated size_drift walks node and once pairwise and names the first child whose xml_size differs, recursing to the leaf, or reports '<name> dropped' / '<name> added'. Only the failure text changes; the pass/fail condition is the same. Next: set-proof generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 on a post-land mirror to read the path for 1.1-Invoice-Sample.json and the 9 documents without empty strings.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 19u32, "2026-10-30T02:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:51 fiscal: DIAGNOSTIC RUN QUEUED: fiscal-p7-set-ublj (job-1793328748327), mirror p7ublj (post-window-4 lib: file_system 81140E3E), pack 7 pinned (staged copy, core 9C899B30495F7DC5, dll F2F6F4CB5A18), tree generator 414BE185 with the size-drift message, and the format-step dotnet fix (FISCAL-GENERATOR-FORMATS n27), so the generator claim can hold this time. It prints 'N -> M at <path>' for the 22 UBL-JSON documents. (--heavy refused on the node: 'needs spiral's scripts/heavy.ps1: set EOIE_HEAVY_GATE', so it was queued without it.)")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 20u32, "2026-10-30T10:27Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 06:27 fiscal: GROOM: fiscal-p7-set-ublj (pack 7, post-land p7ublj, generator 414BE185 with the size-drift message) finished: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 still BROKEN (1 failed of 1), and the format step now passes (its generator claim held). The 'N -> M at <path>' detail is not in the set-proof summary log (set-proof-c doesn't forward unit output); next: read it from the unit's raw notebook output on the node (p7ublj/fiscal/generated/generated_ubl_invoice_2_1) to name the drifting element.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 21u32, "2026-10-30T10:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 06:31 fiscal: CORRECTION: my 10-29 diagnostic broke the unit. fiscal-p7-set-ublj's real failure is a TYPE ERROR in the emitted size_drift helper: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1.spi:66762: 'Got: list xml_node * list xml_node / Expected: list (list xml_node * xml_node)'. The emitted pattern '| x :: xs, y :: ys =>' parses as x :: (xs, y) :: ys, because in this syntax the tuple comma binds tighter than '::' in patterns, so the run never reached the round trip and no drift path was printed. Fixed in the tree: generator.spi 414BE185 -> CB7E07C7 (patterns '(x :: xs), (y :: ys)', '(x :: _), []', '[], (y :: _)'). Re-run queued: fiscal-p7-set-ublj2 (job-1793356268570, pack 7, post-land mirror p7ublj2). Lesson: emitted code is only proven by compiling a generated unit, not by the generator's own tests.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 22u32, "2026-10-30T15:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:25 fiscal: fiscal-p7-set-ublj2 (job-1793356268570, mirror p7ublj2, generator CB7E07C7 with the size_drift diagnostic, pack 7) is VOID, not red. generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's cell was killed at its own budget, 5108672 ms. That budget is the generator's cell_budget_ms = max(2400000, bytes/10*16), i.e. ~85 min for the 3.2 MB unit, which only fits a quiet node (rustc ~47 min quiet). The 3 broken claims after it (private nominals 0 files, no sample written, 0 namespace messages) all depend on that unit, and the generator step's 3 failures are the same per-test cap under load. Still no size-drift verdict. Rerun: fiscal-p7-set-ublj3 (job-1793373950641-fiscal-p7-set-ublj3), same mirror, units ^generated_ubl_invoice_2_1$, after the e3lv chain so it runs uncontended by fiscal, cap 18 h incl. wait. MIRROR-ONLY change, stated so it isn't mistaken for the tree: p7ublj2/fiscal/src/generator.spi has cell_budget_ms factor 16 -> 48 (CB7E07C7 -> DDCE9521, original kept as generator.spi.budget16), ~4.25 h for this unit. This changes only the emitted --timeout header, not the code under test. Tree follow-up (after FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, because it rewrites every generated header): make the budget hold under a shared node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 23u32, "2026-10-30T22:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:52 fiscal: DRIFT DIAGNOSED (the size_drift diagnostic finally ran: fiscal-p7-set-ublj3, generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 compiled and executed with the x3 budget; generator 22/22): 22 real UBL-JSON documents do not read back unchanged; first deps/corpus/my/myinvois/1.1-Invoice-Sample.json: 408 -> 430 at ID//ExtensionURI added. So the JSON reader -> writer path ADDS ExtensionURI elements (22 extra nodes: the UBLExtensions/UBLExtension/ExtensionURI shape), likely the transcoder or writer emitting an element the JSON did not carry (a required-in-XSD field filled on write, or an extension wrapper mapped twice). Next: read the 1.1-Invoice-Sample.json UBLExtensions block against the generated ExtensionURI writer, then fix in the generator's JSON transcode. The private-nominals claim's 0 files on this one-unit run (vs 2 for CL+MDF-e) looks like a claim scoped to units with validated nominals, which the UBL Invoice unit may not have; check before treating it as a regression.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 24u32, "2026-10-30T22:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:54 fiscal: FIRST LEAD on the drift (reading only). 1.1-Invoice-Sample.json has ONE ExtensionURI (UBLExtensions[0].UBLExtension[0].ExtensionURI = urn:oasis:names:specification:ubl:dsig:enveloped:xades, then ExtensionContent/UBLDocumentSignatures/...); 1.1-Invoice-Sample.xml has two. The read-back has 22 more nodes, with the first difference reported after ID (ID//ExtensionURI added), so the extension subtree is likely emitted a second time, around ID, on the way back. Hypothesis to test first: the JSON -> XML transcoder follows JSON key order while the typed reader/writer follows xs:sequence order (UBLExtensions first), so the subtree appears at both positions. Check by transcoding this one sample and diffing child order under Invoice. The fix is in the generator's JSON transcode (src/generator.spi), ordered after FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (anchors).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 25u32, "2026-10-31T09:18Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 05:18 fiscal: DRIFT LEAD TESTED BY READING (no runs). (1) The reported LOCATION is an artifact: the emitted size_drift paired children by POSITION, and 1.1-Invoice-Sample.json orders Invoice's keys ID, IssueDate, ... InvoiceLine, UBLExtensions, Signature (UBLExtensions second to last) while the typed writer follows xs:sequence (UBLExtensions first). So pair 1 was (ID, UBLExtensions), and 'ID//ExtensionURI added' is ID's text child vs UBLExtension's children, not an added element. (2) The COUNT is real and still unexplained: my count of the JSON tree with the size convention (elements + non-empty text + non-xmlns attributes, empty '_':'' = no text node) reproduces 408 exactly, so the transcoded side is understood and the typed re-emission adds 22. Not empty text (the sample has only 4 '_':'' elements, all inside UBLExtensions). The XML twin 1.1-Invoice-Sample.xml is NOT the same document (414 nodes; 4 AdditionalDocumentReference vs fewer in JSON; UBLExtensions 69 vs 63; ONE ExtensionURI, correcting n: 'the XML has two'), so it cannot serve as the expected output. (3) FIX TO THE DIAGNOSTIC in the tree (src/generator.spi json_round_trip, unstaged): size_drift now pairs each child with the first unconsumed sibling of the SAME NAME (take_named), so key order can no longer hide where nodes are added; 'X dropped' / 'Y added' now mean a name present on one side only. Next proof: regenerate generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 and run its reads_its_documents cell (3.2 MB unit, ~4 h at factor 48; node or a quiet box slot); the new path names the element that gains the 22 nodes, and the fix goes into the transcoder or writer that path names.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 26u32, "2026-10-31T10:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 06:06 fiscal: the name-aligned size_drift (n25) PROVEN as emitted text: fiscal-box12-size-drift-probe (job-1793440130616, box, compiler EEBCBFF8, Cells rust) compiles the exact lines json_round_trip now emits (xml_size/xml_sizes, take_named, size_drift; edition 2 like the generated units) and passes size_drift_pairs_children_by_name: <r><a/><b/></r> vs <r><b/><a/><c/></r> reports 'r/c added' (the positional version blamed a), and a missing sibling reports 'r/a dropped'; 0 type errors. So regenerating generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 with the new generator cannot break the unit's compile on this code. Still open: that regeneration plus the 4 h reads_its_documents cell that names the element gaining the 22 nodes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 27u32, "2026-10-31T12:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 08:09 fiscal: drift run queued on the node (box heavy-build held): node job-1793448496635-fiscal-p8-t1031-set-events-cfdi-ubl (set-proof-c on NEW mirror t1031 = the box spiral tree fd70dccf + the fiscal tree with today's unstaged src, digest 862A2909; deps/corpus seeded from the box by tar, 1156 files, never from an older mirror; pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A), unit generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 regenerated with the name-aligned size_drift; its reads_its_documents line names the element that gains the 22 nodes.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 28u32, "2026-10-31T13:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 09:30 fiscal: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 regenerated with the name-aligned size_drift (fiscal-stages3-example-cr-ubl's last step: generates_ubl_invoice_2_1 passes; raw 3,193,482 B) and brought into the tree FORMATTED (format-generated.ps1, pack 8): diff vs HEAD +23/-10 = the take_named/size_drift lines plus the emitted --timeout header (5108672 -> 5109504, from cell_budget_ms of the slightly longer text). Its compile and the 22-node verdict come from the node set-proof on t1031, which regenerates and builds this same unit.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 29u32, "2026-10-31T16:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 12:50 fiscal: t1031 run VOID for the drift verdict: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's one cell was killed at its OWN emitted cap (5,109,504 ms = cell_budget_ms factor 16) under node load, like 10-30's ublj2; the dependent 'no sample' claim is VOID too. Rerun with a mirror-only header raise (as ublj3 did) queued next.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 30u32, "2026-10-31T19:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 15:49 fiscal: DRIFT LOCALIZED by the name-aligned size_drift (node job-1793465646409-fiscal-p8-t1031-ubl-drift, mirror t1031, pack 8, the unit's cell cap raised mirror-only to 18,000,000 ms; compiled and ran in ~2.8 h; the XSD sample is now written): '22 real documents do not read back unchanged; first: 1.1-Invoice-Sample.json: 408 -> 430 at Delivery/Shipment/FreightAllowanceCharge/Amount/here'. 'here' = same name, same children, different size, so the difference is in Amount's own ATTRIBUTES. The JSON has exactly 22 Amount-type members, each with '_' a number and currencyID MYR, so +22 = one extra attribute per currency amount on the typed side. Ruled out by reading lib json_schema.spi:341-346: the transcoder keeps currencyID (every non-underscore scalar becomes an attribute; '_' becomes text for numbers too), so the transcoded Amount carries currencyID. So the TYPED writer adds an attribute to every AmountType value: candidates (a) an optional AmountType attribute (e.g. currencyCodeListVersionID) emitted although absent, (b) currencyID written under a second (prefixed) name. Next probe: a cell that reads one cbc:Amount with currencyID MYR through x_amount_type_of_xml / _to_xml from generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 and prints both attribute lists (needs the 3.2 MB unit compiled once, so a node job).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 31u32, "2026-10-31T19:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 15:54 fiscal: ROOT CAUSE found by reading the generated writer + the schemas: UDT AmountType restricts CCT AmountType re-declaring currencyID, and xsd_emit keeps the base's currencyID AND adds the re-declared one, so every currency amount writes currencyID twice (22/22). Filed as XSD-RESTRICTION-ATTRIBUTE-OVERRIDE (P1, xsd_emit fix + regression test, then UBL regen); this item's drift closes when that lands and reads_its_documents shows 0 drift.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 32u32, "2026-11-01T07:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 03:11 fiscal: the UBL-JSON round trip HOLDS on the live lib: node job-1793505518611 ran generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 over 155 XML + 22 JSON documents with 0 drift (XSD-RESTRICTION-ATTRIBUTE-OVERRIDE and FISCAL-TYPEFEATURE-DRIFT closed on it). Re-check this item's remaining done criteria against that verdict at the next groom.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 33u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:49 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (round 5). DONE (part 1, 11-01 03:10): the UBL-JSON round trip holds: generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 reads 155 XML + 22 JSON real documents with 0 drift (job-1793505518611). DONE WHEN (rest): the official LHDN MyInvois 1.1 sample set (sdk.myinvois.hasil.gov.my, pinned by sha256 in init.ps1 under deps/corpus/my) reads back through the generated UBL Invoice/CreditNote/DebitNote units in both XML and JSON with 0 drift, as one corpus_checks test pinning the count. NEXT STEP: fetch the SDK samples (downloads standing-OK), count them, add the test. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the two syntaxes are a union \":| ubl_syntax = | UblXml | UblJson\" with one reader per syntax as a prototype instance over the codec, so no \"json\"/\"xml\" string switch appears; MyInvois-specific constraints become a ubl_profile case (MyInvois) beside Bis3/Pint, never a branch on a country string.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 34u32, "2026-11-03T07:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 03:28 fiscal: GROOM: Active -> Planned (untouched 41 h; part 1 done 11-01). NEXT STEP: pin the official LHDN MyInvois 1.1 sample set (sdk.myinvois.hasil.gov.my) by sha256 in init.ps1 under deps/corpus/my and add them to the UBL family documents; owner fiscal.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 35u32, "2026-11-03T17:59Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:59 fiscal: DoD 'one corpus_checks test pinning the count' WRITTEN (fiscal src/corpus_checks.spi, unstaged, +18 lines, 862 lines total): ':| ubl_syntax = UblXml | UblJson' (the plan's union, so no 'json'/'xml' string switch), invoice_manifest syntax (the init-written ubl-invoice-documents.txt / ubl-invoice-json-documents.txt), myinvois_entries syntax (manifest lines under my/), and test every_myinvois_sample_reaches_the_ubl_invoice_unit_in_both_syntaxes pinning (22, 22). Measured on the box tree: corpus/my holds 1+21 XML and 1+21 JSON; both invoice manifests carry exactly 22 my/ entries (every LHDN sample is an Invoice root; the creditnote/debitnote manifests carry 0). Those manifests ARE the documents generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 reads (families manifest_documents), and that unit read 155 XML + 22 JSON with 0 drift on 11-01 (job-1793505518611), so the count pins the read-back set. PROOF so far: vultr --check of corpus_checks with the test (module and bodies) exit 0; the runtime cell needs the corpus, so it runs with the next corpus_checks gate on the node or in CI. LEFT for the plan: the syntax-indexed reader as a prototype instance over the codec (after XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES) and a MyInvois ubl_profile case.")
