inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 37u32, "2026-11-04T01:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 21:37 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793754211554-fiscal-corpus-checks, core A63F4C2A8E8029C2, one compiler): with scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write run first (src/corpus.txt 580 lines) and the box manifests, the live corpus_checks.spi is 28/28 -- incl. every_myinvois_sample_reaches_the_ubl_invoice_unit_in_both_syntaxes, every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit, and models_the_corpus_census / resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet (the 2 rows VOID this afternoon; the NotFound root cause is confirmed).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 38u32, "2026-11-04T06:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:53 fiscal: MyInvois ubl_profile case DONE (fiscal src/profiles.spi in place, 461F4F9B -> 4A09BE84; backup profiles.before-ubl.spi in the session scratchpad). Grounded in the corpus: the 22 LHDN XML samples carry NO CustomizationID/ProfileID and split 11 x InvoiceTypeCode listVersionID='1.0' / 11 x '1.1'; SUNAT carries CustomizationID '2.0' (58), PEPPOL BIS 3 its billing URN (8), the CEN EN16931 examples 'urn:cen.eu:en16931:2017' (11). So ':| ubl_profile = UblEn16931 | PeppolBis3 | SunatUbl20 | MyInvois : myinvois_version' with ':| myinvois_version = MyInvoisV10 | MyInvoisV11' (the version is a type, not a string), and ubl_profile_of customization list_version (customization decides when present; MyInvois is the no-customization + list-version case; unknown marks -> None). Test ubl_documents_are_classified_by_their_customization_or_list_version. PROOF vultr pack27: format clean, --check module + bodies exit 0, both profiles bodies to Rust exit 0. LEFT: the syntax-indexed reader as a prototype instance over the codec (unblocked now that the codec landed; it will read the profile marks from the typed UBL root instead of strings).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 39u32, "2026-11-04T11:27Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:27 fiscal: DESIGN for the last piece (syntax-indexed reader), grounded in how the generated units already read JSON: json_document_checks converts a UBL-JSON text with lib json_schema.json_document <root> text into an xml_node and then runs the SAME typed reader (<t>_of_xml), so the syntax is only the entry point. Plan (lib, after XSD-DECODE-RESULT lands, since it returns that item's result type): phantom ':! xml_syntax = ()', ':! json_syntax = ()'; ':| document_text s = | XmlText :: string -> document_text xml_syntax | JsonText :: string -> document_text json_syntax'; 'document_of \\* s t. (root : string) (read : xml_node -> result t (list decode_error)) (text : document_text s) : result t (list decode_error)' -- XmlText reads one root via read_xml, JsonText via json_schema.json_document root, both then 'read'; a non-single root is Unexpected, not a raise. Generic over every UBL family (the reader is passed in), so MyInvois 1.0/1.1 in both syntaxes reads through one call, and with profiles.spi's ubl_profile_of the version marks become types at read time. Test: the 22 MyInvois samples, XML and JSON, give equal typed documents pairwise (same invoice in both syntaxes).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 40u32, "2026-11-04T11:31Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:31 fiscal: SYNTAX-INDEXED READER DRAFTED + PROVEN (the design of n39), new lib module %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\\lib\\spiral\\document_syntax.spi (6B55B078): phantom xml_syntax/json_syntax, ':| document_text s = XmlText :: string -> document_text xml_syntax | JsonText :: string -> document_text json_syntax', single_root (exactly one root, else Unexpected), and document_of root read text -- XML via read_xml, JSON via json_schema::json_document root, then the same typed reader. Test one_reader_serves_both_syntaxes: the same invoice decodes to Ok 'A1' from XML and from JSON; a JSON document without ID reports 'missing ID'; no root is reported, not raised. vultr pack27 (on the XSD-DECODE-RESULT xml_codec draft, registered after json_schema): --check module + bodies exit 0, format clean, test to Rust exit 0. LANDS AFTER XSD-DECODE-RESULT (it uses that item's decode types); with lib's derived modules, landing is just the new file. Next after the land: the 22 MyInvois samples pairwise XML vs JSON through generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's reader.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 41u32, "2026-11-05T05:48Z", "fiscal", "DESIGN FACT for the post-land pairwise test (11-05 01:5x local, corpus my/samples): 21 XML/JSON pairs, all UBL <Invoice> roots (credit/debit/refund/self-billed differ only by InvoiceTypeCode). The two syntaxes carry DIFFERENT lexical forms of the same values: 1.0-Invoice-ForeignCurrency has XML PayableAmount 1436.50 and JSON \"_\": 1436.5 (a JSON number); 1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency has XML abc and JSON 1436.5. With XSD-FACET-TYPES' lexical carriers (value + raw text, so each syntax round-trips byte-exactly), structural equality of the two typed documents would differ on every trailing-zero amount. So the test must compare VALUES (decimal.compare on the carriers' .value, or a value projection of the document), never = on documents: byte identity is the per-syntax read-back, cross-syntax identity is value identity. Expected result: 20 pairs value-equal, and 1.1 ForeignCurrency a recorded LHDN sample defect (the XML does not decode, Invalid PayableAmount abc, while its JSON twin decodes to 1436.5).")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 42u32, "2026-11-05T11:08Z", "fiscal", "document_syntax LANDED, 11-05 07:0x local: new lib file document_syntax.spi 6B55B078 (base new) through lib_land_window fiscal-document-syntax-1105, CLOSED GREEN on top of the decode land (it uses xml_codec's result / decode_error): 0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (1 test typed), respell_drift 0, lib digest C37FAC0CF9C87E23, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-065925. Unstaged in spiral. LEFT for 100%: the 21-pair XML vs JSON test through generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's reader, comparing VALUES (n41), plus the LHDN 1.1 ForeignCurrency pair as a recorded defect once the facet types land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 43u32, "2026-11-05T16:06Z", "fiscal", "11-05 12:0x local fiscal: LIB HALF OF THE PAIRWISE TEST DRAFTED + PROVEN (for n41: the 22 MyInvois XML/JSON twins, paired by file stem, compare by VALUE). Drafts in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\\lib\\spiral (bases recorded beside them): (1) xml.spi 3D9AC927 -> 765A371D: first_difference_at / first_child_difference take the text equality, new public first_difference_by (same) (expected) (actual); first_difference = first_difference_by (=), signature and behaviour unchanged; lib test first_difference_by_lets_the_caller_decide_text_equality. (2) xml_codec.spi 5694B36A -> EFAE1583: same_value (equal as strings or as decimal::parse values, so 1436.50 = 1436.5 = and 1.0 = 1), value_difference = first_difference_by same_value, and twin_difference read write first second (both documents through ONE typed reader, then value_difference of what it writes back; an undecodable side is reported by name); lib test twins_in_two_syntaxes_compare_by_value. Formatter round trip: my lines are stable (xml.spi's 2 formatter diffs are pre-existing lines 146 / 692). VULTR (box core + box lib with both drafts; pinned core dc49ffdc170199df): xml 16 :# bodies and xml_codec 8 bodies (incl. both new tests) compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors; MUTANT (same_value = plain string equality) run exit 1 with exactly 'texts are equal as strings or as decimals'. lib_land_window DRY RUN running on the box (label fiscal-value-twins-1105, bases 3D9AC927 / 5694B36A), log land-value-twins-dry.log in the session scratchpad. NEXT (generator half, after the facet window lands): document_checks emits, for each XML document whose stem has a JSON twin in ubl_json_documents (22 MyInvois pairs; the recorded LHDN defect 1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency is left out like its read-back), a twin check calling xml_codec.twin_difference with the unit's reader/writer; generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 regenerates and gates on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_my_myinvois_44 () = Note ("FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS", 44u32, "2026-11-05T16:12Z", "fiscal", "11-05 12:1x local fiscal: GENERATOR HALF DRAFTED + text-proven. %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\\fiscal\\src3\\generator.spi CD099775 (= the facet companion src2 6ADC38CB + twins; base copy beside it): path_stem, twin_of / twin_pairs (each KEPT XML document, i.e. without the recorded defects, paired with the JSON documents of the same stem), twin_check_text emits 'inl twin (xml_path) (json_path)' that reads both through xml.read_xml / json_schema.ubl_json_document and calls xml_codec.twin_difference (<t>_of_xml<witness>) (<t>_to_xml root) x j, twin_lines appends one twin call per pair to the unit's failures; document_checks = read_back_list ++ document_reads ++ defect_lines ++ twin_lines ++ failures_raise. Test xml_and_json_twins_compare_by_value: 21 MyInvois pairs for ubl_invoice_2_1 (the 22 stems minus the LHDN 1.1-Invoice-ForeignCurrency defect), every pair shares its stem, the invoice unit calls xml_codec.twin_difference, the credit note (no JSON twins) emits no twin. VULTR eff-tw1793895104 (facet stage + the xml / xml_codec drafts): that test + a_recorded_document_defect_is_asserted_not_read_back compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors; formatted. LEFT: the emitted twin code itself runs only in generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's reads_its_documents test, i.e. a regen of that unit with src3 + its gate on the node, after the facet window lands src2 (src3 is a layer on top of it).")
