inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source: cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts; mirror thegreenter/ubl-validator@980bad9412eab51516e4879b06d8d2e723c62f0d src/xsd/2.1/ (header says UBL 2.1 CS1: diff against fiscal's OASIS os copy first). Rules are XSL; official XSL UNVERIFIED.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 2u32, "2026-10-27T19:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:01 fiscal: sourcing: UBL 2.1 mandatory since 2019-03-01 (RS 164-2018). Official per-document XML guides are PDFs under cpe.sunat.gob.pe/sites/default/files/inline-files/ (factura, boleta, nota de debito). The portal pages answer scripted requests with 403 (bot protection), so the XSD set, the samples and the SFS validation XSLT (SUNAT's rules) are not reachable from init. NEEDS: a browser download of SUNAT's XSD + SFS package once, then init pins it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 3u32, "2026-10-27T23:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:36 fiscal: sourcing: cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts. greenter's parser fixtures are UBL 2.0 / customization 1.0 (pre-2018 format; one looks like a real retail receipt): rejected. Most code-search hits carry real RUCs: skipped. Chosen: project-openubl/xhandler-java (Apache-2.0) @9b0af749 xbuilder e2e/homologacion: 58 SUNAT homologation cases (28 Invoice, 15 CreditNote, 15 DebitNote; UBL 2.1, customization 2.0; test RUC 12345678912), unsigned. Their ONLY schema fault is the empty signing slot (ExtensionContent): 58/58 valid without it. init drops that slot (throws if any ExtensionContent has content), like GST's nulls; no signature is faked.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 4u32, "2026-10-27T23:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 19:37 fiscal: IN THE TREE: init block deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion (58 pinned files). Manifests: invoice 127 -> 155, creditnote 6 -> 21, debitnote 3 -> 18; all 58 schema-valid (validate-manifests); no BOM; set-proof stage includes them. Open: SUNAT's own rule XSLs (official site 403s scripts).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 5u32, "2026-10-28T08:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 04:16 fiscal: RUNTIME: its real UBL documents are among the 155 invoices that read back unchanged through the generated UBL Invoice reader/writer on the node (set-proof setc, job-1793162726520, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357, generator with the count-type fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 6u32, "2026-10-28T10:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:31 fiscal: BLOCKED on user download: SUNAT's current validation XSL package (ValidaExprReg*.xsl etc. from cpe.sunat.gob.pe, which answers 403 to scripts). Documents are done: 58 homologation cases round-trip on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 7u32, "2026-10-30T14:18Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:18 fiscal: GROOM: stays agent (mixed blockers, so not R1). (a) Your download of SUNAT's validation XSL package (cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts; Chrome extension not connected 10-30), and (b) XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS, whose end-to-end evidence is fiscal-p7-set-ublj2 (running 10-30, on generated_ubl_invoice_2_1).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 8u32, "2026-10-31T13:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 09:36 fiscal: GROOM R1 -> user-batch. Blocker (b) is gone: XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS closed 10-30 (namespace claim re-proven on the live lib; see FISCAL-SA-ZATCA's groom note). The only open step is (a), yours: download SUNAT's current validation XSL package (ValidaExprReg*.xsl etc.) from cpe.sunat.gob.pe, which answers 403 to scripts, into fiscal/deps/corpus/pe/sunat/ (the 58 homologation documents already round-trip). Then the agent wires it like the other rule-set profiles (DIAN/ZATCA/RO pattern, CPU-light + one box gate). Assignee agent -> user, tag user-batch added.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 9u32, "2026-10-31T22:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 18:10 fiscal: the download gate is lifted (user 10-31 ~18:00), so this is agent work again, but cpe.sunat.gob.pe still answers 403 to scripts. Leads: SUNAT publishes its validation rules as XSLT inside the SFS (Sistema de Facturacion Electronica, the free Facturador SUNAT) package; esolutions/xml (packagist) says its rules are extracted from those XSLTs; greenter/validator and Kembec/facturacion-electronica-sunat-sdk are related tools. Next: fetch the official SFS distribution (or an archive.org snapshot of it) and take the ValidaExprReg*.xsl files from it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 10u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:49 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (round 5). TODAY: cpe.sunat.gob.pe answers 403 to scripts, but the project-openubl xbuilder homologation cases are already in deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion (init.ps1). DONE WHEN: the SUNAT UBL 2.1 customization reads through the EXISTING generated UBL units (no new family code): every homologation case reads back with 0 drift as one corpus_checks test pinning the count, and the SUNAT customization rules (from the openubl rule set, pinned) run as a profile with pinned findings. NEXT STEP: count the cases in deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion, add the read-back test beside ubl_tr_samples_keep_their_main_schematron_findings. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: Peru is a ubl_profile case (PeSunat) with its rules as typed schematron patterns; catalog codes (SUNAT catalogs 01-59) become validated nominals from their published lists, never raw strings.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 11u32, "2026-11-03T20:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:34 fiscal: DoD part 1 (the count test) WRITTEN, unstaged in fiscal src/corpus_checks.spi: test every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit pins the 58 project-openubl homologation cases (deps/corpus/pe/sunat-homologacion, all XML) as 28 Invoice, 15 CreditNote and 15 DebitNote entries of the init-written UBL manifests, which ARE the documents the existing generated UBL units read back (no new family code, as the DoD asks). Typed: ':| ubl_kind = InvoiceKind | CreditNoteKind | DebitNoteKind' with ':| ubl_syntax = UblXml | UblJson' select the manifest (ubl_manifest), and entries_under prefix kind syntax counts a country's entries; the MyInvois test (FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS) now uses the same reader, so one function serves every country. PROVEN on vultr (pack27): corpus_checks --check with bodies exit 0; both tests compiled --backend Rust against the box's 4 real manifests run exit 0; MUTATION (one SUNAT debit note removed from its manifest) exits 1. LEFT for the DoD: the read-back verdict per case comes from the UBL units' own reads_its_documents tests (the next full regen gate); the SUNAT customization rules as a pinned profile (openubl rule set) and the catalog nominals.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 12u32, "2026-11-04T01:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 21:37 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793754211554-fiscal-corpus-checks, core A63F4C2A8E8029C2, one compiler): with scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write run first (src/corpus.txt 580 lines) and the box manifests, the live corpus_checks.spi is 28/28 -- incl. every_myinvois_sample_reaches_the_ubl_invoice_unit_in_both_syntaxes, every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit, and models_the_corpus_census / resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet (the 2 rows VOID this afternoon; the NotFound root cause is confirmed).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 13u32, "2026-11-04T07:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:13 fiscal: CATALOG 07 AS A TYPED GADT (new fiscal src/sunat.spi 06BA8C08, registered in package.spiproj + spiral.toml after profiles; unstaged). SOURCE PINNED, not memory: project-openubl/xbuilder main xbuilder/src/catalogs.rs (blob 6f73783d32b75e16001fb2bcd398a06a4458d8d3, 23,678 bytes, fetched as data): Catalog7 codes 10-17 Gravado, 20-21 Exonerado, 30-36 Inafecto, 40 Exportacion -- and Catalog7::group maps 40 to EXONERADO (not its own group), which the model follows. Model: phantom groups gravado/exonerado/inafecto, ':| igv_affectation g' (18 cases each indexed by its group), ':| affectation = Taxed | Exempt | Unaffected' for parsing (one typed case per group), affectation_code / affectation_of / code_of / is_onerosa, and igv_line rate (line : igv_affectation gravado) base: charging IGV on a non-taxed line is a COMPILE error. Grounded in the corpus: the 58 homologation cases use TaxExemptionReasonCode 10, 11, 12, 13, 20, 21, 30, 31 (all parse); InvoiceTypeCode is catalogo01 '01' on the 28 invoices. Tests: every_catalog_07_code_round_trips_through_its_group, the_homologation_cases_use_known_codes, only_taxed_lines_charge_igv, an_exempt_line_cannot_charge_igv fails 'Unification failure' (vultr: fails with 'Got igv_affectation gravado, Expected igv_affectation exonerado'). PROOF vultr pack27: format clean, --check module + bodies exit 0, the 3 bodies to Rust exit 0. LEFT: other catalogs the corpus uses (01 document type, 05 tax scheme, 09/10 note reasons, 16 price type) the same way, then the openubl rule set as a profile.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 14u32, "2026-11-04T07:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:19 fiscal: CATALOGS 01, 09, 10 added to sunat.spi (36BDD4C5), same pinned source (openubl catalogs.rs blob 6f73783d): document_type (01 Factura, 03 Boleta, 07 NotaCredito, 08 NotaDebito, 09 GuiaRemisionRemitente), credit_note_reason (catalog 09, 10 cases), debit_note_reason (catalog 10: 01 InteresPorMora, 02 AumentoEnElValor, 03 PenalidadOtrosConceptos); each with an exhaustive code match and a parser from one all_* list via the generic coded lookup. UPSTREAM DEFECT FOUND: openubl maps DevolucionPorItem to '06' (same as DevolucionTotal) and never emits '07', in a list otherwise contiguous 01-10; a code table must be injective, so fiscal uses 07 and the test pins unique codes 01..10 (worth an upstream issue, but no public-project interaction from here). Corpus: the 30 note ResponseCode values are all '01'. Test catalogs_01_09_10_have_unique_codes_that_round_trip. PROOF vultr pack27: format clean, module + bodies exit 0, the negative still fails 'Got igv_affectation gravado', all 4 bodies to Rust exit 0. LEFT: catalogs 05/16 as needed, the openubl rule set as a profile.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 15u32, "2026-11-04T07:22Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:22 fiscal: CATALOG 05 + the 07->05 mapping added (sunat.spi 8A0EBE17), ported from the pinned source's Catalog7::tax_category, not inferred: tax_scheme (1000 IGV, 1016 IVAP, 2000 ISC, 9995 EXP, 9996 GRA, 9997 EXO, 9998 INA, 7152 ICBPER, 9999 OTROS), tax_category over the group-indexed igv_affectation (onerosa lines get their own scheme; every free transfer, retiro or gratuita, gets 9996 GRA; IVAP 17 -> 1016), scheme_code_of for a parsed affectation. FIX found by the same read: is_onerosa had missed GravadoIvap (17), which openubl's onerosa marks true. Grounded: the corpus's TaxScheme IDs (multi-line XML) are 1000 x142, 2000 x36, 9996 x122, 9997 x22, 9998 x22, all parse. Test every_affectation_has_the_tax_scheme_openubl_assigns. PROOF vultr pack27: format clean, module + bodies exit 0, negative still 'Got igv_affectation gravado', all 5 bodies to Rust exit 0.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 16u32, "2026-11-04T07:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:25 fiscal: RULE-SET SOURCE CHECKED (DoD part 3): project-openubl ships NO pinnable SUNAT rule set. Its active repos (xhandler-rust, xhandler-java, ublhub, xbuilder catalogs) contain no .xsl/.xslt/.sch files: openubl encodes SUNAT knowledge as code (catalogs.rs, enrich rules), which fiscal has now ported as typed catalogs (01, 05, 07, 09, 10 in sunat.spi). SUNAT's own rules are its published validation XSLs (the 'validaciones' packages on cpe.sunat.gob.pe), and that host answers 403 to scripts (n?). OPTIONS for the profile: (a) fetch the SUNAT validation package once through the user's browser (Chrome tooling) and pin it by sha256 in init.ps1 under deps/corpus/pe/sunat-validaciones; (b) derive a typed rule subset from the ported catalogs (e.g. every line's TaxScheme = tax_category of its TaxExemptionReasonCode; a credit note's ResponseCode parses as catalog 09) and check it over the 58 homologation cases -- runnable now, no download. Next: (b), as a corpus_checks test pinning 0 findings over the homologation cases.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 17u32, "2026-11-04T07:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:32 fiscal: RULE (b) DONE AND HELD BY THE CORPUS (sunat.spi B3AC871C): every TaxCategory that carries a TaxExemptionReasonCode must carry the TaxScheme ID that openubl's Catalog7::tax_category assigns (category_findings/findings_within walk any UBL document; scheme_finding names the line). Tests: a_tax_category_carries_the_scheme_of_its_affectation (synthetic: a retiro under 9996 passes, code 10 under 9996 and an unknown 99 are findings) and the_homologation_cases_carry_the_scheme_of_each_affectation: over the 58 SUNAT homologation cases (pe/ lines of the 3 UBL manifests) 233 TaxCategory elements are checked and 0 findings -- 233 also matches an independent grep of the lines carrying TaxExemptionReasonCode, so the walk misses none. PROOF vultr pack27 (with the pe corpus + manifests staged): module + bodies exit 0, negative still fails as typed, all 7 bodies to Rust exit 0; MUTATION (code 11 retiro -> IGV) fails the suite (caught first by the mapping test). DoD part 3 is met in the typed form (option b); the SUNAT XSL package (option a) stays optional. LEFT: the read-back verdict per case at the next full regen gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 18u32, "2026-11-04T07:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:46 fiscal: catalog 16 (price type: 01 PrecioUnitarioIncluyeIgv, 02 ValorReferencialUnitarioEnOperacionesNoOnerosas; same pinned source) added to sunat.spi (DF106C6C) with price_type_of; corpus PriceTypeCode values are 01 x133, 02 x100. A per-line '02 iff non-onerosa' rule was NOT asserted: the counts show lines carry both prices, so it needs a per-line study first. PROOF vultr pack27: format clean, --check exit 0, all 7 bodies to Rust exit 0 (corpus rule still 233 checked, 0 findings).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pe_sunat_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-PE-SUNAT", 19u32, "2026-11-04T07:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:51 fiscal: SECOND CORPUS RULE (sunat.spi E76F8F3C): a line's PriceTypeCode follows its affectation's onerosa flag (01 PrecioUnitarioIncluyeIgv for onerosa, 02 ValorReferencial for free transfers). Studied before asserting (the aggregate counts had looked inconsistent): per line, the 58 cases give exactly 133 lines 'prices=[01] onerosa' and 100 lines 'prices=[02] non-onerosa', nothing else. Test every_homologation_line_prices_by_its_onerosa_flag: synthetic (a 21 line priced 01 is the only finding) + corpus 233 lines checked, 0 findings. PROOF vultr pack27: format clean, --check exit 0, all 8 bodies to Rust exit 0; MUTATION (code 11 marked onerosa) fails the suite (first at the onerosa-flags assertion; the corpus test would also fail on the code-11 lines). Six SUNAT catalogs typed (01, 05, 07, 09, 10, 16) and two rules held over the full homologation set.")
inl fiscal_co_dian () = Task ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", "Colombia DIAN UBL 2.1 Anexo tecnico v1.9 (Caja de herramientas FE V19, files 2026-07-31)", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", "fiscal,generic,country,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_co_dian () = Planning ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified, 26 MB): https://www.dian.gov.co/impuestos/factura-electronica/Documents/Caja-de-herramientas-FE_V19_v2026.zip: XSD/maindoc/DIAN_UBL_Structures.xsd + UBL maindocs, XSL/DIAN-UBL21-model-compiled.xsl, Ejemplificaciones/XMLs de ejemplo/*.xml. v1.9 effective date UNVERIFIED. A copy sits in the session scratchpad dl/co.zip.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 2u32, "2026-10-27T13:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:50 fiscal: corpus IN THE TREE (fetch block in scripts/init.ps1, unstaged): deps/corpus/co/dian: Caja-de-herramientas-FE_V19_v2026.zip (036EAC8C, 26 MB; 33 Invoice, 3 CreditNote, 3 DebitNote, 5 ApplicationResponse examples, DIAN_UBL_Structures.xsd, XSL rules). init.ps1 fetches it through Save-Pinned (sha256-pinned, refuses changed content, 3 in-memory attempts for flaky hosts) and Expand-Pinned. Its Invoice documents join generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's real documents through the new manifest deps/corpus/ubl-invoice-documents.txt, which init rewrites every run from every corpus .xml whose PARSED root is Invoice in urn:oasis:...:Invoice-2 (87 today: DIAN 33, UBL-TR 35, CEN 10, Peppol 7, ANAF 1, LHDN 1; Turkish StandardBusinessDocument envelopes are excluded by the root check); the generator reads the manifest (manifest_documents) and UBL's example cell round-trips each through the typed reader/writer with xml.first_difference.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 3u32, "2026-10-27T20:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 16:41 fiscal: census IN THE TREE: regional_rules_census also pins DIAN-UBL21-model.sch (36 rules, 192 assertions, 169 fatal). It is a <pattern>-rooted fragment the parent schema pulls in by <include>, which the lib reader does not resolve (it reads 0 rules); the test wraps it as the include would. Lib gap: schematron <include> resolution. Missing functions for DIAN: format-number, current-dateTime, xs:dateTime, xs:dayTimeDuration.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 4u32, "2026-10-27T20:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 16:54 fiscal: schematron <include> DRAFTED, held for TRAIN: C:\\home\\git\\fiscal\\lib-programs\\schematron-include.kit (unstaged). read_schematron_resolved (load : string -> option string) path keeps schematron pure: a pattern-rooted fragment is spliced as its pattern, a schema-rooted file contributes its children, paths resolve relative to the including file, depth capped at 16; read_schematron shares patterns_of_children. Test folded into lets_and_includes_assemble_the_schema (non-vacuous: 1 pattern, 1 failure on a bare line). Type-checked; equals the draft on a fresh copy.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 5u32, "2026-10-27T21:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 17:55 fiscal: format-number DRAFTED, held: fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-format-number.kit (6th). Picture '#0.00' only (DIAN's 3 PayableAmount lets); rounds HALF-TO-EVEN to cents as XPath requires (lib decimal.round_to is half-up: 10.005 would give 10.01); other pictures refused; non-numbers give 'NaN'. Tests: 10.005->10.00, 10.015->10.02, 7->7.00, -0.5->-0.50. 6-program chain applies to the live lib. Deferred: AA12b/AA12c need dateTime parse + dayTimeDuration arithmetic + an injected now.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 6u32, "2026-10-27T22:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 18:08 fiscal: DIAN date window DRAFTED, held: fiscal/lib-programs/xpath-datetime.kit (7th, last). xs:dateTime and xs:dayTimeDuration evaluate to seconds (epoch UTC, offsets normalized; days via lib date_time.days_from_civil), so AA12b/AA12c's now +10d / -5d windows use the existing numeric + - < >. current-dateTime reads the caller's today (date-only = midnight UTC); none = VError. Tests: offset equality, 2024 leap day, both window edges, refusal. 7-program chain applies to live; fiscal type-checks. DIAN now has no missing functions.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 7u32, "2026-10-28T00:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 20:33 fiscal: the one DIAN document that fails stock UBL 2.1 (Ejemplificaciones/XMLs de ejemplo/'Ejemplicacion Impuestos Saludables.xml', 20 messages) is an ANNOTATED ILLUSTRATION: Spanish explanations sit as text inside cac:TaxSubtotal after each element (10 text nodes, e.g. 'Resultado de la operacion (PerUnitAmount * BaseUnitMeasure / 100)'); all 20 messages are 'TaxSubtotal cannot contain text'. Not a malformed invoice; its round trip is expected to differ by exactly that text. Option: exclude Ejemplificaciones from manifests.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 8u32, "2026-10-28T00:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 20:33 fiscal: CORRECTION to the previous note: drop 'its round trip is expected to differ'. The DIAN examples were in the invoice manifest from 09:50, and today's all-proof failed only VeriFactu and GST, so the UBL invoice unit already passed with this document; no exclusion needed.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 9u32, "2026-10-28T08:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 04:16 fiscal: RUNTIME: its real UBL documents are among the 155 invoices that read back unchanged through the generated UBL Invoice reader/writer on the node (set-proof setc, job-1793162726520, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357, generator with the count-type fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 10u32, "2026-10-30T02:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:00 fiscal: GROOM, next step defined: documents round-trip (10-28), but DIAN's validation rules are not yet evaluated. The xpath/schematron fixes live since window 4 (10-29 19:49) are the prerequisite. Next: find whether Caja de herramientas FE V19 ships a schematron (or only the Anexo tecnico rule table); if schematron, add co_dian_samples_pass_the_dian_rules modeled on the ZATCA test; if not, record that DIAN validation is a rule table and size an encoder.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 11u32, "2026-10-30T14:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:43 fiscal: ANSWERED, does Caja de herramientas FE V19 ship a schematron? Yes, but the readable one is STALE, and the current rules ship only compiled. Evidence, all in deps/corpus/co/dian (v2026). (1) Schemes/DIAN-UBL21-model.sch (2019-02-20, 36 rules, 192 asserts, 116 lets; the one corpus_checks' census reads) uses rule ids AA02/DA17/DC01a and unprefixed root tests boolean(/Invoice), which under XPath never match a namespaced UBL root, so those branches are dead. The assembly Schemes/DIAN-UBL21-model.sch (queryBinding xslt3) also includes listacodigos/DIAN_UBL21-listacodigos_v2.0.sch, which is NOT shipped (only v1.5/v1.6). (2) XSL/DIAN-UBL21-model-compiled.xsl (554 KB, XSLT 3.0 from Oxygen's skeleton; output is Fatal: text, not SVRL) carries the CURRENT scheme: prefixed roots (/ubl:Invoice, /cn:CreditNote, /dn:DebitNote, /app:ApplicationResponse), ids FAA02/CAA02/DAA02/AAA02, FAB19a, FAD06...: 42 rule templates, 251 when-tests, 207 variables, 88 distinct invoice ids. (3) The Anexo Tecnico v1.9 PDF (pdftotext) uses the XSL scheme: FAA02/CAA02/DAA02/AAA02 present, 471 distinct FA ids, and DA17/DC01a/AA02 appear 0 times. So the XSL is authoritative and covers 88 of the Anexo's 471 invoice rules; the rest are presumably server-side. Evaluator coverage: every function in the model or the XSL is in xpath.spi (sum, round, format-number, tokenize, translate, normalize-space, xs:dateTime, distinct-values, matches, if-then-else XIf), EXCEPT current() (11 uses in the XSL, 5 in UBL21-Structure3.sch). Samples: Ejemplificaciones/XMLs de ejemplo has 33 Invoice + 3 CreditNote + 3 DebitNote, and Eventos RADIAN has 5 ApplicationResponse. Decision (rule: validate against what the authority runs, gate met is not goal met): no co_dian test against the stale .sch. Plan, sized by milestones: (a) XSL-to-schematron extractor in Spiral over the xml lib (template match + mode M* -> rule context; xsl:choose when/otherwise -> assert test + message id; xsl:variable -> let), checked by count (42 rules, 251 tests, 88 ids) 180m; (b) current() in xpath_eval as the rule-context node (lib, via a window) 60m; (c) co_dian_samples_pass_the_dian_rules as a measurement first (per-sample counts printed, pins after hand-verifying each finding kind, like UBL-TR) on the edition-3 corpus_checks once FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND lands 120m. The census test pinning 36/192/169 stays as a parser regression check of the stale file.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 12u32, "2026-10-30T14:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:54 fiscal: MILESTONE (a) DRAFTED, the extractor in the lib, not fiscal (generic: any Oxygen/ISO skeleton output). Draft C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-xslt\\schematron.spi (59A7D2CA, base = live C36C6296, base copy schematron.base.spi): read_compiled_schematron(_with) turns each xsl:template whose mode is M<n> and whose priority is >= 0 into a rule, in file order (the skeleton's priorities already descend per mode: checked on DIAN M18-M22). Each xsl:choose of when + otherwise/xsl:message becomes an assert: the when test, a Fatal:/Warning: label as severity, and xsl:text plus {value-of select} as the message and id, as SVRL names an unnamed assert. Each xsl:variable with a select becomes a let. Left out: the generate-id modes, text() fallbacks (priority -1), the skeleton's xsl:if path machinery and the top-level document-uri. New lib test a_compiled_schematron_reads_back_into_its_rules covers mode grouping, exclusions, order, lets, both labels, value-of ids, and census. Formatter: my lines are clean (pack 7 re-lays only 3 pre-existing >120 lines of the live file, L114/L149/L387, identically on base and draft). Proof queued: fiscal-p7-dxsl-schematron (job-1793371933905, mirror dxsl = spiral cec8840c + draft, hash-checked; pass = 4/4 schematron tests). Pins fixed BEFORE running, derived independently with .NET XmlDocument over the XSL (M modes only): patterns 5, rules 84, assertions 249 (fatal 228, warning 21), lets 201, 109 distinct FA ids. Correction to n11: 42/251/207 came from a regex that assumed attribute order; the real numbers are these. Fiscal-side test drafted in edition-3 spelling on the e3live draft: C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live-dian\\src\\corpus_checks.spi (4646DDDB, formatter-clean), dian_compiled_rules_read_fully pins that shape and prints the invalid count (expected > 0: current() x11, and XPath 2 except in the first rule context ext:*[* except ext:*]//*, which xpath.spi doesn't parse). (b) is now current() + except.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 13u32, "2026-10-30T15:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:03 fiscal: (a) EXTRACTOR HOLDS: fiscal-p7-dxsl-schematron (job-1793371933905, mirror dxsl = spiral cec8840c + draft schematron 59A7D2CA, pack 7 F2F6F4CB5A18): schematron.spi 4/4 passed, 0 type errors, 0 memo hits; a_compiled_schematron_reads_back_into_its_rules 98.8 s, the 3 existing tests still green. (b) DRAFTED as C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-xpath (bases in base\\): xpath.spi 382A551C -> F77C1BFA: OpIntersect/OpExcept nodes operators, keywords union/intersect/except, a precedence level above | (XPath 2: intersect/except bind tighter), current() as ValueFunction FnCurrent. xpath_eval.spi 34646246 -> F5A81731: scope gains current : located; current() = VNodes [s.current]; intersect/except filter the left operand by node identity (located_where over has_located, document order kept); new test except_intersect_and_current_follow_xpath_2 (precedence, parenthesized step ../( ), current() fixed inside a predicate). schematron_run.spi B9D3079F -> 1E8B9B6C: check_contexts sets current = each rule's context node; new test current_is_each_rule_context_node uses DIAN's exact shape, not(../(* except current())[...]). xsd_constraints.spi A28E8D9C -> 41714D60: its scope literal. Only these 3 files build scopes (grep over C:\\home\\git). All formatter-clean (xpath_eval's 16 formatter lines are pre-existing, identical on base). Why it matters: the 2 DIAN asserts using current() (duplicate-languageID checks) and 5 rules using except, including the first context, ext:*[* except ext:*]//*. Proof chain on dxsl (both drafts, hashes verified on the node): xpath_eval job-1793372554285 -> schematron_run job-1793372560095 -> xpath job-1793372563284 -> xsd_constraints job-1793372573390 -> schematron job-1793372583590; pass = every module's tests green, 0 type errors.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 14u32, "2026-10-30T15:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:40 fiscal: (b) PROOF 3 of 4 modules HOLD so far on dxsl (both drafts, pack 7): xpath_eval 8/8 (new except_intersect_and_current_follow_xpath_2 455 s; job-1793372554285), schematron_run 4/4 (new current_is_each_rule_context_node 396 s; job-1793372560095), xpath 4/4 (job-1793372563284), all 0 type errors; xsd_constraints is running, then schematron re-checks with the xpath change. LAND PROGRAM READY: C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-lib\\dian-xslt-xpath.kit (133819A6, 19,288 B): edit + patch for schematron, xpath, xpath_eval, schematron_run, xsd_constraints, 22 hunks. Rehearsed with kit do on fresh base copies: 5 files, 22 replacements, every result hash-equal to its proven draft (59A7D2CA, F77C1BFA, F5A81731, 1E8B9B6C, 41714D60). Bases re-checked against the live lib at 2026-10-30 11:40 (C36C6296, 382A551C, 34646246, B9D3079F, A28E8D9C, all unchanged). Next: when the last 2 modules hold, ask main for a lib window (lib-guarded-do + base pins).")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 15u32, "2026-10-30T15:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:47 fiscal: dxsl chain verdicts. HOLD: xpath_eval 8/8, schematron_run 4/4, xpath 4/4, schematron 4/4 (re-run on top of the xpath change, job-1793372583590), all 0 type errors. VOID (not red): xsd_constraints' only test, unique_items_are_checked_per_owner, killed at 301015 ms against the 300000 ms default cell cap (headroom 1.0; job-1793372573390). It compiles the same xpath_eval that schematron_run and xpath_eval itself give 900000 ms, so the draft now carries the sibling header ///- --timeout 900000 on that test (xsd_constraints 41714D60 -> E1CE6C63). Program regenerated: dian-xslt-xpath.kit F6FA4C7B, rehearsed again on fresh bases (5 files, 22 replacements, all hash-equal). Re-proof fiscal-p7-dxsl-xsd_constraints2 (job-1793375234948).")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 16u32, "2026-10-30T15:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:49 fiscal: (c) DRAFTED as a measurement, UBL-TR style. dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings in C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live-dian\\src\\corpus_checks.spi (707B53A9, edition-3 spelling, formatter-clean). It reads DIAN-UBL21-model-compiled.xsl through schematron::read_compiled_schematron and validates (on evaluated_on () = 2026-10-29) all 44 toolkit samples: 33 Invoice, 3 CreditNote, 3 DebitNote under Ejemplificaciones/XMLs de ejemplo, plus 5 RADIAN ApplicationResponse under Eventos RADIAN. Every count is pinned at 0 for the first run, so that run fails by design while printing each sample's count and first 3 findings (dian failures/dian failure lines). Next: hand-verify each finding kind against the XML, then pin the real counts, as UBL-TR n of 10-29 22:16. Per-test ///- --timeout 3600000 (44 samples; the file's 1200 s default wouldn't hold under node load, PACKAGE-COVERAGE n10). sample_failures is now region_failures with a region label, and sample_failures = region_failures ubl_tr, so UBL-TR's output is unchanged. Runs once the lib program lands (read_compiled_schematron, current, except), on the init'd e3lv mirror.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 17u32, "2026-10-30T15:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:56 fiscal: (b) COMPLETE ON THE NODE: fiscal-p7-dxsl-xsd_constraints2 (job-1793375234948) HOLDS 1/1 (292 s, 0 type errors), so all 5 lib modules of the program hold on dxsl, pack 7. LAND QUEUED by main in today's window, after compiler's -Accept and tibia's land, serially through the reader guard. Main's close then runs hashes, kit's signature check, document_test and type_probe; no overlap with tibia's 14 files. Lander: scratchpad land-1029\\lander14.ps1 (durable copy + supervisor in C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-lib). It base-pins the 5 files, STOPs with exit 5 on any drift, and checks targets after landing. I start only on main's go. Post-land gate: a fresh pack-8 node mirror (the node serves pack 8 since 11:5x: core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52, host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9). Meanwhile the fiscal tests run on dxsl (lib drafts + e3live + e3live-dian, corpus seeded from the box 1156/72,079,269 B): fiscal-p7-dxsl-init (job-1793375593553) -> dian_compiled_rules_read_fully (job-1793375596498) -> ro_cius_examples_pass_the_ro_rules (job-1793375644951) -> dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings (job-1793375648506, a measurement, expected to fail with counts).")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 18u32, "2026-10-30T16:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 12:11 fiscal: EXTRACTOR ON THE REAL XSL HOLDS: dian_compiled_rules_read_fully (job-1793375596498, dxsl = lib drafts + e3live + e3live-dian, corpus_checks 707B53A9, pack 7) passed in 74 s. read_compiled_schematron turns DIAN-UBL21-model-compiled.xsl into exactly the shape derived beforehand with .NET XmlDocument: patterns 5, rules 84, assertions 249, fatal 228, lets 201. The 44-sample measurement (job-1793375648506) is running; its raw output is saved by fiscal-p7-dxsl-keep-dian-raw (job-1793376641424) to remote-stage\\recgroups\\fix-dxsl-dian-samples.txt.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 19u32, "2026-10-30T16:22Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 12:22 fiscal: FIRST REAL-DATA MEASUREMENT (fiscal-p7-dxsl2-dian_samples..., job-1793375648506, 902 s, raw saved as remote-stage\\recgroups\\fix-dxsl-dian-samples.txt). All 44 samples report findings: 6 (Propina, 030 Acuse_ReciboFEV) up to 50 (otra Moneda UBLExtension-CustomTagGneral-InvoiceLine), most around 18-23. NOT pinnable yet: every count includes a FATAL context error from rule 1, 'context ext:*[* except ext:*]//*: trailing tokens'. Cause: xpath name_end split the prefix wildcard ext:* into ext / : / *, a gap no unit test covered (mine used * except b). Most of the rest is UBL IND5 warnings (M18, empty elements). FIX drafted: name_end keeps p:* as one name (a colon followed by * ends the name after the *; :: is untouched), and name_matches matches p:* by the WRITTEN prefix. The evaluator compares names prefix-agnostically, so a local-name rule would make * except ext:* empty. New test a_prefix_wildcard_matches_the_written_prefix includes DIAN's rule-1 context. xpath 3EAD89A2, xpath_eval 40180DBF; program dian-xslt-xpath.kit 3B1AD30F (24 hunks, rehearsed hash-exact); lander14 retargeted; main told to hold my go until the proof holds. Clean serial re-proof fiscal-p7-dx4-*: 5 lib modules -> census -> RO -> 44-sample measurement, with each raw log copied right after its job. (The RO rerun job-1793376646592 was stopped as VOID: I swapped xpath files under it mid-compile.) Note: the measurement reported timeout_ms 1200000 even though the test carries ///- --timeout 3600000; the file header seems to win. It finished in 902 s anyway; to look into after the land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 20u32, "2026-10-30T16:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 12:58 fiscal: LIB LANDED 12:55:02 in main's window (after tibia), via lander14 (lib-guarded-do, reader guard, base pins), hashes verified: schematron C36C6296 -> 59A7D2CA, xpath 382A551C -> 3EAD89A2, xpath_eval 34646246 -> 40180DBF, schematron_run B9D3079F -> 1E8B9B6C, xsd_constraints A28E8D9C -> E1CE6C63. Proven before landing on dxsl (pack 7), the fiscal-p7-dx4-* chain: 9/9, 4/4, 4/4, 4/4, 1/1, 0 type errors. Round trip right after: document_test on the live lib Result: 22 passed (once == spi_text holds). Main's close over its 21 files follows. UNDO = the pre-land bases in C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-xslt\\schematron.base.spi + dian-xpath\\base\\, NOT git HEAD: 4 of the 5 carry unstaged window-4 lands. Progress 40 -> 65 by milestone: (a) extractor + (b) current/except/prefix wildcards landed and proven = 2 of 3; left: (c) the pinned sample measurement, which waits on the dx4 rerun counts and the edition-3 land. Next: post-land gate on a fresh pack-8 node mirror.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 21u32, "2026-10-30T17:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 13:01 fiscal: POST-LAND GATE QUEUED on PACK 8: fresh mirror pl8 (spiral cec8840c + landed lib, REMOTE-SYNC-OK + MIRROR-DEPS-OK; the 5 hashes on the node match the landed ones). The compiler is pinned to a staged copy of the node's installed pack 8 (C:\\home\\remote-stage\\spiral-bin-1030-p8, DLL EEBCBFF8658A, = box install 11:46). Chain after the dx4 measurement: fiscal-p8-pl8-xpath_eval (job-1793379653294) -> xpath -> schematron_run -> schematron -> xsd_constraints (job-1793379671919). Pass = 9/4/4/4/1 with 0 type errors.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 22u32, "2026-10-30T17:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 13:03 fiscal: MAIN'S CLOSE PASSED, lib window closed 13:02: document_test 22/22 and type_probe 21/21 over the window's 21 files; my 5 are at target (59A7D2CA, 3EAD89A2, 40180DBF, 1E8B9B6C, E1CE6C63). Main recorded the undo as the fiscal-drafts bases, not git HEAD. The post-land pack-8 node gate (fiscal-p8-pl8-*) is queued.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 23u32, "2026-10-30T17:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 13:43 fiscal: MEASUREMENT RE-RUN on the landed-equivalent lib (fiscal-p7-dx4-samples, job-1793377277865, raw fix-dxsl-dx4-samples.txt): counts fell after the prefix-wildcard fix (Combustible 19 -> 8, otra Moneda UBLExtension 50 -> 29, Propina 6 -> 5...). Rule 1 now parses and claims the extension subtree first (first-match), so IND5 stops double-reporting it. HAND-VERIFICATION FOUND A FALSE POSITIVE BEFORE PINNING: IND8 (mode M20, context = 172 cbc:* text elements, test not(../(* except current())[name(.) = name(current())][not(@languageID)])) fired 3x on Combustible, where by hand it fires 0 times (22 listed elements, none with a same-name sibling). A path probe (fiscal-p7-dxsl-ind8-probe2; failure paths decoded element-only) puts all 3 on Invoice/ext:UBLExtensions/ext:UBLExtension/ext:ExtensionContent/ds:Signature/ds:SignedInfo/ds:Reference x3. CAUSE: xpath_eval.name_matches compares LOCAL names, so the rule's cbc:Reference matches ds:Reference, and the three signature references are same-name siblings without languageID. The other 5 decode to plausible nodes: FAD09c Invoice/cbc:IssueDate 2019-06-20 (time-relative, true under evaluated_on), FAJ44 the supplier PartyLegalEntity/cbc:CompanyID 800197268, FAY10 TaxSubtotal/TaxCategory/cbc:Percent 0.00, IND5 TaxRepresentativeParty//cbc:Name empty, IND5 an empty attribute. Those are verified next. FIX (lib, a second window): namespace-aware name tests WHEN a rule set supplies a prefix -> URI map. The node's URI resolves from in-scope xmlns on it and its ancestors; with no map, today's local-name behaviour is unchanged for every existing caller (Peppol/ZATCA/UBL-TR pins stay as they are). read_compiled_schematron supplies the map from the stylesheet's xmlns declarations. No pins until it lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 24u32, "2026-10-30T17:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 13:51 fiscal: NAMESPACE-AWARE NAME TESTS DRAFTED, C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-ns (bases = the live lib as landed 12:55, in base\\). xpath_eval 40180DBF -> B340FC5B: scope gains namespaces (prefix -> uri); filtered_by_test / kind_matches take the map and the located item; name_matches_in, with a prefixed element test whose prefix is in the map, compares the node's in-scope URI (xmlns:q or xmlns on the node or the nearest ancestor) and its local name (p:* by URI). Unprefixed tests, attributes, unmapped prefixes and an EMPTY map keep the old local-name rule exactly. New evaluate_in (evaluate_on = evaluate_in []). New test a_namespace_map_matches_names_by_uri covers no map = old behaviour (3), a map separating cbc:Reference (1) from ds:Reference (2 via its own prefix), the default-namespace root, and a URI wildcard. schematron 59A7D2CA -> DC131CD3: pattern gains namespaces; read_schematron sets [] (unchanged for every existing caller: Peppol/ZATCA/UBL-TR/CEN/RO); read_compiled_schematron sets the stylesheet root's xmlns:* map; its test checks the map. schematron_run 1E8B9B6C -> 2BF3348E: validate_on seeds the scope from the patterns' maps; new test compiled_rules_match_names_by_namespace (cbc:Reference vs 2 ds:Reference -> 1 finding). xsd_constraints E1CE6C63 -> 2AE15BD5 (the scope literal). All formatter-clean on my lines. Proof chain on dxsl, PACK 8 staged (EEBCBFF8658A): fiscal-p8-ns-xpath_eval (job-1793382599400) -> schematron_run -> schematron -> xsd_constraints -> census -> samples (job-1793382662798) -> keep raw as fix-dxsl-ns-samples.txt. Expect IND8 gone from Combustible (8 -> 5). Then verify the remaining kinds and pin.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 25u32, "2026-10-30T18:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:09 fiscal: COMBUSTIBLE'S 8 FINDINGS HAND-VERIFIED (paths decoded element-only): 4 TRUE, 4 FALSE. TRUE: (1) FAD09c, cbc:IssueDate 2019-06-20 is more than 5 days before current-dateTime: time-relative, so every old sample fires it under evaluated_on. (2) FAJ44, supplier PartyLegalEntity/cbc:CompanyID 800197268 has schemeID=9, while the DIAN mod-11 DV (weights 3,7,13,...,71) is 4, as the same party's PartyTaxScheme copy correctly says: an error in DIAN's own sample. (3) FAY10, TaxScheme 04 INC at Percent 0.00, which the rule's allowed list for 04 ('2.004.008.0016.00', a contains-test) lacks; IVA 19.00/16.00 pass. (4) IND5 element, TaxRepresentativeParty//cbc:Name is empty. FALSE: (5-7) IND8 x3 on ds:Reference (cbc:Reference matched by local name; fixed by the namespace-aware drafts). (8) IND5 attribute on ds:Reference/@URI='' (attribute -2): M19's context is @*[normalize-space(.) = ''] except //*[namespace-uri()='...xmldsig#' and local-name()='SignedInfo'][1]/*[namespace-uri()='...xmldsig#' and local-name()='Reference']/@URI, a deliberate exemption of the signature's empty URI. namespace-uri() was UNSUPPORTED, and kept_at treats a predicate's VError as false (effective_boolean VError = false), so the exemption silently matched nothing. FIX added to the drafts: FnNamespaceUri (xpath A22B51A7), namespace_uri_value resolving through in_scope_namespace (xpath_eval D94679EC), plus 2 regression lines (default namespace; DIAN's exemption shape). Expected Combustible after the fix: 4. Re-proof chain fiscal-p8-ns2-* (xpath_eval job-1793383646721 ... samples job-1793383717081, raw kept as fix-dxsl-ns2-samples.txt); the stale ns chain was stopped (it lacked namespace-uri). SEPARATE FINDING (not changed here, it would move every rule set): predicate errors are swallowed as false in kept_at, so an unsupported function inside a predicate hides instead of failing. Candidate: surface a predicate VError as a context error, like and/or propagation (Peppol n of 10-29).")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 26u32, "2026-10-30T18:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:12 fiscal: formatter check of the dian-ns drafts (box freed by main): xpath A22B51A7, schematron DC131CD3, schematron_run 2BF3348E and xsd_constraints 2AE15BD5 are clean on my lines. xpath_eval had one of my test lines over 120 and is re-laid (D94679EC -> CFD7A7F3, layout only). The running ns2 chain proves D94679EC. CFD7A7F3 is staged at remote-stage\\dian-ns and goes into dxsl only after the chain (fiscal-p8-ns2-put-xpath_eval, job-1793383889072), then re-proven alone (fiscal-p8-ns2-xpath_eval-final, job-1793383906056), so the file that lands is the file proven.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 27u32, "2026-10-30T18:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:16 fiscal: POST-LAND GATE ON PACK 8 HOLDS: fresh mirror pl8 (the landed lib, verified hashes), staged pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A: fiscal-p8-pl8-xpath_eval 40180DBF 9/9, xpath 3EAD89A2 4/4, schematron_run 1E8B9B6C 4/4, schematron 59A7D2CA 4/4, xsd_constraints E1CE6C63 1/1, all 0 type errors. Milestones (a) extractor and (b) current/except/prefix wildcards are landed and proven on both pack 7 (pre-land) and pack 8 (post-land). The namespace round (dian-ns) is proving on dxsl.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 28u32, "2026-10-30T18:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:19 fiscal: MORE KINDS HAND-VERIFIED from the dx4 first-3-lines catalogue (132 lines: IND8 54, IND5 attribute 41, IND5 element 29, FAC03 3, FAD03 3, FAB22b 1, FAD09c 1), all TRUE except the two already fixed: (a) No se encuentra el grupo ds:Signature on 030 Acuse_ReciboFEV, Multiples Adquirientes and Propina: none carries a ds:Signature (unsigned samples). (b) FAD03, test . = 'DIAN 2.1' (equality, though the message says 'no contiene'): those three have ProfileID 'DIAN 2.1: ...' (Combustible's plain 'DIAN 2.1' passes). (c) FAB22b, 030's sts ProviderID 900373979 has schemeID 9 while the mod-11 DV is 1. So far 2 false kinds (IND8, the IND5 attribute = ds:Reference/@URI), both fixed in dian-ns; 7 true kinds. The first-3-lines view can't show every kind, so a full probe is queued: dian_kinds_probe prints every failure (path + rule) for all 44 samples on the namespace-fixed lib. fiscal-p8-put-kinds-probe (job-1793384351837) -> fiscal-p8-dian-kinds-probe (job-1793384368094) -> raw kept as fix-dxsl-kinds.txt, after ns2-xpath_eval-final.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 29u32, "2026-10-30T18:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:56 fiscal: NAMESPACE ROUND, lib HOLDS on dxsl pack 8 (fiscal-p8-ns2-*): xpath_eval D94679EC 10/10 (a_namespace_map_matches_names_by_uri 303 s), xpath A22B51A7 4/4, schematron_run 2BF3348E 5/5 (compiled_rules_match_names_by_namespace 462 s), schematron DC131CD3 4/4, xsd_constraints 2AE15BD5 1/1, all 0 type errors. Census on the landed lib also HOLDS on pl8 (job-1793380197708). Next in the chain: census + 44-sample re-measure on the namespace lib, then xpath_eval-final (re-laid CFD7A7F3), then the kinds probe.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 30u32, "2026-10-30T18:57Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:57 fiscal: SECOND LAND PREPARED (not requested yet): C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-lib\\dian-namespaces.kit (F4EF40B1, 20 hunks) + lander15.ps1, base-pinned on the live lib as landed 12:55 (schematron 59A7D2CA -> DC131CD3, xpath 3EAD89A2 -> A22B51A7, xpath_eval 40180DBF -> CFD7A7F3, schematron_run 1E8B9B6C -> 2BF3348E, xsd_constraints E1CE6C63 -> 2AE15BD5). Rehearsed on fresh base copies: 5 files, 20 replacements, all hash-equal; every base equals the live file at 14:57. The undo is exact this time: dian-ns\\base\\ = live. Window request goes to main once fiscal-p8-ns2-xpath_eval-final (CFD7A7F3) HOLDS and the re-measure shows the IND8/IND5-attribute false positives gone.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 31u32, "2026-10-30T19:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 15:24 fiscal: RE-MEASURE ON THE NAMESPACE LIB (fiscal-p8-ns2-samples, job-1793383717081, dxsl pack 8, 1495 s; raw kept as fix-dxsl-ns2-samples.txt). The PREDICTION HOLDS: Combustible 8 -> 4 (the 4 hand-verified true kinds: FAD09c, FAJ44, FAY10, IND5 element). Every sample dropped (dx4 -> ns2): Factura otra Moneda 28 -> 13, otra Moneda UBLExtension 29 -> 11, Impuestos Saludables 32 -> 28, nota credito sin referencia 23 -> 19, Consumidor Final 16 -> 12, Multiples Adquirientes 16 -> 16, Propina 5 -> 5, the 4 RADIAN ApplicationResponse 9/8/8/8 -> 5/4/4/4, 030 Acuse 5 -> 5; the rest 3-10. The census also holds on the namespace lib (job-1793383705966). Next: the full kinds probe (every failure, path + rule) on the final lib, verify each remaining kind, then pin and request the dian-namespaces.kit window.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 32u32, "2026-10-30T19:27Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 15:27 fiscal: KINDS ON THE NAMESPACE LIB (ns2 first-3-lines catalogue, 132 lines: FAD09c 32, IND5 29, FAD03 22, FAJ44 9, IND5-attr 9, FAS16 7, FAB03 5, FAB22b 5, FAY10 5, FAC03 3, and once each FAI04, FAJ04, FAR08, FAT07, FAU02, CBF02). Newly verified TRUE: (1) IND5 attribute: the 9 left are real empty attributes, cbc:TaxLevelCode/@listName='' (Transporte de Carga 2, Compra o Venta 2, Propina 1...); Combustible's only empty attribute, the first SignedInfo's ds:Reference/@URI, is now EXEMPT as M19 intends (namespace-uri() works). (2) FAB03, count(ext:UBLExtension/ext:ExtensionContent/sts:DianExtensions) = 1, on CreditNote, DebitNote and the two impuestos salidables notes: they bind sts to the OLD v1 namespace http://www.dian.gov.co/contratos/facturaelectronica/v1/Structures, while v1.9's stylesheet binds sts to dian:gov:co:facturaelectronica:Structures-2-1. A namespace-aware validator (DIAN's Saxon) rejects them, and the OLD prefix-agnostic matcher would have passed them silently. That is the payoff of the namespace fix. Running total: 9 kinds verified TRUE, 2 FALSE (both fixed). Still to verify: FAS16 (code-list column 5.2.2 on the IBUA/ICUI/INPP samples) and the singles; the full kinds probe gives every instance.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 33u32, "2026-10-30T19:27Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 15:27 fiscal: FAS16 VERIFIED, TRUE AGAINST THE SHIPPED RULES, and a staleness finding. Context cac:TaxTotal//cac:TaxCategory/cac:TaxScheme/cbc:ID (+ WithholdingTaxTotal); test contains('010203040506070820212223242526ZyZZ', .). The IBUA/ICUI/INPP samples use TaxScheme 34 (IBUA), 35 (ICUI), 33 (INPP), the 2023 health-tax and plastics codes, which this list predates. So the toolkit's compiled XSL is OLDER in its code tables than its own Ejemplificaciones: the evaluator reproduces the shipped rules faithfully (the goal), and these findings would differ from DIAN's live service. The pinned test documents this rather than patching DIAN's rules. Running total: 10 kinds TRUE (FAD09c, FAJ44, FAY10, IND5 element, IND5 attribute, ds:Signature missing, FAD03, FAB22b, FAB03, FAS16), 2 FALSE fixed. Left: the singles FAI04, FAJ04, FAR08, FAT07, FAU02, CBF02, from the full probe.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 34u32, "2026-10-30T19:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 15:40 fiscal: ARITHMETIC KINDS VERIFIED, all TRUE (the evaluator's decimals hold). (1) Payable total, Generica: PayableAmount 15024.07, but LineExtension 12600.06 + taxes 2424.01 - withheld 0 - prepaid 1000 = 14024.07; the sample forgot to subtract the prepayment. (2) FAU02, Generica ingresos terceros: header LineExtensionAmount 12600.06 vs sum of line LineExtensionAmount 112600.06. (3) FAT07, EmisorAutoretenedor: there are TWO WithholdingTaxTotal; the document-level one is consistent (1000 x 2.50% = 25), the LINE-level one has TaxableAmount 0, Percent 2.50, TaxAmount 25, so round(0) <> round(25). A probe (fiscal-p8-pl8-fat07-probe, job-1793388579332) that evaluated each sub-expression at the document-level node gave true everywhere (2500, 25, 25, every ... true), which first looked like an evaluator bug. The firing node is the line-level total, and the rule (context cac:WithholdingTaxTotal, 3 asserts for schemes 05/06/07, no lets) is right to fire. Lesson: decode the failure's path before probing. Running total: 13 kinds TRUE, 2 FALSE (fixed). Left: FAI04, FAJ04 (ActividadEconomica-2.1.gc code list), FAR08, CBF02, from the full kinds probe.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 35u32, "2026-10-30T20:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 16:34 fiscal: FAJ27 VERIFIED TRUE (32 hits in 17 samples, the largest unverified kind). Its code list is delimited: contains('&#x7f;04&#x7f;05&#x7f;', concat('&#x7f;', ., '&#x7f;')), the U+007F delimiters written as character references (the .NET view decoded them invisibly, which made it look like contains('0405', '') = true). With the delimiters, an empty listName is '\\x7f\\x7f', not in the list, so FAJ27 correctly rejects every TaxLevelCode/@listName='' (the same attributes IND5 flags). A probe of the extracted assertion (job-1793391930658) confirmed the engine evaluates the real source. Side findings filed as XML-XPATH-FIDELITY: read_xml leaves numeric character references undecoded (consistent here, so the result is right by accident), and name(@attr) returns '@listName'. FAV05 (unitCode, 19) and FAD02 (CustomizationID, 10) use the same delimited contains form; their values (CC/GRM/MLT, CustomizationID 10/15) are checked next against the decoded lists.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 36u32, "2026-10-30T20:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 16:39 fiscal: INDEPENDENT ORACLE + LAST KINDS. A .NET XPath-1.0 oracle (scratchpad dian\\oracle.ps1; the node console had double-encoded the raw log, UTF-8 read as CP850, repaired first) decodes every finding path to its node, finds the assertion by its message and evaluates DIAN's own test there with the stylesheet's namespace map. 210 of 327 findings CONFIRMED (test false at that node): FAS16 51, IND5 52, FAJ27 32, FAY10 22, FAV05 19, FAD02 10, FAC03 6, FAB03 5, FAJ73 4, FAQ04 2, FAR03 2, FAR02 1, FAN03 1, FBD03 1, FAI04 1, AAH03 1. ZERO oracle-true: no false positive left among them. The rest are XPath-2-only tests (n/a for the oracle) or curly-quote messages, verified by hand: FAD09c 44, FAD03 31, FAJ44 10, FAB22b 5, FAT07 1, FAU02 1, plus today: FAJ21 (issuer NIT 860003456 schemeID 2, DV 9), FAR08 x3 (payable totals off by the prepaid 1000, and 2023060 vs 2003060), FAU04 (TaxInclusive 2062060 vs 2062000), CBF02 x2 (the notes 'sin referencia' have no reference, by construction), FAK21/FAK44 x3 (the XSL's own DV formula covers NIT lengths 5-15 only,  = '' for the 3/4-digit dummies 610/1832, so DIAN's rules reject them; faithful). Unverified, 9 of 327: FAJ04 x5 (ActividadEconomica list), DC54-56 (xades signed properties), FAU03, FAU05, FAI06. 318/327 (97%) verified; all false kinds (IND8 and the IND5 attribute) were evaluator bugs, now fixed. Pinning next with these 44 counts.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 37u32, "2026-10-30T20:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 16:45 fiscal: PINNED. dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings now carries the 44 counts measured on the namespace lib (fiscal-p8-ns2-samples; total 327 = the kinds probe's 327 lines), e.g. Combustible 4, Propina 5, Impuestos Saludables 28, nota credito sin referencia 19, Multiples Adquirientes 16, Factura otra Moneda 13, the RADIAN ApplicationResponses 5/4/4/4/5. Layer corpus_checks C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live-dian\\src\\corpus_checks.spi 1F0376FB (formatter-clean). Basis: 318/327 findings verified true (oracle + hand); the 9 unverified (FAJ04 x5, DC54-56, FAU03, FAU05, FAI06) are pinned as observed and named here. Proof on the box gate (lib = namespace + predicate drafts): fiscal-box-dian-dian_compiled_rules_read (job-1793393084600) -> fiscal-box-dian-dian_samples_keep_their_ (job-1793393084765). If the pins hold there, the predicate-error change also leaves DIAN's results unmoved. Window for dian-namespaces.kit (F4EF40B1, lander15) requested from main.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 38u32, "2026-10-30T20:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 16:49 fiscal: ROUND TRIP CHECKED PRE-LAND (main's request; main-drafts\\roundtrip-one.exs, parse_spi -> to_livemd -> parse_livemd -> to_spi_tested, the document_test.exs:493 assertion): all 5 dian-namespaces drafts print 'round-trips true fixpoint true' (xpath A22B51A7, xpath_eval CFD7A7F3, schematron DC131CD3, schematron_run 2BF3348E, xsd_constraints 2AE15BD5). The land is canonical as is. Canonical outputs in C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-lib\\canon\\.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 39u32, "2026-10-30T21:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 17:26 fiscal: SECOND LIB LAND DONE 17:24:36 (main's dian2 slot after compiler's e3 matrix; lander15, base-pinned, reader guard with -ExemptAncestry for my own scratch box-gate jobs, which never read lib/spiral; it waited for tibia's idle Cells daemon to retire): schematron 59A7D2CA -> DC131CD3, xpath 3EAD89A2 -> A22B51A7, xpath_eval 40180DBF -> CFD7A7F3, schematron_run 1E8B9B6C -> 2BF3348E, xsd_constraints E1CE6C63 -> 2AE15BD5. Pre-land round trip 'round-trips true fixpoint true' for all 5; post-land document_test 22 passed. Undo = dian-ns\\base\\ (exact). The live lib now evaluates DIAN's compiled v1.9 rules namespace-aware, with namespace-uri(). Progress 65 -> 85 by milestone: (a)+(b) landed, the measurement pinned (318/327 verified); left: the pinned test enters the tree with the edition-3 layer, and the post-land gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 40u32, "2026-10-30T21:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 17:55 fiscal: BOX RESULTS. PASS: dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings with the 44 pins (job-1793395514146) and dian_compiled_rules_read_fully, on the namespace + predicate lib (the predicate change leaves DIAN's counts unmoved). POST-LAND GATE ON THE BOX IS VOID, not red: 9 of my BelowNormal gates ran in parallel beside compiler's e3 matrix, and every failing row was killed at its cell cap (xpath 324959 ms vs 300000; schematron 284415 ms, headroom 0.95; schematron_run 893392 vs 900000; 'Spiral cell timed out ... process tree was killed'). xsd_constraints passed 1/1. Re-run after main's box-open (~18:25), at most 2 gates at a time. The landed hashes already hold on the node: the identical files passed there pre-land (dxsl, fiscal-p8-ns2-*), and main's close passed type_probe 5/5.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 41u32, "2026-10-30T21:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 17:56 fiscal: post-land xpath_eval (the landed CFD7A7F3, exact copy of the live lib in boxgate3, pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A) PASSES 10/10, 0 type errors, headroom 0.83 (job-1793395640158). With xsd_constraints 1/1 that makes 2 of 5 post-land modules proven on the box; xpath, schematron and schematron_run re-run after main's box-open (their first box runs voided on cell caps).")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 42u32, "2026-10-30T22:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:35 fiscal: POST-LAND GATE COMPLETE on the box (exact copy of the live lib after the 17:24 land, pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A, 2 at a time): xpath_eval CFD7A7F3 10/10, xpath A22B51A7 4/4, schematron DC131CD3 4/4, schematron_run 2BF3348E 5/5, xsd_constraints 2AE15BD5 1/1, all 0 type errors (r3 jobs + the earlier xpath_eval/xsd_constraints). The second DIAN land is fully gated.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 43u32, "2026-11-01T03:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 23:40 fiscal: MOVED (groom 10-31 night). The DIAN corpus_checks tests (dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings, 44 pins; dian_compiled_rules_read_fully) are NOT in the committed src/corpus_checks.spi: they lived in the e3live-dian layer, archived today as stale. NEXT (CPU-light, no box): restore that layer's src/corpus_checks.spi from kit archive 20261031-085551 into a scratch dir, port the two tests into the tree's corpus_checks.spi (current syntax), then queue one box gate on the two tests.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_44 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 44u32, "2026-11-01T04:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 00:25 fiscal: PORTED into the tree (unstaged): src/corpus_checks.spi 78DD9F9C -> 6C7AA32C. Source: the archived e3live-dian layer (kit archive 20261031-085551, blob 1F0376FB). Only the layer was taken, diffed against e3live 5220335B, and path :: was turned back to . (cons :: untouched). Adds dian_compiled_rules_read_fully, dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings (44 pins), ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings, and region_failures (sample_failures now delegates to it). Header timeout 3600000. Installed formatter: only adds the final newline. GATE: node job-1793505898845-fiscal-p8-t1031u-dian-ro-tests (whole corpus_checks file, t1031u mirror). Done on green.")
inl note_of_fiscal_co_dian_45 () = Note ("FISCAL-CO-DIAN", 45u32, "2026-11-01T04:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:40 fiscal: GREEN on the node (job-1793505898845, t1031u, whole src/corpus_checks.spi 6C7AA32C): dian_compiled_rules_read_fully, dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings (44 pins, 1,185 s) and ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings all PASS; 19/25 overall. The 6 failures are unrelated to the port: 5 pattern/DFA tests need build.ps1's gitignored pattern-oracle outputs (src/patterns.txt, probes), which the mirror sync skips; en16931_rules_parse_completely pinned 979 assertions while the 1.3.17 pin has 981 (fixed in the tree; see FISCAL-EN16931-1-3-17). The port is in the tree, unstaged, for the user's next commit. CLOSED.")
inl fiscal_ro_cius () = Task ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", "Romania ANAF RO_CIUS 1.0.9 (EN16931 CIUS) schematron over UBL", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "XSD-IMPORTED-NAMESPACE-ELEMENTS", "fiscal,generic,country,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_ro_cius () = Planning ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 1u32, "2026-10-27T11:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 07:32 fiscal (user 10-27 06:3x: add most suggested countries, as generic as possible): Source (verified): https://mfinante.gov.ro/static/10/eFactura/ro16931-ubl-1.0.9.zip (cius-ro/RO16931-rules.sch, EN16931-CIUS_RO-UBL-validation.sch, abstract/UBL/codelist/preprocessed .sch); samples .../exemple_Invoice_CreditNote.zip. Host is flaky: -OutFile failed 3 times while an in-memory download worked, so init needs a retry. Copy in scratchpad dl/ro.zip.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 2u32, "2026-10-27T13:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 09:50 fiscal: corpus IN THE TREE (fetch block in scripts/init.ps1, unstaged): deps/corpus/ro/cius: ro16931-ubl-1.0.9.zip (sha 818E7DD7; 10 schematron) + exemple_Invoice_CreditNote.zip (3C1DDCFC; 1 Invoice, 1 CreditNote). init.ps1 fetches it through Save-Pinned (sha256-pinned, refuses changed content, 3 in-memory attempts for flaky hosts) and Expand-Pinned. Its Invoice documents join generated_ubl_invoice_2_1's real documents through the new manifest deps/corpus/ubl-invoice-documents.txt, which init rewrites every run from every corpus .xml whose PARSED root is Invoice in urn:oasis:...:Invoice-2 (87 today: DIAN 33, UBL-TR 35, CEN 10, Peppol 7, ANAF 1, LHDN 1; Turkish StandardBusinessDocument envelopes are excluded by the root check); the generator reads the manifest (manifest_documents) and UBL's example cell round-trips each through the typed reader/writer with xml.first_difference.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 3u32, "2026-10-27T19:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:05 fiscal: function census: RO16931-rules and both ROeFactura validation files need only matches (1 call each) beyond what the engine (with the held Peppol program: lets, if/then/else) supports; the CEN core they include needs nothing more. So RO_CIUS is one function away from running under the lib engine.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 4u32, "2026-10-27T19:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-27 15:29 fiscal: RO census IN THE TREE: corpus_checks' Peppol census cell renamed regional_rules_census (0 outside refs) and now also reads ROeFactura-UBL-validation-Invoice_v1.0.8.sch (the self-contained preprocessed file; RO16931-rules.sch has no concrete rules): pins 19 rules, 113 assertions, 113 fatal (counted with .NET; the same counter reproduces Peppol's 93/159/135) and prints the parse-invalid count. Type-checked.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 5u32, "2026-10-28T08:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 04:16 fiscal: RUNTIME: its real UBL documents are among the 155 invoices that read back unchanged through the generated UBL Invoice reader/writer on the node (set-proof setc, job-1793162726520, lib as landed 20:17, compiler 4FD712E9E357, generator with the count-type fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 6u32, "2026-10-30T02:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 22:00 fiscal: GROOM, next step defined: documents round-trip (10-28), but the RO_CIUS schematron is not yet evaluated. The evaluator fixes it needs are live as of window 4 (10-29 19:49: pattern lets shared, path-step flattening, floor, #.00/0.00 pictures, and/or error propagation; Peppol and ZATCA's CEN copies green on them). Next: add ro_cius_samples_pass_the_ro_rules to corpus_checks, modeled on zatca_samples_pass_the_zatca_rules (examples_fatal_in + first_failures with evaluated_on ()), over the RO_CIUS 1.0.9 schematron and CEN-EN16931-UBL; run it on a post-land node mirror.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 7u32, "2026-10-30T15:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 11:07 fiscal: RULE SOURCE SETTLED + TEST DRAFTED. Bundle deps/corpus/ro/cius/ro16931-ubl-1.0.9: the entry EN16931-CIUS_RO-UBL-validation.sch includes the CEN core as ISO abstract patterns (abstract/EN16931-model + syntax, abstract=true, bound by UBL/EN16931-UBL-*.sch is-a=model with 272 params), which the lib reader does not implement (0 is-a support). The preprocessed/ROeFactura-UBL-validation-Invoice_v1.0.8.sch is STALE against 1.0.9: it lacks BR-RO-020_1, BR-RO-020_2, BR-RO-DT001..DT006 and DT003_CN (and still has the old BR-RO-020). But cius-ro/RO16931-rules.sch (the 1.0.9 RO rules, 113 ids) is CONCRETE: root pattern ROmodel, 6 lets, 29 rules, 114 asserts + 8 reports, all fatal, no abstract/extends/except. Every function it uses is in xpath.spi (normalize-space, string-length, substring-after, matches...). So 1.0.9 is evaluable today, with no lib change: RO 1.0.9 rules + the bundle's preprocessed CEN. Test ro_cius_examples_pass_the_ro_rules (ZATCA-shaped: examples_fatal_in + first_failures over eInvoice_ex.xml and creditNote_ex.xml; census pinned at rules 29, assertions 122, fatal 122 so 0 rules can't pass vacuously) is in C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live-dian\\src\\corpus_checks.spi (88C9DAAD, edition-3 spelling, formatter-clean; same layer as FISCAL-CO-DIAN's dian_compiled_rules_read_fully). Proof: on e3lv after its edition-3 chain settles (it is the one init'd fiscal mirror). Abstract-pattern support (is-a + param substitution) would let the bundled CEN be read from source rather than preprocessed: a generic lib follow-up, not needed for RO's own rules. [CHECKED 11:10: the bundle's preprocessed CEN is v1.3.8 (2022-04-08), and its assert ids equal exactly those of the bundle's abstract model + syntax + codelist sources (977 = 977, 0 unique to either side). So it is those sources compiled, the same CEN ANAF ships with RO_CIUS 1.0.9, and is-a support is NOT needed here. Fiscal's own eu/en16931 copy is newer, v1.3.17 (2026-10-09), but RO is evaluated against its own bundle.]")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 8u32, "2026-10-30T16:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 12:11 fiscal: FIRST RUN, RED as expected of a real finding: ro_cius_examples_pass_the_ro_rules (job-1793375644951, dxsl, pack 7) failed with creditNote_ex.xml has fatal findings: 1; ro: BR-RO-001; cen: (none). Census pins held (no census failwith). HAND-VERIFIED: BR-RO-001 (context /ubl:Invoice | /cn:CreditNote) tests cbc:CustomizationID = RO-CIUS-ID, where RO-CIUS-ID = urn:cen.eu:en16931:2017#compliant#urn:efactura.mfinante.ro:CIUS-RO:1.0.1 (let RO-MAJOR-MINOR-PATCH-VERSION = 1.0.1). BOTH official examples carry ...CIUS-RO:1.0.0, so the finding is a TRUE POSITIVE, and eInvoice_ex.xml must fail it too: the examples predate the 1.0.9 rule set. Not an evaluator bug: name_matches compares local names, so /ubl:Invoice matches the unprefixed default-namespace root, and the failure message names only the head of examples_fatal_in's reversed list. So 'examples pass' is the wrong pass line for this bundle; the test becomes a UBL-TR-style measurement with pinned, verified counts. A rerun prints both samples' counts (fiscal-p7-dxsl3-ro-rerun, job-1793376646592; the raw log was overwritten by the next job before I read it). Pin rule fixed before seeing it: if eInvoice shows exactly BR-RO-001 too, pin both at 1; any other count gets hand-checked first.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 9u32, "2026-10-30T17:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 13:11 fiscal: COUNTS VERIFIED, PINS SET BY THE PRE-REGISTERED RULE. Rerun fiscal-p7-dx4-ro (job-1793377261930, dxsl, landed-equivalent lib drafts, pack 7; raw saved as fix-dxsl-dx4-ro.txt): ro_cius fatal: creditNote_ex.xml 1 and eInvoice_ex.xml 1. Exactly 2 entries over the RO and CEN lists combined. BR-RO-001 must fire on both (both carry CIUS-RO:1.0.0, the rule requires 1.0.1), so both entries are RO BR-RO-001 and CEN is clean on both. That matches the rule fixed at 12:11 (eInvoice shows exactly BR-RO-001 too -> pin both at 1). The test in the layer is now the measurement ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings: census pins 29/122/122, CEN fatal must be empty, RO counts pinned eInvoice 1 and creditNote 1 (C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\e3live-dian\\src\\corpus_checks.spi 0C6ADC10). Proof on the POST-LAND pack-8 mirror pl8 (landed lib + e3live + this layer + box corpus): fiscal-p8-pl8-ro (job-1793380224408), after the pl8 lib gate and init. Pass = HOLDS. Progress 40 -> 75 when it holds; then only the edition-3 land stands between it and the tree.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 10u32, "2026-10-30T18:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:56 fiscal: PINNED MEASUREMENT HOLDS ON PACK 8, POST-LAND: fiscal-p8-pl8-ro (job-1793380224408, mirror pl8 = landed lib + e3live + layer corpus_checks 0C6ADC10 + box corpus, staged pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A) passes ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings (census 29/122/122, CEN fatal empty, RO counts eInvoice 1 + creditNote 1 = BR-RO-001 true positives), 0 type errors. Progress 40 -> 75 per n9's rule. Left: the test enters the tree with the edition-3 layer (FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND), then 100.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 11u32, "2026-11-01T03:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 23:40 fiscal: MOVED (groom 10-31 night). ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings (census 29/122/122, RO counts eInvoice 1 + creditNote 1) is NOT in the committed src/corpus_checks.spi (it was in the archived e3live-dian layer). NEXT (CPU-light): port it from kit archive 20261031-085551 into the tree's corpus_checks.spi together with CO-DIAN's two tests, one box gate for all three.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 12u32, "2026-11-01T04:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 00:25 fiscal: PORTED into the tree (unstaged): src/corpus_checks.spi 78DD9F9C -> 6C7AA32C. Source: the archived e3live-dian layer (kit archive 20261031-085551, blob 1F0376FB). Only the layer was taken, diffed against e3live 5220335B, and path :: was turned back to . (cons :: untouched). Adds dian_compiled_rules_read_fully, dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings (44 pins), ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings, and region_failures (sample_failures now delegates to it). Header timeout 3600000. Installed formatter: only adds the final newline. GATE: node job-1793505898845-fiscal-p8-t1031u-dian-ro-tests (whole corpus_checks file, t1031u mirror). Done on green.")
inl note_of_fiscal_ro_cius_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-RO-CIUS", 13u32, "2026-11-01T04:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:40 fiscal: GREEN on the node (job-1793505898845, t1031u, whole src/corpus_checks.spi 6C7AA32C): dian_compiled_rules_read_fully, dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings (44 pins, 1,185 s) and ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings all PASS; 19/25 overall. The 6 failures are unrelated to the port: 5 pattern/DFA tests need build.ps1's gitignored pattern-oracle outputs (src/patterns.txt, probes), which the mirror sync skips; en16931_rules_parse_completely pinned 979 assertions while the 1.3.17 pin has 981 (fixed in the tree; see FISCAL-EN16931-1-3-17). The port is in the tree, unstaged, for the user's next commit. CLOSED.")
