inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_1 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 1u32, "2026-10-28T10:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 06:38 fiscal: found by set-proof setd (job-1793178481148, BOM-free corpus): generated_gr_mydata_2_0_2 reads 1 of 2 real documents back; request-doc-with-delivery-lifecycle loses /InvoicesDoc/invoice/deliveryLifecycle/deliveryEvents/transportDetails/location/longitude. LocationType is an xs:all (longitude, latitude); lib xsd has no xs:all particle (grep of xsd*.spi: 0). Corpus users: gr/mydata TransportTypes, pt/saft saftpt1.04_01. Plan: model all as unordered required children (min/max 0..1 each); reader claims each child by name in any order; writer emits declaration order; test with a reordered document.")
inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_2 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 2u32, "2026-10-28T11:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 07:05 fiscal: DRAFT ready, lands in the 14:00-16:00 window (after kit's fix-forward): fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-all-groups.kit: particle_of reads xs:all as a Sequence of its elements (readers claim children by name via first_child/children_named, so any document order reads; writers emit declaration order, valid for xs:all) + test all_groups_keep_their_elements. Before the fix, xs:all content was DROPPED entirely (particle_of returned None). Type-checks (xsd, probe, xsd_emit, xsd_resolve, json_schema, fiscal generator + corpus_checks); applies fresh = draft. Node: xsd.spi gate HOLDS 9/9 incl the new test (job-1793185188686). Greece + Portugal regeneration proof running on mirror setall with the overlay.")
inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_3 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 3u32, "2026-10-28T15:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 11:07 fiscal: setall (job-1793186085227) VOID, not red: 13 of 21 generator cells timed out at the 1,400 s package-line budget on a node at 100% (12 jobs), so the GR/PT units were never built. Replaced by a narrow proof on the same mirror (xsd.spi overlay 147F773B, budget raised to 5,400,000 in the stage copy only): generator cells generates_mydata_2_0_2 (job-1793199986948) and generates_saft_pt_1_04_01 (job-1793200015262), each --after-ok its unit gate (job-1793200006172, job-1793200029875). Land only on all four green.")
inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_4 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 4u32, "2026-10-29T11:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 07:47 fiscal: generator cells HOLD (gen-mydata job-1793199986948, gen-saft job-1793200015262); both unit gates were VOID: my proof script hashed generated_mydata_2_0_2 / generated_saft_pt_1_04_01, but the units are named generated_gr_mydata_2_0_2 / generated_pt_saft_1_04_01. Rerun with the real names: fiscal-all-unit2-gr job-1793273742074, fiscal-all-unit2-pt job-1793273745610 (setall mirror, A4E48020). Land on both green.")
inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_5 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 5u32, "2026-10-29T12:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 08:20 fiscal: land NOT done yet: lib-guarded-do refused at 07:52 and 08:00 (another lane's formatter candidate gate, then the compiler pack6 review's heavy-build window). Waiting for kit's 'TRAIN3 published' (lib-guarded-do runs the kit tree's kit.exe, whose swap a running copy would block). Then xsd-all-groups.kit: xsd 1D437DBF -> 147F773B.")
inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_6 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 6u32, "2026-10-29T16:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 12:01 fiscal: LANDED 11:37:52: xsd-all-groups.kit, xsd 1D437DBF -> 147F773B, via lib-guarded-do (git-a6's pack6b window exempted at its native phase; no live reader), hash equal to the node-proven copy; post-land mirror post1029 reproduces the proof mirrors' hashes exactly; main's document_test (spi -> livemd -> spi) GREEN over it; full live-tree gates queued as the fiscal-post-* chain. Undo = git HEAD.")
inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_7 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 7u32, "2026-10-30T16:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 12:15 fiscal: PROGRESS 60 -> 90 by milestone: landed 10-29 11:37 (xsd 147F773B, still the live hash), lib tests and document_test green. The last milestone is the real-document proof: the Greek myDATA document that lost location/longitude without xs:all must round-trip. Queued as fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-grptcr (job-1793376912165). Closes on that HOLDS.")
inl note_of_xsd_all_groups_8 () = Note ("XSD-ALL-GROUPS", 8u32, "2026-10-31T03:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 23:00 fiscal: CLOSED, last milestone met: the real-document proof HOLDS (fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-grptcr (node job-1793376912165, mirror e3lv = live lib + edition-3 draft + box corpus, pack 7 F2F6F4CB5A18; generator 22/22, 0 memo hits)). generated_gr_mydata_2_0_2 1/1; the Greek myDATA document whose xs:all LocationType lost longitude now round-trips unchanged through the generated reader/writer (xsd 147F773B, landed 10-29). 90 -> 100, Done.")
inl xsd_signing_stages () = Task ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", "xsd_emit: documents with a required ds:Signature get a stage index (unsigned | signed), so unsigned documents read and signed ones keep their guarantee", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "-", "fiscal,xsd,typefeatures,team:fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xsd_signing_stages () = Planning ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_1 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 1u32, "2026-10-28T11:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 07:14 fiscal: DESIGN (no code). Census of corpus schemas: required ds:Signature refs in BR NF-e 38, CT-e 25, MDF-e 4, CL DTE 2, CR v4.4 9 (all 9 documents). Today a reader needs the signature, so an unsigned document (what fiscal's own writer produces, and the 7 hacienda-cr cases) cannot be read. Plan, GADT-first: a stage index on documents whose type references a required Signature: signature_slot s = Pending : signature_slot unsigned | Present : xml_node -> signature_slot signed; the record field becomes signature_slot s; T_of_xml_unsigned accepts the element absent, T_of_xml (signed) requires it; T_to_xml writes Present only; examples build T unsigned. Rejected: minOccurs 0 (loses the signed-carries-a-signature guarantee in the type).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_2 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 2u32, "2026-10-28T12:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 08:43 fiscal: DESIGN PROVEN on A4E48020 (node --check): nominal unsigned/signed; union stage s = Unsigned/Signed :: string -> stage <tag> (versioned witness idiom); type x_doc s = { ..; signature : signature_slot s }; reader forall s. (witness : stage s); writer takes x_doc signed, matches only Present. Controls fail as wanted: writer on unsigned doc and Present in an unsigned doc are unification errors. Refined: (1) family config lists staged elements (xmldsig Signature now; later PAC stamps/protocols), not a hard-coded ds:Signature; (2) the index propagates to every type that transitively holds a staged type (TEnviNFe holds TNFe).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_3 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 3u32, "2026-10-28T14:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 10:39 fiscal: MILESTONES (pre-registered): M1 staged_type_names (which types carry the stage index), M2 type emission with the index, M3 readers take the stage witness, M4 writer takes signed only, M5 examples unsigned, M6 BR NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e + CR regen: CR's 7 unsigned hacienda cases read. Facts: ref elements keep their QName text (ds:Signature) since tag names are not qualified, so staged = local names of ref-only elements, per family.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_4 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 4u32, "2026-10-28T14:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 10:39 fiscal: M1 DRAFTED, held as lib-programs/xsd-staged-type-names.kit (xsd_emit, +144, 2 hunks: after has_name + 1 test at the end; independent of the other xsd_emit programs; draft %TEMP%\\tc-ss-draft). Direct = content REQUIRES a staged ref (min >= 1 on the path; a choice only if every branch requires it); closure = any field (optional/repeated too), inline type or base that mentions a staged type, to a fixpoint. Test covers direct, container, inline root, optional (not staged), plain. Proof job-1793198427541 fiscal-fix-ss (after fix-ac).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_5 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 5u32, "2026-10-28T14:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-28 10:47 fiscal: M2 SHAPE PROVEN (node --check, A4E48020): ONE shared slot per unit, union staged s a = Pending :: forall a. string -> staged unsigned a | Present :: forall a. a -> staged signed a; staged types take s (type x_doc s = { ..; signature : staged s x_signature }), containers pass it (x_batch s = { docs : list (x_doc s) }); reader helper staged_of forall s a. (witness : stage s) (read : () -> a); writer present (x : staged signed a). Controls fail as wanted: signed writer on an unsigned doc, and an unsigned batch holding a signed doc.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_6 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 6u32, "2026-10-29T11:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 07:47 fiscal: M1 proof fix-ss (job-1793198427541) was RED: 6 ETY-ValueRestriction at grow_staged (xsd_emit:688): 'listm.length next = listm.length names' leaves the generic length result type unsolved (lib annotates it the same way, listm':840). Fixed in lib-programs/xsd-staged-type-names.kit: (listm.length next : i32). fix-ss2 (job-1793273962189, live xsd_emit + M1 = 20136A82, mirror header raised): the test passes, 0 type errors in the whole file. M1 lands after the emit gate verdict; M2 drafting next.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_7 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 7u32, "2026-10-29T12:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 08:20 fiscal: M1 lands with XSD-ALL-GROUPS after TRAIN3 (xsd_emit 841B97D2 -> 20136A82). M2 design: emit_record has no staged list, so M2 either threads the staged names through emit_named_type/emit_record or post-processes the emitted items; either way it stays unwired from generated_units until M3/M4, so generated units keep compiling between milestones.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_8 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 8u32, "2026-10-29T13:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 09:12 fiscal: M2 DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-staged-type-emission.kit (stacks on indirection + M1: xsd_emit E88E120D -> F87980B0; rehearsed): staging_prelude (nominal unsigned/signed + union staged s a = Pending :: forall a. string -> staged unsigned a | Present :: forall a. a -> staged signed a, the n5 shape), staged_items post-pass over emitted items: a staged type's header becomes 'type x s =', fields of staged types pass s (x, option (x), list (x)), the required signature field becomes 'staged s string' (ref-only elements emit string). Not wired into generated_units until M3/M4, so generated units keep compiling. Test staged_types_take_the_stage_and_pass_it_on (M1's schema). Proof on fresh mirror m2x1029: jobs 1793279563913 (M2 test) and 1793279583021 (M1 test on the same file). Known gap for M3: a choice union holding a staged type is not staged yet.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_9 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 9u32, "2026-10-29T13:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 09:44 fiscal: M2 PROVEN on fresh mirror m2x1029 (live xsd_emit + indirection + M1 + M2 = F87980B0, + mirror header = 3000D720, A4E48020): staged_types_take_the_stage_and_pass_it_on passes, M1's test still passes, 0 type errors in the whole file (fiscal-m2-* jobs). Lands after the indirection and M1 (post-TRAIN3). Next: M3, readers take the stage witness.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_10 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 10u32, "2026-10-29T13:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 09:54 fiscal: M3 SHAPE PROVEN by a probe in the generated units' exact shape (fiscal-m3-probe job-1793281953956, mirror m2x1029, A4E48020, rust, 0 type errors): union stage s = Unsigned :: stage unsigned | Signed :: stage signed; inl staged_of forall s a. (witness : stage s) (read : () -> a) : staged s a matches the witness (Pending / Present (read ())); readers in the generated 'let rec ... and let ...' group take 'forall s. (witness : stage s)' and pass the witness to the readers of the staged types they hold (x_batch -> x_doc); a function over 'x_doc signed' matches only Present and the test on the unsigned read matches only Pending, with no impossible arms needed. So readers of unsigned documents never touch the signature, and signed readers must produce one. M3 build plan: a reading instance that carries the staged names (record_texts adds the witness to staged types' _of_children/_of_xml and returns 'ty s'; element_part passes the witness to staged children and wraps the signature in staged_of), the other reading instances delegate, and it stays unwired until M4/M5.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_11 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 11u32, "2026-10-29T14:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 10:11 fiscal: M3 DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-staged-readers.kit (stacks on M2: xsd_emit F87980B0 -> 7A9F19FF; rehearsed): staging_prelude gains union stage s (Unsigned/Signed) and staged_of; a staged_reading family (StagedReading (staged, signatures)) whose record_texts gives staged types 'forall s. (witness : stage s)' readers returning 'ty s', whose element_part wraps a required signature in staged_of witness and passes the witness to staged children, and whose other 12 prototypes delegate to Reading; module_parts_with / walk_texts_with take the reading family (module_parts = module_parts_with Reading, so every generated unit is unchanged). Test staged_readers_take_the_witness_and_stage_the_signature. Mirror m2x1029: names_follow_spiral_conventions passes and the whole file has 0 type errors (job-1793283015882); the M3 and M2 tests are running.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_12 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 12u32, "2026-10-29T14:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 10:29 fiscal: M4 DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-staged-writers.kit (stacks on M3: xsd_emit 7A9F19FF -> E96F45C2; rehearsed): prelude gains signed_value (matches Present only); a staged_writing family whose record_texts gives staged types writers over 'ty signed' (_children/_attributes/_to_xml), whose element_part writes the required signature from (signed_value x.signature), and whose witness prototypes return none for staged owners (their _field witness helpers would name ty without its stage), so staged types take the concat path; the other prototypes delegate to Writing. module_parts_by (walk) now carries the body; module_parts_with reader and module_parts_staged staged signatures (StagedReading + StagedWriting) both go through it, and module_parts = module_parts_with Reading leaves every generated unit unchanged. Test staged_writers_take_signed_documents_only. Proof on mirror m4x1029 (E96F45C2 + header = 2B9A8753), chained after fiscal-set-ublj to keep fiscal at <= 2 node jobs (x's verify29): M4 test, M3 test, complements writer test. Still open for M5/M6: examples build unsigned values, wiring into generated_units per family (BR NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e + CR), and choice unions holding staged types.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_13 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 13u32, "2026-10-29T14:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 10:39 fiscal: re SPIRAL-CHECK-PRINTS-ERRORS (host --check exits 0 on parse errors): n2 and n5's design proofs were --check only, so they did not prove the syntax. Both shapes are now re-proven by a real build: fiscal-m3-probe (job-1793281953956) is a Cells rust run of a superset (nominal unsigned/signed, union staged s a, union stage s, staged_of, staged record types, staged readers), 1/1 passed, 0 type errors. No fiscal land today rests on --check: every gate is a Cells build + run (fix-proof-d / set-proof-c).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_14 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 14u32, "2026-10-29T14:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 10:41 fiscal: M3 PROVEN on mirror m2x1029 (live + indirection + M1 + M2 + M3 = 7A9F19FF, + mirror header = 383FC5A9, A4E48020, Cells rust): staged_readers_take_the_witness_and_stage_the_signature passes, M2's staged_types_take_the_stage_and_pass_it_on still passes, names_follow_spiral_conventions passes, 0 type errors in the whole file (fiscal-m3-* jobs). M3 lands after M2.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_15 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 15u32, "2026-10-29T14:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 10:45 fiscal: M5 DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-staged-examples.kit (stacks on M4: xsd_emit E96F45C2 -> E76BD66A; rehearsed): a staged_exampling family whose record_texts gives staged types '_example (k : i32) : ty unsigned', whose element_part sets the required signature to Pending (a staged child's own example is already unsigned, so containers need nothing more), and whose other prototypes delegate to Exampling; staged_walk_texts now uses StagedReading + StagedWriting + StagedExampling. Test staged_examples_are_unsigned. Proof after M4's chain (fiscal <= 2 node jobs until verify29 reports). Remaining for M6: wire module_parts_staged into generated_units for families with required signatures (BR NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e, CL DTE, CR v4.4), give unit document checks a stage (read unsigned unless the document carries a signature), and stage choice unions that hold staged types.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_16 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 16u32, "2026-10-29T15:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 11:09 fiscal: DECISION, M4 REVISED before landing (n3 pre-registered 'M4 writer takes signed only'). Why: an XML-DSig enveloped signature is computed over the document serialized WITHOUT its Signature element, so fiscal must write unsigned documents in order to sign them; a signed-only writer would also break every unit's _writes_its_example check now that examples are unsigned (M5). The guarantee that matters is on the read side and M3 gives it: a Signed read requires the signature, an Unsigned read never touches it. New M4 (fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-staged-writers.kit, M3 7A9F19FF -> 6DA69F57): staged writers are 'forall s.' over 'ty s', and the signature is written through prelude staged_list (Pending -> no element, Present v -> the element); signed_value stays for callers that hold a signed document. Test renamed staged_writers_write_any_stage_and_only_a_present_signature. M5 rebased onto it (6DA69F57 -> 21E27223; its test hunk was re-anchored by hand after the M4 test changed). The old queued M4 jobs were stopped before running. New proof chain on mirror m4x1029 (21E27223 + header = CF70840D), one job at a time after fiscal-set-ublj: M5, M4, M3 and the complements writer test (jobs 1793286618627, 1793286620722, 1793286624299, 1793286627888).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_17 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 17u32, "2026-10-29T15:13Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 11:13 fiscal: M6 lib half DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-staged-units.kit (stacks on M5: xsd_emit 21E27223 -> F49F611A; rehearsed): units_of_parts (any_content, prelude, parts) is the shared tail; generated_units_with = units_of_parts any_content '' (module_parts schema), so existing units are byte-identical; new generated_units_signed signatures any_content schema stages a schema with required signatures (module_parts_staged + the M2 type pass + staging_prelude) and falls back to generated_units_with when nothing is staged. Test a_family_with_required_signatures_generates_staged_units (staged prelude/types/readers present; an unsigned schema's unit equal to generated_units). Mirror m4x1029 now holds M6 (F49F611A + header = B3FF1D04); the queued M5/M4/M3/complements chain runs on it, then fiscal-m6-staged_units (job-1793286904819). M6 generator half (fiscal): signatures_of family for BR NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e, CL DTE, CR v4.4, generated_units_signed in write_family_modules, and document checks reading signed real documents with the Signed witness (unsigned CR cases with Unsigned).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_18 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 18u32, "2026-10-29T15:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 11:21 fiscal: M6 generator half DRAFTED, held as fiscal/lib-programs/generator-signed-families.kit (stacks on generator-complements: fiscal/src/generator.spi FF920D9F -> 7CCC1E85; rehearsed): signatures_of gives ['Signature'] to BR NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e/GTVe, CL and CR families (an explicit prefix list, so no other schema's ref named Signature gets staged); write_family_modules generates every family through generated_units_signed (unstaged schemas are byte-identical), and when the root type is staged, the real-document checks read with the Signed witness and the bench re-reads its written example with Unsigned (examples are unsigned since M5); document_round_trip, document_checks and family_bench take the witness text ('' for unstaged roots, so their output is unchanged). Apply order in the fiscal tree: generator-complements.kit, then generator-signed-families.kit, after the lib chain M1..M6 has landed. Proof then: set-proof on the BR/CL/CR units.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_19 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 19u32, "2026-10-29T16:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 12:01 fiscal: M1, M2 and M3 LANDED 11:38:56-11:58:43 (xsd_emit CF7BBF4D -> E88E120D -> F87980B0 -> 7A9F19FF), via lib-guarded-do (git-a6's pack6b window exempted at its native phase; no live reader), hash equal to the node-proven copy; post-land mirror post1029 reproduces the proof mirrors' hashes exactly; main's document_test (spi -> livemd -> spi) GREEN over it; full live-tree gates queued as the fiscal-post-* chain. Undo = git HEAD. M4-M6 lib programs wait on the fiscal-m45/m6 chain; nothing is wired into generated_units until M6 + the generator half land, so every generated unit is unchanged.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_20 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 20u32, "2026-10-29T16:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 12:04 fiscal: M4 (revised) and M5 PROVEN on mirror m4x1029 holding the M6 file (F49F611A + header = B3FF1D04, A4E48020): staged_examples_are_unsigned, staged_writers_write_any_stage_and_only_a_present_signature, staged_readers_take_the_witness_and_stage_the_signature and complements_read_and_write_typed_cases_and_keep_unknown_elements_whole all pass; 0 type errors in the whole file (M6 code included). M6's own test fiscal-m6-staged_units is running; on its pass, lander6 lands M4 -> M5 -> M6 (xsd_emit 7A9F19FF -> 6DA69F57 -> 21E27223 -> F49F611A).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_21 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 21u32, "2026-10-29T17:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 13:26 fiscal: LIVE-TREE GATE HOLDS for the whole chain: fiscal-post-xsd_emit (mirror post1029, live xsd_emit F49F611A = M1..M6 + mirror header = B3FF1D04, A4E48020): 23/23 tests, 0 type errors. The lib half of signing stages is DONE (M1-M6). Remaining: apply generator-complements.kit + generator-signed-families.kit to the fiscal tree (after the CFDI operator fix lands), then set-proof the BR/CL/CR units.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_22 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 22u32, "2026-10-29T19:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 15:28 fiscal: generator half APPLIED to the fiscal tree (generator-signed-families.kit, after generator-complements; tree now 84A609E1): BR NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e/GTVe, CL and CR families generate through generated_units_signed, real-document checks read with Signed, and the bench re-reads its example with Unsigned. Proof: fiscal-6b-set-signed (MDF-e 3.00 + CL Envio DTE among its units).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_23 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 23u32, "2026-10-30T16:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 12:15 fiscal: PROGRESS 30 -> 80 by milestone, with weights fixed before counting: lib 40, generator 20, family proofs 40. Lib M1-M6 DONE (live-tree gate 23/23, 10-29 13:26) = 40. Generator half applied to the tree (generator-signed-families, 10-29 15:28) = 20. Proofs: CL DTE + Envio DTE and MDF-e 3.00 GREEN on the live lib with M6 (fiscal-p7-set-cl-mdfe, 10-30) = 20 of 40. Open: CR (generated_cr_factura_4_4 in fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-grptcr, job-1793376912165) and BR NF-e/CT-e (a set-proof on their units after it). [Queued 12:16: BR proof fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-brsigned (job-1793376988214-fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-brsigned), units ^generated_(nfe_v4|cte_v4_00)$ (the NF-e unit is named generated_nfe_v4, without _00; a first queue with nfe_v4_00 was stopped before it ran), after grptcr.]")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_24 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 24u32, "2026-10-31T03:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 23:00 fiscal: BUG FOUND + FIX DRAFTED. fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-grptcr broke generated_cr_factura_4_4: signature typed 'staged s (list ...)' but read and written as a plain list. Cause: staged_signatures (type side) stages every signature field by name, while element_part staged_reading / staged_writing stage only when is_required_once; CR 4.4 declares ds:Signature minOccurs=1 maxOccurs=5. Rule now shared by both sides, matching particle_requires_staged (line 575): a signature is staged iff occurs.min >= 1. Draft xsd_emit 4D56FBA1 (base 161D00F5 = live): new is_staged_signature; the reader wraps any required signature read (once or list) in staged_of witness; the writer keeps staged_list for exactly-once and writes listm.concat (staged_list (fun vs => listm.map (fun v => ...) vs) x.f) for a required list. Test a_required_signature_list_is_staged_as_one_slot (CR's 1..5 shape + a single-signature control). Round trip true; formatter: only the lib-wide bracket spacing the neighbouring tests also get. Proof queued (fiscal-box7-signature-list-stages, behind main's tree-write window): a CONTROL first (live code + the new test, which must fail through the bug's own path), then the whole xsd_emit module on the draft. Then: regenerate CR (and mdfe_v3_00 / cl_envio_dte_v10 in signed2) on a lib with the draft.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_25 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 25u32, "2026-10-31T03:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 23:10 fiscal: SCOPE of the list fix (read from today's generated units in the tree, generator = e3lv's): CR 4.4 is the only required-LIST signature (minOccurs=1 maxOccurs=5). mdfe_v3_00 has 'signature : option (x_signature_type)' (minOccurs=0, unstaged) and 'signature : staged s x_signature_type' (required once); cl_dte_v10 / cl_envio_dte_v10 have required-once staged signatures only. So their 10-29 breaks in fiscal-6b-set-signed (mdfe: unification against staged s {signed_info...}; cl: ETY-KindError at 5572) are NOT this list bug; node job fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-signed2 (after brsigned) shows whether they still break on today's lib. Separately: generated_nfe_v4's signature is 'x_signature_type' (not staged at all) although its root is a signed document; checked when signed2 and brsigned report.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_26 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 26u32, "2026-10-31T03:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 23:15 fiscal: FINDING, NF-e 4.00 is outside the staging. generated_nfe_v4 is written by the generator's older direct path (write_generated_module 'generated_nfe_v4' (text ++# sample_helper () ++# self_check)), not through family/signatures_of, so signatures_of's 'generated_nfe_' prefix never reaches it: x_tn_fe has 'signature : x_signature_type' (required, unstaged; leiauteNFe_v4.00.xsd:6683 ref ds:Signature), while the protocol wrapper's is option. Effect: an unsigned NF-e 4.00 (the document a signer receives) cannot be built or written by the generated code, unlike nfe_v2_00 / nfe_v3_10 / every CT-e, MDF-e, GTV-e, CL and CR family. Fix direction: move NF-e 4.00 onto the family path (its own family entry with root TNFe), then its example and documents use the Unsigned / Signed witnesses like the others; size it after the CR list fix lands, since both change the same staged readers.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_27 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 27u32, "2026-10-31T07:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 03:06 fiscal: LIST FIX PROVEN on the box (job-1793425243907-fiscal-box7-signature-list-stages2, compiler EEBCBFF8, Cells rust): CONTROL = live xsd_emit CDA88705 (161D00F5 + the new test + gate header) failed a_required_signature_list_is_staged_as_one_slot through the bug's own path ('the reader stages the whole list', main.rs:31432), so the test detects the defect; DRAFT 102EEE65 (4D56FBA1 + header) passed the whole module, 25/25 tests, 0 type errors. Round trip of 4D56FBA1: ok (slice-roundtrip-sweep, positive control holds). Land program fiscal-drafts/xsd-stages/xsd-stages.kit (4 hunks) rehearsed on a copy of live: 161D00F5 -> 4D56FBA1 hash-equal. Land queued (land-lib-program, undo by hash) behind kit's train5e heavy-build window, which counts as a lib reader. Then: regenerate CR 4.4 on the landed lib.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_28 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 28u32, "2026-10-31T07:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 03:49 fiscal: NF-e 4.00 MOVED ONTO THE FAMILY PATH, in the fiscal tree (unstaged): src/generator.spi drops the hand-built test generates_the_nfe_v4_model (generate_module + write_generated_module, unstaged signature) and adds nfe_v4_00 () : family_root (module generated_nfe_v4, nfe_v4.00.xsd, NFe/TNFe), so signatures_of's generated_nfe_ prefix now stages it like v2.00/v3.10; its unit-specific runtime checks (TCodUfIBGE round trip, CNPJ validator, TEnderEmi read/write) move into the unit through unit_checks_of (same per-module hook shape as complements_of) and run beside the family's writes_its_example / bench / keeps_raw_strings_out; new generator test generates_nfe_v4_with_a_staged_signature asserts 'type x_tn_fe s =', 'signature : staged s x_signature_type' and an unsigned example. The sample is now samples/generated_nfe_v4_example.xml (validate-example.ps1 default and family-gates.ps1 updated; no workflow names it). family_roots stays at 12, so generates_every_family_version is untouched. Proof queued as fiscal-box10-nfe4-family (scratch root boxgate10 = live lib + xsd_emit 4D56FBA1, my src): generator test, then the regenerated unit's whole test set, then XSD validation of the unsigned sample (expected: only the missing ds:Signature). Regenerated generated/generated_nfe_v4 enters the tree after the proof (drift guard).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_29 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 29u32, "2026-10-31T09:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 05:29 fiscal: FAMILY PROOFS READ (node, e3lv lib, set-proof, 0 broken claims each): fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-brsigned (job-1793376988214, finished 10-30 23:53): generator 22/22, generated_cte_v4_00 2/2 (staged family path, Signed real-document reads + Unsigned example) and generated_nfe_v4 1/1 (the OLD direct path, unstaged; its move onto the family path is n28, proof fiscal-box10-nfe4-family running). fiscal-p7-e3lv-set-signed2 (job-1793403473254, finished 10-31 02:23): generated_cl_envio_dte_v10 2/2 and generated_mdfe_v3_00 2/2, so n25's 10-29 breaks are gone on today's lib. Progress per n23's weights (lib 40, generator 20, family proofs 40): proofs now CL DTE + Envio DTE, MDF-e 3.00, CT-e 4.00 = 30 of 40, open CR 4.4 (list fix, landing when the live lib has no reader) and NF-e 4.00 (n28) = 80 -> 90.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_30 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 30u32, "2026-10-31T09:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 05:37 fiscal: NF-e 4.00 STAGED, PROVEN (fiscal-box10-nfe4-family, job-1793432980506, box, compiler EEBCBFF8; scratch root boxgate10 = live lib + xsd_emit 4D56FBA1 + the tree's src with n28): generates_nfe_v4_with_a_staged_signature passes (0 type errors); the regenerated unit generated_nfe_v4 (4682ED118018, 1,972,656 B) passes 3/3 (writes_its_example with the bench cell, generated_nfe_model_type_checks carried over through unit_checks_of, keeps_raw_strings_out), 0 type errors; its unsigned sample (1598 B) gets exactly ONE XSD message from validate-example.ps1 against nfe_v4.00.xsd, NFe incomplete expecting infNFeSupl (optional) or Signature, i.e. only the missing signature, like MDF-e. Unit shape vs the old direct path: same 255 types, 251 validators, 1216 and-lets, 88 let-recs; unions +staged +stage -x_tn_fe_field -x_t_envi_n_fe_field -x_t_nfe_proc_field (the staged owners' field witnesses, dropped by design since M4: staged owners take the concat writer); 38,347 -> 29,395 lines. The proven unit is now in the tree's generated/generated_nfe_v4 (unstaged, for the user's commit with src/generator.spi; the drift guard then matches). Proofs per n23's weights: CL, MDF-e 3.00, CT-e 4.00, NF-e 4.00 = 35 of 40; open: CR 4.4, which waits on the xsd_emit list-fix land (live has had another lane's lib reader at every try since 03:04) and then a CR regeneration. 90 -> 95.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_31 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 31u32, "2026-10-31T10:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 06:43 fiscal: CR 4.4 REGENERATED on the list fix (fiscal-box13-cr-factura, job-1793440924432, boxgate10 = live lib + xsd_emit 4D56FBA1): generates_hacienda_factura_4_4 passes and the unit now stages the whole list on the READ side (staged_of witness (fun () => listm.map ... children_named ds:Signature)) and the WRITE side (listm.concat (staged_list ...)), but the unit is RED: 2 type errors at line 5468, the EXAMPLE: 'signature = [x_signature_type_example (k + 0i32)]' where the type is staged s (list ...). Third site: staged_exampling's element_part still staged only is_required_once. FIX in the draft: it now uses is_staged_signature like the reader and writer (Pending is forall a, so it fits staged unsigned (list ...)); a_required_signature_list_is_staged_as_one_slot gains 'no signature = [' in the emitted functions. Draft 4D56FBA1 -> AE0A917F (round trip ok; land program xsd-stages.kit rebuilt, 5 hunks, rehearsed on live 161D00F5 -> AE0A917F hash-equal). The 4D56FBA1 land loop was stopped before it ever landed (every try refused by live readers; live still 161D00F5), so the land is the combined AE0A917F. Proof chain queued as ONE serial job fiscal-stages3-example-cr-ubl (scratch roots under TEMP, so lib-guarded-do never counts them as live readers): control (AE0A917F with only the example rule reverted) must fail at the new assertion; whole xsd_emit module on AE0A917F; CR Factura regenerated + its unit; then generated_ubl_invoice_2_1 regenerated with the new size_drift (FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS n25/n26) for the tree's drift guard.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_32 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 32u32, "2026-10-31T12:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 08:46 fiscal: CORRECTION to n30. (1) The unit I copied into the tree at 05:3x was RAW generator output; the committed generated/ is FORMATTED (build.ps1 runs format-generated.ps1 before its drift check), so CI would have flagged it. Now formatted with the repo's format-generated.ps1 and pack 8 EEBCBFF8 (verified as the committed layout's formatter: committed generated_mdfe_v1_00 is a format --check fixpoint under it): generated_nfe_v4 0D73AB909800, 38,384 lines, diff vs HEAD +143/-106 (the real staging change; n30's '38,347 -> 29,395 lines' compared raw against formatted and is void). (2) The family path also writes generated_nfe_v4_certificates (new, formatted AB41CF4A35C5, 19,429 lines), which the old direct path never had; it is now in the tree too and is being gated (fiscal-box17-nfe4-certificates, queued for a free slot). The unit-shape comparison in n30 (types, validators, and-lets, the three dropped _field witness unions) is unaffected by layout.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_33 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 33u32, "2026-10-31T13:06Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 09:06 fiscal: CR 4.4 PROVEN, the last family proof (fiscal-stages3-example-cr-ubl, job-1793444866796, box, compiler EEBCBFF8; scratch roots under TEMP): (1) CONTROL (AE0A917F with only the example rule reverted) fails a_required_signature_list_is_staged_as_one_slot at the new assertion 'the example leaves the whole signature list pending', so the test sees the third site; (2) the WHOLE xsd_emit module on AE0A917F passes 25/25, 0 type errors; (3) generates_hacienda_factura_4_4 on it, and the regenerated generated_cr_factura_4_4 passes 2/2, 0 type errors, its example now 'signature = Pending \\n unsigned example\\'. The unit is in the tree FORMATTED (format-generated.ps1, pack 8): diff vs HEAD +7/-3, exactly the three sites (reader staged_of over the list, writer listm.concat over staged_list, example Pending); its _certificates unit is byte-identical to HEAD. Family proofs per n23 = 40/40 (CL, MDF-e 3.00, CT-e 4.00, NF-e 4.00, CR 4.4). LAND armed (fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-stages.kit, live 161D00F5 -> AE0A917F, land-lib-program retrying every 2 min until no live reader; kit's heavy-build window holds it now). The item closes on that land; the other 8 CR v4.4 documents then regenerate in one batch.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_34 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 34u32, "2026-10-31T13:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 09:49 fiscal: generated_nfe_v4_certificates PROVEN (fiscal-box17-nfe4-certificates, job-1793454061842, box, compiler EEBCBFF8; the FORMATTED tree file AB41CF4A35C5 in scratch root g17 on boxgate10's lib): generated_nfe_v4_certificates_hold passes 1/1, 0 type errors. So both NF-e 4.00 family units in the tree (generated_nfe_v4 0D73AB909800 + its certificates companion) are proven as committed.")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_35 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 35u32, "2026-10-31T16:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 12:50 fiscal: NF-e 4.00 family re-proven on a second machine: generated_nfe_v4 3/3 in node job-1793448496635-fiscal-p8-t1031-set-events-cfdi-ubl (mirror t1031 = box spiral fd70dccf + today's fiscal tree, corpus seeded from the box, pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A; generator all tests pass, 0 memo hits).")
inl note_of_xsd_signing_stages_36 () = Note ("XSD-SIGNING-STAGES", 36u32, "2026-10-31T18:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 14:17 fiscal: CLOSING. The list fix LANDED 14:13:53: live lib/spiral/xsd_emit.spi 161D00F5 -> AE0A917F90E02A6A, hash-equal to the proven draft (control red at the example assertion, whole module 25/25, CR Factura 4.4 regenerated 2/2; n33), via land-lib-program + lib-guarded-do (fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-stages.kit, 5 replacements; no live lib reader at apply time, my own scratch gates exempt by ancestry), round trip of the landed file ok, undo at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\kit\\\\undo\\\\xsd-stages. Done criteria per n23 met: lib M1-M6 + the list fix (reader, writer and example share is_staged_signature), generator half applied, family proofs 40/40 (CL DTE/Envio, MDF-e 3.00, CT-e 4.00, NF-e 4.00 with its certificates, CR 4.4). Follow-ups live elsewhere: the other 8 CR v4.4 documents (FISCAL-CR-HACIENDA, regenerating now), NF-e events (FISCAL-LIFECYCLE-EVENTS).")
inl hopacsota_d4_restart () = Task ("HOPACSOTA-D4-RESTART", "hopacsota D4 canonical-order restart: a foreign claim of an abandoned key / a wrong D16.3 hint (HopacsotaConflict, spiral_compiler.fs:53978) restarts the affected evaluation in canonical single-flight order instead of raising, so speculation can recover from a wrong guess", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,hopacsota,parallel,determinism,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_hopacsota_d4_restart () = Planning ("HOPACSOTA-D4-RESTART", Minutes 300u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_hopacsota_d4_restart_1 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-D4-RESTART", 1u32, "2026-10-28T14:43Z", "compiler", "compiler 10-28 (split from HOPACSOTA-P3 note 21 at main's call to track D4 as its own row). Today PartEvalEngine Check() (spiral_compiler.fs:53976-53978) RAISES HopacsotaConflict when conflicts+cycles>0 (\"the canonical-order restart (D4) is not built yet, rerun with SPIRAL_HOPACSOTA_POLICY=inline\"). D4 turns that conflict into a DETERMINISTIC RESTART: on a foreign claim of an abandoned key (or a wrong D16.3 return-type hint), abandon the speculative claims and re-run the affected evaluation in canonical (single-flight depth-first) order, yielding SF-hash-equal output. Blocks D16.3 (HOPACSOTA-P3) and MEGA-PARALLEL lever B. Estimate 300m FROM MILESTONES: restart mechanism (abandon speculative claims + canonical re-run) 180m; POSITIVE-CONTROL test (fault injected through the REAL path: force a wrong hint / conflicting claim, REQUIRE a restart then SF-hash-equal output, NOT a raise -- proves the nack fully discards speculative work) 60m; determinism gate under forced conflicts (w1/w2/w4/w8 x5 = SF hash, DISAGREE 0) 60m. Sum = 300m. BLOCKER: a build slot (both heavy slots busy today). deps: none.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_d4_restart_2 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-D4-RESTART", 2u32, "2026-10-29T13:51Z", "compiler", "10-29 09:51 compiler: D4 IMPLEMENTED as a whole-build canonical restart: apps/compiler/packs/apply-hopacsota-d4-restart.ps1, 7 anchored edits. On a HopacsotaConflict (Engine.Check: foreign claims of abandoned keys or wait-for cycles, incl. a cycle raised on a body thread and re-raised at Drain), PartEvalSeams.with_conflict_restart reruns peval FROM SCRATCH with inline_restart = true. peval's tables (join_point_method/closure, ...) are created per call, so no speculative or pending entry survives. start_for returns no session, so every defer evaluates inline = canonical single-flight order, single-flight-hash-equal by construction (P2's inline proof). Plumbing: PartEvalTopEnv.inline_restart on both pair sides; the gpt5parallel driver passes false (it has its own pevalWithInlineRestart); the single-flight/hopacsota driver and single-flight peval change only through PartEvalSeams calls (D10 seam rule). The no-op seams make start_for/with_conflict_restart pass-throughs, so single-flight builds are unchanged. A ThreadLocal or mutable flag was rejected (G2 bans ThreadLocal; overlapping builds would race). Positive control: SPIRAL_HOPACSOTA_FORCE_CONFLICT=1 makes Check raise through the real path, and the Check message no longer says D4 is missing. Scratch: 7/7 anchors; pair-drift 0 one-sided; G1/G2 clean; composes with the P3 shard + IVar appliers (lint and pair-drift clean on all three). PROOF RUNNING on the node (job-1793281990840-compiler-p3d4-proof, mirror pack7check): builds single-flight + hopacsota from the same source (shard + IVar + D4), then measure-arms on apps/spiral/spiral.spi, 2 rounds, arms sf (reference) / w1 / w8 shards16 / w8 shards1 (= IVar alone) / w8 FORCE_CONFLICT. DONE RULE for this row: the forced arm prints the D4 restart line AND its output hash is SAME as sf; every other arm SAME as sf (determinism under load does not depend on wall time). Wall times from that node are not P3 evidence (oversubscribed); P3's speed table runs on a quiet slot.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_d4_restart_3 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-D4-RESTART", 3u32, "2026-10-29T14:40Z", "compiler", "10-29 10:40 compiler: D4 PROVEN on the real path (node job-1793282628758-compiler-p3d4-proof-2; single-flight + hopacsota built from ONE source = HEAD + P3 shard + P3 IVar + D4 core + D4 host; apps/spiral/spiral.spi, --backend Fsharp, gcServer=0). Round 1, every arm exit 0 with output B47B5749C215A6F8 (the same hash as P2's installed single-flight output, HOPACSOTA-P2 n74): sf, w1, w8 shards16, w8 shards1, and w8 SPIRAL_HOPACSOTA_FORCE_CONFLICT=1. The forced arm's stderr shows the engine stats line, then 'hopacsota parallel conflict: 0 foreign claims of abandoned keys, 0 wait-for cycles; restarting the build in canonical single-flight order (D4)', and its output is byte-equal to sf, so the conflict path discards the speculative attempt and the inline rerun reproduces single-flight. Its wall (417 s vs 271 s for w8) is the parallel attempt plus the inline rerun, as designed. A first proof run failed to build (FS0764: the host Program.fs:377 builds a PartEvalTopEnv) and was fixed by apply-hopacsota-d4-restart-host.ps1. Round 2 is running. Left for 100%: n1's full gate under forced conflicts (w1/w2/w4/w8 x5 = sf hash) on a quieter node.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_d4_restart_4 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-D4-RESTART", 4u32, "2026-10-29T15:01Z", "compiler", "10-29 11:01 compiler: round 2 done (job-1793282628758): 10 of 10 runs across 2 rounds output B47B5749C215A6F8 = sf, including the forced-conflict arm both times (restart line printed, output byte-equal). D4's restart is deterministic under load. Remaining for 100%: n1's gate at w1/w2/w4/w8 x5 under FORCE_CONFLICT on a quieter slot.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_d4_restart_5 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-D4-RESTART", 5u32, "2026-10-29T19:16Z", "compiler", "10-29 15:2x compiler: GATE MET, 100%. Forced-conflict matrix job-1793294062916 (node, p3d4 build = 6b + P3 shard/IVar + this item's core and host appliers; entry apps/spiral/spiral.spi to F#; measure-arms 5 rotated rounds; SPIRAL_HOPACSOTA_POLICY=parallel, SHARDS=16, FORCE_CONFLICT=1): w1, w2, w4 and w8, 5 runs each, 20 of 20 exit 0 with output B47B5749C215A6F8, byte-identical to single-flight (sf 5/5 B47B5749). Medians: sf 130 s wall / 123 s CPU; w1force 188 s CPU, w2force 205, w4force 230, w8force 269. The forced arms cost more than unforced w8 (~180 s CPU, P3 runs) and w1 (102 s): that is the abandoned parallel attempt plus the inline canonical-order rerun, so the restart path really ran in every one. The stats' conflicts=0 counts natural conflicts only (FORCE_CONFLICT raises at Engine.Check regardless; earlier proof: 10/10 = sf plus the restart message). Wall times are noisy (load 95-100%, other node jobs ran concurrently) and are not part of this gate. Ships with PACK-7 (apply-hopacsota-d4-restart + apply-hopacsota-d4-restart-host); the single-flight side is a no-op seam (pair-drift 0 one-sided).")
inl profile_wipe_recovery () = Task ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", "Recover from the 2026-10-28 profile wipe: reinstall toolchains, restore configs, rescue live data, map what is lost", TaskKind, P0, D5, 99u32, Blocked, "WIPE-REDO-LEDGER,PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE", "recovery,machine,team:main,wipe-redo,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_profile_wipe_recovery () = Planning ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", Minutes 15u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_1 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 1u32, "2026-10-28T22:19Z", "main", "10-28 18:2x main: INCIDENT. Between ~10:55 and 11:09:34 a recursive delete emptied most of C:\\Users\\i574n (only files held open by running processes survived; free disk 50 -> 421 GB). Cause not found (no PowerShell 4104 events; all pre-wipe transcripts gone). Repos under C:\\home\\git, C:\\ProgramData\\scoop, spiral-bin\\bin + toolchains survived. LOST for every lane: %TEMP% scratchpads and drafts (pack-*, lib-gate-*, tmp-retire, delphi64-matrix, every session scratchpad), %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit job/window/lease state, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\main-archive (cleanup archives), spiral-bin candidates/packs/runs/study/baseline, ~/.claude memory (159 files now PARTIAL recoveries from index + backlog notes), settings + hooks, credentials, all transcripts before 11:09, ~/.ssh + ~/.config/remote-machines.json, ~/.secrets, OneDrive (Desktop/Documents/Pictures), AppData\\Local\\Programs (Swift, VS Code, Zed), scoop apps + persist (browser profile, Telegram, Discord, Electrum data, rclone.conf, rustup, nvm node). HEALED by 18:2x: shell, scoop core + buckets (incl. mold restored as a dotfiles checkout), ~25 apps so far (reinstall in priority order, log in main's scratchpad scoop-bootstrap\\reinstall.log), Rust nightly-2026-10-18 + wasm32 targets, ~/.gitconfig (identity + core.autocrlf=false), remote-machines.json (laptop + node), ~/.ssh config + NEW laptop_ed25519 (node must authorize it: user step), settings.json + tree-lease and stop-gate hooks (pipe-tested; style-check hook not rebuilt), tibia MariaDB rescued from the live server into C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\canary-tables.sql (46 tables; never stop mariadbd 12464 before re-importing), Swift 6.4.1 installing. Every lane, when unpaused: assume your %TEMP% drafts are gone, rebuild from repo state + your backlog notes, and run no cleanup or delete script until the cause is known.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_2 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 2u32, "2026-10-28T22:36Z", "main", "10-28 18:4x main: heal progress + cause evidence. Healed since note 1: python312 (the stall was a robocopy writing through a surviving persist junction to a wiped scoop\\persist target; 55 persist dirs pre-created), uv, Rust nightly-2026-10-18 proven (rustc builds and runs against VS 2022 Community + Windows SDK), mpmath, the mold bucket as a dotfiles checkout plus the vim links, ~/.claude/settings.json gained CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_BG_SHELL_PRESSURE_REAP=1 (it also survives as a User env var), 5 partial memories got verified facts from main's session record. Running: the scoop reinstall, Swift 6.4.1 (winget --skip-dependencies; its Python 3.10 dependency failed with MSI 1603), cupy into python312 (the scoop `python` is 3.15.2, which has no cupy-cuda12x wheel; env.ps1 prefers scoop\\apps\\python\\current, so Python rows need SPIRAL_PYTHON pointed at python312 until cupy ships for 3.15), the WGSL runner rebuild into spiral-bin\\toolchains\\wgsl-run. LOST in spiral-bin, compiler lane's to rebuild: the oracle baseline (EXPECTED.tsv, toolchain.tsv), scoreboards, compile/native memos, r2r-cache, run history, and toolchains bend (bend2), calyx-src (calyxir/calyx d6bcdc8, cider + auxin), kotlinc (scoop kotlin covers it); then a full single-flight -Suite all -Native -Accept. Swift 6.4.1 paths differ from env.ps1's 6.4.0 defaults (set SPIRAL_SWIFTC / SPIRAL_SWIFT_SDK / SPIRAL_SWIFT_RUNTIME or update the defaults). CAUSE evidence (not conclusive): NVWMI logged tibia's spiral-wgsl.exe launches 10:48-11:08:58, so tibia's K4 run (build.ps1 -> Cells run_notebook per file) was active through the window; build.ps1 deletes only target\\ci-metrics. Cells mounts.ex remove! unlinks junctions with an unchecked `cmd /c rmdir` and then File.rm_rf's the mount: a failed unlink lets rm_rf delete through the junction. Current mounts and deps link chains point only at C:\\home\\git repos, so nothing ties it to the profile yet; hardening that cleanup is worth an item. Shadow copies exist only from 12:20 (post-wipe). Full map: C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\loss-map.md.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_3 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 3u32, "2026-10-28T23:00Z", "main", "10-28 main: RESUME CHECKLIST per lane (read before your first heavy job; full map C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\loss-map.md). Everyone: /login, then expect every %TEMP% draft and session scratchpad to be gone; the repos, lib and the backlog are intact; do not run any cleanup or delete script; kit job/window/lease history is empty (node-side jobs and mirrors on laptop-6e8c14g survive, reachable once the user authorizes the new key). compiler: rebuild the unlanded apply scripts (DELPHI NOREGVAR prelude, RUST-EMIT-UNIT-ARG, GLEAM-COMPACT pack, OpenQasm tanh + Bend float packs and samples) from your backlog notes; rebuild the native toolchains still missing (bend2 + bun; Swift 6.4.1 is installed but swiftc dies 0xC0000142); then a full single-flight -Suite all -Native -Accept to recreate the lost oracle baseline; the cache SDK is now 11.0.100-rc.3; FPC is scoop 3.2.2 (trunk 3.3.1 is gone). fiscal: the xsd-any-complements-writer, ubl-json-transcoder and json_schema (54CFD0B2) drafts are gone, rebuild from your notes (the transcoder silent-drop fix included); node proofs may still hold results. tibia: re-import C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\canary-tables.sql into a fresh datadir BEFORE mariadbd 12464 stops (its data dir is empty); the canary server install (tibia-local\\canary) is gone; the LIB-PORT-HIDE staged lib copy is gone (the build.ps1 canary edit survived); K4 must re-run. kit: TRAIN3 never published (the kit tree is unchanged since 09h); its snapshot zip and all of %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit state are gone; re-run TRAIN3 from the repo. x: the GLEAM-COMPACT compact.do draft is gone; the 3 untracked e2e files survived in the repo; node verify outputs may survive in C:\\home\\remote-stage on the node.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_4 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 4u32, "2026-10-28T23:10Z", "main", "10-28 19:1x main: TOOLCHAIN PROOF. test.ps1 -Suite smoke -Native (run single-flight-20261028-185810, 159 rows, SPIRAL_CC = scoop gcc 15.2): every row compiles (Zig's contract_illegal_transition error is the expected rejection); C, Rust, Delphi (FPC 3.2.2), F#, Gleam, Kotlin, Lua, OpenQasm, Python (python312 + cupy via SPIRAL_PYTHON), Wasm, WGSL (runner rebuilt from tests/native-shims/wgsl-run) and eBPF agree with the C oracle on every row, DISAGREE 0. Lean's 10 rows timed out while elan downloaded v4.35.0 on first use (installing it now, then re-run Lean + Calyx rows). Not runnable yet: Swift (every toolchain binary crashes at startup, 0xC0000142/0xC0000409, even after VC++ 14.51; a forced reinstall is running), Bend and TypeScript (bun queued), Calyx (cider + auxin built at 19:04, after the run started). Committed sample outputs regenerated byte-identical. Also healed since note 3: ~/.claude.json restored from the live sessions' post-wipe backups; the compiler cache SDK reinstalled (11.0.100-rc.3; it had been gutted to 27 files); User env vars DOTNET_ROOT, MSBuildSDKsPath and DOTNET_HOME that the reinstall added (absent before the wipe) removed; SPIRAL_SWIFT* point at 6.4.1; the tree-lease hook verified live.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_5 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 5u32, "2026-10-28T23:53Z", "main", "10-28 19:5x main: BACKENDS PROVEN against the C oracle (smoke -Native, SPIRAL_CC = scoop gcc 15.2): C, Rust, Delphi (FPC 3.2.2), F#, Gleam, Kotlin, Lua, OpenQasm, Python (python312 + cupy), Wasm, WGSL (rebuilt runner), eBPF (run 185810), Calyx 4/4 + TypeScript 10/10 (run 194804, cider + auxin rebuilt from calyxir/calyx d6bcdc8 with Rust 1.90; bun 1.4.4), Bend 10/10 (run 195252; bend2 now lives at github.com/bendlang/bend, cloned shallow into spiral-bin\\toolchains\\bend at 4f99f4c; upstream rewrites history per release). DISAGREE 0 everywhere. Open: Lean (v4.35.0 toolchain: elan deadlocked on its own lock three times, now downloading the release zip directly), Swift (6.4.1 reinstalled twice; every toolchain binary still crashes at startup: compiler lane). Also restored: VS Code + Zed (per-user), Node 26.13.0, babashka, clj-deps, monaspace, buckets scoop-clojure/nerd-fonts/rasa; git credential.helper back to manager (GCM 2.9.1; GitHub credential survived in Windows Credential Manager). No scoop PATH entry lost to the concurrent installs (path-check 0 missing).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_6 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 6u32, "2026-10-29T00:01Z", "main", "10-28 20:0x main: Lean PROVEN 10/10 vs C (run 195908) on v4.35.0, installed from the official leanprover/lean4 release zip into scoop\\persist\\elan\\.elan\\toolchains\\leanprover--lean4---v4.35.0 after elan deadlocked three times on its own install lock. Every smoke backend now agrees with C except Swift. Swift handoff to the compiler lane: 6.4.1 installed twice (second with --force); swiftc dies 0xC0000142 and the toolchain's clang, lld-link and swift-frontend die 0xC0000409 at startup, with a minimal PATH, through cmd, and with VC++ 14.51 (all six runtime DLLs updated, no pending renames); scoop LLVM clang 23.1.4 runs fine; the binaries are full size. Untried: the skipped Python 3.10 dependency (winget's Python 3.10 MSI fails 1603, likely a stale per-user registration whose files were wiped) and Swift 6.4.0. FPC handoff: scoop only offers 3.2.2 (installed; Delphi smoke rows agree on it); trunk 3.3.1-21298 is gone and its install method isn't recorded.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_7 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 7u32, "2026-10-29T00:19Z", "main", "10-28 20:2x main: Swift, last attempts: 6.4.0 (pre-wipe version, env.ps1's default) refuses to install beside 6.4.1 (MSI 1638, another version installed), and winget uninstall Swift.Toolchain finds no per-user package to remove. Next (compiler lane or user): uninstall Swift 6.4.1 via Settings -> Apps, winget install --id Swift.Toolchain --version 6.4.0 --scope user --skip-dependencies, then delete the User vars SPIRAL_SWIFTC / SPIRAL_SWIFT_SDK / SPIRAL_SWIFT_RUNTIME so the 6.4.0 defaults apply. Final env/PATH checks clean: 0 scoop PATH entries missing; User env differs from the pre-reinstall baseline only by bun's and uv's data-dir vars and main's SPIRAL_PYTHON / SPIRAL_SWIFT*. Leftover-process sweep clean (only the running scoop download). The scoop reinstall loop keeps running past 21:00 in main's session (log: main scratchpad scoop-bootstrap\\reinstall.log; ~80 of 137 done at 20:18, the rest are desktop apps and tools).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_8 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 8u32, "2026-10-29T00:21Z", "main", "10-28 20:2x main: wider proof, -Suite frontier -Native (run single-flight-20261028-201908, 174 rows, 13 samples): Bend, C, Calyx, Delphi, F#, Gleam, Kotlin, Lean, Lua, OpenQasm, Python, Rust, TypeScript, Wasm, WGSL and Zig agree with C on every row, DISAGREE 0; non-ok compiles only on the two deliberate negative samples; Swift build-fails 11/11 (handoff in note 7); committed outputs byte-identical. The machine is usable for every lane except Swift rows; what remains is user-side (logins, node key, secrets) and the compiler lane's oracle re-accept.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_9 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 9u32, "2026-10-29T00:25Z", "main", "10-28 20:2x main: Swift, two more rule-outs. (1) Files: msiexec /fa repair of all seven 6.4.1 MSIs (exit 0 each) changed nothing. (2) Environment: clang.exe and swiftc.exe die 0xC0000142 with an environment holding only SystemRoot/TEMP/3-entry PATH. 0xC0000142 matches desktop-heap exhaustion of the agent's non-interactive session (user32-loading programs only). Decisive test is the user's: swiftc --version in a normal terminal tab. Stale pre-wipe registrations remain (HKCU Swift Developer Toolkit 6.4.0, HKLM Swift Android Platform Support 6.4.0) with no files; they block installing 6.4.0 (MSI 1638).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_10 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 10u32, "2026-10-29T00:27Z", "main", "10-28 20:3x main: CORRECTION to note 9: desktop-heap exhaustion is ruled out. swiftc --version run on the interactive desktop through a one-off schtasks /it task (deleted right after) also exits 0xC0000142, so Swift 6.4.1 is genuinely broken on this machine, not only in agent shells. Next: uninstall Swift 6.4.1 plus the stale 6.4.0 registrations via Settings -> Apps, then install 6.4.0 (env.ps1's default) and delete the SPIRAL_SWIFT* User vars.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_11 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 11u32, "2026-10-29T01:21Z", "main", "Swift healed 21:2x. 6.4.1 uninstalled via its bundle (Package Cache {8ECD6BAA-...} installer.exe /uninstall /quiet, exit 0) and 6.4.0 reinstalled (winget, user scope); same crash, so the version was never the cause. Procmon trace of swiftc --version: every DLL resolved (VC++ 14.51 from System32), then WerFault; Application log event 1000 names the toolchain's own mimalloc.dll (0xC0000005, offset 0xcd20). MIMALLOC_DISABLE_REDIRECT=1 fixes swiftc, swift-frontend, clang and lld-link; a test program compiles, links and runs. Set at User scope; SPIRAL_SWIFTC/SDK/RUNTIME removed (env.ps1's 6.4.0 defaults apply). Shells older than 21:2x need the variable set by hand. Root cause of the redirect failure unknown (OS DLLs unchanged since 2023, no IFEO, no MIMALLOC_* in any surviving record). Smoke -Native re-run queued to prove the Swift rows.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_12 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 12u32, "2026-10-29T01:31Z", "main", "FPC trunk restored 21:2x from the recipe in FPC-TRUNK-EVERYWHERE note 1 (archive): official snapshot zips (i386 + x86_64 built on i386) hash the same as the 10-25 install (320759F0DC48DA0A / 2206D8D866360844), so fpc -iW = 3.3.1-21298-g814ece0205 again, byte-identical to the node. Extracted to scoop\\apps\\freepascal\\3.3.1-20261025, fpcmkcfg, read-only current junction repointed, 3.2.2 kept. Proven: Delphi agrees with C on smoke 10/10 (single-flight-20261028-213009) and frontier 11/11 (single-flight-20261028-213022; the other 2 are the negative samples); git status unchanged. Also restored ~\\.wslconfig as recorded in NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE note 2 ([wsl2] memory=12GB; other keys unrecorded).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_13 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 13u32, "2026-10-29T01:35Z", "main", "Style hook rebuilt (EOIE-HEAL-EDIT-HOOK note 4), pipe-tested 9/9, wired into settings.json PostToolUse. Loss map updated: Swift, FPC trunk, .wslconfig and the style hook move from lost to healed.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_14 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 14u32, "2026-10-29T01:45Z", "main", "21:4x main: scoop reinstall loop finished 21:43 (every surviving app folder reinstalled except graalvm-nightly-jdk17, lassie, nftup: no manifest; processhacker: superseded; rustdesk-nightly: upstream hash drift, stable rustdesk installed; azuredatastudio-insiders: product retired, host gone). Scoop core self-update stuck: the git clone in apps\\scoop\\new is ready but the user's Windows PowerShell tab (pid 18068) holds YamlDotNet.dll in current; swap after it closes. Config snapshot outside the profile: C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\profile-snapshot-20261028-2137 (no private keys) + toolchain-zips (FPC trunk). Correction: the style-hook note is EOIE-HEAL-EDIT-HOOK note 5, not 4. Remaining user steps: /login per tab (peers unregistered), node key (still rejected 21:39), secrets, OneDrive/Electrum checks, clean exits of long-running apps, close the PowerShell tab.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_15 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 15u32, "2026-10-29T06:31Z", "main", "10-29 02:3x main: overnight heals so far (each recorded in its own item):\n(1) Lost drafts rebuilt in committable places: the COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE mover plus its apply and undo (apps/compiler/packs/tmp-retire, rehearsed 11/11; n29-n30); the NOREGVAR applier (packs/apply-delphi64-noregvar.ps1; all 413 Delphi residuals agree 32/64-bit with it; DELPHI-64BIT-DFA-DISAGREE n7); the host splitArgs applier (packs/apply-rust-emit-unit-arg.ps1; RUST-EMIT-UNIT-ARG n9); the kit Export codemod (i574n.github/scripts/bang-export-rewrite.ps1, reproducing n35's numbers; BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP n38); am'.average's Rust arm (staged; LIB-DOTNET-ONLY-BODIES n11).\n(2) The oracle baseline rebuild is running: run 1 was stopped at 14 min when its phase line showed the Swift batch building 0 of 451. The agent shell's environment predates tonight's User env and lacked 17 registry variables (MIMALLOC_DISABLE_REDIRECT, SDKROOT, SPIRAL_PYTHON, KOTLIN_HOME and others). The wrapper now imports them (names logged), and run 1b is job main-oracle-review-1b. Side result of run 1: all 7,367 compiles rewrote the committed samples byte-identically (git status samples: 0).\n(3) 9 memory files rebuilt from evidence (listed in MEMORY.md line 1).\n(4) Node: the client side is verified (ssh config uses ~/.ssh/laptop_ed25519 with IdentitiesOnly; the public line is main-to-laptop-2026-10-28, SHA256:/wzdU2nSCfzQQt/8r3R9tLa7Fy66GkxN9NCiyzYZK2c); still rejected, because the laptop's administrators_authorized_keys holds the old line.\n(5) mariadbd 12464 is still alive. Its install dir holds only 5 files, so the tibia re-import first needs MariaDB installed into a separate version folder (loss map updated). PowerShell tab 18068 is still open, so the scoop core swap still waits.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_16 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 16u32, "2026-10-29T07:50Z", "main", "10-29 03:5x main: ORACLE BASELINE REBUILT (the wipe had taken spiral-bin\\baseline). Installed compiler: host A4E480202BD40D80; the tree core equals HEAD cec8840c. SPIRAL_CC pinned to scoop gcc 15.2, and the jobs import the 17 registry variables the agent shell lacked. (1) Review run single-flight-20261029-022008 (job main-oracle-review-1b, 44 min, 3 workers): 7,367 jobs (contracts 728, examples 6,569, frontier 65, mega 5); native 6,846 ran, 9 build-fail, oracle agree 6,118, DISAGREE 0; git status samples: 0, so every compile reproduced the committed outputs byte-identically. (2) Cross-check against CI run 40691709422 (Linux, same commit; its compiler-oracle artifact): with both sides on the same toolchain only 14 behavior rows differ, all explained. zig_exit_wide (7 backends) is 305 vs 49 (8-bit exit codes on Linux). abi_external_buffer_length_negative and managed_string_invalid_utf8_slice abort: 3 on Windows vs 134 SIGABRT. native_cube_* are known POSIX-only. mega_omniledger_erp_kernel [F#] spawns /bin/sh (POSIX-only, no Known entry). dynamic_array_reserve_zero [C] is a real latent use-after-free in its shim, filed as C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS. The 112 residual diffs are CI-OFFLOAD n35's CRLF naming. (3) Accept run single-flight-20261029-030844 (job main-oracle-accept-2, 41 min, 4 workers): identical totals, and compare-runs against the review: 0 differing cells over 7,367 rows (residual hashes included). Accepted 7,367 rows into spiral-bin\\baseline\\EXPECTED.tsv (03:49), with toolchain.tsv recorded. The next review or accept compares against it.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_17 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 17u32, "2026-10-29T08:17Z", "main", "10-29 04:1x main: HEALED a silent post-wipe break: sccache was gone. The spiral CLI's rust command (apps/spiral/spiral.spi:257) sets RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache for every Rust cell built with dependencies ('rust -d ...'), and scripts/init.ps1:78-80 had installed sccache with 'cargo binstall' into ~\\.cargo\\bin, which the wipe deleted. cargo now runs from scoop rustup, and cargo-binstall is gone too. So every 'rust -d' Cells test failed before compiling: 'could not execute process sccache ...rustc.exe -vV (never executed) ... program not found'. Found by main's lib file_system gate (its control and fixed arms both failed for this reason, so that run was VOID). Installed: scoop install sccache gives 0.19.0 from the main bucket (hash OK), shim C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\shims\\sccache.exe; the exact failing call 'sccache <nightly-2026-10-18 rustc> -vV' now prints rustc 1.101.0-nightly. Main's lib sweep (job main-lib-sweep) started before the install; the files it reached by then had no failing rows.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_18 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 18u32, "2026-10-29T08:18Z", "main", "10-29 04:2x main: the rest of init.ps1's ~\\.cargo\\bin tools, checked by running Get-Command for each: cargo-binstall and trunk were missing too. Installed the way init.ps1 does it: scoop install cargo-binstall gives 1.26.1 (hash OK), then 'cargo binstall -y --locked trunk@0.21.14' (init.ps1:72) puts trunk.exe in C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\persist\\rustup\\.cargo\\bin, on PATH; trunk --version prints 'trunk 0.21.14'. Still missing: Playwright's browsers. init.ps1:91's 'bunx --bun playwright@1.44.0 install' downloads from the retired playwright.azureedge.net (HTTP 400 on CI too), so it needs the Playwright pin bumped in init.ps1 and the three package.json files (spiral lib/spiral/near/wallet, dice ui/e2e, polyglot apps/spiral/temp/extension), then an e2e run.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_19 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 19u32, "2026-10-29T09:17Z", "main", "10-29 05:1x main: FIRST FULL LIB GATE on the post-wipe toolchains (job main-lib-sweep, lib_sweep.ps1 over the live lib, compiler A4E480202BD40D80, registry env imported, SPIRAL_CC gcc 15.2; rows in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\lib-sweep-20261029.tsv). 73 files with test blocks, 515 tests discovered, 421 passed, 21 failed, 0 type errors, 71 min. All 21 failures sit in 8 files. Six of them fail every test with Cells' 'package spiral is listed twice' (cells.ex:1112): decimal, dictm, float_text, json_schema, schematron and schematron_run open with '///- --package .', and inside lib that names lib itself, which Cells already adds for a lib notebook. The headers came on 10-24 (0ec501fb); the duplicate check dates from 10-17. The other two, lustre.spi (2/2) and near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi (2/2), are being read. Every other file passes, including am'.spi 17/17 with tonight's average test and json_scan. sccache was reinstalled 11 minutes into the sweep (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n17); the 'rust -d' files it reached before that (am', array_dim, async, base, benchmark, channel) show no failures.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_20 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 20u32, "2026-10-29T10:40Z", "main", "10-29 06:4x main: lib after tonight's heals: 439 of 516 tests pass across 73 files, 0 type errors, and only the 4 lustre_ui Hex-conflict tests fail (LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE n5). Node still rejects the new key (06:4x).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_21 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 21u32, "2026-10-29T11:22Z", "main", "10-29 07:2x main: NODE REACHABLE again, with redundancy. Causes, in order: (1) the node account is 'alias', not i574n (the sshd log said 'Invalid user i574n'); (2) administrators_authorized_keys needed one clean key line and SYSTEM+Administrators-only access; (3) the 10-28 private key had an accidental passphrase (PowerShell 7 passes -N '\\\"\\\"' as two quote characters), so the client could not sign in BatchMode (archived as laptop_ed25519.passphrase-*.bak). Now: User alias in ~/.ssh/config; 3 route aliases (laptop = LAN name, laptop-ip = 192.168.2.28, laptop-ts = 100.97.57.53); 2 passphrase-free keys, both authorized and each tested alone; remote-machines.json gains lanAddresses. i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1 Resolve-MachineAddress (unstaged, inside the file's existing unstaged changes) now probes every candidate route with a no-op login and caches the winner; with no route working it reports each as 'port 22 unreachable' or 'login refused'. Controls: dead LAN plus live Tailscale falls through to 100.97.57.53; all routes dead gives '192.0.2.1 (port 22 unreachable: a network problem)'. New i574n.github/scripts/node-reach.ps1: 3 routes x 2 keys OK, the git ssh client OK, node pwsh OK. The node side was already sound: sshd Automatic with restart on failure, port 22 allowed on all profiles, the Tailscale adapter Private. Node mirrors survived (C:\\home\\remote 46, C:\\home\\remote-stage 273); a name search found delphi64-probe-instrumented.ps1 and the renameproof/*.do and tibia-gaps land/undo programs.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_22 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 22u32, "2026-10-29T11:28Z", "tibia-lane", "10-29 07:28 tibia: MARIADB HEALED (checklist n3, tibia item 1). MariaDB 13.0.2 (the scoop main manifest, sha256 verified) was installed into apps\\mariadb\\13.0.2 without touching current. A fresh datadir was initialized with root password canary (per live\\world.ps1) and imported on side port 3318: CREATE DATABASE canary, then canary-tables.sql and canary-active_livestream_casters.sql. Result: 47 tables, row counts equal to the still-running pid 12464 on all 47 (0 mismatches), and CHECKSUM TABLE EXTENDED equal on all 15 non-empty tables (accounts 1, players 7, player_items 22, player_deaths 31, towns 8, ...). Cutover: both servers shut down gracefully with mariadb-admin. The emptied old datadir (only ib_buffer_pool after shutdown) is archived to C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\mariadb-data-emptied-20261029-0727. The new one is promoted to tibia-local\\mariadb-data (my.ini port 3317). scoop current is repointed to 13.0.2; it is a read-only junction, so attrib -R /L, rmdir, junction, attrib +R /L. manifest.json and install.json were added, so scoop list shows 13.0.2. The 12.1.2 skeleton is kept. Consumer path: live\\world.ps1 Start brings the DB up (then throws at canary.exe, which is still gone: item 2), and Status gives database=True. mariadbd now runs as pid 3868 from current\\bin. Pid 12464 is gone, so that guard is lifted. Trap for later: world.ps1 Stop kills any mariadbd under current\\bin.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_23 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 23u32, "2026-10-29T12:52Z", "main", "10-29 08:5x main: three wipe leftovers rechecked and closed. (1) Swift WORKS: swiftc 6.4 RELEASE (Toolchains\\6.4.0+Asserts) answers --version with MIMALLOC_DISABLE_REDIRECT=1 from the User env, so the 0xC0000142 handoff (n7) is resolved by that variable, as kit-env-in-old-shells says. The stale HKCU and HKLM 6.4.0 registrations are harmless while 6.4.0 is installed. (2) The scoop core swap is unblocked: PowerShell tab 18068 is gone and 'scoop update' succeeds (core e6aa3b36 = 0.6.0, the newest; buckets refreshed). (3) The node key works since 07:0x (3 routes x 2 keys, REMOTE-LAPTOP-LANE). Left: 'scoop update *' for apps WAITS for a quiet window after TRAIN3 and the pack-6 install, because toolchains must not swap under live trains. User-side, by name only: /login per tab, ~/.secrets/x-api.env, rclone.conf (0 bytes), OneDrive's online recycle bin (30 days from 10-28), Electrum, and the canary server install (tibia).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_24 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 24u32, "2026-10-29T15:18Z", "main", "10-29 11:2x main: scoop status after the core update. Only 4 minor app updates are pending (antigravity, neovim-nightly, opencode2, vlc-nightly), no toolchains, so the 19:33 'scoop update *' window is small. FOUND: 5 apps are 'Install failed, Manifest removed': fork, greenshot, notepadplusplus, systeminformer-nightly and wfc. Each has an apps\\<app>\\current folder but no manifest.json, so they run from half-installed folders. They are exactly the processes whose open handles survived the wipe, which is why the reinstall loop skipped them. Fork (since 10-27), Greenshot (since 10-07), Notepad++ and SystemInformer are STILL RUNNING, so reinstall them after the user closes them (user step). wfc (Windows Firewall Control) is not running, but it is security software, so its reinstall is the user's call. Also listed: azuredatastudio-insiders and rustdesk-nightly 'Install failed' (retired / superseded by stable rustdesk, n15); 'scoop uninstall' cleans their status rows, after the user confirms.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_25 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 25u32, "2026-10-29T21:27Z", "main", "10-29 17:2x main: memory recovery progress. 175 memory files; 130 still carry the PARTIAL RECOVERY banner. Rebuilt or rewritten by main this afternoon from today's evidence: live-runs-alone, recompile-drafts-after-compiler-change, keep-node-busy (all three partly reconstructed, sources cited in each). New today: ps-wrapper-exit-semantics and backend-probe-runners (the second records how six lib bugs surfaced). kit rebuilt backend-switch-idiom and part of heavy-gate-lessons. MEMORY.md line 1 lists every rebuilt file. The rest stay partial by design: each is rewritten when its fact comes up, never guessed.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_26 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 26u32, "2026-10-29T22:46Z", "main", "10-29 18:46 main, closing for 10-29: recovery is at the move-forward state; see WIPE-REDO-LEDGER's closing note. Left for the USER: /login per tab; re-issue x-api.env; rclone.conf (0 bytes, holds credentials); Electrum; the OneDrive online recycle bin (a possible restore source that EXPIRES around 11-27); close, then scoop-reinstall Fork, Greenshot, Notepad++, SystemInformer and wfc; the durable mirror schedule (scheduled task vs hook, PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE n7); one commit in spiral (apps/compiler/scripts plus 39 stubs, 26 moved files and type_probe.ps1, together with the day's 56 lib/Cells entries). Memories: 130 of 175 still carry the partial banner, rebuilt as their facts come up.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_27 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 27u32, "2026-10-29T23:05Z", "main", "10-29 19:05 main: found and healed a wipe artifact. On 10-28 at 17:54 the scoop reinstall wrote 7 Start Menu shortcuts (cmake-gui, PowerShell Core, 7-Zip File Manager and Help, Git Bash, CMD and GUI) as untracked spiral/Programs/Scoop Apps, because the profile's Start Menu was missing. All 7 targets exist. The shortcuts are copied into the real Start Menu\\Programs\\Scoop Apps (hash-verified) and the repo copy is archived at C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\stray-programs-in-spiral. No other stray Programs\\Scoop Apps exists under C:\\home, C:\\home\\git\\* or the profile. Close-out for the user's commit: C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1029\\commit-suggestion.md (git-a6 confirmed all of tmp/samples plus matrix.psd1 stay out until the pack-7 accept).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_28 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 28u32, "2026-10-29T23:30Z", "main", "10-29 19:30 main, NEW wipe loss (not in any ledger until now): the gh CLI extension 'actions-lock' (v0.2.0, installed 10-22) is gone. gh extension list is empty, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\GitHub CLI\\extensions doesn't exist, and 'gh actions-lock' gives 'unknown command'. gh 2.103.3 itself and its config.yml/hosts.yml are present. Impact: every workflow edit that changes a uses: line needs 'gh actions-lock --no-interactive' to regenerate .github/workflows/actions.lock, or the workflow fails at startup with no log (memory actions-lock-on-workflow-edits). No workflow edit can land until it's reinstalled. USER STEP: reinstalling is a download, so it waits on the user's yes and source; the backlog never recorded the extension's repository. Found while re-checking CI-ACTIONS-LATEST. CORRECTION (10-29 20:19, sweep 9): the source WAS recorded, in archive/done-notes.spi (CI-ACTIONS-LOCKFILE n1, 10-17: 'installed gh extension github/gh-actions-lock'; n6/n7, 10-19: v0.2.0, latest). My grep covered only state/agile.spi. The USER STEP is now exact: 'gh extension install github/gh-actions-lock' (a download, so it needs the user's yes), then 'gh actions-lock --no-interactive --no-fix' in each repo with an actions.lock as the positive control.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_29 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 29u32, "2026-10-29T23:36Z", "main", "10-29 19:36 main, machine upkeep SKIPPED (scheduled 19:33): git-a6's pack-7 review (job-1793314021578) is running and holds heavy-build window win-1793314021784-17040 (253 min left). A scoop update plus the toolchain runs would be box work under a compile-quiet window. Not run: scoop update *, the toolchain checks, the User env diff. Next chance: next session, after the review and the pack-7 install (the install is a CompilerInstall window, so run upkeep after it, not alongside). Hourly profile mirror at 19:34: OK (7935 files, 229.3 MB, node C:/home/profile-mirror/profile-mirror-20261029-193449.tgz, sha256 6581DE78...). CORRECTION (10-29 20:19, sweep 9): this 'OK' was WRONG. The 19:34 archive (profile-mirror-20261029-193449.tgz) is TRUNCATED (1 entry), as found minutes later (PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE n10). Its sha256 matched only because the check compared the copy with the local file. Fixed since 904250655ECB; the 19:39 and 20:05 archives list fully.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_30 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 30u32, "2026-10-30T02:02Z", "main", "10-29 22:02 main, the USER's 21:54 ask: heal dangling processes on both machines, groom for 10 min, have the lanes do the same (all 5 lanes asked at 21:54).\nHEAL (main): 0 dangling processes of main's on the box or the node. Box: main's tree = claude 27220 + the running command's shells only; 0 of 24 interesting processes have a dead parent (positive control: the same test finds 16 boot-time orphans of any name). Node: 63 interesting processes, all explained: the node user's 304-day desktop terminals; x's xv30 verify and x-verify32 (6.2 h, alive: stdout 21:57); fiscal's sgnset2; one 6-min elixir.bat orphan in x's xqueue2 (routed to x). Not dangling and not main's: box kit job node-watch (job host claude 28236, 24 h timeout, deliberate). git-a6's 3 overnight node jobs FINISHED exit 0 (missed at first because the node's job list shows only the latest 20).\nGROOM (main, 21:57:50-22:07:50): 19 stale Actives Paused by the WIP rule, progress kept (main Active 69 -> 50); DOTA plus 2 Planned children Paused/P4 as superseded by the user's 10-25 WoW pivot, with DOTA-LUA-BINDINGS cross-linked to WOW-LUA-SANDBOX as prior art; 3 sizing questions where estimates have no milestones (KINO-WITHOUT-ELIXIR, LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS, TOOLCHAIN-LATEST); 4 Planned items marked READY (all deps Done: HOPACSOTA-P4, QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER, EXECUTABLE-ATLAS, CODEGEN-READABLE-2); 3 stale Blocked items re-verified. Ownership findings routed: 122 open items tagged eoie but not kit are invisible to --team kit (rename gap; kit to run migrate-tags preview), and 4 FISCAL items are double-owned via a main tag (fiscal to drop it).\nLANES: kit reported (0 dangling; 11 items groomed). x, fiscal, git-a6 and tibia are pending. LANE REPORTS (22:05): KIT: 0 dangling; 11 items groomed, all fields filled; built a guarded per-item retag for the 122 eoie->kit items (applies next session in a quiet moment). FISCAL: 0 dangling (its live sgnset2 tree kept); M6 HOLDS 24/24 post-land; Peppol/ZATCA/UBL-TR progress raised; dropped 'main' from its 4 double-owned items (verified team fiscal only); every open fiscal item has all fields filled. X: 0 dangling. The node's Cells compiler daemon (cmd 15160 -> erl -> 3 dotnet) detaches by design and retires after 30 min idle. Groomed 9 items: X-WIP-VERIFY and 3 others re-opened from a premature Done (re-proof pending). FOUND by x: x-s3 RED/VOID (5 overweight cells failed x-compat, so parity ran on old modules); verify33's launcher regex never matched '0 finding(s)' (fixed); the node clock runs about 95 s ahead of the box (last NTP sync 14:12); a half-open node sshd-session 20748/21764 from 20:36 with a dead client and unprovable owner, LEFT ALONE (harmless). node-watch (box job host 28236) is the compiler lane's. git-a6 and tibia are pending. UPDATE (22:08): GIT-A6: 0 dangling. node-watch is its deliberate 24 h node monitor, kept. Groomed: COMPILER-CROSS-MACHINE-REPRO Done (the node rebuild hash-matches the box); broke a PACK-7 <-> RUST-DERIVE-INFERENCE cycle; 3 pack riders now depend on PACK-7; COMPILER-GEN0-BUDGET DECIDED 64 MB, with the 'peak never grows' claim withdrawn (small compiles +138 MB at 256). FOUND: kit agile check fails because KIT_DOTNET/SPIRAL_DOTNET were lost in the wipe (routed to kit). DEPENDENCY CYCLES, by main's whole-backlog scan: 3 distinct. (1) fiscal broke EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML -> SYMBOLS-MIGRATION, but EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION -> FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND -> EDITION3-280-SPLIT -> SYMBOLS-MIGRATION remained. The user's 10-19 text says the split comes AFTER the migration, so fiscal was asked to drop FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND -> 280-SPLIT. (2) WIPE-REDO-LEDGER -> PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY was backwards; main dropped it. (3) C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP <-> KINO-C-FLAGS-PARITY: both Done, historical, left. TIBIA pending. CYCLES RESOLVED (22:09): fiscal dropped FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND -> EDITION3-280-SPLIT (n14). Its deps are now 3 Done items plus its own EDITION3-SPIRAL-TOML, and any fiscal cell over 280 is split inside the round. Rescan: 1 distinct cycle left in the whole backlog, C-SELF-TAIL-LOOP <-> KINO-C-FLAGS-PARITY, both Done, so it blocks nothing.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_31 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 31u32, "2026-10-30T10:32Z", "main", "10-30 06:32 main: the REINSTALL ENV TRAP recurred. At 06:23, after the reboot, scoop apps dotnet3-sdk and dotnet-nightly were rewritten (by whom is unknown; no scoop process was running by 06:34), and dotnet3-sdk's manifest env_set put User DOTNET_ROOT=scoop\\apps\\dotnet3-sdk\\current and MSBuildSDKsPath=...\\sdk\\3.1.426\\Sdks back (found by the user's git-51 session). Both are known traps: they didn't exist before the wipe, and the user's own setting is the DISABLED _MSBuildSDKsPath. Main removed them from User env again at 06:34 (backup C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1030\\user-env-removed-0634.txt); the bundled .NET 11 SDK still resolves. Lanes were told to check their process env. LEFT for the user: DOTNET_HOME=scoop\\apps\\dotnet-nightly\\current (provenance unknown, so not removed). Lasting fix, the user's call: hold or uninstall dotnet3-sdk so the next scoop update can't re-apply env_set.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_32 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 32u32, "2026-10-30T14:09Z", "heal", "Heal lane 614162e5, 10-30 06:30-10:30: deep undelete finished; nothing more is recoverable. C: is BitLocker + SSD TRIM, so deleted clusters read as noise (verified on PhysicalDrive0: TRIMmed sectors are all zero; 300/300 sampled trimmed clusters were noise). Only MFT-resident files (< ~700 B) and a few hundred partial text files came back: ~380k files, ~0.75 GB of verified content. Layout C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\: originals in place where the path was free; Temp and orphans (_lost) under the root; partial\\ (noise runs replaced by \"<<< N KB lost >>>\" markers); conflicts\\; skip-resident\\ (app configs); noise\\ = 16.5 GB of garbage, safe to delete. Per-lane draft status: lane-lists-status.md (main 9/90 recovered, kit 0/71); per-file verdicts: triage-*.tsv, restore-report-*.tsv. Carved transcript lines (890, almost all post-wipe): node C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\carved-sessions\\<sid>.jsonl. Also done: ~/.ssh a + codespaces.auto back in place (old laptop_ed25519 in conflicts\\); Notepad++ 8.9.8.1 reinstalled with a 6-tab session.xml; greenshot, systeminformer-nightly, mariadb (persist data kept) and rustdesk-nightly reinstalled; buckets games/Ash258/dorado/emulators/retools/scoopet re-added (the jetbrains repo no longer exists); known folders Favorites/NetHood/PrintHood/Startup/Templates recreated; node: 27 idle rust target dirs, 42 node_modules/obj, scoop cache and NuGet cache removed (~15 GB). Lost for good: Edge Bookmarks (never synced), OneDrive Documents (check its online recycle bin), all pre-wipe transcripts, lane drafts > 700 B. Left for the user: FancyZones relink (live layouts newer than mold's); wfc 6.11 hash mismatch upstream (6.9.9.3 kept); azuredatastudio-insiders retired (host gone).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_33 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 33u32, "2026-10-30T14:12Z", "x", "2026-10-30 x, batched after healing's all-clear: x's wipe recovery is COMPLETE except one artifact. Method: main's read-only lost-path census for author x (C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\tools\\lost-paths-by-author.ps1 -Author x; agile.spi + archive/done-notes.spi notes <= 10-28): 217 TEMP/profile/scratchpad paths in 59 items, 153 under Done/archived items (harmless), 64 under open items, each classified: (a) already in WIPE-REDO-LEDGER (x-world sim drafts = live modules now; x-simland-0214 and x-precommit-next dropped with reasons; x-shell redone as x/scripts/sim-shell.ps1, proven; X-DONE's landing tools for landed work); (b) results recorded in the citing note (EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION n32 inventory script, X-PARALLEL-CENSUS n3 scratch copies, LIST-SUGAR-SCAN n3 tool after its 148-site refactor landed, EOIE-GENERATED-PROFILE n1 stopgap measure.ps1 whose method the note describes); (c) the draft landed (LIB-PAR-MAP n10 par'.spi is in lib since 10-26; POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS n2 M1 PreviewThreads is in apps/client cli.spi and fields.spi; X-FRAMES-SPLIT landed n84). The one artifact absent from every node mirror (live xunits + all 9 archived x mirrors under C:\\home\\remote-archive\\20261029-x-preretire carry spiral.ex 5AA365731E1A with no unit routing), the X-HAND-UNITS G1 Elixir routing, CAME BACK via healing's undelete (MFT-resident, triage verdict 'good' 1.00): C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--home-git\\b7595ac3-...\\scratchpad\\gleam-units\\ spiral-ex.do (405 B; one anchored replace in apps/sim/lib/xsim/spiral.ex: @units map checked_text/commute_text/breaking_text/masked_text -> :xsim_checks, world_files -> :xsim_world, default :xsim_flow) + frames-gleam.toml, checks/flow/world gleam.toml. Opened and read; content is whole and matches the G1 design. Archived to C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\gleam-units\\ (spiral-ex.do D039DC4C74EA). Lost (noise): census.ps1 2,398 B, fetched\\xc.rs, fetched\\xsim_checks.gleam: all regenerable outputs or superseded by the G2 measurement. split/gleam.toml was not in the folder. x's recovery is now 100%: nothing x-authored remains unrecovered or unrecorded.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_34 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 34u32, "2026-10-30T14:14Z", "kit", "10-30 10:1x kit: kit's recovery summary, after heal's n32.\nRESULT: 0 of 71 kit drafts recovered (62 had MFT traces, all TRIMmed or overwritten; 9 had no trace). Per-file list: C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\recovery\\kit-lost-drafts-priority.md; heal's verdicts: C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\lane-lists-status.md.\nTECHNIQUES (reusable by every lane):\n(1) Find lost drafts from the backlog, not from memory: kit notes cite drafts as 'scratch <dir>/<file>' (only 1 of 970 kit notes holds a full profile path, so a full-path search returns 0 for kit; that was the positive control). Match the full '<dir>/<file>' pair: a bare file name over-matches generic names like apply.ps1 and probe-run.ps1.\n(2) The owning item = the nearest preceding 'Note (\"<ID>\"' in agile.spi. Priority = the highest open priority among a file's owners; Done-only files are skipped (landed).\n(3) Before asking for an undelete, drop drafts whose effect is already live: shipped features (check the installed kit's usage text), other lanes' rescued or surviving copies (tibia rescue dir, node remote-stage, fiscal-drafts), and three-way merges that put the content in live.\n(4) Hand the undelete lane the MFT tail '\\scratchpad\\<dir>\\<file>' (any session) and ask for every version, newest picked by date.\n(5) Count with explicit booleans in PowerShell: a Where-Object block emitting two values counts as truthy and gave a false '115/115 present' (the truth was 114 missing).\n(6) Git: 'git fsck --no-reflogs --unreachable' is read-only; never gc, prune or lost-found during a recovery.\nNEXT (kit): rebuild from the notes in priority order, but only where the owning item is open AND its change is not already in the live tree (grep the change's distinctive text first). First up: the 5 LIB-MACRO-HEAL probe runners and the GRANULAR-LINT port.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_35 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 35u32, "2026-10-30T14:16Z", "compiler", "10-30 10:1x compiler: lost-draft census for the compiler/kit2 teams, run against healing's restore. Notes on 15 open items cite 25 scratch paths from session 88a146f8's pre-wipe scratchpad (list: C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\lost-drafts-compiler.csv; tool: lost-drafts.ps1). Matched against C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\...\\88a146f8-...\\scratchpad (129 files) and the triage/restore TSVs: 1 came back, ci-cli-path-fix.do (409 B, EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW), and its fix is already in kit (src\\kit_dev\\selected_tests.spi:67, ancestors() search), so nothing needs restoring. The other 24 are gone (TRIM). Each item's notes carry enough to redo its step; MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS records this in its own note.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_36 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 36u32, "2026-10-30T14:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 10:16 fiscal: fiscal's wipe census, COMPLETE, nothing to redo. Method: every TEMP/profile/scratchpad path cited in fiscal notes dated on or before 10-28 (19 lost paths across 10 items), each checked for whether it still exists and what replaced it. All 19 are covered: landed (programs in the lib, re-verified by hash after the 10-30 crash), superseded by later drafts, or main's tools. None needs a rewrite. Heal's verdict (n32): only MFT-resident files came back, so fiscal relies on landed state, not restores. Lost: gadt-proto/xsd_proto.spi (overwritten), an experiment superseded by the landed xsd_emit work. The surviving lib-programs are now at C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\lib-programs. [Precision, checked: xsd_proto.spi was the 10-25 design prototype of the sort-indexed xsd model remodel (note at FISCAL backlog 16:3x 10-25). It landed as lib xsd.spi's union rec xsd ... -> xsd particle form (xsd.spi:63-74), so the prototype is superseded by xsd.spi, not by xsd_emit.]")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_37 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 37u32, "2026-10-30T14:25Z", "heal", "10-30 10:3x heal (git-51): CORRECTION to n32's 'in place'. Restoring app STATE in place was wrong: it put back stale control files. These are now MOVED into C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\ (same relative paths): ~30k %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit files (a 10-27 jobs\\held marker, two 10-28 jobs\\hosts pid records); 47 ~\\.claude runtime files (autonomous\\<sid>.passed/.blocks and ready-*.txt gate inputs, daemon keys, task .locks, sessions, plugins state); 6,316 AppData\\Local files (WindowsApps execution aliases recreated as plain 0-byte files, 549 files inside the OneDrive client's version folder, UWP Packages state, caches). Rule: move only files whose creation time falls in the restore window (08:15-10:05) and whose mtime predates the wipe, so nothing written since was touched. KEPT in place: AppData\\Roaming (DPAPI master keys in Microsoft\\Protect, so Edge's surviving Login Data and Cookies may decrypt again; Crypto\\RSA; Recent; SendTo; dictionaries; app settings), Downloads/Music/Videos, ~/.ssh, tibia-local, scoop\\persist, .claude\\projects transcripts. Checked afterwards: the Start menu package is Ok, wsl resolves to System32, kit job list is clean. Mirror re-run 10:13 (39,607 files / 324 MB, sha256 OK on the node). Memory: undelete-bitlocker-trim.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_38 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 38u32, "2026-10-30T14:26Z", "main", "10-30 10:26 main: main's wipe census, batched after heal's n32. Of the 90 lost paths in 46 open main items (C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1030\\main-lost-drafts-refined.md, 8 of them P0), heal restored 9. Main opened each one before trusting it: respell-exclusions-manual.tsv (448 B), test-blocks-families\\run.ps1 (470 B) and lib-xsdemit-fit\\apply.ps1 (331 B) are clean text with 0 control chars; pins-fix-control (3 files), lib-console (1), lib-xpathfix (416 files, 249 KB), dir-tree-args-lib (32) and edition3-spread\\zed-fixtures (6) are present under C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\Temp. The other 81 are lost. RULE, applied from now on: a lost draft is redone only when its item is picked, and ONLY after checking the live tree first, because two of today's resumes showed the tree had moved past the draft. (1) LIB-PAR-MAP: tibia's par'.spi had already landed on 10-26 (gate 6/6 today), so it's Done with nothing to redo. (2) LIB-OTP-ACTORS: the lost lib-otp-single draft is superseded by lib/spiral/channel.spi (a Rust mpsc + Gleam Subject mailbox), so the Rust arm goes on channel.spi instead (n28). So there are no blanket rewrites: each open item's next note says whether its lost draft still matters.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_39 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 39u32, "2026-10-30T14:31Z", "heal", "10-30 10:4x heal (git-51): CAUSE EVIDENCE from the deleted-record MFT catalog (VSS shadow of 10-28 12:20; times are the directory mtimes, minute resolution, UTC-4 applied). (1) The wipe ran 11:08 to ~11:58 local, not ~10:55-11:09:34. The earlier window was the last write before it and the first recreated file after. (2) Its root was C:\\Users\\i574n itself, walked depth-first in name order: 11:08 '.a*' (a 2023 VS Code-style extension tree, probably .azuredatastudio), .bun, .claude.json (last intact write 11:08:36), then 11:09 .cargo/.codex/.dotnet/.gemini/.grok, 11:10 .nuget/.pack, 11:11 .rustup/.secrets/.ssh, 11:12 .vscode, 11:12-11:41 AppData (spiral-bin\\cells-mounts at 11:20), 11:41 Downloads, scoop until 11:57, tibia-local 11:57-11:58. About 1M entries in 50 min, single-threaded. (3) It did NOT follow junctions: cells-mounts (junctions into C:\\home\\git) went at 11:20 and the repos survived. That rules out Windows PowerShell 5.1 Remove-Item -Recurse and fits pwsh 7 Remove-Item, Elixir File.rm_rf, Rust remove_dir_all or .NET Directory.Delete. (4) The start lines up with n2's NVWMI record: tibia's K4 spiral-wgsl.exe launches ran 10:48-11:08:58. The earlier cells-mounts deletions at 10:47 and 11:01 are ordinary per-run mount cleanups. Most likely shape: a recursive delete whose target resolved to the profile, e.g. temp_dir()/GetTempPath() with TEMP stripped (= C:\\Users\\i574n, memory temp-root-falls-back-to-profile) plus an empty child name, or a mount whose junction targeted the profile. Lead: what in a Cells/K4 run deletes temp_dir()-derived or mount paths at a notebook's end. Script: heal scratchpad wipe_order.py over catalog.tsv.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_40 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 40u32, "2026-10-30T14:36Z", "heal", "10-30 10:5x heal (git-51): REFUTED, the n2 junction hypothesis for Cells. Measured on the box (Elixir 1.20.4 / OTP 27): :file.read_link_info reports a junction as :symlink, and File.rm_rf of a folder holding a junction removes the link and leaves the target's files (keep.txt, sub\\keep2.txt) intact. So the Cells cell-dir cleanup (cells.ex:72 rm_rf of tmp_dir()\\spiral_cells\\<stamp>, whose package mounts are junctions) cannot delete through a mount. Every Cells rm_rf site deletes a unique or fixed child (spiral_cells\\<stamp>, spiral_cells_fs_<n>, warm\\src, build\\<mode>\\<target>\\<name>), never System.tmp_dir!() itself. Note that Elixir's System.tmp_dir!() falls back to the CWD when TMPDIR/TEMP/TMP are unset and C:\\tmp is absent, so a cwd of C:\\Users\\i574n makes it the profile, but each site still adds a child. The remaining lead is outside Cells: a recursive delete with target = the profile or temp root, started at ~11:08 (n39), not following junctions (pwsh 7 Remove-Item, Rust remove_dir_all, .NET). Main's audit (DELETE-ROOT-GUARD n1-n3) found no such SURVIVING site, so the culprit was most likely a %TEMP% scratch script that the wipe itself destroyed.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_41 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 41u32, "2026-10-30T14:52Z", "main", "10-30 10:52 main: ROOT CAUSE of n31's 06:23 env trap, plus a second casualty (found by compiler's PACK-8 toolchain check). Between 06:21:40 and 06:27:06, every scoop app's 'current' junction was rewritten in alphabetical order (systeminformer ... zoom, about 130 apps): a full 'scoop reset *' sweep during the reboot heal, writer unknown. The same sweep re-applied dotnet3-sdk's env_set (06:23:22; n31). Of the 30 apps with more than one version installed, ONLY freepascal ended up off its newest: current -> 3.2.2 instead of trunk 3.3.1-20261025. The reset takes the bucket manifest's version, and the hand-placed trunk dir has no scoop install record, so 'scoop reset freepascal@3.3.1-20261025' fails with 'isn't installed'. main tried to repoint the junction by hand at 10:4x; rmdir on current gave 'Access is denied' and was not forced. Until it's flipped back, an unpinned Delphi run on the box uses FPC 3.2.2, and Cells' Toolchain.fpc follows current. The PACK-8 review and main's install runbook pin SPIRAL_FPC to the trunk fpc.exe (116,736 B). RULE: after any heal or reboot, check that every multi-version scoop app's current points at the expected version before trusting toolchain-sensitive verdicts.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_42 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 42u32, "2026-10-30T15:01Z", "main", "10-30 11:01 main, relayed from tibia (verified in tibia's session), restore lessons for every lane: (1) Use heal's in-place small files as a FINGERPRINT of the exact pinned version. Fetch the pinned release fresh and hash-compare after EOL normalisation before overwriting anything (tibia: 679/684 otclient files and 11/11 nExBot files matched); small provenance files such as TIBIA_CLIENT_SOURCE.txt can name the repo and tag. (2) Re-run deterministic generators and diff them against recovered outputs: 'format --manifest toml' reproduced all 7 recovered spiral.toml byte for byte, which proves both the files and today's converter. (3) MariaDB: compare count(*) from information_schema.tables with schema.sql's CREATE TABLE count. ENGINE=MEMORY tables keep only a tiny definition file, so the wipe drops them (canary lost players_online and logged errors every minute); fix with the schema's own CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS. (4) Re-prove rewritten drafts on a mirror whose deps link is REAL. A copy without deps never type-checks; a node mirror with a matched lib digest caught an unbound am' in core-only src. (5) Turn every hand-built environment into an idempotent setup script in the repo (tibia live/setup.ps1: pins, .setup-pin markers, mismatches moved to _replaced-<stamp>, never deleted). (6) PowerShell trap: '& pwsh -File x.ps1 | Select-Object -First 1' stops the child after its first output line and can half-apply an edit script; use -Last 1 or Out-Null.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_43 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 43u32, "2026-10-30T15:03Z", "main", "10-30 11:03 main, follow-up to n41. FPC is FIXED: compiler flipped freepascal\\current back to 3.3.1-20261025 at 11:0x. The 'Access is denied' came from scoop's read-only attribute on the junction itself, not a handle; the recipe is attrib -R current /L; rmdir current; mklink /J current 3.3.1-20261025; attrib +R current /L. main verified: the shim's fpc -iV prints 3.3.1, fpc.exe is 116,736 B, and 3.2.2 stays installed beside it. The next 'scoop reset *' will repeat the flip, since the trunk dir has no install record; memory scoop-reset-flips-fpc holds the recipe. WRITER of the 06:21-06:27 sweep: NOT healing (its 06:19-06:29 calls were the Start menu repair only, and its scoop work began at 09:5x with single installs). It stays unknown. Also from healing: tibia-local's MariaDB has all 48 tables from schema.sql, including the ENGINE=MEMORY players_online, so nothing is missing there.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_44 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 44u32, "2026-10-30T16:41Z", "heal", "10-30 12:3x heal (git-51): CORRECTION to n37's 'Edge Login Data and Cookies may decrypt again': they will NOT. Edge's Local State was recreated 10-28 11:28 (post-wipe), and all 27 saved logins (created 2022-12 to 2026-08) carry the v20 app-bound prefix, whose key lived only in the deleted Local State. Restoring the DPAPI master keys can't bring it back, and the old cookies are dead the same way. The user gets a site+username list (no passwords) to re-login or reset: C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\edge-saved-logins-sites.tsv (ACL: user + SYSTEM only).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_45 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 45u32, "2026-10-30T18:01Z", "heal", "10-30 13:xx heal (git-51), second scavenging round. (1) NEW TIERS: probed the never-checked skip (2.3M files) and overwritten (1.0M) tiers on PhysicalDrive0. 14.6 GB and 49 GB of clusters were untrimmed, but nearly all of it is OTHER files' data. Of 11,365 restored skip files, 8,777 sit on clusters live files own now, and samples of the 2,588 'free' ones are foreign too (.rs holding Zig, .lua holding a C header, .spi holding PDF xref). All moved to noise\\skip-real-foreign. Edge's real Bookmarks (overwritten tier) is foreign text too: no bookmark JSON in it. (2) CORRECTION to n32/n37: larger (> ~700 B) files from the EARLIER rounds are mostly foreign as well, even when the head looks right (e.g. partial\\Downloads\\spiral_compiler_alpha555.fs holds Rust syn code). A per-type check (plausible_sig.py) failed 1,951 of them; moved to noise\\implausible\\ (45 were in place, incl. RustDesk2\\config\\RustDesk.toml, which would have fed RustDesk a garbage config). Only in-place files untouched since the restore were moved. RULE FOR LANES: trust only restored files < ~700 B (MFT-resident, always intact). Accept a larger one only after an exact match against a known copy (a hash vs an upstream pin or tag, tibia's method: 679/684 otclient matched). (3) x-api.env (756 B): noise (14.7% control bytes), so x's 'not recovered' stands. Telegram key_datas is back but its account map is noise, so the session is lost. Memory: undelete-bitlocker-trim.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_46 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 46u32, "2026-10-30T18:03Z", "main", "10-30 14:03 main: CORRECTION to n38's trust test, after heal's n45. 'Clean text, 0 control chars' does NOT prove a restored file is intact: files over ~700 B are mostly other files' data. Re-checked main's 9 recovered paths by size: respell-exclusions-manual.tsv, test-blocks-families\\run.ps1, lib-xsdemit-fit\\apply.ps1, pins-fix-control (3), lib-console (1), dir-tree-args-lib (32) and edition3-spread\\zed-fixtures (6) are ALL under 700 B, so MFT-resident and trustworthy. lib-xpathfix: 400 of 415 files are under 700 B; the 15 larger ones are Gleam build cache (gleam@otp@task.cache 30,772 B, gleam@function.erl 1,176 B, *.cache_meta ...). They're build output, not drafts, so they're NOT trusted and nothing should read them; rebuild instead. One file of that folder has already moved to noise (416 -> 415).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_47 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 47u32, "2026-10-30T20:43Z", "heal", "10-30 16:5x heal (git-51): MEASURED, the n45 rule. Hashed every still-present non-resident (> ~700 B) restored file (8,646) as a git blob, LF variant included, and compared against all 620,765 blobs in every repo under C:\\home\\git plus tibia-local's checkouts. 9 matched. 7 of those sit under tibia-local\\otclient-src, which tibia replaced with a fresh checkout at 10:44, so those paths hold tibia's files, not my restore. That leaves about 3 genuine (2 vBot .otui under Roaming\\otcr, _lost\\6882676\\oracles\\pattern-examples.ps1 = a fiscal repo file), all already in repos. So nothing unique larger than ~700 B came back. Treat every larger restored file as unproven-and-probably-foreign unless it matches your own pin. Per-file verdicts: C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\verify-blob-match.tsv (record, path, blob sha1, MATCH repo or unmatched); scratchpad heal\\blob_match.py.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_48 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 48u32, "2026-10-31T01:55Z", "heal", "10-30 21:xx heal (git-51): MEMORY SWEEP done. (1) Disk: all 185 deleted memory records checked (front-matter name == file name test); none is original (clusters hold NTFS INDX, registry hbin, gzip, binaries), so disk recovery of memory is closed. (2) 57 PARTIAL memory files rebuilt from pre-wipe backlog notes (user quotes inside), repo docs (kit/AGENTS.md, agent-sync.md, PLAN.md) and settings/hooks; each ends with its source list. 2 subagents, read+grep+edit only; 202 files validated (front matter, every [[link]] resolves). (3) 3 memories lost outright on 10-28 morning (written 08:54/09:41/11:07, no file and no index line since) rebuilt from the backlog notes written with them: erlang-port-pwsh-needs-hide (tibia, TIBIA-BACKEND-MAP n29) merged into erlang-port-hide-console-apps; node-contention-cell-budget (fiscal, LIB-LIST-SUGAR-REST n23) merged into job-timeout-counts-queue-wait; optimizer-miscompile-localization (compiler, DELPHI-64BIT-DFA-DISAGREE n4) recreated + indexed. (4) duplicate detached-process-visible-console(s) merged. (5) node archives: no memory deleted or shrunk since 10-29. Still PARTIAL (13, no evidence anywhere; user to restate): listed in memory profile-wipe-2026-10-28.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_49 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 49u32, "2026-10-31T03:52Z", "heal", "10-31 00:xx heal (git-51), round 3, new sources. (1) NODE COPIES OF LOST DRAFTS: the node keeps what lanes shipped with jobs (remote-stage, remote-archive, mirrors). 297,953 pre-wipe node source files were matched against the deleted-file catalog by name + exact size + parent folder, then git-blob hashed against all 623,864 repo blobs. 1,395 node files hold content found in NO repo; they restore 12,588 lost box paths byte-exact into C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\from-node\\ (from-node-manifest.tsv: path, node source, sha256). tibia 2,988, kit 934, fiscal 237, x 168, main 30, compiler 29, %TEMP% drafts 4,730 (lib-gate-kit, respell-repo, bang-*, pack-next5*, train3/4-bundle, shadows-bundle...). Priority lists: +1 kit (node-kit\\notebook-probe-node.ps1), +1 main (json_schema.spi copies). (2) NODE JOB EVIDENCE: 620 pre-wipe job records survive on the node (C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\eoie\\jobs, stdout/exit/argv); node-job-evidence.tsv maps the 374 the backlog cites. (3) MEMORY: 0 partial left. 13 inferred on the user's order (confidence lines). 53 enriched from the 10,649 backlog notes that cite memories by slug (spiral-macro-gotchas recovered 3 entries of its lost lines 140-210; heavy-gate-lessons' BelowNormal rule from EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN n141). backend-switch-idiom completed from backend.spi (unit missing arms are silent no-ops). 204 files validated. (4) DEAD ENDS: git history (no memory ever committed), node .claude (none), Grok memory (3 tiny files), the 10-21 eoie/memory/claude.spi snapshot of every memory (deleted 10-22 by EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES n24; no node copy found).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_50 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 50u32, "2026-10-31T04:41Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 00:41 tibia: verdict on healing's round 3, the 2,988 recovered ac4b4e98 scratchpad files (84 folders): NOTHING LOST. Method:\n(1) New committed tool i574n.github/scripts/recovered-drafts-census.ps1 -Root <recovered scratchpad>. Per folder it reports the share of distinctive lines (trimmed, 20+ chars) found in the same-named live files across the repos: 25 landed, 47 partial, 9 absent, 3 empty. Partial mostly means a whole-lib snapshot that the lib has since moved past.\n(2) The 9 absent folders, checked by content. lib-seqtrim and lib-xcompat-json-2/3 are whole-file base64 appliers: decoded, 0 of 139 seq lines and 0 of 101 json lines are missing from live (json-3 superseded json-2). gaps-upload's exit_with (env.spi:238), path_join_native (file_system.spi:1787) and set_base (am'.spi:36) are live. process-heal-slice's capture code is live in process.spi:1137-1160. luafix's CRLF fix is in the shipped compiler (spiral_compiler.fs:170194). hunting_pack and pack_sim are pre-retire mirror snapshots.\n(3) Tibia files, checked against EVERY version in tibia's git history plus the live tree: 2,226 lines in 36 files were never committed. The landed structure they describe is live: combat normal_attempt/draw_stats/with_draw, the competitor split's moment/heal_ready/can_step, family 5's monsters_described/forget_dead/called_text/footing_of/target_line. The leftovers are identity-check controls, negative controls, the split vs splitfam5 variants and formatter reflows superseded before commit 23d93fd. bits_body/clauses_from (map-postable) were reshaped later, and tibia is at 0 overweight. Not checked line by line: the 151 older versions in from-node-older, which are earlier states of the same files.\nThe one real tibia-side loss stays DOTA-LUA-BINDINGS note 7 (never on the node either).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_51 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 51u32, "2026-10-31T04:49Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 00:49 tibia: note 50's open part is closed. The 151 older versions (from-node-older) were checked against tibia's full git history too: 174 never-committed lines in 5 files. 154 are in ed3-toml's tree-copy build.ps1, which is the compiler's MSBuild build.ps1 matched only by file name, not tibia's. The rest are the same map/gpu_sim/client/scoreboard intermediates as in the main set. Nothing lost.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_52 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 52u32, "2026-10-31T06:31Z", "heal", "10-31 02:3x heal (git-51): DEAD END, pagefile as a memory source. pagefile.sys (84 GB, never TRIMmed, an allocated file) was scanned for memory-file text ('**How to apply:**' and originSessionId, UTF-8 + UTF-16, 31 min): 9 hits. All sit in Windows memory-compression pages (Xpress-compressed, readable only in fragments), and the readable fragments are post-wipe memory text (10-29 dotnet rc.3 / kit_process notes, the profile-wipe ssh-key lines). No pre-wipe memory version is recoverable from it. Hits kept ACL-restricted at C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\memory\\pagefile-memory-hits.jsonl. Also confirmed: no copy of the 10-21 eoie/memory/claude.spi snapshot anywhere on the node (dir /s over C:\\home and the profile).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_53 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 53u32, "2026-10-31T06:36Z", "heal", "10-31 02:4x heal (git-51): CONFIG DRIFT from the rebuild, found by diffing the small (MFT-resident, so intact) pre-wipe originals in conflicts\\ against live: 1,955 originals, 299 differ. RESTORED (the user's own settings, dropped by the rebuild): git --global core.longpaths=true and credential.helperselector.selected=manager; scoop config aria2-enabled=false and MSIEXTRACT_USE_LESSMSI=true; AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Spelling\\neutral\\default.dic (live was empty, original 5 custom words). LEFT FOR THE USER (deliberate post-wipe choices or bigger changes): (a) .gitconfig user.name was '프리마' pre-wipe, live 'stewshka'; (b) .wslconfig pre-wipe memory=6GB + [experimental] networkingMode=mirrored, live memory=12GB without mirrored; (c) scoop itself was Ash258's Scoop-Core fork (scoop_repo github.com/Ash258/Scoop-Core, branch main; mold's 'shovel' commands), live is official ScoopInstaller/Scoop, plus a lost 'xelatex' alias; (d) RustDesk2.toml pre-wipe original vs the reinstall's regenerated one. KEPT AS IS: DPAPI Protect\\<SID>\\Preferred (live correctly names the post-wipe master key; the old keys are restored beside it). The rest are cygwin package db / app asset files, not settings. Originals: C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028\\conflicts\\.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_54 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 54u32, "2026-10-31T08:25Z", "heal", "10-31 04:2x heal (git-51), pending items healed on the user's 'heal what's pending autonomously; adapt where not smooth': (1) PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE durable trigger: scheduled task, proven, item Done. (2) gh-actions-lock v0.4.0 reinstalled, so CI-ACTIONS-LATEST is unblocked. (3) Global dotnet tools from the pre-wipe catalog reinstalled: ilspycmd 11.2, fantomas 8.1, dotnet-outdated 4.8.1, dotnet-repl 0.3.259, Microsoft.dotnet-interactive 1.0.712001. (4) scoop: the original shovel/shovel.cmd/shovel.ps1 shims (MFT-resident, byte-exact; they call apps\\scoop\\current\\bin\\scoop.ps1) are restored, so mold's 'shovel' commands run on official Scoop without going back to the Ash258 Scoop-Core fork; the xelatex alias (luahblatex) is restored. (5) .wslconfig set to the true pre-wipe original (memory=6GB + [experimental] networkingMode=mirrored); 10-28's 12GB came from an older note; the rebuilt one is in recovery\\replaced-live. (6) FancyZones re-linked to mold\\dist\\appdata\\FancyZones: mold held the user's tuned layouts 1-3 + hotkeys 1-3 on both desktops, while live held 3 'Custom layout 1' re-creations with no hotkeys. Live is archived in recovery\\replaced-live, its gitignored runtime files were carried over, PowerToys restarted, and mold is clean. (7) Node .wslconfig gains guiApplications=false; it takes effect at the VM's next restart. NOT restarted: k3s-server + iggy-server run in it. (8) wfc: the 6.38 installer is Authenticode-valid (Malwarebytes, DigiCert) and staged via scoop --skip-hash-check, but NOT run: it would restart firewall enforcement beside 6 lanes' network jobs. The old 6.9.9.3 folder is back so the stopped wfcs service path stays valid. (9) git user.name 'stewshka' is the user's own (their 10-30 22:33 commit), so it stays. (10) Toolchain run-check (rustc/cargo nightly, zig, gleam, OTP 29, lean 4.35, fpc 3.3.1, gcc 16.2, swift 6.4, kotlin 2.4, dotnet rc.1, node, python, uv, sccache, wasmtime, go) all green; spiral-bin dotnet runtimes 193/193 DLLs. LEFT FOR THE USER: RustDesk security options (access-mode full, remote config modification, direct-server; changing them needs a restart that would drop a remote session); wfc enforcement; the OneDrive recycle bin.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_55 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 55u32, "2026-10-31T08:53Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 03:4x tibia: note 51 re-proved with the committed tool instead of a scratch script. i574n.github/scripts/recovered-drafts-census.ps1 gains -History: a line also counts as known if it appears in ANY git version of a same-named file in -Repos (git log --all), not only in the live tree. This replaces the session-scratch never-seen.ps1, which is removed. Without -History the output is unchanged (85 rows on the main set, 0 differences against the earlier TSV). On the older set (from-node-older, 53 folders), with -Repos tibia,spiral -History: 33 landed, 16 empty, 2 partial (c2-words 94%, target 94%), 2 absent. ed3-toml goes from 81% with tibia alone to 98% once spiral is included, which confirms note 51: the 154 lines are the compiler's build.ps1. The 2 absent ones: eoie-table-empty-cells is 96% in kit's history, and c-prim-to-string is an applier whose own name was never committed, but its payload is live (sm'.spi:224 '?> !!!!PrimToString(x)'). Nothing lost.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_56 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 56u32, "2026-10-31T11:25Z", "heal", "10-31 07:3x heal (git-51), dangling/backlog pass (user request via main). PROCESSES: none of this lane's left; the only matches were this shell and x's 'job wait job-1793440847072-x-verify40' ssh (x's, untouched). CRONS: the 3 session-only mirror-bridge crons were deleted (their windows had passed; the Task Scheduler task profile-mirror-to-node replaces them). JOBS/WINDOWS: none held by this lane on the box or the node. BACKLOG: PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE (Done) assignee user->agent and tag user-batch removed (agent-finished 10-31). PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY 98->99%, assignee agent->user, tag +user-batch, estimate 600m->15m (R1: only user steps remain). The 3 user steps: (1) the OneDrive online recycle bin before ~11-27 (the only copy of OneDrive\\Documents); (2) the RustDesk pre-wipe options (access-mode full, allow-remote-config-modification, direct-server, both-passwords verification), which need a RustDesk restart; (3) running the staged, signed wfc 6.38 installer, which restarts firewall enforcement. Checklist: C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\user-checklist-1030.md. Earlier DECIDED/NEXT notes on this item were already corrected in place (n37 and n44 correct n32 and n37; n45 and n47 set the rule that only <700 B restores are trusted).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_57 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 57u32, "2026-10-31T14:08Z", "resilience", "10-31 10:0x resilience (git-51), role settled (user renamed the session 'resilience', gave 30 min to settle it). The lane's ongoing mandate is durability/recovery/memory-integrity/forensics, TIME-BOXED to a few days (winds down like tibia/x; kit+main persist). Built this session and now scheduled so they outlive the lane: profile-mirror-to-node (15 min), profile-restore-drill (daily, verified), config-baseline-check (daily; CONFIG-BASELINE Done: fingerprint+drift, controls both ways), resource-report morning/evening (main's). New ready light item MEMORY-INTEGRITY-SWEEP (Active). Charter + 'what lanes ask me' in memory resilience-lane-role (indexed by lane-roles). All six lanes notified with what to bring me so they don't rebuild backup/recovery/memory tooling. This item's own remainder is unchanged: the 3 user-only steps (OneDrive recycle bin, RustDesk options, wfc enforcement).")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_58 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 58u32, "2026-11-01T14:40Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 10:40 tibia WIPE VERDICT (checked against the tree and the mirror script, not notes): TIBIA IS SET, EXCEPT 2 open items and 1 transient. SET: the repo (outside the profile; the user committed 8c8f6c3 at 10:01, which carries tonight's respell and its 3 regression fixes); world data (tibia-mariadb-dumps is a whole tree in profile-mirror.ps1 line 24); memories and transcripts (in the mirror); tibia-local's canary, otclient and mariadb-data (rebuilt 10-30 from pinned downloads, rebuildable again). OPEN: (1) TIBIA-MEMORY-REASONS: 5 tibia memories are still PARTIAL (rules kept, the user's original reasons missing; DoD and next step on the item); (2) DOTA-LUA-BINDINGS: the one true loss (the prototype had no copy anywhere), its redo at 40%. TRANSIENT: apps/suite/suite.spi (tonight's retype, unstaged in tibia) and 1 polyglot file (tibia's 10-30 heals) exist only on the box until committed. A profile wipe would not touch C:\\home\\git, but a disk loss would. ACCEPTED LOSSES, no action: the pre-10-28 arena hunter logs (tibia-local\\arena-logs now holds 4 files from 10-14; the outcomes survive as results/*.tsv rows, which DATA-ROWS-TYPED will type) and pre-wipe transcripts. No tibia state lives in C:\\home\\data or %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive.")
inl note_of_profile_wipe_recovery_59 () = Note ("PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY", 59u32, "2026-11-02T14:31Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: Secrets cannot be recreated by agents, so the default makes them non-blocking. For each consumer of a lost secret (x-api.env -> xc live mode, rclone.conf, ~/.secrets), the agent verifies it FAILS CLOSED with a one-line message naming the file, and that every gate runs without it (x e2e uses the sim). PASS iff 100% of consumers fail closed and 0 gates need a secret. The user re-enters secrets only when they want a live feature. BACKUP/UNDO: No file is written; the checks are read-only. OWNER: resilience.")
inl cells_mount_cleanup_harden () = Task ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", "Cells mount cleanup must never delete through a junction: check each unlink and refuse rm_rf while any reparse point remains", TaskKind, P3, D3, 0u32, Planned, "CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS", "cells,safety,recovery,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden () = Planning ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_1 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 1u32, "2026-10-28T22:36Z", "main", "10-28 main, from the profile-wipe cause hunt: apps\\cells\\lib\\spiral\\cells\\mounts.ex remove!(dir) calls remove_child on each entry (rmdir_junction = cmd /c rmdir <link>, result ignored; shadow dirs: rmdir per child dir, File.rm per file, then File.rm_rf(link)) and finally File.rm_rf(dir). If any unlink fails (in use, path quoting, a hard-link fallback from link_file's mklink /H), rm_rf walks into the still-present junction and deletes the TARGET's files, skipping only locked ones; that is the same survival pattern as the 2026-10-28 wipe, though no mount found pointed at the profile. Done rule: (1) every unlink's exit is checked; (2) before File.rm_rf(dir), list reparse points under dir and refuse (error, no delete) if any remain; (3) a guard that refuses to delete outside spiral-bin\\cells-mounts; (4) a test that mounts a junction to a scratch target, makes the unlink fail, and proves the target's files survive (positive control via the bug's own path). Milestones: checks 40m, reparse-point refusal + path guard 40m, failing-unlink test 40m.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_2 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 2u32, "2026-10-28T22:43Z", "main", "10-28 18:4x main: TESTED, the delete-through-a-junction path does not exist on this Elixir/OTP: File.rm_rf on a folder holding a mklink /J junction and a mklink /D symlink to a scratch target removed the links only, and the target's file survived in both cases (scratchpad rmrf-test\\run.ps1 via .exs). So Cells' rm_rf of a mount folder cannot be what emptied the profile. Downgraded to P3 defense-in-depth: checking each unlink's exit and refusing rm_rf outside spiral-bin\\cells-mounts still costs little.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_3 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 3u32, "2026-10-29T12:30Z", "kit", "10-29 08:3x kit: kit half of the env-restore guard (the wipe lead from GRANULAR-HEAL n89 and the loss map's TEMP/LOCALAPPDATA hypothesis). Hazard: kit_jobs/jobs.spi:12 restored each adopted job's environment from text_or_empty <job>/env; an empty or cut-short file made lib env.spi:317-319 remove_var every variable except KIT_JOB_* (TEMP, LOCALAPPDATA, USERPROFILE, PATH). A second effect: jobs_root is recomputed on every job_file call, and with KIT_JOBS_HOME and LOCALAPPDATA gone it falls back to the RELATIVE '.kit-jobs' in the supervisor's cwd.\nFix, in the live tree (unstaged), riding TRAIN3 (job-1793275863025): kit_jobs/model.spi gains snapshot_verdict (SnapshotUsable | SnapshotEmpty | SnapshotDropsRoot name) and snapshot_verdict_of, checking NUL-separated entries without regard to case. job_environment_adopted restores only a usable snapshot, and keeps a refused file as evidence. kit_job_env exports the refusal text, and supervise_job settles the job as spawn-failed (125) with 'job environment not adopted: ...' before any spawn. Also migrated: !!!!Export -> lib export; std::process::id -> env.process_id. Proofs so far: model tests 8/8 on Rust, including the new a_snapshot_that_would_remove_a_path_root_is_refused (empty, cut at 'Syst', PATHEXT not counted as PATH, unset roots not required). Generated Rust is published (env_adopt.rs 243 lines, supervise.rs 700). The stop_cli e2e case (a hand-written job folder with a cut and an empty env file, run through 'kit job supervise': exit 125, detail shown, env file kept, no stdout.log) needs a full binary, so it runs in TRAIN3's candidate notebooks. Hard limit kept: no process ever ran with a stripped environment; the negative side is unit-level only.\nRefinement found 08:3x, to apply after TRAIN3: the supervisor's environment is the per-owner job HOST's, not the caller's, so 'a root set now but missing from the snapshot' can be a legitimate difference (a caller without HOME under a host that has it). Shrink path_roots to names every Windows process has (PATH, SystemRoot, TEMP, TMP, USERPROFILE, LOCALAPPDATA, APPDATA); the env block is sorted, so a cut snapshot still loses the late ones. Drop HOME and KIT_JOBS_HOME, and add a test where the host has HOME and the caller doesn't. Checked: no notebook drops any of these variables, so TRAIN3's verdicts aren't affected.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_4 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 4u32, "2026-10-29T15:31Z", "kit", "10-29 11:3x kit: two more kit-guard facts. (1) The e2e case PASSED in TRAIN3's first candidate run (a_job_whose_environment_snapshot_is_empty_or_cut_short_never_starts, job-1793275863025), and real NUL-joined vars_os snapshots are accepted (each_job_runs_with_the_environment_of_its_own_caller passed). (2) The refinement (universal roots only) is drafted as C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\env-guard-roots\\universal-roots.do, and the dry run applies (2 replacements). path_roots becomes PATH, SystemRoot, TEMP, TMP, USERPROFILE, LOCALAPPDATA, APPDATA, identical to main's lib guard list on Windows, so kit refuses first with 125 and the lib failwith stays a backstop. A new expectation (host has HOME and KIT_JOBS_HOME, caller doesn't -> usable) fails on the old list and passes on the new one. Applies after TRAIN3 installs; rides TRAIN4.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_5 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 5u32, "2026-10-29T15:56Z", "kit", "10-29 11:5x kit: universal-roots APPLIED in kit/src: path_roots = PATH, SystemRoot, TEMP, TMP, USERPROFILE, LOCALAPPDATA, APPDATA (identical to main's landed lib guard on Windows). kit_job_env regenerated and published (1 changed owner). Proven on candidate 8CD04145: kit_jobs/model.spi PASS, including the new 'host has HOME/KIT_JOBS_HOME, caller doesn't -> usable' expectation, and stop_cli.spi PASS (the env-guard e2e plus the real-snapshot job test). Ships in TRAIN4. The kit half is then complete; the lib half (main's environment_snapshot_usable) landed 11:34.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_6 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 6u32, "2026-10-31T11:49Z", "heal", "10-31 07:4x heal (git-51): PREMISE CHECK. Measured 10-30 on the box (Elixir 1.20.4 / OTP 27): :file.read_link_info reports a junction as :symlink, and File.rm_rf on a folder holding a junction removes the link and leaves the target intact (scratch test, PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n40). So rm_rf cannot delete THROUGH a mount junction on this OTP; the residual risk is only a failed cmd rmdir leaving the link, which rm_rf then unlinks safely. Keep the item for older OTPs and the node, or close it after the same check runs there.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_7 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 7u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM: absorbed by CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS (mounts.ex moves to typed Spiral, and refusing to delete through a junction becomes a type-level rule). Do it standalone only if a junction deletion happens before that port.")
inl note_of_cells_mount_cleanup_harden_8 () = Note ("CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN", 8u32, "2026-11-04T16:17Z", "main", "11-04 12:2x main ORPHAN SWEEP: dep PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY replaced by CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS, matching x's 11-02 groom (absorbed by the typed mounts port). The old dep was unrelated and hid the item behind a Blocked recovery epic.")
inl c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias () = Task ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", "C native shim dynamic-array-reserve-zero reallocs the array handle in place, so aliases dangle: glibc aborts (CI exit 134), msvcrt passes by luck", TaskKind, P1, D2, 90u32, Blocked, "", "compiler,c,native-shims,matrix,ci,user-batch,team:compiler,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias () = Planning ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned User)
inl note_of_c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias_1 () = Note ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", 1u32, "2026-10-29T07:08Z", "main", "10-29 03:1x main: found by diffing main's post-wipe oracle review (single-flight-20261029-022008, Windows) against CI run 40691709422 (Linux, same commit cec8840c). samples/dynamic_array_reserve_zero [C] exits 134 on CI and 0 locally; it is the only C row that differs that way, and its sibling dynamic_array_* rows exit 0 on both. Mechanism: tests/native-shims/dynamic-array-reserve-zero-c-shim.h:9-20 grows the array with realloc((raw), header + elements) and reassigns only the macro's local raw. The sample takes inl ~alias = xs before reading the capacity, so when realloc moves the block, alias and every refcounted holder point into freed memory: glibc's heap checks abort at the later free (134 = SIGABRT), while msvcrt grows small blocks in place and the Windows row passes by luck. It is the only shim that reallocs the handle (git grep 'realloc((raw)' in native-shims: 1 hit); geometric-growth and the resize shims only track capacity. Options for the compiler team: (a) give the shim a stable header (create allocates the requested capacity up front, so reserve never moves the block, and capacity is bookkeeping as in the geometric-growth shim), or (b) keep the realloc and abort when it returns a different pointer while refc > 1, making the alias hazard explicit. Done when the row exits the same on Windows and Linux (CI's compiler-oracle artifact against a local run, compare-runs.ps1) with the sample's own check unchanged.")
inl note_of_c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias_2 () = Note ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", 2u32, "2026-10-29T11:55Z", "main", "10-29 07:5x main: the fix is drafted and proven on a scratch copy (main scratchpad c-shim-reserve/shim.new.h). It is NOT landed yet, because git-a6's pack-6 review reads apps/compiler/tmp live until ~08:30.\nThe mechanism is worse than an alias: DynamicArrayReserve0 runs inside method0(Array0 * v0), which takes the handle BY VALUE, so the macro's '(raw) = realloc(...)' never reaches the caller. Any move leaves xs AND alias dangling, so a Reserve that can move the block is never correct here.\nFix, option (a) in shim-local form. The shim wraps malloc with a fixed slack (#define malloc -> malloc(size + 256)) and reserves only within the real allocation (_msize / malloc_usable_size, the SPIRAL_ALLOCATED_ELEMS idiom from dynamic-array-resize-union-managed). It aborts when a request exceeds the block, and it never reallocs. Resize and Capacity are unchanged, and so is the sample.\nProof, with gcc 15.2 -O2 on Windows:\n- Old shim exits 0 (the luck case), and gcc warns -Wstringop-overflow 'writing ... into a region of size 0' at its Resize0 memset, so gcc itself sees the overflow.\n- New shim exits 0, and the only warning left is the generated code's unused ArrayLit0.\n- Positive control through the bug's own path: a header forcing realloc to move the block and poison the old one. The OLD shim then dies with 0xC0000374 (heap corruption, the Windows face of CI's glibc 134), and the NEW shim exits 0.\nDone when a CI run shows samples/dynamic_array_reserve_zero [C] at exit 0 on Linux, like Windows. Land: copy shim.new.h over tests/native-shims/dynamic-array-reserve-zero-c-shim.h after the pack-6 review, then let the next CI run or matrix row prove it.")
inl note_of_c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias_3 () = Note ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", 3u32, "2026-10-29T13:12Z", "main", "10-29 09:1x main: LANDED (unstaged). tests/native-shims/dynamic-array-reserve-zero-c-shim.h is now the proven shim.new.h (n2): malloc gets a fixed slack, Reserve0 reserves only within _msize/malloc_usable_size and aborts past it, and it never reallocs. Landed at 09:1x right after git-a6's pack-6 review job timed out (exit 124), so no test.ps1 or review was reading the shim. The live file was hash-equal to the proven original first, and equal to the proven new text after. The original is in main scratchpad c-shim-reserve/shim.orig.h. Remaining proof: the next matrix run or CI row of samples/dynamic_array_reserve_zero [C], exit 0 on Linux like Windows (the item's done rule).")
inl note_of_c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias_4 () = Note ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", 4u32, "2026-10-29T16:24Z", "main", "10-29 12:2x main: proven on Windows inside the pack-6b review: samples/dynamic_array_reserve_zero [C] exit 0 at parity, with the landed shim. The Linux row still needs a CI run after the user pushes; that is the item's done rule.")
inl note_of_c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias_5 () = Note ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", 5u32, "2026-10-30T14:16Z", "compiler", "10-30 10:1x compiler, BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030 R1: the item's only remaining step is the Linux CI row after the user pushes (main 10-29 12:2x). The Windows proof is done (pack-6b review: dynamic_array_reserve_zero [C] exit 0 at parity). So assignee -> user, tag user-batch; grooms do not re-verify it. Unblocks on the user's push; then any compiler-team agent reads the CI row and closes it.")
inl note_of_c_shim_reserve_realloc_alias_6 () = Note ("C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS", 6u32, "2026-11-02T14:07Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
inl lib_package_dot_listed_twice () = Task ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", "lib notebooks with a ///- --package . header fail every lib_gate test: Cells reports package spiral is listed twice (decimal, dictm, float_text, json_schema, schematron, schematron_run)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,cells,lib-gate,notebooks", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_package_dot_listed_twice () = Planning ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_package_dot_listed_twice_1 () = Note ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", 1u32, "2026-10-29T09:25Z", "main", "10-29 05:3x main: found by the first post-wipe full lib gate (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n19). The six lib files with test blocks that open with '///- --package .' (decimal, dictm, float_text, json_schema, schematron, schematron_run; xpath and xpath_eval carry the header but have no test blocks) fail EVERY test in 8-9 s with Cells' 'package spiral is listed twice' (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells.ex:1112, mount_entries), while all 65 other lib files pass. The headers came on 10-24 (0ec501fb); the duplicate check dates from 10-17 (59b477ba). Ruled out by experiment, each reverted by hash afterwards: deduplicating mount_packages' targets by Path.expand, and then case-insensitively on Windows, changed nothing (still 0 of 6). So the two 'spiral' entries are two DIFFERENT directories that share Mounts.mount_name (the directory base name), as in XSD-NAMESPACE-NAMES n4, where a 'baseline\\spiral' beside 'lib\\spiral' collided the same way. Inside lib, '--package .' names lib itself, and Cells already brings in another directory named spiral for a lib notebook. Next step: log the two {target, name} pairs in mount_packages for decimal.spi. Then either (a) drop the header from these lib files, if no other consumer path needs it (check what the 10-24 header was for), or (b) make mount names unique, so different directories with the same base name don't collide. Proof: lib_gate on the six files passes, and the Cells mix tests stay green (targets_test 23 passed; document_test 20/22, unchanged).")
inl note_of_lib_package_dot_listed_twice_2 () = Note ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", 2u32, "2026-10-29T09:28Z", "main", "10-29 05:3x main: DIAGNOSED. Cells' error now names both directories (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells.ex:1111-1112: 'package spiral is listed twice: <existing> and <new>'; unstaged; targets_test 23 passed and document_test 20/22, both unchanged, 0 warnings). For decimal.spi it reports 'c:/home/git/spiral/deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral and c:/home/git/spiral/lib/spiral'. That is the SAME directory reached two ways: spiral's deps\\polyglot links to polyglot, whose deps\\spiral links back to C:\\home\\git\\spiral. Cells' automatic lib lookup takes the link route (the lookup order also lists deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral, like lib_gate.ps1's root walk), and '--package .' takes the direct one. Path.expand keeps both spellings, which is why main's two dedupe experiments (string, then case-insensitive) changed nothing. Fix options, sharpened: (a) compare packages by their link-resolved path (resolve each component's links before comparing; neither Path.expand nor Erlang has a realpath), or (b) make the automatic lib lookup prefer the direct lib/spiral spelling when the notebook sits inside it, or (c) drop the '--package .' headers from these 6 lib files. (b) is the smallest change with no effect on other notebooks.")
inl note_of_lib_package_dot_listed_twice_3 () = Note ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", 3u32, "2026-10-29T09:29Z", "main", "10-29 05:3x main: the resolver behind it, for option (b). apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/notebook.ex find_spiral_lib (:1251-1261) walks the notebook's ancestors, and in each ancestor tries @lib_rels (:29-35) in order: deps/polyglot/deps/spiral/lib/spiral FIRST, then deps/spiral/lib/spiral, then lib/spiral. For a notebook inside spiral's own lib, the walk reaches C:\\home\\git\\spiral and returns the link-chain spelling before it tries the direct lib/spiral. Smallest fix: when an ancestor itself is a lib root (it ends in /lib/spiral and holds package.spiproj, i.e. the notebook lives inside that lib), return it before the @lib_rels lookup. Physically nothing changes (same directory), but it re-spells lib resolution for every lib notebook, so the proof is a full lib sweep (lib_sweep.ps1, about 71 min on this box) with 0 new failures, plus the 6 header files passing. Not landed tonight: too little time left before 07:00 for that proof, and the resolver is shared by every lane.")
inl note_of_lib_package_dot_listed_twice_4 () = Note ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", 4u32, "2026-10-29T09:32Z", "main", "10-29 05:3x main: option (b) is being PROVEN, not assumed. Draft applied (unstaged, with a hash backup): find_spiral_lib checks lib_root_itself(dir) before the @lib_rels lookup (an ancestor that ends in /lib/spiral and holds package.spiproj is returned as-is). Job main-lib-root-sweep runs the full lib_sweep.ps1 into lib-sweep-20261029-libroot.tsv and compares each file with the 05:16 sweep. It KEEPS the change only if no file loses a passing test or gains a type error, at least one of the 6 header files now passes, and all 73 rows exist; otherwise it restores notebook.ex by hash. Result by about 06:45.")
inl note_of_lib_package_dot_listed_twice_5 () = Note ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", 5u32, "2026-10-29T10:40Z", "main", "10-29 06:4x main: PROVEN and KEPT (unstaged; the original is saved in main's session scratchpad as lib-root/notebook.ex.before). With lib_root_itself in find_spiral_lib, the full lib sweep (job main-lib-root-sweep, lib-sweep-20261029-libroot.tsv, 70 min) has 73 files, 516 tests, 439 passed and 4 failed (it was 421/21 at 05:16). Better: decimal 0->3, dictm 0->5, float_text 0->1, json_schema 0->5, schematron 0->1, schematron_run 0->2 (6 of 6 header files fully pass), and file_system 28->29 (tonight's drive test). Worse: none (no file lost a passing test or gained a type error). The 4 left are lustre.spi and near_wallet.spi, the lustre_ui/gleam_stdlib Hex conflict (GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS n24). Done.")
inl note_of_lib_package_dot_listed_twice_6 () = Note ("LIB-PACKAGE-DOT-LISTED-TWICE", 6u32, "2026-10-29T10:43Z", "main", "10-29 06:4x main: the Cells mix tests after the lib-root change (the sweep proved only the lib gates): targets_test 23 passed, notebook_spiral_lib_test (lib resolution) 3 passed, document_test 20/22 (the same two existing round-trip reds, NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE n8), 0 compile warnings.")
inl wipe_redo_ledger () = Task ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", "Read every lane's history for 2026-10-28 wipe losses; ledger each as recovered, recoverable (with its source) or redo; groom the redo items so all lanes are move-forward-only by 2026-10-29 21:00", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "-", "wipe,recovery,grooming,coordination", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_wipe_redo_ledger () = Planning ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", Minutes 600u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_1 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 1u32, "2026-10-29T11:43Z", "main", "10-29 07:4x main, from the user at 07:4x: \"do multiple readings in the entire history of the lanes later so we try having a better grip into what can be recovered etc, coordinate with the lanes when you're at it. until 9pm we gotta leave the damage behind, getting to a state of move-forward only, like we were. then coordinate backlog groomings to know what will need to be redone\".\nSources:\n(1) Each live lane's own context. Lanes that were running at the wipe still hold pre-wipe knowledge, and this is the richest source.\n(2) The 6 post-wipe transcripts in ~/.claude/projects/C--home-git, whose compaction summaries carry pre-wipe history.\n(3) The node: C:\\home\\remote, C:\\home\\remote-stage, and its untouched %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit job logs.\n(4) The backlog plus done-notes.spi, and git reflogs and stashes.\n(5) C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28: loss-map.md, and missing-paths-cited-in-backlog.tsv with 510 rows.\nLedger row format, one row per lost thing: LOST <what> | WAS <path or place> | SOURCE <node:path | transcript | backlog:ID nN | regenerate:<how> | gone> | STATE <recovered | recoverable | redo | dropped> | ITEM <backlog ID>.\nReadings: pass 1 at 08:xx (each lane on its own history, main across the transcripts and the missing-paths list), pass 2 at ~14:00, a final pass at ~19:00. Grooming at ~16:00 and ~20:00: every redo row gets an item tagged wipe-redo with all fields filled. Done when every row is recovered, dropped, or has a groomed item, and no lane has a known-lost dependency that isn't ledgered.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_2 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 2u32, "2026-10-29T11:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 07:49 fiscal: PASS 1, fiscal's own losses (read from fiscal's context, its backlog notes and its node jobs; nothing secret involved). Every fiscal land payload lived in the repo (fiscal/lib-programs/*.kit) and survived; what died were working drafts and launchers in the session scratchpad/%TEMP%.\nLOST UBL-JSON transcoder working draft (+ json_schema 54CFD0B2) | WAS %TEMP%\\tc-uj-draft | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/ubl-json-transcoder.kit + node:C:\\home\\remote\\uj3\\spiral\\lib\\spiral\\json_schema.spi | STATE recovered (landed 10-29 07:28:51, hash = proven copy) | ITEM FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\nLOST complements writer + any-content indirection lib drafts | WAS %TEMP% draft dirs | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/xsd-any-complements-writer.kit, xsd-any-content-indirection.kit | STATE recovered (writer landed 07:28:50; indirection proof fix-ac2 queued) | ITEM XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS\nLOST complements generator half (cfdi_tfd_1_1 + cfdi_pagos_2_0, complements_of CFDI) | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\complements\\src\\generator.spi | SOURCE backlog:XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS n10 n11 | STATE redo | ITEM XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS\nLOST ubl_json_documents generator draft (UBL Invoice unit reads 22 JSON + 155 XML) | WAS session scratchpad (generator.spi copy) | SOURCE backlog:FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS n9 n11 | STATE redo | ITEM FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\nLOST edition-3 respell draft of the fiscal tree | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\edition3\\src | SOURCE regenerate:SpiralCompiler format --spelling symbols on the fiscal tree (proof ge3e = gbase2, 0/70 units differ) | STATE recoverable | ITEM FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND\nLOST landing schedule + job ids of uj3/fix-ss/census/fix-ac (decisions only in TEMP) | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\notes\\landing-schedule-1028.md | SOURCE node:kit job list (all fiscal-* jobs and outputs survive) | STATE recovered (verdicts read and noted 10-29) | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST set-proof launcher (launch-set-proof.ps1; set-proof.ps1 beside it) | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\recgroups\\ | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote-stage\\recgroups\\set-proof.ps1, set-proof-c.ps1, compare-generated.ps1, fix-proof-d.ps1 (all survive); regenerate:the local launcher wraps remote.ps1 sync + job start | STATE redo | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST Delphi Cells -Px86_64 applier (targets.ex:321, targets_test.exs:43, README:223; dry run 3/3) | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\recgroups\\delphi64-cells-apply.ps1 | SOURCE backlog:FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n47 | STATE redo (after the NOREGVAR prelude install; main rebuilt the compiler-side applier) | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH\nLOST Delphi interim -OoNOREGVAR applier | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\recgroups\\delphi64-noregvar-apply.ps1 | SOURCE backlog:FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n46 | STATE dropped (superseded by n47's in-source prelude fix) | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH\nLOST Delphi step-1 probe | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\delphi-step1.ps1 | SOURCE backlog:FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n12 n13 | STATE redo | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH\nLOST bench folders bench-acbr, dfe-net, compare (bench scripts + svn/git exports) | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\bench-acbr, \\dfe-net, \\compare | SOURCE backlog:FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n7 n8 n14 (sources, export set, rules); svn 1.14.5 back via scoop | STATE redo | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH\nLOST method folders cells-ab, typefeature, delphi-survey | WAS TEMP\\claude\\C--home-git\\84b53718\\scratchpad\\cells-ab, \\typefeature, \\delphi-survey | SOURCE backlog notes hold their results | STATE dropped (results recorded; a reused method becomes a kit command) | ITEM FISCAL-COMMIT-HYGIENE\nLOST scratch sweep archive 20261028-064245 (1773 throwaway files of landed work) | WAS %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261028-064245 | SOURCE gone | STATE dropped (classed throwaway in FISCAL-COMMIT-HYGIENE n22) | ITEM FISCAL-COMMIT-HYGIENE\nLOST fiscal's local kit job history | WAS %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\jobs | SOURCE gone (node-side history intact) | STATE dropped | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_3 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 3u32, "2026-10-29T11:52Z", "kit", "10-29 07:5x kit, pass 1 batch 1 (kit lane: release trains, renameproof programs, kit state). Method: three-way SHA1 of every .spi/.spiproj/.toml in node:remote-stage\\train{3,4}-bundle\\{base,cand} against the live kit tree; kit do --dry-run plus a new-text presence check for each renameproof .do; node %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit listing.\nLOST TRAIN3 apply programs (8: kit-text, settle-receipt, doctor servers crate, seal, argument-count/after-flag/at, window-watch-to-lib) and train3 staging | WAS %TEMP% scratchpad clean\\train3 | SOURCE live tree: all 45 TRAIN3 files are byte-equal to node:remote-stage\\train3-bundle\\cand (the release had applied them in place); kit_jobs/model.spi differs only by today's env guard (+43 lines) | STATE recovered | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN\nLOST TRAIN3 run record and per-notebook results (job-1793192300314, exit 1, 67/69 candidate notebooks; reds ps_cli kill_with_mine_refuses and stop_cli a_job_over_its_memory_cap) | WAS %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\jobs | SOURCE gone (the summary survives only in tibia's 10-28 message) | STATE redo: retry TRAIN3 from the live tree, reproduce both reds first, and name table_cli/table_test_cli in the report (EOIE-TABLE-EMPTY-CELLS) | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN\nLOST TRAIN4 kit programs (kit-clip, kit-lines, waits-column, kit-part-at, rename-retry, text-replace-cas) | WAS scratchpad clean\\train4 + build-train4-copy.ps1 | SOURCE node:remote-stage\\train4-bundle\\cand: 18 files whose live copy equals base, so copying cand reproduces the programs exactly | STATE recoverable | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (also EOIE-AGILE-QUERIES n23, EOIE-DO-CONCURRENT-EDITS n6/n8, EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION n77/n78)\nLOST TRAIN4 lib half (fixed lib-clip, sm'.split_nth) | WAS scratch lib copy | SOURCE node:remote-stage\\train4-bundle\\cand\\src\\spiral\\sm'.spi and am'.spi; both DIVERGED from the live lib (later lands plus main's 07:39 blank-line normalization), so recover by diffing cand against base and re-applying onto live | STATE recoverable | ITEM LIB-DOTNET-ONLY-BODIES, EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION\nLOST renameproof programs, 21 .do of 10-25/26 | WAS kit lane scratch | SOURCE node:remote-stage\\renameproof\\scripts | STATE recovered (10 fully landed in the live tree: argument-counts-to-lib, drop-unused-std-string, kit-named-length, list-planning-index-granular, path-predicates-to-lib, route-arity, sequences-static-skip, stop-cli-deterministic, string-builders-to-lib, word-after-whitespace); dropped (10 superseded, their anchors no longer exist: declared-edition3, heal-arith, heal-expect, heal-title-notes, lint-join-points, list-planning-index (replaced by -granular), subcommand-find-b/-c (variants), table-csv-quoted plus its revert); dropped (heal-task-rename: still applies, but it would fold the agile_rename_rewrite crate into agile_task_rename and no note asks for that) | ITEM KIT-RENAME\nLOST pre-wipe kit job history, windows, events and tree leases | WAS %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\{jobs,windows,tree-leases,supervisor} | SOURCE gone; node %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit holds only node-local state (tree-leases 60, supervisor 14, state-backups 1, todo-cache 1, newest 10-27) | STATE dropped (history only; the job store is live again since 10-28 ~20:18, job-1793228918503) | ITEM PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY\nLOST kit archive manifests and unstaged/state backups (archive\\20261027-054550, -064527, 20261028-064245; backups\\unstaged; state-backups\\agile-20261027-133935) | WAS %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit | SOURCE gone | STATE dropped (the repos they backed up are intact; DISK-CLEANUP n32 and FISCAL-COMMIT-HYGIENE n22 cite them as receipts only) | ITEM DISK-CLEANUP\nLOST snapshot 20261028-085735-before-release-TRAIN.zip | WAS %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit | SOURCE gone | STATE dropped (the tree it protected is intact and fully accounted for above) | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN\nLOST todo-cache (KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS warm cache) | WAS %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\todo-cache | SOURCE regenerate: the next 'kit agile todos' run rebuilds it | STATE recovered on first use | ITEM KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS\nLOST shell environment in pre-wipe and old agent shells: 11 User variables missing (KIT_LEASE_POLICY, MIMALLOC_DISABLE_REDIRECT, SPIRAL_PYTHON, UV_*, BUN_*) | WAS process env | SOURCE regenerate: import the User env before kit calls; without KIT_LEASE_POLICY=renewing every mutating 'kit agile' verb fails 'lease authority blocked ... should_wrap=1' (seen 08:0x) | STATE recovered (per call) | ITEM PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY\nAlso done in this batch: view-add wipe-redo (list all --tag wipe-redo), for the 16:00 and 20:00 groomings. Next batch: kit drafts from 10-28 that lived only in scratch (TODO-markers M5, kit_do_commit split, tree-write, remote status M1, lib-set-env and the census lib slices, x's lint shadows), each checked against the node mirrors before it's called redo.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_4 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 4u32, "2026-10-29T11:55Z", "compiler", "10-29 08:0x compiler (session 88a146f8 = kit2 on 10-25, compiler lane 10-27/28), PASS 1. Sources read: my 208 backlog notes (126 distinct file references, each checked for existence), the missing-paths TSV (2 rows cite my notes), the node (C:\\home\\remote mirrors + eoie job logs), and the live packs/lab dirs. My pre-wipe transcript and compaction summaries are gone (file recreated 10-28 15:09Z), so the backlog is the record.\nLOST compiler-lane transcript + context | WAS ~/.claude/projects/C--home-git/88a146f8-*.jsonl | SOURCE backlog:208 kit2/compiler notes | STATE dropped (facts live in the notes) | ITEM PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY\nLOST P3 shard prototype applier + runner | WAS compiler TEMP scratchpad | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote\\scripts\\apply-hopacsota-p3-shard.ps1, hopacsota-p3-shard-proto.ps1 | STATE recovered (fetched to session scratch; superseded by packs/apply-hopacsota-p3-shard.ps1, HOPACSOTA-P3 n22: the old one shards by the structural hash of the whole id, which races on the shared per-body Dictionaries) | ITEM HOPACSOTA-P3\nLOST P3 shard prototype RESULT (never noted) | WAS node job-1793189883882-hopacsota-p3-shard-proto | SOURCE node:%LOCALAPPDATA%\\eoie\\jobs | STATE recovered, verdict INCONCLUSIVE: node oversubscribed (SF wall 285-290 s vs 26.5 s clean; w1 548-752 s); w8 284.7 s; w8 bridges 100,935 (~unchanged vs 103k); cut before w8-b by the wipe -> redo the measurement on a quiet slot with the n22 applier | ITEM HOPACSOTA-P3\nLOST P3 IVar-variant applier + runner + result | WAS TEMP | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote\\scripts\\apply-hopacsota-p3-ivar.ps1, hopacsota-p3-ivar-proto.ps1, job-1793187175380 (build 1 FS0001, build 2 ok, measure from 07:42) | STATE recoverable (scripts fetched; measure output to read in pass 2) | ITEM HOPACSOTA-P3\nLOST P2 determinism gate + P3 contention/trace probes | WAS TEMP | SOURCE node:C:\\home\\remote\\scripts\\hopacs