inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_25 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 25u32, "2026-10-29T14:37Z", "compiler", "10-29 10:3x compiler, batch 5 (closes the 3 rows from main's 10:05 sweep + new rows):\nLOST host --check diagnostics patch | WAS %TEMP%\\check-prints-errors\\apply.ps1 | SOURCE backlog:SPIRAL-CHECK-PRINTS-ERRORS n4+n7 | STATE redo-done: apps/compiler/packs/apply-check-parse-errors.ps1. While redoing it, a FALSE GREEN was found on the installed host: --check exits 0 on a parse error ('inl x = = = 3' -> 'checked package'); the applier makes parse errors fail and print path:line:col (SPIRAL-CHECK-PRINTS-ERRORS n8) | ITEM SPIRAL-CHECK-PRINTS-ERRORS\nLOST GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT compact.do | WAS x scratchpad gleam-compact\\compact.do | SOURCE backlog:GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT n2 + n4 | STATE redo-done: apps/compiler/packs/apply-gleam-compact-arms.ps1 (5 anchors; multi-line arms byte-identical by construction) (GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT n5) | ITEM GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT\nLOST CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS negative set (crd-negative-set.txt, JOBS.tsv, RESULTS.tsv) | WAS TEMP | SOURCE regenerate: the CRD n4-n11 recipe over spiral-bin\\baseline\\EXPECTED.tsv (rebuilt 10-29 03:49) | STATE deferred (derived data, regenerated in seconds at the start of the build-bound Part 2; a stored copy would go stale with every accept, so it is not kept) | ITEM CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS\nNOT A WIPE LOSS, but a hiccup found during upkeep: node INSTALLED compiler 4 days stale (built 10-25 from core source 34519b92, core 826D67C6) | WAS node %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\bin\\single-flight | SOURCE box install shipped byte-equal | STATE recovered at 10:02 (core 05E94769A86A9B9C, host A4E480202BD40D80; old kept as net11.0.stale-34519b92-20261029; node-upkeep.log; REMOTE-LAPTOP-LANE n17) | ITEM REMOTE-LAPTOP-LANE\nNOT A WIPE LOSS: Cells runner spiral.exe stale and different on box (7CEC582F, 10-26) and node (04C10A36, 10-25) vs apps/spiral 3f1b7588 (10-27); node checkout stale too (d095f13d, lib 112 file