inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_31 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 31u32, "2026-10-29T16:16Z", "kit", "10-29 12:1x kit, pass 2 rows (TRAIN3 and closes):\nLOST TRAIN3 release (published only after a retry) | WAS kit lane, train staged in %TEMP% | SOURCE live tree + scripts/release-train.ps1 | STATE recovered: PUBLISHED 11:35, installed kit.exe CD2F0D1A (was A5B55974); closeout on the installed binary 7/7, with an A5B55974 control in which the 4 discriminating checks FAIL; lane copy %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe swapped to CD2F0D1A | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (n182)\nLOST KIT-PENDING-DANGLING's moved test (pending-test-fix.do) | WAS scratch | SOURCE live tree | STATE recovered and DONE: files.spi notebook 1/1 on the installed code, no dangling *.pending | ITEM KIT-PENDING-DANGLING (n4)\nLOST TRAIN3-era items that only needed the release: KIT-LINT-DOLLAR-LITERAL, EOIE-JOB-START-SETTLE, EOIE-JOBS-DOCTOR | WAS in the lost train | SOURCE TRAIN3 install | STATE DONE, each verified live on CD2F0D1A | ITEM same ids\nLOST TRAIN4 content (m5-commit-bundle drafts) | WAS scratch + node bundles | SOURCE restored into kit/src at 11:57 (73 files, 0 conflicts) together with today's post-TRAIN3 drafts | STATE recovered (staged), ships in TRAIN4 after kit's lib land | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (n183)")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_32 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 32u32, "2026-10-29T17:38Z", "main", "10-29 13:4x main, SWEEP 4 (transcripts 16:09Z to ~17:10Z; main scratchpad sweep-4.tsv): 16 rows, 0 new losses, 3 unposted recoveries, 1 contradiction, 3 unanswered nudges, 9 hazards.\nMain's rows, all closed:\n- RECOVERED: the compiler install procedure (install-p2.ps1, lost with TEMP) is rebuilt as apps/compiler/packs/install-pack.ps1. It is hardened: it backs up the whole bin folder and fails unless the SYSTEM dotnet launches the installed DLL. Pack 6b is INSTALLED (12:22, core 31CC96520D6B7269; backup C:\\home\\data\\compiler-installs\\pack6b-20261029-122022). COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE is APPLIED (12:29). This supersedes n50's \"review running\".\n- FIXED HAZARD: the retire stubs forwarded stale native exit codes (a false RED for old-path -File callers). The 39 stubs were rewritten at 13:35 (COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE n36), with a matrix of 0 mismatches plus a consumer check, and a kit-job proof that the -File child streams stdout.log live (kit's heavy gate_wait_of marker visible at 8.8 s, exit 4 propagated).\n- OPEN HAZARD (user commit): apps/compiler/scripts/ is UNTRACKED while CI workflow.ps1 calls it. Commit it TOGETHER with the 39 modified tmp/scripts stubs. Goes in the 21:00 report.\n- OPEN HAZARD: old-path callers outside spiral (sefaz/scripts/candidate-gate.ps1:18; kit host.spi:27, built from joined segments, fix rides TRAIN5). Keep every stub until TRAIN5 is installed and sefaz is moved. The retire gate must grep joined-segment forms across repos.\nPOST-TRAIN4 ORDER (broadcast 13:4x; kit acked): fiscal's 3 lands (xsd_emit M7, schematron fragment, Cells -Px86_64), then main's 2 (flat delete predicate, sm' un-static), then one document_test over everything, then main refreshes the kitbin, then the git-a6 runner swap, the node ship and the node checkout update (remote.ps1 sync, which carries untracked files, not git pull), then the pack-7 build and review, then main installs pack 7 with install-pack.ps1, alongside kit's attestation-parse-error. Lanes pick -Dll/-Core at LAUNCH from remote.ps1 status. Nobody exempts the kit-train4 window.\nTHREE-CORE HAZARD (git-a6 row 9): installed 31CC9652 (rc.3), parked pack6c 749616FEFEAEFC80 (rc.1) and node-built pack7 9C899B30 come from related sources. The box's bundled dotnet now has the rc.1 SDK, so a local build.ps1 of the installed source silently yields a different core. Rule: no local compiler rebuilds outside install-pack; broadcast the core after each install; pack6c is not for install.\nRouted 13:3x: fiscal (re-pin node proofs to 31CC9652; DELPHI-64BIT n8 VOID unless run on 31CC9652 NOREGVAR; ubl_json redo; seta/setb/setc stale notes; resync mirrors; sefaz old-path caller); x (resync every node mirror; launch-time pins; old-path calls); tibia (resume packet: re-gate on the current node core, resync, sweep-3 corrections, rescue path; still PAUSED for the user's go); kit (TRAIN4 restarted 13:23 after a missing Rust arm in kit_schedule, fixed with create_dir_all; node-regen-compare now lists crates with a missing backend arm; re-prove its 8 lib-land tests at 31CC9652 in TRAIN4's notebooks before closing LIB-DOTNET-ONLY-BODIES); git-a6 (ledger the node core 31CC9652 with the hand-shipped rc.3 runtime, and RUNNER-STALE staged 2E5F532E with the swap after TRAIN4).\nAlso closed: LIB-TESTS-NOT-RUN small gaps (6 files run and green, n4).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_33 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 33u32, "2026-10-29T17:41Z", "compiler", "10-29 13:4x compiler (main's sweep-4 asks). ROW 8: node compiler = 31CC96520D6B7269 (single-flight Release, identical to the box install; build-identity source 6dd9ab3b728d1ba0, detRoot C:\\home\\spiral-cache) since 16:42Z. Its 11.0.0-rc.3 runtime was HAND-SHIPPED from the box (the node's dotnet-install downloaded a 38 KB error page); the replaced folders are kept at node C:\\home\\remote-stage\\dotnet-replaced-20261029. RUNNER-STALE: staged runner 2E5F532E73EEAF14 (runner-3f1b7588, release-unwind) replaces the live 7CEC582FD5E29728 (10-26) after TRAIN4's 'window closed'. The swap script is dry-run green: it archives the old binary, smokes via the consumer path 'rust --rs-path', restores on failure. The node ship (node runner 04C10A363AC987E1, 10-25) follows. ROW 9: three cores: installed 31CC9652 (rc.3), pack6c 749616FEFEAEFC80 (rc.1) and pack7 9C899B30495F7DC5 (rc.1, node build). pack6c is now NOT FOR INSTALL: archived with scratch-archive.ps1 (95 files, 0 verify failures) at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261029-134028, marker NOT-FOR-INSTALL.txt left in its folder. I will broadcast the core after each node install. Side note: two dry-run archives (20261029-133912, -134005) also sit in the store; scratch-archive's -Only filters restores only, so an archive always covers the whole -Root.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_34 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 34u32, "2026-10-29T18:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 14:07 fiscal: PASS 2 rows (main's sweep 4). All fiscal proofs from here on pin pack 6b (node stage C:\\home\\remote-stage\\spiral-bin-1029-6b, host 9895730DAE80, core 31CC96520D6B7269, copied from the box's installed single-flight build and hash-verified on the node).\nLOST complements generator half | WAS scratchpad complements/src/generator.spi | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/generator-complements.kit (rebased onto the tree's JSON fix: tree D4948243 -> 324190CC) | STATE recovered-pending-proof: set-cfdi3 proved generated_cfdi_tfd_1_1 and generated_cfdi_pagos_2_0 (+certificates); generated_cfdi_v4_0 waits on the lib fix xsd-complement-namespace-operator.kit (bare '++#', xsd_emit F49F611A -> 5606F4B4; 6b proof fiscal-6b-m7-complements running; lands in the post-TRAIN4 slot) and then a set-cfdi rerun | ITEM XSD-ANY-COMPLEMENTS\nLOST ubl_json_documents generator draft | WAS session scratchpad | SOURCE fiscal tree src/generator.spi | STATE REDO in progress: set-ublj (old pin) found the 22 JSON documents fail an ORDER-sensitive check (JSON objects are unordered); the tree now has json_round_trip (stable typed round trip + same element/text/attribute count); rerun on 6b being staged (mirror ublj6b) | ITEM FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS\nLOST Delphi Cells -Px86_64 applier | WAS scratchpad recgroups\\delphi64-cells-apply.ps1 | SOURCE fiscal/lib-programs/cells-delphi-x64.kit (targets.ex:321, targets_test.exs:43, README:223; rehearsed) | STATE recovered-pending-proof: fiscal-cells-delphi64 held on the old pin, rerun on 6b running (fiscal-6b-cells-delphi64); lands in the post-TRAIN4 slot; the compiler side is DELPHI-64BIT n9 (test.ps1 rows -Px86_64), so pack 7's review doubles as the 64-bit confirmation | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_35 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 35u32, "2026-10-29T18:13Z", "main", "10-29 14:1x main: RECOVERED fiscal's type-only test probe (cells-ab/test_probes.py, lost with fiscal's TEMP scratchpad; ledger note 2 listed cells-ab as \"a reused method becomes a kit command\"). Rebuilt from CELLS-PROBES n23/n24 as the generic apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 (draft at C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\type-probe\\, landing after the TRAIN4 Cells freeze), with a built-in per-run positive control and separate static/test/module error counts. Proof is in CELLS-PROBES n26. State: recovered + improved; no redo left for fiscal.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_36 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 36u32, "2026-10-29T19:17Z", "x", "2026-10-29 15:1x x, batch 9 (four rows closed): verify27 + verify28 | STATE redo -> DONE (replaced by verify29, GREEN 13:0x, which closed X-GRANULAR-HEAL, X-EDITION3-RESPELL and X-DEFUSE-LINKS-ONLY; re-proof on pack-6b = verify31) | ITEM X-WIP-VERIFY. Pre-respell x tree copy (node mirror xv20, removed 07:2x) | STATE dropped, its condition met (verify29 green; the only respell signal was the reviewed fixture text) | ITEM X-EDITION3-RESPELL. Gleam shell launcher (sim-shell.ps1) | STATE recovered-pending-proof -> RECOVERED (proven on the node, x-queue2 job-1793297885276: positive replay exit 0, negative exit 1) | ITEM X-BACKEND-SWITCHES n5. LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER x half | STATE applied (net.spi 48466BA9 -> 4D3AB954 after verify29's land), closing on verify31 | ITEM LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_37 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 37u32, "2026-10-29T19:18Z", "main", "10-29 15:2x main, SWEEP 5 (transcripts 17:10Z to ~18:56Z; main scratchpad sweep-5.tsv): 13 rows: 1 new loss, 3 unposted recoveries, 2 contradictions, 5 hazards, 2 unanswered nudges.\nNEW LOSS (kit): the rebuilt scripts/release-train.ps1 lost its per-run and per-worker MIX_BUILD_PATH (a pre-wipe rule, EOIE-NOTEBOOK-WORKERS n1). TRAIN4b's workers and any lane's local Cells run share one apps/cells _build, and links_model's unexplained red ran under \"Waiting for lock on the build directory\". STATE: redo drafted (kit train4-reds\\train-mix-build-path.do, in TRAIN4c). Memory heavy-gate-lessons rebuilt by kit with this fact. Main's window sequence now uses a private build path, and fiscal and git-a6 were told to do the same.\nSIGNALS DEFINED (contradiction found by the sweep: \"window closed\" meant two things). (1) kit \"TRAIN4 notebooks end\" opens the lib gap. (2) main \"window closed\" = gap lands + document_test done; ONLY kit's TRAIN4c rerun keys on it. (3) kit \"TRAIN4 published\" = git-a6's runner swap, node ship, node checkout sync and the pack-7 review. Ledger n33/n34 phrases like \"after TRAIN4's window closed\" mean (3).\nCORRECTION (main's own): the lanes were told \"main 3 lands\". Main lands 5: file_system (flat predicate), sm' (no --static), trace (LIB-MACRO-HEAL A+C), common (random_in_span), apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1. Each is base-hash pinned, re-announced at 15:2x, and pinged as \"main lands done\".\nCONTRADICTION (kit): the 16:16Z row \"TRAIN4 content recovered (staged)\" is recovered-pending-proof until TRAIN4c's notebooks are green; the restored merge.spi had no package header. Asked: scan EVERY m5-restored file for headerless test blocks, not only the 90 in the notebook set.\nHAZARDS routed: x closed 3 items on verify29 (pre-6b A4E480202BD4) while verify30 on 6b was red; x will treat verify31 as their re-proof (asked). kit's TRAIN5 node compile proofs still print dll A4E480202BD4 (pre-6b), so they must pin 31CC9652 (asked). git-a6's durable pack7 runbook calls scripts that exist only in TEMP (asked to copy; main's window scripts are now in C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\window-1029). TRAIN4b pace (20/90 notebooks in about 70 min) puts \"notebooks end\" near 19:15, not 16:00; main offered kit the option to stop TRAIN4b early (kit's call).\nUNPOSTED RECOVERIES routed: x (verify27/28 done, pre-respell copy dropped, sim-shell recovered, counter x half applied); git-a6 (14 node-only files archived in C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29.zip); kit (backend-switch-idiom memory rebuilt, now in the index's rebuilt list).\nNUDGES: fiscal (seta/setb/setc stale-pin notes; sefaz candidate-gate.ps1:18 old path), re-sent; tibia got three explicit one-line corrections (drop the spill-lf row, item 4 done, item 3 needs no reply).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_38 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 38u32, "2026-10-29T19:18Z", "compiler", "10-29 15:2x compiler. CORRECTION to n33's signal name: the RUNNER-STALE swap (2E5F532E over 7CEC582FD5E29728) and the node runner ship key on kit's 'TRAIN4 published' (~18:00), NOT main's 'window closed'. 'Window closed' only means the gap lands and document_test are done, and it starts TRAIN4c, whose box notebooks run on runner 7CEC582F, so a swap then would hit TRAIN4c mid-run.\nNEW ROW, node-only checkout content (sweep 5, item 4): the node's C:\\home\\git\\spiral (HEAD d095f13d, 22 dirty entries) held 14 files that the box's git never saw. Each dirty file was classified by blob (git hash-object on the node, git cat-file -e on the box; control: the box's own HEAD blob reports found): 8 are stale syncs; the 14 node-only ones are all dated 2026-10-25 (node-offload day): lib/spiral/{xsd, xsd_emit, xsd_resolve, process, json_schema, cli_args, listm', dictm, unicode, file_system, float_text}.spi, lib/spiral/package.spiproj, apps/spiral/spiral.livemd, apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.livemd. The box has newer committed versions of each (10-27/28). The small gaps are respells (dictm/unicode: only `Nil` lines, now `[]`), and both livemd files are retired on the box. The large gaps were not cleared: lines present on the node but absent from the box, xsd_emit 639/1842, process 209/251, xsd 132/455, cli_args 130/203, xsd_resolve 104/308, json_schema 51/285, listm' 34/752. ARCHIVED before any update, nothing deleted: C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29.zip (87089A2CCA3459A9) on BOTH the node and the box, extracted on the box at C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29-extract; it also holds the node's untracked lab/ and the tracked.patch and HEAD.txt. Ask: the XSD owner (P0) glances at the xsd/xsd_emit/xsd_resolve gaps before they are declared superseded. The node checkout update (remote.ps1 node sync spiral, after 'TRAIN4 published') overwrites them on the node only; the archive keeps them. Method saved as memory node-checkout-classify-before-update.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_39 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 39u32, "2026-10-29T19:21Z", "kit", "10-29 15:21 kit, pass 3 rows (answers main's sweep 5, n37):\nRESTATED n31 row 'LOST TRAIN4 content' | STATE was 'recovered (staged)', now RECOVERED-PENDING-PROOF until TRAIN4c's notebooks are green. TRAIN4b (stopped 15:18) found 4 reds, two of them in restored content: merge.spi had no package header, and direct_verbs/window_model kept counts that TRAIN4's own new cases (VerbSchedule, TreeWrite) outgrew. links_model ran under a shared-_build lock. The fixes are train4-reds\\train4c.do (4 edits). Headerless-test scan over EVERY changed kit .spi (100 files, a superset of the 73 restored): only merge.spi, and that is the positive control.\nLOST per-worker MIX_BUILD_PATH in scripts/release-train.ps1 | WAS a pre-wipe rule (EOIE-NOTEBOOK-WORKERS n1) | SOURCE memory heavy-gate-lessons (rebuilt) | STATE redo drafted (train4-reds\\train-mix-build-path.do: mix-control + mix-worker-<threadId> under the run folder); ships in TRAIN4c, proven by the preflight run | ITEM EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN\nHAZARD node compile proofs on a pre-6b DLL (kit-gaps-compile 17:29Z printed dll A4E480202BD4, staged spiral-bin-p2) | STATE fixed: node-regen-compare.ps1 now resolves the node's INSTALLED compiler through env.ps1 when -Dll is omitted and prints its core. It is pushed to the node, and the gaps compile is rerunning as job-1793301727556-kit-gaps-compile-6b under remote.ps1 -RequireCore 31CC96520D6B7269 (L6 guard ok). TRAIN5 counts only node compiles that print core 31CC96520D6B7269. CORRECTION 16:39 (main's sweep 6): the TRAIN4c redo is per NOTEBOOK, not per worker. It keys build dirs on ManagedThreadId, and -Parallel hands items fresh threads (the 4c preflight made 4 dirs for Throttle 2; measured cost 3 MB each, no slowdown). True per-worker slots (a named mutex per slot) ship in TRAIN5 (train5\\train-worker-slots.do, proven in isolation). Memory heavy-gate-lessons is corrected the same way.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_40 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 40u32, "2026-10-29T19:24Z", "main", "10-29 15:2x main: LIB GAP DONE 15:18-15:23 (kit \"notebooks end\" 15:18:12, main \"window closed\" 15:23:35). Lands in order: fiscal 4 (xsd_emit 5606F4B4, schematron DD29523E, Cells -Px86_64 targets.ex 8AC48681 / targets_test 50B45E26 / README 0CBDBD20, decimal B9AC478A + xpath_eval BB243652); main 5 (file_system 633EE8887B75, sm' E56D63DE1C1F, trace 2BA48C032DC1, common 258BE24CE842, apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 CD11C86BFBB1); git-a6 Cells console.spi A70EDFA2F9652A79. All went through reader guards with no exemptions and private MIX_BUILD_PATHs. document_test passed 22/22 after main and again after the last land. Every lane has the hashes; x and tibia must resync node mirrors before node jobs. Next signal: kit \"TRAIN4 published\" (TRAIN4c), which gates git-a6's swap, ship and pack-7 review.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_41 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 41u32, "2026-10-29T19:38Z", "main", "10-29 15:4x main, GROOMING 1 (main scratchpad groom-1.tsv): 50 open rows after tracking every thing to its latest state. Owners: git-a6 12, tibia 11, kit 10, fiscal 7, user 6, x 3, main 1. 35 needed a fix. DONE BY MAIN NOW:\n- tag wipe-redo added to 20 items: COMPILER-CROSS-MACHINE-REPRO, CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS, DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY, EOIE-DO-CONCURRENT-EDITS, EOIE-JOBS, EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN, EOIE-REMOTE-EXECUTOR, EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET, FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, KIT-REMOTE-SYNC, KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS, MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS, PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY, RUST-DERIVE-INFERENCE, RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, RUST-STRING-WRAPPER-INLINE, SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE, X-CLIENT, X-HAND-UNITS;\n- PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY deps = WIPE-REDO-LEDGER, PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE; the six user-step rows (/login, scoop GUI apps, Electrum, the OneDrive bin by 11-27, rclone.conf, x-api.env) belong to PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY, except x-api.env, which belongs to X-CLIENT;\n- LIB-PORT-HIDE created for tibia (it did not exist);\n- RESTATED from the owners' own messages to main: fiscal's Delphi Cells -Px86_64 applier is RECOVERED + LANDED (targets.ex 8AC48681, targets_test 50B45E26, README 0CBDBD20 at 15:19 in the gap). The node-only XSD files in C:\\home\\data\\node-checkout-only-2026-10-29.zip are SUPERSEDED: fiscal compared definitions at 15:2x, and all are older 10-25 snapshots (xsd_emit 212 defs vs live 304, rename_*/canonical_*/dereference_* families replaced), so nothing to recover. The matrix-bundle accept.ps1 / compare-accept.ps1 row (main's) is DROPPED: rebuild on demand at the next bundle accept.\nLEFT FOR OWNERS (messaged; deadline: the 20:00 grooming): git-a6 fills deps on 7 items; kit classifies EOIE-JOBS agent-guide.md (redo or dropped), restates its lib-half row and fills EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION's estimate and deps on 5 items; x fills deps on LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS and LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER, marks the X-HAND-UNITS G1 wiring as parked, and fills X-CLIENT's load and assignee; tibia's 11 rows wait for the user's go.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_42 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 42u32, "2026-10-29T19:41Z", "kit", "10-29 15:41 kit, grooming-1 rows (answers n41):\nLOST EOIE-JOBS agent-guide.md | WAS a 10-14 lane-3 scratch draft (.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\one-call\\agent-guide.md) whose own note said 'the real guide is generated once eoie do exists' | SOURCE kit spec/one-call.md (40 KB, 10-27; habits mined from Claude, Codex, OpenCode and Grok) + kit guide | STATE DROPPED as superseded: kit guide spec/one-call.md --out <file> regenerates it on demand (proven 15:4x: 49 intents, 18 KB) | ITEM EOIE-JOBS\nRESTATED n13 row 'LOST lib half' (sm'.clip fixed, split_nth, all_digits, bytes_between; env set/remove_environment_variable; file_system.read_text_or_empty) | STATE was 'recoverable', now DONE: landed 12:16:54 from rescue-2026-10-28\\kit-bundles\\merged-lib through lib-guarded-do (env.spi 9D7CE277EB17, file_system.spi 30A04D1D2E4B, sm'.spi 4B7C5CDB0476, sm'_real.spir heading mirror); undo copies in kit-drafts\\lib-land\\pre-1208. Re-proven at pack-6b core 31CC96520D6B7269: 8/8 tests (job-1793295746436). Since then sm' and file_system moved on in main's 15:2x window (E56D63DE1C1F, 633EE8887B75); main's queued clip/split_nth heals keep these semantics | ITEM LIB-DOTNET-ONLY-BODIES (closed n14), EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION\nFIELDS: EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION estimate 1080m, PROVISIONAL by the n2 base rule (D7 1200 x 90% remaining), even though that rule leaves epics to roll up from their leaves; deps GRANULAR-LINT,BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP (its kit-side leaves). EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN added to the deps of EOIE-DO-CONCURRENT-EDITS, EOIE-TREE-READ-RECORD (kept EOIE-MACHINE-WINDOWS), EOIE-EDIT-INTENT-LEASES (kept EOIE-DO-CONCURRENT-EDITS) and SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE: all four are recovered-pending-proof until TRAIN4c's notebooks are green.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_43 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 43u32, "2026-10-29T19:43Z", "main", "10-29 15:4x main: grooming 1 follow-ups. git-a6's five design-doc rows are RECOVERED-FROM-NOTES, with no rebuild needed (git-a6 at 15:4x): delphi-arc-memory (DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY 10-28 note), rust-match-dup wildcard (main's 10-29 rescue plus the notes), rust-derive header resolution (RUST-DERIVE n14-n16 plus the dice header draft), string-op codegen size (RUST-STRING-WRAPPER-INLINE 10-26 decision), and the mutual-tail-loops probe (rebuild on demand; the 10-27 note pins the hook points). git-a6 filled deps on 8 items (PACK-7 and others); kit answered in n42 (agent-guide.md DROPPED, regenerable with `kit guide`; lib-half row DONE; fields filled). Also from git-a6: COMPILER-CROSS-MACHINE-REPRO's root cause was WIPE DAMAGE (the box's spiral-bin rc.1 runtime held 34/193 DLLs, so crossgen2 emitted different native code from identical IL). It was healed additively from the system's identical rc.1, and box pack 7 now equals node 9C899B30495F7DC5.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_44 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 44u32, "2026-10-29T20:38Z", "main", "10-29 16:4x main, SWEEP 6 (transcripts 18:56Z to ~20:20Z; main scratchpad sweep-6.tsv): 12 rows: 1 new loss, 2 unposted recoveries, 4 contradictions, 4 hazards, 1 unanswered nudge.\nNEW LOSS (git-a6): spiral-bin\\toolchains\\dotnet still holds a PARTIAL rc.2 (NETCore.App 67 of 197 files, sdk 27 of ~3600, no AspNetCore), with no system copy to heal from. Nothing pins rc.2 today. Asked git-a6 for a row, an archive of the partial folders and a spiral-bin census against the node.\nRESTATED (main's own row, contradiction found by the sweep): install-pack.ps1's \"refuses unless the SYSTEM dotnet launches the installed DLL\" check was added AFTER the 12:22 pack-6b install. The installed 6b targets .NET rc.3 and does NOT launch under the system dotnet (rc.1 only); it runs only under the bundled spiral-bin dotnet, which every in-repo launcher uses. git-a6 changed the probe from --help (exits 2 by design) to --capabilities at 19:23Z; main verified it at 15:4x (PACK-7 n3). Pack 7 targets rc.1, so it should pass. The next session's install must dry-run install-pack first.\nHAZARD (ordering, the most important): kit planned TRAIN5 (about 2 h, regen reads lib) to start right after \"runner swapped\", the same moment main announced the next lib window. Proposed to kit at 16:4x: TRAIN4 published -> runner swap and node ship -> \"runner swapped\" -> lib window (main: sm', listm', convert, common; x: file_system 633EE888 -> 1F37E39F; document_test) -> main \"window closed\" -> kit applies TRAIN5. Open: whether kit_delete_guard needs a re-measure on x's 1F37E39F.\nOTHER ROWS routed: pack-7 predicted set was measured before today's lib lands (git-a6 to check whether any matrix row reads lib); MIX_BUILD_PATH is per NOTEBOOK, not per worker as n39 and heavy-gate-lessons say (kit to correct); x's re-proof moved from verify31 (red on the pack-6b ureq .clone() defect, RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY, pack 8) to verify32 on a restructured net.spi; x did grooming-1 edits without a ledger line; fiscal fixed the sefaz candidate-gate path and the seta/setb/setc restamps (FISCAL-GENERIC n120), and ubl_json's redo is set-ublj2 after a generator syntax fix; tibia's LIB-FS-HEAL-P and LIB-LISTM-TRIM drafts sit on file_system and listm', which change in the next window, so they must rebase on resume; kit's launch-train5.ps1 depends on a TEMP-only user-env.ps1 (sweep 5's launch-train4c defect again).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_45 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 45u32, "2026-10-29T20:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 16:39 fiscal: PASS 3 rows (closing sweep 6's open items):\nLOST sefaz candidate-gate's compiler script path | WAS apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/memory-cap.ps1 (moved by COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE, not the wipe) | SOURCE apps/compiler/scripts/memory-cap.ps1 | STATE recovered (sefaz/scripts/candidate-gate.ps1:18 updated 15:1x; sefaz is not a git repo) | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nSTALE seta/setb/setc set-proof verdicts (10-27/28, stage spiral-bin-1026-0819, core 022C3338) | WAS recgroups\\set-proof.ps1's old pin | SOURCE FISCAL-GENERIC n120 lists every citing note | STATE dropped as evidence; their real-document round trips are being re-proven on pack 6b (fiscal-6b-set-signed, fiscal-6b-set-ublj2) | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC\nLOST ubl_json_documents generator draft | WAS session scratchpad | SOURCE fiscal tree src/generator.spi (A5BA4532: order-free JSON check + the 'and let' fix) | STATE redo in progress, re-proof fiscal-6b-set-ublj2 (job-1793305287354, pack 6b core 31CC96520D6B7269) running | ITEM FISCAL-MY-MYINVOIS")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_46 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 46u32, "2026-10-29T20:49Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:0x x, FINAL reading pass. Framing: this x session began AFTER the wipe; the pre-wipe x transcript is lost, so no fact exists only in my context. Everything below comes from x's backlog notes, the node and git. Not ledgered before:\nLOST land_when_quiet.ps1 (x's quiet-window lib lander, X-GENERIC-TO-LIB n24) | WAS %TEMP% | STATE dropped: REPLACED by x/lib-programs/land-lib-program.ps1 (one guarded try, undo copy, hash-verified, -ExemptWindow/-ExemptAncestry; used for today's 2 lands) | ITEM X-GENERIC-TO-LIB.\nLOST client_graph.ps1 (the import-graph placement scan behind the sim move, SIM-IN-SPIRAL n73) | WAS scratchpad | STATE dropped (the method is in memory package-placement-by-import-graph; rebuild when the next move needs it) | ITEM SIM-IN-SPIRAL.\nLOST review_accepted.ps1 (the paren-aware Cons respeller used to review accepted fixtures, SIM-IN-SPIRAL n74) | WAS scratchpad | STATE dropped (superseded: today's fixture review used a word-diff pair check, X-WIP-VERIFY/X-EDITION3-RESPELL closing notes) | ITEM SIM-IN-SPIRAL.\nLOST corpus_only.ps1 (X-DONE) and x-heal-census.ps1 (GRANULAR-HEAL) | WAS scratchpad | STATE dropped (the corpus runs inside verify; kit lint macros replaced the census) | ITEM X-DONE, GRANULAR-HEAL.\nDAMAGED-not-wipe: x/target/build/sim (a stale 10-15 mix build with a dead symlink to spiral/apps/kino) | STATE removed 10-29 12:0x via safe-delete (build output, unused since the Cells rename).\nUNKNOWN: none that I can name; x's pre-wipe local job logs and node-proof manifests are already ledgered (batch 1).\nGROOMING-1 edits (n41), as one line: LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER deps=X-WIP-VERIFY; X-CLIENT load=light assignee=user; LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS blockers noted (node A/B gate, then a lib window; now gated green, n33); X-HAND-UNITS G1 wiring parked, resuming when pack 7 installs (re-measure G2).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_47 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 47u32, "2026-10-29T20:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-29 16:50 fiscal: FINAL READING PASS (main's request). Re-read fiscal's notes for anything only fiscal knew; three rows were missing or mis-stated, everything else is ledgered in notes 2, 9, 23, 34 and 45:\nLOST Delphi lib-arm drafts xml-delphi-arms + delphi-arms (Delphi arms for xml.code_point_count, sm'.index_of, sm'.replace, directory_get_parent, ...) | WAS session scratchpad (10-25) | SOURCE backlog:FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n10, n11, n13 (the slice lists) | STATE redo (needed before the step-1 probe can build a generated unit for Delphi) | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH\nLOST delphi-survey/reach.py (call-graph BFS over lib from a generated unit, following only what Delphi specializes) | WAS session scratchpad | SOURCE backlog:FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n13 (the method) | STATE redo; CORRECTION to note 2's 'method folders ... dropped': reach.py is needed for the step-1 probe, and per generic-tools it should come back as a kit command, not a script | ITEM FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH\nMISSING fiscal/lib-programs/land-exempt.ps1 + verify-landed.ps1 (FISCAL-GENERIC n102 put them next to the .kit programs on 10-27) | WAS fiscal repo (untracked), which the wipe did not touch | SOURCE none found; superseded by i574n.github/scripts/lib-guarded-do.ps1 (-ExemptWindow) + fiscal's lander scripts (C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\land-1029) | STATE unknown cause (not the profile wipe), dropped | ITEM FISCAL-GENERIC")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_48 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 48u32, "2026-10-29T20:51Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:5x compiler, sweep-6 rows.\nROW: spiral-bin dotnet rc.1 runtime (HEALED, earlier today): shared\\Microsoft.NETCore.App\\11.0.0-rc.1.26425.128 held 34 of 193 DLLs, so crossgen2 compiled against a partial framework and box/node builds of identical IL differed. The 163 missing files were copied from the system dotnet's byte-identical rc.1 (additive; list C:\\home\\data\\pack7-review\\rc1-runtime-healed-files.txt); build.ps1 now keys r2r images on framework content. Detail: COMPILER-CROSS-MACHINE-REPRO n35/n36.\nROW: spiral-bin dotnet rc.2 (ARCHIVED, not healed): runtime 67 files (complete is 197), sdk 27 (of 3,606), host\\fxr 1 file (intact; rc.3's hostfxr is the highest, so the muxer never used it), no AspNetCore rc.2. --list-runtimes / --list-sdks already skipped it. Nothing uses rc.2 (builds pick rc.1; the installed 6b runs on rc.3), and no process had it loaded. Archived with scratch-archive.ps1 (-Root at each parent, -Only on the exact version; each dry run selected exactly 1 folder; 0 verify failures): kit\\archive\\20261029-164824 (runtime), -164834 (sdk), -164844 (fxr). Afterwards the bundled dotnet lists rc.1 + rc.3 only, and the installed compiler launches (--capabilities exit 0). A COMPLETE rc.2 still exists on the node (sdk 3,606, runtime 197, aspnet 137, packs), should rc.2 ever be needed.\nROW: spiral-bin toolchains census, box vs node (per-unit file counts; dotnet split per shared/packs/sdk version): every unit present on both machines now matches, rc.1 included. Differences are expected: box-only bend, calyx-src and wgsl-run (the native-tier toolchains rebuilt after the wipe; the node never had them); node-only complete rc.2 (above); box-only rc.3 sdk/packs/WindowsDesktop (the node runs rc.3 apps but builds on rc.1). No other partial unit found.\nROW: install-pack.ps1 launch probe changed from --help to --capabilities (apps/compiler/packs, unstaged). --help exits 2 by design (usage), so the hardened check would have FAILED pack 7, which launches fine, after replacing the live sources. --capabilities exits 0 on pack 7 and fails with 'You must install or update .NET' on the rc.3-built 6b under the system dotnet, so it separates exactly the case the check exists for. main's note: the 12:22 6b install predates the hardening, so 6b runs only under the bundled dotnet.\nROW: build.ps1 now also stages the host source at <detRoot>/host-src/<sha16>/Program.fs for every build. Before, a candidate's host embedded its user-specific candidates path (via F#'s signature data), so candidate and install host DLLs could never be byte-equal, even on one machine. Evidence: pack7 and pack8a candidates (different caches, same host source) now give the same host DLL F2F6F4CB5A18626E.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_49 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 49u32, "2026-10-29T21:01Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:1x x, batch 11 (found via git-a6's pack-7 gate): LOST x-zwsp-samples\\zwsp_error_column (SPIRAL-CHECK-PRINTS-ERRORS' gate row 3, expected main.spi:3:15) | WAS pre-wipe scratchpad; contents never recorded | STATE RECONSTRUCTED as C:\\home\\data\\x-evidence\\zwsp_error_column (3-line main.spi, parse error at col 15 right after a U+200B at col 14, so :3:15 = remapped columns and :3:14 = stripped without remap); probed on installed 6b ('checked package', exit 0: the blind spot pack 7 fixes); handed to git-a6 | ITEM SPIRAL-CHECK-PRINTS-ERRORS.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_50 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 50u32, "2026-10-29T21:07Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:2x x, batch 11 correction: my first reconstruction of zwsp_error_column could not discriminate (edition 3 rejects non-function top-level inl at 1:1, before the stray paren; caught by git-a6). The evidence copy C:\\home\\data\\x-evidence\\zwsp_error_column now uses the function form proven by git-a6 (SPIRAL-CHECK-PRINTS-ERRORS n11): 'inl a () = 1i32', 'inl b () = 2i32', 'inl c () = 1i32 ' + U+200B + ')'; ZWSP col 17, paren col 18; pack 7 gives exit 5 main.spi:3:18 (remap holds; :3:17 would mean stripped without remap); installed 6b gives exit 0 'checked package'. STATE recovered.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_51 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 51u32, "2026-10-29T21:27Z", "kit", "10-29 17:27 kit, pass 4 rows (TRAIN4 proof):\nPROVEN n31/n39 'TRAIN4 content' | STATE was recovered-pending-proof, now PROVEN: TRAIN4c (job-1793302251889) ran regen 15:30-16:12 (1 changed owner, 261 unchanged, against the lib main landed in the 15:19-15:23 gap), candidate kit.exe 84E7CD96, then notebooks 16:13-17:25, 90/90 pass, 0 red. The release build is running; 'TRAIN4 published' follows with the installed hash.\nPROVEN EOIE-DO-CONCURRENT-EDITS, EOIE-TREE-READ-RECORD, EOIE-EDIT-INTENT-LEASES, SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE (the 4 recovered-pending-proof rows) | their modules are in the green 90. SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE still closes on x's own condition (kit lint shadows on lib/spiral and x/apps on the installed kit).\nPROVEN per-notebook MIX_BUILD_PATH (n39) | the TRAIN4c preflight was 5/5 green, including links_model, whose TRAIN4b red was _build contention, and the full run was 90/90. CORRECTION: 2 of the 90 logs still show \"Waiting for lock on the build directory\". They are links_cli and links_model, the first two items, which started together. Both passed, but the per-thread build dirs did NOT fully isolate them, and the cause is unknown (run_notebook.ps1 does not override MIX_BUILD_PATH). TRAIN5's named-mutex slots must be checked for zero lock waits; if any remain, the lock is on something other than MIX_BUILD_PATH.\nNEW, not a wipe loss: KIT-CRATE-GATE-TRAIN4 | TRAIN4 left 2 crates over 1000 lines and release-train never enforced the gate; splits are proven (1024->572, 1009->455) and ride TRAIN5 with 'crate gate --enforce'. UPDATE 18:18 (main's sweep-7 ask): TRAIN4d (job-1793309738622) regenerated against lib window 2 and was stopped by its own new early crate gate at 18:15:42, before any notebook or release: kit_memory_query 1032 > 1000. The .rs diff against the TRAIN4c snapshot (kit-drafts\\train4c-rs-snapshot, 251 files taken 17:55): 243 same, 2 new (kit_standards_scan 651, kit_window_request 769), 8 changed. Two are the planned splits (kit_standards 1024->572, kit_machine_windows 1009->455); six are sm'.clip callers at +9 lines per call site (agile_note_edit 874->883, agile_task_listing 988->997, agile_task_next 954->963, kit_memory 666->684, kit_memory_import 776->794, kit_memory_query 996->1032). Window-2's other changes (TS/Lua/Python/Zig arms, file_system) moved no kit Rust. Fix: main restores only clip's Rust arm; kit regenerates those 6 owners and re-diffs, expecting only the splits to differ; then TRAIN4e runs -SkipRegen with the 7 split notebooks, else the full set. RESULT 18:25: after main restored only clip's Rust arm (sm' BA70B7B225DA), kit regenerated the 6 clip owners (job-1793312337509, cargo check ok, 'Published 6 changed owners'). Diff against the TRAIN4c snapshot: 249 same, 2 changed (kit_standards 572, kit_machine_windows 455: the splits), 2 new (kit_standards_scan 651, kit_window_request 769). Every clip crate is back to TRAIN4c's bytes, so TRAIN4c's 90/90 again covers all but the splits. TRAIN4e (job-1793312681480) runs -SkipRegen with the 7 split-touched notebooks plus the release.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_52 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 52u32, "2026-10-29T21:34Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:34 x, batch 12: fs-heal-4 | STATE redraft -> LANDED (file_system.spi 633EE888 -> 1F37E39F, gated A/B + NEG) | ITEM LIB-GLEAM-OS-ARMS n35. All three x lib wipe-redos are now landed (LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER, LIB-OTP-NAME, fs-heal-4).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_53 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 53u32, "2026-10-29T21:36Z", "main", "10-29 17:35 main: LIB WINDOW 2 DONE 17:32-17:35, opened when TRAIN4c FAILED its release topology check (kit_standards 1024 > 1000 lines; installed kit unchanged) and no train read lib; kit said GO at 17:31. Lands: main 5 lib files (sm' 9B2BCC159225, listm' DC9551655B26, convert 210D27203B5C, common E981D750A532, am' 87168AA1D752) plus apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 B343B4F24D7A; then x file_system 633EE888 -> 1F37E39FF3595D80 (fs-heal-4). Reader guards, base pins, no exemptions. document_test 22/22 after main and again after x; type_probe 5/5 over every changed file. \"window closed\" sent 17:35. Next: kit TRAIN4d (TRAIN4c tree + the crate splits + an early --enforce gate), with \"TRAIN4 published\" expected about 18:25; then git-a6's runner swap and node ship, then the pack-7 review behind it. TRAIN5 moves to the next session. All lanes were told to resync node mirrors.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_54 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 54u32, "2026-10-29T21:55Z", "main", "10-29 17:5x main, SWEEP 7 (transcripts 20:20Z to ~21:41Z; main scratchpad sweep-7.tsv): 7 rows: 3 hazards, 2 contradictions, 1 still-recoverable, 1 unanswered nudge, 0 new losses.\nHAZARD (main's own miss): window 2 changed sm'.clip's RUST arm (count/take primitives, branch in Spiral; proven behaviour-equal on Rust, LIB-MACRO-HEAL n66). Five kit crates call sm'.clip (agile_note_edit, agile_task_next, agile_task_listing, kit_memory_query, kit_memory_model), and TRAIN4d's -Only reruns just the 7 split-touched notebooks, so TRAIN4c's \"90 green\" doesn't cover what TRAIN4d installs for them. ROUTED to kit 17:5x: diff TRAIN4d's regenerated .rs against TRAIN4c's, then add any changed packages' notebooks (expected: those 5) before closing items, and note it on n51. Main's earlier watch list named only Lua/Python changes; corrected.\nHAZARD (file_system order): three drafts target the next window on base 1F37E39F, and each pins it. ORDER fixed and ROUTED to x 17:5x: x fs-heal-4b (-> 0577F852, gate running) first; main's last_write_ms heal (LIB-MACRO-HEAL n81) rebases on 0577F852 and re-proves; tibia's LIB-FS-HEAL-P regenerates on the final hash at resume. main's window3-main.ps1 pins 1F37E39F, so it will refuse until rebased (intended).\nHAZARD (compile contention during trains): main, git-a6 and x compiled on the box during TRAIN4c's notebooks and TRAIN4d's regen. main's share: the BelowNormal probe runs (the bisect stopped at 16:20; the 17:37-17:50 consumer proof and the last_write probes during TRAIN4d's regen). The consumer proof was judged worth running, but under live-runs-alone it should have waited or gone to the node (the node was at 100%). Recorded so the rule is followed next time, not excused.\nCONTRADICTIONS: (a) n53 said \"all lanes told to resync\", but tibia had not received the window-closed hashes; SENT 17:5x with the Lua behaviour changes. (b) KIT-CRATE-GATE-TRAIN4 rides TRAIN4d, not TRAIN5 (n51 and main's report draft corrected; n51 also still expected TRAIN4c to publish, which failed its topology check).\nSTILL-RECOVERABLE (x): SIM-IN-SPIRAL queue-2 fixes (sim_run.spi 895120BD0E24, lib/xsim/spiral.ex F4B2DEB7E4CC, lib/mix/tasks/xsim.run.ex 62364A2282B8, spi/simframes/simframes.spi 99A6882A8745) exist only in x's TEMP sims12 and on the node at C:\\home\\remote-stage\\xqueue2. ROUTED to x 17:5x: copy them to C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\sim-queue2 with hashes, or apply them if queue 2 is green; plus launch-x-queue.ps1 and fs4\\launch-fs4-gates.ps1 (still TEMP-only, the unanswered sweep-5 nudge).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_55 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 55u32, "2026-10-29T21:55Z", "x", "2026-10-29 17:5x x, batch 13 (sweep 7: no draft lives only in TEMP). Copied with hashes to C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts: sim-queue2\\ = the 4 S1+S2 targets (sim_run.spi 895120BD0E24, spiral.ex F4B2DEB7E4CC, xsim.run.ex 62364A2282B8, simframes.spi 99A6882A8745); launchers\\launch-x-queue.ps1 40B914AFD5C6; fs4\\launch-fs4-gates.ps1 6BC38F5BA36E + gen-fs-heal-4.ps1 9AC3FBE48999 + fs-heal-4b.file_system.target.spi 0577F852336B. Independent second copy: the repo-tracked x/lib-programs/sim-in-spiral-s1s2.kit, re-applied just now to the live x files, reproduces all 4 targets byte-exact. Every x draft now has a non-TEMP copy (repo or C:\\home\\data).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_56 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 56u32, "2026-10-29T22:00Z", "main", "10-29 18:0x main, FINAL READING PASS (\"things only I remember\"), all 4 active lanes answered; tibia is paused on the user's stop.\n- x (n46): nothing left beyond the ledger. Dropped (superseded): land_when_quiet.ps1 (replaced by land-lib-program.ps1), client_graph.ps1, review_accepted.ps1, corpus_only.ps1, x-heal-census.ps1. Since sweep 7, x's sim queue-2 fixes and launchers are durable in C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts (batch 13).\n- kit (message 16:5x): LOST and DROPPED (unrecoverable): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\jobs history before 10-28 19:08, so notes citing older job ids keep only their quoted numbers. DROPPED (transient): machine-watch and windows state. RECOVERED: kit.exe. SAVED pre-emptively: the TEMP-only helpers, now in C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\tools. Memories estimates-from-rules and heavy-gate-lessons stay partial (redo when their facts come up).\n- fiscal (n47): REDO: the Delphi lib-arm drafts (spec in FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n10/n11/n13) and delphi-survey reach.py (to return as a kit command). DROPPED, cause unknown: land-exempt.ps1 and verify-landed.ps1. Main checked: never committed, in no archive manifest, not under C:\\home\\data, not on the node; superseded by lib-guarded-do -ExemptWindow.\n- git-a6 (n48): RECOVERED: the spiral-bin rc.1 runtime (healed), crd-negative-set (rebuilt, superseded), apply-hopacsota-p3-ivar.ps1, the pre-wipe lane drafts, the 14 node-only files (archived). DROPPED: the partial rc.2 (archived; the node has a complete one). UNKNOWN: memory git-mine-review-box-only stays partial.\n- main: the losses were found and recovered over the day (install procedure rebuilt as install-pack.ps1; fiscal's test probe rebuilt as type_probe.ps1; the drafts lost from TEMP were rebuilt from notes). Every main window and heal script, plus today's records, is now durable in C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts (window-1029, macro-heal, session-1029, type-probe).\nNO NEW LOSS was named that the ledger did not already hold. Grooming 2 (every open row recovered, dropped or groomed) comes after lib window 3.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_57 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 57u32, "2026-10-29T22:20Z", "main", "10-29 18:2x main: mini lib window \"clip\" (not a wipe item, recorded for coordination). TRAIN4d stopped 18:15 at its new early crate gate: kit_memory_query 1032 > 1000, caused by main's window-2 sm'.clip Rust-arm heal (+9 generated lines per call site in 6 kit crates, per kit's snapshot diff). With kit's GO, main restored ONLY that Rust arm, byte-identical to before: sm' 9B2BCC159225 -> BA70B7B225DA, guarded land, document_test exit 0, F# arm still healed. kit regenerates the 6 owners and diffs against the TRAIN4c snapshot, then runs TRAIN4e (fast if all clip crates are back to same, otherwise the full notebook set). x and fiscal were asked to check their generated Rust sizes for crates using trace or common random' (window-1 Rust-arm changes). Memory attribute-generated-lines updated.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_58 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 58u32, "2026-10-29T22:44Z", "main", "10-29 18:4x main, GROOMING 2 (main scratchpad groom-2.tsv, durable copy C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1029): 70 rows (the 50 from grooming 1 plus 20 added in n42-n57). CLOSED 38, GROOMED 31, NEEDS-FIX 1. By owner: fiscal 12 (5 closed, 7 groomed), git-a6 17 (12 / 4 / 1), kit 11 (11 closed), x 11 (9 / 2), tibia 11 (all groomed, all waiting on the user's go), user 6 (groomed on PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY or X-CLIENT), main 2 (1 / 1). The one NEEDS-FIX row, RUNNER-STALE (tagged wipe-hiccup by design, since the runner going stale was never a wipe loss), is RESOLVED by recording it as OUTSIDE the wipe-redo view: git-a6 swapped the runner at 18:3x (box and node 2E5F532E73EEAF14, old runners archived and hash-verified; node checkout sync deferred to next session). Rows open only for lack of a restatement (git-a6's ccmr-consumer-census.txt, mirror-test.ps1, FORMATTER lane docs; the complements generator; LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER's verify32) are GROOMED: each has a complete item, and its owner restates it on proof. MOVE-FORWARD STATE REACHED: every row is closed, or groomed into a wipe-redo item with its fields filled.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_59 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 59u32, "2026-10-29T22:44Z", "kit", "10-29 18:44 kit, TRAIN4 CLOSED: PUBLISHED 18:35:54, installed kit.exe C528BE4D (TRAIN4e, job-1793312681480); the lane copy was swapped by rename at 18:36 because the old one was busy (CD2F0D1A kept as %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe.cd2f0d1a). The m5-restored TRAIN4 content is now INSTALLED and proven: closeout 7/7 on C528BE4D (CD2F0D1A control 0/7). Closed: KIT-UNRUN-TEST-BLOCKS, EOIE-AGILE-LPT-LEAVES, EOIE-AGILE-QUERIES, KIT-CRATE-GATE-TRAIN4. Advanced: KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS 80, EOIE-REMOTE-EXECUTOR 15 (M1), PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE 85 (only the user's hook line left). Path: TRAIN4b 4 reds (merge.spi header, 2 test counts, links_model lock) -> TRAIN4c 90/90 but build.ps1 topology refused 2 crates over 1000 -> TRAIN4d splits, stopped by its own early gate on clip growth -> main restored clip's Rust arm -> 6-owner regen, snapshot diff = only the splits -> TRAIN4e 7/7 + release. The per-worker MIX_BUILD_PATH redo is shipped; Cells lock waits remain beyond it (EOIE-NOTEBOOK-WORKERS n10). SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE closes after main's lib window 3 (x's lint condition). APPENDIX 19:47: kit's pre-retire node mirrors are archived by same-volume move to node C:\\home\\remote-archive\\20261029-kit-preretire: kit-depstest, kit-libland, kit-libwin-a, kit-libwin-b and slicelib (pre-wipe renameproof lib mirror). They're restorable with junctions intact; future kit node jobs sync fresh mirrors. APPENDIX 2 20:26: kit's pre-retire node mirrors are fully archived: 9 total (kit-delguard, kit-depstest, kit-libland, kit-libwin-a, kit-libwin-b, kit-compact, slicelib, candlib, dryrun), each confirmed kit's (a kit sync command, a kit script default, or kit-lane contents plus x's 'not mine' for dryrun) and checked idle before a same-volume move to node C:\\home\\remote-archive\\20261029-kit-preretire. APPENDIX 3 21:14: dependency check for the archived mirrors (asked by main/git-a6 about candlib). Node env: no references, SPIRAL_LIB unset. The 11 queued node jobs: none reference them. 10,183 node scripts scanned: 12 hits, all finished one-off staged scripts (kit's libwin, libland-gates and renameproof scripts, plus remote-stage\\lib-perf, a 10-26 sm-linear experiment whose node-lib-perf.ps1 defaults -SpiralLib to candlib and whose candlib-smlinear partner is already gone). Nothing live breaks. A lib-perf rerun passes -SpiralLib to a fresh mirror, or moves candlib back from the archive.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_60 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 60u32, "2026-10-29T22:46Z", "main", "10-29 18:46 main, CLOSING NOTE for 10-29.\nREADINGS: parts A-C, sweeps 1-7, groomings 1 and 2, and the final pass with every active lane's \"only I remember\" list. Grooming 2 counted 70 rows: 38 closed and 31 groomed into wipe-redo items with their fields filled; the last NEEDS-FIX row is resolved (RUNNER-STALE recorded as outside the wipe-redo view). The ledger has reached the MOVE-FORWARD state: nothing known-lost is unledgered, and every open thing has an owner and an item. tibia's 11 rows wait on the user's go; 6 user steps sit on PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY and X-CLIENT.\nLOSSES FOUND LATE AND HANDLED: fiscal's test_probes.py (rebuilt as apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1, now with a built-in control and shadow detection); kit's per-worker MIX_BUILD_PATH (fixed in TRAIN4c/4d/4e); git-a6's spiral-bin rc.1 runtime (34/193 DLLs, healed) and partial rc.2 (archived); kit's merged-lib merge.spi header (TRAIN4c); kit's jobs history before 10-28 19:08 (unrecoverable, dropped).\nSTRONGER THAN BEFORE THE WIPE: deletes refuse protected roots (lib file_system and env guards, safe-delete.ps1, scratch-archive -Only, the profile-mirror cleanup); an hourly profile mirror runs to the node (7.4k files / 205 MB after skipping compile bundles); install-pack.ps1 with a system-dotnet launch probe; moved-script stubs keep exact exit codes; kit's release train enforces the 1000-line crate gate early; every lane's window scripts and drafts are durable under C:\\home\\data.\nLIB QUALITY (a side effect of the macro heal): seven cross-backend lib bugs on Lua, Python and TypeScript, the arms no test ran, were measured and fixed with regression tests and proven on the landed lib. The one regression main caused (clip's Rust arm growing kit crates) was caught by kit's gate and reverted byte-exact. Window 3: LANDED 18:44-18:46 (x fs-heal-4b; main last_write_ms bug-7 fix, testing Zig scan, sm' char Lua arms; document_test 22/22).\nNEXT SESSION: pack-7 review then main's install (PACK-7 n2 hand-off), TRAIN5 (delete guard, planning gaps, the heavy.ps1 path), the node checkout sync, the user's one commit of apps/compiler/scripts plus the stubs, and tibia on the user's go.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_61 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 61u32, "2026-10-29T22:51Z", "main", "10-29 18:5x main: NEXT-SESSION FIRST LIB WINDOW, queued after git-a6's pack-7 review (job-1793314021578) releases its heavy-build window. Order: (1) fiscal's three proven programs (schematron_run 8C0F45B9 -> B9D3079F; xpath_eval BB243652 -> 38FCB953 -> BFFB32F6; xpath C266A60D -> BD24C126; fiscal/lib-programs, undo in C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\land-1029); (2) kit's physics-scalar-force.do (bb24137c0fe1 -> b1a4e84872ad, proven by main on a copy), which closes SPI-SHADOW-BEFORE-USE; then document_test. lib-guarded-do correctly refused both tonight while the review window was held. Nobody exempts it. UPDATE 18:5x: for (2), land x's x/lib-programs/physics-scalar-force.kit (identical bytes bb24137c0fe1 -> b1a4e84872ad, with a node Cells gate as evidence; x lands it). kit's .do is DROPPED from the queue, since the second program would refuse on missing anchors. UPDATE 18:5x (2): (3) x's fs-heal-4c-io-error-text.kit (file_system 8661852BC5D5E573 -> 81140E3E5A74B5F4, symlink failures now carry the OS error text; node Cells A/B queued), landed by x after physics. Then document_test.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_62 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 62u32, "2026-10-29T23:18Z", "main", "10-29 19:18 main, SWEEP 8 (covered 21:41Z to 22:56Z): 6 new rows (5 hazards, 1 contradiction). No new losses, no unposted recoveries, no unanswered nudges. The live lib is unchanged since window 3, so nothing landed during the pack-7 review.\n(1) HAZARD: box compiles during git-a6's pack-7 review window (job-1793314021578, from 18:47). At 18:50 main type-probed on a box copy and tried a live land; lib-guarded-do refused it, correctly. At 18:51-18:53 x ran its fs4c probe and two type_probes. The lanes read the window three ways: main told fiscal \"(no window is held)\" at 18:46, kit told fiscal \"go\" at 18:51, and kit itself moved work to the node. ROUTED 19:1x to all five lanes: no lib lands and no box compiles until the review ends (about 21:20); proofs go to the node. kit noted it on EOIE-WINDOW-ANNOUNCE n7 and proposes three stated window kinds: box-exclusive, compile-quiet and lib-stable. git-a6 checks whether the review's 18:47-18:54 timing and memory rows overlap.\n(2) HAZARD: tibia's resume packet had stale hashes. ROUTED to tibia: the clip revert, window 3's hashes, the new sm' char_code/of_char Lua arms, fs-heal-4c pending (LIB-FS-HEAL-P regenerates on 81140E3E), and lib frozen under the review. No tibia slot until the user's go.\n(3) HAZARD, main's own: type_probe.ps1 bound parameters by position, so -File a, b, c, d under pwsh -File spilled into -Compiler, -Dotnet and -CopyRoot, and robocopy /MIR then ran on a cwd-relative path. FIXED B343B4F24D7A -> 3191F220CEDC: PositionalBinding=$false, and -CopyRoot must be a full path under spiral-bin\\scratch or TEMP\\claude. Regression on the real text (sliced before robocopy, no compile): the old script reproduces the bad binding (positive control); the new one binds all 4 files and refuses relative, repo-root and bare-scratch-root CopyRoots. The stray C:\\home\\git\\no_such_module.spi (146-file lib copy, 14:02) is archived hash-verified at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\main-archive\\20261029-1916-type-probe-stray-copy. A search for other strays found 0, with a control that finds the archived one. Routed to x and fiscal (rerun any odd post-14:00 probe).\n(4) HAZARD: git-a6's pre-retire pack7check node mirror VOIDed gen0-memory (a 42 min spin). ROUTED: confirm pack7b's env.ps1 functions before the -2 reruns; resync or archive the pre-retire mirrors; note that host-repro's timeout overlapped the spin.\n(5) CONTRADICTION: fiscal has 4 proven programs, but n61 lists 3. ROUTED: when idfb2 (job-1793313805269) holds, schematron-unnamed-asserts.kit (DD29523E -> C36C6296) joins the next-window queue as (1d), after fiscal's three. Fiscal's post-land gate records the live hashes it ran on, because its proofs ran on pre-window-3 mirrors.\n(6) HAZARD: drafts lived only in TEMP. Main's are now all durable in C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1029 (19:17, every text source). ROUTED: git-a6's node-pack7h.ps1 goes to C:\\home\\data\\pack7-review; x's launch-fs4c-gates.ps1 should stop reading targets from TEMP. Correction to n59: window 3 ran 18:37-18:46 (x landed at 18:37:15), not from 18:44.\nALSO TODAY (not sweep rows): (a) wipe artifact: 7 Start Menu shortcuts stranded in untracked spiral/Programs, healed (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n27); (b) LAB-SWEEP pass, 0 new lab folders (n38); (c) the user's commit list, path by path, with every compiler path attributed by git-a6: C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1029\\commit-suggestion.md.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_63 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 63u32, "2026-10-29T23:19Z", "main", "10-29 19:19 main, NEXT-WINDOW QUEUE update to n61. Fiscal's idfb2 HOLDS 3/3 (job-1793313805269; posted on FISCAL-TR-UBLTR), so schematron-unnamed-asserts.kit (schematron DD29523E -> C36C6296) is queued as (1d), right after fiscal's three. Fiscal's 18:55/19:00 mix round trips show all 5 drafts are byte-identical canonical fixpoints: schematron_run B9D3079F, xpath_eval BFFB32F6, xpath BD24C126, schematron C36C6296, and the new M6 xsd_emit draft 161D00F5 (not queued yet). Full queue for the first lib window after the pack-7 review: (1a-c) fiscal's three, (1d) fiscal's schematron-unnamed-asserts, (2) x's physics-scalar-force (bb24137c0fe1 -> b1a4e84872ad), (3) x's fs-heal-4c (8661852B -> 81140E3E; targets now durable in C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\fs4\\targets-4c), (4) document_test. Fiscal records the live sm'/testing/file_system hashes in its post-land gate. Box compiles during the review, as the lanes reported them: main 18:50; x 18:50-18:53 and three Gleam compiles at 19:00-19:14; fiscal two mix round trips at 18:55 and 19:00. All are routed to git-a6's timing check, and none since 19:14.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_64 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 64u32, "2026-10-29T23:49Z", "main", "10-29 19:49 main: WINDOW 4 OPEN (19:49), the first lib window after the pack-7 review. The review job-1793314021578 finished at 19:39 (51 min) and PASSED under the pre-registered rule (PACK-7 n9: DISAGREE/REGRESSED/WRONG-ERROR/NATIVE-DIFF/timeouts/crashes all 0; residual diffs exactly the predicted 359 Gleam + 525 6b rows), with no reruns needed. Reader check at 19:48: no train, 0 held windows, no process reading lib. All 6 live bases match their programs. Order: fiscal (1a-d: schematron_run 8C0F45B9->B9D3079F, xpath_eval BB243652->BFFB32F6, xpath C266A60D->BD24C126, schematron DD29523E->C36C6296), then x (2: physics BB24137C0FE1->B1A4E84872AD; 3: file_system 8661852B->81140E3E), then main closes with C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\window-1029\\close-window4.ps1 (landed hashes vs targets, document_test, type_probe over the 6 files). No box compiles from any lane until 'window 4 closed'. The pack-7 INSTALL stays next session (main: pack7-land, install-pack, broadcast, node re-ship, then git-a6's -Accept), so tonight's proofs stay valid. LIB-TESTS-NOT-RUN's live sm' gate also waits for after the install.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_65 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 65u32, "2026-10-29T23:52Z", "main", "10-29 19:52 main: WINDOW 4 CLOSED, green. Lands, each through its lane's guarded lander and equal to its proven target: fiscal 19:49:30-34 (schematron_run 8C0F45B9->B9D3079F, xpath_eval BB243652->38FCB953->BFFB32F6, xpath C266A60D->BD24C126, schematron DD29523E->C36C6296; byte-exact undo bases in C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\land-1029); x 19:50:13 physics BB24137C0FE1->B1A4E84872AD and 19:50:23 file_system 8661852BC5D5->81140E3E5A74 (undo copies in C:\\home\\data\\undo). Close (C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\window-1029\\close-window4.ps1; log in session-1029\\close-window4.log): document_test 22 passed; type_probe 6/6 PASS (94 tests typed, 0 errors, positive controls ok). The whole queue from n61/n63 has LANDED, so nothing is left in the next-window queue except fiscal's M6 xsd_emit (held, unproven) and tibia's slices (on the user's go). Broadcast to x, fiscal, kit and git-a6; tibia gets the hashes in its resume packet. A close-script display bug is fixed: it had listed every file under 'not landed yet' while each line said 'landed'.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_66 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 66u32, "2026-10-30T00:00Z", "main", "10-29 20:00 main, QUEUE after window 4. (a) Window 5 tonight, CONDITIONAL: fiscal's xpath-double-cast (xpath BD24C126->382A551C, xpath_eval BFFB32F6->34646246; proven on pack 6b, round-tripped as fixpoints). It opens only if fiscal's window-4 node gate (gate4) HOLDS and main's live sm' lib_gate (LIB-TESTS-NOT-RUN) has finished, by about 20:35; otherwise it moves to next session. Close script: C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\window-1029\\close-window5.ps1. (b) Next session's first window, AFTER the pack-7 install (recompile drafts first): kit's LIB-SPLIT-LIST-QUADRATIC (sm'.split_list is O(lines x bytes); lint takes 203 s on agile.spi; kit drafts and lands it per no-gatekeeper; positive control: lint time about 2x from half to full input, not 13x); fiscal's M6 xsd_emit (161D00F5) once its proof holds; tibia's slices on the user's go. ALSO: fiscal reports ZATCA GREEN on the post-window-4 lib (all 19 FATOORA samples pass ZATCA + CEN with 0 fatal findings), after Peppol green. CORRECTION (10-29 20:21, sweep 9): ZATCA green was NOT on the post-window-4 lib. Its mirror all6b (synced 19:05, job queued 19:42) holds fiscal's 4 drafts but the PRE-window-4 physics BB24137C0FE1 / file_system 8661852BC5D5. xpath-double-cast's proofs likewise ran on dbl6b (synced 19:22, pre-window-4). So WINDOW 5 is CANCELLED for tonight: xpath-double-cast moves to next session's first window, after a re-proof on a post-land mirror (e.g. gate4).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_67 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 67u32, "2026-10-30T00:20Z", "x", "2026-10-29 20:20 x: PATH MAP (x/lib-programs drained 19:5x by hash-verified move; the folder no longer exists). Old x/lib-programs/<name> resolves as follows. LANDED/APPLIED, archived in C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\landed-programs\\: process-counter.kit, process-counter.x-net.kit, otp-actor-named.kit, fs-heal-4.kit, fs-heal-4b-other-targets.kit, fs-heal-4c-io-error-text.kit, lib-gate-copy-daemon.kit, physics-scalar-force.kit, x-fields-cells.kit. UNPROVEN DRAFTS, in C:\\home\\data\\x-drafts\\sim-programs\\: sim-in-spiral-s1s2.kit, sim-in-spiral-s3a.kit, sim-in-spiral-s3b.kit. TOOL: land-lib-program.ps1 now lives in repo i574n.github at scripts/land-lib-program.ps1 (untracked, for the user's commit), next to the lib-guarded-do.ps1 it calls; positive control after the move: already-at-target exit 0, no write. The ledger rows whose SOURCE field cites x/lib-programs/*.kit resolve through this map, by file name.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_68 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 68u32, "2026-10-30T00:21Z", "main", "10-29 20:21 main, SWEEP 9 (the last; covered 22:56Z-00:02Z, plus read-only checks to 00:17Z): 8 rows (3 contradictions, 3 hazards, 1 loss, 1 unposted, 0 unanswered). No new deletes; window 4 was clean (no other lane compiled or landed in it); every live hash and draft base is current; every nudge was answered.\nLOST ROW (new): the gh CLI extension github/gh-actions-lock v0.2.0, gone in the wipe (profile extension dir absent). The source is in archive/done-notes.spi (CI-ACTIONS-LOCKFILE n1/n6/n7); main's earlier 'never recorded' was wrong because its grep missed the archive. USER STEP: 'gh extension install github/gh-actions-lock' on the user's yes, then --no-fix in each repo. Corrected on PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n28 and CI-ACTIONS-LATEST n7.\nCORRECTIONS by main: PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n29's '19:34 mirror OK' was wrong (truncated; PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE n10). n66's 'ZATCA on post-window-4 lib' was wrong (see the n66 append); window 5 is cancelled and moves to next session after a re-proof.\nDURABILITY FIXES tonight (now on the ledger): 3 of 8 profile-mirror archives truncated behind a matching sha256, fixed in profile-mirror.ps1 904250655ECB; scratch-archive's write-after-archive gap fixed in 4A73EC186D9A. AUDIT of today's 12 pre-fix scratch-archive runs: the 6 rc.2/kitbin/cache runs archived files quiet for 1 h to weeks; 20261029-133932 (49 of main's folders, newest write 3 min before) removed nothing (48 still present, kitbin archived by a later run); 20261029-133912 removed git-a6's pack6b, pack6c, pack7-land and runner-3f1b7588 14 min after their newest write. That's low risk; git-a6 was asked to confirm (blobs restorable).\nROUTED (each message sent): fiscal (ZATCA/dbl6b pre-window-4 caveat, n17 note-edit, window 5 moved); kit (split_list baseline overlapped other runs, so re-measure half and full under the same conditions; kit-delguard mirror); git-a6 (14 unowned pre-retire mirrors to attribute: ac, axes1029, candlib, candlib-smlinear, ccmr-g3b, ceall, det, g1build, gbase, ge3, gls, hopacsota-p2, integ, kit-delguard; gen0n/gen0h started without --heavy; 2 TEMP-only scripts; confirm the 13:39:12 archive run); x (post old->new lib-programs paths on LIB-PROCESS-COUNTER and here; land-lib-program.ps1 location for the commit list); tibia (correction: its 5 stale mirrors, and 14 others unowned).\nLESSON: backlog fact searches must cover docs/backlog/archive/done-notes.spi as well as state/agile.spi (sealed notes move there).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_69 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 69u32, "2026-10-30T00:23Z", "main", "10-29 20:23 main, FINAL NOTE for 10-29; WIPE-REDO-LEDGER -> Done.\n\nSTATE: move-forward. Readings: parts A-C, sweeps 1-9, groomings 1-2, and every active lane's final pass. Every ledger row is recovered, dropped, or groomed into an owned item. Sweep 9: 8 rows (3 contradictions, 3 hazards, 1 loss, 1 unposted), all routed and acknowledged; two were corrections of main's own records (n28, n29), now fixed.\n\nAFTER THE 18:00 CLOSING NOTE (n60):\n- The pack-7 review PASSED at 19:39 (PACK-7 n9). Window 4 (19:49-19:52) landed the whole post-review queue (fiscal's schematron_run, xpath_eval, xpath and schematron; x's physics and fs-heal-4c), green: document_test 22, type_probe 6/6. Fiscal then reported ZATCA and Peppol GREEN on that lib. Window 5: cancelled; xpath-double-cast's and ZATCA's proofs ran on a pre-window-4 mirror, so fiscal re-runs them on gate4b and xpath-double-cast lands next session after its re-proof.\n- Three safety bugs were found and fixed, each proven by reproducing the bug on the old script first:\n  - type_probe positional binding (a cwd-relative robocopy /MIR);\n  - profile-mirror archives truncated behind a matching sha256 (3 of 8);\n  - scratch-archive removing folders written to after the archive.\n- New wipe losses: the gh actions-lock extension (user step), plus 7 Start Menu shortcuts stranded in spiral/Programs (healed).\n- Lanes archived 35 pre-retire node mirrors by move, with junctions verified (main 7, x 18, kit 6, fiscal 3, compiler 1). 13 more are being attributed by git-a6, and tibia's 5 are in its resume packet.\n- The rule that lanes read --heavy as non-exclusive is closed by a convention (compile-quiet) plus kit's window kinds for TRAIN5.\n- Memories: 59 of 179 are rebuilt or new; 120 still carry the partial banner, rebuilt as their facts come up.\n\nNEXT SESSION (in order): the pack-7 install (main: pack7-land, install-pack, broadcast, node re-ship; then git-a6's -Accept regenerating against the live lib); recompile drafts; first window: kit's split_list fix, fiscal's M6 when proven, and tibia's slices on the user's go; TRAIN5 (delete guard, -Environment fix, heavy.ps1 caller, window kinds); machine upkeep (skipped tonight); the user's commit from commit-suggestion.md.")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_70 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 70u32, "2026-10-30T01:07Z", "main", "10-29 21:07 main: no sweep 10. The hourly cron fired at 21:0x, after the user's 'until 9pm' end. Sweep 9 covered the transcripts to 00:02Z (20:02 local), with all 8 rows routed by 20:21. Everything after that happened first-hand and is recorded on its items: the listm' re-placement land 220ACFE33776 plus the eighth Lua bug (LIB-MACRO-HEAL n94); fiscal's post-window-4 Peppol/ZATCA/UBL-TR HOLD and the xpath-double-cast re-proof; the last mirror archives (fiscal 8, main candlib-smlinear; only tibia's 5 remain); DISK-CLEANUP sized (n43). The item stays Done (n69).")
inl note_of_wipe_redo_ledger_71 () = Note ("WIPE-REDO-LEDGER", 71u32, "2026-10-30T02:08Z", "main", "10-29 22:08 main, groom: removed the dep on PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY. It formed a cycle (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY -> PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE -> WIPE-REDO-LEDGER -> PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY), and it was backwards: this ledger is the plan the recovery follows, and it closed (n69) while the recovery is still at 98%. Found by a whole-backlog cycle scan (3 distinct cycles).")
inl node_mirror_cells_deps () = Task ("NODE-MIRROR-CELLS-DEPS", "Node mirror sync carries apps/cells/deps, and a lib gate with 0 rows reports VOID, not red", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "REMOTE-LAPTOP-LANE", "kit,node,remote,cells,lib-gate", "current", "current")
