inl note_of_lib_port_hide_1 () = Note ("LIB-PORT-HIDE", 1u32, "2026-10-29T19:38Z", "main", "10-29 15:4x main (grooming 1, filed for tibia, which is paused on the user's stop): ledger row n16/n27. The draft survives in two places: on the node in remote-stage\\lib-gate-LIB-PORT-HIDE, and on the box in C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\tibia-lib-stages. Its old stage verdicts are stale (n27; they predate pack 6b). Before landing: diff against the live lib/spiral process.spi (process.spi changed since 10-27), re-gate with remote.ps1 -RequireCore set to the node's installed core at launch time, then land through lib-guarded-do in a lib window. Owner: tibia, when the user says go.")
inl note_of_lib_port_hide_2 () = Note ("LIB-PORT-HIDE", 2u32, "2026-10-30T15:21Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 11:2x ROOT CAUSE of the RED re-gate (a_powershell_program_runs_and_reports_its_exit_code/gleam: exit 7 right, stdout ''). An escript probe on the node (scratch portprobe.escript) opens pwsh through open_port spawn_executable with [binary, exit_status, args]: WITHOUT 'hide' the port receives only {exit_status,0} and no data, for Write-Output, -NonInteractive and [Console]::Out.Write alike. WITH 'hide' it receives <<\"spiral\">>, <<\"\\r\\n\">>, exit 0. python gets its data either way. So the slice's 'hide' is the right fix, but it reached only port_for: process.gleam_captured (behind capture_stdout_list/capture_combined_list) opens its own port. Candidate LIB-PORT-HIDE-2 = the merged slice + 'options = windowless (...)' in gleam_captured (line kept under 120). Its gate is job-1793373641184. erlang_port.erl_halt_port stays unhidden (a test helper that reads only the exit status of erl -noshell).")
inl note_of_lib_port_hide_3 () = Note ("LIB-PORT-HIDE", 3u32, "2026-10-30T15:31Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 11:3x LIB-PORT-HIDE-2 GREEN (job-1793373641184, mirror tibia-ed3 = box lib digest 6A4CA91C7F22EE10, core 9C899B30): process.spi 10/10 tests, 20 rows, 0 red, with a_powershell_program_runs_and_reports_its_exit_code passing on Rust and Gleam. The merged candidate is node C:\\home\\remote-stage\\tibia-regen\\out\\LIB-PORT-HIDE-2\\process.spi with applier apply-LIB-PORT-HIDE-2.ps1 (guarded on the live hash). It lands in the next lib window with the other GREEN slices (do + undo, reader guard, gate as its own job).")
inl note_of_lib_port_hide_4 () = Note ("LIB-PORT-HIDE", 4u32, "2026-10-30T16:50Z", "tibia-lane", "10-30 12:49 LANDED: process.spi 65230F12FD9D (PORT-HIDE-2: hide on port_for and on gleam_captured). Undo: C:\\home\\data\\undo\\LIB-PORT-HIDE-2. The post-land node gate follows after main's close.")
