inl rust_host_move_only () = Task ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", "codegenRust clones a non-Clone host type (ureq::RequestBuilder) when rustMoveOnLastUse bails on a fn holding the compiler's own LIT.with(|lit| ...) literal cache: E0599 in x's xc_net on pack 6b", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "PACK-7", "compiler,rust,codegen,x", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rust_host_move_only () = Planning ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rust_host_move_only_1 () = Note ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", 1u32, "2026-10-29T19:56Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:1x compiler: found by x (verify31, xc_net fails E0599 on the installed pack-6b 9895730DAE80); root-caused and fixed in a draft. Evidence: x's failing output C:\\home\\data\\x-evidence\\verify31-net-clone\\net.6b-failing.rs (4D255C39), source net.spi (4D3AB954): in exchange_0 the if-branches end 'v8.clone()' / 'v9.clone()' on ureq::RequestBuilder<WithBody>, which is not Clone.\nTWO DEFECTS, each sufficient alone: (1) codegenRust's nonCloneRustType (spiral_compiler.fs:164250) knows reqwest's RequestBuilder but not ureq's, so var (:164354) emits vN.clone() for it. (2) rustMoveOnLastUse (:164125), the post-pass that strips a clone at a variable's last use, bails out of a whole fn when any line looks like a closure (:164140-164142), and that includes the compiler's own capture-free string-literal cache 'LIT.with(|lit| lit.clone())'. Here the literal 'xc_requests', which lib common.spi's new process_counter_add brought into exchange, disabled the post-pass for exchange_0, so the clones that verify29 had stripped survived. x's net.spi was unchanged.\nFIX (1) drafted: apps/compiler/packs/apply-rust-ureq-move-only.ps1 (unstaged; 1 exact anchor; matches once on the live 6b core and on the pack-7 core). It adds ureq::RequestBuilder (both typestates), ureq::http::Response, ureq::Body and ureq::Error to the move-only types. Regression sample (-Samples): rust_host_move_only_branch, a ureq-typed if-branch plus a string literal in the same fn, through BackendSwitch (other arms return 0). PROOF, through the bug's own path: installed 6b -> rustc E0599 'no method named clone found for struct RequestBuilder'; candidate job-1793303462826 (6b + this applier; core EA1571826ABFCF3B) -> 0 clones on those locals, rustc ok, exit 0. C row exit 0 on both. Land: matrix-add-to-list Rust rust_host_move_only_branch. Rides pack 8.\nFIX (2), recommended but NOT drafted: exclude the compiler's own LIT/CASE/CLOSURE.with(|x| x.clone()) idioms from the bail-out regex. It is correct (they capture nothing) and would restore the move optimization in every Rust fn that has a string literal, but it changes many Rust residuals, so it needs its own measured pack (residual census first).\nx's workaround until pack 8: its branches return the (i32, string) reply instead of the builder.")
inl note_of_rust_host_move_only_2 () = Note ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", 2u32, "2026-10-29T19:57Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:0x compiler: END-TO-END CONFIRMED by x on its real failing source (scratch client package, net.spi 4D3AB954C2B38B3B). Installed 6b: 2 ureq-typed branch clones in exchange_0 (:40, :43, the E0599 lines). Candidate (core EA1571826ABFCF3B, 6b + apply-rust-ureq-move-only): 0. x's function-scoped scan, positive-controlled on 6b's output; SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL was set only for that one build. x keeps its restructure (cleaner anyway); the matrix sample rust_host_move_only_branch is the regression guard, so x's code need not stay shaped around the bug. Remaining: ship in pack 8 (fix 1), and the separate measured pack for the LIT.with post-pass bail (fix 2).")
inl note_of_rust_host_move_only_3 () = Note ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", 3u32, "2026-10-29T20:12Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:2x compiler: FIX 2 SIZED without a build. The post-pass rustMoveOnLastUse was ported faithfully to PowerShell (scratchpad postpass-census.ps1: same fn spans, word regex, self-rebind skip, closure/loop bail, last-use cut). CONTROL: on the 477 committed samples/**/main.rs (outputs the real pass already processed) the port changes 0 files, the expected fixed point. With the ONE change (strip the compiler's own capture-free idioms LIT/CASE/CLOSURE.with(|x| x.clone()) before the bail test), it would change 206 of 477 Rust outputs and remove 1,642 clones. The largest effects are on the hottest code: mega_brzozowski_derivatives runtime_bench -206, inventory_closed_dfa_runtime -167, runtime_native -142, indexed_dfa_state_cardinality -116, then the heap_union array families -19 to -23. Each removed clone is an Rc refcount round trip or a deep copy in generated Rust, so this is a performance item in its own right. Its pack-8 review gets a ready predicted set (these 206 files, Rust only) plus the safety net that every Rust row must still compile and agree with C. Correctness basis: the idioms capture nothing (thread_local literal/case/closure caches), so a last use moved past them cannot be observed by them. Recommend: draft as a pack-8 applier in its own commit, then bench-pair runtime_bench Rust (with an A/A) for the speed claim.")
inl note_of_rust_host_move_only_4 () = Note ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", 4u32, "2026-10-29T20:28Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:3x compiler: FIX 2 IS NOT A FREE WIN, so it is ON HOLD for pack 8. Bench (box, BelowNormal, under kit's TRAIN4c load; scratchpad postpass-bench.ps1): mega_brzozowski_derivatives runtime_bench Rust, A = committed main.rs (856 clones), Aaa = an A/A copy, B = the same file through the fixed post-pass port (650 clones); rustc nightly-2026-10-18 -O2; 7 rotated rounds. Medians: A 2,925 ms, Aaa 2,792 ms (per-round A/A ratio 1.379), B 7,211 ms (ratio 1.408). Exits 0 and stdout equal in every arm. The A/A spread makes this run INCONCLUSIVE as a measurement, but B's median is 2.5x A's, so 'fewer clones = faster' is unsupported and possibly wrong. Plausible mechanism: moving an Rc on its last use hands the final reference to the callee, which then runs the DEEP DROP of a large structure in its hot path, where the caller's clone used to defer it. Next: a quiet re-measure (node, after the gen0 runs) with per-round raw rows and an A/A, plus a perf look at where B spends time, before fix 2 goes anywhere. Fix 1 (ureq move-only) is unaffected: it only changes host non-Clone types.")
inl note_of_rust_host_move_only_5 () = Note ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", 5u32, "2026-10-30T02:28Z", "compiler", "10-29 22:2x compiler: FIX 2 (post-pass literal-cache bail) OFF HOLD, from job-1793326681838-compiler-postpass-bench-3 (node, exit 0). Workload lengthened so one process reads ~15.5 s of cpu: spiral_main looped 60 times inside one process, the same edit to A and B (anchor asserted once), mega_brzozowski_derivatives runtime_bench, A 856 clones vs B 650, rustc nightly-2026-10-18 -O2, 9 rotated rounds, cpu from TotalProcessorTime, all 27 runs exit 0. Per-round cpu ratio vs A, median (min-max): A/A 1.027 (0.981-1.067), B 0.977 (0.933-1.029). READING: B is NOT slower. The box's 2.5x (n4: A 2,925 ms vs B 7,211 ms) was load noise: its own A/A read 1.379, it measured wall with PowerShell capturing stdout, and it ran under TRAIN4c. B sits ~2-5% below A and just under the A/A band's floor: a marginal cpu gain, not a speed claim, plus 206 fewer clones and an 8 KB smaller exe. DECISION: fix 2 goes into PACK-8 with the claim 'cpu-neutral to -2% on mega_brzozowski runtime_bench (node), 24% fewer clone calls'. Script: C:\\home\\remote-stage\\postpass-bench\\node-bench-3.ps1 (durable copy in the compiler scratchpad night\\). Correction: the durable copy is C:\\home\\data\\pack8-drafts\\node-bench-3.ps1, not the scratchpad.")
inl note_of_rust_host_move_only_6 () = Note ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", 6u32, "2026-10-30T04:18Z", "compiler", "10-30 00:2x compiler: REGRESSION SAMPLE PROVEN BOTH WAYS (node, pack8 mirror's samples tree): samples/rust_host_move_only_branch (written by apply-rust-ureq-move-only.ps1 -Samples) on the installed pack 7 gives rustc error[E0599] 'no method named clone found for struct RequestBuilder<T>' (the bug), and on the pack8 candidate (core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52) rustc ok, exit 0. It lands through C:\\home\\data\\pack8-review\\pack8-land.ps1 before the PACK-8 install. NO matrix row: Rust is a default backend and the sample's BackendSwitch covers Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (the applier's old 'matrix-add-to-list Rust' hint was wrong: there is no Rust list; message fixed).")
inl note_of_rust_host_move_only_7 () = Note ("RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY", 7u32, "2026-10-30T16:56Z", "compiler", "10-30 12:56 compiler: INSTALLED AND ACCEPTED in pack 8 (main installed 11:46, core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52 host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9, equal=True, node shipped; the live tree core 4191A77FB3D3A335 carries it; accept run single-flight-20261030-120324, PACK-8 n13). DONE: samples/rust_host_move_only_branch is in the oracle on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi, all compile ok and native exit 0 (Rust oracle agree). main's live probe: build-fail on the pack-7 control, exit 0 on pack 8.")
