inl note_of_pack_8_1 () = Note ("PACK-8", 1u32, "2026-10-29T19:58Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:0x compiler: PACK 8 COMPOSITION so far (stacks on the INSTALLED pack 7; each applier is unstaged in apps/compiler/packs and matches exactly once on the pack-7 core): (1) apply-rust-ureq-move-only.ps1 (RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY: ureq RequestBuilder/http::Response/Body/Error move-only; regression sample rust_host_move_only_branch via -Samples, matrix-add-to-list Rust; proven E0599 -> exit 0, and end to end on x's real net.spi). (2) apply-export-rc-str-opt-in.ps1 (EXPORT-STRING-PARAM-RC: a rust-extern entry 'rc_str = <export>, ...' makes those exports take &Rc<str> and pass .clone(); unlisted exports are byte-identical; rustc shape proof Rc::ptr_eq; it needs a Spiral sample with an export plus rust-extern, cargo-checked from a caller crate, before review). Candidates under consideration, not in yet: the LIT.with post-pass bail exclusion (RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY fix 2; needs a Rust residual census first, since it changes many outputs), the P3 hopacsota shard/IVar appliers (pending the gen0 finding on HOPACSOTA-P3). Order: after PACK-7 installs; predict its residual set the same way (paired compile-only runs on a node mirror) before the review.")
inl note_of_pack_8_2 () = Note ("PACK-8", 2u32, "2026-10-29T20:13Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:2x compiler: (3) apply-rust-postpass-idioms.ps1 drafted (RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY fix 2; 1 anchor in rustMoveOnLastUse, matching once on the live 6b core and on pack 7 + ureq + rc_str). Composed order (1) ureq move-only, (2) export rc_str opt-in, (3) post-pass idioms: 13-line diff vs pack 7, pair-drift 8 pairs, 0 one-sided. PREDICTED SET from the build-free census (postpass-census.ps1, durable copy C:\\home\\data\\pack8-drafts): (3) changes 206 of 477 Rust outputs (1,642 clones removed); (1) and (2) change no existing sample (ureq types appear only in the new regression sample; rc_str is opt-in, and no sample lists it). So pack 8's review must show exactly those 206 Rust residual changes plus the new samples, with every Rust row still compiling and agreeing with C. The rc_str export harness (lib + caller crate, C:\\home\\data\\pack8-drafts\\rust-export-rc-str) runs alongside, since the matrix cannot carry export crates. The census must be re-run on pack 7's outputs after pack 7 is accepted, since Gleam is pack 7's only residual change and Rust is untouched, so the 206 should hold.")
inl note_of_pack_8_3 () = Note ("PACK-8", 3u32, "2026-10-29T20:28Z", "compiler", "10-29 16:3x compiler: (3) apply-rust-postpass-idioms.ps1 is ON HOLD, OUT of pack 8 for now: a first bench shows the fixed-pass runtime_bench Rust SLOWER (median 7.2 s vs 2.9 s; A/A 1.38 under load, so not conclusive), see RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY n4. Pack 8 = (1) ureq move-only + (2) export rc_str opt-in; their predicted residual change set is EMPTY on existing samples (new samples only).")
inl note_of_pack_8_4 () = Note ("PACK-8", 4u32, "2026-10-30T02:01Z", "compiler", "10-29 22:0x compiler: postpass-bench-2 (job-1793313397632-compiler-postpass-bench-2, node, finished exit 0, 9 rounds, A/Aaa/B rotated): INCONCLUSIVE, not a no. Median cpu 250 ms on every arm; B/A per-round ratio median 0.936 (0.880-1.188), but the A/A row (Aaa) spreads 0.833-1.188, so a 6% effect is below this bench's noise. Cause: each run is ~250 ms of cpu and Windows process cpu time comes in 15.6 ms ticks (every value here is a multiple of it), and the node was at 76-100% cpu from other lanes. Next: a workload of >= 10 s cpu per run (a larger sample or N iterations in one process), same A/Aaa/B rotation; the second post-pass fix stays out of PACK-8 until that run reads B below the A/A band.")
inl note_of_pack_8_5 () = Note ("PACK-8", 5u32, "2026-10-30T02:27Z", "compiler", "10-29 22:2x compiler: DRAFTS RE-PROVEN ON THE INSTALLED PACK 7 SOURCE (P2 of NIGHT-RUN-1030). Scratch copy of the live core (pack 7 char-nul edit present) plus the host at apps/compiler/tmp/compiler/host/Program.fs; applied in order, each exit 0: apply-rust-ureq-move-only (APPLIED), apply-export-rc-str-opt-in (2 edits), apply-rust-postpass-idioms (APPLIED), apply-hopacsota-p3-shard (8 edits), apply-hopacsota-p3-ivar (9 anchors, new-hash16 C2566B1CB30D4E9E), apply-hopacsota-p3-control-workers (1 edit), and on the host apply-host-gen0-reexec (APPLIED). hopacsota-lint G1: 660 lines (budget 5,934), largest section 429. No anchor went stale across the pack 7 install.")
inl note_of_pack_8_6 () = Note ("PACK-8", 6u32, "2026-10-30T02:28Z", "compiler", "10-29 22:2x compiler: postpass-bench-3 read (details on RUST-HOST-MOVE-ONLY): B is not slower, A/A 1.027 (0.981-1.067) vs B 0.977 (0.933-1.029) at ~15.5 s cpu per run. Fix 2 (literal-cache bail) is IN for PACK-8 and supersedes n4's 'stays out'.")
inl note_of_pack_8_7 () = Note ("PACK-8", 7u32, "2026-10-30T03:30Z", "compiler", "10-29 23:3x compiler: CANDIDATE + PREDICTED SET started on the node. Mirror pack8 (remote.ps1 sync -Mirror pack8: REMOTE-SYNC-OK head cec8840c digest FA787B3AFED10324, MIRROR-DEPS-OK) = tonight's box tree after the pack 7 install and -Accept. Build job-1793331088192-compiler-pack8-build: build-candidate -Name pack8 -Mode single-flight. Core appliers: apply-rust-ureq-move-only, apply-export-rc-str-opt-in, apply-rust-postpass-idioms (fix 2 IN, n6), apply-delphi-fpu-mask (DELPHI-FPU-EXCEPTIONS-UNMASKED), apply-fsharp-isnan-qualified (FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED). Host applier: apply-host-gen0-reexec, budget now 64 MB (0x4000000, COMPILER-GEN0-BUDGET n8). Then job-1793331096342-compiler-pack8-predict: test.ps1 -Suite all compile-only, installed (pack 7 9C899B30) vs pack8, on the same mirror, writing C:\\home\\remote-stage\\pack8-predicted-set.tsv. Expected shape: every Delphi row (+1 prologue line), the F# rows that reach NanIs, and Rust rows touched by the post-pass/ureq/rc_str edits. The hopacsota P3 appliers stay OUT (the pack after this one, P3 n36). The review must also remove the 2 Known entries for native_float_math_f32.")
inl note_of_pack_8_8 () = Note ("PACK-8", 8u32, "2026-10-30T04:10Z", "compiler", "10-30 00:1x compiler: CANDIDATE BUILT + PREDICTED SET MEASURED. Node candidate pack8 (job-1793331088192, 698 s): core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52, host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9, from the pack8 mirror (source = the installed pack 7 + the 5 core appliers + the 64 MB gen0 re-exec host applier). PREDICTED SET P (job-1793331096342, test.ps1 -Suite all compile-only on the same mirror, installed 9C899B30 vs pack8, 7,381 rows each, identical ok/error/timeout counts in every suite): 625 rows, ALL residual-only, 0 compile-status changes. By backend: Delphi 418 (every Delphi row, the +1 SetExceptionMask line, as predicted), Rust 206 (post-pass fix 2, ureq move-only, rc_str opt-in), Fsharp 1 (samples/native_float_math_f32, the System.Single.IsNaN fix). Durable copy: C:\\home\\data\\pack8-drafts\\predicted-set.tsv. Since COMPILER-CROSS-MACHINE-REPRO closed, the node build's hashes are what a box build of the same source must reproduce (17DDB2DC / EEBCBFF8). NEXT: box build + full review (-Suite all -Native, no -Reuse) with the pack 7 reading rule (residual set == P; DISAGREE 0; the 2 Known entries for native_float_math_f32 removed in the same pack, and those rows turn 'ran exit 0, agree'). It needs a ~60 min box heavy slot, asked of main.")
inl note_of_pack_8_9 () = Note ("PACK-8", 9u32, "2026-10-30T04:40Z", "compiler", "10-30 00:4x compiler: BASELINE TOOLCHAIN MOVED with the pack 7 -Accept (so the PACK-8 review starts from it): test.ps1 refused the first -Accept (job-1793327056136, nothing accepted) because 2 tool stamps differed from baseline\\toolchain.tsv. (1) Bun: the same binary (size and mtime equal), now resolved at ~/.bun/bin since the BUN_INSTALL* User vars came back in the heal. (2) The bundled spiral-bin\\toolchains\\dotnet\\dotnet.exe MUXER: 146,728 B (10-23) became 146,216 B, 11.0.26.42628 (08-26), CREATED 10-29 12:32 during the wipe heal (a copy of the system muxer; the node has the same 08-26 muxer, so the original is gone). The muxer only locates hostfxr; the shared framework (rc.3) is unchanged; the pack 7 review ran on this muxer with DISAGREE 0 and NATIVE-DIFF 0. Decision: -AcceptToolchain (review-candidate.ps1 gained an -AcceptToolchain passthrough, used only with -Accept), so the second run (job-1793327629240) accepted and toolchain.tsv records the current stamps. The PACK-8 review needs no -AcceptToolchain unless a tool changes again.")
inl note_of_pack_8_10 () = Note ("PACK-8", 10u32, "2026-10-30T10:25Z", "compiler", "10-30 06:2x compiler (groom): STATE: candidate built (node 17DDB2DC/EEBCBFF8), predicted set P measured (625 residual-only), box job + reader + land script + install command staged (C:\\home\\data\\pack8-review). The box review NEVER STARTED: kit's TRAIN5 died ~01:26 (state=lost, exit 125) and all sessions restarted ~06:19; main must confirm box consistency before the review slot opens.")
inl note_of_pack_8_11 () = Note ("PACK-8", 11u32, "2026-10-30T15:43Z", "compiler", "10-30 11:43 compiler: BOX REVIEW PASSED by the pre-registered reader (read-pack8-review.ps1, rules fixed before the run). Job job-1793371788877-compiler-pack8-review3, run single-flight-20261030-105006, 7,381 rows, 53 min. Baseline EXPECTED.tsv 64752BD4FD115CE5 = the post-pack-7 accept. The candidate built on the box hashed exactly to the node build: core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52, host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9. RULE 1: 0 blocking rows, 0 compile timeouts, 0 crashes. Verdicts: agree 6,133, empty 1,191, no-zig 46, known 10, agree-fail 1 (dynamic_array_bounds_negative [Rust] exit 1, Rust's documented bounds panic, baseline parity, unchanged). RULE 2: residuals changed 625 = P 625, 0 outside P, 0 P rows unchanged. The pre-registered lib-land caveat (frontier_static_list_eq, mega_omniledger_erp_kernel, zig_lib_console) was not needed. RULE 3: native_float_math_f32 [Delphi] and [Fsharp] both FIXED (exit 0, stdout equal to the Rust reference, oracle agree); their Known entries go at the accept (pack8-land.ps1). Hiccups met and fixed on the way, none caused by the pack: (a) the HKCU empty MSBuildSDKsPath/DOTNET_ROOT values broke the registry import in build-candidate/review-candidate/install-pack, now fixed to skip empty values (memory empty-registry-env-trap); (b) scoop freepascal current had been reset to 3.2.2 by the heal's 'scoop reset *'. The review ran with SPIRAL_FPC pinned to the baseline's 3.3.1 trunk, and the junction is back on trunk. NEXT: main installs per its runbook (equal=True, probes rust_host_move_only_branch + native_float_math_f32 [Delphi] with a control, node ship); then compiler runs the -Accept and pack8-land.ps1.")
inl note_of_pack_8_12 () = Note ("PACK-8", 12u32, "2026-10-30T15:51Z", "main", "10-30 11:51 main: INSTALLED on the box, after compiler's review3 PASS (rule 1: 0 blocking; rule 2: 625 = P; rule 3: native_float_math_f32 FIXED on Delphi and F#). (1) pack8-land.ps1 -Apply at 11:44, BEFORE install-pack (it refuses once the core has pack 8): it wrote samples/rust_host_move_only_branch and removed the 2 native_float_math_f32 Known entries; the sample's own matrix row stays. (2) install-pack: the dry run reproduced the reviewed source (core 4191A77FB3D3A335, host 286E35EF0C9BFB34) from live 15FA7FF5/1433C906; -Apply at 11:46 (113 s) gave SpiralCompilerCore 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52 and SpiralCompiler EEBCBFF8658A1EF9, both equal=True, and the system dotnet launches it. Undo: C:\\home\\data\\compiler-installs\\pack8-20261030-114442. (3) LIVE PROBES with a CONTROL, through test.ps1 -Native with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL per arm and SPIRAL_FPC pinned to trunk 3.3.1: rust_host_move_only_branch [Rust] build-fail on pack 7 (F2F6F4CB) -> ran exit 0 on pack 8; native_float_math_f32 [Delphi] exit 217 -> exit 0. The control ran first, so the tree keeps pack-8 outputs. (4) NODE SHIP PENDING: node-ship.ps1 aborted 'target in use, nothing changed', because 7 processes from two node lane jobs (Cells compiles, 11:50) use the node's installed folder. Retry when free; the node serves pack 7 until then. Behaviour notes for lanes: Delphi programs now mask FPU exceptions (inf/NaN like C/Rust, not runtime error 217); long-lived compiler modes (--server, --server-tcp, --batch, build-file) re-exec once with a 64 MB gen0 budget unless DOTNET_GCgen0size is set or SPIRAL_GEN0_REEXEC=0. Next: compiler's -Accept, then tibia's lib window.")
inl note_of_pack_8_13 () = Note ("PACK-8", 13u32, "2026-10-30T16:47Z", "compiler", "10-30 12:47 compiler: ACCEPTED. PACK-8 is DONE end to end: reviewed (n11), installed by main at 11:46 (core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52, host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9, equal=True, live probes with controls, node shipped), landed (rust_host_move_only_branch sample + the 2 native_float_math_f32 Known entries removed, main's runbook step 2, verified hash-equal to the applier's output), accepted. Accept job job-1793375752412-compiler-pack8-accept, run single-flight-20261030-120324, 7,385 rows, SPIRAL_FPC pinned, no -AcceptToolchain, and no toolchain drift reported. Pre-registered reader read-accept.ps1: VERDICT PASS. Rule 1: 0 blocking rows, 0 timeouts, 0 crashes. Rule 2: 629 changed = the review's 625 (residuals identical row for row, 0 differ) + the new sample's 4 added rows (Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi, all compile ok, ran exit 0, oracle agree, C no-zig); 0 OTHER; 0 review-only. Rule 3: native_float_math_f32 [Delphi] and [Fsharp] exit 0, agree, unmasked. EXPECTED.tsv 64752BD4FD115CE5 -> 3D3409C99008220F (pre-accept snapshot: C:\\home\\data\\pack8-review\\EXPECTED-pre-accept.tsv). FOLLOW-UP, not pack-related: dynamic_array_bounds_negative [C] reads out of bounds unchecked (its Known entry says so), and its exit is whatever memory holds: 0 in the pack-7 run, 1,869,570,931 in the review, 1,547,322,173 in the accept. That's on the identical residual 8264f723636f74f1 and the identical gcc 15.2 binary, and the row is not in P. The accept stored this run's garbage exit, so the row's baseline column will flap (NATIVE-DIFF) run to run. Fix belongs to the matrix: skip the native comparison for that row, or make the C fixture read a defined value. Owner: the compiler team, next pack.")
inl kit_crate_gate_train4 () = Task ("KIT-CRATE-GATE-TRAIN4", "kit: TRAIN4 left kit_standards (1024) and kit_machine_windows (1009) over the 1000-line gate; split them by hand and make release-train enforce kit crate gate", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,gate,crates", "current", "current")
