inl note_of_night_run_1030_2 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 2u32, "2026-10-30T02:23Z", "main", "10-29 22:23 main: P1 DONE. Pack 7 is installed on the box and node with exact hashes and live-probed with a control (PACK-7 n12). The compiler-install window is released. ROUTED (each message sent): 'PACK 7 INSTALLED' to git-a6 (-Accept now), fiscal (re-prove xpath-double-cast + M6), kit (re-prove split_list), x (verify33 may use pack 7 on the node) and tibia (read-only Lua diffs, plus the overdue heal+groom answer). Lane plans received from kit, fiscal, x and git-a6, all consistent with the sequence. P2 is in progress.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_3 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 3u32, "2026-10-30T02:27Z", "x", "2026-10-29 22:3x x: P1 done with zero box compiles: split the oversized S3 cells. Since pack 7, two short box x-compat checks (22:23:19-29, 22:24:06-11, before git-a6's accept at 22:24:16): all 4 sim layers (s1s2/s3a/s3b/s1b) read '0 finding(s) in 29 file(s)'. Node: x-s3-p7 launching on pack 7 (core 9C899B30495F7DC5), with x-compat gated in the job per layer and stop-on-red builds. verify32 (xv30, 6b) still running; verify33 (pinned 9C899B30495F7DC5, gate regex fixed) launches into xv30 when it ends. Then S1b (after x-s3-p7), X-HAND-UNITS drafting, X-PRECOMMIT-SPEED bench. No lib program for window 5. Box: compile-quiet until ACCEPT DONE.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_4 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 4u32, "2026-10-30T02:33Z", "main", "10-29 22:33 main: node disk cleanup done early (+7.7 GB, 32.76 GB free; DISK-CLEANUP n45). The pack-7 -Accept is running (git-a6, job-1793327056136, box compile-quiet until ACCEPT DONE). Box-compile correction broadcast at 22:2x after my early 'allowed again'; x reported its 2 x-compat checks, both before the accept started. LIB-MACRO-HEAL at 90% (last 2 candidates are not heals). 8 more memories rebuilt (108 partial left).")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_5 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 5u32, "2026-10-30T03:20Z", "main", "10-29 23:20 main: P2 core done. ACCEPT DONE (23:13): residual set equals the expected one; PACK-7 at 98%, pending Known entries for native_float_math_f32 [Delphi]/[Fsharp], 2 pre-existing bugs filed as PACK-8 riders. 'ACCEPT DONE, box free' and the '\\0' lib heads-up ROUTED to fiscal, kit, x and tibia (each sent). Node: the WSLg crash loop is the disk-growth root cause, contained hourly (DISK-CLEANUP n46; the fix is the user's). Next: window 5 when fiscal and kit report ready; close script C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\window-1029\\close-window5.ps1 to be extended with M6 + sm' targets from their ready messages.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_6 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 6u32, "2026-10-30T03:30Z", "compiler", "23:3x git-a6 (compiler): P2 DONE (pack 7 -Accept 23:13, residual set = expected with a positive control; 2 known-wrong rows marked Known with their fix items; PACK-7 closed by main). Node jobs, no box use: compiler-p3hc-build -> compiler-p3hc-ab (HOPACSOTA-P3: striped join-point hash-consing, decision change in PLAN.md first) and compiler-pack8-build -> compiler-pack8-predict (PACK-8 predicted set). Box: only the gen0_64 A/A slot after window 6 and TRAIN5, as main schedules; holding lib-reading box compiles during window 5.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_7 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 7u32, "2026-10-30T03:50Z", "main", "10-29 23:50 main, HOURLY CHECK. Box: no train, no held window, only git-a6's node-watch. Node: C: 34.8 GB free (37.7 after the 22:5x containment; WSL dumps back to 10 since then), CPU 100%; live jobs compiler-derive-gate, x-s3-p7b, compiler-pack8-predict, fiscal-p7-set-ublj, compiler-p3hc-ab, x-verify33 (all under 1.1 h, none stuck). Lanes: fiscal, git-a6 and kit busy; x in a shell; tibia idle (paused by design; its 21:54 heal/groom answer is still owed). DELTAS this hour: PACK-7 CLOSED Done (n14). WINDOW 5 (merged): fiscal's xpath-double-cast + M6 landed at 23:47 (xpath 382A551C, xpath_eval 34646246, xsd_emit 161D00F5) and closed green (document_test 22, type_probe 3/3). Kit's split_list was held out: its pack-7 gate shows 5 sm' tests failing on cuda only, and whether base sm' fails them too on pack 7 is unknown (main's 72/72 was on 6b), so it's a possible pack-7 lib regression, routed to kit (base gate) and git-a6 (heads-up). CELLS WINDOW OPEN (23:5x) for fiscal's spiral.toml manifest change (8 files), with the before-control proven (the old Cells rejects with 'Spiral package was not found'). ROUTED (each sent): window 5 closed + Cells window to fiscal, kit, x, git-a6 and tibia.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_8 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 8u32, "2026-10-30T04:11Z", "main", "10-30 00:11 main: BOX TIMELINE for the rest of the night (estimates from measured phases): kit's sm' A/B to ~00:55; split_list lib window ~01:00-01:10; kit's TRAIN5 ~01:10-03:20 (kit: about 2h05, range 1h50-2h20, all on pack 7); git-a6's PACK-8 review ~03:20-04:35 (predicted set measured: 625 residual-only rows, Delphi 418 / Rust 206 / F# 1, 0 compile-status changes; the 2 Known entries must flip to agree); main's PACK-8 install ~04:35-04:55 (same procedure as pack 7); git-a6's PACK-8 -Accept ~04:55-05:45; machine upkeep last. ALSO since the last note: CELLS WINDOW closed green (fiscal's spiral.toml change, proven by before/after); the shared lib-guarded-do's dry-run that wrote files is fixed (5F913C088DED); the box CUDA failures are traced to a Kepler GPU vs cupy-cuda12x (a toolchain choice for the user); node containment ran at 00:10 (35.17 GB free).")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_9 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 9u32, "2026-10-30T04:21Z", "main", "10-30 00:21 main, HOURLY CHECK. Box: kit's sm' A/B (job-1793333150121, compile window, 15 min in, ETA about 00:55) plus git-a6's node-watch; nothing else. Node: C: 34.1 GB free, CPU 100%; 7 live jobs, the oldest x-verify33 at 1.7 h, none stuck. Lanes: fiscal and git-a6 busy, kit and x in shells, tibia idle for over 2 h. DELTAS this hour: CELLS WINDOW closed green; lib-guarded-do's dry-run that wrote files is fixed; the box CUDA failures are traced to a Kepler GPU vs cupy-cuda12x (a user choice); PACK-8 install runbook written and materials verified (C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\night-1030\\pack8-install-runbook.md); box timeline fixed and published (TRAIN5 ~01:10, PACK-8 review ~03:20, install ~04:35); node containment 00:10 (+1.2 GB). ROUTED (sent): tibia nudged (heal answer + archive its 5 mirrors). Memories: 73/180 still partial.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_10 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 10u32, "2026-10-30T04:53Z", "main", "10-30 00:53 main: WINDOW 6 closed green (split_list landed, sm' F8378BD6937F; document_test 22; type_probe 71/0). TRAIN5 STARTED 00:52:09 (kit, job-1793335928930, heavy, on pack 7; kit_delete_guard + agile_planning_gaps crates, 9 src edits incl. the heavy.ps1 dual path and the dotnet fallback); expected publish ~03:00, with the lib/Cells freeze until then. CUDA ROOT CAUSE settled: spiral.process_cuda runs the first python on PATH and ignores SPIRAL_PYTHON. Measured: main's shell resolves python312 first (numpy present), which is why its 19:53 72/72 passed, while kit's resolves scoop 3.15.2 (no numpy), hence 67/72 on the same lib. Routed to git-a6 as a runner fix with that test case. The Kepler/cupy-cuda12x issue is secondary (real cupy calls only).")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_11 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 11u32, "2026-10-30T05:23Z", "main", "10-30 01:23 main, HOURLY CHECK. Box: TRAIN5 running (heavy window, 30 min in; stdout written at 01:19, so progressing), node-watch; nothing else. Node: C: 34.2 GB free, CPU 100%; 7 live jobs, the longest x-verify33 (2.7 h) and fiscal-p7-set-ublj (2.5 h), plausible under load; plus git-a6's compiler-cuda-runner proof (0.3 h). Lanes: git-a6 busy, fiscal/kit/x in shells, tibia holding under a direct user STOP (not nudged, by design). DELTAS: window 6 closed green (split_list); TRAIN5 started 00:52; the CUDA cause settled (the runner ignores SPIRAL_PYTHON; PATH-order dependent); SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON filed by git-a6, source edit after TRAIN5, runner swap ~05:35; upkeep script ready; CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD filed. No routing needed this hour.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_12 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 12u32, "2026-10-30T10:25Z", "main", "10-30 06:25 main: THE BOX CRASHED at 01:26 (System log: event 6008 'previous system shutdown at 1:26:00 AM was unexpected', Kernel-Power 41) and REBOOTED at 06:09, so about 4h45 lost; every lane session restarted about 06:19 (the compiler lane now appears as git-51/compiler). TRAIN5 (job-1793335928930) is state=lost exit=125: it died in its read-only notebook phase (last stdout 01:19:26, 'phase notebooks: start'), AFTER applying its 9 source edits to kit's repo at 00:51 and building candidate kit.exe 01FDAB64, but BEFORE publish. The installed kit.exe is unchanged (C528BE4D). So PACK-8's review, the runner fix, its swap and upkeep never ran. POST-CRASH INTEGRITY (main, 06:26): all 7 lib files landed tonight still at their targets (xpath 382A551C, xpath_eval 34646246, xsd_emit 161D00F5, sm' F8378BD6937F, listm' 220ACFE33776, file_system 81140E3E, physics B1A4E848); the installed compiler is still exactly pack 7 (core 9C899B30495F7DC5, host F2F6F4CB5A18626E); the backlog loads (913 items). The node stayed up; C: fell 35.6 -> 30.9 GB with containment lapsed (main's session crons died with the session; restored now). The crash cause is unknown (no bugcheck read yet); a heavy notebook phase on 4-5 GB free RAM is plausible but unproven. CORRECTION (06:26): main's crons did NOT die. CronList shows all of them still scheduled after the resume; they just couldn't fire while the box was down 01:26-06:09. The 06:40 final report is still scheduled. CORRECTION (06:30): the compiler lane is the session named 'compiler'. 'git-51' is NOT a lane: the user started it after the reboot to fix the Windows 'Start menu isn't working' popup (fixed; Start's package status is Ok; cause and recipe recorded in memory profile-wipe-2026-10-28.md). It touched no backlog items.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_13 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 13u32, "2026-10-30T10:28Z", "main", "10-30 06:28 main, CRASH CAUSE (read-only evidence): NOT a software crash. Kernel-Power 41 with BugcheckCode=0, no minidump or MEMORY.DMP, no resource-exhaustion warnings, and 0 System events in the 6 min before 01:26 (the PowerButtonTimestamp 06:09:20 is the user's power-on, not the crash). The box is a LAPTOP (chassis 9) on AC, with a battery reporting EstimatedChargeRemaining=247%, which is impossible and points to a failed battery or gauge. A sudden power loss like this fits (a) an AC interruption with no working battery to bridge it, or (b) a firmware thermal hard-off after hours at 100% load (these leave no log). Not distinguishable from the logs. The user's call: check AC/charger and battery health (powercfg /batteryreport) and laptop cooling. Until then, avoid unattended multi-hour heavy box jobs. KIT reports its tree is CONSISTENT at the TRAIN5-applied state (8 edited files at their post-apply sha256, both crates whole, Cargo.lock lists both), so TRAIN5 can rerun from there; FISCAL lost no box job and its tree is intact.")
inl note_of_night_run_1030_14 () = Note ("NIGHT-RUN-1030", 14u32, "2026-10-30T10:38Z", "main", "10-30 06:38 main, CLOSING NOTE for the overnight run (10-29 22:1x to 10-30 07:00). DONE: pack 7 installed, live-probed, re-shipped and accepted (PACK-7 Done); 3 lib windows plus 1 Cells window landed and closed green (fiscal xpath-double-cast + M6, kit split_list, fiscal's Cells spiral.toml support); shared lib-guarded-do dry-run write fixed; node disk leak found (WSLg crash loop) and contained; CUDA failures traced to a runner ignoring SPIRAL_PYTHON; about 70 memories rebuilt. LOST to the 01:26 power loss: TRAIN5 (tree consistent; reruns), the PACK-8 review/install/accept, the runner fix and swap, and upkeep, all staged and held for the user. Post-crash integrity verified. The 06:2x groom of all lanes closed 6 items Done. Morning report: C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1030\\report-0700.md. Lanes needed most next: kit (TRAIN5 rerun), then compiler (PACK-8 review), both on the user's go.")
inl fsharp_isnan_unqualified () = Task ("FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED", "codegenFsharp emits NanIs as Single.IsNaN(x) / Double.IsNaN(x) with no open System, so the native F# build fails with FS0039 'Single' is not defined (native_float_math_f32 [Fsharp] build-fail, new in pack 7); qualify as System.Single / System.Double", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "PACK-8", "compiler,fsharp,codegen,bug", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fsharp_isnan_unqualified () = Planning ("FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fsharp_isnan_unqualified_1 () = Note ("FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED", 1u32, "2026-10-30T03:16Z", "compiler", "10-29 23:2x compiler: found by the pack 7 -Accept (run single-flight-20261029-223356): the new pack 7 sample native_float_math_f32 is the first to reach NanIs on the F# native build. Row detail: 'error FS0039: The value, namespace, type or module 'Single' is not defined'. Code: spiral_compiler.fs:163733-163734, sprintf 'Single.IsNaN(%s)' / 'Double.IsNaN(%s)'. dotnet fsi opens System implicitly and runs the script (exit 0), so only the matrix's warm F# build sees it. Applier: apps/compiler/packs/apply-fsharp-isnan-qualified.ps1 (2 edits, dry run on the live core ok). The accepted baseline now holds this row as native=build-fail, so it would read as parity: the fix is checked by the row turning 'ran exit 0, agree' in the PACK-8 review. Regression sample: native_float_math_f32 itself (no new sample).")
inl note_of_fsharp_isnan_unqualified_2 () = Note ("FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED", 2u32, "2026-10-30T03:22Z", "compiler", "10-29 23:2x compiler: the row is now an explicit Known entry in apps/compiler/tmp/tests/matrix.psd1 (reason 'KNOWN-WRONG until PACK-8 ... (FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED)'), so the oracle reads 'known' instead of DISAGREE or silent parity. Verified: test.ps1 -Suite examples -Native -Filter native_float_math_f32 (run single-flight-20261029-232113): Delphi exit 217 oracle=known, Fsharp build-fail oracle=known, DISAGREE 0. DONE RULE now also includes REMOVING that Known entry in the same pack that lands the fix; the review must then show the row as 'ran exit 0, agree'.")
inl note_of_fsharp_isnan_unqualified_3 () = Note ("FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED", 3u32, "2026-10-30T03:32Z", "compiler", "10-29 23:3x compiler: CLASS CENSUS, so no sibling stays hidden. A regex over string literals in codegenFsharp (:163255-163832) for an unqualified System type before a member access (Math., Single., Double., Char., Int16/32/64., UInt*, Byte, Decimal, BitConverter, Convert, String, Console, Environment, TimeSpan, DateTime, Array, Buffer, Random, GC, ...) finds exactly the 2 lines this item fixes (the positive control). Every other emitted .NET reference in the F# section is qualified (12 lines emit 'System.'), and the shared CodegenUtils/Adapter sections (:162097-163254) have 0 hits. So the applier covers the whole class.")
inl note_of_fsharp_isnan_unqualified_4 () = Note ("FSHARP-ISNAN-UNQUALIFIED", 4u32, "2026-10-30T16:57Z", "compiler", "10-30 12:56 compiler: INSTALLED AND ACCEPTED in pack 8 (main installed 11:46, core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52 host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9, equal=True, node shipped; the live tree core 4191A77FB3D3A335 carries it; accept run single-flight-20261030-120324, PACK-8 n13). DONE: native_float_math_f32 [Fsharp] builds and runs exit 0, oracle agree, with its Known entry removed. The 10-29 class census found no sibling unqualified System type in codegenFsharp.")
inl delphi_fpu_exceptions_unmasked () = Task ("DELPHI-FPU-EXCEPTIONS-UNMASKED", "Delphi programs leave FPC's FPU exceptions unmasked, so inf - inf raises EInvalidOp (runtime error 217) where C/Rust/F# yield NaN (native_float_math_f32 [Delphi] DISAGREE); mask all FPU exceptions in the program prologue", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "PACK-8", "compiler,delphi,codegen,bug,float", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_delphi_fpu_exceptions_unmasked () = Planning ("DELPHI-FPU-EXCEPTIONS-UNMASKED", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_delphi_fpu_exceptions_unmasked_1 () = Note ("DELPHI-FPU-EXCEPTIONS-UNMASKED", 1u32, "2026-10-30T03:16Z", "compiler", "10-29 23:2x compiler: found by the pack 7 -Accept (run single-flight-20261029-223356): native_float_math_f32 [Delphi] exit 217, oracle DISAGREE, the run's only blocking row. PROVEN BY HAND (fpc -Px86_64 -O2, scoop fpc): the committed main.pas (control) prints 'EInvalidOp: Invalid floating point operation' and exits 217 at v5 := v4 - v4 (Infinity - Infinity); the same file plus one prologue line 'SetExceptionMask([exInvalidOp, exDenormalized, exZeroDivide, exOverflow, exUnderflow, exPrecision]);' after SetTextBuf exits 0. Math is always in the uses clause (spiral_compiler.fs:165797), and on x86_64 SetExceptionMask also sets the SSE MXCSR. Applier: apps/compiler/packs/apply-delphi-fpu-mask.ps1 (1 edit at the program assembly, :165807; dry run ok). RESIDUAL COST: every Delphi output gains that line, about 437 rows, all the same one-line delta, so the PACK-8 predicted set gains 'every Delphi row'. Behaviour: float overflow and divide-by-zero now give inf/NaN as on C/Rust; integer division by zero still raises (not an FPU trap). Any Delphi row that only agreed BECAUSE of a trap would show up as a verdict change in the review.")
inl note_of_delphi_fpu_exceptions_unmasked_2 () = Note ("DELPHI-FPU-EXCEPTIONS-UNMASKED", 2u32, "2026-10-30T03:22Z", "compiler", "10-29 23:2x compiler: the row is now an explicit Known entry in apps/compiler/tmp/tests/matrix.psd1 (reason 'KNOWN-WRONG until PACK-8 ... (DELPHI-FPU-EXCEPTIONS-UNMASKED)'), so the oracle reads 'known' instead of DISAGREE or silent parity. Verified: test.ps1 -Suite examples -Native -Filter native_float_math_f32 (run single-flight-20261029-232113): Delphi exit 217 oracle=known, Fsharp build-fail oracle=known, DISAGREE 0. DONE RULE now also includes REMOVING that Known entry in the same pack that lands the fix; the review must then show the row as 'ran exit 0, agree'.")
inl note_of_delphi_fpu_exceptions_unmasked_3 () = Note ("DELPHI-FPU-EXCEPTIONS-UNMASKED", 3u32, "2026-10-30T16:57Z", "compiler", "10-30 12:56 compiler: INSTALLED AND ACCEPTED in pack 8 (main installed 11:46, core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52 host EEBCBFF8658A1EF9, equal=True, node shipped; the live tree core 4191A77FB3D3A335 carries it; accept run single-flight-20261030-120324, PACK-8 n13). DONE: native_float_math_f32 [Delphi] runs exit 0, oracle agree, with its Known entry removed (pack8-land). main's live probe with FPC pinned to trunk: exit 217 on the pack-7 control, exit 0 on pack 8.")
inl cells_suite_flaky_under_load () = Task ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", "Cells full mix test has 4 intermittent failures on a loaded box (each file passes alone, 73/73): MemoTest 'editing a package file the project does not list keeps the key', MemoDepsTest 'editing a dependency module the program never reaches keeps the key', DocumentTest 'spiral library .spi files load as notebooks' (compile failed: compiler blew up), TargetsTest 'a gleam build without a kept lock...'; investigate DocumentTest's compiler crash first", TaskKind, P2, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "cells,test,flaky,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load () = Planning ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_1 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 1u32, "2026-10-30T04:29Z", "main", "10-30 00:29 main, from x's full-suite run (box, env imported, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, on pack 7, after fiscal's spiral.toml Cells land): 321/325. The 4 failures are intermittent: re-run alone, those 4 files go 73/73. Main's own post-land run earlier showed only the 2 postability failures (since fixed by x), so these 4 appear with load or concurrency, not deterministically. Priority within the item: DocumentTest's 'compiler blew up' is an uncaught compiler crash, not a timeout, so capture its stderr (lib_gate -RawOut-style) in a full-suite run and check whether it reproduces on pack 6b (the backup at C:\\home\\data\\compiler-installs\\pack7-20261029-221710). Method: run the full suite N times under the same load with an A/A row, and count per-test failure rates (no-quiet-machine-wait).")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_2 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 2u32, "2026-11-01T01:24Z", "x", "2026-10-31 21:24 x: evidence from an IDLE node mirror (xqueue3, nothing else running in it), tests run alone, 6 runs each, during CELLS-SPI-LIB's discriminating check (its n5-n6):\n- targets_test.exs:321 'gleam cells with the same manifest run in a warm package whose src is replaced' failed 6 of 6. That is not load: it fails deterministically on the node, so either a real bug or a node environment gap in the warm Gleam package.\n- cells_test.exs:698 'a missing pinned Rust toolchain is installed once' failed 3 of 6, alone and idle. A real flake, not only under load.\nBoth are independent of apps/cells/spi's package reference. I'm not fixing either, since they're main's Cells tests. Recorded so the next suite comparison treats :698 as noise and :321 as a known red on the node.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_3 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 3u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM, evidence since n2: four more LOAD reds on a saturated node, each disproved by a discriminator. x-cells-c3-pre1 (suite 1,216 s) gave MemoTest \"an unqualified name resolves in opened modules...\"; x-cells-c3-memo1 then passed it 26/26 three times. x-cells-c4-pre1 (suite 2,117 s) gave MemoTest \"a target run is reused when the generated code is the same\", MemoDepsTest \"editing a dependency module the program never reaches keeps the key\", and TargetsTest \"a Gleam cell runs from the notebook's directory\"; x-cells-c4-domain1 showed byte-identical domain.gleam. node_cells_window_proof -Tests (scoped suites) is the current mitigation. The CELLS-PORT-* oracles inherit this list, so a red from it needs a discriminator, not a revert.")
inl note_of_cells_suite_flaky_under_load_4 () = Note ("CELLS-SUITE-FLAKY-UNDER-LOAD", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. Likely mechanism, from fiscal n4: concurrent Cells runs on one mirror share %TEMP%\\spiral_cells and the mirror lib, and that produced os error 3 rows and locked files there. That fits the load reds listed in n3, which all came from saturated nodes with other Cells work present. Discriminator to run next, rule written now: the same scoped suite twice on an idle node, (A) alone and (B) beside a second Cells gate on the same mirror. The hypothesis holds iff A has 0 of n3's reds and B reproduces at least one.")
inl spiral_cuda_runner_python () = Task ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", "spiral cuda (apps/spiral process_cuda) runs the first python on PATH and ignores SPIRAL_PYTHON, so Cells cuda rows fail with ModuleNotFoundError numpy wherever a numpy-less python wins PATH; resolve the interpreter from SPIRAL_PYTHON (fallback python) for the run and the pip install", TaskKind, P1, D2, 90u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,compiler,runner,cuda,python,cells", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python () = Planning ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", Minutes 60u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 1u32, "2026-10-30T05:06Z", "compiler", "10-30 01:0x compiler: ROOT CAUSE from kit's raw stderr on the base side (via main, 00:5x): spiral.rs:20438 'spiral.process_cuda / child failed'; main.py:141 numpy.empty(3, dtype=object) gives ModuleNotFoundError numpy. Code: apps/spiral/spiral.spi:1213 Pip runs the literal python \"<path>\", and :1202 runs the PATH pip install. Measured by main: its shell resolves python312 first (numpy 2.x), so 72/72; kit's resolves scoop python 3.15.2 (no numpy), so 67/72 on the same lib, failing the 5 cuda rows of sm' (to_char_array, format, show, to_char_array_2, concat_array). NOT a compiler or lib bug: pack 7 vs 6b Python+Cuda codegen of to_char_array is byte-identical. FIX drafted: C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\apply-spiral-cuda-python.ps1, 3 anchored edits: := python = SPIRAL_PYTHON or python; Pip install = <python> -m pip install -r requirements.txt; Pip run = <python> <path>; Poetry unchanged. Proof running on the node (job-1793336805393): build spiral.exe from the patched source in a private CARGO_TARGET_DIR, then spiral cuda --py-path on a numpy script with a numpy-less python first on PATH. The control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset) must fail on numpy; the fixed run (SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312) must print. Ships through the runner rebuild (RUNNER-STALE). Related, NOT fixed here: SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR n11, the Pip deps transform writes Poetry-style lines (numpy='*') that pip rejects.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 2u32, "2026-10-30T10:25Z", "compiler", "10-30 06:2x compiler (groom): node proof job-1793336805393 is VOID, not a fail of the fix. The applier applied (3 edits) on the pack8 mirror, but compiling apps/spiral/spiral.spi with the installed pack 7 returned 'BuildFile returned no code and no diagnostic arrived', so no spiral.rs carried the fix and the cuda test never ran. Next: re-run the compile with TRACE_DIAGNOSTICS and the mirror's own build.ps1 compile path (BuildSpiral), then the same control/fixed test. Status Active 30 (fix drafted + anchors proven, proof pending).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 3u32, "2026-10-30T10:41Z", "compiler", "10-30 06:4x compiler: VOID CAUSE FOUND, a bug in my draft, not the runner. Inside process_cuda the record parameter { py_path env deps } binds a field named env (the Pip/Poetry choice), which SHADOWS the env module, so env.get_environment_variable there type-checks as a field access on a cuda_env value. TRACE_DIAGNOSTICS showed it: 'Expected: (cuda_env : *) In the definition: run.' The first run printed no diagnostic. FIX REVISED: the applier now adds a top-level ':= cuda_python () : string' (SPIRAL_PYTHON, else 'python') above process_cuda, which only calls 'cuda_python ()'. Re-run job-1793356308358 on the node: spiral.spi now COMPILES (spiral.rs 1,480,375 B); cargo build and the control/fixed numpy test are in progress. Lesson for probes: a lib module name can be shadowed by a record field of the same name inside a function.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 4u32, "2026-10-30T11:10Z", "compiler", "10-30 07:1x compiler: PROOF PASSED (node job-1793356308358, exit 0). The pack8 mirror's spiral.spi reset to its checkout (= the box's clean HEAD file) + the revised applier (3 edits; top-level cuda_python, because the record field env shadows the env module inside process_cuda) compiled with installed pack 7 to spiral.rs 1,480,375 B; cargo release-unwind in a PRIVATE target dir (31 min cold) gave spiral.exe EB706BDE50B84FA4. Test: 'spiral cuda --py-path' on a numpy.empty(3, dtype=object) script, with Programs\\Python312 (no numpy) FIRST on PATH. Control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset): exit 1, ModuleNotFoundError numpy (the bug's own path). Fixed (SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312): exit 0, the ok line printed. LEFT: land the source edit in apps/spiral/spiral.spi (do+undo, a small text edit) after healing's all-clear; then the runner swap (RUNNER-STALE) and CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's done rule (the 5 sm' cuda rows on box and node). Applier: C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\apply-spiral-cuda-python.ps1.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 5u32, "2026-10-30T14:30Z", "compiler", "10-30 10:3x compiler: SOURCE LANDED (unstaged). Applied apply-spiral-cuda-python.ps1 to the live C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\apps\\spiral\\spiral.spi. The pre-land blob baba6978 equals the node proof mirror's checkout, and the post-land blob 6a1b8a73 is byte-identical to the file the node compiled and ran in job-1793356308358. Diff: 8+/2-. format --check exits 0. Undo copy: scratchpad cuda-land\\spiral.spi.undo. spiral.rs was NOT regenerated in the tree: the committed .rs comes from a pre-pack-7 compiler, so any regen churns about 14k lines. The regen goes with the runner rebuild. The proof's exe EB706BDE is NOT shippable, because its mirror (pack8) predates 4 lib lands: sm', xpath, xpath_eval, xsd_emit. Rebuild started from a fresh mirror of the current tree (runner1030, REMOTE-SYNC-OK digest 15B10991A48EB8CD, head cec8840c), job-1793370467510-compiler-runner1030: regen spiral.rs, cargo release-unwind in a private target, smoke (--help, a closure_pair Rust cell), and the cuda control/fixed test. LEFT: read that job; bring its spiral.rs into the tree; swap the runner on box+node, coordinated with main/kit as on 10-29 (RUNNER-STALE); then CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's 5 sm' cuda rows on both machines.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 6u32, "2026-10-30T15:46Z", "compiler", "10-30 11:46 compiler: spiral.rs LANDED (unstaged) to match the landed spiral.spi. The fresh-mirror regen (node runner1030, current box tree, installed pack 7 core 9C899B30) is 1,480,455 B, 5ECE8F9946287738, BYTE-IDENTICAL to the proof's spiral.rs. So the 4 lib lands after the pack8 mirror (sm', xpath, xpath_eval, xsd_emit) do not reach apps/spiral, and the proof's cargo build (exe EB706BDE, control exit 1 / fixed exit 0) already built exactly this file. Diff: 13,926 lines, mostly the pre-pack-7 -> pack-7 regen; 1 SPIRAL_PYTHON line, mimalloc tail kept. Undo copy: scratchpad cuda-land\\spiral.rs.undo (= HEAD blob). The runner1030 cargo build (job-1793370467510) is still running as the re-proof. LEFT: its smoke, then the runner swap on box+node coordinated with main/kit (RUNNER-STALE), then CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's 5 rows.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 7u32, "2026-10-30T16:55Z", "compiler", "10-30 12:55 compiler: RUNNER READY TO SWAP (staged, not swapped). Built on the BOX from C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace with the landed spiral.spi + spiral.rs (5ECE8F9946287738), cargo +nightly-2026-10-18 release-unwind in a private target seeded from the 10-29 warm target: 4 min, exe F1DD2E34F1E816C8, staged at C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\runner-F1DD2E34.exe. Why the box and not the node proof's exe (EB706BDE, built from the identical spiral.rs and Cargo.lock): spiral.rs reads env!(CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR) at 4 sites, so the proof exe's cells report code_path under c:/home/remote/pack8 (a mirror). A swap runner must be built from the real checkout path (memory runner-bakes-manifest-dir). The node's checkout has the same path, so this box exe ships to the node as on 10-29. Smoke: --help exit 0 (13 lines, same as live). A rust --rs-path cell (closure_pair) exits 0 with output byte-identical to the live 2E5F532E (1,437 B, 46ED123B03DE33A7, code_path included). Cuda: SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312 (numpy 2.5.4) exit 0 with the ok line; SPIRAL_PYTHON = a nonexistent path exits 1 'cannot find the path', so the runner takes its interpreter from SPIRAL_PYTHON. The no-numpy control ran on the node (n5). Swap script C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python\\runner-swap.ps1 (10-29's, re-parameterized): dry run ok, live 2E5F532E, 0 users. Waiting on main + kit's go, then node-ship.ps1 for the node, then CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY's 5 sm' cuda rows on both machines.")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 8u32, "2026-10-30T18:04Z", "compiler", "10-30 14:04 compiler: SWAP REVERTED by a pre-registered rule; the box is back on 2E5F532E73EEAF14 (hash-verified, smoke exit 0); the node was never shipped. Sequence: box swap to F1DD2E34 at 13:0x (main + kit go), then kit's sm' gate on the new lib under kit's failing condition (numpy-less python 3.15 first on PATH, SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312): 63/72. Kit's 5 cuda failures (to_char_array, format, show, to_char_array_2, concat_array) PASS, so the cuda fix works. But 9 others failed. A quiet-box rerun of the 9 alone (job-1793382555570), same lib (sm' A683500F), per arm: NEW F1DD2E34 7/9, failing show_floats [zig] and show_floats_in_python_repr_layout [delphi] with 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed' (the slowest passing cell took 79 s, so this is a hang); OLD 2E5F532E 9/9. The other 7 were load (tibia saw the same file's load reds on the node this morning). The hang's target moved between runs (loaded: delphi/zig the other way round), so it's nondeterministic. Rule (agreed with main before the read): new fails and old passes = runner, so restore. F1DD2E34 is kept at C:\\home\\data\\runner-archive-2026-10-30\\spiral.exe.F1DD2E34F1E816C8. Checked so far: the child-process pipe sites (wait/BufReader) have the same shape in the committed (old) and regen (new) spiral.rs, so it's not an obvious pipe-order change. NEXT (box time needed, queued behind tibia's smoke and main's Cells window): (1) repeat the 2 tests 3x per arm to rule out a flake; (2) if it holds, run show_floats on the new exe under a CPU sampler (busy hang vs blocked wait); (3) build a runner from HEAD spiral.spi (no cuda edit) with the installed compiler. If that hangs too, it's a pack-7 Rust codegen regression in the regen, not the cuda edit; then bisect the 13,926-line regen diff by function. 2) Workaround for kit's cuda cells: scoop python312 first on PATH (72/72 this morning).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 9u32, "2026-10-30T19:52Z", "compiler", "10-30 15:52 compiler: NODE RUNNER SWAPPED to F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (kit confirmed TRAIN5 is box-only, so the node could move now; the box stays on 2E5F532E until TRAIN5 publishes). node-ship.ps1 -Label runner-F1DD2E34. Pre-swap smoke on the node (the swap runs only on SMOKE-OK): a closure_pair rust --rs-path cell's JSON output from the staged new exe is byte-identical to the node's live old runner's, code_path included (the exe was built from C:\\home\\git\\spiral on the box, the same path as the node checkout). Digest 4DAB82B4CC4A96DF verified after the copy; the previous runner is kept as spiral.exe.replaced-runner-F1DD2E34. Post-swap cuda test on the node through the live runner, with numpy-less Programs\\Python312 FIRST on PATH: control (SPIRAL_PYTHON unset) exit 1 'No module named numpy' (the bug's own path); fixed (the node's User SPIRAL_PYTHON = scoop python312) exit 0 with the ok line. So the node half of CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY is done. LEFT: the box swap after TRAIN5 publishes (runner-swap.ps1, byte-equal smoke + auto-restore), then the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar; the 5 cuda cells already passed on F1DD2E34 on the box at 13:3x).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 10u32, "2026-10-31T15:19Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 11:19 compiler: BOX SWAP READY, gated on train6 (not TRAIN5 any more). TRAIN5 has published, but kit-train6-20261031 is running now (holds heavy-build), and a release train exercises the runner, so the swap waits for train6 to finish, by the same reason as the old gate. Tooling: runner-swap.ps1 and runner-F1DD2E34.exe were archived with C:\\home\\data\\cuda-python (20261031-094304) and restored to %TEMP%\\runner-restore\\cuda-python; the script's archive dir moved from C:\\home\\data\\runner-archive-2026-10-30 to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runner-archive\\2026-10-31 (C:\\home\\data is closed). Dry run now: live 2E5F532E73EEAF14, staged F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (hash re-verified), 0 live users. The swap keeps its byte-equal smoke (closure_pair rust --rs-path, new vs old JSON identical) and auto-restore. After it: the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 11u32, "2026-10-31T17:05Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 13:05 compiler: BOX RUNNER SWAPPED to F1DD2E34F1E816C8. train6 ended (its job hit the wall-clock cap at 12:5x), and its resume gate is held behind cells-window-6 (to 18:06) and pack10-install (to 19:38), so no train will run on the old runner for hours. runner-swap.ps1 -Apply: live had 0 users; the old 2E5F532E73EEAF14 is archived at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runner-archive\\2026-10-31\\spiral.exe.2E5F532E73EEAF14; smoke 'rust --rs-path samples/closure_pair/main.rs' gave new exit 0 (1437 B) and old exit 0 (1437 B), identical: SMOKE-OK; live is now F1DD2E34F1E816C8. Box and node now run the same runner. LEFT for Done: the box sm' cuda cells under kit's failing PATH (72/72 bar).")
inl note_of_spiral_cuda_runner_python_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-CUDA-RUNNER-PYTHON", 12u32, "2026-10-31T20:21Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 16:21 compiler: the box sm' cuda gate (job-1793474272154, 'scoop python' 3.15 numpy-less FIRST on PATH, SPIRAL_PYTHON = python312, runner F1DD2E34, sm' D3FCCD791E27FED1) is VOID: it hit my 60 min cap (exit 124) on a box at 100% (train6 + PACK-11 builds) before lib_gate printed its summary; cells were compiling, not hung (one-shot compiler processes at 4-7 s CPU per 5 s, 15:36). The cap was too tight for the load (memory job-timeout-counts-queue-wait). Rerun with a 3 h cap AFTER tibia lands its test-only sm' change (D3FCCD79 -> 94A51BB5; tibia's land waits for this gate as the only live sm' reader), so the gate proves the new base and doesn't block tibia again.")
