inl note_of_backlog_dangling_1030_1 () = Note ("BACKLOG-DANGLING-1030", 1u32, "2026-10-30T11:09Z", "compiler", "10-30 07:3x compiler (git-a6), on the user's order: 'see what else in the backlog is dangling so we try advancing autonomously, to prevent another full-day run of useless work'. Census: C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\dangling-census.ps1 (read-only; rows in dangling.csv). 389 open; 192 flagged: Blocked 21, Paused 121, assignee user 6 / pair 21, latest note waits on the user 22, Active with no note >= 3 d 18, every dep Done but Planned/Blocked/Paused 27.\nWHY RUNS GO USELESS: lanes re-verify the same user-blocked items every groom ('re-verified Blocked: still the USER's ...'), and ready work sits unpicked ('Paused only for want of a picker'), so 'agile next' offers little real work. RULES (apply from now): (R1) an item whose ONLY blocker is a user action gets assignee=user and tag user-batch, and grooms do not re-verify it; it moves only when the user acts. (R2) every DEPS-DONE/RESUMABLE item gets an owning team tag (lane-roles), so 'agile next --team' hands it out. (R3) an Active item with no note in 3 d gets, in the next groom, either a concrete next step with an owner or Paused with the reason; never left Active-silent. (R4) a 'decision for the user' that a recorded rule or memory answers is decided by the agent and recorded (decide-autonomously); only outward or irreversible acts stay the user's (commit/push, publish, the user's own look).\nGROUP A, USER-ONLY (one sitting clears them all):\n- commits and pushes (the agents never commit): TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL (Zed look + commit apps/zed + rev bump); SOCIAL-PROFILES-LOCAL and X-CLIENT (commit apps/client/e2e/social_stub.py, links.txt, apps/sim/fixtures/prelude.parity.txt); UPSTREAM-POST-2-C-SELF-TAIL (commit the fork files); PACKAGE-REGISTRY-DESIGN (commit the 10-27 lib primitives); PIPELINES-GREEN and CI-ACTIONS-LATEST (the unstaged bumps); push spiral with pack 7, which unblocks C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS (Linux CI), RUST-DERIVE-INFERENCE (dice CI), NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-EXPORT (gh-pages deploy) and SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT.\n- publishing: TREE-PAGES-V2 (approve the dir-tree-html release), TIBIA-ARENA-RELEASE.\n- the user's own check: ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES (in-Zed check). Paused by the user: TIBIA-BASELINES, TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT, SPIRAL-BIGNUM-MODEXP, WORKFLOW-END-TO-END (resume is the user's).\nGROUP B, AUTONOMOUS NOW (no user input; owner team in brackets):\n- 'downloads the user must do' are autonomous with the Claude-in-Chrome browser tool (a real browser, not a script): FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE (official Facturae 3.2.2 sample) and FISCAL-PE-SUNAT (SUNAT XSL package that 403s scripts) [fiscal].\n- rule-answered decisions: LIB-CANON-NAMES (pick a non-colliding canon name for runtime or merge into process.spi; a naming call) [lib/main]; CI-K3S (placement: deploy manifests in i574n.github per org-tooling-in-dot-github) [main]; CUDA-CELLS-FLEET-PARITY (filed 07:1x, rules inside) [compiler].\n- ready, unpicked: LIB-PAR-MAP first (it gates Active BACKEND-BALANCE) [lib]; FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS 95% [compiler]; CODEGEN-READABLE-2, QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER [compiler]; EXECUTABLE-ATLAS, PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES 82%, SPIRAL3-EDITIONS, LIB-OTP-ACTORS, LIB-OTP-TYPED-CALL, LIB-OTP-ETS/PG/CODE-CHANGE, HANGULIZE-IN-SPIRAL [lib/main by need]; DELPHI-FILE-READ-BUFFER, SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD [compiler]; EOIE-MACHINE-HEALTH, EOIE-AGILE-REQUESTED, EOIE-TABLE-JSONL, EOIE-LEGACY-STATE-TRIAGE, EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE, EOIE-GAP-INTAKE (check TRAIN2c, likely Done) [kit]; X-HAND-UNITS (parked by its own rule) [x].\n- stale actives needing a next step or Paused (R3): P0 LIB-IGGY-CLIENT 75% and IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE (iggy is P0 per the 10-26 priority) [kit]; EOIE-HAND-CRATE-UNITS 90% [kit]; FISCAL-APP, FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE [fiscal]; FORMATTER-SPEED 85% (7 d), MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS, GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT [compiler]; KINO-HOT-PATHS, LIB-REACTORS, LIB-USAGE-DIAGNOSTICS, SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR [main]; EOIE-JOB-RECHAIN, LIB-GENERATED