inl gleam_inline_single_use () = Task ("GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE", "Gleam codegen: inline single-use pure literal/constructor lets and fold tail 'let vN = e; vN' blocks (the Gleam twin of RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE)", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,gleam,codegen,x,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gleam_inline_single_use () = Planning ("GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_gleam_inline_single_use_1 () = Note ("GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE", 1u32, "2026-10-30T15:07Z", "x", "2026-10-30 11:2x x: filed from a measurement, not a guess. In x's events unit after G3 (node units-g3\\g3\\xsim_events.gleam, pack 7, 1,728 lines), 186 lines are binding noise that GLEAM-COMPACT-OUTPUT (single-expression arms only) does not reach. 103 are one-use string-literal lets (let v36 = \"at\" then field_26(v36, v37)), 6 are int-literal lets and 23 are constructor lets (Uh1Nil / None); all pure and mostly used once. 51 are tail lets inside multi-statement blocks (let v15 = bit_array.byte_size(...) then v15). The Gleam twin of RUST-INLINE-SINGLE-USE: inline a pure literal/constructor binding into its single use, and fold a block's final 'let vN = e; vN' into e. Done rule: an applier in apps/compiler/packs, the predicted-row set of the next pack review accepted with 0 Gleam verdict changes, and x's events unit re-measured. X-HAND-UNITS (P1, parked) needs about 164 lines beyond the BEAM decoder lever (n25); this pass (~180) plus x's remaining source levers (~80: short_escape as a table slice, typed field helpers, :~ parent_of) would bring P under 950. Not a list-literal pass: UhNCons chains are Spiral's own recursive union, not Gleam lists.")
inl note_of_gleam_inline_single_use_2 () = Note ("GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE", 2u32, "2026-11-04T01:12Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:11 x: ORPHAN SWEEP (MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP, x's corner: open x items with no note in 48 h). Owner team:compiler (x filed the measurement); next step compiler's: one-use Gleam bindings in xsim_events. x re-measures when a compiler pack claims it.")
inl note_of_gleam_inline_single_use_3 () = Note ("GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE", 3u32, "2026-11-05T08:21Z", "compiler", "11-05 04:2x compiler: IMPLEMENTED + REVIEWED (native). Program %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE\\1-gleam-tidy.kitdo (2 replacements): gleamTidy, a text pass after UnusedGlobals.prune on every generated .gleam, per top-level function (a 'pub fn'/'fn' line ending in '{' through its column-0 '}', so @external declarations are skipped). (1) Single-use inline: 'let vN = <int | float | \"string\" | Constructor>' whose vN occurs exactly once elsewhere in the function, outside any string literal, is dropped and its value substituted at that use (never a negative literal right after '-'). Repeats until nothing changes, so an alias of an inlined value inlines next. (2) Tail fold: a single-line 'let vN = e' (no braces) immediately followed by a bare 'vN' at the same indent becomes 'e'. Gleam bindings are immutable, so both rewrites keep evaluation order. REVIEW (node compiler-tidy, control = pack43 bin core 531FD54E, candidate = pack43 + tidy, core 35DCBD04): test.ps1 -Suite examples -Backend Gleam -Native -TimeoutSec 300, 442 rows per arm, 442 compiled ok on both, native 440 ran + 2 build-fail on both (the same rows). VERDICT differences (compile/native/exit/stdout) 0. Residual changes 411 (the intended rewrites). Generated Gleam over the 450 sample .gleam files: 40,028 -> 37,934 lines (-2,094, -5.2%). x's own measure (xsim_events) is for x to repeat after install. Ships in the next pack together with COMPILER-RELATED-DIAGNOSTIC-RACE program 2 (host only; independent files). Node stage deleted.")
inl note_of_gleam_inline_single_use_4 () = Note ("GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE", 4u32, "2026-11-05T08:45Z", "compiler", "11-05 04:4x compiler: INSTALLED on the BOX in pack44 (04:39-04:44, compiler's chain): SpiralCompilerCore.dll 657DA4B173F9D3D3 and SpiralCompiler.dll E441B6B3F8865B02, both equal=True to the reviewed combined candidate (pack43 + COMPILER-RELATED-DIAGNOSTIC-RACE program 2 + GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE program 1; source core 35DCBD04 / host A1E7136E, the two separately reviewed sources). Undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack44-20261105-043957. Install wait 1 min (cleared 04:39 after a 04:38 start), the first install under CELLS-GATE-PINNED-COMPILER's narrowed check; tonight's earlier installs waited 21-63 min behind gates. Node: main ships it with notice to kit and x. Done under installed-is-done.")
inl note_of_gleam_inline_single_use_5 () = Note ("GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE", 5u32, "2026-11-05T08:47Z", "x", "2026-11-05 04:47 x: RE-MEASURED (the item's done rule), box pack44 core 657DA4B173F9D3D3: x/apps/client/events/events.spi -> xsim_events.gleam = 1129 lines. Remaining binding noise by the 10-30 patterns: string-literal lets 16, int-literal lets 0, constructor lets 0, tail lets (let vN = e then bare vN) 3; total 19, against 186 measured on 10-30 (103 string, 6 int, 23 constructor, 51 tail). Caveat: the source changed since 10-30 (x-next6/8 landed), so 1728 -> 1129 lines is not a pure compiler delta, but the pattern counts are the measure. The 16 string lets left are likely multi-use (the pass only inlines single-use ones); not checked line by line.")
