inl note_of_lib_macro_heal_clip_rust_1 () = Note ("LIB-MACRO-HEAL-CLIP-RUST", 1u32, "2026-10-30T15:18Z", "main", "10-30 11:18 main: split from LIB-MACRO-HEAL. The clip Rust heal LANDED and was REVERTED on 10-29 (n86): Spiral's branch inlined at every Rust call site and pushed kit crates past 1000 generated lines (kit_memory_query 996 -> 1032, +9 per call site). Kit's GRANULAR-LINT port flags sm'.spi:754 as the lib's 1 remaining CANDIDATE (GRANULAR-LINT n31). Retry per n86: one ':~' join point (not inlined), called from the Rust arm; regen the kit crates that call clip (kit_memory_query, kit_memory, kit_memory_import, agile_note_edit, agile_task_listing, agile_task_next) and require 0 growth past 1000 (kit_memory_query sits at 996) BEFORE any land. If a join point still grows them, the one-block host form stays as the compact form for hot Rust call sites, so classify it exempt and close.")
inl note_of_lib_macro_heal_clip_rust_2 () = Note ("LIB-MACRO-HEAL-CLIP-RUST", 2u32, "2026-10-30T22:32Z", "main", "10-30 18:32 main: DRAFTED (CPU-light, not yet proven): C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1030\\clip-rust\\apply.ps1 (1 anchor in sm'.spi, dry run 1/1 on the live lib A683500F9D51). The Rust arm becomes 'clip_rust width s', a ':~' (non-recursive JOIN POINT, so it's emitted once and every call site is one call, not the inlined branch that grew kit's crates by +9 lines per site on 10-29). clip_rust has the F# arm's shape in Spiral: count via one host call (chars().count through i32::try_from, no as-casts), the <= branch and the keep arithmetic in Spiral, head via one host call (chars().take with usize::try_from), then the ellipsis append. PROOF PLAN, pre-registered: on a scratch lib copy, (1) lib_gate sm'.spi: clip_keeps_short_text_and_cuts_long_text_on_char_boundaries passes on fsharp and rust; (2) regen kit's 6 clip-calling crates (kit_memory_query 996, kit_memory, kit_memory_import, agile_note_edit, agile_task_listing, agile_task_next) against the copy with kit's own regen tool, and require each crate to grow by at most +1 generated line per call site AND stay under 1000. If any crate grows past that, classify the Rust arm EXEMPT (compact host form for hot sites) and close. Needs a box slot when CPU frees, plus kit's regen on a scratch lib.")
inl note_of_lib_macro_heal_clip_rust_3 () = Note ("LIB-MACRO-HEAL-CLIP-RUST", 3u32, "2026-10-30T23:38Z", "main", "10-30 19:3x main: step 1 PASSED on a scratch lib. Draft C:\\home\\data\\main-drafts\\session-1030\\clip-rust\\apply.ps1 replaces clip's Rust arm with a ':~ clip_rust' join point (char count through i32::try_from(chars().count()), take through usize::try_from); anchor 1/1; lib_gate -File sm'.spi on the scratch copy with the clip test filter: tests passed 1 of 1 (70 filtered by design), type errors 0. NEXT (step 2, kit team): regen kit's 6 clip-calling crates against a scratch lib with the draft applied and check every crate stays under 1,000 lines and grows at most +1 line per call site; then land in a lib window (hashes, kit's 14 signatures, document_test, type_probe).")
