inl kit_agent_commit_guard () = Task ("KIT-AGENT-COMMIT-GUARD", "kit do git commit refuses in an agent session unless the same program created the repo with git init, so the user's never-commit rule holds in the tool (10-30: two kit commits by an agent had to be undone)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,git,safety,dangling", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_agent_commit_guard () = Planning ("KIT-AGENT-COMMIT-GUARD", Minutes 15u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_agent_commit_guard_1 () = Note ("KIT-AGENT-COMMIT-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-10-30T16:06Z", "kit", "10-30 12:0x kit: built and LANDED UNSTAGED. Found while sizing EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES F2e (n42): 'kit do' has 'git commit <repo> all \"msg\"', with which the kit session committed 4e756cc/05da38a on 10-29 against the user's rule (never-commit-leave-unstaged).\n- Guard (kit_do_git/run.spi): in an agent session (AI_AGENT or CLAUDECODE set, the same detection 'agile note --as' uses), 'git commit' is refused unless an earlier 'git init' of the same repo is in the same program. Fixtures are built exactly that way: every spec/one-call.md case is files first, then 'git init x; git commit x all ...'. The refusal: 'refused: an agent session commits only to a repo this program created with git init; the user reviews, stages and commits their own repos', exit 1, nothing written. The check is stateless: created_before scans the program's earlier records, so git_tally doesn't grow.\n- Unit split: 'git status' (repos_status, state_row) moved into kit_do_git_reports, beside history/days, behind a new kit_do_git_status export, so kit_do_git stays clear of the gate. Under pack 8: kit_do_git 892 -> 747, kit_do_git_reports 349 -> 456. The pack-8 control regen of the unchanged crates kept their line counts.\n- Test: new CLI notebook kit_do_git/git_cli.spi (registered in kit_dev_spiral_tests): agent init+commit allowed; agent commit to a repo it did not create refused with exit 1; the same commit with the agent variables dropped succeeds. 1/1 pass against the candidate binary.\n- ACCEPTANCE on a full candidate kit.exe (cargo build --locked -p kit-cli of live + candidate, 03BBED21), 11/11 (C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\agent-commit-guard\\candidate-acceptance.ps1). Covers this guard (4 rows, incl. the git log unchanged after the refusal); 'git status' byte-identical to the installed kit on kit, i574n.github and spiral; and re-proofs of today's append-parents, lint (0 flow rows on lib), note stdin and next skipping user-batch.\n- Side finding: 'append' can't share a program with 'git' ('append cannot share one program with git yet'), so the spec setup at spec:344 (append and commit in one program) would be rejected as written.\nCloses when installed.")
inl note_of_kit_agent_commit_guard_2 () = Note ("KIT-AGENT-COMMIT-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-10-30T22:43Z", "kit", "10-30 18:4x kit: Active -> Blocked. The code is landed unstaged and passed the 18-row acceptance on a candidate; the only step left is installing it, which rides TRAIN5, and TRAIN5 waits on the user's OK (and AC power). Unblock: after TRAIN5 installs, rerun C:\\home\\data\\kit-drafts\\agent-commit-guard\\candidate-acceptance.ps1 against the installed kit, then close.")
inl note_of_kit_agent_commit_guard_3 () = Note ("KIT-AGENT-COMMIT-GUARD", 3u32, "2026-10-31T11:48Z", "kit", "10-31 07:4x kit: DONE (installed-is-done). release-acceptance.ps1 on the installed kit E14F1F0B (TRAIN5e DONE 07:43, 140/140 notebooks; the binary was swapped retire-then-move while lanes ran) passed 23/23 at 07:44. Rows: an agent commits a repo its program created; an agent is refused on a repo it did not create, and the refused commit wrote nothing; a non-agent run still commits.")
inl xpath_predicate_errors () = Task ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", "xpath_eval: an error inside a predicate (unsupported function, bad cast) is swallowed as false by kept_at; surface it as a rule error so rule sets cannot silently lose an exemption or a filter", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:fiscal,xpath,schematron,correctness,fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xpath_predicate_errors () = Planning ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_1 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 1u32, "2026-10-30T18:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:09 fiscal: FOUND via DIAN (FISCAL-CO-DIAN n of this time). kept_at reduces a predicate's value with effective_boolean, and effective_boolean (VError _) = false (xpath_eval.spi:344), so M19's signature exemption, written with the then-unsupported namespace-uri(), matched nothing and flagged ds:Reference/@URI='' as an empty UBL attribute. namespace-uri() is now drafted (dian-ns), but the general hazard stays: any unsupported construct inside a predicate quietly changes a rule's meaning. Plan, sized by milestones: (1) kept_at / values_kept return the first VError instead of filtering, so it reaches check_rules / check_assertions as a Broken/context failure, like the and/or propagation landed 10-29 (Peppol n of 10-29) 45m; (2) lib test: a predicate calling an unknown function yields an error failure, not silence 30m; (3) re-run every pinned regional rule set (CEN, Peppol, ZATCA, UBL-TR, RO, DIAN) and treat each new error row as a found gap, not a regression 45m. Order: after the dian-ns land, so the DIAN counts it moves are already namespace-correct.")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_2 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 2u32, "2026-10-30T18:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 14:34 fiscal: milestones 1 + 2 DRAFTED (40 by the weights in n1: 45 + 30 of 120 minutes are written, nothing proven yet). C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-pred\\xpath_eval.spi (48CB4D7B, layered on dian-ns CFD7A7F3, base copy in base\\): kept_by and kept_at return xvalue. A predicate's VError returns at once instead of filtering as false. XFilter and step_nodes pass the error up, so it reaches check_rules / check_assertions as a context or Broken failure. New test a_predicate_error_reaches_the_caller: an unknown function inside a predicate yields VError; boolean and positional predicates still filter. Formatter-clean on my lines. Milestone 3 queued in the same chain on dxsl (pack 8): put -> xpath_eval -> schematron_run -> every pinned regional test (cen_examples, cen_rules_catch_mutated, peppol, zatca, ubl_tr samples + other documents, ro_cius), each raw kept as fix-dxsl-pred-<test>.txt. The namespace drafts underneath change nothing for read_schematron rule sets (empty map), so any new red is a predicate error coming to light, and gets treated as a found gap.")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_3 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 3u32, "2026-10-30T20:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 16:43 fiscal: MILESTONES 1 + 2 PROVEN on dxsl pack 8: fiscal-p8-pred-xpath_eval (job-1793385042548, xpath_eval 48CB4D7B) 11/11, a_predicate_error_reaches_the_caller 422 s; fiscal-p8-pred-schematron_run (job-1793385051894) 5/5 on top of it; 0 type errors. 40 -> 60 (75 of 120 minutes proven). Milestone 3 (the regional re-runs) MOVED TO THE BOX on main's policy change (box open for correctness runs at BelowNormal while the node is saturated): scratch gate C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\boxgate (lib = live + dian-ns + dian-pred, fiscal = e3live + layer, deps junctions to the scratch lib and the live corpus, compiler pinned to a frozen copy of pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A). Chain fiscal-box-pred-r-* (cen_examples -> cen_rules_catch_mutated -> peppol -> zatca -> ubl_tr x2 -> ro_cius), raws in boxgate\\raw\\. The node's queued regional jobs were stopped; its running cen_examples (job-1793385064942) finishes as a cross-check.")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_4 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 4u32, "2026-10-30T20:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 16:49 fiscal: ROUND TRIP: the predicate draft xpath_eval 48CB4D7B printed 'round-trips false fixpoint true'. Byte diff: it lacks the final newline (my test append dropped it; 72506 vs 72507 bytes, nothing else differs). Adopted the canonical form -> 3BCD928E. 48CB4D7B stays the semantics evidence (node lib proof 11/11 and the box regional re-runs); before its land, 3BCD928E gets a one-module xpath_eval re-proof, and the round trip check runs as standard pre-land practice.")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_5 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 5u32, "2026-10-30T21:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 17:28 fiscal: MILESTONE 3, first results on the box gate (lib = namespace + predicate drafts, xpath_eval 48CB4D7B; pinned pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A; BelowNormal): cen_examples_pass_the_en16931_rules, cen_rules_catch_mutated_invoices, peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules, zatca_samples_pass_the_zatca_rules and ubl_tr_samples_keep_their_main_schematron_findings all PASS (1/1 each, the UBL-TR pins unchanged). Surfacing predicate errors uncovered NO hidden error in the CEN, Peppol, ZATCA or UBL-TR rule sets. ubl_tr_other_documents and ro_cius are still running. Meanwhile the canonical-newline draft 3BCD928E is re-proving alone (fiscal-box2-pred-xpath_eval-canon, job-1793395508188, scratch boxgate2).")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_6 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 6u32, "2026-10-30T21:55Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 17:55 fiscal: MILESTONE 3 COMPLETE, no hidden predicate error in any pinned regional rule set: ubl_tr_other_documents_keep_their_main_schematron_findings and ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings PASS too (after cen_examples, cen_rules_catch_mutated, peppol, zatca, ubl_tr_samples), plus DIAN's 44 pins hold on this lib. The canonical draft's re-proof (fiscal-box2-pred-xpath_eval-canon, 3BCD928E) is VOID: 3 of 11 rows hit the 900 s cap under the 9-parallel box load (slowest 919677 ms); 8 passed. Re-run alone after box-open. Progress 60 -> 85 (milestones 1-3 proven; left: the canonical re-proof, then its own lib window).")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_7 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 7u32, "2026-10-30T22:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:45 fiscal: READY TO LAND. The canonical draft 3BCD928E re-proved alone on the box: 11/11, 0 type errors (fiscal-box-r3-pred-xpath_eval-canon3); round trip 'round-trips true fixpoint true'. Program C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-lib\\xpath-predicate-errors.kit (749C4500, 3 hunks) + lander16.ps1, base = the live xpath_eval CFD7A7F3 (landed 17:24), rehearsed hash-exact to 3BCD928E. Undo = dian-pred\\base\\xpath_eval.spi (= live). Window granted by main: lands as soon as compiler's bench + compile-hold windows clear in kit window list (background wait-clear -> lander16 -> document_test). 85 -> 95.")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_8 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 8u32, "2026-10-30T23:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:00 fiscal: LAND MECHANICS FIXED (not landed yet; live xpath_eval still CFD7A7F3). The first attempt waited for compiler's bench to clear (18:44) and then retried the reader guard, held off by main's Cells window. But lander16 checks only readers, not kit windows, and compiler opened a SECOND bench window (compiler-p3cw-ab), so a later retry could have landed mid-bench. It was stopped before any write. Now land-pred-when-clear.ps1 loops: kit window wait-clear bench,compile-hold,test-suite, then ONE guarded attempt (lander16-once, base-pinned), then 60 s and repeat, so every attempt starts with clear windows. The ancestry exemption widened to fiscal-drafts\\boxgate\\d*\\ (my own scratch gates incl. boxgate4). document_test runs right after the land. Background task in my session; nothing queued as a kit job.")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_9 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 9u32, "2026-10-30T23:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:39 fiscal: LANDED 19:09:45: xpath-predicate-errors.kit, xpath_eval CFD7A7F3 -> 3BCD928E (hash equal to the box-proven canonical draft, 11/11), by land-pred-when-clear.ps1: the windows cleared (bench, compile-hold, test-suite), then one base-pinned guarded attempt passed the reader guard. Post-land document_test (spi -> livemd -> spi) 22/22. Undo = C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\dian-pred\\base\\xpath_eval.spi (CFD7A7F3), not git HEAD. All milestones met: an error inside a predicate now reaches the caller, and no pinned regional rule set (CEN, Peppol, ZATCA, UBL-TR x2, RO, DIAN 44 pins) had a hidden one. 95 -> 100, Done.")
inl note_of_xpath_predicate_errors_10 () = Note ("XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS", 10u32, "2026-10-31T02:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 22:21 fiscal: STATUS RE-APPLIED. Note 9's close (kit agile set 100 Done at 19:39, which answered ok progress=100 status=Done) was lost: the record now reads 95 Active with tags 'team:fiscal,xpath,schematron,correctness,fiscal', a trailing 'fiscal' it did not have, so a later tag edit rewrote the Task record from a copy taken before the close (lost update; HU-NAV and GST, closed later, kept Done). Re-set to 100 Done; the land and its document_test 22/22 are unchanged.")
inl test_toolchain_guard () = Task ("TEST-TOOLCHAIN-GUARD", "test.ps1 refuses a -Native run whose CC or FPC differs from the baseline toolchain.tsv unless -AcceptToolchain (an unpinned PATH compiler fakes NATIVE-DIFF rows)", Story, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,matrix,toolchain,determinism", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_test_toolchain_guard () = Planning ("TEST-TOOLCHAIN-GUARD", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_test_toolchain_guard_1 () = Note ("TEST-TOOLCHAIN-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-10-30T20:34Z", "compiler", "10-30 16:34 compiler: filed on main's ask after today's E3 samples check. A hand-written test.ps1 -Native wrapper pinned SPIRAL_FPC but not SPIRAL_CC, the kit job's PATH resolved scoop mingw 16.2 instead of the baseline's gcc 15.2, and two C rows with UNCHANGED residuals went NATIVE-DIFF (exit 3 -> 0xC0000409). The pre-registered rule then rolled back 1,252 good files (about 1 h lost). test.ps1 only PRINTS toolchain drift unless -Accept. DRAFT (ready, not landed): C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\apply-test-toolchain-guard.ps1, one anchored edit in apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1's toolchain block: any -Native run throws when CC or Fpc differs from baseline toolchain.tsv (path|size|mtime stamp) unless -AcceptToolchain, naming both stamps; other tools keep today's warning. Checked: anchor 1x on the live test.ps1, the patched copy parses, and the selector picks a CC change and ignores a Bun-only change. LAND RULE (main): through a normal window AFTER TRAIN5 publishes, so the train's harness doesn't move under it. DONE RULE: landed, and the positive control is a test.ps1 -Native -Filter <one C sample> run with mingw 16.2 first on PATH and no SPIRAL_CC, which must refuse with both CC stamps in the message; the same run with SPIRAL_CC = gcc 15.2 must start.")
inl note_of_test_toolchain_guard_2 () = Note ("TEST-TOOLCHAIN-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-10-31T12:21Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 08:21 compiler: LANDED in place (uncommitted): apps/compiler/scripts/test.ps1:400-401 (draft C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\apply-test-toolchain-guard.ps1 -Apply, anchor 1x, the file parses). Land rule checked: TRAIN5 has published (train6-20261031 is the current train), and train6 runs kit\\scripts\\release-train.ps1 on a snapshot that never calls the compiler's test.ps1; no test.ps1 process was live. DONE RULE MET: (1) -Native -Filter samples/union_case_ambiguity_negative with no SPIRAL_CC (PATH gcc = scoop mingw 16.2.0) -> exit 1, message names both stamps (CC: gcc\\15.2.0\\bin\\gcc.exe|2239488|... -> mingw\\16.2.0-rt_v14-rev1\\bin\\gcc.exe|3309056|...); (2) the same run with SPIRAL_CC = scoop gcc 15.2 -> started and finished, 4/4 parity, exit 0 (run single-flight-20261031-081703); the sample folder is unchanged.")
inl xml_xpath_fidelity () = Task ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", "lib xml/xpath fidelity gaps found by the DIAN probes: read_xml decodes only the 5 named entities (numeric character references &#NNN; / &#xHH; stay literal text), and xpath name()/local-name() of an attribute returns its internal @-prefixed name", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:fiscal,xml,xpath,correctness,fiscal", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xml_xpath_fidelity () = Planning ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_1 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 1u32, "2026-10-30T20:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 16:34 fiscal: FOUND by fiscal-p8-pl8-faj27-assert (job-1793391930658) and fiscal-p8-pl8-faj27-probe. (1) xml.spi decode_entities (xml.spi:80) replaces only &lt; &gt; &quot; &apos; &amp;, so a numeric reference stays literal. DIAN's compiled XSL writes every code list delimited by U+007F as &#x7f;, e.g. FAJ27 contains('&#x7f;04&#x7f;05&#x7f;', concat('&#x7f;', ., '&#x7f;')). That matches by accident because both sides carry the same literal text, but a value containing &, #, x, 7, f or ; could match a delimiter falsely, and any document text using &#NNN; (accented Spanish, for one) compares wrong. Only 1 fiscal corpus document contains &#. (2) node_name_value returns node_name of an attribute node, which is the internal XmlElement name '@listName'; XPath name(@listName) must be 'listName' (local-name likewise). Plan, sized by milestones: decode &#NNN; and &#xHH; (BMP + astral, via xml.code_point_string) in decode_entities after the named ones, ampersand last 45m; strip the @ in node_name_value for attributes 15m; lib tests for both 30m; re-run the round-trip and regional gates (CEN, Peppol, ZATCA, UBL-TR, RO, DIAN), since decoding changes text that writers re-emit 60m. Order: after the dian-ns land and XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_2 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 2u32, "2026-10-30T22:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 18:54 fiscal: DRAFTED (milestones 1-3 written, 40 by n1's weights). C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\xml-fidelity (bases in base\\): xml.spi 58CA22E1 -> 3300361F: decode_entities now runs decode_numeric_references after the named entities and BEFORE &amp; (so &amp;#x41; stays the literal text &#x41;). numeric_references_from scans &#...; with find_from, parses decimal and hex (x/X) up to U+10FFFF via hex_digit/reference_value, and emits code_point_string; malformed references (&#xZZ;, &#;, no semicolon) stay as written. decode_entities moved below find_from, still above its first caller read_attributes. New test numeric_character_references_decode (DIAN's U+007F-delimited form, decimal 233, the escaped ampersand, malformed, and attribute + text through read_xml). xpath_eval 3BCD928E (= the predicate draft, the next land) -> 83EAA3FC: node_name_value drops the internal @ of an attribute, so name(@n) = 'n', local-name drops the prefix; new test name_of_an_attribute_is_its_xml_name. Both formatter-clean on my lines and 'round-trips true fixpoint true'. Gates queued on scratch boxgate4 (live lib + both drafts), behind wait-clear test-suite,bench,compile-hold. Then milestone 4: the regional + round-trip gates, since decoding changes text that writers re-emit.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_3 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 3u32, "2026-10-30T23:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:51 fiscal: FIRST BOX GATES + A REAL BUG FOUND (pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A, scratch boxgate4). xml 3300361F: 9/12, and the 3 'failures' are VOID: each cell died at the 300 s file cap (rust 232 s + zig 94 s in one cell; headroom 1.09), so numeric_character_references_decode passed and nothing red. xpath_eval 83EAA3FC: 11/12; name_of_an_attribute_is_its_xml_name RED on rust at its own assert 'a prefixed attribute keeps its prefix in name()'. A probe cell printed name(a/@x:k) = 'k' and the attribute names as n,k. ROOT CAUSE: xml.node_name returns local_name of the written name, so for '@x:k' it cuts through the colon and drops the '@' too. Consequences in live xpath_eval: (1) is_attribute (starts_with '@' (node_name node)) is FALSE for every prefixed attribute; (2) name() of a prefixed element (cbc:ID) returned the local name, the same as local-name(); (3) name_matches_in sent a prefixed attribute down the element branch and looked up 'xmlns:@x', so a mapped-prefix attribute test (@ds:..., @xsi:... with a mapping) could never match; (4) namespace-uri() of any attribute was ''. FIX (draft CC078F4B, base 3BCD928E = live): written_name (the XmlElement's own name), is_attribute and the new qualified_name (written name minus '@') use it; node_name_value, name_matches, name_matches_in and namespace_uri_value read qualified_name; a mapped prefix on an attribute resolves by URI from its element, and an unprefixed attribute is in no namespace. The test now declares xmlns:x and also pins name(x:b) = 'x:b', local-name(x:b) = 'b', namespace-uri(a/@x:k) = 'urn:x', namespace-uri(a/@n) = '', count(a/@y:k) = 1 and count(a/@y:n) = 0 under y -> urn:x. No other lib module uses is_attribute; the new names clash with nothing. Formatter: no new diffs; round trip true. Re-gate queued (fiscal-box4-fidelity-r2: xpath_eval then xml, with gate-only --timeout 1800000 headers) behind main's tree-write window. Milestone 4 (regional re-runs) matters more now: rules with mapped-prefix attribute tests change meaning.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_4 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 4u32, "2026-10-30T23:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 19:53 fiscal: MILESTONE 4 SCOPE from a corpus census (39 rule files under deps/corpus). Prefixed attribute tests (@p:x): only @xml:id / @xml:lang / @xml:space in DIAN's tooling XSLs (utils\\Crane-*, iso skeleton), which fiscal does not evaluate, so no evaluated rule set changes through the attribute fix. Bare name() calls, which now keep element prefixes: DIAN compiled XSL 21 (name(.) 9, name() 6, name(current()) 6, mostly the skeleton's location-path output), UBL21-Structure3.sch 4, EN16931 preprocessed 3 and Peppol's CEN copy 3 (ends-with(name(), 'Amount' / 'BinaryObject'), true with or without the cbc: prefix), RO 1+3+1+1+7, ZATCA 2+1. Re-run set for milestone 4: dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings (44 pins), cen_examples_pass_the_en16931_rules, cen_rules_catch_mutated_invoices, peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules, zatca_samples_pass_the_zatca_rules, ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings; any moved pin is read before it is re-pinned.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_5 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 5u32, "2026-10-31T00:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:09 fiscal: LAND PROGRAMS BUILT and rehearsed on fresh copies of the live lib. C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\delphi\\delphi-arms.kit (4 files, 13 hunks) gives sm' 8113E287, unicode F3E7BE24, xml D540BC09, date_time 468359D2, each hash-equal to its draft. C:\\home\\data\\fiscal-drafts\\xml-fidelity\\xml-xpath-fidelity.kit (2 files, 8 hunks; bases xml 58CA22E1, xpath_eval 3BCD928E = live) applies cleanly ON TOP of the Delphi program: xpath_eval CC078F4B (= draft), and the combined xml.spi is D20A5A18. Both drafts change xml.spi from the same base, so D20A5A18 (Delphi + fidelity) is the file that would actually land, and it has not been gated yet: before landing both, gate xml.spi D20A5A18 as a whole module (rust, zig, delphi rows), plus round trip and formatter.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_6 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 6u32, "2026-10-31T00:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:10 fiscal: HASH UPDATE (supersedes D540BC09 / D20A5A18 above). The formatter re-lays delphi_sequence_width (one line over 120 columns) as a two-line body; adopted, so the Delphi xml draft is E8614181 (layout only; the code-points proof ran on D540BC09). Programs rebuilt and re-rehearsed on fresh live copies: delphi-arms.kit -> xml E8614181 (= draft); then xml-xpath-fidelity.kit -> xml E8F8E8F3, xpath_eval CC078F4B. The combined xml E8F8E8F3 shows only the formatter diffs live already has (2), and its round trip on the pre-relayout combination was true. The full-module gate before landing runs on E8F8E8F3.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_7 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 7u32, "2026-10-31T00:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 20:50 fiscal: r2 GREEN (fiscal-box4-fidelity-r2, pack 8): xpath_eval 12/12 (gate 7CE0A3C7 = draft CC078F4B with header 1800000), incl name_of_an_attribute_is_its_xml_name and its new prefixed-element, namespace-uri and mapped-attribute asserts; xml 12/12 (gate 6BFF1CB7 = 3300361F + header), so its earlier 3 reds were cap VOIDs. The xml run's Cells compile probably fell inside main's tree-write window 5, so treat it as provisional; the combined xml E8F8E8F3 gets its own full gate before the land anyway. Milestone 4 (six regional tests on boxgate = live + both fidelity drafts) is running as fiscal-box-fidelity-m4. 40 -> 70.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_8 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 8u32, "2026-10-31T02:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-30 22:11 fiscal: MILESTONE 4 PARTIAL (fiscal-box-fidelity-m4; boxgate = live lib + xml 3300361F + xpath_eval CC078F4B; fiscal corpus_checks 1F0376FB; pack 8): dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings PASSES (all 44 pinned counts unchanged), cen_examples_pass_the_en16931_rules, cen_rules_catch_mutated_invoices and peppol_examples_pass_the_peppol_rules PASS. So the name()/attribute fix and numeric character references move no pinned finding in DIAN, CEN or Peppol. zatca and ro_cius are still running.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_9 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 9u32, "2026-10-31T12:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 08:25 fiscal: MILESTONE 4 COMPLETE (read from fiscal-box-fidelity-m4's raw rows in boxgate\\\\raw, which the 22:11 note left running): zatca_samples_pass_the_zatca_rules PASSED (rust, 3,566,439 ms, headroom 0.99: inside the cap but close, so a slower box would VOID it) and ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings PASSED (611,504 ms). With the four from the 22:11 note, all six regional tests (DIAN 44 pins, CEN examples, CEN mutations, Peppol, ZATCA, RO) are unchanged on live + xml 3300361F + xpath_eval CC078F4B, so the numeric-reference decode and the attribute name() fix move no pinned finding. Remaining: the combined xml BA1B4166 (Delphi arms + fidelity) and xpath_eval CC078F4B full-module gates (running in fiscal-box9-delphi-modules, after sm' 73/73 and unicode 9/9), then the land after the Delphi program.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_10 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 10u32, "2026-10-31T16:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 12:15 fiscal: the combined xml (fidelity + Delphi arms, re-anchored on today's live: 52B745FA) passes its whole module 14/14 on the box (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH n79); xpath_eval CC078F4B's full gate is running. Then the land: delphi-arms.kit, then xml-xpath-fidelity.kit, both in fiscal/lib-programs.")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_11 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 11u32, "2026-10-31T17:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 13:00 fiscal: xpath_eval FULL MODULE GREEN: CC078F4B + gate header (53EF96CB) passes 12/12, 0 type errors (fiscal-cr-docs-4-4, box, compiler EEBCBFF8, scratch root g18 = today's live + the re-anchored candidates). With xml 52B745FA 14/14 (n10), both files of xml-xpath-fidelity.kit are proven on today's live; the land goes after delphi-arms.kit (xml's target includes both programs), once fiscal-delphi4-reanchored passes sm', unicode, file_system (date_time already 43/44, 0 failed).")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_12 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 12u32, "2026-10-31T20:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 16:46 fiscal: land program moved here from fiscal/lib-programs (a folder I invented; programs live in backlog notes so land-lib-program.ps1 -Note can read them): XML fidelity for xml + xpath_eval (applies after the Delphi program).\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit xml.spi\r\npatch <<<\r\n@@ -77,14 +77,6 @@\r\n \r\n := is_name_end (c : string) : bool = is_space c || c = \"/\" || c = \">\" || c = \"=\"\r\n \r\n-:= decode_entities (text : string) : string =\r\n-    text\r\n-    |> sm'.replace \"&lt;\" \"<\"\r\n-    |> sm'.replace \"&gt;\" \">\"\r\n-    |> sm'.replace \"&quot;\" \"\\\"\"\r\n-    |> sm'.replace \"&apos;\" \"'\"\r\n-    |> sm'.replace \"&amp;\" \"&\"\r\n-\r\n :~ ^ skip_spaces (s : string) (pos : i32) : i32 =\r\n     ? pos < sm'.length s && is_space (at s pos) ?> skip_spaces s (pos + 1i32) |: pos\r\n \r\n@@ -99,6 +91,48 @@\r\n             := found = sm'.substring pos (sm'.length s - pos) s |> sm'.index_of needle\r\n             ? found < 0i32 ?> -1i32 |: pos + found\r\n \r\n+:= hex_digit (c : string) : i32 =\r\n+    := lower = sm'.index_of c \"0123456789abcdef\"\r\n+    ? lower >= 0i32 ?> lower\r\n+    |:\r\n+        := upper = sm'.index_of c \"ABCDEF\"\r\n+        ? upper >= 0i32 ?> upper + 10i32 |: -1i32\r\n+\r\n+:~ ^ reference_value (digits : string) (base : i32) (i : i32) (acc : i32) : i32 =\r\n+    ? i >= sm'.length digits ?> acc\r\n+    |:\r\n+        := d = hex_digit (sm'.substring i 1i32 digits)\r\n+        ? d < 0i32 || d >= base || acc > 1114111i32 ?> -1i32 |: reference_value digits base (i + 1i32) (acc * base + d)\r\n+\r\n+:~ ^ numeric_references_from (text : string) (pos : i32) (acc : string) : string =\r\n+    := start = find_from \"&#\" text pos\r\n+    ? start < 0i32\r\n+    ?> acc ++# sm'.substring pos (sm'.length text - pos) text\r\n+    |:\r\n+        := before = acc ++# sm'.substring pos (start - pos) text\r\n+        := semi = find_from \";\" text start\r\n+        ? semi < 0i32\r\n+        ?> before ++# sm'.substring start (sm'.length text - start) text\r\n+        |:\r\n+            := body = sm'.substring (start + 2i32) (semi - start - 2i32) text\r\n+            := hex =\r\n+                sm'.length body > 1i32 && (sm'.substring 0i32 1i32 body = \"x\" || sm'.substring 0i32 1i32 body = \"X\")\r\n+            := digits = ? hex ?> sm'.substring 1i32 (sm'.length body - 1i32) body |: body\r\n+            := value = ? sm'.length digits = 0i32 ?> -1i32 |: reference_value digits (? hex ?> 16i32 |: 10i32) 0i32 0i32\r\n+            ? value < 0i32 || value > 1114111i32 ?> numeric_references_from text (start + 2i32) (before ++# \"&#\")\r\n+            |: numeric_references_from text (semi + 1i32) (before ++# code_point_string (conv value))\r\n+\r\n+:= decode_numeric_references (text : string) : string = numeric_references_from text 0i32 \"\"\r\n+\r\n+:= decode_entities (text : string) : string =\r\n+    text\r\n+    |> sm'.replace \"&lt;\" \"<\"\r\n+    |> sm'.replace \"&gt;\" \">\"\r\n+    |> sm'.replace \"&quot;\" \"\\\"\"\r\n+    |> sm'.replace \"&apos;\" \"'\"\r\n+    |> decode_numeric_references\r\n+    |> sm'.replace \"&amp;\" \"&\"\r\n+\r\n :~ ^ reverse_nodes (rest : list xml_node) (acc : list xml_node) : list xml_node =\r\n     ?= rest ?|\r\n     | x :: xs => reverse_nodes xs (x :: acc)\r\n@@ -587,3 +621,20 @@ test white_space_and_fixed_attributes_follow_the_xsd_rules =\r\n     ? collapsed_space \" \\n\\t \" <> \"\" ?> failwith \"only spaces collapse to nothing\"\r\n     ? listm.length (checked_fixed \"Version\" \"4.0\" [(\"Version\", \"4.0\")]) <> 1i32 ?> failwith \"the fixed value reads\"\r\n     ? listm.length (checked_fixed \"Version\" \"4.0\" []) <> 0i32 ?> failwith \"an absent fixed attribute stays absent\"\r\n+\r\n+///> rust\r\n+test numeric_character_references_decode =\r\n+    := delimiter = code_point_string 127u32\r\n+    ? decode_entities \"&#x7f;04&#127;\" <> delimiter ++# \"04\" ++# delimiter\r\n+    ?> failwith \"hex and decimal references decode\"\r\n+    ? decode_entities \"caf&#233;\" <> \"caf\" ++# code_point_string 233u32\r\n+    ?> failwith \"a decimal reference becomes its code point\"\r\n+    ? decode_entities \"&amp;#x41;\" <> \"&#x41;\" ?> failwith \"an escaped ampersand stays a literal reference\"\r\n+    ? decode_entities \"&#xZZ; &#; &#12\" <> \"&#xZZ; &#; &#12\" ?> failwith \"malformed references stay as written\"\r\n+    ?= read_xml \"<a k=\\\"&#x7f;05&#x7f;\\\">x&#62;y</a>\" ?|\r\n+    | XmlElement (_, attributes, children) :: [] =>\r\n+        ?= attribute_of \"k\" attributes ?|\r\n+        | Some v => ? v <> delimiter ++# \"05\" ++# delimiter ?> failwith \"attribute values decode references\"\r\n+        | None => failwith \"the attribute reads\"\r\n+        ? text_in children <> \"x>y\" ?> failwith \"text decodes references\"\r\n+    | _ => failwith \"one element\"\r\n>>>\r\nedit xpath_eval.spi\r\npatch <<<\r\n@@ -25,7 +25,16 @@\r\n \r\n := attribute_node (name : string) (value : string) : xml_node = XmlElement (\"@\" ++# name, [], XmlText value :: [])\r\n \r\n-:= is_attribute (node : xml_node) : bool = sm'.starts_with \"@\" (node_name node)\r\n+:= written_name (node : xml_node) : string =\r\n+    ?= node ?|\r\n+    | XmlElement (name, _, _) => name\r\n+    | XmlText _ => \"\"\r\n+\r\n+:= is_attribute (node : xml_node) : bool = sm'.starts_with \"@\" (written_name node)\r\n+\r\n+:= qualified_name (node : xml_node) : string =\r\n+    := name = written_name node\r\n+    ? is_attribute node ?> sm'.substring 1i32 (sm'.length name - 1i32) name |: name\r\n \r\n :~ ^ reversed_digits (text : string) (pos : i32) (acc : list i32) : option (list i32) =\r\n     ? pos >= sm'.length text ?> Some acc\r\n@@ -177,8 +186,8 @@\r\n \r\n := name_matches (test : string) (node : xml_node) : bool =\r\n     ?= node ?|\r\n-    | XmlElement (name, _, _) =>\r\n-        := own = ? is_attribute node ?> sm'.substring 1i32 (sm'.length name - 1i32) name |: name\r\n+    | XmlElement _ =>\r\n+        := own = qualified_name node\r\n         ? is_prefix_wildcard test ?> name_prefix own = name_prefix test\r\n         |: test = \"*\" || local_name test = local_name own\r\n     | XmlText _ => !-\r\n@@ -201,10 +210,14 @@\r\n \r\n := name_matches_in (namespaces : list (string * string)) (test : string) (item : located) : bool =\r\n     ?= item.node ?|\r\n-    | XmlElement (name, _, _) ?& is_attribute item.node = !- && name_prefix test <> \"\" =>\r\n+    | XmlElement _ ?& name_prefix test <> \"\" =>\r\n         ?= mapped_namespace (name_prefix test) namespaces ?|\r\n         | Some uri =>\r\n-            := own = in_scope_namespace (namespace_key (name_prefix name)) (item.node :: item.ancestors)\r\n+            := name = qualified_name item.node\r\n+            := prefix = name_prefix name\r\n+            := own =\r\n+                ? is_attribute item.node && prefix = \"\" ?> \"\"\r\n+                |: in_scope_namespace (namespace_key prefix) (item.node :: item.ancestors)\r\n             own = uri && (is_prefix_wildcard test || local_name test = local_name name)\r\n         | None => name_matches test item.node\r\n     | _ => name_matches test item.node\r\n@@ -1155,15 +1168,17 @@\r\n :& :~ node_name_value (local : bool) (first : xvalue) : xvalue =\r\n     ?= first ?|\r\n     | VNodes ((item :: _)) =>\r\n-        := full = node_name item.node\r\n+        := full = qualified_name item.node\r\n         VText (? local ?> local_name full |: full)\r\n     | _ => VText \"\"\r\n :& :~ namespace_uri_value (first : xvalue) : xvalue =\r\n     ?= first ?|\r\n     | VNodes ((item :: _)) =>\r\n         ?= item.node ?|\r\n-        | XmlElement (name, _, _) ?& is_attribute item.node = !- =>\r\n-            VText (in_scope_namespace (namespace_key (name_prefix name)) (item.node :: item.ancestors))\r\n+        | XmlElement _ =>\r\n+            := prefix = name_prefix (qualified_name item.node)\r\n+            ? is_attribute item.node && prefix = \"\" ?> VText \"\"\r\n+            |: VText (in_scope_namespace (namespace_key prefix) (item.node :: item.ancestors))\r\n         | _ => VText \"\"\r\n     | _ => VText \"\"\r\n :& :~ substring_value (arguments : list xvalue) : xvalue =\r\n@@ -1513,3 +1528,25 @@ test a_predicate_error_reaches_the_caller =\r\n         ? effective_boolean (value \"count(a[@n = '2']) = 1\") = !- ?> failwith \"boolean predicates still filter\"\r\n         ? effective_boolean (value \"count(a[2]) = 1\") = !- ?> failwith \"positional predicates still filter\"\r\n     | _ => failwith \"one document\"\r\n+\r\n+///> rust\r\n+test name_of_an_attribute_is_its_xml_name =\r\n+    ?= read_xml \"<doc xmlns:x=\\\"urn:x\\\"><a n=\\\"1\\\" x:k=\\\"2\\\"/><x:b/></doc>\" ?|\r\n+    | document :: [] =>\r\n+        := top = { node = document; ancestors = ((document_root document).node :: []); path = (0i32 :: []) }\r\n+        := holds_in namespaces rule =\r\n+            effective_boolean (evaluate_in namespaces \"\" document top (lift_code_lists (parse rule)))\r\n+        := holds rule = holds_in [] rule\r\n+        := mapped = (\"y\", \"urn:x\") :: []\r\n+        ? holds \"name(a/@n) = 'n'\" = !- ?> failwith \"name() of an attribute has no @\"\r\n+        ? holds \"local-name(a/@n) = 'n'\" = !- ?> failwith \"local-name() of an attribute has no @\"\r\n+        ? holds \"name(a/@x:k) = 'x:k'\" = !- ?> failwith \"a prefixed attribute keeps its prefix in name()\"\r\n+        ? holds \"local-name(a/@x:k) = 'k'\" = !- ?> failwith \"local-name() drops the prefix\"\r\n+        ? holds \"name(x:b) = 'x:b'\" = !- ?> failwith \"a prefixed element keeps its prefix in name()\"\r\n+        ? holds \"local-name(x:b) = 'b'\" = !- ?> failwith \"local-name() of a prefixed element drops the prefix\"\r\n+        ? holds \"namespace-uri(a/@x:k) = 'urn:x'\" = !- ?> failwith \"a prefixed attribute is in its prefix's namespace\"\r\n+        ? holds \"namespace-uri(a/@n) = ''\" = !- ?> failwith \"an unprefixed attribute is in no namespace\"\r\n+        ? holds_in mapped \"count(a/@y:k) = 1\" = !- ?> failwith \"a mapped prefix reaches an attribute by URI\"\r\n+        ? holds_in mapped \"count(a/@y:n) = 0\" = !- ?> failwith \"a mapped prefix never matches an unprefixed attribute\"\r\n+        ? holds \"name(a) = 'a'\" = !- ?> failwith \"element names are unchanged\"\r\n+    | _ => failwith \"one document\"\r\n>>>")
inl note_of_xml_xpath_fidelity_13 () = Note ("XML-XPATH-FIDELITY", 13u32, "2026-10-31T23:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 19:50 fiscal: CLOSING. LANDED 19:49:22 (after the Delphi program): xml 52B745FA (numeric character references decode + Delphi arms) and xpath_eval CC078F4B (attribute name()/local-name() and namespace matching by the written name), each equal to its proven target; whole modules 14/14 and 12/12 on the box; the six regional pins (DIAN, CEN x2, Peppol, ZATCA, RO) unchanged under the fidelity drafts (n9); round trip canonical + fixpoint.")
inl matrix_ub_exit_unpinned () = Task ("MATRIX-UB-EXIT-UNPINNED", "dynamic_array_bounds_negative's unchecked backends read out of bounds (UB): the C exit is garbage and the accepted oracle pinned one value, so the row flaps NATIVE-DIFF", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,matrix,oracle,determinism", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_matrix_ub_exit_unpinned () = Planning ("MATRIX-UB-EXIT-UNPINNED", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_matrix_ub_exit_unpinned_1 () = Note ("MATRIX-UB-EXIT-UNPINNED", 1u32, "2026-10-30T22:18Z", "compiler", "10-30 18:18 compiler: filed from PACK-8 n13 (no existing item; only CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE notes mention the sample). samples/dynamic_array_bounds_negative [C] reads an array out of bounds UNCHECKED (C, Delphi, Wasm, Kotlin, Lua and WGSL rows all do; their Known entries say 'reads 0'). The read is undefined behaviour: on the identical residual 8264f723636f74f1 and the identical gcc 15.2 binary, the C exit was 0 in the pack-7 run, 1,869,570,931 in the PACK-8 review and 1,547,322,173 in the accept, which stored that garbage into EXPECTED 3D3409C9. So the row's baseline column flaps NATIVE-DIFF run to run; main and compiler agreed to treat it as noise meanwhile, and every pre-registered reader today carries a special case for it. Fix options (pick in the next pack): (a) matrix: a Known-entry field such as Native = 'unchecked' that skips the exit/stdout comparison for that row in test.ps1's baseline and oracle code; (b) fixture: give the unchecked backends a defined outcome (e.g. a guard sample variant) so the exit is pinned. Owner: compiler team. Done when two consecutive -Suite all -Native runs show no NATIVE-DIFF on the row without any reader exception.")
inl note_of_matrix_ub_exit_unpinned_2 () = Note ("MATRIX-UB-EXIT-UNPINNED", 2u32, "2026-10-30T23:05Z", "compiler", "10-30 19:05 compiler: option (a) DRAFTED, not landed: C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\apply-matrix-unpinned-exit.ps1, 3 anchored edits over 2 files. matrix.psd1 gains an oracle-independent `UnpinnedExit` table (Known entries are scoped per oracle, but the baseline exit comparison isn't) holding only the C row, the one backend observed to flap. test.ps1 builds $unpinnedExit from it (empty when the table is absent), and the baseline `nativeMatch` accepts a listed row whenever it ran. Checks on scratch copies: all anchors 1x on live; patched test.ps1 parses; the patched matrix loads exactly as test.ps1 loads it (Import-PowerShellDataFile -SkipLimitCheck), with 1 UnpinnedExit entry and Known unchanged at 22; the selector matches the C row and not the Rust row. LAND RULE: same as TEST-TOOLCHAIN-GUARD (shared harness; land through a window after TRAIN5 publishes). Done rule unchanged: two consecutive -Suite all -Native runs with no NATIVE-DIFF on the row and no reader exceptions.")
inl note_of_matrix_ub_exit_unpinned_3 () = Note ("MATRIX-UB-EXIT-UNPINNED", 3u32, "2026-10-31T12:59Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 08:59 compiler: FIXED AT THE SOURCE (option b), so the drafted matrix exception (option a, C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\apply-matrix-unpinned-exit.ps1) is NOT landed and is obsolete. The sample returned the out-of-bounds value as its exit code. samples/dynamic_array_bounds_negative/main.spi now keeps the read but compares it with a sentinel (? index xs i =. 1234567i32 ?> 1i32 |: 0i32; the slim samples core spells equality =.), so the partial evaluator still emits the read on every backend, checked backends still trap, and unchecked ones exit a defined 0. Result (gcc 15.2 and FPC 3.3.1 pinned): Zig 3, Rust 1, Bend 3, Lean 3 (trap as the fixture intends); C, Delphi, Wasm, Wgsl, Kotlin, Lua 0. Accepted the sample's 10 rows (-Filter, run single-flight-20261031-084558; baseline 7,386 rows unchanged in count; C row now 97d22986b02be1a1 exit 0, was 8264f723 exit 1,547,322,173). DONE RULE: two consecutive -Suite all -Native runs filtered to the row after the accept (085111, 085436): 10/10 parity, DISAGREE 0, exit 0, no NATIVE-DIFF and no reader exception. matrix.psd1's 5 Known reasons 'reads 0' -> 'the read misses the sentinel, exit 0' (loads, Known count unchanged). The sample's 11 outputs are rewritten (uncommitted). Readers can drop their special case for this row.")
inl pack_9 () = Task ("PACK-9", "Compiler pack 9: --batch/related-diagnostics package-closure fix (host only, empty predicted residual set), plus later candidates; predicted-set review like PACK-7/8", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,pack,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_pack_9 () = Planning ("PACK-9", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_pack_9_1 () = Note ("PACK-9", 1u32, "2026-10-30T23:45Z", "compiler", "10-30 19:45 compiler: opened as the collector for the next compiler pack, review method as PACK-7/8 (predicted residual set from paired compile-only runs, a pre-registered reader, box review, main installs, compiler -Accept). READY CONTENT (gated): (1) apps/compiler/packs/apply-host-related-diagnostics-closure.ps1 (CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS n27-n28): host only, so the predicted residual set P is EMPTY. Its own gate passed on Zig contracts (foreign TypeErrors blocks 226 -> 4, all 4 legitimate closure members; 0 rows differ in compile/residual/oracle/baseline). Review rule to pre-register: -Suite all -Native with SPIRAL_CC/SPIRAL_FPC pinned; 0 residual changes; any negative whose oracle verdict changes (a pin that passed only through leaked text) is listed, re-pinned on its own first error and explained, never accepted blind. CANDIDATES not yet ready: the hopacsota P3 BackendSwitch-validation lever (HOPACSOTA-P3 n52-n53, decision entry not yet written); formatter rewrapComments stays (by the user's Q5 decision). NOT pack content (harness scripts that land through windows after TRAIN5): TEST-TOOLCHAIN-GUARD, MATRIX-UB-EXIT-UNPINNED. Diagnostic appliers that stay in packs/ as records, in no pack: hopacsota worklist-trace, bridge-trace, bridge-split, wait-log, wait-keys, control-workers (NOT ADOPTED), hashcons-striped (NOT ADOPTED), host-batch-foreign-entry-diagnostics (superseded).")
inl note_of_pack_9_2 () = Note ("PACK-9", 2u32, "2026-10-31T00:29Z", "compiler", "10-30 20:29 compiler: predicted-set measurement RUNNING (box job job-1793403942556-compiler-pack9-predict, script C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\pack9-predict.ps1): paired compile-only -Suite all runs, installed vs crd2 (the closure fix), residual hashes compared row by row. Expected P = empty (host only). The box is at 100% from other lanes, so many small rows hit the 20 s compile timeout and --batch workers restart (34 worker files at 54% of the first arm), and it will finish after 21:00. The script excludes rows with a timeout on either side from P and lists them separately for a rerun alone. READ: kit job tail job-1793403942556-compiler-pack9-predict 30; the set is written to C:\\home\\data\\backlog-census\\pack9-predicted-set.txt. Pass condition for pre-registering the review: P = 0 rows and 0 non-timeout compile-status differences.")
inl note_of_pack_9_3 () = Note ("PACK-9", 3u32, "2026-10-31T00:46Z", "compiler", "10-30 20:46 compiler: the predicted-set job TIMED OUT at its 1 h cap (my cap was too tight for a box at 100%, per memory job-timeout-counts-queue-wait). The installed arm completed: run single-flight-20261030-194555, 7,385 rows, 32 load timeouts, compile phase 3,030 s. The crd2 arm was killed mid-run, so no P yet. Checked afterwards: 0 empty sample outputs were left in the tree (no restore needed). REDO: the same script with a 3 h cap, ideally when the box is below ~60%. Only the crd2 arm needs rerunning; the script would need a small change to reuse run single-flight-20261030-194555 as the installed arm.")
inl note_of_pack_9_4 () = Note ("PACK-9", 4u32, "2026-10-31T00:47Z", "compiler", "10-30 20:47 compiler: REDO started: job-1793407641444-compiler-pack9-predict2 (3 h cap). pack9-predict.ps1 now takes -InstalledRun, reusing the finished installed arm single-flight-20261030-194555, and runs only the crd2 arm. Read with kit job tail job-1793407641444-compiler-pack9-predict2 30; the pass condition for pre-registering the PACK-9 review stays P = 0 and 0 non-timeout status differences.")
inl note_of_pack_9_5 () = Note ("PACK-9", 5u32, "2026-10-31T04:20Z", "compiler", "10-31 00:20 compiler: the PACK-9 predicted-set run job-1793407641444 is VOID: it hit its 3 h cap (exit 124) at about 5,000 of 7,385 crd2 rows. Cause: pack9-predict.ps1 set itself BelowNormal, and from about 22:30 the box sat at 100% from normal-priority work, so the test workers starved (the same script took a 6 s compile past 120 s; memory below-normal-starves-on-saturated-box). Its timeouts are starvation, not crd2 results. Fixed: the BelowNormal line is removed from the script, and a -ReuseCompile switch replays every compile the crd2 DLL already stored in compile-memo, so only the missing rows compile. Queued as job-1793420393064-compiler-pack9-predict3 (8 h cap including the wait), after job-1793412988469-compiler-guard-predict. Pass line unchanged: P empty and 0 non-timeout status diffs.")
inl note_of_pack_9_6 () = Note ("PACK-9", 6u32, "2026-10-31T04:51Z", "compiler", "10-31 00:51 compiler: PACK 9 = crd2 (apply-host-related-diagnostics-closure.ps1, CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS) + manifest-model (manifest-model\\apply-core.ps1 + apply-host.ps1, EDITION3-MANIFEST-MODEL, the user's request tonight). Stack checked on scratch copies of the live tree: every anchor 1x; pair-drift on the combined core 0 one-sided pairs. SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD is NOT in pack 9: its EMacro edit sits on PartEval's single-flight side only, and pair-drift refuses that ('PartEval changed only on the single-flight side'); it needs a gpt5parallel side first. One edit to main's pack: apply-host.ps1's parameter got [Alias('HostSource')], so build-candidate.ps1 can pass it (no behaviour change). Jobs: job-1793422084299-compiler-pack9-build (heavy, building now in slot 2), then job-1793422087891-compiler-pack9-predict (installed run reused; pass = residual set P empty and 0 non-timeout status diffs). Then the review proper (re-read every pinned negative whose detail loses a foreign block, per CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS n29) and main's install. apply-cells.ps1 lands on the Cells tree separately after the install; samples/manifest_derived_order joins samples/ after the install too.")
inl note_of_pack_9_7 () = Note ("PACK-9", 7u32, "2026-10-31T05:13Z", "compiler", "10-31 01:13 compiler: pack 9 candidate BUILT (job-1793422084299, 543 s): core 4AB4E03E921BD3C3, host 51E332E6621912DE. Consumer-path smoke on main's regression sample (manifest-model\\sample\\manifest_derived_order, spiral.toml with prelude = [\"helpers\"] and NO modules key), compiled to C from a scratch copy: installed compiler -> exit 5 'PackageErrors ... spiral.toml'; pack 9 -> exit 0 with main.c written. The predicted-set run job-1793422087891 is running (Normal priority, installed arm reused).")
inl note_of_pack_9_8 () = Note ("PACK-9", 8u32, "2026-10-31T05:37Z", "compiler", "10-31 01:37 compiler: PREDICTED-SET GATE MET. job-1793422087891 (pack9-predict.ps1 -Candidate pack9, Normal priority, compiled in 1,503.6 s): residual set P = 0, compile-status diffs 0, baseline-verdict diffs 0; pack-9 arm 7,397 rows with 0 timeouts (7,385 parity + 12 new). The 32 timeouts of the reused installed arm are all parity on pack 9 (24 ok, 8 error). Review rule for pinned negatives: every ExpectedErrors row is parity, so no pin depended on leaked foreign text. The 12 new rows: frontier_hopacsota_deferred_validation_mismatch (error, matching its ExpectedErrors pin; stays) and backend_switch_missing_arm_negative + backend_switch_validated_gap. The last two are the missing-arm guard's samples, which pack 9 doesn't contain, so they compile ok here. Parked under apps/compiler/packs/missing-arm-guard/sample with their matrix line (matrix-expected-error.txt), so the accept doesn't record them as ok. Handed to main for install (message 01:3x).")
inl note_of_pack_9_9 () = Note ("PACK-9", 9u32, "2026-10-31T05:42Z", "main", "10-31 01:42 main: INSTALL QUEUED. Dry run of install-pack.ps1 -Name pack9 (core manifest-model\\apply-core.ps1; host apply-host-related-diagnostics-closure.ps1 then manifest-model\\apply-host.ps1): today's live core 4191A77FB3D3A335 and host 286E35EF0C9BFB34 plus the appliers reproduce the reviewed candidate's sources exactly (core 4585FC131BC34C80, host 57F3152B25E561E0). It refuses only on IN USE: compiler's lib-gate-dll seq.spi and kit's train5e. Installing mid-train would change the compiler under kit's release run, so packs/install-when-clear.ps1 (new, in the repo) waits until no running kit job has 'train' in its label AND the dry run passes, then takes an exclusive compiler-install window and runs -Apply (backup to C:\\home\\data\\compiler-installs). After the install: core DLL must equal the candidate's (4AB4E03E921BD3C3); smoke a few samples in place with both DLLs; then apply-cells.ps1 on Cells and copy samples/manifest_derived_order (manifest-model).")
inl note_of_pack_9_10 () = Note ("PACK-9", 10u32, "2026-10-31T11:36Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 07:35 compiler: SUBSUMED by PACK-10 (groom): pack 10 contains all of pack 9, and its delta over pack 9 is P = 0 (PACK-10 n2). Proposed to main: install PACK-10 once and close both. If main prefers pack 9 alone first, its own gate (n9) still holds.")
inl note_of_pack_9_11 () = Note ("PACK-9", 11u32, "2026-10-31T19:04Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 14:59 compiler: INSTALLED as part of PACK-10 (main verified 14:30; PACK-10 n3).")
inl lib_notebook_headings_cleanup () = Task ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", "lib/spiral: drop the notebook-era headings. Remove the '/// ### name' lines that only repeat the next definition's name (1,816 of 2,125) and the .spir mirror headings that head no code (206 of 222; sm'_real.spir alone 191 of 204), after re-keying Cells' spi+spir interleave so it no longer needs them (user request, 2026-10-30 after 21:07)", Story, P1, D4, 95u32, Done, "LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", "lib,cells,cleanup,livemd,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup () = Planning ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_1 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 1u32, "2026-10-31T01:28Z", "main", "10-30 21:28 main, census and plan (user: the _real files followed the old pattern of exporting the single sm.dib's markdown cells; the function-name headings lost their purpose since docs and the polyglot interactive notebooks are no longer used). CENSUS, lib/spiral (114 .spi/.spir files, bench and build excluded): 2,125 '/// ###' headings, 1,816 of them exactly the next definition's name; 213 '/// #' and '/// ##' module and section headings; 82 '///' prose lines in .spi and 0 in .spir. The 4 .spir files hold 222 headings, 206 heading NO code (sm'_real 191/204, cli_args_real 12/13, json_real 2/3, routes_real 1/2): they exist only because the interleave rule requires each .spir to mirror every .spi heading. WHY they are load-bearing today: Document.parse_spi(spi, spir) -> Domain.from_spi interleaves real-mode cells by heading (SPIR-INTERLEAVED-LIVEMD, done 10-12, so the Livebook view of sm' matched the old notebook), and document_test asserts the spi -> livemd -> spi round trip. PLAN: (1) Cells first: pair .spir cells with their .spi definitions by name, or stop interleaving (livemd export is being retired, NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE); update document_test to the new format; one Cells window. (2) A generic, idempotent remover (a kit command or a lib script, not a one-off) that drops a '/// ### X' line only when the next non-blank line defines X, drops .spir headings with no code under them, and leaves '///>' target lines and '///-' cell options alone. (3) Land in lib windows by file batches; each batch closes with kit's signatures, the round trip of the NEW canonical form, type_probe and document_test. (4) DECIDE in step 1 from SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES (files organized by sections): keep '/// ##' sections; drop the '/// #' module titles that only repeat the file name; review the 309 non-name '###' headings one by one. Then the same for consumer repos (alphabet, dice, tibia, fiscal, x, kit), each by its own team.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_2 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 2u32, "2026-10-31T01:29Z", "main", "10-30 21:29 main, step 1 READ (apps/cells/spi/document.spi): (a) interleave (:861) walks the .spir cells; a .spir markdown cell must equal a later .spi markdown cell (:871), and non-matching .spi cells are passed over (:872). So the FORWARD direction (spi+spir -> livemd) never needed the empty mirror headings: a .spir needs a heading only where it has real code. (b) The empty mirrors come from the REVERSE direction (livemd -> to_spi_tested), which writes every heading into both files, and document_test's round trip then demands them. Fix: emit a heading into the .spir only when a real-mode cell follows it before the next heading. (c) name_tested (:827) derives a test cell's default name from the last heading (heading_test_name, :306); when the derived name differs from the test block's own name it inserts a '#### name (test)' markdown cell. Dropping '### name' headings therefore only changes the livemd rendering (more '#### name (test)' cells), not .spi test names, because test blocks carry explicit names. (d) spir_cell (:107) keys real-mode cells on the '///- ... --real' option line, so the '///- --real' lines must stay. Step 1 = (b) in the reverse writer, re-run document_test on all 114 files, and add the edge case of a .spir with no heading at all.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_3 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 3u32, "2026-10-31T02:10Z", "main", "10-30 22:10 main, STEP 1 PROVEN on a scratch spiral tree (apps/cells + lib/spiral copies, deps junction): headings-cleanup\\apply-cells.ps1 (document.spi: drop_bare_docs + export_docs, so to_spir keeps a markdown cell only when its own code follows before the next heading; document_test's pair fixture updated to the new form). canon-pairs.exs regenerated the 4 .spir files through spi+spir -> livemd -> spi/spir: every .spi is unchanged and every .spir is a fixpoint; sm'_real.spir 1,282 -> 900 lines, cli_args_real 96 -> 72, json_real 129 -> 125, routes_real 35 -> 33. document_test :432 (pair round trip over all 4 lib pairs plus the fixture) and :493 (every lib .spi loads as a notebook, blocks >= 370): 2 passed. LAND = ONE combined window (Cells document.spi + document_test.exs, and the 4 canonical .spir in lib), because document_test spans both trees; queued with the other proven Cells drafts (apply6 epic line, apply7 retire-stop) for one Cells window plus a lib window. Steps 2-4 (the '### name' remover over the .spi files) follow.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_4 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 4u32, "2026-10-31T07:17Z", "main", "10-31 03:17 main, STEP 2 BUILT: apps/cells/spi/drop_name_headings.exs <spiral dir> <out dir> [files] (generic; consumer repos run the same command). Drops '/// ### X' when the next non-blank line defines X (after the sigil token :=/:!/:~/:==/:|/:?/:+ or 'test', and an optional '^'; markdown-escaped backslashes unescaped) or when nothing follows it; drops the blank line it leaves; skips nested packages (spiral.toml/package.spiproj, e.g. bench/parsing) and .spi files paired with a _real.spir (the interleave matches headings across both files: sm'/cli_args/json/routes wait for NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE or a re-key). Writes the canonical form and accepts a file only if non-blank lines are unchanged and the result is a fixpoint. DRY RUN over lib/spiral: 110 .spi, removed 1,601, failed 0; second pass over its own output removes 0 and is byte-identical. Readers of '/// ###' outside Cells: none (grep of compiler fork, kit, scripts). Scratch proof of document_test :449 (pairs) and :494 (every .spi loads, blocks >= 370; fewer headings merge cells) running (bttk1748l). Outputs: %TEMP%\\headings-step2\\out. Land plan: batches by file, files touched by queued lands (process, erlang_process, base, seq, listm') regenerated after those land.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_5 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 5u32, "2026-10-31T08:22Z", "main", "10-31 04:22 main, STEP 2 PROVEN + STEP 3 QUEUED. The tool also checks Document.tests names before/after (unchanged in all 106 edited files: test names come from test blocks, not headings). Scratch A/A of document_test :494 (every lib .spi loads, one test cell per test block, blocks >= 370): A original PASS, B edited PASS; :432 red on BOTH sides from a stale generated domain.gleam (CELLS-DOMAIN-DIGEST-STALENESS, fixed live 03:39), not from the edit. Pending drafts anchored on '/// ###' lib lines: none outside sm'.spi (paired, untouched); the rescued compiler packs anchor on F# '    /// ###'. LAND SET: 53 files, 1,341 headings (am'_prototypes.spi left out: blank-only canonicalization; process/erlang_process/base/seq/listm' held for their queued lands, regenerate after). 3 lib_land_window batches with per-file base hashes, chained after the lambda-parens land (bcpzy2cat), stop on the first red. Outputs %TEMP%\\headings-step2\\out, set in land-set.json.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_6 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 6u32, "2026-10-31T08:48Z", "main", "10-31 04:48 main, STEP 4 DATA (on the step-2 outputs, 106 files). (a) '/// #' module titles: 56, 55 equal the file stem, the 56th (rust/testing.spi 'rust/testing') is the relative path: all repeat the file name -> DECIDED drop; drop_name_headings.exs now also drops '/// # <stem or relative path>' (dry run on the step-2 outputs running, brjgxljuh; second land wave after the 3 batches). (b) 106 non-name '###' headings left, classified: 42 name-is-part-of-def (backend-switch helpers grouped under the public name: slice' -> slice'_switch, await -> await_send), 25 overload labels (iter_collect vec, (~:>) any), 33 other single words (mostly section-like: equable over append), 4 over another heading/doc line, 2 multiword with real notes (iggy rd_str_utf8 payload note). These carry information: proposed rule = group labels become '/// ##' sections (kept per plan), real notes become plain comments beside the code, the rest reviewed by file. Paired files (sm'/cli_args/json/routes) wait for the interleave decision.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_7 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 7u32, "2026-10-31T08:51Z", "main", "10-31 04:51 main, module-title rule dry run over the 106 step-2 outputs: removed 56 (one per file), failed 0 (content, fixpoint and test names kept). WAVE 2 PLAN: after the 3 batches and the held lands (pg, lambda-parens, debris) finish, rerun drop_name_headings.exs on the LIVE lib (idempotent) and land the whole remaining diff (module titles + the 5 held files' name headings) with fresh base hashes.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_8 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 8u32, "2026-10-31T11:03Z", "main", "10-31 07:03 main, BATCH 1 LANDED green 06:43: 18 files, 467 name headings (am', async, backend, benchmark, channel, cli_flags, common, console, conversation, convert, crypto, csv, cursor_walk, date_time, env, erlang_port, erlang_term, file_system; every live file equals its draft; undo lib-land-undo\\20261031-063330). BATCHES 2 and 3 CLOSED RED and auto-undid: each had exactly ONE type_probe failure (17/18 and 16/17); signatures and document_test were green. A comment-only edit should not change types, so the likely cause is a file already red on the live lib: A/A type_probe of batches 2-3 on the unedited live files running (b0svnawyb). If the same files fail on live, land the batches without them (and file their reds); if not, the edit is at fault in that file.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_9 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 9u32, "2026-10-31T11:14Z", "main", "10-31 07:14 main, A/A ANSWER: batches 2-3's single reds are PRE-EXISTING on the live lib (near_wallet.spi 4 and reflection.spi 6 ETY-UnionCaseAmbiguous errors; filed LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS). Requeued batch 2 (17 files, without near_wallet) and batch 3 (16, without reflection) after the running queue, followed by lambda wave 2 (13 files, without reflection). The two files' headings land after their reds are fixed.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_10 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 10u32, "2026-10-31T12:13Z", "main", "10-31 08:13 main, STEP 4 DECIDED (technical call, per the user's point that names above code lost their purpose): drop_name_headings.exs also drops a single-word '/// ### X' whose next definition is named X_... (the group/switch-helper heading: slice' over slice'_switch, await over await_send). Dry run on the module-title outputs: 32 more removed in 23 files, 0 failed (content, fixpoint, test names kept). KEPT for now: multiword overload labels (iter_collect vec, (~:>) any), prose notes (iggy rd_str_utf8), and the 10 prefix cases without '_' (array -> array'). FINAL WAVE: after batches 2-3 (queued) and LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS land, rerun the tool on the live lib once and land the whole remainder (name headings of the held files + module titles + prefix rule).")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_11 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 11u32, "2026-10-31T12:38Z", "main", "10-31 08:38 main: Cells window 6 (carries this item's step 1) gained apply9: '@tag timeout: 900_000' on document_test's 'the spiral library .spi files load as notebooks' test, which hit ExUnit's 60 s default 3 times on 10-31 under load (any lane running document_test saw a false red). Window 6 is stopped from its 07:04 wait (it would have timed out at 11:04 behind kit's train6) and requeued (b7jnac6rj): it starts after land-queue-0820 exits and no train job runs; kit asked to leave a gap after train6.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_12 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 12u32, "2026-10-31T13:19Z", "main", "10-31 09:19 main: BATCH 2 LANDED green 08:51 (17 files: float_native, guid, iggy, iter, leptos/leptos, lustre, mapm, math, networking, oauth, optionm', otp_actor, otp_supervisor, par', parsing, physics, platform; undo lib-land-undo\\20261031-082918) and BATCH 3 LANDED green 09:06 (16 files: reactors.spi, resultm.spi, rust/clap.spi, rust/near_workspaces.spi, rust/near.spi, rust/rust.spi, rust/testing.spi, step_runtime.spi, stream.spi, testing.spi, threading.spi, trace.spi, unicode.spi, util.spi, wasm.spi, xml.spi; undo lib-land-undo\\20261031-085137). Every live file equals its draft. Batches 1-3: 51 files. LEFT for the final wave (after LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS and the sm' lambda land, both queued): reflection.spi and near_wallet.spi name headings, the 5 earlier-held files (process, erlang_process, base, seq, listm'), the 56 module titles and the 32 prefix-rule headings, all from one tool run on the live lib.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_13 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 13u32, "2026-10-31T14:08Z", "main", "10-31 10:08 main: FINAL WAVE queued (land-queue-1010, 3 batches + Cells window 6 as the last step so the two never overlap). One drop_name_headings.exs run over a copy of the live lib (plus reflection.spi's re-merged lambda edit): 110 .spi, removed 363 more, failed 0 (content, fixpoint, test names kept): the 5 earlier-held files' and reflection/near_wallet's name headings, the 56 module titles, and the 32 prefix-rule headings. 56 files (am'_prototypes.spi left out again: blank-only). Batches 19/19/18 files, 139/72/152 headings. Window 6 waits for no train (hold cells-window-6 until 18:06) and releases the hold when done.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_14 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 14u32, "2026-10-31T15:07Z", "main", "10-31 11:07 main: the PAIRED files are no longer skipped. drop_name_headings.exs now reads a .spi's _real.spir, keeps every .spi heading whose exact line also appears in the .spir (the interleave pairs those), drops the rest by the same rules, and accepts the file only if the spi+spir round trip leaves the .spir byte-identical (plus content, fixpoint and test names, read with the .spir). Sanity run on today's live pairs: sm' 0 removed (200 .spir headings kept), cli_args 0 (13), json 0 (3), routes 0 (2), .spir unchanged in all 4, failed 0: today every .spir still mirrors every .spi heading. After Cells window 6 lands (its canonical .spir keep a heading only where real code follows: sm'_real.spir 1,282 -> 900 lines), rerun the tool on the live lib: most of sm'.spi's 195 headings become removable. Then land that as the last wave and close this item (the 106 labelled overload/prose headings stay by decision).")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_15 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 15u32, "2026-10-31T15:18Z", "main", "10-31 11:18 main: FINAL WAVE LANDED green: 1/3 at 10:27 (19 files, 139 headings; undo lib-land-undo\\20261031-101227), 2/3 at 10:53 (19, 72; ...-103313), 3/3 at 11:06 (18, 152; ...-105322). All 56 live files equal their drafts. Totals on lib/spiral today: 1,341 (batches 1-3, by 09:06) + 363 = 1,704 headings removed in 107 files (name headings, module titles, prefix-rule group headings). LEFT: (a) the 4 paired files (sm', cli_args, json, routes) after Cells window 6 lands (the window is the queue's last step, waiting for kit's train6); (b) consumer repos (alphabet, dice, tibia, fiscal, x, kit): each team runs the same command on its own Spiral sources.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_16 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 16u32, "2026-10-31T15:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-10-31 11:21 fiscal: fiscal's own sources checked: fiscal/src (corpus_checks, corpus, fiscal_paths, generator, lifecycle) has 0 '///' lines, so drop_name_headings has nothing to drop there; generated/ units are generator output (headings come from xsd_emit, already cleaned in lib).")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_17 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 17u32, "2026-10-31T15:29Z", "main", "10-31 11:29 main: live lib is at the tool's FIXPOINT (rerun over all 110 .spi, paired files included: removed 0, failed 0). CONSUMERS, main's share DONE (unstaged): dice contract/dice_contract.spi -7 headings, alphabet apps/documents/documents.spi -1, dice lib/dice.spi already clean; Cells document_test 22/22 with them (it reads both repos and checks their byte-for-byte write-back). kit, x, fiscal and tibia were sent the command for their own sources.")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_18 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 18u32, "2026-10-31T17:34Z", "main", "10-31 13:27 main: STEP 1 LANDED with Cells window 6: document.spi's .spir export keeps a heading only where its own code follows (drop_bare_docs), the 4 lib .spir are in their new canonical form (sm'_real.spir FB2680503D46 etc.), and document_test's 'library .spi files load' test has a 15-min timeout tag. NEXT: the paired-file pass (sm', cli_args, json, routes) on the live lib, after the F# retire lands (they touch sm'.spi).")
inl note_of_lib_notebook_headings_cleanup_19 () = Note ("LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP", 19u32, "2026-10-31T18:13Z", "main", "10-31 14:13 main: PAIRED FILES LANDED green 14:03 (sm' 174, cli_args 11, json 2, routes 1 = 188 headings; .spir byte-identical; undo lib-land-undo\\20261031-135448; cli_args 00551F373A6A, json 1BB05E862F48, routes 6D36AF342DF8). lib/spiral is DONE: ~1,892 notebook-era headings removed on 10-31; the 106 labelled overload/prose headings stay by decision. Left: consumer repos (main's dice/alphabet done; kit, x, fiscal, tibia have the command).")
