inl planning_of_lib_process_test_debris () = Planning ("LIB-PROCESS-TEST-DEBRIS", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_process_test_debris_1 () = Note ("LIB-PROCESS-TEST-DEBRIS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T02:48Z", "main", "10-30 22:48 main (user asked what the log files in lib/spiral were): process-started-{quick,slow,directory}.log were test debris from 3 process.spi tests (a_started_program_logs_and_reports_its_exit, a_running_program_is_killed_by_its_pid, a_program_runs_in_its_directory). They called start_logging with relative log names, so they wrote into the test's cwd (lib/spiral in a 10-29 06:19 run), and the directory test also wrote a marker into the cwd's parent. The 3 untracked files were removed (0-7 bytes). FIX DRAFTED: process-test-logs\\apply.ps1 (3 anchors): logs go to an absolute path under file_system.get_temp_path (), and the directory test runs in the temp dir. type_probe: 15 tests typed, 0 errors. Gate run FROM INSIDE the scratch lib dir: debris in lib dir 0 and in its parent 0 (the purpose is proven). Test VERDICTS VOID: 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s' on an overloaded box (rows took 396 s to 35 min). NEXT: on a quiet box, gate the 3 tests on base and on edit (both Rust and Gleam), then land in a lib window.")
inl note_of_lib_process_test_debris_2 () = Note ("LIB-PROCESS-TEST-DEBRIS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T04:48Z", "main", "10-31 00:48 main: PROVEN on the node (job-1793421472339, at Normal priority; the box runs were load-starved). Each arm was gated from INSIDE its lib dir. BASE: 3/3 tests pass on Rust and Gleam and leave 3 debris files in the lib dir (the positive control: the debris check sees the bug). EDIT (apply.ps1): 3/3 pass and leave 0. The node mirror's process.spi equals live (DE4A46A670FB). The debris came back in the live lib at 00:17-00:19 from another lane's run, and was removed again. LANDING now with the new repo tool apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 (draft rebuilt from live, base pinned).")
inl note_of_lib_process_test_debris_3 () = Note ("LIB-PROCESS-TEST-DEBRIS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T11:57Z", "main", "10-31 07:57 main, LANDED green 07:04 through lib_land_queue (retry; the first attempt gave up at 04:10 after 180 min behind kit's train, which read the live lib): process.spi -> 54452C34E854 (undo lib-land-undo\\20261031-070142). Close: 14 signatures unchanged, document_test 22/22, type_probe PASS. Node proof: base 3 debris files, edit 0.")
inl kit_agile_lost_updates () = Task ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", "agile writers must never overwrite another lane's write: set rolled back whole-file and no swap checked the file was unchanged since read (fiscal lost two Done states on 10-30)", TaskKind, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "KIT-TRAIN7", "kit,agile,correctness,data-loss", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_agile_lost_updates () = Planning ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_1 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 1u32, "2026-10-31T03:38Z", "kit", "10-30 23:4x kit: filed from fiscal's two reports (XPATH-PREDICATE-ERRORS reverted around 19:39, FISCAL-GR-MYDATA around 23:05; both went from Done back to an older Active, and fiscal re-set both). Found in kit: (1) agile set (agile_state_runtime/state_terminal.spi) wrote with no compare-and-swap, and when post-write validation failed (readback or attestation, which a concurrent write can trigger) it 'rolled back' by writing the WHOLE file it had read at the start, restoring stale records over other lanes' writes. begin and the series append had the same rollback. (2) agile edit, add, planning-field writes, roots and migration swap via replace_file_checked without checking the file is unchanged since read; note, note-edit, rename, record and title-notes already do (state_written). FIXED in kit/src (unstaged; kit_agile_state regenerated in place, cargo check passed): set re-reads before writing and refuses ('changed since it was read; nothing written, run the call again'); every rollback restores only if the file still holds exactly its own write, otherwise it reports and keeps the other write. LEFT: route edit/add/planning/roots/migration through the same compare-before-swap (state_written), and a Done-to-open guard (set refuses to reopen a Done item without --reopen) so a script replaying stale values cannot revert a closure. The attribution of fiscal's two incidents is not proven; the whole-file rollback is the only kit path found that writes an older copy. Ships in the train after TRAIN5c.")
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_2 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 2u32, "2026-10-31T04:31Z", "kit", "11-01 00:3x kit: the LEFT parts are done (unstaged, regenerated in place, cargo check passed). (1) edit, add, planning-field writes, roots and migration now swap through agile_task_text.replace_records_unchanged. It asks kit_agile_records' new export kit_agile_records_unchanged(path, original), which re-reads the file, normalizes it like records_text, and compares with the writer's normalized original; on a mismatch nothing is written (new file_replacement case ChangedSinceRead: 'the file changed since it was read; nothing written, run the call again'). The check lives in the records crate because inlining it pushed agile_task_creation to 1007 lines (crate gate stop in TRAIN5d); now 990. (2) Reopen guard: set refuses to move a Done item back to an open status unless KIT_AGILE_REOPEN=1, so a script replaying stale values cannot revert a closure (both of fiscal's incidents were Done -> Active). An env var instead of a flag, because set's arguments are parsed upstream in kit_agile_mutation (831 lines) and the help crates. Ships in TRAIN5e (queued 00:30, snapshot, -SkipRegen after in-place regens).")
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_3 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 3u32, "2026-10-31T07:48Z", "kit", "10-31 03:3x kit groom: Active -> Blocked. The only remaining step is installed-is-done: TRAIN5e (job-1793421047190, snapshot 00:31) carries this change, and KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES's last part ships in the train after it. Unblock and verify once kit.exe is installed. Moved so that 'agile next --team kit' stops ranking an install wait above actionable work (43 kit items were Active).")
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_4 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 4u32, "2026-10-31T12:12Z", "kit", "10-31 07:4x kit: TRAIN5e installed (E14F1F0B). The replace_records_unchanged follow-up (edit/add/planning/roots/migration) landed around 00:3x, at the edge of the 00:31 snapshot, so it is NOT counted as shipped. Stays Blocked on the next train; acceptance = two concurrent writers, the second refused with 'changed since read'.")
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_5 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 5u32, "2026-11-01T12:44Z", "kit", "11-01 08:5x kit (Blocked rule, main 08:5x: the blocker must be named). blocked by: EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN (the TRAIN7 install; the replace_records_unchanged follow-up missed TRAIN5e's snapshot). Unblocks when TRAIN7 is installed; acceptance = the two-writer race test on the installed binary.")
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_6 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 6u32, "2026-11-01T13:17Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit: blocked by: KIT-TRAIN7 (the TRAIN7 install, now its own closable item split from EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN).")
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_7 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 7u32, "2026-11-01T19:27Z", "kit", "11-01 15:27 kit ACCEPTANCE on the INSTALLED TRAIN7 binary (kit.exe A25B8FBD, installed 15:24): two-writer race on a fresh backlog under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\accept-train7. 10 rounds in parallel (ThrottleLimit 10), each round 'agile set RACE-A <5i> Active' plus 'agile note RACE-B round i'. Result: 0 refusals, 0 lost writes. RACE-B has all 10 notes, RACE-A ends Active at progress 50, and agile check ok (build_attested=2). The live store's round-5 data agrees (KIT-SCALE n6: 45 writes, contiguous byte chain). DONE.")
inl note_of_kit_agile_lost_updates_8 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T04:20Z", "main", "11-04 00:2x main, from the star exchange: under one simultaneous groom (7 lanes, 00:10-00:25) the optimistic check rejected writes for every lane (\"state/agile.spi changed since it was read; nothing written\"). main lost 3 of 36 sets; compiler, tibia and x-dumps also hit it, and x-dumps retried up to 8 times per operation. Every rejection succeeded on an identical rerun, so no update was lost (the guard works) but turns were. Asks: (1) note/set retry the conflict themselves, re-reading and re-applying, up to N times; (2) the real fix is EOIE-AGILE-EVENT-LOG (append-only events merge by union, so they never conflict). The same window took the box to 100% CPU; kit agile wip took 152 s against 1.3 s for list. Owner: kit.")
inl cells_domain_digest_staleness () = Task ("CELLS-DOMAIN-DIGEST-STALENESS", "Cells spiral_domain compiler: decide domain.gleam staleness by an inputs digest (sources + compiler DLL identity), not mtimes", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,build,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_domain_digest_staleness () = Planning ("CELLS-DOMAIN-DIGEST-STALENESS", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_domain_digest_staleness_1 () = Note ("CELLS-DOMAIN-DIGEST-STALENESS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T08:13Z", "main", "10-31 04:13 main. TRAP (10-30 23:28 -> 10-31 03:39): a failed Cells window regenerated the shared, git-ignored src/spiral_cells/domain.gleam from its edited document.spi, then restored document.spi with Copy-Item, which keeps the old 10-29 mtime; spi/domain_compiler.ex stale? compares mtimes only, so live Cells ran the reverted edit (drop_bare_docs) and document_test's pair fixture went red. Every queued lib land closes with document_test, so all would have undone themselves. Found by an A/A scratch run (same red on unedited lib). FIXED LIVE 03:39 (touch document.spi + mix compile under a tree-write window, domain.gleam 53976A6B1CB7 -> EFC9CE38DA22; fixture :432 green). Tools: lib_land_window.ps1 Copy-Retry and cells-window6.ps1 restores now set LastWriteTime. ROOT FIX drafted on the scratch tree %TEMP%\\headings-scratch\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\spi\\domain_compiler.ex: sha256 over sorted spi/*.spi + package.spiproj contents and the compiler DLL path/size/mtime, stamped in build/spiral_domain.inputs (git-ignored), regenerate when output missing or digest differs; also catches compiler installs, which mtimes never did. Proof steps 1-2 green (regenerates the stale copy to EFC9CE38DA22; no-op on no change); steps 3-4 (edit, then old-mtime restore must regenerate) running (b8ix6jwdt).")
inl note_of_cells_domain_digest_staleness_2 () = Note ("CELLS-DOMAIN-DIGEST-STALENESS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T08:42Z", "main", "10-31 04:42 main, LANDED live apps/cells/spi/domain_compiler.ex 1F4AE942D15A -> 9FA1A52ABA63 (undo %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\domain-digest-20261031-042544). Scratch proof all green: (1) no stamp regenerates the stale copy, (2) no change is a no-op, (3) content edit regenerates, (4) edit then Copy-Item restore with the old 10-29 mtime REGENERATES (the trap; mtime logic never did), fixture :432 passed. Live: compile 1 regenerated + stamp written, fixture :432 passed. Live compile 2 also regenerated, but main's window 6 overlapped (it edited document.spi at 04:12 and compiled concurrently): the no-op check is repeated on the live tree after window 6 ends.")
inl note_of_cells_domain_digest_staleness_3 () = Note ("CELLS-DOMAIN-DIGEST-STALENESS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T09:25Z", "main", "10-31 05:25 main, DONE. Live no-change compiles kept regenerating: the stamp ping-ponged (8153.. -> E37B.. -> 25BA..) because lanes compile Cells with different SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL values or spellings, and the digest included the compiler path/size/mtime. For a generated file SHARED by every lane that makes each lane's compile regenerate (~80 s) and race. FINAL: the digest covers source contents only (spi/*.spi + package.spiproj), domain_compiler.ex 730499FEFF4F; compile 1 regenerated once (digest format change), compile 2 regenerated=False, stamp stable 39E0DB15AB00, domain.gleam EFC9CE38DA22, fixture :432 passed. Compiler installs invalidate explicitly: apps/compiler/packs/install-pack.ps1 removes apps/cells/build/spiral_domain.inputs after a successful install. Processes that loaded the old module before 05:3x may write one old-format stamp until they exit (one extra regeneration each, same output).")
inl pack_10 () = Task ("PACK-10", "Compiler pack 10: gpt5parallel retired (core 190k -> 36k lines, host collapsed) + missing-arm guard, stacked on pack 9", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "PACK-9,GPT5PARALLEL-RETIRE,SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD", "compiler,pack,hopacsota,cleanup", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_pack_10 () = Planning ("PACK-10", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_pack_10_1 () = Note ("PACK-10", 1u32, "2026-10-31T08:58Z", "compiler", "10-31 04:58 compiler: composition = pack 9 (manifest-model core+host, crd2 host) + packs/apply-retire-gpt5parallel.ps1 (core and host) + packs/apply-missing-arm-guard.ps1 (single-flight half). Stack checked on scratch copies (every step applied; hopacsota projection unchanged 85AD38718D544B11; core 190,175 -> 35,579 lines; host 1,420 -> 1,395). Jobs: job-1793437028349-compiler-pack10-build, then job-1793437031950-compiler-pack10-predict against pack 9's own run (single-flight-20261031-010020), so P measures only what pack 10 adds (expected P = 0, status diffs 0). At install: re-create the guard's samples (SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD n10) and its ExpectedErrors line, then the step-2 script/doc cleanup (GPT5PARALLEL-RETIRE n5). Mutual tail loops are NOT in it: they change Rust residuals and get their own review.")
inl note_of_pack_10_2 () = Note ("PACK-10", 2u32, "2026-10-31T11:32Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 07:32 compiler: PREDICTED-SET GATE MET. Candidate built (job-1793437028349, 942 s): SpiralCompiler.dll 7827E9406813BB24, SpiralCompilerCore.dll D1C49B8BDC3318F7 at C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack10\\cache\\bin\\single-flight\\SpiralCompiler\\Release\\net11.0. Build warnings identical to pack 9's (1 FS0026, 5 FS0046, 1 FS0760, every line shifted by the same -150,767), so the retirement adds none. Predict job-1793437031950 against pack 9's own run single-flight-20261031-010020: residual set P = 0, compile-status diffs 0, baseline-verdict diffs 0, 0 timeouts; run single-flight-20261031-051310 has 7,389 rows. The 8 missing rows are exactly backend_switch_missing_arm_negative and backend_switch_validated_gap x {Fsharp,C,Rust,Delphi}, the guard samples archived until install. Pack 9 is still NOT installed (installed core 17DDB2DCEF2A2D52 = pack 8), and pack 10 contains all of pack 9, so ONE install of pack 10 covers both (pack 9's own gate met at n9). Handed to main for install with that proposal.")
inl note_of_pack_10_3 () = Note ("PACK-10", 3u32, "2026-10-31T11:37Z", "main", "10-31 07:37 main: install queued. Dry run reproduces the reviewed candidate from today's live source (live core 4191A77FB3D3A335 host 286E35EF0C9BFB34 -> appliers core 5B4655EC4BF5990B host 19C0215F2E8C594F = candidate source). The pack-9 waiter is replaced: this install covers pack 9. install-when-clear (600 min) waits for no running train job (kit train5e holds heavy-build ~228 min more) and for the installed compiler to be free (3 erl.exe use it now), then installs under a compiler-install window. install-pack.ps1 also removes the Cells domain stamp, so domain.gleam regenerates with the new compiler. After the install, main checks that the installed DLLs equal the candidate (SpiralCompiler 7827E9406813BB24, Core D1C49B8BDC3318F7) and tells compiler to start its follow-ups.")
inl note_of_pack_10_4 () = Note ("PACK-10", 4u32, "2026-10-31T18:25Z", "main", "10-31 14:25 main: install still WAITING (install-when-clear pid 27880, 600-min cap from 07:37). Train6 ended 12:57; since then the dry run refuses only because the installed compiler is in use: at 14:24 by fiscal's job-1793460946299-fiscal-cr-docs-4-4 (docs.ps1 -> gate.ps1 -> lib_gate.ps1 -> erl), which starts gate after gate; the waiter rechecks every 2 min and installs in the first gap. The train hold pack10-install blocks kit's train6 resume (kit-r6-holds-then-resume), which gives up at about 16:57. RULE: if pack 10 has not installed by 16:15, main releases the hold so kit can resume, and requeues the install for the next gap between trains. The verifier (main scratchpad pack10-verify.ps1) runs right after the waiter exits.")
inl note_of_pack_10_5 () = Note ("PACK-10", 5u32, "2026-10-31T18:31Z", "main", "10-31 14:31 main: INSTALLED and VERIFIED 14:27-14:30 (covers pack 9). Installed SpiralCompiler.dll 7827E9406813BB24 and SpiralCompilerCore.dll D1C49B8BDC3318F7 = the reviewed candidate; system dotnet launches it; --capabilities includes resolve-manifest; Cells domain stamp removed (domain.gleam regenerates on the next mix compile). Undo: spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack10-20261031-142743. The waiter found a gap between fiscal's gates at 14:27. Train hold pack10-install RELEASED (kit's train6 resume can go); compiler told to start its follow-ups.")
inl note_of_pack_10_6 () = Note ("PACK-10", 6u32, "2026-10-31T18:59Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 14:59 compiler: INSTALLED and VERIFIED (main, 14:27-14:30): installed SpiralCompiler.dll 7827E9406813BB24 and SpiralCompilerCore.dll D1C49B8BDC3318F7, equal to the reviewed candidate; the live core and host are byte-identical to the candidate's sources (5b4655ec4bf5990b / 19c0215f2e8c594f). FOLLOW-UPS DONE: (1) GPT5PARALLEL-RETIRE step 2 applied (55 edits, 15 files); (2) the guard's samples backend_switch_missing_arm_negative + backend_switch_validated_gap restored byte-exact from the 10-31 archive, plus its ExpectedErrors line; (3) main's samples/manifest_derived_order added (7 files, spiral.toml with a derived module order); all 12 rows accepted (baseline 7,386 -> 7,398) after a run where the negative errors with the guard's text on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi, validated_gap compiles on all 4 (Rust/Delphi agree with C), manifest_derived_order exits 50 on all 4; the confirming run is 12/12 parity, DISAGREE 0. (4) Installed appliers archived (apply-retire-gpt5parallel, apply-missing-arm-guard, apply-host-related-diagnostics-closure, apply-retire-gpt5parallel-tooling) with scripts/pair-drift.ps1, its tmp/scripts stub and lanes/gpt5parallel: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-145532. Covers PACK-9.")
inl claude_hooks_in_repo () = Task ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", "Claude Code hooks live in i574n.github (claude/hooks), settings.json points at the repo copy: reviewable in git diff, survive a profile wipe", Story, P2, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:main,hooks,heal,workflow", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_claude_hooks_in_repo () = Planning ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_1 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 1u32, "2026-10-31T10:36Z", "kit", "2026-10-31 06:4x kit (filed during the user's 'fix hooks, memories' heal; hooks are main's, so main decides): the five Claude Code hooks (autonomous-gate, kit-tree-lease, kit-style-check, kit-work-in-repo, plus settings.json's wiring) live only in ~/.claude/hooks, outside any repo. The 10-28 profile wipe destroyed them and they were rebuilt from evidence (kit-hooks memory). Tonight alone they changed 5 times (gate wake-source text, the new work-in-repo hook, its string-form timeout that blocked a Write, style-check's $\" probe, lease narrowing by the regen), and each change was reviewable only through .bak files. Proposal: i574n.github/claude/hooks/*.ps1 becomes the single copy, and settings.json points at the repo paths directly (no install copy, so no second record to drift; work-in-the-repo memory). Every change then shows up in git diff for the user's review, and a wipe loses nothing that is committed. tree-lease-hook-test.ps1 already lives in i574n.github/scripts. Done = settings.json commands name repo paths, ~/.claude/hooks holds only archive/, and every hook's pipe test passes from the repo path.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_2 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 2u32, "2026-10-31T15:03Z", "main", "10-31 11:03 main: DECISION NEEDED FROM THE USER (batched into main's 18:00 report). The move only works as a whole: copy the five hooks to i574n.github/claude/hooks AND point ~/.claude/settings.json's hook commands at the repo paths. Changing settings.json is persistent configuration of the user's Claude Code setup, so main doesn't do it unasked; copying the hooks without repointing would create a second, drifting copy (worse than today). Ready to do in ~15 min on a yes: copy, repoint, run each hook once (gate dry run, tree-lease test, style-check probe), keep the old ~/.claude/hooks copies as .bak until the user commits.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_3 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:33Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: Agent moves the hooks: copy ~/.claude/hooks/*.ps1 to i574n.github/claude/hooks (unstaged), back up settings.json to settings.json.bak-<stamp>, rewrite only the hook paths, then run every hook's pipe test from the repo path. KEEP iff all pass and a live PowerShell call succeeds; otherwise restore the .bak at once. Exception: the kit-tree-lease entry's command/onFailure shape is NOT changed, because the harness says that one is the user's. BACKUP/UNDO: settings.json.bak-<stamp>; the old hook files stay in ~/.claude/hooks. OWNER: kit.")
inl note_of_claude_hooks_in_repo_4 () = Note ("CLAUDE-HOOKS-IN-REPO", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. From resilience n5: the fleet-wide hook block (this lane's PowerShell was blocked twice on 11-02) comes from Claude Code not finding Git Bash. A scoop-only git is not at the standard path, so the hook runner times out and the tree-lease hook defaults to block. The fix is the env var CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH pointing at scoop's bash.exe, not a hook rewrite. That is resilience's/kit's settings step, with a settings.json.bak and the same keep/restore test as this item's record v2.")
inl lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds () = Task ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", "lib: qualify union cases the compiler now reports as ambiguous (ETY-UnionCaseAmbiguous) in reflection.spi and near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi tests", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,compiler,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds () = Planning ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds_1 () = Note ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T11:14Z", "main", "10-31 07:14 main. type_probe on the UNEDITED live lib (A/A for the heading-cleanup batches 2-3, which each closed red on exactly one file): reflection.spi FAIL 6 test errors (:105:41, :184:30, :215:25, :219:25, :244:25, :248:25 'The union case Wasm is defined by more than one opened module'), near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi FAIL 4 test errors (:63:36, :64:36 Incr; :65:36, :79:36 Decr). Fix: qualify the cases (module.Wasm etc.) or open one module; prove with type_probe + the files' lib_gate; land with lib_land_window. Until then lib_land_window closes red for any batch containing these files: heading batches 2-3 and lambda wave 2 are requeued without them (land-queue-0710). Also: iggy.spi came back VOID in that A/A (scratch copy missing type_probe_iggy.spi), PASS inside the land run: a scratch-copy flake, not a red.")
inl note_of_lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds_2 () = Note ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T11:59Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 07:59 compiler: ROOT CAUSE is the PROBE, not the lib. type_probe.ps1 types a file's tests in a generated module that repeats the file's opens (:< lustre), adds :< testing, and then OPENS the module itself (:< near.wallet.src.near_wallet). near_wallet's own msg = Incr | Decr and lustre.spi:113-114's Incr | Decr then arrive through two opens, and ETY-UnionCaseAmbiguous fires exactly as the user's 10-12 rule (QUALIFIED-UNION-CASES) wants. In the real file, the local union is a definition, so it shadows lustre's (inferTop BundleNominal -> AInclude replaces the term; markAmbiguousUnionCases runs only on BundleOpen, spiral_compiler.fs 51978). reflection.spi is the same with Wasm. The item's suggested fix CANNOT work: a module can't write near_wallet.Incr inside itself, and qualifying lustre.Incr would change what the test means. FIX (edited in place, apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1, uncommitted): when the module is openable, the probe COPIES the module's own lines (minus its :< opens, its test blocks and their ///> ///- directives) instead of :< module, so tests see the file's real scope; copied lines map back to file:line as kind 'module'. Smoke: reflection.spi PASS (10 tests typed), near_wallet.spi PASS (2 typed), control ok, 83 s. A/B over every lib file with both opens and tests (56 files; A = HEAD script, B = new) running as job-1793447920777-compiler-typeprobe-ab (outputs in my scratchpad probe-A.out / probe-B.out). Pass = the 2 reds flip to PASS and no other verdict or error set changes; then main requeues heading batches 2-3 and lambda wave 2 with these files.")
inl note_of_lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds_3 () = Note ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T12:25Z", "main", "10-31 08:25 main, PROVEN, land queued. Fix: reflection.spi's local test union reflection_test_target renames its case Wasm -> Browser (backend.spi:95 also defines Wasm; 11 lines incl. the case-insensitive lookup strings 'browser'/'Browser'); near_wallet.spi renames its counter cases Incr/Decr -> Increment/Decrement (lustre.spi:113, opened by :< lustre, defines the same names; no non-.spi file uses them). Box type_probe on a scratch lib: both PASS (10 + 2 tests typed, 0 errors). Node lib_gate with the drafts (job-1793447802349): reflection tests 10/10, near_wallet 2/2, type errors 0 (the unedited A runs hit a _build permission error on the mirror tree: environment, and the unedited files are known red). Canonical round trip ok. Queued in land-queue-0820 after heading batches 2-3 and lambda wave 2, bases 635E3884D05B / 09AF48CA55F7.")
inl note_of_lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds_4 () = Note ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", 4u32, "2026-10-31T13:30Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 09:30 compiler: A/B PASSED, DONE with NO lib edit. job-1793448079301-compiler-typeprobe-ab2 over every lib file that has both :< opens and test blocks (56 files): A (HEAD type_probe.ps1) pass 54 / fail 2; B (the in-place fix) pass 56 / fail 0. The only differences are near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi FAIL (2 typed, 4 errors) -> PASS (2 typed, 0) and reflection.spi FAIL (10 typed, 6 errors) -> PASS (10 typed, 0). Every other output line (verdicts, typed counts, lifted statics, shadow notes) is byte-identical across the arms. The fix stays uncommitted in apps/cells/spi/type_probe.ps1 (one block: copy the module's own lines instead of ':< module'; copied lines map back as kind 'module'). Main: lib_land_window can requeue heading batches 2-3 and lambda wave 2 WITH these two files.")
inl note_of_lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds_5 () = Note ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", 5u32, "2026-10-31T13:39Z", "main", "10-31 09:39 main: compiler found the root cause in type_probe.ps1 (it re-opened the module, so a locally defined case arrived through two opens) and fixed it; the lib rename is optional. DECIDED: keep the queued rename (land-queue-0820 step 4). It is proven (lib_gate 10/10 and 2/2 with the drafts), removing it would mean racing the running queue runner between steps, and a local test case named Wasm that also exists in backend.spi confuses readers as it confused the probe.")
inl note_of_lib_union_case_ambiguous_reds_6 () = Note ("LIB-UNION-CASE-AMBIGUOUS-REDS", 6u32, "2026-10-31T13:42Z", "main", "10-31 09:42 main: LANDED green 09:31 (land-queue-0820 step 4): reflection.spi 4F8834164282, near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi 5655B671772D (undo lib-land-undo\\20261031-092127).")
inl lib_xcompat_tibia_tests () = Task ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", "tibia's lib share, TEST cells: split the overweight test cells left in process.spi (9, incl. split_args 1383 and split_command 726) and threading.spi (1, new_disposable_token) into named fixtures plus short tests, as done for otp_actor, listm' and env (POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS n144-n146); each proven with i574n.github/scripts/lib-program-gate.ps1 (positive plus a negative through the fixture path) and kept as a kit do program in its note", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "-", "team:tibia,tibia,lib,postability,x-compat", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests () = Planning ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests_1 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T12:27Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 08:3x tibia: DRAFTED, both files; the gates are queued. Milestones: drafted 40, gated 80, recorded with programs 100.\nprocess.spi base 54452C34E854D974 -> 9A8D268C5188B40B, overweight 39 -> 30, all 9 test cells fit and no new fixture is over. Formatter clean, round trip ok. split_args and split_command keep one test each over fixture case lists joined with ++; every case and expected value is unchanged, and the path case moves to the end of the list. tests (1189) becomes reading_a_missing_file_fails and utf8_text_round_trips_in_a_working_directory, each in its own temp dir (hash tagged \"missing\" or \"utf8\") so they cannot collide if Cells runs them concurrently. tests_2 keeps its name over five_lines (). a_missing_or_failing_program_captures_nothing loses its stderr case to a new test, a_succeeding_program_captures_its_stderr. a_started_program_logs_and_reports_its_exit becomes a_started_program_reports_its_exit plus a_started_program_logs_its_output (started_log name gives the same log paths as before). a_running_program_is_killed_by_its_pid, a_spawned_command_reports_its_exit_code and a_program_runs_in_its_directory keep their names over fixtures. The orphaned \"/// #### tests\" heading is dropped, in line with LIB-NOTEBOOK-HEADINGS-CLEANUP. Negative: 9 mutations, one per fixture path (dry run ok).\nthreading.spi base 85DFC69608D22502 -> FF00AD96DB06343F, overweight 8 -> 7. new_disposable_token's local generic run becomes run_before_and_after_dispose, its counter count_by_cancellation, and its task disposal_count_task (). Negative: an uncancelled call adds 2, not 1 (12 <> 11).\nGate chain (box, serial test-suite windows, lib-program-gate.ps1, which now has -Control to run the same tests on the unchanged base first): (1) env diagnosis: POSTABLE n144-147's env slice was RED on 2 rows (remove_environment_variable/rust, try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset/lua; the other rows of both tests passed, and its negative caught all 7 mutated tests). It reruns the two tests alone with a control. (2) process with -Control (A/A for cuda, which fails on the box's Kepler GPUs). (3) threading.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests_2 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T13:44Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 09:4x tibia: GATE VERDICTS, round 1.\n(a) env tests (POSTABLE n144-147's env slice): PROVEN. Control on the unchanged base 7D334BD1: remove_environment_variable/rust and try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset/rust FAIL there too, so those reds predate the slice. The candidate rerun alone passes both on every row (the earlier lua red was load). The full run passed the other 7 tests; the negative caught all 7 mutated tests.\n(b) process: VOID, 2 type errors from a scoping rule. Test blocks see modules later in package.spiproj (crypto) and the \"test process static\" prelude opens (</>), but top-level fixtures do not. Fixed: probe_path uses file_system.(</>); probe_dir uses a fixed temp dir \"spiral-process-probe-<tag>\" instead of a crypto hash. Memory: lib-test-scope-vs-top-level. The control had also run 0 tests, because the new test names do not exist on the base; lib-program-gate -Control now passes only names present in the base file and reports NOT RUN separately from RED.\n(c) threading: DROPPED from this item. new_disposable_token's body needs async, which comes after threading in package order, so it cannot move to top-level fixtures (6 ETY-UnboundVariable). The cell stays as it is (676/263) until the module order or the test's placement changes.\nRe-gating now in one chain: process with the tests and defs programs together (with LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS part 1), and env with the tests and defs programs together (DEFS part 2), each with -Control and with both negatives concatenated.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests_3 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T14:49Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 10:4x tibia: PROCESS SLICE PROVEN (this item's process tests plus LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS part 1's 6 process_command_* builders, one program). process.spi base 54452C34E854D974 (still live) -> 83D7F96DC5830EF0, overweight 39 -> 24. Formatter clean, round trip ok.\nGate (box test-suite window, lib-program-gate.ps1 -Control): the control on the unchanged base ran the 7 tests whose names exist there and was RED on split_args/rust, split_command/rust and a_missing_or_failing_program_captures_nothing/gleam. The candidate is RED on exactly the same places: split_args/rust and split_command/rust, plus a_succeeding_program_captures_its_stderr/gleam, which is the stderr assertion moved out of a_missing_or_failing; that test now passes on gleam. Every other test passes; the cuda rows of split_args and split_command passed; 0 type errors. By the rule, every candidate red is red on the unchanged base. Negative (one mutation per fixture path plus current_dir ignoring its argument): 9 tests failed, 0 type errors: CAUGHT.\nPRE-EXISTING LIB REDS on the box, for their owners: split_args and split_command fail on rust, and process stderr capture fails on gleam (the python stderr case). Not caused by this slice.\nLAND: land-lib-program.ps1 -Note LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS/<this note> -File process.spi -Base 54452C34E854D974 -Target 83D7F96DC5830EF0\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit process.spi expect files 1 replacements 8\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_args =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    [\n        \"a b c\",\n        ;[ \"a\"; \"b\"; \"c\" ]\n\n        \"e f \\\"g h\\\" i\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"f\"; \"g h\"; \"i\" ]\n\n        \"\\\"j k\\\" \\\"l\\\" \\\"m\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"j k\"; \"l\"; \"m\" ]\n\n        \"s -t \\\"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"s\"; \"-t\"; \"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\" ]\n\n        \"n -o \\\"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"n\"; \"-o\"; \"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\" ]\n\n        \"r -s \\\"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"r\"; \"-s\"; \"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\" ]\n\n        $'\"x -y \\\\\\\"$z -a \\'(b=\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}\\', { \\`$_[1] + \\`$d++ }\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"x\"; \"-y\"; \"$z -a '(b=\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$d++ }\" ]\n\n        \"e -f \\\"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"-f\"; \"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\" ]\n\n        $'\"--l \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\'\\'\\' m \\'\\'\\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \"',\n        ;[ \"--l\"; \"''' m '''\" ]\n\n        $'\"n --o --p q --r \\\\\\\"s:/t u/v.w\\\\\\\" --x \\\\\\\"y:/z.a\\\\\\\" --b c.d \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\e{f-g}\\\\\\\" h.i \\\\\\\"j (k)\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[\n            \"n\"; \"--o\"; \"--p\"; \"q\"; \"--r\"; \"s:/t u/v.w\"; \"--x\"; \"y:/z.a\"; \"--b\"; \"c.d\"; \"\\\\e{f-g}\"; \"h.i\"; \"j (k)\"\n        ]\n\n        $'\"l \\\\\\\"m n:\\\\\\\\o.p\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"l\"; \"m n:\\\\o.p\" ]\n\n        $'\"--r s \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\' t \\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" u v w \\\\\\\\\\\\\"x y\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"--r\"; \"s\"; \"' t '\"; \"u\"; \"v\"; \"w\"; \"x y\" ]\n    ]\n    |> _assert_fn split_args\n  >>> with <<<\n:= split_args_plain_cases () =\n    [\n        \"a b c\",\n        ;[ \"a\"; \"b\"; \"c\" ]\n\n        \"e f \\\"g h\\\" i\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"f\"; \"g h\"; \"i\" ]\n\n        \"\\\"j k\\\" \\\"l\\\" \\\"m\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"j k\"; \"l\"; \"m\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_escaped_cases () =\n    [\n        \"s -t \\\"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"s\"; \"-t\"; \"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\" ]\n\n        \"n -o \\\"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"n\"; \"-o\"; \"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\" ]\n\n        \"r -s \\\"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"r\"; \"-s\"; \"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_regex_case () =\n    [\n        $'\"x -y \\\\\\\"$z -a \\'(b=\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}\\', { \\`$_[1] + \\`$d++ }\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"x\"; \"-y\"; \"$z -a '(b=\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$d++ }\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_backtick_regex_case () =\n    [\n        \"e -f \\\"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"-f\"; \"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_quote_cases () =\n    [\n        $'\"--l \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\'\\'\\' m \\'\\'\\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \"',\n        ;[ \"--l\"; \"''' m '''\" ]\n\n        $'\"l \\\\\\\"m n:\\\\\\\\o.p\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"l\"; \"m n:\\\\o.p\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_spaced_quote_case () =\n    [\n        $'\"--r s \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\' t \\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" u v w \\\\\\\\\\\\\"x y\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"--r\"; \"s\"; \"' t '\"; \"u\"; \"v\"; \"w\"; \"x y\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_path_input () =\n    $'\"n --o --p q --r \\\\\\\"s:/t u/v.w\\\\\\\" --x \\\\\\\"y:/z.a\\\\\\\" --b c.d \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\e{f-g}\\\\\\\" h.i \\\\\\\"j (k)\\\\\\\"\"'\n\n:= split_args_path_expected () =\n    ;[ \"n\"; \"--o\"; \"--p\"; \"q\"; \"--r\"; \"s:/t u/v.w\"; \"--x\"; \"y:/z.a\"; \"--b\"; \"c.d\"; \"\\\\e{f-g}\"; \"h.i\"; \"j (k)\" ]\n\n:= split_args_path_case () = [ split_args_path_input (), split_args_path_expected () ]\n\n:= split_args_cases () =\n    split_args_plain_cases () ++ split_args_escaped_cases () ++ split_args_regex_case ()\n    ++ split_args_backtick_regex_case () ++ split_args_quote_cases () ++ split_args_spaced_quote_case ()\n    ++ split_args_path_case ()\n\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_args =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    split_args_cases () |> _assert_fn split_args\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_command =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    [\n        \"\",\n        (\"\", None)\n\n        \"/a/b/c\",\n        (\"/a/b/c\", None)\n\n        \"d e.f\",\n        (\"d\", \"e.f\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\g.h i.j k.l\",\n        (\"../../g.h\", \"i.j k.l\" |> Some)\n\n        \"m:\\\\n\\\\o.p \\\"q.r s.t\\\"\",\n        (\"m:/n/o.p\", \"\\\"q.r s.t\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\u v\\\\w.x\\\" \\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\",\n        (\"../../u v/w.x\", \"\\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\" |> Some)\n\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\d e.f\\\" -g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../d e.f\", \"-g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\j k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../j\", \"k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n    ]\n    |> _assert_fn split_command\n  >>> with <<<\n:= split_command_unquoted_cases () =\n    [\n        \"\",\n        (\"\", None)\n\n        \"/a/b/c\",\n        (\"/a/b/c\", None)\n\n        \"d e.f\",\n        (\"d\", \"e.f\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\g.h i.j k.l\",\n        (\"../../g.h\", \"i.j k.l\" |> Some)\n    ]\n\n:= split_command_quoted_cases () =\n    [\n        \"m:\\\\n\\\\o.p \\\"q.r s.t\\\"\",\n        (\"m:/n/o.p\", \"\\\"q.r s.t\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\u v\\\\w.x\\\" \\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\",\n        (\"../../u v/w.x\", \"\\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\" |> Some)\n    ]\n\n:= split_command_escaped_cases () =\n    [\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\d e.f\\\" -g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../d e.f\", \"-g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\j k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../j\", \"k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n    ]\n\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_command =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    split_command_unquoted_cases () ++ split_command_quoted_cases () ++ split_command_escaped_cases ()\n    |> _assert_fn split_command\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n/// #### tests\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest tests =\n    := content = \"╭─[ 你好，世界！こんにちは世界！ ]─╮\"\n\n    := file_name = ~~ \"test.txt\"\n    := temp_dir, disposable =\n        #?*(file_name, content)\n        |> crypto.hash_text\n        |> file_system.create_temp_dir'\n    disposable |> use |> ignore\n    := path = temp_dir </> file_name |> file_system.normalize_path\n    := exit_code, result =\n        execute (\"pwsh -c \\\"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\" ++# path ++# \"')\\\"\")\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 1\n    result |> _assert sm'.contains \"not find file\"\n\n    content |> file_system.write_all_text path\n\n    := exit_code, output =\n        execution_options \\ x =>\n            { x ?|\n                command =\n                    (\n                        \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; \"\n                        ^^ \"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\"\n                    )\n                    ++# file_name\n                    ++# \"')\\\"\"\n                working_directory = Some temp_dir |> optionm'.box\n            }\n        |> execute_with_options\n\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 0i32\n    output |> _assert_eq content\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest tests_2 =\n    := exit_code, output =\n        execution_options \\ x =>\n            { x ?|\n                command =\n                    \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; for ($i = 0; $i \"\n                    ^^ \"-lt 5; $i++) { Write-Output `\\\"Line$i`\\\"; Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200 }\\\"\"\n            }\n        |> execute_with_options\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 0i32\n    output |> _assert sm'.contains \"Line4\"\n  >>> with <<<\n:= probe_text () : string = \"╭─[ 你好，世界！こんにちは世界！ ]─╮\"\n\n:= probe_dir (tag : string) = file_system.create_temp_dir' (\"spiral-process-probe-\" ++# tag)\n\n:= probe_path (temp_dir : string) : string = file_system.(</>) temp_dir (~~ \"test.txt\") |> file_system.normalize_path\n\n:= read_command (path : string) : string = \"pwsh -c \\\"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\" ++# path ++# \"')\\\"\"\n\n:= missing_file_read () : i32 * bool =\n    := temp_dir, disposable = probe_dir \"missing\"\n    disposable |> use |> ignore\n    := exit_code, result = execute (read_command (probe_path temp_dir))\n    exit_code, result |> sm'.contains \"not find file\"\n\n:= utf8_read_command () : string =\n    \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; \"\n    ^^ \"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\" ++# ~~ \"test.txt\" ++# \"')\\\"\"\n\n:= utf8_read_in (dir : string) : i32 * string =\n    execution_options \\ x =>\n        { x ?|\n            command = utf8_read_command ()\n            working_directory = Some dir |> optionm'.box\n        }\n    |> execute_with_options\n\n:= utf8_round_trip () : i32 * string =\n    := temp_dir, disposable = probe_dir \"utf8\"\n    disposable |> use |> ignore\n    probe_text () |> file_system.write_all_text (probe_path temp_dir)\n    utf8_read_in temp_dir\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest reading_a_missing_file_fails =\n    missing_file_read () |> _assert_eq (1, !+)\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest utf8_text_round_trips_in_a_working_directory =\n    utf8_round_trip () |> _assert_eq (0i32, probe_text ())\n\n:= five_lines_command () : string =\n    \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; for ($i = 0; $i \"\n    ^^ \"-lt 5; $i++) { Write-Output `\\\"Line$i`\\\"; Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200 }\\\"\"\n\n:= five_lines () : i32 * string =\n    execution_options \\ x => { x ?|\n        command = five_lines_command ()\n    }\n    |> execute_with_options\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest tests_2 =\n    := exit_code, output = five_lines ()\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 0i32\n    output |> _assert sm'.contains \"Line4\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest a_spawned_command_reports_its_exit_code =\n    := program, flag, script = ? platform.is_windows () ?> \"cmd\", \"/C\", \"exit 4\" |: \"sh\", \"-c\", \"exit 4\"\n    := command = shared_command_new program\n    shared_command_arg command flag\n    shared_command_arg command script\n    shared_command_quiet command\n    := child = shared_command_spawn command\n    (shared_child_id child > 0u32, shared_child_code child) |> _assert_eq (!+, 4i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= exit_four_shell () = ? platform.is_windows () ?> \"cmd\", \"/C\", \"exit 4\" |: \"sh\", \"-c\", \"exit 4\"\n\n:= exit_four_child () =\n    := program, flag, script = exit_four_shell ()\n    := command = shared_command_new program\n    shared_command_arg command flag\n    shared_command_arg command script\n    shared_command_quiet command\n    shared_command_spawn command\n\n///> rust\ntest a_spawned_command_reports_its_exit_code =\n    := child = exit_four_child ()\n    (shared_child_id child > 0u32, shared_child_code child) |> _assert_eq (!+, 4i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\ntest a_missing_or_failing_program_captures_nothing =\n    try_capture_combined_list \"spiral-no-such-program\" [] |> _assert_eq None\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.exit(4)\" ] |> _assert_eq None\n    := args = [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.stderr.write('warned')\" ]\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" args |> optionm.map sm'.trim |> _assert_eq (Some \"warned\")\n  >>> with <<<\ntest a_missing_or_failing_program_captures_nothing =\n    try_capture_combined_list \"spiral-no-such-program\" [] |> _assert_eq None\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.exit(4)\" ] |> _assert_eq None\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_succeeding_program_captures_its_stderr =\n    := args = [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.stderr.write('warned')\" ]\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" args |> optionm.map sm'.trim |> _assert_eq (Some \"warned\")\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_started_program_logs_and_reports_its_exit =\n    := log = file_system.get_temp_path () ++# \"/spiral-process-started-quick.log\"\n    := s = start_logging \".\" \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"print('ready')\" ] log\n    (started_pid s > 0i32) |> _assert_eq !+\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    await_exit_within s 0i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    file_system.read_all_text log |> sm'.trim |> _assert_eq \"ready\"\n  >>> with <<<\n:= started_log (name : string) : string =\n    file_system.get_temp_path () ++# \"/spiral-process-started-\" ++# name ++# \".log\"\n\n:= start_quick (log : string) = start_logging \".\" \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"print('ready')\" ] log\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_started_program_reports_its_exit =\n    := s = start_quick (started_log \"quick\")\n    (started_pid s > 0i32) |> _assert_eq !+\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    await_exit_within s 0i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_started_program_logs_its_output =\n    := log = started_log \"logged\"\n    await_exit_within (start_quick log) 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    file_system.read_all_text log |> sm'.trim |> _assert_eq \"ready\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_running_program_is_killed_by_its_pid =\n    := sleeper = [ \"-c\"; \"import time; time.sleep(30)\" ]\n    := s = start_logging \".\" \"python\" sleeper (file_system.get_temp_path () ++# \"/spiral-process-started-slow.log\")\n    await_exit_within s 300i32 |> _assert_eq None\n    kill_tree_of_pid (started_pid s)\n    := ended =\n        ?= await_exit_within s 10000i32 ?|\n        | Some _ => !+\n        | None => !-\n    ended |> _assert_eq !+\n  >>> with <<<\n:= start_sleeper () = start_logging \".\" \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"import time; time.sleep(30)\" ] (started_log \"slow\")\n\n:= has_ended (s : started) (ms : i32) : bool =\n    ?= await_exit_within s ms ?|\n    | Some _ => !+\n    | None => !-\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_running_program_is_killed_by_its_pid =\n    := s = start_sleeper ()\n    has_ended s 300i32 |> _assert_eq !-\n    kill_tree_of_pid (started_pid s)\n    has_ended s 10000i32 |> _assert_eq !+\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_program_runs_in_its_directory =\n    := dir = file_system.get_temp_path ()\n    := marker = \"spiral-process-started-directory-marker.txt\"\n    := write = [ \"-c\"; \"open('\" ++# marker ++# \"', 'w').write('here')\" ]\n    := s = start_logging dir \"python\" write (dir ++# \"/spiral-process-started-directory.log\")\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    (file_system.file_exists (dir ++# \"/\" ++# marker), file_system.file_exists marker) |> _assert_eq (!+, !-)\n    file_system.file_delete (dir ++# \"/\" ++# marker)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= directory_marker () : string = \"spiral-process-started-directory-marker.txt\"\n\n:= write_marker_args () : list string = [ \"-c\"; \"open('\" ++# directory_marker () ++# \"', 'w').write('here')\" ]\n\n:= marker_writer_exit (dir : string) : option i32 =\n    := s = start_logging dir \"python\" (write_marker_args ()) (started_log \"directory\")\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32\n\n:= marker_places (dir : string) : bool * bool =\n    file_system.file_exists (dir ++# \"/\" ++# directory_marker ()), file_system.file_exists (directory_marker ())\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_program_runs_in_its_directory =\n    := dir = file_system.get_temp_path ()\n    marker_writer_exit dir |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    marker_places dir |> _assert_eq (!+, !-)\n    file_system.file_delete (dir ++# \"/\" ++# directory_marker ())\n  >>>\nedit process.spi expect files 1 replacements 6\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\\\(args, $'\"true; std::process::Command::args(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\\\(args, $'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::args(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\($'\"true; std::process::Command::stdout(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::stdout(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool)\n    |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\($'\"true; std::process::Command::stderr(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::stderr(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool)\n    |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\($'\"true; std::process::Command::stdin(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::stdin(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool)\n    |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\\\(dir, $'\"true; std::process::Command::current_dir(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\\\(dir, $'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::current_dir(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\\\((key, value), $'\"true; std::process::Command::env(&mut !c, &*$0, &*$1)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\\\((key, value), $'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::env(&mut !c, &*$0, &*$1)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>>")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests_4 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", 4u32, "2026-10-31T15:07Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 11:0x tibia: two untracked 0-byte files were in the LIVE lib dir: lib/spiral/process-started-slow.log and process-started-directory.log, created 03:54 today by another run on the live tree. Cause: committed HEAD (fd70dccf) still has the old process tests, which pass RELATIVE log names (\"process-started-slow.log\"), and start_logging's Gleam arm does file_system.write_all_text log \"\" before spawning, so with cwd = lib/spiral the empty logs landed in the tree. The unstaged working tree already uses file_system.get_temp_path () ++# \"/spiral-process-started-*.log\" (and this item's program keeps that through started_log), so the cause is fixed once the user commits the lib. Removed both files (0 bytes, test output, no references).")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests_5 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", 5u32, "2026-10-31T18:28Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 14:3x tibia: PROCESS SLICE RE-PROVEN on the NODE on the frozen base (main froze process.spi until 16:30). This SUPERSEDES n3, whose base moved to DAC63B6A00F64C20 under main's headings wave. The program is unchanged and re-applies -> BE258A03A77A9E1A, overweight 23 after. Formatter clean, round trip ok. Gate: node mirror tibia-gates (synced 13:2x, digest BEC35FF2108C2C55; process.spi there = DAC63B6A), lib-program-gate.ps1 -Control, eoie.exe. Control on the unchanged base: split_command/typescript failed (pre-existing; it is not repeated below). Candidate: all 12 tests passed on every row, 0 type errors. Negative: 9 tests failed, 0 type errors: CAUGHT.\nLAND: land-lib-program.ps1 -Note LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS/<this note> -File process.spi -Base DAC63B6A00F64C20 -Target BE258A03A77A9E1A\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit process.spi expect files 1 replacements 8\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_args =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    [\n        \"a b c\",\n        ;[ \"a\"; \"b\"; \"c\" ]\n\n        \"e f \\\"g h\\\" i\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"f\"; \"g h\"; \"i\" ]\n\n        \"\\\"j k\\\" \\\"l\\\" \\\"m\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"j k\"; \"l\"; \"m\" ]\n\n        \"s -t \\\"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"s\"; \"-t\"; \"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\" ]\n\n        \"n -o \\\"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"n\"; \"-o\"; \"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\" ]\n\n        \"r -s \\\"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"r\"; \"-s\"; \"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\" ]\n\n        $'\"x -y \\\\\\\"$z -a \\'(b=\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}\\', { \\`$_[1] + \\`$d++ }\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"x\"; \"-y\"; \"$z -a '(b=\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$d++ }\" ]\n\n        \"e -f \\\"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"-f\"; \"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\" ]\n\n        $'\"--l \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\'\\'\\' m \\'\\'\\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \"',\n        ;[ \"--l\"; \"''' m '''\" ]\n\n        $'\"n --o --p q --r \\\\\\\"s:/t u/v.w\\\\\\\" --x \\\\\\\"y:/z.a\\\\\\\" --b c.d \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\e{f-g}\\\\\\\" h.i \\\\\\\"j (k)\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[\n            \"n\"; \"--o\"; \"--p\"; \"q\"; \"--r\"; \"s:/t u/v.w\"; \"--x\"; \"y:/z.a\"; \"--b\"; \"c.d\"; \"\\\\e{f-g}\"; \"h.i\"; \"j (k)\"\n        ]\n\n        $'\"l \\\\\\\"m n:\\\\\\\\o.p\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"l\"; \"m n:\\\\o.p\" ]\n\n        $'\"--r s \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\' t \\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" u v w \\\\\\\\\\\\\"x y\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"--r\"; \"s\"; \"' t '\"; \"u\"; \"v\"; \"w\"; \"x y\" ]\n    ]\n    |> _assert_fn split_args\n  >>> with <<<\n:= split_args_plain_cases () =\n    [\n        \"a b c\",\n        ;[ \"a\"; \"b\"; \"c\" ]\n\n        \"e f \\\"g h\\\" i\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"f\"; \"g h\"; \"i\" ]\n\n        \"\\\"j k\\\" \\\"l\\\" \\\"m\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"j k\"; \"l\"; \"m\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_escaped_cases () =\n    [\n        \"s -t \\\"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"s\"; \"-t\"; \"u \\`\\\"v\\`\\\" w\" ]\n\n        \"n -o \\\"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"n\"; \"-o\"; \"p \\\\\\\"q\\\\\\\" r\" ]\n\n        \"r -s \\\"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"r\"; \"-s\"; \"t \\\\\\\"u\\\\\\\"\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_regex_case () =\n    [\n        $'\"x -y \\\\\\\"$z -a \\'(b=\\\\\\\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}\\', { \\`$_[1] + \\`$d++ }\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"x\"; \"-y\"; \"$z -a '(b=\\\\\\\"c-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$d++ }\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_backtick_regex_case () =\n    [\n        \"e -f \\\"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\\\"\",\n        ;[ \"e\"; \"-f\"; \"$g -h '(i=`\\\"j-id=)[a-fA-F0-9]{8}', { `$_[1] + `$k++ }\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_quote_cases () =\n    [\n        $'\"--l \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\'\\'\\' m \\'\\'\\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \"',\n        ;[ \"--l\"; \"''' m '''\" ]\n\n        $'\"l \\\\\\\"m n:\\\\\\\\o.p\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"l\"; \"m n:\\\\o.p\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_spaced_quote_case () =\n    [\n        $'\"--r s \\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\' t \\'\\\\\\\\\\\\\" u v w \\\\\\\\\\\\\"x y\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\"',\n        ;[ \"--r\"; \"s\"; \"' t '\"; \"u\"; \"v\"; \"w\"; \"x y\" ]\n    ]\n\n:= split_args_path_input () =\n    $'\"n --o --p q --r \\\\\\\"s:/t u/v.w\\\\\\\" --x \\\\\\\"y:/z.a\\\\\\\" --b c.d \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\e{f-g}\\\\\\\" h.i \\\\\\\"j (k)\\\\\\\"\"'\n\n:= split_args_path_expected () =\n    ;[ \"n\"; \"--o\"; \"--p\"; \"q\"; \"--r\"; \"s:/t u/v.w\"; \"--x\"; \"y:/z.a\"; \"--b\"; \"c.d\"; \"\\\\e{f-g}\"; \"h.i\"; \"j (k)\" ]\n\n:= split_args_path_case () = [ split_args_path_input (), split_args_path_expected () ]\n\n:= split_args_cases () =\n    split_args_plain_cases () ++ split_args_escaped_cases () ++ split_args_regex_case ()\n    ++ split_args_backtick_regex_case () ++ split_args_quote_cases () ++ split_args_spaced_quote_case ()\n    ++ split_args_path_case ()\n\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_args =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    split_args_cases () |> _assert_fn split_args\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_command =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    [\n        \"\",\n        (\"\", None)\n\n        \"/a/b/c\",\n        (\"/a/b/c\", None)\n\n        \"d e.f\",\n        (\"d\", \"e.f\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\g.h i.j k.l\",\n        (\"../../g.h\", \"i.j k.l\" |> Some)\n\n        \"m:\\\\n\\\\o.p \\\"q.r s.t\\\"\",\n        (\"m:/n/o.p\", \"\\\"q.r s.t\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\u v\\\\w.x\\\" \\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\",\n        (\"../../u v/w.x\", \"\\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\" |> Some)\n\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\d e.f\\\" -g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../d e.f\", \"-g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\j k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../j\", \"k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n    ]\n    |> _assert_fn split_command\n  >>> with <<<\n:= split_command_unquoted_cases () =\n    [\n        \"\",\n        (\"\", None)\n\n        \"/a/b/c\",\n        (\"/a/b/c\", None)\n\n        \"d e.f\",\n        (\"d\", \"e.f\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\g.h i.j k.l\",\n        (\"../../g.h\", \"i.j k.l\" |> Some)\n    ]\n\n:= split_command_quoted_cases () =\n    [\n        \"m:\\\\n\\\\o.p \\\"q.r s.t\\\"\",\n        (\"m:/n/o.p\", \"\\\"q.r s.t\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\u v\\\\w.x\\\" \\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\",\n        (\"../../u v/w.x\", \"\\\"y z.a\\\" b.c\" |> Some)\n    ]\n\n:= split_command_escaped_cases () =\n    [\n        \"\\\"..\\\\..\\\\d e.f\\\" -g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../d e.f\", \"-g \\\\\\\\\\\"h i\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n\n        \"..\\\\..\\\\j k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\",\n        (\"../../j\", \"k.l -m \\\\\\\\\\\"n o\\\\\\\\\\\"\" |> Some)\n    ]\n\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest split_command =\n    Debug |> set_trace_level\n    split_command_unquoted_cases () ++ split_command_quoted_cases () ++ split_command_escaped_cases ()\n    |> _assert_fn split_command\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n/// #### tests\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest tests =\n    := content = \"╭─[ 你好，世界！こんにちは世界！ ]─╮\"\n\n    := file_name = ~~ \"test.txt\"\n    := temp_dir, disposable =\n        #?*(file_name, content)\n        |> crypto.hash_text\n        |> file_system.create_temp_dir'\n    disposable |> use |> ignore\n    := path = temp_dir </> file_name |> file_system.normalize_path\n    := exit_code, result =\n        execute (\"pwsh -c \\\"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\" ++# path ++# \"')\\\"\")\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 1\n    result |> _assert sm'.contains \"not find file\"\n\n    content |> file_system.write_all_text path\n\n    := exit_code, output =\n        execution_options \\ x =>\n            { x ?|\n                command =\n                    (\n                        \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; \"\n                        ^^ \"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\"\n                    )\n                    ++# file_name\n                    ++# \"')\\\"\"\n                working_directory = Some temp_dir |> optionm'.box\n            }\n        |> execute_with_options\n\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 0i32\n    output |> _assert_eq content\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest tests_2 =\n    := exit_code, output =\n        execution_options \\ x =>\n            { x ?|\n                command =\n                    \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; for ($i = 0; $i \"\n                    ^^ \"-lt 5; $i++) { Write-Output `\\\"Line$i`\\\"; Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200 }\\\"\"\n            }\n        |> execute_with_options\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 0i32\n    output |> _assert sm'.contains \"Line4\"\n  >>> with <<<\n:= probe_text () : string = \"╭─[ 你好，世界！こんにちは世界！ ]─╮\"\n\n:= probe_dir (tag : string) = file_system.create_temp_dir' (\"spiral-process-probe-\" ++# tag)\n\n:= probe_path (temp_dir : string) : string = file_system.(</>) temp_dir (~~ \"test.txt\") |> file_system.normalize_path\n\n:= read_command (path : string) : string = \"pwsh -c \\\"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\" ++# path ++# \"')\\\"\"\n\n:= missing_file_read () : i32 * bool =\n    := temp_dir, disposable = probe_dir \"missing\"\n    disposable |> use |> ignore\n    := exit_code, result = execute (read_command (probe_path temp_dir))\n    exit_code, result |> sm'.contains \"not find file\"\n\n:= utf8_read_command () : string =\n    \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; \"\n    ^^ \"[IO.File]::ReadAllText('\" ++# ~~ \"test.txt\" ++# \"')\\\"\"\n\n:= utf8_read_in (dir : string) : i32 * string =\n    execution_options \\ x =>\n        { x ?|\n            command = utf8_read_command ()\n            working_directory = Some dir |> optionm'.box\n        }\n    |> execute_with_options\n\n:= utf8_round_trip () : i32 * string =\n    := temp_dir, disposable = probe_dir \"utf8\"\n    disposable |> use |> ignore\n    probe_text () |> file_system.write_all_text (probe_path temp_dir)\n    utf8_read_in temp_dir\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest reading_a_missing_file_fails =\n    missing_file_read () |> _assert_eq (1, !+)\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest utf8_text_round_trips_in_a_working_directory =\n    utf8_round_trip () |> _assert_eq (0i32, probe_text ())\n\n:= five_lines_command () : string =\n    \"pwsh -c \\\"[System.Console]::OutputEncoding = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8; for ($i = 0; $i \"\n    ^^ \"-lt 5; $i++) { Write-Output `\\\"Line$i`\\\"; Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 200 }\\\"\"\n\n:= five_lines () : i32 * string =\n    execution_options \\ x => { x ?|\n        command = five_lines_command ()\n    }\n    |> execute_with_options\n\n///> rust -d chrono encoding_rs encoding_rs_io regex sha2\ntest tests_2 =\n    := exit_code, output = five_lines ()\n    exit_code |> _assert_eq 0i32\n    output |> _assert sm'.contains \"Line4\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest a_spawned_command_reports_its_exit_code =\n    := program, flag, script = ? platform.is_windows () ?> \"cmd\", \"/C\", \"exit 4\" |: \"sh\", \"-c\", \"exit 4\"\n    := command = shared_command_new program\n    shared_command_arg command flag\n    shared_command_arg command script\n    shared_command_quiet command\n    := child = shared_command_spawn command\n    (shared_child_id child > 0u32, shared_child_code child) |> _assert_eq (!+, 4i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= exit_four_shell () = ? platform.is_windows () ?> \"cmd\", \"/C\", \"exit 4\" |: \"sh\", \"-c\", \"exit 4\"\n\n:= exit_four_child () =\n    := program, flag, script = exit_four_shell ()\n    := command = shared_command_new program\n    shared_command_arg command flag\n    shared_command_arg command script\n    shared_command_quiet command\n    shared_command_spawn command\n\n///> rust\ntest a_spawned_command_reports_its_exit_code =\n    := child = exit_four_child ()\n    (shared_child_id child > 0u32, shared_child_code child) |> _assert_eq (!+, 4i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\ntest a_missing_or_failing_program_captures_nothing =\n    try_capture_combined_list \"spiral-no-such-program\" [] |> _assert_eq None\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.exit(4)\" ] |> _assert_eq None\n    := args = [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.stderr.write('warned')\" ]\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" args |> optionm.map sm'.trim |> _assert_eq (Some \"warned\")\n  >>> with <<<\ntest a_missing_or_failing_program_captures_nothing =\n    try_capture_combined_list \"spiral-no-such-program\" [] |> _assert_eq None\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.exit(4)\" ] |> _assert_eq None\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_succeeding_program_captures_its_stderr =\n    := args = [ \"-c\"; \"import sys; sys.stderr.write('warned')\" ]\n    try_capture_combined_list \"python\" args |> optionm.map sm'.trim |> _assert_eq (Some \"warned\")\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_started_program_logs_and_reports_its_exit =\n    := log = file_system.get_temp_path () ++# \"/spiral-process-started-quick.log\"\n    := s = start_logging \".\" \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"print('ready')\" ] log\n    (started_pid s > 0i32) |> _assert_eq !+\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    await_exit_within s 0i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    file_system.read_all_text log |> sm'.trim |> _assert_eq \"ready\"\n  >>> with <<<\n:= started_log (name : string) : string =\n    file_system.get_temp_path () ++# \"/spiral-process-started-\" ++# name ++# \".log\"\n\n:= start_quick (log : string) = start_logging \".\" \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"print('ready')\" ] log\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_started_program_reports_its_exit =\n    := s = start_quick (started_log \"quick\")\n    (started_pid s > 0i32) |> _assert_eq !+\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    await_exit_within s 0i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_started_program_logs_its_output =\n    := log = started_log \"logged\"\n    await_exit_within (start_quick log) 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    file_system.read_all_text log |> sm'.trim |> _assert_eq \"ready\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_running_program_is_killed_by_its_pid =\n    := sleeper = [ \"-c\"; \"import time; time.sleep(30)\" ]\n    := s = start_logging \".\" \"python\" sleeper (file_system.get_temp_path () ++# \"/spiral-process-started-slow.log\")\n    await_exit_within s 300i32 |> _assert_eq None\n    kill_tree_of_pid (started_pid s)\n    := ended =\n        ?= await_exit_within s 10000i32 ?|\n        | Some _ => !+\n        | None => !-\n    ended |> _assert_eq !+\n  >>> with <<<\n:= start_sleeper () = start_logging \".\" \"python\" [ \"-c\"; \"import time; time.sleep(30)\" ] (started_log \"slow\")\n\n:= has_ended (s : started) (ms : i32) : bool =\n    ?= await_exit_within s ms ?|\n    | Some _ => !+\n    | None => !-\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_running_program_is_killed_by_its_pid =\n    := s = start_sleeper ()\n    has_ended s 300i32 |> _assert_eq !-\n    kill_tree_of_pid (started_pid s)\n    has_ended s 10000i32 |> _assert_eq !+\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_program_runs_in_its_directory =\n    := dir = file_system.get_temp_path ()\n    := marker = \"spiral-process-started-directory-marker.txt\"\n    := write = [ \"-c\"; \"open('\" ++# marker ++# \"', 'w').write('here')\" ]\n    := s = start_logging dir \"python\" write (dir ++# \"/spiral-process-started-directory.log\")\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32 |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    (file_system.file_exists (dir ++# \"/\" ++# marker), file_system.file_exists marker) |> _assert_eq (!+, !-)\n    file_system.file_delete (dir ++# \"/\" ++# marker)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= directory_marker () : string = \"spiral-process-started-directory-marker.txt\"\n\n:= write_marker_args () : list string = [ \"-c\"; \"open('\" ++# directory_marker () ++# \"', 'w').write('here')\" ]\n\n:= marker_writer_exit (dir : string) : option i32 =\n    := s = start_logging dir \"python\" (write_marker_args ()) (started_log \"directory\")\n    await_exit_within s 20000i32\n\n:= marker_places (dir : string) : bool * bool =\n    file_system.file_exists (dir ++# \"/\" ++# directory_marker ()), file_system.file_exists (directory_marker ())\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest a_program_runs_in_its_directory =\n    := dir = file_system.get_temp_path ()\n    marker_writer_exit dir |> _assert_eq (Some 0i32)\n    marker_places dir |> _assert_eq (!+, !-)\n    file_system.file_delete (dir ++# \"/\" ++# directory_marker ())\n  >>>\nedit process.spi expect files 1 replacements 6\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\\\(args, $'\"true; std::process::Command::args(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\\\(args, $'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::args(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\($'\"true; std::process::Command::stdout(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::stdout(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool)\n    |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\($'\"true; std::process::Command::stderr(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::stderr(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool)\n    |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\($'\"true; std::process::Command::stdin(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::stdin(&mut !c, std::process::Stdio::piped())\"') : bool)\n    |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\\\(dir, $'\"true; std::process::Command::current_dir(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\\\(dir, $'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::current_dir(&mut !c, &*$0)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n    (!\\($'\"true; let mut !c = !c\"') : bool) |> ignore\n    (!\\\\((key, value), $'\"true; std::process::Command::env(&mut !c, &*$0, &*$1)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>> with <<<\n    (!\\\\((key, value), $'\"true; let mut !c = !c; std::process::Command::env(&mut !c, &*$0, &*$1)\"') : bool) |> ignore\n  >>>")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests_6 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", 6u32, "2026-10-31T18:29Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 14:28 tibia: LANDED process.spi DAC63B6A00F64C20 -> BE258A03A77A9E1A (n5's program: process tests plus LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS part 1's builders), tree-write window, applied with no live lib reader. Undo: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\undo\\LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS-n5. Post-land on the live file: round trip ok, x-compat 23 overweight (39 this morning). Left in this item: the file_system test slice (node re-gate running on the frozen base 89493A55).")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_tests_7 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", 7u32, "2026-10-31T18:56Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 14:5x tibia: FILE_SYSTEM TEST SLICE PROVEN on the frozen base (the F# retire removed ///> fsharp from 2 of its tests, now dropped from the program too). Control 3/3 GREEN; candidate 3/3; negative 3 failed, CAUGHT; overweight 79 after (82). Gate: node mirror tibia-gates re-synced 14:2x (REMOTE-SYNC-OK digest A6842A82921F0194), lib-program-gate.ps1 -Control, eoie.exe, inside main's 14:12-16:30 freeze. Formatter clean, round trip ok.\nLAND: land-lib-program.ps1 -Note LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS/<this note> -File \"file_system.spi\" -Base 89493A5501DC6425 -Target 7F2BD05876A52531\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\n\nedit file_system.spi expect files 1 replacements 3\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest read_text_or_empty_reads_a_file_or_gives_empty =\n    := path = get_temp_path () </> \"spiral-read-text-or-empty.txt\"\n    write_all_text path \"kept\"\n    path |> read_text_or_empty |> _assert_eq \"kept\"\n    (path ++# \".missing\") |> read_text_or_empty |> _assert_eq \"\"\n  >>> with <<<\n:= read_text_or_empty_probe () : string =\n    := path = get_temp_path () </> \"spiral-read-text-or-empty.txt\"\n    write_all_text path \"kept\"\n    path\n\n///> rust\ntest read_text_or_empty_reads_a_file_or_gives_empty =\n    := path = read_text_or_empty_probe ()\n    (read_text_or_empty path, read_text_or_empty (path ++# \".missing\")) |> _assert_eq (\"kept\", \"\")\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\ntest file_exists_on_gleam_tells_files_from_missing_paths =\n    := ~path = \"spiral-file-exists-probe.txt\"\n    write_all_text path \"x\"\n    := written = file_exists path\n    file_delete path\n    (written, file_exists path, file_exists \"spiral-no-such-file.txt\") |> _assert_eq (!+, !-, !-)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= written_then_deleted (path : string) : bool * bool =\n    write_all_text path \"x\"\n    := written = file_exists path\n    file_delete path\n    written, file_exists path\n\n///> gleam\ntest file_exists_on_gleam_tells_files_from_missing_paths =\n    := ~path = \"spiral-file-exists-probe.txt\"\n    (written_then_deleted path, file_exists \"spiral-no-such-file.txt\") |> _assert_eq ((!+, !-), !-)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest append_all_text_adds_to_the_end_of_a_file =\n    := probe = get_temp_path () </> \"spiral-append-probe.txt\"\n    file_delete probe\n    append_all_text probe \"a\"\n    append_all_text probe \"b\"\n    read_all_text probe |> _assert_eq \"ab\"\n    file_delete probe\n  >>> with <<<\n:= appended_text () : string =\n    := probe = get_temp_path () </> \"spiral-append-probe.txt\"\n    file_delete probe\n    append_all_text probe \"a\"\n    append_all_text probe \"b\"\n    := text = read_all_text probe\n    file_delete probe\n    text\n\n///> rust\ntest append_all_text_adds_to_the_end_of_a_file =\n    appended_text () |> _assert_eq \"ab\"\n  >>>")
inl land_lib_program_from_note () = Task ("LAND-LIB-PROGRAM-FROM-NOTE", "land-lib-program.ps1 reads the kit do program straight from a backlog note (-Note <ITEM>/<n>, the block after 'PROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):'), so a proven lib slice lives only in its item note and landing needs no drafts file; refuse when the note has no program block or its text differs from what was gated (hash in the note)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "team:tibia,tibia,tools,lib,org-scripts", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_land_lib_program_from_note () = Planning ("LAND-LIB-PROGRAM-FROM-NOTE", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_land_lib_program_from_note_1 () = Note ("LAND-LIB-PROGRAM-FROM-NOTE", 1u32, "2026-10-31T11:57Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 08:0x tibia: DONE in i574n.github/scripts/land-lib-program.ps1 (unstaged). It now takes -Note <ITEM>/<n> as the alternative to -Program <file>, exactly one of the two. It reads the note through kit agile show --json (note n = notes[n-1]), takes the text after the \"PROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\" marker, and writes it to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\undo\\<ITEM>-n<n>\\program.kitdo beside the undo copy, so the landed program is kept with its undo. A note without the marker exits 3. The title's \"refuse when it differs from what was gated\" needs no extra hash: the existing target-hash check already restores the base when the result is not the gated -Target. Proof, with a deliberately wrong -Base so nothing lands: POSTABLE-ALL-REPOS/146 and /147 extract byte-identical to the gated programs (exit 4, re-anchor); /145 (no block) exits 3; live otp_actor.spi unchanged.")
