inl note_of_sim_diff_cli_1 () = Note ("SIM-DIFF-CLI", 1u32, "2026-10-31T11:48Z", "x", "2026-10-31 x: S5 removed apps/sim's mix project (SIM-IN-SPIRAL n145); xsim.diff was a dev tool with no caller in x, so it went without a CLI twin. Its source stays in git history (apps/sim/lib/mix/tasks/xsim.diff.ex). Port: run_opts root/spiral_lib = dirname of the .spi, Notebook.evaluate twice, compare outputs per cell; one export (cli_diff) per the one-export-per-path rule. Proof: one node run on a lib .spi printing 'XDIFF done identical=true'.")
inl note_of_sim_diff_cli_2 () = Note ("SIM-DIFF-CLI", 2u32, "2026-10-31T12:16Z", "x", "2026-10-31 08:16 x: DRAFTED in x (unstaged): 'scripts/sim-run.ps1 diff --spi FILE [--cells N]' as its own export cli_diff (sim-run routes 'diff'). sim_args.diff_args (--spi required, --cells default 5, the same messages as the mix task); cells_executor.evaluated_cells = Notebook.evaluate(cells_doc sources, [root, spiral_lib] = the .spi's directory), exactly the mix task's run_opts; indexed reads result.verdicts / result.outputs by cell index; elixir_inspect calls Elixir.Kernel.inspect, so the XDIFF lines keep the mix task's formatting (printable_limit 600 for outputs). Output: 'XDIFF status a=<status> b=<status> verdict a=<v> b=<v>' for the last cell, one 'XDIFF cell i' block per differing output, then 'XDIFF done identical=<bool>'; exit 0 like the mix task; a missing --spi prints 'XSIM rejected diff: missing --spi' and exits 1. Local: x-compat 0 in 29 files, kit standards 0, and no line over 120 in any spi file (kit standards checks 23 of the 29 files and missed 4 long lines in simframes' subfolder; wrapped them). PRE-REGISTERED x-diffprobe (scratchpad launcher, xqueue3): build exit 0; D1 'diff --spi spiral/lib/spiral/math.spi --cells 3' exits 0 with an 'XDIFF status a=:ok b=:ok' line and 'XDIFF done identical=true'; D2 'diff --cells 3' exits 1 with 'XSIM rejected diff: missing --spi'.")
inl note_of_sim_diff_cli_3 () = Note ("SIM-DIFF-CLI", 3u32, "2026-10-31T12:27Z", "x", "2026-10-31 08:27 x: x-diffprobe (job-1793449201196, 305 s) by n2's rule: PASS. Build exit 0; D1 'sim-run.ps1 diff --spi spiral/lib/spiral/math.spi --cells 3' exit 0 with 'XDIFF status a=:ok b=:ok verdict a=:passed b=:passed' and 'XDIFF done identical=true' (Elixir inspect formatting, as the mix task printed); D2 'diff --cells 3' exit 1 with 'XSIM rejected diff: missing --spi'. (The job's own exit 1 is D2's exit leaking as the scratch launcher's last command; not part of the rule.) DONE: the code is in x, unstaged; the next x verify covers it through the build of simframes.")
inl wipe_recovery_toolkit () = Task ("WIPE-RECOVERY-TOOLKIT", "Turn scripts/wipe-recovery (the 10-30 undelete and restore scripts that saved the profile data) into a parameterized toolkit: no hard-coded partition offset, recovery root, node python path or wipe window; one runbook entry in order (deleted-file catalog from a VSS/live MFT, PhysicalDrive TRIM probe, node-copy match + repo-blob filter, MFT-resident restore via the safe in-place mover, per-type triage, citation-based memory rebuild); each step keeps its positive control", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "-", "main,wipe,recovery,tooling,durability", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_wipe_recovery_toolkit () = Planning ("WIPE-RECOVERY-TOOLKIT", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_wipe_recovery_toolkit_1 () = Note ("WIPE-RECOVERY-TOOLKIT", 1u32, "2026-10-31T11:48Z", "heal", "Filed 10-31 07:4x by heal (git-51). Source: 44 scripts copied unstaged from the heal scratchpad into i574n.github/scripts/wipe-recovery (87 KB). Method and lessons: memory undelete-bitlocker-trim, PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY n32-n56. Constants to lift: trim_probe PART_OFF 122683392, REC C:\\home\\recovery\\wipe-20261028, node_sink NODE_PY, select_tiers wipe window.")
inl note_of_wipe_recovery_toolkit_2 () = Note ("WIPE-RECOVERY-TOOLKIT", 2u32, "2026-10-31T12:15Z", "heal", "10-31 08:2x heal (git-51): 80%. New recovery_config.py is the single settings module (env overrides: WIPE_DATE, WIPE_RECOVERY_ROOT, WIPE_NODE_HOST/PYTHON, WIPE_MEMORY_DIR, WIPE_VOLUME, WIPE_AT, WIPE_RESTORE_FROM/TO, WIPE_LOST_MAP, WIPE_CUTOFF_EPOCH). It DERIVES the physical drive and partition offset via IOCTL_STORAGE_GET_DEVICE_NUMBER + IOCTL_DISK_GET_PARTITION_INFO_EX (positive control: PhysicalDrive0 / 122683392, equal to the old constant). 24 scripts were refactored onto it (refactor script in the heal scratchpad; 3 escaping slips fixed by hand); all 45 .py compile. Smoke: trim_probe.py ran end to end through cfg on the real catalog (10 records). RUNBOOK.md gives the stage order (copies first, undelete last; resident-only trust; files not state; triage; settings drift; cause). LEFT (20%): one-call entry (a run-stage wrapper) and lifting the backlog paths in cite_counts/notes_at; user_checklist.py stays as the 10-30 report generator.")
inl note_of_wipe_recovery_toolkit_3 () = Note ("WIPE-RECOVERY-TOOLKIT", 3u32, "2026-10-31T12:27Z", "heal", "10-31 08:3x heal (git-51): DONE. The last 20% landed: recover.py is the one-call entry ('python -I recover.py <stage> [args]', 20 stages from config/catalog/probe/restore through triage, node-match, memory-cites, settings-drift and cause; no stage prints the usage list). Backlog paths were lifted into recovery_config.BACKLOG_FILES (env WIPE_BACKLOG_FILES), used by cite_counts.py and notes_at.py. cite_counts now writes into cfg.REC rather than beside the script. Proofs: 'recover.py config' gives the derived PhysicalDrive0/122683392 (exit 0); 'recover.py memory-cites' ran end to end on today's backlog (10,913 notes, 152 of 214 memory slugs cited); all 46 .py compile. Everything is unstaged in i574n.github/scripts/wipe-recovery for the user's review.")
inl note_of_wipe_recovery_toolkit_4 () = Note ("WIPE-RECOVERY-TOOLKIT", 4u32, "2026-10-31T23:01Z", "resilience", "10-31 18:3x resilience (git-51): ARCHIVED per the ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME decision (spiral-first-tooling; the wipe is recovered). The 48-file toolkit (46 .py + recover.py/recovery_config.py + RUNBOOK.md) moved from i574n.github/scripts/wipe-recovery to the node: C:\\home\\remote-archive\\wipe-recovery-toolkit-20261031.tgz (verified 48 entries, box copy removed). If another wipe hits, restore it: scp from the node and run per RUNBOOK. Method also preserved in memory undelete-bitlocker-trim. Not living org tooling anymore.")
inl profile_restore_drill () = Task ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL", "Scheduled restore drill for the profile mirror: weekly, open the newest node archive, sha256 the memory files and compare with the live copies unchanged since the archive time, and alert (backlog note + nonzero exit) on any mismatch or a tar entry-count shortfall; registered in register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 at Priority 5", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE", "main,wipe,backup,durability,node", "current", "current")
