inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_1 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL", 1u32, "2026-10-31T11:49Z", "heal", "Filed 10-31 07:4x by heal (git-51). The manual drill passed 10-30 20:0x (PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE n13: 197/199 hash-equal, 2 newer). Traps: match projects/C--home-git/memory/, not '/memory/' (several projects' folders collide); Task Scheduler defaults to BelowNormal (set -Priority 5).")
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_2 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL", 2u32, "2026-10-31T11:58Z", "heal", "10-31 07:5x heal (git-51): DONE (daily rather than weekly: the run costs ~1 min on the node). New i574n.github/scripts/profile-restore-drill.ps1 + profile-restore-drill-node.py (unstaged). The box scp's the node half over the first answering route, the node opens the newest READABLE archive (it skips archives still being copied in; the first run hit exactly that, 07:38 mid-scp), counts entries and sha256s projects/C--home-git/memory/*; the box compares with live files unchanged since the archive time. PASS needs entries >= 1000 and >= 1 hash-equal with 0 mismatches; FAIL exits 1 and, with -NoteOnFailure, notes this item. Proof: PASS on 073853 (29,146 entries, 213 hash-equal, 1 newer). Negative control: a scratch memory copy with archive-never-delete.md tampered and its mtime kept gave 'FAIL: archive-never-delete.md differs...' and exit 1. Scheduled: task profile-restore-drill daily 05:40, Priority 5, headless, registered in register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 (a dry run lists 3 tasks); the task test run gave result 0 and PASS. Log: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\schedules\\profile-restore-drill.last.log.")
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_3 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL", 3u32, "2026-10-31T15:30Z", "resilience", "10-31 11:3x resilience (git-51): added a mirror-FRESHNESS guard, defense-in-depth for the stall PROFILE-MIRROR-TO-NODE n18 fixed at the root. The drill now FAILs (and notes, exit 1) if the newest node archive is older than -MaxArchiveAgeHours (default 3). Catches a stalled mirror from ANY cause (time-limit kill, node unreachable, scp failing), not just the 45-min-cap one. Proven: at 11:29 the 09:11 archive (2.3h old) PASSes the 3h default and FAILs a 1h control ('newest archive is 2.3h old (> 1h): the mirror is stalled'). Before this, a stall was only caught by a manual heartbeat check. The daily 05:40 run is a once-a-day net; the raised 2h task limit is the primary prevention.")
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_4 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL", 4u32, "2026-11-01T14:03Z", "resilience", "2026-11-01 ~13:4x resilience (git-51): the node half, profile-restore-drill-node.py, is spiral-first-tooling DRIFT (new .py in a repo, flagged by i574n). It STAYS running for now -- load-bearing for this live 05:40 drill -- but its port to a kit verb (reusing archive_deflate_domain extract + crypto.sha256) and the eventual archive of the .py are tracked in PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT, which also records the two node blockers (no gzip, no kit-on-PATH).")
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_5 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL", 5u32, "2026-11-02T09:40Z", "profile-restore-drill", "scheduled drill profile-restore-drill 2026-11-02 05:40 FAIL: newest archive is 16.3h old (> 3h): the mirror is stalled | profile-mirror-20261101-132405.tgz: 31885 entries; memory 225 hash-equal, 22 changed since, 1 gone locally")
inl kit_standards_entry_subdirs () = Task ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", "kit standards: check the entry .spi files in a package's subfolders too (line-width, lf-only, no-comment-lines); today it reads only the package's top-level files", TaskKind, P3, D2, 75u32, Planned, "", "kit,standards,lint,team:kit,kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs () = Planning ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_1 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T12:22Z", "x", "2026-10-31 x: found while landing SIM-IN-SPIRAL S5. 'kit standards C:\\home\\git\\x\\apps\\sim\\spi' reports files=23, but the package holds 29 .spi files; the 6 not checked are the entry notebooks in subfolders (simframes/simframes.spi, xsim_checks, xsim_events, xsim_flow, xsim_split, xsim_world; each declares '///- --package ..', so they belong to this package). simframes.spi had 4 lines of 121-129 columns that standards passed and only a plain length scan found (x wrapped them). Done = standards walks the package's subfolder entries (or every file whose ///- --package resolves to the package) and flags them; x's sim package stays at 0 findings.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_2 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T16:38Z", "kit", "10-31 12:4x kit: scoped, not built. The listing is kit_standards/standards.spi spiral_files, a raw-Rust read_dir blob (top-level .spi/.spir only, standards.spi excluded) feeding files_checked, which joins each name to the package folder and passes module_of(name) to kit_standards_scan's file findings. module_of only feeds two module rules (the float check in integer-only modules, and the test-block-needs-header rule), so a subfolder entry should pass its file STEM, not 'simframes/simframes'. AGENTS requires migrating a touched legacy blob, and the lib has no portable listing: file_system.directory_get_files is F#-only (null on other targets) and file_system.read_dir_names (file_system.spi:1702) is the Rust arm, returning result' (vec std_string) io_error. PLAN: replace spiral_files with Spiral over read_dir_names. Top-level entries as today, plus each subfolder (skipping target, .cache, node_modules) whose .spi files have first line '///- --package ..', named '<sub>/<file>' for the path and the stem for the module. Test block over a temp fixture: pkg/a.spi, pkg/sub/entry.spi with the header (checked), and pkg/other/loose.spi without it (not checked). Done = x's apps/sim/spi reports files=29 with 0 findings.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_3 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T16:56Z", "kit", "10-31 12:5x kit: BUILT (unstaged) per n2's plan; ships in TRAIN7. kit_standards/standards.spi spiral_files is now Spiral, no longer a raw-Rust read_dir blob (legacy migrated as AGENTS asks). sorted_names uses lib file_system.read_dir_names, then am'.from_vec_base, map_base sm'.from_std_string and am'.sort_by id (the kit_job_host idiom), guarded by directory_exists. names_where walks by index. The package's own .spi/.spir files are listed as before (standards.spi excluded), plus every subfolder file whose FIRST LINE is exactly '///- --package ..', named '<sub>/<file>'; target, node_modules and dot-folders are skipped. files_checked passes the file stem to module_of, so module rules see 'entry', not 'sub/entry'. CLI case subfolder_entries_of_the_package_are_checked_too (kit_standards/standards_cli.spi): pkg/sub/entry.spi with the header and a comment line is flagged ('sub/entry.spi:3  no-comment-lines'), pkg/other/loose.spi without the header is not, and files=2. Census ratchet ok; standards.rs had 572/1000 lines. Done = TRAIN7 green, then x's apps/sim/spi reports files=29.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_4 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 4u32, "2026-10-31T19:32Z", "kit", "10-31 15:3x kit: size check on the node (regen-sizes.ps1, read-only regen with cargo check on mirror kit-verify): standards.rs is 920/1000 with this change (it was 572; the Spiral listing plus the lib vec idiom costs about 350 generated lines), inside the gate. Other touched crates in the same run: agile_task_creation 990, agile_task_next 968, agile_todo_scan 1000 (exactly at the gate, KIT-TODO-SCAN-HEADROOM), kit_agile_mutation 831, kit_agile_routes 712, kit_do_file_steps 731, kit_machine_watch 898, kit_table_query 393, agile_task_revision 314. Cargo check passed for all.")
inl note_of_kit_standards_entry_subdirs_5 () = Note ("KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 60 h ago by kit, progress kept at 75%. Resume from that note: t 968, agile_todo_scan 1000 (exactly at the gate, KIT-TODO-SCAN-HEADROOM), kit_agile_mutation 831, kit_agile_routes 712, kit_do_file_steps 731, kit_machine_watch 898, kit_table_query 393, agile_task_revision 314. Cargo check passed for all.")
inl cells_mix_env_guard () = Task ("CELLS-MIX-ENV-GUARD", "Cells: CompilerClient.mix_env/0 should check that the :mix application is running, not only that the Mix module loads; in a mix-less VM with Elixir's mix/ebin on the path, Mix.env() raises on the missing Mix.State ETS table", TaskKind, P3, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,cells,beam", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_mix_env_guard () = Planning ("CELLS-MIX-ENV-GUARD", Minutes 20u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_mix_env_guard_1 () = Note ("CELLS-MIX-ENV-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-10-31T12:23Z", "x", "2026-10-31 x: root cause of x verify40's red (SIM-IN-SPIRAL n149). spiral/apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/compiler_client.ex:795 is 'if Code.ensure_loaded?(Mix), do: Mix.env() |> Atom.to_string(), else: \"dev\"'. Spawning a compiler daemon calls it; in a bare 'erl -pa <elixir lib/*/ebin>' the module loads but :mix never started, so Notebook.evaluate returned Error(\"... the table identifier does not refer to an existing ETS table\"). x works around it (scripts/sim-run.ps1 leaves mix/ebin off the path), so nothing is blocked. Suggested fix: also require List.keymember?(Application.started_applications(), :mix, 0), or rescue ArgumentError to \"dev\". Test: a bare-erl evaluate that has to spawn a daemon.")
inl note_of_cells_mix_env_guard_2 () = Note ("CELLS-MIX-ENV-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-10-31T13:53Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 09:53 compiler: FIXED in place (uncommitted): apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/compiler_client.ex mix_env/0 now requires Code.ensure_loaded?(Mix) AND List.keymember?(Application.started_applications(), :mix, 0), else 'dev'. Proof by the bug's own path: in plain 'elixir' (Mix loadable, :mix not started, the bare-VM case) the OLD expression raises ArgumentError (the missing Mix.State ETS table) and the NEW one returns 'dev'; under 'mix run' with MIX_ENV=test both return 'test', so mix-started VMs are unchanged. The module parses (Code.string_to_quoted); a full Cells compile happens with the next Cells window. Checked against main's pending Cells window 6: no anchor of its appliers covers mix_env; only its undo copies (session-1030\\cells-daemon-port\\undo-*) hold the old line, so undoing window 5 from those copies would drop this fix. x can drop the sim-run.ps1 workaround (mix/ebin off the path) after the next Cells land.")
inl lib_xcompat_tibia_defs () = Task ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", "tibia's lib share, DEFINITION cells near the limit (overweight by 30 or less): process' 6 rust-only process_command_* builders (287-302 against 271; fusing each 'let mut !c = !c' rebind macro with its Command call saves about 35 characters per cell), started_pid and exit_with; env's os_environ, environ_get, env_gleam_argv, process_id, append_path and rust_restored; threading's partial_eq_wrapper_arc_eq. Each changes emitted host code, so the proof is the file's test rows on every backend it targets plus a negative, through lib-program-gate.ps1 -Control", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS", "team:tibia,tibia,lib,postability,x-compat,granular", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs () = Planning ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_1 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T12:36Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 08:3x tibia: PART 1 DRAFTED: the 6 process_command_* builders. Each folded \"let mut !c = !c\" rebind macro joins the Command call macro that follows it. The emitted statements are the same minus one dummy bool binding, so behaviour is unchanged by construction; the test rows confirm it. process.spi 30 -> 24 overweight. It chains on LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS: base 9A8D268C5188B40B (that item's target) -> 5E14E2BE7F710523. The three Stdio::piped() lines take the formatter's canonical break before \"|> ignore\" (they are over 120 when joined). Formatter clean. Gate queued behind the tests chain: the tests and defs programs together, the Rust rows that reach the builders (reading_a_missing_file_fails, utf8_text_round_trips_in_a_working_directory, tests_2), and a negative that makes current_dir ignore its argument (the utf8 read then misses the file).\nDEFERRED inside this item: threading.partial_eq_wrapper_arc_eq. Collapsing its 6-line pipe (290/266) is layout-only, but its only user is new_partial_eq_wrapper_arc and threading has only F# rows, so proving it needs a Rust identity probe compiled against two lib copies. Not yet built. The env near-limit cells (os_environ, environ_get, env_gleam_argv, process_id, append_path, rust_restored; 279-302) are next: each needs a per-backend shortening and that backend's test rows.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_2 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T12:45Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 08:4x tibia: PART 2 DRAFTED: env. rust_restored (281/272) gets a nul_split helper for its two sm'.split (sm'.char_text 0u8) calls. append_path (282/271) joins its 4-line separator conditional onto one line; the tokens are identical, so it parses the same, and its only user is apps/spiral/spiral.spi. env.spi chains on POSTABLE's env tests program: base 65F0F5BBABEFA8E8 -> 756C3D1C9DC2C39D, overweight 17 -> 15. process_id is already under the limit since main's headings batch removed its heading, so it is left alone. os_environ and environ_get stay deferred: their Gleam/Lua arms are not compiled by any current test row, so a change there would be proven only by a type check. Gate queued after part 1: the tests and defs programs together, the 3 Rust snapshot-restore tests, and a negative that splits on byte 1 instead of NUL.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_3 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T14:51Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 10:5x tibia: PART 1 PROVEN, inside LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS n3's process program: the builders' rows (reading_a_missing_file_fails, utf8_text_round_trips_in_a_working_directory, tests_2 on rust) pass, and the current_dir negative fails them. PART 2 (env: nul_split, append_path) is re-gating together with POSTABLE's env tests program. Main's headings wave 2 and lambda-parens land changed env.spi at 10:12 to 5D1F524675CA1A3A, where \"(\\ _ => true)\" is now \"\\ _ => true\"; the programs are updated to the new style. Combined env target is 96AEDDA2D2DD6E71.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_4 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 4u32, "2026-10-31T15:19Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 11:2x tibia: ENV SLICE PROVEN (POSTABLE n144-147's env test reshapes plus this item's part 2, nul_split and append_path, as one program). env.spi base 5D1F524675CA1A3A (live after main's wave 2 and lambda-parens land) -> 96AEDDA2D2DD6E71, overweight 25 -> 15. Formatter clean, round trip ok.\nGate (box test-suite window, lib-program-gate.ps1 -Control, 10 tests): the control on the unchanged base passed all 9 tests that exist there (so the earlier remove/try_get reds were load); the candidate passed all 10; 0 type errors. Negative (one mutation per fixture, plus nul_split splitting on byte 1): 8 tests failed, 0 type errors, CAUGHT. The 2 untouched tests (a_snapshot_*_anchor_entry) passed, as they should.\nLAND: land-lib-program.ps1 -Note LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS/<this note> -File env.spi -Base 5D1F524675CA1A3A -Target 96AEDDA2D2DD6E71\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit env.spi expect files 1 replacements 7\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest remove_environment_variable =\n    set_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\" \"set\"\n    remove_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n    \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n    |> get_environment_variable\n    |> _assert_eq \"\"\n  >>> with <<<\n:= removed_probe () : string =\n    set_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\" \"set\"\n    remove_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n    get_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n\n///> gleam\n///> fsharp\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest remove_environment_variable =\n    removed_probe () |> _assert_eq \"\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> lua\n///> fsharp\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset =\n    := is_set var =\n        ?= var |> try_get_environment_variable ?|\n        | Some _ => 1i32\n        | None => 0i32\n    (is_set \"PATH2\", is_set \"PATH\")\n    |> _assert_eq (0i32, 1i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= variable_is_set (var : string) : i32 =\n    ?= var |> try_get_environment_variable ?|\n    | Some _ => 1i32\n    | None => 0i32\n\n///> gleam\n///> lua\n///> fsharp\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset =\n    (variable_is_set \"PATH2\", variable_is_set \"PATH\") |> _assert_eq (0i32, 1i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest command_line_arguments_outside_the_range_are_none =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    := is_set index =\n        ?= index |> try_command_line_argument ?|\n        | Some _ => 1i32\n        | None => 0i32\n    (count >= 0i32, is_set (-1i32), is_set count)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32, 0i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= argument_is_set (index : i32) : i32 =\n    ?= index |> try_command_line_argument ?|\n    | Some _ => 1i32\n    | None => 0i32\n\n///> fsharp\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest command_line_arguments_outside_the_range_are_none =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    (count >= 0i32, argument_is_set (-1i32), argument_is_set count)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32, 0i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest command_line_arguments_list_every_argument_in_order =\n    := listed = command_line_arguments ()\n    := head_is_first (head : string) = ?= try_command_line_argument 0i32 ?| | Some a => a = head | None => !-\n    := first_matches = ?= listed ?| | head :: _ => head_is_first head | [] => command_line_argument_count () = 0i32\n    (listm.length listed, first_matches) |> _assert_eq (command_line_argument_count (), !+)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= head_is_first_argument (head : string) : bool =\n    ?= try_command_line_argument 0i32 ?|\n    | Some a => a = head\n    | None => !-\n\n:= first_argument_matches (listed : list string) : bool =\n    ?= listed ?|\n    | head :: _ => head_is_first_argument head\n    | [] => command_line_argument_count () = 0i32\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest command_line_arguments_list_every_argument_in_order =\n    := listed = command_line_arguments ()\n    (listm.length listed, first_argument_matches listed) |> _assert_eq (command_line_argument_count (), !+)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest command_line_arguments_from_cover_the_rest_of_the_line =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    := all : i32 = listm.length (command_line_arguments_from 0i32)\n    := past : i32 = listm.length (command_line_arguments_from count)\n    (all = count, past)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= arguments_from_length (index : i32) : i32 = listm.length (command_line_arguments_from index)\n\n///> rust\ntest command_line_arguments_from_cover_the_rest_of_the_line =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    (arguments_from_length 0i32 = count, arguments_from_length count) |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest an_empty_snapshot_is_refused_and_keeps_the_environment =\n    := refused =\n        catch_unwind_rust\n            (\\ () =>\n                environment_restored \"\" \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n                false\n            )\n            \\ _ => true\n    (refused, \"PATH\" |> get_environment_variable <> \"\")\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+)\n\n///> rust\ntest a_snapshot_is_usable_only_with_its_anchor_entry =\n    := current = environment_snapshot ()\n    := path_first = \"PATH=\" ++# get_environment_variable \"PATH\" ++# sm'.char_text 0u8 ++# current\n    (\n        environment_snapshot_usable \"\",\n        environment_snapshot_usable \"PATH2=x\",\n        environment_snapshot_usable path_first,\n        environment_snapshot_usable current\n    )\n    |> _assert_eq (!-, !-, !+, !+)\n\n///> rust\ntest an_environment_snapshot_restores_to_itself =\n    := before = environment_snapshot ()\n    environment_restored before \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n    (sm'.length before > 0i32, environment_snapshot () = before, \"PATH2\" |> get_environment_variable)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+, \"\")\n  >>> with <<<\n:= empty_snapshot_refused () : bool =\n    catch_unwind_rust\n        (\\ () =>\n            environment_restored \"\" \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n            false\n        )\n        \\ _ => true\n\n///> rust\ntest an_empty_snapshot_is_refused_and_keeps_the_environment =\n    (empty_snapshot_refused (), \"PATH\" |> get_environment_variable <> \"\") |> _assert_eq (!+, !+)\n\n///> rust\ntest a_snapshot_without_its_anchor_entry_is_unusable =\n    (environment_snapshot_usable \"\", environment_snapshot_usable \"PATH2=x\") |> _assert_eq (!-, !-)\n\n:= path_first_snapshot (current : string) : string =\n    \"PATH=\" ++# get_environment_variable \"PATH\" ++# sm'.char_text 0u8 ++# current\n\n///> rust\ntest a_snapshot_is_usable_only_with_its_anchor_entry =\n    := current = environment_snapshot ()\n    (environment_snapshot_usable (path_first_snapshot current), environment_snapshot_usable current)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+)\n\n:= restored_to_itself (before : string) : bool =\n    environment_restored before \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n    environment_snapshot () = before\n\n///> rust\ntest an_environment_snapshot_restores_to_itself =\n    := before = environment_snapshot ()\n    (sm'.length before > 0i32, restored_to_itself before, \"PATH2\" |> get_environment_variable)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+, \"\")\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n        ?> [\"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\"]\n        |: [\"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\"; \"HOME\"]\n  >>> with <<<\n        ?> [ \"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\" ]\n        |: [ \"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\"; \"HOME\" ]\n  >>>\nedit env.spi expect files 1 replacements 2\n  replace once <<<\n        := env_sep =\n            ? platform.is_windows ()\n            ?> \";\"\n            |: \":\"\n  >>> with <<<\n        := env_sep = ? platform.is_windows () ?> \";\" |: \":\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n:= rust_restored (snapshot : string) (kept_prefix : string) : () =\n    := wanted = sm'.split (sm'.char_text 0u8) snapshot\n    := current = sm'.split (sm'.char_text 0u8) (environment_snapshot ())\n  >>> with <<<\n:= nul_split (text : string) = sm'.split (sm'.char_text 0u8) text\n\n:= rust_restored (snapshot : string) (kept_prefix : string) : () =\n    := wanted = nul_split snapshot\n    := current = nul_split (environment_snapshot ())\n  >>>")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_5 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 5u32, "2026-10-31T18:30Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 14:3x tibia: PART 1 LANDED inside the process slice (LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS n5 and n6, process.spi -> BE258A03A77A9E1A). The 6 process_command_* builders are under the limit on the live file. PART 2 (env: nul_split, append_path) re-anchored onto main's frozen base D6A498FCFA13E169, together with the env tests (the F# retire removed 3 ///> fsharp targets that the old anchors carried) -> C66DDE65E676F77F; node gate queued in run2. Still deferred: threading.partial_eq_wrapper_arc_eq (needs a Rust identity probe), env os_environ/environ_get (no row compiles their Gleam/Lua arms), and the rest of the near-limit pool (POSTABLE n151: TLD dots do not cover the excess there).")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_6 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 6u32, "2026-10-31T18:55Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 14:5x tibia: ENV SLICE RE-PROVEN on the frozen base (supersedes n4; the F# retire removed 3 ///> fsharp targets from the anchored tests, now dropped from the program too). Control 9/9 GREEN; candidate 10/10 on every row; negative 8 failed, CAUGHT; overweight 15 after. Gate: node mirror tibia-gates re-synced 14:2x (REMOTE-SYNC-OK digest A6842A82921F0194), lib-program-gate.ps1 -Control, eoie.exe, inside main's 14:12-16:30 freeze. Formatter clean, round trip ok.\nLAND: land-lib-program.ps1 -Note LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS/<this note> -File \"env.spi\" -Base D6A498FCFA13E169 -Target C66DDE65E676F77F\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\n\nedit env.spi expect files 1 replacements 7\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest remove_environment_variable =\n    set_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\" \"set\"\n    remove_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n    \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n    |> get_environment_variable\n    |> _assert_eq \"\"\n  >>> with <<<\n:= removed_probe () : string =\n    set_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\" \"set\"\n    remove_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n    get_environment_variable \"SPIRAL_ENV_REMOVE_PROBE\"\n\n///> gleam\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest remove_environment_variable =\n    removed_probe () |> _assert_eq \"\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> gleam\n///> lua\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset =\n    := is_set var =\n        ?= var |> try_get_environment_variable ?|\n        | Some _ => 1i32\n        | None => 0i32\n    (is_set \"PATH2\", is_set \"PATH\")\n    |> _assert_eq (0i32, 1i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= variable_is_set (var : string) : i32 =\n    ?= var |> try_get_environment_variable ?|\n    | Some _ => 1i32\n    | None => 0i32\n\n///> gleam\n///> lua\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest try_get_environment_variable_is_none_when_unset =\n    (variable_is_set \"PATH2\", variable_is_set \"PATH\") |> _assert_eq (0i32, 1i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest command_line_arguments_outside_the_range_are_none =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    := is_set index =\n        ?= index |> try_command_line_argument ?|\n        | Some _ => 1i32\n        | None => 0i32\n    (count >= 0i32, is_set (-1i32), is_set count)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32, 0i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= argument_is_set (index : i32) : i32 =\n    ?= index |> try_command_line_argument ?|\n    | Some _ => 1i32\n    | None => 0i32\n\n///> cuda\n///> rust\n///> typescript\ntest command_line_arguments_outside_the_range_are_none =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    (count >= 0i32, argument_is_set (-1i32), argument_is_set count)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32, 0i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest command_line_arguments_list_every_argument_in_order =\n    := listed = command_line_arguments ()\n    := head_is_first (head : string) = ?= try_command_line_argument 0i32 ?| | Some a => a = head | None => !-\n    := first_matches = ?= listed ?| | head :: _ => head_is_first head | [] => command_line_argument_count () = 0i32\n    (listm.length listed, first_matches) |> _assert_eq (command_line_argument_count (), !+)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= head_is_first_argument (head : string) : bool =\n    ?= try_command_line_argument 0i32 ?|\n    | Some a => a = head\n    | None => !-\n\n:= first_argument_matches (listed : list string) : bool =\n    ?= listed ?|\n    | head :: _ => head_is_first_argument head\n    | [] => command_line_argument_count () = 0i32\n\n///> rust\n///> gleam\ntest command_line_arguments_list_every_argument_in_order =\n    := listed = command_line_arguments ()\n    (listm.length listed, first_argument_matches listed) |> _assert_eq (command_line_argument_count (), !+)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest command_line_arguments_from_cover_the_rest_of_the_line =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    := all : i32 = listm.length (command_line_arguments_from 0i32)\n    := past : i32 = listm.length (command_line_arguments_from count)\n    (all = count, past)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32)\n  >>> with <<<\n:= arguments_from_length (index : i32) : i32 = listm.length (command_line_arguments_from index)\n\n///> rust\ntest command_line_arguments_from_cover_the_rest_of_the_line =\n    := count = command_line_argument_count ()\n    (arguments_from_length 0i32 = count, arguments_from_length count) |> _assert_eq (!+, 0i32)\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n///> rust\ntest an_empty_snapshot_is_refused_and_keeps_the_environment =\n    := refused =\n        catch_unwind_rust\n            (\\ () =>\n                environment_restored \"\" \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n                false\n            )\n            \\ _ => true\n    (refused, \"PATH\" |> get_environment_variable <> \"\")\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+)\n\n///> rust\ntest a_snapshot_is_usable_only_with_its_anchor_entry =\n    := current = environment_snapshot ()\n    := path_first = \"PATH=\" ++# get_environment_variable \"PATH\" ++# sm'.char_text 0u8 ++# current\n    (\n        environment_snapshot_usable \"\",\n        environment_snapshot_usable \"PATH2=x\",\n        environment_snapshot_usable path_first,\n        environment_snapshot_usable current\n    )\n    |> _assert_eq (!-, !-, !+, !+)\n\n///> rust\ntest an_environment_snapshot_restores_to_itself =\n    := before = environment_snapshot ()\n    environment_restored before \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n    (sm'.length before > 0i32, environment_snapshot () = before, \"PATH2\" |> get_environment_variable)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+, \"\")\n  >>> with <<<\n:= empty_snapshot_refused () : bool =\n    catch_unwind_rust\n        (\\ () =>\n            environment_restored \"\" \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n            false\n        )\n        \\ _ => true\n\n///> rust\ntest an_empty_snapshot_is_refused_and_keeps_the_environment =\n    (empty_snapshot_refused (), \"PATH\" |> get_environment_variable <> \"\") |> _assert_eq (!+, !+)\n\n///> rust\ntest a_snapshot_without_its_anchor_entry_is_unusable =\n    (environment_snapshot_usable \"\", environment_snapshot_usable \"PATH2=x\") |> _assert_eq (!-, !-)\n\n:= path_first_snapshot (current : string) : string =\n    \"PATH=\" ++# get_environment_variable \"PATH\" ++# sm'.char_text 0u8 ++# current\n\n///> rust\ntest a_snapshot_is_usable_only_with_its_anchor_entry =\n    := current = environment_snapshot ()\n    (environment_snapshot_usable (path_first_snapshot current), environment_snapshot_usable current)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+)\n\n:= restored_to_itself (before : string) : bool =\n    environment_restored before \"SPIRAL_KEPT_\"\n    environment_snapshot () = before\n\n///> rust\ntest an_environment_snapshot_restores_to_itself =\n    := before = environment_snapshot ()\n    (sm'.length before > 0i32, restored_to_itself before, \"PATH2\" |> get_environment_variable)\n    |> _assert_eq (!+, !+, \"\")\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n        ?> [\"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\"]\n        |: [\"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\"; \"HOME\"]\n  >>> with <<<\n        ?> [ \"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\" ]\n        |: [ \"PATH\"; \"SystemRoot\"; \"TEMP\"; \"TMP\"; \"USERPROFILE\"; \"LOCALAPPDATA\"; \"APPDATA\"; \"HOME\" ]\n  >>>\nedit env.spi expect files 1 replacements 2\n  replace once <<<\n        := env_sep =\n            ? platform.is_windows ()\n            ?> \";\"\n            |: \":\"\n  >>> with <<<\n        := env_sep = ? platform.is_windows () ?> \";\" |: \":\"\n  >>>\n  replace once <<<\n:= rust_restored (snapshot : string) (kept_prefix : string) : () =\n    := wanted = sm'.split (sm'.char_text 0u8) snapshot\n    := current = sm'.split (sm'.char_text 0u8) (environment_snapshot ())\n  >>> with <<<\n:= nul_split (text : string) = sm'.split (sm'.char_text 0u8) text\n\n:= rust_restored (snapshot : string) (kept_prefix : string) : () =\n    := wanted = nul_split snapshot\n    := current = nul_split (environment_snapshot ())\n  >>>")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_7 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 7u32, "2026-10-31T20:38Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 16:3x tibia: parts 1 and 2 LANDED (process builders in process.spi BE258A03; env nul_split and append_path in env.spi C66DDE65; POSTABLE n157). Left in this item, each needing its own proof shape: process started_pid (+8) and exit_with (+23); env env_gleam_argv (+8), os_environ (+13) and environ_get (+18), whose Gleam/Lua arms no test row compiles; threading partial_eq_wrapper_arc_eq (layout-only, but it needs a Rust identity probe because threading has only F# rows). env process_id no longer counts: main's headings wave took it under the limit.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_8 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 8u32, "2026-10-31T20:42Z", "tibia-lane", "10-31 16:4x tibia: STOPPED here on purpose. process started_pid (+8) and exit_with (+23) have no structural fix; the only cheap cut is shortening their 'no arm for this backend' failwith text, which breaks the lib's error-message convention. PROPOSAL for lib's owners: the fallback arm is repeated across lib (24 occurrences in 9 files). A shared helper (e.g. := no_arm (name : string) = failwith (name ++# ': no arm for this backend'), used as | _ => \\ () => no_arm 'process.started_pid') keeps every message and saves about 18 characters per arm, which is enough to fit several near-limit cells at once. It is new lib API, so it is not tibia's call; filed here as the remaining lever for this item.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_9 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 9u32, "2026-11-01T03:43Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 tibia NEXT STEP (CPU-light drafting; one short compile at the end): a Rust identity probe for threading.partial_eq_wrapper_arc_eq: a tiny entry that calls new_partial_eq_wrapper_arc, compiled to Rust against a lib copy before and after the layout-only collapse, outputs compared byte for byte. The no_arm helper proposal (n8) waits on lib's owners.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_10 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 10u32, "2026-11-01T12:36Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 08:36 tibia QUALITY PASS. DEFINITION OF DONE: 'mix spiral.cell_budget --check' over lib/spiral reports 0 over_budget findings for tibia's lib share (process' 6 process_command_* builders and threading's partial_eq_wrapper definitions; their weights are listed in the title); each split is landed through land-lib-program.ps1 with its lib program gate green on the node (-Negative mutant failing) and a Rust identity probe showing byte-identical generated Rust before and after for the layout-only splits. TYPEFEATURESET: these are layout-only splits of existing definitions, so the types must stay identical. The probe is the guard: any split that changes a signature is out of scope and is filed separately. NEXT STEP (n9): the identity probe entry that calls threading.new_partial_eq_wrapper_arc, compiled to Rust against a lib copy before and after the split, then diff. It depends on LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-TESTS.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_11 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 11u32, "2026-11-01T23:48Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 19:5x tibia, SCOPE IS STALE, census redone before any split: 'mix spiral.cell_budget' over live lib process.spi, env.spi and threading.spi now reports 45 over_budget definitions (process 23, env 15, threading 7), weights up to 10,470 (process.spi:496) and 5,269 (:710). This item was scoped to a handful of definitions 'overweight by 30 or less' (process_command_* at 287-302 vs 271). Something since then (today's :: respell land, the lib-reshape worker's R1a, or a change in what the budget counts) moved these files by orders of magnitude, so the old per-definition plan no longer fits. Decision: paused, no splits now, because 45 splits in files the lib-reshape worker is moving tonight would collide with its lands. Resume when the reshape posts 'landed' for process/env/threading. First step then: rerun this census and decide per file whether a reshape split already covers it. CORRECTION 20:0x: wrong conclusion above. The large weights (process.spi:496 execute_with_options_fsharp at 10,470, etc.) were always far over and were never this item's scope (title: 'overweight by 30 or less'). The reshape worker confirms it doesn't touch process/env/threading, so the item is resumed. Near-limit set today (within 40): process rust_waited +37, captured_by +23, an unnamed block at :1082 +20; env os_environ +10, environ_get +15, env_gleam_argv +7, get_entry_assembly_name +37. The six process_command_* builders are no longer over.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_12 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 12u32, "2026-11-02T00:07Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 20:1x tibia: env_gleam_argv (+7) FIXED and LANDED 19:59 (env.spi A29618D78B8C -> 889C7D7D58CF, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-195947): its multi-line 'global \\\"\\\"\\\"' block (the @external attribute plus the fn line) became two one-line globals, which also heals the multi-line-host-block drift. IDENTITY PROBE (the DoD's guard for layout-only changes): an entry calling env::host_argument_count and env::host_argument, compiled to Gleam against a lib copy before and after: 841 bytes both, identical hash. Close: 14 signatures unchanged, spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22, type_probe PASS (15 tests typed). Remaining near-limit set: env os_environ +10, environ_get +15, get_entry_assembly_name +37; process rust_waited +37, exit_with +20 (the :1082 block), captured_by +23. The last two exceed only through their 'failwith \\\"...: no arm for this backend\\\"' messages, so they wait on n8's no_arm helper decision rather than message edits that would change emitted code.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_13 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 13u32, "2026-11-02T15:03Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia groom: not touched in more than 12 h, so Planned (WIP cap). The no_arm question blocking exit_with and captured_by is a technical call this lane makes (fiscal star-exchange lesson: decide by a rule written before looking, and record the rule and the outcome). At the next pull: write the rule, decide, then land.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_14 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 14u32, "2026-11-04T14:25Z", "tibia", "11-04 10:25 tibia, NO_ARM DECIDED: the rule, written before looking: adopt a shared helper for the 'X: no arm for this backend' failure iff (1) the runtime message stays byte-identical, (2) at least 3 sites use it, (3) no test or consumer matches on the text in a way it would break. Evidence: 28 sites in 10 lib files (process 7, sm' 4, xml 3, convert 3, ...); no consumer greps the text; probes show the message identical. C output is BYTE-IDENTICAL (the partial evaluator folds name ++ suffix into the old literal); Rust uses the folded literal too but keeps the two piece literals as dead thread_local bindings (codegen observation, reported to compiler). So: ADOPT. Placement by import graph: convert is the lowest user (sm' depends on it), the prelude cannot concatenate strings (base's ++ is the append prototype, which string does not satisfy), and backend.spi reaching sm'_real makes a module cycle. So a new lib module unsupported.spi (no_arm_message, no_arm, test a_missing_arm_names_its_function on c/rust/gleam) depending only on sm'_real. Draft drafts spiral\\LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS\\noarm: unsupported.spi + process.spi with all 7 sites as no_arm \"name\" (:< unsupported). process over-budget cells 21 -> 19 (exit_with's cell and captured_by healed). Box gate queued behind main's pack35 install. The other 9 files follow in later lands.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_15 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:04Z", "tibia", "11-04 11:04 tibia: REMAINING SET, measured today: of the cells in this item's title, process_command_*, started_pid, process_id, append_path, rust_restored, env_gleam_argv and threading's partial_eq_wrapper_arc_eq are no longer over. In the noarm draft (gate queued behind main's pack35 install): exit_with's cell and captured_by heal through no_arm; rust_waited (+37) heals through a timed_out helper (process 21 -> 18 over); env get_entry_assembly_name (+37) heals through an fsharp_entry_name helper (env 14 -> 13). IDENTITY: C output byte-identical for a program using captured_by, exit_with and kill_tree_of_pid (1512 B, same hash); Rust output byte-identical for start_logging + await_exit_within, which runs the rust_waited loop (2772 B, same hash). NOT shrinkable as is: env os_environ (+10) and environ_get (+15). Dropping the ': os_environ' / ': string' ascriptions on their failwith arms gives ETY-ValueRestriction (probe on Python and Gleam). Swapping backend_switch for run_target with a _ arm would turn other backends' host compile error (backend_switch_has_no_X_arm placeholder) into a runtime failwith, a behaviour change, so they stay. Next land after this one: noarm2 (sm'.spi and unicode.spi, all 6 sites, each heals one cell: sm' 91 -> 90, unicode 9 -> 8).")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_16 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 16u32, "2026-11-04T16:56Z", "tibia", "11-04 12:56 tibia: noarm GATE READ AGAINST A CONTROL. Box gate (after main's pack35 install): unsupported.spi positive 1/1 and 0 type errors, mutant (message says target) fails exactly a_missing_arm_names_its_function; process.spi draft 16/18, env.spi draft 10/16. CONTROL, the same gate on the UNMODIFIED live files: process 11/18, env 14/16, with the failing targets moving between runs (fsharp, gleam, lua, typescript, rust) and 300 s cell timeouts: the saturated box, not code. process: every draft failure (split_args/split_command fsharp) also fails in the control. env: the draft's lua and gleam failures were not in the control, so identity was checked directly: a program calling get_environment_variable, command_line_arguments and try_get_environment_variable compiles BYTE-IDENTICALLY with live and draft env.spi on Lua (2184 B), Gleam (1884 B) and Rust (2535 B); C and Rust identity for process were shown earlier. So the drafts cannot cause those failures. Landing unsupported.spi (new) + process.spi + env.spi through lib_land_window now.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_17 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 17u32, "2026-11-04T17:19Z", "tibia", "11-04 13:19 tibia: noarm LAND ATTEMPTS. #1 CLOSE FAILED and undone: document_test's notebook round trip (parse_spi -> livemd -> to_spi_tested) rejected unsupported.spi because the new file had no final LF (a 15-line mix run over the drafts showed the first difference at line 14, nil vs an empty line); process/env round-trip exactly. Fixed (unsupported 63F2E25F272E -> 8D785A539A4A, newline only). #2 CLOSE FAILED and undone: signatures 4 unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22 passed, respell 0, but type_probe gave unsupported.spi VOID (control error missing, exit 5; first output line a raw TypeErrors dump at character 4, i.e. the whole probe compile failed). The same probe on a scratch lib with the same three files: PASS, control ok. The probe writes its module into the lib it checks (the live lib during a land) while tibia's box gate compiled against the live lib through deps\\spiral at the same time, which is the suspected cause, not proven. #3 running; if it voids again it reruns with nothing else compiling against the live lib.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_18 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 18u32, "2026-11-04T17:25Z", "tibia", "11-04 13:25 tibia, noarm LANDED green (attempt #3): new lib module unsupported.spi (no_arm_message, no_arm, test a_missing_arm_names_its_function) 8D785A539A4A; process.spi A3BAFCF670B8 -> 9DD18D6D3EF1 (7 sites as no_arm, timed_out helper for rust_waited); env.spi DF0A07FB3677 -> 4BDC76E5E01F (fsharp_entry_name helper). Close: consumer signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe PASS on all 3 (control ok), 0 respell drift; lib digest 66C2F5D06D25CD39; undo lib-land-undo\\20261104-131836. Over-budget cells: process 21 -> 18, env 14 -> 13 (exit_with's cell, captured_by, rust_waited, get_entry_assembly_name healed). CORRECTION to the attempt-#2 note: the tibia box gate was again compiling against the live lib during this attempt and the probe passed, so the #2 VOID was transient and concurrent compilation is NOT shown as its cause. Next: noarm2 (sm' + unicode, all 6 sites, heals one cell each) gate queued on the box, with a live control in the same window.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_19 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 19u32, "2026-11-04T17:50Z", "tibia", "11-04 13:50 tibia: noarm3 drafted (drafts LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS\\noarm3): xml (3 sites), unix_clock (2), file_system (1; its fallback_write_bytes message has a different form, 'file_system.write_bytes / no arm...', so it stays as is), platform (1), env (1, process_id). Two files CANNOT take the helper, both for placement reasons: convert (sm'_real calls convert::, so convert -> unsupported -> sm'_real is a module cycle) and am' (it defines the array instance of the append prototype that seq.to_array relies on without importing am'; adding ':< unsupported' moves am' after seq in the derived module order, giving 'ETY-InstanceNotFound: array does not have the prototype append' in seq.spi). IDENTITY for the five: C output BYTE-IDENTICAL (2075 B, all 8 messages folded to the old literals); runtime messages identical on Lua and Rust, but their code differs: Lua does not fold the concatenation (it now builds name .. ': no arm for this backend' at run time), and Rust keeps the two dead literals next to the folded one (both already reported to compiler). Gate after noarm2.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_20 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 20u32, "2026-11-04T21:27Z", "tibia", "11-04 17:27 tibia: noarm3 IDENTITY across every backend its files' tests target: one probe calling all 8 converted functions (code_point_at, code_point_width, is_file, unix_now_ms, unix_now_nanos, read_text_or_empty, os_command_output, process_id), live vs drafts. C: byte-identical. Lua, Rust, Pascal, Zig, F#, Gleam: the runtime message is identical in every case; the code differs only in how the message is built (each backend except C builds name + ': no arm for this backend' at run time, Rust also keeps dead literals, Zig allocates the joined string through its allocator, all on the failure path only) plus variable renumbering. TypeScript: the probe does not compile on live either, so not comparable. Gate (box, control vs draft per file, full failure lists): unix_clock control 1/1, draft 0/1, a Gleam cell timeout ('timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed'); the Gleam, Rust and F# output for both unix_clock functions is byte-identical live vs draft, so the draft cannot cause it. platform control 2/2, draft 2/2. env, xml, file_system pending.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_21 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 21u32, "2026-11-04T22:03Z", "tibia", "11-04 18:03 tibia: noarm2 GATE READ. sm' (box, control then draft, full failure lists, the noarm3 gate running at the same time): control 67/83, draft 52/83, 40 draft-only failing test/target pairs (builder_*, pad_right, range, replace*, trim_*, lines, length, searches, utf8 bytes, over rust/gleam/fsharp/pascal/zig/lua/c/typescript); both runs ended in 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed'. The draft changes only char_text, bytes_between, all_digits, split_nth (no_arm) and adds ':< unsupported'. IDENTITY on the failing functions: a program using string_builder, builder_append, builder_replace, builder_clear, replicate, trim_end_suffix, replace and lines compiles BYTE-IDENTICALLY live vs draft on Rust (3534 B), Lua (4938 B), Gleam (7271 B), F# (3028 B) and Zig (9511 B); C and Pascal do not compile that probe on live either. With the earlier C/Rust identity of the four changed functions, the draft-only failures are in code the draft does not change: box timeouts, not the change. unicode: draft failures were a subset of control's. Landing noarm2.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_22 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 22u32, "2026-11-04T22:25Z", "tibia", "11-04 18:25 tibia, noarm2 LANDED green: sm'.spi EE0997C518D1 -> B0854BB9B5D7 (4 sites: char_text, bytes_between, all_digits, split_nth) and unicode.spi DCBB8F58895D -> 062491CC0670 (2 sites), both opening unsupported. Close: 30 consumer-used signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe modules 2 pass 2 (sm' with an informational shadowed-name note, 0 errors), 0 respell drift; lib digest D2DFF6523EBF643B; undo lib-land-undo\\20261104-181350. Over-budget cells: sm' 91 -> 90, unicode 9 -> 8. noarm3 gate: xml 15/15 = control, platform 2/2 = control, env and unix_clock each one draft-only failure in code shown byte-identical live vs draft (env: Lua get_environment_variable; unix_clock: a Gleam cell timeout); file_system still running.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_23 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 23u32, "2026-11-04T22:50Z", "tibia", "11-04 18:50 tibia: noarm3 GATE COMPLETE (box, control then draft per file, full failure lists): file_system 39/42 vs 39/42, draft-only 0; xml 15/15 vs 15/15; platform 2/2 vs 2/2; env 9/16 vs 10/16 with one draft-only (get_environment_variable on Lua; Lua code byte-identical live vs draft, 2184 B); unix_clock 1/1 vs 0/1 (a Gleam cell timeout; Gleam/Rust/F# code byte-identical). Every draft-only failure is in code the draft does not change. Landing noarm3 (xml, unix_clock, file_system, platform, env) now.")
inl note_of_lib_xcompat_tibia_defs_24 () = Note ("LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS", 24u32, "2026-11-04T22:59Z", "tibia", "11-04 18:59 tibia, DONE: noarm3 LANDED green (xml B6EED09BD255 -> 3D9AC9274C8A, unix_clock 03D6F2285043 -> 008A014025C6, file_system 76CA7B4DE0CB -> A981A5951BF8, platform 27CD099C4C55 -> 56E326380CF7, env 4BDC76E5E01F -> A3B25AAC97FD): 16 consumer signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe modules 5 pass 5, 0 respell drift; lib digest 2C78D532B74C5E97; undo lib-land-undo\\20261104-185043. ITEM SUMMARY: the near-limit definition cells named in the title are either healed or no longer over (process_command_*, started_pid, process_id, append_path, rust_restored, env_gleam_argv, partial_eq_wrapper_arc_eq, exit_with, captured_by, rust_waited, get_entry_assembly_name), through three lands today: noarm (new lib module unsupported with no_arm, process, env), noarm2 (sm', unicode) and noarm3 (xml, unix_clock, file_system, platform, env). The shared no_arm helper now covers 21 of the lib's 27 'no arm for this backend' sites (process 7, sm' 4, unicode 2, xml 3, unix_clock 2, file_system 1, platform 1, env 1); the other 6 stay for recorded reasons (convert: module cycle through sm'_real; am': it defines the array append instance seq relies on, and a new import reorders it after seq; file_system.fallback_write_bytes: a differently worded message). Kept over on purpose: env os_environ (+10) and environ_get (+15), whose failwith ascriptions are load-bearing (ValueRestriction without them) and whose backend_switch failure mode run_target would change. Codegen notes sent to compiler: Rust keeps dead literal bindings after folding; Lua, Pascal, Zig, F#, Gleam do not fold the concatenation (the message is built at run time on the failure path).")
inl sim_x_serve_users () = Task ("SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", "x sim: serve skeleton (sim-run.ps1 serve, gen_tcp listener, request log, forwarding to stub.ps1) plus the users/by and users-by-ids families", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "x,sim,spiral,e2e", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_sim_x_serve_users () = Planning ("SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_users_1 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", 1u32, "2026-10-31T12:39Z", "x", "2026-10-31 x: slice 1 of SIM-X-FEATURE-PARITY's server design (its n6): scripts/sim-run.ps1 serve WORLD PORTFILE LOG -> simframes export cli_serve; json:decode world + includes; gen_tcp {packet, http_bin} listener on 127.0.0.1:0, port file, accept loop, Connection: close; request log rows in stub.ps1's format; GET /2/users/by and /2/users served from the world, every other request forwarded to a child stub.ps1 on its own port. Proof: e2e.ps1 with XSIM_SERVER=sim gives the stub run's request rows (153 X rows in verify39/40) and exit codes.")
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_users_2 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", 2u32, "2026-10-31T13:11Z", "x", "2026-10-31 09:11 x: DRAFTED in x (unstaged). New module apps/sim/spi/sim_serve.spi (registered in spiral.toml after cells_executor): raw gen_tcp listener on 127.0.0.1:0 (port file), request read until headers + Content-Length bytes, request line/target/query parsed in Spiral, world = json:decode of world.json + its include list (users by lowercase handle and by id, ids as text), auth app/user bearer; GET /2/users/by (data for found handles, errors entries with X's resource-not-found shape for missing ones, each omitted when empty) and GET /2/users (data, always present) answered here with a request-log row {method, path, query, authorized, context} appended to the shared log; a request with no recognised bearer on those paths gets the stub's 401 problem; everything else, and any OAuth/Basic request, is relayed byte for byte to a child stub.ps1 that logs it itself. simframes exports cli_serve; scripts/sim-run.ps1 serve WORLD PORTFILE LOG starts stub.ps1 (own port file, same log), passes its port, and stops it on exit. apps/client/e2e/e2e.ps1: XSIM_SERVER=sim starts sim-run.ps1 serve instead of stub.ps1, and the server is stopped as a process tree (taskkill /T) since the sim server has children. Local: x-compat 0 in 30 files, kit standards 0, no line over 120. PRE-REGISTERED x-serveprobe (scratchpad launcher, xqueue3): sim build exit 0 (compiles sim_serve), client build exit 0, then e2e.ps1 with XSIM_SERVER=sim. PASS = e2e exit 0 with 'RUST-OK x/apps/client / e2e: 37 tutorial steps and 5 extra cases' and its request count line equal to the stub runs' (153 in verify39/40).")
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_users_3 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", 3u32, "2026-10-31T13:26Z", "x", "2026-10-31 09:26 x: x-serveprobe (job-1793452650241, 16 s) RED at compile, nothing run: (1) the record type 'world' collides with the package module world.spi (ETY-ModuleMustBeImmediatelyApplied at every '(w : world)'), renamed api_world; (2) a multi-line record TYPE needs ';' at the end of a continued line (parser 'Expected: }' at sim_serve.spi:111), added. Local x-compat 0, standards 0. Relaunching as x-serveprobe2, n2's rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_users_4 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", 4u32, "2026-10-31T13:54Z", "x", "2026-10-31 09:54 x: x-serveprobe2 (job-1793453501503, 19 min, xqueue3) by n2's rule: PASS. Sim build exit 0 (sim_serve compiles in the Gleam frames build), client build exit 0, e2e.ps1 with XSIM_SERVER=sim exit 0: 'RUST-OK x/apps/client / e2e: 37 tutorial steps and 5 extra cases', '153 requests to the stub' (the stub runs' count), the sim worlds, Mastodon and Bluesky sections unchanged. CAVEAT, stated plainly: the rule cannot tell answered-by-sim from forwarded-to-stub, since both write identical log rows; e2e passing proves the server skeleton, the forwarding and the launcher, but not that /2/users/by and /2/users were answered by the sim. Closed in the next slice: sim_serve writes 'xsim serve / answered <method> <path>' to stderr for every request it answers itself, and SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING's probe counts those lines (pre-registered there). Item stays open until that count shows the users families answered by the sim.")
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_users_5 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", 5u32, "2026-10-31T14:45Z", "x", "2026-10-31 10:45 x: n4's caveat SETTLED by x-serveprobe4 (SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING n4): the sim answered 19 x GET /2/users/by and 3 x GET /2/users itself (its own stderr lines), and e2e passed with the stub's 153 rows. DONE.")
