inl note_of_data_dir_home_26 () = Note ("DATA-DIR-HOME", 26u32, "2026-11-04T11:03Z", "tibia", "11-04 07:0x tibia: tibia share NOW REALLY DONE (my 11-03 check matched only names containing tibia and missed these; fiscal's 02:32 note flagged them). In C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28 tibia owned canary-tables.sql (47 tables, the 10-28 rescue that rebuilt MariaDB on 10-29), canary-active_livestream_casters.sql, the two header-only EMPTY dumps (tibia-mariadb-all.EMPTY-first-attempt.sql, mysql-system-tables.EMPTY-not-dumpable.sql) and the emptied dir mariadb-data-emptied-20261029-0727. Check: tibia's newest daily dump (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\tibia-mariadb-dumps\\canary-20261104-052005.sql, 73 KB) contains all 47 rescue tables plus one newer, and the live DB it dumps was rebuilt from that rescue, so the rescue is superseded. Archived with scratch-archive.ps1 -Root rescue-2026-10-28 -Only tibia-canary-rescue -Apply (dry run first; 5 files, blob verify failures 0) and removed; restore: -Restore C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\archive\\20261104-070324\\manifest.tsv -RestoreTo <dir>. What remains in the rescue tree is other lanes' (kit-bundles, node-temp, toolchain-zips, profile snapshot, startmenu package, the .tsv and loss-map evidence files).")
inl note_of_data_dir_home_27 () = Note ("DATA-DIR-HOME", 27u32, "2026-11-05T05:38Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 01:3x kit: kit share DONE. C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\kit-bundles (88 MB, 10036 files) was kit's 10-29 recovery material: kit-bundles-20261029.tar (train3/train4 bundles + m5-commit-bundle), merge-m5.ps1/merge-tree.ps1, and merged-lib* / merged-m5* lib merge working copies. All superseded: trains since reached TRAIN14c installed and TRAIN27 running, and lib has landed past those merges. Archived with scratch-archive.ps1 -Root C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28 -Only kit-bundles (dry run first, then -Apply; blob verify failures 0) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261105-013524; restore with -Restore '...\\20261105-013524\\manifest.tsv' -RestoreTo <dir>. No other kit-named path under C:\\home\\data (machine-tools is empty; main-drafts, node-checkout-only-2026-10-29* and the rest of rescue-2026-10-28 are not kit's).")
inl note_of_data_dir_home_28 () = Note ("DATA-DIR-HOME", 28u32, "2026-11-05T05:52Z", "compiler", "11-05 01:5x compiler: compiler share DONE. C:\\home\\data\\rescue-2026-10-28\\toolchain-zips held the two FreePascal trunk snapshot zips (fpc-3.3.1.i386-win32.zip 320759F0DC48DA0A, 86 MB; fpc-3.3.1.x86_64-win64.built.on.i386-win32.zip 2206D8D866360844, 79 MB). They are the exact 3.3.1-21298 build that the Pascal backend's native runs use (baseline toolchain.tsv: scoop freepascal\\3.3.1-20261025), and rolling trunk snapshots can't be re-downloaded, so they are KEPT, not archived: moved (same-drive rename, sha256 identical before and after) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\toolchains\\fpc-trunk-3.3.1-21298-zips, beside the other compiler toolchains (calyx-src, bend, wgsl-run), which the profile mirror copies to the node. Use them to rebuild FPC on the box or the node (FPC-TRUNK-EVERYWHERE recipe). No other compiler-owned path under C:\\home\\data. What remains is not compiler's: node-temp, profile-snapshot-20261028-2137, startmenu-package-before-reset-2026-10-30, stray-programs-in-spiral (7 Start-menu .lnk shortcuts), the rescue .tsv/.md evidence files, main-drafts, node-checkout-only-2026-10-29*, empty machine-tools.")
inl note_of_data_dir_home_29 () = Note ("DATA-DIR-HOME", 29u32, "2026-11-05T23:12Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:1x MAIN SHARE: (1) main-drafts\\commit-suggestion.md (37 KB, a pre-commit summary 11-01..11-04) DELETED as stale: every change it listed was committed by the user (698bc3da, 98e51d32, faf422c9 at 11-04 23:18). (2) machine-tools (empty) removed. (3) node-checkout-only-2026-10-29 (the node's spiral checkout at d095f13d 10-25 + its tracked.patch, extracted during the wipe recovery): 324 files hash-checked against all kit archive manifests (33,767 hashes) and the live spiral tree; 66 had no copy (old versions of apps/spiral/spiral.spi etc. and node-only lab/ scripts), so it was ARCHIVED, not deleted: scratch-archive 20261105-191036 (apps, lab, + 1 folder, 324 files, verify 0 failures) and 20261105-191147 (the zip + HEAD.txt + tracked.patch, 3 files, hashes identical before and after the move). C:\\home\\data now holds only rescue-2026-10-28 (node-temp 182 MB, profile-snapshot, startmenu-package backup, loss-map.md, path TSVs: the 10-28 wipe recovery), main's last share, which needs a per-file check against the live profile and the mirror before it goes.")
inl note_of_data_dir_home_30 () = Note ("DATA-DIR-HOME", 30u32, "2026-11-05T23:17Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:1x DRAINED: rescue-2026-10-28 (11,912 files, 0.18 GB) ARCHIVED with scratch-archive 20261105-191452 (unique content 0.14 GB, blobs.zip 0.10 GB, verify 0 failures). Its 13 symlinks (into node paths C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\... and C:\\home\\remote\\<mirror>\\...) were recorded, not followed; 0 of 13 targets exist on the box, checked before removal. C:\\home\\data is now EMPTY. DoD met: every lane's folders went home or to the verified archive.")
inl sim_x_serve_following () = Task ("SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING", "x sim: serve GET /2/users/:id/following from the world (paging by p<n> tokens, following_page_size, the 1..1000 max_results check)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "SIM-X-SERVE-USERS", "x,sim,spiral,e2e", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_sim_x_serve_following () = Planning ("SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_following_1 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING", 1u32, "2026-10-31T13:42Z", "x", "2026-10-31 x: slice 2 of SIM-X-FEATURE-PARITY (its n7): GET /2/users/:id/following in sim_serve.spi, ported from stub.ps1 Get-Following (lines 211-221): max_results default 100, 1..1000 else 400 problem 'Invalid Request' / 'max_results must be 1..1000, got <v>'; start from pagination_token 'p<n>' (default p0); count = min(max_results, world.following_page_size); page of the user's 'following' ids resolved through users by id; meta {result_count, next_token 'p<start+count>' when more remain}; data only when the page is non-empty. Unknown user ids fall through to the stub's 404 (forwarded). Proof: e2e.ps1 with XSIM_SERVER=sim passes with the stub's request rows (the following steps run against carol, loner and mixed).")
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_following_2 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING", 2u32, "2026-10-31T13:58Z", "x", "2026-10-31 09:58 x: DRAFTED in sim_serve.spi (unstaged): GET /2/users/<known id>/following answered by the sim (max_results default 100, 1..1000 else 400 'Invalid Request' with the stub's detail; start from pagination_token p<n>; count = min(max_results, following_page_size from world.json); data omitted on an empty page; meta.result_count and next_token p<start+count> while more remain); unknown ids still forward (stub 404). problem(status, title, detail) replaces the fixed 401 body; status lines carry 200 OK / 400 Bad Request / 401 Unauthorized. NEW: every request the sim answers writes 'xsim serve / answered <method> <path>' to stderr. Local x-compat 0 in 30 files, standards 0. PRE-REGISTERED x-serveprobe3 (same launcher + an answered-lines summary; the lines are read from the job's stdout capture, else its stderr log): PASS = e2e exit 0, 'RUST-OK ... 37 tutorial steps and 5 extra cases', 153 requests, AND at least one 'answered GET /2/users/by' and at least one 'answered GET /2/users/<id>/following'. That also settles SIM-X-SERVE-USERS' caveat (its n4).")
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_following_3 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING", 3u32, "2026-10-31T14:09Z", "x", "2026-10-31 10:09 x: x-serveprobe3 (job-1793455381216, 74 s) RED at the sim build, nothing run: gleam-modules refused xsim_frames/part29 at 1,264 lines. Same mechanism as SIM-IN-SPIRAL n133: with ':=' everything under the recursive 'served' loop (handled -> replied -> answer -> routed -> following/users_by ...) inlined into ONE generated function, and slice 2 pushed it past 1,000. FIX: 21 multi-line mid-level definitions of sim_serve.spi made ':~' (header_value, request_of, included_users, world_of, not_found, users_by, users_by_ids, followed, following_body, following, log_row, logged, users_reply, routed, answer, relayed, forwarded, own_reply, replied, handled, started), so each is its own generated function (memory attribute-generated-lines: ':~' on a multi-line body cuts inlining). Relaunching as x-serveprobe4, n2's rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_sim_x_serve_following_4 () = Note ("SIM-X-SERVE-FOLLOWING", 4u32, "2026-10-31T14:40Z", "x", "2026-10-31 10:40 x: x-serveprobe4 (job-1793456011225, 25 min, xqueue3) by n2's rule: PASS. Sim build exit 0 (no part over 1,000 lines with the ':~' helpers), client build exit 0, e2e.ps1 with XSIM_SERVER=sim exit 0: 'RUST-OK x/apps/client / e2e: 37 tutorial steps and 5 extra cases', '153 requests' (the stub's count). Answered BY THE SIM (its stderr lines, counted): 6 x GET /2/users/<id>/following, 19 x GET /2/users/by, 3 x GET /2/users. So the tutorial's following steps (carol, loner, mixed, with p<n> paging) pass against the sim's own handler. DONE (code in x, unstaged; the next x verify covers it in the sim build).")
