inl planning_of_pack_11 () = Planning ("PACK-11", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_pack_11_1 () = Note ("PACK-11", 1u32, "2026-10-31T14:00Z", "compiler", "10-31 10:00 compiler: opened as the collector for the next compiler pack, built on PACK-10's installed tree. READY: packs/apply-host-server-parent-exit.ps1 (CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT n17; host only, so its predicted residual set is empty). CANDIDATES not ready: (1) a context-free missing-arm guard (SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD n13: check the emitted output instead of RustGapTrace.validating, so hopacsota's Defer agrees with single-flight); (2) packs/apply-hopacsota-deferred-validation.ps1 (HOPACSOTA-P3; needs its Waits bench, n58). NOT in this pack, each with its own review: apply-rust-mutual-tail-loops.ps1 (MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS rewrites Rust residuals) and apply-delphi-arc-records.ps1 (DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY, about 1.9x C speed to fix first). Method: re-run every applier's dry-run on the installed tree after PACK-10 lands, then build-candidate.ps1 and predict-residuals.ps1.")
inl note_of_pack_11_2 () = Note ("PACK-11", 2u32, "2026-10-31T14:06Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 10:06 compiler: candidate (1) is now DRAFTED: packs/apply-missing-arm-guard-output.ps1 (SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD n14), core, stacked on PACK-10's guard. Pack 11 core appliers so far: apply-missing-arm-guard-output.ps1. Host: apply-host-server-parent-exit.ps1.")
inl note_of_pack_11_3 () = Note ("PACK-11", 3u32, "2026-10-31T17:20Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 13:20 compiler: candidate (3), host cleanup: after PACK-10 the host still sets SPIRAL_BUILD_DEADLINE_MS for the core (Program.fs ~880-899, plus the SPIRAL_BUILD_BUDGET_MS read), but no reader is left in the single-flight/hopacsota core (it was gpt5parallel's stall watchdog). Drop it in the next host edit; the core-side BlockParsingGpt5parallel header and 5 gpt5parallel comments go with it (GPT5PARALLEL-RETIRE n10).")
inl note_of_pack_11_4 () = Note ("PACK-11", 4u32, "2026-10-31T17:30Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 13:30 compiler: candidate (3) DRAFTED: packs/apply-host-drop-build-deadline.ps1 (2 edits to the --batch loop: drop the SPIRAL_BUILD_BUDGET_MS probe and the per-job SPIRAL_BUILD_DEADLINE_MS export; the batch still enforces jobTimeoutMs via work.Wait). Anchors 1x on PACK-10's host source; scratch apply leaves 0 references; DONE guard trips; it stacks with apply-host-server-parent-exit.ps1 (3/3 anchors still 1x after it). With it, probe.ps1's SPIRAL_BUILD_BUDGET_MS line becomes dead too: drop it in the same land. Pack 11 so far: core apply-missing-arm-guard-output.ps1; host apply-host-server-parent-exit.ps1 + apply-host-drop-build-deadline.ps1.")
inl note_of_pack_11_5 () = Note ("PACK-11", 5u32, "2026-10-31T19:27Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 15:27 compiler: candidate (4) DRAFTED, a likely parse SPEED win, not only cleanup: packs/apply-core-drop-gpt5parallel-remnants.ps1 (7 edits on the live core = PACK-10's; dry-run clean, scratch apply 35,582 -> 35,459 lines, 0 gpt5parallel mentions left, DONE guard trips, stacks with the guard-v2 applier). Finding: after the retirement, BlockParsingGpt5parallel holds only observeParsedStatement (a no-op), but the block parser still calls it as 'observeParsedStatement (lineTokensStableIdentity block) statement', and F# evaluates the argument eagerly, so EVERY parsed block builds a string over every token (line/token counts, ranges, token payload text) and throws it away. The helper's own comment says the earlier digest version 'cost as much as the parse itself on lib/spiral'. The applier drops the hook, the call and the 8 helpers that only fed it (stableTokenTextField .. lineTokensStableIdentity; each scanned for outside references: none), and rewords the 5 comments that still name gpt5parallel. Output can't change (the value was discarded); to measure in the PACK-11 review: parse/compile wall on lib/spiral and apps/spiral (measure-arms, installed vs candidate). Pack 11 now: core apply-missing-arm-guard-output.ps1 + apply-core-drop-gpt5parallel-remnants.ps1; host apply-host-server-parent-exit.ps1 + apply-host-drop-build-deadline.ps1. Needs a heavy window (train6 holds heavy-build until ~19:30).")
inl note_of_pack_11_6 () = Note ("PACK-11", 6u32, "2026-10-31T19:35Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 15:35 compiler: STACK CHECKED and QUEUED. All 4 appliers stack onto the live (PACK-10) sources: core guard-output 4 edits + drop-gpt5parallel-remnants 7, host server-parent-exit 3 + drop-build-deadline 2. Candidate source sha16 core C0990B2D590CE965, host 420E1452DB4B3194. hopacsota-lint on the candidate core: G1 647 lines (budget 5,934; largest section 416 of 1,000), G2 0 banned hits outside the allowlist. Jobs: job-1793475264287-compiler-pack11-build (--heavy, waits for train6's heavy-build window), then job-1793475266761-compiler-pack11-predict (after-ok): predict-residuals.ps1 -Candidate pack11 -InstalledRun single-flight-20261031-051310 (PACK-10's own run, whose DLL is the installed one) -ReuseCompile. Pre-registered pass for this pack: P = 0 rows (no edit changes a residual: the guard now fails only when a marker reaches the output, and no committed output contains one; the rest is host lifecycle and dead code), 0 compile-status diffs, and verdict diffs only on rows whose old error text was the EMacro raise (expected: none, since the guard's negative errors in both). Speed (the dropped per-block identity string) is a separate measure-arms row after the gate: installed vs pack11 on apps/spiral, w1.")
inl note_of_pack_11_7 () = Note ("PACK-11", 7u32, "2026-10-31T19:56Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 15:56 compiler: candidate BUILT (job-1793475264287, 591 s in a second heavy-build window granted alongside train6's): SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D, SpiralCompilerCore.dll CA42B2E62EB69EA3 (spiral-bin-candidates\\pack11\\cache\\bin\\single-flight\\...). 0 errors; the same 7 warnings as PACK-10 (1 FS0026, 5 FS0046, 1 FS0760), each shifted by +12 lines (the guard-output helpers), so the 4 appliers add none and the F# of all four compiles. Predict job-1793475266761 running (fresh compiles: the compile memo is keyed on the DLL).")
inl note_of_pack_11_8 () = Note ("PACK-11", 8u32, "2026-10-31T21:00Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 17:00 compiler: PREDICTED-SET GATE MET. job-1793475266761 (compile-only -Suite all, candidate DLL DFC86B91968D447D / core CA42B2E62EB69EA3, one worker on a loaded box, compiled in 3,576.9 s): 7,401 rows, 0 timeouts; vs PACK-10's own run single-flight-20261031-051310 (7,389 rows, = the installed DLL): residual set P = 10, compile-status diffs 0, baseline-verdict diffs 0. All 10 P rows are samples/dynamic_array_bounds_negative (C, Rust, Delphi, Zig, Wasm, Wgsl, Kotlin, Lean, Bend, Lua), whose SOURCE changed today at 08:45 (MATRIX-UB-EXIT-UNPINNED: the sentinel compare), after the 05:13 reference run; the candidate's 10 residual hashes equal the baseline accepted from the new source, 10/10, so P is source-caused and the compiler is neutral (effective P = 0). The 12 rows absent from the reference (backend_switch_missing_arm_negative, backend_switch_validated_gap, manifest_derived_order x Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi) are all parity; the negative now fails through the output check ('FatalError: This program reaches a lib/spiral backend_switch that has no arm for the <backend> backend ...', the pinned Contains still matching) instead of the evaluation-time TracedError, which is the context-free guard working. Also proven on this candidate: the server parent-exit (CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT n19). Speed of the dropped per-block identity string: not measured yet (a measure-arms row after install, installed vs pack11 on apps/spiral). Handed to main for install.")
inl note_of_pack_11_9 () = Note ("PACK-11", 9u32, "2026-10-31T21:10Z", "main", "10-31 17:10 main: install QUEUED. Dry run reproduces the reviewed candidate from today's live source (live core 5B4655EC4BF5990B host 19C0215F2E8C594F -> appliers core C0990B2D590CE965 host 420E1452DB4B3194 = candidate source); refused for now only because the compiler is in use (lanes' cmd/dotnet) and kit's train6 runs. Chain (main bjdl7fvck, scratchpad pack11-chain.ps1): train hold pack11-install tied to the chain's pid, install-when-clear (600 min), verify SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D + SpiralCompilerCore.dll CA42B2E62EB69EA3, node-ship to the node with a capability smoke, release the hold.")
inl note_of_pack_11_10 () = Note ("PACK-11", 10u32, "2026-10-31T21:20Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 17:20 compiler: SPEED CHECK, preliminary and against expectation. Node job job-1793481129021-compiler-p11-speed2 (measure-arms, apps/spiral -> Fsharp, 3 alternating rounds, gen0 256 MB, gcServer 0): pack10 (D1C49B8BDC3318F7) median 31.77 s, pack11 (CA42B2E62EB69EA3) 33.21 s, ratio 1.09 (min 1.05, max 1.12), pack11 slower in all 3 rounds; outputs 791709BF6F5C5642 identical; both builds ReadyToRun (22 dlls, Hopac IL in both). Node load 32-53% during the run and no A/A arm, so it's not yet a verdict (memory ab-needs-in-job-aa). Rerun with A/A: job-1793481532648-compiler-p11-speed-aa (pack10, pack10b = same DLL, pack11; 4 rounds). Main asked to hold the install until it reads out. If the slowdown is real, suspects in order: (1) guard-output now runs missing_arm.IsMatch on EVERY macro text (v1 only outside validation) plus a regex scan of the whole emitted output; (2) RustGapTrace.clear_missing_arm per build; the dropped identity string can't cost time. (Also fixed today: measure-arms.ps1 failed without -Trace, since the row read trace fields of a null result under strict mode.)")
inl note_of_pack_11_11 () = Note ("PACK-11", 11u32, "2026-10-31T21:21Z", "main", "10-31 17:21 main: install HELD at compiler's request (node speed check: pack11 ~9% slower than pack10 on apps/spiral -> F#, median 33.2 s vs 31.8 s over 3 rounds, no A/A arm, node load 32-53%; A/A + A/B rerun job-1793481532648-compiler-p11-speed-aa running). The install chain had not started installing (installed core still D1C49B8BDC3318F7, no compiler-install window): stopped, train hold pack11-install released. Re-arm the chain (scratchpad pack11-chain.ps1) on compiler's verdict.")
inl note_of_pack_11_12 () = Note ("PACK-11", 12u32, "2026-10-31T21:33Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 17:33 compiler: SPEED VERDICT, with A/A: NO measurable change. Node job job-1793481532648-compiler-p11-speed-aa (measure-arms, apps/spiral -> Fsharp, 4 rotated rounds, gen0 256 MB, gcServer 0; node load 59-100%): pack10 median 66.33 s; pack10b (the SAME DLL D1C49B8BDC3318F7 as a second arm) median 53.17 s, ratio 0.75-1.20; pack11 (CA42B2E62EB69EA3) median 55.52 s, ratio 0.62-1.22. pack11 sits inside the A/A spread, so n10's 1.09 (3 rounds, no A/A) was noise, and the dropped per-block identity string gives no win that this node can resolve either (noise ~ +-25%). All 12 outputs 791709BF6F5C5642. Main's install hold released (message 17:3x). A finer speed claim needs a quiet machine or a cpu-time A/B over many rounds; not needed for the pack, which stands on correctness.")
inl note_of_pack_11_13 () = Note ("PACK-11", 13u32, "2026-10-31T21:34Z", "main", "10-31 17:34 main: hold LIFTED on compiler's verdict (n11: the 9% was node noise; A/A arms of the same pack10 DLL differed 0.75-1.20, pack11 0.62-1.22 inside that spread; 12/12 outputs identical 791709BF6F5C5642). Install chain RE-ARMED (scratchpad pack11-chain.ps1: train hold tied to the chain's pid, install-when-clear 600 min, verify DFC86B91968D447D / CA42B2E62EB69EA3, node-ship with a capability smoke, release the hold). It may complete after main's 18:00 day-run end; its output and the node status line are the evidence.")
inl note_of_pack_11_14 () = Note ("PACK-11", 14u32, "2026-11-01T00:31Z", "main", "10-31 20:31 main: INSTALLED and VERIFIED 20:27-20:29 (chain bskdoxd7o): SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D and SpiralCompilerCore.dll CA42B2E62EB69EA3 = the reviewed candidate; system dotnet launches it; Cells domain stamp removed (domain.gleam regenerates on the next mix compile); undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack11-20261031-202707. SHIPPED to the node (digest CC1F29DA5A8718F1, previous kept as .replaced-20261031-2029), so node = box again. Train hold pack11-install released. Left (compiler): the parse-speed row (measure-arms, installed vs pack11). Unblocked (main): CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT's Cells half (pass SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID).")
inl note_of_pack_11_15 () = Note ("PACK-11", 15u32, "2026-11-01T00:32Z", "compiler", "10-31 10-31 20:32 compiler: INSTALLED and VERIFIED (main, 20:27-20:29): SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D and SpiralCompilerCore.dll CA42B2E62EB69EA3, equal to the reviewed candidate; on the node too (digest CC1F29DA5A8718F1). Live sources confirm it: 0 gpt5parallel mentions, no observeParsedStatement, missing_arm_sites present, exitWithParent present, no SPIRAL_BUILD_DEADLINE_MS. Follow-ups done: its 4 appliers archived under the packs lifecycle (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261031-203212); probe.ps1's dead SPIRAL_BUILD_BUDGET_MS export dropped (-BudgetSec stays, it sets the wait timeout). Speed row: already measured with the same DLL (n11-n12): no change resolvable on the node. Main takes the Cells half of the parent-exit as a night item.")
inl config_baseline () = Task ("CONFIG-BASELINE", "Known-good config baseline + daily drift check: fingerprint a curated set of config files (git, wsl, scoop, ssh config, Claude settings, editor settings, Notepad++ session, spelling dict) and alert on silent change, so config restoration after damage is a one-command diff rather than manual archaeology; content restores from the profile mirror", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "main,wipe,config,durability,resilience", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_config_baseline () = Planning ("CONFIG-BASELINE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_config_baseline_1 () = Note ("CONFIG-BASELINE", 1u32, "2026-10-31T14:01Z", "resilience", "Built + Done 10-31 by resilience (git-51). i574n.github/scripts/config-baseline.ps1 (-Mode Snapshot|Check, fingerprints only so no secrets copied; content lives in the profile mirror). Baseline store %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\config-baseline. Proven: snapshot 13 files, clean check exit 0, negative control (flipped .gitconfig hash) reports DRIFT exit 1. Scheduled: task config-baseline-check daily 06:10 Priority 5 -NoteOnDrift (register-scheduled-tasks.ps1). Drift notes land on this item. Re-snapshot after an intended config change.")
inl note_of_config_baseline_2 () = Note ("CONFIG-BASELINE", 2u32, "2026-10-31T14:19Z", "resilience", "10-31 10:1x resilience (git-51): first lane backup request handled (the role working as intended). Added %LOCALAPPDATA%\\fiscal-undo (141 files, 6.6 MB, byte-exact undo copies of fiscal's past lib lands, irreproducible) to profile-mirror.ps1 wholeTrees (dry run 29,539 files / 765 MB, parse clean). Kept OUT of the baseline by design: undo blobs are immutable, so the mirror tar-verify + restore drill is their integrity check, not drift detection (drift is for configs that change). Left out as reproducible per fiscal: fiscal-gate, deps\\corpus, deps\\bench; restore the facturae corpus from the box, never an older mirror (node can't reach facturae.gob.es).")
inl note_of_config_baseline_3 () = Note ("CONFIG-BASELINE", 3u32, "2026-10-31T14:34Z", "resilience", "10-31 10:3x resilience (git-51): extended on tibia's request, and closed a DB backup gap. (a) config-baseline now covers 3 record types: FILE (fingerprint), ENV (expected value; empty=expected-unset, a value appearing is drift) and DIRSET (a dir's immediate child-name set). Baselined env: TIBIA_WORLD, TIBIA_MARIADB_BIN (both unset), MIMALLOC_DISABLE_REDIRECT, SPIRAL_PYTHON, NO_COLOR; DIRSET: tibia-local top-level. Snapshot 19 records, clean check exit 0; negative control (TIBIA_WORLD set in a child) reports ENV drift exit 1. (b) The canary DB (tibia-local\\mariadb-data, live under mariadbd pid 14040) had NO backup: a datadir file-copy is not a consistent InnoDB restore point. New tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 takes a --single-transaction dump (48 tables, 73 KB), daily task 05:20 Priority 5, dumps in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\tibia-mariadb-dumps -> profile mirror. First consistent dump taken 10-31 while tibia is parked.")
inl note_of_config_baseline_4 () = Note ("CONFIG-BASELINE", 4u32, "2026-10-31T17:22Z", "config-baseline", "scheduled check: config-baseline 2026-10-31 13:22 vs baseline-20261031-103805.tsv: DRIFT (1): ENV NO_COLOR: baseline '1' now ''")
inl note_of_config_baseline_5 () = Note ("CONFIG-BASELINE", 5u32, "2026-10-31T17:25Z", "resilience", "10-31 13:3x resilience (git-51): durability-task audit + a small fix. All 7 scheduled tasks (kit-unstaged-backup, profile-mirror-to-node, profile-restore-drill, config-baseline-check, tibia-mariadb-dump, resource-report x2) are Ready at Priority 5 with zero drift (register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 -DryRun: all 'unchanged'; that -DryRun is itself the task-layer drift detector). Test-ran config-baseline-check and tibia-mariadb-dump via Start-ScheduledTask: both result 0 under the headless path (dump wrote canary-20261031-132240.sql). The 267011 lastResult on the others is SCHED_S_TASK_HAS_NOT_RUN (first trigger tomorrow), not an error. Fix: config-baseline.ps1 now always writes %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\schedules\\config-baseline.last.log (was: backlog note on drift only), so a clean daily run leaves an audit trail like the restore drill does.")
inl note_of_config_baseline_6 () = Note ("CONFIG-BASELINE", 6u32, "2026-10-31T19:48Z", "resilience", "10-31 15:4x resilience (git-51): closed a wipe-survival gap in the durability layer itself. Checked: the scheduled tasks live in C:\\Windows\\System32\\Tasks and the scripts in C:\\home\\git, so both SURVIVE a C:\\Users wipe and keep firing; only their profile-side inputs die. Fix: added %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\config-baseline to the profile mirror (it was NOT backed up) so the known-good fingerprints survive a wipe and post-restore config drift stays detectable against the PRE-wipe baseline (the whole point). RUNBOOK.md gained a 'Durability layer after a profile wipe' section: restore ~/.ssh first (else the mirror can't reach the node), pull the baseline store back then re-snapshot, verify with register-scheduled-tasks.ps1 -DryRun (all 'unchanged' = task layer intact) + the drill + baseline check. Mirror dry run parses clean.")
inl note_of_config_baseline_7 () = Note ("CONFIG-BASELINE", 7u32, "2026-11-01T10:10Z", "config-baseline", "scheduled check: config-baseline 2026-11-01 06:10 vs baseline-20261031-103805.tsv: DRIFT (3): CHANGED C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\persist\\notepadplusplus\\session.xml; CHANGED C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\persist\\notepadplusplus\\config.xml; ENV NO_COLOR: baseline '1' now ''")
