inl note_of_scrum_xp_s3_1 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S3", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:33Z", "kit", "11-01 00:3x kit, slice of EOIE-SCRUM-XP (user 00:2x via main: 'speed up the agile->scrum/xp migration'; slices of an hour or less). Spec: EOIE-SCRUM-XP M3 DESIGN note (10-30 13:5x) and the 10-22 typestate draft.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s3_2 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S3", 2u32, "2026-11-01T12:37Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD: 'kit backlog sprint start <root> S-1 7 \"ship the sprint verbs\" --items A,B' appends the Sprint row and one SprintItem per item (state diff = only those lines) and prints the committed minutes; it exits 2 with a named reason for a second open sprint (AnotherSprintOpen S-0), a Done or unknown item (ItemNotOpen X) and an unestimated item (ItemUnestimated X); 4 CLI tests, node green. NEXT STEP: the verb in kit_agile_routes' backlog ceremony (M1 routing exists) calling agile_sprint.started over candidates built from the task rows (status -> item_standing, estimate -> minutes), writing via S2's append path. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: start_outcome is already a closed union (Started | AnotherSprintOpen | ItemNotOpen | ItemUnestimated) so each refusal is a pattern with its own exit text, never a string compare; candidate.standing a closed union; days as a nominal (1..30 smart constructor), dates derived, never typed by hand.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s3_3 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S3", 3u32, "2026-11-01T18:15Z", "kit", "11-01 14:15 kit: EMACS-STEALS fold: an over-estimate note (org effort warnings). When ActualMinutes sum > estimate x 1.5, kit writes one typed EstimateExceeded note row (item, estimate, actual) once per item and surfaces it in standup.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s3_4 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S3", 4u32, "2026-11-01T20:34Z", "kit", "11-01 16:34 kit: the over-estimate rule is modeled and proven (unstaged), in src/agile_activity beside actual_minutes. estimate_verdict = WithinEstimate | EstimateExceeded (estimate, actual) | AlreadyNoted; estimate_verdict_of estimate actual noted: exactly 1.5x is within, past 1.5x is exceeded, it is noted once per item, and an item without an estimate never warns. Test an_overrun_past_one_and_a_half_estimates_is_noted_once: Linux worker 3/3 for the package. NEXT (verb half): after each ActualMinutes append, sum actual_total for the item, run estimate_verdict_of with noted = an EstimateExceeded note row already exists, and append one typed EstimateExceeded row; standup (S8) surfaces it.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s3_5 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S3", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:33Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 35 h ago by kit, progress kept at 40%. Resume from that note: ackage. NEXT (verb half): after each ActualMinutes append, sum actual_total for the item, run estimate_verdict_of with noted = an EstimateExceeded note row already exists, and append one typed EstimateExceeded row; standup (S8) surfaces it.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s3_6 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S3", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:51Z", "kit", "11-04 05:3x kit: `kit backlog sprint start <root> <id> <days> <goal> [--items A,B]` BUILT (unstaged). New linked crate kit_agile_sprint (typed sprint_verb union, SprintStart). It reads state/agile.spi and state/sprints.spi, builds candidates through two new direct linkable exports (agile_task_census kit_agile_task_status_of, agile_planning_fields kit_agile_planning_minutes_of; the old lambda exports are kept for their host callers), and calls the existing model `started`, which refuses another open sprint, an unknown or Done item and an unestimated item. On Started it appends via agile_sprint_rows.sprints_appended (self-contained schema on first use) and adds `sprints` to state/package.spiproj once. Dates come from civil_date (days since epoch -> YYYY-MM-DD; tests 1970-01-01, 2026-11-04 and leap day 2000-02-29). Wiring: AgileSprint (root after the mode), routed in kit_agile_mutation as a write (agile lock), and `sprint` added to the backlog ceremony's verbs. vultr --check exit 0 for the crate and the 5 touched files. Box notebook and node size run going; then TRAIN21. CLI test against a backlog COPY after install.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s3_7 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S3", 7u32, "2026-11-04T08:58Z", "kit", "11-04 05:4x: PARKED out of TRAIN21 for size. Node size run: kit_agile_sprint 1390 lines (box notebook 2/2 pass, vultr --check exit 0), and kit_agile_mutation reached 996 with the route. Crate and wiring are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\SCRUM-XP-S3-sprint-start-1104 (crate + wired/ copies). The census and planning direct exports stay in the tree (574 / 817 lines). Next: split so the agile_sprint model + agile_sprint_rows parsing live in one linked unit (sprint_started_rows: inputs as a tuple of strings, output as an array_base of one {code; message; sprints_text} row), with the CLI crate keeping only argv and file I/O. And give kit_agile_mutation headroom first (996): e.g. move agile_entry's lock wrapper or the route table into a unit.")
