inl note_of_scrum_xp_s4_2 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S4", 2u32, "2026-11-01T12:38Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD: 'kit backlog sprint add <root> S-1 C' appends one SprintItem (Committed) and 'sprint drop <root> S-1 A' appends a Dropped row for A without deleting the Committed one (state diff = one appended line each); add refuses ItemNotOpen/ItemUnestimated and a closed sprint; 3 CLI tests. NEXT STEP: two verbs beside sprint start using agile_sprint_rows.sprint_item_row and the S2 append path. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: ChangeItems is already the GADT op sprint_op sprint_running sprint_running, so add/drop only typecheck on a running sprint value; item_fate = Committed | Dropped (closed union), the review reads the last fate per task, never a status string.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s4_3 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S4", 3u32, "2026-11-04T09:21Z", "kit", "11-04 06:3x kit: `kit backlog sprint add|drop <root> <id> <item>` BUILT (unstaged, not wired yet; vultr pack34 + toml lib --check exit 0 for all 3 files, as-is and test bodies). Append-only: add appends a Committed SprintItem row (the sprint must be open; the item must be open and estimated, via the model's first_refusal); drop appends a Dropped row for an item already in the sprint, so the dropped row is kept as history. agile_sprint_rows.items_of now lets the LAST row per task win, in place (test a_later_item_row_replaces_the_earlier_one_for_that_task), so a drop replaces rather than duplicates. The state unit gained sprint_item_appended. Wiring + node size run together with S3/S5.")
