inl note_of_scrum_xp_s6_2 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S6", 2u32, "2026-11-01T12:39Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD: 'kit backlog sprint close <root> S-1' appends a closed Sprint row and prints done/carried/dropped minutes and velocity equal to agile_sprint.reviewed on the same data; carried items get a note naming the next sprint; 'kit backlog velocity <root> --last 3' prints the mean of the last 3 reviews (CLI tests). NEXT STEP: close + velocity verbs over agile_sprint.reviewed / velocity. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: CloseSprint is the GADT op sprint_op sprint_running sprint_closed; sprint_review is a record of nominal minutes plus goal_met bool; velocity returns option minutes (none before any closed sprint), not 0.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s6_3 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S6", 3u32, "2026-11-04T09:31Z", "kit", "11-04 06:5x kit: `sprint close <root> <id>` and `sprint velocity <root> [--last n]` BUILT (unstaged, not wired; vultr pack34 + toml lib --check exit 0 for all 3 files, as-is and test bodies; box notebook queued). Rows: a SprintReview row (id, done, carried, dropped minutes) joins the self-contained sprints schema; head rows now let the LAST row per id win in place, like items. Duplicate inl names in a state module compile (later shadows earlier; verified on vultr), so append-only works. Close: the model's `reviewed` with finished = census status Done; it appends a closed head row plus a review row and prints done/carried/dropped and goal_met. Velocity: the model's `velocity` over reviews_of, newest first. DEVIATIONS: velocity lives under `sprint velocity`, not a new `backlog velocity` route, because kit_agile_mutation sits at 996 lines; carried items don't get a note yet (needs the note writer).")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s6_4 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S6", 4u32, "2026-11-04T10:24Z", "kit", "11-04 09:0x kit: SIZE + SPLIT. Node size run (kit-size-sprint3, current code): kit_agile_sprint 1359 and kit_agile_sprint_state 1135 lines, both OVER the 1000 gate. Split by concern into 4 linked units (unstaged; workspace members + Cargo.lock refreshed, cargo metadata --locked exit 0): kit_agile_sprint_state (open sprint, head, items, appends), NEW kit_agile_sprint_review (review/close text/velocity; exports kit_agile_sprint_review/closed/velocity), NEW kit_agile_sprint_change (add/drop/close/velocity verbs; exports kit_agile_sprint_changed/closed_run/velocity_shown over tuple args), kit_agile_sprint (start/show + verb routing through the change link). vultr pack34 --check exit 0 for all 4, as-is and with test bodies. Pending: box notebooks (kit-sprint-split-tests) and node size run kit-size-sprint4 (queued behind kit-size-lint, behind TRAIN21's heavy slot).")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s6_5 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S6", 5u32, "2026-11-04T12:23Z", "kit", "11-04 09:3x kit: WIRED-SHAPE SIZES (node kit-size-wired + kit-size-keep2, current code): kit_agile_mutation 930 (sprint + lint + gate routes in; the writes table moved to agile_state_access 399), kit_agile_sprint_change 392, kit_ceremonies 218, kit_agile_lint 253. Still OVER: kit_agile_sprint 1307, kit_agile_sprint_state 1204, kit_agile_sprint_review 1262. The kept workspace shows density spread over ~40 generated functions (the biggest is 129 lines), not one giant, so the fix is more seams: the sprint WRITERS (item_row, sprint_appended_text, sprint_item_appended) now live in NEW linked unit kit_agile_sprint_append (start and change link it); state keeps only readers. Next: re-size; if review/CLI are still over, velocity moves to the readers and show to its own unit.")
inl note_of_scrum_xp_s6_6 () = Note ("SCRUM-XP-S6", 6u32, "2026-11-04T14:55Z", "kit", "11-04 12:2x kit: SIZE ROUND 3. A kept workspace showed the sprint STATE-FILE PARSER dominating each small crate (review_of_line alone 137 generated lines), copied into state, review and the CLI. Fix (unstaged): NEW linked crate kit_agile_sprint_read owns the parser and exports flat typed rows (sprint_flat per item, review_flat per review); agile_sprint_rows gains flat_of / sprints_from / reviews_from, so state and review rebuild `list sprint` from the rows (sprints_read) and their logic is unchanged. Sprint START moved to NEW unit kit_agile_sprint_start (date maths, candidates, manifest update; export takes the trailing args as array_base string); kit_agile_sprint is now only the verb router (87 lines). Earlier rounds: append / show / change split out. Round-trip test: flat rows rebuild the same sprints (items, drops, an empty sprint) and reviews. vultr pack34 --check exit 0 for all sprint units (with bodies). Pending: node size run kit-size-all5, box notebooks.")
