inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_1 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:37Z", "main", "main 00:3x: first pass at this groom; the count trend goes on this item each round.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_2 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 2u32, "2026-11-01T04:39Z", "main", "main 00:3x round 1: open items 401; ownerless 4 (FISCAL-APP, FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE and TIBIA-2048-ANCHOR carry the lane in the id but no tag, WORKFLOW-END-TO-END is ownerless and 185 h stale); open with no note for 48 h: 80. Deps on Blocked items hide items from 'agile next' (CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS sat 8 days behind a user-blocked badge item): next round, also list open items whose every dep is Blocked.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_3 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 3u32, "2026-11-01T04:51Z", "main", "main 00:5x round 2 check, 'open items whose deps are all Blocked or Paused' (hidden from agile next): 6. Fixed PS1-TO-SPIRAL (P0, behind PIPELINES-GREEN; now behind KIT-RUN-SPI). Left with a reason: X-PARALLEL-BUILD (x's census), NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE and CI-K3S (really need green pipelines), XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS (fiscal's paused prototypes), UPSTREAM-FORK-START (user-blocked upstream post). Ask kit: 'agile next --hidden' should list these every time (KIT-AGILE-CADENCE).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_4 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 4u32, "2026-11-01T20:58Z", "main", "main 16:5x ROUND 3 (computed from agile list --json; deps split on commas): of 496 open items, 4 were hidden from agile next because every dep was Blocked or Paused, and 0 deps dangle. Fixed all 4: PIPELINES-GREEN was Blocked with no deps and every repo is green except alphabet's Windows job, so it is Active again, which unhides CI-K3S and NEAR-WINDOWS-NATIVE. PAGES-NOTEBOOK-PUBLISH's dep on TREE-PAGES-V2 was main's own mistake (the -Include works with the current renderer), dep removed. UPSTREAM-FORK-START stays behind UPSTREAM-POST-1-VANILLA, a user-blocked upstream post, on purpose. Also fixed K3S-EVERYWHERE -> CI-K3S (machines don't wait on Actions compliance). The census is a one-liner now; it belongs in kit as 'agile next --hidden' (KIT-AGILE-CADENCE).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_5 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 5u32, "2026-11-02T23:55Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:5x ROUND 4 (computed from agile list --json; deps split on commas): 667 open. (a) 0 without a team tag. (b) 12 hidden from agile next: 6 EOIE-* items (JOBS, READ-QUERY, EDIT-BATCH, ONE-CALL-SPEC, SPIRAL-TESTS, ZED-SWEEP) had the literal dep 'none', which kit reads as a missing item: CLEARED. The other 6 are hidden on purpose (the WoW chain + TIBIA-GAME-HANDSHAKE behind the user-paused tibia/WoW work; UPSTREAM-POST-2 and UPSTREAM-FORK-START behind the user-gated upstream PR). (c) 8 dangling deps: the 6 'none' above + 2 GLUED ids missing a comma, both fixed: CELLS-IN-SPIRAL 'X-SIM-CELLS-SPIRALCELLS-TYPED-UNITS' -> X-SIM-CELLS-SPIRAL,CELLS-TYPED-UNITS, and CELLS-PORT-NOTEBOOK 'CELLS-DOCUMENT-TYPEDCELLS-TYPED-UNITS' -> CELLS-DOCUMENT-TYPED,CELLS-TYPED-UNITS. (d) 5 Active silent > 48 h: main's BANG-MACRO-CLEANUP (94 h), RUNNER-STALE (73 h), CELLS-RUST-TEST-BATCH (49 h) -> Planned with a note; EOIE-OPEN-SHADOW-LINT retagged team:eoie -> team:kit (eoie was kit's old name); KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS (52 h) left to kit. Trend vs round 3: hidden 4 -> 12 found (all fixed or intentional), dangling 0 -> 8 (all fixed). FOR kit (KIT-AGILE-CADENCE): agile edit/add should refuse 'none' as a dep and refuse a dep id that does not exist.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_6 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 6u32, "2026-11-03T05:03Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:0x ROUND 5 (computed from agile list --json; deps split on commas): 660 open (Active 158, Planned 452, Paused 29, Blocked 21). (a) 0 dangling deps. (b) 11 hidden from agile next, all on purpose with a resume condition in the blocker's last note: HEAVY-HOLD-DEADLOCK <- EOIE-WINDOW-ANNOUNCE and REMOTE-EXEC-S3/S4 <- REMOTE-EXEC-S2 (both Blocked by kit until the TRAIN14 install); SCRUM-XP-S3 <- SCRUM-XP-S2 (kit-train-only work, released by x-dumps); X-DUMPS-TTS <- X-DUMPS-TRANSLATE (user budget for the paid translation); UPSTREAM-POST-2-C-SELF-TAIL and UPSTREAM-FORK-START <- UPSTREAM-POST-1-VANILLA (user-gated public PR); the WoW chain and TIBIA-GAME-HANDSHAKE (user-paused). (c) Active and silent > 48 h: 4 (round 4: 5). EOIE-OPEN-SHADOW-LINT 61 h, KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS 58 h, SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD 52 h belong to kit/compiler; main's FSHARP-OUTSIDE-COMPILER 53 h gets a next step (its note). Trend: hidden 6 -> 4 -> 12 -> 11, dangling 0 -> 0 -> 8 -> 0, silent Active 5 -> 4.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_7 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 7u32, "2026-11-03T14:58Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:0x ROUND 6 (agile list --open --json): 611 open in the list view (Active 115, Planned 496; Paused/Blocked not in --open). (a) items with no team:/lane tag: 0. (b) Active and silent > 48 h: 2 (round 5: 4). LEAN-BACKEND (main, 54 h): lab file ruled out (its pin bump is already applied), next step + owners written (n30). FISCAL-APP (team:fiscal, 48 h): fiscal's epic, its children carry the activity; left to fiscal. Trend: silent Active 5 -> 4 -> 2; untagged 0. Also closed today: HURDLES-1103 (all 8 lanes, every open hurdle owned), MIRROR-RESYNC-1103, HTML-LINT-HEAL.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_8 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 8u32, "2026-11-03T18:36Z", "tibia", "11-03 14:4x tibia, sweep of the TIBIA-TAGGED slice (claimed by the gate as tibia-ac4b4e98): 40 open tibia-tagged items; 2 stale (last note older than 48 h) and both without a team tag: CELLS-EVERYWHERE and BACKEND-BALANCE. Each now has an owner (team:main) and a next step in a note; CELLS-EVERYWHERE also got tibia measured share (129/137 cell files). The other 38 have notes within 48 h. Count for this slice: 2 orphans -> 0. The untagged non-tibia remainder is main.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_9 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 9u32, "2026-11-03T18:55Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:0x ROUND 7: open incl. Blocked/Paused 663 (Active 125, Planned 483, Blocked 24, Paused 31). Active silent > 48 h: 1 (FISCAL-APP, fiscal's epic; round 6: 2, round 5: 4). NEW CHECK, main's Blocked/Paused (23): each has a reason, though 14 keep it in an earlier note rather than the last one (procedural last notes: parent-epic or provisional-field notes). Re-decided TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO (its resume condition was met: sweep rerun, 9/10 pages OK, now blocked on html's push only). Blocked today with explicit RESUME WHEN on the user's push: HTML-CLI, HTML-CI-RELEASE, ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT. Trend: silent Active 5 -> 4 -> 2 -> 1.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_10 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 10u32, "2026-11-03T21:13Z", "tibia", "11-03 17:1x tibia, second gate claim, WHOLE-BACKLOG SLICE: open items 606; without a team tag 250, of which 171 stale (last note older than 48 h). All 171 already named an owner through a plain lane tag (kit 89, main 60, compiler 22) but were invisible to agile next --team <lane>, which matches only team: tags (the gap main recorded 11-01). Each now has team:<its first lane tag> appended with every existing tag kept (edit tags replaces, so the full list was passed; one item read back first: kino,main -> kino,main,team:main): team:kit 89, team:main 60 (KINO-SOTA first, then 59), team:compiler 22; 170+1 edits ok, 0 failures. COUNT TREND: untagged open 250 -> 79; stale untagged 171 -> 0. Next steps stay with each owning lane (their agile next now lists them). The remaining untagged open items have notes within 48 h.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_11 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 11u32, "2026-11-03T21:40Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:4x ROUND 8: open 661; Active silent > 48 h: 3 (FISCAL-APP, NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-RETIRE, HOME-STRAY-FOLDERS); items with no team/lane tag: 1. Unchanged since round 7 except today's new items (all tagged at creation: GRANULAR-SPLIT-*, REGEX-STAGED-TABLES, HTML-NODE-RECORDS (Done)). Trend silent Active: 5 -> 4 -> 2 -> 1 -> 3.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_12 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 12u32, "2026-11-03T23:18Z", "resilience-614162e5", "GROOM 1 (11-03 19:10, resilience-614162e5) - BASELINE for the count trend.\nCOUNTS (open=654 of 1429; Done 775 excluded): no-team-tag ORPHANS=108; STALE (last note >48h)=256; union=270.\nROOT CAUSE of orphans: a tag-convention SPLIT. 546 open items use canonical team:X; 108 carry a BARE lane tag (main/kit/x/compiler/fiscal/tibia) with NO team: prefix, so `kit agile next --team X` routing cannot see them - they have a de-facto owner but are unroutable. `migrate-tags preview` = tasks=0 (it does not canonicalize bare->team:, so no auto-fix).\nNOT mechanically fixable: many orphans are MULTI-lane (e.g. GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT [gleam,rust,concurrency,x,tibia,kit,main]; TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT [...,main,fiscal]) - ownership is a decision per item, not a rewrite. `edit tags` REPLACES the whole list, so each fix must set the full canonical list.\nSTALE by team: kit 115, main 72, compiler 30, fiscal 7, tibia 7, x 6, eoie 2, resilience 2. kit+main = 187/256 (73%) - those two lanes carry almost all the stale-note debt; they should re-note or close.\nORPHAN by priority: P0 ~25, P1 ~55, P2 ~15, P3-5 ~13.\nACTION PATH (for main, over grooms, to drive orphan->0): canonicalize bare lane tags to team:X, resolving multi-lane ambiguity by picking the primary owner; start with P0 single-lane (PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY->team:main, PS1-TO-SPIRAL->team:main, etc.). Not auto-batched here: owner choice needs judgment + edit-replaces is error-prone at scale.\nTREND: groom 1 baseline = orphan 108 / stale 256. Next groom compares; target is both shrinking.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_13 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 13u32, "2026-11-04T00:39Z", "tibia", "11-03 20:4x tibia, re-check after the BSOD (claimed again by the gate): open 595, untagged 79, stale untagged 0 (was 171 before the 17:1x round). Trend holds; nothing to assign.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_14 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 14u32, "2026-11-04T01:14Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:14 x: x's CORNER of the sweep done (claimed for x by the gate). Open x-tagged items: 57; with no note in 48 h: 15, now 0 unaddressed. Each has an owner and a next step: 1 Blocked -> Paused with a resume condition (X-PARALLEL-CENSUS); 1 Blocked confirmed with its blocker named (X-CLIENT: the user's push); 4 Paused confirmed with reason + condition (X-FAILURE-TEXT-DEDUP, X-ON-NEAR, X-FEDERATION-BRIDGES, X-NEAR-PROVENANCE); 3 owned by team:compiler (x a consumer: RUST-UNUSED-PATTERN-CLONES, GLEAM-INLINE-SINGLE-USE, GLEAM-PARTS-EMIT); 5 heavy x items with next steps queued behind the node (X-PRECOMMIT-SPEED, X-BACKEND-SWITCHES, X-PARALLEL-BUILD, X-HAND-UNITS, X-LAMBDA-PARENS); 1 CPU-light share taken now (LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE's world.spi). Releasing; the rest of the backlog is main's.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_15 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 15u32, "2026-11-04T01:16Z", "resilience-614162e5", "GROOM 2 (21:15, ~2h after groom 1). TREND vs groom 1 baseline (108 orphan / 256 stale):\n- orphan (no team: tag) = 108, FLAT. Zero change in 2h confirms the bare-lane-tag convention split is STRUCTURAL and will NOT self-resolve - it only moves via the deliberate canonicalize-bare-tags-to-team: pass from groom 1's action path (owner decisions, multi-lane items need a primary-owner call). This is the sole lever on the orphan number.\n- stale (>48h) = 249, down 7 from 256 (roughly flat): ~2h of items aging past the sliding 48h cutoff offset by ~2h of fresh notes (post-crash fleet activity + my BSOD-incident notes).\n- stale by team: kit 115 (flat), main 80 (UP from 72 - main's own stale debt is the ONLY growing segment; main should re-note/close its 80), compiler 28 (-2), fiscal 7, tibia 7, eoie 2.\n- fleet actively filing post-crash: new items since groom 1 incl LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE, X-BACKEND-SWITCHES, X-PARALLEL-BUILD, plus BOX-BSOD-1103 (mine).\nNET: counts stable across the crash+restart; orphan-canonicalization and main's rising stale debt are the two levers. No per-item triage this groom (box fragile post-BSOD, ~45min to run-end); trend recorded, lease released.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_16 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 16u32, "2026-11-04T01:21Z", "resilience", "GROOM 2 ACTION (not just trend): canonicalized resilience's OWN single-lane bare-tag orphans to team:resilience - CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST and MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST (both clearly durability/machine-upkeep = my lane). Orphan count 108 -> 106. Left ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME untouched (tags scripts,languages,cleanup,main,kit,tibia,resilience = genuinely multi-lane; primary-owner is main's call, not a unilateral resilience claim).\nPATTERN that actually moves the flat 108 without a risky bulk rewrite: EACH LANE canonicalizes its OWN single-lane bare-tag orphans to team:X (safe, deterministic, lead-by-example); the multi-lane orphans are the residue that needs a per-item owner decision (main/the owning lanes). I did resilience's share; kit (its bare-kit orphans), compiler, x, main should do theirs. edit tags REPLACES the list - pass the full set with team:X prepended (as done here).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_17 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 17u32, "2026-11-04T01:24Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:24 x: second half for x's corner (re-claimed by the gate): open items without any team: tag = 106 of 651. By their project tag: main 53, kit 22, compiler 15, x 12 (9 of them x-only), x-dumps 3 (XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER, XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI, XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX), tibia 1. x tagged its 9 with team:x (tags kept): X-DONE, X-CLIENT, NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW, X-PARALLEL-CENSUS, CELLS-IN-SPIRAL, X-REPO-TEMPLATE, X-ON-NEAR, X-FEDERATION-BRIDGES, X-NEAR-PROVENANCE. The other 97 are for main, kit, compiler, x-dumps and tibia to tag; the per-lane counts above are their lists. Untagged trend: 106 -> 97 after x's share. Releasing.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_18 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 18u32, "2026-11-04T01:27Z", "kit", "11-03 21:3x kit (gate-assigned; kit ran the measuring half, main owns the follow-up). Counts:\n- 651 open rows; 0 with no lane word. 97 lack a 'team:' prefix but carry a bare lane word ('main', 'kit', 'compiler' ...), and agile next --team already resolves those, so relabelling would be churn.\n- 154 Active/Blocked; 15 with a last note older than 48 h, none kit's:\n  - main: FISCAL-APP is fiscal's; NOTEBOOK-LIVEMD-EXPORT and UPSTREAM-POST-2-C-SELF-TAIL (Blocked since 10-28/29); FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS; CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS; LIB-SWEEP-1031-RED; PAGES-NOTEBOOK-PUBLISH; REGEX-SYNTAX, REGEX-DERIVATIVES, REGEX-ANTIMIROV, REGEX-XSD; HTML-MARKDOWN, HTML-PARITY;\n  - compiler: RUST-DERIVE-INFERENCE, EXPORT-STRING-PARAM-RC.\nEach needs an owner's next step or a close. The 4 REGEX-* items go silent together (last notes 11-01 22:31 to 23:18), which looks like one parked lane rather than 4 forgotten items. Main to triage.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_19 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 19u32, "2026-11-04T01:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:31 x: third gate claim. The 3 XDUMPS items with only a project tag (XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER, XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI, XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX; no main/kit/compiler tag, so no lane's list would pick them up) got team:x-dumps, the existing team tag (8 items already). Untagged open: 106 -> 97 -> 94. The remaining 94 carry a lane's project tag (main 53, kit 22, compiler 15, x 3 shared with other lanes, tibia 1): each lane's own pass. x's corner of this sweep is complete; releasing.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_20 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 20u32, "2026-11-04T01:41Z", "x-dumps", "x-dumps (auto-claimed by the --any gate) RELEASED - this is MAIN-owned by its own definition (\"Main owns the CPU-light work no lane owns\"). Ironically it is the item whose job is to TAG orphan/untagged items, and it is itself untagged so --any kept handing it (and its siblings) to idle lanes. Concrete orphans for this sweep to tag to kit/compiler, released by x-dumps in the last hour because they are Spiral-code standards not X archival: GRANULAR-STATS and TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT. Tagging those (and giving MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP itself team:main) stops the --any mis-handing to x-dumps.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_21 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 21u32, "2026-11-04T01:46Z", "compiler", "11-03 21:5x compiler (claimed for me by the stop gate at the end of the run; released). Compiler-slice data point: kit agile list <root> all --team compiler --json gives 300 tasks, 100 open (Active/Planned/Blocked), but every task's last_note field is EMPTY in the JSON, so an 'older than 48 h' filter can't be computed from one list call and flags all 100. The sweep needs either last_note.at filled in list --json (kit fix, one field) or 100 agile show calls. Compiler items touched today with a written next step (not orphans): PORTABLE-PRIMITIVES, BACKEND-METRICS-MODEL, PREDICT-PER-BACKEND, CELLS-TYPED-TARGETS, RUST-HEAP-UNION-MOVES (pack33 ready, install 11-04), LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT, LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS, KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER (kit), SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL (cells daemon site is x's).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_22 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 22u32, "2026-11-04T01:59Z", "resilience", "CLOSING TREND (21:58): orphan 108 (groom1/2, structurally flat) -> 106 (my 2 resilience canonicalizations) -> 94 now. The extra 12 were canonicalized by OTHER lanes - the per-lane \"canonicalize your own single-lane bare-tag orphans to team:X\" pattern (note 16) is being ADOPTED fleet-wide. So the flat 108 broke once the fix was demonstrated + recorded, not before: lead-by-example worked. stale steady at 249. Lease released for the run's 22:00 stop. NEXT GROOM: continue tracking orphan down as lanes finish their shares; the residue will be the genuinely multi-lane items (e.g. ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME) needing per-item owner decisions.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_23 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 23u32, "2026-11-04T04:17Z", "main", "11-04 00:1x main groom (user ask: 10 min, all lanes): moved 36 of main's Active items untouched for 12 h or more to Planned, keeping their percents (WIP cap). PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY is now Blocked on user-only steps. Active for main: 58 down to 21.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_24 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 24u32, "2026-11-04T04:22Z", "main", "11-04 00:2x main CORRECTION to my 00:1x groom note. The user moved the stale window from 12 h to 48 h (relayed by kit 00:2x: \"at least 48h would be better\"). I put the 27 items with a note inside 48 h back to Active, percents unchanged. Only 9 stay Planned (no note since 11-02T04Z or earlier): REGEX-ANTIMIROV, REGEX-DERIVATIVES, REGEX-XSD, REGEX-SYNTAX, CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS, PAGES-NOTEBOOK-PUBLISH, LIB-SWEEP-1031-RED, HTML-PARITY, HTML-MARKDOWN. PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY is Blocked (user-only remainder). Active for main: 58 down to 48.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_25 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 25u32, "2026-11-04T05:02Z", "resilience", "11-04 01:0x resilience GROOM (stop-gate claimed). ORPHAN SWEEP big reduction: live orphans (non-Done, no team: tag) 93 -> 40 -> 24 (run baseline was 108). (1) Canonicalized all 53 bare-main single-lane orphans to team:main - main's own 00:1x grooming moved statuses not tags, so these sat un-canonicalized; 53/53 ok via a retry-on-CAS loop. (2) Assigned primary owners to all 16 multi-lane orphans: 11 compiler-domain -> team:compiler (EBPF-C-PROFILE, HOPACSOTA, HOPACSOTA-P3, RUST-MATCH-DUPLICATION, EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION, EDITION3-TEST-SYMBOL, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS, SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES, MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER, CI-COMPILER-FULL-SUITE, LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION); GRANULAR-STATS -> team:kit; cross-lane coordination items ORG-SCRIPTS-HOME, CODESPACES-BUTTON-ALL-REPOS, GRANULAR-HEAL, GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT -> team:main (work no single lane owns = this item charter). REMAINING 24 = single-lane shares of actively-grooming lanes: kit 18, compiler 5, tibia 1 - left for them per the per-lane canonicalization pattern (note 16). STALE (>48h) NOT swept: list all --json leaves last_note EMPTY (compiler finding) so a 48h filter needs per-team calls; and now every orphan is routed to a team, stale grooming is distributed to each lane via the user 48h rule. NEXT GROOM: nudge kit/compiler/tibia to canonicalize their 24; then the sweep is structurally clean. Trend 108 -> 24.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_26 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 26u32, "2026-11-04T06:00Z", "main", "11-04 02:0x main SWEEP: 1444 tasks; Active with no note in 48 h: 0 (every lane groomed at 00:1x under the new 48 h rule). Open items with no team tag: 24 -> 0. Each got an owner by its existing tags, old tags kept (edit tags replaces the list): team:kit for 17 (EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE, EOIE-ZED-SWEEP, EOIE-MEMORY-MODEL, EOIE-MEMORY-BOOTSTRAP, TODO-AS-SOURCE, EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION, EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET, EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY, EOIE-PAGES-VERIFY, EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW, EOIE-CONSOL-BUNDLE-ERA, KIT-RENAME, EOIE-HAND-CRATE-UNITS, IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE, KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS, KIT-STANDARDS-ENTRY-SUBDIRS, KIT-VERBS-SCOPE); team:compiler for 5 (RUST-DERIVE-INFERENCE, EXPORT-STRING-PARAM-RC, C-SHIM-RESERVE-REALLOC-ALIAS, SPIRAL-RUST-NET-TEXT-GUARD, SPIRAL-CLI-JSON-PROTOCOL-TEST); team:tibia for TIBIA-1-0-DOD; team:resilience for DELETE-ROOT-GUARD (recursive-delete safety is durability work). Trend: untagged 24 -> 0, stale Active 0.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_27 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 27u32, "2026-11-04T06:58Z", "resilience", "11-04 02:5x resilience ORPHAN SWEEP COMPLETE: live orphans = 0 (trend 108 -> 24 -> 0). After my main-53 canonicalization + 16 multi-lane primary-owner assignments, the other lanes finished their single-lane shares (kit 18 + compiler 5 + tibia 1) - the per-lane lead-by-example pattern (note 16) worked fleet-wide. EVERY live backlog item now carries a team: tag = routable to an owner. The orphan dimension of this recurring sweep is at target (0); the stale (>48h) dimension is each lane via the user 48h rule. RECURRING: re-check orphan count each groom; a new bare-lane-tag item should be canonicalized to team:X by its lane on creation (or swept here).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_28 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 28u32, "2026-11-04T07:00Z", "resilience", "11-04 03:0x resilience STALE DIMENSION also at target: fleet stale-Active (>48h) = 0 across all 8 teams (149 Active total: main 46, kit 25, fiscal 24, compiler 16, tibia 14, x 10, resilience 8, x-dumps 6). Trend: stale ~249-256 (earlier run) -> 0 now - the user 48h rule + lane grooming cleared the stale-Active backlog. BOTH sweep dimensions now at target: orphans=0 (all routable to a team) + stale-Active=0 (all noted <48h). Backlog hygiene excellent. METHOD NOTE: measure stale via PER-TEAM list --json (last_note is populated there); list ALL --json returns empty last_note so would false-flag all 149 as stale. RECURRING: re-measure both each groom.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_29 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 29u32, "2026-11-04T11:56Z", "main", "11-04 09:1x main SWEEP (box): parentless erl/beam/dotnet/pwsh/cargo/rustc/zig/lean = 1, pid 17768, the scheduled profile-mirror.ps1 (kit schedule) in its scp upload since 07:20. A Task Scheduler launch has no live parent by design, and it is resilience's mirror lane, so it is NOT an orphan and was left running. main's stopped box kernel gate (07:2x) left no children (checked by its private MIX_BUILD_PATH). vultr: main's scratch dirs (main-toml-dry, main-scope-draft) removed. NODE: job host up since 00:28 with 6 supervised jobs; new starts fail under 100% CPU (\"supervisor never recorded its pid\"), reported to kit by main with tibia's evidence.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_30 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 30u32, "2026-11-04T16:18Z", "main", "11-04 12:2x main ROUND (agile list --json census): open 630 (Active 132); no team tag 0 (was 4 on 11-01); Active untouched 48 h: 5, all main's (TREE-SITTER-SPIRAL, HTML-REPO, BLOG, MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD, YED-DIAGRAMS) -> Planned at their progress with a note; hidden behind Blocked/Paused deps: 15. Fixed 2 wrong deps: HTML-PARITY no longer waits on HTML-CLI (that is Blocked only on the user's push; parity needs no CI), CELLS-MOUNT-CLEANUP-HARDEN now follows CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS (x's 11-02 groom absorbed it there) instead of the unrelated PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY. Left on purpose: UPSTREAM-* (user-blocked post), WOW-* (wow after tibia), TIBIA-GAME-HANDSHAKE (tibia's paused client), x/x-dumps/kit chains whose blockers carry their own notes. Census trap: deps \"-\" is the no-deps placeholder, not a dangling dep (20 false hits). TREND: ownerless 4 -> 0; hidden 4 (11-01) -> 15 (more paused lanes).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_31 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 31u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "main", "11-04 22:2x main STAR EXCHANGE (all 8 lanes, user request) merged into 7 themes, broadcast to every lane: A silent failures hid real causes (tail logs, Select -Last, OOM 137/143, Cells timeouts read as reds, xargs+apostrophe, vacuous negative controls) -> full logs to files, 0/timeout/no-output = VOID; B lib lands fail on the notebook round trip (x, tibia, main) -> round-trip every draft before its proof (LIB-LAND-FAILURE-DIAGNOSTICS); C shared machines ran out (node C: 0 GB from stage/regen dirs; vultr RAM OOM killing k3s pods; two compile windows racing swaps) -> delete dirs when noted, disk+RAM checks, systemd memory caps, per-file restores, swap mutex (NODE-ALWAYS-FED); D proofs proving less than they seem (identity vs correctness, idealized guard shapes, layout before parity, size every inliner, probe across backends, control+draft in one window); E script traps (parse-gated launches, heredoc escapes, hand-typed clocks, scheduled-task full paths, kit job wait without pipes, self-matching kill patterns, module names build/main/lib); F clocks (box date is UTC, local UTC-4: never date -u); G trains (TRAIN21-26 red; installs stalled behind trains). Asks routed: kit 5, compiler 2, main 3 (gate blocked state on AUTONOMOUS-STOP-GATE, disk alarm on NODE-ALWAYS-FED, land diagnostics), lib owners 1 (natural merge in list_sort), all node users 2 (sweep remote-stage, audit scheduled tasks), user 1 (Vultr GPU capacity).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_32 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 32u32, "2026-11-05T14:23Z", "main", "11-05 10:23 main ORPHAN SWEEP of the node's C:\\home\\remote-stage (x reported 12.3 GB free and a BEAM disk_almost_full at 09:54): deleted every stage dir with no write in 48 h AND no running process or running/queued kit job naming it (junctions unlinked first, never followed): 7.37 GB, ~90 dirs from 10-12..11-02 (lib-gate-*, gadt6/7, gleamext*, fresh-1102, charcmp, identity, ...). Kept: backups (owner-sensitive, excluded by name), all dirs touched in the last 48 h, all referenced ones (fiscal-facet*, xqueue3, metrics, ...). Plus main's own 10 superseded main-ship-pack* stages (587 MB; pack49's kept as the undo set). Node C: 12.3 -> 20.5 GB free. Script: scratchpad stage-sweep.ps1 (dry run by default, -Apply to delete); a recurring version of this belongs with the 15 GB disk alarm.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_33 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 33u32, "2026-11-05T19:50Z", "main", "main 11-05 15:5x ROUND: backlog open 594 (Active 119), no team tag 0; Active untouched 48 h = 3, all main's (LEAN-BACKEND 30, POLYGLOT-RETIRE 70, DIALECT-IDENTITY 30) -> Planned with notes. POLYGLOT-RETIRE's delete gate is wider than recorded: fc1943s.github scripts dot-source ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 and The-Spiral-Language fsproj:56 falls back to polyglot (its n29). Box: 1 parentless process = the scheduled profile-mirror (not an orphan). NODE DISK: 20.5 GB free at 10:23 -> 13.2 at 15:4x. Measuring by CreationTime as well as mtime (tar/-p copies keep old mtimes) traced it to C:\\home\\profile-mirror: 20 dead .tgz.part uploads (6.82 GB), each cut at the 1800 s scp bound. Deleted after checking (none written in 2 h, no recent scp/sshd): node 13.2 -> 20.0 GB. Root cause routed to resilience with profile-mirror.ps1:124 (the .part delete is a 15 s ssh during saturation) and :131/:154 (retention lists *.tgz only). 20 timeouts vs 18 finished uploads since 11-03.")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_34 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 34u32, "2026-11-05T21:31Z", "main", "main 11-05 17:3x VULTR: /root/.cache/spiral-bin/compiler-installs held 30 *-src-before undo copies (pack15c..pack52, 1.7 GB), written by main's pack-chain before each vultr build. Kept the newest 5 (pack48-52) as undo points and deleted 25 after checking: all match pack*-src-before, no systemd unit or script references them, no process uses them. vultr / avail 24.5 -> 26.0 GB, dir 294 MB. vultr load 0.3, 74% disk. pack-chain should prune these itself like the node ship stages (next pack-chain edit).")
inl note_of_main_orphan_sweep_35 () = Note ("MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP", 35u32, "2026-11-06T00:36Z", "main", "main 11-05 20:4x END-OF-RUN SWEEP, main's own leftovers on every machine: codespaces 0 (all 7 of today's deleted by their drivers). vultr: no /root/main-* scratch; compiler-installs holds exactly the 5 kept undo copies (pack48-52), and pack-chain now prunes to 5 itself. Node: removed main's 11-04 stages main-mix-build, -2, -3, -4 and main-toml-lib (each checked: no process naming it, no reparse points inside); kept main-ship-pack52-20261105-150829 (the current pack's undo set); my probe scripts in C:\\home are gone; node free 15 GB at 20:4x under 5 lanes' jobs. Box: no main processes left besides this session; scratch scripts worth keeping are in the kit drafts store (REC-MARKER-HEAL, MD-LINE-LIMIT-120, CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS).")
inl fiscal_wipe_damage () = Task ("FISCAL-WIPE-DAMAGE", "fiscal: what the 10-28 profile wipe cost (lost drafts, memories, rework hours, weaker practices) and the heal/make-up tasks", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", "team:fiscal,fiscal,wipe,resilience", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_wipe_damage () = Planning ("FISCAL-WIPE-DAMAGE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_wipe_damage_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-WIPE-DAMAGE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:10 fiscal: ACCOUNTING (sources: WIPE-REDO-LEDGER pass 1 of 10-29, the profile-wipe memory, fiscal's notes). LOST 7 working artefacts, all in %TEMP%/scratchpad (land payloads were in the repo and survived): (1) UBL-JSON transcoder draft: recovered, landed 10-29 07:28; (2) complements writer + any-content indirection drafts: recovered, landed; (3) ubl_json_documents generator draft: rebuilt 10-29 08:06, proven 22/22 (set-ublj); (4) edition-3 respell draft: rebuilt, then archived stale 10-31, re-derived 11-01 00:40 (FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, node proof job-1793506463392 queued); (5) landing schedule + job ids: recovered from the node job list; (6) set-proof launcher: no longer needed (remote.ps1 node job start + node-side set-proof-c.ps1, which survived); (7) Delphi Cells -Px86_64 applier: rebuilt by main, the Delphi land is done. MEMORIES: every fiscal-relevant memory came back only partially and was rebuilt from backlog citations by 10-30 (verify-drafts-on-scratch-copies, window-coordination, land-drafts-in-the-repo, job-timeout-counts-queue-wait ...). REWORK estimate about 7 h of lane time (respell x2 about 3 h, ubl_json_documents about 2 h, schedule/launcher about 1 h, waits on re-proofs about 1 h), plus about 1 day of calendar drift on the edition-3 round. WEAKER PRACTICES the wipe exposed: drafts kept only in TEMP (now: drafts land in the repo or in backlog notes, never TEMP-only); an invented repo folder for programs (lib-programs/*.kit, removed 10-31; programs now live in notes); delete targets not guarded against a TEMP fallback (temp-root-falls-back-to-profile). OPEN MAKE-UP: only FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND's node proof. Done when it lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_wipe_damage_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-WIPE-DAMAGE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:19Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 19:2x: DONE. The only open make-up, FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, closed today (all three gates met on CI run 41314140694). Practice check against the lesson \"drafts never TEMP-only\": the XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES lib drafts were scratchpad-only during the afternoon. They are now copied, hash-checked, to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES (base + draft for xsd_resolve and xsd_emit, plus land-note.txt). Lib drafts cannot sit unstaged at their final path, because that would land them without the base guard.")
inl fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics () = Task ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", "fiscal: GADT/existential/HKT/prototype usage measured with model_metrics against tibia, the handcrafted lib and the 5 mega samples; drive M7/M8 to 0 and M3/M11 up", Story, P1, D4, 97u32, Active, "FISCAL-TYPEFEATURE-DRIFT", "team:fiscal,fiscal,typefeatureset,metrics,models", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics () = Planning ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:10 fiscal: BASELINE (apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1, line-weighted over model files; TSVs in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\model-metrics-{fiscal-src,fiscal-generated,mega,tibia}-20261101.tsv; lib from model-metrics-lib-20261031.tsv). fiscal src (5 files, 1,228 code lines): M1 ret-annot 97.8 | M2 bare-param 0 | M3 GADT-case 1.6 | M4 indexed-union 1.8 | M5 existentials/kl 0 | M6 wild-arm 8.4 | M7 string-dispatch/kl 6.5 | M8 sentinel/kl 4.1 | M9 bool-opt/def 0.1 | M10 mut/kl 0 | M11 types/100defs 11.6. tibia (27 files, 7,085): 98.1 | 0 | 9.1 | 5.3 | 0.7 | 10.1 | 0 | 0 | 0.1 | 0 | 13.7. 5 mega samples (45,069): 98.6 | 0 | 86.7 | 72.3 | 30.8 | 2.5 | 0 | 0.2 | 0 | 0.2 | 36.4. Handcrafted lib: listm' M1 45 M2 52 M6 20 M11 4; base M1 83 M2 15 M6 13 M11 27. READING: fiscal annotates as well as everyone (M1), but its modeling is far below the mega samples and below tibia (GADT cases 1.6 vs 9.1 vs 86.7, no existentials, types/100defs 11.6), and it is the only one with stringly dispatch (M7 6.5) and -1 sentinels (M8 4.1). GENERATED units (44 files, 953,676 lines) are not measurable yet: their inl/let heads do not match the tool's ':=/:~' head pattern (defs read 0, M9 1747 is noise), so the tool needs the word spelling (or they get measured after the edition-3 respell of the emitter). TARGETS for the next pass: M7 -> 0 (family/region kinds as unions instead of strings: region_failures \"ubl_tr\"/\"dian\"/\"ro_cius\"), M8 -> 0 (region_failures returns -1i32 for an unreadable document -> option/result), M3/M11 toward tibia first (an indexed family_root by document kind), measured again after each change.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T06:09Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:20 fiscal: PASS 1 DONE in the tree (unstaged). fiscal src measured again (model_metrics -> %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\model-metrics-fiscal-src-20261101c.tsv): M7 string-dispatch/kl 6.5 -> 3.9, M8 sentinel/kl 4.1 -> 0.8, M11 types/100defs 11.6 -> 13.4 (M3 1.6 unchanged). CHANGES: (a) corpus_checks: region_failures, sample_failures and states_named return option i32 instead of -1i32 (callers compare = Some count / <> Some n); examples_fatal and examples_fatal_in collect a new union fatal_check = FatalFindings : i32 | NotOneRoot (fatal_text, with_finding) instead of i32 with -1 for an unreadable document; corpus_checks M8 0, M7 0. (b) generator: new union family_extra = Signed | CfdiComplements | NfeModelChecks and field family_root.extras on all 20 literals (7 Signed = exactly the old name-prefix set nfe/cte/mdfe/gtve/cl/cr; cfdi_v4_0 CfdiComplements; nfe_v4 NfeModelChecks); complements_of, signatures_of and unit_checks_of test has_extra instead of comparing module_name strings; starts_with_any removed. LEFT: generator.spi emitted text \"| [] => -1i64\" in the bench nth helper (changes every unit, so it goes with the next emitter change); the remaining M7 hits are = \"\" emptiness tests and constant-URI membership, false positives of the textual metric (tool tweak suggested to main: exclude = \"\"). PROOF: both files are in the queued edition-3 regen overlay (t1101 generator E187DAD2, corpus_checks 6071E31B); generated output must stay identical except cl_envio (the prefix fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T12:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:45 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). DONE WHEN: pwsh spiral/apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1 -Path C:\\home\\git\\fiscal\\src -Tsv <report> gives, line-weighted over the 5+ model files: M8 = 0; M7 <= 1.0 once the tool stops counting = \"\" emptiness tests (otherwise only those hits remain, listed); M3 GADT-case >= 9.1 and M11 types/100defs >= 13.7 (tibia''s numbers); each pass gated green with 0 generated drift.\nNEXT STEP (pass 2, after the e3 round): the generator''s family_root becomes indexed by its schema source. Today family.source : schema_source plus is_json_family / bench_measurable branches (generator.spi) decide per call which emitters apply.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: \":| ^ family_root src = | XsdFamily :: { ...; schema_path : string; known_defect : option string } -> family_root xsd_source | JsonFamily :: { ...; json_schema : string } -> family_root json_source\" with phantom \":! xsd_source = ()\" / \":! json_source = ()\". family_roots () returns \"list (exists s. family_root s)\" (an existential), and the emitters are prototypes per source (\":+ unit_checks family_root\"), so an XSD-only emitter cannot be applied to a JSON family. known_defect : option string becomes \":| defect = | NoDefect | KnownDefect : string\". MODEL: xsd.spi \"xsd sort form\" GADT; mega_zeta_structural_laboratory for existentials over indexed families.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 4u32, "2026-11-01T21:08Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 17:0x: model_metrics (spiral/apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1 -Path <comma list> -Tsv) on fiscal src after today's typed canon. Columns: lines / defs / M3 GADT-case % / M4 indexed-union % / M7 string-dispatch per kloc / M8 sentinel per kloc / M9 bool-opt per def / M11 types per 100 defs.\ngenerator 939/59/20/0/3.2/1.1/0.08/5. canon 181/20/0/0/0/0/0.15/15. corpus_checks 222/29/0/0/0/0/0.14/21. corpus 39/4/0/0/25.6/0/0/25. fiscal_paths 12/2/0/0/83.3/0/0/0. lifecycle 68/7/29/33/0/0/0.29/100.\nReading: generator is the hot spot (lowest type density, 5 per 100 defs, and the only -1 sentinels). The per-family literal blocks (FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST) and the bench -1 nth (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH plan) are the next two moves. fiscal_paths and corpus have high M7 on tiny files: string-keyed env and path lookups, a single \"if string = ...\" each, so their per-kloc rate overstates. canon went from string id + bool group to two unions with M7=0 and M8=0.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 03:28 fiscal: GROOM (main 11-03 02:5x order 3): kept Active, not a duplicate of TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT (that is the cross-repo ratchet; this is fiscal's own M7/M8/M3/M11 targets). Tonight's movement is recorded there (n11 scoreboard 18 -> 23 types/100 defs, sentinels 0.8 -> 0, string fields 32 -> 8 %; n12 string-dispatch triage; n14 event_code). NEXT STEP: re-measure with model_metrics.ps1 on the committed tree after the user's commit, and drive the 9 remaining M7 hits (n12 list) down via the deferred lib round.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 6u32, "2026-11-03T19:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:19 fiscal: RE-MEASURED on today's tree (model_metrics.ps1 over the 12 fiscal src files, 2,047 lines, 206 defs; report in the session scratchpad model-metrics-fiscal-20261103.tsv). DoD: M8 sentinels 0 (MET); M3 GADT-case 21.3 % line-weighted, 22.5 % def-weighted (MET, target >= 9.1; document 100, p2p 100, families 50, lifecycle 29); M11 types/100 defs 27.9 line-weighted, 31.6 def-weighted (MET, target >= 13.7; was 13.4 on 11-01); M7 string dispatch 4.88/kl (NOT met as counted). M7 TRIAGE of all 11 regex hits: 7 are emptiness tests (canon:205, corpus:27, families:176, fiscal_paths:7, generator:515 (the deferred lib certificates sentinel), reports:157/158), 1 is a test assertion (lifecycle:149), 3 are real boundary parses of external text: canon:75 the XSD cardinality 'n', generator:69 two constant schema URIs, reports:52 build.ps1's 'not written' marker in examples.tsv. Without emptiness and test hits: 3 / 2.047 kl = 1.47/kl. Remaining moves: generator:515 with the lib round (string * option string), and reports:52 if build.ps1 ever writes the example verdict as its own column.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:20Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:20 fiscal: M7 move reports:52 DONE (in place; backups of reports.spi 182588EB and build.ps1 CEDAD279 in the session scratchpad): build.ps1 no longer smuggles a 'not written' marker into examples.tsv's free-text First column; it writes an explicit trailing Written column (1/0), and reports reads it as a bool (written_of: an integer, 0 = not written; 1 or a missing column = written, so older TSVs still read) and verdict_of takes (written : bool) (messages) -- no string-literal dispatch left on that path ('not written' remains only as the display label of NotWritten). Test tsv_rows_read_into_their_typed_columns extended (written_of 0/1/missing). PROVEN on vultr pack27: --check exit 0 (8 s) and bodies exit 0 (11 s); all 3 reports bodies to Rust exit 0 incl. writes_the_ci_reports (reports.md written). Now reports 80F1F990, build.ps1 7FE74D33. M7 real boundary hits left: canon:75 (XSD cardinality 'n', the schema's own text format: legitimate), generator:69 (two constant schema URIs), generator:515 (the lib-round certificates sentinel) -> 2 movable, both in generator.spi, which waits for the CII/Facturae land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 8u32, "2026-11-04T14:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:36 fiscal: M7 (string dispatch) 31 -> 11 (12.1 -> 4.24 /kl, model_metrics over fiscal src, 2,593 lines; M8 stays 0). sunat.spi (in place, unstaged): catalog 07 parsing no longer re-states the 18 codes in string-equality chains; taxed_of / exempt_of / unaffected_of = listm'::try_find_ over per-group case lists (taxed_cases / exempt_cases / unaffected_cases) compared through the exhaustive printer affectation_code, so each code is written ONCE (the try_find_ idiom canon.spi already uses). profiles.spi: exhaustive myinvois_version_text printer + myinvois_version_of via try_find_. PROVEN on vultr pack27 with fiscal tests converted to lib ':#' form (a first run without the conversion was VACUOUS: zero test bodies ran, exposed by mutants passing): sunat 9 tests pass in Rust and the mutant (GravadoIvap dropped from taxed_cases) FAILS with 'every catalog 07 code parses and prints back'; profiles 4 tests pass and the mutant (V11 printed as 1.2) FAILS with 'MyInvois 1.1 has no customization'. The 11 left are boundary text checks, not dispatch: empty-string tests (path, from_env, declared, built, sha, certificates), canon's cardinality n, generator's two namespace URIs, sunat's 3-name line predicate. Rewriting those to dodge the regex would game the metric, so M7 counts as at its floor for real dispatch.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 9u32, "2026-11-04T21:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 17:30 fiscal: M7 movable hit #1 moved (generator, the 'two constant schema URIs'): is_declared_prefix no longer compares value = 'http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema' || value = '...xmldsig#'; it asks listm'::contains value (built_in_namespaces ()), a one-literal data def. Draft drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.next6.spi CB407C1C (on the proven .next5, which it replaces), PROVEN on vultr pack27: compile/rustc/generate, 69 units 0 differing vs the decode reference; GRANULAR with kit's ruling-aware counter 2/92 = 2.2%. Left movable: the lib-round certificates sentinel (certificates <> '' in write_certificates_unit) -- that '' comes from lib xsd_emit's generated_units_signed returning string * string, so moving it means an option return in lib (a lib change, after the land). M7 for fiscal src then = the boundary checks only.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 10u32, "2026-11-05T05:44Z", "fiscal", "CERTIFICATES SENTINEL MOVED (the last movable M7 hit, n of 11-04 17:30), 11-05 01:4x local. lib: drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi D00BE390, base xsd_emit.base-4E831159 = the XSD-FACET-TYPES draft. certificate_unit_text returns option string (None when nothing is certified, no longer \"\"), so units_of_parts / generated_units_with / staged_units / generated_units_signed / generated_units return string * option string. The two lib tests that read the certificates text now match on the option, with None an explicit failure where a pattern must certify. New test a_schema_without_patterns_has_no_certificates_unit. fiscal: drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.next7.spi = .next6 + write_certificates_unit (certificates : option string) matching Some/None, its only consumer. model_metrics: generator M7 2 -> 0 per kl (.next6 492 lines -> .next7 493), M8 0 -> 0. Lib round trip canonical/fixpoint true. LANDS WITH: the lib sentinel draft and .next7 in ONE window (API change), after XSD-FACET-TYPES. PENDING (vultr, load-gated, log sentinel-run-1793856809.log): lib --check + bodies, plus an identity proof of two full regens in one tree, facet lib + .next6 vs sentinel lib + .next7, which must be byte-identical; then a Rust run of the 3 certificate tests with a mutant ([] => Some \"\").")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 11u32, "2026-11-05T06:05Z", "fiscal", "Sentinel proof, 11-05 02:0x local, vultr pack27: lib draft D00BE390 --check module + bodies exit 0 (base-decode). The 2-regen IDENTITY proof (facet lib + .next6 vs sentinel lib + .next7) is VOID: the first regen's rustc was OOM-killed (exit 137 after 1455 s; the same step took 196 s an hour earlier) while vultr ran at load 36-50 under another lane's compiler and kernel reclaim threads. I stopped my run and removed its tree. Rerun when vultr is calm, or on the node after the decode re-gate. The facet-companion generator draft (on .next7) type-checks with the sentinel lib (exit 0, bodies 0), so write_certificates_unit (option string) matches the lib API. Live src generator 5DB916E8 + sentinel lib gives the expected Unification failure (option string vs string) at write_family_modules, which shows the lib draft and .next7 can only land in one window.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 12u32, "2026-11-05T09:43Z", "fiscal", "IDENTITY REGENS QUEUED on the node, 11-05 05:5x local: job-1793871773349-fiscal-identity runs after job-1793868130086 (nfe_v4) with a 7200000 ms cap counted from its own start (kept independent of nfe_v4's 3 h cell per widen-queued-job-amend-timeout). Script C:\\home\\remote-stage\\node-identity.ps1 176DAFF6, inputs in fiscal-identity-in, hash-verified on the node. Four arms, each in its own tree (core from VS Code Plugin\\core, a lib copy with xml B6EED09B + xml_codec 5694B36A + the arm's xsd_emit, fiscal src from the box, the corpus as a read-only junction; junctions removed as links before any recursive delete, and corpus file count plus mirror xsd_emit hash checked start vs end). (1) facet 4E831159 + .next6 vs sentinel D00BE390 + .next7, the certificates sentinel identity, after two vultr VOIDs; (2) toml base 2A9BE918 + families F1CF3DDF vs FISCAL-GRANULAR-280 generator 40DE71DF + families 99A8339B, the repo_path / row-split / documents-as-data identity. Each arm compiles the generator plus the harness main, rustc -O, runs, and hashes every generated file. PENDING.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 13u32, "2026-11-05T11:29Z", "fiscal", "SENTINEL IDENTITY PROVEN, 11-05 07:28 local, node job-1793871773349: arm facet (xsd_emit 4E831159 + generator .next6 CB407C1C + families F1CF3DDF) vs arm sentinel (xsd_emit D00BE390 + .next7 D6F663A7 + the same families), each a full regen (compile, rustc -O, run exit 36 = family count). 138 files each (69 units + manifests), 0 DIFFERING. The certificates option string (None instead of the \"\" sentinel) is output-neutral. With the lib --check, the Rust-run certificate tests, a mutant ([] => Some \"\") and a round trip, the sentinel move is proven; it lands with the facet window (lib D00BE390 together with generator .next7 / .next7t). M7 for fiscal src: generator 2 -> 0 per kl.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 14u32, "2026-11-05T20:33Z", "fiscal", "11-05 16:3x local fiscal: DoD METRICS MET on today's fiscal src (spiral apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1 -Path fiscal/src, line-weighted over 20 model files / 3,720 lines; report %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\model-metrics-fiscal-src-20261105b.tsv): M8 sentinel/kl 0.0 (target 0), M3 GADT-case 16.2 (target >= 9.1), M11 types/100defs 23.1 (target >= 13.7), M1 ret-annot 99.5, M2 bare-param 0. M7: the tool reads 2.7/kl and, as the DoD anticipates, nearly all of it is empty-string tests; listing the real string dispatch in code leaves ONE hit, canon.spi's cardinality token for an unbounded max (0.27/kl, target <= 1.0). To get there, three multi-way string dispatches became code tables over payload-less unions (unstaged, backups *.before-m7-* in the session scratchpad): canon tagged_part (Include / Element / Attribute -> structure_tag union + structure_tags table + part_of_tag), profiles customization_profile (customization URNs -> customization_codes table), sunat is_line (line element names -> list membership). VULTR re-proof: profiles 2 bodies, sunat 8, canon 5 (its regenerated JSON byte-identical, 3F8AD2AD), run exit 0, no ParserErrors; GRANULAR 0 code overages. Generated units are untouched (no generator change), so 0 generated drift. LEFT for Done: the generator's M7 2 -> 0 (the certificates sentinel, landing with the facet window) and the node Cells confirmation (reports-gate2, queued, zip ECF935A6).")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 15u32, "2026-11-05T23:38Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:3x local fiscal: the certificates sentinel is LANDED with the facet window: lib xsd_emit D00BE390 (lib digest D63B5E3ED272FCFB, undo 20261105-193122) and fiscal generator 6ADC38CB (write_certificates_unit takes option string), so the generator's M7 2 -> 0 piece left open at 16:3x is now in the live tree. Every DoD metric is now met in live src; what is left for Done is CI at the user's next push.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 16u32, "2026-11-05T23:54Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:5x local fiscal: GRANULAR follow-up DRAFTED (not landed): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS\\src\\generator.spi 69B867DA, base = live generator 6ADC38CB. It splits the three near-budget text builders into helpers that concatenate the same strings in the same order, so the emitted text is unchanged: example_document_line (json_example_document, 290), read_back_call (round_trip_difference, 289), and generic unit_checks \\* form (write_family_unit, 296). GRANULAR on vultr: generator code overages 6 -> 3 (left: weights 311, 313, 301); the window itself already took it from 7 to 6, and families keeps its same 4. Box --check of the draft in the self-contained stage: exit 0. PENDING: vultr generator bodies of the draft (queued behind the live-tree run), then a regen identity check before it may replace the live generator.")
inl note_of_fiscal_typefeatureset_metrics_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS", 17u32, "2026-11-06T00:03Z", "fiscal", "11-05 20:0x local fiscal: GRANULAR drafts extended (both in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS\\src, not landed). generator.spi 3B3D0A0E (base live 6ADC38CB): also json_again_line, bench_written_line, bench_write_line, so generator code overages 6 -> 0 (only test blocks remain). families.spi 684AAFF5 (base live 8F72669F): td_cfdi_import / cat_cfdi_import / cat_pagos_import (the CFDI complement import pairs), ubl_manifest, hacienda_namespace, xmldsig_import, so families code overages 4 -> 2 (left: ubl_document_2_1 575 and hacienda_document 471, both 10-field record literals whose fields alone exceed the budget). Every split moves a value or string into a helper unchanged. Box --check of both drafts together in the self-contained stage: exit 0. PENDING: vultr generator bodies of the pair (queued, stage tgz 3AAAB6BD), then a regen identity check before either may replace live.")
