inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:10 fiscal: MEASURED (body characters after the header line, Latin weight 1): 169 top-level definitions in src/*.spi, 83 over 280. Biggest five with their split plan: (1) corpus_checks.spi:227 test regional_rules_census 6,112 -> one census helper plus one test per region (UBL-TR, ZATCA, RO, DIAN, PEPPOL), each pinning only its own row; (2) generator.spi:750 family_bench 3,553 -> emit_bench_header / emit_bench_timing / emit_bench_write pieces joined by one 1-line def; (3) generator.spi:620 json_round_trip 3,424 -> emit_json_read, emit_json_write, emit_json_compare; (4) corpus_checks.spi:700 dian_samples_keep_their_compiled_rule_findings 3,109 -> the 44-row expected table as its own data definition (dian_expected_findings), split by toolkit folder (Ejemplificaciones vs Eventos RADIAN), and a short check; (5) corpus_checks.spi:606 zatca_samples_pass_the_zatca_rules 2,352 -> rule loading, findings collection and the assertion as three defs. Do AFTER the edition-3 respell lands (it rewrites every line), one file per change, with a full src gate each.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 2u32, "2026-11-01T06:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:33 fiscal: SPLIT 2 of 5 DRAFTED (generator.spi family_bench, 3,553 chars). Scratch draft scratchpad granular/generator.spi (26FFBDAC, base = tree 84EDD77C): family_bench becomes 20 defs, all <= 280 body chars: bench_measurable, bench_one, bench_text, bench_insert, bench_nth, bench_runs_head, bench_clock, bench_parse, bench_write, bench_accumulate, bench_runs_end, bench_rounds, bench_row, bench_row_end, bench_ours_read, bench_ours_folder, bench_ours_write, bench_ours_end, bench_measure, bench_report, and family_bench itself (one line). PROOF so far: the string literals of the pieces, concatenated in call order, are identical to the old body's (the one/bench_one text excluded, which moved from a local binding into a helper), so the emitted bench text is unchanged by construction. Formatter-stable (only the 4 pre-existing long-line hunks in the test section). Kept OFF the queued edition-3 regen overlay on purpose, so a mistake here cannot void that proof. NEXT: after the e3 regen lands, re-derive on the edition-3 tree (respell), gate the generator on the node, and require 0 generated drift. Measured method for the other splits: the same literal-order check plus the 280 count per piece.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 3u32, "2026-11-01T06:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:38 fiscal: SPLIT 3 of 5 DRAFTED (generator.spi json_round_trip, 3,424 chars) in the same scratch draft (granular/generator.spi 1C45F572): 18 defs, all <= 280: json_xml_size, json_xml_sizes, json_take_named, json_take_rest, json_size_drift, json_size_drift_some, json_size_drift_end, json_size_drift_added, json_document_head, json_typed (one parameterised emitter for the identical once/twice lines), json_stability, json_size_check, json_drift_detail, json_drift_lost, json_not_one, json_helpers, json_check, json_round_trip (one line). PROOF: literal content identical in call order; the once/twice lines checked by expansion of json_typed. Formatter: only the pre-existing over-long emitted literal lines (now inside the pieces). Remaining over 280 in generator: json_document_checks (1,876) and json_example_check (1,231), next.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 4u32, "2026-11-01T06:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:43 fiscal: SPLIT 4 DRAFTED (json_document_checks, 1,876 chars) in the same scratch draft (granular/generator.spi): document_check_head, document_list, document_check_read, document_check_compare, document_check_verdict, document_failures, document_failure_message, document_checks_text, json_document_checks (guard only); literal content identical in call order; all <= 280. NEW METRIC (overflow = top-level defs whose body exceeds 280 chars / all defs; same counter for every file): generator tree 45/85 (53%) -> split draft 42/130 (32%); corpus_checks 32/62, corpus 2/6, fiscal_paths 1/2, lifecycle 3/18. Record and family literals (family_roots 1,855, nfe_events 760, fatturapa 742 ...) are the bulk of what is left: data, which splits by moving each literal's long fields into named helpers. Still deliberately off the e3 overlay; gate after the e3 regen lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 5u32, "2026-11-01T12:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 08:46 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 4). DONE WHEN: the overflow counter (top-level defs whose body exceeds 280 chars / all defs, the script in note 4) reports <= 10% for src/generator.spi and src/corpus_checks.spi (today 45/85 and 32/62), each split proven by (1) the literal-order check (string literals of the pieces concatenated in call order = the old body''s) and (2) a node regeneration with 0 generated drift and every gate green.\nNEXT STEP: after the e3 round, re-derive the scratch draft (granular/generator.spi, splits 2-4) on the edition-3 tree, gate it, then the record literals (family_roots 1,855, nfe_events 760 ...): move each literal''s long fields into named helpers.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a split must not lower the typing: no piece may take or return a raw string where the original had a typed value; prefer one parameterised emitter (json_typed in split 3) over copy-pasted pieces; the family literals shrink when FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS pass 2 turns them into GADT cases.")
