inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 10u32, "2026-11-04T05:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:11 fiscal: corpus_checks.spi pass (in place, output-identical by construction; backup in the session scratchpad corpus_checks.before-granular.spi 63395956 -> FBD411B5): model_census 882 -> 585 (Complex/Derived arms -> complex_census, Element/Attribute inline arms -> inline_census, kind-polymorphic members of the same recursive group; every arm now one line); resolve_corpus 648 -> 332 (the 4-counter record -> resolved_file + one_if); examples_fatal 487 -> 446 and examples_fatal_in 508 -> 468 (shared read-one-root-and-count -> fatal_of (count : xml_node -> i32), each keeping its own validator). vultr pack27: --check exit 0, bodies exit 0 (NB: needed --check --timeout-ms 180000; vultr load 11-15 tonight makes the 30 s default attestation time out with exit 3 on unchanged code too). RUNTIME PROOF QUEUED: node job-1793769101331-fiscal-corpus-checks2 (after the ds:Object regen job), predicted corpus_checks 28/28 with the same counts (580 files, 12077 elements, 2238 complexTypes, 5389 simpleTypes). Still over the proxy here: multi-parameter signatures and a 9-arm GADT walk (one concept each); generator.spi/families.spi wait until the CII/Facturae draft lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 11u32, "2026-11-04T11:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:51 fiscal: LINE-WIDTH PASS (kit standards over fiscal src: 17 findings -> 8, all remaining 8 in families.spi/generator.spi, which carry pending drafts and are fixed with those lands). Fixed in place, meaning-preserving (backups in the session scratchpad width-backup): canon x2 (a bound 'terms' sub-expression; the types list one per line), corpus_checks x2 (the counted tuples bound as 'counts') + its missing final newline, generated_runtime x1 (the emitted test line split into two string pieces -- identical concatenated text), lifecycle x4 (cancel's signature wrapped, the Authorized GADT case's '-> document r authorized' on its own line, two test expressions bound to names). Now: canon CDD54AC0, corpus_checks 08330A6D, generated_runtime 10B9A650, lifecycle 811CF253. PROOF vultr pack27: --check exit 0 for all four, formatter accepts each unchanged, lifecycle's 5 bodies to Rust exit 0 (canon/corpus_checks read the corpus at test time: type-level only here; corpus_checks' node proof job-1793769101331 runs the pre-width FBD411B5, the width change is binding-only).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 12u32, "2026-11-04T14:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:28 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793769101331-fiscal-corpus-checks2, pinned core 0758BAF496AE4E7D start and end, pattern-oracle outputs written first as build.ps1 does, box manifests): corpus_checks discovered 28 executed 28 passed 28 failed 0 -- the prediction (28/28) met, including the 2 rows VOID on 11-03 (NotFound) and the new MyInvois rows; the granular corpus_checks split (complex_census / inline_census / resolved_file / one_if / fatal_of) is proven under Cells. MEASURE now (rules 1+2 applied, tests excluded, my scratch approximation of the counter): fiscal src 423 defs, 68 flat dispatches, 61 over 280 = 14.4%; by file generator 39.4% (13/33), families 45.1% (23/51), corpus_checks 11.8%, canon/document/lifecycle/sunat 12-15%, p2p/reports/profiles ~10%. Largest: generator's emitted-code templates (json_round_trip 3136, family_bench 2593, unit_text 2051, json_document_checks 1613, unit_checks_of 1449) and families' data table family_roots 1615. generator.spi and families.spi carry pending drafts (decode generator 7C315FDB, families F1CF3DDF), so their splits follow those lands.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 13u32, "2026-11-04T14:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:42 fiscal: BATCH in place (unstaged; backups in the session scratchpad *.before-granular.spi): canon.spi 4DE1FE49 (business_terms -> is_business_term_reference + reference_terms; visit_element -> term_names + declared_data_type; read_children Include branch -> included_terms (group member); structure_terms -> document_section_terms; term_json -> term_kind_text + ubl_json): canon 11.1% -> 3.8%. PROOF (vultr pack27, base with fiscal_paths + json_schema, fiscal tests converted to ':#'): before and after BOTH write en16931-terms.json byte-identical (9DBC4B63), 160 terms / 30 groups; a mutant (BUSINESS_TERM misspelled) FAILS '160 EN 16931 terms and 30 groups'. (The committed canon/en16931-terms.json is the pretty-printed form, 2094 lines; the test writes compact JSON -- a pre-existing gap, unrelated.) generated_runtime.spi 7AFC49F9: unit_text (2017 chars) -> one section per emitted function (sample_root/sample_path, run_count, run_at, insert_run, median, sorted_runs, two test sections); PROVEN by evaluation: one module with the old body renamed old_unit_text and a test unit_text () = old_unit_text () passes in Rust; a one-char mutant FAILS. fiscal_paths.spi ED33DAB9: root -> checkout_root (check exit 0, format 0). MEASURE (rules 1+2, tests excluded): fiscal src 441 defs, 58 over = 13.2%; WITHOUT families.spi + generator.spi (pending drafts) 357 defs, 22 over = 6.2%. The remaining distance to 10% is entirely in those two files and follows the decode land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 14u32, "2026-11-04T14:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:51 fiscal: GRANULAR-GENERATOR draft (kit drafts fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.spi 28372016, on the decode generator 3564751D) PROVEN output-identical on vultr pack27: regen of all 69 units, 0 differing vs the decode reference (vultr's generator restored after, DA6BE426 = the decode draft + its harness main). Change: typed_round_expression factors the emitted 'T_to_xml root (xml_codec.expect_decoded (T_of_xml<witness> <source>))' text that four sites wrote out by hand (two JSON checks, json_round_trip's once/twice via typed_pass_text). Formatter: the draft adds 0 drift (18 lines, all pre-existing in the base). Further template splits held for the GRANULAR-STATS ruling ask (notes 32-33).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:02Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:02 fiscal: CORRECTION of notes 12-13 (14.4% / 6.2%): scratch approximation. kit's ACTUAL counter (Spiral.Cells.CellBudget.over_budget, default profile, top_level_blocks for the denominator; run on vultr's synced Cells, private MIX_BUILD_PATH), test blocks excluded: xsd_emit decode base 145/329 = 44.1%, split draft 7FDA3007 177/432 = 41.0%; live xpath_eval 63/235 = 26.8%; fiscal src: families 56.5, generator 60.0 (granular draft 56.3), canon 28.0, corpus_checks 27.7, generated_runtime 25.0, sunat 22.4, document 17.4, posting 16.7, lifecycle 15.4, p2p 14.3, profiles 11.8, reports 10.9, fiscal_paths 0. Main gap vs my scratch counter: the real weight counts EVERY character incl. leading indentation (mine trimmed it), and the counter does not apply the 11-04 rules (1)/(2).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 16u32, "2026-11-04T15:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:07 fiscal: kit RULED (b) at ~11:0x by message: the DoD is the counter WITH rules (1)/(2); signature-only and flat-dispatch overages count as compliant until kit's CellBudget change lands in apps/cells, then re-measure. Ruled measure meanwhile via my draft Spiral.Cells.CellBudgetRuled (kit drafts cells\\CELLBUDGET-RULES, real weights incl. indentation, tests excluded, run on vultr): fiscal src lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6, document 13.0, corpus_checks 14.9, canon 16.0, generated_runtime 16.7, generator 46.7 (granular draft 43.8), families 52.2 (data records; data/template ruling still open in GRANULAR-STATS 32-33).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_17 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 17u32, "2026-11-04T16:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 12:40 fiscal: canon.spi 6AE6468D (in place, unstaged; backup canon.before-ruled.spi in the session scratchpad) under the RULED measure (kit's CellBudgetRuled, tests excluded): 8/50 -> 5/54 = 9.26%. Splits: add_terms -> term_row_of, cardinality_of -> cardinality_parts, term_id_of -> term_id_from, visit_element -> element_terms. PROVEN on vultr (fiscal tests converted to ':#'): before and after write en16931-terms.json byte-identical (9DBC4B63), 160 terms / 30 groups; mutant (BUSINESS_TERM misspelled) FAILS the 160/30 assertion. Fiscal src ruled now: canon 9.3, lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6, document 13.0 (2 of its 3 are type declarations + one record literal), corpus_checks 14.9, generated_runtime 16.7 (2 template sections), generator 46.7 / families 52.2 (pending drafts; template/data ruling open).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_18 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 18u32, "2026-11-04T17:47Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 13:47 fiscal: corpus_checks.spi 901E881A (in place, unstaged; backup corpus_checks.before-ruled.spi 08330A6D in the session scratchpad) under the RULED measure (kit's CellBudgetRuled, tests excluded): 7/47 -> 1/53 = 1.9% (the one left is resolved_file, a single record literal). Splits: census_corpus -> schema_census, resolve_corpus -> resolve_file, region_failures -> report_failures, catalog_states -> with_large_catalog, examples_fatal -> en16931_example_fatal, examples_fatal_in -> example_fatal_in. PROVEN on vultr pack27 (new base base-fiscal-corpus = base-fiscal + fiscal's corpus module; FISCAL_ROOT dec-gen/fiscal with src/corpus.txt generated as pattern-oracle.ps1 writes it: 580 DFe.NET xsd): module + all 28 tests typed (--check and bodies exit 0); the 5 tests reaching the changed functions (models_the_corpus_census, resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet, cfdi_catalogs_become_minimal_dfas, cen_examples_pass_the_en16931_rules, ro_cius_examples_keep_their_ro_findings) PASS in Rust; mutant (schema_census drops the element census) FAILS with '12077 modeled elements, got 9662'. Two earlier attempts were VOID harness gaps (corpus module missing; src/corpus.txt is git-ignored), not verdicts.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_19 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 19u32, "2026-11-04T17:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 13:49 fiscal: ALL 14 src modules measured with kit's CellBudgetRuled (code-only, vultr): canon 9.3, corpus 16.7 (1/6), corpus_checks 1.9, document 13.0, families 52.2, fiscal_paths 0, generated_runtime 16.7 (2/12), generator 46.7, lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, posting 16.7 (1/6), profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6. Every over-10% file outside generator/families is over ONLY through data literals or type declarations, no logic left to split: corpus add_file (one 6-counter record), posting invoice_lines (a 3-entry ledger list), document (term_value GADT + canon_document record type + canon_record record literal), generated_runtime (2 emitted-text template sections). Open: (a) kit's template/data ruling (GRANULAR-STATS 32-33) decides whether literals/types count; (b) generator + families land first (decode), then their split.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_20 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 20u32, "2026-11-04T18:29Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 14:29 fiscal: kit RULED (msg 14:2x, full text on GRANULAR-STATS): data = a type declaration or a def whose body is ONE record/list/tuple literal of constants + constructor applications only -> exempt, reported as its own row; a template counts per emitted section only if it ONLY concatenates string literals, and a template interpolating logic (match/if/fold/call on a non-constant) is measured whole as CODE. Applied to generator: next-layer draft drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.next.spi ECBD351B on top of FC53C8CA (land draft unchanged, frozen): generated_folder + capped_unit_text (write/remove share the folder), is_declared_prefix + prefix_pair (declared_prefixes), json_schema_model (family_schema), family_checks + family_any_content + write_certificates_unit + write_family_module (write_family_modules = recursion only). PROVEN on vultr pack27 with the land xsd_emit AB4B0165: compile/rustc/generate as always, 69 units 0 differing vs the decode reference. Ruled code-only 14/32 -> 12/41 (29.3%). The 12 left are interpolating templates (example_document, json_example_check, json_document_checks, document_round_trip, json_round_trip, document_checks, xsd_example_check, family_bench, unit_checks_of, ...): by the ruling they are code and need per-section splitting next. families: its 24 rows call fiscal_paths::under and ++#, so they are NOT data yet; making schema/catalog paths relative constants resolved where read would make all 24 exempt (next layer after the land).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_21 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 21u32, "2026-11-04T18:48Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 14:48 fiscal: template splits under kit's ruling, next-layer drafts in drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src (land draft generator.spi FC53C8CA untouched): .next2 75916581 PROVEN on vultr pack27 (compile/rustc/generate, 69 units 0 differing vs the decode reference): example_document -> root_declaration; document_round_trip -> round_trip_reader/difference/arms; xsd_example_check -> pinned_defect + example_write; json_example_check -> json_example_document/write/round; document_checks -> quoted_paths + both_failures + document_reads; shared emitted lines written ONCE: failures_raise () (was emitted by 2 templates), relative_sample_read () (3); unit_checks_of -> a guard + nfe_model_checks () (pure literal template). Ruled list after .next2 (14 over of 58; pure-literal templates nfe_model_checks 2002 and failures_raise 379 are exempt-per-section under the ruling but CellBudgetRuled does not implement that yet): json_round_trip 3346, family_bench 3255, json_document_checks 784, write_family_module 692, json_member_check 532, json_example_write 488, family_checks 430, document_reads 418, json_example_round 417, example_write 362, example_document 350, write_generated_module_with 275. .next3 CEC6452A (proving): json_round_trip -> json_size_helpers () + json_round_trip_verdict () (pure literal) + json_round_trip_reads; family_bench -> is_measurable, bench_timer/insert_runs/row_tail/folder (literal), bench_parse_line (one line emitted at 2 indents), bench_run_tail/report/sample/write; json_document_checks -> json_documents_head/test + schema_read_line (shared with json_example_write). Ask for kit: CellBudgetRuled could mark a def whose body only joins string literals as a template row, per the ruling.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_22 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 22u32, "2026-11-04T19:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:00 fiscal: families under kit's data rule, ANALYSIS (no edit): of its 24 overages, only ~12 are single record literals that a path change would turn into data (cfdi_v4_0, nfe_v4_00, fatturapa, ksef, chile x2, facturae, verifactu, saft, mydata, hacienda_factura, nav, gst...): they fail the rule only through fiscal_paths::under / ++# path joins; a nominal ':! repo_path = string' field (constructor application = data) resolved where read (generator: qualifies_children, prefix_declarations, family_schema, json_schema_model; catalog entries likewise; repo_relative(under x) = x so emitted text stays identical) would exempt them. The rest are CODE by the rule and stay so: family_roots / nfe_events / hacienda_documents build rows through a local builder (calls), ubl_* rows read manifests (manifest_documents), cfdi_complement takes parameters -- expanding builders into literal rows would trade a shared shape for repetition. Deferred: it touches families F1CF3DDF + generator, both frozen in the decode land set; do it as a next layer after the land.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_23 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 23u32, "2026-11-04T19:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:07 fiscal: generator.spi MEETS the GRANULAR DoD in its draft chain. drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src: generator.spi FC53C8CA (land draft: decode + typed_round_expression/typed_pass_text + 3600 s cap) -> .next ECBD351B -> .next2 75916581 -> .next3 CEC6452A -> .next4 585F5F7E -> .next5 48E4A89D; EACH layer PROVEN on vultr pack27 with the land xsd_emit AB4B0165: compile/rustc/generate, all 69 regen units 0 differing vs the decode reference. Ruled (kit CellBudgetRuled, tests excluded): 14/32 (43.8%) -> 12/41 -> 14/58 -> 19/74 -> 15/82 -> 8/91 = 8.8% RAW; 6 of the 8 are literal-only templates (failures_raise, json_size_helpers, json_round_trip_verdict, bench_timer, bench_insert_runs, nfe_model_checks) that kit's 11-04 ruling measures per section, so code-only = 2/85 = 2.4% (family_bench 292, write_family_module 360). Every emitted line that two templates shared is now written once (failures_raise, relative_sample_read, sample_folder_line, sample_write_call, single_failures, schema_read_line, bench_parse_line at 2 indents, quoted_paths); write_unit_package is now the one place a unit manifest is written (the TOML migration's hook). Land: the .next5 file replaces the land draft (same base) once the decode set lands; generator tests then run in the node gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_24 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 24u32, "2026-11-04T19:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:21 fiscal: generated_runtime.spi 2F02F888 (in place, unstaged; backup generated_runtime.before-ruled.spi 7AFC49F9 in the session scratchpad): sample_path_text called sample_root_text (code by the ruling) -> split into sample_path_tail () (literal-only) + a one-line composition. Ruled 2/12 -> 1/13 raw; the one left, median_tests_text, is a literal-only template (exempt per section) -> code-only 0/12. PROVEN on vultr pack27: the new file swapped into the regen harness with the GRANULAR-GENERATOR .next5 generator regenerates all 69 units 0 differing vs the decode reference, generated_fiscal_runtime included; harness restored (35D02A45). Fiscal src code-only (kit ruling, literal templates + data exempt): canon 9.3, corpus_checks 1.9, generated_runtime 0, lifecycle 3.8, p2p 4.8, profiles 5.9, reports 6.5, sunat 8.6, fiscal_paths 0; document/corpus/posting over only through data defs (document's canon_record calls decimal::add, so it stays code: 1/21 = 4.8% once the two type declarations are exempt); generator 2.4% in its draft chain; families waits on the land (see note 22).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_25 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 25u32, "2026-11-04T19:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:21 fiscal: CORRECTION to note 24: corpus add_file (counter arithmetic: totals::x + xml::count_named ...) and posting invoice_lines (ledger::debit/credit calls) make non-constructor calls, so by kit's rule they are CODE, not data: corpus 1/6 and posting 1/6 = 16.7% each stay over 10% (one record-building def in a six-def file; splitting the record would scatter one fact). Only document's two type declarations are data.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_26 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 26u32, "2026-11-04T19:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 15:39 fiscal: RE-MEASURED with kit's ruling-aware counter (box apps/cells cell_budget_ruled.ex 79B1FC32, loaded with mix run -r on vultr since vultr's mirror still has D4E2BEFB; code-only, tests excluded), fiscal src as it will land: canon 5/54 9.3, corpus 1/6 16.7, corpus_checks 1/53 1.9, document 1/23 4.3, fiscal_paths 0/4, generated_runtime 0/13, generator (.next5 draft) 2/91 2.2, lifecycle 0/26, p2p 0/21, posting 1/6 16.7, profiles 1/17 5.9, reports 3/46 6.5, sunat 3/58 5.2, families (land draft F1CF3DDF) 24/47 51.1. AGGREGATE 42/465 = 9.0% (<= 10%); without families 18/418 = 4.3%. Per FILE, three stay over: families (rows built through calls; repo_path plan in note 22, after the land), corpus add_file and posting invoice_lines (one record-building def in a six-def file). Which reading is the DoD -- aggregate or per file?")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_27 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 27u32, "2026-11-04T21:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 17:30 fiscal: generator's land file is now drafts\\fiscal\\GRANULAR-GENERATOR\\src\\generator.next6.spi CB407C1C (supersedes .next5 48E4A89D, removed; adds built_in_namespaces for M7); proven identical (69 units), 2/92 = 2.2% with kit's ruling-aware counter.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_28 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 28u32, "2026-11-05T04:02Z", "fiscal", "Rebase fact, 11-05 00:1x local: the user commit bb1ebad (11-04 23:18) put my unstaged 11-04 src into HEAD. Live src/generator.spi 5DB916E8 = the decode base 7C315FDB minus test generates_cii_d16b, which was dropped because live families.spi B59F8A10 has no cii_d16b (). That family exists only in the FISCAL-CII-PROFILES draft F1CF3DDF, which also switches local_xmldsig to w3c_xmldsig and adds the Facturae documents. So generator .next6 CB407C1C (it still has generates_cii_d16b) must land in one window with families F1CF3DDF, or drop the test; it can never land alone over 5DB916E8. Diff each draft against live before -Apply: generator.base-3564751D differs from live by 46 lines, and those are the decode changes that land with XSD-DECODE-RESULT.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_29 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 29u32, "2026-11-05T06:52Z", "fiscal", "REPO_PATH LAYER DRAFTED, but MEASURED 0 gain (11-05 02:5x local). Drafts drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src\\families.spi 53B36EFD (base F1CF3DDF) and generator.spi C54163F3 (base = the toml draft 2A9BE918): \":! repo_path = string\" with repo_text / repo_file; schema_path : repo_path; \"Xsd : list (string * repo_path)\" plus catalog_of; every single-family literal spells its paths in full (no fiscal_paths::under, no local ++# joins; long literals joined with ^^); the generator reads repo_file family::schema_path, emits repo_text (so the emitted text is identical to the old repo_relative output) and deletes the now unused repo_relative. Ruled counter (box apps/cells cell_budget_ruled.ex F1489A93, code defs only): families 24/49 before and 24/50 after; generator 2/91 -> 2/90. WHY 0: CellBudgetRuled.data_literal? rejects any lowercase identifier followed by an argument, so nominal constructor applications (module_id \"x\", tag_name \"x\", definition_name \"x\", namespace_uri \"x\", repo_path \"x\") count as calls; only uppercase union constructors pass. So the 11-04 premise (\"constructor application = data\") does not hold for :! nominals under the counter. Options: (a) the counter treats names declared with \":!\" as constructors (asked on GRANULAR-CELLBUDGET-RULES); (b) families become rows of plain strings typed by ONE converter into family_root, which gives up nominal typing at the literal only to satisfy a lexical rule (not done: it would game the metric). The repo_path draft is kept as a cleanup (typed repo-relative paths, no path joins) but is NOT a GRANULAR fix; its identity regen is planned on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_30 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 30u32, "2026-11-05T07:31Z", "fiscal", "TYPE-CHECKS PASS, 11-05 03:30 local, vultr pack27 (deps trees built with cp -rL; reference dec-gen xsd_emit 5B274B48 checked before and after; MemAvailable gate >= 2100 MB). Generator --check + bodies exit 0 for all three: (1) repo_path layer, generator C54163F3 + families 53B36EFD over the decode lib; (2) generator.next7t AA09ECE1 (sentinel + toml) + families F1CF3DDF over the sentinel lib D00BE390; (3) facet companion generator.toml A9622AB3 + families 8472AD8B over the sentinel lib. The identity regens (sentinel vs facet, repo_path vs toml base) stay PENDING: both vultr attempts went VOID (memcg kill exit 137; rustc timeout exit 124 after 2402 s while the VM was starved). They move to the node after its nfe_v4 gate.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_31 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 31u32, "2026-11-05T07:54Z", "fiscal", "WITH KIT'S NOMINAL RULE (11-05 03:5x local; kit built it unstaged in spiral apps/cells: applications of any :!-declared name count as data constructors): box mix spiral.cell_budget --granular, code defs only. families base F1CF3DDF 24/49 = 49% (unchanged: every literal still calls fiscal_paths::under); repo_path draft 53B36EFD 14/53 = 26.4%. The repo_path layer is now the fix it was planned to be. The 14 left: 8 are CODE by design (cfdi_tfd / cfdi_pagos call cfdi_complement; family_roots, nfe_events and hacienda_document(s) are builders; ubl_invoice / ubl_creditnote / ubl_document_2_1 / mydata / nav read manifest_documents). 3 are pure literals blocked only by the call w3c_xmldsig () (facturae 1282, verifactu 707, hacienda_factura 579). NEXT: make w3c_xmldsig a parameterless value if edition 3 allows it (a bare name counts as data), otherwise inline the one repo_path literal; then 11/53 = 20.8%. The aggregate DoD (fiscal src <= 10%) holds well before that.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_32 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 32u32, "2026-11-05T08:30Z", "fiscal", "repo_path families FINAL, 11-05 04:3x local: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src\\families.spi E91CEC5C = 53B36EFD with w3c_xmldsig () inlined as the repo_path literal at its 5 uses (facturae, verifactu, hacienda_factura, hacienda_document, fatturapa already literal). A parameterless value (:= w3c_xmldsig : repo_path = ...) is NOT valid edition 3: \"Global inl/let statements should all return functions known at parse time\" (vultr --check, exit 5). The inline variant --check + bodies exit 0 (with generator C54163F3, decode lib). With kit's nominal rule: 11/52 = 21.2% (base F1CF3DDF 24/49 = 49%); the 11 left are builders, manifest readers and parameterized rows, i.e. code by design. Identity regen (repo_path vs toml base): PENDING on the node. Also VOID on vultr, 04:2x: the emitter-level sentinel identity probe. rustc of xsd_emit alone needs more than 1.6 GB (opt-level 1: memcg kill at 1.63 GB RSS; opt-level 0: 1800 s timeout while reclaiming), so every identity proof moves to the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_33 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 33u32, "2026-11-05T08:53Z", "fiscal", "sunat.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 04:5x local, in place and unstaged (backup sunat.before-granular.spi AF9FFB8C in the scratchpad): 3/56 -> 0/60 code defs over (box mix spiral.cell_budget --granular with kit's nominal rule). Splits: scheme_verdict out of scheme_finding; category_here plus a shared tallied (also used by line_findings, which had the same tally arms) out of category_findings; price_verdict out of price_finding, rewritten as one guarded arm over optionm::map (same semantics: an unknown reason gives None, a match gives None, otherwise the message). PROOF vultr pack27 (dec-gen lib, pe corpus present): --check + bodies exit 0; all 8 bodies run in Rust with exit 0 (corpus rules over the homologation set included); MUTANT (price_verdict <> flipped to =) FAILS 'an onerosa line prices with 01, a free transfer with 02'.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_34 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 34u32, "2026-11-05T08:57Z", "fiscal", "reports.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 05:0x local, in place and unstaged (8987026C; backup reports.before-granular.spi in the scratchpad): 3/45 -> 0/49 code defs over. Splits: count_part (was a local closure) plus main_counts out of status_counts; ci_stamp out of stamp; failing_lines out of tests_section. Nothing pinned the summary text before, so I added test status_counts_cover_every_status ('2 passed, 1 failed, 1 static, 1 skipped, 2 other' from TSV-shaped rows, not_run and an unknown status both counted as other). PROOF vultr pack27: --check + bodies exit 0; all 4 bodies run in Rust with exit 0; MUTANT ('passed' relabelled 'pass') FAILS the new test.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_35 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 35u32, "2026-11-05T09:03Z", "fiscal", "canon.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 05:1x local, in place and unstaged (FB518FCA; backup canon.before-granular.spi): 5/51 -> 1/57 code defs over (the one left: read_child, 287 > 272; each arm names one recursive call with the threaded arguments, so it stays). Splits: node_terms out of business_terms; element_data_type and element_cardinality out of element_terms; read_child (joined to the :& group) out of read_children; included_file and parent_folder (above the group) out of included_terms; term_head_fields out of term_json. PROOF vultr pack27 (peppol-bis3 structure present): --check + bodies exit 0; both bodies run in Rust with exit 0 (en16931 terms: 160 terms, 30 groups, unchanged). Mutants: breaking included_file's separator CRASHES with NotFound (the corpus includes part/*.xml), so the changed include path is exercised. Two mutants were EQUIVALENT on this corpus, and that is a coverage note, not a pass: dropping the business-term guard in node_terms (no non-Reference element carries BT ids) and breaking parent_folder (no included file includes another).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_36 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 36u32, "2026-11-05T09:13Z", "fiscal", "corpus / posting / profiles GRANULAR, 11-05 05:2x local, in place and unstaged (backups *.before-granular.spi in the scratchpad). corpus AA8939D1: 1/5 -> 0/7 (add_file built in three record-update steps add_elements -> add_type_counts -> enumeration and pattern). posting 61145219: 1/5 -> 0/6 (the local in_currency is now the top-level amount_as). profiles FDC32F7C: 1/21 -> 0/23 (customization_profile + list_version_profile out of ubl_profile_of). PROOF vultr pack27: all three --check + bodies exit 0; Rust bodies run with exit 0 (corpus 1, posting 2, profiles 2). Corpus needed its gitignored src/corpus.txt in the work tree, copied from dec-gen; the first run without it was an environment VOID (NotFound). MUTANTS fail: profiles '2.0' -> '2.1' fails ('SUNAT UBL 2.0'); corpus count_named pattern -> patternX fails ('2055 patterns'). LEFT: document canon_record (1/33, an 8-field record literal; splitting it would need placeholder amounts) and canon read_child (1/57). fiscal src without families/generator: 2/313 code defs over (was 15/301).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_37 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 37u32, "2026-11-05T09:13Z", "fiscal", "Correction to n36's aggregate: the per-file denominators sum to 320 code defs (canon 57, document 33, sunat 60, reports 49, corpus 7, posting 6, profiles 23, lifecycle 44, p2p 26, generated_runtime 12, fiscal_paths 3; corpus_checks read as 0 by my line probe, since its first test sits above its code), so 2/320 = 0.62% without families/generator, not 2/313.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_38 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 38u32, "2026-11-05T09:19Z", "fiscal", "corpus_checks.spi GRANULAR, 11-05 05:3x local, in place and unstaged (9B9D3A66; backup corpus_checks.before-granular2.spi): the block-classifying ruled measure (scratch ruled.exs over CellBudgetRuled; my line probe had read this file as 0 defs because its tests come first) found resolved_file over; now 0/53. Split: unresolved_counts (record update of the two unresolved counters) out of resolved_file. PROOF vultr pack27 (src/corpus.txt copied from dec-gen): --check + bodies exit 0; the one test over this code, resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet, runs in Rust with exit 0 (the whole 580-file corpus, 5 s); MUTANT (with_unresolved counts missing-include files too) FAILS 'no dangling type reference where every include is present'. Fiscal src by the ruled measure (families/generator excluded): 2/343 = 0.58% (canon read_child, document canon_record).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_39 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 39u32, "2026-11-05T09:24Z", "fiscal", "families ROW SPLIT, 11-05 05:4x local: drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src\\families.spi 5A989889 (on E91CEC5C). The row tables are now pure data, each with a top-level converter: signed_family (one data-only record over 5 strings; its constructor applications count as data under kit's rule); dfe_rows (12 tuples with a short portal kind nfe / cte / mdfe) + dfe_root + family_roots = map; nfe_event_rows + nfe_event + nfe_events = map; hacienda_rows + hacienda_documents = map over the unchanged hacienda_document. All values are identical (same strings, same namespace text), so the units stay identical; the identity regen is still PENDING on the node. Measured with the mix task (kit's nominal rule): 11/52 -> 8/58 = 13.8% (base F1CF3DDF 24/49). Note that the older CellBudgetRuled entry point (scratch ruled.exs) does NOT carry kit's nominal rule and reads 22/55, so quote the mix task. The 8 left all call something: cfdi_tfd / cfdi_pagos (catalog lists into cfdi_complement), ubl_document_2_1 and hacienda_document (computed names), and ubl_invoice / ubl_creditnote / mydata / nav (manifest_documents). Making the last four data needs a documents-source union (Listed / Manifest repo_path) resolved in the generator: a model change, filed as the next step, not done here. vultr pack27 generator --check + bodies exit 0 with this families draft.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_40 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 40u32, "2026-11-05T09:28Z", "fiscal", "DOCUMENTS AS DATA, 11-05 05:5x local: families.spi 99A8339B + generator.spi B5D81CCA in drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-GRANULAR-280\\src. ':| document_source = Listed : list string | Manifest : repo_path'; family_root documents / ubl_json_documents : document_source; documents_of resolves Listed paths as they are and Manifest m through the existing manifest_documents 'deps/corpus/' (repo_text m) (that prefix was the same at every use). Every literal now says Listed [...] or Manifest (repo_path ...), constructor applications only. The generator's 5 reads go through documents_of. FAMILIES 8/58 -> 4/60 = 6.7% (mix task, kit's nominal rule; base F1CF3DDF was 24/49 = 49%), so the file is under 10% on its own. The 4 left are genuinely parameterized builders: cfdi_tfd_1_1 / cfdi_pagos_2_0 (catalogs into cfdi_complement), ubl_document_2_1, hacienda_document. Generator unchanged at 2 code defs over (family_bench, write_family_module). vultr pack27: generator --check + bodies exit 0 with both drafts. The identity regen (units identical to the toml base) is PENDING on the node. The later facet / defect generator layer must take documents_of too (its kept_documents reads family::documents).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_41 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 41u32, "2026-11-05T09:33Z", "fiscal", "generator draft 40DE71DF (FISCAL-GRANULAR-280 layer): the last 2 code overages are split. bench_parts out of family_bench, which keeps only the measurability gate; write_family_parts \\\\* form. out of write_family_module, which keeps only the three lookups. Same calls in the same order. Mix task: 0 code defs over of about 92. The --check is PENDING (vultr refused at MemAvailable < 2100 MB; a background retry waits for headroom). With this layer fiscal src is: families 4/60, generator 0/92, others 2/343.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_42 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 42u32, "2026-11-05T09:37Z", "fiscal", "Generator split draft: the type-check (pending in n41) PASSED, 11-05 05:4x local, vultr pack27 once MemAvailable cleared the gate. With the documents-as-data families draft, generator --check + bodies exit 0 (vultr hash 40DE71DF after CRLF stripping). Both FISCAL-GRANULAR-280 drafts type-check; the identity regen stays PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_43 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 43u32, "2026-11-05T09:43Z", "fiscal", "IDENTITY REGENS QUEUED on the node, 11-05 05:5x local: job-1793871773349-fiscal-identity runs after job-1793868130086 (nfe_v4) with a 7200000 ms cap counted from its own start (kept independent of nfe_v4's 3 h cell per widen-queued-job-amend-timeout). Script C:\\home\\remote-stage\\node-identity.ps1 176DAFF6, inputs in fiscal-identity-in, hash-verified on the node. Four arms, each in its own tree (core from VS Code Plugin\\core, a lib copy with xml B6EED09B + xml_codec 5694B36A + the arm's xsd_emit, fiscal src from the box, the corpus as a read-only junction; junctions removed as links before any recursive delete, and corpus file count plus mirror xsd_emit hash checked start vs end). (1) facet 4E831159 + .next6 vs sentinel D00BE390 + .next7, the certificates sentinel identity, after two vultr VOIDs; (2) toml base 2A9BE918 + families F1CF3DDF vs FISCAL-GRANULAR-280 generator 40DE71DF + families 99A8339B, the repo_path / row-split / documents-as-data identity. Each arm compiles the generator plus the harness main, rustc -O, runs, and hashes every generated file. PENDING.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_44 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 44u32, "2026-11-05T09:50Z", "fiscal", "Coverage gap from n35 CLOSED, 11-05 05:5x local, canon.spi A9821EE2 in place: new test only_business_term_references_name_terms (synthetic: a BUSINESS_TERM Reference 'BT-1, BG-2', a Description 'BT-9' and a SYNTAX Reference 'BT-7'; business_terms must give exactly [BusinessTerm 1; BusinessGroup 2]). The guard-dropping mutant that was EQUIVALENT on the corpus now FAILS this test ('only BUSINESS_TERM references name terms; other elements' text does not'). vultr pack27: --check + bodies exit 0, all 3 bodies run in Rust with exit 0 (en16931 160 terms / 30 groups unchanged).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_45 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 45u32, "2026-11-05T11:59Z", "fiscal", "GRANULAR IDENTITY PROVEN, 11-05 07:58 local, node job-1793871773349: arm toml (decode xsd_emit 5B274B48 + generator 2A9BE918 + families F1CF3DDF) vs arm granular (the same lib + generator 40DE71DF + families 99A8339B: repo_path, row split, documents as data, bench_parts / write_family_parts), each a full regen. 138 files each, 0 DIFFERING. Shared-mirror guards held: corpus files 1290 start = end, mirror xsd_emit 738935CD start = end; junctions removed as links before deletion. NEXT: land generator 40DE71DF + families 99A8339B into fiscal src in one window, with generated/ moved to spiral.toml manifests and generated_cii_d16b added.")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_46 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 46u32, "2026-11-05T12:01Z", "fiscal", "GENERATOR + FAMILIES WINDOW LANDED in fiscal src, 11-05 08:0x local, in place and unstaged (backups generator.before-granular-land-385DD926.spi and families.before-granular-land-B59F8A10.spi in the session scratchpad): src/generator.spi 385DD926 -> 40DE71DF and src/families.spi B59F8A10 -> 99A8339B, in one window. That brings .next6 (decode + GRANULAR split + generates_cii_d16b back), the toml manifests, repo_path, the row split, documents as data, and bench_parts / write_family_parts; identity proven node-side (0 differing). generated/: all 82 unit manifests converted package.spiproj -> spiral.toml exactly as module_package writes them (dependencies in order; CFDI lists runtime, tfd, pagos), and generated_cii_d16b added (C3C111BE, formatter-stable) with its toml. README line 145 now names the per-unit spiral.toml. fiscal working tree: 222 changed paths. PENDING: the CI run after the user commits (generator tests regenerate units and diff; the generator's own CFDI test now checks spiral.toml).")
inl note_of_fiscal_granular_280_47 () = Note ("FISCAL-GRANULAR-280", 47u32, "2026-11-05T12:23Z", "fiscal", "FORMAT PASS on live fiscal src, 11-05 08:3x local, box installed compiler (format, then format --check exit 0 for each): families 99A8339B -> E6AC72B3, generator 40DE71DF -> 03111A90 (the landed drafts were not formatter-clean: long literals and conditionals unwrapped), canon A9821EE2 -> 8457C66F, corpus_checks 9B9D3A66 -> 2AC1F2A4, posting 61145219 -> CBEE84E5 (line endings only); sunat, reports, corpus, profiles and lifecycle were already clean. The facet companion drafts in src2 were formatted too: families 889D2546 -> 8F72669F, generator 96302219 -> 6ADC38CB (the running node facet gate uses the pre-format text; the format pass is semantics-preserving). Re-verified on vultr pack27: generator, canon, corpus_checks and posting --check + bodies exit 0. Pre-format copies are in the session scratchpad.")
inl fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand () = Task ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", "fiscal: drop the tracked src/corpus.txt (a derived list of the 580 DFe.NET schemas); enumerate the folder on demand", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", "team:fiscal,fiscal,drift,data", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand () = Planning ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:39Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:10 fiscal: src/corpus.txt (38,755 bytes, the only tracked .tsv/.txt in fiscal) is EXACTLY the sorted list of all 580 .xsd files under deps/corpus/DFe.NET (0 missing, 0 extra), so it is derived data that is tracked. Readers: src/corpus.spi:31 (file_system.read_all_text), scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1:4,22, scripts/resolve-check.ps1:19, README.md:173. FIX: corpus.spi enumerates deps/corpus/DFe.NET for *.xsd (sorted ordinally) instead of reading the file; the two scripts do the same (or call the Spiral list once PS1-TO-SPIRAL ports them); delete src/corpus.txt and the README row. Do after the edition-3 respell lands. Proof: corpus tests pass with the same 580 paths.")
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 2u32, "2026-11-01T06:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 02:35 fiscal: DONE in the tree (unstaged), one user step left. The lib has no portable recursive file listing (file_system.directory_get_files is F#-only, read_dir_names is Rust-only and non-recursive), so corpus.spi keeps reading src/corpus.txt, but the file is now a BUILD PRODUCT like src/patterns.txt: scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1 derives the Brazilian list from deps/corpus/DFe.NET (same Sort-Object order) and -Write writes src/corpus.txt; build.ps1 runs it before any test, and so does the node e3 regen script. resolve-check.ps1 enumerates the folder itself. .gitignore gains /src/corpus.txt; README layout row updated. PROOF: the written corpus.txt is byte-identical to the tracked one; an A/B of HEAD's pattern-oracle against the new one gives identical patterns.txt / pattern_probes.txt / pattern_expected.txt (336 patterns, 2041 probes). Side fix: README said 271 patterns (196 + 75); it is 336 (196 + 140), as the tests already pin. USER STEP: git rm --cached src/corpus.txt in the next commit (it is tracked, so the ignore rule alone does not untrack it). FOLLOW-UP (lib): a typed recursive file listing primitive in file_system, so corpus.spi can enumerate without the file.")
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 3u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit: this item closes fiscal's only tracked .txt in MIGRATE-TXT-FILES; when it lands, mark fiscal done there.")
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 4u32, "2026-11-01T14:48Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 11:02 fiscal: QUALITY SPEC (groom round 5). DONE WHEN: git ls-files src/corpus.txt prints nothing (the user's git rm --cached in the fiscal commit now listed in main's commit-suggestion.md), CI's pattern-oracle step writes it (\"wrote patterns.txt, pattern_probes.txt, pattern_expected.txt and corpus.txt\"), and corpus_checks reads 580 schemas. FOLLOW-UP (lib, not this item): a typed recursive listing primitive in file_system, then corpus.spi enumerates deps/corpus/DFe.NET itself and the file disappears entirely. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN for that primitive: return \"list corpus_path\" where \":! corpus_path = string\" is built only by the lister (relative, forward slashes), so a corpus path cannot be confused with a sample or schema output path; no \"\" entries (the manifest_paths filter for empty lines goes away).")
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 5u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 6u32, "2026-11-02T15:06Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 11:01 CORRECTION to x's 10:08 note: the user step is NOT met. git ls-files still lists src/corpus.txt at HEAD 9093af3. Pushed repos don't imply that a 'git rm --cached' happened. The tree side is done (pattern-oracle derives the list on demand). Remaining: the user's 'git rm --cached src/corpus.txt' (in main's commit guide) plus a green fiscal run after it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 7u32, "2026-11-02T15:39Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 11:39 REMOVED by fiscal (user 11-02: 'those git removals need to be done by you guys, i just stage and commit'). Deleted fiscal/src/corpus.txt from the worktree; it shows as ' D src/corpus.txt' (unstaged). It was already gitignored (.gitignore:11) and build.ps1 rewrites it through pattern-oracle -Write before corpus.spi:31 reads it, so local and CI builds are unaffected. Closes on the first green fiscal run after the user commits the deletion.")
inl note_of_fiscal_corpus_list_on_demand_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-CORPUS-LIST-ON-DEMAND", 8u32, "2026-11-03T09:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 05:57 fiscal: DONE: the tracked src/corpus.txt is deleted (committed in b35fae6) and CI stays green without it: CI run 41598162815 (push 741c715 with spiral 98e51d32), ubuntu-24.04 AND windows-2025: \"build.ps1 / generated / matches the committed copy\", generated_fiscal_runtime 3/3, generated_pt_saft_1_04_01 2/2, \"all 87 test files green and every example validates\".")
inl main_wipe_damage () = Task ("MAIN-WIPE-DAMAGE", "What the 10-28 profile wipe cost the main lane, measured, healed and made up (user 11-01 00:2x: 'the damage for each lane because of the wipe gotta be measured (even if only emotional), healed then made up somehow with new tasks')", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "wipe,heal,main,memory,cadence", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_main_wipe_damage () = Planning ("MAIN-WIPE-DAMAGE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_main_wipe_damage_1 () = Note ("MAIN-WIPE-DAMAGE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T04:40Z", "main", "main 00:4x LEDGER. LOST: every memory file (185); none came back verbatim except 2. 72+ were rebuilt as index line plus practice ('original wording lost') and 13 as INFERRED rules with confidence lines, so main's rules are paraphrases of the user's words, which is how the spiral-first rule, the lab rule and the codespaces habit slipped. All pre-wipe transcripts are gone, so no session can quote the user's 10-12..10-27 design talks except through backlog notes. TEMP drafts were lost (packs, tmp-retire, lib-gate, groom; rebuilt 10-29). The settings, hooks and standing file had to be rebuilt; the Stop gate is a rebuild. COST: 10-28/29 went to the heal; main's measured wait share peaked at 0.42-0.43 per note on 10-28/29 (resilience). WEAKER PRACTICES ('emotional' part): quoting the user exactly; CPU-light-while-blocked; standing directions such as codespaces quota use and no new .ps1/.py that existed only in transcripts; lab-instead-of-in-place drafts. HEAL, now: (1) every main memory that is INFERRED or 'wording lost' gets the user's real words from the backlog notes that quote them (resilience owns the sweep; main checks its own 10); (2) standing directions live as backlog items with an owner, not only as memory (CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS unblocked tonight, PS1-TO-SPIRAL plan, TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT); (3) the browser direction conversation the user will export lands only after the stabilization round (user: 'we're not ready to receive that jolt'). MAKE-UP: MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP every round, the WIP cap, and HEAVY-HOLD-DEADLOCK.")
inl note_of_main_wipe_damage_2 () = Note ("MAIN-WIPE-DAMAGE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T04:48Z", "main", "main 00:4x, another measured loss: the gh CLI token re-created after the wipe has no codespace or user scope, which silently blocked CODESPACES-QUOTA-RUNS. Heal: the user refreshes the scopes (gh auth refresh -s codespace,user).")
inl note_of_main_wipe_damage_3 () = Note ("MAIN-WIPE-DAMAGE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T00:22Z", "main", "main 20:2x CLOSED. MEASURED (n1/n2): every memory lost (185, 2 verbatim), all pre-wipe transcripts, TEMP drafts, settings/hooks/standing, gh token scopes; 10-28/29 went to the heal (wait share 0.42-0.43). HEALED since: the gh scopes work (two codespace runs today, 11-01); memories rebuilt with the user's words where findable (MEMORY-REASONS-AUDIT), and today the three disciplines the user named as lost are back as memories: granular one-expression bindings (strengthened), export-not-bang-export (new, resilience), nameof-not-string-mapping (new, resilience); stale-status and backup-silence lessons are memories (status-files-need-age; resilience's profile-mirror fail-loud fix); the drafts store is mirrored off-box. MADE UP with mechanical enforcement, so a future wipe of memories can't silently drop the rules again: EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET (P0, baseline: kit 659 !!!!Export / 568 multi-line macros), TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT (scoreboard baseline per repo), SPIRAL-NAMEOF + -HEAL (P0), GATE-HEALS-1101, HEARTBEAT-STALENESS-GUARD, and the drafts rule (known destination -> repo; unknown -> mirrored store). What can't be healed: the pre-wipe transcripts and the original wordings, so the backlog notes stay the only record of 10-12..10-27 design talks.")
inl granular_stats () = Task ("GRANULAR-STATS", "Granularity stats per repo per round, so we see what is left behind (user 11-01 00:2x: 'code should become more and more granular, we gotta have stats for what's being left behind... the early llms rewrote my code with a fkin rust block inside macros, losing all the granular effort'). Per repo and per file: host macro count and bytes ($' text), multi-line host blocks (a Rust or Gleam body inside a macro), !!!! intrinsics, definitions over the 280 cell budget, typed-modeling share (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT), list-sugar drift (LIST-SUGAR-DRIFT-GUARD); exported through KIT-EXEC-METRICS, trended on dir-tree-html", Story, P0, D3, 80u32, Blocked, "GRANULAR-LINT", "granular,metrics,lint,lib,team:kit,main", "current", "current")
