inl kit_groom_round () = Task ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", "kit groom start --until HH:MM: a groom round with a deadline in the store, the Stop gate refuses to idle before it, the report computed from the state", Story, P0, D3, 70u32, Active, "", "kit,agile,groom,cadence,hooks,team:kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_groom_round () = Planning ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_groom_round_1 () = Note ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", 1u32, "2026-11-01T06:00Z", "kit", "11-01 02:0x kit (main round 3; user 01:5x: 'why all lanes stopped instead of continuously groom until deadline with a report?'). In round 2 every lane replied at minute 8-15 and went idle, because nothing held them to the deadline. DESIGN: 'kit groom start <root> --until <HH:MM> [--team <t>] [--report-to <who>]' writes a typed GroomRound row (team, started, until, report_to) to the agile state (append-only); 'kit groom status' prints the open round and minutes left; 'kit groom end' closes it with the report counters taken from the state itself (notes written, items moved and closed per team inside the window), so the report is computed, not typed by hand. The Stop gate (autonomous-gate.ps1, thin glue) reads 'kit groom status --team <t>' and refuses to idle while a round is open, naming the next light item, the same way it handles the armed autonomous window today. NEXT CONCRETE STEP (CPU-light): typed model groom_round + window counters (reuse agile_cadence's tracked rows) with tests on a fixture, in the agile_cadence package, since the counters are cadence numbers.")
inl note_of_kit_groom_round_2 () = Note ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", 2u32, "2026-11-01T06:39Z", "kit", "11-01 02:4x kit (round 3): typed core DONE in the tree (unstaged), in src/agile_cadence beside the round counters: groom_round = { team; until_minute; report_to }; idle_verdict = MayIdle | KeepWorking (minutes left), the longest open round of the team wins, other teams' rounds never hold it. Test an_open_groom_round_keeps_its_team_working_until_the_deadline. PROOF: node job-1793514810043-kit-node-r3g, agile_cadence/model.spi 5/5. LEFT: GroomRound rows in the state, 'kit groom start|status|end' (end computes the report with round_counters_of), and the Stop gate line.")
inl note_of_kit_groom_round_3 () = Note ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", 3u32, "2026-11-01T12:33Z", "kit", "11-01 08:3x kit QUALITY PASS. DoD: 'kit groom start <root> --until 08:42 --team kit --report-to main' writes one GroomRound row; 'kit groom status --team kit' prints minutes left; the Stop gate hook (autonomous-gate.ps1) blocks idling while a round is open (pipe test: open round -> block JSON naming the next light item; no round -> exit 0 silent); 'kit groom end' prints notes, moved and touched counts equal to agile_cadence's round_counters_of on the same window; CLI tests in the new crate, node green. NEXT STEP: GroomRound row codec in a new agile_groom_rows package (same pattern as agile_sprint_rows, '///- --no-respell' state), then the three verbs. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the round is a typestate: phantom round_open / round_closed with a GADT groom_op (Start :: groom_op none round_open, End :: groom_op round_open round_closed) so 'end' on a closed round does not typecheck; idle_verdict stays a union (MayIdle | KeepWorking minutes), never -1; minutes and team as nominals; report counters as a record, not a joined string.")
inl note_of_kit_groom_round_4 () = Note ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", 4u32, "2026-11-01T14:42Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit (round 5, user list item 6: lanes still wait on shells instead of pulling light items). STOP-GATE SPEC, extending the DoD: the gate returns one of three typed verdicts, computed in < 1 s from the state with no sleeps (EOIE-AUTONOMOUS-GATE rule): PullItem id (an open groom round or an armed run AND kit agile next --team <t> --load light --ready returns an item -> block with \"take <id>: <title>, NEXT: <its NEXT line>\"), KeepWaiting job (a background job of THIS session is running AND no ready light item exists -> allow idle, because the job notification is the wake source), MayStop (no round, no armed run, no ready light item, no own job -> exit 0 silent). Never spin: the gate refuses to block twice in a row on the same item id inside 10 minutes (stop_hook_active plus a per-session last_pulled row), so a lane that cannot progress an item stops instead of looping tokens. MODEL: extend agile_cadence idle_verdict from MayIdle|KeepWorking to a 3-constructor union PullItem|KeepWaiting|MayStop with the anti-spin rule as a pure function of (last_pulled, now); tests: ready item -> PullItem; same item pulled 3 min ago -> MayStop; own job running and nothing ready -> KeepWaiting. NEXT: that model change + 3 tests in src/agile_cadence (CPU-light, node notebook proof).")
inl note_of_kit_groom_round_5 () = Note ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", 5u32, "2026-11-01T15:02Z", "kit", "11-01 11:02 kit: the 3-verdict gate model is in the tree (unstaged), in src/agile_cadence/model.spi beside idle_verdict. It adds gate_verdict = PullItem id | KeepWaiting job | MayStop; gate_input {held; ready_light; own_jobs; pulled; now_minute}; held_by (an open round or an armed run holds the lane); and recently_pulled. The anti-spin rule: an item pulled under 10 minutes ago is skipped, so a lane that can only re-pull the same item stops. The test the_stop_gate_pulls_a_ready_light_item_waits_on_own_jobs_and_never_spins has 6 expectations. PROOF PENDING: it is not pushed to the node yet, because the kit-verify mirror must stay frozen while the TRAIN7 pre-proof (job-1793545254729) regenerates from it. The node notebook run of agile_cadence/model.spi goes right after that job ends. agile_cadence is not a TRAIN7 owner, so the train is unaffected.")
inl note_of_kit_groom_round_6 () = Note ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", 6u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 40 h ago by kit, progress kept at 35%. Resume from that note: fy mirror must stay frozen while the TRAIN7 pre-proof (job-1793545254729) regenerates from it. The node notebook run of agile_cadence/model.spi goes right after that job ends. agile_cadence is not a TRAIN7 owner, so the train is unaffected.")
inl note_of_kit_groom_round_7 () = Note ("KIT-GROOM-ROUND", 7u32, "2026-11-04T16:50Z", "kit", "11-04 16:2x kit: RESCOPED + the report half BUILT (unstaged). The hold-until-deadline half is now main's armed run (autonomous-gate.ps1 blocks every stop until standing until= and lists the team's light items), so no GroomRound row/verbs are needed for it. The part nobody had shipped is the COMPUTED report: `kit agile cadence <root> --round <hours>` prints, per note author inside the last N hours, \"kit agile cadence round author=<a> notes=<n> items=<distinct ids>\" plus \"round ok authors=<k> window_hours=<N>\", via agile_cadence's existing round_counters_of. Feed: agile_quality_state.note_events_of (export kit_agile_note_events, linked) parses every note line (Note (\"ID\", seq, \"stamp\", \"author\", ...)) to {id; hour; author}. Tests: one event per note line + item id (state_rows), a_round_report_counts_notes_and_items_per_author_inside_the_window (cadence: 3 notes on 2 items, a note before the window not counted). vultr --check ok with bodies; box notebooks queued. Use: the 21:00 run report quotes `--round <hours of the run>`.")
inl lib_keyed_rng () = Task ("LIB-KEYED-RNG", "Move tibia/src/rng.spi (counter-based keyed RNG: mix32 lowbias32 plus roll_key {seed, tick, entity, purpose}, rolls agree across C, Rust and WGSL) into lib/spiral as a generic module with test blocks per backend; tibia then imports it; the first lib candidate from TIBIA-HARVEST", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:tibia,tibia,lib,harvest", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_keyed_rng () = Planning ("LIB-KEYED-RNG", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_keyed_rng_1 () = Note ("LIB-KEYED-RNG", 1u32, "2026-11-01T12:33Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 08:33 tibia QUALITY PASS. DEFINITION OF DONE: (a) lib/spiral/keyed_rng.spi exists with test blocks pinned to c, rust, lua and wgsl; the agreement test 'the same key draws the same u32 on every backend' passes 4/4 under lib_gate.ps1 on the node (lib program gate, -Negative mutant: flip one mix32 shift, which must fail 4/4); (b) tibia/src/rng.spi is deleted and its 4 importers (combat, search, gpu_sim, hunt_sim) import keyed_rng; tibia build.ps1 is green on the node with gpu_sim and hunt_sim draws unchanged (the existing seed-pinned assertions are the oracle). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN, fixing today's smell: roll_key = { seed; tick; entity; purpose : u32 } lets callers swap the four u32s and pass magic purposes (search.spi's 100u32 + gene, combat.spi's 201u32). Lib shape: (1) nominal wrappers ':! seed = u32', ':! tick = u32', ':! entity = u32', so argument order is checked by the type checker (the search.spi ':! vector' idiom); (2) the PURPOSE as a PHANTOM-indexed key: 'roll_key p' carries a phantom domain tag p, and a prototype 'purposed p' with 'purpose_code : p -> u32' maps each caller's own union (tibia: ':| combat_roll = | HitChance | ArmorRoll | ...', search: '| GeneNudge of u32') to its code in one place, so no literal purpose numbers remain at call sites; (3) draw and roll_between stay total (no -1 sentinel; roll_between with low > high is a type-level precondition expressed by taking a 'span = { low; width }' record). The model to follow is lib sm'/am' prototypes plus tibia search.spi's nominal vector. NEXT STEP: write lib/spiral/keyed_rng.spi from tibia src/rng.spi lines 5-22 plus the wrappers; register it in lib's package after 'math'; the first test is the 4-backend agreement on key {seed 3, tick 1, entity 2, HitChance}; gate with lib_program_gate.ps1 -Program on the node. ESTIMATE stays 120m (light: one module plus 4 importer edits). P2 because it's a harvest item with no consumer outside tibia yet; it rises to P1 when WOW-LUA-SANDBOX needs deterministic rolls. CORRECTION (git grep 'rng::' over src and apps): 6 importers, not 4: combat, hunt_sim, hunting_pack, network, pack_sim, search (gpu_sim does not import it). DoD (b) covers all 6.")
inl note_of_lib_keyed_rng_2 () = Note ("LIB-KEYED-RNG", 2u32, "2026-11-01T19:12Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 15:2x tibia, LIB HALF PROVEN, LANDING NOW. Draft: kit drafts store spiral\\LIB-KEYED-RNG\\keyed_rng.spi (canonical 96D5E1FD8BC75C6A) plus package.spiproj (live 2648C280B53B8CBA + '    keyed_rng' after math). Shape: mix32 as in tibia; nominal ':! seed = u32', ':! tick = u32', ':! entity = u32' (argument order checked); prototype ':? purpose_code p : p -> u32'; ':== roll_key p = { seed; tick; entity; purpose : p }'; draw and roll_between take '\\* p {purpose_code}.' and keep tibia's exact arithmetic (mix32 (s + mix32 (t + mix32 (e + mix32 code)))), so tibia's seed-pinned asserts stay the oracle; NEW 'sub_key key index : roll_key derived' (code * 256 + index) generalizes combat.spi's sub_key so combat stays generic over the caller's purpose type. PROBE (box compile, scratch package): an instance for a lib prototype must name it bare after ':< keyed_rng'; ':+ keyed::purpose_code t' is a ParserError ('Expected: lowercase variable'); cross-module dispatch folded to the expected code at compile time. DECISION vs n1 plan (3): no span record; roll_between keeps low/high, since a { low; width } record moves the precondition (width 0 divides by zero) instead of removing it, and tibia has no -1 sentinel here. NODE GATE (mirror tibia-rng, synced 14:57 after the :: respell land; job-1793559951324-tibia-keyed-rng-gate-2): positive 5/5 passed on c, rust and lua (prediction was lua red on u32 multiply overflow; WRONG, the Lua backend wraps), wgsl unsupported on the node (no runner; run on the box after land); cell budget 0 findings; negative mutant (first mix32 shift 16 -> 17) CAUGHT, 3 failed, 0 type errors. Roundtrip: canonical after dropping one blank line under the heading. TOOL GAP CLOSED: lib_land_window.ps1 could not land a NEW file (it backed up the absent live file); it now marks absent files New, skips their backup and base type_probe, and its undo moves a landed new file into the undo folder (unstaged in spiral apps/cells/spi). Next: tibia half (6 importers to typed purpose unions, src package gains lib) after the land closes green.")
inl note_of_lib_keyed_rng_3 () = Note ("LIB-KEYED-RNG", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:01Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 19:0x tibia, CONSUMER INTERIM (job-1793562329522, tibia-gates mirror synced 15:44 with lib keyed_rng 96D5E1FD8BC7; full build, 3 h 13 min so far, at measure of ~66 alphabetically): every migrated importer reached is green with its seed-pinned asserts unchanged: combat 8/8 (truncated-normal stats 2055/0/4093, armor bounds, arrow facts), hunt_sim 9/9, hunting_pack 2/2, gpu_sim 3/3 (its wgsl rows unsupported on the node). Still to come: network, pack_sim, search. Three failures so far are node-environmental, not code, and none of those files imports rng or quantity: block_plan (cell timed out after 300 s), damage (compiler connection :noproc), map (rustc: temp main.rs vanished). The node was running 7 jobs from 5 lanes. Next: final rows, then Done if the 3 remaining importers are green; the environmental reds go to tibia CI after the user's next push.")
inl note_of_lib_keyed_rng_4 () = Note ("LIB-KEYED-RNG", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:20Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 19:2x tibia, DONE. DoD (a): lib keyed_rng.spi landed 15:12, tests green on c/rust/lua (node) and wgsl (box), negative mutant caught. DoD (b): tibia src/rng.spi removed and its 6 importers migrated to typed purpose unions (combat_roll, hunt_roll, pack_roll, network_roll, search_roll, plus lib sub_key/derived), committed by the user in b08cd87; tibia CI run 41350993071 on b08cd87 completed SUCCESS on build (windows-2025) and build (ubuntu-24.04), so every seed-pinned draw assertion held on both OS. The node full build was stopped as redundant after CI proved it (it had reached every rng importer except network/pack_sim/search green; CI covered those).")
