inl direction_1031 () = Task ("DIRECTION-1031", "Direction from the user's browser conversation 10-29..10-31 (claude.ai share eab494f1, 29 messages, 8 research reports): rogue route vs Rust, a Brzozowski product with definitions of done, the single .spi extension, naming and the i574n dialect, what to steal from other languages, a 575/1000 standardization score. Staged: one parent, focused children; candidates that are gated stay in notes", Epic, P1, D6, 39u32, Active, "", "direction,research,main,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_direction_1031 () = Planning ("DIRECTION-1031", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_direction_1031_1 () = Note ("DIRECTION-1031", 1u32, "2026-11-01T12:03Z", "main", "main 08:0x SOURCE: public share https://claude.ai/share/eab494f1-d9c0-4ecb-bf89-f2f98eb21c05 (conversation d21da8dc). Full JSON via https://claude.ai/api/chat_snapshots/<id>?rendering_mode=messages&render_all_tools=true; archived with the extraction (conversation.md, 8 reports, 14 generated files, patch scripts) in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261101-080304. NOT IN THE SHARE: the zips sent to the user (spiral_v303_verificacao.zip, spiral_vitrines.zip) and single-spi-extension.patch, which lived in the browser sandbox; the patch is rebuildable from the two python edit scripts in the archive (spir-patch-edit1/2). DROPPED by the user, not filed: the Sigenius/Abu Dhabi business track ('never mind this company or erp stuff'). CHILDREN filed: CHECK-SILENT-DROP, SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION, BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT, SPELLING-PROFILES, NAMING-LEXICON-RATCHET, LIB-LAYERS, DIALECT-IDENTITY, REPO-HYGIENE-LICENSES. CANDIDATES (not filed, gated): nerode-mask (certified constrained-decoding masks), nerode-pretok (cl100k/o200k pre-tokenizer), nerode-xdp (regex to eBPF/XDP), all after BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT M4/M7; typed_llama ('one source, five backends, proven shapes'); a Bend mission after the CIC kernel. Steal list: 29 features with priorities and a 24-month roadmap (governance first: conformance suite, spelling profiles, editions as contract + light RFCs, JSON diagnostics, doc-tests; then OxCaml-style modes, Perceus, typed quotation Code<T>, effects, CIC + laws/proofs as an agent gate). Rust showcases S1-S6 (+S7 post-CIC) and the v303 verification are in the archive's files/.")
inl note_of_direction_1031_2 () = Note ("DIRECTION-1031", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:35Z", "main", "main 10:3x RESEARCH, Syl (https://thenumb.at/Syl-Intro/, Max Slater, user link 11-01): an experimental systems language whose compile-time computation lives in a MODAL type system (two-level type theory, after Kovacs; OxCaml-style modes). Every value has a mode on two axes, static/dynamic and erased/unerased; static/erased parameters monomorphize; types are ordinary erased values; 'dependently typed at compile time, simply typed at runtime'; HKTs work, reflection basic (repr), fuel limits stop runaway typechecking; no benchmarks, no LLVM backend yet, WIP. RELEVANCE: it's the closest prior art to Spiral's inl/let/real staging, with a cleaner foundation, while Spiral is far ahead in implementation (partial evaluation in production, join points, 15+ backends). Steal: modes as the principled form of the inl/let/real split (feeds SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION's per-statement mode and the CIC kernel's multiplicity 0 = erased); modules as dependent records. 'Still winning?': on shipping code yes; on foundations Syl is ahead, so the CIC kernel work matters.")
inl note_of_direction_1031_3 () = Note ("DIRECTION-1031", 3u32, "2026-11-03T02:16Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:2x ROLLUP of the 8 children (mean progress, from agile list --json): CHECK-SILENT-DROP 100 Done; REPO-HYGIENE-LICENSES 75 Active (AGPL v3 on all 17 repos, alphabet README rewritten, dice README drafted pending its uniformity test); DIALECT-IDENTITY 30 Active (spiral/NOTICE; the dialect/edition split handed to compiler); SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION, BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT, SPELLING-PROFILES, NAMING-LEXICON-RATCHET, LIB-LAYERS 0 Planned. So 25%, Planned -> Active. BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT is the one with momentum: tonight's regex work (language oracle, laws over 241,560 checks, automaton typestate, check_dfa certificates) is its foundation.")
