inl codebase_diamond () = Task ("CODEBASE-DIAMOND", "Deterministic rewrite-distance gauge: obligations per code unit (backend deliberation, typed domain, saga compensation, ...) discharged by mechanical, adjudicated or proven evidence; diamond = all proven", Epic, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "DIAMOND-S5,DIAMOND-S6,DIAMOND-S8", "kit,team:kit,typefeatureset,metrics,gauge,standards,fiscal,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_codebase_diamond () = Planning ("CODEBASE-DIAMOND", Minutes 720u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_codebase_diamond_1 () = Note ("CODEBASE-DIAMOND", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, from the user (11-01 ~09:0x): 'what if we had deterministic metrics like a game (of course needing a sota llm intelligence in the middle) to gauge how far a codebase is from needing to get rewritten considering its bad modeling compared to the typedfeatureset's top gains, like knowing that every bit of code passed through the deliberation of if it should've been running in the gleam or rust side, also its domain modeling able to achieve saga compensations with iggy ... keep rewritting apps over and over until reaching a diamond artifact stage of knowing that some kind of internal phantom benchmark proof was achieved which isn't limited by performance alone, something only achievable with the state of this spiral fork ... give kit an even stronger role, it'll also dogfeed itself ... the compiler will be the last one because we're stalling the rewrite there until hopacsota matches upstream's speed. fiscal will be a different kind of metric provider, because since it's based on existing finite deterministic xsds ... it's possible to know when the last drop of milk was modeled'.\nDESIGN. A codebase carries OBLIGATIONS, one per (code unit, rubric question): backend deliberated (Gleam/BEAM vs Rust/native per component, BACKEND-BALANCE's rule), domain typed (no stringly ids, no sentinels, closed unions), effects compensated (saga steps carry compensations, replayable through iggy), state concurrency (event log, no lost updates), granularity (host-free, lib-referenced), plus later families. Each obligation is discharged by EVIDENCE of one of three strengths: Mechanical (census, lint, crate gate; no LLM), Adjudicated (an LLM verdict against a pre-registered rubric, stored as a typed row keyed by unit content hash + rubric version + model, so replay is deterministic and a unit is re-asked only when its hash or the rubric changes), or Proven (types or tests enforce it, e.g. a step without its compensation does not typecheck plus an iggy fault-replay test). REWRITE DISTANCE = weighted open obligations; DIAMOND = every obligation at rubric vN is Proven. Rubric versions ratchet up with the fork's feature frontier, so the diamond is relative to what this Spiral fork can express. FISCAL is the calibrator: its XSD constructs give a finite denominator, so typed coverage can reach 100% and the gauge is tested against ground truth before judging open-ended code. Order: kit dogfoods first, then lib, x, tibia, fiscal (calibration runs in parallel), and the compiler last, after the hopacsota rewrite reaches upstream's speed.\nFEEDERS, not duplicated: TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT and GRANULAR-STATS (mechanical counts), EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET and the census (baseline + ratchet), GRANULAR-LINT (macro classes), BACKEND-BALANCE and GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT (the backend rubric), KIT-EXEC-METRICS (measured costs when a rubric needs numbers), KIT-AGILE-QUALITY-LINT (item-level quality), LIB-IGGY-CLIENT (the event log the saga proofs replay through).\nDoD (epic): 'kit gauge <repo>' prints a typed scorecard per package (obligations open by family and evidence strength, rewrite distance, diamond flag) that is byte-identical across two runs on the same tree and verdict ledger; kit itself scored and ratcheted; fiscal's XSD coverage reported with its finite denominator; one saga proof discharged end to end.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: obligation_family closed union; evidence GADT indexed by strength (Mechanical :: census_fact -> evidence mechanical | Adjudicated :: verdict -> evidence adjudicated | Proven :: proof -> evidence proven) so 'diamond' is a type-level fact: a scorecard whose evidence list is all 'evidence proven'; obligations as an existential row (\\? s. unit * obligation_family * evidence s); unit identity a phantom-tagged content hash; verdicts typed rows, never free text; weights and rubric version as data in the repo's standards.spi.")
inl note_of_codebase_diamond_2 () = Note ("CODEBASE-DIAMOND", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:11Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit, DIGEST of the neighbouring items (user: groom longer). (1) A MECHANICAL DISTANCE IS COMPUTABLE TODAY: TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT's model_metrics (11 metrics, spiral/apps/cells/spi/model_metrics.ps1) already scored repos on 11-01 00:4x: GADT M3 / existential M5 / types M11 = fiscal 1.6 / 0 / 11.6, tibia 9.1 / 0.7 / 13.7, the 5 MEGA SAMPLES 86.7 / 30.8 / 36.4; only fiscal has string dispatch M7 (6.5) and sentinels M8 (4.1). So the first rewrite distance needs no LLM: per metric, the gap to the mega samples (the diamond reference for 'typed domain') for M3/M5/M11, and absolute counts for M7/M8 (target 0). Adjudication starts where counts cannot decide (backend choice, saga need). (2) FAMILIES MAPPED TO EXISTING SOURCES: typed domain <- model_metrics M3/M5/M7/M8/M11 (via TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT); granularity <- GRANULAR-STATS (cell budget 280: lib 1,186 definitions over on 11-01, max 21,205; host-macro bytes; multi-line host blocks) and GRANULAR-LINT classes; state concurrency <- STATE-CONCURRENCY-SOTA lessons L1-L6 (typed mirror lease, fine-grained backlog transactions, compiler-core guard: each lesson is a rubric question WITH a known proof shape); backend <- BACKEND-BALANCE's rule (S4); effects/sagas <- S5 over LIB-IGGY-CLIENT. (3) TOOL CONSTRAINT carried from fiscal: model_metrics' regexes read 0 definitions in generated units (954k lines, M9 noise); the gauge must count with the compiler's tokens, never regex. (4) PROPOSED DEFAULTS for the two open user decisions (the user decides; these are only defaults): WEIGHTS: sentinels and string dispatch weigh most (the user named both as rewrite causes), then missing typestate on shared resources (STATE-CONCURRENCY-SOTA), then granularity, then counts below the mega-sample ratio; weights live as data in each repo's standards.spi so a change is a reviewed diff. OFFICIAL JUDGE: every verdict row keeps its model id; the scorecard reports the newest model's verdicts as official and lists disagreements with the previous judge per unit, so a model change never silently rewrites history.")
inl note_of_codebase_diamond_3 () = Note ("CODEBASE-DIAMOND", 3u32, "2026-11-01T13:19Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit groom: the backlog already DECLARES obligations. The round-4 TYPEFEATURESET PLAN lines (25 kit items, e.g. 'task_id as a nominal over string', 'StartsIn | AlreadyRunning instead of the 0 sentinel', 'phantom-tagged hashes in run_key') are per-unit obligations written before the code. The gauge can read them (the same marker parsing as KIT-AGILE-QUALITY-LINT) and score each package against its own item's plan: a plan line not yet true in the code is an open obligation, Mechanical when a census metric can see it (a sentinel, a raw string id), Adjudicated otherwise. That closes the loop between grooming and code: a lazy plan fails the quality lint, and an unkept plan raises the rewrite distance.")
inl note_of_codebase_diamond_4 () = Note ("CODEBASE-DIAMOND", 4u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "kit", "11-01 10:3x kit (round 5): new Mechanical feeder KIT-REUSE-METRICS (duplicated logic, lib-vs-app share of generic code). Rewrite-distance reading: a high dup_ratio or low lib_share is an obligation the gauge can discharge mechanically (lift to lib), unlike modeling obligations that need Adjudicated evidence.")
inl note_of_codebase_diamond_5 () = Note ("CODEBASE-DIAMOND", 5u32, "2026-11-02T14:00Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: The two open user decisions n2 names (text truncated after 'PROPOSED DEFAULTS for the two open user d...'). RULE (written before acting): Adopt n2 (4)'s proposed defaults as written. The gauge is a read-only metric, so any default is reversible. The mechanical distance comes from model_metrics (M3/M5/M11 gap to the mega samples, M7/M8 absolute counts, target 0), counted with compiler tokens, never regex. BACKUP/UNDO: No state changes. Gauge outputs are new files. OWNER: kit. NEXT: Record n2's two defaults as adopted in a note and build the first mechanical distance from model_metrics. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl diamond_s1 () = Task ("DIAMOND-S1", "Typed obligation model: families, evidence by strength, score and diamond as pure functions", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,team:kit,gauge,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_diamond_s1 () = Planning ("DIAMOND-S1", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_diamond_s1_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S1", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: a HostFree package kit_gauge_model with test blocks: a scorecard of 3 units scores the same twice; diamond is true only when every obligation's evidence is Proven; adding an Adjudicated obligation drops diamond. NEXT STEP: new package src/kit_gauge_model. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: evidence GADT indexed by phantom strength (mechanical | adjudicated | proven); obligation row existential over strength; obligation_family closed union; unit_id a phantom-tagged content hash; distance = sum of typed weights (nominal), never floats parsed from text.")
inl note_of_diamond_s1_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S1", 2u32, "2026-11-03T05:30Z", "kit", "11-03 01:3x kit: DONE (unstaged), new HostFree package src/kit_gauge_model (gauge.spi + standards.spi).\nModel: the evidence GADT is indexed by phantom strength (Measured -> mechanical, Judged -> adjudicated, ProvenBy -> proven), so evidence construction is typed. Rows cannot be existential over strength (existentials are compile-time only, memory existentials-compile-time-only), so polymorphic obligation_of projects each piece of evidence into a closed strength_kind union stored on the obligation record. obligation_family is a closed union. weight is a nominal (Weight u64). distance_of = the sum of weights of obligations that are not Proven, no floats. diamond_of = non-empty and every obligation Proven. scored/scorecard are pure functions.\nDoD proof (vultr notebook-batch, 2/2 blocks): a 3-unit scorecard scores the same twice; all-proven is a diamond at distance 0; a Measured obligation is distance 2, not a diamond; no obligations is no diamond; adding a Judged (adjudicated) obligation drops the diamond (distance 4). The gleam block repeats two of them. kit standards 0 findings; ratchet clean.\nDeviation from the plan: unit_id is a nominal union over the content hash, not phantom-tagged (no unit kinds exist yet to tag with). Add the phantom when DIAMOND-S2 introduces unit kinds.")
inl diamond_s2 () = Task ("DIAMOND-S2", "Mechanical feed: census, lint and crate gate facts become obligations, deterministically", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "DIAMOND-S1,TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT,GRANULAR-STATS", "kit,team:kit,gauge,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_diamond_s2 () = Planning ("DIAMOND-S2", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_diamond_s2_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S2", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: 'kit gauge src --mechanical' on kit prints per-package open mechanical obligations equal to the census and lint baselines (cross-check test on a fixture tree); two runs byte-identical. NEXT STEP: adapters from kit_style_census rows and kit_lint_model violations into obligations. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: census_fact = typed census row (package, metric union, count); each metric maps to an obligation family by a total match.")
inl note_of_diamond_s2_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S2", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:11Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit, refined: the mechanical feed reads model_metrics' 11 metrics through TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT's kit verb (compiler tokens, not regex: fiscal showed the regex version reads 0 definitions in generated units) and GRANULAR-STATS' columns (cell budget 280, host-macro bytes), so it now depends on both. Distance for M3/M5/M11 = gap to the mega samples' values (86.7 / 30.8 / 36.4 on 11-01); M7 string dispatch and M8 sentinels count absolutely (target 0). DoD addition: the mechanical scorecard for fiscal reproduces fiscal's 11-01 numbers (1.6 / 0 / 11.6, M7 6.5, M8 4.1) from the same tree.")
inl note_of_diamond_s2_3 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S2", 3u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:4x kit: Mechanical feeders now: GRANULAR-STATS (host-text drift, cell budget) and KIT-REUSE-METRICS (dup_ratio, lib_share, reuse_fanout). S2 consumes their rows, it does not re-walk the tree.")
inl diamond_s3 () = Task ("DIAMOND-S3", "Verdict ledger: adjudicated evidence keyed by unit hash + rubric version + model, replayable", TaskKind, P1, D3, 90u32, Blocked, "DIAMOND-S1", "kit,team:kit,gauge,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_diamond_s3 () = Planning ("DIAMOND-S3", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_diamond_s3_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: a ledger of typed verdict rows; replaying a score with the ledger and an unchanged tree gives identical output; changing one unit's content invalidates only that unit's verdicts (test); a rubric version bump invalidates all verdicts of that rubric (test). NEXT STEP: package kit_gauge_ledger with verdict rows in a '///- --no-respell' state module (agile-state style). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: verdict = { unit : unit_id; rubric : rubric_id * version nominal; model : model_id; answer : answer union per rubric }; answers are closed unions per rubric question (e.g. Beam | Native | EitherWithReason of reason), never free text.")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 2u32, "2026-11-04T01:43Z", "kit", "11-03 21:4x kit: typed model DRAFTED in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S3\\src\\kit_gauge_ledger (not in the tree: an unproven test file would run in the next train's notebooks). Nominal ids rubric_id, rubric_version, model_id and content_hash as single-case unions over kit_gauge_model.unit_id. backend_answer is a closed union (Beam | Native | EitherWithReason : string), never free text. verdict is a record; verdict_standing is VerdictCurrent | VerdictStale. current_verdicts tree rubric version ledger keeps a verdict only when its unit's content hash is unchanged and its rubric version is current. Two tests encode the DoD: a content change stales only that unit; a rubric bump stales every verdict of that rubric and none of another's. LEFT: the '///- --no-respell' state module the ledger rows persist in (agile-state style), and a replay test (same ledger + unchanged tree -> identical score output). Prove on scratch (vultr --check plus a Cells run) before landing. Record field renamed unit -> target (unit may be reserved).")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_3 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 3u32, "2026-11-04T07:58Z", "kit", "11-04 04:2x kit: kit_gauge_ledger LANDED in the tree (unstaged; module package, no crate; vultr pack31 --check exit 0 as-is and all test bodies). Three tests cover the DoD: a content change invalidates only that unit's verdicts; a rubric version bump invalidates every verdict of that rubric (other rubrics stand); and replaying an unchanged tree with the ledger gives identical verdicts. Typed throughout: rubric_id/rubric_version/model_id/content_hash single-case unions, backend_answer closed union, verdict record, verdict_standing union. Remaining for Done: persistence of verdict rows as a state module (agile-state style) once the gauge verb (DIAMOND-S6, parked for size) has a home. Rides TRAIN21 notebooks.")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_4 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 4u32, "2026-11-04T08:07Z", "kit", "11-04 05:0x kit: PERSISTENCE as a typed state module (unstaged). ledger.spi gains verdict_of (a full constructor: target, hash, rubric, version, model, answer) and ledger_source, which renders a ledger as Spiral source: `///- --no-respell`, `:< kit_gauge_ledger.ledger`, `:= ledger () : list verdict = [ verdict_of ... ]`, with strings escaped and EitherWithReason payloads quoted. Test the_ledger_persists_as_a_typed_state_module pins the exact text (escaped quotes included) and that a persisted row rebuilds an equal verdict. The rendered text was itself checked as a real module (kit_gauge_state/verdicts.spi on vultr pack31: exit 0), so a program loads the ledger by compiling it, as agile.spi works. All DoD tests pass --check (as-is and bodies). Remaining for Done: the verb that writes state/verdicts.spi, which comes with the gauge verb's home (DIAMOND-S6, waiting on fiscal's split-or-program choice).")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_5 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 5u32, "2026-11-04T08:10Z", "kit", "11-04 05:2x kit: the answer is now a per-rubric union, verdict_answer = BackendAnswer backend_answer | XsdReading xsd_reading, where xsd_reading is {complete : bool; wildcards; modeled; declared : i32} (the row shape fiscal asked for: per schema set, keyed by unit hash + rubric version). The persistence test pins both shapes (booleans render as !+/!-), and a sample state module with an XsdReading row passes --check on vultr. Remaining: the verb that appends a verdict row to state/verdicts.spi from a calibration run's output (fiscal's program on vultr then hands kit the reading).")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_6 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 04:10 fiscal: will hand kit one XsdReading { complete; wildcards; modeled; declared } per schema set when the append verb lands, from the vultr calibration program over lib xsd_census (the 11-03 run's readings are on DIAMOND-S6: NF-e, Chile DTE, myDATA, SAF-T and CII D16B complete; UBL 15 wildcards, all in signature/extension parts). Key: unit hash + rubric version + model, as kit's ledger defines.")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_7 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 7u32, "2026-11-04T08:11Z", "kit", "11-04 05:3x kit: ledger_recorded (pure, latest wins): recording a verdict drops any earlier verdict for the same target + rubric + model and appends the new one last, while other rubrics keep their slots. Test recording_a_verdict_replaces_that_units_rubric_slot. vultr --check exit 0 as-is and bodies. The append verb is then: read state/verdicts.spi's ledger (compile, or keep a sibling typed row list), ledger_recorded, ledger_source, write. That last I/O step waits for a caller; fiscal's calibration program is the first.")
inl note_of_diamond_s3_8 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S3", 8u32, "2026-11-04T08:13Z", "kit", "11-04 05:4x kit: the code is complete for kit's side (typed ledger, replay, invalidation, latest-wins recording, persistence as a typed state module with BackendAnswer/XsdReading rows). The last step, the append I/O, has its first caller in fiscal's calibration program (DIAMOND-S6 decision (b)). parked: waiting on fiscal's calibration run to hand a reading.")
