inl note_of_diamond_s4_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S4", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: the rubric text pre-registered in standards (questions, allowed answers, evidence needed), from BACKEND-BALANCE's rule; kit's components each get one verdict; the gauge reports deliberated vs undeliberated components; a component compiled to a backend its verdict rejects is an open obligation. NEXT STEP: write the rubric module, then adjudicate kit's components once (verdicts committed with the tree). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: backend_answer = Beam of beam_reason | Native of native_reason | Either; reasons as closed unions (Supervision | ManyActors | Distribution | DataParallel | ShortLivedCli | NativeLib ...) so the deliberation is countable.")
inl note_of_diamond_s4_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S4", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:14Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit: kit's first backend verdict is EOIE-BACKEND-MAP's pre-registered window-arbiter decision (Gleam actor vs polling, release-to-grant <= 100 ms median). Kit has zero Gleam code today, so S4 on kit starts with every component undeliberated; dep added.")
