inl note_of_diamond_s6_1 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:06Z", "kit", "11-01 09:0x kit, slice of CODEBASE-DIAMOND (user 09:0x). DoD: 'kit gauge fiscal --xsd' prints, per schema set, constructs modeled with typed Spiral / all constructs (denominator enumerated from the XSDs, deterministic); at least one schema set reaches 100% and is marked complete; the number matches fiscal's own generator census. NEXT STEP: enumerate XSD constructs via lib xsd_* modules (xsd_resolve, xsd_emit) and match against fiscal's generated units. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: xsd_construct closed union (ComplexType | SimpleType | Element | Attribute | Restriction | ...) with schema-qualified names as nominals; coverage a record of nominal counts; completeness a type (Complete | Partial of missing list).")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_2 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 05:26 fiscal: FISCAL HALF DRAFTED (DIAMOND-S1 is Done in kit's tree, so this slice is unblocked). The census both the gauge and fiscal must agree on lives in LIB, not in kit or fiscal: draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\DIAMOND-S6\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_census.spi, a new module after xsd. Typed per this item's plan: ':| xsd_construct = ComplexTypeConstruct | SimpleTypeConstruct | ElementConstruct | AttributeConstruct | GroupConstruct | WildcardConstruct'; ':== construct_census = { constructs; modeled; wildcards }'; ':| completeness = Complete | Partial : i32'. One GADT walker 'construct_walk \\* k form. (item : xsd k form)' over type_def / particle / attribute_decl (the same shape as xsd_emit.dereferenced_in), schema_census over simple_types + complex_types + elements, completeness_of. DENOMINATOR RULE (deterministic, enumerated from the parsed XSD): every complex/simple type, element, attribute and sequence/choice group is a construct; a construct is MODELED when xsd_emit emits it as typed Spiral, i.e. everything except xs:any (emitted as untyped any_content); a schema set with 0 wildcards is Complete. Test every_construct_is_counted_and_a_wildcard_is_not_modeled (8 constructs on the typed schema, Partial 1 on the xs:any one). QUEUED: job-1793697977422-fiscal-xsd-census (after the codec layer; one Cells run per node). FOR KIT (when this lands): 'kit gauge fiscal --xsd' calls xsd_census.schema_census per fiscal family schema and prints constructs/modeled/completeness; no XSD logic in kit.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_3 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 3u32, "2026-11-03T11:52Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 07:52 fiscal: TYPE-CHECKED ON IDLE VULTR (pack24 compiler, lib = spiral HEAD 98e51d32 + this draft, SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR = the shipped core; mutation-proven: an appended ill-typed definition exits 5 / ETY-TermError): xsd_census.spi exit 0 in 4 s. Its test still runs in queued job-1793697977422.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_4 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 11:28 fiscal: FIRST CELLS RUN FAILED IN THE HARNESS, not in the census: the test body used 'open' (a Spiral keyword) as a binding name ('    := open ='), so the test block failed to parse, Cells dropped it and reported 'ETY-UnboundVariable: spiral_cells_test' (job-1793697977422). --check had passed because it skips test blocks. FIX: the binding is now 'wildcard' (draft 2C510F3B); a vultr check that rewrites test headers into definitions now parses and types every test body (the old text reproduces the exact Cells parser error, exit 5; the fixed one passes). RERUN queued: job-1793719669429-fiscal-xsd-census2 (after the families proof).")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_5 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 5u32, "2026-11-03T20:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:29 fiscal: LANDED THROUGH lib_land_window (label fiscal-lib-1103, closed green, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261103-161039, lib digest 0B967D8878EF2C4A): signatures 0 consumer-used changed; apps/spiral compiles; document_test 22 passed; type_probe 4/4 (money 2, ledger 4, event_log 4, xsd_census 1 tests typed; 9 fails negatives skipped as designed); respell_drift 0 findings. Respelled before landing (exists -> \\?, fun -> \\, true/false -> !+/!-) and re-proven under pack27 on vultr (check + bodies + pinned negatives + Rust runs). Unstaged in spiral. xsd_census.spi 17B2E8EC (new, after xsd; formatted). Before landing: Rust run of its test body on a group_part lib exit 0 (vultr, pack24 then pack27). The queued node census job (fiscal-xsd-census4) remains as the Cells confirmation.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_6 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 6u32, "2026-11-03T21:32Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 17:32 fiscal: FIRST REAL NUMBERS from the landed lib census (a probe main appended to a vultr copy, compiled --backend Rust, pack27, reading the corpus XSDs): SAF-T PT 1.04_01: constructs 708, modeled 708, COMPLETE (DoD 'at least one schema set reaches 100%': met, fiscal side); Facturae 3.2.2: constructs 436, modeled 435, PARTIAL 1. AGREES WITH THE GENERATOR (DoD 'matches fiscal's own generator census'): SAF-T has 0 xs:any and generated_pt_saft_1_04_01 has 0 any_content; Facturae has exactly 1 xs:any (Facturaev3_2_2.xsd:1716, namespace ##other, the Extensions slot) and generated_es_facturae_3_2_2 carries any_content for it. Single-file schemas only so far: multi-file sets (NF-e, UBL, CFDI) need the census run after xsd_resolve's include/import resolution, which is the kit gauge's part ('kit gauge fiscal --xsd'). Remaining here: kit's gauge command (team kit) consuming lib xsd_census.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_7 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 7u32, "2026-11-03T21:42Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 17:42 fiscal: MULTI-FILE SETS MEASURED with include/import resolution (xsd_resolve.load_schema_tree, then xsd_census.schema_census; Rust probe on vultr, pack27, group_part lib): NF-e 4.00 (5 files) 1988/1988 COMPLETE; Chile DTE v10 (3) 1147/1147 COMPLETE; Greece myDATA 2.0.2 (5) 328/328 COMPLETE; Portugal SAF-T 1.04_01 (1) 708/708 COMPLETE; Italy FatturaPA 1.2.3 357/357, Costa Rica Hacienda 4.4 318/318, Spain VeriFactu LR (2) 300/300 all COMPLETE but each with 1 MISSING import (the xmldsig schema: a remote w3.org URL or a path outside the uploaded tree; the generator supplies it through its catalog, so these 3 are measured without the signature types); UBL Invoice 2.1 (14 files) 5622 constructs, 5607 modeled, PARTIAL 15. The 15 is EXACT: 1 xs:any in UBL-ExtensionContentDataType, 2 in UBL-XAdESv132, 12 unprefixed <any> in UBL-xmldsig-core-schema (a literal count over the 14 files gives 15), so the census counts wildcards across files and prefix spellings. 7 of 8 sets reach 100%; UBL's gap is entirely signature/extension wildcards. Next for exact parity with the generator: run with each family's catalog (families.spi source = Xsd catalog) so the xmldsig imports resolve.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_8 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 8u32, "2026-11-03T22:04Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:03 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job fiscal-xsd-census4, core 2ABF22D79E6B6943, one compiler): xsd_census 1/1 on the node mirror.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_9 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 9u32, "2026-11-04T01:12Z", "kit", "11-03 21:1x kit: kit's half of the DoD started (fiscal's lib census is landed and proven). New owner crate kit_gauge_xsd in the tree (after the TRAIN17b snapshot; HostFree, no host macros): 'kit gauge xsd <schema.xsd>' loads the schema tree with lib xsd_resolve.load_schema_tree (includes and imports resolved), runs lib xsd_census.schema_census, and prints: files, missing, constructs, modeled, wildcards, and completeness (complete | partial:N via kebab). The verb is a reflected gauge_verb union. GENERIC per kit's contract: it names no project (the DoD's 'kit gauge fiscal --xsd' becomes 'kit gauge xsd <file>'), and a test asserts 'fiscal' is not a verb. Registered (workspace member, test row). Proof: job-1793754669860-kit-precheck-gauge, queued after precheck-s4.\nNEXT: (1) route it: add VerbGauge to command_spec_domain.direct_verbs plus its help and usage, and make kit_cli_model's VerbGauge call kit_gauge_xsd.gauge.gauge_run through a link (packages + link in kit_cli_model and kit_cli, plus the Cargo dep), NOT a new host hop; (2) run it on the SAF-T 1.04_01 corpus XSD and match fiscal's 708/708 COMPLETE, which is this item's 'matches fiscal's census' check.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_10 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 10u32, "2026-11-04T01:16Z", "kit", "11-03 21:2x kit: ROUTED (tree, unproven). VerbGauge is a new case of command_spec_domain.direct_verbs, with a help line ('gauge xsd <schema.xsd> ...'). kit_cli_model routes '| VerbGauge => kit_gauge_xsd.gauge.gauge_run ()' as a LINKED call (kit_gauge_xsd under packages and link in kit_cli_model and kit_cli, Cargo dep in kit_cli, lock refreshed), not a new host-string hop like its neighbours. kit_cli_model is the only exhaustive match over direct_verb. Proof widened by closure: job-1793754669860-kit-precheck-gauge now covers command_spec_domain, kit_cli, kit_command_help, kit_command_usages, kit_gauge_xsd and kit_legacy_operations. Watch kit_cli's size (kit.rs was 1265 at TRAIN16b) and grep kit.rs for kit_gauge_xsd:: to confirm the link. LEFT: the SAF-T 708/708 cross-check once a train installs it.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_11 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 11u32, "2026-11-04T01:17Z", "kit", "11-03 21:2x kit: Blocked on proof, not on work. The verb and its routing are in the tree (n9, n10). Unblock when job-1793754669860-kit-precheck-gauge is green; then, after a train installs it, run 'kit gauge xsd' on the SAF-T 1.04_01 XSD and match fiscal's 708/708 COMPLETE.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_12 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 12u32, "2026-11-04T04:44Z", "kit", "11-04 00:4x PARKED out of TRAIN18: kit_gauge_xsd generated 4964 lines (gate 1000), because lib xsd_resolve + xsd_census inline whole into the one crate that calls them. Crate and wiring are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S6-parked-1104 (src/kit_gauge_xsd, plus wired/ copies of direct_verbs, model, spiprojs, Cargo files). Also fixed in the parked copy: main moved under `///> _` (the TRAIN17b Zig trap). Options: (a) split the census over linked units (resolve unit -> array of construct rows -> census unit), each <1000; (b) run the gauge as a lib program on vultr/the node instead of a kit verb. Fiscal (the owner of the calibration) decides which; (a) is kit's default.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_13 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 13u32, "2026-11-04T08:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 04:07 fiscal: DECIDED with kit (11-04 04:1x): option (b). The XSD gauge stays a lib/fiscal program run on vultr or the node when a family or the XSD model changes (that is how the 7/8-complete numbers were made: vultr probes over lib xsd_census, pack27), and kit stores the verdict rows in DIAMOND-S3's typed ledger (per schema set, keyed by unit hash + rubric version: set, complete, wildcards, modeled/declared counts). The kit verb split (option a: resolve unit -> census unit over linked units, ~2 h + a train slot) is deferred until a CLI need appears; the parked draft stays at drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S6-parked-1104.")
inl note_of_diamond_s6_14 () = Note ("DIAMOND-S6", 14u32, "2026-11-04T08:09Z", "kit", "DONE 11-04 05:2x (decision by fiscal, 05:1x: option (b)). The XSD gauge is a calibration run when a family or the XSD model changes, not a per-command tool, so it stays a lib/fiscal one-call program on vultr or the node (how the 7/8-complete numbers were produced over lib xsd_census, pack27). The kit verb split (4964 generated lines) is dropped; the parked crate stays in drafts\\kit\\DIAMOND-S6-parked-1104 as a record, and (a) can follow if a CLI need appears. kit's part becomes storing verdicts: DIAMOND-S3's ledger now has an XsdReading answer {complete; wildcards; modeled; declared} keyed by unit hash + rubric version.")
