inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_1 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:30 fiscal: FOUND by fiscal's edition-3 proof (node job-1793506463392, mirror t1101, installed compiler pack 10 DFC86B91968D). In an EDITION-3 package (fiscal src respelled; src/package.spiproj \"edition: 3\" + spiral.toml), corpus_checks tests resolves_the_nfe_tree and resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet fail in rustc: error[E0425] \"cannot find value `st` in this scope\" at generated main.rs:4568 \"st = Group94::M97(v6, v10);\" (and :4645 \"st = Group99::M102(v6, v10);\"); rustc suggests \"let st = ...\". So the Rust backend emits an assignment to a binding it never declared. The tests call lib xsd_resolve (edition-2 lib code inlined into the edition-3 package); the test sources contain no `st`. The SAME tests PASS in edition 2: CI run 41281571029 (ubuntu, spiral main e0461f15) and node t1031u (pack 8 EEBCBFF8658A). Two variables differ from the green runs (edition 3 vs 2; pack 10 vs CI/pack 8), so the first bisect step is the edition-2 tree with pack 10. REPRO: node mirror C:\\home\\remote\\t1101 (kept for this), pwsh t1101\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\spi\\lib_gate.ps1 -Lib t1101\\fiscal\\src -File corpus_checks.spi -Compiler process with SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL = the installed pack 10; the failing notebook is C:\\home\\remote-stage\\fiscal-e3-regen\\corpus_checks.spi.txt.ipynb. DONE WHEN both tests pass on t1101 in edition 3. BLOCKS FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (the respell is not applied to the fiscal tree until then).")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_2 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:22Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:22 compiler: ROOT CAUSE FOUND, MINE (PACK-12's mutual-tail group loops, MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS). NOT edition-3 specific: edition 3 only changes the order in which methods are first emitted. Mechanism (spiral_compiler.fs codegenRust): emit_group (~14375) sets group_loop = Some(GroupN, members) while it emits the member bodies. A method referenced for the FIRST time from inside a member body is emitted right then by the jp printer callback (~14327), which saved/cleared self_loop but NOT group_loop. So that nested ordinary fn's tail call to a group member hit the TyJoinPoint arm at ~13903 (members.Contains) and emitted 'st = GroupN::M<k>(...)': no 'st' in that fn, rustc E0425. MINIMAL REPRO (box, installed pack13a): count_even/count_odd mutual tail pair + 'bump' called NON-tail from count_even, with bump tail-calling count_odd; the Rust output has 'fn bump_2 ... st = Group0::M1(v2, v3);', rustc E0425 at main.rs:9. FIX (one kit do program, apps/compiler/packs/pack14/1-group-loop-scope.kitdo): the method printer saves group_loop, sets None for the method's whole body, restores after (the closure and while paths already reset it via without_self_loop). Candidate pack14a building (job-1793539338732). PROOF PLAN: (1) the repro builds under rustc and exits 0 like C; (2) predict vs pack13a's run: only Rust rows with a mutual group may change, compile-status diffs 0; (3) fiscal's resolves_* on t1101 with the candidate; (4) regression sample samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_3 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 3u32, "2026-11-01T13:25Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:25 compiler: (1) DONE: candidate pack14a (core DBC5EC18F14C354C) on the 3-function repro: bump_2 has no 'st =', rustc -O builds, exit 0 = C's exit 0. (2) predict vs pack13a's run (single-flight-20261101-080900) running: job-1793539488130. (3) fiscal's two resolves_* on t1101 with the candidate (binaries shipped to node C:\\home\\remote\\e3assign\\pack14a-bin, hash verified, SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL) running: job-1793539537261. Regression sample staged: apps/compiler/packs/pack14/samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee (enters samples/ at install; today's compiler makes it a Rust build failure).")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_4 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 4u32, "2026-11-01T13:30Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:30 compiler: FIX PROVEN, all 3 checks green (repro builds and agrees; fiscal resolves_* 2/2 on t1101 with pack14a; predict 0 diffs in 7,413 rows). Handed to main as PACK-14. Done when installed and fiscal's FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND gate is green on the installed compiler.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_5 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 5u32, "2026-11-01T13:33Z", "main", "main 09:3x: FIXED on the box by pack14a (installed 09:31). compiler's evidence: the 3-function repro builds and exits 0 = C, and fiscal's resolves_the_nfe_tree + resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet pass 2/2 on t1101 with the candidate. Main's check: the new sample's generated Rust compiles under rustc and runs exit 0. Node gets it at the 10:23 ship. Close after fiscal's rerun on the box or the node.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_6 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 6u32, "2026-11-01T13:36Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:34 compiler: fix INSTALLED (PACK-14, 09:31). Lanes rerun the rows they VOIDed with the E0425 signature on the box. Done when fiscal's FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND gate is green on the installed compiler.")
inl note_of_edition3_rust_undeclared_assign_7 () = Note ("EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", 7u32, "2026-11-01T13:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 09:40 fiscal: VERIFIED FIXED on the box with pack14a (installed 09:31; SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C at 09:33, where codegen lives; the CLI SpiralCompiler.dll hash DFC86B91968D unchanged). Rerun of the edition-3 respelled fiscal src (fresh respell of the current tree, package.spiproj \"edition: 3\" + spiral.toml, corpus_checks 244E17E3912A after the cap bump) through fiscal/scripts/box-gate.ps1 -Test: resolves_the_nfe_tree 1/1 passed, resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet 1/1 passed, type errors 0, no E0425 (raw outputs in the fiscal session scratchpad e3-gate\\*.txt). Cause per compiler: the PACK-12 group-loop leak; edition 3 only changed emission order. CLOSED.")
inl kit_train7 () = Task ("KIT-TRAIN7", "TRAIN7: ship tonight's verified kit changes (note segments, typed lint baselines, todo fix, no-respell writers ...) via a node pre-proof + manifest-checked box train", Story, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN", "kit,team:kit,release,train,node", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_train7 () = Planning ("KIT-TRAIN7", Minutes 180u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_train7_1 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:17Z", "kit", "11-01 09:1x kit groom: split out of EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN, which has 208 notes at 45% and has become the log of every train run, so 'install TRAIN7' (what KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES, EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL and EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS are blocked by) was not a closable unit anywhere. CONTENT of TRAIN7: note-segment readers and writer (EOIE-AGILE-EVENT-LOG), typed .spi lint baselines and the string-literal arith fix (GRANULAR-LINT), the TODO-scan --tagged fix (KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS n18), the resume freshness guard, copy-literal, lint --opens, standards subfolders, the no-respell writers (scaffold, views, lease, receipts), respells, plus tonight's new packages as they get wired. DoD: (a) node pre-proof: candidate-build of every owner changed since TRAIN6 green and notebook-batch over every touched module with 0 RED, with a sha256 manifest of the generated crates; (b) the box train runs -SkipRegen only after its tree matches that manifest; (c) installed kit.exe hash recorded; acceptance rows green; (d) the three Blocked items above closed by acceptance runs on the installed binary. NEXT STEP: the pre-proof job on node mirror kit-verify with the full owner list (memory remote-kit-worker-node: no re-sync between regen and build). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: n/a for the release itself; the manifest is typed rows (crate, file, sha256 nominal) compared as sets, as specified for the kit train port on EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_2 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:23Z", "kit", "11-01 09:2x kit (main's heads-up): KNOWN COMPILER REGRESSION in the installed compiler (pack12b / pack13a): pack 12's mutual-tail group loops can emit a tail call as 'st = GroupN::M..(..)' inside a function that has no 'st', and rustc fails with E0425. RULE for this train: a regen or candidate-build row failing with E0425 on an 'st = Group' line is VOID (compiler's bug, not kit's), recorded with that signature, never chased as a kit fix; if it reds the train, wait for compiler's pack14a, which main installs on hand-over, then rerun. CONSEQUENCE FOR THE DoD: tonight's node proofs (candidates 923AAF5A, FB34FD11, BBF31C2A, 81741E5A; 01:30-02:20) ran on the node's compiler from BEFORE pack 12 was installed on the box (03:14), so they do not certify the compiler this train will use (memory node-proof-skips-regen: one compiler; the run must pin the box's installed DLL, core hash equal). DoD (a) is therefore: the node pre-proof pins SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL to the box's installed core (pack14a once installed; recorded by hash) and reruns the full owner regen + notebook batch there; earlier proofs count as design evidence only. Order: wait for pack14a, pin, pre-proof, then the box train with -SkipRegen against the manifest.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_3 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 3u32, "2026-11-01T13:24Z", "kit", "11-01 09:2x kit: blocked by: EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN (compiler, P0; the 'st = GroupN::M..(..)' E0425 regression, fixed in pack14a). Added as a dep so the wait is visible in agile next; the train starts once pack14a is installed and pinned.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_4 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 4u32, "2026-11-01T13:34Z", "kit", "11-01 09:3x kit: pack14a (the E0425 'st = GroupN::' fix) installed on the box 09:31 (EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN 85%, closes after fiscal's rerun); the node gets it in the one-shot ship at 10:23, after compiler's A/B. kit VOIDed nothing with that signature (no kit build ran on pack12b), so there is nothing to rerun. PLAN: right after the node ship, verify the node's effective compiler core equals the box's installed pack14a core (by hash, memory node-stale-compiler-dll), then start the pre-proof: full owner regen + notebook batch over every module touched since TRAIN6 + the sha256 manifest. The dep on EDITION3-RUST-UNDECLARED-ASSIGN stays until compiler closes it; the pre-proof itself is evidence for that closure.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_5 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 5u32, "2026-11-01T14:46Z", "kit", "11-01 10:46 kit: at 10:4x ssh laptop failed once to resolve desktop-6e8c14g (mDNS); it resolved again at 10:46 (hostname DESKTOP-6E8C14G). The pre-proof check of the node core vs pack14a runs right after groom round 5 (10:53), not at the 10:33 wake, which was held by the round.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_6 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 6u32, "2026-11-01T14:51Z", "kit", "11-01 10:51 kit: precondition MET. remote.ps1 node status: node compiler DBC5EC18F14C354C (2026-11-01 09:33) = box compiler DBC5EC18F14C354C (pack14a); runners equal F1DD2E34F1E816C8. main shipped early at 09:35 (node-upkeep.log, digest 0AF644516C09E959). The pre-proof (full owner regen + notebook batch over every module touched since TRAIN6 + sha256 manifest) starts right after groom round 5 closes; the node also runs compiler-libord-seq (peak 5 GB of 8 GB cap), so the kit job runs at default parallelism and retries lower on a memory kill (retry-after-memory-kills).")
inl note_of_kit_train7_7 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 7u32, "2026-11-01T15:01Z", "kit", "11-01 11:01 kit: PRE-PROOF STARTED, node job job-1793545254729-kit-train7-preproof (3 h cap) on mirror kit-verify. Core check: node compiler DBC5EC18F14C354C = box pack14a; runners F1DD2E34 equal. Mirror synced BEFORE the job (REMOTE-SYNC-OK kit d486fd04 digest 51010DD4, spiral 7a4c960e digest F1FC35A8); no re-sync until the job ends. Owners (41): the 34 of the norespell proof plus the module-package mapping since TRAIN6 (agile_todo_model -> agile_todo_fields/lines/merge/paths/roots/sources/scan, kit_lint_model -> kit_lint_classify/macros/scan/walk, agile_state_runtime -> kit_agile_state). Notebooks (19): the 13 changed model modules plus todo/views/notes/agile/roots/table CLI notebooks. Manifest: C:\\home\\remote\\kit-verify\\train7\\manifest.spi (typed rows Crate (path, sha256) + Candidate sha256). NEXT after green: fetch the manifest, box train with -SkipRegen against it, then acceptance runs for KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES, EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL, EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_8 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 8u32, "2026-11-01T15:53Z", "kit", "11-01 11:53 kit: NODE PRE-PROOF RESULT (job-1793545254729, 49 min): candidate-build GREEN for all 41 owners (regen + cargo check + publish + cargo build, candidate sha256 F3B96644...); manifest 42 crate rows. Notebooks 18/19: the one RED, state_receipt_serializer_domain/model.spi, is MY module-selection error, not a regression. That module has no package header and no test blocks (discovered 0), so a standalone notebook cannot see char_backslash from its package dependency state_receipt_codec_model. Its proof is the crate regen + cargo check, which passed. BOX ACCEPT: 28 of 42 generated .rs on the box differed (pre-pack14a codegen, e.g. kit_resume 464 -> 766 lines); I copied the node's 28 files into the tree (unstaged; git holds the old ones). The manifest check is 42/42 sha256 equal, and freshness holds (no owner .spi newer than the regen). BOX TRAIN STARTED with -SkipRegen: launcher job-1793548387233 -> heavy job job-1793548391365-kit-TRAIN7, runner pinned F1DD2E34F1E816C8; launch-train.ps1's default RunnerHash 2E5F532E is stale and needs updating. Lesson for the pre-proof script: select notebook modules by '///- --package' header + test blocks, never by 'changed'.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_9 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 9u32, "2026-11-01T16:01Z", "kit", "11-01 12:01 kit: the BOX TRAIN STOPPED at the crate gate (job-1793548391365, 11 s): kit_lint_macros lint.rs 1,040 and agile_todo_scan todo_scan.rs 1,021 lines, both over the 1,000-line gate. The node pre-proof never ran the gate, a gap in my script (proof-must-run-consumer-path); the fix script now runs 'crate gate --enforce' on the node. CAUSE: the committed .rs had lagged their sources (kit_resume 464 -> 766 and kit_standards 572 -> 920 are other lanes' source work, not codegen), plus tonight's typed-baseline CLI branch in lint (+133) and pack14a layout plus text_may_hold in todo_scan (+28). HAND SPLIT (hand-modeled-build-units), unstaged: (1) the baseline exports move from kit_lint_walk to kit_lint_classify (774 lines, already imports kit_lint_model), plus a new export kit_lint_baseline_write (writes the typed baseline, returns the row count); lint.spi calls classify; classify's !!!!Export migrated to export. (2) New crate agile_todo_standing (todo_standing union, standing_of, standing_label, standings record, standings_from), with workspace member, Cargo deps, Cargo.lock and census row added; todo_scan keeps one cross-crate call and drops its agile-task-census dependency. The ratchet over the 5 packages shows 0 regressions. Node proof: job-1793548828042-kit-node-split (regen of the 5 owners, crate gate, split manifest, todo_cli + kit_lint_model notebooks), then the --write-baseline consumer check. The kit-style hook flagged the cross-crate \\$' calls, which are kept on purpose: crates can only call each other through them, and the edit removes 2 and adds 1.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_10 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 10u32, "2026-11-01T16:19Z", "kit", "11-01 12:19 kit: SPLIT PROVEN on the node in two rounds. Round 1 (job-1793548828042): classify grew 774 -> 1,245, because the baseline code is about 470 generated lines, so it could not live in classify. Round 2 (job-1793549384149): a new crate kit_lint_baseline (619 lines) holds kit_lint_baseline_rows and kit_lint_baseline_write. Final sizes: agile_todo_standing 123, agile_todo_scan 937, kit_lint_baseline 619, kit_lint_classify 774, kit_lint_macros 967, kit_lint_walk 651. Crate gate ok: 272 crates, 0 over (node and box). Notebooks: todo_cli 4/4, kit_lint_model 10/10. CONSUMER PATH: the candidate converts the live 909-row standards/lint-macros.spi to 909 typed rows, and 'lint macros <kit>/src --baseline' against either the converted or the live typed baseline gives violations 906, new 0, exit 0. Box accept: split manifest 6/6, TRAIN7 manifest 38/38 for the rows not superseded. launch-train.ps1's default RunnerHash was updated 2E5F532E -> F1DD2E34F1E816C8 (the runner box and node share). BOX TRAIN RELAUNCHED as TRAIN7b with -SkipRegen: launcher job-1793549960043.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_11 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 11u32, "2026-11-01T17:27Z", "kit", "11-01 13:27 kit: TRAIN7b (job-1793549962708, 62 min): crate gate ok (272), candidate 1D93A1E4, notebooks 55/56; nothing installed. The one red, kit_do_file_steps/steps.spi, was NOT a test failure: its test passed 1/1, then the notebook built the untargeted main on Cells' default Zig target ('Export with 2 args not supported in the Zig backend'; memory notebook-main-default-zig). The module became a notebook when the EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL test block was added. FIX (unstaged): '///> _' above main, the idiom 10 other kit modules use. Node proof job-1793553852998: regen publishes 0 changed owners (steps.rs sha256 B84B76A5... = the TRAIN7 manifest), notebook 1/1. TRAIN7c launched with -SkipRegen (launcher job-1793554041486) over the full notebook set; launch-train has no -Only, and a full rerun on the candidate is the stronger evidence anyway.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_12 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 12u32, "2026-11-01T18:59Z", "kit", "11-01 14:59 kit: TRAIN7c (heavy job-1793554047930) is still in its notebook phase at 14:58 (started 13:28; slower than TRAIN7b's 59 min on a loaded box). main landed the lib '::' respell at 14:53 (EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION n59) DURING that phase, so notebooks after 14:53 read the respelled lib. A red in TRAIN7c is first judged against that land (undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-132117) before kit code is suspected.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_13 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 13u32, "2026-11-01T19:38Z", "kit", "11-01 15:38 kit: TRAIN7 INSTALLED. TRAIN7c (heavy job-1793554047930): crate gate 272/0 over, candidate 1D93A1E4, notebooks 56/56, release build ok, installed kit.exe A25B8FBD at 15:24, smoke ok; the lane copy was refreshed and the old binary kept in kit\\retired. ACCEPTANCE on the installed binary closed KIT-AGILE-LOST-UPDATES (10-round two-writer race: 0 lost, 0 refused), EOIE-DO-COPY-LITERAL (a literal file copies 1 file) and EOIE-NOTEBOOK-PROGRESS (the watch prints the batch line). DONE.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_14 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 14u32, "2026-11-02T00:26Z", "kit", "11-01 20:26 kit: TRAIN8 launched (launcher job-1793579152082, -SkipRegen). Node pre-proof job-1793576729929: crate gate 272/0 over; owners kit_os_launch (605: the --after RemoteSession owner fix), kit_job_state (937: the placement suffix), kit_table_query (725: table to-spi with the rows index and --open), agile_planning_revision (271: the no-op edit short-circuit); notebooks 8/8. Box accept: manifest 4/4, crate gate ok. Also riding: x-dumps' Linux dotnet discovery (hand-written kit_process/native_compiler.rs), the attestation contract heals, notebook-batch/user-env portability. Held out for TRAIN9: KIT_JOB_SLOTS (kit_job_host over the gate), kit k3s (3,221 lines, being reworked to typed .spi rows), the bindings verb (parked by the user's 17:4x direction). Main holds lib-reshape R1b+R2 until this installs (21:50 at the latest).")
inl note_of_kit_train7_15 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 15u32, "2026-11-02T00:35Z", "kit", "11-01 20:35 kit: TRAIN8 caveat (main 20:3x): x landed into the LIVE tree at 20:31 during TRAIN8 (lib/spiral/package.spiproj 9D730998 -> 12690959, additive erlang_* modules; apps/cells/spi cell.spi, main.spi, package.spiproj, new daemon.spi). TRAIN8 runs without a snapshot (started before KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN made snapshots the default), so a red after 20:31 is judged against that land first (undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\x-c3c4-lib-20261101-203122). From TRAIN9 on, launch-train snapshots kit and lib by default (-LiveTree opts out).")
inl note_of_kit_train7_16 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 16u32, "2026-11-02T02:57Z", "kit", "11-01 22:57 kit: TRAIN8 INSTALLED at 22:55: kit.exe 7C559D83 (TRAIN8s, snapshot kit+lib; candidate 9248993C; notebooks 44/44; release checks ok; lane copy refreshed, previous binary in kit\\retired). Main asked to ship it to the node (the --after owner fix). Acceptance: REMOTE-EXEC-S1 (job list byte-identical), KIT-SCALE no-op (unchanged, 1 ms), table to-spi on a tibia tsv: all green.")
inl note_of_kit_train7_17 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN7", 17u32, "2026-11-02T02:59Z", "kit", "11-01 22:59 kit: main shipped TRAIN8's kit.exe 7C559D83 to the NODE by renaming the running exe aside (the running x-verify48b job kept running; the old binary kept as kit-4983F9C0-replaced.exe), the deploys-never-wait-for-idle rule in practice. RemoteSession owner fix PROVEN on the node: a --after job queued over ssh got host_home=shared and ran after its predecessor, exit 0. The node --after queuing works again for every lane.")
