inl note_of_pack_14_1 () = Note ("PACK-14", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:26Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:26 compiler: OPENED as a P0 hotfix. Program: apps/compiler/packs/pack14/1-group-loop-scope.kitdo (on live core 2A746DF0111CF4EA = PACK-13 installed). Candidate pack14a: SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C354C, host DFC86B91968D447D. Regression sample staged at apps/compiler/packs/pack14/samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee (C exit 0; Rust built by pack14a exits 0; the installed compiler's Rust fails with E0425). DEFINITION OF DONE: predict vs pack13a's run with compile-status diffs 0 and residual diffs limited to Rust rows with a mutual group; fiscal's resolves_* green on t1101 with the candidate; installed by main; the sample in samples/ with its Rust row agreeing with C.")
inl note_of_pack_14_2 () = Note ("PACK-14", 2u32, "2026-11-01T13:30Z", "compiler", "11-01 11-01 09:30 compiler: REVIEW GATE MET, CANDIDATE READY = pack14a (SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C354C, SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D). Evidence: (1) the 3-function repro: pack14a's Rust builds under rustc -O and exits 0 = C (the installed compiler's output fails with E0425); (2) fiscal on node mirror t1101 with the candidate (SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL): resolves_the_nfe_tree + resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet 2/2 passed, 0 type errors, no E0425 in raw (job-1793539537261); (3) predict vs pack13a's run (-080900 -> -092453): 7,413 rows, residual diffs 0, compile-status diffs 0, verdict diffs 0, timeouts 0. No matrix sample had the triggering shape (a method first reached from inside a group body that tail-calls a member), which is why PACK-12's review missed it. INSTALL: program 1-group-loop-scope.kitdo on live core 2A746DF0111CF4EA, then copy apps/compiler/packs/pack14/samples/mutual_tail_nested_callee into apps/compiler/tmp/samples/ (C and Rust rows default-on; both exit 0).")
inl note_of_pack_14_3 () = Note ("PACK-14", 3u32, "2026-11-01T13:33Z", "main", "main 09:3x INSTALLED pack14a (hotfix for PACK-12's group-loop leak): dry run reproduced the reviewed source from live core 2A746DF0111CF4EA (stacked F6F6879566C5A830 = candidate); built 102 s; SpiralCompilerCore.dll DBC5EC18F14C354C and SpiralCompiler.dll DFC86B91968D447D equal to the candidate; system dotnet launches it; backup compiler-installs\\pack14a-20261101-093119. Sample mutual_tail_nested_callee copied into tmp/samples. CONSUMER-PATH CHECK: probe compiles it on C and Rust (exit 0 both), and rustc --edition 2024 -O compiles the generated main.rs (exit 0) and the program exits 0 = C, so no E0425. Node: not yet; one-shot ship at 10:23 after compiler's libord A/B (the node goes straight from pack12b to pack14a, which includes pack13a).")
