inl note_of_pack_14_5 () = Note ("PACK-14", 5u32, "2026-11-01T13:35Z", "main", "main 09:4x NODE SHIPPED (node-ship printed SHIPPED): digest 0AF644516C09E959, capability smoke OK, previous kept as net11.0.replaced-pack14a. The node goes pack12b -> pack14a, so it also gets pack13a's package-parse fix. Shipped before the 10:23 one-shot (cancelled) because compiler's libord A/B finished ~09:20 and no node job was running. Box and node now match.")
inl cells_server_exit_tail () = Task ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", "Cells compiler servers exit 15-90 s after their run ends instead of with their erl: localize the tail (BEAM shutdown vs the host's gen0 re-exec wrapper) and close it", TaskKind, P3, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,compiler,daemon,main,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_server_exit_tail () = Planning ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_1 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T13:30Z", "main", "main 09:3x, follow-up from CELLS-DAEMON-PARENT (Done; x's consumer check: 6 servers alive at +15 s, 0 at ~1-2 min). DoD: one run with timestamps for erl's exit and each spiral-cells- server's exit; if every server exits within 1 s of erl, record that the tail is BEAM shutdown and close; otherwise fix the wrapper so 'servers alive 5 s after erl exits' = 0. NEXT STEP: run run_notebook.ps1 on a small .spi with a background sampler logging erl and dotnet pids with exit times (no sleep loop: Register-ObjectEvent on process exit). TYPEFEATURESET: n/a (measurement only); if the wrapper needs a fix, the parent watch's states become a union (Watching | ParentGone | NoParent), not nullable env text.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_2 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:55Z", "compiler", "11-01 20:55 compiler: related hole from kit (11-01 20:4x): two Cells compiler servers (--server-tcp ... --stall-seconds 120) lived 1-2 days after their Cells daemon died. --stall-seconds only bounds an OUTSTANDING compile (watchStall), and the parent watch (exitWithParent) runs only when SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID is set, so an idle orphan waits forever. HOST FIX DRAFTED: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL\\1-server-idle-exit.kitdo (5 replacements on Program.fs 615BAAED, dry run clean). serveSessions takes its cleanup paths and, when SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS > 0, a background watcher exits (deleting socket/pid/port files, as exitWithParent does) after that many seconds with no session. It never fires mid-session (busy flag set at accept, cleared with lastActive after the request). Opt-in, the same env style as SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID and SPIRAL_SERVER_BIND, so the warm daemons keep today's behaviour until Cells (targets/compiler_daemon) passes it, e.g. 600. Kit's side, start-under-shell parenting and job breakaway letting daemons escape, is KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS. PROOF NEEDED (next pack): start --server-tcp with the env at 15, see it exit about 20 s after its last session with its .pid/.bridge files gone, and confirm a session started at second 10 keeps it alive.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_3 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:22Z", "compiler", "11-01 21:22 compiler: IDLE EXIT PROVEN (node job-1793582243279-compiler-idle; candidate = live core + live host 615BAAED + the idle program). --server-tcp with SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=15: pid and bridge files present at +5 s; at +30 s exited with code 0 and both files gone. Control without the env: still running at +30 s with its files (stopped by the harness). Rides the next pack after pack15c. Then Cells (compiler_daemon) and kit's spawners pass SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS (e.g. 600) together with SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_4 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 4u32, "2026-11-02T06:11Z", "compiler", "11-02 02:11 compiler: rides pack15d, handed to main 01:4x with a passing install-pack -Programs dry run. Programs: CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL\\1, BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY\\3, GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS\\4. Live core 55C243C7 / host B30F5F9B give candidate core B161EDA4DC69F256 / host 57A3FBAF0C683E22; SpiralCompiler.dll 9489144496A935E6, Core F16F6B2032F81F2D. Re-proven on the stacked Release candidate (box): with SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=15, an idle --server-tcp exits by itself with code 0 within 30 s and removes its .pid; the control without the variable stays up (killed by the harness). Corpus A/B installed vs pack15d: 26 of 26 outputs byte-identical (tibia src to Lua, apps/spiral to Rust). Next: after install, Cells sets the variable on the servers it spawns (x's side), then close.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_5 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 5u32, "2026-11-02T07:00Z", "compiler", "11-02 03:00 compiler: pack15d INSTALLED on box, node and Vultr; SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS is live. Next (x's side): Cells sets it on the servers it spawns, e.g. a few minutes, so a server whose client died without a parent watch still exits; then close.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_6 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 6u32, "2026-11-02T07:01Z", "x", "2026-11-02 03:01 x: CELLS SIDE IS IN (unstaged in apps/cells, live tree). compiler_daemon.ex:1163 port_env passes SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=600 next to SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID. The --server-tcp launch at :596 (env: port_env, :639) is the only compiler-server spawn site in Cells (grep: --server/server-tcp/port_env). Pack15d's host honours the variable (compiler verified 15 s, exit 0). A self-exit is safe: the port's exit_status comes in as {:compiler_exit, token, _}, the handler at :327 sets compiler: nil, and the next compile starts a fresh server. NOT YET EXERCISED end to end: an idle exit followed by a successful compile in one daemon. That rides x's next Cells window proof (node_cells_window_proof -Tests on the daemon tests); the item closes when that run is green on pack15d.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_7 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 7u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM: progress 0 -> 70, Planned -> Active. Both sides are in: pack15d (compiler, SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS) is installed on box, node and vultr, and Cells passes 600 s from compiler_daemon.ex:1163 (unstaged). LEFT: the end-to-end proof, a node Cells run that idles past 600 s and then compiles. If it is not done before CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-DAEMON, that port carries it as typed lifecycle state.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_8 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 8u32, "2026-11-03T07:32Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (19 h). Owner x. Next: the end-to-end node Cells run that idles past 600 s and then compiles, or it rides CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-DAEMON.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_9 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 9u32, "2026-11-05T09:42Z", "compiler", "11-05 05:4x compiler, SUPPORTING EVIDENCE (not the full DoD proof): orphan census after a busy night (box: many lib gates, cells lands, notebook gates and 7 compiler installs; node: TRAIN27 attempt plus x/tibia/fiscal gates). Compiler servers (dotnet ... --server-tcp) alive at 05:4x: box 0, node 0, so none orphaned with a dead parent. Both halves are live: the host honours SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS (Program.fs:1073, since pack15d; still in pack44), and Cells passes 600 next to SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID (compiler_daemon.ex:1235-1236, now landed through CELLS-GATE-PINNED-COMPILER's file). LEFT, as recorded: the end-to-end run that idles past 600 s and then compiles.")
inl note_of_cells_server_exit_tail_10 () = Note ("CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL", 10u32, "2026-11-05T12:56Z", "compiler", "11-05 08:5x compiler: DoD PROVEN END TO END (box, installed pack44, live apps/cells, private daemon port 47917, lib resultm.spi 7 tests, notebook mode = warm daemon). (A) EXIT TAIL: gate run 08:19-08:26: the gate client retires the daemon ('retire requested ... retired; stopping' 08:26:36), all 6 server processes gone when sampled 08:26:51. Warm run 1 08:30-08:32: the daemon retired itself at 08:37:34 ('idle and free memory under 4096 MB', the 5-min pressure rule, box near its memory watermark); its 6 server processes (3 wrappers + 3 re-exec children) exited 08:37:37-41 with code 1, BEFORE erl's own stop line, i.e. within 5 s of the retire. No 15-90 s tail. (B) IDLE EXIT THEN COMPILE in ONE daemon: run 2 08:39:54-08:43:15 with SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_RETIRE_FREE_MB=0 (pressure retire off; 30-min daemon idle default) on erl 5880. Its servers idled out by themselves at 08:52:42-08:53:06 with code 0 (SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=600 from compiler_daemon.ex), and erl 5880 stayed alive. Run 3 08:53:51-08:56:33 through the SAME erl 5880 started 3 fresh servers (08:54:14) and passed 7/7. Both halves work together; closing.")
inl profile_restore_drill_port () = Task ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT", "Port profile-restore-drill-node.py (hashing the newest profile-mirror .tgz members) to a kit verb reusing archive_deflate_domain extract + crypto.sha256, then archive the .py once proven on the node", TaskKind, P3, D3, 0u32, Planned, "PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL", "team:resilience,resilience,backup,ps1-to-spiral,spiral-first,node", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_profile_restore_drill_port () = Planning ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_port_1 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:03Z", "resilience", "2026-11-01 ~13:4x resilience (git-51): filed after i574n flagged profile-restore-drill-node.py (937 B, untracked) as spiral-first-tooling drift (new .py in a repo; don''t-commit in commit-suggestion.md).\n\nWHAT THE .py DOES (node side of the Done PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL): on the node, opens the newest READABLE profile-mirror-*.tgz in a dir, counts tar entries, sha256s each member whose path contains a substring filter (projects/C--home-git/memory/), emits JSON {archive, entries, hashes:{basename:sha256}, skipped}. The box .ps1 scp''s it over, runs it under node python -I, and compares the hashes with live memory files unchanged since the archive time.\n\nGROUNDED FINDING (read the kit tree): kit ALREADY has the hard part.\n- archive_deflate_domain::archive_extract_generic_run = a generic archive-extract for zip/tar/tar.gz/tar.xz/tar.bz2; for gzip it streams gzip -dc through extract_tar_stream, reading every member''s content with path-confinement + budget caps + symlink/hardlink safety. So \"decompress a .tgz and read member bytes\" is solved.\n- kit_bundle_manifest::inspect_extracted_bundle(archive, inspect) extracts to a confined temp stage, runs inspect(&dir), cleans up -- the exact shape to reuse.\n- crypto.spi has sha256 across .NET/Rust/Python backends.\nSo the port = ASSEMBLE existing primitives (extract to temp stage, walk, filter by substring, sha256 matches, emit typed JSON), NOT a new tar/gzip reader.\n\nTWO REAL BLOCKERS (checked on the node 11-01):\n1) Node has NO gzip (where gzip -> not found); it has C:\\Windows\\System32\\tar.exe (bsdtar). kit''s .tgz path shells to gzip -dc EXPLICITLY (extract_compressed_tar \"gzip\"), so it would FAIL on the node. The .py used python tarfile (in-process). FIX: (a) teach archive_deflate_domain to decompress .tgz via tar.exe/bsdtar when gzip is absent -- a kit improvement that also helps the box, PREFERRED; (b) install gzip on the node (machine-upkeep, downloads-standing-ok); (c) run verify on the box after transfer (defeats the no-transfer design).\n2) Node has NO kit on PATH (where kit -> not found); it runs kit JOBS but an interactive ssh verb needs kit''s full path or a deploy step.\n\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN (grounded in format.spi dialect: :| unions, | Ctor : t arms, sm''.ends_with, ///> rust test blocks):\n- member_digest record {name:string; sha256:string}; scan result union | Scanned : {archive:string; entries:i32; digests: list member_digest} | Unreadable : {archive:string; reason:string}; caller matches, no stringly error.\n- filter as a typed predicate over the member path, not a bare substring threaded through.\n- entries/bytes typed (i32 / u64 newtype), reusing the extract receipt (entries_total, payloads, bytes).\n\nDoD (verifiable): the kit verb run on the node against the same newest .tgz emits digests whose {basename:sha256} map EQUALS the .py''s output for that archive (A/B parity on one real archive); test block green. THEN rewire profile-restore-drill.ps1 to call the kit verb over ssh instead of scp+python. ONLY AFTER a scheduled run PASSes with the kit verb: archive profile-restore-drill-node.py to the node (archive-never-delete) and drop it from commit-suggestion.md. Until then the .py STAYS -- load-bearing for the live 05:40 drill.\n\nGATES: box compile of the kit package needs a quiet window (window-coordination). SHARED PRIMITIVE: \"inspect a tar (count entries, hash/verify members)\" is also what KIT-ARCHIVE-OFFBOX-MIRROR''s dir-mirror verify (size + tar-count) wants -- one tar-inspect primitive serves both. Ties PS1-TO-SPIRAL.")
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_port_2 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT", 2u32, "2026-11-03T23:22Z", "resilience", "11-03 19:15 resilience groom-refresh (was stale since 11-01; keeping, not closing). STILL LIVE: profile-restore-drill-node.py (937B) is still untracked spiral-first drift, and profile-restore-drill.ps1 still scp's+runs it - confirmed in active use (I edited that .ps1's ssh ConnectTimeout 8->12 TODAY under box-starvation). Next step unchanged + grounded: teach archive_deflate_domain to decompress .tgz via tar.exe/bsdtar when gzip is absent (node has no gzip; PREFERRED fix - also helps the box), then assemble the kit verb from archive_extract_generic + crypto.sha256 + the typed member_digest/scan union. Box-gated (kit build). Owner team:resilience.")
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_port_3 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT", 3u32, "2026-11-05T04:42Z", "resilience", "STALE-CHECK (resilience): the item says port profile-restore-drill-node.py to a kit verb, but scripts/ now has ZERO .py files (62 files, all .ps1) - profile-restore-drill-node is already .ps1, not .py. So the .py->port framing is outdated; either the .py was already ported to .ps1 or lost in the 10-28 wipe. Re-scope: decide whether profile-restore-drill-node.ps1 should become a kit verb (reusing archive_deflate_domain extract + crypto.sha256 per the original intent) or stay as thin glue; the .py-porting part is moot. resilience.")
inl note_of_profile_restore_drill_port_4 () = Note ("PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL-PORT", 4u32, "2026-11-05T22:01Z", "resilience-614162e5", "11-05 ~13:5x resilience PREMISE STALE - the .py drift is ALREADY RESOLVED (tree reality-check). This item was filed to port profile-restore-drill-node.py off the repo (spiral-first drift) + archive the .py. CURRENT STATE: there is NO .py - i574n.github/scripts has 0 .py files; profile-restore-drill-node.ps1 is SELF-CONTAINED pwsh (grep: zero python/.py/tarfile refs), so the drill logic was reimplemented pure-pwsh (no python shell-out, which also sidesteps note-1 blocker: node has no gzip). The drill is HEALTHY: profile-restore-drill task Last 11-05 05:40 Result=0, daily, Next 11-06 05:40.\nSO: the URGENT half (remove the .py spiral-first drift + keep the restore drill working) is DONE. The .py no longer exists to archive. REMAINING = only the lower-value quality goal: port the pwsh logic into a kit Spiral verb (reuse archive_deflate_domain extract + crypto.sha256 per the design), which stays P3, kit-tree, and still carries note-1 node-env blockers (node has no kit on PATH, kit .tgz path shells to absent gzip). Recommend: drop the drift-urgency framing; this is now a pure spiral-first quality port, not a drift fix. Dep PROFILE-RESTORE-DRILL already Done. resilience-614162e5.")
inl cells_plot_export () = Task ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", "Cells' HTML export renders plots and animations at least as well as the pre-vibecode dib notebooks did: F# plotting produced an SVG shown in the VS Code cell and in the exported HTML (lib physics); Cells has code coloring dib lacked but no plots. Reproduce the ~Nov 2025 polyglot state minimally (just enough to export the physics HTML), then make the Cells exporter render plot outputs inline and the guitar-string example as an animation (scroller, GIF or web video) instead of stacked frames", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "cells,html,plots,lib,physics,main,team:main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_plot_export () = Planning ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:34Z", "main", "main 10:3x (user 11-01 10:3x). DoD: (1) a minimal checkout of polyglot at its Nov-2025 state (sparse/shallow, under 500 MB) exports the physics notebook to HTML with its SVG plots, kept as the reference artifact; (2) Cells' export of lib/spiral/physics.spi shows the same plots inline (SVG, no screenshots) plus code coloring; (3) the guitar string renders as one animated element, not stacked frames; (4) a side-by-side page in dir-tree-html. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a cell output as a union (Text | Svg of svg_doc | Animation of frame list * fps | Table of typed rows), with plot specs as typed records (axes, series), not raw SVG strings assembled by hand. NEXT STEP: find polyglot's Nov-2025 commit with the physics notebook and its plotting code (git log in C:\\home\\git\\polyglot), and list the plot functions physics.spi calls today.")
inl note_of_cells_plot_export_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PLOT-EXPORT", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:40Z", "main", "main 10:4x STEP 1 DONE, cheaper than planned: the reference export already exists in polyglot's git history, so no Nov-2025 rebuild is needed for the reference. 'git -C C:\\home\\git\\polyglot show 706e6beb~1:lib/spiral/physics.dib.html' (2025-01-13, the last version before the deploy commit 706e6beb deleted it) is 2,612,633 bytes with 82 inline <svg>, 101 data:image embeds and plotting scripts (plotly/vega references). The plotting code lives in polyglot lib/fsharp/Plotting.dib (F#) and apps/plot (a Rust plot crate: plot.rs, lib.rs). REVISED NEXT STEP: diff that page's per-cell outputs against Cells' current export of lib/spiral/physics.spi to list the missing output kinds (inline SVG, frame sequences), then port Plotting.dib's plot spec to a typed Spiral module (the output union in this item's plan) rendered by Cells' html.ex. The DoD's polyglot checkout is still needed only if ERL-VS-DIB-BENCH wants live dib timings.")
