inl note_of_x_sota_model_84 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 84u32, "2026-11-05T09:51Z", "x", "2026-11-05 05:51 x: x-next7c's LAND is WAITING, not failed. Its lib step (date_time ECE2A9DD6806) passed the new round-trip precheck at 05:42, then lib_land_window waits for LIVE READERS: main's notebook gate on apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi (since 04:58, about 2 h of window left) compiles against the live lib. The wait is 30 min, then it throws (about 06:12) with nothing applied. CORRECTION: tonight's earlier land stalls were this same reader wait, not the RAM floor I blamed (main added -MinFreeMb anyway; harmless). Asked main for a gap or a per-file reader check. The levers run waits for this land (overlapping generated Rust).")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_85 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 85u32, "2026-11-05T10:09Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:09 x: x-next7 LANDED (green run x-next7c): lib date_time ECE2A9DD6806 via lib_land_window (closed green, document_test 26/26, undo 20261105-055129; it first waited behind main's replay.spi reader); the x files landed, including the join-point fix (simframes 835CC894AF9B, sim_progress 5131B6D893A3), envoy manifests (frames gleam.toml 4811C1FFBCF0, manifest.toml FE8F552066A8), the X-NO-COMMENTS heal (posts 1D3DBF4AE0C2, run_signals, sim_publish, digest, prelude), lambda parens, the heading strip and requests; x/postability/tlds.txt removed (byte-identical to spiral apps/cells/data/tlds.txt). node-proof applied 27 generated outputs; 1 conflict, apps/client/README.md, correctly LEFT at the land's MIGRATE-TXT-FILES draft (F6BA371E172E, the new tlds path); the run's copy was the pre-migration README, because the node mirror never had that draft. x's live tree now has 1 comment line left (timeline_serve.spi:9, which x-next9 replaces). NEXT: x-levers1 LAUNCHED (job-1793873376874, node, pack44 core 657DA4B173F9D3D3): splitter with the long_form fix, plus lever-2 mimalloc.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_86 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 86u32, "2026-11-05T12:14Z", "x", "2026-11-05 08:2x x: SLICE (reflection codecs, the smallest piece): sim invariants' rule names are DERIVED, not hand-mapped (memory nameof-not-string-mapping). invariants.spi drops demand_rule_name and the 6-arm rule_name match (12 lines); rule_name r = reflection::typed_case_name r |> reflection::typed_name_snake, so SequentialEquivalence reads sequential_equivalence and a renamed case renames its finding. The strings are a protocol (runner findings lines, all_held), so a new test rule_names_are_the_snake_case_of_their_cases pins all 6 literally, including breaking_edits_fail, which no test covered before. Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\x\\X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES\\invariants.spi 16705919CAF4 on live 95CD1AC6975C: cell budget 0 findings, round trip canonical + fixpoint + byte-exact, vultr --check exit 0 (pack44, live lib reflection.spi). --check does not run UnionCaseName codegen, so the rust + gleam tests ride x-next10 (its gate now runs invariants.spi besides sim_serve.spi; launch and land scripts updated and parse-checked; the dry run refuses only the expected sim_serve base, which x-next9 sets). Model status from the code today: platform prototype DONE (splitter.spi); open: post typestate, command GADT (cli.spi command is a plain union), invariant prototype, executor HKT, reflection codecs beyond names, iggy family.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_87 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 87u32, "2026-11-05T12:44Z", "x", "2026-11-05 09:1x x: GROOM of the target model against today's code, each part re-decided with its evidence. (1) POST TYPESTATE: DROPPED as written. Every post lifecycle in x is runtime-driven: scenario.spi draws edits from seeded randomness over a pool of rooted posts, sim_serve's writes come from requests, and final_state.spi folds a runtime event list (deleted : bool). A post s phantom can only guard code whose sequence is static, which in x is only test fixtures, so it would add ceremony without guarding a real path. The runtime stream stays nested unions (content | revision | reaction), as this item already said. (2) EXECUTOR HKT: MET without an HKT. executors.spi has executor = list string -> task_result, with fake_executor, leaking_executor and cells_executor as values, and runner_shell takes one. The pair-of-records indirection the model wanted gone is gone. An index \\* m. executor m would only add an effect index that every instance leaves unused, since all three are synchronous calls returning task_result. (3) INVARIANT PROTOTYPE: DROPPED in favour of the union plus derived names. The checks have different shapes (sequential_equivalence needs a baseline, commute takes two snapshots, the rest take one), so one ':? check i' signature cannot hold them without wrapping. The rule union already makes the finding list exhaustive, and its names are now derived by reflection (X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES, in x-next10). STILL OPEN: (4) command GADT, blocked: cli's command reaches xc's Rust main as the 15-field parsed_args tuple across a crate link, which is X-TYPED-UNITS' job, and that waits on TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 (Planned 0%); (5) reflection codecs beyond names (wire field lists); (6) iggy event family (LIB-IGGY-CLIENT). DONE: platform prototype (splitter.spi), auth phantom (sim_serve caller c), endpoint reads r / writes r (wire.spi).")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_88 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 88u32, "2026-11-05T13:31Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:2x x: GROOM (5) REFLECTION CODECS for wire: DROPPED, like the case-name arms in posts.spi. The wire.spi field lists map EXTERNAL protocol keys, and those differ by platform for the same field: X 'text', 'author_id', 'created_at' (wire.spi:279-298, 353); Mastodon 'content' (402); Bluesky 'createdAt' and app.bsky.feed.post (414-422). A codec derived from record field names would force record names to equal one platform's keys and still need per-platform maps for the others. Reflection stays where the names are x's own: the invariant rule names (X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES, in x-next10). (6) IGGY FAMILY: its dependency moved today. LIB-IGGY-CLIENT's M3 gap (Gleam rd_str_utf8 stub) is drafted (LIB-IGGY-GLEAM-UTF8 92B9E9D4CFB3, rust + gleam round trips plus a NotUtf8 test, in x-next10's lib gates). Once it lands, the sim's event stream can map onto the family. Open now: (4) command GADT (blocked on typed links) and (6) the sim-to-iggy mapping.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_89 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 89u32, "2026-11-05T14:23Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:3x x: CORRECTION, scope of my vultr --check claims today. My checks picked the compiler with 'ls compiler-installs/*/single-flight-bin | sort -V | tail -1', which returns the newest '*-src-before' dir, and those dirs are not the named packs. Measured cores: pack44-src-before ea36ca047fa29828, pack48-src-before 96df7d2a78a2469e, pack49-src-before dc49ffdc170199df (= vultr's installed core). None equals the box or node pack cores (pack44 657DA4B173F9D3D3, pack48/49 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3). So where my notes say 'vultr --check exit 0 on pack44' or 'on pack48', read 'on vultr's older installed compiler (core shown above)'. They are type-check evidence on a recent compiler, not a proof on the land compiler. The node runs (pinned compiler, core read at launch) remain the proof, unchanged.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_90 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 90u32, "2026-11-05T18:44Z", "x", "2026-11-05 14:4x x: X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES RED in x-next10 (job-1793894849167, node, pinned pack51 core E190545B5F30A7B4): invariants.spi 10/10 tests FAILED on rust, including the 9 tests that predate the change, so the module does not compile for rust. The error text did not survive (stdout keeps only the last notebook's tail; the Cells work dirs were cleaned). The same draft built and ran fine on GLEAM: the sim build (sim accept 0, 0 fixtures changed) and e2e (RUST-OK) both used it. Every other notebook in the run passed: sim_serve, timeline_serve 17/17, remote_chunks, sim_progress, sim_publish, xsim_split, feed_merge 6/6, run_signals 2/2, census 4/4. HYPOTHESIS: !!!!UnionCaseName (reflection.case_name) is proven on rust only for STATIC values. reflection.spi's own ///> rust test names constants (Contract |> case_name), while rule_name in invariants runs on dynamic values (the tests use := ~s = ... snapshots, and findings_text maps rule_name over runtime findings). DECISION: drop this draft from the land; the pre-registered rule says no red notebook lands. Because x-next10's generated Gleam was built with the draft, its outputs cannot land without it, so the x side goes to a rerun, x-next10b, without invariants. That rerun also measures whether the LIVE invariants (hand-mapped names) passes rust on pack51. NEXT for this slice: confirm the hypothesis with a one-test rust probe (case_name on a ~dynamic union value). If confirmed, it is a compiler gap to file (UnionCaseName on a dynamic union in Rust); if not, find the real rust error. Until then, the hand-mapped rule_name stays.")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_91 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 91u32, "2026-11-05T19:46Z", "x", "2026-11-05 15:3x x: (6) iggy family dependency moved: LIB-IGGY-CLIENT's Gleam UTF-8 decode is LANDED (iggy.spi 92B9E9D4CFB3, 7/7 rust + gleam). (5)/names: X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES stays OUT; its red was the pre-existing SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH, not the draft (the live and HEAD invariants fail the same 9/9 in a scratch tree).")
inl note_of_x_sota_model_92 () = Note ("X-SOTA-MODEL", 92u32, "2026-11-06T00:24Z", "x", "2026-11-05 20:1x x: X-SOTA-INVARIANT-NAMES LANDED (green run x-next11, job-1793917404429, node, pinned pack52 core A688EE5AD426A5A0): sim invariants.spi 95CD1AC6975C -> 16705919CAF4. rule_name is derived (reflection::typed_case_name |> typed_name_snake); the 12-line hand-written demand_rule_name / rule_name match is gone; the new test pins all 6 protocol names. node-proof applied 38 generated outputs, 0 conflicts, 95 unchanged. Evidence: sim accept 0, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK, census SAME over 82 files with 0 cells over one post, invariants notebook 10/10 on rust + gleam (green now that SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH's Cells fix landed at 17:11; it was 0/9 for every version before). Model parts: (names) DONE; still open: command GADT (blocked on typed links) and the sim-to-iggy mapping (its codec dependency LIB-IGGY-CLIENT Gleam decode landed today).")
inl fiscal_generic_provable () = Task ("FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE", "fiscal fully generic + provable: one generator over any downloadable schema set (no per-country code), generated units reusing lib/shared closures, one generic law suite over every generated family", Epic, P0, D8, 0u32, Planned, "FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND", "team:fiscal,fiscal,generic,proofs,typefeatures", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_generic_provable () = Planning ("FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE", Minutes 2400u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_provable_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:40 fiscal: TARGET (user 11-01, via main: \"fiscal gotta both be super generic in generating all spi code from downloadable canon schemas, and using these generated files to build a provable [system]\"). (A) ONE generator that takes ANY downloadable schema set (XSD closure, UBL, Peppol/PINT, national) as DATA, with no per-country Spiral code: a family is a row of a manifest (source URL + pin, root element, documents), not a hand-written family_root function. (B) Generated units that reuse lib/core and shared closure modules instead of re-emitting helpers and shared types. (C) Proofs over the generated types: laws checked for every family by one generic test, not per-family tests.\nMEASURED TODAY (11-01): src/generator.spi has 42 of 85 defs / 489 of 1,055 lines (46%) per-country (the 20 family literals, family_roots 33 lines, nfe_events, unit_checks_of''s NF-e branch); src/corpus_checks.spi has 21 of 59 defs / 551 of 805 lines (68%) of region-specific rule pins; scripts/init.ps1 (773 lines) is per-source download code; scripts/family-gates.ps1 repeats 27 module -> schema rows the generator already holds. Generated: about 453,000 of 954,000 lines (48%) are top-level definitions repeated byte for byte across units (shared DFA pattern functions in 14-16 units, whole UBL/CT-e record types in 6 units); 43-44 units each re-emit sample_path, insert and nth, which lib has (file_system.find_parent, am''.sort, listm''.try_item).\nDONE WHEN (measurable): (1) per-country lines in generator.spi = 0 (families come from a manifest file read by the generator; one Spiral module per schema-system kind: xsd, json-schema); (2) repeated generated lines < 5% (FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES: shared closure modules); (3) 0 emitted helpers that lib has (FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB); (4) one generic law suite runs for every generated family and passes: of_xml (to_xml x) = x on the example and on every real document; to_xml is idempotent through a re-read; every validated nominal refuses a value outside its facets; the example validates against the official schema. Each law is a prototype-polymorphic test over the codec prototype (XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES), written once.\nPLAN (children, in order): FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND (now 99%) -> XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES -> FISCAL-EMITTED-HELPERS-TO-LIB -> FISCAL-VERSIONED-FAMILIES -> family manifest (replaces the 20 family_root literals; filed as the next step of this epic) -> generic law suite -> FISCAL-CANON-MODEL bindings.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the manifest row is typed (\":| schema_system = | XsdSystem | JsonSchemaSystem | UblJsonSystem\"; source as a pinned record with a sha256 nominal), read once into \"list (exists s. family_root s)\" (the GADT of FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS pass 2). Laws are prototype-indexed tests (\"law_round_trip : xml_codec t => t -> bool\"), so a new family gets every law without new code. No strings for family identity: a family_id nominal.")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_provable_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:53 fiscal: THE TWO COUNTERS (so DONE WHEN (1) and (2) are re-runnable by anyone; pwsh, read-only).\n(1) PER-COUNTRY LINES in src/generator.spi: split top-level defs (a line starting \":=\", \":~\", \":&\", \":==\", \":|\" or \"test \" up to the next non-indented line); a def counts as per-country when its body matches  module_name = \"generated_|generated_\\w+_\\d|\"deps/corpus/(br|mx|cl|cr|es|pt|gr|hu|in|it|pl|my|pe|sa|tr|co|ro)|hacienda|cfdi|nfe_|ksef|fatturapa|facturae|verifactu|saft|mydata|nav_|gst_|chile|dte_  . 11-01: 42 of 85 defs, 489 of 1,055 lines. Target 0 (families as manifest data).\n(2) REPEATED GENERATED LINES: over generated/**/*.spi except *_certificates, split top-level \"inl|let rec|and let|let <name>\" defs to the next non-indented line; key = name + sha1(body); repeated lines = sum over keys seen in >= 5 units of lines x (units - 1). 11-01: 453,477 of about 954,000 lines (48%). Target < 5%.\nBoth counters ran in the fiscal session 11-01 10:34-10:36; the first PS1 port of them is a Spiral metrics cell beside model_metrics (PS1-TO-SPIRAL rule: no new .ps1 tools).")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_provable_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:17Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 00:16 fiscal: GROOM 11-04 (last note 11-01): owner fiscal. Progress since: the CII D16B family needed 0 generator code (a family row only); Facturae, VeriFactu, FatturaPA and CR read real documents after the W3C xmldsig fix, except Facturae's XAdES QualifyingProperties (the ds:Object wildcard). NEXT: counter (1) = families generated from a row alone; counter (2) = real documents that read back; record both as a reports.spi section.")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_provable_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T06:59Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:59 fiscal: COUNTER (1) MEASURED on the catalog draft (families F1CF3DDF + generator 7C315FDB): 18 family_root definitions; family_extra has 3 cases (Signed, CfdiComplements, NfeModelChecks); the generator branches on an extra in exactly 2 places (has_extra Signed: the generic signature staging; has_extra NfeModelChecks: hand-written NF-e TESTS, not generation logic). So 18/18 families generate from their catalog row plus generic mechanisms (CII D16B, added 11-03, needed 0 generator lines), and 1/18 adds hand-written checks. Re-runnable: grep -c '^:= [a-z_0-9]+ () : family_root' families.spi; grep -n 'has_extra' generator.spi. COUNTER (2), real documents that read back, has new evidence: Facturae 10/10 on vultr with the decode drafts (FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE n21), CII D16B 15/15 (node, 11-03), MyInvois 22 XML + 22 JSON (11-01); a full tally comes with the next node regen.")
inl note_of_fiscal_generic_provable_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T12:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:19 fiscal: COUNTER (2) -- real documents that read back, PROVEN TONIGHT under the decode readers (vultr Rust read-back bodies, each failing on any drift): UBL Invoice 155 XML + 22 JSON (PEPPOL, CEN, MyInvois, SUNAT, Turkey, Saudi Arabia, Colombia, Romania), UBL CreditNote 21, Facturae 10 signed (XAdES kept), CII D16B 15 CEN examples; plus example round trips for NF-e, VeriFactu, FatturaPA, CR Factura 4.4. Total real documents read back unchanged: 223 across 4 families in 2 syntaxes. Not yet re-run under decode: UBL DebitNote 18, ApplicationResponse 14, DespatchAdvice 5, ReceiptAdvice 4 (they read back on the 11-03 codec state); the node's full decode regen gates them all. Counter (1) stays 18/18 families from catalog rows.")
