inl note_of_fiscal_family_manifest_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:37Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-01 10:45 fiscal: CHILD of FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE (step \"family manifest\"). TODAY: 20 hand-written family_root literal functions in src/generator.spi (cfdi_v4_0, nfe_v4_00, ubl_document_2_1, hacienda_document, ... ; 489 per-country lines) plus a parallel 27-row table in scripts/family-gates.ps1 and per-source download blocks in scripts/init.ps1.\nDONE WHEN: one typed manifest (src/families.toml or a Spiral data module) lists every family as data: schema system, pinned source (URL + sha256), root element/type, namespace, documents, preload/resolve flags; the generator reads it and contains 0 per-country lines (the measurement counter of the epic); family-gates.ps1 and the per-family init.ps1 blocks are generated from or replaced by it; the regenerated units are byte-identical to today''s (0 generated drift).\nNEXT STEP: after FISCAL-EDITION3-ROUND, write the manifest for the 20 families from the literals (each literal field becomes a manifest field), add a reader, and prove 0 drift by regenerating.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: rows parse once into \"list (exists s. family_root s)\" (indexed by schema system, FISCAL-TYPEFEATURESET-METRICS pass 2); a pinned source is \":== pinned = { url : string; sha256 : digest }\" with \":! digest = string\" built only by a hex validator; per-family traits stay the family_extra union; nothing in the generator matches on a family name.")
inl note_of_fiscal_family_manifest_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:15Z", "fiscal", "groom 11-01 19:1x SPLIT (480 min): S1 (about 2 h): the typed manifest record \":== family_row\" (root schema, catalog, documents, extras : list family_extra, signature, unit name) read from one JSON file through json_schema, with 3 families moved (cfdi_v4_0, ubl_invoice_2_1, ksef_fa_3) and per-family regeneration 0 diff. S2 (about 2 h): the other 17 families move; the generator's 20 literals are deleted; the per-country line count from the FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE counter drops (it was 489 of 1,055 lines). S3: family-gates.ps1 rows are derived from the manifest (no duplicated 27-row table). DONE per step = its gate + 0 regeneration diff.")
inl note_of_fiscal_family_manifest_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST", 3u32, "2026-11-03T12:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 08:01 fiscal: S1+S2 MOVE DONE IN THE TREE (unstaged), proof queued. The family data is now a Spiral data module: src/families.spi holds schema_source, family_extra, has_extra, module_id/module_text, family_root, root_type_name, all 20 family literals and lists (cfdi..gst) and the manifest_documents helpers (lines 60-488 of generator.spi moved verbatim, 417 non-blank lines), plus test every_family_has_its_own_module_name (all lists concatenated; no two families write the same unit). src/generator.spi opens families and keeps 0 per-country lines (984 -> 591 non-blank). Both registered in package.spiproj and spiral.toml after generated_runtime. Type-checked on idle vultr in seconds (pack24; families and generator exit 0; an injected ill-typed definition in families exits 5). PROOF queued: job-1793707217418-fiscal-families-move (t1101, after the group_part proof; pinned compiler): families 1/1, generator 23/23, and a full regen compared with the committed 741c715 generated/ manifest (164 files), PREDICTION 0 differ. The typed-manifest step (TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: rows as 'list (exists s. family_root s)' indexed by schema system, pinned sources with a digest nominal) builds on this module.")
inl note_of_fiscal_family_manifest_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST", 4u32, "2026-11-03T20:12Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:12 fiscal: MOVE PROVEN OUTPUT-IDENTICAL: job-1793707217418-fiscal-families-move (t1101, pinned compiler core 7C49B7A6AFC05D2C start and end): families 3/3 (every_family_has_its_own_module_name, every_regime_lists_its_own_families 16/6/1, a_ubl_family_takes_no_brazilian_access_key fails Unification), generator 23/23, format 82 units 0 failed, regenerated output vs the committed 741c715 manifest: 164 files, 0 differ, 0 extra. So the 20 families and their types live in src/families.spi with 0 per-country generator lines and no generated byte changes; it also shows the pack change (this core differs from the one 741c715 was generated with) leaves generated output unchanged. On top (also unstaged): pt_saft documents = [ the SAF-T sample ] with the FISCAL-PT-SAFT landing, and the regime-index test lines wrapped to 120 columns (vultr --check with bodies exit 0, negative exit 5).")
inl note_of_fiscal_family_manifest_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:10Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:10 fiscal: THE DUPLICATION BIT: scripts/family-gates.ps1 still carries its own family table (16 DFe rows, CFDI, UBL loop, FatturaPA/KSeF regimes, the 'resolved' map), and it preloaded SEFAZ's restricted xmldsig (DFe.NET/CTe xmldsig-core-schema_v1.01.xsd, Algorithm fixed to rsa-sha1) for the Mexican, Costa Rican, Facturae, VeriFactu, myDATA and FatturaPA examples -- the same defect fixed in families.spi on 11-03 (FISCAL-ES-FACTURAE), living on in the second copy. FIXED in place (family-gates.ps1 B952056F, backup in the session scratchpad): both preloads now use the full W3C schema eu/ubl21/common/UBL-xmldsig-core-schema-2.1.xsd. Before/after on the box's samples: 15 documents each, the same 2 with messages, no new or lost finding. PRE-EXISTING example defects surfaced by the same run (generator-side, not this change): generated_fatturapa_1_2_3_example.xml contains a NUL (0x00) at line 1 pos 246 (plus an invalid child), generated_ksef_fa_3_example.xml writes P_1 = '0000-00-00'. REMAINING 5% (the fix for the class): the generator writes the gate rows from the catalog (example, schema_path relative to root, catalog locals as preloads, resolve flag) into target/ci-metrics/family-gates.tsv, and family-gates.ps1 iterates it, so no per-family path lives outside families.spi.")
inl note_of_fiscal_family_manifest_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST", 6u32, "2026-11-04T11:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:11 fiscal: CORRECTION to n5's 'pre-existing example defects': both are STALE SAMPLES, not live defects. The box's samples/generated_fatturapa_1_2_3_example.xml and generated_ksef_fa_3_example.xml date from 10-25; the NUL came from a \\p{IsBasicLatin} class picking U+0000, fixed in lib xsd_regex on 10-27 (spiral 3f1b7588, test broad_classes_pick_a_printable_example: (0,127) -> 'A'); today's emitter has no '0000-00-00' literal either. A fresh build regenerates both; nothing to fix.")
inl showcases_spiral_vs_rust () = Task ("SHOWCASES-SPIRAL-VS-RUST", "Bring the browser session's six compiled Spiral-vs-Rust showcases into the spiral repo as reproducible samples, each with the best stable-Rust attempt and its real rustc error: GADT rules interpreted away (S1), policies with hidden stages (S2), one rule as validation/simulation/audit via HKT (S3), type-level decimal scales (S4), audit diffs by reflection (S5), one fiscal kernel emitted to 6 languages (S6); S7 (post-CIC proofs) stays vision", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "samples,showcase,rust,typefeatureset,main,team:main", "current", "current")
