inl note_of_formatter_parens_misses_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-PARENS-MISSES", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. DOD: a table shape -> sites per repo, produced by a kit command reading the compiler token stream (paren pair whose removal leaves the same parse tree, checked by re-parsing), plus for each shape with 0 parse-tree changes over the corpus a formatter rule that removes it, proven by format-corpus round trip and an identical generated-output hash on the matrix. NEXT STEP: run the parse-tree-equality check over lib/spiral first (no compile needed: parse only, CPU-light). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: ParenShape = Atom | TailLambda | TailApply | TupleInTuple | PipeOperand | Annotated (needs parens, kept) as a union; the safe set is a value of the union, not a list of strings.")
inl spiral_nameof () = Task ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", "A nameof stronger than F#: nameof of a union case, record field, function, module path and type, plus a derived case-name printer and parser per union (no hand-written enum->string match), usable in macros and on every backend", Feature, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,typefeatureset,language,codegen", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_nameof () = Planning ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. Better than F#: F# nameof is only an identifier; ours also yields (1) the full case table of a union as a compile-time list (cases_of), (2) a total to_name / of_name pair derived per union, of_name returning an option, (3) qualified names (module::case) and (4) a stable rename-safe name checked by the formatter. DOD: a sample nameof_cases whose test block asserts to_name/of_name round-trip on a 5-case union on all ///> backends, and peval folds nameof to a string literal (grep the generated Rust: no match arm for the printer when the case is static). NEXT STEP: census the existing hand mappings (SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL) to pick the API shape from real call sites, then a prototype op in the Infer section. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: nameof returns a phantom-tagged name (name t), not a bare string, so names of different types do not mix; of_name returns option t, never -1 or a default case; the case table is a GADT-indexed list so its length is known at compile time.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:38 compiler: lane-map placement: theme language/typefeatureset, after SPELLING-PROFILES in the compiler queue; SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL census runs first (CPU-light) to shape the API from real call sites.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:47Z", "main", "main 17:4x RAISED P1 -> P0 (user 11-01 17:4x: 'lanes are still writing non granular code ... also writing functions to map strings to types instead of nameof, we gotta prioritize that'). Compiler: this ships before more enum<->string code accumulates. SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL's detector runs right after it.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 4u32, "2026-11-01T21:56Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 (consumer evidence): (1) fiscal src/canon.spi ubl_document_name maps UblInvoice -> \"ubl-invoice\" by hand; with union-case nameof it becomes kebab(nameof d). (2) DESIGN INPUT: generated XSD enum unions cannot derive their printer/parser from case names. XSD values are not identifiers (\"01\", \"00\", \"Brasil\" vs \"BRASIL\", which collide under case folding in Pascal) and case names are sanitized (\"TEnderEmi_xPais_BRASIL\"), so the derived printer needs a per-case value attribute (an annotated literal), with nameof as the default when absent. Otherwise every generated unit keeps its hand-emitted x_..._to_string / _of_string matches.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 5u32, "2026-11-01T21:59Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:00 compiler: CENSUS (the n1 next step; tracked .spi/.spir outside deps, samples, target, backlog and generated). Detector: a match arm whose case name and string literal are the same word after case/underscore/hyphen folding. to_name arm `| Case => \"case\"`, of_name arm `| \"case\" => [Some] Case`. RESULTS (to_name / of_name / files): kit 160 / 0 / 30 (src/kit_exec_metrics/metrics.spi 13, kit_standards/rules.spi 7, kit_do_program/compiled.spi 3, ...); x 15 / 6 / 4 (apps/sim/spi/invariants.spi 5/6, personas.spi 4, apps/client/posts.spi 5, wire.spi 1); tibia 11 / 0 / 3 (apps/host/arena_host.spi 5, apps/suite/suite.spi 5, arena/competitor.spi 1); fiscal 10 / 0 / 2 (src/lifecycle.spi 8, canon.spi 2; generated units excluded, they are XSD-emitted); dice 9 / 0 / 2 (ui/src/components/menu_tabs.spi 8); spiral 3 / 2 / 4 (lib async.spi, xsd_regex.spi, cli_args.spi, apps/spiral/spiral.spi 0/2; apps/cells/spi/targets.spi has 9 exact-name arms on top). TOTAL about 208 to_name arms and 8 of_name arms. API SHAPE FROM THE SITES: printing dominates, about 26 to 1. Most sites print lower or snake case, not the exact case name, so a name STYLE is part of the API. EXISTING PIECES in lib reflection.spi: union_try_pick (of_name; accepts the exact or lowercased key; option), union_to_string (to_name, but only cuda/rust/typescript tests, and string-split based), get_union_fields_untag (the compile-time case table as (string * t) list). PLAN (smallest total, portable cut first): (1) lib `case_name \\* t. (style : name_style) (x : t) : string` for payload-free unions, a fold over get_union_fields_untag whose comparisons peval folds to a literal when x is static; name_style = Exact | Lower | Snake | Kebab is a union, never a string flag. Plus `case_of_name \\* t. (style) (text : string) : option t`, a total parse returning an option, never a default case. (2) the compiler op (n1: phantom-tagged name t, GADT case table) replaces the fold for payload unions and emits one match per backend. HEAL ORDER after (1) lands: kit's 30 files first (160 arms). Each site becomes `case_name Snake x`, and the detector (this regex as a kit command) runs in the gates so new arms cannot appear.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 6u32, "2026-11-01T22:57Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 18:4x tibia: INTERIM, so no more hand tables accumulate before this ships: lib case_labels.spi LANDED 18:43 (9EFC57121E95). case_label prefix separator x and case_of_label prefix separator label derive a union's labels from its case names via reflection::get_union_fields_untag (PascalCase -> separator-joined lower case, optional prefix strip). No string table is written by hand. Proven lua + rust (Vultr gate, mutant caught). tibia uses it in apps/suite/suite.spi (backend_name, status_name, memo_name, budget_kind_name/_of: 23 hand-mapped lines removed) and results/arena_rows.spi (competitor_of, monster_of: 12 removed). When SPIRAL-NAMEOF's derived to_name/of_name land, case_labels should become thin wrappers or be retired: its callers pass only a prefix and a separator, which is the API shape real call sites needed (input for SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 7u32, "2026-11-01T23:07Z", "main", "main 19:2x (user 11-01 19:1x: 'we're using nameof in reflection now, but that's an workaround, we gotta check later how to change the compiler itself, to get an even better result than what the fsharp compiler has, search for user input history or tasks when i mentioned about this'). This item IS that task (its title: 'a nameof stronger than F#'). The lanes' interim is lib reflection (nameof for record fields, union_to_string/union_try_pick for cases: tibia, kit today). The compiler version should make those library calls unnecessary. Design input from fiscal: generated XSD enum maps need a per-case VALUE attribute (values like '01' and 'Brasil'/'BRASIL' aren't distinct identifiers), so the derived printer/parser takes an optional per-case label.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 8u32, "2026-11-01T23:09Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:16 compiler: GROOM split. The portable lib cut (exact case names, payload-free unions) moved to SPIRAL-NAMEOF-LIB-CUT (120m). This item is now the compiler op only (re-estimated to 240m): a phantom-tagged name t, name styles (Exact | Lower | Snake | Kebab, applied at compile time), payload unions, and peval folding to a literal. DoD unchanged (n1 sample nameof_cases).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 9u32, "2026-11-03T07:30Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (32 h). Next: the compiler op slice 1, nameof on a payload-free union case folding to a literal in peval, with sample nameof_cases (n1 DoD).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 10u32, "2026-11-03T11:48Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:0x compiler: DoD MEASURED AGAINST TODAY'S LIB, and both checks are already met by lib reflection (no new compiler op needed for them). (1) Round trip: a 5-case union (Alpha..Epsilon) through reflection::case_name -> case_of_name, plus case_name -> \"Delta\" and of_name \"epsilon\" -> None, on rust, gleam, lua, typescript and fsharp: box lib gate 12/12 tests, 0 failed targets, 0 not_run (cuda lines stripped: the cuda runner crashes on the node, access violation, as does the node's stale-runner lua). (2) Static fold: reflection::case_name Gamma compiles to 534 bytes of Rust with 0 case literals and 1 match arm (the whole length folds to a constant); a dynamic case emits the printer (5 literals, 23 arms), as expected. Landing the test block nameof_cases_round_trip into lib reflection.spi (job compiler-lib-land-nameof, base 6EA85EE1CBD0F2F2). Left on this item beyond its DoD: the typefeatureset extras (a phantom-tagged name t instead of string, name styles, qualified module::case names); I propose closing on the DoD and filing those as SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF", 11u32, "2026-11-03T12:14Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:1x compiler: DONE on the DoD. The test block nameof_cases_round_trip (5-case union nameof_probe through reflection::case_name / case_of_name, plus an unknown name -> None) LANDED in lib reflection.spi (closed green: document_test 22 passed, type_probe 12 typed tests; reflection.spi EA0F566D6A274B80; undo 20261103-080849; the first land attempt was undone for a missing final newline, landed from lib_roundtrip's canonical form). Static fold measured: reflection::case_name Gamma compiles to 534 bytes of Rust with no case literal. The typed extras (phantom name t, name styles, module::case) move to SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED.")
