inl edition3_main_symbol () = Task ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", "Edition-3 symbol for the program entry instead of the English name main: pick :> (mirrors :< open; flows out), lexed as the entry declaration, plus a census of every other hardcoded English word the compiler requires", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "EDITION3-SYMBOLS-MIGRATION", "team:compiler,edition3,language,lexer,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_edition3_main_symbol () = Planning ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_edition3_main_symbol_1 () = Note ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. PICK: :> for the entry (one operator token, like :#; 0 uses expected, the DOD checks it). CENSUS (step 1, recorded here): words the compiler hardcodes beyond keywords: main (entry lookup), test (done, :#), and the names it resolves by string in core/prelude (e.g. failwith, true/false, unit, the numeric type names); each gets a decision symbol/keep with a reason. DOD: :> lexes and the entry resolves through it on every backend (a sample entry_symbol with ///> on all backends), format --spelling symbols rewrites := main to :> and back (round trip byte-identical), and the census table is on this item. NEXT STEP: grep the lexer and the entry lookup (main string) in spiral_compiler.fs, and count :> uses in all repos. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: entry is a union EntryDecl = Named of name | Symbol, resolved once; no string comparison to main after the parser.")
inl note_of_edition3_main_symbol_2 () = Note ("EDITION3-MAIN-SYMBOL", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:43Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:43 compiler, STEP 1 READ (CPU-light): (a) collision check for :> in all repos *.spi: 3 hits, all inside macro text emitting F# upcasts (lib/spiral/common.spi:24 $!x :> `u, mega_omniledger_erp_kernel/main.spi:11832-11833 inside a backend string), 0 as a Spiral token, so a column-0 :> is free. (b) the compiler finds the entry by the string main in 4 places in spiral_compiler.fs: 24852 (C: main is never static), 27155 (C++ host ArgsCppHost main), 35017 and 35086 (entry resolution via Map.tryFind main env.term, per backend). PLAN: same route as :# (lexed to TokVar test): the parser turns a column-0 :> definition into EntryDecl.Symbol and binds it under the internal entry name once, so those 4 sites read the EntryDecl and no longer compare strings; := main stays valid (EntryDecl.Named) for edition 2. Next: draft that as a .kitdo in apps/compiler/drafts plus the sample entry_symbol.")
inl spiral_nameof_heal () = Task ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", "Mechanical detector of enum->string mapping spam (match arms whose bodies are only the case name as a literal) across every repo, reported periodically like the Nil->[] heal, with each site rewritten to nameof once SPIRAL-NAMEOF ships", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-NAMEOF", "team:compiler,compiler,heal,census,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_nameof_heal () = Planning ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. DOD: a kit command (kit heal nameof, Spiral, not .ps1) that lists every match whose arms map N>=3 nullary cases to string literals equal (case-insensitively) to the case name, with repo/file/line and a count per repo; run once on spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice, alphabet, recorded here; zero false positives on a hand-checked sample of 20. NEXT STEP: write the detector over the compiler tokens command output (lexemes), no regex over source text. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a finding is a record { site : site; cases : list case_name; kind : HealKind } with HealKind = NameMapping | ReverseMapping | Partial, never a string kind.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:47Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:46 compiler, DESIGN FINDING from a first regex probe: exact equality (| Foo => \"Foo\") finds 0 arms in spiral, yet lib has the spam in other shapes: json_schema.spi:112 and :455 | JsonNull => \"null\" (type prefix stripped and lowercased, mapping written twice in one file), async.spi:411 | Error _ => \"error\" (payload ignored). So the detector must normalize the case name before comparing: strip the union-name prefix, case-fold, and accept snake/kebab joins, and count payload-ignoring arms (Case _) too. Duplicated mappings of one union across files are the strongest heal signal. The probe was a regex over text, a throwaway; the DOD detector stays token-based (kit heal nameof).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:54Z", "x", "2026-11-01 17:54 x: x's AUDIT of its last day's diffs (user 17:4x). Multi-line host macros: 0. Case<->string mappings: 12 functions, triaged.\n- TRUE nameof case (1): Cells C4 draft daemon.spi request_line, where Hello/Status/Pool/Retire become \"hello\"/\"status\"/\"pool\"/\"retire\" (the lowercased case names). It switches to the derived printer when SPIRAL-NAMEOF ships. The draft is in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CELLS-IN-SPIRAL-C4, not landed yet.\n- NEAR-name, a wire/log vocabulary (2): x sim_serve.spi:269 caller_word (AppBearer -> \"app\", ...) and sim_run.spi:180 status_word (Done -> \"ok\", ...). Both feed request-log/outcome rows that tests compare byte for byte. They become derivable only if the cases are renamed to their words, so it's a decision for the detector's rules.\n- WIRE ENCODINGS, not names (9): Cells cell.spi main_text (\"0\"/\"1\"/\"2\", read by cell.ex/notebook.ex), shown_of (\"1\"), run_output_text ('0\\n'/'1\\n' prefixes), directives.spi timeout_text (\"-\"), daemon.spi wait_text/wait_of (\"-1\"), retiring_text/retiring_of (\"false\"), free_text (\"-\"). Each mirrors an existing Elixir or daemon protocol, so a nameof printer can't produce them. They go away when the Elixir readers are ported (CELLS-IN-SPIRAL C5+), not through nameof.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 4u32, "2026-11-01T21:59Z", "compiler", "11-01 18:00 compiler: census done; numbers, method and heal order recorded on SPIRAL-NAMEOF n5 (one record per fact). Detector regex: to_name '\\|\\s*([A-Z]\\w*)\\s*(?:\\w+\\s*)?=>\\s*\"([\\w\\-]+)\"' and of_name '\\|\\s*\"([\\w\\-]+)\"\\s*=>\\s*(?:Some\\s+)?([A-Z]\\w*)', keeping only pairs equal after removing _ and - and lowercasing. About 208 + 8 arms in 47 files; kit holds 160.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 5u32, "2026-11-03T12:40Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:4x compiler: DETECTOR BUILT AND RUN. lib nameof_heal.spi (token-based, no regex over source): parses SpiralCompiler tokens rows (line, from, nearTo, class) into typed token records, groups them by line in one pass (join point over the token array, no per-line rescans), matches arm shapes on the token list (| Case => \"lit\", | Case _ => \"lit\", | \"lit\" => Case, | \"lit\" => Some Case; same-length shapes tried in order inside one case, after a first draft lost the OfName shapes to an earlier same-length pattern), compares case and literal after lowercasing and dropping _ and -, and reports runs of >=3 consecutive same-kind arms as finding records { kind : ToName | OfName; first_line; arms; cases : list string }. Node gate 1/1 on rust + gleam vs the box lib tree, round trip canonical. Landing queued (job compiler-lib-land-heal: nameof_heal.spi new + package.spiproj F2B334FD -> 8FB24F8A). CENSUS (git-tracked hand-written .spi of spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice, alphabet; samples/state/deps skipped; 163 pre-filtered files, tokens via the installed compiler): 30 findings, 144 arms. kit 20 findings / 108 arms / 13 files (largest: kit_adoption_habits 17 arms, command_spec_domain and toolchain receipt 8 each, window_model 9), x 4 / 13, spiral 3 / 12 (cells daemon request_line, lib metrics suite_label + suite_of), dice 2 / 8 (menu_tabs twice), tibia 1 / 3, fiscal 0, alphabet 0. Kinds: ToName 28, OfName 2. Hand check of 22 first arms: 0 false positives (all case -> lower/upper/kebab name, some with a -- flag prefix). Not yet caught by design: prefix-stripped names (BackendC => \"c\", JsonNull => \"null\"); kit_style_probes is untracked so it was skipped (probe_word, 19 arms, will count once committed). Left for the DoD: the kit command wiring (kit heal nameof: list files, run tokens, call nameof_heal::findings), which is kit's to land; then rewrite sites to reflection::case_name.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 6u32, "2026-11-03T12:50Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:5x compiler: nameof_heal LANDED (closed green: document_test 22 passed, type_probe 1 typed test; nameof_heal.spi BC4D16D71E48923D, package.spiproj 8FB24F8AD13A2580; undo 20261103-083954). First rewrite done in my own lane: lib metrics suite_label = sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name s) and suite_of = reflection::union_cases_find (suite_label s = name), replacing 2 hand maps of 4 arms each (node gate 14/14 rust + gleam; landing queued, job compiler-lib-land-metrics12). kit asked to wire kit heal nameof (its call); remaining sites per lane: kit 20, x 4, cells daemon 1, dice 2, tibia 1.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 7u32, "2026-11-04T04:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 00:1x compiler groom: stays Active (user 11-04 00:2x: Active = a note within 48 h). The lib side is landed (nameof_heal.spi, metrics rewrite). Next concrete step is kit's: wire kit heal nameof (list files, tokens, nameof_heal::findings). Then each lane rewrites its own sites (kit 20, x 4, cells daemon 1, dice 2, tibia 1).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 8u32, "2026-11-04T04:35Z", "kit", "11-04 00:4x kit: `kit heal nameof <dir>...` wired, unstaged and not yet built: the new crate kit_heal_nameof (heal.spi). Typed verb union HealNameof, read back by reflection. It walks .spi files, skipping target/.git/.cache/node_modules/deps/_build, runs `dotnet <SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL or the deployed single-flight dll> tokens <file>` per file through lib process, and feeds lib nameof_heal.findings. Output: one `nameof <file>:<line> to-name|of-name arms=N cases=A,B,C` line per finding, then per root `files= unreadable= findings= arms=`, then `kit heal nameof ok roots= arms=`. It exits 0 (a census, not a gate). Type-checked on vultr with pack31 (exit 0 in 6 s; an injected field error was rejected with ETY-RecordIndexFailed, exit 5). Registered as VerbHeal in direct_verbs with a help line, routed in kit_cli_model, link: in kit_cli_model and kit_cli, a Cargo dep, a workspace member and Cargo.lock. Next: rides TRAIN18, then the census on spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice and alphabet gets recorded here. Cost note: one dotnet start per file; `tokens --stdin` batching is the follow-up if a root takes minutes.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 9u32, "2026-11-04T05:31Z", "kit", "11-04 01:3x kit: kit's own sites. A local census with compiler's to-name regex (suffix matches counted) found 82 arms in 17 places. First rewrites, unstaged; vultr pack31 --check exit 0 as-is and test bodies:\n(1) kit_mirror drift_word = union_case_kebab \"\" drift. The case SameOnBoth -> Same, so \"same\" comes from the name; its 6 uses are in kit_mirror only, and the existing test pins \"same\".\n(2) kit_job_start_args start_flag_word = kit_flag_words.flag_word (union_case_suffix \"Start\" flag). All 9 cases prefixed Start*, with QuietStart -> StartQuiet and FrontStart -> StartFront, so --quiet and --front come from the names. New test start_flag_words_come_from_the_case_names pins all 9 words.\nSKIPPED (need a decision, not a mechanical rewrite): exec_metrics phase_word is snake_case (\"slot_wait\"), CBackend -> \"c\", machine-watch Healthy -> \"ok\" (an Ok case would clash with result), ci tools ToolRebar -> \"rebar3\" (spans 3 crates), payload cases (mirror state_word, task_query filters), and the GADT-indexed query_flag. Next batch after TRAIN19: field_rendering, todo content_label, kit_do_model query verbs, habits (17 arms).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 10u32, "2026-11-04T05:44Z", "kit", "11-04 01:5x PARKED out of TRAIN19: kit_heal_nameof generated 2120 lines (arms_from_21 = 1111) because lib nameof_heal's arm matchers are all `:=` and inline into each of arms_from's two push_arm calls. Proposed to compiler: push_arm, arm_of, to_name_arm, of_name_arm and named become `:~` (behaviour-identical, each emitted once). The crate and wiring are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL-parked-1104 (src + wired copies). They come back when the lib change lands. kit's own rewrites (kit_mirror drift_word, kit_job_start_args flags) stay in the tree; they don't depend on the heal crate.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 11u32, "2026-11-04T06:01Z", "compiler", "11-04 01:5x compiler: LIB FIX LANDED for kit's crate gate (kit 11-04: kit heal nameof stopped TRAIN18; heal.rs was 2120 lines, arms_from_21 alone 1111, because everything arms_from reaches was := and inlined). named, to_name_arm, of_name_arm, arm_of and push_arm became :~ (emitted once, called by name), behaviour-identical. Proof on box, installed pack33, a Rust consumer counting findings over the fixture: 1,620 -> 861 lines, arms_from 1,111 -> under 86 (largest now arm_of 111); both builds exit 2 under rustc -O. Lib land window closed green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe pass, 0 respell-drift. nameof_heal.spi BC4D16D7 -> 0CA4C9B0, lib digest 67ABD08F69EA1D44, undo 20261104-015609. kit un-parks its crate (drafts kit SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL-parked-1104) for TRAIN19.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 12u32, "2026-11-04T06:36Z", "kit", "11-04 02:2x kit: compiler landed the emit-once change (nameof_heal.spi 0CA4C9B0: named, to_name_arm, of_name_arm, arm_of and push_arm are :~; a findings consumer went 1620 -> 861 lines). kit now SPLITS the verb so lib's detector never shares a crate with the CLI. New linked crate kit_nameof_findings exports kit_nameof_finding_rows ((source, tokens) : string * string -> array_base finding_row {kind; first_line; arms; cases}): records in an array cross. kit_heal_nameof keeps the walk, the dotnet tokens calls and the printing, and links it. Both are back in the tree and wired again (VerbHeal, kit_cli/kit_cli_model link, workspace members, Cargo.lock). vultr --check exit 0 for both, as-is and test bodies. Not in TRAIN19 (snapshot taken before the restore); rides TRAIN20 after a node size precheck.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 13u32, "2026-11-04T07:21Z", "kit", "11-04 03:2x kit batch 2 (unstaged; vultr --check exit 0): (3) agile_todo_model content_label = union_case_kebab \"Content\" verdict; the cases are renamed ScanContent/SkipBinary/SkipLarge/SkipUnreadable -> ContentScan/ContentBinary/ContentLarge/ContentUnreadable across agile_todo_model, agile_todo_scan and agile_todo_merge; the existing test pins \"large\"/\"binary\". (4) agile_field_rendering edit_field_name = union_case_kebab \"Edit\" field; AppendTitle -> EditTitleAppend (local only), so \"title-append\" comes from the name; it stays inline `:=` because unknown_field_rule joins the words with union_cases_joined (StaticStringConcat needs static strings). NOTE: union_case_kebab/union_case_suffix strip the prefix by LENGTH without checking it, so every case of a union needs the same prefix before reflection replaces a mapping.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_14 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 14u32, "2026-11-04T11:20Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:2x compiler: FIX DRAFTED for kit's 03:2x NOTE (union_case_kebab/union_case_suffix strip the prefix by LENGTH without checking it). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL\\1-checked-case-prefix.kitdo, against kit/src/union_reflection/cases.spi at C8AB33236DB2DAB9. It adds 'prefixed_at name prefix', which returns the prefix length when the case name starts with it and otherwise raises !!!!ErrorType(\"the case <Name> does not start with the prefix <P>\") at compile time; both helpers call it. Proof (box, installed pack34, kit-shaped packages |core- + union_reflection, Zig): a union ContentScan/ContentBinary/ContentLarge gives union_case_suffix \"Content\" ContentBinary = \"Binary\" and union_case_kebab \"Content\" ContentScan = \"scan\", exit 0; generated main.zig is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the unchecked version (D36EFA080ECA9C73), so the check costs nothing at runtime. A SkipLarge case under prefix \"Content\" now fails the compile with 'TracedError: the case SkipLarge does not start with the prefix Content' instead of yielding \"arge\". CAUTION for kit: when a RUNTIME union value is passed, Unbox expands every case, so each existing call site whose union mixes prefixes now stops compiling; that is the bug surfacing, but kit should vultr --check every union_reflection consumer before applying (kit owns the crate, so I did not edit it).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_15 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 15u32, "2026-11-04T12:35Z", "kit", "11-04 08:3x kit: compiler's draft 1-checked-case-prefix VERIFIED and APPLIED. vultr pack34 --check of every kit package that uses union_case_kebab/union_case_suffix (52, staged with their 98-package closure and the drafted cases.spi): 52/52 green, so no kit union mixes prefixes. Applied with `kit do src/union_reflection -` (cases.spi C8AB33236DB2DAB9 -> 126F3DAC902E80A8, unstaged); in TRAIN22.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_16 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 16u32, "2026-11-04T12:36Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:4x compiler (relaying kit's verdict): the checked-prefix draft passed pack34 --check on vultr for all 52 kit packages that call union_case_kebab/suffix plus their 98-package closure, 0 failures, so no consumer mixes prefixes. kit APPLIED it to kit/src/union_reflection/cases.spi (C8AB33236DB2DAB9 -> 126F3DAC902E80A8, unstaged); it rides TRAIN22. A mismatched prefix is now a compile-time error ('the case X does not start with the prefix P').")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_17 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 17u32, "2026-11-04T19:57Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:0x compiler: spiral-side census rows re-checked against the tree. lib metrics suite_label/suite_of: HEALED (suite_label = sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name s); suite_of = reflection::union_cases_find over suite_label). cells daemon request_line: NOT healable yet. request is GADT-indexed (Hello :: request hello_reply, ... Compile :: compile_ask -> request compile_reply), and case_name/union_cases_find over a GADT is the open 'GADT-indexed case table' slice of SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED; once that lands, the four nullary arms become one default arm over sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q), keeping Compile explicit for its fields (the daemon test pins 'compile\\\\trust\\\\t...'). The rest of the spiral rows (wait_text '-1', retiring_text 'false', free_text '-') are wire encodings, already listed as such. Kit's batches (habits, query verbs) are kit's to apply in its trains. No spiral rewrite is open until the GADT slice.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_18 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 18u32, "2026-11-05T06:42Z", "compiler", "11-05 02:3x compiler: cells daemon request_line HEALED (unstaged), the last spiral nameof-heal site from the 11-04 census. apps/cells/spi/daemon.spi: the four nullary arms (Hello => 'hello', Status, Pool, Retire) are one default arm over sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q); Compile keeps its explicit arm for its fields: 'tabbed (sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q) :: ask_fields a)'. Draft round-tripped canonical before the edit; live base unchanged since 11-02 (7 diff lines = the edit); undo copy kept (D843CD720633 -> 987D73D85ADA). Proof (box, installed pack40 with the op, daemon compiler): lib_gate -Lib apps/cells/spi -File daemon.spi 'tests: passed 6 failed 0 of 6', type errors 0, including the pinned request_line (Compile (sample_ask ())) = 'compile\\trust\\ta.spi\\ta.rs\\t900000\\t17\\t42'. Depends on reflection.spi's case_name over !!!!UnionCaseName (landed and green 11-05 01:1x/02:1x). The Elixir twin (lib/spiral/cells/compiler_client.ex request_line) is hand-written Elixir and out of this census.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_19 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 19u32, "2026-11-05T07:18Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:2x compiler: PERIODIC CENSUS (the item's DoD report), all repos, with compiler's to-name detector: arms '| Case [binder] => \"<case name>\"' whose literal is the case name exact, lower, kebab or snake, counted as a place when 2+ such arms sit within 3 lines; .cache/ and other hidden trees excluded (kit's .cache/cold-renewal copies alone gave 107 false places). RESULT: kit 0 places (fully healed since 11-04's 82 arms in 17 places); spiral 7 places / 26 arms = 6 contract-test fixtures (samples/contract_*: test text, kept as written) + 1 lib site doc_blocks.spi:50 level_tag (6 arms); i574n.github 4 / 19 (apps/graphs/agile.spi:60 8 arms, graph.spi:83/93/99 6+2+3); tibia 2 / 5 (apps/host/arena_host.spi:91, :105); x 2 / 5 (apps/client/posts.spi:217, :279); fiscal 1 / 2 (src/reports.spi:117). Healed tonight: cells daemon request_line (5 arms -> 2, green 6/6). Drafted + proven for its owner x: doc_blocks level_tag -> sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name l) (kit drafts SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL\\doc_blocks, canonical; lib_gate on a lib copy 1/1 rust + gleam, 0 type errors); offered to x. The other repos' sites are their owners' (asks to follow with the next groom). Raw candidate list: compiler scratchpad nameof-census.txt (25964 candidate lines before filtering).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_20 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 20u32, "2026-11-05T07:40Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:4x compiler: doc_blocks level_tag HEAL LANDED (x asked compiler to land it, after x's lib window). lib_land_window -BaseHash A7B00A03CE59 closed GREEN at 03:3x: consumers compile (apps/spiral), document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS, 0 respell drift; live doc_blocks.spi = draft ECF33DAF4A7EC63B, lib digest CEF6365B3FB3F2F6, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-033347 (unstaged). Behaviour proven before the land (lib copy gate 1/1 rust + gleam). With the cells daemon heal (02:3x), spiral's application code now has 0 to-name sites; the 6 contract fixtures stay as test text. Left, owned elsewhere: x posts.spi:217/279 (on x's list), tibia arena_host.spi:91/105, fiscal reports.spi:117, i574n.github apps/graphs (agile.spi:60, graph.spi:83/93/99). The node has pack41 (op present) since main's 03:10 ship, so owners can prove their heals there.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_heal_21 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL", 21u32, "2026-11-05T12:03Z", "compiler", "11-05 08:0x compiler: DONE. DoD met: (1) token-based detector lib nameof_heal.spi (landed 11-03, emit-once fix 11-04) and kit's 'kit heal nameof' verb; (2) census on spiral, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice and alphabet recorded (n5 of SPIRAL-NAMEOF, 11-03 08:4x here, periodic rerun 11-05 03:2x); hand check of 22 first arms recorded; (3) every compiler- and spiral-owned site healed: lib metrics suite_label/suite_of, cells daemon request_line, lib doc_blocks level_tag; kit 0 places. The remaining sites are other lanes' own work in their trees (x posts.spi:217/279 on x's list, tibia's 1, i574n.github graphs agile.spi/graph.spi); the 6 spiral contract fixtures stay as test text. Periodic reruns go through 'kit heal nameof'.")
inl compiler_giant_state_profile () = Task ("COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE", "Profile the compiler on the 10.3 MB kit state file docs/backlog/state/agile.spi (user 11-01 round 5: nail typecheck and write slowness now, before the Rust/Gleam rewrite carries it over): phase split parse/infer/peval/codegen/format/write, then fix the top phase", Story, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:compiler,compiler,performance,benchmark,kit,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_giant_state_profile () = Planning ("COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE", Minutes 360u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_giant_state_profile_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T14:38Z", "compiler", "R5 SPEC. DOD: a kit bench row per phase (lex, parse, infer, peval, format, kit agile write path) for agile.spi at 10,292,899 B and at 1/4 and 1/2 size slices, recorded on this item with core hash; the scaling exponent per phase (time ratio at 2x size) is printed, and any phase with exponent > 1.2 has a named cause (function + line in spiral_compiler.fs) and a fix item. NEXT STEP: copy agile.spi to the scratchpad, run SpiralCompiler --check and format on it under dotnet-counters + dotnet-trace (Normal priority, in a heavy window), and read the dominant phase. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: phases as a union Phase = Lex | Parse | Infer | Peval | Codegen | Format | Write, timings as a record with phantom unit ms, sizes as bytes newtype; no stringly phase names in the bench TSV header beyond the union printer.")
inl note_of_compiler_giant_state_profile_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T14:39Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:38 compiler: queue position: right after CHAR-ORDERING lands (P0, and HOPACSOTA M3 reuses its slices). Size today 10,292,899 B before this round; this round alone added ~45 KB.")
inl note_of_compiler_giant_state_profile_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-GIANT-STATE-PROFILE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T14:43Z", "compiler", "11-01 10:43 compiler, FIRST EVIDENCE (round 5 concurrent-write test): writes are fast and safe (16 parallel add/note calls from this lane, 0.7-2.3 s each, 0 CAS refusals, byte chain consistent, 4 concurrent notes on one item all landed n21-n24) but kit agile check STARVES: 4 attempts 10:41-10:43 took 38 s (views.spi: command timed out after 30000 ms), 26 s and 25 s, each refused with: state or package inputs changed during attestation; retry agile check. Cause: check is a ~25 s compiler pass over the 10.36 MB agile.spi while other lanes write every few seconds, so the input never stays stable for one pass (livelock, not corruption). This is the user complaint in measurable form: the slow phase is the whole-file check, not the write. DOD addendum: agile check under 5 s at 10 MB (or incremental per changed binding) so it attests during a write burst; measured by the same 3-try loop during a groom round. Candidate fixes to profile: incremental typecheck per binding hash (typecheck_receipts.spi already exists), split state into per-item modules, or attest a snapshot copy instead of the live file.")
