inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_3 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 3u32, "2026-11-04T22:18Z", "kit", "11-04 18:3x kit: CENSUS RE-RUN + DECISIONS (git ls-files *.txt): kit 0, i574n.github 0, tibia 0, fiscal 0 (corpus.txt gone), polyglot out of scope; 7 remain. DECIDED: (1) spiral/apps/zed/tree-sitter-spiral/test/corpus/{definitions,symbols,test_headers,test_symbol}.txt -> ALLOWLIST: tree-sitter's test runner requires its corpus as .txt under test/corpus (tool format, not our rows). (2) spiral/requirements.txt (mpmath) -> ALLOWLIST: pip's fixed manifest name. (3) spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt and x/postability/tlds.txt -> byte-identical 7516 B IANA TLD lists (upstream data): ALLOWLIST one copy as upstream text with its source and date in the allowlist reason, and x reads it from the spiral copy (or both derive it from the IANA list on demand) so the duplicate goes. NEXT: write the 3 allowlist entries where NoUntypedRows reads them (owner of the census probe), and hand the tlds dedupe to x (their repo).")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_4 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T22:20Z", "kit", "11-04 18:4x kit: found that the NoUntypedRows refusal this item's DoD leans on is NOT implemented anywhere (the name appears only in backlog notes; no .spi in kit, spiral or lib defines it), so there is no allowlist file to write the 3 decisions into yet. They stay recorded here (tree-sitter corpus x4, pip requirements.txt, one IANA tlds.txt with source + date) for whoever builds the probe. What is DONE for this item: every tracked .txt in the org has a decision; kit, i574n.github, tibia and fiscal track none. LEFT: the probe itself (or fold it into the census as a \"tracked-txt\" count with these exemptions) and x's tlds dedupe.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_5 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T22:25Z", "x", "2026-11-04 18:25 x: x's SHARE PLANNED and drafted (rides x-next7, which follows x-next6d): x/postability/tlds.txt is byte-identical (cmp) to spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt. Readers in x: (1) apps/client/tlds.spi's parity test now reads ../../../spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt (x builds with spiral cloned beside it, scripts/common.ps1 SpiralRoot; node mirrors use the same sibling layout) and is renamed the_list_matches_cells_data_tlds_txt (draft 16879E85697F); (2) postability/x.json top_level_domains_file -> ../../spiral/apps/cells/data/tlds.txt (no code reads that key today; CD95B0C1D176 -> CCD8A70C597E); (3) scripts/gate.ps1 drops it from dataFiles (6487C87D09A5 -> BFAFFC5C7967); (4) apps/client/README.md names the shared IANA copy (9FB6AD176816 -> F6BA371E172E). land-x-next7 deletes x/postability/tlds.txt only if still byte-identical to the spiral copy. No other repo reads x's copy (grep over x, spiral/apps, i574n.github/scripts, kit/src).")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_6 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T23:16Z", "kit", "11-04 19:2x kit: the PROBE is written and parked as a known-good draft in the kit store (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\MIGRATE-TXT-FILES-tracked-text\\kit_tracked_text, linked-crate shape): `standards --tracked-text <repo>...` runs `git -C <repo> ls-files *.txt`, exempts only this item's decisions through a typed text_allowance (ToolCorpus = tree-sitter test/corpus, ToolManifest = requirements.txt, UpstreamData = spiral apps/cells/data/tlds.txt), prints each other path and \"kit standards tracked-text ok repos=N untyped=M\", exit 1 when M > 0. Test: x's postability/tlds.txt duplicate is NOT allowed, CRLF and blank rows ignored. vultr --check ok with bodies. WHY PARKED, not routed: the natural route is a FlagTrackedText case in kit_style_census, but that package already fails its own typed-density ratchet (forall 1/227 at baseline -> 1/335 now; its only \"forall\" is a fixture string), so the style hook refuses ANY edit there, and \"baselines only shrink\" forbids re-recording. NEXT: either add real typefeatureset use to kit_style_census (restoring the ratchet) and route it, or give it its own verb.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_7 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T23:36Z", "kit", "11-04 19:4x kit: the probe is ROUTED after all, not through kit standards (blocked by kit_style_census's own ratchet) but as `kit lint tracked-text <repo>...`: LintTrackedText case in kit_lint_cli (precheck's shape: rest -> array_base string), kit_tracked_text restored from the draft store as a linked crate (output lines now \"kit lint tracked-text ...\"), workspace member + lock (cargo metadata --offline --locked exit 0). vultr --check ok with bodies on text.spi and cli.spi. Size + notebooks pending (kit-size-hookverbs / kit-hookverbs-tests). After install: `kit lint tracked-text C:\\home\\git\\spiral C:\\home\\git\\x` should list only x's postability/tlds.txt until x-next7 lands.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_8 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T23:37Z", "kit", "11-04 19:4x kit: usage gap, deliberately NOT fixed tonight: command_spec_domain/direct_verbs.spi VerbLint usage names only `lint macros` and `lint shadows` (already missing growth and precheck, now tracked-text too). That domain feeds kit_cli, last measured at 995 generated lines, so adding usage text needs a size run on kit_cli first. Do it with the next size batch.")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_9 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T23:45Z", "kit", "11-04 19:4x kit: `kit lint tracked-text` GREEN: node size kit_lint_cli 226, kit_tracked_text 469; box notebooks cli 1/1, text 1/1. Rides TRAIN27. The VerbLint usage text stays as is (command_spec_domain is below its typed-density baseline, so the style hook refuses edits; see TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n44).")
inl note_of_migrate_txt_files_10 () = Note ("MIGRATE-TXT-FILES", 10u32, "2026-11-05T20:22Z", "main", "main 11-05 16:2x CLOSE: DoD met. Box recount (git index, 11 repos: spiral, kit, x, fiscal, tibia, regex, html, dice, alphabet, i574n.github, blog): tracked .txt = 0 apart from the reasoned allowlist (tree-sitter test/corpus = tool-mandated; spiral cells/data/tlds.txt and x postability/tlds.txt = external IANA data read by name; LICENSE/requirements), 0 new untracked .txt, 0 tracked-but-ignored (TSV-TXT-GITIGNORE-HEAL n6). polyglot's 1 goes with POLYGLOT-RETIRE. The Write hook now advises on any new .txt in a repo. kit's 'lint tracked-text' (n of 11-04 19:4x) is NOT in the installed kit yet: 'kit lint tracked-text <root>' falls through to 'lint macros' (usage lists only macros), so the CI-side ratchet waits for kit's install and is tracked on TSV-TXT-GITIGNORE-HEAL.")
