inl note_of_upstream_fork_pages_6 () = Note ("UPSTREAM-FORK-PAGES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T16:50Z", "main", "11-04 12:5x main VERIFIED LIVE (it already happened, unrecorded): the user committed the fork files as f4e54a0e (11-01 20:22, on origin/master); its gh-pages workflow run 41366851863 succeeded 11-02 00:23Z and pages-build-deployment 41440069652 succeeded 11-02 11:51Z. https://i574n.github.io/The-Spiral-Language/ is built (source gh-pages) and serves the tree page (200, 545 KB) with both posts: posts/c_self_tail_loop/c_self_tail_loop.spi.html 200 (16.6 KB) and posts/upstream_consolidation/upstream_consolidation.spi.html 200 (39 KB), plus the .spi, .ipynb and fix diffs. The codespace pre-proof was overtaken by a green first CI run, and today's codespace proof (SPIRAL-DEVCONTAINER-CI-PARITY Done) covers the devcontainer side. DONE.")
inl kit_drafts_store () = Task ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", "kit drafts put|list|promote: unfinished drafts live in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\<repo>\\<ITEM>\\, always tied to a backlog item, and promote moves a draft into its repo only after a check (typed Spiral or thin glue, never .py/.tsv/.txt) (user rule 11-01 13:0x via main)", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,agile,drafts,standards,drift,typefeatureset,team:kit,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_drafts_store () = Planning ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_1 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T17:01Z", "kit", "11-01 13:1x kit. USER RULE (13:0x, relayed by main): unfinished drafts and tmp .py/.tsv junk leave the repos and live in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\<repo>\\<ITEM>\\ until they are ready to commit as glue or typed Spiral; kit owns the store. Seeded by main: i574n.github\\SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT (3 .py) and The-Spiral-Language\\UPSTREAM-FORK-PAGES (posts, scripts). VERBS: kit drafts put <repo> <ITEM> <path...> (moves files into the store, refuses an ITEM that is not in the backlog, appends a note on the item naming the files); kit drafts list [--repo r] [--item I] [--older-than Nd] (one typed row per draft: repo, item, path, bytes, age); kit drafts promote <repo> <ITEM> <draft> <repo-path> (runs the check, then moves the draft into the repo, unstaged, and notes the item). CHECK (promote refuses with the fix printed): the extension is not .py/.tsv/.txt/.csv/.rows; a .spi passes kit standards for its target package (ratchet, no regressions); a .ps1 is glue only (under 40 lines, calls kit or a repo script, no new parsing logic, per spiral-first-tooling); anything else is refused. QUALITY LINT HOOK: KIT-AGILE-QUALITY-LINT gains a rule flagging an open item whose drafts are older than N days (default 7) and a Done item that still owns drafts (promote or archive them). The store is outside every repo, so it also needs a backup line (backup-mirror-coverage-boundary: the profile mirror does not cover %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit). DoD: the three verbs plus CLI tests (put refuses an unknown item; promote refuses a .py and a .spi with a ratchet regression and accepts a clean .spi; list --older-than filters by age); the quality-lint rule with one test; kit drafts list over the store run live. NEXT: a typed model in a new HostFree package kit_drafts_model (draft row record, check_verdict union Promotable | RefusedKind ext | RefusedStandards findings | RefusedGlue reason, the age rule) with tests (CPU-light). TYPEFEATURES: check_verdict union; phantom markers :! InStore / :! InRepo on draft paths so promote is the only function that turns one into the other.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_2 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T17:16Z", "kit", "11-01 13:16 kit: the store's off-box copy is resilience's KIT-ARCHIVE-OFFBOX-MIRROR (seeded 13:0x, 81 entries byte-exact). The dir-mirror --full snapshot mode the drafts need (edits and deletes) is specified there (kit builds the verb). kit drafts put/promote should trigger nothing remote themselves; the scheduled --full run picks the changes up.")
inl note_of_kit_drafts_store_3 () = Note ("KIT-DRAFTS-STORE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T18:15Z", "kit", "11-01 14:15 kit: RULE NARROWED (user 14:0x via main): when we know where a file lands (a new app or lib module already decided), it starts at its FINAL path in the repo. The store holds only work whose landing is unknown. promote changes: its destination must be a decided landing (an existing package/app dir, or one named on the item), and every stray or committed-junk file (py/ps1/tsv/txt/md) gets a deliberate decision row (Land path | Draft item | Archive reason) instead of silently staying.")
