inl note_of_lib_wire_checksums_1 () = Note ("LIB-WIRE-CHECKSUMS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:03Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 16:1x tibia: DoD: lib module with xtea_key/xtea_encrypt/xtea_decrypt and adler start/update/digest, known-answer tests from public vectors (Adler-32 of 'Wikipedia' = 0x11E60398; an XTEA round-trip plus one published vector) on c/rust/lua plus wgsl if u32 only, node gate with a negative mutant (delta constant off by one), then tibia src/wire.spi archived. Next step: draft from src/wire.spi (104 lines) with the vectors added.")
inl note_of_lib_wire_checksums_2 () = Note ("LIB-WIRE-CHECKSUMS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:57Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 18:4x tibia: LANDED 18:43 (lib wire.spi 9A087F870122; same close as LIB-FIXED-VIEWS). GATE (Vultr): positive 5/5 on c/rust/lua plus zig, wgsl unsupported there; negative (XTEA delta off by one) CAUGHT: both published-vector tests failed and the round trip still passed, as it must (a wrong delta still inverts itself). The node's two runs were VOID: the first missed the compiler-daemon start under load (my gate script shared MIX_BUILD_PATH with lib_gate, fixed), the second failed every test because my case_labels draft (missing ':< sm'_operators') sat in the same gate package, and a package type-checks every module. tibia src/wire.spi (unregistered, 0 importers) removed from the tree (git history keeps it). Next: box wgsl run, then Done.")
inl note_of_lib_wire_checksums_3 () = Note ("LIB-WIRE-CHECKSUMS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:22Z", "tibia-lane", "11-01 19:2x tibia, DONE. Box wgsl: xtea_published_vector_on_gpu passed 1/1 against the live lib. With the Vultr gate (c/rust/lua/zig, mutant caught) and the 18:43 land, every DoD point holds; tibia src/wire.spi removal is in the user's commit 2aa39c6.")
