inl note_of_regex_skeleton_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SKELETON", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:25Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. DOD (BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT n5 D9/D10): scripts/init.ps1 links deps/spiral (dir-tree-html shape), build.ps1 = one BuildSpiral per crate + cargo build + the self-test, scripts/workflow.ps1 + scripts/publish.ps1 call only those; one .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml + actions.lock; green on ubuntu-24.04 AND windows-2025; publish-tree renders the repo with -Include for the bench HTML; no .py/.tsv/.txt; paths portable (multi-segment Join-Path). NEXT STEP: land the files unstaged in C:\\home\\git\\regex, prove build.ps1 on vultr (box compile window held), then ask the user to push and watch the first run. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the glue has no logic; every decision (which crate, which verdict) is Spiral: the self-test returns a typed verdict union and exits by it. FIELDS: estimate 240, load medium (compiles on vultr/node), assignee agent, owner main (regex worker).")
inl note_of_regex_skeleton_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SKELETON", 2u32, "2026-11-01T21:08Z", "regex", "regex 17:1x PROGRESS (unstaged): scripts/init.ps1 (copied from dir-tree-html), scripts/workflow.ps1, scripts/publish.ps1 (publish-tree -Include report.html), build.ps1 (BuildSpiral bench -> 1000-line check -> cargo -> bench/report.html -> run_notebook --gate over src/*.spi, requires a spiral-tests total line), .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml (dir-tree-html shape + erlef/setup-beam for Cells, fail-fast false, artifact 90 d) + actions.lock (setup-beam entry copied from tibia's lock, verify with gh actions-lock), Cargo workspace (bench crate regex-bench, thin LTO, cu 16), README with tables. NOT proven yet: build.ps1 end to end; the bench crate size.")
inl note_of_regex_skeleton_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SKELETON", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:27Z", "regex", "regex 19:3x CI EVIDENCE: the user committed and pushed the tree as 2f4b88f (\"tests\", 18:52); run https://github.com/i574n/regex/actions/runs/41359359048: ubuntu-24.04 AND windows-2025 both print spiral-tests total discovered 50 executed 50 passed 50 failed 0 unsupported 0 (memo off, 10 notebooks, rust+gleam); bench/bench.spi compiled (5 s) and cargo built it (4-5 s) and regex-bench exited 0 on both; BOTH jobs then went RED only at build.ps1's 1000-line gate (bench.rs 4209 lines), so no page was published. The glue works end to end on both OSes from a fresh runner (init, Ensure-SpiralCompiler 90 s, mix deps, Cells, cargo). Remaining for this item: green, which needs only the bench split (REGEX-BENCH-PAGE).")
inl note_of_regex_skeleton_4 () = Note ("REGEX-SKELETON", 4u32, "2026-11-02T00:44Z", "regex", "regex 20:4x E2E PROOF of the 6 unstaged files: node job-1793578918369-regex-build-e2e ran build.ps1 exactly as CI does on the current tree (mirror regex-1): spiral-tests total 50/50 passed, bench compiled (15 s) + cargo + regex-bench exit 0 + bench/report.html written, the 1000-line gate printed its ::warning (4463 lines), REGEX-OK, build.ps1 exit 0 in 1185 s (log drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SKELETON\\build-e2e.txt). So the next push should go green and publish the page, provided GitHub Pages serves the gh-pages branch (user setting).")
