inl note_of_regex_skeleton_6 () = Note ("REGEX-SKELETON", 6u32, "2026-11-04T14:24Z", "main", "11-04 10:3x main 48 h groom: no lane drives the last 5% this window (regex bench.rs over the 1000-line gate, REGEX-AGREEMENT n3), so Active -> Planned. Resume when bench.rs is split or the gate rule changes.")
inl regex_syntax () = Task ("REGEX-SYNTAX", "regex typed syntax: AST and char-set unions (normalized code ranges, counted repeat with a typed upper bound, & and ~), similarity smart constructors, nullability as GADT evidence", Story, P1, D4, 90u32, Active, "-", "regex,automata,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_syntax () = Planning ("REGEX-SYNTAX", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_syntax_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:25Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. DOD (n5 D1): code ranges are {low;high} u32 records in a sorted disjoint set built only by a normalizing constructor; repeat is Repeat (re, low, Bounded n | Unbounded), never unrolled; Owens-Reppy-Turon similarity (ACI alt, assoc seq, Nothing/Empty units, star idempotence, & and ~ units) in smart constructors; nullability returns accepts|rejects evidence values; test blocks per law (idempotence, commutativity order, units, evidence text) pinned to rust + gleam, 0 failures, cell budget 0 findings. NEXT STEP: write syntax/ (charset.spi, re.spi, nullable.spi) as notebooks and gate them on vultr. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: phantom-indexed char sets (char_set normal vs raw) so only normalized sets reach the AST; nullable_evidence GADT indexed by accepts_empty/rejects_empty (xsd_regex shape, but the index never grows: constant index works at runtime); upper bound as a union, no -1; ordering of AST nodes via a comparison union (Below|Same|Above), not i32. FIELDS: estimate 300, load light, assignee agent.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 2u32, "2026-11-01T21:08Z", "regex", "regex 17:1x PROGRESS (unstaged in C:\\home\\git\\regex): src/ package (packageDir ../deps/spiral/lib) with 9 notebooks: charset (GADT char_set loose|normal, normalized code ranges), syntax (re union with And/Not/counted Repeat, order union, similarity smart constructors), nullable (GADT evidence accepts_empty|rejects_empty), derivative (Brzozowski + remainder theorem), dfa (classes, eager DFA, state nominal, Dead case, typed cap), minimal (Moore refinement, live analysis), certificate (distinguishing words checked on the derivative matcher, equivalence by product exploration), partial (Antimirov + support bound), agreement (keyed_rng corpus, 4 engines). Tests pinned rust+gleam. First Cells gate running on the node (job-1793566876167-regex-cells1, mirror regex-1; vultr dropped per main's one-job rule). Scripts: drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SYNTAX\\{cells-gate,typecheck}.ps1. Cell budget NOT yet met (several definitions > 272).")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:27Z", "regex", "regex 17:3x CELL BUDGET (measured by block length, not yet by mix spiral.cell_budget): 35 definitions over ~267 chars, mostly full matches over the 9-case re union (derive 524, points_of 408, partials 543, alphabetic_width 403, order_re group 969, nullability_of group 1378, evidence GADT 1266). PLAN, decided: re-shape the AST so no match has more than ~4 arms: re = Leaf leaf (Nothing|Epsilon|Set) | Pair (pair_op = SeqOp|AltOp|AndOp, re, re) | Unary (unary_op = NotOp|StarOp, re) | Repeat; each engine then dispatches per family into a small helper. The evidence GADT splits by family the same way (leaf, pair, unary evidence). Do this after the first green Cells run so the shape change is the only diff.")
