inl note_of_regex_syntax_5 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 5u32, "2026-11-04T12:24Z", "main", "11-04 08:4x main CELL BUDGET MEASURED by x (xc postable census, node build 11-04 07:07): regex/src 15 hand files, 548 cells, 96 over 272 chars (posts 672). Bands: 273-320 = 33 (trims), 321-544 = 51 (one split each), >544 = 12 (the real reshapes: language ends 1522, nullable evidence 1266 / nullability_of 1378 / accept_reason 1298, xsd class_body 1075 / alternation 1043, syntax order_re 969, semantics bt 905, dfa build_rows 661, lazy empty_store 646, certificate columns_sound 573, lazy grow_to 548); 17 of the 96 are test cells. Per file: certificate 16, lazy 13, xsd 9, semantics 8, minimal 7, partial 7, syntax 6, table 6, agreement 5, language 4, and 3 each in charset, derivative, dfa, laws, nullable. DECISION: split per measured cell (largest first, re-measured with xc) instead of n3's whole-AST reshape. The 12 big ones are where n3's 4-arm idea applies (the 9-case re matches). Re-measure: %TEMP%\\xc-node\\xc.exe postable census <files>.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_6 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 6u32, "2026-11-04T13:06Z", "main", "11-04 09:1x main CELL BUDGET 96 -> 61 over (xc postable census, box): charset 3->0, table 6->0, derivative 3->0, laws 3->0, syntax 6->0, dfa 3->0, agreement 5->0, partial 7->1 (reconstruction_from: its function-typed split parameter makes every helper header ~160 chars). KEY TECHNIQUE (proven; memory mutual-group-blank-line-splits-cells): a blank line may precede :& and the group still binds (vultr --check, negative control fails ETY-UnboundVariable), and x confirmed xc counts each blank-separated :& block as its own cell. So recursive matches split into :& arm chains (derive -> derive_seq/derive_rest/derive_unary; normalize; order_re -> order_same/order_pair/order_unary/order_repeat_with; build_rows -> build_next/build_step; partials; alphabetic_width; agree_from/search_accepted/agree_on_words; assign) with every call fully applied: no closures, no eager evaluation. Non-recursive steps are plain helpers. Exceptions: charset order_ranges evaluates the tail comparison eagerly (after_tie), same result. VERIFIED: whole package --check clean on vultr (planted-error control rejected). PENDING: the vultr Cells gate (started on the 96->72 tree); the later splits need one more gate. LEFT: certificate 16, lazy 13, xsd 9, semantics 8, minimal 7, language 4, nullable 3, partial 1.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_7 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 7u32, "2026-11-04T13:17Z", "main", "11-04 09:2x main VULTR GATE 1 GREEN: regex Cells (15 notebooks, rust+gleam) 86/86 passed, 0 failed, on the first-wave tree (charset, table, laws, derivative tests, first syntax/dfa/agreement splits). Since then: semantics 8->0, minimal 7->0, language 4->0, partial 7->1, and the :& chains in derivative/laws/syntax/dfa/agreement. 42 over left (certificate 16, lazy 13, xsd 9, nullable 3, partial 1). Package --check clean on vultr after every file. GATE 2 (current tree) PENDING on vultr.")
inl note_of_regex_syntax_8 () = Note ("REGEX-SYNTAX", 8u32, "2026-11-04T13:36Z", "main", "11-04 09:4x main CELL BUDGET 96 -> 2 over (xc census, box: 15 hand files, 729 cells). VULTR GATE 2 GREEN: Cells 88/88 (wave 2: :& chains, semantics, minimal, partial, language). Wave 3 (nullable, xsd, lazy, certificate) package --check clean, Cells gate 3 PENDING. Techniques beyond n6: a type alias (:== seen_pairs = list (target * target)) to shorten headers; a sound_ctx record threading d/n/width/lows through rows_sound/columns_sound, with a generic first_of choosing the first violation (later checks now evaluate eagerly, same result, and a sound DFA checks every column anyway); existing eager_of and flip_accepting reused in place of inline copies; accessors nodes_of/steps_of/links_of plus a generic regrow/resized_copy in the array store (non-recursive helpers only on the hot path). LEFT (asked x): nullable evidence GADT declaration (1266, type, class question), partial reconstruction_from (375; its function-typed split parameter makes every helper header ~160 chars).")
