inl note_of_regex_derivatives_1 () = Note ("REGEX-DERIVATIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:25Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. DOD (n5 D2a-b, D3d): derive c r for every constructor incl. counted repeat (d(R{n,m}) = dR . R{n-1,m-1}), & and ~; matcher = fold of derivatives then nullable; the remainder theorem a.w in L(r) <=> w in L(d_a r) checked on the seeded corpus; interned engine hash-conses nodes (a node is its number, children below parent), caches d per (node, class) and agrees with the plain matcher on the corpus; (0|00)*1 vs 0^26 decides in linear steps. NEXT STEP: derive/ notebook with derive, matches and the remainder-theorem test. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: interned nodes are a nominal (interned_node) only the store hands out; derivative classes a nominal over the class index; the matcher typestate raw -> decided as a GADT (legacy bit_matcher_state phase) so a result cannot be read before deciding. FIELDS: estimate 300, load light, assignee agent.")
