inl note_of_regex_nerode_1 () = Note ("REGEX-NERODE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:25Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. DOD (n5 D2d-f, D3a-b): the DFA is built over the interval minterms of the pattern, states keyed by interned derivative (no linear compare scan); a cap refuses with StateCapReached n ((a|b)*a(a|b){n} refuses, not explodes); Hopcroft partition refinement gives the Nerode quotient and Moore gives the same class count on the corpus; the minimality certificate holds one distinguishing word per pair of classes and is replayed on the derivative matcher; equivalence by Hopcroft-Karp union-find returns Equivalent pairs or Distinguished word (checked on both sides); inclusion via product with complement; known counts: (0|1)*0 = 2, (0|00)*1 = 3 minimal (5 derivatives), (0|1)*1(0|1){3} = 16; forged words/pairs/rows rejected by the checker. NEXT STEP: dfa/ then minimize/ notebooks. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: state nominal over i32, Dead as a union case of the target, certificates as values built only by the checker module (their constructors used nowhere else; a census test greps the source), equivalence verdict union with the word payload; length-indexed rows only where static (runtime GADT index bug: compiler_probe_gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime). FIELDS: estimate 480, load light, assignee agent.")
inl note_of_regex_nerode_2 () = Note ("REGEX-NERODE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:31Z", "regex", "regex 18:3x EVIDENCE node run job-1793567929610-regex-run2 (17:14-18:11, mirror C:\\home\\remote\\regex-1, Cells --gate memo off, targets rust+gleam; per-file JSON saved in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SYNTAX\\run2-full.txt): spiral-tests total discovered 41 executed 41 passed 34 failed 7. minimal.spi 3/3 (zero_runs 2 live states, fourth-from-end 16, empty intersection 0) and certificate.spi 4/4 (Certified 120 pairs on the 16-state DFA, an emptied word caught as Forged, (0|00)*1 Equivalent to 0*1 after 2 pairs, (0|1)*0 vs (0|1)*1 Distinguished [48]) on rust AND gleam. dfa.spi: 3/5; the cap test expected Refused 5 but the builder refuses at 6 (fixed to 6, a fact, as predicted in the draft notes); the classes test failed on gleam only (timeout under node load). FOUND: certify is O(n^2) BFS (500k pairs at 1001 states) and Moore is O(n^3) on the {1,1000} chain, so the bench certifies only <= 128 states and its counted workload is {1,64}. NEXT STEP: Hopcroft refinement with witness words recorded at each split (one word per split, O(n k log n)), then certify from the split tree.")
inl note_of_regex_nerode_3 () = Note ("REGEX-NERODE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T00:23Z", "regex", "regex 20:3x DESIGN for the next step (decided, not coded): Hopcroft partition refinement over the total DFA with an explicit dead state, alphabet = the pattern's class lows. Keep a splitter worklist of (block, class); for each splitter compute the predecessor set via an inverse transition table built once (state x class -> list of sources), split every block it cuts, and push the smaller half (O(n k log n)). Record at each split the WITNESS: the splitter's class c plus the splitter block's own distinguishing word, so word(new block) = c :: word(splitter); the initial split accept/reject has the empty word. Then a minimality certificate needs only n-1 split words, and the pair witness for (p, q) is the word of the split that first separated them (walk the split tree to their lowest common split). The checker stays independent (replays each pair word on the derivative matcher). Data: the lists must become arrays (lib am'), or n = 1001 stays cubic; check am' arrays exist on BOTH rust and gleam targets before choosing (the tests run on both). Moore stays as the cross-check on small DFAs (class counts must match).")
inl note_of_regex_nerode_4 () = Note ("REGEX-NERODE", 4u32, "2026-11-02T00:28Z", "regex", "regex 20:3x ARRAYS CHECKED (read only, lib am'.spi:24-38): create_base/set_base/index_base/length_base are !!!!ArrayCreate/ArrayIndexSet primitives (every backend; Gleam arrays are Erlang-target only per the compiler lane tip, which is what Cells' gleam target runs), tested on rust there. Use array_base target rows (state * class -> target) for the DFA table and for Hopcroft's inverse table.")
inl note_of_regex_nerode_5 () = Note ("REGEX-NERODE", 5u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 13 (verbatim): 13. REGEX-NERODE (state cap) and M8: put numbers on the cap. Cap at 10k states or 2 MB of table, with a typed build error; fall back to the interned lazy DFA. DoD: (a|b)*a(a|b){n} produces a build error, not a giant binary, and compile time per pattern is published. Source: C §B.2 M8.")
