inl note_of_regex_aot_targets_1 () = Note ("REGEX-AOT-TARGETS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:26Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. DEFERRED from the share. DOD: staged DFA from a static regex (build.rs/proc-macro), no_std, no alloc, zero init; throughput >= regex-automata sparse serialized and <= 1.1x dense, binary <= dense, cargo build time published (cut > 1.25x -> \"certificate + multi-target\"); prefilters memchr/rare byte/Teddy with the necessity certificate L <= S*.Lits.S* (freeze below 30% gain); Unicode classes as UTF-8 byte automata, states <= 1.5x regex-automata on 50 patterns, 10^7 fuzz inputs 0 divergences (cut > 3x on \\w/\\pL -> adopt regex-automata's construction as reference); eBPF/XDP verifier-accepted by construction (cut ~1k states); WGSL; Delphi 64-bit DFA disagreement explained first (DELPHI-64BIT-DFA-DISAGREE); 24 h cargo-fuzz vs regex with 0 divergences, any unexplained divergence blocks publication. NEXT STEP: none until REGEX-REBAR GATE 1. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: targets as backend prototype instances; staged twins only for static regexes; length-indexed rows where the regex is static. FIELDS: estimate 2400, load heavy, assignee agent.")
inl note_of_regex_aot_targets_2 () = Note ("REGEX-AOT-TARGETS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x MOVED OUT (share re-read contradiction (a)): M1 UTF-8/byte classes -> REGEX-BYTES-UTF8, M3 spans -> REGEX-SPANS, M5 prefilters -> REGEX-PREFILTER, because GATE 1 cannot be measured fairly without them. This item keeps AOT/no_std/C header/eBPF/WGSL/fuzz.")
inl note_of_regex_aot_targets_3 () = Note ("REGEX-AOT-TARGETS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITIONS 14 and 18 (verbatim): 14. REGEX-AOT-TARGETS additions: compare against logos and re2c as well as regex-cli generate serialize (dense and sparse); generate the state loop by the first Futamura projection (specialize the DFA interpreter on the static table); version the readable generated Rust in the repo, with the regen command and the pinned compiler version. DoD: a page table with throughput, binary size and cargo build time for each competitor. Source: C §B.2 M6, §F.1; E \"Diretrizes práticas\" 1. 18. REGEX-AOT-TARGETS (eBPF) or NEW REGEX-XDP. DoD: the kernel verifier accepts 100% of DFAs within the cap; packets/s published against a hand-written Aya version of the same pattern; counts on a reference pcap match the core engine; Spiral rejects negatives for the verifier's own reasons (unbounded loop, out-of-packet access). Cut: verifier rejecting DFAs above about 1k states means restricting to small patterns. Timebox 3 weeks. Source: C §F.5; E §7 #2.")
