inl note_of_regex_rebar_1 () = Note ("REGEX-REBAR", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:26Z", "regex", "regex 16:4x. DEFERRED from the share (cccab1fd B.2, 4edd442c s7). DOD: rebar measure --test prints OK for the engine on curated/01-literal, then every count/count-spans/grep benchmark a DFA-only engine can contest (01, 02, 06 first; 03/08 need case-insensitive + Unicode \\b; captures groups 04/05/07/09/11 out); counts match rebar's (a mismatch is not collected); M0 cut: plain DFA loop > 3x regex-automata dense::DFA -> fix codegen first; GATE 1: rebar rank --intersection geomean <= 2.0x continue, 2-4x prefilters only, > 4x close the throughput front; semantics declared per engine (leftmost-longest from derivatives, leftmost-first via priorities or per-engine counts like RE#); forward + reverse DFA for spans; upstream rebar PR only after >= 1 external dependent 60 days after release. NEXT STEP: after REGEX-BENCH-PAGE, the KLV runner as a Spiral bin. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: rebar models as a union, KLV fields parsed into a typed record at the boundary, match semantics as a union (LeftmostLongest | LeftmostFirst). FIELDS: estimate 2400, load heavy (rebar runs), assignee agent.")
inl note_of_regex_rebar_2 () = Note ("REGEX-REBAR", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ITEMS 1-6 (verbatim): 1. REGEX-REBAR: the KLV protocol, exactly. Parse the keys name, model, pattern, case-insensitive, unicode, haystack, max-iters, max-warmup-iters, max-time, max-warmup-time into a typed record. Answer rebar's version query (the \"receipt\" that the engine is available). Print one \"nanoseconds,count\" line per sample (the format of mach-regex, rebar PR #40). DoD: rebar measure --test prints OK on curated/01-literal, and an unknown key is refused with a typed error. Source: C §B.1 \"Protocolo\".\n\n2. REGEX-REBAR: every model gets a verdict. Supported: compile, count, count-spans (sum of match lengths in bytes), grep (count of matching lines). Refused with a typed reason: count-captures, grep-captures, regex-redux. Unsupported options (case-insensitive, Unicode) must raise a measurement error, never return a wrong count. DoD: a page table listing every benchmark as contested or refused, with the reason. Source: C §B.1 \"Modelos\", \"Recursos não suportados\".\n\n3. REGEX-REBAR: confirm the curated groups the source left open. The models of 10-bounded-repeat, 12-dictionary (multi-pattern), 13-noseyparker and 14-quadratic were not checked one by one in the source. Read rebar's benchmarks/definitions/curated/*.toml at a pinned commit. DoD: a typed table of all 14 groups; target 5-9 contestable groups and at least 28 benchmarks, matching RE#'s entry. Source: C §B.1 \"Curados\".\n\n4. REGEX-REBAR: only a runtime engine enters rebar. rebar hands over the pattern at run time, so the staged/AOT DFA goes on the page as a separate \"AOT\" category, explicitly not comparable. The runtime arm is the interned lazy or eager DFA. DoD: the page labels each arm Runtime or AOT, and the AOT arm never appears in rebar rank tables. Source: E §7 #1 M1; C §A.1 \"Onde não ganha\".\n\n5. REGEX-REBAR: semantics plan with a cut. Ship leftmost-longest first, then leftmost-first through priority derivatives (Frisch-Cardelli greedy). Cut: if leftmost-first needs more than 2 extra weeks, publish leftmost-longest with per-engine counts in the fork's toml, as RE# does. DoD: counts match rebar on every selected count/count-spans/grep benchmark. Source: C §B.1 \"Semântica\", §B.2 M3.\n\n6. REGEX-REBAR: publish through a public fork first. Precedents: ieviev/rebar (RE#) and eaftan/rebar (SafeRE). The fork carries an engines.toml entry, a Dockerfile, the declared hardware, and rebar rank --intersection (rebar's README calls a single number \"fraught\"). DoD: the fork's results reproduce from a single command on the CI runner. Source: C §B.1 \"Aceitação upstream\"; E \"Diretrizes práticas\" 2. CONTRADICTION b: E §7 says PR upstream at M4; C says only after a real user (one external dependent within 60 days); the backlog follows C.")
