inl note_of_yed_diagrams_1 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T20:46Z", "yed", "Headless route works: yed.jar (3.25.1, yGuard-obfuscated yFiles 2.x) on classpath, JDK 27, -Djava.awt.headless=true. Graph2D=y.J.gA, HierarchyManager=y.J.A.A (reflection: class/package clash), GraphMLIOHandler=y.H.Q, ImageIoOutputHandler=y.H.A, SVGIOHandler=B.A.D.C, yEd layout modules y.B.* run synchronously via YModule.ă(graph); options via OptionHandler. Work dir C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_2 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T21:03Z", "yed", "Subject chosen by measurement: backlog dependency graph = 1157 items, 696 in the dep graph, 751 dep edges (39 dangling), 4 kinds, 5 statuses, 10 area groups (team tag, else lane tag). Org manifests scan was too slow on the busy box (spiral alone 925 manifests, compiler excluded anyway). Generator src/Gen.java (TSV from kit agile list --json -> yFiles ygraphml: shape=kind, fill=status, border=priority, groups=area). Lab.java runs yEd layout modules (y.B.J IHL, y.B.r SmartOrganic, y.B.u Orthogonal, y.B.o CompactOrtho, y.B.z Circular, y.B.p Radial, y.B.H Balloon, y.B.e Tree, y.B.x SeriesParallel, y.B.M Cactus, y.B.I CompactDisk; routers y.B.c/T/Y) and exports GraphML+SVG+PNG; Metrics.java scores crossings, node-edge overlaps, overlaps, area, aspect. Baseline IHL area-grouped: 14 s layout, 35253x5133, 4822 crossings, aspect 6.9.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_3 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:36Z", "yed", "Trap found: yEd layout modules compare enum-like string options with reference equality (if_acmpne on the interned constant), so OptionHandler.set(name, value) with a non-interned String is accepted, reads back equal, and is silently ignored (EDGE_ROUTING=CURVED stayed orthogonal; several round-1 variants rendered byte-identical). Fix: intern string option values. 13 round-1 runs quarantined to out\\void-uninterned and requeued.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_4 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 4u32, "2026-11-01T21:49Z", "yed", "Round 1 (17 valid runs, contact sheet out\\contact-sheet-r1.png): leader = Compact Orthogonal (y.B.o, channel-HQ router, aspect 1.4, flat): 6292x3877, 502 crossings (0.67/edge), 0 node-edge, 0 overlaps, labels legible even at 2400 px preview. Orthogonal flat: only 22 crossings but 22518x10926 and sparse. Tree flat: 239 crossings but 14.5:1 aspect. Area-grouped layouts all suffer from cross-area deps: IHL 4822 crossings, SmartOrganic 4000+ with clumps in oversized groups, Orthogonal-with-groups 1119 crossings in 46k px. Radial/Cactus/CompactDisk bundled = artistic, unreadable. Round 2 (33 runs) = compact-ortho variants, Louvain-clustered SmartOrganic, recursive IHL, re-runs of the 13 voided specs.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_5 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 5u32, "2026-11-01T23:08Z", "yed", "Groom 19:1x. 52 layout runs ranked (out\\runs\\ranking.tsv, contact sheet out\\contact-sheet-all.png). Ranking: (1) Compact Orthogonal flat, aspect 1.0 (y.B.o): 446 crossings, 0 node-edge, 0 overlaps, 12k x 8k px with ID+title labels, best by numbers and by eye; (2) its row-packed variant 378 crossings but 40% more area; (3) Orthogonal flat 22 crossings but 4x sparser; (4) Louvain-clustered SmartOrganic + polyline router 551 crossings, 0 node-edge; best grouped = IHL left-to-right with RECURSIVE_LAYERING (1744 crossings, areas as blocks in dependency order). Area-grouped SmartOrganic/IHL-global/Orthogonal: 1100-6400 crossings, worse. Hybrid RecursiveGroupLayouter(compact ortho per area) via a y.B.o subclass that wraps the layouter in launchLayouter: 3917 crossings with orthogonal inter-edge routing. Images: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\BEST-backlog-compact-orthogonal.png (12260x8862, header+legend), C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\RUNNERUP-backlog-hierarchic-recursive-areas.png, GraphML C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\final\\final-cortho-ar10.graphml (opens in yEd), SVGs beside them. Headless drive: java -Djava.awt.headless=true -cp bin;yed.jar Lab <in.graphml> <outprefix> <module[+module]> 'OPT=v;...|...'; Graph2D y.J.gA + HierarchyManager y.J.A.A, GraphML y.H.Q, PNG y.H.A (view y.J.U fit + zoom), SVG B.A.D.C, module.ă(graph) = synchronous start. No GUI window was ever opened.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_6 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 6u32, "2026-11-01T23:29Z", "yed", "FINAL 19:3x. Best = Compact Orthogonal, aspect 1.2, grid 10 (sweep of 6 on the titled graph; A/A rerun byte-identical, so the module is deterministic; EDGE_CROSSING_COST had no effect): 438 crossings, 0 node overlaps, 0 edges through nodes, 10788x6242 layout units. Image C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\BEST-backlog-compact-orthogonal.png (13130x8371, header+legend; preview .preview.png). GraphML for yEd: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\final\\final-cortho-ar12-grid10.graphml, SVG same stem .svg. Runner-up with area groups: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\RUNNERUP-backlog-hierarchic-recursive-areas.png + C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\final\\final-ihl-recursive-lr-area.graphml. Reproduce (JDK = scoop temurin-jdk 27, Y=C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\apps\\yed\\current\\yed.jar): (1) kit agile list C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github\\docs\\backlog all --json > C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\data\\backlog-all.json; (2) javac -encoding UTF-8 -cp Y -d C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\bin C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\src\\*.java; (3) java -cp C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\bin Gen C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\data\\backlog-all.json C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\graphml\\backlog-flat-final.graphml --titles (add --groups=area for groups); (4) java -Xmx2500m -XX:ActiveProcessorCount=1 -Djava.awt.headless=true -Dzoom=2.0 -Dmaxpx=100000000 -cp C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\bin;Y Lab C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\graphml\\backlog-flat-final.graphml C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\final\\final-cortho-ar12-grid10 y.B.o 'USE_VIEW_ASPECT_RATIO=false;ASPECT_RATIO=1.2;GRID=10'; (5) java -cp C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\bin Compose <png> C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\BEST-backlog-compact-orthogonal.png '<title>' '<subtitle>'; ranking: java -cp C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\bin Rank C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\runs [contact.png]. Specs: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\specs-round1/2/3/final/sweep.tsv. Left: Mermaid export, a Pages home for the image, and a top-level IHL arrangement for the per-area compact-ortho hybrid (RgCortho).")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_7 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 7u32, "2026-11-02T00:39Z", "yed", "Pivot (user 19:3x): diagram spiral_compiler.fs itself, single-flight vs hopacsota. Two models. (1) Curated architecture: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\model\\compiler.model (DSL: G/N/E lines with source line refs) -> src\\GenModel.java -> nested-group GraphML with HTML labels and 9 edge kinds: 24 groups, 186 nodes, 281 edges. Covers the PartEvalSeams API (16 ops), the #else inline single-flight impls, the hopacsota Session (policy/defer/markers/Finish replay/conflict restart) and the Engine (Table.Decide state machine, MVar guard, wait-for Graph, Worklist tokens, 1.5 GB body threads), the 35 peval call sites, divergence notes, env switches, the pipeline, 19 backends and the supervisor. (2) Auto-extracted: src\\Extract.java turns every ## section and ###/top-level decl into nodes and identifier references into edges: 58 modules, 1319 items, 3739 edges (seam names link to both builds). First layouts on (1): IHL left-to-right, global layering: 726 crossings, aspect 1.86 (best so far); recursive top-to-bottom: 1025 crossings, aspect 1.15. A user interrupt killed the background suite mid-run (void run quarantined in out\\void-interrupted); requeued.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_8 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 8u32, "2026-11-02T01:15Z", "yed", "Compiler diagram FINAL 21:1x. Best (grouped): C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\BEST-compiler-singleflight-vs-hopacsota.png (14322x8504, header + node/edge legend), GraphML C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\compiler\\final-compiler-ihl-lr.graphml: IHL left to right, global layering, generic edge labels; 726 crossings, 0 overlaps, 0 edges through nodes. Same-crossings flat alternative: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\YED-DIAGRAM\\out\\ALT-compiler-compact-orthogonal-flat.png (Compact Orthogonal, 4x smaller area, groups shown by colour only). Ranked 11 layouts on the 186/281 model (out\\compiler\\ranking via Rank). Stress test: the auto-extracted 1319-node / 3739-edge reference graph laid out with recursive IHL in 137 s (175k crossings, 144k x 127k units: unreadable, so the extractor needs module-level aggregation); Compact Orthogonal on it did not finish in 15 min on the loaded box. Reproduce: java -cp bin GenModel model\\compiler.model graphml\\compiler-noroot-final.graphml --no-root; java -Djava.awt.headless=true -Dzoom=2.0 -Dmaxpx=110000000 -cp 'bin;<yed.jar>' Lab graphml\\compiler-noroot-final.graphml out\\compiler\\final-compiler-ihl-lr y.B.J 'ORIENTATION=LEFT_TO_RIGHT;EDGE_LABELING=EDGE_LABELING_GENERIC;COMPONENT_ARRANGEMENT_POLICY=POLICY_COMPACT'; java -cp bin Compose <png> <out> '<title>' '<subtitle>' compiler. Full extract: java -cp bin Extract C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\apps\\compiler\\spiral_compiler.fs model\\compiler-full.model.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_9 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 9u32, "2026-11-02T10:16Z", "yed", "CI wiring 11-02 (user: new apps/graphs + workflow entry). Unstaged in i574n.github: apps/graphs/{build.ps1, src/Graphs|Agile|Model|Mermaid|Compose.java, spiral-compiler.model, out/*}, .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml (new step 'pwsh apps/graphs/build.ps1' on ubuntu, before workflow.ps1; no new uses:, actions.lock unchanged), scripts/publish.ps1 (-Include the 8 output names so untracked outputs reach dist/dir-tree-html). build.ps1: picks JDK 17+ (JAVA_HOME_<n>_X64, JAVA_HOME, scoop temurin, PATH), yEd 3.25.1 from scoop or the yworks zip pinned by sha256, javac + java -Djava.awt.headless. Graphs parses docs/backlog/state/agile.spi directly (no kit in CI): 1206 items, 786 deps, Compact Orthogonal; spiral-compiler from the checked-in model, IHL LR. Outputs png (header+legend), svg, mmd, graphml. Tested: box (Windows, JDK 27, 13 min under load) and codespace yed-graphs-test (Alpine, openjdk21, fresh yEd download + sha check): 79 s, two runs byte-identical on all 8 files; both .mmd parse and render with mermaid-cli; backlog.mmd needs maxEdges>=800 and maxTextSize>=150000 (default config renders an error), spiral-compiler.mmd renders with defaults. Codespace stopped (1 h retention). Follow-ups: Spiral->Kotlin port of apps/graphs (typefeatureset dogfood), mermaid limits in dir-tree-html, port build.ps1 per PS1-TO-SPIRAL n56.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_10 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 10u32, "2026-11-02T11:24Z", "yed", "Spiral->Kotlin port DONE 11-02 (user: rewrite apps/graphs in Spiral compiled to Kotlin, commit the .kt, no Java). i574n.github/apps/graphs now = package.spiproj + host.spi (Kotlin host boundary: one call per primitive; phantom-typed i32 handles handle t because Kotlin rejects macro types) + graph.spi (typed model: node_kind/edge_kind/shape/stroke/build unions, styles by exhaustive match) + emit.spi (layout union -> yEd module/settings, GraphML + Mermaid emitters, typed legend drawn on a host canvas, typestate GADT stage modeled -> stage laid_out, per-format prototypes extension_of/written_as on on_graphml/on_mermaid/on_svg/on_png) + compiler_model.spi (the model as typed rows: region union, one part union per region, relations reference parts by constructor so a dangling edge is a compile error) + compiler.spi + agile.spi (parses docs/backlog/state/agile.spi into typed work/priority/status/area) + main.spi, and the generated graphs.kt (885 KB, 16.5k lines). Java + spiral-compiler.model archived to drafts YED-DIAGRAM/archive-java-apps-graphs. build.ps1: pinned kotlinc 2.4.21 + yEd 3.25.1 (sha256), kotlinc graphs.kt, run; -Regenerate recompiles the .spi. Verified on vultr: fresh CI-like run 2m19s, two runs byte-identical on all 8 outputs, same diagrams as the Java version. CI step now continue-on-error so a yworks outage keeps the committed outputs; publish-tree copies regenerated tracked outputs. Open: graphs.kt is 16.5k lines (1k-line gate; Kotlin backend emits one file), lib Kotlin arms in spiral/lib unstaged and need landing, Windows path of build.ps1 untested (box kept compile-free).")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_11 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 11u32, "2026-11-02T11:27Z", "yed", "Rule status 11-02 (main): (1) KNOWN 1000-line gate exception: apps/graphs/graphs.kt (generated, 16,548 lines) until Kotlin multi-file emission lands (BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY, note on Kotlin multi-file emission). Not a silent pass. (2) The JVM is required: yEd's layout engine exists only as Java bytecode in yed.jar. build.ps1 stays thin glue: pinned downloads, kotlinc, java. (3) The CI step in gh-pages.yml is continue-on-error, so a failed render keeps the committed outputs; watch the step log, a red step does not fail the job. (4) The Windows path of build.ps1 (scoop kotlinc.bat, Windows JDK discovery) is UNTESTED; it was verified only on Linux (vultr), with the box kept compile-free. (5) The lib Kotlin arms are being landed by main through lib_land_window (drafts kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\kotlin-arms\\); do not run build.ps1 -Regenerate against the box lib until main confirms the land.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_12 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 12u32, "2026-11-02T11:31Z", "yed", "11-02 07:27 main: the lib Kotlin arms (base.spi =. <>.; sm' slice index_of starts_with ends_with contains split replace) LANDED green via lib_land_window (14 signatures unchanged, apps/spiral + apps/wasm compile, document_test 22/22, type_probe sm' PASS 72; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261102-072714). build.ps1 -Regenerate against the box lib is now safe; point (5) of n11 is resolved.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_13 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 13u32, "2026-11-02T12:15Z", "yed", "11-02 08:1x Regenerate proof after the lib land (spiral 32a1b808 carries the Kotlin arms): apps/graphs/main.spi compiled to Kotlin against the landed lib (git archive HEAD lib) on vultr (box at 100% CPU; vultr idle, no kit jobs) gives graphs.kt sha256 DF73C1CEEF3D111F, byte-identical to the committed apps/graphs/graphs.kt (884,804 bytes). The committed .kt is reproducible from the .spi plus the landed lib.")
inl note_of_yed_diagrams_14 () = Note ("YED-DIAGRAMS", 14u32, "2026-11-02T14:55Z", "yed", "Recycle lessons (11-02): (a) PUBLISH: spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 -Include now matches tracked AND untracked files and copies the working-tree copy over git checkout-index, so committed outputs (i574n.github apps/graphs/out/*) show the CI-regenerated version in dir-tree-html. i574n.github/scripts/publish.ps1 passes the 8 output names. (b) REGENERATE PROOF RECIPE (vultr, box busy): git -C spiral archive HEAD lib -> tar to vultr; build a stage tree <stage>/git/{spiral -> extracted lib dir, i574n.github/apps/graphs (*.spi + package.spiproj)} so packageDir ../../../spiral/lib resolves; cd /home/remote/git/spiral (|core- resolves from the compiler cwd) and run dotnet /root/.cache/spiral-bin/bin/single-flight/SpiralCompiler/Release/net11.0/SpiralCompiler.dll --backend Kotlin <stage>/.../main.spi <stage>/.../graphs.kt; compare sha256 with the committed graphs.kt (DF73C1CEEF3D111F). (c) JVM is required (yEd layout is Java bytecode only; yed.jar is obfuscated yFiles 2.x: Graph2D y.J.gA, HierarchyManager y.J.A.A, GraphML y.H.Q, PNG y.H.A, SVG B.A.D.C, modules y.B.*; string option values must be interned or they are silently ignored). Kotlin gaps are on BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY n12 (macro types, O(n) string index, nested match lowering, missing lib arms) and n13 (single-file emission vs the 1000-line gate).")
