inl rust_union_default_array_create () = Task ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", "Rust: array create of a record with a union field fails E0599 (union has no Default)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,rust,codegen,self-hosting", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rust_union_default_array_create () = Planning ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_1 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:11Z", "compiler", "11-01 21:1x compiler: filed from x-dumps' report (vultr, single-flight core f6f6879566c5a830, rustc nightly 2026-10-31). WHAT: Rust array create of a tuple element whose fields include a union (`vec![<(Rc<str>, US0, Rc<str>, bool)>::default(); n]`) fails with E0599 'US0: Default not satisfied'. codegenRust emits `impl Default` for a union only when every case field has a default expression (AGENTS.md, Rust array create), so an option-like union (None | Some of string) never gets one. Reached through lib json.decode into a record with an `array_base r` field where r has an option field. json.spi's decode_reads_arrays_of_records passes only because its element is all scalars. x worked around it in kit/src/k3s_manifest, so nothing is blocked. MINIMAL SAMPLE (x's candidate): `:== r = { a : option string }`, `:== w = { xs : array_base r }`, `decode \"{\\\"xs\\\":[{\\\"a\\\":\\\"x\\\"}]}\" : w`. DEFINITION OF DONE: a regression sample with an array of a record holding a union field, created at runtime size, set and read back, agrees with C on Rust (exit code + stdout); the existing array-create rows are unchanged. FIX OPTIONS: (a) a union with at least one payload-free case gets `impl Default` returning that case (option's None), which is sound because array create's slots are overwritten before any read on every backend that matches C; (b) emit array create without Default (Vec::with_capacity, then a push of the element's zero per slot, from the same zero expressions the other backends use). (a) is the smaller change and also fixes nested heaps. TYPEFEATURESET: the default case is chosen by a typed rule over the union's case list (first payload-free case, else every field defaultable), never by a name such as 'None'. NEXT STEP: reproduce with the minimal sample on the installed compiler (one Rust compile + rustc), then read codegenRust's Default emission to apply (a).")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_2 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T21:22Z", "compiler", "11-01 17:22 compiler: REPRODUCED AND ROOT-CAUSED. Sample samples/rust_union_default_array_create (landed unstaged): union opt = Nothing | Just : string; `create n` of array (string * opt * bool), set both slots, read slot 0. Expected 7. On node t1101 with the installed pack15a: C exits 7; Rust fails with E0599 on `vec![<(Rc<str>, US0, bool)>::default(); v0 as usize]`. ROOT CAUSE: the union DOES get a Default body (rust_union_default uses the first case, a payload-free Nothing), but the pass that keeps only reached impls (codegenRust's tail, regex `(\\w+)>+::default\\(\\)` plus reach_defaults) only sees `<Name>::default()`. For a tuple element `<(Rc<str>, US0, bool)>::default()` the character before '>' is ')', so nothing is reached and US0's impl is dropped. So x's fix options (Vec::with_capacity, or deriving Default only where possible) are not needed: the impl already exists. FIX: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE\\1-reach-defaults-inside-tuples.kitdo, 2 replacements. The regex captures the whole balanced type inside <...>::default() (.NET balancing groups), and every identifier inside it that names a default impl is reached. Unit-checked on the 3 real shapes: the tuple gives '(Rc<str>, US0, bool)', '<US1>::default()' gives 'US1', '<Vec<UH2>>::default()' gives 'Vec<UH2>'. Residual effect: only programs that failed rustc gain impl blocks; a program that compiled already had every reached name. PROOF RUNNING: node job job-1793568095969-compiler-rdef (live core + this program; Rust exit must be 7). It joins the pack after pack15b (whose predict already started), with the sample's C/Rust rows as its gate.")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_3 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T21:36Z", "compiler", "11-01 17:32 compiler: PROVEN. Node job job-1793568095969-compiler-rdef (live core F6F6879566C5A830 + the reach-defaults program; host 98D282B5): samples/rust_union_default_array_create compiles to Rust, the output now carries 'impl Default for US0', and the exe exits 7 = the C oracle (installed: E0599). It rides the pack after pack15b; DONE when that pack's suite shows the sample's Rust row agreeing with C, with no other Rust residual changed except programs that previously failed rustc. x-dumps can then drop the k3s_manifest workaround.")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_4 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:18Z", "compiler", "11-01 19:19 compiler: holds on the pack15c candidate (node job-1793574178127, the 9-program stack): the repro's Rust exe exits 7 = C.")
inl note_of_rust_union_default_array_create_5 () = Note ("RUST-UNION-DEFAULT-ARRAY-CREATE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T00:51Z", "compiler", "11-02 20:5x compiler: DONE. The reach-defaults fix is live (installed since pack15c). Native check on node t1101 with the installed compiler: samples/rust_union_default_array_create emits impl Default for US0, the Rust exe exits 7 and the C exe exits 7 (oracle agrees). The node examples runs today (1981 rows, Rust/C/Zig/Gleam) compile both rows ok. x-dumps can drop the k3s_manifest workaround.")
inl cells_kit_merge_study () = Task ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", "Study merging Cells into kit (user 11-01 17:4x: 'consider merging cells and kit later, kit lane didn't like the idea but this might be the unavoidable direction, gotta experiment and philosophize, with a task so we don't forget'): one runner/job/notebook core across Gleam+Rust, now that iggy (Rust) and k3s join the balance", Story, P2, D5, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,cells,architecture,research,team:main,main,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_kit_merge_study () = Planning ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_kit_merge_study_1 () = Note ("CELLS-KIT-MERGE-STUDY", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:48Z", "main", "main 17:4x: the user's framing. The balance equation now has Gleam and Rust (Spiral backends), iggy (Rust, adopted rather than rewritten), and k3s (adopted, memory-hungry but needed for Windows + WSL + Linux reuse). At SOTA we know what can be rewritten: early on we bound clap, and now lanes prefer from-scratch typefeatureset implementations. DoD: a written comparison (kit's job/window/agile core vs Cells' runner/daemon/notebook core): overlap measured in definitions and lines, the shared typed models (job, run, cell, verdict), the costs of merging versus not (startup, memory, BEAM vs native), and one prototype seam (e.g. kit running a Cells notebook through a typed job, or Cells using kit's job host), measured. Then a decision for the user with a recommendation. The kit lane's objection is recorded as an input, not a veto. Typefeatureset: the merged core's verdict and phase types as GADTs shared by both.")
inl html_repo () = Task ("HTML-REPO", "New repo i574n/html (C:\\home\\git\\html), a from-scratch typefeatureset rewrite of dir-tree-html's roles (tree pages, markdown/README rendering, per-file viewers, notebook pages, later Spiral->TS/Wasm rendering with a leptos/tachys front end). Feature parity first, binaries built in GitHub Actions, then every repo switched to it, then the dir-tree-html repo retired (user 11-01 17:4x)", Epic, P0, D6, 35u32, Planned, "", "html,pages,dir-tree-html,regex,blog,lib,dogfood,team:main,main,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_html_repo () = Planning ("HTML-REPO", Minutes 1200u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_html_repo_1 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:49Z", "main", "main 17:4x, the user's words: 'since dir-tree-html deals also with markdown now and not only the tree, with probably having more roles in the future with rendering inner files with ts compiled from spiral or compiling to rust to use wasm in a leptos/tachys rewrite with the typefeatureset ... i created a new repo called html, we'll take this chance to start over instead of moving dir-tree-html's code, so we model things better considering the typefeatureset and the new lessons ... we gotta have feature parity with dir-tree-html asap, with the binaries being generated in gh actions etc, then adapting all repos, so we can delete the dir-tree-html repo without issues ... html will be another dogfeed challenge, with blog also, the reuse gotta be crazy, knowing what will be kept in lib and which repo will have which in deps, how many pre built binaries we can reuse'. PARITY CHECKLIST (dir-tree-html today, incl. 11-01 work): tree page with sizes and folder details, top README (GFM tables, ordered lists, inline code/links/images/badges/emphasis, \\\\| escape), --viewers per-file pages (.spi/.tsv/.md/.toml/.ps1/...) that never overwrite notebook pages, --self-test, a release binary, used by publish-tree.ps1 across 12 repos. DoD: (1) html renders every repo's Pages byte-equivalent or better (a diff report per repo); (2) GitHub Actions builds and publishes html's binaries (Linux + Windows), and repos download the release instead of building the renderer; (3) all 12 publish-tree callers switched; (4) dir-tree-html archived, with a redirect README. Lane tips: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT\\lane-tips-20261101.md applies here too. Generic pieces (markdown, html escaping, file walk, size labels) are candidates for lib, decided by the reuse metrics (LIB-RESHAPE / KIT-REUSE-METRICS). Typefeatureset: a document model as unions/GADTs (Block, Inline, Viewer, Page), typed exports across crates, nameof instead of string maps.")
inl note_of_html_repo_2 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:38Z", "html", "html 21:3x STATE: C:\\home\\git\\html, unstaged on top of the user's f2dd71c. src/ has 7 Cells notebooks with 44 tests. They passed 44/44 at digest 22318F43 (node job html-cells-3). After the line-width re-lay (kit standards src: 0 findings), 42/44 passed (job html-cells-4). The 2 failures came from a parenthesised _assert_eq argument split over two lines. Moving those two expectations into fixture functions fixed it: render+pages 14/14 (job html-cells-6, digest F0A34AA5); the other 5 files passed 30/30 unchanged in cells-4. PARITY: byte-identical with dir-tree-html on 232/232 pages (HTML-PARITY n2). OPEN: the 1000-line gate (markdown/entry.rs 2169, cli/html.rs 1701 lines). The generated .rs files in the tree are stale box builds, and build.ps1 regenerates them. The first GitHub run needs the user's push and the Pages setting. LESSON: one of my box probes ran with C:\\home\\git\\alphabet as the cwd and left a stray file `x` there. Main moved it to drafts\\html\\HTML-REPO\\strays. From now on, probes run from the drafts folder and use absolute output paths. NEXT, in order: (1) split the markdown and cli crates (HTML-CLI n2); (2) the user pushes and we watch CI; (3) the release job (HTML-CI-RELEASE); (4) spiral/scripts/html.ps1 and the 12 callers (HTML-ADOPT-REPOS); (5) lib lands for html escaping and size labels (HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES).")
inl note_of_html_repo_3 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: GIT CONDITION RE-CHECKED from the tree (groom of user waits). A read-only survey at 09:4x shows every active repo 0 commits ahead of origin: the user committed and pushed alphabet, blog, dice, dir-tree-html, kit, fiscal, html, polyglot, regex, spiral, tibia and x in the last 1-3 h. i574n.github.io is the exception (3 unstaged files, last commit 2 years ago). So this item's user step is probably MET. What is left is deterministic and belongs to the owner, not the user: confirm the step's files are in HEAD (git log -- <paths>) and that CI on HEAD is green (gh run list --commit <HEAD>), then close it. Only a red or missing file sends it back to the user queue. Pages enablement (HTML, REGEX-BENCH-PAGE) is a real user step, since it is a public repo setting.")
inl note_of_html_repo_4 () = Note ("HTML-REPO", 4u32, "2026-11-02T14:28Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: Same rule as HTML-CI-RELEASE (Pages once the gh-pages branch exists, then 200). BACKUP/UNDO: Undo: gh api -X DELETE repos/i574n/html/pages. OWNER: main.")
