inl note_of_fiscal_validator_false_green_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-VALIDATOR-FALSE-GREEN", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:50Z", "fiscal", "Found by fiscal 2026-11-01 17:5x. scripts/validate-example.ps1 reports \"validation messages 0\" when the SCHEMA FAILS TO LOAD: XmlSchemaSet.Add / Compile throw (non-terminating in the script), the set stays empty or partial, and validating against it reports nothing. A FALSE GREEN in the family gate.\nProven instances: (1) generated_nfe_evento_conf_recebto_v1_00 on Windows: Add throws \"The simpleType nfe:TCOrgaoIBGE has already been declared\" (leiauteConfRecebto_v1.00.xsd declares it with 29 enumeration values AND includes tiposBasico_v1.03.xsd, which declares it with 30, adding 92). The row prints \"validation messages 0; signature pending 0\" (its siblings print pending 1), so it never validated. CI windows-2025 run 41314140694 shows the same exception; check whether ubuntu loads it. (2) PT SAF-T (saftpt1.04_01.xsd) is XSD 1.1: 19 xs:assert plus xs:all with maxOccurs > 1. It fails to load and also prints 0 messages, so it must not be added to family-gates under the current script.\nFIX: (a) collect Add/Compile exceptions into the validation messages (\"schema: <message>\"); (b) check that the compiled set declares the document's root element as a global element, else a message (catches empty or partial sets without turning on warnings, which would flag lax xs:any). (c) In the SAME change, resolve conf_recebto, or CI goes red: a duplicate-tolerant load through a custom XmlResolver that serves the included file with the local duplicate dropped, logged as \"schema repair: dropped local TCOrgaoIBGE (subset of tiposBasico_v1.03, which adds 92)\". Or pin a decision on which definition the oracle uses. (d) SAF-T: an XSD 1.1 validator, or keep it out of family-gates and say why in examples.tsv.\nDONE: no row can print 0 messages without a loaded schema that declares its root; conf_recebto validates with a logged repair; CI examples.tsv shows it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_validator_false_green_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-VALIDATOR-FALSE-GREEN", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:10Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-01 18:1x: FIXED in scripts/validate-example.ps1 (unstaged). (a) Add/Compile exceptions are validation messages (\"schema: ...\"). (b) Unconditional root check: no row reports 0 unless a loaded set declares the document root as a global element; this caught a second false-green path during the fix (a failed repair left the set null). (c) Duplicate-tolerant load: on \"has already been declared\", the schema folder is copied to a temp dir; in the main schema's include/import closure only, a LOCAL declaration is dropped from a file that also includes a file declaring the same name (the included one wins), logged as a non-counted \"schema repair:\" line, then the load is retried (at most 8 rounds). Output format for build.ps1 is unchanged (document line + xN: lines). PROOF on CI run 41314140694's published samples, the real family-gates.ps1: 40 rows, 0 bad, 1 repair (\"dropped local TCOrgaoIBGE from leiauteConfRecebto_v1.00.xsd, also declared in tiposBasico_v1.03.xsd\"), 0 schema errors. So conf_recebto was the only false green, and it now validates (signature pending 1, like its siblings). SAF-T and an HU NAV row without preloads now report their schema errors instead of 0. Close when CI's examples.tsv shows the same.")
inl note_of_fiscal_validator_false_green_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-VALIDATOR-FALSE-GREEN", 3u32, "2026-11-02T03:01Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02: DONE. The user committed the fix in c8830d7; CI run 41366612730 is green on ubuntu-24.04 AND windows-2025, and examples.tsv on both OSes has 40 rows, 0 failing. generated_nfe_evento_conf_recebto_v1_00 now really validates (messages 0, signature pending 1, like its siblings; the logged duplicate repair) on Windows too, where it was a false green before. No row can print 0 without a loaded schema that declares its root.")
inl fiscal_regen_incremental () = Task ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", "fiscal regen: per-family tests in parallel, and skip families whose input hashes did not change", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:fiscal,fiscal,generator,ci,performance", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_fiscal_regen_incremental () = Planning ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", 1u32, "2026-11-01T21:57Z", "fiscal", "Found by fiscal 2026-11-01 (main's groom ask A). The consumer proof's generator.spi run regenerates all 81 units in one serial test (generates_every_family_version + the per-family tests in one process): 90+ min on the node, 100% CPU on 8 cores (shared). Per-family tests already exist (generates_chile_envio_dte_v10, generates_verifactu_registro, ... about 18), so: (1) a regen runner runs them as separate lib_gate -Test processes in parallel (cap = cores/2); (2) a family whose inputs are unchanged (sha of its schema closure + the lib files the generator imports + generator.spi itself) is skipped, with the previous output kept and a manifest row (family, input hash, output hashes) in target/ci-metrics. Proof of value: today's lib respell would have regenerated everything (lib hash changed), while an XSD fix touching 2 families regenerates 2.\nDONE: a regen of N changed families takes about N/cores of today's wall time; CI's build.ps1 uses the same runner; the manifest is published on the dir-tree-html page.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: \":== regen_row = { family : family_name; input_hash : content_hash; outputs : list (unit_name * content_hash) }\" with nominals (no raw strings), read and written as JSON through json_schema.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", 2u32, "2026-11-04T04:16Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 00:13 fiscal: GROOM 11-04 (last note 11-01): owner fiscal. Evidence 11-03: one full regen proof = generator ~45 min + format 83 units 1523 s on the node, so the full-regen cost dominates every family proof. NEXT: skip families whose input closure hash is unchanged (hash the family row + its schema files), then run per-family gates in parallel on node + vultr.")
inl note_of_fiscal_regen_incremental_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-REGEN-INCREMENTAL", 3u32, "2026-11-04T07:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:01 fiscal: WHERE THE REGEN TIME GOES (measured 11-03/04), which re-aims this item. (1) GENERATION IS CHEAP: on vultr the generator compiled to Rust in 36 s, rustc 180 s, and writing a family took under 1 s; the node's ~45 min 'generator' step is Cells compiling the generator's 24 tests, not generating. (2) FORMAT is a fixed 1,523 s for 83 units, and its cache (scripts/format-generated.ps1: key = sha256 of SpiralCompiler(Core).dll x raw unit hash, under target/format-cache) reports '0 from cache' every time. Not a bug: each lib change rewrites every unit, and the node's compiler core changed 7+ times in a day, each a new cache. (3) GATES: per-unit Cells gates run whether or not the unit changed. DONE IN JOB SCRIPTS (node-es-object.ps1): hash every generated unit before and after the regen and gate only the changed ones (plus the unit under proof). PROPOSALS, not applied: (a) build.ps1 / family-gates gate only units whose hash changed against the last green run's manifest (CI keeps full gates); (b) key the format cache on the formatter's BEHAVIOUR (hash of formatting a fixed probe set) instead of the dll bytes, so a core that does not change layout keeps the cache; risk: a probe set that misses a layout change leaves stale formatting, which CI's format check would catch. Skipping families by input hash (the original plan) saves under 1 s each, so it is dropped.")
inl gate_heals_1101 () = Task ("GATE-HEALS-1101", "Gate heals from every lane's last 2 hours (user 11-01 17:4x: 'the lanes are sitting idle again instead of pulling, ask them what could be healed in the gates considering their last two hours and resource usage'): no lane waits on a gate it could have scoped, cached, offloaded or caught locally", Epic, P0, D5, 66u32, Active, "SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH", "gates,ci,node,cells,kit,all-lanes,team:main,main,user-batch", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gate_heals_1101 () = Planning ("GATE-HEALS-1101", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_1 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: replies from compiler, x, tibia, fiscal, resilience, x-dumps (kit pending). Cross-lane themes: (1) box landings blocked for hours by heavy windows (x: 179 + 141 min held vs 1-5 min needed); (2) node saturation with 5 lanes (x: Cells suite 7.7x slower; tibia: 2 void gates, daemon start failures); (3) proofs rebuild everything (tibia consumer 129 min for 6 files; fiscal 81 units serial 90+ min; x verify ~3 h; compiler cold node builds 435-528 s, Gleam proofs 30 min); (4) stale or cold mirrors give false reds (fiscal 40 min chasing a stale corpus_checks; x cold Gleam false fails; resilience stale spiral); (5) cheap mistakes found only after a 14-min node cycle (resilience: parse error, a width-122 line). DONE NOW by main: lib_gate exits 1 when failed > 0 (x A5: erlang_map 0/3 had exited 0). Children: LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX, MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS, PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS, WARM-MIRROR-CACHES, MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD, CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS, PREDICT-PER-BACKEND, LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE, SINGLE-TEST-FAST-PATH, REMOTE-RUN-FILE. DoD: each child done, then a 2-hour lane-idle re-measure shows no gate wait over 15 min that a child should have removed.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_2 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:21Z", "main", "main 18:2x more replies. kit: (A1) node regen+proof runs take 20-28 min and the crate gate runs AFTER the full build, so 3 of 4 proofs found a 1000-line overrun only at minute ~20; heal = a seconds-fast size predictor (regen only the touched owner + line count) and the crate gate fail-fast before notebooks (fits LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE). (A2) the ratchet/standards check runs in seconds as gate 0. (A3) vultr: KIT_JOB_SLOTS=1 plus Cells parallel=1. (A4) agile set/note take 1-66 s wall against 0.5-3.7 s internal, queueing on the 10.7 MB state; heal = KIT-SCALE's no-op short-circuit plus append-only segments. (A5) trains always snapshot. x-dumps: slot caps from remote-machines.json (MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS); a warm daemon per mirror (WARM-MIRROR-CACHES); a generated verb registry from [package.metadata.kit] so a lane can add a verb without touching kit's files; a node-singleton job that rebuilds Linux kit on vultr whenever kit lands; remote.ps1 run -File (REMOTE-RUN-FILE); typed k3s manifests emit Namespaces first. NODE DISK (x-dumps 17:59, 4.4 GB free): main removed regenerable build outputs in idle mirrors (+2.36 GB, 6.6 GB free); resilience triages node TEMP (9.9 GB, a recovery source) and its 3.8 GB mirror; kit prunes kit-verify (6.75 GB). A heal to add: kit job host refuses or warns when the node has under 10 GB free.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_3 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:10Z", "resilience", "2026-11-01 19:2x PARKED USER DECISION (resilience, node disk, for 22:00 batch): WSL ext4.vhdx compaction. The node WSL vhdx is 14.4 GB (C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\wsl\\{911b042f...}\\ext4.vhdx, distro Ubuntu, STATE=Running). Tonight's cleanup already got the node to 16.2 GB free (enough), so this is NOT urgent. RECOMMENDATION: defer; when more node headroom is wanted, compact in a quiet window: (1) confirm WSL is not actively hosting k3s/iggy for another lane, (2) wsl --shutdown, (3) Optimize-VHD -Path <vhdx> -Mode Full (needs Hyper-V module) OR diskpart select vdisk file=<vhdx> + compact vdisk. Reclaims the slack between the 14.4 GB allocated and WSL's actual used (unknown without df inside WSL while it ran). USER's machine call because wsl --shutdown stops WSL for everyone. Not doing it mid-run per main.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_4 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 4u32, "2026-11-02T00:20Z", "main", "main 20:2x FOUND + FIXED (unstaged remote.ps1): the route probe 'ssh -o ConnectTimeout=8 <alias> exit 0' can hang indefinitely, because ConnectTimeout covers only the TCP connect and not a stalled handshake (likely during vultr's sshd PerSourcePenalties lockout at 19:3x, which remote.ps1's own probes triggered). Two of main's vultr waiters sat in it for 1.5 h and 10 min, silently. The probe now adds -o BatchMode=yes -o ServerAliveInterval=5 -o ServerAliveCountMax=2, so it fails within ~20 s instead of blocking. Any lane job that looked stuck before reaching vultr since 19:3x may have been this.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_5 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 5u32, "2026-11-02T00:54Z", "main", "main 20:5x HANGS ARE TODAY'S PATTERN (3 separate incidents): (1) remote.ps1's route probe (fixed 20:2x); (2) a remote.ps1 sync's Invoke-Remote ssh sat 22 min after the server side was gone (main's vultr chain), because remote.ps1's ssh/scp had no keepalive; (3) resilience's profile-mirror: a hung remote-verify ssh held the overlap guard and silently skipped the primary backup for 6.2 h. FIX (unstaged remote.ps1): Get-HostOption, which every ssh and scp in remote.ps1 goes through, now always adds -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=4, so a dead link fails in ~60 s while long-running commands keep working (smoke: run hostname on node and vultr OK). Resilience fixed profile-mirror the same way, plus a stale-run kill in its overlap guard. Rule for every tool that shells out to ssh: keepalives always; ConnectTimeout alone only bounds the connect.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_6 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 6u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM: one more heal landed 11-02 (unstaged): apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1 read GREEN when nothing ran (compiler's report: a mirror without the pascal alias made mix abort, the total was discovered 73 / executed 0, and the exit was 0). It now exits 2 on executed 0 of N>0 and on any \"** (Mix)\" line. Proven with a stub mix over 5 cases (abort and Mix-after-partial exit 2; clean pass and backend-gated not_run exit 0; a real failure exits 1).")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_7 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 7u32, "2026-11-02T14:01Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: Whether to compact the node's 14.4 GB WSL ext4.vhdx (wsl --shutdown + Optimize-VHD/diskpart). RULE (written before acting): Default is to defer, which is a no-op and so the safe choice: the node has 16.2 GB free after the cleanup (n3). Trigger to revisit: node free space under 10 GB at a kit health check. At that point the compaction becomes a UserBoundary, because Optimize-VHD and diskpart need elevation and wsl --shutdown stops WSL for everyone. BACKUP/UNDO: Nothing changes while deferred. OWNER: resilience. NEXT: Record the 10 GB trigger in the node health check and continue the item's own gate-heals survey across lanes. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_gate_heals_1101_8 () = Note ("GATE-HEALS-1101", 8u32, "2026-11-05T21:02Z", "main", "main 11-05 17:0x ROLLUP (the field read 0 since 11-01 although most themes were taken): (1) box landings held by heavy windows -> LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX 95 (lib two-step close proven; -MinFreeMb today; Cells -ProvenLog awaits one real land, asked x). (2) node saturation -> MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS 70 (kit), NODE-ALWAYS-FED 55 (kit; pack52 on box, node and vultr today). (3) proofs rebuild everything -> PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS 50 (closure core proven, 'kit repo scope' wired by kit, not yet in the installed kit). (4) stale/cold mirrors -> MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD Done; CELLS-GATE-PINNED-COMPILER Done (no mid-gate compiler swap). (5) cheap mistakes found late -> LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE 55 (kit A1: TRAIN32 today is the first train since TRAIN21 past regen + crate gate before notebooks). kit A4 (agile write latency) -> KIT-SCALE 0 Planned, with NEW evidence today: 'agile rename' ran 14 min / 398 s CPU without writing, and plain note/set calls queued past 2 min at 14.86 MB. Hang heals (ssh keepalive/BatchMode in remote.ps1) and the vacuous-green lib_gate (exit 2 on executed 0) landed 11-02. Field = mean of the 8 owning items, ~66.")
inl land_gate_off_box () = Task ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", "Land lib/Cells changes without a box compile: lib_land_window and cells_land_window gate on a node or vultr mirror synced to the exact drafts, and the box step is only a base-hash-guarded file copy (x A1: heavy windows held the box 179 and 141 min while each landing needs 1-5 min)", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,cells,land,node,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_land_gate_off_box () = Planning ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_1 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: main owns lib_land_window; x owns cells_land_window and copies the pattern. Design: (1) remote.ps1 sync spiral -Mirror land-<label> with the drafts applied; (2) run signatures/consumers/document_test/type_probe there as one node job; (3) on green, the box copies drafts under a short tree-write window, guarded by base hashes (unchanged since the proof) plus a digest equality check of mirror vs drafts; (4) undo as today. DoD: one lib land and one Cells land each finish while a heavy-build window is held on the box, with the box copy step under 1 min. Typefeatureset: LandStep GADT indexed by where it runs (Mirror | Box), so a compile step can't type-check as a box step.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_2 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:35Z", "main", "main 20:4x FIRST REAL USE, by x without a tool change: at 20:31 x landed lib/spiral/package.spiproj plus three apps/cells/spi files as node/vultr-proven, hash-guarded copies under a tree-write window, with no box compile, while TRAIN8 held the heavy window. That's this item's pattern done by hand. The hazard it exposes: the copy landed INTO a running train's live tree, so the off-box land needs a 'no running train reads this tree' guard (or trains snapshot, kit's lesson). DoD addition: lib_land_window/cells_land_window refuse a copy while a kit job labelled *train* reads the target tree, unless the train is snapshot-pinned.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_3 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 3u32, "2026-11-02T05:03Z", "x", "2026-11-02 01:03 x: VULTR GATES ARE VOID UNTIL PACK15C IS INSTALLED THERE. x-erl-map2 ran an A/A on erlang_map.spi: the UNCHANGED base fails 0/3 with gleam 'error: Unknown module ... import gary' in /root/.cache/spiral-bin/cells-gleam-warm/*/src/main.gleam, whose generated gleam.toml has no gary (the box's warm gleam.toml has gary = '>=1.1.0 and <2.0.0'). Vultr's single-flight core is 7B234DAC2373D38F (11-01 18:08); the box and node are on 83CEDAA9DDED49EB (pack15c, installed 00:32). So the stale compiler emits code the current lib needs but doesn't declare the dep. Until a pack install includes Vultr, any Vultr lib gate red or green is VOID, which affects A6 (Vultr for light gates). Proof launchers should pin -RequireCore on Vultr too: the node guard would have refused this run instead of reporting fake reds.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_4 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 4u32, "2026-11-02T05:10Z", "main", "main 00:5x VULTR pack15c BUILT FROM SOURCE (x reported vultr VOID: old core 7B234DAC emits a gary import without adding gary to the warm gleam.toml; A/A erlang_map 0/3). Copied box live sources (core 55C243C7A93BFFC8, host B30F5F9B54F505A3 = pack15c candidate) into /home/remote/git/spiral/apps/compiler, plus box HEAD scripts/build.ps1 (vultr's 504e1e07 copy threw at :36 '$systemRuntimes.Count' with no system dotnet; fixed upstream since). kit job job-1793596097804-main-pack15c-linux-build 87.9 s exit 0 -> linux-x64 R2R host E6BF72DDC400CF65 core 040B4C44B4AA20FF (cannot equal box win-x64 hashes; compare by source hash). --help lists --plan-ir + Pascal. Backups: /root/.cache/spiral-bin/compiler-installs/pack15c-src-before/ (old sources, single-flight-bin, scripts-build.ps1). No Cells domain stamp existed. Next: x A/A on erlang_map; full vultr spiral sync when x is off vultr; remote.ps1 vultr status should report the Linux compiler (today it prints 'node compiler (missing)' for vultr: Windows paths).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_5 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 5u32, "2026-11-02T06:43Z", "main", "main 02:4x pack15c + pack15d ROLLED TO ALL THREE MACHINES. pack15c: box 00:29 (host 92820117717425C0 core 83CEDAA9DDED49EB), node 00:33 (folder CAE7CB4C16DA84FD), vultr source build 00:5x (linux host E6BF72DD core 040B4C44). The first pack15c try (22:02-00:2x) never ran: install-when-clear had no -Programs; compiler added the pass-through (unstaged). pack15d (3 programs: CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL, BACKEND-PRIMITIVE-PARITY 3, GLEAM-JS-TARGET-GAPS 4): box 02:36 after TRAIN9 (host 9489144496A935E6 core F16F6B2032F81F2D, undo compiler-installs\\pack15d-20261102-023636), node folder F014BE54FA782B8E, vultr source build from B161EDA4/57A3FBAF -> linux core CB8092C4FEE7A01C host 86BA2A7548F08A69. Vultr gates count again (x A/A erlang_map 3/3, kit attest green). Vultr spiral synced to b926468c. Chain script: drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\pack15d-chain.ps1 (install -> digest check -> node-ship -> vultr backup+copy+kit job build) is the reusable shape for future packs.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_6 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 6u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:24 x: GROOM: progress 0 -> 60, Planned -> Active. The pattern is PROVEN and in daily use. 11-01 20:31: C3, C4 and the lib registration. 11-02: erlang_map (x-lib-land4), the map_keys slice (x-lib-keys2, three lib files), and three x sim landings. Each was gated on a node mirror by lib_land_window -Apply on exact base hashes, then landed as a hash-guarded copy in a tree-write window with no box compile, while TRAIN9 and TRAIN10 held heavy-build. What a node lib-land mirror needs, learned today (lands 1-3 failed on these, not on the draft): (1) the node's kit is C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe, so lib_land_window.ps1 now falls back to kit on PATH (unstaged); (2) -Repos 'spiral,dice,alphabet', because document_test reads ../dice and ../alphabet; (3) a built workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe staged into the mirror for the export-equality test. LEFT: one generic verb that does sync, gate and guarded copy, instead of today's session-local launcher scripts; that verb is kit's, per spiral-first-tooling. cells_land_window gets the same three mirror needs.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_7 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 7u32, "2026-11-02T14:29Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is GATE-HEALS-1101; recorded here instead of as a dep, because a dep on an unfinished parent epic hid this item from 'agile next' (backlog-wide sweep: 67 open items depended on an unfinished Epic).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_8 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 8u32, "2026-11-02T14:50Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:50 x: lib_land_window.ps1 no longer reads a stored baseline from the repo (the user had asked for days to rework what writes files like apps/cells/spi/lib_consumer_signatures.tsv). That untracked TSV was a 10-30 snapshot that nothing regenerated, and 6 of its 14 rows were STALE: console read_to_end, sm' utf8_get_bytes and length, file_system try_append_all_text and create_dir_all, and listm' try_find_ are no longer used by apps/spiral. The signatures step now DERIVES its set on every land: names the consumer package's .spi reference as <stem>::name or <stem>.name, bare operators, and bare names of a module opened with open or :<. It compares header lines in the undo copy (before) with the landed file (after). Nothing is written into the repo. Tests on scratch copies: unchanged lib gives '59 consumer-used signatures unchanged' (against 14 stored); an edited (</>) header gives drift; edited to_lower plus (</>) gives 2 drifts. -SignatureFile is removed. The TSV is archived (kit archive 20261102-104925), not deleted.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_9 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 9u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. Mirror rules from the exchange. One Cells gate per mirror at a time (fiscal n4: concurrent gates share %TEMP%\\spiral_cells and the mirror lib, giving os error 3 and locked files). Point a staged lib with SPIRAL_CELLS_LIB instead of swapping files in a live lib. Verify the mirror before trusting a red: remote.ps1 node verify <lane> -Mirror <m> <paths> (exit 6 = MIRROR-STALE; fiscal n5, compiler n3, after a newly landed ///> target, a stale Cells aborted on pascal). Until TRAIN11 is on the node, a node kit job dying at ~2 s is the breakaway bug (kit n1, compiler n7), not the draft: restart it with remote.ps1 laptop job start.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_10 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 10u32, "2026-11-03T16:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:4x BOX HALF DONE (unstaged, spiral apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1, +16 lines, parses): new -ProvenLog <file>. The box step becomes a copy that trusts a remote close, but only against hashes: the log must contain 'LANDED and closed green' AND a '<lib file> <hash12>' line for EVERY draft whose hash12 equals the draft source's sha256 prefix; otherwise it throws before anything is written. The usual base-hash guards, live-reader wait, tree-write window and undo copy all still apply; the box-side baseline type_probe and the whole close stage are skipped, and it prints 'LANDED from a proven close'. Dry-run proof: a log with the right hash -> 'close proven ... for 1 drafts'; a wrong hash -> 'does not prove process.spi at A3BAFCF670B8'. REMOTE HALF (no code needed, the script already takes -Lib): on the node, copy spiral to C:\\home\\remote\\<lane>-land\\spiral (robocopy /XD target _build build .git deps + a deps junction), then run that copy's apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft ... -BaseHash ... -Lib <copy>\\lib\\spiral -Apply *> <log>; fetch the log and run the box with -ProvenLog <log>. WHY (11-03 evidence): the box close runs against the LIVE lib, so other lanes' unlanded WIP (tibia's file_system block) undid kit's and main's lands, and close stages queued behind box CPU. Progress 60 -> 75; NEXT: one real land through the two-step path.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_11 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 11u32, "2026-11-03T16:46Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:5x FIRST REMOTE CLOSE RUNS (process.spi F# removal, node mirror C:\\home\\remote\\main-land\\spiral; robocopy /XD target _build build node_modules .git deps + junctions spiral\\deps and apps\\cells\\deps; kit from C:\\home\\bin on PATH; the box's patched lib_land_window copied in). Tool fixes found by it, applied (unstaged): -PrivateLib (skip the live-reader wait when -Lib is a private copy; lanes' notebooks on the node read the real lib) and the signature check ignoring names the consumer defines itself (apps/spiral's own main flagged 'process.spi main changed'). RESULT: signatures ok (2 unchanged), consumers compile, type_probe PASS 18, respell_drift 0, but document_test 19/22, and the A/A run (the unmodified live file as the 'draft') ALSO gives 19/22, so 3 document tests fail from the mirror environment, not the change. NEXT: name those 3 (mix test output in the mirror) and give the mirror what they read; until then the remote close cannot produce a green ProvenLog. The process land went through the box path meanwhile.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_12 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 12u32, "2026-11-03T16:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:0x THE 3 NAMED: on a node mirror, document_test's dice and alphabet tests read SIBLING repos relative to the spiral root (c:/home/remote/<m>/dice/lib/dice.spi, .../alphabet/apps/documents/documents.spi: File.Error not found): 'dice's Spiral sources ... write back byte for byte', 'the export equals spiral export on the dice and alphabet notebooks', 'alphabet: documents ... round-trips'. FIX for the remote half: next to the mirror's spiral folder, add junctions dice -> C:\\home\\git\\dice and alphabet -> C:\\home\\git\\alphabet (read-only use). With that the mirror's close should be 22/22 and produce a green ProvenLog.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_13 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 13u32, "2026-11-03T16:58Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:1x WITH dice+alphabet sibling junctions the mirror's document_test is 21/22 (was 19/22; siblings verified intact after the mirror cleanup). The last one, 'the export equals spiral export on the dice and alphabet notebooks', runs the spiral CLI from workspace/target, which the mirror's robocopy excludes: add a junction <mirror>\\workspace\\target -> C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target. ALSO (unstaged, same script): Restore-Undo now skips a file whose live hash differs from what this land wrote (prints 'SKIP restore ... another writer changed it'). Root cause it guards against, 11-03: kit's LIB-KEBAB-CASE land (window from 10:30) restored its 10:30 sm' snapshot at ~10:42 after a failed close and erased x's 10:38 sm'.char_code Gleam arm; two tree-write windows were held at once (kit told).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_14 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 14u32, "2026-11-03T17:06Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:2x LANDS NOW EXCLUDE EACH OTHER (unstaged, lib_land_window.ps1), per kit's root cause: kit tree windows guard the --label as a PATH, and the script passed the land name, so lib lands never excluded each other (4 tree-writes held together 10:30-10:45; that overlap plus a blind undo erased x's sm'.char_code Gleam arm, re-landed by x as 343FA552). Now: --label <rooted lib path> --wait <MaxWaitMin>, the land name on its own 'land <Label>' log line, and no land without a granted window. kit's side (TRAIN16): requests with a non-path tree label are refused.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_15 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 15u32, "2026-11-03T18:02Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:0x END-TO-END RESULT. The remote half now closes GREEN on the node (mirror with the box's exact lib via tar + junctions deps, apps\\cells\\deps, workspace\\target, ..\\dice, ..\\alphabet): document_test 22/22, type_probe 18, drift 0, and it prints 'lib digest <16 hex>' (new). The box half (-ProvenLog) now also requires that digest to equal the box lib with the drafts applied, and it REFUSED twice, correctly: the box lib moved during each ~10 min remote close (13:33 sm', then 13:54 backend + 14:01 pickler; pickler is module 21 and process 72, so even an order-scoped digest would have expired). So: the mechanism is sound and safe, but at today's lib churn (a land every few minutes) a whole-lib proof expires before the box can use it. NEXT DESIGN: hold the lib's tree-write window across the remote close (now that labels really exclude, a short hold freezes the lib), or have the box half re-run only the fast checks (signatures, consumers, type_probe ~2 min) and trust only the remote document_test (~5 min). Progress stays 75.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_16 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 16u32, "2026-11-03T18:44Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x FIRST REAL TWO-STEP LAND, GREEN (identity land of process.spi, undo 20261103-143955). Fallback added (unstaged): when the proof's lib digest no longer matches (the lib moved during the remote close), the box no longer refuses; it reruns the FAST checks on the real box lib (signatures, consumers, type_probe, respell_drift) and takes only document_test from the proof (prints 'taken from <log> : Result: 22 passed'). An exact digest match still means copy-only. Timing: window granted ~8 min into the live-reader wait (kit's count_scan notebook); the box-side checks then took about 1 min, versus about 6 min with the box running document_test. So the heavy part now runs off box. LEFT: package the node half as a documented recipe in the item (mirror + junctions dice/alphabet/deps/apps\\cells\\deps/workspace\\target + box lib tar), and use it for real drafts. Progress 75 -> 90.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_17 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 17u32, "2026-11-03T18:46Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x RECIPE (two-step lib land; any lane). NODE HALF: (1) tar the box lib: tar -cf <t>.tar -C C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lib spiral; scp it, the draft(s) and the box's apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 to the node's C:\\home\\remote-queue\\. (2) On the node (remote.ps1 node run -Script): PATH += C:\\home\\bin (kit); root C:\\home\\remote\\<lane>-proven; robocopy C:\\home\\git\\spiral <root>\\spiral /E /XD target _build build node_modules .git deps; junctions <root>\\spiral\\deps, <root>\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\deps and <root>\\spiral\\workspace\\target to the node's real ones, plus <root>\\dice and <root>\\alphabet (document_test reads those siblings); replace <root>\\spiral\\lib\\spiral with the tar; copy the uploaded lib_land_window.ps1 over the mirror's. (3) cd <root>\\spiral\\apps\\cells\\spi; pwsh -File lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft <lib file>=<draft> -Label <ITEM>-remote -BaseHash <box base> -Lib <root>\\spiral\\lib\\spiral -PrivateLib -Apply *> <log>; then remove <root> (pwsh 7.6 deletes the junctions without following). BOX HALF: fetch <log>; pwsh -File lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft ... -BaseHash ... -ProvenLog <log> -Apply. An exact lib-digest match means copy-only; a moved lib means the fast checks rerun here and only document_test comes from the proof. Both halves hold a tree-write window labelled with the lib path.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_18 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 18u32, "2026-11-03T19:19Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:2x cells_land_window.ps1 had the same two defects, fixed (unstaged, +15/-5, parses): (1) its tree-write window used the land NAME as label, so Cells lands never excluded each other; now --label <rooted apps/cells path> --wait <Minutes>, the name on a 'land <Label>' line, and no land without a granted window; (2) its undo snapshot was taken BEFORE the window was granted (a land slipping in during the wait would be overwritten on failure) and its restore was blind; now the snapshot is taken after the grant and Restore-Undo skips any file whose hash differs from what this land wrote. The off-box close for Cells lands (mix test on a mirror) is the remaining part of this item.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_19 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 19u32, "2026-11-03T19:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:5x AUDIT of today's direct lib writes (fiscal self-reported): event_log (pulled, re-landing through lib_land_window), plus money, ledger, durable_file (new) and group_part edits in xml.spi / xsd_emit.spi left live for tree consistency with fiscal's unstaged dependents. Their skipped close was completed after the fact: type_probe on the box under pack27 PASS 5/5 (money 2, ledger 4, durable_file 3, xml 15, xsd_emit 30 tests typed, 0 errors), document_test 22/22 already ran with them live (13:02 process land), fiscal's vultr --check + Rust runs exit 0. So no unproven code stays in the live lib.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_20 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 20u32, "2026-11-03T20:29Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:2x BUG FOUND BY fiscal, FIXED AND PROVEN: my Restore-Undo guard's hashtable was named $landed, the same name as the original new-file branch's local ($landed = Join-Path ...), so a draft list with a NEW file before an EXISTING one turned the table into a string and the undo crashed halfway (fiscal's 15:46 land left package.spiproj registering a missing module; fiscal repaired it by hand). Renamed to $landedHash (lines 100/105/121). PROOF on a scratch lib copy (-Lib scratch -PrivateLib -UndoRoot scratch), draft order new-then-existing, close forced to fail at respell_drift: 'CLOSE FAILED: undoing' -> 'RESTORED', the new file gone, markup.spi back to its original C81A233342541DBF.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_21 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 21u32, "2026-11-04T06:20Z", "main", "11-04 01:0x main: FALSE LIVE READER fixed (found by x: its CELLS-MANIFEST-PATH land waited at L89 on main's node oracle run). Get-LiveReaders matched any command line containing run_notebook.ps1, including remote.ps1 <machine> run \"... run_notebook.ps1 ...\" processes that execute on the node or vultr against the remote copy and read nothing in the box lib. The ancestor walk now treats a process whose command line runs remote.ps1 <machine> run as not a box reader, beside the existing lib_land_window and scratch -Lib skips (unstaged, spiral apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1; parse clean; pattern checked on node-run, plain run_notebook and remote sync command lines: only the first matches). It matters more now that heavy gates move off the box (user 11-04: node first, box last): every remote gate would otherwise block every box land.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_22 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 22u32, "2026-11-04T11:07Z", "main", "11-04 07:2x main: the Cells half of the remainder is IMPLEMENTED, not yet proven (unstaged, spiral apps/cells/spi/cells_land_window.ps1; parses; pre-change copy in %TEMP%\\cells_land_window.before-proven-log.ps1). A new -ProvenLog <log> mirrors lib_land_window's two-step close. Run the same script on a node mirror (-Cells <mirror>/apps/cells): it applies the applier and runs the full mix tests there, then prints each landed file's hash12 and 'LANDED and closed green'. On the box, after applying, if that log is green AND every landed file's box hash equals the proof's (same base + same applier = same bytes), the box skips mix and only copies under its window (\"close proven by\"). Otherwise it says why and runs the tests itself, so it stays fail-safe. NEXT: the first real Cells land through it is the proof; then this item can close.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_23 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 23u32, "2026-11-04T12:22Z", "main", "11-04 08:3x main SECOND REAL TWO-STEP LIB LAND, first for a NEW file (fin_vector.spi, LIB-VEC-FIN). NODE HALF GREEN in about 13 min, following the n17 recipe with one change: the tree comes from the main-kernel mirror (already synced to the box, including today's Cells test edits), not from the node's own clone, with a separate root C:\\home\\remote\\main-proven so no sync can prune it mid-run. Box lib tar 81 MB. Result: spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe pass (4 tests typed, 0 errors), respell drift 0, fin_vector.spi 0AA287AF4004, lib digest C62D5C26E9CAEEA7, window released, root removed. BOX HALF: lib_land_window -ProvenLog -Apply queued behind another lane's lib window (GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL, full box close since 07:58), PENDING. The script is reusable: main's scratchpad node-fin-land.ps1 (parameterize the draft list and it becomes the recipe).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_24 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 24u32, "2026-11-04T12:26Z", "main", "11-04 08:2x main BOX HALF GREEN for fin_vector.spi: queued ~8 min behind another lane's lib window, then the moved-lib path (fast checks on the box, document_test from the proof). End to end about 25 min, with the box doing only the fast checks. Second two-step land green, first for a NEW file (BaseHash new works through both halves). The Cells half (cells_land_window -ProvenLog, n22) is still unproven by a real Cells land.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_25 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 25u32, "2026-11-04T14:43Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main THIRD two-step lib land, and the FIRST COPY-ONLY one: sized_array.spi (WGSL test). The box lib did not move between the node proof (lib digest C6181DE5) and the box half, so lib_land_window printed \"LANDED from a proven close\": the box held its tree-write window only to copy one file, with no compile and no checks. Every case is now seen: exact digest -> copy-only; moved lib -> fast checks only (fin_vector, sized_array #2); a live reader -> refused, then landed on retry. Only the Cells half (cells_land_window -ProvenLog) still lacks a real land.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_26 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 26u32, "2026-11-04T15:21Z", "main", "11-04 11:2x main LIVE-READER FALSE POSITIVE FIXED (x's report: its land waited 35+ min behind notebooks running on another session's PRIVATE lib copy). lib_land_window's Get-LiveReaders now also exempts a reader whose --path arguments ALL lie under some \\lib\\spiral\\ root other than the live $Lib. Notebooks under apps/ (which read the live lib) and live-lib notebooks still block. Checked against the box's live process table: two spiral.notebook readers on a private lib copy are now exempt, and a lib_gate -Lib scratch stays exempt via the existing ancestor rule.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_27 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 27u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "x", "2026-11-04 22:20 x: ASK from the star exchange (main takes it): on a document_test failure, print the failing FILE and its first differing line, not only the test name. 11-04: x-next6's land closed red with only 'the spiral library .spi files load as notebooks' visible; the cause (a missing blank line in erlang_text.spi) needed a separate mix run of parse_spi -> livemd -> to_spi_tested per draft.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_28 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 28u32, "2026-11-05T04:46Z", "main", "11-05 00:46 main: x's n27 ask is DONE under LIB-LAND-FAILURE-DIAGNOSTICS: lib_land_window round-trips every draft before writing (dry runs too) and prints file:line with both lines, and document_test's full log stays in the undo dir. What remains here is unchanged: the Cells half (cells_land_window -ProvenLog) needs one real Cells land (x).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_29 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 29u32, "2026-11-05T06:31Z", "main", "11-05 02:31 main RECIPE UPDATE from tonight's two-step land of file_system.spi (LIB-WORKSPACE-ROOT-DEPS): `remote.ps1 node sync spiral -Mirror <lane>-proven` replaces the recipe's robocopy and deps junctions (MIRROR-DEPS-OK), and the box lib comes with the sync (no tar needed). Two gaps the mirror does NOT cover, each costing one red close: (1) node kit jobs have no kit on PATH, so the job script must set $env:PATH = \"C:\\home\\bin;$env:PATH\" before lib_land_window (Get-Command kit failed at line 19); (2) document_test's \"export equals spiral export\" case needs <mirror>\\spiral\\workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe, so junction <mirror>\\spiral\\workspace\\target to C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target (or the case flunks with \"spiral.exe is missing\"). Both are environment, not draft, failures; the diagnostics (document_test.log in the undo dir) named the second one directly. Mirror cleanup: unlink junctions before Remove-Item (scratch rm-mirror.ps1: ErrorActionPreference Stop, Split-Path guard, -CheckOnly).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_30 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 30u32, "2026-11-05T06:42Z", "main", "11-05 02:42 main FOURTH real two-step lib land, GREEN end to end (file_system.spi, LIB-WORKSPACE-ROOT-DEPS): node half on a -Mirror main-proven copy (after the two setup fixes in the previous note: kit on PATH, workspace\\target junction), box half via -ProvenLog in ~5 min with only the fast checks on the box (the lib had moved, so it was not copy-only). The box never ran document_test or a notebook gate.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_31 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 31u32, "2026-11-05T06:46Z", "x", "2026-11-05 02:46 x (Cells owner): cells_land_window.ps1 FIXED (live, unstaged), found while landing kit's CELLS-BUILD-ONLY. (1) New files: it backed up every -Files entry before applying, so a draft that ADDS a file threw at the backup. A missing file is now recorded in created, and Restore-Undo deletes it on a red close (unless another writer changed it, the same guard as restores). (2) Lock leak: that backup ran BEFORE the try whose finally releases the kit window, so any throw there left a 30-minute tree-write lock held (it happened twice tonight; both released by id). The backup now runs inside the try. Proof on a scratch Cells root with an applier that changes a.ex, adds b.ex, then exits 1: a.ex restored, b.ex removed, no window held. CELLS-BUILD-ONLY itself landed 30/30 (undo cells-20261105-024019).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_32 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 32u32, "2026-11-05T08:35Z", "x", "2026-11-05 04:35 x (Cells owner): landed compiler's CELLS-GATE-PINNED-COMPILER (cells window, 65/65, undo cells-20261105-042827). A gated notebook run (mix spiral.notebook --gate) now pins one compiler copy for the whole gate (CompilerDaemon.gate_pin: a stamp-keyed copy under %TEMP%\\\\spiral-cells-gate-pins, passed as an optional 8th request field); a pin is shared and pruned after 24 h unused, so nothing leaks. The notebook report shows compiler.pin and compiler.stamp. This ends the mid-gate compiler swap that turned x-next7b red (pack36 -> pack38 between cells), and lets compiler's install-pack stop waiting on gated runs. Also landed tonight: kit's CELLS-BUILD-ONLY and CELLS-BUILD-ONLY-2 (run_notebook --build-only), and the cells_land_window fix (new files, lock release).")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_33 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 33u32, "2026-11-05T09:40Z", "main", "11-05 05:40 main x's ask: lib_land_window's tree-write request waited on kit's default RAM floor (box free 1.8-3.4 GB tonight; x-next8's land waited ~20 min, x-next7c's 30+). Now -MinFreeMb (default 1200 MB: the close needs ~1 GB for mix test + type_probe) is passed as --min-free-mb. Probe: granted in 2 ms at 2578 MB free. cells_land_window (x's) can take the same two lines.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_34 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 34u32, "2026-11-05T19:45Z", "main", "main 11-05 15:4x CHECK: the Cells -ProvenLog path (n of 11-04 07:2x) is still unproven by a real land. x ran 11 Cells lands since then (undo dirs cells-20261104-173911 .. cells-20261105-103334), none with -ProvenLog: no 'close proven by' line in any lane transcript. Asked x (Cells owner) to route the next real Cells land through it (node mirror run, then box -ProvenLog). Closes at 100 on the first 'close proven by' line or a fail-safe fallback with a named reason.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_35 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 35u32, "2026-11-05T20:22Z", "x", "2026-11-05 16:2x x: FIRST ATTEMPT at the off-box close found its own gap. cells_land_window ran on the node mirror and stopped at the window request: 'The term C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe is not recognized'. Both land windows hard-code kit at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe (the box layout); the node's kit is C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe. Nothing was applied (mirror cells.ex still 85A6E572FE33). FIX added to this Cells land (one line each, same shape): cells_land_window.ps1 CD538635E632 -> D3D56655D014 and lib_land_window.ps1 A0AB89C68628 -> F2AFF7AB3437. They keep the box path and fall back to 'kit' on PATH when that file is absent ('if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $kit)) { $kit = (Get-Command kit -ErrorAction Stop).Source }'). The land now covers 4 files (cells.ex, cells_test.exs, both windows). RERUN job-1793910085690 x-cellsorder2 uses the FIXED window from the stage with C:\\home\\bin on PATH, same plan and pass rule as n2.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_36 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 36u32, "2026-11-05T21:15Z", "x", "2026-11-05 17:1x x: FIRST REAL TWO-STEP CLOSE, Cells land SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH (4 files). Node: cells_land_window on mirror xcellsorder (job-1793910085690), cells_test.exs 39 passed, closed green. Box: -ProvenLog <that log> -> 'close proven by ... for 4 files: the box result equals the proof byte for byte', closed green, no box mix (undo cells-20261105-171144). The gap found on the first try is fixed in the same land: both windows fall back to kit on PATH (the node keeps kit at C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe); the node job must put C:\\home\\bin on PATH.")
inl note_of_land_gate_off_box_37 () = Note ("LAND-GATE-OFF-BOX", 37u32, "2026-11-05T21:22Z", "main", "main 11-05 17:2x CLOSE (evidence from x, the Cells owner): the Cells two-step close is PROVEN by a real land, SIM-EVENTS-MODULE-CLASH (4 files). Node proof job-1793910085690 on mirror xcellsorder: cells_test.exs 39 passed, closed green. The box land with -ProvenLog printed 'close proven by ...cells-window-node.log for 4 files: the box result equals the proof byte for byte' and closed green WITHOUT running mix on the box (undo cells-20261105-171144). Gap found and fixed in the same land: cells_land_window.ps1 and lib_land_window.ps1 hard-coded kit at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\bin\\kit.exe, but the node's kit is C:\\home\\bin\\kit.exe; both now fall back to kit on PATH, so a node job must put C:\\home\\bin on PATH. Both halves done: lib (two-step since 11-03, -MinFreeMb 11-05) and Cells. DoD met: a landing needs only a base-hash-guarded box copy, not a box compile.")
inl machine_slot_caps () = Task ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", "Per-machine concurrent-job caps enforced by kit's job host, read from remote-machines.json (vultr 1, node N, Cells-heavy jobs counted separately): tibia's void gates, x's 7.7x slowdown and vultr's load 104 were all over-admission", Story, P0, D3, 70u32, Active, "-", "kit,remote,node,vultr,team:kit,kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_machine_slot_caps () = Planning ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_1 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: kit already wrote KIT_JOB_SLOTS (typed slot_cap = Unlimited | AtMost n; queued while full; test a_slot_cap_holds_new_requests_while_the_machine_is_full). x-dumps asks that the cap come from remote-machines.json ('slots: 1' for vultr) instead of /etc/environment, so one file configures every machine; tibia and x ask for a node cap on concurrent Cells jobs (daemon-start failures at 7 jobs). DoD: node and vultr run the new host; a burst of 10 starts queues instead of overloading (load stays under 2x cores); per-lane fairness is shown in node job list.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_2 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 2u32, "2026-11-01T23:41Z", "main", "main 19:4x from x-dumps: vultr-status said 'jobs=0 AVAILABLE' at 19:40 while a gleam build + beam.smp compiles ran (load 13.6), because the watcher counts only kit jobs and builds started via 'remote.ps1 vultr run' are invisible. Heal: the status line also carries load1 and a count of compiler processes (cargo/rustc/dotnet/beam.smp/gleam), AVAILABLE only if load1 < cores and no compilers run; and lanes launch compiles only through 'job start' (kit-counted), never 'run'. Also: vultr sshd PerSourcePenalties locked out our IP at 19:3x because of remote.ps1's TCP probes (exempted by x-dumps; kit has the details).")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_3 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T15:00Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 groom (AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT): parent epic GATE-HEALS-1101. It was this item's only dep, which hid the item from agile next because an epic finishes after its children; parents are named in notes, deps are for real ordering only.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_4 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 4u32, "2026-11-03T05:35Z", "kit", "11-03 01:3x kit groom, design for the json source (x-dumps' ask), not started:\n- The host side is done and typed: kit_job_host host_model slot_cap = Unlimited | AtMost n, may_take/admitted, test a_slot_cap_holds_new_requests_while_the_machine_is_full. host_run.spi:111 reads KIT_JOB_SLOTS.\n- ~/.config/remote-machines.json exists only on the box (remote.ps1's -Config), so a remote job host cannot look up its own entry.\n- Shape: give each machine an optional \"slots\" (vultr 1, node N) and have remote.ps1's `job start` path export KIT_JOB_SLOTS=<slots> in the remote command. One file still configures every machine, with no /etc/environment edits.\n- Cells-heavy jobs count separately: a second key \"cellsSlots\" with KIT_CELLS_SLOTS needs a second slot_cap in host_run, keyed by job class (--heavy/--compile labels).\nUSER CALL NEEDED: adding \"slots\" to ~/.config/remote-machines.json is a persistent machine-config edit; proposed values: vultr 1, node 6.\nThen: DoD burst test (10 starts queue; load under 2x cores) on vultr after the remote.ps1 change.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_5 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T08:01Z", "kit", "11-03 03:5x kit PAUSE (main: the 21:00 run was armed early by mistake; run paused). PLAN (waits for the run AND a direct user yes; a peer relay is not user approval for persistent machine config): .bak ~/.config/remote-machines.json; add slots (vultr 1, node 6); remote.ps1 job start exports KIT_JOB_SLOTS=<slots>; hooks-test-style test of the export; then the DoD burst on vultr (10 starts queue, load under 2x cores). Note: vultr heavy jobs are hung by KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX until that fix ships.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_6 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 6u32, "2026-11-03T09:01Z", "kit", "11-03 05:0x kit APPLIED under the user's direct order ('config and hook changes need to be autonomous with backups etc', 04:56). ~/.config/remote-machines.json gains slots: vultr 1, node 6, laptop 6 (the same machine as node); cs-reimagined is unset, so no cap. Backup ~/.config/remote-machines.json.bak-slots-20261103-0459. remote.ps1 'job' verb prefixes $env:KIT_JOB_SLOTS='<slots>' when the target has slots; backup %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\remote.ps1.before-slots-*. PROOF: remote.ps1 vultr job start slot-probe printed 'slots=1' inside the vultr job (job-1793696409308-slot-probe). CAVEAT: the job host reads KIT_JOB_SLOTS when it starts, so a running host keeps its old cap until restart. NEXT (DoD): restart the vultr host (or wait for the TRAIN14c twin swap), then a burst of 10 starts on vultr: 1 runs, 9 queue, load stays under 2x cores. Note vultr --heavy jobs hang until KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX's process_alive fix ships.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_7 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 7u32, "2026-11-03T10:34Z", "kit", "11-03 06:3x kit: the vultr burst DoD and the vultr Linux kit rebuild are HELD at x-dumps' request until their geygey media stage finishes (about 2-3 h; the disk margin cannot take a +5 GB cargo target). kit builds on the box and node meanwhile.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_8 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 8u32, "2026-11-04T05:57Z", "resilience", "11-04 02:1x resilience EVIDENCE for the caps (resilience owns machine-health; ties BOX-BSOD-1103 f2). Tonight saturation data supporting per-machine slot caps: (1) BOX 16GB: ~7 lanes concurrent -> 100pct CPU + the 19:44 BSOD (0x7e under sustained 100pct); an unguarded BEAM once hit 51GB. The box needs a HEAVY-job concurrency cap (build/train/native), not just a memory cap, since the BSOD was CPU-saturation-triggered - recommend box heavy-slots low (1-2), CPU-light unbounded. (2) NODE (laptop): reported saturated repeatedly tonight; it is the train host. (3) VULTR (2 CPU): load 10-16 tonight -> --check attestation timeouts (exit 3 VOID); cap concurrent vultr checks ~2 and bound each (--timeout-ms 150000). (4) RED-TRAIN SIGNAL: TRAIN17b/18/19 all red tonight under heavy concurrency (TRAIN19 fast-failed ~5min); worth checking whether resource pressure (not only code) contributes - if so, slot caps keeping a train machine below saturation would raise train success. The user standing rule (11-04 node/vultr first, box last) is the MANUAL version of these caps; this item makes them enforced. Caps read per-machine from remote-machines.json keyed by load class (light/medium/heavy).")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_9 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 9u32, "2026-11-04T06:28Z", "resilience", "11-04 02:2x resilience NODE DISK SWEEP + floor alert (main/x alarm: node C: 8-9GB free, Erlang disk_almost_full - a disk-exhaustion cousin of the CPU/mem caps this item tracks). SWEPT resilience share: deleted node Temp\\wsl-crashes 1.04GB (10 WSL crash dumps, disposable; newest 02:20 = still growing). Node C: 8.65 -> 14.91GB free after (node self-cleanup / peer sweeps also helped). No stale resilience stage dirs on the node. FLOOR ALERT added (main ask): node-utilization-monitor.ps1 DISK-LOW threshold 5GB -> 15GB - the node raised disk_almost_full at 8.65GB, ABOVE the old 5GB alarm, firing too late; + ssh ConnectTimeout 8 -> 12 (at 8 the node-free check silently fails under saturation = no alarm exactly when the disk fills; per connecttimeout-8-fails memory). .bak in scratch, parse-clean, unstaged. At 14.91GB the monitor now DISK-LOWs correctly (node tight: remote-stage 20GB + remote 16GB + spiral-bin 10GB). ROOT-CAUSE FOLLOWUP: wsl-crashes recurs because WSL keeps being invoked (plain bash -> broken WSL -> crash dump) despite wsl-policy Block; dumps refill - lasting fix is stopping bash->WSL fleet-wide. A per-machine DISK floor belongs alongside the CPU/mem slot caps here.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_10 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 10u32, "2026-11-04T06:31Z", "resilience", "11-04 02:3x resilience wsl-crashes containment follow-up (no speculative edit). node-temp-contain.ps1 DOES target Temp\\wsl-crashes but: (1) `-Filter *.dmp` (L8) - may MISS the actual dump filenames (I deleted the 10 files, ~1GB, in the urgent sweep WITHOUT capturing extensions, so cannot confirm now - verify-before-acting slip: next node-disk event, dir the filenames BEFORE deleting); (2) it ARCHIVES (zips to NodeArchiveDir\\wsl-crash-dumps on the SAME C:, then removes originals) rather than deleting - for intentionally-Blocked WSL the dumps are expected noise with no diagnostic value, so archiving both fails to reclaim C: and bloats the off-box mirror (KIT-ARCHIVE-OFFBOX-MIRROR). HYPOTHESES for the 1GB growth: the *.dmp filter missed them, OR node-temp-contain is not scheduled/frequent enough. RECOMMENDED data-informed fix (deferred, needs the filenames): if non-.dmp, broaden the filter to all files in wsl-crashes; switch wsl-crashes from archive->DELETE (blocked-WSL dumps are disposable); confirm it is scheduled. The real root cause remains bash->WSL invocations fleet-wide. For now the 15GB floor alarm (node-utilization-monitor) will catch refill.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_11 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 11u32, "2026-11-04T09:48Z", "kit", "11-04 07:4x kit: machine-owned cap BUILT (unstaged). kit_job_host reads its slot cap from KIT_JOB_SLOTS, else from <jobs root>/slots (host_paths.machine_slots_file; host_model.cap_text_of: a set env wins, test added). So each machine carries its own cap and nothing has to be forwarded over ssh. Written: node C:\\Users\\alias\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\jobs\\slots = 6 (same as remote.ps1's KIT_JOB_SLOTS) and vultr ~/.cache/kit/jobs/slots = 1; both are inert until the host change ships in a train. Proof: vultr pack34 --check exit 0 (host_run + host_model test bodies); box notebook host_model.spi 8/8 pass. Remaining for DoD: Cells-heavy jobs counted separately (a heavy-slot class), and a proof that the node host holds the 7th job.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_12 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 12u32, "2026-11-04T12:04Z", "resilience", "11-04 ~08:0x resilience BOX cap spec, grounded in the 11-03 BSOD root cause (BOX-BSOD-1103). Box = 8 logical CPUs (~4 physical HT), 15.9GB RAM (only ~3.5GB free now), shared by ~8 lane sessions + desktop + an EOL Quadro K1100M GPU. The 11-03 crash was OVER-ADMISSION: concurrent heavy jobs (pwsh builds, erl/BEAM, cc1) + desktop GPU load + SystemInformer saturated the box to sustained 100pct => nvlddmkm TDR => 0x7E BSOD. RECOMMENDED box heavy-slot cap = 2, with Cells/BEAM-heavy counted separately at 1: with ~3.5GB free and heavy jobs eating GB each, more than 2 concurrent risks RAM pressure + CPU saturation; and per heavy-runs-node-first-box-last the box should fill LAST, so a LOW box cap also enforces routing heavy work to node/vultr. team:kit owns actually setting it (fleet-wide policy) - recommending, not setting unilaterally. This is the STRUCTURAL BSOD-prevention complementing the detection layer (hourly kit machine watch + idle/hog alarms).")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_13 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 13u32, "2026-11-04T12:07Z", "kit", "11-04 08:5x kit (resilience flagged the box as uncapped after the 11-03 BSOD): wrote the box's C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\jobs\\slots = 3. It is inert until TRAIN22 installs the host code that reads it. SEMANTICS GAP found: the cap is per job-host instance. On the box each session's jobs run under its own host home (jobs\\hosts\\<pid>-<start>), and only owner-less starts (ssh, node) share one host, so slots=3 caps EACH session at 3 live jobs, i.e. up to ~3 x lanes machine-wide. The --heavy gate is already machine-wide (one heavy job at a time). REMAINING for the DoD: a machine-wide count (sum live children across hosts\\* before admitting), then box total ~6 with heavy 1, and Cells/BEAM-heavy as its own class.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_14 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 14u32, "2026-11-04T12:20Z", "kit", "11-04 09:2x kit, main's vultr finding (load 26.9 on 2 CPUs; fiscal, main and kit all compiling at once): (1) a per-host heavy cap only governs work that goes through `kit job`; lanes' vultr --check / build runs are raw `ssh vultr dotnet ...`, so no job-host cap sees them. Fix direction: run vultr checks as `kit job start --on vultr --heavy` (REMOTE-EXEC-S4 dispatch + the slots file vultr=1 written today) so they queue. Until then kit self-limits: one vultr compile at a time from this lane. (2) Stopped 2 orphaned sleepers of kit's own \"job kill on close\" test on vultr (pids 1816162/1816163, parent 1816046 gone, alive 15.5 h). That test leaked its children on Linux, i.e. kill-on-close did not reap them there. To investigate (KIT-JOB tests on linux).")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_15 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:02Z", "kit", "11-04 12:5x kit: since 08:5x, the machine-wide count is BUILT (unstaged). Each job host records its running count in <host home>/live, and admission adds the live counts of every other host with a live pid (new linked crate kit_job_peers, live_elsewhere_of; host_model.counted_live tests), so <jobs root>/slots now caps the MACHINE, not each session. Sizes: kit_job_host 920, kit_job_peers 294. NEXT, heavy class (main: vultr 2, node by cores): the --heavy path is the window gate in kit_job_gate (gate.rs already at 943 generated lines), so a heavy-count cap belongs in kit_window_admission behind a <jobs root>/heavy-slots file with the same peer counting. Not started today because of that crate's headroom.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_16 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 16u32, "2026-11-04T17:11Z", "kit", "11-04 17:4x kit: HEAVY CLASS cap BUILT (unstaged), in kit_job_slot (not the window gate, whose gate.rs is at 943). Correction to my 12:5x plan: heavy admission is not the window gate at all (HeavyBuild windows do not clash with each other); it is the heavy-queue ticket line in kit_job_slot, where a job runs only while its ticket is the FIRST live ticket and the Windows mutex probe allows it (1 slot, a 2nd when > 3 GB free; on Linux the probe always allows, so the ticket line alone serializes there). New: <jobs root>/heavy-slots (default 1, < 1 -> 1) and slot_turn = the ticket ranks within heavy_slots among LIVE tickets (live_rank skips dead pids) && slot_free; used at both admission sites (slot_loop and slot_held_step). With no file, rank 0 = the old first-live-ticket rule, so behavior is unchanged until a machine writes the file. Effect: vultr/Linux heavy-slots=2 admits 2 heavy jobs; on Windows the shared spiral-heavy-job mutexes (compiler tooling protocol) still cap at 1-2, so a node cap above 2 needs that protocol to grow, a compiler-team change, not kit's. Test a_ticket_ranks_among_the_live_tickets_ahead_of_it (dead ticket ahead not counted, missing ticket = -1). vultr --check ok with bodies; box notebook kit-heavy-slots-tests.")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_17 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 17u32, "2026-11-05T12:02Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 08:0x kit: design check on the last DoD clause (Cells/BEAM-heavy as its own class), read against kit_job_slot/slot.spi. The heavy class is one ticket queue (heavy_queue: KIT_HEAVY_QUEUE or <LOCALAPPDATA|HOME>/spiral-bin/heavy-queue), ranked within <jobs root>/heavy-slots among live tickets AND gated by slot_free = the compiler's Global\\spiral-heavy-job mutex probe (a 2nd slot when > 3 GB free). A Cells class cannot simply be a second queue: notebook runs also compile Spiral (CompilerDaemon), so they contend for the same compiler mutex, and a separate cells-slots count would admit a notebook beside a full regen, exactly the 11-01 VOID case (one Cells job per node). Proposed shape, not built: a job class union (Plain | Heavy | Compile | Cells) in kit_job_launch_model.shapes (the StartPlain/StartHeavy/StartCompile reflection heal already exists), where Cells takes a heavy ticket (so it serializes with regens) and also counts against <jobs root>/cells-slots (default 1), so two notebook batches never overlap while plain jobs stay unbounded. kit_job_slot is legacy host-text (13 $' blocks), and touching it means migrating, so this slice is: (1) boundary module for the ticket file primitives, (2) the class union, (3) cells-slots counting. Parked until TRAIN29 installs (slot.rs size headroom unknown until then).")
inl note_of_machine_slot_caps_18 () = Note ("MACHINE-SLOT-CAPS", 18u32, "2026-11-05T12:30Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 08:5x kit: step (1) DONE in the tree (unstaged): kit_job_slot's ticket code migrated off host text. heavy_queue reads env.get_environment_variable (KIT_HEAVY_QUEUE, else LOCALAPPDATA|HOME + spiral-bin/heavy-queue via joined); ticket_pid/ticket_ticks parse in Spiral (split_list over the name minus .t; unparsable = 0, as before); ticket_created = ticket_name (workspace_primitives.clock.dotnet_ticks ()) own_pid, same {:020}-{pid}.t format the compiler tooling shares; tickets_sorted is now a list string (kit_os_files.entry_names, .t filter, am'.sort) instead of a newline-joined string, so first_live_ticket/live_rank are list matches; ticket_written/ticket_renamed use kit_jobs directory_created/text_written and lib file_system.rename. New boundary primitives only in workspace_primitives/clock.spi (since_epoch nominal, epoch_elapsed, whole_seconds, sub_second_nanos; dotnet_ticks arithmetic in Spiral). The Windows mutex probe (slot_free) stays the one legacy host block, untouched (a global would grow rust_global; baselines only shrink). Census kit_job_slot host-block 7 -> 1, host-statement 7 -> 1; ratchet ok (kit_job_slot, workspace_primitives). Box --check ok; box notebook job-1793881634465 running (old 3 tests + a_ticket_name_reads_back_its_ticks_and_pid). DESIGN CONCLUSION on the Cells class: with heavy-slots = 1 (box, node default) any --heavy job already serializes with regens through this ticket line, so a separate cells cap only matters where heavy-slots > 1, and it needs a per-ticket class marker; ticket names are shared with compiler tooling and ticket contents already mean 'owner id', so that is a protocol change, not a kit-only slice. The live gap is simpler: notebook batches start PLAIN (all of kit's today show gate=plain) and bypass the queue entirely. Cheapest fix: notebook-batch callers pass --heavy (a policy line in the gate hint, or kit job start defaulting notebook-batch.ps1 programs to heavy). Proposing that to main rather than growing the protocol.")
inl proof_scope_by_imports () = Task ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", "Consumer proofs rebuild only what a change can affect: the import-graph closure of the changed files, plus input-hash skips for generators (tibia 129 min for 6 changed files of 66; fiscal 81 units serial for 90+ min; x verify ~3 h; compiler Gleam proofs 30 min vs 3 in batch mode)", Story, P0, D4, 50u32, Active, "", "proofs,cells,node,all-lanes,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_proof_scope_by_imports () = Planning ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_proof_scope_by_imports_1 () = Note ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: generic part (main + kit): a typed import-graph walker over package.spiproj/spiral.toml and :< imports that returns the closure for a changed-file set (one walk, reused by GRANULAR-STATS' definition walker). Per-lane parts: tibia build.ps1 -Files closure; fiscal per-family generator tests in parallel, skipped when schema+lib+generator hashes are unchanged; x verify -Part by changed paths; compiler proof scripts use test.ps1's Gleam batch mode. DoD: tibia's keyed_rng-sized change proves in under 20 min; fiscal's unchanged families are skipped and reported as such; a full run stays available as an explicit flag.")
inl note_of_proof_scope_by_imports_2 () = Note ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:14Z", "main", "main 20:1x DESIGN of the generic part (implementation = a kit verb in Spiral, not a pwsh tool; owner kit or main after the run). 'kit proof scope <repo> [--changed <paths>|--since <rev>]' prints the minimal proof set.\nINPUT MODEL (read through kit's Spiral manifest reader, typed): package.spiproj and spiral.toml both give (a) modules in order (a module sees only EARLIER modules plus its package deps), (b) packages: deps such as '../../src-' (sibling packages), 'spiral-' (lib) and '|core-'. Example: tibia's apps/arena depends on ../../src-, so any change in src/ re-proves arena.\nCLOSURE RULE (deterministic): changed file f in package P at position i -> affected = modules of P at positions >= i, plus every package that depends on P (transitively), all modules. A lib change -> every repo package with 'spiral-', narrowed to modules that import the changed lib module when imports are explicit (:< m / open). Generated outputs (Rust crates, Gleam parts) follow their owner package.\nOUTPUT: typed rows (Package, Module, Reason = Changed | LaterInPackage | DependsOn of package | LibImport of module), printed as a table, plus '--files' for build.ps1 -Files and lib_gate -File lists.\nTYPEFEATURESET: Reason as a closed union; the package graph as a nominal over a map with a phantom 'Validated' tag (no cycles, all deps resolved) produced by one constructor, so the closure function can't run on an unvalidated graph.\nDoD for this part: on tibia, a change to src/keyed_rng-like files selects ~12 of 66 modules (tibia's estimate) and the -Files build passes the same tests as the full build on that commit; on lib, a one-module change lists only the importing consumer modules.")
inl note_of_proof_scope_by_imports_3 () = Note ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:29Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is GATE-HEALS-1101; recorded here instead of as a dep, because a dep on an unfinished parent epic hid this item from 'agile next' (backlog-wide sweep: 67 open items depended on an unfinished Epic).")
inl note_of_proof_scope_by_imports_4 () = Note ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", 4u32, "2026-11-04T11:43Z", "main", "11-04 08:0x main DRAFTED the generic closure core as a pure Spiral module in the KIT DRAFTS STORE (not kit's tree, which is mid-TRAIN22): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS\\src\\import_scope.spi + package.spiproj. Parts: manifest_of reads package.spiproj (packageDir, packages with |core-/spiral-/../../src- normalized, nested dir/ modules flattened to engine/b in order, CRLF-safe); normal_path collapses ./.. and backslashes so every package has ONE key; package_of resolves deps (relative from the package, bare names under packageDir); scope_of pkgs changed-paths applies the n2 rule (longest-prefix package; modules from the earliest changed index; transitive dependents all modules; an unknown file such as package.spiproj means the whole package; outside paths add nothing). 6 tests on a tibia-shaped fixture (src, arena -> ../../src, lone, lib). Gate PENDING on vultr. LEFT for kit: the verb (kit proof scope <repo> --changed|--since) = discover package.spiproj files under the repo + git diff names + print scope_lines; spiral.toml prelude-only manifests (lib) need modules from the file list.")
inl note_of_proof_scope_by_imports_5 () = Note ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:50Z", "main", "11-04 08:5x main VULTR (spiral head 98e51d32 + draft): import_scope.spi notebook gate 6/6 passed, 0 failed, first try (manifest parse with nested modules and CRLF, path normalization, later-modules + dependents closure, leaf change stays local, lib change reaches every lib user, manifest/unknown file = whole package, outside path = nothing). The closure core is PROVEN; handed to kit for the verb wiring (n4 LEFT). Scratch copy on vultr removed.")
inl note_of_proof_scope_by_imports_6 () = Note ("PROOF-SCOPE-BY-IMPORTS", 6u32, "2026-11-05T11:09Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 07:1x kit: the verb main handed over is WIRED (unstaged): kit repo scope <root> --changed a,b[,...] (repeatable) prints one line per proof set (<package dir>: <modules to reprove>) and then 'kit repo scope ok packages=N proof_sets=M'. Exit 2 on bad words. Layout after two size rounds: NEW crate kit_proof_scope_manifests (manifest.spi = main's parser + path normalizing; manifest_walk.spi = package.spiproj walk skipping target/.git/node_modules/.cache/_build/deps/bin/obj, depth 8; exports manifests_under root -> array_base manifest_row {dir; deps; modules} and anchored_paths (root, changed)). kit_proof_scope keeps main's closure (import_scope.spi, now fed by rows) + scope_run.spi (args, print) and links the manifests crate. Routed via kit_cli_routes RepoScope. NODE: sizes manifests 761, scope 961, routes 217 (first cut 1393, then 1475 because a curried export inlined; exports must take a tuple or a single argument). cargo check -p kit-proof-scope -p kit-proof-scope-manifests exit 0. BOX: first-cut notebooks green (import_scope 6/6, scope_run 1/1, routes 1/1); re-cut set job-1793876386435 running (manifest.spi 2/2 so far). Rides TRAIN29.")
inl warm_mirror_caches () = Task ("WARM-MIRROR-CACHES", "Node/vultr mirrors stop starting cold: one shared node build cache keyed by source sha (compiler: 435-528 s cold vs 98-268 s on the box), a Cells memo store shared across mirror syncs (tibia: fresh mirrors start at memo_hits 0), one warm Cells build per mirror (tibia: lib_gate recompiled Cells' 44 .ex files per step), warm daemons in iterate mode (x-dumps: cold 5-14 min proofs)", Story, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "-", "node,cells,cache,kit,team:kit,kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_warm_mirror_caches () = Planning ("WARM-MIRROR-CACHES", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_warm_mirror_caches_1 () = Note ("WARM-MIRROR-CACHES", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: kit owns the job/mirror plumbing; compiler shares how the box's shared cache and r2r cache are keyed. DoD: a second proof on a fresh mirror of the same tree shows memo hits and no Cells recompile, and a node candidate build reuses obj/bin across stage dirs (time measured before and after in one job).")
inl note_of_warm_mirror_caches_2 () = Note ("WARM-MIRROR-CACHES", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:00Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 groom (AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT): parent epic GATE-HEALS-1101. It was this item's only dep, which hid the item from agile next because an epic finishes after its children; parents are named in notes, deps are for real ordering only.")
inl mirror_freshness_guard () = Task ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", "Every proof prints a box-vs-mirror hash table of its inputs and refuses stale ones; remote.ps1 sync retries until REMOTE-SYNC-OK; gitignored inputs (fiscal deps/corpus, deps/bench) are mirrored or checked first (fiscal 40 min chasing a stale corpus_checks.spi; x's first sync stopping before deps; resilience's stale node spiral)", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "remote,node,proofs,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_mirror_freshness_guard () = Planning ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_1 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x: main owns remote.ps1. Parts: (1) sync retries on a missing REMOTE-SYNC-OK, up to 3 times, then fails loudly; (2) a 'remote.ps1 <m> verify <repo> -Mirror <m> -Paths ...' verb printing box vs mirror digests per path (route check style, exit 6 on mismatch); (3) an optional -Include for gitignored input dirs. DoD: a deliberately stale mirror file makes the proof refuse to start, in seconds.")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_2 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:54Z", "main", "main 19:0x PART 1 DONE (unstaged remote.ps1): sync now retries up to 2 times on ANY nonzero remote exit (it used to retry only exit 7, a digest mismatch), naming the cause: 255 ssh dropped, 5 remote checkout failed, 6 remote untar failed, 7 tree changed while packed. The counter is REMOTE_SYNC_RETRIED, so a persistent failure still fails loudly after 2 tries. Smoke: a normal sync of spiral to vultr still prints REMOTE-SYNC-OK (exit 0). Found on the way: syncing a repo that has no clone on the target (dir-tree-html on vultr) dies at 'git bundle failed'; it should say 'no clone of <repo> on <machine>: clone it first'. Left: part 2, a 'verify -Paths' box-vs-mirror digest table, and part 3, mirroring gitignored inputs.")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_3 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:45Z", "main", "main 19:5x PART 2 DONE (unstaged remote.ps1): 'remote.ps1 <m> verify <repo> [-Mirror <name>] [paths...]' hashes each path on the box and in the mirror (default paths: the box's changed and untracked set, as sync uses) and prints one line per stale path, then 'MIRROR-STALE ... re-sync before trusting a proof' with exit 6, or 'MIRROR-FRESH <n> paths match'. First real use caught a stale file: node shared-current's apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1 predates today's exit-on-failure change (box 449F0AFF vs mirror A0C55439). Proof scripts should call verify on their input paths before starting. Left: part 3 (gitignored inputs such as fiscal deps/corpus and deps/bench, via an -Include on sync).")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_4 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 4u32, "2026-11-02T14:29Z", "main", "main 11-02: parent epic is GATE-HEALS-1101; recorded here instead of as a dep, because a dep on an unfinished parent epic hid this item from 'agile next' (backlog-wide sweep: 67 open items depended on an unfinished Epic).")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_5 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 5u32, "2026-11-04T16:17Z", "main", "11-04 12:2x main ORPHAN SWEEP: Active with no note for 48 h, so back to Planned at 65% (WIP cap: Active means touched). Owner stays main; resume from the last note.")
inl note_of_mirror_freshness_guard_6 () = Note ("MIRROR-FRESHNESS-GUARD", 6u32, "2026-11-05T07:25Z", "main", "11-05 03:25 main PART 3 DONE (unstaged i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1): `remote.ps1 <m> sync <repo> [-Mirror <n>] -Include <path>[,<path>...]` adds gitignored inputs (files or whole dirs) to the synced set, so they are tarred, extracted AND counted in the tree digest that sync already compares end to end; remote `git clean -fd` leaves ignored files alone, so nothing undoes them. A missing include path refuses before any remote step (\"-Include <p> does not exist under <repo>\"); -Include on any verb but sync is refused. PROOF on vultr: sync regex -Mirror main-inc -Include bench/bench.rs (gitignored, 194476 bytes) -> \"include: 1 files\", digest E9368009E2299CDC on both sides, REMOTE-SYNC-OK, and the mirror's bench.rs hashes 42734932F95B = box; both refusal cases checked; the scratch worktree removed with git worktree remove. With part 1 (sync retries) and part 2 (verify -Paths box-vs-mirror table, exit 6 on stale), the DoD holds: fiscal-style gitignored corpora can now travel with a mirror, and verify refuses a stale one in seconds.")
inl cells_check_defaults () = Task ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", "spiral --check / Cells check default SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR like the CLI does and take --timeout-ms (compiler: without the env var all 90/90 packages failed falsely at 15:3x; the 30 s cap exits 3 on big fiscal units)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,compiler,check,team:compiler,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_check_defaults () = Planning ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_1 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:00Z", "main", "main 18:0x from compiler A5. DoD: --check without the env var resolves |core- the same way the CLI does; --timeout-ms 120000 lets a big fiscal unit finish; both have tests.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_2 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:42Z", "compiler", "11-02 10:40 compiler: dep cleared (main sweep 11-02): GATE-HEALS-1101 is this item's PARENT epic, not a blocker, so the dep hid it from `agile next`. Parent: GATE-HEALS-1101.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_3 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T21:21Z", "compiler", "11-02 17:25 compiler: PROGRAM DRAFTED: drafts CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS\\1-check-package-dir-and-timeout.kitdo (core 1 + host 1 replacement; dry-applies on live 1B00A6B3, stacked after COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS\\1). ROOT CAUSE: with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR unset, resolve_packages used <get_workspace_root()>/deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin, and get_workspace_root() is SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT or else the CURRENT DIRECTORY. So --check run from fiscal looked in fiscal\\deps\\The-Spiral-Language and every |core- package failed (the 90/90 false failures). FIX: the core walks the ancestors of the workspace root and of the package folder, trying deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin, a vendored deps/spiral/deps/..., and a sibling ../spiral/deps/..., and takes the first that exists; the env var still wins, and the old path is the last resort. That matches Cells' Toolchain.package_dir intent (spiral root + core package) without a compile-time root. Host: `--check --timeout-ms N <file>` (positive int32, as --plan-ir; default stays 30000), so a big fiscal unit can take 120000. PROOF PLAN (node, with the pack19 build): --check on a fiscal unit from C:\\home\\git\\fiscal with the env var unset (control fails, candidate passes), plus --timeout-ms 120000 on the largest fiscal unit.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_4 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T22:54Z", "compiler", "11-02 18:50 compiler: shipped in pack19 (handed to main 18:5x, install-when-clear running). Node proof: --check with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR and SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT unset: control exit 5 (|core- unresolved), candidate exit 0; --check --timeout-ms 120000 exit 0.")
inl note_of_cells_check_defaults_5 () = Note ("CELLS-CHECK-DEFAULTS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:32Z", "compiler", "11-02 22:5x compiler: DONE, live in the installed compiler (pack19, host 6B30D2F521660878, core 32912F27BC9DBEAC). Box checks with SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR and SPIRAL_WORKSPACE_ROOT unset: --check lib/spiral/metrics.spi (|core-) -> checked package C:/home/git/spiral/lib/spiral, exit 0 in 7 s; --check dice/contract/dice_contract.spi (sibling repo, via ../spiral) -> checked package C:/home/git/dice, exit 0; --check --timeout-ms 60000 parses. A package with no spiral checkout among its ancestors (a Temp scratch dir) still fails with the explicit SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR hint, by design.")
