inl note_of_predict_per_backend_1 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:01Z", "main", "main 18:0x from compiler A2: the native memo already keys per backend. DoD: a pack touching only the Gleam section predicts in under 20 min with the other backends' rows read from memo, and the residual verdict is unchanged versus the full run on one sample pack.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_2 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:41Z", "compiler", "11-02 10:40 compiler: dep cleared (main sweep 11-02): GATE-HEALS-1101 is this item's PARENT epic, not a blocker, so the dep hid it from `agile next`. Parent: GATE-HEALS-1101.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_3 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 3u32, "2026-11-03T01:03Z", "compiler", "11-02 21:0x compiler: EVIDENCE for the node-mirror half. Today every compiler pack review ran on node t1101 with nothing on the box: pack19 (1220 s total incl. build, both arms), pack19b, paramesc, paramesc2, pack20 (control + candidate). Per arm, examples -Backend Rust,C,Zig,Gleam (1981 rows) took 3.6-4.6 min and contracts (728 rows) 3-4 min, plus about 5 min for the candidate build; compare-runs reads residual and behavior cells in-process. So a pack predict without -Native costs about 20 min of node time and 0 box time. Still open for the DoD: the native half (-Native rows from memo for unchanged backends), which needs a toolchain-complete mirror (node lacks the Wgsl adapter and the Delphi/Lean runners) or vultr.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_4 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 4u32, "2026-11-03T23:34Z", "compiler", "11-03 19:3x compiler: EVIDENCE for the native half, from today's 7 node reviews (pack27 E0505, pack28 E0507 x3, pack29, pack30, pack31; 0 box time). Recipe that held every time: (1) examples on ONLY the backends whose codegen section the program touches (Rust for RUST-MOVE, Zig/contracts for LINKED-UNITS-ZIG, Lua for the IIFE fix), both arms, no -Native: about 2 min per arm; (2) compare-runs, then derive the changed rows (residual differs on both sides) and rerun ONLY those with -Native -Filter '^samples/(a|b|...)$' on both arms: 117 rows in about 3 min for slice 4, 1 row for E0507; (3) downstream rows that examples lack (regex certificate Cells A/B, apps/spiral cargo check, kit crates), because examples missed both pack26 bugs. The derive-and-filter step is a few lines (node-pack29.ps1 in the scratchpad, written inline by me each time); folding it into test.ps1 as '-Native -OnlyChangedFrom <results.tsv>' is the concrete next step for this item.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_5 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 5u32, "2026-11-04T00:17Z", "compiler", "11-03 20:1x compiler: n4's next step DONE in tree (unstaged): test.ps1 -ChangedBetween <control results.tsv>,<candidate results.tsv> keeps only samples whose residual differs (matched by id + backend), refuses -Accept/-Record, never counts as a full schedule, and exits 0 at once when nothing changed. Proof on the box: a copy of single-flight-20261102-131037 with one Rust residual altered -> '-ChangedBetween: 1 samples', 1 job; the same file twice -> 'nothing changed', exit 0. Documented in apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md. A pack review's native half is now: both arms without -Native, then both arms -Native -ChangedBetween control,candidate. Left for the DoD: per-backend scheduling from the touched codegen section, and node/vultr toolchain completeness for -Native.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_6 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 6u32, "2026-11-04T00:21Z", "compiler", "11-03 20:3x compiler: per-backend scheduling DONE in tree (unstaged): test.ps1 -BackendsFrom <before.fs>,<after.fs> sets -Backend (when none is given) to the backends whose codegen the change touches. It aligns the two sources positionally (resync on 3 equal lines within 400; a first multiset-diff cut flagged generic lines like '| _ -> false' all over the file and was replaced), maps each changed line to its file's nearest '/// ## Codegen<X>' (or '/// ### codegen<X>' inside the shared Wgsl range: Calyx/Kotlin/Swift/OpenQasm/Ebpf), and keeps every backend for any change outside codegen. Proof on today's packs (candidate sources): pack31 -> Lua; pack30 -> Rust; pack28 -> Rust; pack29 -> every backend (it changed ExternCalls in PartEval and exportedUnionNames in CodegenUtils; correct). 6-11 s per call. With -ChangedBetween (n5) a pack review is now: -BackendsFrom both arms without -Native, then -Native -ChangedBetween. Documented in AGENTS.md. Left for the DoD: node/vultr toolchain completeness for -Native rows.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_7 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 7u32, "2026-11-04T06:25Z", "compiler", "11-04 02:3x compiler: NODE TOOLCHAIN GAP CLOSED (the item's last DoD point), except Swift. Before: Get-SpiralNativeTools on the node (DESKTOP-6E8C14G) found no Auxin, BendMain, CalyxRoot, Cider, Java, Kotlinc, Swiftc/SwiftRuntime/SwiftSdk or WgslRun; the box has all of them, so -Native rows for Bend, Calyx, Kotlin, Swift and Wgsl could only run on the box. Shipped from the box's toolchains (9.3 MB tar, only what runs): wgsl-run\\release\\spiral-wgsl.exe, bend\\bend2 (runs on the node's bun) and calyx-src without target\\ plus its release auxin.exe and cider.exe. scoop on the node: bucket java, temurin25-jdk 25.0.5 and kotlin (same packages as the box). Proof (node, installed compiler, examples -Native -Filter): Wgsl i64_scalar ran exit 0; Calyx arithmetic_branch ran exit 0; Bend arithmetic_branch ran exit 0. Java and Kotlinc now resolve (openjdk 25.0.5). Left: Swift 6.4 (Windows installer plus SDK, several GB; the node had 8.8 GB free before my stage sweep, 19.1 GB after). So a pack touching codegenSwift still needs the box for native rows; everything else can run node-first.")
inl note_of_predict_per_backend_8 () = Note ("PREDICT-PER-BACKEND", 8u32, "2026-11-04T13:15Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:2x compiler: CLOSED. Delivered: test.ps1 -BackendsFrom (per-backend scheduling from the codegen sections a change touches, proven on packs 28-31), -ChangedBetween, and node toolchains for Bend/Calyx/Kotlin/Wgsl/Java (proven -Native rows exit 0 on the node). Today every review ran node-first. The one gap, Swift native rows on the node, is split off as NODE-SWIFT-TOOLCHAIN (P3); until it lands, a pack touching codegenSwift runs its Swift native rows on the box.")
inl local_pre_proof_gate () = Task ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", "A seconds-long local check before any node proof: parse every touched .spi, the 120-width check, kit standards on touched packages, the cell budget on touched definitions (resilience: a top-level global parse error and a width-122 line each cost a full ~14-min node cycle)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 55u32, Active, "-", "kit,proofs,standards,team:kit,kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_local_pre_proof_gate () = Planning ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_1 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:01Z", "main", "main 18:0x from resilience. DoD: kit's proof/sync path runs it by default and refuses to ship a draft that fails, in under 10 s for a typical change.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_2 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:00Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 groom (AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT): parent epic GATE-HEALS-1101. It was this item's only dep, which hid the item from agile next because an epic finishes after its children; parents are named in notes, deps are for real ordering only.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_3 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T20:41Z", "kit", "11-04 22:0x kit: FIRST SLICE BUILT (unstaged): `kit lint precheck <file.spi>...` (new linked crate kit_lint_precheck, routed through kit lint's own LintPrecheck case, so kit_cli (995) is untouched). Pure text checks, milliseconds per file: WidthOver (any line > 120) and OpenString (a line with an odd number of unescaped quotes outside host macros, a quote char literal and /// headers, i.e. a string literal broken across lines: exactly the \"\\\\n written through a heredoc becomes a real newline\" trap that hit kit 3 times on 11-04, once only caught by grep before a train). Prints one \"file:row: ...\" line per finding and \"kit lint precheck ok|refused files=N findings=M\", exit 1 on any finding. Tests: escaped quotes + a quote char are fine, a split string is 2 findings, a host-macro line is skipped, a 141-wide line. vultr --check ok with bodies (precheck + lint cli); box notebooks kit-precheck-tests. NEXT slices: the parse check (compiler --check is ~20-60 s, so seconds-long needs the compiler server), kit standards on touched packages, the cell budget, and wiring into remote.ps1 sync as a default refusal.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_4 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T20:52Z", "kit", "11-04 22:3x kit: first slice PROVEN on the box: kit_lint_precheck precheck.spi 1/1 (escaped quotes + a quote char clean; a string split across two lines = 2 OpenString findings; a host-macro line skipped; a 141-wide line = WidthOver) and kit_lint_cli cli.spi 1/1 (precheck routes to LintPrecheck). The first run was RED on a rustc recursion limit, not on logic: sm'.replicate 120 \"x\" with a literal count unrolled into 120 nested format! calls (memory spiral-constant-replicate-unrolls); the fixture is now built from 10-char pieces. Ships with the next train after TRAIN23.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_5 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T22:29Z", "kit", "11-04 18:5x kit: a third precheck from today's failures (unstaged): `kit lint precheck` also takes Cargo.toml paths and refuses a crate whose output is build.rs, main.rs or lib.rs (\"output build.rs is a name Cargo reserves in a crate root (build.rs = build script); rename the module\"). TRAIN23 died 70 min into regen on exactly that (kit_run_build's module was named build); now it fails in milliseconds before any node run. Test a_crate_output_named_like_a_cargo_file_is_refused (build.rs refused, builder.rs fine). vultr --check ok with bodies; box notebook kit-precheck-tests3.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_6 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T22:34Z", "kit", "11-04 18:4x kit: the reserved-output precheck is PROVEN on the box (kit-precheck-tests3 2/2: build.rs refused, builder.rs fine). Separately, node size run kit-size-post25 caught agile_task_listing at 1015 generated lines (OVER) after today's list_root change, which built the whole argument list just to read one value; list_root now calls a new kit_agile_list_root export in the linked kit_agile_list_args crate (argument_owned 1i32, the HEAD reader). vultr --check ok on both; the re-size (kit-size-listing) is pending on the node. The other 6 sized fine: note_listing 832, task_inspection 679, lint_cli 211, lint_precheck 506, job_entry 421, kit_process 70.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_7 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T22:43Z", "kit", "11-04 18:4x kit: re-size GREEN on the node (kit-size-listing2): agile_task_listing 1015 -> 936, kit_agile_list_args 213. Every crate changed since TRAIN25's snapshot now sizes under 1000; the next train carries them.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_8 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T23:04Z", "kit", "11-04 19:0x kit: TRAIN25 RED at the crate gate on exactly the crate kit-size-post25 had already flagged: agile_task_listing task_listing.rs 1015 OVER (crates=337 over=1). Everything else passed: regen published 274 changed owners, 63 unchanged. The fix was already in the tree and node-sized (listing 936, kit_agile_list_args 295 with the typed root reader, kit_remote_status 996 = only 4 lines of headroom; split it before adding anything). TRAIN26 launched at 19:04 (job-1793833466593-kit-TRAIN26-node, same command as TRAIN25 reusing the train25 mirror; node at 100% load with 4 other jobs, 11.1 GB free). It carries everything since TRAIN25's snapshot (all kit's, all sized): listing/args fix, kit_process --timeout-ms, the reserved-output precheck, lease_corpus, the S10 re-lease fix, stop_cli checks, and the remote-status disk floor. It is the first train through the launcher's new 5 GB floor.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_9 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 9u32, "2026-11-05T00:14Z", "kit", "11-04 20:1x kit: TRAIN26 PAST THE GATE on the node: 20:09:20 regen ok (275 changed owners published, 62 unchanged, 0 errors), 20:09:22 crate gate ok (crates=337 over=0 limit=1000). First train today past regen + gate (TRAIN22 gate x3 crates, TRAIN23 build.rs, TRAIN24 disk full, TRAIN25 gate x1). Every crate it carries had been node-sized first. Now in the candidate phase (debug build of kit-cli and kit-dev); notebooks and release follow, so the install lands after 21:00 (pending).")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_10 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 10u32, "2026-11-05T02:15Z", "kit", "11-04 22:1x kit (groom): TRAIN26 still PENDING on the node at 22:10: notebook phase 147/205 done, 4 RED so far, none in packages kit changed tonight: agile_task_notes notes_cli (agile_add_lands_a_groomed_item_in_one_call, cell exited 1; file unchanged since 10-25), command_spec_domain direct_verbs (shared_lines_print_once, cell exited 1; TRAIN26's 19:04 snapshot predates kit's 19:38 edit+exact revert), kit_bundle_manifest (archive_permissions_keep_executable_and_readonly_intent) and kit_do_verbs (2 tests), both \"File main has a type error\", both files last changed 11-04 00:31. If they stay red, TRAIN26 ends red and does not install. NEXT session: diagnose these four before any install or TRAIN27.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_11 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 11u32, "2026-11-05T05:27Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 01:2x kit: WIRING DRAFTED, not applied: launch-train.ps1 is the live launcher of TRAIN27 (memory never-patch-running-launcher). Draft: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE\\scripts\\launch-train.ps1 (base 316F243DFCCE2529, CRLF kept). Before kit job start it lists the touched src/*.spi and Cargo.toml (git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all) and runs kit lint precheck on them. A 'refused' verdict throws in seconds with the findings, so no node train starts on a width-121 line, a split string or a crate output named build.rs. An installed kit without the verb prints 'precheck unavailable in the installed kit; skipped' instead of refusing. DRY RUN on the box against the live tree: 13 touched files, installed kit = skipped path (correct; the verb ships with TRAIN26/27's tree). APPLY after TRAIN27 ends (it also carries the S4 draft's 4 hunks on the same base). Left after that: the parse slice (needs the compiler server) and the cell budget slice.")
inl note_of_local_pre_proof_gate_12 () = Note ("LOCAL-PRE-PROOF-GATE", 12u32, "2026-11-05T07:37Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:3x kit: WIRING APPLIED (unstaged) to scripts/launch-train.ps1 now that TRAIN27 has ended and no launcher runs: live was exactly the draft's base 316F243DFCCE2529, and the only difference is the 7-line precheck block before kit job start (live now BA23C6A309D51580, CRLF kept, PowerShell parse errors 0). The next train launch runs kit lint precheck on the touched src .spi/Cargo.toml and refuses on findings. With the installed kit (no precheck verb yet) it prints 'skipped', so TRAIN28 itself still launches; from the install that carries the verb onward it enforces. The S4 draft (base 316F) now needs a rebase onto BA23 before it applies.")
