inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:44Z", "main", "11-01 18:4x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep, read-only). SITES (each read in place; Spiral-level bindings only, raw Rust #[test] fixtures inside global blocks excluded). kit, ms: src/agile_lease_terms/terms.spi:91 clock_now_ms; src/kit_cli_check/cli.spi:175 now_ms; src/kit_experiments/ledger_host.spi:12 now_ms; src/kit_jobs/host.spi:18 now_ms; src/kit_machine_watch/jobs_watch.spi:5 now_ms; src/kit_receipt/receipt.spi:11 now_ms and :17 elapsed_text; src/rust_std_process/model.spi:55 wall_clock_millis and :59 elapsed_millis; src/workspace_primitives/clock.spi:1 unix_ms and :3 ms_since; src/rust_std_fs/model.spi:3 file_modified_ms (epoch part); src/kit_notebook_progress/progress.spi:8 now_ms (via reactors.physical_micros). kit, seconds: src/rust_std_env/clock.spi:10,13,17 (session_deadline_from_now, should_wrap, within_budget); src/kit_machine_sample/sample.spi:60 now_seconds; src/kit_resume/resume.spi:10 clock_text; src/kit_machine_watch/run.spi:16 now_text. x: apps/client/oauth1.spi:17-23 (system_now, since_epoch, whole_seconds, sub_micros: a copy of lib file_system.spi:1766-1769 rust_since_epoch/rust_elapsed_ms); apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi:88 clock_ms and :257 now_ms (Gleam erlang:monotonic_time millisecond). lib (private copies of the same read): guid.spi:91 rust_unix_nanos; trace.spi:338 rust_epoch_nanos; reactors.spi:301; file_system.spi:1766 rust_since_epoch; date_time.spi:144 zig_micros_now. LIB TARGET: date_time (existing module; date_time.now returns a chrono naive local date_time, not an epoch count, so it is NOT the replacement EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY n21 assumed for unix_ms). TYPED SHAPE: nominals :! unix_ms = u64, :! unix_seconds = u64, :! unix_nanos = u128 (or one epoch_count with phantom units :! millis / :! seconds / :! nanos so a ms value cannot be compared to seconds), :! monotonic_ms = i64 kept separate from wall time. Granular one-expression host bindings: rust_system_now (), rust_since_epoch (moved here from file_system), rust_whole_millis, rust_whole_seconds; Gleam arms via erlang:system_time/1 and erlang:monotonic_time/1 through erlang_term::apply; F# DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeMilliseconds. Public: unix_now_ms () : unix_ms, unix_now_seconds () : unix_seconds, unix_now_nanos () : unix_nanos, ms_since (start : unix_ms) : u64 (saturating), monotonic_now_ms () : monotonic_ms. No multi-line host macros. DoD: (1) date_time defines them with a :# block (ms > 1.7e12, seconds = ms / 1000 within 1, ms_since of now is < 1000, monotonic non-decreasing across two reads) passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) every site above calls the lib function, each proven by its repo's own gate (kit: the touched packages' notebooks + crate regen; x: the client and xsim builds); (3) the old copies are deleted, lib's private copies included (guid, trace, reactors, file_system call date_time).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 2u32, "2026-11-02T23:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:24 x: STEP 1 drafted (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK). PLACEMENT DECIDED by the line gate, not by the n1 target: date_time.spi is already 1,492 lines (over the 1k gate), so the clock is a new granular lib module, unix_clock.spi, after erlang_term in package.spiproj. It has nominals unix_ms, unix_seconds and unix_nanos (u64 each, so units can't be mixed), and one-expression host bindings: rust_system_now, rust_since_unix_epoch, rust_whole_millis and rust_whole_nanos; erlang_system_time through erlang_term::apply; fsharp_unix_millis and fsharp_unix_nanos. Public: unix_now_ms, unix_now_seconds, unix_now_nanos, ms_since (saturating), and the ms_count, seconds_count and nanos_count accessors. Monotonic ms stays as date_time::monotonic_milliseconds (Gleam, it already exists); a typed monotonic_ms nominal can wrap it when a consumer needs one. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-lib-clock1, after x-cells-pb1 frees the node): lib_land_window applies with document_test green, and lib_gate on unix_clock.spi gives the block 'the_unix_clock_reads_epoch_counts_in_their_own_units' passed on rust, fsharp and gleam with executed > 0 and 0 failed. STEP 2 (after the land): the call sites in n1 switch over, x's first (apps/client/oauth1.spi and apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi), each proven by its repo's gate; then lib's private copies (guid, trace, reactors, file_system).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 3u32, "2026-11-02T23:56Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:56 x: STEP 2, x's half, drafted (kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK); it waits for step 1's land. (1) apps/client/oauth1.spi (base 2C25BE4C24EB -> 15741F2FAB39): the private system_time/elapsed nominals and system_now, since_epoch, whole_seconds and sub_micros are deleted. clock_seed reads unix_clock::unix_now_nanos / 1000 (the same micros), and unix_seconds reads unix_clock::unix_now_seconds. (2) apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi (base FC47D2493A17 -> 534B8E8105A7): clock_ms and now_ms no longer call erlang:monotonic_time themselves. They read date_time::monotonic_milliseconds, and the deadline stops being a raw Erlang term: it is a nominal deadline_ms = i64, so deadline_after, left_until, next_reply and harvested are typed and the term arithmetic (erlang + - max) is gone. Proof on land: the x client gate (oauth1 blocks) and the sim proof (launch-sim-proof).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 4u32, "2026-11-03T00:14Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:14 x: STEP 1+3 SCOPE AND RULE, revised before any run. (a) Lint-clean macros: kit's standards/lint-macros-lib.spi baselines lib macro findings (cast, arith, block). So unix_clock's host bindings are one-expression reads only (SystemTime::now, duration_since, as_secs, subsec_nanos, UtcNow.Ticks, ToUnixTimeMilliseconds), and every unit conversion and offset is Spiral arithmetic. No 'as' casts, no F# arithmetic in a macro. (b) lib's own copies ride the same land: guid.spi drops rust_unix_nanos (the hasher seeds from unix_clock nanos, write_u64) and reactors.spi's rust_physical_micros becomes nanos / 1000. That retires kit lint entry lint_known_223 (reactors rust_physical_micros cast). Two copies stay, for stated reasons: trace.spi's rust_epoch_nanos is NEAR chain time under cfg (near_sdk block_timestamp), not a wall clock; file_system's rust_since_epoch converts a FILE's modified SystemTime, not now. RULE (x-lib-clock1, launch-lib-clock): lib_land_window applies 4 files (unix_clock new, package.spiproj, guid, reactors) with document_test green and the consumer signatures unchanged; lib_gate exits 0 with executed > 0 on each of unix_clock.spi, guid.spi and reactors.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:34Z", "x", "2026-11-02 22:34 x: x-lib-clock1 NOT GREEN, undone by lib_land_window as designed. Passed: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, and type_probe passed 4/4 (unix_clock 1 test typed, guid 2, reactors 8, erlang_map 7). Failed: document_test 21/22, 'the spiral library .spi files load as notebooks, one test cell per test block'. That test requires every lib .spi to round-trip byte-exact through the notebook form, and the new unix_clock.spi was the only file written without a trailing newline. Fixed by adding one LF. Also, before clock1, the launch caught a stale package.spiproj base (another lane added sized_array and metrics; rebased, with a recorded-base guard added). Rerun: x-lib-clock2, rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 6u32, "2026-11-03T03:01Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:01 x: x-lib-clock2 NOT GREEN, with the same single failure as clock1 (document_test 21/22, the notebook round-trip test; signatures, consumer compile and type_probe 4/4 all passed), so the trailing newline wasn't the cause. lib_land_window prints only the test name, so x-lib-doc2 runs document_test on the same mirror with full failure output, base tree first and then the 5 drafts, which shows whether the failing file is mine or comes from tonight's parallel lib edits (other lanes changed file_system, sm' and xsd_emit and added metrics.spi and sized_array.spi between 20:54 and 22:17). CORE SWITCH: the node's single-flight core is now 4E48590A5408C14B (8960CAB701FEF46E refused, 'verifying'). Every x launcher is re-pinned; tonight's earlier lands ran wholly on 8960, before the switch.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 7u32, "2026-11-03T03:06Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:06 x: ROOT CAUSE found by x-lib-doc2 (base 22 passed, draft 21/22 with the failure in erlang_map.spi): my new values_are_every_value_once block was inserted after the file's last block with two blank lines before it, and the notebook round trip normalizes to one, so once == spi_text failed (document_test.exs:513). Fixed to one blank line. All 5 lib drafts now have 0 triple newlines and a single final LF. The unix_clock trailing-newline fix from clock2 stays (harmless, and the right ending). Rerun x-lib-clock3 on core 4E48590A5408C14B, rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 8u32, "2026-11-03T03:17Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:17 x: STEP 1+3 LANDED on the box live lib (unstaged, window win-1793675828426): unix_clock.spi 03D6F2285043 (new), package.spiproj 2A0004126191 (live 5F520E796BAC plus unix_clock after erlang_term), guid.spi 72FF1D8AF174 (rust_unix_nanos gone; the hasher seeds from unix_clock nanos), reactors.spi 4BCE905C7EF0 (rust_physical_micros = nanos / 1000), erlang_map.spi 708AB4996ABD (map_values). PROOF x-lib-clock3 on core 4E48590A5408C14B: lib_land_window closed green (0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe 4/4), lib_gate unix_clock 1/1, guid 2/2, reactors 8/8, erlang_map 7/7, 0 type errors. Undo on the node: spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261102-231207. NEXT: x-e2e-quote-clock1 (x's oauth1 and cells_executor on unix_clock and date_time, plus the json.quote switches) is launched.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_9 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 9u32, "2026-11-03T03:42Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:42 x: x-e2e-quote-clock2 NOT GREEN. The sim build passed (cells_executor on date_time::monotonic_milliseconds, typed deadline_ms and map_values all compile), but the client e2e failed 8 checks: 'xc post-thread sent 11 posts, the sim splits oauth1.spi into 17', and the read-back mismatched. Cause: the e2e posts oauth1.spi ITSELF as a thread and compares it with the committed fixture apps/client/e2e/thread-oauth1.expected.json, which the sim build regenerates from oauth1.spi only under -Accept. The fixture still held the old file (system_time, elapsed, since_epoch), so any edit to oauth1.spi needs its fixture regenerated (memory x-sim-fixtures-embed-client-sources). RERUN RULE, set before x-e2e-quote-clock3 runs: apps/sim/build.ps1 -Accept -fast 1 on the mirror, where the ONLY changed fixture must be thread-oauth1.expected.json; then sim build exit 0, client build exit 0 and e2e RUST-OK with no FAILED line, so xc's split of the new oauth1.spi equals the sim's (two independent splitters) and reads back byte-exact. The regenerated fixture comes back in OUT and lands with oauth1.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_10 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 10u32, "2026-11-03T04:07Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:07 x: x-e2e-quote-clock3 NOT GREEN, judged honestly. The e2e half passed: sim build 0, client build 0, RUST-OK 37 tutorial steps + 5 extra cases, sim exit 0, and only thread-oauth1.expected.json changed. 141 requests vs 153 is fully explained: the new oauth1.spi threads as 11 posts, not 17, so there are 6 fewer POSTs and 6 fewer DELETEs. But the -Accept build exited 1 on CELL-BUDGET: my cells_executor.spi:75 memo_counted weighed 311 > 272, from its single long map_values line. FIX: memo_flags (result) is its own definition (an annotated erl_map term term view, then map_values), and memo_counted calls it. RULE for x-e2e-quote-clock4, set before it runs: the n9 rule PLUS sim accept exit 0 (cell budget clean); the request count must be 141, the 153 baseline minus the 12 shorter-thread requests.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_11 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 11u32, "2026-11-03T04:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:31 x: STEP 2 (x's half) LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793680193133): apps/client/oauth1.spi 15741F2FAB39 (clock_seed and unix_seconds read lib unix_clock; six private Rust clock bindings gone), apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi 9742F928099C (clock_ms reads date_time::monotonic_milliseconds; typed deadline_ms; memo_flags through erlang_map::map_values; flag_count folds a list), and apps/client/e2e/thread-oauth1.expected.json 25D526E8C76E (regenerated by -Accept; its program equals the new oauth1.spi byte for byte; 11 posts). PROOF x-e2e-quote-clock4 on core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF, green on every pre-registered condition: sim accept exit 0 (cell budget clean), only thread-oauth1.expected.json changed, sim build 0, client build 0, 141 requests (153 minus the predicted 12), RUST-OK 37 tutorial steps + 5 extra cases, sim exit 0. Clocks 1-3 failed honestly (wire's json shadow, the stale fixture, then the cell budget). LEFT: kit's 14 sites (kit lane) and lib file_system/trace, kept for the reasons in n4.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_12 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 12u32, "2026-11-03T05:05Z", "x", "2026-11-03 01:05 x: x's share DONE and landed tonight (see the notes above), so team:x is removed from the tags. The other teams' tags stay, for the remaining kit and main sites. Resume condition for x: none, unless a lane hands an x site back.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_13 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 13u32, "2026-11-04T14:10Z", "main", "11-04 10:1x main: MAIN'S SITE found. regex bench/host.spi elapsed_nanos is a private Rust Instant (OnceLock START, elapsed().as_nanos()), a MONOTONIC read that unix_clock's wall-clock unix_now_nanos (SystemTime) must not replace, since a benchmark across an NTP step would be wrong. DRAFT (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK\\date_time.spi, base 8E2666DB0CE5): date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds () : u64, beside monotonic_milliseconds, with a Rust arm (the same Instant code) and a test that it never goes back; no Gleam arm on purpose (erlang:monotonic_time may be negative, so it cannot be a u64). Lib --check clean on a vultr lib copy; notebook gate and two-step land PENDING; then regex's elapsed_nanos reads lib and its private binding goes.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_14 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 14u32, "2026-11-04T14:55Z", "main", "11-04 11:0x main date_time draft GREEN on vultr: 27/27 twice in a row on a lib copy (monotonic_nanoseconds now a :~ function, so the Rust static START is one per program; the first draft was := and every inlined call site got its own static, which the test caught: b < a). The single date_time_utc Lua red in the first gate is a flake (absent in both reruns and in the live file's run). NEXT: two-step land of date_time.spi (base 8E2666DB0CE5), then regex bench/host.spi elapsed_nanos -> date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds and its private binding goes.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_15 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:17Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main: first date_time land closed RED at document_test 21/22 and undid itself cleanly: the inserted test ran straight into the next ///> gleam cell with no blank line between them (the here-string ate it; memory lib-land-roundtrip-first). Fixed, and lib_roundtrip.exs on vultr now prints canonical true, fixpoint true. Re-land node half running.")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_16 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 16u32, "2026-11-04T16:12Z", "main", "11-04 12:1x main LANDED date_time.spi 1A9E63FCD880 (lib digest 7D28CCC6FF55E6E1) by the two-step land: node half green (document_test 22, type probe PASS, 0 respell drift), box half from the proof with fast checks (box lib had moved). New: :~ monotonic_nanoseconds () : u64 (Rust arm, process-start-relative Instant, failwith on other backends) + test the_monotonic_nanosecond_clock_does_not_go_back. CONSUMER: regex bench/bench.spi now calls date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds and the private elapsed_nanos in bench/host.spi is gone (unstaged); regex bench build on vultr PENDING (node busy with TRAIN22).")
inl note_of_lib_move_unix_clock_17 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", 17u32, "2026-11-04T16:43Z", "main", "11-04 12:5x main CONSUMER GREEN: regex build on vultr (regex a9c2e259 + unstaged, spiral lib with the landed date_time 1A9E63FC) REGEX-OK; bench/bench.spi compiled to Rust in 8 s and regex-bench ran, its deterministic rows and arm counts agreeing, now timed by date_time.monotonic_nanoseconds; the private elapsed_nanos binding in bench/host.spi is gone. The clock moved to lib and its one consumer uses it: DONE.")
inl lib_move_civil_date () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", "lib date_time gets chrono-free civil date math (civil_of_days next to the existing days_from_civil), a typed ISO-8601 UTC stamp and a typed local UTC offset; x xsim world.spi's own copy, kit agile_note_model's Spiral copy and five kit host macros that inline the same Hinnant arithmetic or Win32 GetLocalTime call it", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT,LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK", "lib,generic,main,team:main,team:kit,team:x,typefeatureset,date_time", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_move_civil_date () = Planning ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:45Z", "main", "11-01 18:4x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (read in place). Civil date from days / days from civil: x apps/sim/spi/world.spi:277 day_of_year, :279 days_from_civil (i32 copy of lib date_time.spi:1331), :285-299 year_of_era/day_in_era/month_of/civil_of/civil_from_days, :301 moment_of (ISO parse), :305 padded, :308-317 clock_text/date_text/stamped (ISO format); kit src/agile_note_model/model.spi:215 civil_of_days and :227 utc_stamp (pure Spiral, the best lib seed); kit host macros inlining the same arithmetic in one multi-line $'...' each: src/kit_adoption/host.spi:28 cutoff_day, src/kit_do_lab/host.spi:38 note_age_days, src/kit_do_write_host/host.spi:30 clock_filled. Local offset / local stamp via Win32: src/kit_receipt/receipt.spi:23 local_offset_minutes (GetLocalTime vs GetSystemTime, 15-minute rounding; callers agile_note_model/model.spi:149, kit_do_file_steps/steps.spi:33,58, kit_do_process/run.spi:108, kit_process_table/run.spi:32) and :34 clock_text; src/kit_experiments/ledger_host.spi:30 local_stamp (second Win32 copy). LIB TARGET: date_time (existing). Kit cannot take date_time.now/utc_now as is: their Rust arm needs the chrono crate, which the kit crates avoid; the new functions are arithmetic in Spiral plus one granular host read each. TYPED SHAPE: :== civil = { year : i64; month : month_of_year; day : i64 } with month_of_year a union (or a nominal checked 1..12), :! epoch_days = i64, :! utc_offset_minutes = i64; civil_of_days (d : epoch_days) : civil, days_of_civil (c : civil) : epoch_days (the existing days_from_civil re-expressed on the record), iso_utc_text (s : unix_seconds) : string and iso_local_text (s : unix_seconds) (o : utc_offset_minutes) : string, iso_utc_parsed (text : string) : option unix_seconds; local_offset_minutes () : utc_offset_minutes with granular one-expression arms (Rust: two small extern bindings GetLocalTime/GetSystemTime under cfg(windows), 0 elsewhere or libc localtime_r; F# TimeZoneInfo.Local.GetUtcOffset; Gleam calendar.local_offset). Uses LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK's unix_seconds. DoD: (1) date_time definitions with a :# block (1970-01-01 = day 0, 2000-02-29 round trip, 2026-11-01 = 20758, 1969-12-31 = -1, ISO text of 0 = 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z, parse of that text round trips, offset in -720..840 and a multiple of 15) passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) every site above calls the lib functions, proven by kit's touched notebooks + crate regen and x's xsim build; (3) the copies are deleted (the three kit host macros shrink to lib calls, kit_receipt and kit_experiments share the lib offset).")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 2u32, "2026-11-04T01:13Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:11 x: ORPHAN SWEEP (MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP, x's corner: open x items with no note in 48 h). x's share is concrete and CPU-light: apps/sim/spi/world.spi civil-date copies (day_of_year, days_from_civil and friends at :277-299) switch to lib date_time. x drafts it now.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T01:16Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:16 x: x's SHARE DRAFTED (kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE\\world.spi, base 561F876D817C -> B4CDE32E0EA6, formatted, max cell 270, 480 -> 463 lines): the sim's 7 hand-rolled civil-date helpers (day_of_year, days_from_civil, year_of_era, day_in_era, month_of, civil_of, civil_from_days) collapse to 2 thin i32 wrappers over lib date_time (days_from_civil in i64; civil_from_days via civil_of_micros, whose first three fields are y m d). Lib uses floor_div, which is correct before 1970 where the sim's truncating '/' was not; for the sim's 2026 dates they agree, and the sim accept (fixtures embed timelines and stamps) proves it. Runs as x-next5 after x-replay2.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T01:30Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:30 x: x-next5 now also carries the 3 line-width fixes the default standards rules flagged in apps/sim/spi/cells_executor.spi (base 3C5E776B7871 -> draft CFCE9C3B5DC0: 'at' and 'text_at' bodies wrapped, ok_value's tag test named ok_tagged; widest line 120, max cell 271). Both files are hash-guarded in land-x-next5.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:34Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:34 x: x-next5c (job-1793782508291, pinned core 0758BAF4, 2 h 32 min) PASSED its pre-registered rule and LANDED (9 hash-guarded drafts + 42 regenerated outputs, 0 conflicts): sim accept 0 with NO fixture changed, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, all Rust units under 1k, census SAME over 77, notebook gate one fresh process per file: feed_merge 6/6, timeline_serve 4/4 (x-next5b's 3/4 was the stale warm server). LANDED for this item: apps/sim/spi/world.spi B4CDE32E0EA6: the sim's 7 civil-date helpers are now 2 thin wrappers over lib date_time; no fixture changed. x's share is DONE.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T17:03Z", "x", "2026-11-04 13:03 x: x's SHARE DRAFTED (it was NOT done: client/requests/requests.spi kept its own days->civil copy). (1) lib date_time.spi gains civil_of_days (i64 -> year, month, day), the inverse of the existing days_from_civil, as small cells civil_era / civil_year_of_era / civil_day_of_year / civil_month / civil_month_day (Hinnant's algorithm with floor_div, as requests had it); tests civil_of_days_names_known_dates (0 -> 1970-01-01, -1 -> 1969-12-31, 11016 -> 2000-02-29) and civil_of_days_inverts_days_from_civil (round trip over -719468..2932896), rust and gleam. date_time 1A9E63FCD880 -> 4582C7AD3F17 (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE), 0 new cells over 272. (2) requests.spi drops era_parts/year_of_era/month_of/day_parts and its civil_of becomes a 3-line i32<->i64 adapter over date_time::civil_of_days (EB1622AE69A1 -> 03044B269FB3, 152 -> 136 lines). vultr --check 0 for both. PROOF rides x-next7 (now 31 files): its notebook gate runs lib date_time's tests (execution, not just typing), and e2e covers requests. land-x-next7 lands date_time through lib_land_window FIRST (base 1A9E63FCD880, proven draft 4582C7AD3F17), then the x files. The kit share (agile_note etc.) stays with kit.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 7u32, "2026-11-05T00:48Z", "x", "2026-11-04 20:48 x: PRE-LAND FIX (caught by running lib_land_window's document_test checks on the draft BEFORE x-next7): date_time.spi did not round-trip spi -> livemd -> spi, because no blank line separated the civil_of_days_inverts_days_from_civil test from ':= micros_of_guid_prefix'. Blank line added: draft 4582C7AD3F17 -> 5ACE9C13DD10, unproven so far (x-next7 proves it), land-x-next7 pins updated. The same defect made x-next6's lib land close red at 20:35.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 8u32, "2026-11-05T03:07Z", "x", "2026-11-04 23:07 x: date_time draft stripped of its 17 inherited /// section headings (5ACE9C13DD10 -> ECE2A9DD6806; round trip OK 48/48); land-x-next7 pin updated.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_9 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 9u32, "2026-11-05T06:26Z", "x", "2026-11-05 02:26 x: CONTROL (box, pack40 core DDCA78971B4EAB36, run_notebook --gate): the STRIPPED date_time draft ECE2A9DD6806 passes 46/46, the lua target included. So the heading strip does NOT break timestamp_guid_from_timestamp; x-next7b's lua red came from the node's compiler changing mid-run (pack36 -> pack38 at 00:34, main's unannounced ship). The compiler lane confirms no lua codegen change across those packs, so a mid-run core swap is the remaining suspect. The unstripped arm is still running as the formal control. x-next7 re-runs on the node (now a stable pack40) after x-next8b frees the shared mirror.")
inl note_of_lib_move_civil_date_10 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-CIVIL-DATE", 10u32, "2026-11-05T10:10Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:09 x: LANDED via x-next7 (green run x-next7c, node). lib date_time ECE2A9DD6806 (chrono-free civil date math; 17 headings stripped) and requests.spi.")
inl lib_move_json_quote () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", "One complete JSON string quoter in lib json (RFC 8259: backslash, quote and every control below 0x20, \\u00XX escapes) replacing lib's own three partial copies (json.quote, json_schema.json_quoted, conversation.json_string) and 10 copies in x and kit, three of which do not escape at all", Story, P1, D3, 75u32, Active, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT", "lib,generic,main,team:main,team:kit,typefeatureset,json", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_move_json_quote () = Planning ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:48Z", "main", "11-01 18:5x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (read in place). lib, three partial quoters with different coverage: json.spi:13 quote (\\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t, other controls raw); json_schema.spi:97-108 json_escaped/json_quoted_from/json_quoted (same set, char by char); conversation.spi:46-69 json_specials/json_escape_of/json_string (only \\\\ \\\" \\n). x: apps/client/jsonl/jsonl.spi:11 quoted and apps/client/wire.spi:25 json_string (both serde_json::Value::from(s).to_string(), Rust only); apps/sim/spi/events.spi:45-64 hex_digit/unicode_escape/short_escape/control_escape/controls_from/without_controls/quoted (the only complete one, Gleam-safe Spiral); apps/sim/spi/simframes/simframes.spi:226 json_quoted (erlang json:encode + iolist_to_binary). kit: src/kit_memory_model/model.spi:152-153 escaped/quoted; src/agile_todo_model/model.spi:329 json_escaped; src/kit_grep_query/search.spi:84 json_text and src/kit_read_query/slice.spi:4 json_text (byte-identical multi-line host macros); src/kit_table_rows/rows.spi:13 escaped (\\\\ and \\\" only). NOT ESCAPING AT ALL (latent bug if a title holds a quote): src/agile_planning_model/model.spi:186 json_quoted, src/agile_task_inspection/task_inspection.spi:91 json_string, src/agile_task_listing/task_listing.spi:165 json_string. Excluded: lib xsd_emit.spi:107 escape_text (Spiral literal escaping, not JSON). LIB TARGET: json (existing module); json_schema and conversation import it. TYPED SHAPE: :! json_text = string (a nominal for already-encoded JSON, so a quoted value is never quoted twice or concatenated as raw text); quote (s : string) : json_text; field (name : string) (value : json_text) : json_text; json_text_raw (t : json_text) : string at the output edge. Implementation in plain Spiral (x events.spi's algorithm: short escapes for \\b \\t \\n \\f \\r, \\u00XX for other controls), no host macro, so it runs on every backend; an optional Rust fast arm may be one expression (serde is not a lib dependency, so no). DoD: (1) json.quote with a :# block (empty, plain, quote, backslash, each short escape, U+0001 -> \\u0001, U+001F, non-ASCII kept verbatim, round trip through json_scan's string reader) passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) lib's json_schema and conversation call it and their copies are deleted; (3) every x and kit site above switched, proven by x's client + xsim builds and kit's touched notebooks + crate regen (kit_grep_query and kit_read_query JSON receipts byte-identical on a fixture); (4) the three non-escaping kit sites get a regression row with a quote in the title.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:20Z", "kit", "11-01 21:19 kit, the three kit sites read in place: kit_memory_model/model.spi:152 (escaped: \\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t) and agile_todo_model/model.spi:329 (json_escaped: the same set) are PARTIAL (controls below 0x20 other than \\n\\r\\t pass raw, which is invalid JSON only for those rare inputs); kit_grep_query/search.spi:84 json_text is COMPLETE (\\u00XX for all controls) but a multi-line host block. None of kit's three is \"no escaping\". KIT PLAN: when lib json.quote is complete (RFC 8259; lift x apps/sim events.spi:45-64, the complete Gleam-safe Spiral version), kit replaces all three with json.quote (TRAIN9), adds a test with quote, backslash, \\n and \\x01 to agile_todo_model and kit_memory_model, and removes the host block in kit_grep_query.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:20Z", "main", "main 21:2x CORRECTION from kit (read in place): kit's copies are PARTIAL, not 'no escaping'. kit_memory_model/model.spi:152 and agile_todo_model/model.spi:329 escape backslash, quote, \\n, \\r and \\t, but other controls below 0x20 (\\b \\f \\x01) pass raw; kit_grep_query/search.spi:84 json_text is COMPLETE (\\u00XX for every control) but a multi-line host block. The three non-escaping copies must be in x or lib; re-locate them before quoting the claim again. PLAN (agreed with kit): (1) lib json.quote becomes complete per RFC 8259 by lifting x's apps/sim events.spi:45-64 (complete and Gleam-safe), with tests for quote, backslash, \\n, \\x01 and \\u001f; owner x, since lib-reshape has finished. (2) kit switches its three sites to json.quote in TRAIN9. (3) The other copies in x and lib follow.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:26Z", "x", "2026-11-01 21:26 x: LIB HALF STARTED (main 21:2x handed it to x). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE\\json.spi (base 514F84651989): json.quote is now RFC 8259 complete, lifted from x apps/sim events.spi:45-64. It escapes backslash and quote, uses short forms \\b \\t \\n \\f \\r, and writes every other control below 0x20 as \\u00XX via hex_digit/unicode_escape/controls_from (unicode.char_of, which sits before json in lib's module order). 3 new test blocks on rust + gleam: quote/backslash, \\n\\t short forms, \\x01 and \\x1f as \\u0001\\u001f. Behaviour change for callers: only strings containing \\b, \\f or other controls now escape (before, they passed raw and produced invalid JSON). PROOF x-json-quote1 (Vultr, lib_gate -Test on the 3 blocks), rule written before the run: PASS iff 3 executed, 3 passed, 0 failed/unsupported on both targets. Land through lib_land_window after lib-reshape R1b+R2 closes (re-base then), then tell kit for TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_5 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 5u32, "2026-11-02T01:30Z", "x", "2026-11-01 21:30 x: x-json-quote1 (Vultr, 55 s) by n4's rule: PASS. The mirror's json.spi equalled the draft's base (514F84651989), and the draft C82278F5C371 reports 'tests: passed 3 failed 0' for the 3 filtered blocks (15 in the file), type errors 0. A target-level failure would mark its test failed, so rust and gleam both passed. LAND: lib_land_window -Draft json.spi=<store> -BaseHash 514F84651989 after lib-reshape R1b+R2 closes. If R1b moved json.spi, rebuild the draft from live first (the swap anchors on the old quote body). Then tell kit, which switches its 3 partial copies to json.quote in TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_6 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 6u32, "2026-11-02T02:07Z", "x", "2026-11-01 22:07 x: LANDED 22:06 as a guarded copy (tree-write win-1793585196666; TRAIN8s builds from a snapshot): lib/spiral/json.spi 514F84651989 -> C82278F5C371, the exact text gated 3/3 on Vultr (n5). Undo: spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\x-json-quote-20261101-220636. Consumer proof: x-verify48 (x has no json.quote caller, so it only proves lib still compiles in x's build). NEXT: tell kit to switch its 3 partial copies in TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_7 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 7u32, "2026-11-02T02:12Z", "main", "main 22:1x lib half DONE: x landed the RFC 8259-complete json.quote at 22:06 as a guarded copy (lib/spiral/json.spi 514F84651989 -> C82278F5C371, the vultr-gated text). Kit is told and switches its 3 partial copies in TRAIN9. The remaining copies in x and lib follow under this item.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_8 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 8u32, "2026-11-02T02:15Z", "kit", "11-01 22:15 kit: switched (unstaged, TRAIN9) after x's complete lib json.quote (22:06). (1) agile_todo_model finding_json now uses json.quote for path, id and text (the partial json_escaped is removed), plus the test finding_json_escapes_quotes_backslashes_newlines_and_controls (quote, backslash, \\n and \\x01 -> \\u0001); (2) kit_grep_query json_text = json.quote text (a 6-line host block removed). (3) kit_memory_model escaped/quoted was NOT switched: it writes Spiral string literals into generated memory .spi modules (Spiral source, not JSON), so JSON's \\u00XX escapes do not apply there; the sweep misclassified it. Ratchet ok for both packages; the notebook proof rides the TRAIN9 pre-proof.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_9 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 9u32, "2026-11-02T06:47Z", "kit", "11-02 02:5x kit: CODE SIZE. lib json.quote's controls_from takes a static c, so every consumer unrolls all 32 control passes. Each of the 32 sm'.replace calls has its escape string precomputed, which gives a 94-line function in each crate. kit TRAIN9 stopped at the crate gate on this: agile_todo_lines todo_lines.rs went 960 -> 1053, and a :~ wrapper alone only got it to 1032. kit_grep_query is 780. FIX: make c dynamic (~c), so it becomes a runtime loop with the same output. Base json.spi 794C9C3AAEA3CA73. PROOF kit-json-dyn (node, job-1793602015364). Rule, written before the run: PASS iff lib_program_gate runs the 3 quote blocks with 3 passed, 0 failed, 0 type errors, AND the regenerated agile_todo_lines is under 1000 lines with the crate gate at 0 over. Then land with land-lib-program -Note LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE/<this n> and run kit TRAIN10.\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit json.spi expect files 1 replacements 1\nreplace once \":~ ^ controls_from (c : i32) (t : string) : string =\" with \":~ ^ controls_from (~c : i32) (t : string) : string =\" RETRACTED 02:5x by kit: the diagnosis was WRONG. controls_from is already a runtime loop, because :~ ^ join-point arguments are dynamic, so the ~c program changes nothing (proof kit-json-dyn: lib gate GREEN 3/3, but todo_lines stays at 1032). Its 94 lines are just the loop body: char_of validation, the short-escape option chain and the \\u00XX list join. DO NOT LAND this program. See the next note for the real fix.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_10 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 10u32, "2026-11-02T06:59Z", "kit", "11-02 02:5x kit: RUST FAST ARM for json.quote, the 'optional Rust fast arm' this item's design allows. Rust now escapes in one pass: kit's old proven complete escaper (char::from(34/92), no backslashes in the macro) plus short forms for codes 8/9/10/12/13 via b\"btn_fr\". Every other backend keeps the plain Spiral path unchanged. A new test covers \\b \\f \\r on rust and gleam. Why: the Spiral body generates about 120 lines in every Rust consumer, and that pushed kit agile_todo_lines over the 1000-line crate gate (TRAIN9 stop). PROOF kit-json-fast (node, job-1793602449709), rule written before the run (note 9 + gate): lib_program_gate GREEN, 4 passed 0 failed, 0 type errors, base 794C9C3AAEA3CA73 -> target 20C39CB971506A36; kit regen agile_todo_lines 1032 -> 909, kit_grep_query 780 -> 662, crate gate 0 over of 273; agile_todo_model notebook 13/13 on the fast arm. Round trip: canonical true, fixpoint true. LAND: land-lib-program -Note LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE/10 -File json.spi -Base 794C9C3AAEA3CA73 -Target 20C39CB971506A36.\nPROGRAM (kit do <lib> -):\nedit json.spi\npatch <<<\n@@ -29,3 +29,10 @@\n := quote (s : string) : string =\n-    := escaped = s |> sm'.replace \"\\\\\" \"\\\\\\\\\" |> sm'.replace \"\\\"\" \"\\\\\\\"\" |> controls_from 0i32\n-    sm'.concat_list \"\" [ \"\\\"\"; escaped; \"\\\"\" ]\n+    run_target \\|\n+        | Rust => \\ () =>\n+            $'std::rc::Rc::<str>::from({ let q = char::from(34u8); let b = char::from(92u8); let mut out = String::from(q); \\\n+                for c in (!s).chars() { let n = c as u32; match n { 34 | 92 => { out.push(b); out.push(c); } 8 | 9 | 10 | 12 | 13 => \\\n+                { out.push(b); out.push(char::from(b\"btn_fr\"[(n - 8) as usize])); } n if n < 32 => out.push_str(&format\\!(\"{b}u{n:04x}\")), \\\n+                _ => out.push(c) } } out.push(q); out }.as_str())' : string\n+        | _ => \\ () =>\n+            := escaped = s |> sm'.replace \"\\\\\" \"\\\\\\\\\" |> sm'.replace \"\\\"\" \"\\\\\\\"\" |> controls_from 0i32\n+            sm'.concat_list \"\" [ \"\\\"\"; escaped; \"\\\"\" ]\n@@ -41,2 +48,7 @@\n     quote \"x\\ny\\tz\" |> _assert_eq \"\\\"x\\\\ny\\\\tz\\\"\"\n\n+///> rust\n+///> gleam\n+:# quote_uses_short_forms_for_backspace_formfeed_and_return =\n+    quote (sm'.concat_list \"\" [ unicode.char_of 8i32; unicode.char_of 12i32; unicode.char_of 13i32 ]) |> _assert_eq \"\\\"\\\\b\\\\f\\\\r\\\"\"\n+\n>>>")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_11 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 11u32, "2026-11-03T00:53Z", "x", "2026-11-02 20:5x x: x's remaining copies, read in the tree. (1) apps/client/wire.spi json_string and (2) apps/client/jsonl/jsonl.spi quoted both call serde_json::Value::from(s).to_string(), which matches the complete Rust fast arm of lib json.quote byte for byte (short forms for 8/9/10/12/13, lowercase \\u00xx otherwise, quote and backslash escaped, DEL kept). Both are DRAFTED as json::quote s in kit drafts x/LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE (wire A99E258DE7EB to 84D5D141C3C2, jsonl 6BC0D61A28C2 to A3688F90194D). (3) The sim simframes json_quoted uses Erlang json:encode and writes byte-compared frame files, so it stays until a frames proof covers the switch. (4) The escape helpers in the sim events module are the DECODE side (an unescaper), not a quoter, so they're out of scope; their replacement is the Cells json_value parser once lib can host it. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-e2e-quote-clock1, one x e2e run together with LIB-MOVE-UNIX-CLOCK's x sites after x-lib-clock1 lands): sim build exit 0, client build exit 0, and x e2e RUST-OK with the request count unchanged from the last green e2e and no FAILED line.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_12 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 12u32, "2026-11-03T03:29Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:29 x: x-e2e-quote-clock1 failed at the sim build. wire.spi declares its own nominal ':! json = serde_json::Value' (line 14), so inside that module json::quote resolves to the local type, not the lib json module (ETY-TermError: Got serde_json::Value, Expected .quote). The wire switch is DROPPED from this batch. Making it needs wire's json nominal renamed (serde_value) across the module, a separate slice with its own e2e. jsonl.spi doesn't see a json name (its opens aren't transitive) and stays in x-e2e-quote-clock2 with the clock sites, rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_13 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 13u32, "2026-11-03T03:32Z", "x", "2026-11-02 23:32 x: DECIDED by rule (the item replaces PARTIAL or hand-rolled quoters): wire.spi's json_string STAYS as serde_json::Value::from(s).to_string(). It's serde's own complete RFC 8259 escaper, in a module whose whole JSON layer is typed serde_json::Value (the json nominal; about 900 references in the file). Switching would mean renaming that nominal module-wide to free the json name, which is risky churn for a one-line dedupe that changes no bytes. So x's share ends with jsonl.spi (in x-e2e-quote-clock2) plus simframes (Erlang json:encode, kept for its byte-compared frames).")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_14 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 14u32, "2026-11-03T04:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:31 x: jsonl.spi LANDED on lib json::quote (A3688F90194D), proven in x-e2e-quote-clock4 (client build 0, RUST-OK 37+5). x's share is DONE: jsonl switched; wire's serde quoter and simframes' Erlang json:encode kept by recorded rule (n13, n11).")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_15 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 15u32, "2026-11-03T05:05Z", "x", "2026-11-03 01:05 x: x's share DONE and landed tonight (see the notes above), so team:x is removed from the tags. The other teams' tags stay, for the remaining kit and main sites. Resume condition for x: none, unless a lane hands an x site back.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_16 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 16u32, "2026-11-04T20:58Z", "kit", "11-04 22:4x kit: a LIVE repro of why one complete quoter matters: `kit agile show <root> KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS --json` (installed TRAIN14c) prints invalid JSON (\"Invalid control character at char 25475\" in python json.load). A note on that item holds a raw BEL (0x07) where \"\\agile todos\" was typed (a \\a escape turned into a control char on the way in), and the JSON writer passes it through unescaped. RFC 8259 requires \\u0007 there, which is exactly the control-below-0x20 clause of this item's title. Test to add with the fix: a note containing 0x07 and 0x1B round-trips through show --json as \\u0007 / \\u001b.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_17 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 17u32, "2026-11-04T21:27Z", "kit", "11-04 23:2x kit: kit's two partial quoters behind `agile show --json` are FIXED (unstaged): agile_note_model.note_json_at copied each note's stored Spiral literal straight into JSON (Spiral's \\\" \\\\ \\n escapes happen to be JSON, so it mostly worked, but a raw control byte like the 0x07 on KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS passed through); it now decodes the literal with the model's own unquoted and re-encodes with lib json.quote (complete: quote, backslash, every control below 0x20). agile_task_inspection.json_string wrapped title/tags/deps in quotes with NO escaping at all (a quote in a title broke the JSON); it is now json.quote. Touching note_json_at also migrated it off rust_std_string concat5 to sm'.concat_list (the style hook's rule). vultr --check ok (note_listing, task_inspection); consumers sized in job kit-size-json; the notes CLI checks (exact at/author/text output) ride the next train.")
inl note_of_lib_move_json_quote_18 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-JSON-QUOTE", 18u32, "2026-11-05T23:26Z", "main", "main 11-05 19:3x CHECK on the installed kit (kit.exe of 11-03 06:07): 'agile show <backlog> KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS --json' still emits the raw 0x07 at char 25475, so it's still invalid per RFC 8259 (PowerShell's ConvertFrom-Json is lenient and accepts it; python json.load rejects it, per kit n). kit's fix (note_json_at + json_string through lib json.quote, 11-04 23:2x) is not installed yet: TRAIN32 has kit reds, so it won't install, and the fix rides TRAIN33. Verify after that install with a strict parser, plus the 0x07/0x1B round-trip test kit named.")
inl lib_reshape () = Task ("LIB-RESHAPE", "Reshape lib/spiral destructively and flat: drop the m suffix and primes (old->new table), merge x_real.spir into x.spi, flatten rust/ (leptos/ui stays), with every consumer repo switched in the same land and proven by its own gate; compatible with upstream core (core names untouched)", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "-", "lib,naming,structure,edition3,typefeatureset,main,team:main,kit,x,tibia,fiscal,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_reshape () = Planning ("LIB-RESHAPE", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_reshape_1 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:50Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 11-01 18:5x PLAN (user 11-01 ~17:40: finish the destructive changes, merge spir into spi, drop the m postfix, flat layout except leptos/ui, :: kept). MEASURED FIRST, so the order follows evidence. (A) UPSTREAM CONSTRAINT, PROVEN ON THE NODE (compiler DBC5EC18, job dir C:\\home\\remote-stage\\lib-reshape-repro): a lib MODULE named like a core TYPE shadows the type. Package |core- + module option.spi + main.spi 'let x : option i32 = Some 3i32' fails 'main.spi:2:13: ETY-ExpectedSymbolAsRecordKey: Expected symbol as a record key. Got: i32'; the same package with the module named optionx compiles. Cause: inferIn_module (spiral_compiler.fs ~4486) and in_modulePrepass (~7148) put every module into the TYPE env under its own name. So am'->array, listm'->list, optionm'->option, resultm->result are BLOCKED on a compiler change (MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE, filed); core's names (option, result, list, array, listm, optionm, arraym, sm) stay untouched, which keeps upstream compatibility. (B) COLLISION SCAN of every candidate name against the flat modules (core base/core/types, lib am'_prototypes/backend/base/iter_prototypes/sm'_prototypes/trace/common): only option/result/list/array collide; map, dict, text, parallel, *_prototypes, *_operators are free. (C) RENAME TABLE old -> new (flat, underscore scales: family prefix, no folders): am'_prototypes -> array_prototypes; sm'_prototypes -> text_prototypes; optionm'_operators -> option_operators; par' -> parallel; mapm -> map; dictm -> dict; sm' -> text; sm'_operators -> text_operators; sm'_real.spir -> text_real.spir (then merged into text.spi); rust/rust -> rust; rust/rust_operators -> rust_operators; rust/near -> near; rust/near_workspaces -> near_workspaces; rust/clap -> clap; rust/testing -> rust_testing (testing.spi exists); BLOCKED on MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE: am' -> array, listm' -> list, optionm' -> option, resultm -> result (array_dim stays, already canon). SPIR MERGES, BLOCKED on SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION (compiler lane, parser per-statement segment): cli_args_real.spir -> cli_args.spi, json_real.spir -> json.spi, routes_real.spir -> routes.spi, sm'_real.spir -> text.spi. FOLDERS: leptos/ (ui/, svg/) stays (user); bench/ is its own package, stays; near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi lives inside the wallet project (848 files), stays until dice decides; rust/ is flattened: it buys nothing, because ':< rust_operators' already resolves flat today (am', async, crypto use it) and the folder only adds the 'rust.rust_operators' spelling plus the open-path resolution trap (LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED: ':< leptos::leptos' from inside the folder gives ETY-ModuleIndexFailedInOpen; '::' in open paths itself parses). (D) CONSUMERS, git grep over C:\\home\\git (uses/files; eoie is a junction to kit and is not counted): sm' spiral 1180/66, kit 1201/195, fiscal 1681/48, x 318/56, dice 147/13, tibia 69/17, polyglot 69/4, alphabet 65/1, blog 23/8, dir-tree-html 5/2, plus ':< sm'_operators' opens in about 350 files of every repo (also Cells document_test.exs fixtures and x e2e fixture texts); am' spiral 372/32, kit 211/60, dice 140/11, alphabet 30/2, polyglot 15/2, tibia 12/6; optionm' spiral 336/36, kit 85/64, dice 74/15, alphabet 19/1; resultm spiral 343/28, dice 48/5, alphabet 39/1, kit 19/16, polyglot 17/1, x 3/3, fiscal 2/1; listm' spiral 203/25, kit 83/36, fiscal 76/9, dice 15/3, x 7/3; dictm x 217/10, kit 6/2, spiral 1/1; mapm spiral 18/5 (apps/spiral 6, lib benchmark/dictm/sm'/state_core), kit 4/3 (kit_log_counts, kit_log_sections, kit_log_sequences), dice 4/2; par' 0 outside lib (kit standards/lint-macros-lib.spi:209 names the file 'par'.spi'); rust.rust_operators opens dice 16, polyglot 2, alphabet 1, apps/spiral + apps/wasm 2; clap spiral 103/3, alphabet 20/1. (E) STEPS, in order, each one land of lib + consumers through apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 (now with -Remove/-RemoveHash and 'new' base hashes, added today), each consumer repo proven by its own gate on the node first: R1a TODAY lib-only, zero consumers: the four prototypes/operators/par' renames. R1b mapm -> map: lib 5 files + apps/spiral 6 sites + kit 3 files + dice 2 files; hazard: a file that opens a module exporting a term 'map' (listm', am') sees the function, not the module; the compile catches it. R2 rust/ flatten: pre-step rewrites consumers to ':< rust_operators' (already resolves, zero risk), then the move; rust/testing -> rust_testing. R3 dictm -> dict with x (217 sites). R4 sm' family -> text family: the big one (5,000+ sites, every lane); hazard: a local named 'text' shadows the module (compile-detected); pre-step per repo renames such locals; one coordinated land with each lane's node gate, no alias shims (aliasing := f = text::f risks closures on C/WGSL, memory spiral-eta-reduction-makes-closures). R5 after MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE: array/list/option/result. R6 after SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION: the four spir merges. (F) TOOLS TO TOUCH per step: lib/spiral/build.ps1 notebook list, apps/cells/spi/lib_consumer_signatures.tsv, type_probe.ps1, Cells document_test.exs fixtures, kit standards/lint-macros-lib.spi known rows, kit/x/tibia/fiscal package manifests that name lib modules, apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/lib-usage-*.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_2 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:51Z", "main", "main 18:5x DoD: (1) lib/spiral holds no file or module name with an apostrophe or an m suffix except the four blocked on MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE until it lands, then none; (2) no .spir file in lib after SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION (the four merges done, lib_sweep equal per file before/after); (3) no subfolder in lib except leptos/ (ui/, svg/), bench/ (own package) and near/wallet (project dir); (4) every consumer repo (spiral apps, kit, x, tibia, fiscal, dice, alphabet, dir-tree-html, regex, polyglot, blog) has 0 uses of any old name (git grep with the rename table, word-bounded) and passes its own gate on the node after each step; (5) each step's lib land closed green through lib_land_window (signatures, consumers, document_test, type_probe with no new failures) with its undo dir recorded in a note; (6) every lane was told the files and time before and the re-base after. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the rename table is data, a union per change (RenameModule of old * new | MoveFile of old_path * new_path | MergeReal of real_file * typed_file) with a nominal module_name, consumed by one kit do program per step, never per-site sed strings; the collision check (module name vs flat type/term names) is a fold over typed definition rows (the usage census rows, LIB-USAGE-DIAGNOSTICS). NEXT STEP: R1a land after the held heavy window (compiler-pack15b-predict) releases.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_3 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 3u32, "2026-11-01T23:04Z", "main", "main 19:1x R1b DRAFTED (mapm -> map), not landed: drafts in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\r1b\\<repo>\\<path> (made by a word-bounded transform 'mapm' before '::'/'.' -> 'map'; 26 sites in 10 files, base hashes): spiral lib benchmark 3 (1C4173712C3A), dictm 4 (BE9F5ABEE05C), sm' 4 (F0F51690C5BB), state_core 2 (E46E265D4D79), apps/spiral/spiral.spi 6 (22D4D3739948); kit src/kit_log_counts/count_scan.spi 2 (EC491500B29E), kit_log_sections/section_scan.spi 1 (D6CCE8400AEF), kit_log_sequences/sequences.spi 1 (D0D44734A20F); dice ui/src/components/app.spi 1 (0B92EECAD19E), ui/src/model/near/rpc.spi 3 (A5433610FD92); plus map.spi (= mapm.spi, 0 self-references), lib/spiral/build.ps1 notebook list \"mapm\" -> \"map\" (E356CA57C2ED), and the live manifest's 'mapm' line at land time. Hazard scan: no consumer file opens a module exporting a term 'map' (am', iter, listm', mapm, optionm', par', resultm, seq, stream do); state_core.spi:333 has a parameter named map in a function without map uses. Other references in spiral: none. NEXT: node gates (kit's three packages via kit's own build on a kit mirror, dice ui compile on a dice mirror, apps/spiral compile), then one land through lib_land_window with the kit and dice files edited in the same minute, with the kit lane told first.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_4 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 4u32, "2026-11-01T23:08Z", "main", "main 19:2x groom + drift count (user: lanes drift back to !!!!Export and big macro blocks). In the 9 lib files R1a/R1b touch: !!!!Export 0. Long host-text macros: sm'.spi 6 (159 and 161 wasm call chains with '\\' continuations, 679 a Rust iterator chain, 1244 a Zig concat, 1514 a Zig 'blk: { ... }' block, 2339 an F# let-in), state_core.spi 2 (11 and 83, rexie builder chains); par'/prototypes/operators/mapm/benchmark/dictm 0. NOT fixed in R1b: the rename transform stays byte-minimal so its proof is 'only mapm -> map changed'; the 8 go to GRANULAR-HEAL's queue as one-expression primitives (sm' 1514 first: a whole Zig block). R2 FINDING: consumers reach rust/testing.spi's run_tests/run_tests_log as 'testing.run_tests' (apps/spiral/spiral.spi:1753, alphabet apps/documents/documents.spi:686, polyglot lib/math/math.spi:480), because the folder module shadows top-level testing.spi after the rust open. So flattening rust/testing to rust_testing (its ':# rust_testing static' header already uses that name) means those 3 sites become rust_testing.run_tests, and kit's standards/lint-macros-lib.spi:243 row 'rust/testing.spi' becomes 'rust_testing.spi'. R2 sites in total: rust::rust_operators 22 + rust.rust_operators 2 (spiral), 14 (dice), 1 (alphabet), 2 (polyglot), plus those 3 testing sites. Fields checked: estimate 900, load medium, assignee agent, tags, DoD (n2), next step (R1a land after the heavy window, then R1b node gates).")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_5 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 5u32, "2026-11-01T23:13Z", "main", "main 19:1x R1a PROVEN ON THE NODE (mirror C:\\home\\remote\\lib-reshape-r1a at box head b3fd292b + working tree, digest 6477DB01DD5D7A13, compiler DBC5EC18; drafts copied in, the 4 old files removed): type_probe 6/6 PASS (array_prototypes, text_prototypes, option_operators 0 tests; parallel 6 tests typed; base 25 and sm' 72 as flat-module consumers of the renamed prototypes), apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles to Rust (1,476,448 B). Land script: session scratchpad land-r1a.ps1 (re-derives package.spiproj from live, then lib_land_window -Draft/-BaseHash 'new'/-Remove/-RemoveHash). Waiting on the compiler's heavy window (compiler-pack15b-predict) for the box close.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_6 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 6u32, "2026-11-01T23:19Z", "main", "main 19:2x R2 open question, recorded so the next pass doesn't rediscover it: flattening rust/near.spi gives a top-level module 'near', and the near/ folder (near/wallet/src/near_wallet.spi) also makes a module 'near'. The compiler merges same-name modules (spiral_compiler.fs ~7132, EModule x + EModule x'), so both may resolve. PROVE on a node mirror that near.gas_to_usd (dice 77 uses in 6 files, polyglot chat_contract 25, lib near_workspaces 3) and the wallet module both still resolve. If they don't, move near_wallet.spi flat (dice owns the wallet project's build path) rather than renaming near.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_7 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 7u32, "2026-11-01T23:26Z", "main", "main 19:2x R1b SPIRAL SIDE PROVEN ON THE NODE (same mirror, R1a applied first, then the R1b drafts, the manifest line mapm -> map and mapm.spi removed): 0 mapm uses left in the mirror; type_probe 5/5 PASS (map 0 tests, benchmark 2, dictm 5, sm' 72, state_core 0); apps/spiral compiles to Rust, same 1,476,448 B. Still open for R1b: kit's 3 packages (compile via each package's entry.spi on a kit mirror against this lib; kit lane gate) and dice ui (app.spi, rpc.spi). R2 EVIDENCE that rust/ doesn't pay: the compiler carries a special 'index module' rule (spiral_compiler.fs ~8058, module_member) only so that rust.box works when rust names the folder rust/ holding rust.spi, plus an ambiguity error for keys that are both a sibling and a member; flattening makes that rule dead weight (a compiler cleanup item once R2 lands).")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_8 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 8u32, "2026-11-01T23:50Z", "main", "main 19:5x R2 TRIED ON THE NODE AND RED, cause found (nothing landed): the naive flatten (6 files moved out of rust/, rust/testing -> rust_testing, the four manifest blocks flattened, 24 'rust::rust_operators'/'rust.rust_operators' sites rewritten to 'rust_operators') fails type_probe 12/12 and both apps (apps/spiral, apps/wasm exit 5) with resultm.spi:33 'Got .<term> Expected () -> result t exn' and am'.spi:468 'Got i32 Expected .for''. CAUSE: 45 files say ':< rust' (lib 38 incl. 14 leptos/ui+svg, apps/spiral, apps/wasm, dice 3, alphabet 1, polyglot 2). Today that opens the FOLDER module, which brings only the submodule names (clap, near, testing, rust_operators, near_workspaces) into scope: rust.spi's own members are reachable only through the compiler's index-module rule for 'rust.x'. After the flatten the same line opens rust.spi's 88 members, among them 'loop' (rust.spi:425) and 'try' (a type, rust.spi:40), which shadow core's loop module and base's try. RULE FOR R2: delete every bare ':< rust' (the submodules are top-level after the flatten, so nothing is lost), don't rewrite it. Then the 'testing.run_tests' sites (spiral.spi:1753, alphabet documents.spi:686, polyglot math.spi:480), which reach rust/testing through that open, become rust_testing.run_tests. Rerun the node proof with that rule before any land.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_9 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 9u32, "2026-11-01T23:55Z", "main", "main 19:5x R1a LANDED AND CLOSED GREEN (lib_land_window, tree-write window win-1793576904886, 19:48-19:54): lib/spiral am'_prototypes.spi -> array_prototypes.spi (400665235053), sm'_prototypes.spi -> text_prototypes.spi (4A6F6F92AA77), optionm'_operators.spi -> option_operators.spi (4B2963B26B89), par'.spi -> parallel.spi (DD557ECD8D3B; ':# parallel static' and the 'parallel.map: a worker crashed' label), package.spiproj 9D730998B805 (re-derived from live, so tibia's wire/fixed_views/case_labels lines are kept). Close: 14 signatures unchanged; apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles; document_test 22 passed; type_probe 4/4 PASS. Undo: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-194824 (the 4 old files + the old manifest). Left for others: kit standards/lint-macros-lib.spi:209 'par'.spi' -> 'parallel.spi' (kit lane, told). Tool change landed with it: lib_land_window.ps1 gained -Remove/-RemoveHash (removed files go to the undo dir and come back on any red) and 'new' as the -BaseHash of a new file.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_10 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 10u32, "2026-11-02T00:03Z", "main", "main 20:0x R2 v2 GREEN ON THE NODE, spiral side (same mirror, stacked on R1a + R1b): with the n8 rule (40 bare ':< rust' lines deleted in 38 files, none rewritten) plus 'testing.run_tests' -> 'rust_testing.run_tests' in apps/spiral/spiral.spi, type_probe is 14/14 PASS (rust, rust_operators, rust_testing 3 tests, near, near_workspaces, clap 3, date_time 43, common 7, am' 18, crypto 7, file_system 36, process 18, resultm 6, sm' 72). apps/spiral compiles to Rust at 1,476,448 B, byte-for-byte the same size as before R1a/R1b/R2, so codegen is unchanged; apps/wasm compiles (202,858 B). Draft program: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\r2-node-proof.ps1 + r2b-node-proof.ps1 (the transforms). Left before an R2 land: dice (3 ':< rust', 14 rust.rust_operators), alphabet (1 + 1 + documents.spi:686 testing.run_tests), polyglot (2 + 2 + math.spi:480), kit (3 'rust' references to check), each compiled against the mirror lib, and the leptos/ui+svg modules (14 of the 38 files; type_probe baseline-red, so dice's ui compile is their proof).")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_11 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 11u32, "2026-11-02T00:12Z", "main", "main 20:1x sequencing with the cell-budget splits (main FYI): R4/R6 touch sm'.spi + sm'_real.spir, both top-10 by excess weight. Filed LIB-SPLIT-TEXT (rename first, split after, on text.spi). R2 only deletes one ':< rust' line in file_system/process/date_time/state_core etc., a transform that re-derives on any base, so it doesn't collide with splits of those files (tibia LIB-XCOMPAT-TIBIA-DEFS, told to resume).")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_12 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 12u32, "2026-11-02T00:26Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 20:2x HANDOFF: R1b+R2 is READY and HELD for kit's TRAIN8 (main's call 20:2x: the train reads the live lib, so this lands only after kit reports TRAIN8 installed, or at 21:50 at the latest). Main lands it. COMMAND (re-derives every draft from the live tree, so tibia/fiscal lands in between are kept; it refuses if a base hash moved): pwsh -NoProfile -File C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\land-r1b2.ps1 (dry run lists 53 drafts and 7 removes), then the same with -Apply. It calls apps/cells/spi/lib_land_window.ps1 with -Draft (51 lib files + '../../apps/spiral/spiral.spi' + '../../apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.spi'), -BaseHash (each live hash; 'new' for clap, near, near_workspaces, rust, rust_operators, rust_testing, map), -Remove 'rust/rust.spi,rust/rust_operators.spi,rust/testing.spi,rust/near.spi,rust/near_workspaces.spi,rust/clap.spi,mapm.spi' with -RemoveHash taken live, and -Consumer apps/spiral/spiral.spi + apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.spi. lib_land_window now skips type_probe for '../' pairs. Bases at 20:2x: package.spiproj 9D730998B805, build.ps1 E356CA57C2ED, mapm.spi 9A72B1B86979, rust/rust A5A927AA1E49, rust/rust_operators ADBE15F56ADD, rust/testing 1F94D7AD1D25, rust/near 7217E5044434, rust/near_workspaces 22997B54C812, rust/clap CD60529CFCF6, apps/spiral/spiral.spi 22D4D3739948, apps/wasm/spiral_wasm.spi 0DA16176B84A. The transforms: mapm before ::/. -> map; delete a line that is only ':< rust'; rust::rust_operators / rust.rust_operators -> rust_operators; in the apps, testing.run_tests -> rust_testing.run_tests. AFTER IT CLOSES GREEN: (1) remove the empty lib/spiral/rust/ folder; (2) consumers: pwsh -File C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\r1b2-consumers-apply.ps1 -Apply edits dice 14 files, alphabet 1 (apps/documents/documents.spi), polyglot 2 (apps/chat/contract/chat_contract.spi, lib/math/math.spi) and kit 3 (only the 4 mapm sites), with backups and -Undo; (3) kit updates its standards/lint-macros-lib.spi rows (par'.spi, rust/clap 2, rust/near 9, rust/rust 2, rust/testing 3) (told); (4) tell all lanes to re-base; (5) remove the node junction C:\\home\\remote\\lib-reshape-r1a\\kit\\src\\spiral before deleting that mirror (memory unlink-mirror-junctions-first). PROOF so far (node mirror C:\\home\\remote\\lib-reshape-r1a): lib type_probe 14/14 + 5/5, apps/spiral 1,476,448 B (unchanged), apps/wasm compiles, kit_log_sections/counts/sequences compile; dice/alphabet/polyglot compiles: see the next note.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_13 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 13u32, "2026-11-02T00:36Z", "main", "main 20:3x re-base check after x's 20:31 lib land (package.spiproj 9D730998B805 -> 1269095979F8, erlang_text/erlang_map/erlang_file registered): land-r1b2.ps1 re-derives every draft from the live tree, and its dry run is clean on the new base (53 drafts, 7 removes). The n12 base list is informational only; the script takes hashes live.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_14 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 14u32, "2026-11-02T00:54Z", "main", "main 20:5x R1b+R2 CONSUMERS PROVEN ON THE NODE (mirror C:\\home\\remote\\lib-reshape-r1a; same transforms as r1b2-consumers-apply.ps1; packageDir pointed at the mirror lib): dice 21 sites, alphabet 3, polyglot 5 rewritten, and every entry compiles to Rust: dice contract/dice_contract.spi 173,582 B, dice ui/src/dice_ui.spi 1,833,009 B (this also proves the 14 leptos/ui+svg modules that type_probe can't check, LEPTOS-UI-TYPE-PROBE-RED), alphabet apps/documents/documents.spi 957,793 B, polyglot apps/chat/contract/chat_contract.spi 84,848 B, polyglot lib/math/math.spi 297,256 B. With n7 (lib 14/14 + 5/5, apps/spiral unchanged size, apps/wasm) and the kit compiles (kit_log_sections/counts/sequences), every consumer of R1b+R2 is green. Cargo builds weren't run (Spiral -> Rust only); the land close and each repo's next CI cover them. Ready for main after TRAIN8 (n12 has the command).")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_15 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 15u32, "2026-11-02T00:57Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 21:0x CLOSING NOTE (time box), for main and the next pass. AFTER main runs land-r1b2.ps1 -Apply and r1b2-consumers-apply.ps1 -Apply (n12), rerun these consumer proofs on the box's real trees: (a) the land close already covers apps/spiral + apps/wasm (consumers), document_test and type_probe; (b) kit: compile src/kit_log_sections/entry.spi, src/kit_log_counts/entry.spi and src/kit_log_sequences/sequences.spi (or kit's own gate for those 3 packages); kit's next TRAIN covers them in full; (c) dice: contract/dice_contract.spi and ui/src/dice_ui.spi (Spiral -> Rust, then the ui cargo build in dice CI); (d) alphabet: apps/documents/documents.spi; (e) polyglot: apps/chat/contract/chat_contract.spi and lib/math/math.spi. Node evidence for every one is in n14; if any goes red, run r1b2-consumers-apply.ps1 -Undo and the lib undo dir that lib_land_window prints. REMAINING STEPS, in order: R3 dictm -> dict: lib dictm.spi + 1 spiral site, x 217 sites in 10 files, kit 6 in 2 (agree the timing with x; the same transform-and-prove pattern as r1b2, with x's own gate on a node mirror). R4 sm' family -> text family (sm', sm'_operators, sm'_real.spir -> text, text_operators, text_real.spir): 5,000+ sites plus about 350 ':< sm'_operators' opens. MEASURED HAZARD (21:0x): files that use sm' AND bind a local named 'text' (a parameter, a lambda or a := binder) would see the local instead of the module: spiral 29 of 66, kit 138 of 197, x 33 of 56, tibia 13 of 21, fiscal 3 of 48, dice 2 of 13, others 1-2 each, about 225 files and 245 binder sites. DECISION (by rule: NAMING-LEXICON-RATCHET's lexicon names the 'text' module): keep the name text; the pre-step renames those binders (to s/input/line by role) repo by repo as its own proven change, then the rename runs as one transform per repo, all landed in one window with every lane's node gate; no alias shims. LIB-SPLIT-TEXT follows R4/R6. R5 (after MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE): am' -> array, listm' -> list, optionm' -> option, resultm -> result. R6 (after SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION): merge cli_args_real/json_real/routes_real/text_real .spir into their .spi. R7: compiler cleanup item for the index-module rule (spiral_compiler.fs ~8058) once no lib folder has an index module (leptos/leptos.spi still is one: check before filing). Also open: near/ folder vs flat near.spi is resolved by the R2 proof (dice near.* compiles), so nothing is needed there.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_16 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 16u32, "2026-11-02T01:09Z", "main", "main 21:1x R3 (dictm -> dict) PROVEN ON THE NODE, not landed (stacked on the R1b+R2 mirror): lib dictm.spi -> dict.spi (':# dict static'), manifest line, and the qualified 'dictm.'/'dictm::' plus ':< dictm' rewritten: x 262 sites, kit 6 (src/agile_task_listing/task_listing.spi), spiral 0 outside dict.spi. type_probe dict.spi PASS (5 tests). x apps/sim/spi/simframes/simframes.spi -> Gleam 1,306,833 B and xsim_split.spi -> Gleam 132,487 B compile; kit agile_task_listing/task_listing.spi -> Rust 58,574 B compiles. Program: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\r3-node-proof.ps1 (the transforms). Before landing: x's own gate (apps/sim/build.ps1 incl. gleam-modules and the sim e2e runs) on a mirror, agree the timing with x, and kit's lint row 'dictm.spi' (standards/lint-macros-lib.spi:98) -> 'dict.spi'. Land it like r1b2: a land script deriving from live + a consumer apply with -Undo.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_17 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 17u32, "2026-11-02T02:05Z", "main", "main 22:0x R1b+R2 LANDED GREEN (land-r1b2.ps1 via lib_land_window, 21:01-22:01): 14 signatures unchanged, apps/spiral and apps/wasm compile, document_test 22 passed, type_probe with no new failures (18 leptos svg/ui modules failed before the land too). Undo: spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261101-210258. Consumers applied by r1b2-consumers-apply.ps1: dice 14, kit 3, polyglot 2, alphabet 1 (undo dir drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\r1b2-consumers-undo). The empty lib/spiral/rust/ is removed. Lanes got the re-base notice at 22:0x. Fiscal's XSD-CROSS-NAMESPACE-NAMES landed right after (22:02). Next per the plan: dictm->dict (agree a time with x), sm'->text (local renames first), MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE (compiler), spir merges (SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION).")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_18 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 18u32, "2026-11-02T02:12Z", "main", "main 22:1x SCHEDULE for dictm -> dict (217 x sites by x's count, plus 6 in kit): run it only AFTER x-verify48's outputs land (node job-1793585509485, ~3-5 h), because renaming x sources under its sync manifest makes that land refuse them. x messages when landed; if not by 08:00 (11-02), go ahead and x re-verifies on top. R1b touched nothing in x.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_19 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 19u32, "2026-11-02T04:42Z", "main", "main 00:4x R3 (dictm -> dict) LANDED GREEN via land-r3.ps1 / lib_land_window (00:36-00:41): 14 signatures unchanged, apps/spiral + apps/wasm compile, document_test 22/22, type_probe dict PASS (5) json PASS (15). Undo: spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261102-003654. Consumers by r3-consumers-apply.ps1: x 10 files / 262 sites (apps/sim/spi), kit 2 files / 6 sites (task_listing.spi + lint_known_98 row -> dict.spi); undo drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\r3-consumers-undo. 0 module refs left in spiral/x/kit; local helpers dictm_first/dictm_last/dictm_term_sorted kept (not module refs). Upstream forks, eoie and backlog notes untouched. FIRST ATTEMPT 00:26 refused (CLOSE FAILED, auto-restored): document_test 20/22 on the tree WITHOUT R3 too; cause json.spi:48 double blank from x's 22:06 json.quote land (round-trip collapses it) -> fixed in the R3 drafts. Gate gap: that land skipped document_test; x told. x re-verifies on top. Next: sm' -> text needs local renames first; am'/listm'/optionm'/resultm blocked on MODULE-TYPE-NAMESPACE; spir merges on SINGLE-SPI-EXTENSION.")
inl note_of_lib_reshape_20 () = Note ("LIB-RESHAPE", 20u32, "2026-11-02T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-02: status reads 0% Planned although the respell, R1a, R1b+R2 and R3 landed green (notes n12-n19); the status update was lost. Correct status to Active ~60% when next touched. LIB-SPLIT-REVIEW (filed 11-02) reviews whether the reshape improved or regressed lib.")
inl lib_move_read_text () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT", "kit's private read-a-file-or-empty host bindings (11 copies across 10 packages, plus rooted and CRLF-normalizing variants) switch to lib file_system.read_text_or_empty, which already exists and which 4 kit packages already call; lib gains the two missing variants (read under a root, newline-normalized) and a typed read outcome for the callers that need the error", Story, P2, D2, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT", "lib,generic,main,team:main,team:kit,typefeatureset,file_system", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_move_read_text () = Planning ("LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_move_read_text_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-READ-TEXT", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:50Z", "main", "11-01 18:5x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (read in place). Exact copies of lib file_system.spi:877 read_text_or_empty (Rc::<str>::from(std::fs::read_to_string(&*!path).unwrap_or_default())): kit src/kit_experiments/ledger_host.spi:16 file_text; src/proxy_text_replacement/text_replacement.spi:30 file_text; src/kit_jobs/host.spi:54; src/rust_std_fs/model.spi:124 (loaded_text wrapper); src/kit_machine_watch/jobs_watch.spi:109 (inline in previous). Variants: src/kit_guide/guide.spi:11 text_of (strips \\r); src/agile_lease_terms/terms.spi:45 trimmed_file_text (trims); src/kit_table_logs/logs.spi:30 file_text (lossy UTF-8 from bytes); src/cold_proof_domain/native_binary_tests.spi:6 read (unwrap = lib read_all_text); rooted (root joined with a relative path): src/kit_do_git_host/host.spi:33 and src/kit_do_write_host/host.spi:45-46 file_text. Already on lib (the pattern to copy): src/kit_standards/standards.spi:9, src/agile_memory_links/links.spi:9, src/kit_memory_model/model.spi:9 exact_text, src/kit_style_census/census.spi:8. Error-carrying reads that format their own message (candidates for the typed outcome): src/kit_cli_model/argument_file.spi:21, src/owner_growth_runtime/growth.spi:11, src/rating_guard_runtime/guard.spi:9, src/patch_driver_domain/source_authoring_terminal.spi:131. Overlap: EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY owns kit's rust_std_fs package as a whole; this item is only the read-text family and lands through it if that lane prefers. LIB TARGET: file_system (existing). TYPED SHAPE: :| text_read = TextRead of string | TextMissing | TextUnreadable of string (reason), read_text (path) : text_read; read_text_or_empty stays the total form; read_text_lf (path) : string (CRLF -> LF, built on read_text_or_empty + sm'.replace, no host code); rooted reads use the existing (</>) on a :! root_dir nominal, not a new host macro; lossy decoding as one granular binding rust_text_lossy (bytes). DoD: (1) file_system definitions with a :# block (missing file -> TextMissing and \"\", CRLF file -> LF, invalid UTF-8 -> lossy text with U+FFFD) passing in Cells on rust and fsharp (gleam arm for read_text_or_empty added if missing); (2) every kit site above calls lib, proven by the touched packages' notebooks + crate regen (cargo check), outputs byte-identical; (3) the private copies are deleted.")
inl lib_move_x_sim_erlang () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-X-SIM-ERLANG", "x's xsim (cells_executor, simframes, sim_serve) still calls erlang_term::apply directly for ~25 host operations that lib erlang_file, erlang_map, erlang_process, erlang_port, unicode and xml already wrap; switch them and move the 6 real gaps (term type tests, list length/nth, stderr text, BEAM memory MB, plain argv, byte size) into those lib modules", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT,LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB", "lib,generic,main,team:main,team:x,typefeatureset,erlang", "current", "current")
