inl note_of_lib_usage_verb_1 () = Note ("LIB-USAGE-VERB", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:54Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 11-01 19:0x. WHAT EXISTS (found first): the compiler's SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT recorder (spiral_compiler.fs ~7752, PrepassReferences: def/use rows with path+line, open-resolved names, nominal constructors and prototypes since pack 4) writes TSV rows at process exit; apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1, lib-usage-consumers.ps1, lib-usage-references.ps1 aggregate them (pwsh, untyped); kit has 'standards --census' (rule counts) and 'lint macros'/'lint shadows' (host macros, shadowing), none of which count calls; Cells reports test rows per file. Nothing yields per-definition call counts by repo. INTERIM TODAY (text census, a throwaway pwsh glue in the session scratchpad, not a repo tool): typed rows in C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-RESHAPE\\usage_census.spi, 4,056 rows, schema 'union repo = Spiral | Kit | X | Tibia | Fiscal | Dice | Alphabet | DirTreeHtml | Regex | Polyglot | Blog', 'union kind = Inl | Let | Type | Nominal | Union | Prototype', 'union verdict = UsedOutside | LibOnly | FileLocal | Unused', 'nominal usage = { module; name; kind; self_uses; lib_uses; outside_uses; by_repo : list (repo * i32); verdict }'. The verb should emit exactly these rows (the shape is the spec). DoD: (1) 'kit lib usage <spiral-root> <repo-root>...' builds each repo's consumer entry points with SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT set (on the node by default; one job), resolves every use row to a lib definition by the recorder's E identity, and writes the rows file plus a per-module summary (defs, unused, file-local, outside uses, repos); (2) tests with a fixture lib of 3 modules and 2 consumer packages: a qualified use, an open-resolved use, a type-position use, a prototype instance, and an operator each land in the right repo column, and an unused definition gets Unused; (3) the three lib-usage-*.ps1 scripts are deleted after one run agrees with them on the 10-18 baseline names; (4) LIB-RESHAPE and LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT cite its rows for keep/test/drop. TYPEFEATURESET: phantom-tagged paths (:! Lib / :! Consumer) so a lib row can't be counted as outside, the verdict union above, repo a closed union read from the roots' manifests, no string-keyed maps in the output.")
inl note_of_lib_usage_verb_2 () = Note ("LIB-USAGE-VERB", 2u32, "2026-11-01T22:58Z", "main", "main 19:0x groom: NEXT STEP (kit, CPU-light): the typed row model (repo/kind/verdict unions, usage nominal) plus the use-row resolver as a HostFree kit package with the fixture tests from the DoD; the compiler-run half (SPIRAL_REFERENCES_OUT over each repo on the node) comes second. Owner kit, main reviews the rows against the 11-01 text census (usage_census.spi in the LIB-RESHAPE drafts dir). Estimate 480m, load medium.")
inl lib_move_text_helpers () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", "Small text helpers re-implemented per package (number-to-text i32_text/u64_text/decimal_text/count_text in ~28 places, padded in 8, lines_joined in 10, unquoted in 8) switch to lib sm' (decimal_text, pad_left/pad_right exist); sm' gains the two missing ones (a newline join that skips empty sides, strip one surrounding quote pair) and a code-point-counting pad, since kit's padded counts chars while sm' pads by length", Story, P2, D2, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT", "lib,generic,main,team:main,team:kit,typefeatureset,sm", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_move_text_helpers () = Planning ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_1 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 1u32, "2026-11-01T22:56Z", "main", "11-01 19:0x main (lib-reshape generic-code sweep). SITES (kit src/<pkg>/<file>:line unless marked, read in place). NUMBER TEXT (all = sm'.decimal_text, sm'.spi:2323, or sm'.show): i32_text agile_task_census/task_census:11, kit_standards/rules:45, kit_grep_query/search:90, agile_memory_links/links:8, kit_handoff_render/render:30, host-macro copies kit_table_query/cells:52, workspace_primitives/numbers:6, kit_experiments/ledger_host:29; u64_text kit_cli_check/cli:97, command_spec_domain/model:369, kit_adoption/run:9, agile_lease_terms/terms:84, kit_machine_watch/run:12, host-macro copies workspace_primitives/numbers:8, proxy_failure_classification/failure_classification:50; decimal_text kit_jobs/stop_cli:145, kit_lcov/lcov:66, kit_do_program/compiled:8, kit_receipt/receipt:15, kit_repo_state/repo:55, kit_jobs/host:16; count_text kit_process_table/model:58, kit_guide/guide:28, kit_memory_model/model:20, kit_resume/resume:16, kit_machine_watch/jobs_watch:7, kit_table_logs/logs:10, kit_style_census/census:7, x apps/client/posts.spi:121, lib xsd_regex.spi:756 (hand-rolled digit recursion). PADDING: identical host macro (pads to chars().count()) agile_planning_fields/planning_fields:7, agile_planning_rollup/planning_rollup:43, agile_task_listing/task_listing:42, agile_task_next/task_next:23; format!(\"{:<w$}\") kit_cli_check/cli:221, kit_process_table/listing:97; zero pad x apps/sim/spi/world.spi:305 (= sm'.pad_left w '0'); lib xsd_regex.spi:872 padded. NEWLINE JOIN skipping empty sides (? right = \"\" ?> left |? left = \"\" ?> right |: left ++ \"\\n\" ++ right): kit_do/run:57, kit_do_jobs/run:33, kit_do_lab/run:33, kit_do_read/run:40, kit_do_tables/run:20, kit_do_write/run:41, kit_do_facts/run:69, kit_do_git/run:41, kit_do_process/run:41, kit_do_edit/run:64. STRIP ONE QUOTE PAIR (byte_slice token 1 (len - 1)): agile_planning_gaps/gaps:20, agile_planning_rollup/planning_rollup:94, agile_planning_tally/planning_tally:34, agile_task_next/task_next:22, agile_task_listing/task_listing:40, agile_planning_migration/planning_migration:93, quote_stripped variants agile_note_model/model:134, agile_task_inspection/task_inspection:51. Not the same concept, left alone: kit_standards/rules:131 and kit_ci_model/tools:37 (remove every quote). LIB TARGET: sm' (existing). TYPED SHAPE: :! column_width = i32 counted in code points (unicode.code_point_count), pad_right_to (w : column_width) (fill : char) (s : string) and pad_left_to; the existing pad_left/pad_right keep their length semantics and say so in their test; line_joined (left : string) (right : string) : string; quote_pair_stripped (q : char) (s : string) : option string (None when s is not wrapped in q, so a caller cannot strip an unquoted token silently). DoD: (1) sm' definitions with :# blocks (pad of 'é' to 3 = 'é  ', pad of a longer text unchanged, line_joined with each side empty, quote_pair_stripped on '\"a\"', 'a', '\"', '') passing in Cells on rust, fsharp and gleam; (2) every site above switched, proven by kit's touched notebooks + crate regen with byte-identical table output (agile list, kit do receipts), x's xsim build, and the lib xsd_regex gate; (3) the copies deleted. Overlap: EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY covers workspace_primitives/numbers as a package; this item covers the per-package copies.")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_2 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:10Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:10 x: x's SHARE. (1) apps/client/posts.spi count_text is already a one-line call to sm'.obj_to_string (no re-implementation), so x leaves it; the call sites read better through the name. (2) apps/sim/spi/world.spi padded (a hand-rolled zero pad) becomes sm'::pad_left width '0' (sm'::obj_to_string n): pad_left is backend-neutral (replicate) and its twin pad_right is gated on gleam. Draft kit drafts x\\LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS\\world.spi, base 357D2B331A6A -> 561F876D817C. It rides the next x sim proof (the clock and date texts reach it through the sim e2e; the -Accept build checks the budget). Nothing else of x's is on this item's site list.")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_3 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 3u32, "2026-11-03T20:17Z", "x", "2026-11-03 16:17 x: x's SHARE LANDED: apps/sim/spi/world.spi 357D2B331A6A -> 561F876D817C (padded = sm'::pad_left width '0' (sm'::obj_to_string n)), proven in x-next1b (sim accept 0 with no fixture changed, sim build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5), plus its 1 regenerated sim output. x has nothing else on this item's site list.")
inl note_of_lib_move_text_helpers_4 () = Note ("LIB-MOVE-TEXT-HELPERS", 4u32, "2026-11-04T12:24Z", "x", "2026-11-04 08:24 x: dropped team:x (as with LIB-MOVE-CLI-PRELUDE). x's share landed 11-03 (x-next1b). Re-checked now over x/apps/*.spi for local i32_text/u64_text/decimal_text/count_text/padded/lines_joined/unquoted/pad_*: 3 definitions, all one-line wrappers over lib sm' (client posts count_text = sm'::obj_to_string; census count_text = label plus sm'::obj_to_string; sim world padded = sm'::pad_left width '0'), none re-implements a helper. The rest is kit's sites (team:kit/main).")
inl lib_move_dth_fs () = Task ("LIB-MOVE-DTH-FS", "dir-tree-html shared.spi carries its own host bindings for path join, is-file, write, mkdir and temp dir plus a hand-rolled i64-to-text, all of which lib file_system and sm' already provide; switch its 40 call sites to lib and delete the copies (its write/mkdir return an error flag, so lib gains typed result-returning forms if write_all_text's unit return is not enough)", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "LIB-GENERIC-AUDIT", "lib,generic,main,team:main,typefeatureset,file_system,dir-tree-html", "current", "current")
