inl note_of_html_model_7 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 7u32, "2026-11-03T02:39Z", "tibia", "11-02 22:4x tibia (auto-claimed by the gate): the DoD's CELL BUDGET RUN done and it is NOT clean. mix spiral.cell_budget --check over html src/*.spi (7 files, html 05162bd, box tree): cell-budget report: 38 finding(s) in 7 file(s) (autolink 6, hashtag 4, mention 1, over_budget 27); exit 1 \"27 definition(s) over the cell budget; split them\". Largest: src/tree.spi:72 (weight 560 > 272), tree.spi:98 (375), tree.spi:103 (371), tree.spi:130 (324). No edits made: splitting 27 definitions in main's html tree is main-lane code, so tibia releases the item with this measurement. Next for main: split the 27 over-budget definitions (helpers per definition, as the cell budget asks), then rerun the budget and the 44 Cells tests.")
inl note_of_html_model_8 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 8u32, "2026-11-03T02:40Z", "tibia", "11-02 22:4x tibia, re-claimed by the gate; RELEASED again, with the full list so main can plan the split (it is a refactor of main's markdown engine, not a mechanical edit for another team). The 27 over-budget definitions (weight > 272), html 05162bd: parser state machines markdown.spi:160 blocks_from 1801, inline_parse.spi:74 inlines_from 1482, markdown.spi:67 classify 549, :132 close 464, :141 continued 445; renderers render.spi:83 block_html 577, :21 inline_html 513, :45 cells_html 317, tree.spi:72 node_html (with the :& nodes_html group) 560, file_views.spi:57 viewer_body 413, :45 tab_cells 290, pages.spi:66 head_html 307, :81 file_page_of 299, tree.spi:67 file_html 282, model.spi:101 escape_from 311, tree.spi:30 compare_from 335; small loops markdown.spi:96 cells_from 299, :107 delimiter_chars 279, :115 delimiter_aligns 281, :153 numbered 289, :192 lines_from 284; data and fixtures pages.spi:11 style () 971 (a CSS literal: split into several literals joined with ^^), render.spi:146 table_md 407, :158 readme_md 388, tree.spi:98 nested_a 375, :103 nested_b 371, :130 (a test block) 324. Suggested order: fixtures and the CSS literal first (mechanical, no behavior), then the small loops, then the renderers, and the two parser loops last, as extracted per-case helpers.")
inl note_of_html_model_9 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 9u32, "2026-11-03T02:44Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:5x CELL BUDGET run (box, mix spiral.cell_budget over html src/cli/markdown, 9 files): 43 findings (over_budget 31, autolink 7, hashtag 4, mention 1); src has 27 over_budget + 11 link-like. FIXED so far (unstaged, 0 findings per file now): model.spi (escape_from 311 -> escape_step, a non-recursive (start, acc) step, + a plain recursive loop; NOTE: a ':&' mutual group counts as ONE cell, so splitting into a mutual pair raised it to 402; 'optionm.map' -> 'optionm::map', the edition-3 separator a renderer won't read as a domain) and file_views.spi (tab_cells 290 -> a cell_of helper; viewer_body 413 -> source_view/table_view/prose_view; 'listm.map' -> 'listm::map'). LEFT: inline_parse.spi:74 (weight 1482, the inline parser loop), markdown.spi 9 + 3 link-like, render.spi 5, tree.spi 6 + 2, pages.spi 3 + 4; cli/html.spi 4 + 1. Semantics proof: node html gate after the regex job (parallel Cells interfere).")
inl note_of_html_model_10 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 10u32, "2026-11-03T02:57Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:0x CELL BUDGET progress (unstaged; over_budget counts per file now): model 0, file_views 0, render 0 (inline_html/inlines_html mutual pair -> inline_by r x with the list renderer passed in; per-case helpers; fixture blocks separated by blank lines, since adjacent defs count as one cell), pages 1 (only style (), the 971-weight CSS string; split it only with a byte-identity pin, its test checks just the tail), cli/html 0 (the walk/nodes_of/node_at triple -> walk passed as 'descend'; put_page, page_at, render_mode helpers; mode_of/write_file_page lose a needless ^). Hashtag/mention/autolink findings are warnings only (--check fails on over_budget alone) and are CSS colors/@media/README.md names: left. LEFT over_budget: inline_parse.spi:74 (1482), markdown.spi 9, tree.spi 6. PROOF: box Cells gate over src running; then a node html full build (also tests pack19 Step B vs the 1000-line gate).")
inl note_of_html_model_11 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 11u32, "2026-11-03T03:00Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:1x tree.spi 0 over_budget (compare_from -> char_order; file_html -> raw_link; the node_html/nodes_html mutual pair -> node_by r + folder_html; nested_a/nested_b fixtures split into a1/b1 parts, names kept because cli/html.spi's self-test uses them; plain_fixture for the last test). The first box re-gate (model/file_views/render/pages edits) was 44/44, memo off, pack20. NOT DONE TONIGHT, design recorded instead: markdown.spi 9 (the main one is blocks_from at 1801: a 4-way mutual group blocks_from/line_step/row_step/resume) and inline_parse.spi:74 (1482, the inline loop). Splitting them is a parser restructure, not a mechanical split. Plan: (1) a cursor record { lines : list string; state : pending; blocks : list block }; (2) every step (code_step, table_step, line_step, row_step) is NON-recursive and returns the next cursor (resume becomes plain construction; the InTable non-row case returns lines unchanged with state Idle so the line is re-read); (3) blocks_from is the only recursive function: [] -> finish, else step and loop. Same shape for the inline parser. Proof bar: the 9 markdown + 7 inline_parse + 10 render tests incl. the dir-tree-html README fixture byte-for-byte, and pages' head/file-page tests.")
inl note_of_html_model_12 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 12u32, "2026-11-03T03:06Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:2x RE-GATE GREEN after the tree.spi + pages.spi splits: html src 44/44 on the box (pack20, memo off), per file unchanged (file_views 4, inline_parse 7, markdown 9, model 5, pages 4, render 10, tree 5). The cli/html.spi splits are proven by the full build (BuildSpiral + cargo + --self-test), next on the node.")
inl note_of_html_model_13 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 13u32, "2026-11-03T03:12Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:1x FULL BUILD on the node (mirror htmlm, html 05162bda + tree, pack20): BuildSpiral markdown/entry.rs (7 s) and cli/html.rs (11 s) compile, and 'dist/html --self-test' PASSES, so the cli/html.spi cell-budget splits are proven end to end. The build then stops at the 1000-line gate: markdown/entry.rs has 2218 lines (2570 before Step B). The remaining shrink is html adopting link: units (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS, whose Rust/Gleam slices 3+4 ship in pack21, installing now), so HTML-CI-RELEASE stays behind that item, not behind this one.")
inl note_of_html_model_14 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 14u32, "2026-11-03T03:14Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:2x TWO DRAFTS of the blocks_from split, both on a scratch copy only (scratchpad md-split), NOT applied: (a) a cursor record { lines; state; blocks } with non-recursive steps: 13 over_budget, every step pays 'c::state c::blocks' repetition; (b) the loop passed as a parameter k (the inline_by trick from render.spi) with ':== loop = list string -> pending -> list block -> list block': 12 over_budget, and blocks_from itself reads 671, which suggests the function-type alias does not end a cell (the next definitions merge into it). Both are worse than today's 9. LESSON: mechanical splits work for leaf-heavy matches (model/file_views/render/pages/tree/cli all went to 0), but a 4-way recursive state machine needs (1) a check of how cell_budget delimits ':==' aliases, and (2) smaller per-state step functions written by hand. Kept at 95%; the remaining DoD is exactly markdown.spi's 9 and inline_parse.spi's 1.")
inl note_of_html_model_15 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 15u32, "2026-11-03T03:21Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:2x markdown.spi: 11 'listm.' sites respelled 'listm::' (the edition-3 separator; unstaged), removing both autolink warnings and one over_budget (115: delimiter_aligns 281 -> under); markdown gate 9/9 on the box (pack20, memo off). How cell_budget delimits cells (cell_budget.ex:98 top_level_blocks): a block starts at a non-indented line after at least one blank line; dots in member access ('.') cost extra weight (defused_dots), '::' does not. Remaining over_budget: markdown 8 (classify 549, cells_from 301, delimiter_chars 279, close 468, continued 445, numbered 289, blocks_from group 1802, lines_from 285) + inline_parse 1.")
inl note_of_html_model_16 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 16u32, "2026-11-03T03:24Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:2x markdown.spi leaf splits (unstaged): classify -> listed (bullet/number fallthrough), close -> finished, continued -> joined_trim, delimiter_chars -> table_char, numbered short names; over_budget 9 -> 7; markdown gate 9/9 on the box (pack20, memo off). Two tries made weights worse (a local binding in lines_from, a line break in cells_from: each line carries its own weight) and were reverted. Left over_budget in markdown: classify 309, cells_from 301, close 420, continued 377, numbered 275, the blocks_from group 1802, lines_from 285; plus inline_parse 1. Stopping here for tonight; the group needs the design pass in n14.")
inl note_of_html_model_17 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 17u32, "2026-11-03T03:28Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:3x markdown.spi over_budget 7 -> 4 by renaming locals inside lines_from (acc, start), cells_from (acc, stop, cell) and numbered (no logic change); markdown gate 9/9 (box, pack21, memo off). Left: classify 301, close 420, continued 377, the blocks_from group 1802; inline_parse 1.")
inl note_of_html_model_18 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 18u32, "2026-11-03T03:32Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:4x markdown.spi: close -> numbered_block/table_block payload helpers (354 -> 315); continued -> a non-recursive grow (the state update) + a continues predicate (an explicit 3-case match, not an or-pattern) so continued itself is under budget; markdown gate 9/9 (box, pack21, memo off). Over_budget left in markdown: classify 301, close 315, grow 285, the blocks_from group 1802; inline_parse 1. html cell budget overall: 31 over_budget at 22:5x -> 5 now.")
inl note_of_html_model_19 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 19u32, "2026-11-03T03:38Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:4x markdown.spi: classify -> shaped (row/heading/list fallthrough), close gets bullets_block/code_block payload helpers + short locals; classify is now under budget, close 282, grow 283 (each ~10 over). Gate 9/9 (box, pack21, memo off). CAUGHT ON READ-BACK: an automated rename bs -> b collided with the pattern variable 'InBullets b' (':: b' would have meant the bullets tuple); renamed the pattern variable to u before gating. html total over_budget now 4: markdown close 282, grow 283, the blocks_from group 1802, and inline_parse:74 1482 (plus pages' style () data string, intentionally whole). Stopping the cell-budget pass here for tonight.")
inl note_of_html_model_20 () = Note ("HTML-MODEL", 20u32, "2026-11-03T04:46Z", "main", "main 11-03 00:4x DONE. 'mix spiral.cell_budget --check' over all 9 html files (src, cli, markdown) exits 0: 0 over_budget, down from 31 at 22:5x; the 8 findings left are warnings only (4 CSS hashtag colors, 1 @media mention, 3 README.md/dotted autolinks). Last steps: (1) markdown's 4-way recursive blocks_from group (1802) is now small NON-recursive steps returning (lines, state, blocks) tuples (resume, row_step, item_step, ended, plain_step, line_step, code_step, table_step via a (state, line) tuple match, step), with blocks_from the only recursive function; (2) inline_parse's guarded loop (1482) is now typed tries (code/escape/strong/auto/image/badge/link) returning option (next, inline), chained by a lazy or_else (b : () -> found) (a : found) in the original check order, with inlines_from the only recursive function (it passes itself into strong_try for the nested parse); (3) pages' style () CSS (971) is split into style_1..style_6 joined with newlines, PINNED by a new test: length 728 and code sum 56008, identical before and after the split. PROOF: html src 44/44 on the box after the parser rewrites (render's README fixture byte-for-byte included), pages 5/5 with the pin; kit standards 0; full build compiles + --self-test (node). The full build's 1000-line gate (markdown/entry.rs 2218) is HTML-CI-RELEASE's, through link: units.")
