inl note_of_html_markdown_1 () = Note ("HTML-MARKDOWN", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED. DOD: parse : string -> list block plus parse_inline : string -> list inline; render (parse text) reproduces dir-tree-html selftest readme_body() byte for byte (headings, paragraphs, bullets, nested bullets flattened, fenced code, ---, GFM tables with :- -: :-: alignment and \\| escape, ordered lists with start=, lazy continuation, inline code, links, images, badges [![..](..)](..), **bold**, <https://..> autolinks, backslash escapes, non-ASCII text); one :# test per construct; generated Rust per crate < 1000 lines. NEXT STEP: line classifier union (Blank|Fence|Heading|Rule|TableRow|Bullet|Numbered|Plain) and the fold over lines, tests first. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the line kind is a closed union produced once by classify (no repeated prefix probes); the open block is a GADT-indexed builder state (open_para|open_list|open_ordered|open_code|open_table) so closing emits the right block by construction; table rows carry their alignment list from the delimiter row, never a re-parsed delimiter string as dir-tree-html does. FIELDS: estimate 300m, load light, assignee agent.")
