inl note_of_html_tree_1 () = Note ("HTML-TREE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:42Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED. DOD: walk : string -> list node (Folder name rel children | File name rel bytes), symlinks skipped, dirs first then ordinal name order; size_label 1024 -> 1024.00 B, 1025 -> 1.00 KB, 1048576 -> 1024.00 KB, 1048577 -> 1.00 MB; page = doc head + tree + README section + close, byte-identical to dir-tree-html fixture_body/order_body; tests write fixtures under get_temp_path with one guid dir per test. NEXT STEP: pure render of a node list (no I/O) under test first, then the walk crate. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: entry kind as a GADT (node folder | node file) so folder_bytes and file links only accept the right kind; sort via an ord prototype instance on entry keys instead of an i32 is_dir flag; the walk returns a typed result with the OS error kept (granular-style), not a silent ChildEnd. FIELDS: estimate 240m, load light, assignee agent.")
