inl note_of_html_tree_3 () = Note ("HTML-TREE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T04:48Z", "main", "main 11-03 00:5x STATE after HTML-MODEL Done: parity holds (tree.spi splits kept html src 44/44; nested and plain fixtures byte-identical; cli walk restructured with walk passed as 'descend', proven by the node full build's --self-test). The line-width part is done (kit standards 0). LEFT: (1) the 1000-line gate is HTML-CI-RELEASE's (markdown/entry.rs 2218 lines; html adopts link: units, which pack19..21 now support); (2) the deferred typed upgrades from n1: a node-kind GADT (node folder | node file), the sort through an ord prototype instance instead of folder_rank + compare_from, and a walk that keeps the OS error (names_of drops a read_dir error into []). Each changes the node union across tree, pages and cli, so it is a planned slice, not a midnight edit. Progress 75 -> 85.")
inl note_of_html_tree_4 () = Note ("HTML-TREE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:08Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:1x SLICE 'walk keeps the OS error' DONE (unstaged, cli crate only; the node union and the linked units are unchanged): cli/html.spi gains listing = Listed (list string) | Unreadable string; names_of returns it (the io_error rendered with sm'.format_debug, no new host text). render_tree refuses an unreadable root (Refused -> exit 2, no page written) instead of drawing an empty tree; walk reports an unreadable subfolder on stderr and draws it empty. Self-test case missing_refused added. Vultr fast build: HTML-OK (self-test incl. the new case), cli/html.rs 962 lines (< 1000), probe on /nonexistent: 'html: cannot read ...: Os { code: 2, kind: NotFound, ... }' exit 2, no page. cli/html.rs regenerated byte-identical on box and vultr (983999E7). kit standards cli 0. LEFT: the node-kind GADT and the ord-prototype sort (both change node across tree/pages/cli: one coordinated slice). Progress 85 -> 90.")
inl note_of_html_tree_5 () = Note ("HTML-TREE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T16:59Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:1x SLICE 'sort through a prototype' DONE (unstaged, html_pages/tree.spi): ':? listed_before t : t -> t -> bool', instance ':+ listed_before node' (dir-first, then ordinal names, the existing before), and the insertion sort generic over it: insert_by/sort_by \\* t {listed_before}; sort_nodes = sort_by. First prototype + instance + constrained generic in html (census prototype column was 0). pages.rs 887 -> 890 lines under pack26 (vs the pre-change file compiled with the same pack). PROOF vultr: tree.spi 5/5 (incl. folders_come_first_then_names_in_ordinal_order), pages.spi 5/5, fast build HTML-OK (self-test renders the nested fixture byte for byte). LEFT: the node-kind GADT. Progress 90 -> 95.")
inl note_of_html_tree_6 () = Note ("HTML-TREE", 6u32, "2026-11-03T17:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:1x DONE. DECIDED by rule, node-kind GADT RULED OUT: every node list is heterogeneous (a folder's children mix files and folders), so a kind index is erased exactly where the code works, and no operation needs kind-specific typing beyond the pattern matches already there. The real remaining typed gain, named fields instead of positional string * string tuples, is filed as HTML-NODE-RECORDS (P2). This item delivered: the typed walk with dir-first ordinal sort and size labels at dir-tree-html parity (232/232 pages earlier), the 1000-line gate via the split, the walk keeping OS errors (refused root), and sorting through the listed_before prototype.")
