inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_1 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:43Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED. DOD: rg 'dir-tree-html|dir_tree_html|dtl_' across all sibling repos returns only history/backlog hits (dangling-check-by-stem); dir-tree-html README points to i574n/html; spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 removed (archive-never-delete: archived copy in scratch archive); the user archives the GitHub repo. NEXT STEP: blocked on HTML-ADOPT-REPOS. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: n/a. FIELDS: estimate 60m, load light, assignee user (archive is a GitHub action).")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_2 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T12:27Z", "regex", "regex 08:3x ADVANCED for the user (11-02 \"advance what's needed to delete dir-tree-html\"): (1) html CI was red because its workflow (copied from dir-tree-html) lacked BEAM while build.ps1 runs Cells: fixed unstaged in C:\\home\\git\\html (erlef/setup-beam + actions.lock, gh actions-lock valid; HTML-CI-RELEASE n3); (2) repo metadata: i574n/html description set, dir-tree-html's description now says it is being replaced by i574n/html, LICENSE (AGPL v3) added to html; (3) i574n/html Pages can only be enabled after a green run creates gh-pages (next: enable right after). REMAINING ORDER: user push html -> green CI (both OSes) -> enable Pages -> HTML-CI-RELEASE release binaries -> HTML-ADOPT-REPOS (switch spiral/scripts/publish-tree.ps1 + dir-tree-html.ps1 and every caller: alphabet, blog, dice, eoie/kit, fc1943s.github, fiscal, fork-spiral-patch, i574n.github (build.ps1 builds ../../dir-tree-html), polyglot, spiral, tibia, x, regex, mechahaze/tapas2/vault via polyglot) -> HTML-PARITY re-run -> dangling check by stem -> this item: archive the dir-tree-html repo on GitHub (gh repo archive, user go) and the local clone (scratch-archive).")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_3 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:29Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:28 x: DECISION RECORD v2 (user 11-02: 'why mine? try healing autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups the pending decisions'). Only git commits (the user's standing rule) and the harness hook config (the harness itself says Claude must not change it) stay user-only. Everything else gets a precondition, a check and an undo; actions only the user's accounts can take get a non-blocking default. kind=ByTest. RULE: Agent archives i574n/dir-tree-html iff (a) rg over every sibling repo finds dir-tree-html/dir_tree_html/dtl_ only in history or backlog, (b) the README redirect is in dir-tree-html HEAD (committed by the user), and (c) no workflow in any repo installs it (TREE-PAGES-V2 pins by SHA). Then gh repo archive i574n/dir-tree-html --yes. BACKUP/UNDO: Undo: gh repo unarchive i574n/dir-tree-html --yes. OWNER: main.")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_4 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T07:58Z", "main", "main 11-03 03:5x INVENTORY + PLAN (paused until the user starts the run). dir-tree-html = 880 lines of Spiral in 7 files (shared, markdown, inline, tree, viewer, dir_tree_html, selftest), plus gh-pages.yml (a reusable workflow), actions.lock, a .devcontainer, and scripts init/publish/workflow/build. COVERED in html, as named tests: size labels per power; dir-first ordinal sort; folder byte sums; viewer pages with a raw link; TSV as a table with a header row; source escaped into pre/code; markdown viewer; headings (space, at most 6 hashes); paragraphs; nested bullets with lazy lines; ordered lists with a start; fenced code; GFM tables with alignment and escaped pipes; inline code, links, images, badges, strong, autolinks, backslash escapes; head/close/page bytes; the README and nested fixtures byte for byte. HTML-PARITY showed 232/232 identical pages on tibia, dir-tree-html and regex, viewers included. STILL TO CHECK: viewers never overwrite an existing .html (notebook pages); html's --self-test covers dir-tree-html's viewers_test and order_fixture. CALLERS: almost all go through ONE shim, spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 (it clones dir-tree-html at a643950e and builds it). That shim is the switch point: point it at html's release binary, and alphabet, dice (init and publish-bin), mechahaze-album1 and publish-tree.ps1 all follow. Exceptions: fc1943s.github/scripts/publish.ps1 still calls polyglot/apps/dir-tree-html/dist (a polyglot leftover; port it to the shim), and i574n.github's graphml mentions are generated text only. ORDER WHEN THE RUN STARTS: (1) HTML-CLI drop-in flags; (2) HTML-CI-RELEASE binaries (blocked on COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS); (3) the shim switch; (4) fc1943s.github off polyglot; (5) retarget DIR-TREE-MARKDOWN-GFM, PAGES-FILE-VIEWERS and TREE-PAGES-V2 to html, so dir-tree-html gets no new work; (6) delete dir-tree-html after a stem grep.")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_5 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T08:49Z", "main", "main 11-03 04:1x ORG EXIT DONE BY THE USER (11-03): dir-tree-html left the i574n org and is now fc1943s/dir-tree-html; GitHub redirects the i574n URL. This item's 'archive the GitHub repo (user step)' is therefore done. What remains is the code side: switch the shim spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 to html's release (HTML-ADOPT-REPOS), port i574n.github init/build off the dir-tree-html clone, then delete the local C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html after a stem grep plus a proper check that html holds every behaviour (the n4 inventory). Until the switch, every gh-pages run depends on the redirect (ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT a).")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_6 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 6u32, "2026-11-03T09:44Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:0x INVENTORY CHECKS from n4 resolved. (1) Never overwrite an existing .html (a Cells notebook page): html's cli write_file_page skips a file when path.html exists (cli/html.spi:68), the same rule as dir-tree-html's write_viewer. (2) dir-tree-html's self-test cases, mapped: page/fixture -> tree.spi nested fixture byte for byte plus the cli --self-test; total bytes -> folder_bytes_sum_their_children; order fixture -> folders_come_first_then_names_in_ordinal_order; readme -> render.spi readme fixture byte for byte; close -> pages.spi close_wraps_the_readme_before_the_body_end; size labels -> size_labels_switch_units_past_each_power; viewers_test -> NOT covered end to end. ADDED (unstaged) to html's cli --self-test: a viewer fixture (a.spi with an existing a.spi.html 'kept', b.tsv, c.txt) must write exactly 1 page, create b.tsv.html, leave a.spi.html as 'kept' and create no c.txt.html. That is dir-tree-html's viewers_test PLUS the no-overwrite rule, which neither project tested. Proof: the html full build's --self-test on the node after MIRROR-RESYNC-1103.")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_7 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 7u32, "2026-11-03T13:50Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:5x i574n.github PORTED OFF the dir-tree-html clone (unstaged, 8 deletions, both files parse): scripts/init.ps1 no longer clones dir-tree-html or runs its init; scripts/build.ps1 no longer builds it. Reason: spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 (the shim) provisions its renderer itself (clone at the pinned rendererCommit, init, build) when the exe is missing; the i574n.github clone at HEAD made the shim skip its pinned checkout (an unpinned renderer). Safe in any push order: before the shim switch the shim clones dir-tree-html via the redirect, after it html. Backups %TEMP%\\i574n-{init,build}.ps1.before-dth. LEFT: the shim switch (after the user pushes html), then the local dir-tree-html deletion after a stem grep.")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_8 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 8u32, "2026-11-03T13:52Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:5x STEM GREP of tracked .ps1/.yml/.spi/.toml/.json in alphabet, blog, dice, fiscal, kit, regex, spiral, tibia, x, vault, html, dotfiles: every caller goes through the shim spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 (alphabet init.ps1:28, dice init.ps1:32 + publish-bin.ps1:38, spiral publish-tree.ps1:14 + workflow.ps1:39, vault publish.ps1:69). No direct clone or build left. So the switch is one file (the shim); the later rename to html.ps1 touches exactly these 6 lines.")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_9 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 9u32, "2026-11-03T17:12Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:2x WORKFLOW CHECK: no .github/workflows file in alphabet, blog, dice, fiscal, kit, regex, spiral, tibia, x, vault, html or i574n.github, and no row in i574n.github's typed scripts/pins/workflows.spi, references dir-tree-html or polyglot. So its reusable gh-pages.yml has no caller and its loss can't break CI. Remaining gate unchanged: the shim switch after the user pushes html, then the local delete after the stem grep (n8: all 6 callers go through the shim).")
inl note_of_html_retire_dir_tree_10 () = Note ("HTML-RETIRE-DIR-TREE", 10u32, "2026-11-03T18:45Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x LOCAL COPY CHECKED: C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html is an exact mirror of its origin (github i574n/dir-tree-html, which redirects to fc1943s/dir-tree-html): main @ 71c801f, 0 ahead / 0 behind after fetch, clean, 0 untracked, no links inside. Deleting it loses nothing; it stays only until the shim switch so the current shim keeps a local clone to build from.")
inl html_parity () = Task ("HTML-PARITY", "html parity report: render the same repo trees (tibia, dir-tree-html, regex) with both renderers and diff the pages; every gap becomes an item", Story, P0, D3, 85u32, Active, "-", "html,pages,dir-tree-html,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
