inl note_of_html_parity_1 () = Note ("HTML-PARITY", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:43Z", "html", "html 19:4x FILED. DOD: for each of 3 repos, publish-tree-style dist copy rendered by dir-tree-html and by html, index.html and every viewer page compared byte for byte; the report lists equal/different counts and the first differing line per page, as typed rows rendered by html (no .txt); each difference is either fixed or an item. NEXT STEP: after the first node build of html. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: verdict union (Equal | Differs first_line | MissingLeft | MissingRight). FIELDS: estimate 120m, load medium, assignee agent.")
inl note_of_html_parity_2 () = Note ("HTML-PARITY", 2u32, "2026-11-02T01:02Z", "html", "html 20:5x PARITY RESULT (box, dist/html.exe vs C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html\\dist\\dir-tree-html.exe): index pages tibia/dir-tree-html/regex byte-identical; --viewers mode 232/232 pages byte-identical (tibia 179, dir-tree-html 29, regex 24). Known intentional differences not exercised by these trees: html escapes href/name of tree entries and viewer links (old wrote them raw, so names with & < > \" differed), ordered-list start is parsed as a number capped at 9 digits (old copied the digit text, '01.' gave start=\"01\"). Runner: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\html\\HTML-PARITY\\parity.ps1 (drafts store; port to a Spiral kit command under KIT-RUN-SPI before landing anywhere). NEXT STEP: rerun after each change and on the remaining publish-tree repos (spiral, kit, x, fiscal, blog, dice, polyglot, i574n.github, fork-spiral-patch).")
inl note_of_html_parity_3 () = Note ("HTML-PARITY", 3u32, "2026-11-04T16:16Z", "main", "11-04 12:2x main ORPHAN SWEEP: dep on HTML-CLI removed. Parity itself never needed CI green (HTML-CLI is Blocked only on the user's push), and the dep hid this item from agile next. NEXT STEP: rerun the parity diff with today's html (Picture and Diagram viewers, read_lossy) against dir-tree-html on tibia/regex/html trees on the node, and list each difference as intentional (new viewer) or a gap.")
inl note_of_html_parity_4 () = Note ("HTML-PARITY", 4u32, "2026-11-05T05:46Z", "main", "11-05 01:46 main PARITY RERUN with TODAY's html (68ccb00f, the 11-04 23:21 commit; built on the node by job main-html-build in 73 s, --self-test ok) against dir-tree-html.exe (11-01), box, parity.ps1 from the drafts store. INDEX MODE, 11 repos: byte-identical on dir-tree-html, regex, x, blog, dice (2 pages), alphabet, i574n.github, html, spiral (2 pages). VIEWERS MODE: dir-tree-html 29/29, regex 31/31, tibia 190/192. EVERY difference is a dir-tree-html defect that html fixes, none is a gap: (1) tibia README.md:271-274 and kit README.md:122-123 have code spans that cross a line break; CommonMark allows that (the line ending renders as a space), html renders <code>... -HealBelow 160 -StrikeAbove ...</code>, the old renderer left the backticks literal (tibia index + README viewer, kit index). (2) fiscal: dir-tree-html CRASHES reproducibly on fiscal's tree (exit -1073740791 = 0xC0000409 fail-fast), html renders a complete 65 KB index (closing </html>, 333 links), exit 0. So html is at parity or better everywhere; polyglot is retired and fork-spiral-patch is not on the box. LEFT by the DoD: the report as typed rows rendered by html (verdict union Equal | Differs first_line | MissingLeft | MissingRight), i.e. port parity.ps1 to a Spiral kit command under KIT-RUN-SPI; and once html replaces dir-tree-html, nothing here blocks the deletion (DIR-TREE-HTML retirement).")
inl html_lib_candidates () = Task ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", "html lib candidates: decide by reuse which generic pieces (html escaping, markdown model+parser, size labels, path joins, file walk, char classes) move to spiral/lib and which repo deps on which", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "HTML-MODEL", "html,pages,dir-tree-html,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_html_lib_candidates () = Planning ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_1 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 1u32, "2026-11-01T23:43Z", "html", "html 19:4x LIB CANDIDATES (reuse read 11-01, by grep): (1) HTML ESCAPING: four copies today - lib xml.spi escape_text_xml/escape_attribute_xml (xml.spi:401/407), blog engine/html.spi escape, dir-tree-html inline.spi escape_from, html src/render.spi. Decision: html's typed escape (escaped-text phantom) goes to lib as html.spi beside xml.spi, xml's escapes call it; blog and html import it. Users: html, blog, regex (bench report), x/tibia pages. LIB. (2) MARKDOWN MODEL + PARSER: users html (READMEs, .md viewers), blog (posts are .spi today, markdown planned), regex/fiscal READMEs via html. Decision: stays in html until a second consumer (blog) imports it; then lib markdown.spi. HOLD. (3) SIZE LABELS (show_hundredths, 1024 scale): users html, kit (byte counts in reports), tibia bench pages. Decision: lib units.spi already exists, add bytes_label there. LIB. (4) PATH JOINS (host_join, join_rel with '/', parent_text, leaf_name): file_system.spi already has path helpers; html must use them, adding only a url-relative join (always '/') to lib. LIB (small). (5) FILE WALK (sorted dir-first listing, symlinks skipped, sizes): users html, kit (census walks), publish-tree port to Spiral. Decision: lib file_system walk returning a typed tree with the OS error kept. LIB after HTML-TREE proves it. (6) show_i64/digit: lib already has number formatting (sm'.format / convert); html uses lib, no copy. NOT NEW. (7) DOC HEAD/CSS: html only (blog has its own style.spi). STAYS. PREBUILT BINARIES: one html release binary reused by all 12 Pages repos (HTML-CI-RELEASE) instead of 12 builds per push. NEXT STEP: land (1) and (3) through lib_land_window after HTML-MODEL tests pass on the node. FIELDS: estimate 120m, load light, assignee agent.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_2 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:50Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:2x DECIDED BY REUSE (user 11-03: 'multiple projects reimplement the same markdown logic ... now that we're having everything in spiral, we can reuse properly ... standardization inside the code too'). CENSUS (git grep of .spi/.ex over all org repos, 11-03): HTML escaping is implemented 5 times: html src/model.spi escape, blog engine/html.spi escape, kit src/agile_report_model escaped, dir-tree-html inline escape (retiring), and Cells apps/cells/spi/html_markdown.spi. Hand-built HTML tables, pages and headings appear in 4 more places: blog engine/post.spi (its own block model: Heading/Paragraph/code + render_block) and engine/index.spi, kit agile_report_model (cell/table/page shell), and regex bench/bench.spi (bench page table, unescaped). Markdown parsing exists 3 times: html src/markdown.spi + inline_parse.spi, Cells html_markdown.spi, and dir-tree-html (retiring).\nRULE, written first: a piece with 2 or more consumer repos moves to lib/spiral, which stays flat (lib-first-all-projects); a consumer's local module must not reuse the lib module's name (lib-module-name-shadows-core-type).\nDECISION: (1) lib/spiral/markup.spi gets the typed HTML markup core from html src/model.spi + render.spi: escape, the markup nominal, element and attribute builders, table_of, and the page shell. (2) lib/spiral/markdown.spi gets the block/inline model and parser from html src/markdown.spi + inline_parse.spi, portable with x's gleam targets (CELLS-HTML-PARITY). (3) html keeps the product: tree, pages, file_views, the CLI.\nCONSUMERS AND OWNERS after (1)-(2) land: blog engine (html.escape, post render_block -> lib markdown/markup; owner blog's team or main), kit agile_report_model (kit), regex bench page (main), Cells html_markdown.spi -> lib markdown (x, already planned), html itself (main). DONE per consumer: its own escape/render code is deleted and its pages are byte-identical, or the diff is reviewed.\nORDER: after HTML-CI-RELEASE's unit split, since the lib move and the split touch the same modules; one move, then one split.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_3 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T09:54Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:0x REVISED by compiler's lu9: types defined in lib cannot cross linked units (each crate re-emits them), so the markdown MODEL and PARSER stay in html as linked units (HTML-CI-RELEASE). lib/spiral/markup.spi gets only what carries no shared type: escape and the markup string builders (element, attribute, table cell/row, page shell). The consumers' escape/table/page code (blog, kit agile report, regex bench, Cells) moves to lib markup. Their markdown parsing (Cells; blog's block model) uses html's src modules as a package; Gleam inlines them, with no link needed.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_4 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T09:59Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:2x DRAFT lib/spiral/markup.spi (now in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES\\markup.spi): the typed markup union (Markup : string), markup_text/trusted/joined/concat, escape (html's escape_from, verbatim), attribute/attributes (escaped values), element, row_of, table (a th header row, then td rows), and document (an escaped title, a head and a body). 5 tests on rust + gleam. Single-crate consumers (blog, kit agile report, regex bench) inline lib, so the typed markup needs no link. html keeps its own markup until LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES covers lib types. SLIP: main first wrote it plus its registration into the LIVE lib to gate it; reverted within ~4 min (05:55-05:59), as soon as the node mirror main-markup held the copy. The live lib is clean (package.spiproj = HEAD). Gate running in the mirror. NEXT: lib_gate -File markup.spi plus a mutant rerun in that mirror, the lib_roundtrip, then lib_land_window -Draft markup.spi + package.spiproj (one added line after csv).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_5 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 5u32, "2026-11-03T12:32Z", "main", "08:19 markup.spi landed in lib/spiral via lib_land_window (retry after the type_probe VOID); close green: document_test 22, type_probe markup PASS 5 tests; undo 20261103-081917.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_6 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 6u32, "2026-11-03T14:31Z", "main", "main 11-03 10:3x CONSUMERS MOVED (unstaged): (a) regex bench/bench.spi renders its page through lib markup: escaped cells via markup::escape, markup::table for the arm table, element h1/h2/p, markup::document for the page; report.html is now typed markup::markup. Vultr run: page renders, 55 rows (5 workloads x header+10 arms). (b) blog engine/html.spi escape delegates to markup.escape |> markup.markup_text (same 4 entities, & first = single pass, so pages are unchanged); its 22 call sites stay. Vultr blog gate 29/29 executed passed, 1 unsupported (the chrono -d test, as before). Also LANDING a lint heal of markup.spi itself (10 non-recursive ^ dropped, 4 rewraps, ///- --package . header; vultr 5/5, round-trip canonical). LEFT: kit agile_report_model (kit) and Cells html_markdown.spi (x).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_7 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 7u32, "2026-11-03T15:12Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:2x markup.spi LINT HEAL LANDED (live C81A2333 = draft; base 40397C40, undo 20261103-104522). The 10:45 land was cut off by main stopping its wrapper shell after apply and before close (memory stopping-jobs-that-mutate, 11-03 slip). The close stage was then run by hand once LIB-KEBAB-CASE's land had exited: type_probe markup PASS (5 tests), respell_drift 0, consumer apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed. Window released. kit standards on the file: 0 (was 15).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_8 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T06:28Z", "main", "11-04 02:2x main DECISION (by this item's reuse rule): the html block model and renderer move into spiral lib. x's X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND is the second real consumer (x's client package sees only core and spiral). Options weighed: (a) x depends on the html repo (CI checks out html; rejected, app-to-app checkouts don't scale); (b) lib move (chosen); (c) x emits its own minimal HTML (rejected, duplicate renderer). x does the move via lib_land_window with html's tests as the gate (vultr pack33: tree 5/5, pages 5/5, HTML-OK). Then html's model/render units import the lib modules, with no copies left. Generic names only.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_9 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T06:38Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:37 x: MOVE (b) under way, decided by main 02:3x (x's timeline page is the 2nd consumer). FINDING first: lib/spiral/markup.spi ALREADY holds html model's markup core (markup type, markup_text, trusted, entity, run_of, escape, plus element/attribute/table/document) with the escape tests, and NO consumer uses it yet; html_model keeps a duplicate. So the move builds ON lib markup, with no second markup type. DRAFTED (kit drafts spiral\\HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES): lib doc_blocks.spi (3AD47CC53B37: level, align, inline, block, level_of, level_tag, 1 test) and lib doc_render.spi (17B8B227EE9D: render lines 10-120 verbatim, plus local (++) = joined; wrap = element t [] and anchor = element 'a' [(href, h)], byte-identical to html's forms; quoted; digit and show_i64; 3 render tests), registered after markup in lib package.spiproj (DF7923212DBB -> draft). Generic names (no repo names). Vultr pack33 --check: both exit 0. STAYS in html: the markdown front-end (markdown_html, md and the md-driven tests in render; markdown, inline_parse) and the dir-tree types in model (viewer, node, page kinds). NEXT: a node notebook gate on both modules (rust + gleam) plus html build.ps1 -fast 1 still HTML-OK, then lib_land_window. html's side (model and render import lib's markup + doc_blocks + doc_render and delete their copies; linked units regen) is main's after the land, as offered.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_10 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 10u32, "2026-11-04T07:18Z", "x", "2026-11-04 03:18 x: x-libdoc1 PREPARED (scratchpad launch-libdoc.ps1; node mirror xcells1 with html; staged and cleaned in the mirror only). Proves the lib batch: doc_blocks, doc_render and list_sort (LIB-LIST-SORT, a merge sort for x's sim and route), plus one package.spiproj registering all three after markup (base DF7923212DBB). PRE-REGISTERED RULE: notebook gate exit 0 with spiral-tests failed=0 over doc_blocks (1 test), doc_render (3) and list_sort (2), each on rust + gleam; AND html build.ps1 -fast 1 exit 0 with an HTML-OK line, against the mirror lib with the new modules (html's own units are unchanged, so this proves the addition is non-breaking). Else FAIL. LAND: lib_land_window with the 4 files ('new' for the 3 modules), then message main the landed hashes for html's switch. It launches when the node queue reaches it (x-next5b is running; x-next6/7 come first).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_11 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 11u32, "2026-11-04T08:50Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:50 x: ADAPTED to LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION (main, 04:49): lib/spiral now has a prelude-only spiral.toml and derives its modules from the files, and package.spiproj is gone. x-libdoc1 no longer stages or guards a lib package.spiproj; it stages only doc_blocks, doc_render and list_sort (new files, guarded as 'must not exist'). The HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES and LIB-LIST-SORT package.spiproj drafts are obsolete (kept in drafts, never landed). The lib land (lib_land_window) takes just the 3 new .spi files. x's vultr check stage gets re-staged from the new lib layout before the next lib check.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_12 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 12u32, "2026-11-04T08:52Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:52 x: RE-CHECKED under the new lib layout (spiral.toml prelude-only, modules from files; vultr stage rebuilt from the current tree, no package.spiproj) with vultr's newest compiler, pack34: doc_blocks, doc_render and list_sort --check exit 0 just by dropping the files in. Nothing else to adapt; x-libdoc1 is ready.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_13 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 13u32, "2026-11-04T08:59Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:59 x: x-libdoc1 NOTEBOOK HALF PROVEN on the box (it was idle at 35%, as the gate prompted; the node was busy with x-next5c): a scratch copy of lib\\spiral (bench/target excluded; the live tree untouched) with the 3 drafts, run_notebook --gate once per file, SPIRAL_CELLS_WARM=0, a private MIX_BUILD_PATH: doc_blocks 1/1, doc_render 3/3, list_sort 2/2, all exit 0. The remaining half of the pre-registered rule (html build.ps1 -fast 1 stays HTML-OK against the mirror lib with the new modules) runs on the node as x-libdoc1 -HtmlOnly.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_14 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 14u32, "2026-11-04T09:42Z", "x", "2026-11-04 05:42 x: LIB SIDE LANDED, closed green (lib_land_window, after kit paused its back-to-back box notebooks that kept the reader check from clearing): doc_blocks.spi 3AD47CC53B37, doc_render.spi 17B8B227EE9D, list_sort.spi EC96EE545E32 (new files; lib derives modules from files). Close checks: consumer apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe 3/3 PASS, 0 respell drift; lib digest C92986570894D275; undo dir spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261104-053901. Proof: notebook 6/6 on the box and node x-libdoc1 html build -fast 1 HTML-OK. Hashes sent to main for html's switch (html_model/html_render import lib markup + doc_blocks + doc_render and drop their copies).")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_15 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 15u32, "2026-11-04T10:10Z", "main", "11-04 06:0x main: HTML SIDE DONE (unstaged in html). After x's lib land (markup + doc_blocks + doc_render), html_model/model.spi keeps only its own types (viewer, node, page) and trim helpers, with page_text; its markup core, block types, level_of/level_tag, escape, wrap/anchor/quoted and digit/show_i64 copies are gone (tests now trim + page; the escape/level tests live in lib). html_render/render.spi drops the 108-line block renderer that doc_render holds byte for byte and keeps the to_html prototype, markdown_html, md and fixtures. Every html module opens what it uses: run_of users open markup, block users doc_blocks, renderers doc_render. Trap: lib markup exports `table`, so markdown.spi must open html's `table` module before markup. Gate: full html build.ps1 on vultr (pack34, toml lib): 46/46 notebooks, linked-unit regen + cargo release + self-test, largest generated file 962 lines, HTML-OK. Lib-declared types cross html's linked units cleanly.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_16 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 16u32, "2026-11-04T10:10Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:10 x: the BLOCK MOVE IS COMPLETE, one source of truth. Lib side landed by x 05:4x (doc_blocks 3AD47CC53B37, doc_render 17B8B227EE9D); html side done by main (html_model keeps only viewer/node/page and trim; html_render keeps markdown_html/md/to_html; every html module opens lib markup/doc_blocks/doc_render), full html build.ps1 on vultr green: 46/46 notebooks, linked units regenerated, HTML-OK. Second consumer: x's timeline_page (draft E9FEA5CE9BED line) opens lib markup + doc_blocks + doc_render; checked against main's open-order trap (lib markup exports 'table'): no module opened after markup collides with a markup export.")
inl note_of_html_lib_candidates_17 () = Note ("HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES", 17u32, "2026-11-04T13:48Z", "main", "11-04 09:5x main CLOSE: the decision and the move are both done (n14 lib side landed by x, n15 html side, n16 full html build on vultr 46/46 HTML-OK). Re-confirmed today: html builds HTML-OK on vultr with Cells 46/46 and the generated cli html.rs at 998 lines, every html module opening lib markup/doc_blocks/doc_render. Remaining html work is tracked on its own items (HTML-VIEWERS: picture/mermaid pages).")
inl lib_split_text () = Task ("LIB-SPLIT-TEXT", "Split the over-budget definitions of the text family (sm'.spi 85 defs, 29k excess over 272; sm'_real.spir 8 defs, 36k excess) into granular cells, on the renamed and merged text.spi after LIB-RESHAPE R4 (sm' -> text) and R6 (spir merge), so splits and renames never collide", Story, P2, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "lib,granular,cell-budget,main,team:main,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_split_text () = Planning ("LIB-SPLIT-TEXT", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_split_text_1 () = Note ("LIB-SPLIT-TEXT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T00:12Z", "main", "main lib-reshape 11-01 20:1x, from the post-respell cell-budget census (GRANULAR-STATS latest; raw file on the node C:\\home\\remote\\shared-current\\cell-budget-1101.txt). SEQUENCING DECISION: rename first, split second. LIB-RESHAPE R4 is a mechanical transform derived from the live text in minutes, while splits are hand-anchored drafts that a later rename would stale (memory anchors-stale-across-respell). So the splits are drafted on text.spi after R4 and, for sm'_real's 8 giant definitions, after R6 merges them into text.spi. DoD: every definition in text.spi under 272 weighted chars (mix spiral.cell_budget over_budget 0 for the file) or a recorded exception per definition with the reason (one host primitive that can't split); lib_land_window close green; Cells gate rows for text.spi equal before/after (passed/failed per backend); the generated apps/spiral crate unchanged in behavior (compiles, same test rows). TYPEFEATURESET: helpers extracted as :~ functions with typed records/unions instead of tuple/string plumbing; long host macros (sm' 159/161/679/1244/1514/2339) become one-expression primitives. NEXT STEP: wait for R4; then rank text.spi's definitions by excess weight and split from the top. The other files in LIB-RESHAPE's path (R2 deletes one ':< rust' line in file_system/process/date_time/state_core) don't collide with splits, since a one-line transform re-derives on any base.")
inl fiscal_pages_reports () = Task ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", "fiscal pages: rendered HTML report views (examples, bench, tests) per OS, with commit and run stamps", Story, P2, D3, 85u32, Active, "", "team:fiscal,fiscal,ci,pages,reports", "current", "current")
