inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T00:14Z", "fiscal", "Found by fiscal 2026-11-01 judging the dir-tree-html page after the first fully green run (41351043040). The page lists everything, but the reports are raw TSV (bench.tsv, examples.tsv, files.tsv, tests.tsv). The regex repo's rule (main 11-01: results shown on the dir-tree-html page as HTML, no committed .tsv) is the bar.\nDONE: (1) target/ci-metrics gets rendered HTML views generated in CI (an index with the examples table, Messages per family plus the first message; the bench table with parse/write medians per unit and OS; the slowest files; the tests table filterable by status) linked from the page root; (2) both OS jobs publish their metrics under os-labelled names (examples-windows-2025, bench-ubuntu-24.04, ...), and the index compares them; (3) the page shows the commit id, run id and build time; (4) the README \"Reports\" section links the views.\nTYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the TSV rows become typed records (FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH bench_row, an example_row with \":| example_verdict = | Valid | Invalid : i32 | NotWritten | SchemaUnloadable\"), written as JSON through json_schema and rendered from the typed rows, never by regex over text.\nNEXT STEP: check whether dir-tree-html renders .html files next to TSVs; emit the index from a Spiral cell in build (no new .ps1).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 2u32, "2026-11-03T19:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:07 fiscal: DoD (1), (3) and (4) WRITTEN, unstaged in fiscal. (1)+TYPEFEATURESET: NEW src/reports.spi F198DEF3 (registered last in package.spiproj and spiral.toml): the TSVs become typed rows (test_row with ':| test_status = Passed | Failed | Static | Skipped | Unsupported | NotRun | TimedOut' parsed by lib case_labels.case_of_label, so no status string table; ':| reported_status = Known | Unknown' keeps an unexpected label; file_row with decimal seconds; bench_row; example_row with the planned ':| example_verdict = Valid | Invalid : i32 | NotWritten | Unmeasured'), rendered to target/ci-metrics/reports.md: stamp, status counts, every test that did not pass, the 10 slowest files, the bench, the example verdicts (cells escape '|'). Rendering goes through MARKDOWN tables on purpose: the page renderer (dir-tree-html now, html's HTML-CLI drop-in next) turns markdown into HTML, so fiscal adds no HTML code of its own and moves with the html repo (the 11-03 'finish html, retire dir-tree-html' priority). (3) the stamp: commit GITHUB_SHA, a run link from GITHUB_RUN_ID, build time from FISCAL_BUILD_TIME (build.ps1 sets it); a local build says so. (4) README Reports links reports.md first. Glue (no new .ps1): build.ps1 +4 lines (the stamp, 'reports' excluded from the main pass and run after the TSVs are written with FISCAL_METRICS_SUFFIX), publish.ps1 includes 'reports.md'. PROVEN on vultr: --check with bodies exit 0; all 3 bodies as Rust exit 0; a real render of the box's regen7 TSVs printed the expected tables (19 failed generator tests of that red run listed, bench rows, slowest file). OPEN: DoD (2) the windows job's metrics on the page (only ubuntu publishes today; needs the push job to merge both artifacts), and the html renderer's view of .md files under target/ (verify on the first green page).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 3u32, "2026-11-03T19:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:11 fiscal: DoD (2) DESIGN, not applied today: fiscal's push job is the shared org helper verified_pages_push_job (i574n.github/scripts/pins/workflows.spi:217; YAML is generated from it, never hand-edited), and scripts/pins/{pins.ps1,workflow.spi,workflows.spi} carry another lane's unstaged edits right now. The change: a push-job variant taking extra artifact names, downloading ci-metrics-ubuntu-24.04 and ci-metrics-windows-2025 (actions/download-artifact@v8.0.2, already in fiscal's actions.lock, so the lock does not change) into gh-pages/target/ci-metrics-<os>/ before the deploy; each OS's reports.md then sits under its own os-labelled folder. Apply when the pins WIP lands (regenerate with pins.ps1, verify with gh actions-lock --no-fix).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 4u32, "2026-11-03T20:24Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 16:24 fiscal: REUSE: build.ps1's GitHub step summary no longer builds its own markdown tables in PowerShell (slowest 8 files, bench); it writes the heading line (label, file count, minutes) and appends target/ci-metrics/reports.md minus its title, so the summary and the published report come from the same typed rows (-5 PowerShell lines). Parse check 0 errors; the block was simulated with a sample reports.md (heading + report body).")
