inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 6u32, "2026-11-04T05:28Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 01:28 fiscal: DoD (2) APPLIED (unstaged). The 11-03 blocker was another lane's pins WIP, untouched since 11-03 06:16, i.e. settled, so it is built on top: i574n.github/scripts/pins/org_jobs.spi gains artifacts_download (pattern) (path) and verified_pages_push_job_with (extra : list step), which inserts steps after the pages download; verified_pages_push_job = the [] case, so the other 6 workflows on the helper stay BYTE-IDENTICAL (checked: of all 11 org workflow files only fiscal's gh-pages.yml changed). workflows.spi fiscal (): the push job downloads pattern 'ci-metrics-*' into gh-pages/target, so each OS's metrics + reports.md land under gh-pages/target/ci-metrics-<os>/ (a pattern download does not fail when one OS's artifact is missing, unlike a by-name download). Regenerated with pins dist/workflows.exe --write: fiscal gh-pages.yml +5 lines (actions/download-artifact@v8.0.2, already in actions.lock); gh actions-lock --no-fix: valid. NOTE: the same --write also rewrote tibia's gh-pages.yml (pre-existing drift at line 73, not fiscal's); restored byte-identical and reported to tibia. PENDING: proof on CI at the user's next fiscal push (pages show target/ci-metrics-ubuntu-24.04/reports.md and ...-windows-2025/).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 7u32, "2026-11-05T07:41Z", "compiler", "11-05 03:4x compiler (ask from the SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL census, no action needed from compiler): fiscal/src/reports.spi:117 has 2 match arms that map union cases to their own names as string literals. They can become reflection::case_name x (or sm'::to_lower of it) over the !!!!UnionCaseName op (pack39+, box and node since 03:10). Example heals: spiral cells daemon.spi request_line, lib doc_blocks.spi level_tag (green 11-05). Your call when.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_8 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 8u32, "2026-11-05T13:50Z", "fiscal", "11-05 09:5x local fiscal: NAMEOF HEAL APPLIED in fiscal src (in place, unstaged; backup reports.before-nameof-8987026C.spi in the session scratchpad), answering compiler's 07:41 ask. src/reports.spi 8987026C -> E0F37B27: verdict_text keeps the Invalid n arm (payload, own text) and maps every other case through case_labels::label_of_name \"\" \" \" (reflection::case_name v), so NotWritten still prints 'not written' and Valid/Unmeasured print 'valid'/'unmeasured' byte-identically. case_labels::case_label could not be used: it enumerates get_union_fields_untag, which needs payload-less unions, and example_verdict has Invalid : i32. New assertion in tsv_rows_read_into_their_typed_columns pins all four outputs. Also healed the file's 4 respell-drift literals (true/false -> !+/!- in is_unknown, failing_lines, writes_the_ci_reports). Box checks with a pinned compiler copy (core 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3): format --check --respell-drift exit 0, --check exit 0 (29 s). PENDING: the Cells run of reports.spi's 4 rust tests on the NODE, job-1793886615820-fiscal-reports-gate, queued after the facet regen job (one Cells run per node), scratch tree only, mirror untouched.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_9 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 9u32, "2026-11-05T13:54Z", "fiscal", "11-05 09:5x local fiscal (follow-up): a whole-src format --check --respell-drift (14 files) found 2 more, both at HEAD bb1ebad, now fixed in place and unstaged (backups document.before-fmt-249C56E6.spi and generated_runtime.before-fmt-2F02F888.spi in the session scratchpad): document.spi 249C56E6 -> 667309A1 (3 true/false -> !+/!- literals in its tests) and generated_runtime.spi 2F02F888 -> D899E5DE (one formatter line wrap of sample_path_text; the emitted unit text is unchanged). Result: all 14 fiscal src files formatter- and respell-clean (exit 0), package --check exit 0 (box, pinned core 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3). This also removes a formatter-drift red that CI would have shown at HEAD. PENDING on the NODE: job-1793886615820-fiscal-reports-gate, widened before its start to gate reports.spi and document.spi from a fresh src zip 0A8C6282.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_10 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 10u32, "2026-11-05T14:00Z", "fiscal", "11-05 10:0x local fiscal: TWO MORE NAMEOF HEALS in fiscal src (in place, unstaged; backups canon.before-nameof-8457C66F.spi, corpus_checks.before-nameof-2AC1F2A4.spi in the session scratchpad), from a src sweep for match arms that map a case to its own name (the SUNAT catalog codes and MyInvois versions are real code tables and stay literal). (1) canon.spi ubl_document_name = \"ubl-\" ++# case_labels::case_label \"Ubl\" \"\" document (prefix cut, no separator: UblCreditNote -> creditnote), new test each_ubl_document_is_named_by_its_case. (2) corpus_checks.spi kind_label = sm'::to_lower (sm'::replace \"Kind\" \"\" (reflection::case_name kind)), new test each_ubl_kind_names_its_manifest (pins kind_label for all 3 kinds and one full ubl_manifest path). Box: format --check --respell-drift exit 0 for both, package --check exit 0. PENDING on the NODE in the same queued job-1793886615820-fiscal-reports-gate (cap amended 1 h -> 3 h; script 743233C6, src zip 94D86AEA): reports + document + canon all tests, corpus_checks filtered to the new pin plus the two real-manifest tests (myinvois 22/22, sunat 28/15/15). BYTE CHECK for (1): the canon gate rewrites canon/en16931-terms.json, which keys 379 entries by these names; the node output must hash 12A85C78 like the repo's.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_11 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 11u32, "2026-11-05T14:35Z", "fiscal", "11-05 10:5x local fiscal CORRECTION to my 10:0x note: the committed canon/en16931-terms.json (12A85C78) is pretty-printed CRLF, not the Spiral writer's compact LF output, so the node byte check must compare with the 11-02 Spiral baseline 9DBC4B63F0CA (52,597 bytes), not 12A85C78. The canon nameof heal is in fact ALREADY byte-proven: vultr eff-1793888925 ran the healed ubl_document_name (in the same src) and its JSON, with the separate additive 'effective' field stripped, hashes 9DBC4B63F0CA exactly, so all 379 'ubl-invoice'/'ubl-creditnote' keys are unchanged.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_12 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 12u32, "2026-11-05T15:30Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:3x local fiscal: RUST BODY RUN ON VULTR (chain eff-*1793892466; self-contained stage = box core + box lib + live fiscal src + the corpus parts these modules read (pe/ and the root ubl manifests); pinned copy of vultr's installed compiler core dc49ffdc170199df; every non-'fails' test body compiled --backend Rust into one main, rustc -O, run): reports 4 bodies, document 3, lifecycle 7, posting 2, profiles 2, sunat 8 -- compile, rustc and run exit 0 for all six. The harness fails on a wrong pin (mutants earlier today on canon and pint_terms exited 1 with the exact message). The node Cells run (job-1793886615820, queued) stays as confirmation; it now also copies the gitignored oracle files (src/corpus.txt, patterns.txt, pattern_probes.txt, pattern_expected.txt) from the mirror into its tree, without which its corpus gate would have been VOID (a src zip never carries them). Here: reports.spi E0F37B27 (nameof heal + respell) 4 bodies incl. the new verdict pin, document.spi 667309A1 (respell) 3 bodies green.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_13 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 13u32, "2026-11-05T15:35Z", "fiscal", "11-05 11:3x local fiscal: corpus_checks heal FIXED + PROVEN. My 10:0x pin test each_ubl_kind_names_its_manifest had a parse error (its '? cond' continued on a line starting '||' at the same indent as '?'), and the compiler silently LEFT THE BLOCK OUT of the module: format --check and --check were both green on the box; only the vultr --backend Rust compile warned (ParserErrors, 'Expected: then'). Fixed in place (labels bound first, continuation indented): corpus_checks.spi -> EFD329A3, format clean. VULTR eff-cc1793892778 (filter: the pin + every_myinvois_sample_reaches_the_ubl_invoice_unit_in_both_syntaxes + every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit, which exercise kind_label on all three kinds against the real manifests): compile, rustc, run exit 0. No other module run today printed ParserErrors. Node zip re-shipped (BE4D67E0) while job-1793886615820 is still queued.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_14 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 14u32, "2026-11-05T18:58Z", "fiscal", "11-05 15:0x local fiscal: the CI report gains a CANON CENSUS section (reports.spi A135648B, unstaged): after the examples table, reports.md shows per family how the 25 required EN 16931 terms are covered: NF-e 4.00 13 bound / 2 implied / 3 derived / 3 national code / 4 not carried; CFDI 4.0 13 / 1 / 4 / 3 / 4. Built from the typed tables in canon_nfe / canon_cfdi (a ':== census' record per family, gap kinds counted from canon_coverage's ':| gap'), not from text. Test the_canon_census_counts_each_family pins both rows. VULTR: all 5 reports bodies (incl. writes_the_ci_reports, which renders it) compile, rustc, run exit 0, no ParserErrors; GRANULAR 0 code overages. In the queued node Cells job-1793886615820 (zip re-shipped).")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_15 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 15u32, "2026-11-05T20:15Z", "fiscal", "11-05 16:1x local fiscal: two node runs came back VOID (environment, not code), both from the t1101 mirror's STALE lib/spiral: it lacks the box-only lib modules ledger / money (landed unstaged on the box 11-03), xml.first_difference_by (landed today) and xsd_emit.dereferenced_parts, and it still orders modules by package.spiproj, so an xml_codec copied in ahead of decimal cannot see decimal. (1) src Cells job-1793886615820: every module failed together (the package type check needs posting -> ledger / money and canon_coverage -> dereferenced_parts); stopped by me. (2) MyInvois twin job-1793895376229: the regen compile failed (xml_codec: Unbound decimal; document_syntax: Unbound read_text / decoded_by / present). FIX: both now unpack the BOX lib/spiral (lib.zip 1C36B453, toml-ordered, the lib every vultr proof used) into their scratch trees. RE-QUEUED in priority order behind the running facet-extra gates job-1793908968483 (which uses the facet gate's proven setup and is unaffected): job-1793909583928-fiscal-twin2 (script FE325247), then job-1793909634925-fiscal-reports-gate2 (script 89E28B5A, src zip D742F390). The vultr Rust body runs of every module stay the landing evidence; these are the Cells confirmations, pending on the node.")
inl note_of_fiscal_pages_reports_16 () = Note ("FISCAL-PAGES-REPORTS", 16u32, "2026-11-05T23:20Z", "fiscal", "11-05 19:2x local fiscal: pages now also publish fiscal's Cells notebook pages (main's PAGES-NOTEBOOK-PUBLISH ask): scripts/publish.ps1 -Include adds '*.spi.html','*.spi.ipynb','*.spi.livemd' (as tibia; publish-tree lists untracked files without --exclude-standard, so the gitignored notebooks/ is picked up; 19 html + 19 ipynb present locally). gh-pages.yml already runs publish.ps1 after build.ps1 under !cancelled() on ubuntu, so no workflow edit. Unstaged. STILL OPEN for Done: DoD (2) 'the index compares them' (each OS lands its own reports.md under gh-pages/target/ci-metrics-<os>/, nothing compares the two yet), plus the CI proof of every DoD at the user's next fiscal push (none since bb1ebad0).")
inl kit_train_snapshot_pin () = Task ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", "launch-train always snapshots kit AND pins the lib: the train copies the kit tree (existing -Snapshot) and a lib snapshot (passed as release-train -Lib), so lib lands and lane edits never mix versions inside a running train (main 11-01 20:2x)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,release,train,lib,team:kit,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_train_snapshot_pin () = Planning ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_train_snapshot_pin_1 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", 1u32, "2026-11-02T00:21Z", "kit", "11-01 20:21 kit. WHY: TRAIN7c read the live tree and lib while main's respell landed at 14:53 mid-notebooks; TRAIN8 needed main to hold lib-reshape R1b+R2 (20:2x). release-train.ps1 already has -Snapshot (robocopy of the kit tree to .cache/release-tree/<name>) and -Lib <path>; launch-train.ps1 passes neither. DoD: launch-train defaults to -Snapshot plus a lib copy under .cache/release-tree/<name>/lib (robocopy of spiral/lib/spiral, with its sha256 tree digest logged in train.log), and passes -Lib to release-train; a lib land during the train does not change any notebook verdict (test: modify a lib file mid-run in a dry train, verdicts unchanged); disk: the snapshot is pruned after install. NEXT: add -Snapshot by default plus the lib copy step in launch-train.ps1 (pwsh glue, about 10 lines) and one dry-run proof. TYPEFEATURES: none needed (glue); the train log gains typed rows when release-train ports to kit run.")
inl note_of_kit_train_snapshot_pin_2 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:35Z", "kit", "11-01 20:35 kit: DONE in the tree (unstaged): launch-train.ps1 already copied and pinned the lib when -Snapshot was given (lib robocopy into .cache/release-tree/<name>-lib, passed as -Lib to release-train), so the fix is the default: snapshot unless -LiveTree is passed. Parse ok. Proof = the next train (TRAIN9) runs snapshotted, and a lib land during it changes no verdict.")
inl note_of_kit_train_snapshot_pin_3 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:01Z", "kit", "11-01 21:01 kit: first live use. TRAIN8 (live tree) was stopped at 7/44 notebooks (about 22:50 projected) and relaunched as TRAIN8s with the new default snapshot (kit tree + lib copy, -Lib passed), so main's lib-reshape hold and x's Cells hold are released immediately. Proof of the DoD = TRAIN8s verdicts unaffected by the R1b+R2 land happening during it.")
inl note_of_kit_train_snapshot_pin_4 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:29Z", "kit", "11-01 21:29 kit: TRAIN8s train.log shows \"notebooks read the lib at C:\\home\\git\\kit\\.cache\\release-tree\\TRAIN8s-lib\\lib\\spiral\" (the pinned copy, not the live lib). COST measured: the snapshot (kit tree robocopy plus lib copy) took about 18 min on the loaded box (launch 21:01, notebooks start 21:19). Follow-up idea: copy only tracked plus changed files (git ls-files plus the diff set, like remote.ps1 sync) instead of a full /MIR, and skip target/.cache, to cut that to seconds.")
inl note_of_kit_train_snapshot_pin_5 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-SNAPSHOT-PIN", 5u32, "2026-11-02T02:57Z", "kit", "11-01 22:57 kit DoD MET: TRAIN8s ran on its snapshot (lib read from .cache/release-tree/TRAIN8s-lib) while main's lib-reshape R1b+R2 landed into the live lib at 22:01, mid-notebooks; the result was 44/44 notebooks and an install at 22:55 (kit.exe 7C559D83). Lands no longer need a hold. Remaining nicety (copy cost about 18 min on a loaded box) is noted in n4. DONE.")
inl kit_no_escaped_daemons () = Task ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", "No process started through kit may escape its session: kit process start-under-shell parents to the caller's owner session (not explorer) and stays in the job; Cells' compiler servers die with their daemon (user 11-01 20:4x: \"check why kit let all these processes dangle without a parent\")", Story, P1, D3, 65u32, Active, "", "kit,jobs,processes,cells,resilience,team:kit,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons () = Planning ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_1 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T00:47Z", "kit", "11-01 20:46 kit ANALYSIS (box, 20:4x): 14 processes had a dead parent. Kit's share: two Cells compiler servers (dotnet SpiralCompiler.dll --server-tcp ... --stall-seconds 120, started 10-30 22:06 and 10-31 12:40, idle 2 MB) whose parent, the Cells BEAM daemon, was gone; both STOPPED by kit (no established connections). CHAIN: (1) Cells starts its compiler DAEMON through kit (compiler_client.ex daemon_start: kit process start-under-shell); (2) kit_os_launch kit_parented_start uses CREATE_BREAKAWAY_FROM_JOB (flags 0x0900_0220) and, with no owner, parents to GetShellWindow's process = EXPLORER, so the daemon leaves the caller's kit job (whose container allows breakaway, limits 0x2800 = KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE|BREAKAWAY_OK) and outlives every session; (3) the daemon spawns --server-tcp servers and, when it exits, does not stop them; (4) the server has no idle exit or parent watch (--stall-seconds only bounds an outstanding compile, Program.fs:983). This contradicts the rule that kit processes belong to their session (memory kit-live-parent-every-process: never explorer-parent). Others' orphans (not touched): idle interactive pwsh shells, a claude-boost-watcher, a codespaces ssh, a 20:19 vultr probe ssh without BatchMode (fixed in remote.ps1 since), and a 20:26 pwsh loop syncing linux-1101. FIX PLAN: (a) kit: kit_shell_parented_start passes the caller owner (kit_caller_owner) instead of 0, so the parent is the session, never explorer; drop CREATE_BREAKAWAY_FROM_JOB from the tries so the process stays in the caller's job and KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE reaps it with the session; keep BREAKAWAY_OK only if a proven caller needs it (audit first); (b) compiler host: --server-tcp exits when its parent pid is gone or after N idle minutes without a session (compiler lane); (c) Cells: the daemon stops its servers on exit (x lane). DoD: after a notebook batch and the end of its session, no SpiralCompiler --server-tcp or Cells BEAM survives (a process census before/after); a kit job end leaves 0 descendants; tests for the owner choice (owner pid used, explorer never). NEXT: (a) in kit_os_launch (rides TRAIN9) plus the census check as a kit machine watch rule (orphan = dead-parent process whose image is in a kit-launched family).")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_2 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T00:56Z", "kit", "11-01 20:56 kit: compiler's side (b) is drafted for the next pack (CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL): serveSessions exits after SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS with no session (opt-in; it never fires mid-session; it deletes the socket/.pid/.bridge files). A parent watch ALREADY exists behind SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID, but the leaked servers were spawned without it. So the spawner (the Cells daemon, x lane) must set BOTH SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID=<daemon pid> and SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS (for example 600) when it starts a --server-tcp server. Added to (c).")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_3 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T01:01Z", "kit", "11-01 21:01 kit: x confirms Cells has set SPIRAL_SERVER_PARENT_PID on every spawned --server-tcp since 7a4c960e (11-01 09:48, compiler_daemon.ex:1162 port_env = the daemon's os pid), so the stopped pair (10-30/10-31) predates the fix; x adds SPIRAL_SERVER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS=600 to the same port_env. Cells does not need the daemon to outlive its session (cross-session reuse only saves warm-up, and the daemon already idle-retires), so (a) the kit change is unblocked for TRAIN9.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_4 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 4u32, "2026-11-02T01:23Z", "kit", "11-01 21:23 kit: (a) DONE in the tree (unstaged, TRAIN9). kit_os_launch: kit_shell_parented_start passes the caller's owner (kit_caller_owner) as the parent; kit_parented_start no longer falls back to GetShellWindow (explorer) when the owner is 0, so the child stays a plain child of its caller; CREATE_BREAKAWAY_FROM_JOB is dropped from the creation tries (0x0900_0220 -> 0x0800_0220), so the process stays inside the caller's kit job and KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE reaps it with the session; the unused user32 externs are removed; the help texts (direct_verbs.spi, run.spi) now say \"the caller's session as its live parent, inside the caller's kit job\". Ratchet ok. Remaining: TRAIN9 regen and install, then the DoD census (a notebook batch plus session end leave no Cells BEAM or --server-tcp behind).")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_5 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 5u32, "2026-11-02T12:26Z", "resilience", "11-02 08:1x resilience post-analysis census (pre-TRAIN9-install): the pattern persists -- box had 15 dead-parent orphans incl 3 spiral-bin dotnet (57h/43h/6h), CLAUDE_CODE_SHELL_LAUNCHER pwsh, gh codespace logs, ssh codespaces; all reaped. Added a box-side JANITOR complementing kit's upstream fix: i574n.github/scripts/orphan-reaper.ps1 (dead-parent, class-tiered grace compiler/remote 60m vs shells 12h, preserves boost-watcher/mirror singletons, -DryRun lists live orphans). Use orphan-reaper -DryRun as the DoD census tool. Verification signal: once TRAIN9 installs and the Cells daemon sets PARENT_PID+IDLE_EXIT, the janitor should trend to 0 finds.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_6 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 6u32, "2026-11-03T00:50Z", "resilience", "11-02 20:48 resilience: DoD CENSUS VERIFIED POSITIVE (the signal n5 predicted: \"once TRAIN9 installs the janitor trends to 0\"). Ran the designated census (orphan-reaper -DryRun = 0 past-grace, + a direct dead-parent census of ANY age): 22 dead-parent procs total, ZERO kit-launched family - no dotnet, no SpiralCompiler --server-tcp, no erl/beam/epmd with a dead parent. BEFORE/AFTER: n5's 08:1x census found 3 escaped spiral-bin dotnet daemons (57h/43h/6h); NOW 0, AND it holds DURING a live 59-notebook batch (TRAIN13c running as measured) - so kit-launched compiler servers no longer escape their session. TRAIN9 parenting fix (a: caller-owner parent, no explorer, no CREATE_BREAKAWAY, KILL_ON_JOB_CLOSE) + Cells PARENT_PID/IDLE_EXIT (c) are confirmed WORKING post-install (current kit is TRAIN11-era, so TRAIN9 shipped). The 22 dead-parent procs are all NON-kit families, correctly out of this item's scope: 3 git (Claude-Code Fork-lineage, reaper 3m short-grace - the KIT-ORPHAN-SIM short tier, NOT kit-launched), 2 pwsh (by-design detached shells, 720m grace), 1 waitfor (subagent background-waitfor, legit), ~16 Windows service-manager-parented OS/app services (tailscale/rustdesk/mariadbd/gfx/audio - parentless by design, never orphans). REMAINING to close: the owner-choice unit tests (owner pid used, explorer never) + (b) compiler --server-tcp idle-exit fully landed/verified. The census-based DoD (no SpiralCompiler/BEAM survives a batch) PASSES. Bump 40->65.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_7 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 7u32, "2026-11-03T23:07Z", "resilience", "11-03 19:05 resilience ESCAPED-DAEMON AUDIT (box-independent; read the fresh 18:57 resource-report + tied to the live 100%-CPU starvation). FINDING: the invariant currently HOLDS. resource-report.ps1's section \"box processes by name, outside any live kit job's tree and any Claude session, >=200MB WS (candidates for dangling)\" is EMPTY - zero escaped daemons. All box CPU is legitimate lane work under live claude.exe session trees (kit 25 procs/302 CpuSec incl TRAIN17, compiler 14/50, fiscal 16/70, main/x/tibia). So: (a) the no-escaped-daemons invariant is satisfied right now; (b) resource-report.ps1 is ALREADY the live monitor for this (its dangling-candidates section is the detector) - the item's \"make orphans simulable\" (cf KIT-ORPHAN-SIM) is the gap, not detection; (c) the current critical-mirror backup-failure starvation is genuine fleet load (TRAIN17 + compiles), NOT reapable orphans - it eases when TRAIN17 finishes, no CPU to reclaim. Evidence baseline for the item; no enforcement change needed today.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_8 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 8u32, "2026-11-04T11:27Z", "resilience-614162e5", "11-04 ~07:3x resilience ESCAPED-DAEMON RE-AUDIT (under today's heavy churn: SI retune, multi-lane builds, a 90pct-CPU BEAM run). Census: 0 kit-launch-type procs (dotnet/pwsh/erl/beam.smp/mix/escript/SpiralCompiler/node/cargo/rustc) with a DEAD parent AND outside any live claude.exe or kit job root. INVARIANT HOLDS - no kit-launched daemon escaped its session. The box's dead-parent procs are all legit non-kit (firefox, rustdesk, mariadbd, git fsmonitor--daemon [by-design --detach], ms-teams, winlogon, igfx). Resilience-audit half stays green; remaining enforcement (kit process start-under-shell parenting) is team:kit. Re-run each groom via the process-health sweep.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_9 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 9u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "resilience", "11-04 star-exchange ASK (resilience->kit): kit job wait should EXIT when its controlling shell dies. Today a backgrounded `kit job wait <id> | tail` left the kit-job-wait process ALIVE after TaskStop (it reparented to a harness process) and orphaned a tail.exe (user flagged dangling procs). This extends the no-escape invariant to the job-wait waiter specifically.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_10 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 10u32, "2026-11-05T04:07Z", "resilience", "DETECTION signature from real lineage (resilience, frame 2026-11-04 23:38, traced all 61 kit-relevant procs to root): an escaped process is one whose parent chain roots at explorer/wininit/sh (shell or session-manager) instead of the kit job host or the owning lane session. Evidence: ZERO kit-adjacent trees root at a claude owner session; the BEAM/Elixir daemons are the concrete escapees - dotnet<erl<erl<sh, erl<erl<sh, erl<sh all root at a bare git-bash sh, not a kit job object, which is exactly the Cells compiler-servers-should-die-with-their-daemon case (a shell that can exit out from under them). No kit.exe/job-host tree existed in the frame (kit CLI is short-lived), so the escape SURFACE is the long-lived BEAM/compiler daemons, not kit's own process. Also: Claude tool pwsh children root at windowsterminal<explorer not at the claude process, so lane tool-subprocs are not reapable via claude lineage. Detection is un-gated and now specified; the FIX (kit process start-under-shell must parent to the owner session + enroll the tree in a kit job object so it dies with the daemon) is kit-team gated. Pairs with KIT-ORPHAN-SIM proc-frame.v1. resilience.")
inl note_of_kit_no_escaped_daemons_11 () = Note ("KIT-NO-ESCAPED-DAEMONS", 11u32, "2026-11-05T20:22Z", "resilience-614162e5", "11-05 ~12:2x resilience ESCAPED-DAEMON RE-AUDIT (resilience-audit half; point-in-time, box). INVARIANT HOLDS: 0 kit-launched-family procs (dotnet/erl/beam.smp/epmd/mix/escript/SpiralCompiler/cargo/rustc/node) with a DEAD immediate parent. All 6 live kit-family procs have LIVE parents: erl 8852<-22316, dotnet 21380/20532/18980<-17904, erl 3816<-23836, erl 5972<-3816. No daemon escaped its session. Fast-screen method: dead-immediate-parent is the necessary condition; 0 hits means the fuller root-lineage trace (note 77: chain rooting at sh/explorer) is not needed this tick. Latent escape surface (BEAM under a still-alive git-bash sh that orphans on shell-exit) unchanged + kit-tree gated. Half stays green.")
inl kit_hidden_verb_flags () = Task ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", "Hidden or internal kit verbs (job host, supervise ...) refuse unknown flags such as --help instead of starting the real thing (x-dumps 11-01 23:0x: kit job host --help started a real job host over ssh)", TaskKind, P2, D1, 85u32, Active, "", "kit,cli,jobs,team:kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags () = Planning ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_1 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T03:09Z", "kit", "11-01 23:09 kit. WHY: on vultr, kit job host --help started a real job host (it supervised nothing and was killed), right next to the pod's single host, which risks the single-host rule. DoD: every internal verb (job host, job supervise, the host's run entry) refuses any argument it does not define with exit 2 and a one-line usage, and --help/-h prints usage without side effects; a CLI test runs kit job host --help and asserts exit 2 plus no host.pid written. NEXT: find the job host entry's argument parse (kit_job_host host_run.spi host_run reads argument 3/4 for owner pid/start) and add an unknown-flag refusal. TYPEFEATURES: a typed internal_args union (HostArgs owner start | HelpAsked | Unknown flag) instead of positional decimal_u64 reads.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_2 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T04:57Z", "kit", "IN TREE (TRAIN9): kit_jobs/jobs.spi JobHost refuses when argument 3 starts with \"-\" (\"job host is started by kit itself and takes no flags\"), so `kit job host --help` no longer starts a shared host. Found while there: job_command_of in kit_jobs/model.spi is a hand-written word->case map (13 arms). reflection.union_try_pick matches case names or their lowercase, so the migration means renaming JobStart.. to bare verbs, which collide with other unions wherever kit_jobs.model is opened. Deferred to its own change, with a census of the colliding names first.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_3 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:24Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 10:2x job_command_of MIGRATED to reflection (unstaged, src/kit_jobs/model.spi): optionm'.default_value JobUnknown (reflection.union_try_pick (\"job\" ++# word)). union_try_pick matches a case name exactly or its lowercase, so 'start' -> 'jobstart' = lower(JobStart); the Job prefix stays, so the bare-verb collision census that deferred this (n2) is moot: no case renamed. New test every_job_verb_is_its_case_name_without_the_job_prefix: all 13 verbs, 'Start', 'restart' and '' -> JobUnknown. NODE (job-1793628460234): kit_jobs model 9/9. COST, measured: jobs.rs 553 -> 637 (+84): union_try_pick builds the field list twice (exact + lowercased). Kept anyway: the user's no-hand-written-string<->case-map rule outranks my own no-growth rule while the crate is far under the 1000 gate. Follow-up for lib: a lower-only pick (one list) would recover most of the +84 for every caller. Also in this train: the job-host flag refusal message ('job job host') fixed in kit_jobs/jobs.spi.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_4 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 4u32, "2026-11-03T07:34Z", "kit", "kit groom 11-03 03:3x (WIP cap, memory wip-cap-active-means-touched): Active -> Planned, last note 17 h ago by kit, progress kept at 60%. Resume from that note: e while the crate is far under the 1000 gate. Follow-up for lib: a lower-only pick (one list) would recover most of the +84 for every caller. Also in this train: the job-host flag refusal message ('job job host') fixed in kit_jobs/jobs.spi.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_5 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 5u32, "2026-11-04T20:19Z", "kit", "11-04 20:5x kit: half verified on the INSTALLED kit: `kit job host --bogus` refuses (\"job host is started by kit itself and takes no flags; see job --help\") and starts nothing. `kit job supervise --bogus` exits 125 with NO message: it does not appear to start a supervisor, but it does not name the problem either. LEFT: supervise (and the other internal verbs) print the same refusal line as host.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_6 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 6u32, "2026-11-04T20:21Z", "kit", "11-04 21:1x kit: supervise half BUILT (unstaged): kit_job_entry JobSupervise now refuses an empty operand or any operand starting with \"-\" with \"kit error: job supervise is started by kit itself for one job id and takes no flags; see job --help\" (the same rejected path and wording as host), instead of the silent exit 125 seen on the installed kit; the real callers (kit_job_host host_run, kit_job_host_request) always pass a job-... id, so they are unaffected. vultr --check ok. Rides the next train after TRAIN23 (proof: `kit job supervise --help` prints the refusal and starts nothing). With host and supervise covered, the remaining internal verbs (run-serial is a --flag OF chain, not a verb) need no guard.")
inl note_of_kit_hidden_verb_flags_7 () = Note ("KIT-HIDDEN-VERB-FLAGS", 7u32, "2026-11-04T22:02Z", "kit", "11-04 18:0x kit: CLI check WRITTEN (unstaged) in kit_jobs/stop_cli.spi, internal_job_verbs_refuse_flags_instead_of_starting: `job supervise --help` and `job supervise` (no id) exit 2 with \"supervise is started by kit itself for one job id and takes no flags\", and `job host --help` exits 2 with the host refusal (rejected returns 2). The existing refused_adoption check passes a job id to supervise, so it is unaffected. Rides the next train after TRAIN25 (TRAIN25's snapshot predates the supervise guard).")
inl linked_units_no_suffix () = Task ("LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX", "Linked units: two exported unions with the same name are a compile error naming both definitions, not a <name>_<n> rename (spiral_compiler.fs:12463); variants read Command::Add", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", "team:compiler,compiler,rust,gleam,linked-units,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_linked_units_no_suffix () = Planning ("LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_linked_units_no_suffix_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX", 1u32, "2026-11-02T10:49Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x filed from kit-session Explore subagent aaf2a6f472dc70094 (11-02, read-only; report relayed by kit to main). Parent per the report: extend, don't fork the plan.")
inl note_of_linked_units_no_suffix_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:53Z", "compiler", "11-02 06:55 compiler: GROOM. ANCHOR: the rename is spiral_compiler.fs:12482 in exportedUnionNames (`$\"{clean}_{taken.Count}\"`); :12463 is importedTypeUnits. Its consumers are rename_exported_unions (codegenRust 14528) and renameExportedUnions (codegenGleam 18567). CATCH: two keys share a source name in two cases, and only one is an error. (a) Two distinct union DECLARATIONS with one name (two packages each declaring `color`) reachable from one unit's exports: compile error naming both declaring packages. (b) Two INSTANTIATIONS of one generic union (an export taking option i32 and returning option string) are one declaration with different type args. Today that yields option/option_2; an error would reject legal code. For (b) the name comes from the concrete type args (deterministic, e.g. option_i32 / option_string), the same (nominal, type args) key the n9 unit graph carries. So this lands with or after the second cut, keyed by declaring package id (n2 hole 3), never by text. DoD: one sample per case (a) error text names both packages, (b) two instantiations export as two stable names on Rust and Gleam. Variants keep the `Command::Add` style (enum path) on Rust. CORRECTION 07:10: case (b) is mostly handled already. Generic instances get type-arg names from structural_ty_name at nominal_type_apply (spiral_compiler.fs:9913), so model.rs exports box_i32, not box. The _<n> suffix at 12482 then only fires for two distinct declarations whose cleaned names collide (case a, the error) or two structurally named instances that clean to the same text (rare; error too).")
inl note_of_linked_units_no_suffix_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX", 3u32, "2026-11-03T19:46Z", "compiler", "11-03 15:4x compiler: PROVEN (node, control = installed pack27 core 6F83B94F). Program LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX\\1-same-name-unions-error.kitdo (3 replacements; source 11258A53 -> 7DCACFBE, candidate core 738CAFD7842B9C53). exportedUnionNames no longer renames '{clean}_{n}': a second distinct union with the same cleaned source name raises a codegen error naming both shapes and both declaring package dirs (new thread-local packageDirsById, filled from package_ids at the build dispatch). Fixture: packages a and b each declare ':| color', model exports conv : ca::color -> cb::color. Control: Rust pub enum color + color_1, Gleam Color + Color1, Zig color + color_1 (silent). Candidate on all three: 'FatalError: Two unions reached by this unit's exports are both named color: {Red : () | Green : ()} declared in .../fixture/a, and {Blue : () | Gray : i32} declared in .../fixture/b. ... rename one of the two declarations.' Contracts Rust 8 rows and Zig 620 rows vs pack27: 0 differing cells. Census of every unit graph in the user caches (box 1,746, node 97): the only suffixed union was this fixture, so no existing unit depended on the rename. Case (b) of n2 (two instantiations of one generic) is unaffected: structural_ty_name already names them apart (box_i32). Ships in pack29.")
inl note_of_linked_units_no_suffix_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-NO-SUFFIX", 4u32, "2026-11-03T23:07Z", "compiler", "11-03 19:0x compiler: INSTALLED in pack29; downstream green. Matrix row samples/linked_union_name_clash (Rust/Gleam/Zig, Error 'both named color') passes under -Suite linked. DoD met.")
