inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:53Z", "compiler", "11-02 06:55 compiler: GROOM. ANCHORS (live tree): the derive machinery is derive_traits / derive_externs from the rust-extern list (codegenRust 13552-13553), resolve_derives 14570-14611 (the extern symbol lookup is 14594-14603: a trait is derived only if every field type's extern entry declares it), and the default `#[derive(Clone)]` 14314/14609. Cited 13529-13582 / 14580 had drifted. DEPENDENCY: eq_<t>/show_<t> as exported Spiral functions are called across units, which is Step B (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS); deps updated. Retiring the rust-extern derive list touches every package.spiproj carrying `rust-extern: derive ...` (kit). Before the cut, census those lines so kit gets a count. The Spiral eq_/show_ bodies should come from lib's reflection (case_name, landed 6EA85EE1CBD0F2F2) rather than per-type hand code.")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 3u32, "2026-11-03T20:41Z", "compiler", "11-03 16:4x compiler: CENSUS done (the n2 pre-cut step). package.spiproj 'rust-extern:' lines across kit, html, x, spiral lib + apps, regex, alphabet and eoie: only 2 live packages carry the section, kit src/agile_planning_filters and src/agile_planning_fields, and both are FUNCTION externs ('rc_str = kit_agile_planning_selected, ...'), not derives; eoie's 38 hits are .cache/release-tree TRAIN copies of the same two. So ZERO packages declare a derive through rust-extern today: retiring the rust-extern derive symbol lookup (resolve_derives' extern path) breaks no consumer, and kit's count is 0. The remaining work is the positive side only, exported Spiral eq_<t>/show_<t> from reflection (case_name), which needs Step B calls (installed since pack26).")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 4u32, "2026-11-04T11:26Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:2x compiler: STEP 1 DRAFTED, the removal half (census n3: zero packages use it). LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT\\1-retire-extern-derive-lookup.kitdo deletes derive_externs from codegenRust. Clone stays always-allowed; other traits use only std_traits. A leftover 'rust-extern: <Type> = <traits>' entry now raises a codegen error naming the retirement instead of being silently ignored (fail closed). Only 'derive =' and 'rc_str =' keys remain; kit's two live sections (agile_planning_filters, agile_planning_fields) are rc_str and unaffected. Re-grepped 11-04: no other rust-extern section in any repo's package.spiproj, compiler samples included. Proof queued on the node (job compiler-rustrev, chained after compiler-splitu8): contracts Rust -Native, control pack34 vs candidate (this + LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES). Predicted: 0 behavior cells, no residual change from this program. Positive half (exported eq_<t>/show_<t> from reflection) is next.")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_5 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 5u32, "2026-11-04T13:05Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:1x compiler: STEP 1 PROVEN (node job compiler-rustrev2): examples Rust -Native, 518 rows, 0 differing cells vs pack34 (with LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES\\1 stacked), as predicted: the retired rust-extern derive lookup was empty everywhere. Ready for pack37. Next: the positive half, exported eq_<t>/show_<t> from lib reflection.")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_6 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 6u32, "2026-11-04T23:09Z", "compiler", "11-04 19:1x compiler: pack37 INSTALLED on the box 19:01 by main (core 5F6F6E73 / host 08B00F25 = the reviewed candidate; undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack37-20261104-190103). Node ship and vultr source build deferred until kit's TRAIN26 regen finishes (after 21:00). The 6 held Split samples landed in matrix.psd1's Split list (program 7, unstaged): array_cell, array_heap_heap_heap, array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_union_pair_heaps, while_control.")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_7 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 7u32, "2026-11-05T15:18Z", "compiler", "11-05 11:1x compiler: POSITIVE HALF PROVEN, no compiler change needed. New sample tmp/samples/linked_rust_eq_show (unstaged; Linked row 'Backends = Rust; Exit = 2; Calls = model_show'): the model unit exports make, same (Spiral equality over the record's fields) and show (Spiral display); the app compares and displays model points only through them, with no Rust derive. pack50 (= installed bin): linked 1/1, exit 2. Emitted app.rs: make and show are real cross-crate calls (model::model_show(model::point { x: v1, y: v2 }) builds the model's struct from app-side fields, which works since pack42's pub-field export), while same is INLINED into the app as v1 == v3 && v2 == v4 (the harness reports 'inlined: model_same'). That is semantically the same, since Spiral functions are transparent, so an exported eq needs no linkage at all and display is the only one that must cross. Rule for units: export show_<t> for display; write eq_<t> as a plain Spiral function (inlined, no derive). Next: decide whether the remaining 55% is only docs (the convention) or a lib reflection helper that writes eq/show from the record fields (get_record_fields).")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_8 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 8u32, "2026-11-05T15:33Z", "compiler", "11-05 11:3x compiler: LAST PART drafted: retire the 'rust-extern: derive = ...' list too. Census of every package.spiproj/spiral.toml under C:\\home\\git: only kit agile_planning_fields and agile_planning_filters have a rust-extern section, both 'rc_str = ...'; no package uses 'derive', so codegenRust always took the derive_traits = None path (generated unions '#[derive(Clone)]', no marker pass). Program 2 (drafts\\spiral\\LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT\\2-retire-rust-extern-derive.kitdo, generated from the exact source lines, 4 replacements, -47 lines): drops derive_traits, derive_candidates, the \\u0001derive markers and resolve_derives (the per-trait fixpoint over std types), and makes any non-rc_str rust-extern entry, now including derive, a codegen error that names the retirement and the replacement (export Spiral eq/show). Expected: byte-identical Rust output (every package was already on the None path). pack51 = pack50 + 2 building on the box; review = Rust examples + linked vs pack50.")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_9 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 9u32, "2026-11-05T15:48Z", "compiler", "11-05 11:4x compiler: pack51 REVIEWED (= pack50 + program 2; bin core E190545B5F30A7B4, host A1BF06EB). vs pack50: linked 14/14 both arms (includes linked_rust_eq_show), Rust examples 527 rows (500 ok + 27 expected errors), compile-status differences 0, residual differences 0: byte-identical, as the census predicted. Negative test, a package with 'rust-extern: derive = Clone, Debug': pack50 compiles it (exit 0, derive silently honoured), pack51 'FatalError: rust-extern: ''derive = ...'' is retired (LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT): generated types derive Clone only, and linked units export Spiral equality/display functions instead.' exit 5. Installing on the box now (install-when-clear, log %TEMP%\\compiler-pack51-chain.log).")
inl note_of_linked_units_derive_out_10 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT", 10u32, "2026-11-05T15:59Z", "compiler", "11-05 11:5x compiler: DONE. pack51 INSTALLED on the BOX (11:52-11:58): SpiralCompilerCore.dll E190545B5F30A7B4, SpiralCompiler.dll A1BF06EB9AD87F00, both equal=True; undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack51-20261105-115252. All three parts of the title hold: generated types derive Clone only; equality/display across linked units are Spiral functions the owner exports (linked_rust_eq_show: show is a real cross-crate call, eq inlines with the same meaning); the rust-extern derive symbol lookup and now the derive list are retired with a named error. Node: main ships pack51 (supersedes pack50) in a gap.")
