inl note_of_linked_units_gleam_records_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T10:49Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x filed from kit-session Explore subagent aaf2a6f472dc70094 (11-02, read-only; report relayed by kit to main). Parent per the report: extend, don't fork the plan.")
inl note_of_linked_units_gleam_records_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:53Z", "compiler", "11-02 06:55 compiler: GROOM. ANCHOR: the Gleam Export arm is codegenGleam 18283-18296. Parameters are data_free_vars of the domain (flattened, so a record argument arrives as loose fields) and the result is `tup_ty range` (a #(..) tuple). 18229-18242 is TyArrayCreate/TyConv. Rust's struct path is the Export arm at 14073. Shape: a record in an export signature becomes a `pub type <Name> { <Name>(field: T, ..) }` emitted by the unit and imported by the importer, through the same owner map as unions (n9 graph: record nominals reachable from exports). It lands after the second cut, since the importer needs the graph to know the record crosses. Sample: extend samples/linked_unit_union's model with an export returning { r : i32; s : string } and run it on Rust and Gleam.")
inl note_of_linked_units_gleam_records_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS", 3u32, "2026-11-03T19:49Z", "compiler", "11-03 15:5x compiler: GROOM after pack26. The crossing need is met: since pack26 (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS 5-gleam-flat-records, flat_records = true) a record argument crosses flattened into its fields (model.f(v1, v2)), and a record or tuple result comes back as #(..) and is destructured (let #(a, b) = model.make(..)); lu10 exit 13. This item now adds only NAMED record types at the boundary (pub type Name { Name(field: T, ..) }, as Rust's struct path at codegenRust 14482-14496). That helps hand-written Gleam callers but CHANGES the Gleam link ABI that x's Gleam builds use today. Decision rule: do it only when a hand-written Gleam consumer asks, and ship it with a kit/x regen in the same window. Until then it stays P2 Planned, and the Gleam Export arm is at codegenGleam 18734.")
inl note_of_linked_units_gleam_records_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS", 4u32, "2026-11-04T08:12Z", "compiler", "11-04 04:1x compiler: SHIP WINDOW AGREED with x (via main's ask): build and review now, but do NOT install until x messages that x-next7 has landed (x-next5b, 6 and 7 are proved against today's Gleam output with byte-identical accept fixtures; a link-ABI regen mid-stack would void them). x then runs the regen with this change as its own proof. If CELLS-PORT-TARGETS step 4 gets urgent first, x will pause between runs.")
inl note_of_linked_units_gleam_records_5 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS", 5u32, "2026-11-04T08:58Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:0x compiler: NATIVE PROOF GREEN (node job compiler-grnat: a staged tree with the box's -Suite linked, control pack34 vs candidate pack34 plus this program). Every linked row has the same verdict on both arms. linked_records: Zig and Gleam exit 13 (Gleam now through the named records); linked_union: Zig and Gleam 13; linked_rust_host_type 13; linked_rust_list_over_model 108; linked_union_name_clash still refuses with 'both named color' on Rust, Gleam and Zig. Contracts Rust 8, Zig 620, Gleam 8: 0 differing cells (job compiler-gleamrec). Generated Gleam as designed: the model declares pub type Point { Point(x: Int, y: Int) } and Named(name: String, n: Int), and the app builds model.Point(x: v1, y: v2) and reads { let r = model.model_make(v0) #(r.x, r.y) }. READY, and HELD for x's window (after x-next7); then it ships with x's regen as one install.")
