inl note_of_linked_units_opaque_tier_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-OPAQUE-TIER", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:53Z", "compiler", "11-02 06:55 compiler: GROOM. Anchor checks out: lib rust.spi:25 `rust_type * fs rs. (fsharp : string) : $'backend_switch ...'` with uses through :66. The sample is a pass-through unit whose export takes and returns a rust_type-typed value (a host Vec/Rc it never inspects), to show that host types cross as opaque. It needs no compiler change if Rust's Export arm prints the host type verbatim (14073, tyv). Check that first; if it holds, this is samples-only (one sample + matrix row, Known on non-Rust). Smallest of the seven, so it is a good warm-up after the second cut.")
inl note_of_linked_units_opaque_tier_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-OPAQUE-TIER", 3u32, "2026-11-03T20:02Z", "compiler", "11-03 16:0x compiler: PROVEN, NO COMPILER CHANGE NEEDED (the n2 'check first' holds). Fixture lu14 on the installed pack27 (core 6F83B94F): model ':! vec = $''Vec<i32>''' exports push4 (vec -> vec, a host macro body) and vlen (vec -> i32); the app links model. model.rs: 'pub fn model_push4(v0: Vec<i32>) -> Vec<i32>', app.rs: 'model::model_push4(v1)' and 'model::model_vlen(v2)'; rustc rlib + app --extern: exit 13. Why: ExternCalls.plain sees the nominal (YNominal -> resolve gives YMacro, not a record -> plain), so a host type declared through a nominal crosses verbatim, and rust_type values are nominals too. Only a BARE inline macro type (a $''..'' type written directly in an export signature, no nominal) stays inlined, since plain rejects YMacro. A draft that would let bare macros cross (LINKED-UNITS-OPAQUE-TIER\\1-host-types-cross.kitdo) is unneeded and archived. Left for DoD: the sample in the tree (a linked sample needs a multi-package contracts layout like mega_*).")
inl note_of_linked_units_opaque_tier_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-OPAQUE-TIER", 4u32, "2026-11-03T23:08Z", "compiler", "11-03 19:0x compiler: sample in tree, samples/linked_rust_host_type (Exit 13, Calls model_push4,model_vlen), runs under test.ps1 -Suite linked and passes on pack27 and newer; documented in apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md (the -Suite linked paragraph) and memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes. DoD met.")
