inl note_of_template_typed_units_1_1 () = Note ("TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1", 1u32, "2026-11-02T10:49Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x filed from kit-session Explore subagent aaf2a6f472dc70094 (11-02, read-only; report relayed by kit to main). Parent per the report: extend, don't fork the plan.")
inl note_of_template_typed_units_1_2 () = Note ("TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:50Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:0x per-lane adoption rows from the same report (file each when TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1 v1 is green): DTH-TYPED-UNITS (dir-tree-html, P2, after Step B: its 5 crates become link: units), TIBIA-MAP-TYPED-UNITS (P2: template layout for apps/map; Lua probes stay whole-program), FISCAL-TYPED-UNITS (P2: generated units already reference each other as packages; switch to link: when a Rust build is needed), dice/alphabet/polyglot (P3: layout + `template = \"typed-units/1\"` line only). eoie is retired (kit), so no row. X-TYPED-UNITS is filed already. The report's design: 4 unit kinds (model = types + pure fns + eq_/show_ exports; boundary = the only home of host code, one per OS surface; feature; bin), one entry file per package, generated output committed, unit graph is the single source of Cargo/Gleam deps.")
inl note_of_template_typed_units_1_3 () = Note ("TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:13Z", "main", "main 11-02 GROOM ROUND RESULT (ask 1: units per repo under typed-units/1). compiler: core is one F# file; Spiral side proposed lib-model (core types, reflection, sm') / lib-boundary (rust.spi rust_type, file_system/date_time) / lib-feature (xml, xpath_eval, unicode) + samples as bin units; HELD: conflicts with the user's lib-FLAT rule, parked as a user decision (lib as one unit, or split). x: x_model (protocol, posts, fields, paging, glyphs, tlds, defuse, splitter), x_boundary (net, wire, token, oauth1, transport; 89 host lines), x_features (fetch, timeline, thread, ...), xc (bin), xsim (Gleam bin via link:); debt 15 client + 3 sim modules carry host lines (X-1-0-DOD n1). x-dumps: xarchive_model, xarchive_boundary (HTTP, sha256 cache, rate/backoff, all fs IO), xarchive_harvest, xarchive_history (timeline.rs 17.5 KB = 1000-line risk), xarchive (bin); xarchive is hand-written Rust with NO git (resilience asked for an off-box copy). tibia: model = src rules; feature = sim + results/; boundary = apps/host + offscreen + canary (62 $' lines); bin = suite + predict; apps/arena (169 $' lines) stays whole-program. fiscal: fiscal_model, fiscal_host (boundary: all 67 file_system calls, today spread over corpus_checks 37 / generator 25 / canon 4 / corpus 1), fiscal_corpus, fiscal_generator, fiscal_regen (bin); 81 generated units stay model packages via link:, but 68 of 81 are over 1000 lines (UBL Invoice 57,667), the hardest gate in the org. kit: phases on KIT-TYPED-CRATES n13/n14. DRAFT 1.0 DoDs filed: SPIRAL-COMPILER-1-0-DOD, X-1-0-DOD, X-DUMPS-1-0-DOD, TIBIA-1-0-DOD, FISCAL-1-0-DOD (all dep ORG-VERSIONING, which waits on the user). Raw answers: main session scratchpad groom-1102-answers.md.")
inl note_of_template_typed_units_1_4 () = Note ("TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1", 4u32, "2026-11-02T14:03Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByModel. QUESTION: Under typed-units/1, is lib one unit or split into lib-model/lib-boundary/lib-feature, given the user's lib-FLAT rule? RULE (written before acting): Both coexist: lib stays physically flat (lib-FLAT kept), and units are declared as groupings in spiral.toml over the flat files. Each unit carries a phantom kind index (unit model | unit boundary | unit feature), and link: between units is checked so a model unit importing a boundary unit is a compile error. 'lib as one unit' is the degenerate grouping (every file in one unit), selectable behind a typed switch. The split is enabled only where the 1000-generated-lines gate or a measured parallel-build win (>=15% median wall over 5 runs, A/A < 5%) demands it. Tie-break: one unit. BACKUP/UNDO: The groupings live only in manifest lines, and the flat file layout is untouched. Revert = drop the [units] section (unstaged for the user's review). OWNER: main. NEXT: Add the unit-kind grouping to the mini example repo first (Rust and Gleam green), then apply it to lib with the one-unit default. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
inl note_of_template_typed_units_1_5 () = Note ("TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1", 5u32, "2026-11-02T14:59Z", "main", "main 11-02 DECIDED: lib stays ONE unit. RULE (fixed before looking, per the user via fiscal 11-02: \"those things can be decided autonomously\"; technical calls are ours, decided by a pre-stated rule with rule and outcome recorded). Rule: a standing user rule beats a template default. The user's rule 'lib stays FLAT, no subfolders except leptos/ui' rules out compiler's model/boundary/feature split, because separate unit packages need their own directories. Outcome: lib is one link: unit; typed-units/1 applies to apps and repos. Revisit only if the user lifts the flat rule. ALSO from the 11-02 star exchange (compiler #13, kit #8): since pack16c a unit with exports writes <stem>.unit.json beside its .spi, and an importer of an unbuilt link: unit fails 'build X first'. So the template must (1) gitignore *.unit.json and (2) build units in link: order, and staged regens must carry .unit.json along with the .rs.")
