inl note_of_kit_load_proof_e2e_2 () = Note ("KIT-LOAD-PROOF-E2E", 2u32, "2026-11-02T10:54Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 07:0x GROOM. DoD made checkable: (a) the e2e suite = the train's notebook set (69 in TRAIN10) plus the smoke verbs, run once under coverage on the NODE (box CPU is scarce; hit counts don't depend on load, so the node's answer is valid here); (b) the output is a per-function hit table for every crate reachable from kit-cli, kept as a report under .cache, with the run's tree head and lib hash; (c) prune candidates = zero-hit functions and packages, minus an allowlist file (first entry: the bundle/archive code, 29 packages / 8 crates / 4,631 lines, kept for EOIE-REMOTE-EXECUTOR n8/n12); (d) any pruning goes through scratch-archive.ps1 (archive, never delete) and lands through a train. Static 'reached by no crate' packages (116, KIT-TYPED-CRATES n13 K4) are a separate, cheaper list: they need no coverage run. ORDER: before KIT-TYPED-CRATES K2/K3 (prune first, migrate less). First step: check that kit_lcov / kit_coverage_smoke still build and give a hit table on one notebook, before the full run.")
