inl note_of_x_1_0_dod_1 () = Note ("X-1-0-DOD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 07:08 x: DRAFT DoD, nothing here is adopted. Gaps:\n(1) typed-units/1 via X-TYPED-UNITS. 5 units: x_model (protocol, posts, fields, paging, glyphs, tlds, defuse, splitter), x_boundary (net 41 host lines, wire 23, token 15, oauth1 7, transport 3: the only home for host code), x_features (fetch, timeline, thread, chain, write, refs, users, resume, digest, select, view, ...), xc (bin: xc, cli, args), and xsim (Gleam bin: sim_serve, simframes, xsim_split, joined through link: per X-GLEAM-MANUAL-SPLIT). Host-code debt to move into x_boundary: 15 non-boundary client modules carry host lines (xc 22, write 12, frames 5, defuse 5, fields 4, chunks 3, and 1-2 in args, cells, chain, checks, jsonl, posted, preview, view, weights), plus 3 sim modules. Also: drop the 15-field parsed tuple (xc.spi:32) and the 48 call strings.\n(2) typed-units/1 gates: at most 1000 generated lines per unit (today 29 crates and 0 over, with the sim frames hand-split into 37 parts, so this needs link: units); no $'<unit>::; no union-to-code mapping at a boundary; concrete export signatures; typefeatureset score never down.\n(3) CI green: CI is red at the client gate on committed splitter V1 until the user commits the unstaged V3 and the landed outputs (verify48b, verify51, x-sim-map1, x-sim-keys1).\n(4) SPIPROJ-RETIRE: x has 0 package.spiproj readers. apps/client and apps/sim/spi each carry a matching spiral.toml, so both package.spiproj files go once the compiler host reader is gone.\n(5) A v1.0.0 tag and the template edition, both user decisions.")
inl note_of_x_1_0_dod_2 () = Note ("X-1-0-DOD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:06Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:59 x: DECISION RECORD (typed; groom of user waits, user 11-02: 'decisions waiting on me get met autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset modeling/backups'). kind=ByDefault. QUESTION: Adopt ORG-VERSIONING, the proposal x's 1.0 DoD draft depends on? RULE (written before acting): Default: adopt ORG-VERSIONING provisionally so the draft becomes x's working checklist. It is reversible, and the v1.0.0 tag stays a user git action. Gap (3) is already met: x is in sync and ci run 41426949017 on f26d2c6 is green. BACKUP/UNDO: Keep the DRAFT note; kit state-backups hold the prior agile.spi; revert = re-tag draft. OWNER: x. NEXT: Mark (3) met, drop the draft tag, and drive (1)/(2) through X-TYPED-UNITS. VETO: the user can reverse this at any time; the backup above is the undo.")
