inl regex_dfa_table () = Task ("REGEX-DFA-TABLE", "regex fast DFA core: array-backed transition table over byte (or code point) classes, &[u8]/array input, no Rc or list walk in the hot loop, measured against the regex crate on long inputs", Story, P0, D5, 0u32, Planned, "-", "regex,automata,benchmark,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_dfa_table () = Planning ("REGEX-DFA-TABLE", Minutes 480u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_dfa_table_1 () = Note ("REGEX-DFA-TABLE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:15Z", "regex", "regex 07:3x DOD: the eager and minimal DFA run over an array_base table (state x class -> next state, lib am' create_base/set_base/index_base, every backend) and a class lookup table (256-entry byte map for ASCII/UTF-8 bytes, a range table above), input as an array of bytes or code points instead of a list; the dead state is a union case at the boundary but a sentinel-free reserved row inside the table; Cells tests prove table run = list run = derivative matcher on the agreement corpus (rust + gleam); the bench's long-input table shows the new arm with A/A passing. PRE-REGISTER before the first run: predicted ratio vs the regex crate on 4 x 4000 bits between 0.5 and 2.0 (today 1/0.068). NEXT STEP: add dfa_table.spi with table_of (d : dfa) and run_table, a test against run on the curated corpus, then a bench arm. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: a nominal row_index and class_index over i32 that only table_of hands out; a GADT-free table record; phantom 'built from minimal' vs 'eager' if both tables coexist.")
inl note_of_regex_dfa_table_2 () = Note ("REGEX-DFA-TABLE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:18Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x PRE-REGISTERED before its first run: src/table.spi (array_base table: lows, next (n+1) x k with a reserved dead row, accepting; binary class search; array input) + a TableArm in the bench. QUESTION: median ratio of the table arm vs the list-backed minimal DFA. PREDICTION: long input (4 x 4000 bits) 0.10-0.40; short words 0.5-1.0 (fixed per-word cost dominates). Implication vs the regex crate (0.088 of the list DFA on CI): still 1.2-4.5x behind, so codegen patches remain needed. PASS RULE: A/A within 0.95-1.05 in the same job, counts equal on all 7 arms. First proof on the node (bench compile = type check of every src module), then Cells for the 2 new test blocks.")
inl note_of_regex_dfa_table_3 () = Note ("REGEX-DFA-TABLE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T11:26Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x FIRST RUN (box, compile window win-1793618390327, busy box): src/table.spi + the TableArm compile (bench.rs now 4777 lines; every src module type-checks inside the bench entry) and regex-bench exits 0, i.e. the array table returns the same accepted count as the other 6 arms on every word of every round (correctness MET). TIME: all 5 tables VOID (A/A 0.86-1.12 on the busy box), so the n2 prediction stays open until CI or a quiet runner; VOID rows now also print the unverified median. The 2 new Cells tests in table.spi have not run yet (they run in CI with the rest). Unstaged: src/table.spi, src/package.spiproj, bench/bench.spi.")
inl note_of_regex_dfa_table_4 () = Note ("REGEX-DFA-TABLE", 4u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x M0 FROM THE SHARE (C §B.2 M0, E §7 M0; relayed via main): no Rc or .clone() in the matcher hot loop, a dense loop over &[u8]; CUT RULE: if the plain DFA loop (no prefilter) is > 3x slower than regex-automata dense::DFA on the same pattern, stop and fix codegen first (REGEX-CODEGEN-PATCHES). Today: the list-backed DFA is ~11x behind the regex crate on CI long input; the array table is the first fix.")
inl note_of_regex_dfa_table_5 () = Note ("REGEX-DFA-TABLE", 5u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 10 (verbatim, this item covers it): 10. NEW REGEX-HOT-LOOP: M0 codegen. &[u8] input through an array_base u8; an array-backed state x class table; no Rc or .clone() in the generated matcher function, checked by a census grep that must return 0 (Rc may appear only in setup code); in-process timing. DoD: a page row showing Spiral's dense loop over regex-automata dense::DFA on the same pattern, cut at more than 3.0x. Today's list-backed DFA is about 15x behind the regex crate on long input (REGEX-BENCH-PAGE n9). Source: E §4 \"O Rust gerado usa Rc/clone\", §7 M0; C §B.2 M0.")
