inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_1 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:19Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:50 compiler: AUDIT DONE (main's ask after the export_family regression). HOW THE MATRIX SELECTS: every tmp/samples/<dir> with an entry runs on the default Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (test.ps1 Get-ExampleBackends); the per-backend lists (Zig, Wasm, Wgsl, Calyx, Kotlin, Swift, OpenQasm, Ebpf, Lean, Bend, Gleam, Lua, Python) only ADD backends. So the silent case is a regression sample for a non-default backend with no list row, or a file outside tmp/samples. PASS over 895 sample dirs (backend named in the dir name, or near regression/fix/arm/gap/bug in the head comment, but absent from that backend's list and Backends sets): 2 hits. mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel is a false positive (per-child rows). gleam_dead_arm_let_globals is REAL: a Gleam-only dead-arm marker sample (BackendSwitch Gleam arm with a global import) with no Gleam row, so only its C/Rust arms ever run. tests/families: export_family is the only module missing from families/package.spiproj, and families run only in bench-cells-vs-matrix / fast-tier, not in test.ps1 suites. tests/rust-exports runs via test-rust-exports.ps1, whose wrong_signature case had a stale respell anchor; fixed today. Heuristic limit: it catches only samples that name their backend. TODO: (1) export_family into the Zig path with LINKED-UNITS-ZIG step 0; (2) run gleam_dead_arm_let_globals on Gleam, then add its row (or record it as Known); (3) put families in a test.ps1 suite so a family module that is not wired fails loudly.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_2 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:46Z", "compiler", "11-02 07:50 compiler: TODO (1) done in a better form. The Zig export regression now has a real matrix row, samples/zig_export_fn (Fsharp + Zig), instead of wiring the Cells-only families/export_family.spi; it lands with LINKED-UNITS-ZIG program 1. Left: (2) gleam_dead_arm_let_globals on Gleam, (3) families in a test.ps1 suite.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_3 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (20 h). Next: (2) a Gleam matrix row for gleam_dead_arm_let_globals, (3) the families in a test.ps1 suite.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_4 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T05:28Z", "compiler", "11-04 01:2x compiler: (2) DONE. The Gleam row for samples/gleam_dead_arm_let_globals is wired in matrix.psd1 (unstaged). Box run (examples, Gleam, -Native, pack33): compile ok, native build-fail 'Unknown module', because the Gleam output imports spiral_dead_arm_marker from the dead Rust arm. That is BY DESIGN (COMPILER-DEAD-ARM-GLOBALS): a dead arm validated for the build backend writes the root globals so a join point first specialized there keeps them, accepting an unused import, which Gleam normally only warns about; here the import names a module that does not exist. So the row is recorded as Known (Gleam, with that reason). Rerun: oracle=known, detail 'known: by design ...'. The row now guards against any change in that behaviour; Rust and C remain the rows where the marker must stay out. Generated main.gleam removed (Gleam rows commit no output). Left: (3) families in a test.ps1 suite.")
inl note_of_matrix_unwired_regression_samples_5 () = Note ("MATRIX-UNWIRED-REGRESSION-SAMPLES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T12:15Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:1x compiler: (3) DONE. test.ps1 gains -Suite families (unstaged, edited in place): it reads the module list from tmp/tests/families/package.spiproj (the 11 *_family modules; export_family stays Cells-only, it is not in the manifest), points SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL at the compiler under test, and runs test-blocks.ps1 -Compiler process into the run dir; exit 1 on any DISAGREE; it refuses to combine with other suites, like linked. Box run on installed pack34: 'test-block rows 150: agree 150, DISAGREE 0, not run 0' over all 11 files (array 14, ebpf 6, mut 20, small_int 8, string 8, tagged_union 8, tuple 6, union 20, plus closure, heap, method). The LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE split-suite draft (2-test-suite-split.kitdo) was rebased onto the new suite list. All three parts of the item are done: (1) zig_export_fn row, (2) Gleam row for gleam_dead_arm_let_globals, (3) families suite.")
