inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB items 7, 8, 9, 28 (legacy main.spi reference_derivative 483, language_remainders 565, semantic triangle 625, step certificate 732; remainder_theorem/main.spi 7). DOD: semantics.spi decides membership by language remainders without derivatives and by a textbook backtracking matcher (continuation stack, greedy star) that must agree with every engine on the agreement corpus; laws.spi enumerates every regex of depth <= 2 over a 2-symbol alphabet plus & and ~ and checks remainder law, idempotence of normalization, nullable preserved, reference_derivative ~ canonical derivative (semantic triangle), step certificate; certificate.check_witnesses replays words on the oracle, not on derivatives; a backtracking arm in the bench (ReDoS: (0|00)*1 vs 0^n). Tests on rust + gleam, 0 failures. NEXT STEP: semantics.spi with language_remainders over the re union. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: the oracle returns verdict; a phantom oracle_kind (language | backtracking) on the answer so tests cannot compare an engine with itself.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T23:38Z", "main", "main 11-02 19:4x PART 1 PROVEN: regex src/semantics.spi (NEW, untracked) + package.spiproj (after agreement). LANGUAGE ORACLE without derivatives: ends r t p = the set of end positions q with w[p..q] in L(r), as sorted i32 lists. Nothing = [], Epsilon = [p], Set = [p+1] if the code is in the set, Seq = ends of b from every end of a, Alt = union, And = INTERSECTION, Not = [p..n] MINUS ends (a complement on positions is exactly the language complement for that slice), Star = least fixpoint closure, Repeat = low exact copies then a bounded/unbounded closure. language_answer = n is in ends r w 0. Node gate (mirror sem, regex d7aa16be + tree, memo off): 4/4 passed: the 4th-from-end points, And/Not as set operations, counted repetition, and THE ORACLE AGREES WITH ALL FOUR ENGINES on the seeded corpus (Agree 240, the same 240 words the engine-agreement test uses). PART 2 (in the next gate, all src): textbook backtracking baseline (continuation-passing, greedy star, the And/Not-free fragment, else OutsideFragment); a GADT oracle_verdict by_language | by_backtracking so oracles_agree only accepts one of EACH kind (a negative test 'an_oracle_is_never_compared_with_itself fails Unification failure'); backtracking vs language on the corpus (5 backtrackable patterns x 40 = 200); the ReDoS shape (0|00)*1 on 0^12. LEFT: laws.spi (exhaustive depth-2 corpora), certificate.check_witnesses replaying on the oracle, the bench's backtracking arm.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_3 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T01:08Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:0x PART 2 PROVEN (node gate, all regex src, memo off): semantics.spi 7/7. That covers the textbook backtracking baseline (continuation-passing, greedy star, And/Not-free fragment, else OutsideFragment) agreeing with the language oracle on the seeded corpus (OraclesAgree 200 = the 5 backtrackable curated patterns x 40 words); the ReDoS shape (0|00)*1 on 0^12 answered correctly by both; and the GADT oracle_verdict (LanguageVerdict :: verdict -> oracle_verdict by_language | BacktrackingVerdict :: ... by_backtracking): oracles_agree takes one of EACH kind, and the negative ':# an_oracle_is_never_compared_with_itself fails \"Unification failure\"' holds. LEFT for this item: laws.spi (exhaustive depth-2 corpora over 2 symbols + & ~: remainder law, normalization idempotence, nullable preserved, reference vs canonical derivative triangle, step certificate), certificate.check_witnesses replaying words on the oracle, and the bench's backtracking arm.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_4 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T01:41Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:5x laws.spi PROVEN (node mirror sem, regex d7aa16be + tree, memo off): 2/2 passed in 292 s. every_regex_of_depth_one_keeps_all_five_laws_on_every_short_word (rust + gleam): AllHold 1320. every_regex_of_depth_two_keeps_all_five_laws_on_every_short_word (rust): AllHold 241560, slowest 155 s. That is all 10,980 regexes of depth <= 2 over {0, 1} with Seq/Alt/And/Not/Star x the 7 words of length <= 2, 22 checks each. The five laws hold everywhere: smart constructors preserve the language (oracle), normalization is idempotent (same_re), nullable = accepts the empty word, the remainder law on the oracle, and Brzozowski = oracle. ALSO DONE (unstaged, in the next full gate): language.spi split out of semantics.spi so certificate.check_witnesses replays distinguishing words on the oracle, not on derivatives; bench gets BacktrackingArm (textbook backtracking on every workload incl. ZeroRuns = the ReDoS shape (0|00)*1); counts_agree keeps it honest. LEFT: none of n1's DoD once that gate and the bench run are green.")
inl note_of_regex_semantics_oracle_5 () = Note ("REGEX-SEMANTICS-ORACLE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:15Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:1x DONE (DoD n1 complete). Full regex src gate on the node (mirror sem, regex d7aa16be + tree, memo off, pack18 with the fixed core): 60/63. Every file green except nullable.spi's 3, the separate pack17 GADT-erasure regression (compiler's GADT-ERASE-ONLY-GROWING ships in pack20). language.spi 3/3 (the oracle and its point tests, split out so certificate.check_witnesses replays distinguishing words on it), semantics.spi 4/4 (the oracle agreeing with all 4 engines on 240 words, backtracking agreeing on 200, ReDoS, the self-comparison negative), laws.spi 2/2 (241,560 law checks on every regex of depth <= 2), certificate 6/6 (witness replay on the oracle), table 2/2. BENCH: bench.spi with BacktrackingArm compiled (BuildSpiral 19 s), cargo exit 0, regex-bench exit 0, so counts_agree held for all 8 arms incl. textbook backtracking on every workload (ZeroRuns = (0|00)*1 is the ReDoS shape).")
inl regex_engines_lazy_staged () = Task ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", "regex interned lazy DFA and staged DFA engines (legacy items 29, 30) with bench arms: hash-consed nodes as nominals, memoized derivatives per (node, class), compile-time staged tables for static patterns", Story, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "-", "regex,automata,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
