inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_1 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB items 29, 30, 32 (legacy runtime_interned.spi, runtime_workload.spi staged_accepts, static_* twins main.spi 910-1056/1575-1944). DOD: lazy.spi interns nodes (a node is its number, children below parent, smart constructors normalize as they build) and caches the derivative per (node, class) in an array_base table, so after warm-up a step is two array reads; staged.spi builds the DFA at compile time for a known regex (inl static twins) and emits a constant-transition loop; both agree with every engine on the corpus and appear as bench arms with A/A passing; the lazy engine is the fallback when the eager cap refuses. Legacy timing (C, 2026-10-06): interned 41 ms and staged 40 ms vs 1,350 ms for the plain derivative matcher on 2,000 random words: predict the same order here. NEXT STEP: lazy.spi with the interning store. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: interned_node and class_slot nominals only the store hands out (legacy interned_regex/bit_slot); staged twins only where the regex is static (an inl rec over runtime data never terminates). Links: REGEX-SOTA (lazy is also the speed path for runtime patterns).")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_2 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 2u32, "2026-11-03T05:17Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:2x STARTED + PROVEN slice 1 (node mirror lazy, memo off: lazy.spi 3/3; unstaged, registered after dfa in package.spiproj). src/lazy.spi: an interning store (cache = nodes (re * interned), count, steps ((node, class) -> node)); the nominal 'interned' is handed out only by intern, which normalizes through the smart constructors (same_re key) and maps Nothing to DeadNode; step_lazy memoizes the derivative per (node, class index) so each (node, class) is derived once per cache; run_from_node threads the cache, so a word list warms it. No state cap: it is the fallback where build_within refuses. Tests: on every word of length <= 6 over {0,1} the lazy engine agrees with the eager DFA (0 disagreements) on fourth_from_end, zero_runs and ends_in_zero, visiting 16, 4 and 2 nodes; one word interns only what it visits (fourth_from_end on 1000 = Accepted with 5 nodes, on 0 = Rejected with 1); where build_within 4 refuses, the lazy engine still answers (Accepted on 01011). LEFT: the array_base store (a warm step = two array reads; today it is association lists), the bench arm with A/A, staged.spi (compile-time DFA for static patterns, inl twins only on static regexes). 0 -> 25.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_3 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 3u32, "2026-11-03T05:33Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:3x BENCH ARM added (bench/bench.spi LazyArm 'lazy DFA (interned nodes, memoized steps)'; one_pass threads one cache per pass, cold at each pass start so warm-up is inside the timing; arms % 9; unstaged). Node run (mirror lazy, 15 rounds, 400 words x 25 passes, seed 20261101, bench 490 s): every workload 'agree on 40 words' with the lazy arm in. Median time / minimal DFA (baseline A): (0|1)*0 0.310 (IQR 0.294-0.403), (0|00)*1 0.436, [a-z]{1,64} 0.287, (0|1)*1(0|1){3} 1.276 (1.177-1.411), the same on 4 texts of 4000 bits 1.746 (1.573-2.001). PRELIMINARY: a Cells gate ran on the node at the same time (A/A on the first workload 0.982, IQR 0.894-1.230, wider than the quiet-run band), so rerun alone before quoting. Reading: the association-list memo wins on few states and sparse visits and loses at 16 states x 4 classes, where each step walks the steps list; that is exactly what the DOD's array_base store (two array reads per warm step) fixes, so it is the next slice. Progress 25 -> 35.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_4 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 4u32, "2026-11-03T10:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:2x BENCH RERUN on vultr (no Cells gate beside it, though x-dumps' harvest pods share the VM; bench 177 s, 15 rounds). VERIFIED rows (A/A inside 0.95-1.05): lazy / minimal DFA = 0.385 on (0|1)*0 (IQR 0.201-0.557), 0.511 on (0|00)*1, 0.388 on [a-z]{1,64}. The same direction as the node run (0.31/0.44/0.29). VOID: both fourth_from_end workloads (A/A 0.925 and 1.101; lazy read 1.406 and 1.576, unverified), so the 16-state slowdown stays UNPROVEN, not a result. The bench's own A/A rule refused to report it, as designed. A quiet machine is still needed for those rows; the array_base store slice is what should move them anyway.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_5 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 5u32, "2026-11-03T12:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:1x ARRAY STORE SLICE (lazy.spi, unstaged): store = { width; cap; lows : array_base u32; steps : array_base i32 (node x class, -2 unknown / -1 dead / node index); nodes : array_base re; used : array_base i32 }, preallocated to a cap. intern_in searches nodes only on a miss; step_in is one class binary search plus one array read when warm, and derives and memoizes on a miss. run_in returns store_answer = Answered verdict | Overflowed, so a full cap is an explicit typed answer, not a crash. Vultr gate: lazy 5/5 (the store agrees with the eager DFA on every word of length <= 6 and interns the same 16/4/2 nodes as the list engine; cap 2 on fourth_from_end is Overflowed). Bench arm LazyStoreArm added (arms % 10); its run is next on vultr. Progress 35 -> 55.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_6 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 6u32, "2026-11-03T12:32Z", "main", "store bench 1 (vultr, arms rotated, A/A in band): list lazy 0.33-1.25x of minimal DFA on short words, array store 2.3-3.5x (cold 65536 x width fill per pass), but store 0.706x vs list 1.524x on 4000-bit texts. Slice 2: fill a node's row only on intern (lazy.spi, compiles); rebench running; then size cap from the regex.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_7 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 7u32, "2026-11-03T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:2x VOID: the two rebenches after bench 1 (row-fill-on-intern, then the growable store) ran /home/remote/main-regex/regex, a side copy that remote.ps1 vultr sync never updates (sync lands in /home/remote/git/regex); its lazy.spi was 39B14121 vs the box's B7B8558B. Their numbers say nothing about the new code. Stale copies main-regex and main-ig deleted; scripts repointed to /home/remote/git/*; the growable store (16 slots, doubling to cap, Overflowed bound kept) is regating and rebenching now.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_8 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 8u32, "2026-11-03T13:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:4x GROWABLE STORE WINS (fresh tree /home/remote/git/regex, lazy.spi B7B8558B; gate 5/5). Store = nodes/steps behind 1-slot holders, 16 slots doubling to cap, Overflowed bound kept. Bench (vultr, 15 rounds, rotated), ratio to minimal DFA, VERIFIED rows (A/A in band): (0|1)*0 list 0.324 vs store 0.157; (0|00)*1 0.475 vs 0.209; fourth_from_end 1.326 vs 0.551. VOID rows (A/A 0.948 / 1.061 out of band), indicative only: [a-z]{1,64} 0.368 vs 0.130; 4000-bit texts 1.511 vs 0.315. The store beats the list engine 2-5x and the minimal DFA on short words. NEXT: rerun the two void rows; then the staged slice (store as the default lazy engine, list engine kept as the reference oracle).")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_9 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 9u32, "2026-11-03T13:52Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:5x RERUN verifies the two void rows (A/A in band): [a-z]{1,64} list 0.384 vs store 0.142; fourth_from_end on 4000-bit texts list 1.456 vs store 0.307. Also (0|1)*0 0.313 vs 0.186, fourth_from_end 1.376 vs 0.593 (only (0|00)*1 void this time, matching run 1's 0.475 vs 0.209). So every row now has a verified run: the growable array store beats the list engine 1.7-4.7x and the minimal DFA on all short-word rows. NEXT slice: make the store the default lazy engine (run_lazy via store_of), keep the list engine as the reference oracle in tests.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_10 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 10u32, "2026-11-03T15:26Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:4x SCALE ROW (new bench workload (0|1)*1(0|1){7}, 256-state minimal DFA, certificate skipped >128; vultr, A/A 1.018 in band): list lazy 1.964 vs array store 1.117 of the minimal DFA. On <=65 states the store ran 0.14-0.6x; at 256 it falls behind the minimal DFA. Cause by construction: each cold step's intern does a linear find_slot over all interned nodes with structural same_re, so pass-cold cost grows ~n^2 in states. This is the measured case for the item's remaining 'hash-consed nodes' slice: key interned nodes by a canonical hash (or a dict keyed by the normalized regex text) so a miss is O(1). Other rows unchanged (4000-bit texts: store 0.302, list 1.504).")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_11 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 11u32, "2026-11-03T16:08Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:4x SLICE 3 (hash-cons equivalent, unstaged): the store interns through a binary search tree over syntax's existing total order order_re (slot = Found | Under (parent, side) | Root; tree_slot, attach, place; one links array of child indices, grown with nodes/steps). Linear find_slot removed. PROOF: vultr full regex gate 85/85 over all 15 notebooks (with the same-day formatter + ^ lint heal). BENCH (vultr): (0|1)*1(0|1){7} 256 states, store 0.858 vs 1.117 with the linear scan (-23%; the store now beats the minimal DFA there), but that row's A/A was 0.944 (VOID), so indicative only; verified rows unchanged ((0|1)*0 0.134, (0|00)*1 0.190, 4000-bit 0.334). Rerun queued to verify the 256 row. Progress 70 -> 80; left: the compile-time staged tables.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_12 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 12u32, "2026-11-03T16:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:1x VERIFIED (rerun, A/A 0.980 in band): (0|1)*1(0|1){7}, 256 states: array store with BST intern 0.831 of the minimal DFA (IQR 0.635-0.892), against 1.117 with the linear scan and the list engine's 1.984. The BST cut the 256-state cost by 26% and the store now beats the minimal DFA at every measured size.")
inl note_of_regex_engines_lazy_staged_13 () = Note ("REGEX-ENGINES-LAZY-STAGED", 13u32, "2026-11-03T17:07Z", "main", "main 11-03 13:1x DONE (lazy half): list lazy DFA (slice 1), array-store lazy engine (slice 2, growable from 16 slots), BST intern over order_re (slice 3); vultr regex gate 85/85 over all 15 notebooks; verified bench: the store beats the list engine 1.7-4.7x and the minimal DFA at every measured size up to 256 states (0.831 there). The staged-tables half moves to REGEX-STAGED-TABLES (P2), since its only possible win is setup time, which today's bench doesn't time.")
inl regex_automaton_typestate () = Task ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", "regex automaton typestate built -> minimal -> certified (legacy item 17) plus a negative/ package set that build.ps1 checks must fail to type-check", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "-", "regex,automata,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_automaton_typestate () = Planning ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_1 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB item 17 + typestate negatives (phase_use, derivative_runtime_phase_use, raw_generic_state_seal, seal_unverified_derivative, derivative_skip_normalization, raw_inventory_bypass) and the forgery negatives that make sense at type level. DOD: dfa carries a phase GADT index (built | minimal | certified, constant per value so it works at runtime); run, table_of and the bench accept only certified automata; a negative/ folder of tiny packages, each importing src and doing one forbidden thing, and build.ps1 asserts each fails to compile with its expected error text (failing for the RIGHT reason, the legacy lesson); Cells tests cover the positive path. NEXT STEP: add the phase index to dfa and thread it through minimize/certify. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: GADT phase with refining constructors, the checker is the only producer of the certified index.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_2 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T12:27Z", "regex", "regex 08:3x PLAN CHANGE: negatives as `:# name fails ETY-TermError \"msg\" =` test blocks beside the code (TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC Done; passes only when the diagnostic is located in the test body), replacing the negative/ package set + build.ps1 check of n1. Also from the ERP lessons: authority/witness values behind refusing constructors (the legacy forgery gap: nominal constructors are public), prototypes for phase-dependent operations.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_3 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T01:07Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:0x DONE, phase 1 (main; the DoD in n1/n2 minus refusing constructors). regex src (unstaged): certificate.spi adds phase indices built_phase/minimal_phase/certified_phase and ':| ^ automaton phase' (Eager :: dfa -> automaton built_phase | Minimized :: dfa -> automaton minimal_phase | CertifiedAutomaton :: dfa * i32 -> automaton certified_phase); minimized (built -> minimal), certified (minimal -> option certified, only through check_minimality = Certified), certified_of (re -> certified, failwith if minimize ever fails its own certificate), run_certified; table.spi table_of NOW TAKES automaton certified_phase (minimal_table goes through certified_of); bench.spi builds its table from certified_of; package.spiproj moves table after certificate. Node gate (mirror sem, all src, memo off): certificate 6/6 incl. the single-case GADT match 'certified_pairs' (index refinement works, pairs = 120 for the 4th-from-end) and the negative ':# a_minimized_automaton_cannot_run_as_certified fails \"Unification failure\"'; table 2/2; the 52 other rows unchanged except nullable.spi's 3, which are a separate compiler regression (REC-MARKER-HEAL n9; also red on CI at HEAD). LEFT (phase 2): constructors are public, so the typestate prevents mistakes, not forgery: put CertifiedAutomaton behind a refusing constructor (n2's authority idea). The agreement suite keeps raw run on purpose (it compares raw engines).")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_4 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T01:21Z", "main", "main 11-02 21:3x PHASE 2 SCOPED. Spiral has no private constructors, so CertifiedAutomaton can't be refused at the call site. The lib's precedent for forgery refusal is xsd_certificate.spi: a moves_witness GADT checked by moves_sound with error_type 'a forged certificate row', which fires at COMPILE time because the certificate is static data (its fails-test proves it). Regex automata are computed from the regex, so the same trick means certifying during partial evaluation, which is feasible only for regexes known at compile time and heavy. Decision: keep phase 1 (typestate against mistakes; certified is the only producer in src), and file the compile-time-certified variant as a follow-up only if a consumer needs forgery-proof tables.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_5 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T02:19Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:2x DoD 'run accepts only certified automata': the raw dfa.spi run is RENAMED run_unchecked (unstaged), so every bypass is spelled at its call site: agreement's minimal_dfa answer, bench's 4 quotient arms and built_run (all comparing raw engines on purpose). The typed public path is run_certified (certificate.spi). 0 call sites of the old name left (git grep). Proof rides the next regex node gate.")
inl note_of_regex_automaton_typestate_6 () = Note ("REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE", 6u32, "2026-11-03T04:48Z", "main", "main 11-03 00:5x DONE for its DoD. Phase index GADT built -> minimal -> certified; table_of and the bench accept only certified automata; the raw runner is renamed run_unchecked at every call site (proven: regex src 65/68 + nullable 4/4 under pack20 = 68/68, bench exit 0); negative 'fails Unification failure' test; single-case GADT match refines the index. Forgery-proof certification (n4: compile-time certificates like xsd_certificate's error_type) is a deliberate follow-up, filed only if a consumer needs forgery-proof tables.")
inl regex_closure_certificates () = Task ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", "regex soundness certificates and invariants (legacy items 3, 12, 13, 15, 22, 23, 24, 26): closure soundness, quotient coverage and origins, class partition, canonical form on every state, Antimirov reconstruction and origin slots, forged-row tests", Story, P0, D5, 100u32, Done, "-", "regex,automata,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_regex_closure_certificates () = Planning ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", Minutes 150u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_1 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB items 3, 12, 13, 15, 22, 23, 24, 26 and the witness-forgery negatives as runtime tests (exact_rows_not_soundness_witness, raw_quotient_not_semantic_witness, antimirov_slot_shape, antimirov_support_assignment_count, forge_structural_support_bound). DOD: certificate.check_dfa proves closed, distinct, total, keys distinct, normalized and order-coherent rows, rejecting forged and swapped rows; the minimize block map is checked for coverage and origins and eager ~ minimal is proven equivalent; charset/dfa checkers prove Normal sets are normalized and classes partition [0, 0x10FFFF]; syntax.is_canonical holds on every DFA state and the x*.x* -> x* rule exists; the 2^(positions+1) closure bound is tested; Antimirov reconstruction law and a runtime injective origin assignment; ternary examples incl. tri_cyclic_nonminimal. NEXT STEP: certificate.check_dfa with one forged-row test. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: each check returns a typed verdict naming the violated property (a union per property), never bool.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_2 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T02:26Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:3x STARTED (unstaged, certificate.spi): (1) check_dfa (d) : dfa_check = SoundDfa n | Violates of dfa_violation (OpenTarget (row, col) | NotTotal row | WrongTransition (row, col) | AcceptingMismatch row | DuplicateKey (i, k)). Per row it checks accepting = nullable of the row's regex, one target per class, every target in range and equal to derive low r (Dead iff Nothing; else the same_re state), and pairwise-distinct keys; this covers 'closed, distinct, total, keys distinct' for eager DFAs. (2) check_partition (classes) = Partitions n | Gap at | InvertedClass i | ShortOfTheTop at: the classes cover 0..0x10FFFF contiguously. (3) check_normal (char_set normal) = NormalSet n | Unsorted i | Touching i | InvertedRange i. TESTS: the eager 4th-from-end DFA is SoundDfa; a flipped accepting flag -> AcceptingMismatch 0; an out-of-range target -> OpenTarget (0, 0); classes partition (Partitions 4) and a gap is Gap 48; of_ranges merges (NormalSet 1) and a forged Normal is Unsorted 1. Node gate in flight. LEFT: minimize's block-map coverage/origins, eager ~ minimal equivalence, syntax.is_canonical on every state + x*.x* -> x*, the 2^(positions+1) closure bound, Antimirov reconstruction + origin slots, ternary examples.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_3 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T02:27Z", "main", "main 11-02 22:3x PROVEN: node gate certificate.spi 11/11 (mirror sem, memo off): an_eager_dfa_passes_every_structural_check (SoundDfa), a_forged_accepting_flag_is_named (AcceptingMismatch 0), a_target_outside_the_table_is_named (OpenTarget (0, 0)), the_classes_of_a_dfa_partition_every_code_point (Partitions 4 / Gap 48), normalization_sorts_and_merges_and_a_forged_normal_set_is_named (NormalSet 1 / Unsorted 1), plus the 6 earlier rows.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_4 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T05:17Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:2x PROVEN (node mirror sem, memo off; unstaged): two more DOD points. (1) MINIMIZE BLOCK MAP: certificate.check_quotient (eager) (minimal) : quotient_check = Faithful pairs | Diverges word | Grew (n, m) | Orphan i | Uncovered i checks, in order, that the quotient has no more states than the eager DFA, every quotient state's regex is an eager state key (origins), every eager state is language-equivalent to a quotient state or to Dead (coverage), and the starts are equivalent (eager ~ minimal). Tests: fourth_from_end's eager DFA vs its minimization is Faithful 16; a quotient with its keys replaced is Orphan 0; a quotient with a flipped accepting flag is Uncovered 0. (2) CANONICAL FORM: syntax.seq gains the x*.x* -> x* rule (starred_twice: Star a followed by a or by Seq (a, _) returns the right side), and syntax.is_canonical (r) : canon = Canonical | Breaks (canon_fault, subterm) with canon_fault = SeqNotRightNested | SeqWithUnit | StarsRepeated | AltNotNormal | AndNotNormal | DoubleNot | StarOfTrivial | RepeatNotReduced. Tests: the rule (seq b b = b, seq b (seq b 0) = seq b 0); hand-built terms name their rule; every state of 5 eager DFAs (fourth_from_end, zero_runs, ends_in_zero, an intersection with a complement, a{2,4}) is canonical. GATES after the seq change: syntax 9/9, derivative 6/6, nullable 4/4, dfa 5/5, minimal 3/3, certificate 15/15, table 2/2, agreement 4/4, laws 2/2 (the 241,560 law checks still hold). LEFT: the 2^(positions+1) closure bound, Antimirov reconstruction + origin slots, ternary examples (tri_cyclic_nonminimal). 40 -> 65.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_5 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 5u32, "2026-11-03T05:39Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:4x PROVEN (node mirror sem, memo off; unstaged): minimal 4/4, certificate 16/16, partial 6/6. (1) CLOSURE BOUND: certificate.check_closure (r) : closure_check = WithinBound (n, bound) | PastBound (n, bound), bound = 2^(positions+1) with positions = Set leaves; fourth_from_end 16 <= 64, zero_runs 4 <= 32, ends_in_zero 2 <= 16, (0|1)* & ~ends_in_zero 2 <= 64. (2) ANTIMIROV RECONSTRUCTION LAW: partial.reconstruction_by (split) (r) : reconstruction = Reconstructs classes | SplitsDiffer (class low, word): for every class, the union of the split's terms and the Brzozowski derivative answer alike on every word of length <= 4, judged by language.spi's oracle (no derivatives, no partials). partials reconstructs on fourth_from_end, zero_runs, ends_in_zero (4 classes each); a forged split that drops its first term is caught. (3) TERNARY: minimal.tri_cyclic_nonminimal = (a|aa)*(b|c) has 4 derivative states (r0, (e|a).r0, r0|(e|a).r0, e) and 2 minimal ones, matching the hand derivation. LEFT: only the runtime injective origin assignment for Antimirov terms (each support term mapped to a distinct position). 65 -> 85.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_6 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 6u32, "2026-11-03T05:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:4x DEBT recorded: kit standards on regex src = 73 line-width findings (HEAD 42, so ~31 are from tonight's certificate/lazy/partial/syntax/minimal edits, mostly long test tuples). regex does not enforce line-width yet; rewrap tonight's lines (each file re-gated) before regex adopts the html-style standards gate.")
inl note_of_regex_closure_certificates_7 () = Note ("REGEX-CLOSURE-CERTIFICATES", 7u32, "2026-11-03T12:00Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:0x DONE. Vultr gate (idle machine, pack24, memo off, one Cells run): syntax 9/9, minimal 4/4, lazy 3/3, certificate 16/16, partial 8/8, dfa 5/5 = 45/45. The last point, ANTIMIROV ORIGIN SLOTS: partial.origins (r) : origins = Injective n | Orphaned k | OutsideFragment maps every support term to a distinct position whose continuation (conts_of: Set -> tail; Seq a b -> a with tail b.tail; Alt -> both; Star a -> a with tail Star a.tail) equals the term (same_re), greedily, over the seq/alt/star/set fragment. zero_runs Injective 3, ends_in_zero Injective 2, (a|b)*abb Injective 4 (r, bb, b, e), all derived by hand first and right on the first run; a forged term no position continues is Orphaned 1; a complement is OutsideFragment. Earlier gates for the line-width rewraps (certificate/partial/syntax/minimal/lazy) are in this 45/45 too. ALL DOD POINTS MET: check_dfa (closed, distinct, total, keys distinct, normalized rows; forged rows named), the minimize block map (origins + coverage) and eager ~ minimal (check_quotient), the classes partition and Normal sets, is_canonical on every state plus the x*.x* -> x* rule, the 2^(positions+1) closure bound, the Antimirov reconstruction law plus origin slots, and ternary examples incl. tri_cyclic_nonminimal; every check returns a typed verdict, never a bool.")
inl lib_vec_fin () = Task ("LIB-VEC-FIN", "lib typed vector/finite-index core (Peano lengths, length-indexed vectors, bounded indices, total lookup) shared by regex typed DFA cores, tibia's typed graph (TIBIA-AGENT M3) and the transformer lab's shapes", Story, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "LIB-TYPE-SHAPES", "regex,automata,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_vec_fin () = Planning ("LIB-VEC-FIN", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_1 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:25Z", "regex", "regex 07:4x From REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB item 2 (b) (legacy main.spi finite_length 75, finite_symbol_vector 78, finite_symbol_index 84; probes existential_helper_control, recursive_indexed_definition, finite_vector_rank become its unit tests) and tibia's request (ML-LABS n11, TIBIA-AGENT M3 typed_network.spi: sizes as type indices, raw/planned/frozen typestate). DOD: a lib module with type-level naturals, length-indexed vectors with no fallback arm, bounded indices with a total lookup, C/Rust/WGSL(/Gleam) arms and a generic element type; compile-time only where the index grows (GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX; the FOR-D runtime index bug); its tests are the three legacy probes; the 3-line shadowing repro (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type) run before choosing the module name; consumers: REGEX-TYPED-CORES, TIBIA-AGENT follow-up, TYPED-TRANSFORMER-LAB. NEXT STEP: read tibia's M3 draft and the legacy vec/fin code, then the naming repro. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: GADT naturals, prototypes for dimension arithmetic, existentials only for compile-time chosen sizes.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_2 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:31Z", "main", "main 11-02 07:3x CORRECTION to the absorption map's constraint (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB n1, \"items 2/20/21 must stay compile-time because of the open FOR-D bug\"): the uninhabited-payload runtime GADT bug is GADT-UNINHABITED-PAYLOAD-RUNTIME, DONE since 10-12. compiler's new standalone sample samples/gadt_uninhabited_payload_runtime PASSES today on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (4 ran, 0 disagree), and gadt_rank_matrix passes on 7 backends incl. Cpp. The runtime-index blocker that is still OPEN is GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX (P0, 45%): a let rec join point over a runtime GADT whose recursion GROWS the index (term n -> term (succ n)) hangs the compiler. So a runtime Fin/Vec index is fine as long as recursion does not grow the index; length-growing recursion (cons building a vec n -> vec (succ n) at run time) stays compile-time or on i32 until that item lands. Re-check the typed-core design against this before choosing i32 rows.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_3 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:44Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MINGLED with tibia's 11-02 groom: LIB-TYPE-SHAPES (type_arith over type literals, length-indexed static arrays sa n el with scan/tree-reduce/merge, tuple_list n el, C/Rust/WGSL/Lua arms, dim_of witness; from the ML-library nugget inventory) covers the length-indexed vector half of this item. ONE RECORD PER FACT: this item keeps only what LIB-TYPE-SHAPES lacks, the bounded index (finite_symbol_index / Fin n with a total lookup) and the three legacy probes as its tests (existential_helper_control, recursive_indexed_definition, finite_vector_rank), built ON LIB-TYPE-SHAPES' naturals. Deps now LIB-TYPE-SHAPES. The naming repro (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type) is shared.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_4 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 4u32, "2026-11-04T11:48Z", "main", "11-04 08:3x main DRAFT (drafts store spiral\\LIB-VEC-FIN\\fin_vector.spi, a new lib module; not landed). Peano naturals nat_zero/nat_succ (phantom nominals, xsd_certificate style), vector n el (VectorEnd | VectorCons), fin n (FinFirst at nat_succ n | FinNext), and item : fin n -> vector n el -> el as a TOTAL two-arm match (fin nat_zero is uninhabited, so no fallback; legacy finite_symbol_vector_lookup). Also rank, fin_value, mapped (index-preserving recursion = recursive_indexed_definition), to_list, and the existential some_vector el = SomeVector (\\? n. vector n el) with of_list (the index GROWS at run time, so it also regression-guards GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX), some_rank and some_list = existential_helper_control and finite_vector_rank. 4 tests on c/rust/lua. Names checked against lib, no collisions (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type). Bridge to sized_array (fin n -> index into sized n el) is the next step once green. Gate PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_5 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:57Z", "main", "11-04 09:2x main NODE (spiral 98e51d32, digest C80CFA10, draft placed in the mirror's lib/spiral and removed after): fin_vector.spi notebook gate 4/4 passed, 0 failed. Covered: the total two-arm lookup through all three indices; rank and fin_value; index-preserving mapped; the existential of_list (growing index at run time, no compiler hang) with some_rank/some_list round-tripping a 4-list and the empty list. FINDING: the planned bridge to sized_array does not type as-is. sized n el is indexed by TYPE LITERALS (sized 3) and fin n by Peano nominals (nat_succ ...), so fin can index sized only through a type-level literal <-> Peano conversion. Either (a) fin_vector grows a literal-indexed fin (FinLit n carrying an i32 checked once at construction against type_lit_to_lit n), or (b) type_arith gains a to_peano. (a) is smaller; it can follow the land. NEXT: land fin_vector.spi through lib_land_window (new file, no consumers).")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_6 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 6u32, "2026-11-04T12:26Z", "main", "11-04 08:2x main LANDED (box, lib_land_window two-step): lib/spiral/fin_vector.spi 0AA287AF4004 is IN LIB, unstaged; closed green, undo 20261104-081754. Node proof: document_test 22, type_probe pass, consumer compiles. Box: lib had moved (digest 45EB077C vs the proof's C62D5C26), so signatures, consumer, type_probe (4 tests typed, 0 errors) and respell drift reran on the box, with document_test taken from the proof. NEXT (drafted): sized_array's literal-indexed bounded n (bounded_of checked once, at total), gate PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_7 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 7u32, "2026-11-04T13:09Z", "main", "11-04 09:0x main LANDED #2 (box, two-step, unstaged): lib/spiral/sized_array.spi F9B2C0B3ADC4 (base BA3E5993) gains bounded n = i32, the literal-indexed bounded index: bounded_of checks once against type_lit_to_lit n and returns option, then at : bounded n -> sized n el -> el reads with NO check (bounded_value exposes it). Test: both ends in range, past-the-end and negative refused (c/rust/lua). Node proof: 14/14 notebook, document_test 22, type_probe 13 typed; box: fast checks on the moved lib, first attempt refused for a live kit notebook reader (guard), retry landed. DoD status: Peano naturals + length-indexed vector + total fin lookup + existential + three legacy probes (fin_vector) DONE; literal-indexed bounded index (sized_array) DONE; generic element type DONE; arms C/Rust/Lua DONE. LEFT: a WGSL arm for at (sized_array's gpu test pattern).")
inl note_of_lib_vec_fin_8 () = Note ("LIB-VEC-FIN", 8u32, "2026-11-04T14:43Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main LANDED #3: sized_array.spi 878BA9B92082 adds a ///> wgsl test (a_bounded_index_reads_on_the_gpu: bounded_of + at on the GPU backend). Node notebook 15/15 (a first run showed 4 unrelated reds from main's own mirror sync mid-run; the clean rerun was 15/15), node proof document_test 22 and type_probe 14 typed, box copy-only (exact lib digest). DoD MET: Peano naturals, length-indexed vectors with no fallback arm, bounded indices with a total lookup, C/Rust/Lua/WGSL arms, generic element type, the three legacy probes as tests. Item closes.")
