inl note_of_regex_spans_1 () = Note ("REGEX-SPANS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x FILED from the share re-read (contradiction (a): M3 was parked behind GATE 1). Source C §B.1 \"Semântica\", §B.2 M3. DOD: unanchored search reporting (start, end) spans; leftmost-longest first, then leftmost-first via priority derivatives (Frisch-Cardelli greedy); counts identical to rebar on every selected count/count-spans/grep benchmark; CUT: if leftmost-first needs > 2 extra weeks, publish leftmost-longest with per-engine counts like RE#. NEXT STEP: a reverse-regex function (reverse of re) and the two-pass search over the table engine. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: match semantics as a union (LeftmostLongest | LeftmostFirst) selecting a prototype instance at compile time; span as a record of two nominal byte offsets.")
inl note_of_regex_spans_2 () = Note ("REGEX-SPANS", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 9 (verbatim): 9. REGEX-REBAR (or NEW REGEX-SPANS): unanchored search (M3). A forward DFA finds the match end and a reverse DFA finds the start, as regex-automata does; count-spans and per-line grep are built on top. DoD: counts identical to rebar's. Timebox 3 weeks. Source: C §B.2 M3.")
