inl note_of_regex_rust_dialect_1 () = Note ("REGEX-RUST-DIALECT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x FILED from the share re-read (contradiction (c): BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT dropped regex-syntax HIR as Spiral-first, but no item replaced it; the XSD parser has implicit anchoring and no flags). Source C §B.2 M2. DOD: literals, classes, \\p{..}, Perl classes, {m,n}, alternation, groups (captures non-capturing), flags i s m u x, ^ $ \\A \\z, ASCII \\b parsed into the same re union; everything else refused with a typed reason; 100% of rebar's non-capture curated patterns accepted; a conformance table on the page; agreement with the regex crate on the seeded corpus for every accepted pattern. NEXT STEP: share xsd.spi's scanner pieces in a dialect-neutral lexer, then the Rust dialect grammar. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: dialect as a phantom index on the parser (xsd | rust), shared atoms, dialect-specific escapes as prototype instances.")
inl note_of_regex_rust_dialect_2 () = Note ("REGEX-RUST-DIALECT", 2u32, "2026-11-02T11:28Z", "regex", "regex 07:5x SOURCE: share re-read by subagent a7601c1fd3d1a599f, verbatim at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\REGEX-SOTA\\sota-reread-20261102.md (C = artifact cccab1fd, E = 4edd442c, N = d05f9cdd, S = 76f3f8a7). ADDITION 7 (verbatim; timebox 2 weeks): 7. NEW REGEX-RUST-DIALECT: a Rust-regex syntax front end written in Spiral (M2). This is a real gap: BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT dropped regex-syntax HIR as Spiral-first, but no item replaces it, and the XSD parser has implicit anchoring and no flags. Subset: literals, classes, \\p{..}, Perl classes, {m,n}, alternation, groups (captures treated as non-capturing), flags i s m u x, ^ $ \\A \\z, ASCII \\b. DoD: 100% of the non-capture curated patterns parse, the rest are Refused with a typed reason, and a conformance table is on the page. Timebox 2 weeks. Source: C §B.2 M2.")
