inl note_of_zeta_final_1 () = Note ("ZETA-FINAL", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:13Z", "regex", "regex 08:1x FILED. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to merge the polyglot math zeta code with the zeta mega sample into the true final zeta implementation that has at least parity with the quasi rh code and the anthropic paper from the bun dude's results\". SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a68d3a7d7a786b1d7 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\zeta-report.md; external facts (Anthropic paper, OpenAI quasi-RH release, Liu arXiv 2610.12234) come from its web search and are UNVERIFIED here: re-read the primary sources before relying on a number. STATE: (1) the mega sample apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_zeta_structural_laboratory (main.spi 7,104 lines, 474 definitions, 47 negatives, 17 backend outputs) does NO numerical zeta: it is type-level certified arithmetic (binary positive naturals with add/multiply/successor witnesses, well-founded predecessor/quotient descent, primes and prime-power runs, uniqueness of the prime-power normal form, a von Mangoldt support decision Lambda(n) != 0); 3 goals stay open (uniqueness over arbitrary factorization trees, accessibility over arbitrary strict predecessors with quotient descent, flattened quotient composition), blocked on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX. (2) polyglot lib/math/math.spi (561 lines -> math.rs 4,287 lines, over the 1k gate) uses num-complex + pyo3 0.26 + Python mpmath: Re s > 1 by a 10,000-term Dirichlet sum, otherwise a WRONG reflection formula (pi^s instead of pi^(s-1)), mirror_term returns 0 in the whole critical strip, recursion capped at 3; FALSE-PASS BUG at lines 255-266: zeta__ logs the Spiral value but returns mpmath''s, so all 12 tests test mpmath, not Spiral. (3) The Lambda(n) decision of the mega sample is the shared piece with the Anthropic paper''s explicit-formula inputs. PLACE: lib/spiral/zeta/ as a package of notebooks (test blocks in every .spi, Rust primary, Zig and C parity, hand-modeled units under 1000 generated lines), started as unstaged drafts at that path. DOD: all children Done, the bench page live, the mega sample and polyglot lib/math archived (never deleted). Absorbs ZETA-PY-RETIRE (folded into ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE).")
inl note_of_zeta_final_2 () = Note ("ZETA-FINAL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:37Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MIGRATION DONE RULE (user 11-02: \"make sure all these mega sample migrations have a definition of done so they don't spin forever again, and so we remove their code from the repo asap so we keep only latest code following the new style with test cells etc ... gotta transfer all the goodies before though, different than what regex did, only implemented a sliver then called it done\"). APPLIES TO all five: brzozowski (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB / REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION), lean_cic (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB / CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE), zeta (ZETA-TYPED-ARITH + ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE / ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE), omniledger (FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP / OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE), spiral_proves_spiral (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT + SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS / SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE). (1) A migration is DONE only when the old sample is ARCHIVED out of the repo; a new home that works (regex published, CI green) is NOT done while absorption rows remain (the regex lesson: 9 of 71 legacy items absorbed at \"publishable\"). (2) Before the archive, every absorption-map row is resolved: (a) absorbed = a passing test in the new home in CI on both OSes, citing the legacy line; (b) lib = landed with lib tests; (c) compiler = a minimal regression sample with a matrix row; (d) dropped = a reason the map states. No row is left \"partial\". (3) ANTI-SPIN: the map is written first (one item, <= 4 h), then every (a)/(b) row is worked in priority order with the row count reported on the parent each groom round (absorbed / total); a week with no row closed raises the parent to P0 for the next round; a row blocked only by a compiler bug becomes its (c) regression sample plus a compiler item, and the archive may proceed with that row recorded as blocked-in-compiler (the goodie survives as the repro, in the new style). (4) The archive step runs in the SAME groom round the last row closes (scratch-archive.ps1, hash-verified, restore command in a note, dangling check by stem, user go), and MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER swaps its canary to the new home. (5) The parent item is set Done only after the archive note exists.")
