inl note_of_zeta_typed_arith_1 () = Note ("ZETA-TYPED-ARITH", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:13Z", "regex", "regex 08:1x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a68d3a7d7a786b1d7 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\zeta-report.md; external facts (Anthropic paper, OpenAI quasi-RH release, Liu arXiv 2610.12234) come from its web search and are UNVERIFIED here: re-read the primary sources before relying on a number. DOD: every terminal of mega_zeta_structural_laboratory/all_terminals has an equivalent test block passing on Rust, Zig and C; each of the 47 negatives becomes a pinned diagnostic-expect test block (failing for the RIGHT reason, TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC) or is recorded as retired with its reason; Lambda(n) agrees with a sieve for n <= 10^6; the 3 open goals stay open with their blocker named (GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX) unless it lands. TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: GADT indices static, runtime recursion on erased index-free unions (the proven workaround); witnesses behind refusing constructors (existentials are compile-time only); prime-power certificates stay existentials; region and precision as phantom types; prototypes for the arithmetic laws (the user: mega samples are not the bar because they use no prototypes). NEXT STEP: map the 474 definitions into modules by import graph (memory package-placement-by-import-graph).")
