inl note_of_zeta_numeric_core_1 () = Note ("ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:13Z", "regex", "regex 08:1x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a68d3a7d7a786b1d7 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\zeta-report.md; external facts (Anthropic paper, OpenAI quasi-RH release, Liu arXiv 2610.12234) come from its web search and are UNVERIFIED here: re-read the primary sources before relying on a number. Absorbs ZETA-PY-RETIRE (user 10-24: finish the Spiral rewrite mixed from the zeta mega sample, then delete the py code). DOD: tests assert on the SPIRAL result (fixing the false pass); the first 100 zeros match the LMFDB/Odlyzko table (pinned CI download, never committed) to 1e-10; N(T) exact for T <= 10^4 and every zero there certified on the line by a sign change of Z(t); zeta(2), zeta(-1), trivial zeros, symmetry and reflection 2^s pi^(s-1) sin(pi s/2) Gamma(1-s) zeta(1-s) hold to 1e-12; no pyo3 or mpmath in the build (mpmath at most a one-off dev cross-check recorded in a note). TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: one scalar seam (double, double-double, interval) as a prototype; region (half-plane, critical strip) as a phantom index choosing the method at compile time; results carry their error bound as a typed value. NEXT STEP: Riemann-Siegel Z(t) with test blocks against the first 10 zeros.")
inl note_of_zeta_numeric_core_2 () = Note ("ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:35Z", "regex", "regex 10:1x CORRECTION after the user's question (11-02: \"is the polyglot mpmath scaffolding really that useless/wrong? ... wouldn't having all those logs of internal calls using py hooks be useful for fast rewrites and test generation?\"). Re-read polyglot lib/math/math.spi:195-270: it is a deliberate PORTING HARNESS, not junk. With log on, call1_ installs sys.settrace(trace_calls) around mpmath.zeta/mpmath.gamma and prints every internal call of mpmath (function name, locals with addresses masked, line numbers, caller), then zeta__ prints the mpmath result next to the Spiral z side by side (math.spi:255-266). The tests assert on mpmath's value ON PURPOSE (the oracle) while the Spiral z is shown for comparison; \"false pass\" was the wrong word: the Spiral port is simply not yet asserted. KEEP IT AS THE ORACLE AND SPEC: (1) the traces show which algorithm mpmath runs for each region of s (and its intermediate values), the fastest route to a faithful Spiral port; (2) the same harness generates golden vectors (s -> zeta(s), gamma(s), intermediate terms) for tests. PLAN CHANGE for ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE: step 1 = run the harness with log on over a pinned grid of s (critical line, strip, Re s > 1, negative reals, near zeros) in CI and save the traces + values as typed Spiral row modules or a CI artifact (no .txt/.tsv in repos); step 2 = port region by region following the traces, each test asserting the Spiral z against the oracle value with a stated tolerance; step 3 = flip the assertions from mpmath to Spiral; pyo3/mpmath leaves the BUILD only when every oracle check passes on the Spiral value, and the harness itself moves to a dev/CI-only oracle job (kept, not deleted). Two real bugs remain to fix in the port, not in the harness: the reflection factor pi^s must be pi^(s-1), and mirror_term returns 0 in the whole critical strip.")
