inl note_of_cic_app_scaffold_1 () = Note ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x User 11-02 07:46: \"file backlog items to fully rewrite the lean mega sample in spiral/apps/kernel, drawing every templating lesson from the lanes plus the typefeatureset to properly start the full bottom up implementation, now we have the lean backend to test against\". SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. STATE: spiral/apps/kernel does not exist; spiral scripts/workflow.ps1 runs only apps/spiral/build.ps1 and the root build.ps1 (lines 39-47); apps/cells/spi/ci_gate.ps1 gates only lib/spiral/*.spi, so a new app needs its own build.ps1 wired into workflow.ps1. DOD: the app builds and its Cells gate prints a spiral-tests total line in CI on ubuntu and windows. First draft: restore the archived lab kernel.spi (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261030-232045, -Only 'LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS/*': intrinsic term, existential Apply, substitute_top/beta_top context-polymorphic, gate 8/8) or record why it starts over. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_app_scaffold_2 () = Note ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:13Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:1x discoveries for the scaffold that weren't on file yet:\n(1) LEAN TEST BUDGET: Lean elaboration takes median 3.45 s, p90 10.2 s and max 23.5 s per row (LEAN-BACKEND n5). Set a raised `--timeout` on each notebook's FIRST `///-` line once it has `///> lean` tests. A later line is ignored (memory cells-test-block-structure).\n(2) LEAN IN CELLS: `///> lean` runs `lean --run` on leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0. The binary resolves from SPIRAL_LEAN, then that toolchain under ELAN_HOME / ~/.elan / scoop elan, then PATH (apps/cells/README.md:224-226). The box has scoop elan. CI needs an elan install step, and actions.lock must be regenerated if that step adds a `uses:`.\n(3) The old sample's Lean row in tests/matrix.psd1 (runtime_native) builds a main.lean that returns 0, because everything in it is staged at compile time. It proves nothing about CIC, so don't count it as Lean coverage.\n(4) NEGATIVES: use `:# name fails ETY-TermError \"...\" =` (TEST-EXPECT-DIAGNOSTIC). The diagnostic must be located in the test's own body, so a broken module can't make a negative pass. tibia/src/readiness.spi:81 is a working example.\n(5) DEP: I removed the dep on the parent LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS (fill-all-task-fields trap 1).")
inl note_of_cic_app_scaffold_3 () = Note ("CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD", 3u32, "2026-11-03T20:14Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:1x DONE (unstaged, spiral): apps/kernel/src/package.spiproj (packageDir ../../../lib) + src/syntax.spi (the first CIC-SYNTAX slice: universe level = Zero | Succ | Max | Param, term = Var (de Bruijn) | Sort | Const | App | Lam | Pi | Let, level_text / sort_text (Prop, Type, Sort (l)) / term_text, and loose_range = Lean's loose bound-variable range with is_closed; 3 rust tests) + apps/kernel/build.ps1 (cloned from regex's notebook gate: requires a 'spiral-tests total' line, prints KERNEL-OK). Wired into spiral scripts/build.ps1 (CI on both OSes), together with apps/lisp/build.ps1, which wasn't in CI either. kit standards 0. VULTR: apps/kernel/build.ps1 exit 0, spiral-tests total 3/3, KERNEL-OK. Next: CIC-SYNTAX continues (names/universe params), then CIC-SCOPE and CIC-SUBST.")
