inl note_of_cic_syntax_1 () = Note ("CIC-SYNTAX", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: rust + gleam + lean test targets agree (T1 target agreement: the kernel computes at RUN time, which the old sample never did; its runtime_native/main.lean is 32 lines returning 0). SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_syntax_2 () = Note ("CIC-SYNTAX", 2u32, "2026-11-03T20:29Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:3x FIRST SLICE to spec (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/syntax.spi): name nominal (:! name = string); level = Zero | Succ | Max | IMax | Param name; binder = Default | Implicit | StrictImplicit | InstImplicit (Lean-style printing (x : T) {x : T} ⦃x : T⦄ [x : T]); term = BVar | FVar | Sort | Const (name, levels) | App | Lam | Pi | Let; level_text, sort_text (Prop / Type / Sort (l)), term_text, loose_range (Lean's looseBVarRange) + is_closed, term_size, and structural equality through a prototype :? same_as with level and term instances (alpha-equivalence: binder names and info ignored, as Lean's Expr.eqv). 4 rust tests; kit standards 0 (formatter applied); vultr apps/kernel/build.ps1 4/4, KERNEL-OK. LEFT: hash. Progress 0 -> 80.")
inl note_of_cic_syntax_3 () = Note ("CIC-SYNTAX", 3u32, "2026-11-04T10:24Z", "main", "11-04 06:2x main DONE by its title's DoD: name nominal, level union, term union (Sort/BVar/FVar/Const/App/Lam/Pi/Let, plus Proj for structures), binder info, structural equality through the same_as prototype, size, and now a structural HASH: term_hash/level_hash, polynomial mod 1000000007 so every backend agrees, names hashed by char codes. It ignores binder names and info exactly like same_as. Test: equal-up-to-names terms hash equal; different sorts, projection indices and anagram names differ. vultr: kernel 55/55 KERNEL-OK.")
