inl note_of_cells_port_targets_8 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 8u32, "2026-11-02T23:50Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:50 x: BUILDERS PARSE phase A drafted (kit drafts spiral\\CELLS-BUILDERS-PARSE, combined with M3.3 into one job, x-cells-bm1). apps/cells/spi/builders.spi models the ///> header as types: tool (13 cases), tool_choice (SkipTool | Tool), field, flag_kind (TakesOptional | TakesOne | TakesDeps | TakesCleanup), inline (Bare | Inline), dep_version (NoVersion | AnyVersion | Version), and records dep, builder_values and builder. Errors are a result string carrying the exact ArgumentError text. Elixir's inspect is reproduced from a full code-point sweep: the <<bytes>> form for C0 except \\\\a-\\\\r and \\\\e, C1, U+FFFE/FFFF and invalid UTF-8; \\\\uXXXX for A0 34F 61C 2000-200F 2028-202E 205F-2064 2066-2069 FEFF FFF9-FFFC; named escapes; \\\\#{. Graphemes (tokenizer, short clusters, unquote slices) go through Gleam string.pop_grapheme/length/slice, matching String.graphemes. The wire is length-prefixed fields; Builders.split_spiral decodes it next to the old split. PRE-REGISTERED RULE (x-cells-bm1): builders.spi blocks 1/1 and manifest.spi 3/3; 'builders parity: F files, H headers, N texts compared (E errors), 0 differ' with F > 500, H > 50 and 100 < E < N (tracked .spi files, every ///> line alone, and a 20-tool x 54-argument grid plus extras); the M3.3 rule as registered on CELLS-MANIFEST-SOURCEMAP-SPIRAL; builders_test, crates_section_test, manifest_test and notebook_report_test 0 failures.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_9 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 9u32, "2026-11-02T23:53Z", "x", "2026-11-02 19:53 x: x-cells-pb1 base (A, unmodified tree) came back 67/68. Failing: 'a Gleam cell runs from the notebook's directory, so relative fixture paths resolve' (TargetsTest), an environment failure on the mirror that exists without any draft. RULE AMENDMENT, recorded before B's result is known (B was applied 19:40 and is still running): the pre-registered '0 failures' can't hold when the base itself fails. Pass = B's passed count equals A's (67) and B's failing set is exactly A's (that one test), and nothing else differs. That test is still not evidence for the port either way; the present/failure_trace coverage comes from the command_result, trace, empty-output and plain-text tests, plus the 1569-text parity. If B fails anything else, phase B is red.")
