inl note_of_cells_port_targets_22 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 22u32, "2026-11-03T04:36Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:36 x: TARGETS HOST LANDED (unstaged, window win-1793680554553): targets.spi 7B98288DC0CC (host union FsiHost | PythonHost | LuaHost | JavascriptHost | PowershellHost, host_of, host_name, host_file_extension, is_cl), main.spi AE2FCBD33CDF, domain.ex BBBCE6E60BB1, targets.ex 723 -> 709 (0B9585081D64; host_key's table, host_extension and cl? delegate), targets_host_parity_test.exs EA65F6E5F56A. PROOF x-cells-th1 on core 73A6CCCC548DA7DF: 'targets host parity: 29 cells, 5 hosts, 14 paths, 0 differ', Result 8 passed. targets.ex went 859 -> 709 tonight; what's left there is process running, toolchain lookup and IO.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_23 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 23u32, "2026-11-03T04:37Z", "x", "2026-11-03 00:37 x: NEXT STEPS, groomed from the tree after tonight's 8 lands. DONE in Spiral: builder output presenter, ///> parser (the builders model plus Elixir inspect), deps wire, gleam manifest and warning filter, host languages and the cl check. LEFT, by value: (1) targets.ex process running (run_program, run_status, normalize, budget, timeout_error, format_ms): typed with a run_outcome union over lib erlang_port once process exits are typed there (LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB); (2) toolchain.ex (173): env and path lookup, which waits for a typed lib env/path module, so do it with C8's mounts; (3) PascalTarget (compiler's 22:3x heads-up): add it when a distinct Pascal builder exists (today 'pascal' maps to Delphi in builders.spi); (4) builders.ex's wire decoder and dispatch/argv stay at the Elixir boundary until LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS lets Gleam records cross. Each next slice keeps tonight's pattern: phase A with a corpus parity test against the live Elixir, then an A/B phase B, every rule pre-registered, and land scripts with base hashes recorded at draft time.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_24 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 24u32, "2026-11-03T15:32Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:32 x: groom: step (1)'s blocker is now DRAFTED in lib (LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB note, erlang_port run_collect -> run_outcome Finished | TimedOut), gated in x-cells-mpath1. Once it lands, targets.ex run_program/run_status/normalize become a typed slice over run_outcome, and format_ms plus the timeout message (3 lines of pure text) ride along in the same slice rather than costing their own node run. Steps (2)-(4) still wait as listed in the last note.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_25 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 25u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:13 x: GROOM (user 11-04 00:1x via main). Active -> Planned (WIP cap). Step (1) waits on LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB's run_collect landing, which is gated in the queued node run x-cells-mpath1 (launcher ready). Resume when that lands.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_26 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 26u32, "2026-11-04T04:21Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:21 x: back to Active at 55 under the user's 11-04 00:2x rule (Active = a note within 48 h, relayed by kit). My 11-04 groom parked it under the old 12 h cap; its last real note is under 48 h old, so the parking is undone. Next step unchanged.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_27 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 27u32, "2026-11-05T10:45Z", "x", "2026-11-05 06:45 x (Cells owner): compiler's DELPHI-TO-PASCAL Cells rename LANDED (cells window, 58 passed, undo cells-20261105-064025): DelphiTarget -> PascalTarget, ForDelphi -> ForPascal, console.spi arms, targets.ex pascal_compiler/run_pascal (fpc keeps -Mdelphi), builders.ex :pascal; '///> delphi' still accepted as an alias (test). This port's targets.spi/builders.spi now carry the Pascal names.")
inl note_of_cells_port_targets_28 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-TARGETS", 28u32, "2026-11-05T13:39Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:5x x: RE-GROOM of n-next (11-03 00:37) against today's tree. (3) PascalTarget: DONE by compiler's DELPHI-TO-PASCAL Cells rename (06:40 land). (1) targets.ex process running: its dependency LIB-ERLANG-TYPED-STDLIB is Done, but a slice now would mostly move format strings. run_program, run_status and normalize decide on Elixir exception structs (ProcessError reason :not_found -> :tool_missing, TimeoutError) and on Runner.run's {:ok, %{exit_status, output}} | {:error, {:timeout, info}} maps, so the typed part would be the message texts (timed out after <budget_text>, failed (exit N), was not found [at path], could not start) while every decision stays in Elixir. Each Cells land costs a full suite run on the node. DECISION: (1) moves when the runner itself does, i.e. with C8's runner.ex port (CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS) over lib erlang_port: a run_outcome union (Ran exit output | TimedOut budget | NotFound | CouldNotStart reason) with budget as Unbounded | Within ms, decided in Spiral at the port boundary, then the messages come along. Not before. (2) toolchain.ex: unchanged, waits on a typed env/path lib module (none exists). (4) builders.ex wire/dispatch: waits on LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS (compiler, Blocked 85%). So this item's next step is the C8 runner port; progress stays 55.")
inl cic_subst () = Task ("CIC-SUBST", "kernel substitution: capture-avoiding substitution with the old sample's renaming/lifting laws (identity, composition, associativity) as tests", Story, P1, D5, 65u32, Active, "CIC-SCOPE", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_subst () = Planning ("CIC-SUBST", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cic_subst_1 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: the legacy renaming/lifting/two-cell-swap/one-binder-substitution laws as test blocks on rust, gleam, lean. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_subst_2 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 2u32, "2026-11-03T21:33Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:3x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/subst.spi, registered after scope): the renaming/lifting laws as tests, each checked over a 7-term family (bound vars inside and outside binders, free vars, App, Lam, nested implicit Pi, Let) rather than one example: (1) identity: instantiate (lift t 1) v = t; (2) composition: lift (lift t 2) 3 = lift t 5; (3) commutation: lift (t[0:=v]) 1 = (shift_from t 1 1)[0 := lift v 1]. All hold (alpha-equality via same_as). Vultr apps/kernel/build.ps1 25/25 over 8 modules, KERNEL-OK; kit standards 0. LEFT: associativity of substitution composition and the legacy sample's exact law set. Progress 0 -> 50.")
inl note_of_cic_subst_3 () = Note ("CIC-SUBST", 3u32, "2026-11-04T01:34Z", "main", "21:3x main: the substitution lemma as a law test over the 7-term family: instantiate (instantiate t u) v == instantiate (instantiate_at t 1 v) (instantiate u v), with u and v both carrying loose variables (u = (u #0), v = (w #1)), so it exercises instantiate_at's lift-by-depth and the outer instantiate's lowering. Passes; vultr kernel 47/47.")
inl cells_port_memo () = Task ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", "Cells in Spiral C6: memo.ex (642 Elixir lines) as typed Spiral. Memo keys carry phantom digests (source digest x compiler core x tool identity), so a key from a stale core or toolchain cannot type-check as a hit, and reach-based keys stay byte-equal. Oracle: memo_test, memo_deps_test and memo_tool_identity_test pass unchanged, and the old and new keys are byte-equal over every tracked .spi", Story, P1, D5, 25u32, Paused, "", "team:x,cells,cells-in-spiral,typefeatureset,beam", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_port_memo () = Planning ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_port_memo_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:19 x: added by the Cells groom. The Elixir line counts come from the live tree census at 2026-11-02 08:19 (44 .ex files, 11,380 lines in all).")
inl note_of_cells_port_memo_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", 2u32, "2026-11-02T20:17Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:17 x: C6.1 LANDED (unstaged), the FIRST ELIXIR REMOVED by CELLS-IN-SPIRAL. Memo's reach analysis (strip_line_comment, the identifier scan, block_shape for all four header regexes, the unreached-definition graph walk, and the row drop) is now apps/cells/spi/memo.spi (AAAF5ECD43DA, exported as reached_program). Memo.reached_program delegates to it; the Elixir reached_program body, unreached_definitions and reach_blocks are deleted (memo.ex 642 -> 603). PROOFS on pack17: x-cells-c6a2, the corpus PARITY ORACLE: 134 tracked .spi files (lib plus every app's spi) compared between the Elixir and Spiral reached_program, 0 differ, mix 51 passed, memo.spi blocks 4/4. x-cells-c6c1 (the switch, A/B): memo, memo_deps, notebook and document tests 63 -> 63. The parity test then retired (archive 20261102-161639): after the switch it would compare Spiral with itself. Earlier runs failed honestly first: c6a1 had listm::exists missing from core, and c6b1 used the keyword 'instance' as a record field (memory spiral-keywords-not-identifiers). LEFT in memo.ex: the package-print side (package_index, shaped_blocks/block_shape/references for package prints) and the IO (key, fetch, store, prune, stamps) for later C6 slices. Cells lib Elixir now totals 11344 lines (census was 11,380).")
inl note_of_cells_port_memo_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", 3u32, "2026-11-02T20:17Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:17 x: ORDERING for the rest of C6, read from memo.ex: the package-print side (package_prints, package_index, compiled_blocks, package_print_for, reached_package_print, reach_package_blocks, resolve_references, with_stable_ids) reads manifests (Spiral.Cells.Manifest, i.e. M3 CELLS-MANIFEST-SOURCEMAP-SPIRAL) and mount dependencies (Spiral.Cells.Mounts, i.e. C8 CELLS-PORT-RUNNER-MOUNTS) and builds the term that key/3 hashes. So it ports after M3 and C8. Its oracle changes too: keys hash an Elixir term today, so a Spiral canonical print changes every key once by design. The proof is behavioral (memo_test and memo_deps_test: an unreached edit keeps the key, a reached edit changes it), not byte-equal keys.")
inl note_of_cells_port_memo_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-MEMO", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:28 x: groom (WIP cap: Active means touched within 12 h): Active -> Paused at 25%. Not touched since yesterday, because today's node time goes to Cells-on-html, the sim-erlang slice, the iggy probe and the real-profile replay (four x jobs queued serially). RESUME CONDITION: x's node queue drains (x-events2, x-replay1, x-cells-mpath1, x-html-gleam6 done) or CELLS-HTML-PARITY lands its Cells half; its next step stays n-last (the package-print side first: package_prints, package_index, compiled_blocks).")
inl cic_reduce () = Task ("CIC-REDUCE", "kernel reduction: WHNF with beta/delta/zeta (iota with inductives), fuel as a typed refusal, step trace; shared bottom of BEND2-IN-SPIRAL", Story, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "CIC-SUBST", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
