inl note_of_cic_reduce_1 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: WHNF tests incl. let/delta/spine from the legacy sample; fuel exhaustion is a Rejected reason, never a hang. BEND2-IN-SPIRAL shares this layer (its archived nbe.spi: levels NbE + Pi/Typ + conversion). SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_2 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T20:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:0x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/reduce.spi, registered after universes): weak-head normalization by spine (head + argument list) with beta (a Lam head consumes the first argument through scope's instantiate) and zeta (a Let head unfolds its value), FUEL AS A TYPED REFUSAL (whnf_result = Whnf (term, trace) | OutOfFuel (term, trace); fuel is spent per step, so a term already in WHNF needs none) and a STEP TRACE (step = Beta | Zeta). Tests: (fun x => x) a -> Whnf (a, [Beta]); let f := id; f b -> b in 2 steps (zeta then beta); omega = (fun x => x x)(fun x => x x) -> 'out of fuel after 5' instead of looping. Vultr apps/kernel/build.ps1 13/13 (syntax 4, scope 3, universes 3, reduce 3), KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. LEFT: delta (needs the constants environment), iota (inductives). Progress 0 -> 35.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_3 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T21:27Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:2x DELTA ADDED: new apps/kernel/src/env.spi (decl = Axiom (name, type) | Def (name, type, value); find_decl, unfold) and an env parameter threaded through whnf; a Const head with a Def unfolds (step Delta name in the trace), an axiom stays in WHNF. Test: with id := fun x => x, 'id a' -> Whnf (a, [Delta id; Beta]). Universe-parameter instantiation of constants is not done yet (levels on Const are ignored). Vultr kernel 22/22 over 7 modules under pack28. Progress 35 -> 55; LEFT: iota (inductives), level instantiation.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_4 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T10:11Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main DONE by its title's DoD: WHNF with beta, delta (with universe-level instantiation, unfold_at), zeta, and iota through generated recursors (rule RHS terms, one Iota step); plus quotient lift/ind and structure projection steps (Project); fuel is a typed result (OutOfFuel); every step is traced. Lean oracle 188/188 exercises iota, quotient and projection reduction. Box kernel 54/54.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_5 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T15:03Z", "main", "11-04 11:0x main K-LIKE REDUCTION (Lean's toCtorWhenK; unstaged reduce.spi, package --check clean on a vultr scratch copy). When iota finds a major that is not a constructor and the recursor is K-like (family in Prop: k_family checks its type ends in Sort 0; exactly one rule: single_rule; the constructor has zero fields after the parameters: k_ctor), the major is replaced by the constructor applied to the recursor's parameters. That is sound only when the recursor's index arguments equal the constructor's indices under those parameters (Lean's check), done here as indices_agree: same_as, else both sides to whnf then same_as (sound, incomplete vs Lean's full defeq). Tests: kernel a_proof_of_an_equation_reduces_by_k_only_at_matching_indices (Eq.rec on a free h reduces at index zero, stays stuck at index one); oracle k_like_corpus probe (transport along an arbitrary h : K.Eq Type K.T K.T), Lean comparison pending. Vultr kernel gate PENDING (the run may have seen a mixed tree after main's mid-run sync; a red there gets rerun before it is trusted).")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_6 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T15:14Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main K-LIKE REDUCTION AGREES WITH LEAN: both oracle probes (direct index, and an index equal only after delta-unfolding K.id, which needs the whnf step in indices_agree) are accepted by the kernel and by Lean; box oracle 225/225. The vultr kernel gate earlier showed 63/64 with only the oracle pin list red (it predated the flipped K pin and saw main's mid-run sync). The kernel unit test for K (reduces at matching index, stuck at index one) still needs a clean inductive.spi run.")
inl note_of_cic_reduce_7 () = Note ("CIC-REDUCE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T15:35Z", "main", "11-04 11:3x main CLEAN VULTR KERNEL GATE: KERNEL-OK 65/65 (spiral 98e51d32 + unstaged, synced 11:15 with no sync during the run, compiler pack36 on vultr). Includes a_proof_of_an_equation_reduces_by_k_only_at_matching_indices, nested inductives, universe equivalence and the oracle pins (K probes accepted). K-like reduction is DONE: kernel test + Lean agreement (box oracle 225/225).")
inl cells_port_compiler_client () = Task ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", "Cells in Spiral C7a: compiler_client.ex (824 Elixir lines) speaks the daemon protocol through daemon.spi's landed 'request r' GADT (C4) instead of tab lines. Each call's reply type comes from its request, and the encoder/decoder pair is deleted when the Elixir caller goes. Oracle: compiler_daemon_test and warm_notebook_test pass, plus a CELLS-GATE corpus run with equal pass, fail and memo-hit counts", Story, P1, D5, 45u32, Paused, "", "team:x,cells,cells-in-spiral,typefeatureset,beam", "current", "current")
