inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:19 x: added by the Cells groom. The Elixir line counts come from the live tree census at 2026-11-02 08:19 (44 .ex files, 11,380 lines in all).")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 2u32, "2026-11-02T13:58Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:58 x: MODEL RULE (groom): linked-unit exports must be monomorphic (LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE). request r stays inside cells_model, and cells_boundary exports one concrete function per reply type or an existential. Processes use GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT's concurrency interface where it exists; otherwise otp_actor sits only in cells_boundary. The message GADT is defined once so IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE can reuse it. Oracle addition: the typefeatureset census never goes down (CELLS-TYPED-UNITS n1 baseline).")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 3u32, "2026-11-02T16:34Z", "x", "2026-11-02 12:34 x: SLICE PLAN, revised from the code. Domain exports to Elixir are string -> string with unions flattened to text, so C7a's protocol parsing can't move out through another string export (that would ADD encoded wire). Instead the client itself moves into Spiral over a typed socket boundary.\nC7a.1 (proving now on node xcells1, x-cells-c7a1): apps/cells/spi/client.spi, with one generic transact : port -> stamp -> request r -> result r client_failure. The GADT makes Hello, Status, Pool and Compile share one exchange, with the reply type fixed by the request. client_failure = Unreachable : string | Stale | WaitedOut | Lost : string, mirroring compiler_client.ex's error shapes. The test blocks run a fake daemon on a spawned BEAM process. daemon.spi's compile_of/failed_of now match the Elixir edge cases (exactly 1-2 fields after ok; a sole numeric queue after timeout; a bare 'error' is unexpected; the message after the queue keeps its tabs). Both ride in the drafts store (CELLS-IN-SPIRAL-C7A), since live Cells is shared.\nC7a.2 DONE: lib erlang_tcp.spi LANDED 12:24 (AD74CCCA5A8C; package.spiproj 9A65F56D4191). It provides the typed socket boundary (connect_local/send_line/receive_line/close/listen_local/accept, tcp_failure = Refused | TimedOut | Closed | Failed, tcp_wait = Forever | WithinMs). Proof x-lib-tcp2: closed green, document_test 22, lib_gate 3/3 executed (x-lib-tcp1 failed honestly on a pattern-syntax error, which lib_gate's new Mix-abort guard caught).\nNEXT: C7a.3 is the first Elixir deletion. Cells' BEAM side calls client.transact through a Gleam export once CELLS-TYPED-UNITS defines cells_boundary; until then the daemon process tier (C7b) is the next consumer.")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_4 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 4u32, "2026-11-02T16:47Z", "x", "2026-11-02 12:47 x: C7a.1 LANDED in live Cells (unstaged, hash-guarded, tree-write window): spi/client.spi B4D57D56DBA2 (new), spi/daemon.spi CBD50642E10E (Elixir-parity parsing), spi/package.spiproj F9E7265AE7A6 (client after daemon). PROOF x-cells-c7a2 (node xcells1, eoie path): daemon.spi 6/6 executed and passed, client.spi 4/4 (compile round trip through a spawned fake daemon, Status typed by its request, stale stamp, unreachable port), no Mix abort. x-cells-c7a1 failed first on ETY-UnionCaseAmbiguous: WithinMs exists in both daemon and erlang_tcp, so client.spi writes erlang_tcp.WithinMs. No export yet, so domain.gleam is unaffected and no Elixir test can change. NEXT: C7b's daemon process tier is the first consumer of client.transact.")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_client_5 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", 5u32, "2026-11-03T15:28Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:28 x: groom (WIP cap: Active means touched within 12 h): Active -> Paused at 45%. Not touched since yesterday, because today's node time goes to Cells-on-html, the sim-erlang slice, the iggy probe and the real-profile replay (four x jobs queued serially). RESUME CONDITION: x's node queue drains (x-events2, x-replay1, x-cells-mpath1, x-html-gleam6 done) or CELLS-HTML-PARITY lands its Cells half; its next step stays C7a.2 after the landed C7a.1 (client.spi, daemon.spi).")
inl cic_universes () = Task ("CIC-UNIVERSES", "kernel universes: level normalization, leq/eq with imax, Prop impredicativity (the legacy sample only had Sort0 : Sort1)", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "CIC-SYNTAX", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_universes () = Planning ("CIC-UNIVERSES", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cic_universes_1 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: level law tests and Lean agreement on a level corpus. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_universes_2 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T20:46Z", "main", "main 11-03 16:5x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/universes.spi, registered after scope): the semantic definition of levels: level_value under an assignment of parameters to naturals, with imax a b = 0 when b = 0 (Prop impredicativity); params_into; leq_upto / eq_upto check the relation over EVERY assignment of the levels' parameters up to a bound (a :& every_assignment/every_value group). Named 'upto' on purpose: it refutes by search but is not the complete decision procedure; Lean's normalization-based leq comes next and must agree with it on these tests. pi_level domain codomain = imax. Tests: a Pi into Prop lives in Prop for every domain (imax u 0 = 0), imax u 1 = max u 1; u <= max u v, not u+1 <= u, max u (u+1) = u+1; closed values with imax dropping to 0. Vultr apps/kernel/build.ps1 10/10 (syntax 4, scope 3, universes 3), KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. Progress 0 -> 40.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_3 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T21:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:5x DECISION PROCEDURE for the imax-free fragment: atoms_of normalizes a level to atoms (base = 0 or a parameter, plus an offset); leq_decide a b : option bool says a <= b iff every atom of a is dominated by an atom of b (same parameter with offset >= k, or a constant atom against any atom with offset >= k, since parameters are >= 0), and returns None when either side has imax (outside the complete fragment). TEST: on a 15-level family (grown from 0, 1, u, v, max u 1 by succ and max _ v) the decision agrees with the semantic leq_upto on all 225 ordered pairs. Vultr kernel 26/26 over 8 modules under pack29. LEFT: imax normalization (Lean's case split on the imax's right side), then eq via mutual leq. Progress 40 -> 60.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_4 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T22:12Z", "main", "main 11-03 18:1x IMAX DECIDED: simplify (imax a 0 = 0; imax a (succ _) = max; imax distributes over a max or a nested imax on its right), imax_param finds an imax whose right side is a bare parameter, and leq_full splits that parameter p into p := 0 and p := p+1 (sound and complete: p ranges over {0} and {q+1}); each case simplifies the imax away, then the imax-free decision applies. TEST: on a 15-level family with imax (imax u v, imax v u, imax u 0, imax (u+1) (max u v), u, grown by succ and max _ v) leq_full agrees with the semantic leq_upto on all 225 ordered pairs. Vultr kernel 27/27 over 8 modules. LEFT: eq via mutual leq in conversion (sorts currently use eq_upto), level instantiation of constants. Progress 60 -> 80.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_5 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T13:40Z", "main", "11-04 09:4x main GAP FOUND AND FIXED (unstaged, conversion.spi, gate PENDING): Sort comparison already used leq_full both ways, but constants compared their universe arguments syntactically (same_constant = same_as), so @c.{max u v} and @c.{max v u} were DIFFERENT to the kernel while Lean's is_def_eq treats equivalent level arguments as equal. Now same_constant = same name and equivalent_levels (leq_full both ways per argument), used by lazy_delta's same-head path and by compare_whnf's fallback arm. Test a_constant_matches_itself_at_equivalent_universe_levels: max u v ~ max v u, imax u (v+1) ~ max u (v+1), and u vs v stays different.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_6 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T14:18Z", "main", "11-04 10:2x main VULTR kernel gate (spiral 98e51d32 + unstaged): 63/64; a_constant_matches_itself_at_equivalent_universe_levels PASSED (max u v ~ max v u, imax u (v+1) ~ max u (v+1), u vs v different), and every older conversion/typing test still passes with constants now compared up to level equivalence. The one red is nested.spi's, not this. Progress 80 -> 95; left: a Lean oracle entry once the oracle can state universe-polymorphic examples.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_7 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T14:43Z", "main", "11-04 10:5x main ORACLE ENTRIES ADDED (unstaged oracle.spi, package --check clean on vultr): a Poly entry (universe params + type + value, printed as one line \"section universe u v example : T := v end\" so each entry scopes its own universes), and universe_corpus: axioms K.Pp.{a} : Type and K.pp.{a} : K.Pp.{a}, then K.pp.{max v u} checked against K.Pp.{max u v} (equivalent levels: kernel and Lean should both accept) and K.pp.{v} against K.Pp.{u} (both refuse). Pins !+ !+ !+ !-. Lean comparison PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_cic_universes_8 () = Note ("CIC-UNIVERSES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T15:14Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main LEAN AGREES on the universe entries (box oracle 225/225): K.pp.{max v u} : K.Pp.{max u v} accepted by both, K.pp.{v} : K.Pp.{u} refused by both. Item at 100: level normalization, leq/eq with imax, Prop impredicativity, and conversion up to level equivalence, Lean-checked.")
inl cells_port_compiler_daemon () = Task ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-DAEMON", "Cells in Spiral C7b: compiler_daemon.ex (1,185), compiler_pool.ex (249), slots.ex (123), server.ex (87), memory_guard.ex (81) and file_lock.ex (65), 1,790 Elixir lines, become otp_actor processes on BEAM in Spiral. The pool and slots are typed state, and retire/idle-exit is a typed lifecycle (it absorbs CELLS-SERVER-EXIT-TAIL's end-to-end proof). The process name changes, so kit_machine_watch_model/model.spi:188 (Spiral.Cells.CompilerDaemon) is told in this slice. Oracle: compiler_daemon_test with its idle, retire-race and status tests, compiler_pool_test, slots_test, plus a CELLS-GATE corpus run with equal counts", Story, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-CLIENT", "team:x,cells,cells-in-spiral,typefeatureset,beam", "current", "current")
