inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_daemon_2 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-DAEMON", 2u32, "2026-11-02T13:58Z", "x", "2026-11-02 09:58 x: MODEL RULE (groom): linked-unit exports must be monomorphic (LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE). request r stays inside cells_model, and cells_boundary exports one concrete function per reply type or an existential. Processes use GLEAM-RUST-SPLIT's concurrency interface where it exists; otherwise otp_actor sits only in cells_boundary. The message GADT is defined once so IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE can reuse it. Oracle addition: the typefeatureset census never goes down (CELLS-TYPED-UNITS n1 baseline).")
inl note_of_cells_port_compiler_daemon_3 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-COMPILER-DAEMON", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:55Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:55 x: PORT REQUIREMENT from compiler (relayed by main 00:5x; root cause of the stale Cells daemon after a pack swap): the daemon stamped only the host SpiralCompiler.dll, but packs change only SpiralCompilerCore.dll (the host has been byte-identical, 6B30D2F5, since 11-02). So the per-request restart check passed, and even a fresh daemon reused the shadow-copy dir named from the host stamp, holding the old core. compiler's Elixir fix (unstaged in apps/cells): dll_stamp folds in the core DLL, and build_port uses it; compiler_daemon_test is 27 passed, including a core-only-swap test. The Spiral port MUST carry the same stamp (host + core DLL), and the port's parity test must include the core-only-swap case. See COMPILER-DAEMON-STALE-AFTER-PACK.")
