inl note_of_cic_conversion_1 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: defeq certificate checked independently; legacy structural defeq + conversion-constraint solver behaviours as tests. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_2 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 2u32, "2026-11-03T21:02Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:1x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/conversion.spi, registered after reduce): definitional equality as a TYPED VERDICT defeq = Same (list step) | Different string | NoFuel, where Same carries the reduction steps used as its certificate. Both sides go to WHNF (reduce), then compare_whnf recurses structurally (Lam/Pi: domain then body; App: head then argument, through a lazy 'both'), sorts compare through universes' eq_upto, and ETA in both orientations (fun x => f x ~ f, a Lam against a non-Lam via App (lift other 1, BVar 0)). Tests: (fun x => x) a ~ a is Same [Beta]; eta equal both ways; Prop vs Type is 'different: Prop vs Type'; omega vs f reports 'no fuel'. Vultr apps/kernel/build.ps1 16/16 over 5 modules, KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. LEFT: lazy delta (needs the constants environment), proof irrelevance, the certificate checker. Progress 0 -> 35.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_3 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 3u32, "2026-11-03T22:19Z", "main", "main 11-03 18:2x sorts now compare with the COMPLETE level decision (leq_full both ways, CIC-UNIVERSES n4), replacing the bounded eq_upto, so Sort u ~ Sort v is decided for all assignments, imax included. Vultr kernel 27/27. Progress 35 -> 40.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_4 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 4u32, "2026-11-04T00:53Z", "main", "20:5x main: lazy delta. defeq_with first tries syntactic equality (same_as -> Same []), then, when both sides share a constant head with equal levels, compares the arguments pairwise (args_defeq) before unfolding anything; only on disagreement does it whnf both sides (unfold_both). id (identity a) vs id a = Same [Beta] (was Delta id; Beta; Beta; Delta id; Beta). Sound by congruence, complete because disagreement falls back to unfolding. Vultr kernel 44/44.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_5 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 5u32, "2026-11-04T05:43Z", "main", "11-04 01:4x main: DEFINITIONAL PROOF IRRELEVANCE (Lean's is_def_eq_proof_irrel), placed like Lean's: after the syntactic check, before lazy delta. conversion.spi gains constant_type, a closed type inference for Const and App spines over the env (instantiate_levels on the declared type, whnf the function type to a Pi, instantiate the codomain), plus is_proposition (the type's type whnfs to Sort 0) and proof_type. Two terms whose types are the same proposition are Same. Test: p1, p2 : P : Prop compare 'same in 0'; q1, q2 : T : Type stay 'different: q1 vs q2'. The oracle corpus gains conversion entries (eta through Eq, proof irrelevance through Eq.refl, distinct Type inhabitants refused). vultr kernel 50/50 KERNEL-OK across 11 modules. The Lean side of the new entries runs on the node after the pack33 swap.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_6 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:44Z", "main", "11-04 04:3x main: Lean confirms the conversion entries (oracle 146/146): eta through Eq and definitional proof irrelevance (two proofs of one Prop equal), while two distinct Type inhabitants stay unequal.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_7 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 7u32, "2026-11-04T10:12Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: lazy delta, function eta, struct eta and definitional proof irrelevance are in; Lean agrees on every conversion entry (188/188). Left for the title's 'typed defeq certificate': Same carries the step trace today, not a checkable certificate term.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_8 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 8u32, "2026-11-04T15:23Z", "main", "11-04 11:2x main GAP vs Lean (found while planning unit-like eta): conversion has NO LOCAL CONTEXT. defeq_with env a b fuel infers types only through constant_type (Const/App/Sort), so a free variable's type is unknown. Consequences: (1) definitional proof irrelevance works for closed proofs (constants) but NOT for hypotheses, so (p q : P) -> p = q is refused while Lean accepts it; (2) Lean's unit-like eta (any two values of a one-constructor, zero-field type are defeq, e.g. x y : PUnit) cannot be expressed at all. PLAN: thread the typing context (list (string * term)) through defeq_with and its group (callers: typing's check/infer, inductive's positivity/eliminates_large uses), extend constant_type with an FVar arm via lookup, then add the unit-like rule beside proofs_or_delta. Oracle probes to add with it: (p q : P) -> K.Eq p q, and (x y : K.Unit) -> K.Eq x y (Lean accepts both). Est. 2 h with gates. Not started.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_9 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 9u32, "2026-11-04T15:28Z", "main", "11-04 11:3x main IMPLEMENTED (unstaged, package --check clean on a vultr scratch copy), more simply than the threading plan in n8: typing's check now calls defeq_with on context_env ctx env, which projects the local context into the environment as axioms named fvar:<name> (the colon cannot collide with a constant), and constant_type gained an FVar arm that reads them. Every conversion function keeps its signature. Effects: (1) proof irrelevance now covers hypotheses; (2) a new unit_or_delta step: two values whose types are the same one-constructor, zero-field, index-free family (unit_like/unit_family, reusing reduce's single_rule/axiom_of/through_params/is_pi) are equal after their types are. Tests: kernel two_hypotheses_proving_one_proposition_are_definitionally_equal; oracle probes forall (P : Prop) (p q : P), K.Eq p q, and forall (x y : K.Unit), K.Eq x y (Lean accepts both). Box Lean run and vultr kernel gate PENDING. Limitation kept: comparisons UNDER binders inside conversion still see bound variables, not fvars.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_10 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 10u32, "2026-11-04T15:55Z", "main", "11-04 11:5x main VULTR KERNEL GATE KERNEL-OK 66/66 (sync 11:3x included context_env + unit_or_delta + the new bodies_defeq: binder bodies of Lam/Pi are now compared after opening both with one fresh fvar axiom typed by the domain, so proof irrelevance and unit eta also hold under binders). First box oracle with the probes was 230/234: all 4 reds were kernel=False lean=True on the new probes, which compare under the binders of the example; that motivated bodies_defeq. Box oracle rerun PENDING. Scratch copy also has CIC-LITERALS work (NatLit), package --check clean on vultr; not yet in the live tree.")
inl note_of_cic_conversion_11 () = Note ("CIC-CONVERSION", 11u32, "2026-11-04T16:04Z", "main", "11-04 12:0x main BOX LEAN ORACLE 234/234 agree (pins green, cells 1/1) with context_env + unit_or_delta + bodies_defeq in the live tree; the 4 earlier reds (proof irrelevance and unit eta under the binders of an example) now agree. With the vultr kernel gate 66/66 on the same code, context-aware conversion is DONE: hypotheses and binder-bound variables are typed during conversion, proof irrelevance and unit-like eta hold there.")
