inl note_of_cic_typing_1 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: the 40 legacy negatives (matrix.psd1 ExpectedErrors 291-330) each mapped to a fails block or a runtime Rejected test; subject reduction checked on the corpus. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_2 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 2u32, "2026-11-03T21:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:1x FIRST SLICE (unstaged, spiral apps/kernel/src/typing.spi, registered last): infer / sort_of / check / apply_type as one :& group over a local context (list of fvar name * type). Binders open with fresh names (scope's open_with) and close with abstract_fvar. Pi : Sort (imax l1 l2); Lam : Pi of its body's type; App: the function type goes to WHNF, must be a Pi, and the argument is CHECKED by conversion (defeq), then the codomain is instantiated; Let checks its value, then unfolds. TYPED REFUSALS: refusal = UnknownVar | NotAFunction | NotAType | Mismatch | LooseBound | NoConstants | TooDeep, wrapped as inferred = Typed | Rejected. Tests: the identity on Prop : (x : Prop) -> Prop and the polymorphic identity : (A : Type) -> (a : #0) -> #1; poly_id Prop p : Prop; rejected with named refusals: 'not a function: Prop : Type', 'unknown q', 'mismatch: Type vs Prop'. Vultr apps/kernel/build.ps1 19/19 over 6 modules (syntax 4, scope 3, universes 3, reduce 3, conversion 3, typing 3), KERNEL-OK; formatter applied, kit standards 0. LEFT: the environment (constants with delta), inductives, the legacy negative families as fails blocks. Progress 0 -> 30.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_3 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 3u32, "2026-11-03T21:27Z", "main", "main 11-03 17:2x CONSTANTS: env threaded through infer/sort_of/check/apply_type (and conversion's defeq_with, so lazy unfolding comes from reduce's delta); Const takes its declared type from the environment, an unknown name is refused ('unknown constant foo'). Test: nat : Type (axiom), id p : Prop (def applied), foo refused. Vultr kernel 22/22. Progress 30 -> 40.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_4 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 4u32, "2026-11-03T22:28Z", "main", "main 11-03 18:3x UNIVERSE-POLYMORPHIC CONSTANTS: decl now carries its universe parameters (Axiom (name, params, type) | Def (name, params, type, value)); env gains instantiate_level / instantiate_levels (Param -> the use's level, through Sort and nested Const levels) and unfold_at. Typing instantiates a constant's declared type with the levels at its use and refuses a wrong count ('wrong number of universe levels for id'); reduce's delta instantiates the value. Test: id.{u} : (A : Sort u) -> A -> A used at u := 1 has type (A : Type) -> (a : #0) -> #1; 'id' with no levels is refused. Vultr kernel 28/28 over 8 modules. Progress 40 -> 50.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_5 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 5u32, "2026-11-03T23:20Z", "main", "19:1x main: declaration admission (Lean add_decl shape). typing.admit refuses a duplicate name (AlreadyDeclared), a universe Param the decl does not declare (UndeclaredLevel, via env.stray_in_decl), a type that is not a sort, and a Def whose value does not check against its type; admit_all threads the env. Vultr pack30: kernel 33/33 KERNEL-OK, kit standards 0. Next: inductive types (CIC-INDUCTIVE) need admit as their entry point.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_6 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 6u32, "2026-11-04T10:12Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: infer/check with typed refusals now cover constants, quotients, projections (incl. the Prop-structure rule) and declaration admission; Lean agrees 188/188. Left by the title: port the legacy mega sample's negative families as fails blocks plus runtime Rejected cases (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_7 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 7u32, "2026-11-05T02:15Z", "main", "11-04 22:1x main GROOM: typing now admits 18857 Lean 4.35 library declarations with 0 refusals across five replayed modules (CIC-REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES), and today's typing changes (context-aware check, opaque values checked, semantic Prop test in prop_guard) are oracle-checked 364/364. Progress 80 -> 90. Left by the title, unchanged: port the legacy mega sample's negative families as fails blocks plus runtime Rejected cases.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_8 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 8u32, "2026-11-05T04:44Z", "main", "11-05 00:44 main LEGACY NEGATIVES PORTED (the title's last piece). All 40 mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel negatives are mapped by error class. Runtime Rejected tests: argument mismatch (legacy_application_codomain, general_dependent_application_argument, dependent_cross_pair, total_substitution_domain) -> existing ill_typed_terms_are_rejected_with_a_named_refusal. NEW test the_legacy_negative_families_are_refused_at_runtime (typing.spi, unstaged) covers binder/domain not a type (dependent_pi_domain, general_pi_binder_body, general_dependent_lambda_binder_body), let value vs declared type (legacy_let_codomain), capture/loose variable (capture), dependent result mismatch (dependent_result_type, indexed_dependent_application_result, indexed_unary_constructor_application_result, programmed_dependent_application_result, programmed_endpoint_cross_codomain, recursive_codomain_application_depth) and sort mismatch through whnf/defeq (whnf_sort, atomic_defeq_sort, conversion_constraint_sort, ordinary_identity_beta_source/target_sort, unification_constraint_context): a beta-equal sort is accepted, a beta-unequal one refused. Iota cross-category (3 iota_indexed_*) -> inductive.spi recursor tests plus the replay's recursor-vs-Lean defeq check. NO KERNEL ANALOGUE, by design: 9 metavariable families (meta_*, two_meta_*, unification_assignment, membership_identity_authority, typed_meta_identity_decision); Lean's kernel has no metavariables either, they are elaborator-level. 7 \"authority\" families (*_authority, intrinsic/scalar/obstruction): proof-carrying types of the old encoding, whose content (non-defeq is not defeq) the conversion tests cover. 4+3+1+1+6+6+3+9+7 = 40. Proof: typing.spi 9/9 on vultr (run_notebook --gate). Also today: Init.Data.Array.Basic replays 6875 decls with 0 refusals (new replay test, 475 s on vultr) after the universe simplify fix (CIC-NOCONFUSION-BLOWUP).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_9 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 9u32, "2026-11-05T07:35Z", "main", "11-05 03:35 main CROSS-OS: the whole kernel (apps/kernel/src, 12 modules: conversion env export inductive lean nested reduce scope subst syntax typing universes; oracle excluded, it needs the Lean toolchain) passes 74/74 on WINDOWS (box, one run_notebook --gate holding a test-suite window, 0 failed, 0 unsupported), with tonight's universes.simplify fix, the legacy-negatives, context-exchange and beta-zeta-diamond tests; the same modules were green on Linux (vultr) earlier tonight.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_10 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 10u32, "2026-11-05T10:38Z", "main", "11-05 06:38 main WINDOWS REPLAY attempt 1 (node mirror, pack44): VOID, not red. The first cell over the 300 s default (headroom 1.25, slowest 375 s on the busy node) killed the notebook's whole process tree, so every later replay 'failed' with it, Array.Basic included despite its own header. Real data point: Init.Prelude replays on WINDOWS with 0 refusals (1837, 0, 0). FIX (unstaged apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi): ///- --timeout 1200000 on the Core, Nat, List and WF replay tests (Array keeps 1800000, Prelude the default); the notebook still round-trips canonical + fixpoint. Rerun queued on the node (job main-replay2).")
inl note_of_cic_typing_11 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 11u32, "2026-11-05T11:18Z", "main", "11-05 07:18 main WINDOWS REPLAYS (node mirror, pack44, rerun with the per-test timeouts): Init.Prelude (1837, 0, 0), Init.Core (3479, 0, 0), Init.Data.Nat.Basic (4281, 0, 0), Init.Data.List.Basic (4868, 0, 0), Init.WF (4392, 0, 0): five of six replay on WINDOWS with 0 refusals and EXACTLY the Linux declaration counts. Init.Data.Array.Basic hit its own 1800 s budget (headroom 1.0) on the loaded node (vultr: 475 s): VOID, not red; its header is now ///- --timeout 3600000 (unstaged; replay.spi still canonical). So the kernel's Lean replay is cross-OS for 18857 declarations; Array.Basic's 6875 are proven on Linux.")
inl note_of_cic_typing_12 () = Note ("CIC-TYPING", 12u32, "2026-11-05T11:55Z", "main", "11-05 07:55 main CROSS-OS COMPLETE: Init.Data.Array.Basic replays on WINDOWS (node mirror, pack44, alone, ///- --timeout 3600000): (6875, 0, 0), 1902 s, headroom 0.53. With the earlier rerun, all six Lean 4.35 modules (Prelude 1837, Core 3479, Nat.Basic 4281, List.Basic 4868, WF 4392, Array.Basic 6875 = 25732 declarations) replay through the kernel with 0 refusals on BOTH Linux and Windows, with identical counts. replay.spi carries per-test timeouts (unstaged) so a loaded machine can't turn them into VOIDs.")
