inl note_of_cic_inductives_1 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: the legacy strict-positivity certificates and verified eliminators/iota as tests; Lean agrees on every declaration of the corpus. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_2 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 2u32, "2026-11-04T00:27Z", "main", "20:3x main: first two slices. (1) inductive.spi: Inductive decl (name, level params, former type, constructors); admit_inductive refuses a former that does not end in a Sort, a constructor whose conclusion is not the family (NotConstructorOf), and a non-strictly-positive occurrence (NotPositive: the family inside a binder domain of an argument). (2) Generated recursor + iota: env gains Recursor decls (admit refuses hand-written ones: GeneratedOnly); recursor_type builds motive/minors/major over FVars closed with abstract_fvar, with an IH binder for each direct recursive argument; reduce.iota whnf's the major, picks the constructor's minor and applies args + IHs (step Iota). Nat: Nat.rec pred (succ (succ zero)) whnf = succ zero in [Iota; Beta; Beta], and the application checks against Nat. Scope limits: no inductive parameters/indices yet (recursor only for a former that is exactly Sort (Succ _)), Prop families get no recursor yet, IHs only for direct (not Pi-typed) recursive args. Vultr: kernel 37/37 across 9 modules, KERNEL-OK, kit standards 0.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_3 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 3u32, "2026-11-04T00:43Z", "main", "20:4x main: DESIGN DECISION on structure eta (deferred, not dropped). Doing it through the generated recursor (proj_i x := S.rec params (fun _ => A_i) (fun a.. => a_i) x) makes eta depend on the exact motive/minor spelling a user's projection Def unfolds to, so 'x == mk (fst x) (snd x)' would hold or fail on spelling. The sound route is Lean 4's: a Proj term former (struct name, field index, term) with its own whnf rule (Proj i (mk ps as) -> a_i) and eta in compare_whnf (t vs mk ps as when the ctor is a structure's only ctor: each a_i == Proj i t). That adds a term variant to syntax.spi and every exhaustive match (term_text, same_as, shift_from, instantiate_at, abstract_at, loose_range, instantiate_levels, stray_in_term, mentions). Slice it after indices, as its own story.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_4 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T00:53Z", "main", "20:5x main: two more slices, vultr kernel 44/44 across 10 modules. (3) Prop families get a recursor that eliminates only into Prop (no rec_u level, motive : I -> Prop); True.rec on intro iotas to the minor, and a large motive (True -> Type) is refused with 'mismatch: Type vs Prop'. (4) PARAMETERS: Inductive carries np; params_of opens the former's and every constructor's first np binders with shared FVars p0..; a constructor must conclude in exactly I p0..p(np-1) (uniformity, else NotConstructorOf); the recursor binds params, then motive : (t : I ps) -> Sort u, minors, major; Recursor decls carry np and iota skips np args on both the recursor spine and the constructor spine. List (A : Type): List.rec head-or-zero on cons Nat 1 (nil Nat) = 1 in [Iota; Beta; Beta; Beta] and checks against Nat; a ctor returning Odd Prop is refused. LEFT: indices (Eq), structure eta (Proj former, n3), Pi-typed recursive args' IHs, nested/mutual.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_5 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T01:16Z", "main", "21:0x main: INDEXED FAMILIES + Lean-style recursor rules; vultr kernel 45/45 on pack32. The former's binders after the np params are indices (indices_of opens them as FVars i0..); a constructor must conclude in I p0..p(np-1) j1..jni with index args free of I (concludes_uniformly). The motive abstracts the indices, (i : idx) -> (t : I ps i) -> Sort u; each minor ends in motive (its conclusion's index args) (c ps args); each induction hypothesis uses its recursive argument's own indices. Recursor decls now store (np, ni) and, per constructor, a closed RULE TERM (Lean's RecursorRule.rhs): fun params motive minors args => minor args (rec params motive minors idx_a a)..., built over FVars and closed with lams. Iota instantiates the rule's levels with the recursor's actual levels and substitutes [params, motive, minors] ++ the constructor's non-param args (beta_all), as one Iota step; the per-arg flags and hyps are gone. Test: Eq.{u} (A : Sort u) (a : A) : A -> Prop with refl; Eq.rec Nat zero (fun b h => True) intro zero (Eq.refl Nat zero) = intro in [Iota] and checks against True. LEFT: structure eta (n3), Pi-typed recursive args' IHs, mutual/nested, large elimination for subsingletons like Eq.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_6 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T01:34Z", "main", "21:3x main: Pi-TYPED RECURSIVE ARGUMENTS. An argument a : (xs) -> I ps js (positivity already allowed it) now gets the function hypothesis ih_a : (xs) -> motive js (a xs), and its rule term passes fun xs => rec .. js (a xs) (branches_of opens the argument's own Pi chain as a_x0..; direct arguments are the xs = [] case). Tree with node : (Nat -> Tree) -> Tree: Tree.rec (fun _ => Nat) zero (fun f ih => ih zero) (node (fun _ => leaf)) = zero in [Iota; Beta; Beta; Beta; Beta; Iota] and checks against Nat. Vultr kernel 47/47 on pack32.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_7 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:18Z", "main", "11-04 01:2x main: SUBSINGLETON ELIMINATION (Lean's rule). A Prop family eliminates into any universe if it has no constructors, or exactly one constructor whose every field is a proof (its type's sort is Prop, checked with params and earlier fields in context) or appears among the conclusion's index arguments (Eq). Otherwise Prop only. Such recursors take rec_u first, like Lean's True.rec.{u} / Eq.rec.{u, u_1}. Tests: True.rec at [Zero] and [Succ Zero]; a two-constructor Either refuses large elimination ('mismatch: Type vs Prop'); Eq.rec now takes [Zero; Succ Zero]. vultr kernel 49/49. Found by planning the Lean oracle: the kernel refused True's large elimination, which Lean accepts.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_8 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T09:35Z", "main", "11-04 05:3x main: STRUCTURES + STRUCT ETA. New term former Proj (structure, field index, value), Lean's Expr.proj, handled in every term traversal (syntax text/size/equality/loose range, scope shift/instantiate/abstract, env level instantiation and stray check, positivity mentions, oracle mutants, Lean printer as (e).k). reduce: Proj of a value whnf-ing to the structure's single constructor gives field np+i (step Project). typing: a projection's type is the ctor's i-th field type with params from the value's type and earlier fields replaced by their own projections (Lean's dependent rule); out-of-range or non-structure refuses 'not a structure projection'. env: structure_ctor / structure_of_ctor (one ctor, no indices). conversion: Proj vs Proj componentwise, and STRUCT ETA: a constructor application equals x when every field equals Proj x, tried wherever a mismatch would be reported (or_eta / eta_either). Tests: Pair.1 of mk reduces in one Project step, field types Nat, p equals mk (p.0) (p.1) 'same in 0', index 2 refused. vultr pack34 + toml lib: kernel 53/53 KERNEL-OK. Oracle on the node: 172/172 agree (K.Pair projection typing and reduction, struct eta through Lean's Eq, out-of-range refused). Not yet: mutual/nested inductives; Lean's rule restricting projections out of Prop structures to Prop fields; an explicit structure-type check in struct eta.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_9 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T10:11Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: PROP-STRUCTURE PROJECTIONS (Lean's infer_proj rule). A projection out of a value whose type is a proposition must itself be a proof: prop_guard refuses 'a proposition projects only proofs' when the structure's sort is Prop and the field's sort is not. Because a later field's type is instantiated with earlier projections, a proof whose type depends on a non-proof field (Ex's h : P w) is refused too, matching Lean, which rejected (K.e).2. My first expectation there was wrong and the oracle corrected it. And-like structures (K.Both : Prop with two True fields) project their proofs. Kernel test covers all three. Oracle on the node: 188/188 agree. Box kernel: 54/54 KERNEL-OK across 11 modules. CIC-INDUCTIVES remainder: mutual and nested inductives; a structure-type check inside struct eta.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_10 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 10u32, "2026-11-04T11:30Z", "main", "11-04 07:5x main MUTUAL INDUCTIVES landed in the unstaged kernel (admit_mutual: shared parameter front, one motive per member, group minors, cross-family positivity; admit_inductive = admit_mutual [ ind ]). VULTR kernel gate 58/58 KERNEL-OK (head 98e51d32 + unstaged), which includes a_mutual_pair_recurses_through_both_families and the new subject-reduction law test (beta, delta and iota redexes keep their type after whnf). NODE Lean oracle: the group declaration MTree/MForest is accepted by both sides, and the negative group (BTree/BForest, renamed so it no longer redeclares MTree) is refused by both with Lean's \"non positive occurrence\". 192/198: the 6 disagreements were a PRINTER bug, not kernel. A binder named \"if\" (a Lean keyword) was printed bare. Fixed: fresh_name wraps keywords as «if» and checks shadowing on the quoted form, with a lean.spi test. That rerun is PENDING on the node.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_11 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 11u32, "2026-11-04T11:45Z", "main", "11-04 08:1x main: the node oracle rerun with the printer fix is GREEN, 198/198 (n10 pending resolved). Mutual inductives are proven by the vultr kernel gate 58/58 plus Lean agreement. Kernel coverage: single, parameterized, indexed and infinitely-branching families; Prop elimination with subsingleton/large elimination; quotients; structures with projections and eta; mutual groups. Still open vs Lean: nested inductives (a family under another, e.g. List Tree) and structure-eta for Prop structures. Commit suggestion for the user when they stage: spiral apps/kernel (env, reduce, conversion, typing, syntax, scope, inductive, lean, oracle).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_12 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 12u32, "2026-11-04T14:18Z", "main", "11-04 10:2x main NESTED INDUCTIVES (unstaged nested.spi, Lean-style elimination into an auxiliary mutual group, then back-translation; recursor Tree.rec_1 as in Lean). VULTR kernel gate 63/64: admission (admitted 12, node : List Tree -> Tree), translation (Tree._aux1 and its constructors gone, Tree.rec and Tree.rec_1 present), a container negative in its parameter refused as \"not strictly positive: T._aux1.negmk\", and the unchanged non-nested path all PASS; the oracle test with the nested corpus pins also passes. The single red was MY TEST: iota through Tree.rec / Tree.rec_1 reduced correctly (both defeq checks true: 2 and 3 children counted), but I compared the inferred type's TEXT with \"Nat\" while infer returns the unreduced motive application (fun t => Nat) major. Test now asserts the inferred type is definitionally Nat; rerun PENDING on vultr. The Lean oracle run for nested (node) failed before writing its file, cause unknown; it reruns once the kernel is fully green.")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_13 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 13u32, "2026-11-04T14:35Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main NESTED INDUCTIVES GREEN on vultr: nested.spi 5/5 after the test fix (the inferred recursor type is checked definitionally equal to Nat), on top of the full kernel gate's 63 other passes. Nested families are admitted the way Lean does it: aux mutual group, back-translation, Tree.rec_1. Still to do: the Lean oracle comparison for the nested corpus (oracle test pins already pass in the kernel gate; the node Lean run needs a rerun).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_14 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 14u32, "2026-11-04T14:51Z", "main", "11-04 10:5x main LEAN AGREEMENT FOR NESTED: on the box oracle run (214/217, the 3 reds being an unrelated universe-probe mistake) every nested entry agrees with Lean. Nested inductives are DONE end to end: kernel tests 5/5 + 63 others on vultr, Lean agreement on the oracle. Open vs Lean: K-like reduction (probe added).")
inl note_of_cic_inductives_15 () = Note ("CIC-INDUCTIVES", 15u32, "2026-11-04T15:36Z", "main", "11-04 11:3x main CLEAN VULTR KERNEL GATE 65/65 KERNEL-OK covers mutual + nested inductives (nested.spi 5/5 within). With Lean agreement on every nested/mutual oracle entry, this item's scope (declarations, positivity, recursors, iota, structure eta, mutual, nested) is complete against Lean. Remaining CIC gaps live on their own items (CIC-CONVERSION context, CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY).")
inl cells_port_kino_facades () = Task ("CELLS-PORT-KINO-FACADES", "Cells in Spiral C10, the Kino/Livebook contract: smart_cell.ex (229), display.ex (250), fsi_session.ex (366) and fsi_chain.ex (276), 1,121 Elixir lines, as Gleam facades renamed at BEAM level to their Elixir.Spiral.Cells.* names (the method CELLS-CENSUS n3 proved: beam_lib abstract_code, module attribute swap, compile:forms). Calls out to Kino go through @external(erlang, \"Elixir.Kino...\", ...). Oracle: smart_cell_test, display_test, fsi_session_test and unit_first_test, plus alphabet/apps/hangul/hangul.livemd evaluating its 4 Spiral.Cells cells headless (epic DoD 3)", Story, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "CELLS-PORT-NOTEBOOK", "team:x,cells,cells-in-spiral,typefeatureset,beam", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_port_kino_facades () = Planning ("CELLS-PORT-KINO-FACADES", Minutes 360u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_port_kino_facades_1 () = Note ("CELLS-PORT-KINO-FACADES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "x", "2026-11-02 08:19 x: added by the Cells groom. The Elixir line counts come from the live tree census at 2026-11-02 08:19 (44 .ex files, 11,380 lines in all).")
inl cic_lean_oracle () = Task ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", "kernel Lean oracle (T2): print each corpus term/judgement as Lean 4 source; the kernel's typed verdict must agree with lean on a pinned corpus plus generated mutations", Story, P1, D6, 100u32, Done, "CIC-TYPING", "lean,kernel,typefeatureset,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cic_lean_oracle () = Planning ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_1 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:19Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. DOD: 100% verdict agreement (Accepted cert | Rejected reason vs lean accept/reject) on the pinned corpus and mutations generated from accepted terms (fiscal''s lesson: positives from the model, mutations expected to fail); disagreements listed as typed rows on the page. LEAN-BACKEND: 442/443 rows agree with C, elaboration median 3.45 s, lean4 v4.35.0 via elan. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_2 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 2u32, "2026-11-04T00:53Z", "main", "20:5x main: slice 1, the printer (apps/kernel/src/lean.spi). lean_term prints kernel terms as Lean 4 source: bound variables get their binder names, a shadowed name gets _1, _2..; binders keep their kind ((x : A), {x : A}, {{x : A}}, [x : A]); Sort 0/1 print as Prop/Type, others as Sort with Lean level syntax (u+1, max u v, imax u v, numerals); constants print as @c.{levels} so Lean does not re-elaborate implicits. lean_decl prints axiom/def with .{params}; recursors are skipped (Lean generates them from the inductive). 3 tests, vultr kernel 44/44. NEXT: lean is not installed on vultr (no elan); install elan + the pinned lean4 v4.35.0 there, then emit a corpus file of decls + 'example : T := t' judgements and compare accept/reject with the kernel's verdicts.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_3 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:17Z", "main", "11-04 00:1x main CORRECTION to note 2 and the 11-03 report: Lean IS installed. Box: lean 4.35.0 via scoop elan (restored 10-30 in PROFILE-WIPE-RECOVERY). Node (laptop-ts): scoop elan lean. Only vultr lacks it (no ~/.elan; disk 94% full). The oracle does NOT need CI. NEXT: run the T2 comparison on the NODE (node-first rule), emitting decls plus example judgements from lean.spi and comparing accept/reject with the kernel.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_4 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T05:18Z", "main", "11-04 01:2x main: slice 2+3 of the ORACLE, run on the NODE (lean 4.35.0). New apps/kernel/src/oracle.spi: entry = Declare decl | Judge (ty, value) | Family inductive; the kernel's verdict per entry (admit / admit_inductive, env grown only by admitted entries) is written beside its Lean source, '-- oracle N kernel_accepts=B', into one file (set_option autoImplicit false + noncomputable section). One lean run, error line numbers map to cases. lean.spi gained lean_inductive (params printed once as binders, constructor types without them, short ctor names). First node run 16/19: the 3 misses were Lean's code generator ('K.t not supported by code generator'), not typing; noncomputable section fixed it. Corpus: 20 judgements (identity, Prop impredicativity, universe errors, let, beta in the expected type, universe-polymorphic K.id at .{1} and .{0}) plus 8 inductive entries (K.Nat recursor, iota in an expected type, K.True subsingleton elimination, K.Either refused large elimination). with_mutants adds 3 per judgement: (ty, ty), (bumped ty, v), (ty, bumped v). vultr: kernel 49/49 KERNEL-OK. Lean comparison of the full corpus is running on the node mirror.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_5 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T05:27Z", "main", "11-04 01:3x main ORACLE AGREE 94/94 on the node (lean 4.35.0, mirror main-kernel, private MIX_BUILD_PATH, cells 1/1): 28 corpus entries (20 judgements + 8 declarations/families: K.Nat recursor and iota, K.True subsingleton large elimination, K.Either refused large elimination) plus 66 generated mutants (3 per judgement). Every kernel accept/refuse matches lean's. Method: the oracle test writes %TEMP%\\kernel-lean-oracle.lean with '-- oracle N kernel_accepts=B' on each line; `lean <file>`; a line is lean-refused iff an 'error' diagnostic sits on it; compare. NEXT: (1) widen the corpus (List with a parameter, Eq/indexed, Pi-typed Tree, let/zeta, universe-polymorphic families, definitional unfolding through K.id); (2) mutants beyond bump/self (swap arguments, drop an application, wrong recursor level); (3) move the line comparison out of ad-hoc glue into Spiral (the test reads lean's output when lean is on PATH), so the oracle reruns in one call.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_6 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:44Z", "main", "11-04 04:3x main ORACLE AGREE 146/146 on the node (lean 4.35.0): the 50-entry corpus (20 core judgements; K.Nat/K.True/K.Either; K.List with a parameter, K.Eq indexed and universe-polymorphic, K.Tree with a function-typed recursive argument; eta through Eq, definitional proof irrelevance, distinct inhabitants refused; Lean's prelude Eq + Quot with Quot.lift typing and a lift REDUCTION inside Eq.refl) plus 96 generated mutants. All of tonight's disagreements were printer or harness artifacts, never kernel verdicts, each fixed in lean.spi/oracle.spi: (1) codegen errors on axioms -> noncomputable section; (2) Lean's maxErrors 100 cut off verdicts (set_option has no effect) -> lean -DmaxErrors=100000; (3) curried ((@f a) b) lets Lean instantiate implicit binders after a -> flat spines (@f a b c); (4) an inductive's own universes in its ctor types -> stripped; (5) `axiom K.h : ... Eq` resolved to K.Eq inside namespace K -> every reference printed @_root_.<name>. Lessons in memory lean-oracle-printing. NEXT: move the line comparison from glue into Spiral (a process call to lean when it is on PATH), and widen with mutual/nested inductives and structure projections once the kernel has them.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_7 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T09:16Z", "main", "11-04 05:1x main: 155/155 with Quot.sound + Quot.ind entries (53 hand-written + 102 mutants). Kernel 52/52 on pack34 + toml lib.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_8 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T09:35Z", "main", "11-04 05:3x main: 172/172 with the structure entries (K.Pair projections, struct eta, out-of-range refusal).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_9 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 9u32, "2026-11-04T10:11Z", "main", "11-04 06:1x main: 188/188 (adds K.Ex witness/proof projections and K.Both proof projections). Agreement has held at 100% across 7 corpus extensions since the printer fixes.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_10 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 10u32, "2026-11-04T11:45Z", "main", "11-04 08:1x main NODE (spiral head 98e51d32 + unstaged, digest C80CFA10): ORACLE agree 198/198 (was 188/188 before mutual entries). lean.spi + oracle.spi notebooks 5/5, including the new keyword-binder test (fun («if» : Prop) => (fun (if_1 : Prop) => «if»)). The printer now quotes Lean keywords (fresh_name -> quoted, shadowing checked on the quoted form). The 10 entries the mutual group added all agree, with the negative group (K.BForest.bad) refused by both sides for non-positivity.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_11 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 11u32, "2026-11-04T14:51Z", "main", "11-04 10:5x main BOX run (Lean on the box; tree = 98e51d32 + unstaged incl. nested + universe entries): ORACLE agree 214/217. All NESTED entries agree with Lean (K.Neg nesting refused by both; K.NTree admitted by both; K.NTree.rec and K.NTree.rec_1 judgments and the Eq.refl count agree). The 3 disagreements were MY universe probe: Lean refuses axiom K.Pp.{a} : Type for an \"unused universe parameter\" (an elaborator policy; the kernel may stay permissive), and the other two only followed from K.Pp being undeclared. Fixed: K.Pp.{a} : Sort (a+1). Also added a K-like reduction probe (transport along an arbitrary h : K.Eq Type K.T K.T must reduce to K.v; Lean accepts by K, and the kernel pin is !- because it has no K-like rule yet). Rerun PENDING (after pack36 frees the box compiler, or on the node).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_12 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 12u32, "2026-11-04T15:14Z", "main", "11-04 11:1x main BOX (Lean on the box; installed compiler pack36; tree 98e51d32 + unstaged): ORACLE agree 225/225, and the kernel's pin test passes. New since 188: mutual groups, nested families (K.NTree in K.List, K.Neg refusal, K.NTree.rec_1), universe-polymorphic examples (constants equal up to level equivalence; an unused-universe axiom is Lean front-end policy, fixed in the corpus), and K-like reduction (transport along an arbitrary h : K.Eq Type K.T K.T, plus the same through the definition K.id, both accepted by kernel and Lean).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_13 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 13u32, "2026-11-04T16:05Z", "main", "11-04 12:0x main BOX ORACLE 234/234 (was 225/225 at 11:0x): +K.Unit family, proof irrelevance between hypotheses, unit-like eta, each with mutants. Next corpus growth: literals (CIC-LITERALS, scratch run pending).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_14 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 14u32, "2026-11-04T18:55Z", "main", "11-04 14:5x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 355/355 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; run on the node mirror main-kernel while kit splits TRAIN22's crates) with every kernel change the Prelude replay forced: Lean's never-zero elimination rule (families in Sort u / Sort (max ..) get recursors), structure eta in iota (struct_iota), fuel 20000, BigNat literals (3 probes around 2^64), Nat.succ <lit> read as a literal by the accelerated ops (probe Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296 = true). No regression on the earlier 339 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_15 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 15u32, "2026-11-04T21:41Z", "main", "11-04 17:4x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 364/364 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; node mirror main-kernel synced 17:34, run with --no-memo --no-html --output-dir instead of --gate because of the warm-path bug x is fixing) on the tree with decimal bignum arithmetic (big_arith/small_or_big) and the 3 new probes: Builtin Nat.sub, Nat.pow 2 64 = 18446744073709551616, Nat.sub 2^64 1 = 18446744073709551615. No regression on the earlier 361 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_oracle_16 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-ORACLE", 16u32, "2026-11-05T02:15Z", "main", "11-04 22:1x main GROOM -> DONE: the DoD (kernel verdicts agree with Lean on a pinned corpus plus generated mutations) holds at 364/364 on Lean 4.35.0 (node, final kernel, mutants via with_mutants). Beyond it, Lean's own library is the oracle now: apps/kernel/replay replays Init.Prelude, Init.Core, Init.Data.Nat.Basic, Init.Data.List.Basic and Init.WF with 0 refusals (CIC-REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES). Growth continues there; CIC-BENCH (Planned) depends on this item.")
inl cells_port_clis () = Task ("CELLS-PORT-CLIS", "Cells in Spiral C11, the last Elixir: notebook_cli.ex (187), domain.ex (169, the Gleam bridge), new_project.ex (41), application.ex (15) and the 9 mix tasks (271 lines: spiral.notebook, cell_budget, targets, edit, render_cells, new, compiler_daemon, html, cells_server), 683 lines, replaced by Rust CLIs over one message GADT. Then the mix project goes. Callers switch in the same slice: apps/cells/spi lib_gate.ps1, lib_land_window.ps1, cells_land_window.ps1 and node_cells_window_proof.ps1, x scripts/sim-run.ps1, and CI. Oracle: each CLI's stdout and exit equal the mix task's on the same arguments (CELLS-CENSUS n3 class d)", Story, P1, D5, 0u32, Planned, "CELLS-PORT-NOTEBOOK,CELLS-PORT-KINO-FACADES", "team:x,cells,cells-in-spiral,typefeatureset,beam", "current", "current")
