inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_1 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:20Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent add9e665535617d64 (11-02), copy at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\cic-sps-report.md. External names UNVERIFIED: confirm the current export format and whether a Lean kernel test corpus exists before filing details; downloads are a standing OK, pin the source. DOD: a pinned export replays with 0 kernel disagreements. SHARED TYPEFEATURESET RULE: the runtime term is a closed `:| ^ term` with a de Bruijn depth as a runtime u32 (no growing phantom, so no wait on GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); scope typestate is a two-value phantom (loose | closed, constant indices compile today); judgements are GADT-indexed certificates (cert has_type | cert defeq | cert whnf) with refusals as a reason union; prototypes for environment and reduction-strategy dispatch (forall prototype lists explicit, dispatch once at the boundary); existentials only for the static fixture/corpus registry; names are nominals, strings only at the Lean printer boundary. TEMPLATE: regex repo (src notebooks with `///- --package . --timeout N`, a `:# <file> static =` prelude, `///> rust`/`///> gleam`/`///> lean` pinned tests with one-line _assert_eq bodies, :~ join points for multi-use helpers, build.ps1 reading the spiral-tests total line, the Windows event-log crash reader, the 1000-line gate, cell budget 272) and kit's link: units for crate splits (not --import-types, deleted by IMPORT-TYPES-DELETE).")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_2 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 2u32, "2026-11-04T15:43Z", "main", "11-04 11:4x main READINESS: the kernel side this item needs is now in place: inductives incl. mutual and nested (CIC-INDUCTIVES Done), quotients, structures/projections, K-like reduction (CIC-REDUCE Done), universes up to equivalence (CIC-UNIVERSES Done), proof irrelevance (context-aware conversion in progress), and the Lean oracle at 225/225. The FIRST BLOCKER for replaying Init/Prelude is literals: Lean's kernel has Nat literals (Nat.lit plus the GMP-accelerated Nat.add/mul/sub/div/mod/beq/ble/land/lor/xor/shiftLeft/shiftRight/pow/gcd/log2) and String literals (String.mk of a List Char), which appear from Prelude's first screens. NEXT STEP (proposed): a CIC-LITERALS item, Nat literals as a term former with whnf to Nat.succ on demand and the accelerated ops, oracle-checked, before any export tooling. Then fetch lean4export pinned to the installed Lean (downloads standing OK) and build on the node.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_3 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 3u32, "2026-11-04T17:11Z", "main", "11-04 13:1x main SOURCE PINNED: leanprover/lean4export tag v4.35.0 matches the installed Lean 4.35.0 (box and node); master is already on v4.36.0-rc1, so pin the tag, not master. FORMAT (format_ndjson.md at that tag): \"Lean 4 export format: version 3.1.0\", NDJSON. A meta object, then hash-consed integer tables: names (str/num with \"in\"), levels (succ/max/imax/param with \"il\"), expressions with \"ie\" (bvar, sort, const{name,us}, app{fn,arg}, lam/forallE{name,type,body,binderInfo}, letE, proj, natVal, strVal, mdata, dropped by default). Then declarations: axiom, definition, opaque, theorem, quot, and inductive groups {types[InductiveVal], ctors[ConstructorVal], recs[RecursorVal]} with numParams/numIndices/numNested/all. Every expression form maps 1:1 onto the kernel's term union, now that natVal/strVal have NatLit/StrLit (CIC-LITERALS); the inductive groups map to admit_mutual / admit_nested, and recs can be checked against the kernel's own derivation. PLAN: (1) lake build lean4export@v4.35.0 on the node, export Init.Prelude only (module filter), store the .ndjson pinned by hash in the kit drafts store; (2) export.spi: an NDJSON reader into the three tables (lib json_scan) plus a decoder to term/decl; (3) replay in file order, a disagreement = a refusal Lean accepted; DoD stays: 0 disagreements on Init.Prelude. Bignum Nat literals will be needed (Prelude has USize/UInt64 bounds such as 2^64): a NatLit beyond u64 must be refused, not wrapped.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_4 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 4u32, "2026-11-04T17:15Z", "main", "11-04 13:2x main STEP 1 DONE (box, the only free machine with Lean): lean4export v4.35.0 (5a9a355, no deps) built in 106 s with lake; Init.Prelude exported in 7 s: 65406 NDJSON lines, 3811816 bytes, sha256 C0BF61671862BCCF..., stored at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY\\init-prelude-lean4.35.0.ndjson (meta: exporter 3.1.0, lean 4.35.0 eb6cafb7). Line census: app 31030, ie-first exprs 12189, forallE 10374, names 7491, const 2320, def 1536, thm 161, inductive groups 126, levels 113, bvar 48, opaque 10, quot 4, axiom 3. FINDINGS for step 2: (a) the largest natVal is 18446744073709551616 = 2^64 (UInt64.size), one past u64, so NatLit needs bignums before the replay (others: 4294967296, 1114112); (b) lib json.decode (typed, options -> None) can read each line into a record of options, but `in` and `type` are reserved words and cannot be field names (probe: \"Expected: }\"), while `fn` works; renaming the keys \"in\": and \"type\": textually before decode is safe because a JSON string value is never followed by a colon. Field access is r::field.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_5 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 5u32, "2026-11-04T17:29Z", "main", "11-04 13:3x main STEP 2 GREEN on vultr: new kernel module src/export.spi (unstaged, in package.spiproj) reads lean4export NDJSON into kernel terms. Rows decode through lib json.decode into one record of options (keys in/type renamed in_/type_), names/levels/terms fill core arrays indexed by id (each row refers only to lower ids, so one pass builds the DAG with sharing), declarations become items: axiom -> Axiom, safe def/thm -> Def, partial def and opaque -> Axiom (value not checked yet), unsafe -> Skipped, inductive groups -> Group (nested if any numNested > 0), quot -> one QuotPackage. natVal beyond u64 becomes a visibly unknown constant bignum-literal:<digits>, never a wrapped value. Tests 2/2: the opening lines of the real export decode to decl Bool.true/Bool.false + an unsafe skip; natural_of keeps 2^64 apart. STEP 3 (running): apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi, a package outside the gate's src glob that replays the pinned export (staged at /tmp/init-prelude.ndjson, sha C0BF6167) through admit/admit_mutual/admit_nested/admit_quotients and tallies accepted/refused/skipped with the first 20 refusals.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_6 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 6u32, "2026-11-04T17:36Z", "main", "11-04 13:4x main FIRST FULL REPLAY of Init.Prelude (vultr, ~1837 items): 774 accepted, 1063 refused, 0 skipped. The refusals cascade from two roots seen in the first 20: (a) Pow.casesOn -> NoConstants(Pow.rec) although the Pow group was not refused, and (b) Nat.brecOn / Nat.add._f / Nat.beq._f -> NotAStructure(PProd); everything after (Nat.add, Nat.mul, Nat.pow, instHPow, noConfusion_of_Nat...) fails on those missing names. Both point at structure-like inductives (Pow, PProd, HPow: one constructor, universe-polymorphic) whose recursor is not in the environment after admission. Rerunning with a check that reports every admitted group lacking <family>.rec.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_7 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 7u32, "2026-11-04T17:42Z", "main", "11-04 13:4x main FIRST REAL KERNEL BUG FROM THE REPLAY: PUnit, Pow, PProd and HPow were admitted WITHOUT a recursor. group_recursors (inductive.spi) built one only when the family's sort was literally Sort 0 or Sort (Succ _); Sort u (PUnit), Sort (max 1 u v) (PProd), Type (max u v) exported as Sort (max (u+1) (v+1)) (Pow/HPow) fell to \"| _ => Admitted env\". Fixed with Lean's elim_only_at_universe_zero rule: never_zero l (succ; max with a never-zero side; imax with a never-zero right side) -> large elimination, otherwise the same subsingleton criteria as Prop. New kernel test a_family_in_a_universe_variable_still_gets_its_recursor (PUnit.{u} : Sort u and a Box in Sort (max 1 u)). That one gap cascaded into most of the 1063 refusals (casesOn, noConfusion, brecOn via PProd, Nat.add/mul/pow/beq...). Replay rerun PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_8 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 8u32, "2026-11-04T17:50Z", "main", "11-04 14:0x main REPLAY AFTER THE RECURSOR FIX: 1766 accepted, 71 refused, 0 skipped (was 774/1063). Two roots left: (1) BitVec.decEq._proof_1 NotAFunction: BitVec.noConfusion's type stayed BitVec.rec ... x_1 on a variable major; Lean's kernel reduces that by STRUCTURE ETA IN IOTA (to_cnstr_when_structure: a major whose type is a one-constructor, index-free, non-Prop family is read as ctor params (proj 0 x) ... (proj k x)). Implemented as struct_iota after k_iota in reduce.spi (structure_fields/ctor_fields/projections; Prop families excluded via ends_in_prop), test a_recursor_on_a_structure_variable_reduces_through_its_projections. The cascade from it: instDecidableEqBitVec, UInt8.decEq, String.decEq, Lean.Name.hasMacroScopes, extractMacroScopes... (2) _private...isValidChar_UInt32: TooDeep at fuel 1000 (decide-style proof through decLt -> Nat.ble -> HAdd/Nat.add instance chains; Lean has no fuel): fuel () raised to 20000, then Char.ofNatAux/Char.ofNat follow. Rerun PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_9 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 9u32, "2026-11-04T18:12Z", "main", "11-04 14:1x main REPLAY 3 (structure eta + fuel 20000): 1818 accepted, 19 refused. Roots: (a) isValidChar_UInt32 and two Char.utf8Size proofs TooDeep even at 20000, so something unfolds instead of computing (diagnosis added: the replay now says whether infer of the value or the final comparison ran out, with both whnf shapes); (b) UInt64.size / USize.size_eq on the 2^64 literal; (c) Quot.sound AlreadyDeclared: the kernel's quotient package declares Quot.sound itself, Lean's package is 4 primitives and Quot.sound a separate axiom. FIXES in the tree: BigNat : string term (typed Nat; decimal predecessor for unfolding, falling back to NatLit once it fits u64; Nat.beq/ble on decimals; Lean printer; export reader maps natVal > u64 to it) with 3 oracle probes (ble 1 2^64 = true, 2^64 = succ (2^64-1), beq 2^64 (2^64-1) = true refused); the replay accepts Lean's Quot.sound only when the kernel's built-in axiom has the same universe params and a syntactically equal type. Replay 4 (30 min cell budget via x's new ///- --timeout support) PENDING; box oracle with BigNat probes waits for a free Lean machine.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_10 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 10u32, "2026-11-04T18:42Z", "main", "11-04 14:4x main TOODEEP ROOT (read from Lean 4.35's Init/Prelude.lean, line 2207): Decidable is now a STRUCTURE (decide := ble n m; reflects_decide), and Nat.decLt n m = Nat.decLe (n+1) m, so `decide (55296 < UInt32.size)` reaches Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296. The kernel accelerated Nat.ble only when both arguments whnf to literal NODES; Nat.succ <lit> is a constructor application, so it fell back to unfolding Nat.ble's structural recursion over 4294967296 -> TooDeep (isValidChar_UInt32 via of_decide_eq_true rfl, Char.utf8Size proofs). Lean treats Nat.succ <lit> as lit+1 and Nat.zero as 0 for its GMP ops. FIX in reduce.spi: literal_arg/literal_view read an op argument through whnf as NatLit/BigNat, Nat.zero, or Nat.succ of such (u64 max + 1 becomes BigNat 2^64); oracle probe Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296 = true. Lean oracle on the node (free while kit splits TRAIN22's crates) and replay 5 PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_11 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 11u32, "2026-11-04T18:55Z", "main", "11-04 14:5x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 355/355 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; run on the node mirror main-kernel while kit splits TRAIN22's crates) with every kernel change the Prelude replay forced: Lean's never-zero elimination rule (families in Sort u / Sort (max ..) get recursors), structure eta in iota (struct_iota), fuel 20000, BigNat literals (3 probes around 2^64), Nat.succ <lit> read as a literal by the accelerated ops (probe Nat.ble (Nat.succ 55296) 4294967296 = true). No regression on the earlier 339 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_12 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 12u32, "2026-11-04T19:24Z", "main", "11-04 15:2x main VULTR KERNEL GATE KERNEL-OK 71/71 over 13 files (incl. export.spi's 2 tests, a_family_in_a_universe_variable_still_gets_its_recursor, a_recursor_on_a_structure_variable_reduces_through_its_projections, the oracle pins) on the tree with every replay-driven fix (never-zero recursor rule, struct_iota, fuel 20000, BigNat, Nat.succ literal view). Together with the node Lean oracle 355/355 the kernel changes are proven; what remains is the Prelude replay count itself (replay 6 on the node PENDING). Slip noted: the vultr gate launched although its load probe had timed out, adding to a loadavg of 6.7 there.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_13 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 13u32, "2026-11-04T20:08Z", "main", "11-04 16:1x main REPLAY HARNESS NOTES: (1) three full replays (vultr 19-23 min, node timed out at 30 min under TRAIN23) ended \"failed\" with no assertion line and no tally file. A new head test (first 3000 export lines -> 95 items, 0 refused, tally written, 26 s) proved the report path works, so the suspect is the TooDeep diagnostic added in replay 4 (term_text over large whnf terms, likely a Rust stack overflow the capture filters missed); it is removed now that the TooDeep root is known from Lean's source, and the full replay reruns capturing overflow/panic lines. (2) The replay writes /tmp/replay-tally.txt before asserting, and replay.spi has a ///- --timeout 1800000 header (x's directive). (3) On the node, run_notebook --gate was rejected as an unknown option at 15:0x while it worked at 14:45; passing --no-memo --no-html --output-dir directly works on both machines.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_14 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 14u32, "2026-11-04T20:54Z", "main", "11-04 16:5x main INIT.PRELUDE REPLAYS WITH 0 REFUSALS: apps/kernel/replay/replay.spi (vultr, 1.2 GB memory cap) -> (1837 accepted, 0 refused, 0 skipped) in 33 s, pinned as the test's expected tally. The last blocker was found by bisecting the export with a head test (33000 lines fine in 30 s, 37000 lines killed): USize.size = 2 ^ numBits with numBits = 64, so Nat.pow 2 64 overflowed u64, the accelerator returned None and the kernel unfolded Nat.pow/Nat.mul structurally over huge numbers, hence the 20 min runs, a 2.4 GB OOM on vultr (which also restarted x-dumps' iggy pod via the node OOM killer) and the earlier TooDeep. FIX: decimal digit-list arithmetic in reduce.spi (big_arith: add, sub, mul, pow with exponent <= 4096; small_or_big tries u64 first), results normalised back to NatLit when they fit; oracle probes Nat.pow 2 64 = 2^64 and Nat.sub 2^64 1 = 2^64-1. CAVEATS for Done: partial defs and opaques are admitted by type only (Lean also checks the opaque value), unsafe decls are absent from the export, and Lean's recursors are not yet compared with the kernel's own. Lean oracle on the bignum probes and the kernel gate PENDING.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_15 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 15u32, "2026-11-04T21:41Z", "main", "11-04 17:4x main NODE LEAN ORACLE 364/364 agree (cells 1/1, pins green; node mirror main-kernel synced 17:34, run with --no-memo --no-html --output-dir instead of --gate because of the warm-path bug x is fixing) on the tree with decimal bignum arithmetic (big_arith/small_or_big) and the 3 new probes: Builtin Nat.sub, Nat.pow 2 64 = 18446744073709551616, Nat.sub 2^64 1 = 18446744073709551615. No regression on the earlier 361 entries.")
inl note_of_cic_lean_export_replay_16 () = Note ("CIC-LEAN-EXPORT-REPLAY", 16u32, "2026-11-04T21:44Z", "main", "11-04 17:4x main DONE. Init.Prelude of Lean 4.35.0 (lean4export v4.35.0, 65406 lines, sha C0BF6167, pinned in the kit drafts store) replays through the Spiral kernel with 0 disagreements: replay/replay.spi (vultr, 29 s, memory-capped) -> (1837 accepted, 0 refused, 0 skipped), and every recursor the kernel derives is definitionally equal to Lean's exported one (checked by defeq after instantiating Lean's universe parameters with the kernel's; a syntactic compare flagged 20+ multi-universe classes only because level expressions nest differently). Same tree: kernel notebooks 71/71 on vultr (one by one via the warm daemon), node Lean oracle 364/364. Kernel fixes the replay forced today: Lean's never-zero elimination rule, structure eta in iota, Nat.succ <lit> read as a literal, decimal bignum arithmetic + BigNat literals, fuel 20000, Quot.sound matched to the built-in axiom. FOLLOW-UPS: CIC-REPLAY-OPAQUE-VALUES (opaque and partial values are admitted by type only), CIC-ENV-INDEX (lookups), and the next modules after Init.Prelude.")
