inl note_of_compiler_ci_aot_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-CI-AOT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:20 compiler: filed from the user's directive (relayed by resilience 11-02). KNOWN BLOCKERS TO MEASURE FIRST: (1) F# reflection: %A formatting (sprintf \"%A\" is used in traces and errors) and FSharp.Core printf are trim/AOT-hostile; (2) Hopac and the core's Dictionary/HashIdentity.Structural over F# records (fine) vs any runtime codegen; (3) System.Text.Json (unit graph, program 2) needs source-generated contexts under AOT. STEP 1: a local `dotnet publish -p:PublishAot=true` of tmp/compiler/host with the warnings list (IL2xxx/IL3xxx) as the census. STEP 2: fix or isolate each warning site. STEP 3: a CI job publishing win-x64 and linux-x64 artifacts, with smoke = `--backend C` on samples/hello and the matrix smoke suite run against the AOT binary. DoD: the AOT binary runs the smoke suite with identical residuals to the IL build.")
inl bend_unsafe_minimize () = Task ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", "Bend backend: emit @unsafe only where Bend 2 needs it (today every def is @unsafe: 13,236 in 300 sample outputs), then try Bend 2 proofs/laws for one generated property", Story, P2, D4, 90u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,bend,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_bend_unsafe_minimize () = Planning ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_1 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:24Z", "compiler", "11-02 08:20 compiler: filed from the user's directive (relayed by resilience 11-02: \"reduce bend's unsafe and maybe leverage its proofs/laws\"). MEASURED: codegenBend emits \"@unsafe\\ndef\" unconditionally at 16 sites (spiral_compiler.fs 17318-17701: methods, closures, if/union/while helpers, array/layout helpers, main); 300 of 300 sampled main.bend files are all-unsafe (13,236 defs). STEP 1: learn exactly what @unsafe waives in bend2 (termination? totality? IO?) from the bend2 source in the cache toolchain, then classify the 16 sites (recursive, IO, partial via IO.die, or pure). STEP 2: drop @unsafe on pure non-recursive helpers and measure accepted vs rejected over the Bend matrix list. STEP 3 (laws): one generated property, e.g. a union constructor/match round-trip, stated as a Bend 2 theorem and checked. DoD: the Bend list still agrees with C, with an @unsafe count drop reported.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_2 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:10Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:30 compiler: STEP 1 DONE (read bend2 source, cache toolchains\\bend\\bend2). @unsafe waives exactly three checks. (1) THE TERMINATION WALL (bend.ts:228-235): every live self-call must descend on a strict subterm in its own case tree; an @unsafe def's self-calls skip descent. (2) FORWARD REFERENCES (bend.ts:3829-3834): a call to a def defined BELOW is a live reference to a bodiless def and errs (infer-ref) unless the caller is @unsafe, so mutual recursion cannot bypass the wall. (3) Binder domains may form + at any kind. The verdict (main.ts:900-916) is FAIL (\"N defs rely on unsafe or foreign code\") whenever a def outside Base uses @unsafe, so today every Spiral program is an unverified book. IMPLICATION FOR codegenBend: a def can drop @unsafe only if (a) it is not in a recursive SCC of the call graph (self tail loops, which Spiral emits for while/self-tail calls, can never prove descent because their recursion is not structural), AND (b) every def it calls is emitted ABOVE it. STEP 2 PLAN: emit defs in topological order of the call graph (SCCs together) and mark @unsafe only the defs in a cyclic SCC, plus main (it calls everything) unless main is non-recursive and last. Expected: pure helpers (union/array/layout getters and putters, closures without recursion, if/match helpers) become checked; loops and recursive methods stay @unsafe. MEASURE: @unsafe count over the Bend matrix list before/after, and every Bend row still agrees with C. STEP 3 (laws) stays as filed.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_3 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T07:31Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:3x compiler GROOM (WIP cap: Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (15 h). Next: step 2, emit @unsafe only on defs that fail the termination wall or have forward refs (the 3 waived checks of step 1).")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_4 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T08:42Z", "compiler", "11-04 04:4x compiler: STEP 2 DRAFTED, node review running (job compiler-bendsafe; base pack34, private control copy). kit drafts BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE\\1-unsafe-only-in-recursive-sccs.kitdo, 1 replacement at codegenBend's final assembly. Before emitting, the defs list is reordered callee-first by Tarjan SCCs over the call graph (edges = names of other defs found in a def's body, past its two header lines), so no def calls one defined below it, which is bend2's forward-reference wall. @unsafe stays only on defs in a recursive SCC (size > 1 or self-call) and is dropped from main. If any def lacks the expected '@unsafe\\ndef name(' header, the old order and markers are kept. Measure: @unsafe count over every main.bend after each arm, plus examples Bend -Native compared with control. Risk named in advance: bend2's third waiver (binder domains with + at any kind) may reject some newly safe defs; such rows will be named.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_5 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T09:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:0x compiler: v1 MEASURED, NOT SHIPPABLE (node job compiler-bendsafe; base pack34, private control copy). @unsafe count 15,081 -> 11,524 of 17,933 defs (-24%), but native Bend fell from 414 ran / 0 build-fail to 166 ran / 248 build-fail; 0 DISAGREE among rows that run. bend2's reason (array_bool candidate output, node): SOME PROOFS FAIL, 'expected Data, observed Type' at spiral_main '+v0 : (Chan(Array<Bool>) & U32) <- spiral_array_new_a0(...)', with 'Note: +v0 can be used many times, so its type must be Data'. That is waiver (3) from step 1: Spiral arrays are channels (Chan, a Type), and a + binder on one needs @unsafe. v2 (running, job compiler-bendsafe2) also keeps @unsafe on any def whose text mentions Chan(. Expect a smaller drop and, ideally, 0 new build-fails.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_6 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T09:55Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:5x compiler: v2 MEASURED (keep @unsafe on defs mentioning Chan(): @unsafe 15,081 -> 11,938 of 17,933 (-21%); native Bend 232 ran / 182 build-fail (v1 166/248); 0 DISAGREE. Next bend2 rejection, the same rule on another type: pairs are Type, not Data ('expected Data, observed Type' at spiral_main_field1 '+p: F32 & String' and spiral_main_if1 '+v8: (((U32 & String) & (U32 & String)) & U32)'). v3 (running, job compiler-bendsafe3) also keeps @unsafe on any def mentioning a pair type ' & '. The bend2 rule, as measured: a checked (non-@unsafe) def may bind with + only Data-kind types (scalars, Bool, String alone); Chan and & pairs need @unsafe.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_7 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T10:43Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:0x compiler: v3 NODE REVIEW RED (job compiler-bendsafe3). Candidate = SCC-ordered defs, @unsafe kept only on cyclic SCCs and on defs containing Chan( or ' & ', main not @unsafe. Examples Bend: residual identical, but native 325 ran / 89 build-fail vs control 414 ran / 0; oracle DISAGREE 0. @unsafe dropped only from 15081 to 13150 of 17933 defs (-13%). Every failure is an array of heap unions or heap closures (array_union_heap_heap, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_*closure_union3_*, ...), so bend2 rejects some binder kind on the non-recursive path besides Chan and pairs: heap union or closure values bound with '+'. Not landable as is; reproducing one failing sample on the box (bend2 via bun) to read the exact checker message before widening the keep rule.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_8 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T12:03Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:0x compiler: v4 NODE REVIEW (keep @unsafe also on defs naming a 'type X is Type'): native 376 ran / 38 build-fail (v3: 89), oracle DISAGREE 0, residual-only otherwise; @unsafe 13317 of 17933 defs (control 15081, -11.7%). Every remaining failure is a closure sample (closure_apply, closure_curry, closure_depth, closure_heap, closure_return*). Box repro of closure_apply: bend2 'expected Data, observed Type' on '+v0 : ((U32) -> IO(U32)) <- IO.pure(...)': function types are Type kind too. v5 keeps @unsafe on any def that mentions a function type outside its own return arrow (header line cut at its last ') -> '); queued on the node (compiler-bendsafe5, after compiler-gleamarr). HONEST READING: the saving is shrinking (-13% in v3, -11.7% in v4, less in v5), because most generated Bend defs bind Type-kind values with '+'. If v5 is green but saves under 10%, the item's premise (most @unsafe is unneeded) is refuted; the alternative lever is emitting fewer '+' (dup) binders for Type-kind values, which is a codegen change, not an annotation filter.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_9 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 9u32, "2026-11-04T12:45Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:4x compiler: v5 GREEN (node job compiler-bendsafe5; A/B on one tree, the node's 11-03 t1101 copy, so the comparison holds): examples Bend -Native, control 414 ran / 0 build-fail, candidate 414 ran / 0 build-fail; compare: 414 differing cells, ALL residual (defs reordered callee-first, @unsafe dropped), behavior cells 0, DISAGREE 0, so exit and stdout are identical on every row. Note 'oracle agree 0' on both arms: Bend rows have no C oracle in this suite, so the evidence is unchanged behavior vs control, not agreement with C. @unsafe 15081 -> 13425 of 17933 defs (-11.0%). Keep rule as landed in the draft: cyclic SCC, or the def mentions Chan(, ' & ', a 'type X is Type' name, or a function type outside its own return arrow. READING: green and landable, but the saving is modest; most Bend defs bind Type-kind values with '+', so the bigger lever is fewer '+' (dup) binders for Type-kind values (a codegen change), filed as the next step rather than more filter rules. Pack slot: pack37 with the struct-type fixes.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_10 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 10u32, "2026-11-04T13:05Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:1x compiler: THE BIGGER LEVER WORKS (hand test on box, bend2 via bun): in closure_apply.bend (v4 output), spiral_main bound a closure with '+v0 : ((U32) -> IO(U32)) <- IO.pure(...)' and used it once; deleting only the '+' (and leaving spiral_main without @unsafe) passes bend2's checker and runs, exit 0. So a linear (single-use) binder may have a Type-kind type; only '+' (dup) binders must be Data. Next step: codegenBend emits '+' only for binders the def body uses more than once (count uses per def, as the C refc pass counts last uses), and then the keep rule can drop the Type-kind and function-type clauses for defs whose Type-kind binders are all linear. Expected: far more than v5's -11% of @unsafe.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_11 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 11u32, "2026-11-04T14:32Z", "compiler", "11-04 10:3x compiler: v6 RED (node job compiler-bendsafe6): 407 ran / 7 build-fail (closure_triple, closure_u32_flag, ebpf_nest3, ...), 0 DISAGREE, @unsafe 12821 of 17933 (v5 13425; -15% vs control). All 7 are one class (box repro with the node candidate B6120DF8): a pair-typed parameter used once, only to be destructured, '(+v4, +v5, +v6) = p', loses its '+' and bend2 then cannot infer the destructure ('expected an annotated term (cannot infer), observed _ => Bool' at Pair's Sigma). Restoring '+p' by hand makes closure_triple check and run (exit 0). v7: linearize keeps '+' on any binder that is the right-hand side of a '(...) = name' destructure; queued on the node (job compiler-bendsafe7). HONEST READING: even green, linear binders only moved @unsafe from -11% to about -15%; most @unsafe defs keep it for a + binder of Type kind that is really used twice.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_12 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 12u32, "2026-11-04T15:30Z", "compiler", "11-04 11:3x compiler: v7 GREEN (node job compiler-bendsafe7, the git-root copy): examples Bend -Native, control and candidate both 414 ran / 0 build-fail; compare 414 differing cells, all residual, behavior cells 0, DISAGREE 0. @unsafe 15081 -> 13070 of 17933 defs (-13.3%; v5 without linear binders -11.0%). Programs 1 (SCC order, keep @unsafe only for cyclic SCCs or Type-kind dup binders) + 2 (linear binders lose '+', except destructure sources) are ready for the next pack (pack38: pack37 is already staged and in review). HONEST VERDICT on the item's premise: emitting @unsafe only where bend2 needs it removes about 2000 of 15081; the other 13000 are real: recursive SCCs or values of Type kind (pairs, closures, Type-declared unions) duplicated with '+'. Closing at 90% once installed; any further cut needs Data-kind encodings of pairs/closures, which is a Bend backend design change, not a filter.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_13 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 13u32, "2026-11-04T20:36Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:3x compiler: PACK38 REVIEWED and handed to main (install after pack37; one node build, job compiler-pack38rev, control = pack37 candidate bin). Source core 75AAB501 / host 5D4516B8, bin core 15FD51D7 / host 08B00F25. Delphi -Native 430 ran, residual only, 0 behavior; Bend -Native 414 ran, residual only, plus one exit cell: c_self_tail_loop_heap timing out at 120 s (slowest Bend row, control 80 s today; BOTH arms timed out on it in the v6/v7 reviews, same candidate residual 9b61078f), a timeout boundary, not behavior; C -Native 523 ran, residual 9, 0 behavior, 0 DISAGREE everywhere.")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_14 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 14u32, "2026-11-05T00:56Z", "compiler", "11-04 20:5x compiler: PENDING INSTALL. main's pack38 install-when-clear gave up at 20:56 after 110 min: it waits for running trains as well as an idle compiler, and kit's TRAIN26 ran on the node the whole window. The box stays on pack37 (host 08B00F25 / core 5F6F6E73). pack38 (reviewed; candidate %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack38) installs first in the next run, then pack39 (reviewed; needs live = pack38). The handover commands are in main's inbox from 15:3x (pack38) and 19:2x (pack39).")
inl note_of_bend_unsafe_minimize_15 () = Note ("BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE", 15u32, "2026-11-05T03:57Z", "compiler", "11-04 23:5x compiler: INSTALLED on the BOX in pack38 (23:38, compiler's install-when-clear chain with no train wait, as kit allowed for box-only installs). Dry run: the 7 pack38 programs on today's live source reproduce candidate source core 75AAB501 / host 5D4516B8. After install: SpiralCompilerCore.dll 15FD51D755DD3120 and SpiralCompiler.dll 08B00F25C65C5283, both equal=True to the reviewed candidate; system dotnet launches it. Undo: spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack38-20261104-233851. Node and vultr ship: main's waiter (pack-chain -SkipInstall) once pack39 lands. Done under installed-is-done.")
