inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x FILED. SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". LEGACY (mega_omniledger_erp_kernel): main.spi 11,306 lines, 107 unions, 99 nominals, 624 definitions, 168 existential sites, 548 raw !!!! intrinsics, NO prototypes, NO private constructors, 42 negative packages, all_terminals 78, runtime_native 11 backends, no test blocks. Models purchase-to-payment (nine unit nominals requisition_drafted..period_closed indexing a GADT erp_op from to result: ReserveBudget, CollectApprovals, IssuePurchaseOrder, ReceivePartialGoods, MatchInvoice, NetIntercompany, SettlePayment, ClosePeriod; erp_plan chains steps through an existential middle state), branded string nominals, money currency scale, an FX route GADT with an existential middle currency, a 3-approver quorum, GAAP projections, rounding decisions, balanced journals, and an event store/durability layer (~60% of the file). FISCAL TODAY: 81 generated units (UBL ~57k lines x6, nfe_v4 34k), src/lifecycle.spi typestate issued/authorized/rejected/cancelled, signing stages in generated units, CI green on both OSes 11-02 (86 test files); countries BR, MX, CL, CR, ES, IT, GR, HU, IN, PT, PL, EU UBL (+Peppol, ZATCA, DIAN, RO CIUS, UBL-TR; MyInvois 65%, PINT 30%, SUNAT planned; CII/Factur-X/ZUGFeRD/XRechnung next). ~48% of generated lines repeat across units. CHILDREN (in order): FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP, FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX, FISCAL-ERP-MONEY, FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES, FISCAL-ERP-ADAPTERS-ALL, FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE, FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER, FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG, FISCAL-ERP-ALL-FAMILIES-PIPELINE, FISCAL-ERP-NEW-COUNTRY-DRILL, OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE. LESSONS: prototypes (the user's critique of the mega samples); runtime choice dispatches once per behaviour at the boundary, each arm calling that family's instance, never instances packed into a record of functions (on Rust that blew output from 583 to 1,549 lines); existentials only for compile-time-fixed types, a closed union plus a refusing constructor for a runtime mix of families; private/refusing constructors for every authority and witness (the sample's forgery gap); negatives as `fails` test blocks with pinned reasons, not packages (11 old negatives went stale on unbound names); recursion over runtime values on a fixed index (GADT-JOIN-POINT-GROWING-INDEX); no !!!! intrinsics or host shell calls, lib wrappers; money on lib decimal; typed verdicts; a lib runtime instead of helpers repeated per unit; Linux + Windows CI; test output under the temp path; no new compiler samples: the rewrite lives in fiscal src/, generic pieces in lib.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:38Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x MIGRATION DONE RULE (user 11-02: \"make sure all these mega sample migrations have a definition of done so they don't spin forever again, and so we remove their code from the repo asap so we keep only latest code following the new style with test cells etc ... gotta transfer all the goodies before though, different than what regex did, only implemented a sliver then called it done\"). APPLIES TO all five: brzozowski (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB / REGEX-SPIRAL-DELETION), lean_cic (CIC-MEGA-ABSORB / CIC-MEGA-ARCHIVE), zeta (ZETA-TYPED-ARITH + ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE / ZETA-MEGA-RETIRE), omniledger (FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP / OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE), spiral_proves_spiral (SPS-NOTEBOOK-SPLIT + SPS-NEGATIVES-TO-FAILS / SPS-MEGA-ARCHIVE). (1) A migration is DONE only when the old sample is ARCHIVED out of the repo; a new home that works (regex published, CI green) is NOT done while absorption rows remain (the regex lesson: 9 of 71 legacy items absorbed at \"publishable\"). (2) Before the archive, every absorption-map row is resolved: (a) absorbed = a passing test in the new home in CI on both OSes, citing the legacy line; (b) lib = landed with lib tests; (c) compiler = a minimal regression sample with a matrix row; (d) dropped = a reason the map states. No row is left \"partial\". (3) ANTI-SPIN: the map is written first (one item, <= 4 h), then every (a)/(b) row is worked in priority order with the row count reported on the parent each groom round (absorbed / total); a week with no row closed raises the parent to P0 for the next round; a row blocked only by a compiler bug becomes its (c) regression sample plus a compiler item, and the archive may proceed with that row recorded as blocked-in-compiler (the goodie survives as the repro, in the new style). (4) The archive step runs in the SAME groom round the last row closes (scratch-archive.ps1, hash-verified, restore command in a note, dangling check by stem, user go), and MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER swaps its canary to the new home. (5) The parent item is set Done only after the archive note exists.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_generic_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:42Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 10:41 deps: FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE -> FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST. The epic is the parent theme. The concrete prerequisite in this title ('new countries by a manifest row') is the typed family manifest, and the generated families it runs over exist today (81 units). Parent: FISCAL-GENERIC-PROVABLE.")
