inl note_of_fiscal_erp_absorb_map_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". DOD: every row classed (a) fiscal, (b) lib, (c) compiler regression sample or (d) drop with a reason; fsync/CAS durability goes to (d) pointing at WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB. NEXT STEP: grep the definition families listed in FISCAL-ERP-GENERIC n1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_absorb_map_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-ABSORB-MAP", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:24Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 12:24 ABSORPTION MAP of spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_omniledger_erp_kernel (main.spi 12,080 lines; 43 negative_* packages; all_terminals 77) into fiscal, in the REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB format. Landing: (a) fiscal, (b) lib, (c) compiler regression sample, (d) drop with a reason. Lines are main.spi.\nCONCEPTS (33):\nC1 P2P typestate: 9 unit-nominal states :3-11, GADT erp_op :117, erp_plan with existential middle :167 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE.\nC2 branded ids company/role/period/po/payment :13-30 -> (a) as RUNTIME nominals (:! company_id = string) in FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX/LEDGER. The sample's one-unit-nominal-per-instance (company_a, po_1001) is (d): static instances don't scale to runtime data (kit lesson: existentials are compile-time only).\nC3 money/quantity :35-36, ordered_partial_quantity :37 -> (b) lib decimal via FISCAL-ERP-MONEY.\nC4 tax_witness :62, erp_p2p_receipt_tax_authority :63 -> (a) the authority's proof (nProt, TFD UUID, SdI, KSeF no.) behind a private constructor, FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE; lifecycle.spi protocol_id is the seed.\nC5 invoice_match :65 (three-way) -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE.\nC6 mirror_entry :67, opposed_mirror_pair :69 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER (intercompany).\nC7 settlement_fx_route :92 + ratio certificate :100 (static existential middle currency) -> (b) FISCAL-ERP-MONEY.\nC8 distinct3 :102, approval_quorum :105 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE (approvals as a prototype).\nC9 gaap_projection :113 (ifrs :32 / local_gaap :33) -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER.\nC10 type-level naturals nat_zero/succ :228-229, nat_one..eight :231-238, nat_add :239, mul :247, lt :459, runtime_money_nat :283 -> (b) LIB-VEC-FIN (shared with regex's map).\nC11 fx_currency :307, typed_fx_rate :314, erp_rate_* :332-388, fx_rate_product :312 -> (b) FISCAL-ERP-MONEY (ISO 4217 union in lib).\nC12 rounding floor/half-up/half-even/safe-ceiling decisions :471-719 -> (b) lib decimal rounding as an evidence union; the per-regime choice (EN 16931 two decimals, NF-e TDec) is (a) FISCAL-ERP-MONEY.\nC13 existential_* + *_program pairs :830-837, :977-984, :1060-1067, :1135-1142, :1205-1212 -> (c) GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES (existential program shape).\nC14 debit/credit/posting/balanced journal :938-944, signed scaled :1009-1019, minor_unit_scale :1011 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER (law: journal balances, totals = BT-112/BT-110).\nC15 entity-currency ledger/statement :1110-1212 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER.\nC16 statement commands fresh/applied :1271-1274, stream positions :1294-1389 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (stream-position GADT).\nC17 payload hash, identity collision, event-store decision :1401-1476 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (duplicate/collision evidence union).\nC18 checksummed frame/log/validation :1634-1721 -> (b) LIB-DURABLE-APPEND.\nC19 raw byte stream-position decode :2075-2277 -> (d): fiscal decodes through lib xml/json, never raw bytes.\nC20 CAS writer races two/three/recursive/stale :2410-2960 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (single-writer outbox in fiscal).\nC21 durable commit phases prepared/data-synced/marker-synced :3423-3492 -> (b) LIB-DURABLE-APPEND (child of WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB).\nC22 closed history/facts/observations :3579-3860 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (proof an authority event is already in history).\nC23 proven retry request/result :3967-3982 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (idempotent resubmission with the same key: SEFAZ/SAT/SdI resend).\nC24 history enumeration/index/identity query/membership :4181-4658 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG.\nC25 p2p unit event/store/outbox + commit tree :6008-6117 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (outbox).\nC26 per-step typed decode authorities :6660-8974 -> (a) XSD-DECODE-RESULT + XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES (decode returns a typed authority, never a raw payload).\nC27 payload/outbox message sequences :9145-9149 -> (a) FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG.\nC28 reopened/recursive/external-crash/WAL recovery :9372-10674 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (crash recovery is physical durability).\nC29 fence owner/lock/takeover/stale fence :10812-10944 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (multi-writer fencing).\nC30 cross-process/multiprocess fenced commits, physical owner lineage :11020-11389 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB.\nC31 competing/atomic successor store+outbox, WAL recovery receipts :11666-12009 -> (d) WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB.\nC32 mega_runtime_fail :1 and 548 !!!! intrinsics, /bin/sh sync macros -> (d): lib wrappers only.\nC33 no prototypes, every authority/witness constructor forgeable -> (a) cross-cutting rule for every FISCAL-ERP-* item: prototypes per behaviour, private constructors for authorities.\nNEGATIVES (43), as `fails \"Unification failure\"` blocks beside the code, never negative_ packages:\n(a) 26: P2P-TYPESTATE 7 (erp_step_detached_result, unit_event_multistep_plan, reapply, p2p_two_event_wrong_final_stage, p2p_three_event_skipped_middle, p2p_commit_tree_skipped_middle, p2p_unit_commit_cross_stage); LEDGER 1 (net_intercompany_detached_mirrors); XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES 1 (event_payload_codec_cross_family: a codec of one family must not decode another's payload); EVENT-LOG 13 (p2p_three_event_wrong_version, p2p_three_event_wrong_version_sum, p2p_four_event_wrong_version, p2p_outbox_detached_message, p2p_unit_outbox_detached_message, equal_hash_collision, recorded_hash_changed_caller_collision, top_collision_wrong_identity, top_membership_wrong_identity, closed_fact_input_wrong_history, fact_derived_observation_cross_outcome, specialized_observation_wrong_history, unified_evidence_observation_wrong_history); plus 4 counted under (d) below.\n(c) 5 -> GADT-DOMAIN-STRESS-SAMPLES: four_owner_lineage_cannot_force_nat_two, three_owner_lineage_cannot_force_nat_four, two_owner_lineage_cannot_force_nat_three, physical_lineage_existential_wrong_fixed_depth, physical_selection_cannot_force_fixed_depth (type-level nat vs existential depth).\n(d) 16 -> WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (durability): direct_marker_sync, external_crash_recovery_receipt_version_mismatch, recursive_payload_outbox_version_mismatch, recursive_recovery_receipt_version_mismatch, recursive_wal_recovery_receipt_version_mismatch, competing_successor_fence_wrong_after, cross_process_fence_restart_wrong_after, multiprocess_fenced_commit_wrong_endpoint, multiprocess_fenced_physical_append_wrong_endpoint, physical_owner_payload_not_fence_scalar, recoverable_fenced_lock_receipt_owner_mismatch, three_owner_fenced_lock_receipt_fence_mismatch, three_owner_fenced_lock_receipt_stale_b_source_mismatch, recursive_takeover_program_wrong_endpoint, three_owner_physical_takeover_authority_wrong_endpoint, two_takeover_program_wrong_endpoint.\nTotal 22 (a) + 5 (c) + 16 (d) = 43.\nTERMINALS (77, not 78): (a) 42 = step terminals 20 (receive 4, close 3, net 3, reserve 3, collect 2, issue 2, match 2, settle 1) + erp_p2p flow/outbox 6 -> P2P-TYPESTATE test blocks; typed_fx event-store 16 -> EVENT-LOG tests. (b) 2 = typed_fx_determined_rounding_receipt_program, typed_usd_eur_determined_tie_rounding -> FISCAL-ERP-MONEY. (d) 33 = typed_fx durability 19 + erp_p2p durability 14 -> WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB.\nCOUNTS: concepts 33 = (a) 19 rows, (b) 6, (c) 1, (d) 8 (C2's per-instance half included). About 60% of the sample (durability, C18-C21 and C28-C31) is NOT fiscal's, as the 11-02 report estimated. Every (a)/(b)/(c) row names an existing item, which is OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE's parity gate. CORRECTION (same author, same minute): the NEGATIVES (a) header should read \"(a) 22\" (P2P-TYPESTATE 7 + LEDGER 1 + XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES 1 + EVENT-LOG 13). The phrase \"26 ... plus 4 counted under (d) below\" is wrong; the total line 22 (a) + 5 (c) + 16 (d) = 43 is right.")
