inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: :! br = () and the like; :| ^ regime_witness r; family r k indexed by regime and kind; dispatch at the boundary. DOD: an M7 (stringly dispatch) = 0 check; a negative showing a BR adapter cannot be applied to a UBL family. Deps on FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST S1.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_regime_index_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-REGIME-INDEX", 2u32, "2026-11-03T12:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 08:05 fiscal: FIRST TYPED SLICE IN THE TREE (unstaged, src/families.spi on top of the FISCAL-FAMILY-MANIFEST move): phantom regimes ':! brazil = ()', ':! europe_ubl = ()', ':! mexico = ()'; a regime witness GADT ':| regime_witness r = | Brazil :: regime_witness brazil | EuropeUbl :: regime_witness europe_ubl | Mexico :: regime_witness mexico'; a regime-indexed family ':! regime_family r = family_root' with family_root_of; brazilian_families (16: the 12 NF-e/CT-e/MDF-e roots + NF-e 4.00 + 3 events), ubl_families (6), mexican_families (1); families_of \\* r. (witness : regime_witness r) : list (regime_family r), dispatch at the boundary by GADT refinement, no strings (M7 = 0 for this slice); a Brazil-only adapter access_key_digits (_ : regime_family brazil) : i32 = 44. Tests: every_regime_lists_its_own_families (16 / 6 / 1, and every Brazilian family maps through the adapter) and the DoD NEGATIVE a_ubl_family_takes_no_brazilian_access_key fails \"Unification\". Proven on idle vultr (pack24): families and generator type-check, and the same misuse as a top-level definition fails 'ETY-TermError: Unification failure. Got: list (regime_family europe_ubl)'. The Cells run of all three families tests rides job-1793707217418 (its inbox copy was updated to 0AB7E110). Still open from the DoD: 'family r k' (the document-kind index) and registry rows dispatched at the boundary for every regime.")
