inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: ISO 4217 currency nominals; the FX route GADT (static existential middle currency); runtime rates as a closed union; rounding HalfUp | HalfEven | Floor chosen per regime (EN 16931 two decimals, NF-e TDec). DOD: generic parts in lib units/decimal; ''BRL + EUR does not type'' is a fails test.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_money_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-MONEY", 2u32, "2026-11-03T12:11Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 08:11 fiscal: MODEL DRAFTED AND TYPE-PROVEN (dep XSD-FACET-TYPES is for using money inside generated units; the model itself needs only lib decimal, so per the DoD 'generic parts in lib' it is a lib draft): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-ERP-MONEY\\lib\\spiral\\money.spi (module after decimal). ISO 4217 phantom currencies (:! brl/eur/usd/mxn = ()) with a currency witness GADT; ':! amount c = decimal::decimal' with amount_of / value_of / plus (same currency only); ':! rate a b'; the FX route GADT 'Direct :: \\* a b. rate a b -> fx_route a b | Via :: \\* a b. (exists m. rate a m * rate m b) -> fx_route a b' (static existential middle currency, packed with 'exists (r1, r2)', opened with ':= exists m. first, second = packed'); ':| rounding = HalfUp | HalfEven | Floor' applied by 'rounded' (HalfUp agrees with decimal.round_to, ties toward +inf; HalfEven ties to the even neighbour; Floor via floor_division) and 'converted mode places route amount'. Tests: amounts_add_in_one_currency_and_convert_through_a_route (10 BRL at 0.17 = 1.70 EUR; via USD 0.18 x 0.92 = 1.656 -> 1.66), each_rounding_mode_breaks_ties_its_own_way, and the DoD negative brl_plus_eur_does_not_type fails \"Unification\". PROVEN on idle vultr (pack24): --check exit 0; NEGATIVES as top-level probes both exit 5 'Unification failure': BRL + EUR, and a Via route whose legs do not meet (BRL->USD then EUR->EUR). Cells run of the 3 tests still to come (node, queued later). Regime rounding choice (EN 16931 two decimals, NF-e TDec) attaches when XSD-FACET-TYPES lands.")
