inl note_of_fiscal_erp_document_prototypes_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". DOD: instances for UBL Invoice, NF-e 4.00 and CFDI 4.0; one generic test runs over all three. Deps: XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES, XSD-FIELD-DESCRIPTORS S1, FISCAL-CANON-MODEL milestone 2.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_document_prototypes_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:41Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 12:37 inherits from FISCAL-CANON-TYPED-TERMS (Done): the GADT 'term_value d' indexed by canon.data_type (AmountValue :: decimal -> term_value amount, DateValue :: date -> term_value date, ...) lands here. Each family's instance projects statically-known fields (BT-112 is an Amount in every family), so the index is fixed at compile time. Done-when adds a negative: 'an_amount_term_does_not_take_a_date' fails Unification failure.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_document_prototypes_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 12:36 fiscal: PROTOTYPE LAYER DRAFTED AND TYPE-PROVEN ahead of the codec deps (the generated-family instances still wait on XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES\\src\\document.spi E350882B, destination fiscal/src/document.spi after lifecycle (package.spiproj AND spiral.toml). Inherited from FISCAL-CANON-TYPED-TERMS: phantom data kinds (:! amount_data = () etc.) and ':| term_value d = TextValue :: string -> term_value text_data | AmountValue :: decimal::decimal -> term_value amount_data | ...' (7 kinds), with single-arm GADT readers amount_in / text_in / code_in and data_type_of_term tying each index to canon's runtime data_type. ':== canon_document' fixes each term's kind by its field type (BT-1 identifier, BT-2 date, BT-5 code, BT-27/BT-44 text, BT-109/BT-110/BT-112 amount). ':? canon_of f : f -> canon_document'; the generic law 'totals_reconcile \\* f {canon_of}' (BT-109 + BT-110 = BT-112) is written once for every family. First instance: manual_invoice, the hand-keyed ERP invoice (a real family, not a fixture). Tests: a_manual_invoice_reconciles_its_totals, each_term_value_names_its_canon_data_type, and the negatives an_amount_term_does_not_take_a_date (fails 'Unification failure') and a_string_is_not_a_fiscal_document (fails 'Fails to satisfy: canon_of'). PROVEN on idle vultr (pack24): module and bodies exit 0; negatives exit 5 with Got term_value date_data / Expected term_value amount_data, and 'Constraint satisfaction error. Got: string. Fails to satisfy: canon_of'. LESSON: a constraint failing at a {proto}-bounded call says 'Fails to satisfy: <proto>', not lifecycle's 'does not have the prototype'. Cells run QUEUED: job-1793723783366-fiscal-document after the event-log job, PREDICTION 4/4. NEXT: the UBL Invoice, NF-e 4.00 and CFDI 4.0 instances once the codec layer lands (DoD), then one generic test over all three.")
