inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_typestate_1 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T12:25Z", "regex", "regex 08:2x SOURCE: read-only research by subagent a30fa65e0c5ec60b9 (11-02), recovered verbatim by main at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\regex\\GROOM-1102\\erp-report.md. User 11-02 07:46: \"tasks to fully rewrite the erp sample in fiscal, drawing every lesson and technique to write the generic code who tries to use all generated schemas at the same time, with more countries to come\". TYPEFEATURESET PLAN: MatchInvoice takes a document authorized for any f with {fiscal_document}; the tax witness becomes the authority''s proof (nProt, TFD UUID, SdI receipt, KSeF number) behind refusing constructors; prototypes for approvals and quorum. DOD: >= 10 negatives as fails blocks with pinned reason text.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_typestate_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T16:46Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 12:46 fiscal: DRAFTED AND TYPE-PROVEN on top of the FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES draft and lifecycle: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE\\src\\p2p.spi 3047CBF5, destination fiscal/src/p2p.spi after document. ':| private purchase s' over phantom states requested / approved / ordered / received / matched / paid (the omniledger erp_op chain without its fixed item/location/jurisdiction indices); request / approve / place_order / receive / pay; 'match_invoice \\* r f {canon_of}. (p : purchase received) (invoice : f) (authorization : lifecycle::document r lifecycle::authorized) : option (purchase matched)' = the three-way match (order amount = received amount = the invoice's BT-112 read through canon_of) with the authority's proof as lifecycle's authorized document (only lifecycle.authorize builds one; the matched purchase keeps its access key). Tests: a_purchase_flows_from_requisition_to_payment, a_three_way_mismatch_does_not_match, and the DoD's 10 negatives, each pinned: ordering_an_unapproved_requisition, approving_twice, receiving_before_ordering, matching_before_receipt, matching_an_unauthorized_invoice (document _ authorized vs document nfe issued), matching_a_cancelled_invoice (vs cancelled), matching_a_string_as_the_invoice ('Fails to satisfy: canon_of'), paying_an_unmatched_purchase, paying_twice, receiving_a_paid_purchase. PROVEN on idle vultr (pack24, fiscal src + the document draft): module and bodies exit 0; each negative alone exit 5 with exactly ONE error, the intended edge. TRAP FOUND: in '\\* f r {canon_of}.' the braces bind to the LAST variable (r), giving ETY-ForallVarConstraintError and 'nfe does not have the prototype canon_of' at every call; write the constrained variable last ('\\* r f {canon_of}.'). Cells run QUEUED: job-1793724340886-fiscal-p2p after the document job, PREDICTION 12/12. OPEN: approvals/quorum prototypes (from the TYPEFEATURESET PLAN) and the regime-specific proof constructors once DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES has its generated instances.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_p2p_typestate_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-P2P-TYPESTATE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T17:08Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:08 fiscal: THE REST OF THE OMNILEDGER P2P MOVED (OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n3 'STILL TO MOVE'): p2p.spi now 49BF7E26 (re-uploaded before its job; prediction 14/14). New state 'reserved' between requested and approved: 'reserve (purchase requested) budget_left : option (purchase reserved)' (the omniledger budget token as a budget check); 'approve (purchase reserved) approvers quorum : option (purchase approved)' (approval quorum, approvers kept on the purchase); 'receive_more' accumulates partial receipts and the three-way match uses the total. Tests: the flow test now receives 60.00 + 58.00 against a 118.00 order; budget_and_quorum_gate_a_purchase (over budget -> None, 1 of 2 approvers -> None); new negative approving_an_unreserved_requisition_does_not_type, 11 negatives in all, each exit 5 on vultr with exactly one error at its edge.")
