inl note_of_fiscal_erp_ledger_2 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER", 2u32, "2026-11-03T16:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 12:19 fiscal: CORE MODEL DRAFTED AND TYPE-PROVEN ahead of P2P (the journal needs only money): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER\\lib\\spiral\\ledger.spi 991FA763, a lib module after money. ':| side = Debit | Credit'; ':! line e p c = string * side * money::amount c' (entity, period and currency indices, the first two phantom); debit/credit; side_total over core listm::fold (it joins on a runtime list, so no EJP0040); ':! journal e p c = list (line e p c)' built only through 'balanced' (option) with a 'balances' predicate; turnover; 'intercompany revenue expense x : journal a p c * journal b p c' (from omniledger's opposed_mirror_pair: the seller's due-from and the buyer's due-to, both balanced by construction). Tests: a_journal_is_built_only_when_its_sides_balance, an_intercompany_sale_books_two_balanced_mirror_journals, and the negatives a_eur_line_does_not_join_a_brl_journal / a_buyer_journal_is_not_a_seller_journal, both 'fails Unification'. PROVEN on idle vultr (pack24): module --check clean, test bodies clean, each negative alone gives exactly 'Unification failure' (amount eur vs amount brl; journal seller july_2026 brl vs journal buyer july_2026 brl). Cells run QUEUED: job-1793722745626-fiscal-ledger after the money job, PREDICTION 4/4. STILL OPEN for Done: tax lines per regime and projections per accounting standard (need FISCAL-ERP-DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES and the regime index), and the law 'journal balances and totals equal canon BT-112/BT-110' over every family.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_ledger_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:54Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 12:54 fiscal: THE DoD LAW, DRAFTED AND TYPE-PROVEN over the drafts (lib money + ledger, fiscal document): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\fiscal\\FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER\\src\\posting.spi A9D9576D, destination fiscal/src/posting.spi after document. 'invoice_journal \\* e p c f {canon_of}. (currency : money::currency c) (doc : f) : option (ledger::journal e p c)' books receivable = BT-112 against revenue = BT-109 and tax payable = BT-110 through ledger::balanced, so 'journal balances' and 'BT-112 = BT-109 + BT-110' are the same law, written once for every {canon_of} family. Tests: a_reconciling_invoice_books_a_balanced_journal_of_its_bt_112 (turnover = BT-112) and a_brl_invoice_does_not_book_into_a_eur_journal (fails 'Unification failure'). PROVEN on idle vultr (pack24, a deps tree whose lib carries money+ledger): module and bodies exit 0; the negative exit 5 with exactly Got option (journal _ _ brl) / Expected option (journal seller july_2026 eur). Cells run QUEUED: job-1793724790640-fiscal-posting after the p2p job (places money, ledger, document, posting; restores in a finally), PREDICTION 2/2. With the generated-family instances (DOCUMENT-PROTOTYPES DoD) the same test covers UBL / NF-e / CFDI without new code.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_ledger_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER", 4u32, "2026-11-03T17:00Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:00 fiscal: PERIOD CLOSE MOVED from omniledger (erp_close / close_certificate, listed STILL TO MOVE in OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n3): ledger.spi now 6A740078 (re-uploaded to the node before its queued job started; the job's prediction is updated to 6/6). ':! open_period e p c = list (journal e p c)', ':! closed_period e p c = list (journal e p c) * decimal' (the certificate carries the period turnover), opened / post / close / period_turnover. Tests added: a_closed_period_certifies_the_turnover_of_its_journals, and a_closed_period_takes_no_more_journals (fails Unification; vultr: exactly Got closed_period seller july_2026 brl / Expected open_period seller july_2026 brl). posting.spi re-checked against the new ledger: exit 0. Accounting-standard projections (the mega sample's gaap_projection) remain open.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_ledger_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER", 5u32, "2026-11-03T17:05Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:05 fiscal: EPOCH-INDEXED SETTLEMENT FX MOVED from omniledger (settlement_fx_route source target epoch, STILL TO MOVE in OMNILEDGER-ARCHIVE n3), placed in ledger because the epoch is the ledger's period: ledger.spi now 3A96F956 (re-uploaded before its job; prediction 8/8). ':! quote a b p = money::rate a b', 'quoted', and 'revalued \\* e p a b. mode places (quote a b p) (journal e p a) : option (journal e p b)' (each line converted through money::converted with a Direct route, then re-balanced, because rounding per line can unbalance; the caller then books a rounding line). Tests: a_journal_is_revalued_with_a_quote_of_its_own_period (100 BRL at 0.17 = 17 EUR both sides) and a_july_journal_takes_no_august_quote (fails Unification; vultr: Got journal _ august_2026 brl / Expected journal seller july_2026 brl). posting.spi still exit 0 against it.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_ledger_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER", 6u32, "2026-11-03T17:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:33 fiscal: LANDED UNSTAGED spiral lib/spiral/ledger.spi 3A96F956 (after money) and fiscal src/posting.spi A9D9576D (after p2p). Rust run: ledger 4 bodies, posting 1 body green. RUNTIME-PROVEN on vultr before landing: test bodies compiled --backend Rust (pack24), rustc -O, run exit 0 (harness mutation-tested on durable_file: a flipped expectation exits 1); every fails negative proven alone (exit 5, pinned text). The queued node Cells job stays as confirmation; CI on the joint push is the final gate. Commit TOGETHER: spiral lib (money, ledger, event_log, durable_file + package.spiproj lines) and fiscal src (document, p2p, posting + package.spiproj and spiral.toml lines; fiscal posting needs lib ledger/money). tibia safety: a lib 'ledger' module does not hide tibia's own ':== ledger' record in apps/predict/sweep.spi (vultr repro, exit 0 + non-vacuity exit 5).")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_ledger_7 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-LEDGER", 7u32, "2026-11-03T19:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:33 fiscal: CLOSE CERTIFICATE PER STANDARD MOVED (omniledger close_certificate entity period standard; gaap_projection's index): landed unstaged in ledger.spi -> 03083793 (formatted). Phantom standards ':! ifrs / us_gaap / br_gaap = ()' with a witness GADT ':| standard s = Ifrs :: standard ifrs | UsGaap :: standard us_gaap | BrGaap :: standard br_gaap'; ':! certificate s e p c = closed_period e p c'; 'certified (standard s) (closed_period e p c) : certificate s e p c' and certified_turnover. Test a_closed_period_certifies... also checks an IFRS certificate's turnover (80 BRL); new negative an_ifrs_certificate_is_not_a_us_gaap_certificate (fails Unification; vultr: Got certificate ifrs seller july_2026 brl). PROVEN on vultr: check with bodies exit 0, all 5 negatives exit 5, 4 Rust bodies exit 0, posting still exit 0 against it. confirm-landed2 inbox + prediction updated (ledger 9/9). Still open: per-standard account mapping (a chart of accounts per standard) once a real fiscal consumer needs it.")
