inl note_of_fiscal_erp_event_log_3 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:26Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 12:26 fiscal: PURE CORE DRAFTED AND TYPE-PROVEN ahead of LIB-DURABLE-APPEND (durability stays a lib dependency; nothing here touches files): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG\\lib\\spiral\\event_log.spi 3DEA5A71, a lib module (generic over the event type). DESIGN vs omniledger: the mega sample's stream position is a type-level successor chain (position_next prior) with the history as a type, which only fits a fixed script and grows a GADT index (EJP0041 risk); a fiscal log grows at run time, so the position is a runtime i64 and the typed part is the EVIDENCE: ':| append_outcome ev = Appended (event_log ev) | Replayed i64 | Collided i64 | Stale i64' from 'append expected (command_id) (payload_hash) event log' (idempotency first: the same command with the same hash replays its original position even when the caller's expected position is old; a changed hash collides; only a new command checks the expected position). The static index lives in the outbox typestate: ':| submission s = Queued :: string -> submission queued | Transmitted :: string * i64 -> submission transmitted | Receipted :: string * string -> submission receipted' with transmit / retransmit / acknowledge (receipt = the authority's proof: nProt, TFD UUID, SdI receipt). Tests: an_append_at_the_expected_position_advances_the_log, a_repeated_command_replays_and_a_changed_payload_collides, a_submission_is_receipted_only_after_transmission, and 3 negatives (fails Unification): a_queued_submission_cannot_be_acknowledged, a_payload_hash_is_not_a_command_id, a_log_of_one_event_type_takes_no_other. PROVEN on idle vultr (pack24): module and test bodies exit 0; each negative alone exit 5 with exactly the intended Unification (submission queued vs transmitted; payload_hash vs command_id both slots; event_log i32 vs string). Cells run QUEUED: job-1793723147058-fiscal-event-log after the ledger job, PREDICTION 6/6. OPEN for Done: instantiate with lifecycle.spi's event_code events (fiscal side) and persist through LIB-DURABLE-APPEND.")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_event_log_4 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG", 4u32, "2026-11-03T17:20Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:20 fiscal: dep LIB-DURABLE-APPEND landed unstaged (spiral lib/spiral/durable_file.spi: durable_append + replace_atomic, Rust, runtime-proven on vultr). NEXT here: persist the event_log outbox through durable_file once event_log's Cells run is green (one line per append, the log text replaced atomically on compaction).")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_event_log_5 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG", 5u32, "2026-11-03T17:34Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:33 fiscal: LANDED UNSTAGED spiral lib/spiral/event_log.spi 3DEA5A71 (after ledger). Rust run: 3 bodies green. RUNTIME-PROVEN on vultr before landing: test bodies compiled --backend Rust (pack24), rustc -O, run exit 0 (harness mutation-tested on durable_file: a flipped expectation exits 1); every fails negative proven alone (exit 5, pinned text). The queued node Cells job stays as confirmation; CI on the joint push is the final gate. Commit TOGETHER: spiral lib (money, ledger, event_log, durable_file + package.spiproj lines) and fiscal src (document, p2p, posting + package.spiproj and spiral.toml lines; fiscal posting needs lib ledger/money). tibia safety: a lib 'ledger' module does not hide tibia's own ':== ledger' record in apps/predict/sweep.spi (vultr repro, exit 0 + non-vacuity exit 5).")
inl note_of_fiscal_erp_event_log_6 () = Note ("FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG", 6u32, "2026-11-03T19:25Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 15:25 fiscal: DURABILITY WIRED (landed unstaged, spiral lib/spiral/event_log.spi -> B2261458): 'append_durably text_of path expected id hash event log : result (append_outcome ev) string' runs the typed append and writes ONE tab-separated line (position, command id, payload hash, text_of event) through durable_file.durable_append ONLY for Appended; Replayed / Collided / Stale write nothing, so a retried authority submission cannot duplicate a line on disk. 'written' unwraps the result. The serializer is an explicit parameter: a prototype instance on string is refused (ETY-ExpectedHigherOrder, the same limit as aliases), and a parameter lets each fiscal event type pass its own text. Test only_a_real_append_reaches_the_file: append nfe-1, retry it (replays 1), change its payload (collides 1), append nfe-2 (position 2) -> the file holds exactly the 2 real lines in order. PROVEN on vultr with durable_file registered before it: --check with bodies exit 0; the 3 negatives unchanged (exit 5, Unification); all 4 bodies as Rust exit 0, probe file removed. The confirm-landed2 node job's inbox carries this version (prediction there becomes event_log 7/7).")
