inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_1 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-02 (user: \"we still have junk comments spread out like those repeating the file name at the top, see if we find similar stuff\"). MEASURED across 13 repos: classic file-name headers (// foo.rs, # foo.ps1) 1 (i574n.github); generated outputs 0 (none of 1,012 generated .rs open with a source comment); .spi whose first content line is `/// # <own file name>`: 10, all in spiral lib (decide with Cells: if the notebook title comes from the file name, drop them). Hand comment lines (// in .spi, # in .ps1, not doc/directive): i574n.github 57/10 files (most in resilience's new scripts, e.g. claude-boost-watcher.ps1, and profile-mirror-if-due.ps1), spiral 43/9, kit 5/3, dice 5/2, tibia 2/1, x/fiscal/regex/alphabet/html 0. Also done 11-02: repo descriptions on GitHub dropped the redundant \"written in Spiral\" (fiscal, html, regex), and 3 markdown copies (x client README title, kit AGENTS.md, tibia README).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_2 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 2u32, "2026-11-02T16:01Z", "main", "main 11-02 SCOPE WIDENED + raised to P1 (user: \"the ps1 files are coming full of comments. don't we have a rule that code should be self explanatory somewhere? clean up all useless comments\"). Yes, the rule exists: memory no-comments-self-explanatory (no comments; names and structure explain the code). MEASURED in tracked .ps1 (# lines, not #requires/#!): i574n.github 67 lines in 12 files (worst scripts/remote.ps1 18, which is main's own; then resilience's new scripts), spiral 35 in 7 (worst apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench.ps1 19), dotfiles 9 in 4, dice 5 in 2, tibia 2, polyglot 1, currency_converter 1; kit/x/fiscal/regex/html 0. The fc1943s dump and fork repos are out of scope. Plus the .spi side from n1 (10 lib files headed by their own name, hand // lines). DoD: each comment is either deleted (a better name or a split function says it) or moved to the backlog item it belongs to; then a kit standards ratchet counts comment lines per language per repo and only lets them go down. Scanner: drafts\\i574n.github\\GROOM-1102-MAIN\\repo-hygiene.ps1. Owners: each lane its repo; main does i574n.github and spiral/lib.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_3 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 3u32, "2026-11-02T16:03Z", "main", "main 11-02: removed the 18 comment lines from i574n.github/scripts/remote.ps1. Their facts already live in memory (kit2-lane-remote-offload: offload scope, read-only jobs, fetch not git; node-stale-compiler-dll: the L6 core guard; unlink-mirror-junctions-first: mirrors link deps/ read-only). The removed text, verbatim, for the record:\n# remote.ps1 <machine> run|job|status|sync|fetch - drive a remote kit worker node over ssh.\n# Machines: ~/.config/remote-machines.json. Transport is ssh (+ Tailscale fallback);\n# iggy is parked (unix-only fd hand-off). Internal git on the node is fine (the user\n# owns git only on this review box); the bring-back to this box is non-git (fetch).\n#\n# Offload scope (kit2): only READ-ONLY jobs - compiles, tests, reviews. Pull results\n# to scratch/job folders with `fetch`, never back into a repo tree. Jobs that write\n# into the live tree (eoie/kit regen+publish, lib land.ps1, matrix accept) stay on\n# this box: their outputs race with local edits and the sync digest cannot cover that.\n# `sync` proves the node tree matches: per-file sha256 over the changed set, verified\n# equal on both sides (Get-TreeDigest), atop `git checkout --detach HEAD` + clean.\n# L6 guard: a verify/compile offload runs only if the node's SpiralCompilerCore.dll\n# matches the expected core (the review box's for the synced HEAD). A mismatch means a\n# stale installed compiler, whose results are invalid even when the source digest matched.\n# Worktree mirrors share only tracked files; spiral's deps/ holds untracked\n# dependency clones (The-Spiral-Language, polyglot) that |core- resolution needs\n# and `git clean` strips each sync. After the clean, link deps/ read-only from the\n# node's shared source so every concurrent mirror resolves |core- (a link, no copy).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_4 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 4u32, "2026-11-02T16:07Z", "main", "main 11-02: removed 10 comment lines from i574n.github/scripts/node-watch.ps1 (parse ok; the two running watchers were unaffected, since they parsed the script at start). The one non-obvious fact, verbatim: \"node-jobs counts only eoie jobs; remote.ps1-run work (Cells, builds, verifies) is invisible to it, so CPU% is the real utilization signal. IDLE = cpu<IdleCpu, UNDERUTIL = cpu<UnderCpu\". Usage was \"run as a supervised job: kit job start node-watch 3600000 pwsh -NoProfile -File node-watch.ps1\". The rest of i574n.github goes to its owners: resilience (claude-boost-watcher 3, config-baseline 7, orphan-reaper 6, profile-mirror 9, profile-mirror-if-due 2, register-scheduled-tasks 1, upkeep-tick 2, wsl-policy 5, node-disk-cleanup 2) and x-dumps (linux-worker 2).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_5 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 5u32, "2026-11-02T16:14Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:40 compiler: apps/compiler scripts healed (unstaged; parse-checked, 0 errors each). make-corelib.ps1: help block (9 lines) and 2 notes removed. upstream.ps1: help block (21 lines) removed. env.ps1: 1. alias-count-check.ps1: 4-line header and 2 inline param notes. test-rust-exports.ps1 needs nothing: its `#[test]` is a Rust attribute inside a here-string, not a comment. test.ps1 (4 lines) follows once the running gadt5 A/B releases it; its comments may sit inside native-memo-keyed blocks, so the memo will rerun those backends once. FACTS MOVED HERE FROM THE COMMENTS: (1) make-corelib.ps1 writes runtime/corelib.cuh = upstream corelib.cuh (hcc @ 0cb0fda0) plus the CPU-host deltas; input is `git -C <fork> show \"0cb0fda0:The Spiral Language 2/corelib.cuh\"`; the delta patch goes to stdout. Upstream's dynamic_array_base::operator[] asserts `i < this->length`, a member it lacks (compile error once indexed); the fix uses max_length. Upstream's file ends without a newline; ours ends with one. (2) upstream.ps1 status|import|export <fork> refs: a `/// ## Name` section maps to `The Spiral Language 2/Name.fs` (SignalRSupervisor -> Supervisor.fs); sections without a file are i574n additions. Edits travel as normalized-line patches (blank lines, `/// ###` headings, `#!import` lines and module headers ignored), using difflib.SequenceMatcher's algorithm ported exactly; a line the target changed itself is a reported conflict. (3) env.ps1: the `lua` slot must be Scoop lua51 5.1.5 (the WoW dialect); lua54 is a side command. (4) alias-count-check.ps1 (HOPACSOTA-P2 negative gate): FFI/type-alias declarations must occur the same number of times in the parallel .fsx output as in single-flight's (multiset equal); GREEN = 0 diffs.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_6 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 6u32, "2026-11-02T16:14Z", "resilience", "11-02 12:1x resilience (autonomous run): started. New scripts written comment-free from the start: profile-mirror-monitor.ps1, memory-integrity-sweep.ps1. REMAINING to strip (main's list, 37 lines): profile-mirror 9, config-baseline 7, orphan-reaper 6, wsl-policy 5, claude-boost-watcher 3, profile-mirror-if-due 2, upkeep-tick 2, node-disk-cleanup 2, register-scheduled-tasks 1; also tools/claude-boost-native/Program.cs has a header+inline block. Non-obvious facts already preserved in memories node-upkeep-scripts + claude-code-git-bash-path + the item notes, so comments can be deleted outright. Will clean + parse+smoke each across the run's iterations.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_7 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 7u32, "2026-11-02T16:23Z", "resilience", "11-02 12:2x resilience: COMMENT-HEAL DONE for all resilience scripts. Stripped via the PSParser tokenizer (keeps #requires, write parse-gated): profile-mirror 9, config-baseline 7, orphan-reaper 5, wsl-policy 4, claude-boost-watcher 3, profile-mirror-if-due 2, register-scheduled-tasks 1, plus upkeep-tick 2 + node-disk-cleanup 2 by hand; the two new scripts (profile-mirror-monitor, memory-integrity-sweep) were written comment-free; tools/claude-boost-native/Program.cs also comment-free (source only, no rebuild - running exe unaffected). Parse-checked all; SMOKED orphan-reaper -DryRun, wsl-policy Block, config-baseline Check, + the monitor + sweep - all run clean. Non-obvious rationale preserved in memories node-upkeep-scripts/claude-code-git-bash-path + the CLAUDE-TREE-PRIORITY-BOOST/PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL notes. profile-mirror.ps1 was stripped atomically (read+strip+parse+write in one pass) to dodge the concurrent edit.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_8 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 8u32, "2026-11-02T16:48Z", "compiler", "11-02 12:55 compiler: test.ps1 done too (4 lines, parse-checked). Facts moved here: (1) Invoke-Native returns the exit code even when stdout/stderr stay open 15 s after exit, because a child (mingw gcc) can hold the redirected pipes; dropping the code turned finished compiles into build-fail. (2) cider's interpret path writes the memory dump to stdout and ignores -o. (3) The runner sets SetErrorMode(0x8003) before native children, or abort() waits on WerFault and a 30 s timeout looks like a missed exit 3. Native-memo keys of the edited blocks change, so those rows rerun once. Compiler lane total: 6 scripts, 41 comment lines removed, 0 left (mega_brzozowski bench.ps1 skipped, per main).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_9 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 9u32, "2026-11-02T20:24Z", "main", "main 11-02 16:3x the lib \"/// # <own name>\" headings are RESOLVED, nothing to remove. Cells takes the page <title> from the file name (apps/cells/lib/spiral/cells/html.ex:82), so the heading only adds a visible H1. But only 4 headed files remain (cli_args, json, routes, sm'; 10 this morning, so another lane cleaned the rest), and all 4 have a _real.spir pair, where headings structure the .spi/.spir interleave (document_test \"a _real.spir interleaves with its .spi by heading\"). They are structural, not junk: keep. Remaining comment work is the lanes' own .ps1 lists (resilience 37, compiler 16; x-dumps done; main's 28 done).")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_10 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 10u32, "2026-11-03T19:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:4x RECOUNT i574n.github (tracked + untracked .ps1/.spi, backlog excluded; '#' lines in .ps1 except #requires/#region, '//' lines in .spi): 57 -> 1, the '<# ... #>' header of scripts/linux-worker.ps1 (x-dumps' K3S-EVERYWHERE script; it points to the backlog, so it could simply go, owner's call). main's repos are clean; the lib headings stay as structural (n1). Remaining: the lanes' own .ps1 lists (resilience 37, compiler 16 at n1). Progress 0 -> 80.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_11 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 11u32, "2026-11-04T05:45Z", "main", "11-04 01:4x main RECOUNT across 11 repos, comment tokens by the PowerShell parser over tracked .ps1 (#requires excluded): 29 left. 19 are spiral apps/compiler/tmp/samples/mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench.ps1 (skipped by decision, n8); 3 are dice/contract/build.ps1, a TAGGED TODO (RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE) that kit agile todos tracks by design, so it stays; 7 belong to owners and were notified: resilience heartbeat-staleness-guard.ps1 4 (new code), tibia tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 2, x-dumps linux-worker.ps1 1. kit, x, fiscal, regex, html, alphabet and blog: 0.")
inl note_of_comment_heal_1102_12 () = Note ("COMMENT-HEAL-1102", 12u32, "2026-11-04T11:27Z", "main", "11-04 07:4x main RECOUNT of the 3 owner-notified scripts (PowerShell parser comment tokens, #requires excluded): heartbeat-staleness-guard.ps1 0, linux-worker.ps1 0, tibia-mariadb-dump.ps1 0. All the owners healed theirs. What remains by decision: mega_brzozowski_derivatives/bench.ps1 19 (sample, n8) and dice/contract/build.ps1 3 (tagged TODO tracked by kit agile todos). Nothing actionable is left.")
inl profile_mirror_silent_fail () = Task ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", "The hourly profile mirror failed silently for ~19 h (last archive 11-01 13:39): fixed the ssh option bug, now make a failed run visible (status age check + alert) so a green task result can never hide a dead backup", TaskKind, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "team:resilience,resilience,backup,durability", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail () = Planning ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_1 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 1u32, "2026-11-02T13:16Z", "main", "main 11-02 08:1x, found while recovering from main's 07:55 crash. The node's newest archive was profile-mirror-20261101-132405.tgz although the scheduled task ran every 15 min with result 0. CAUSE: profile-mirror.ps1:105 read `-o ServerAliveCountMax=4$route` (no space), so ssh got ServerAliveCountMax=4laptop and no host; every route failed (\"no route reached the node (laptop, laptop-ts, laptop-ip)\") from the 11-01 keepalive edit on. FIXED by main (one space, unstaged, i574n.github). It stayed invisible because profile-mirror-if-due.ps1 starts the mirror detached and exits 0, and profile-mirror.last.log is overwritten each run. DoD: (1) a manual run lands a verified archive on the node (main started one 08:1x); (2) the task or a status probe fails loudly when the newest node archive is older than 2x the interval (status-files-need-age); (3) remote.ps1 node status prints the newest archive's age; (4) the same \"no space before $var\" bug is grepped across scripts (main found 0 other `CountMax=\\d+\\$` sites). Note: resilience's 11-02 scripts (orphan-reaper.ps1, wsl-policy.ps1, claude-boost-watcher.ps1) are new .ps1 tools in a repo, against spiral-first-tooling; groom their port to kit commands.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_2 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 2u32, "2026-11-02T13:24Z", "main", "main 11-02 08:5x CORRECTION to n1: point (4) is wrong. main's grep DID flag a second site, profile-mirror.ps1:137 (the node-verify ssh, '=4$reached'), but main filed n1 without reading that output. resilience fixed :137 (unstaged), so all three ssh/scp lines are spaced now. main's 08:1x manual run predates that fix and fails at verify, so a re-run follows. Lesson (read-outputs-after-the-writer): never state a check's result before reading its output. resilience owns this item; its guard design is an INDEPENDENT node-side newest-archive-age monitor, never self-reported by the mirror.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_3 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 3u32, "2026-11-02T13:51Z", "main", "main 11-02 09:5x: the 08:40 snapshot is VERIFIED on the node by hand: profile-mirror-20261102-084014.tgz, 398307413 B / 30132 tar entries on both sides (scp landed it at 09:47; only the script's own verify step failed, because :137 was still broken during that run). So the 19 h gap is closed through 08:40. I left the schedule un-marked on purpose, so the next 15-min task runs a full mirror with all three lines fixed; that run is the end-to-end proof for DoD (1).")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_4 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:07Z", "resilience", "11-02 resilience (star-exchange groom): DESIGN locked. Root cause of the 19h silent death = my 11-02 keepalive edit ServerAliveCountMax=4$route (no space) -> ssh saw '4laptop', no host; invisible because if-due launches detached + exits 0 + overwrites .last.log each run (reinforced by main #2, fiscal 'validate from outside', x 'baseline/health from outside'). FIX must NOT be self-reported: an INDEPENDENT node-side monitor reads the newest profile-mirror-*.tgz mtime ON THE NODE and FAILS LOUDLY (story note + nonzero exit) when age > 2x the 15min interval; show that age in node status. The mirror's own status.txt is insufficient - the failure happened BEFORE the status-writing step. Scheduled at Priority 5 (BelowNormal starves on the saturated box - my upkeep task crawled 130s vs 10s). DoD: alarms on a stale newest-archive regardless of the mirror's exit code; test by pointing it at a frozen dir.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_5 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 5u32, "2026-11-02T16:05Z", "resilience", "11-02 12:0x resilience: DELIVERED the independent monitor (scripts/profile-mirror-monitor.ps1, scheduled PT30M Priority 5). It reads the newest profile-mirror-*.tgz mtime ON THE NODE (not the self-reported status file) and fails loudly on OK->stale transition. VALIDATED: it immediately caught a REAL failure - newest node archive was 08:40, 133min stale. Root is NOT the =4$route bug (fixed) - the run stages but the 1.33GB payload (session transcripts in .claude/projects) is too slow over the saturated link to complete within the ~50min cadence, so the mirror falls behind. That slowness is MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST (incremental mirror). Detection half = DONE; the keep-up fix lives in MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_6 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 6u32, "2026-11-02T17:17Z", "resilience", "11-02 13:1x resilience FIXED the mirror hang-forever bug (main diagnosed: the makeDir's explicit pwsh -EncodedCommand could not cold-start on the 99%-CPU node, hung 1h; ServerAlive only kills a DEAD connection, not a slow-to-START remote command). profile-mirror.ps1 fixes: (1) Invoke-Bounded = hard wall-clock timeout (Start-Process + WaitForExit(ms) + kill the ssh tree) on EVERY ssh/scp (makeDir 15s, scp 600s, verify 90s); (2) makeDir via cmd /c if not exist mkdir not remote pwsh - confirmed the node ssh shell runs cmd/c fast; (3) verify+retention now BEST-EFFORT: a tgz landed via scp is SUCCESS (still emits sha256 <hash> so if-due marks ran + the monitor sees a fresh archive) even when the saturated node cannot run the pwsh retention, instead of throwing and discarding a landed backup. Net: the mirror fail-fasts (bounded) or lands, never hangs. Parse OK; test run bqfj8m91c in flight. Deferred (main fix 3): vultr fallback when the node is saturated (needs Linux-path handling).")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_7 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 7u32, "2026-11-02T18:52Z", "resilience", "11-02 14:4x resilience: COMPLETE, all DoD proven. (1) end-to-end: full 256MB profile-mirror-20261102-142151.tgz on laptop node 14:36 + critical-20261102-144042.tar 14:40, 15min cadence (14:10/14:25/14:40); task result 0x0 only on scp success (critical-mirror.ps1:57). (2) independent node-side monitor profile-mirror-monitor.ps1 PT30M fails loudly OK->stale, validated vs real staleness. (3) remote.ps1 node status now prints archive age (verified: node mirror 2026-11-02 14:36 16min-ago 256MB). (4) =N$var bug fixed on all 3 ssh/scp lines, 0 other sites. Laptop node at 100pct CPU + free-disk 10GB (low, trending) yet mirror lands under load via Invoke-Bounded. Residual transfer-cost (incremental) tracked in MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_8 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 8u32, "2026-11-02T19:21Z", "resilience", "11-02 15:2x resilience: hardened the mirror monitor after heartbeat-staleness-guard caught it hung. profile-mirror-monitor.ps1 rewritten: Invoke-Bounded (hard wall-clock timeout + kill ssh tree) + CMD-NATIVE newest-archive via `cmd /c dir /b /o-d`, age parsed from the filename stamp on the box (no node pwsh cold-start, no clock-skew). Ran 4s (was hanging forever), OK via laptop. Also found+fixed the SAME unbounded-remote-pwsh bug in node-utilization-monitor.ps1 (wifi CPU via node powershell -EncodedCommand) - now Invoke-Bounded, timeout->-1 (node reads unknown=not-idle, correct). profile-mirror.ps1 verify was already bounded. All node-touching watchers now hang-proof. Unstaged.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_9 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 9u32, "2026-11-03T04:06Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-03 00:06 UNREACHABLE (node down all routes)")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_10 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 10u32, "2026-11-03T07:36Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-03 03:36 UNREACHABLE (node down all routes)")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_11 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 11u32, "2026-11-03T12:05Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-03 08:05 STALE via laptop: newest profile-mirror-20261103-055309.tgz 132min old (> 120min)")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_12 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 12u32, "2026-11-03T14:06Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-03 10:06 STALE via laptop-ip: newest profile-mirror-20261103-080354.tgz 122min old (> 120min)")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_13 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 13u32, "2026-11-04T07:05Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-04 03:05 STALE via laptop: newest profile-mirror-20261104-005321.tgz 132min old (> 120min)")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_14 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 14u32, "2026-11-04T08:55Z", "resilience", "11-04 04:5x resilience: this item WORKED end-to-end tonight. The scheduled profile-mirror-monitor (with -NoteOnStale) DETECTED the profile-mirror stall + NOTED here at 03:05 (OK->bad transition, 132min stale). Detection + routing are solid. RESIDUAL = action latency: the 03:05 alarm sat ~70min until my restore-drill independently caught it at 04:15 and I acted (manual ship of the built archive + scp-bound 600->1800s fix; full saga on MIRROR-TRANSFER-COST notes 23-26). LESSON (resilience routine, not code): include the profile-mirror-monitor.last.log STALE-check in EVERY per-tick durability pass (the heartbeat directive already says confirm profile-mirror recent/OK) so a stall is acted within one heartbeat (~20min), not caught incidentally 70min later. The alarm-visibility this item built is exactly what made the catch possible - it did its job.")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_15 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 15u32, "2026-11-04T11:35Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-04 07:35 STALE via laptop: newest profile-mirror-20261104-050904.tgz 146min old (> 120min)")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_16 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 16u32, "2026-11-04T16:35Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-04 12:35 STALE via laptop-ts: newest profile-mirror-20261104-102731.tgz 128min old (> 120min)")
inl note_of_profile_mirror_silent_fail_17 () = Note ("PROFILE-MIRROR-SILENT-FAIL", 17u32, "2026-11-04T19:05Z", "resilience", "monitor ALARM (OK->bad transition): profile-mirror-monitor 2026-11-04 15:05 STALE via laptop: newest profile-mirror-20261104-124140.tgz 144min old (> 120min)")
