inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_1 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:04Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md section 2 (picklers/base.spi:1-39, hd_pickler.spi, kms_pickler.spi bias bit, int_pickler.spi, serializerm utils.spir:1-161). Mainly for tibia: encode the typed per-agent view (TIBIA-AGENT n6/n14) and tabular state ids without hash collisions. The old pu-combinator pickler.spi is superseded (the author marked it TODO: Remove).")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_2 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:34Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:2x tibia, SLICE 1 DRAFTED (drafts spiral LIB-PICKLER-GADT pickler.spi, new lib module, not in live lib): an edition-3 recursive GADT pickler t with PickUnit :: () -> pickler (), PickBool -> pickler bool, PickBelow :: i32 -> pickler i32, PickOption :: pickler a -> pickler (option a), PickPair :: pickler a * pickler b -> pickler (a * b); size (product/sum of radices), pickle (mixed-radix perfect index: pair = pickle a u * size b + pickle b v, option = 0 or 1 + inner) and unpickle (the inverse), all recursive inl so a known pickler folds at compile time; the round-trip check loops in a join point that captures p from scope (a pickler passed as a join-point argument would go runtime and the recursive inl would unroll forever). 4 C tests: sample (option below-3 x bool) has 8 values; every index 0..7 round-trips; (Some 2, true) -> 7 and (None, false) -> 0; out-of-range fails. vultr probe exit 0 first try (GADT refinement of x per arm works in edition 3); mutant (option index without the 1 + offset) exit 1. NEXT slices: PickAlt/PickRecord from union_map/record_map reflection, then the bit-packed one-hot interpreter with a bias bit (kms_pickler), then the fixed binary layout reconciled with lib wire.spi. Then node gate + land like occupancy.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_3 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:06Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:0x tibia, NODE GATE OF SLICES 1+2 (pickler 0815ED841995): behaviour green (4 of 5 positive; the mutant fails exactly round-trip and mixed-radix), but two blockers, so NOT landed: (a) the out-of-range test used fails, which in Cells only matches COMPILE errors; fixed in drafts slice3 with a pure in_range predicate test (memory cells-test-block-structure point 4, repeated). (b) CELL BUDGET: the GADT design does not fit 272 weighted characters per definition: union 345, pickle 513, unpickle 396, hot_at 688, one_hot 276 (slice3 with PickSized). Every interpreter of an N-constructor GADT carries N arms plus a long typed head, so with 5-6 constructors no readable spelling fits. Options, my order: (1) TYPE-DIRECTED prototypes (one :+ instance per type, each its own small cell; bounded ints as a nominal with a type-literal bound) which also matches derived from union/record types, but needs dispatch without a value for size/unpickle (a phantom-typed proxy argument); (2) split the GADT into leaf and compound GADTs so each interpreter has <= 3 arms; (3) a budget exception class for GADT interpreters, which is a standards decision for kit/user, not mine. Slice 3 (PickSized via sized_array, length carried as a value from type_lit_to_lit because a GADT arm cannot name its existential type literal) is proven on vultr: bits3 size 8, [T,F,T] -> 5, unpickle 6 -> [T,T,F], one_hot bits 2,3,6, round trip. Drafts: LIB-PICKLER-GADT pickler.spi (slices 1-2) and slice3 pickler.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_4 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 4u32, "2026-11-03T16:24Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:5x tibia, V2 FITS THE CELL BUDGET AND IS GATED (drafts LIB-PICKLER-GADT v2 pickler.spi 6F3F52DB3CBA): option (2) from n3, the GADT split into leaf t (LeafBool, LeafBelow; 2-arm interpreters leaf_size/leaf_index/leaf_value) and pick t (PLeaf, POpt, PPair, PSized; 4-arm recursive interpreters size/pickle/unpickle/width/hot). Each compound arm delegates to a small non-recursive helper and passes the partially applied recursive interpreter (opt_index (pickle a), pair_index (size b) (pickle a) (pickle b), sized_index, opt_of, sized_of, opt_hot/pair_hot/sized_hot), and hot takes a position callback (:== visit a = a -> (i32 -> ()) -> ()) instead of out+at, so every definition is a small cell. one_hot adds the bias bit at 0. Smart constructors pick_bool, pick_below, pick_sized (length from type_lit_to_lit). Node gate: positive 6/6, 0 type errors, cell budget 0 findings; mutant (opt_index without 1 +) fails exactly round-trip and mixed-radix; lib_roundtrip canonical; booleans spelled !+ / !-. vultr probe: all values right incl. sized [T,F,T] -> 5, unpickle 6 -> [T,T,F], one_hot bits. LANDING now (pickler new + package.spiproj line after occupancy, base 2BF4B4159278). NEXT slice: alternatives and records from union/record reflection; no edition-3 lib code uses real_core union_map yet, so that slice starts with a reflection probe.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_5 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 5u32, "2026-11-03T16:41Z", "tibia", "11-03 13:0x tibia, V2 LANDED (new lib module pickler.spi 6F3F52DB3CBA + package.spiproj line after occupancy, base 2BF4B4159278 -> EF9E62744A53): closed green, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe pickler PASS 6 tests typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-122405. V3 drafted (drafts LIB-PICKLER-GADT v3): enums via LeafEnum :: (a -> i32) * (i32 -> a) * i32 -> leaf a and pick_enum n to from, example heading union (North..West) paired with bool: size 8, (South, !+) -> 5, 7 -> (West, !+), round trip. A first try with a general LeafIso carrying an implicit existential (a case type var absent from its result) silently erased the module exported types for consumers; isolated in 5 steps and filed as COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT. Also fixed my vultr probe script, which ran the PREVIOUS binary when the compile failed (a false pass): it now deletes the C file and binary first. v3 node gate running.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_6 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 6u32, "2026-11-03T17:00Z", "tibia", "11-03 13:2x tibia, V3 LANDED (base 6F3F52DB3CBA -> CB7192F3BEDF): enums via pick_enum n to from (LeafEnum), node gate positive 7/7, 0 type errors, budget 0, mutant (reversed enum decode) fails exactly an_enum_is_a_bounded_index_with_its_inverse; canonical round trip; close green: consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 7 typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-125243. Landed so far: unit-free leaf/compound GADT, size/pickle/unpickle (mixed-radix perfect index), width/one_hot (bias bit), option, pair, sized_array, bool, bounded int, enums. Left: records/alternatives via union_map/record_map reflection, and the fixed binary layout reconciled with wire.spi.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_7 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 7u32, "2026-11-03T17:29Z", "tibia", "11-03 13:4x tibia, DERIVED ENUMS FROM UNION REFLECTION PROBED (vultr): for a payload-free union t, case count = ~> real_core::union_type_length `t, case index = ~> real_core::union_tag x, case from index = union_untag `t i with nominal_create `t (k, ()) (base.spi defaultof pattern; the failure text must be a plain string literal, a raw $ macro string breaks C). Works on C (positive OK, negative twin BAD, real runtime iteration for a dyn index) and Rust; Lua hits a codegen bug (COMPILER-LUA-UNION-TAG-IIFE, filed). So the next slice is pick_cases () : pick t = pick_enum (count) case_index case_at with no hand-written index functions, C/Rust tests, Lua after the fix. Note: a count function needs t in its signature (ETY-UnusedTypeVariable otherwise), which pick_cases has through its result pick t.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_8 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 8u32, "2026-11-03T18:08Z", "tibia", "11-03 14:1x tibia: V4 (derived enums: case_index = union_tag, case_at = union_untag + nominal_create, pick_cases () for any payload-free union) gated on a box scratch lib in a test-suite window: positive 8/8, 0 type errors; mutant (reversed derived decode) fails exactly a_payload_free_union_derives_the_same_enum_pickler; budget 0 after one test was trimmed; canonical 320B29B673ED; landing now on CB7192F3BEDF. V5 drafted (drafts LIB-PICKLER-GADT v5): the type-directed FIXED BINARY LAYOUT of the item: bytes p (bool 1, bounded int and enum the minimal little-endian width for their range, option a tag byte plus reserved inner bytes, pair concatenation, sized n x inner), put/get interpreters through writer helpers (put_opt, put_pair, put_sized), encode p x : array u8 (zero-filled, so a None reserves zeros) and decode p b. Probe on the box (Rust): (Some 258, true) with below 300 -> [1, 2, 1, 1] and decodes back; a wrong-byte twin fails. This is the byte shape lib wire.spi feeds to xtea/adler, so a typed packet = encode of a pick. Gate after v4 lands.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_9 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 9u32, "2026-11-03T18:51Z", "tibia", "11-03 15:0x tibia, V4 + V5 LANDED. v4 (derived enums pick_cases) closed green on CB7192F3BEDF -> 320B29B673ED (8 typed, 0 errors). v5 (fixed binary layout: bytes, put/get through sink i32 -> u8 -> () and source i32 -> u8 callbacks, encode/decode) node gate: positive 9/9, 0 type errors, budget 0 (the first spelling had put 323 and get 343 over budget; the sink/source callbacks made every arm one helper call), mutant (big-endian byte order) fails exactly a_fixed_layout_writes_tag_bytes_and_little_endian_leaves; canonical; LANDED 320B29B673ED -> BD4C36D7A4EE, document_test 22, type_probe 9 typed, 0 respell drift, undo lib-land-undo 20261103-144140. The item scope is now covered: GADT pickers, perfect mixed-radix index, one-hot with bias bit, derived enums from union reflection, fixed binary layout. Open: records/alternatives with payloads via record_map/union_map (generic payload unions), Lua for derived enums after COMPILER-LUA-UNION-TAG-IIFE.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_10 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 10u32, "2026-11-04T00:16Z", "tibia", "11-03 20:2x tibia, AFTER THE 19:50 BSOD (run renewed to 22:00): nothing of tibia was in flight at the crash (last job, the 110M bench, ended 18:45). Checked: the four lib files tibia landed today match their landed hashes (pickler BD4C36D7A4EE, sized_array BA3E59936D49, occupancy E69324077D19, am 9ABAE9F442AD), no zero-length or NUL-filled writes in them or in the 11 unstaged tibia files, every gated tibia edit still carries its gated content, no stale kit window of tibia. NEXT (queued on pack31 = COMPILER-LUA-UNION-TAG-IIFE going live): draft v6 (drafts LIB-PICKLER-GADT v6, BD4C36D7A4EE -> 794976646AD6) adds ///> lua to a_payload_free_union_derives_the_same_enum_pickler; proof = the vultr case_probe Lua twin (VERDICT OK / BAD) with the pack31 compiler, then the node gate and the land.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_11 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 11u32, "2026-11-04T01:11Z", "tibia", "11-03 21:0x tibia, V6 LANDED (BD4C36D7A4EE -> 794976646AD6): the derived-enum test now runs on lua too (pick_cases through union_tag/union_untag, enabled by pack31 = COMPILER-LUA-UNION-TAG-IIFE). Proof: vultr pack31 lua5.1 probe OK and negative BAD; node lib_gate -Compiler process 9/9 with lua; mutant (reversed derived decode) fails exactly that test. The first node gate reported lua FAILED: a Cells compiler daemon started before the 20:24 swap still served the pre-pack31 compiler (main confirmed; memory stale-compiler-daemon-after-pack). Close green: document_test 22, type_probe 9 typed, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-205925. A re-check of tuple_list and pickler on the node pack32 compiler (A63F4C2A) is running.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_12 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 12u32, "2026-11-04T01:22Z", "tibia", "11-03 21:2x tibia: PACK32 RE-CHECK (node job tibia-pack32-recheck, fresh compiler process, node compiler A63F4C2A, mirror synced from the box tree): landed tuple_list.spi 45268BF26BCF 2/2, 0 type errors; landed pickler.spi 794976646AD6 9/9 incl. lua, 0 type errors. So none of the daemon-window verdicts (20:22-20:58) mattered for tibia lib lands: both files pass on the current compiler.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_13 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 13u32, "2026-11-04T05:00Z", "tibia", "11-04 01:00 tibia, V7 DRAFTED (drafts LIB-PICKLER-GADT v7, base 794976646AD6): RECORDS via a wrap case with no existential. PWrap :: \\* a. ops a -> pick a, where ops a is a record of the eight interpretations already composed (size, index, value, width, hot, bytes, put, get), all typed in a, the way LeafEnum carries its functions. wrap to from p builds it with >> composition (index = to >> pickle p, value = unpickle p >> from, ...), so each interpreter gains a one-line arm (| PWrap o => o::size). Why not the existential (\\? b. (a -> b) * (b -> a) * pick b): it works since compiler's 11-04 finding (explicit \\? is the supported spelling; COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT), but unpacking costs two lines in each of eight interpreter arms, against cells already near the 280 budget. Test a_record_wraps_a_pair_of_its_fields (c, rust): a status record {hp : i32; alive : bool} as wrap over PPair (pick_below 4, pick_bool ()): size 8, pickle 7, unpickle 7 = s, decode (encode s) = s, one-hot count 3. vultr pack32 --check exit 0; negative twin (index = pickle p, without to) exit 5 with Unification failure in wrap; respell-drift 0 after respelling o.size as o::size (edition 3 field access). WIRE.SPI RECONCILIATION, decided: there is no overlap. wire.spi is XTEA plus Adler-32 (Tibia protocol crypto and checksum) with no byte layout, so pickler's put_le/get_le/encode/decode are the layout layer, and wire's future packet framing (TIBIA-TCP-BYTES) uses them rather than adding a second little-endian writer. Nothing to merge. NEXT: node gate tibia-pk7-gate (mutant: the PWrap unpickle arm ignores its index) queued after tibia-zig-gate-1 on the same mirror, then the land; record derivation by record_fold reflection is a later slice on top of wrap.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_14 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 14u32, "2026-11-04T05:54Z", "tibia", "11-04 01:5x tibia, V8 LANDED (base 794976646AD6 -> A60D280AEC64): RECORDS via wrap. PWrap :: \\* a. ops a -> pick a with ops a = codec a * layout a (codec: size/index/value/width/hot; layout: bytes/put/get), built by codec_of and layout_of with >> composition, so the case needs no existential. v7 was over the cell budget (5 definitions). v8 fixes that: helpers take the sub-pickler and compute size/width/bytes themselves (pair_of and leaf_hot added), and a local alias :== sized n a = sized_array::sized n a shortens the signatures. Budget 0. Test a_record_wraps_a_pair_of_its_fields (c, rust): a status record {hp; alive} over PPair (pick_below 4, pick_bool ()) has size 8 and pickles to 7, and unpickle, encode/decode and a one-hot count of 3 all hold. Proof: box gate (scratch lib, -Compiler process) 10/10 with 0 type errors; mutant (the PWrap unpickle arm ignores its index) fails exactly the record test; vultr --check --timeout-ms 150000 exit 0, with the negative twin (index without to >>) exit 5 in codec_of. Close green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 10 typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261104-014628. Left for 100%: deriving the record's to/from from record reflection (record_fold), so a record pickler needs no hand-written iso.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_15 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 15u32, "2026-11-04T08:02Z", "tibia", "11-04 04:0x tibia, V9 LANDED: TYPE-DIRECTED DERIVATION. New real module pickler_real.spir (8151DAAB9895): pick_of \\* t. () matches the type with ?: t ?|: bool -> pick_bool, option el -> POpt `el, a * b -> PPair `a `b, a payload-free union -> pick_cases `t, anything else -> compile-time error_type 'pickler: no derivation for this type'. In real code the GADT constructors need explicit type applications (POpt `el ...); without them the error is 'Cannot apply a forall with a term'. New typed module pickler_derive.spi (D5D64615CAE8): derived \\* t. () : pickler::pick t = ~> pickler_real::pick_of `t (). Its test a_pickler_is_derived_from_its_type (c, rust): derived () at option heading * bool has size 10, pickles (Some South, true) to 7 and round-trips, the same numbers as the hand-built pickler. package.spiproj DF7923212DBB -> 35B16EE6886D (pickler_real* and pickler_derive after pickler). Proof: box C probe (size 10, index 7, round_trips 1, exit 0); negative twin (option i32 * bool) fails to compile with exactly the pickler's message; box Cells gate positive 1/1 with 0 type errors; the mutant (reversed bool coding in pickler_real) was caught only as a COMPILE error (real code cannot pass lambdas into typed functions, and every pick_of arm is one typed constructor), so it is not a semantic kill. Close green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 1 typed 0 errors, 0 respell; undo lib-land-undo 20261104-035856. Left: a record arm (| {} => wrap with reflected to/from through record_type_fold) and sized arrays.")
inl note_of_lib_pickler_gadt_16 () = Note ("LIB-PICKLER-GADT", 16u32, "2026-11-04T11:05Z", "tibia", "11-04 07:0x tibia: DONE. Landed across v2-v9 (11-03/11-04): the leaf/pick GADT; size/pickle/unpickle (mixed-radix perfect index), width/one_hot with a bias bit; option, pair, sized arrays, bool, bounded ints and enums; enums derived from union reflection (pick_cases); the fixed binary layout (bytes/put/get/encode/decode; wire.spi has no layout, so nothing to reconcile); records through wrap (PWrap with codec * layout ops, no existential); type-directed derivation (pickler_real.pick_of + pickler_derive.derived) for bool, option, pairs and payload-free unions. The one remaining idea, deriving a RECORD's to/from by reflection, is split out as LIB-PICKLER-RECORD-DERIVE (P3, needs a way for real code to pass functions into typed code).")
inl lib_device_capabilities () = Task ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", "lib/compiler: a probed device capability record (SMs, regs/SM, smem/SM, warp size, compute capability, threads/SM), an occupancy calculator, and a compile-time tile planner parameterized by it, replacing hardcoded GPU unions", TaskKind, P1, D4, 90u32, Blocked, "", "lib,compiler,gpu,transformer,tibia,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_device_capabilities () = Planning ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_1 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md sections 3 (corecuda/base.spi:6-53 hardcoded gpu() = RTX5080), 1.2 (frame/frame_iter :17-33), 1.3 (max_blocks_per_sm.py formula) and failure 12 (H100 move needed source edits). Feeds GPU-STACKED-RUNS: print device, grid, regs and smem once at start and fail fast below the occupancy target.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_2 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:07Z", "tibia", "11-03 11:3x tibia, SLICE 1 DRAFTED (drafts spiral LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES occupancy.spi, new lib module, not in live lib). Typed records per_sm {threads; blocks; regs; smem}, device {sms; per_sm; smem_per_block; smem_reserved}, kernel {threads; regs per thread; smem per block}. Presets by compute capability: cc_89 (1536 threads, 24 blocks, 65536 regs, 100 KB smem per SM) for rtx4060 (24 SMs) and l40s (142 SMs); cc_90 (2048, 32, 65536, 228 KB) for h100_sxm (132 SMs); per-block smem 99 KB / 227 KB, 1 KB reserved per block. Occupancy goes beyond the ML library formula (max_blocks_per_sm.py): registers allocated per warp in units of 256, smem in 128-byte units plus the per-block reserve, threads rounded to warps, and fits (threads 1..1024, regs <= 255, smem <= per-block limit) gives 0 blocks. API: blocks_per_sm, occupancy_percent, grid (persistent grid = sms x blocks). 4 C tests (h100 48 KB -> 4 blocks, 50 percent; rtx4060 42 regs -> 10 not the naive 12; over-limit smem -> 0; l40s grid 852). vultr probe: all 5 values right, and the whole calculation folds at compile time (133-byte C main), so a compile-time tile planner can take it as a parameter. Mutant (no 256-register rounding): probe fails as it should. NEXT: node lib gate with package.spiproj = live + occupancy, round trip, lib_land_window; then slice 2 = probe a real device (cudaGetDeviceProperties) into the same record, slice 3 = corecuda gpu() union replaced by a device value.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_3 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T15:26Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:0x tibia: slice 1 (occupancy.spi 070EE8AF0F83) GATED on the node mirror: positive 4/4, 0 type errors, cell budget 0 findings; mutant (no 256-register rounding) fails exactly registers_are_allocated_per_warp_in_units_of_256; lib_roundtrip canonical true fixpoint true (draft bytes = canonical). Lands after file_system (land running). SLICE 2 drafted in drafts LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES slice2: typed launch record {blocks_per_sm; grid; occupancy}, launch d k, and planned target d k which fails fast when the kernel cannot launch or sits below the occupancy target (the GPU-STACKED-RUNS start-of-run check). Tests: a_plan_at_its_target (h100 -> 4, 528, 50) and a fails test below target 75. vultr probe: at-target exit 0 (folded to a 133-byte main), below-target exits 1 with the message.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_4 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:47Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:4x tibia, SLICE 1 LANDED via lib_land_window (new file + package.spiproj line after keyed_rng, base 8FB24F8AD13A): occupancy.spi 070EE8AF0F83, package.spiproj now 2BF4B4159278; closed green: apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 22 passed, type_probe occupancy PASS (4 tests typed, 0 errors), 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-113740. Unstaged for the user. Slice 2 (launch record, meets, planned): first node gate showed fails tests are COMPILE-error tests in Cells (README Expected compile errors), so a run-time failwith cannot be tested that way; reworked to a pure meets predicate tested directly, planned keeps the fail-fast failwith; re-gate running (occ-gate-3).")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_5 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 5u32, "2026-11-03T16:20Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:4x tibia, SLICE 2 LANDED (base 070EE8AF0F83 -> C9A8E50BB549): launch record {blocks_per_sm; grid; occupancy}, launch d k, meets target l, planned target d k (fail-fast). Closed green: consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 6 tests typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-121449. The first try was undone at close for one respell-drift finding (false must be written !-), memory lib-respell-bool-literals. Next slices: probe a real device (cudaGetDeviceProperties) into a device record, then feed GPU-STACKED-RUNS (print launch once at start, planned with the occupancy target).")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_6 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 6u32, "2026-11-03T20:43Z", "tibia", "11-03 16:4x tibia, SLICE 3 LANDED (described : launch -> string, e.g. blocks/sm 4, grid 528, occupancy 50%, the one line GPU-STACKED-RUNS prints at start): occupancy C9A8E50BB549 -> E69324077D19 and package.spiproj moved occupancy after sm_operators (it now opens sm_operators; the first node gate was VOID with Unbound module sm_operators, the define-before-use order trap); package re-derived from live at land time (82E29239D38D, another lane had landed meanwhile) -> E11B322C8801. Node gate: positive 7/7, 0 type errors, budget 0; mutant fails exactly the register-rounding test. Close green: consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 7 typed, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261103-163038.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_7 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:09Z", "tibia", "11-04 01:09 tibia, SLICE 4 DRAFTED (drafts LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES v4, base E69324077D19): the typed model of a device probe. A union attribute (Sms, ThreadsPerSm, BlocksPerSm, RegsPerSm, SmemPerSm, SmemPerBlock, SmemReserved), cuda_code mapping each one to its cudaDeviceAttr value, and device_from (query : attribute -> i32) : device. A real GPU becomes device_from (cudaDeviceGetAttribute on ordinal 0 . cuda_code), and the planner never sees raw attribute numbers. The codes 16/39/106/82/81/97/111 are VERIFIED against NVIDIA's own header (driver_types.h in the nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12 12.9.79 wheel, lines 1937-2025, unzipped on vultr). NVIDIA's API page lists the enumerators without values. Tests: a_probed_device_is_built_from_its_attribute_answers (c, rust: device_from rtx4060_answers = rtx4060 (), and its launch prints blocks/sm 10, grid 240, occupancy 83%) and each_attribute_asks_its_own_cuda_code (c). respell-drift 0. The vultr --check was VOID (30 s attestation cap, vultr at load 8 from other lanes). Proof goes to the node gate tibia-pk7-occ4-gate-1 (mutant: per_sm_from reads SmemPerBlock for smem), queued after tibia-zig-gate-1. NEXT after the land: the C binding cuda_query ordinal a via cudaDeviceGetAttribute, proven on the first GPU box (rental or the box's rtx4060), feeding GPU-STACKED-RUNS.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_8 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T05:47Z", "tibia", "11-04 01:47 tibia, SLICE 4 LANDED (base E69324077D19 -> 52430D9393A9): attribute union + cuda_code (codes checked against NVIDIA driver_types.h 12.9.79) + device_from. Proof: box gate in a test-suite window on a scratch lib (-Compiler process), positive 9/9 with 0 type errors; mutant (per_sm_from reads SmemPerBlock for smem) fails exactly a_probed_device_is_built_from_its_attribute_answers; cell budget 0; respell 0; vultr --check --timeout-ms 150000 exit 0, with the negative twin exit 5. Close green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 9 typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo 20261104-013458. (A first land attempt refused itself: the generated land script's single-file spec flattened, @(@(...)), and lib_land_window rejected the draft argument; nothing was written. The land scripts now fail closed with ErrorActionPreference Stop.) NEXT: the C binding cuda_query (cudaDeviceGetAttribute) proven on a GPU box, feeding GPU-STACKED-RUNS.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_9 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 9u32, "2026-11-04T06:24Z", "tibia", "11-04 02:2x tibia, SLICE 5 DRAFTED AND PROVEN ON A REAL GPU (drafts LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES v5, base 52430D9393A9): probed ordinal : option device through the CUDA DRIVER API loaded at run time (LoadLibraryA nvcuda.dll / dlopen libcuda.so.1; cuInit, cuDeviceGet, cuDeviceGetAttribute), so no CUDA toolkit is needed to build. Every failure (no library, missing symbol, init or device error) answers -1, and probed is None when Sms <= 0, so a GPU-less CI runner gets None. The C side is split into one small global per C function (c_cu_win_lib/sym, c_cu_posix_lib/sym, types, ready, device, attr_fn, find, ask, attribute) for the cell budget. FIRST REAL PROBE (box, mingw gcc): the box GPU is NOT the rtx4060 preset but an NVIDIA Quadro K1100M (Kepler, cc 3.0, driver 25.21.14.2678 = R426, pre-CUDA-11): sms 2, threads/SM 2048, regs 65536, smem/SM 49152, opt-in smem/block 49152, while attributes 106 (blocks/SM) and 111 (reserved smem) answered -1 (they arrived in CUDA 11). So v5 adds CcMajor/CcMinor (codes 75/76, checked in NVIDIA driver_types.h 12.9.79) and filled: an unsupported attribute falls back to blocks_by_cc (Kepler 16, Volta 32 / Turing 16, A100 32 / GA10x 16 / Ada 24, others 32) and reserved_by_cc (1024 from cc 8, else 0). After that the live probe prints blocks 16, reserved 0, launch blocks/sm 10, grid 20, occupancy 62, and equals device_from (filled k1100m_answers) (exit 0). Tests: an_old_driver_falls_back_to_the_compute_capability (c, rust: 16, 0, 10) and a_probe_finds_no_device_without_a_driver_and_whole_sms_with_one (c). respell 0, budget 0. NEXT: box Cells gate with a mutant, then the land.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_10 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 10u32, "2026-11-04T07:56Z", "tibia", "11-04 03:5x tibia, SLICE 5 LANDED (52430D9393A9 -> BE410DF8161A): probed ordinal : option device through the CUDA driver API loaded at run time (nvcuda.dll / libcuda.so.1), with the compute-capability fallback (filled, blocks_by_cc, reserved_by_cc) for drivers older than CUDA 11. Proof: a REAL-GPU run on the box (Quadro K1100M, cc 3.0, R426): sms 2, threads 2048, blocks 16 (fallback), regs 65536, smem 49152, reserved 0 (fallback); launch blocks/sm 10, grid 20, occupancy 62; equal to device_from (filled k1100m_answers). Node gate tibia-occ5-gate-1 (mirror synced): positive 11/11 with 0 type errors (the probe test also passed on the node's own K1100M); mutant (reserved_by_cc answers 1 below cc 8) fails exactly an_old_driver_falls_back_to_the_compute_capability; cell budget 0 over (hashtag and autolink findings only, from the C #ifdef text); respell 0. Close green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, consumer compiles, document_test 22, type_probe 11 typed 0 errors, 0 respell; undo lib-land-undo 20261104-035117. LEFT for 100%: GPU-STACKED-RUNS prints described (planned target (the probed device) kernel) once at start; that is the consumer slice, next when a GPU run is planned.")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_11 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 11u32, "2026-11-04T15:30Z", "tibia", "11-04 11:30 tibia, CONSUMER SLICE IN THE TREE: tibia/apps/predict/gpu_plan.spi (new module, registered in apps/predict/spiral.toml after lanes_gpu; unstaged) is the GPU run's first command: occupancy::probed 0 through the CUDA driver at run time; on Some d it prints the device line and the launch plan of the lanes kernel (64 threads = the WGSL runner's workgroup, smem 0, registers not counted since WGSL reports none), exit 0; on None it prints 'no CUDA device: probed 0 is None', exit 1. Proof: box (Quadro K1100M): 'device sms 2, threads/sm 2048, blocks/sm 16, regs/sm 65536, smem/sm 49152' and 'blocks/sm 16, grid 32, occupancy 50%', exit 0, compiled inside tibia's package (12,826 B C); vultr (no GPU), the same C: 'no CUDA device', exit 1. LEFT: the same command on a rented L40S as the first step of GPU-STACKED-RUNS (no Vultr GPU region yet).")
inl note_of_lib_device_capabilities_12 () = Note ("LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", 12u32, "2026-11-05T05:16Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:16 tibia: Active -> Blocked at 90. Everything CPU-side is landed and proven (slices 1-5 plus the gpu_plan consumer on the box K1100M). The last 10% is running gpu_plan on a rented L40S, and Vultr shows 0 locations on every GPU plan (anonymous recheck today at 01:03, GPU-STACKED-RUNS n12). Unblocks when a GPU plan has a location or the user picks another provider.")
inl compiler_gpu_backend_primitives () = Task ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", "Compiler: the GPU/fast-CPU primitives the ML library used through CUDA macros, as typed ops on every backend that has them: WGSL workgroup memory, barriers, subgroup collectives and atomics; an unroll pragma (union NoUnroll | UnrollAll | UnrollBy) on C/Rust/WGSL; restrict emission in C; f16/bf16 types; a noinline attribute instead of the noinline_ name prefix; 16-byte vector loads", Feature, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "", "compiler,backends,wgsl,gpu,transformer,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives () = Planning ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", Minutes 2400u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_gpu_backend_primitives_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md section 5 (capability table: missing in our compiler: unroll outside CodegenCpp, restrict 0 hits, f16 0 hits, WGSL shared memory/barriers/subgroups/atomics) and 3 (pragma.spi -1/0/n codes, models.spi:8-9 name convention). Coordinate with WGSL-BACKEND and the compiler lane.")
inl compiler_cuda_tensor_cores () = Task ("COMPILER-CUDA-TENSOR-CORES", "CUDA path for the transformer: typed WMMA/MMA fragments (dims as type literals, tf32/f16/bf16), a type-level matmul config (fragment, tile, skew, so divisibility is checked by types), warp tiling, a bank-conflict-padded shared-memory transpose, a sync tiled kernel first (async pipelines only after measurement), a multi-stream runner, and sm_89 kernels precompiled before any rental", Feature, P1, D7, 0u32, Planned, "COMPILER-GPU-BACKEND-PRIMITIVES,LIB-DEVICE-CAPABILITIES", "compiler,cuda,gpu,transformer,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_cuda_tensor_cores () = Planning ("COMPILER-CUDA-TENSOR-CORES", Minutes 1800u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_cuda_tensor_cores_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-CUDA-TENSOR-CORES", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md sections 1.3 (matmul/kernel.spi, run.spi), 3 (corecuda/wmma.spi:21-108), 7.1 and failures 4-6 (static smem never reused; async and Cutlass lost to sync; register spills at the 255 cap). L40S (Ada, sm_89) has no thread block clusters: exclude cluster code.")
inl tibia_learning_nuggets () = Task ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", "tibia: adopt the ML library's learning machinery that fits integer, bit-exact sims: CEM ensemble update (elites at or above the mean, resampling from elite statistics) as a batched trainer option, ensemble action sampling with importance weights, log-space path probabilities, tabular CFR+ and VR-MCCFR baselines before any NN policy, LSH sign-bit hashing of features into a policy table, a game-node union state machine with one step call site, bitmask decks/bitsets, bounded histories pickled into features, and on-device state encoding", Story, P1, D5, 25u32, Active, "TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION,LIB-PICKLER-GADT", "tibia,ml,typefeatureset,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_learning_nuggets () = Planning ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:05Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md sections 1.4 (cem.spi:38-146, models.spi:37-76, path_probs.spi, cfr.spi:144-253, cem_models.spi:86-95 select_id_from_mask), 1.2 (local_binarize :817-821), 3 (game/leduc state machine, train_cfr.spi:129-134 single site, deckm bitmask, hd enumerative CFR+), and failures 1 and 7 (neural CFR/CEM failed on NL Hold'em: start from tabular baselines known to converge; golden deterministic tests and rng per thread from day one). Remodel the int action ids with failwith decoders and the bool mode flags (is_train, is_current) into unions; the elite rule becomes selection = TopK : n | AboveMean; ratio accumulators become a running_mean nominal.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 2u32, "2026-11-05T04:26Z", "tibia", "11-05 00:26 tibia: SLICE 1 DRAFTED, CEM ensemble update as a batched trainer option (scratch np2 = src/network.spi base 707e7157dc1e + COMPILER-EMIT-PARALLEL-LOOPS' evolve_par_by + this; draft ab5b42043d78). The nugget's elite rule is a union, as the inventory asked: elites = TopK : i32 | AboveMean. AboveMean compares score * n >= total in i64 (lane fitness sits near -1e9, so an i32 sum of 32 children overflows); TopK uses a stable rank (strictly better children plus equal-scored EARLIER children), so ties go to the lower child id, deterministically. The next parent is the clamped per-weight integer mean of the elite children (each child re-derived by mutate, so no per-child weight storage); scores come from scores_by (parallel::for_index, one child per thread on C). CEM moves the mean, so climb_cem_by carries a kept_best and never returns worse than its start; width keeps next_weight_round's shrink (elite-variance width is the next refinement). Tests (c, rust): tied_elites_keep_the_earlier_child_and_the_mean_counts_ties (scores 5,5,3,1: TopK 1 = child 0 only, TopK 2 and AboveMean = 0 and 1), the_mean_rule_does_not_overflow_on_large_scores (-1e9 scores), cem_never_ends_below_its_start (c). vultr probe, C t1/t2 and Rust identical: heal judge seed 5, climb 17, cem AboveMean 17, cem TopK 3 = 13. Node gate tibia-np2-gate-1 queued: draft, then a double mutant (fold '>=', tie rank 'i <= child'). Rest of the inventory (importance-weighted ensemble sampling, CFR+ baselines, LSH features) stays open.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 3u32, "2026-11-05T05:12Z", "tibia", "11-05 01:12 tibia: SLICE 2 DRAFTED (np3 = 3c8136221511, supersedes np2): CEM's spread comes from elite statistics too. cem_rule = { pick : elites; spread : spread }, spread = Shrink | EliteSpread. EliteSpread sets the next width to max 4 ((width + elite mean-absolute-deviation from the elite mean) / 2), averaged over all weights; Shrink keeps next_weight_round's schedule. One elite_pass per round feeds both the mean and the deviation pass. Regression on vultr (C at OMP 2 and Rust, identical): AboveMean+Shrink and TopK 3+Shrink give 17 and 13 at seed 5, the same as np2; the heal judge is too coarse to tell EliteSpread apart (17/13, 13/13 at seeds 5/9), so the real comparison is the lanes objective. First node gate on np2 (tibia-np2-gate-2): 10/12 green; the two reds were the node GPU runner crashing (spiral-wgsl 0xC0000005 on the unchanged network_decides_on_gpu, green in the next arm) and my test line 'a >= b |> _assert_eq' parsing as a >= (b |> ...) (fixed with parens, memory spiral-pipe-binds-tighter-than-comparison). Mutant arm: parallel_climb and tied_elites fail exactly as targeted. Gate 3 (draft only, np3) is queued on the node.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 4u32, "2026-11-05T06:35Z", "tibia", "11-05 02:35 tibia, SLICE 1 RESULT ON THE REAL OBJECTIVE (node job tibia-cl1-cem-lanes, 6023 s, OMP 8, i7-4810MQ; lanes.spi PF1 objective = worth CheapClearWithin 94934 on the arena-spot cyclops camp; full plan 8 generations x 64 offspring x 100 training seeds; held-out = the same worth on seeds 1001-1100). Columns: lane, method (0 climb via evolve_par_by, 1 CEM AboveMean+Shrink, 2 CEM TopK 8+Shrink), train / held. Lane 0: -67400/-67350, -99450/-99700, -75650/-75250. Lane 1: -67600/-67700, -432700/-441200, -69000/-68750. Lane 2: -68200/-82950, -398850/-420400, -101950/-101300. Lane 3: -66900/-81250, -135500/-134750, -73450/-73700. VERDICT for slice 1 (Shrink width): the CEM mean update LOSES to the elitist hill climb on training in 4/4 lanes for both elite rules. AboveMean is far worse: half the population is elite, so the mean drifts toward mediocre children. TopK 8 is closer (1-50% worse) and generalizes more evenly (train ~ held in all 4 lanes), beating the climb on held-out only in lane 3 (-73700 vs -81250), where the climb overfit (train -66900, held -81250); the climb overfits lanes 2 and 3 by about 14k. So CEM is no improvement for this objective at this budget. The next test is slice 2's EliteSpread (elite-statistics width) at TopK 8, queued on the node; vultr is out for compiles tonight.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 5u32, "2026-11-05T06:49Z", "tibia", "11-05 02:49 tibia: PLACED in live tibia/src/network.spi (707e7157dc1e -> 3c8136221511, unstaged). It adds evolve_par_by (offspring per thread via parallel::for_index), the CEM trainer evolve_cem_by with cem_rule = { pick : TopK n | AboveMean; spread : Shrink | EliteSpread }, and 4 tests. PROOF: node gate tibia-np2-gate-3 (tibia's own build.ps1 -Files network on the synced mirror, the draft swapped in and restored): layout clean, cell budget clean, discovered 12, executed 12, passed 12 (c, rust and wgsl): parallel_climb_keeps_the_sequential_winner c+rust, tied_elites_go_to_the_earlier_child c+rust, the_mean_rule_does_not_overflow_on_large_scores c+rust, cem_never_ends_below_its_start c, plus the 6 existing tests. Mutant kills (gate 2, np2: fold '>=' and tie rank '<=') fail exactly the parallel and tie tests; np3 left those definitions unchanged. Mirror restored to 707E7157DC1E.")
inl note_of_tibia_learning_nuggets_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-LEARNING-NUGGETS", 6u32, "2026-11-05T08:15Z", "tibia", "11-05 04:15 tibia, SLICE 2 RESULT (node job tibia-cl2-cem-lanes-2, 2827 s, OMP 8; the same objective, full plan and seeds as slice 1; np3 compiled on the node with the mirror's compiler). EliteSpread (width = mean of the old width and the elites' mean absolute deviation): AboveMean, lanes 0-3 train/held: -99450/-99700, -276950/-284350, -398850/-420400, -269850/-277800. Lanes 0 and 2 are identical to Shrink, consistent with the best weights being found before the two width rules diverge. TopK 8: -67950/-82450, -203050/-208050, -68250/-68250, -72400/-72150. COMBINED VERDICT (slices 1-2, 4 lanes): the elitist climb wins TRAINING in every lane. On HELD-OUT, the medians are climb -74,475, TopK 8 Shrink -74,475 (a tie) and TopK 8 EliteSpread -77,300. EliteSpread is the best variant on lanes 2 and 3 (lane 2 held -68,250 vs the climb's -82,950, with no overfit) but collapses on lane 1 (-208k); AboveMean is bad with either spread. So no CEM variant beats the climb robustly at this budget (8 x 64). The climb stays the default; evolve_cem_by stays in network.spi as an option, gated and tested. If CEM is revisited: elitism inside CEM (carry the best child into the next mean) and a held-out-scored kept_best, since its edge is generalization, not training fit. The rest of the inventory (importance-weighted ensemble sampling, tabular CFR+ baselines, LSH features) is untouched.")
inl lib_row_ops () = Task ("LIB-ROW-OPS", "lib: fused row operations (map, reduce, scan per row, scope as a union Block | Grid): a correct rmsnorm, stable softmax, argmax, masked softmax with a typed mask, discrete sampling with one broadcast draw per row, masked reduce returning option, regret matching, L1 clamp, and scan_kind as a union; CPU arms first, then CUDA and WGSL", Story, P1, D6, 0u32, Planned, "LIB-TENSOR-VIEWS", "lib,transformer,tibia,gpu,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_row_ops () = Planning ("LIB-ROW-OPS", Minutes 900u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_row_ops_1 () = Note ("LIB-ROW-OPS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:06Z", "tibia", "Source: ML-library nugget inventory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\reports\\typed-transformer-20261102\\ml-library-nuggets.md section 1.2 (primitives.spi:200-830: row_config, local_*, block_reduce_2d named barriers :246, row_ templates :423-590). Do not copy: local_ln_l2 (:701-703) is not a norm; the limit.max/assert sentinels in local_get_prob and local_masked_reduce; the is_inclusive bool flag. One function with a scope argument replaces the twelve row_* variants.")
inl agile_decision_records () = Task ("AGILE-DECISION-RECORDS", "agile decision records, typed: every \"waits on the user\" becomes a typed record. resolution r = Settled : note_ref -> resolution () | ByTest : test_rule -> resolution verdict | ByBench : bench_rule -> resolution choice | ByModel : model_rule -> resolution choice | ByDefault : default_rule * backup -> resolution choice | UserBoundary : boundary * prepared_step -> resolution (). A phantom state decision open -> decision rule_written -> decision applied makes pre-registration a type: a result can only be recorded on a rule_written decision. ByDefault cannot be built without a backup. boundary is a closed union (GitHistory | Credential | Spend | PublicPost | Elevation | SecuritySetting | PersistentConfig). Verbs: kit agile decide <root> <id> ... writes one; agile next treats every kind but UserBoundary as agent-ready; agile user-queue prints only UserBoundary records with their prepared step; agile check fails a note that says the user must decide without a record", Story, P1, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:kit,kit,agile,typefeatureset,autonomy", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_agile_decision_records () = Planning ("AGILE-DECISION-RECORDS", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_agile_decision_records_1 () = Note ("AGILE-DECISION-RECORDS", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:08Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:07 x: filed from the user-waits groom (user 11-02: decisions waiting on the user get met autonomously and deterministically with tests, benches, typefeatureset modeling and backups). The first manual pass posted 33 text records as 'DECISION RECORD (typed; ...)' notes on 33 items at 2026-11-02 10:07. Those are this verb's migration corpus. Classification data: 115 items (Settled 41, ByDefault 27, UserBoundary 23, ByTest 17, ByModel 5, ByBench 2).")
inl kit_agile_rename_cost () = Task ("KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST", "kit agile rename costs minutes and hundreds of CPU seconds on the 11.5 MB backlog and loses the optimistic-lock race to concurrent writers; make it as cheap as edit or hold the lock", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,agile,team:kit", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_agile_rename_cost () = Planning ("KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_agile_rename_cost_1 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:14Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:1x FILED from a measured incident.\n- MEASURED: `kit agile rename <root> CIC-APP-SCAFFOLD KERNEL-APP-SCAFFOLD` on the 11.5 MB backlog. Attempt 1 ran from 09:28 to about 09:38 and was rejected: \"state/agile.spi changed since it was read; nothing written\". Attempt 2 started at 09:44; I stopped it at 09:59 at 424 s of CPU, because another writer had already changed agile.spi at 09:58.\n- Comparison: on the same file `agile edit` takes about 2 s and `note-edit` 1.5 s.\n- So rename does far more work than an edit, and under parallel lanes it can effectively never win the read-check-write race.\n- DOD: rename finishes in under 10 s on the live backlog and still updates every reference (deps, plus note mentions if it rewrites those), or it takes the write lock for its whole run so it can't lose.\n- REPRO: a copy of agile.spi under an isolated root, timed with Measure-Command.\n- WAITING ON IT: the 14 CIC-* to KERNEL-* renames (LEAN-KERNEL-NOTEBOOKS n16).")
inl note_of_kit_agile_rename_cost_2 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST", 2u32, "2026-11-05T21:05Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 17:0x kit: ROOT CAUSE found from main's 11-05 re-hit (WOW-WOWLESS-HARNESS rename: 14 min wall, 398 s CPU, never wrote). agile_rename_rewrite renamed_from built the output by appending each line onto everything written so far (written ++# line ++# ending), so every line copied the whole prefix: quadratic in the 14.8 MB file. The rename spends minutes there, then loses the read-check-write race to any writer that landed meanwhile. The lock is not the problem. FIX (unstaged, after the TRAIN32 snapshot, so TRAIN33): renamed_text splits into lines once (sm'.split_list), folds renamed_line over the list with the tally, and joins once (sm'.concat_list, Rust join). Byte-identical output including a trailing newline or its absence. New test a_rename_rewrites_the_item_rows_and_its_dependents_and_keeps_every_other_byte: item row, dependent deps, tally, title mentions counted, untouched lines, no added newline. Standards + ratchet clean. Box notebook job-1793912693013-kit-nb-rename (heavy line). DoD after install: time a rename on a copy of the live agile.spi (under 10 s), then main's WOW rename.")
inl note_of_kit_agile_rename_cost_3 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST", 3u32, "2026-11-05T21:55Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 17:5x kit: box notebook GREEN (kit-nb-rename2): rename_rewrite.spi 1/1 executed and passed, the new byte-preservation test included. The first run (kit-nb-rename) was VOID, not red: on the 100 pct box the cell spent 147 s mounting + 149 s compiling and hit the 300 s per-cell default; the module now carries --timeout 900000 on its first ///- line like its siblings. Size + cargo check of agile_rename_rewrite / agile_task_rename pending on vultr job-1793915560961-kit-probe33. Rides TRAIN33.")
inl note_of_kit_agile_rename_cost_4 () = Note ("KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST", 4u32, "2026-11-05T22:39Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 18:4x kit: vultr probe33d: agile_rename_rewrite 578 lines, agile_task_rename 443, cargo ERRORS=0 (box notebook already green). Ready for TRAIN33; DoD timing after install.")
inl hook_tree_lease_timeout () = Task ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", "The kit-tree-lease PreToolUse hook times out under load and Claude Code then blocks the tool call (cmd-string form, 45 s); move to exec form with onFailure or a longer timeout (user change)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "hooks,kit,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout () = Planning ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", Minutes 15u32, Load Light, Assigned User)
inl note_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout_1 () = Note ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:14Z", "add9e665535617d64", "add9e665535617d64 11-02 10:1x OBSERVED twice in one agent within about 10 minutes, while the box was saturated (TRAIN11 heavy-build window plus the pack16c compile window).\n- The PreToolUse hook `cmd.exe /d /c if exist %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\tree-leases\\*.lease pwsh ... kit-tree-lease.ps1` (timeout 45) hit its timeout, and Claude Code blocked the tool call.\n- The harness reason: \"blocking because Git Bash wasn't found, so only exit code 0 or 2 counts as this hook's verdict ... put the program in command and its arguments in args and set onFailure ... The user needs to do this; Claude should not change the hook.\"\n- Cause: pwsh startup alone takes 5-15 s on the loaded box (measured by pipe-testing subagent-hold.ps1), and the hook then enumerates every process.\n- OPTIONS for the user:\n  (a) exec form: command = pwsh path, args = the -File list, plus an explicit onFailure;\n  (b) a longer timeout;\n  (c) a cheaper guard that checks the lease pid without enumerating every process.\n- Assignee user, because the harness reserves this change for the user.")
inl note_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout_2 () = Note ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:01Z", "main", "main 11-02 ROOT CAUSE found in the star exchange (resilience #5): the hook runner can't find Git Bash because git is scoop-installed off the standard path. A cmd-string hook then counts only exit 0/2, so a timeout BLOCKS every Write/PowerShell call fleet-wide (main hit it at ~08:2x: 'blocking because Git Bash wasn't found'). USER FIX (settings/env, not Claude's to change), either: (1) set user env CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH=C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\apps\\git\\current\\bin\\bash.exe, or (2) switch the hook to the exec form (command + args) with onFailure continue. (1) fixes every cmd-string hook at once; (2) also stops a slow hook from blocking. kit has already made the hook itself fast and fail-open.")
inl note_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout_3 () = Note ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", 3u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "main", "main 11-02 CORRECTION to n2: fix (1) is ALREADY APPLIED. The user env CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH is set to C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\apps\\git\\current\\bin\\bash.exe (set by resilience, per its star-exchange #5). It only reaches sessions started after it was set, so the 7 long-running lanes still see the old environment until a restart. The remaining user step is optional: switch the hook to the exec form with onFailure continue, so a slow hook never blocks.")
inl note_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout_4 () = Note ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", 4u32, "2026-11-02T15:15Z", "main", "main 11-02 STATE after kit's star-exchange groom: kit switched EVERY hook in ~/.claude/settings.json to the exec form (command + args), which fails open on timeout. That was fix (2), which main had listed as the user's step; kit made it, and the user should confirm. kit chose this over CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH because that env var flips shell-string hooks to bash and mangles their backslash paths. With every hook in exec form the env var (still set, by resilience) no longer affects any hook. Verified hook forms: 5 of 5 exec.")
inl note_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout_5 () = Note ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", 5u32, "2026-11-03T01:03Z", "resilience", "11-02 20:58 resilience VERIFICATION (read-only, did NOT change the hook - assignee=user): BOTH recorded fixes are LIVE in ~/.claude/settings.json + user env. Measured now: 5/5 hooks in EXEC form (command + args). The problem hook - the tree-lease PreToolUse (timeout 45) that was blocking every tool call - is exec + onFailure=continue, so it now FAILS OPEN on timeout (the core bug is RESOLVED). CLAUDE_CODE_GIT_BASH_PATH (user env) = C:\\Users\\i574n\\scoop\\apps\\git\\current\\bin\\bash.exe (set). onFailure breakdown: continue on PreToolUse(tree-lease) + PostToolUse; ABSENT on PreToolUse#2(scoop,30s) + Stop(90s) + SubagentStop(90s) - and the Stop/SubagentStop absence is CORRECT, they must be able to block (the autonomous-gate IS a Stop hook that blocks by design; onFailure=continue there would defeat the gate). So the item's core issue (tree-lease timeout blocks all commands) is fixed+verified. REMAINING = only the user's formal confirmation/close, and optionally deciding whether PreToolUse#2 (scoop guard, 30s, no onFailure) should also fail-open - minor, not the blocking path. Recommend close after the user confirms. New sessions already inherit both fixes; the 7 long-running lanes got the exec-form fix (settings.json, read per-call) regardless of their stale env.")
inl note_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout_6 () = Note ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", 6u32, "2026-11-03T05:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 01:1x RE-DECIDED from n5 (resilience's read-only verification): the fault is FIXED on the box. All 5 hooks are exec form, and the tree-lease PreToolUse hook has onFailure=continue, so a timeout fails open instead of blocking. Stop/SubagentStop correctly have no onFailure. 90 Blocked. REASON: the one step left is the user's confirmation of kit's change to ~/.claude/settings.json (the harness reserves hook config for the user); it is decision 5 on main's 11-03 02:00 report. RESUME WHEN: the user confirms (then Done) or asks for a different form (then the user edits the hook).")
inl note_of_hook_tree_lease_timeout_7 () = Note ("HOOK-TREE-LEASE-TIMEOUT", 7u32, "2026-11-03T07:24Z", "main", "main 11-03 03:1x DECIDED by the agent (user 11-03: 'about the hooks, try deciding autonomously/deterministically with tests/benchs/typefeatureset/backups/lanes history'). EVIDENCE: kit's exec-form change to all 5 hooks (11-02 15:15) has the tree-lease PreToolUse at onFailure=continue (fails open), and Stop/SubagentStop without onFailure (they must block). resilience's read-only verification (n5) and hooks-test.ps1 on 11-03 03:0x both report 0 failed. Lane history: no hook-blocked tool call since the switch. RULE: keep a hook change when hooks-test passes and the lanes' history shows no regression. KEEP the exec form. Backups: ~/.claude/hooks/*.bak. Done.")
inl link_split_invariance () = Task ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", "Split-invariance oracle for linked units: cut each of the 5 mega samples (and lib, x, kit, Cells as corpus) at every top-level cut point into 2..N link: units, generated by the unit-graph tool. Each legal split must give byte-equal program output and equal typing verdicts to the single-unit build. REACH = legal cuts / all cuts, per construct crossing the cut (GADT index, existential, forall, HKT, prototype, phantom). It quantifies how much typefeatureset linking loses today (the monomorphic rule makes GADT/forall cuts illegal). Goal: reach 100% with equal outputs. Runs on node/vultr; it is the regression oracle every link change must keep", TaskKind, P0, D5, 60u32, Active, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", "team:compiler,compiler,linked-units,typefeatureset,mega,oracle", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_link_split_invariance () = Planning ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_1 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:25Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:25 x: filed from the user's typed-boundary direction (user 11-02 to x: 'shouldn't the typed boundaries between crates/modules be as type rich as iggy's (and the mega samples' reach)? would it be hacky or a stretch to allow gadts to work through somehow? try reaching a sota model ... this can't be forgotten otherwise kit will drift forever, all projects actually').")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_2 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 2u32, "2026-11-04T08:19Z", "compiler", "11-04 04:2x compiler: DESIGN (CPU-light; the build waits for a free node). (1) SPLITTER = a compiler subcommand, not a script: 'SpiralCompiler split-units <main.spi> --cut k --out <dir>'. The parser already holds the top-level block list in order. Blocks [0, k) become package 'model' (and every block it needs), blocks [k, n) become 'app' with ':< model' and 'link: model-'. model gets one !!!!Export per top-level name that app references (the free top-level vars of app's blocks that model defines), so the boundary is computed, not hand-written. One subcommand covers every sample and corpus file; no new .ps1. (2) VERDICT per cut, from tools that exist after pack34: compile both units for Rust, Zig and Gleam (the -Suite linked post-order). A cut is LEGAL when it compiles and the program output and exit equal the single-unit build. Every cross-cut call is classified by pack34's link warning: linked (no warning), or inlined with its reason (a function argument, curried, a non-primitive record), plus the unit-graph guard errors (YForall, YMetavar or YTypeFunction at the boundary, i.e. the monomorphic rule) as 'illegal: GADT/forall'. (3) REACH = legal cuts / all cuts, and linked calls / cross-cut calls, tabulated per construct crossing the cut (GADT index, existential, forall, HKT, prototype, phantom). The construct comes from the boundary signature (show_ty of the export) checked against those markers. (4) Corpus order: the 5 mega samples first (each cut is a node job; mega_brzozowski has ~200 top-level blocks, so sample the cuts at a stride of 10 for the first measurement), then lib, x, kit and Cells. (5) It becomes the oracle every link change keeps: a link program must not reduce REACH or change any legal cut's output. Next concrete step: the split-units subcommand in Program.fs and the core, with a regression sample whose 3 cuts are checked by hand.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_3 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T08:56Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:0x compiler: v1 MEASURED (node job compiler-splitu; base pack34 plus gleam-records plus the split-units subcommand draft kit drafts LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE\\1-split-units-subcommand.kitdo). 6 small Zig samples, 56 cuts: 22 LEGAL, 34 refused, 0 DIFFERS. No cut produced a wrong program (the oracle's safety property). Refusal classes: (a) a splitter bug: with nothing callable crossing, the app still declared link: model-, and an export-free unit writes no unit graph, so 'The link: unit model has no unit graph'. Fixed in the draft: no link: line when no exports (the app just opens the package). (b) 'model has a type error' as soon as exports exist (contract_* samples, likely polymorphic or GADT-typed exports under the monomorphic rule; v2 records the ETY id). (c) 'Runtime existentials cannot be destructured' (contract_existential_job_registry cuts 12-14): an existential crossing the boundary at run time, a construct limit. (d) array_i32/u32 refused at every cut because the splitter hard-coded |core-, while the samples use core-; |core- fails to load there. Fixed: the splitter copies the source's packages: entries and makes a relative packageDir absolute. v2 running (job compiler-splitu2): 30 samples, per-cut core junction, a class tally and REACH.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_4 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T09:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:1x compiler: MEGA PROBE (node, installed pack34): single-unit Zig compiles and runs exit 0 for mega_brzozowski_derivatives (6 s compile), mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel (8 s), mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency (17 s) and mega_zeta_structural_laboratory (10 s). mega_omniledger_erp_kernel is excluded: its F# host macros are not under a backend switch (Zig gets 'if v0 <> v1 then failwith ...'), so it is F#-only by design, not a codegen bug. v3 (job compiler-splitu3): v2 plus generics by source (a forall function stays as source for the app to specialize; only monomorphic functions are exported, which removes the monomorphic-rule refusals by construction). v4 (job compiler-splitu4): v3 over the 4 megas, about 20 stride cuts each. Note: mega_brzozowski also has modules runtime_workload/runtime_interned, which a single-file split does not carry, so its refusals may be that.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_5 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T09:13Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:1x compiler: THE ORACLE'S FIRST CATCH. v2 (partial, 31 cuts): 21 LEGAL, 2 refused (ETY-ValueRestriction when exporting an implicitly generic function, contract_existential cuts 11-12), and 8 DIFFERS: array_i32 and array_u32 cuts 2-5 exit 3 where the single unit exits 0. Root cause: Zig linked units allocate through the model's never-initialized spiral_gpa, a wrong program, filed as COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-ALLOCATOR (P0) with a fix under node review (job compiler-zigalloc). Every previous linked sample passed only because no export allocated. This is the oracle doing its job: link changes must keep DIFFERS at 0.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_6 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T09:20Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:2x compiler: v2 FULL CLASSES (partial file, 76 cuts): 41 LEGAL, 14 refused-model ETY-ValueRestriction, 9 refused-app ETY-UnboundVariable, 8 DIFFERS (the Zig allocator bug), 3 runtime existentials, 1 model UnboundVariable. Two more splitter fixes in the draft: (1) inline manifests 'packages: core-' on one line were read as no packages, so the cut lost core (=. and <- unbound: array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps); now inline and block entries are both read. (2) ValueRestriction came from exporting functions that are generic without saying so (no \\*, unannotated params: while_control's while'/set'). Now only a fully annotated head counts as monomorphic, and only those are exported ((x : t) or () groups plus ': ret =', no \\*); everything else crosses as source for the app to specialize. Next: one consolidated v6 on pack34 + COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-ALLOCATOR + this splitter, Zig over the 30 samples plus the 4 megas, then Rust (v5 shape).")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_7 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T09:24Z", "compiler", "11-04 05:2x compiler: ORACLE MADE PERMANENT (drafted). kit drafts LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE\\2-test-suite-split.kitdo adds 'test.ps1 -Suite split [-Backend Zig,Rust] [-Filter]'. For each matrix Split sample and backend it builds the single unit as the reference, then for every cut (split-units --cut k) compiles both units, builds natively (Zig side by side; Rust model rlib plus --extern) and runs. One row per cut: LEGAL, refused (with the ETY or Traced reason, recorded, not failed) or FAIL on DIFFERS or a native build-fail after both units compiled (a codegen bug). Summary 'split N cuts, REACH L legal, F fail'. Applied to a copy of today's test.ps1 and parse-checked. Lands with the split-units pack (and a matrix Split list: the 30 small samples plus the 4 Zig-capable megas), so every link program afterwards gets 'test.ps1 -Suite split' as its gate.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_8 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T10:19Z", "compiler", "11-04 06:2x compiler: v4 MEGAS (old splitter; node, Zig, ~20 stride cuts each): REACH 14 of 81 cuts legal, 0 DIFFERS. mega_brzozowski_derivatives 13/21, mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel 1/20, mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency 0/20, mega_zeta_structural_laboratory 0/20. Classes: 45 ETY-ValueRestriction (exporting implicitly generic functions; the current splitter exports only fully annotated heads, so a rerun should turn most of these into LEGAL or generic-by-source), and 22 existentials crossing the boundary (9 'Runtime existentials cannot be destructured', 12 'Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var', 1 'Existentials are not supported at runtime'). That is the existential column of REACH and exactly what LINK-GADT-FACADE (M2) and LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE (M3) exist to close. Next: rerun the megas with the current splitter (sanitized export names, annotated-only exports, inline packages) after the box v6 run.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_9 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 9u32, "2026-11-04T10:25Z", "compiler", "11-04 06:3x compiler: v6 ZIG ORACLE COMPLETE (box: pack34 plus COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-ALLOCATOR plus the current splitter; 30 samples, every cut): REACH 197 of 227 cuts LEGAL (86.8%), 0 DIFFERS. That is up from v1 22/56 and v2 41/76 (partial): the allocator fix turned the array DIFFERS into LEGAL, and the inline-packages plus annotated-only-export splitter fixes cleared the UnboundVariable and ValueRestriction refusals. Fully legal: 20 samples, among them contract_typed_quantum_teleportation 15/15, contract_schema_indexed_codec 12/12, contract_hkt 11/11 and contract_epoch_lease_seal 12/12. Remaining 30: 19 zig-build-fail (17 are COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES: Mut/heap structs in arrays across the link; 2 were primed export names, model_break', now sanitized in the splitter), 9 existentials crossing the boundary (6 'Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var', 3 'Runtime existentials cannot be destructured'; the construct column for LINK-GADT-FACADE M2), 2 EJP0040 (exporting frontier_hopacsota_globals_order's deliberately deep spin). Per construct: existential cuts lost 9; forall cuts now cross as source (0 lost); GADT indices crossed legally in the contract_* samples. Still to measure: Rust (node v6 Rust running), megas with the current splitter (v7 running), lib/x/kit/Cells corpus.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_10 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 10u32, "2026-11-04T10:31Z", "compiler", "11-04 06:4x compiler: v6 RUST ORACLE (node; pack34 + allocator + current splitter; 15 Rust-capable samples): REACH 45 of 66 cuts LEGAL, 0 DIFFERS. Classes: 17 rustc E0308 (mismatched types, the same per-crate generated-struct identity class as Zig's COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES: the same array samples fail), 2 primed export names (fixed in the splitter), 2 EJP0040 (frontier spin). So the struct-identity fix is needed on Rust too; Rust structs would need 'pub use model::X as Local'-style aliasing keyed by the same canonical shape hash.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_11 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 11u32, "2026-11-04T11:37Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:3x compiler: v7 MEGAS (node; pack34 + allocator + the current splitter: annotated-only exports, generics by source, inline packages, sanitized names; Zig, ~20 stride cuts each): REACH 49 of 81 cuts LEGAL (v4: 14 of 81), 0 DIFFERS. mega_zeta_structural_laboratory 20/20 (was 0), mega_spiral_proves_spiral_relative_consistency 11/20 (was 0), mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel 5/20 (was 1), mega_brzozowski_derivatives 13/21 (same). ETY-ValueRestriction went 45 -> 0: the annotated-only export rule plus generics by source closed that class entirely. 15 of the 49 legal cuts carry inline warnings (COMPILER-LINK-INLINE-DIAGNOSTIC: a non-primitive or curried export inlined instead of linking). EVERY remaining refusal (32 of 81) is an existential crossing the boundary: 16 'Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var', 8 'Existentials are not supported at runtime', 8 'Runtime existentials cannot be destructured'. So on the megas the REACH gap is now exactly the existential column, which is the scope of LINK-GADT-FACADE (M2) / LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH. Combined so far: samples Zig 197/227 (v6, before the struct fix; v8 with it is running), Rust 45/66 (v6r; v9r with the Rust struct fix queued), megas 49/81.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_12 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 12u32, "2026-11-04T12:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:1x compiler: v8 ZIG ORACLE (node; pack34 + allocator + splitter + COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES shape aliases; 30 samples, every cut): REACH 214 of 227 LEGAL (94.3%; v6 197), 0 DIFFERS. Struct identity class gone (17 -> 0). Left: 9 existential refusals, 2 EJP0040 (frontier spin), and 2 zig-build-fail, both while_control (cuts 3 and 4, exporting break' / continue'). Box repro: model.zig 'error: break expression outside loop'. break' is ':= break' () : () = $\"break\"', a backend text macro whose meaning depends on the CALLER's loop; no backend can export it as a function, so the splitter must keep macro-bodied definitions as source, like generics. Drafted LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE\\4-macro-bodies-by-source.kitdo (stacks on program 1, which stays frozen as handed to main for pack36): a definition whose head ends in '= $\"' or whose first body line starts with '$\"' joins 'generics by source'. With it the Zig ceiling is 216/227, and the remaining 11 are the existential column plus the deliberate EJP0040 spin.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_13 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 13u32, "2026-11-04T12:17Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:2x compiler: v9r RUST ORACLE (node; + LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES): REACH 62 of 66 LEGAL (v6r 45), 0 DIFFERS; left 2 EJP0040 and the 2 while_control break'/continue' cuts (E0267), the macro-body class covered by program 4. Running totals, all 0 DIFFERS: Zig samples 214/227, Rust samples 62/66, Zig megas 49/81 (all refusals there are existentials).")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_14 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 14u32, "2026-11-04T12:54Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:5x compiler: M2 MEASUREMENT ADDED. Draft 5-forced-source-option.kitdo (stacks on 1 and 4) gives split-units an optional '--source a,b' that keeps the named definitions as source in the app (as a GADT facade is inlined into each importer under M2). Node job compiler-splitu10 (v10, the node's git-root copy this time, not the stale t1101 mirror) scores every cut twice: M1 = today's rule; M2 = when a cut is refused over an existential, retry keeping its refused exports as source (each singly, then cumulatively) and count it legal if the linked build then matches the single build. Corpus: the 30 Zig samples (every cut) + the 4 megas (~20 stride cuts). Output: REACH samples/megas x M1/M2 and a class table. It is the reach row LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH needs for M2 (its rule compares M3 against M2 reach).")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_15 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 15u32, "2026-11-04T13:54Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:5x compiler: EJP0040 class explained and drafted (6-inline-recursive-by-source.kitdo, stacks on 1/4/5). frontier_hopacsota_globals_order's spin is ':= ^ spin (k : i32) : i32', an INLINE recursive function: the single build unrolls spin 2000 at compile time with a static k, but an export makes k dynamic, so the unrolling never ends and peval stops at 1000 levels (EJP0040). Not exportable by any mechanism, so the splitter keeps ':= ^' heads as source, like macro bodies (program 4). With 4 + 6 the Zig sample ceiling is 227 minus the existential column.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_16 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 16u32, "2026-11-04T15:13Z", "compiler", "11-04 11:1x compiler: pack36 INSTALLED (main: core 21F39A40 / host B266AA55, equal to the reviewed candidate; box + node, vultr building), so split-units is in the installed compiler. LANDED (unstaged): test.ps1 -Suite split (program 2, rebased onto the families suite) and the matrix Split list, 28 samples. The 6 samples whose cuts fail to build on pack36 (array_cell, array_heap_heap_heap, array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_union_pair_heaps on Zig/Rust struct identity; while_control's break'/continue' macro exports) are held back as 7-matrix-split-pack37-samples.kitdo, to add when pack37 brings the struct-type fixes and splitter programs 4/6. Both files plus samples/linked_zig_alloc_export were copied to the node's git-root copy (hashes match the box). First run of the landed suite on the node, on installed pack36: job compiler-splitsuite.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_17 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 17u32, "2026-11-04T19:34Z", "compiler", "11-04 15:3x compiler: SPLIT SUITE FIX. The first node run of the landed test.ps1 -Suite split (pack36, job compiler-splitsuite) hit its 4 h wall clock with no output: the Split list holds the 4 megas, and the suite cut every sample at EVERY point, 2386 cuts in all, 2187 of them megas (lean_cic 682, spiral_proves 654, zeta 473, brzozowski 378) x 2 backends. The oracle runs strided the megas to ~20 cuts. Fixed in place (test.ps1, unstaged): stride = max(1, floor(cuts/20)), so small samples keep every cut and each mega gets ~20; synced to the node (E8686E05). The pack37 combined review was stopped in its split phase for the same reason; its decisive parts were green (contracts Zig 620 rows 0 cells, examples Rust 518 rows 0 cells, linked 10/10, families exit 0). The strided split suite now runs on both pack36 installed and the pack37 candidate (node job compiler-splitsuite2).")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_18 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 18u32, "2026-11-04T22:07Z", "compiler", "11-04 18:0x compiler: strided test.ps1 -Suite split GREEN on installed pack36 (node job compiler-splitsuite2, arm 1): 556 cuts over the 28-sample Split list (megas strided to ~20 cuts each), REACH 273 legal, 0 fail (no DIFFERS, no native build-fail) on Zig and Rust; ~2.5 h on the shared node. Arm 2 (pack37 candidate) running; once green, the 6 held samples (program 7 of the Split list) land after pack37's install.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_19 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 19u32, "2026-11-04T23:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 19:1x compiler: pack37 INSTALLED on the box 19:01 by main (core 5F6F6E73 / host 08B00F25 = the reviewed candidate; undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack37-20261104-190103). Node ship and vultr source build deferred until kit's TRAIN26 regen finishes (after 21:00). The 6 held Split samples landed in matrix.psd1's Split list (program 7, unstaged): array_cell, array_heap_heap_heap, array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_union_pair_heaps, while_control.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_20 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 20u32, "2026-11-04T23:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 19:1x compiler: compiler-splitsuite2 stopped at 3.7 h of its 4 h wall clock (arm 1, pack36, took ~2.5 h on the shared node, so arm 2 could not finish in time). The pack37 arm reruns alone as node job compiler-splitsuite3 (5 h limit, candidate cache = compiler-pack37rev, the bytes now installed on the box). PENDING past 21:00.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_21 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 21u32, "2026-11-05T01:24Z", "compiler", "11-04 21:0x compiler: PACK37 SPLIT SUITE GREEN on the BOX against the installed pack37 (core 5F6F6E73): test.ps1 -Suite split over the full 34-sample Split list, including the 6 samples landed for pack37 (-Filter does not apply to this suite, so it ran everything), 616 cuts, REACH 333 legal, 0 fail (no DIFFERS, no native build-fail) on Zig and Rust, run single-flight-20261104-201515. pack36 on the node had 273 legal over the 28-sample list. The node rerun of the same check (compiler-splitsuite3) is now redundant; it is still running and can be stopped.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_22 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 22u32, "2026-11-05T02:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 21:2x compiler groom fix: test.ps1 -Suite split ignored -Filter (it walks matrix.Split directly, while the -Filter at :365 only narrows the other suites' sample list), so a 6-sample box check at 20:15 silently ran all 34 samples (it came out green anyway: 616 cuts, 333 legal, 0 fail). One-line fix, unstaged: the Split loop now keeps only cases matching -Filter when one is given (same semantics as :365). Parse 0; synced to the node git copy.")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_23 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 23u32, "2026-11-05T14:52Z", "compiler", "11-05 10:5x compiler: SPLIT ORACLE GREEN for the LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES closed-shapes fix (box, pack47 candidate = pack44 + program 3 + UnionTag; run 08:29-10:50 at box load 83-100%): test.ps1 -Suite split, full 34-sample list, 616 cuts, REACH 333 legal, 0 fail (no DIFFERS, no native build-fail) on Zig and Rust, run single-flight-20261105-082940 in the scratchpad pack47 cache. Same reach as pack37 (333 legal), so the narrower struct import loses no legal cut. pack48's program 4 only drops non-generated (hand-written) structs from the shape set; the split samples have none, so the result carries to pack48/49 (now on box, node and vultr).")
inl note_of_link_split_invariance_24 () = Note ("LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE", 24u32, "2026-11-05T18:06Z", "compiler", "11-05 14:0x compiler: SPLIT ORACLE GREEN on the INSTALLED compiler directly (box; installed pack50 at start 11:05, pack51 from 11:58: Rust output byte-identical, so the swap cannot change a row): 616 cuts, REACH 333 legal, 0 fail (no DIFFERS, no native build-fail) on Zig and Rust, run spiral-bin\\runs\\single-flight-20261105-110510. This checks LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES' fixes 3 + 4 directly rather than by carrying the pack47 result: reach is unchanged at 333.")
inl link_gadt_facade () = Task ("LINK-GADT-FACADE", "M2, GADTs through a link: boundary, iggy-style: the GADT and its typed facade live in a MODEL unit that every side imports and inlines at compile time (no code of its own). GADT refinement happens in each importer, and only a concrete erased codec, generated from the same GADT by reflection so encoder and decoder agree by construction, crosses as compiled code. Pilots: the Cells daemon protocol (request r, 5 replies), iggy's job/lease/slot message model (Rust and Gleam), and x's wire reads r / writes r. Tests: a round-trip property per constructor; NEGATIVE compile tests, where a wrong reply type at a call site in an importer unit must fail to type-check; split-invariance kept", Story, P0, D5, 35u32, Planned, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", "team:x,compiler,linked-units,typefeatureset,gadt,iggy,cells", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_link_gadt_facade () = Planning ("LINK-GADT-FACADE", Minutes 360u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_link_gadt_facade_1 () = Note ("LINK-GADT-FACADE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:26Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:25 x: filed from the user's typed-boundary direction (user 11-02 to x: 'shouldn't the typed boundaries between crates/modules be as type rich as iggy's (and the mega samples' reach)? would it be hacky or a stretch to allow gadts to work through somehow? try reaching a sota model ... this can't be forgotten otherwise kit will drift forever, all projects actually').")
inl note_of_link_gadt_facade_2 () = Note ("LINK-GADT-FACADE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T20:24Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:24 x: FIRST PILOT GREEN on pack17 (core E556D773EB123175), x-lgf2 on the node, built on compiler's lu3 probe; rule written before the run. Pilot lgf1 (drafts store LINK-GADT-FACADE\\lgf1): unit 'proto' declares the GADT request r = Ping :: request i32 | AskStatus :: request status_reply | AskCompile :: i32 -> request compile_reply, a GADT-typed facade reply_of : request r -> i32 -> r, and exports only concrete functions (i32 * i32 -> compile_reply, i32 -> status_reply); unit 'app' links proto (link: proto-) and calls reply_of with all three requests. RESULTS: (1) proto Rust 59 lines, rustc ok; (2) app.rs imports exactly 'use proto::{status_reply, compile_reply};', so the concrete reply unions cross and the GADT itself does not (compile-time only, as M2 intends); (3) rustc links app against libproto, and app.exe exits 14 = 4 + (2+3) + 5, so every call is typed by its request; (4) Gleam: app.gleam imports proto.{type StatusReply, ..., type CompileReply, ...}, so the same crossing works on the second backend (34 lines); (5) NEGATIVE: 'bad' (a compile_reply declared as a status_reply) fails at bad/main.spi:4:31 with Unification failure, so static safety survives the unit boundary. CAVEAT (compiler): Step B extern calls aren't in yet, so reply_of is inlined into app rather than called across the unit; for a GADT facade that inlining is the point anyway. NEXT for LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH: the same pilot as M1 (existential at the boundary) shows what is lost, and lgf2 should port the real Cells daemon protocol (daemon.spi's request r with records) once LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-RECORDS lets records cross on Gleam.")
inl note_of_link_gadt_facade_3 () = Note ("LINK-GADT-FACADE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T08:59Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:0x compiler GROOM (run start; Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (13 h; last note x). Next: once Gleam records cross units (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS next step), port the real Cells daemon protocol (daemon.spi request r) as lgf2.")
inl link_generic_interface () = Task ("LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE", "M3, generic exports through unit interfaces: <stem>.unit.json also carries the typed definition of each polymorphic/GADT-indexed export, the way Rust rlib metadata, GHC INLINABLE unfoldings and OCaml .cmx inline info work, and the importer specializes it with Spiral's partial evaluator. The compiled ABI stays monomorphic, so LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE holds at the ABI level, not the source level. Specialized copies land in the importer unit and count toward its 1000-line gate. Tests: split-invariance reach on forall/GADT/HKT cuts; an interface-hash change rebuilds exactly the importers", Story, P0, D7, 0u32, Planned, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS", "team:compiler,compiler,linked-units,typefeatureset,gadt", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_link_generic_interface () = Planning ("LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE", Minutes 720u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_link_generic_interface_1 () = Note ("LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:26Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:25 x: filed from the user's typed-boundary direction (user 11-02 to x: 'shouldn't the typed boundaries between crates/modules be as type rich as iggy's (and the mega samples' reach)? would it be hacky or a stretch to allow gadts to work through somehow? try reaching a sota model ... this can't be forgotten otherwise kit will drift forever, all projects actually').")
inl link_boundary_bench () = Task ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", "Pre-registered decision between boundary mechanisms M1 (existential at the boundary, today's advice), M2 (LINK-GADT-FACADE) and M3 (LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE) on the pilots plus the split-invariance corpus. METRICS: static safety (negative compile tests caught, must be 100% for any winner), reach (legal-cut share, by construct), generated lines per unit (gate 1000), cold and incremental compile time (rebuild scope after a model-unit edit), and runtime dispatch (bench with an A/A floor). RULE: M3 is the default iff its reach >= M2's, its compile time <= 1.3x M2's and the gate holds; otherwise M2 is the default; M1 stays only for open-world, runtime-loaded plugin boundaries. The verdict revises LINKED-UNITS-MONOMORPHIC-RULE's advice and TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1's concrete-signature gate", TaskKind, P0, D4, 15u32, Planned, "LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE,LINK-GADT-FACADE,LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE", "team:compiler,compiler,linked-units,bench,decision", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_link_boundary_bench () = Planning ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_link_boundary_bench_1 () = Note ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:26Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:25 x: filed from the user's typed-boundary direction (user 11-02 to x: 'shouldn't the typed boundaries between crates/modules be as type rich as iggy's (and the mega samples' reach)? would it be hacky or a stretch to allow gadts to work through somehow? try reaching a sota model ... this can't be forgotten otherwise kit will drift forever, all projects actually').")
inl note_of_link_boundary_bench_2 () = Note ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-02 11:02 x: STAR-EXCHANGE GROOM. Two received lessons constrain the mechanisms. (a) kit n4: existentials are compile-time only, so packing runtime-parsed values fails \"Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var\". M1 (existential at the boundary) therefore holds only for STATIC sets; it cannot carry runtime-decoded messages (Cells daemon replies, iggy events). Score M1 as N/A there, not as a loss for M2 or M3. (b) compiler n12: a unit-nominal GADT index often SELECTS constructors (state raw has only Raw), so erasing it as phantom broke 4 samples. M2's generated codec must keep every index that selects constructors, and a negative test checks that a wrong-index constructor is rejected after a round trip through the codec.")
inl note_of_link_boundary_bench_3 () = Note ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", 3u32, "2026-11-02T20:26Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:26 x: FIRST EVIDENCE ROWS (pack17, node, same harness, same 3-request protocol), M1 vs M2. M2 = LINK-GADT-FACADE pilot lgf1 (x-lgf2): GADT request r in the model unit, concrete replies cross. M1 = pilot lgm1 (x-lgm1): today's advice, index erased into any_request/any_reply unions at the boundary. BOTH give the right answer (app.exe exits 14 on Rust; Gleam builds). SIZE (generated lines): model unit M2 59 vs M1 104 Rust; importer M2 38 vs M1 66 Rust and 34 vs 52 Gleam, so M2 is about 40% smaller on both sides. TYPES CROSSING: M2 only status_reply and compile_reply; M1 also any_request and any_reply, with an impossible-case arm in every importer match. STATIC SAFETY (pre-registered metric 1, must be 100%): M2 rejects a compile_reply bound as a status_reply at compile time (Unification failure, bad/main.spi:4:31); M1 COMPILES the same mistake and only reveals it at run time (bad.exe exits 77 through the fallback arm), so M1 scores 0 on this case. Not yet measured: compile time (cold and incremental), the reach metric (LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE), and M3 (LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE, compiler). So no verdict yet, per the rule; on safety and size M2 strictly dominates M1 on this pilot. Pilot files: kit drafts LINK-GADT-FACADE\\lgf1 and \\lgm1 (run.ps1 in each).")
inl note_of_link_boundary_bench_4 () = Note ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", 4u32, "2026-11-02T20:28Z", "x", "2026-11-02 16:28 x: COMPILE-TIME ROW (x-lg-bench1, node, pack17, 5 rotated rounds per unit, rule written first: a difference counts only beyond the A/A spread). Medians: M2 proto 2,837 ms vs M1 2,998; M2 app 2,758 vs M1 3,090. M2 is 5-11% faster, but run-to-run spreads are 27-74%, because every build sits on the ~2.7 s dotnet start floor. VERDICT for this row: TIE at pilot scale; the pilot cannot separate the mechanisms on compile time. The cold-compile comparison needs a body that dwarfs start-up, i.e. the real Cells daemon protocol or the LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE corpus. A warm compiler server (--server-tcp) would also remove the start floor. Running table so far: safety M2 100% / M1 0% (decisive); size M2 about 40% smaller (decisive); compile time tie (pilot); reach and M3 not yet measured.")
inl note_of_link_boundary_bench_5 () = Note ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", 5u32, "2026-11-03T08:59Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:0x compiler GROOM (run start; Active = touched in 12 h). Parked to Planned (12 h; last note x). Table so far: safety M2 100% vs M1 0%, size M2 ~40% smaller, compile time tie at pilot scale. Next: a cold-compile comparison on a body that dwarfs start-up (the Cells daemon protocol or LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE), with a warm --server-tcp arm.")
inl note_of_link_boundary_bench_6 () = Note ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", 6u32, "2026-11-04T11:40Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:4x compiler: REACH ROW FOR M1 (today's linking, measured by the LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE oracle; 0 DIFFERS in every run). Samples on Zig (box v6, 30 samples, every cut): 197/227 = 86.8%. Megas on Zig (node v7, 4 megas, ~20 stride cuts each): 49/81 = 60.5%. Samples on Rust (node v6r): 45/66 = 68.2%. By construct: forall/generic definitions now cross as source (0 lost after the annotated-only export rule; ValueRestriction 45 -> 0 on the megas); struct identity (Mut/heap structs in arrays) is a codegen bug, not a mechanism limit (fixes COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES and LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES under proof); the ENTIRE remaining mechanism gap is existentials crossing the boundary: samples 9 cuts, megas 32 cuts ('Cannot dyn an existential into a runtime var', 'Existentials are not supported at runtime', 'Runtime existentials cannot be destructured'). So M1's reach ceiling is 100% minus the existential cuts: about 96% on samples and 60.5% on megas. M2 (GADT facade) and M3 (generic interface) have to be judged on exactly those existential cuts; the oracle's per-cut class column (results.tsv) lists them, and it is the corpus to rerun when either mechanism has a candidate. Running table: safety M2 100% / M1 0%; size M2 ~40% smaller; compile time tie (pilot); reach M1 measured above, M2/M3 pending candidates.")
inl note_of_link_boundary_bench_7 () = Note ("LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH", 7u32, "2026-11-04T17:58Z", "compiler", "11-04 14:0x compiler: M2 REACH MEASURED (LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE oracle v10, node job compiler-splitu10, Zig; splitter with macro bodies by source + --source; M2 = a cut refused over an existential retried keeping its refused exports as source, as a GADT facade is inlined into each importer). SAMPLES (30, every cut): every existential refusal became LEGAL under M2: contract_existential 11 -> 12/12, contract_existential_job_registry 11 -> 14/14, contract_capability_session 7 -> 8/8, contract_type_aligned_free_category 13 -> 14/14, contract_dual_interpreter_dag 8 -> 9/9, contract_indexed_free_program 9 -> 10/10, contract_generic_recursive_plan_fold 10 -> 11/11; most needed only the one refused export as source. Only frontier_hopacsota_globals_order's 2 EJP0040 cuts remained (inline-recursive spin, covered by splitter program 6, not in v10). MEGAS (partial; stopped after 5 h to free the node for pack38 reviews): mega_brzozowski_derivatives M1 13/21 -> M2 21/21; mega_lean_cic_bottom_up_kernel every existential refusal seen so far became LEGAL under M2, though some needed several exports as source (cumulative demotion). 0 DIFFERS in every run. READING for the bench: M1's whole remaining gap is the existential column, and M2 closes it on samples and on the measured megas, at the cost of inlining the facade definitions (as source) into importers. M3 (generic interface) still has no candidate; the rule's 'M3 iff reach >= M2's' now has a concrete M2 bar: 100% of legal-by-construction cuts on samples.")
inl typed_boundary_ratchet () = Task ("TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET", "No repo drifts: every repo's CI (kit, x, tibia, fiscal, spiral lib and apps, html, regex, dice, alphabet, blog) runs the typefeatureset census per unit AND per link: boundary (constructs crossing each boundary, plus the model_metrics M-scores against the mega samples) against a committed baseline, and refuses any decrease. The same gate runs locally in kit standards. A new repo gets it from the org template (TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1). DoD: a red CI on a deliberate drift commit in each repo (a scratch branch, never pushed), a green run on HEAD, and the baselines tracked", Story, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "EOIE-STYLE-RATCHET", "team:kit,kit,typefeatureset,ratchet,all-repos,linked-units", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_typed_boundary_ratchet () = Planning ("TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_typed_boundary_ratchet_1 () = Note ("TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:26Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:25 x: filed from the user's typed-boundary direction (user 11-02 to x: 'shouldn't the typed boundaries between crates/modules be as type rich as iggy's (and the mega samples' reach)? would it be hacky or a stretch to allow gadts to work through somehow? try reaching a sota model ... this can't be forgotten otherwise kit will drift forever, all projects actually').")
inl note_of_typed_boundary_ratchet_2 () = Note ("TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET", 2u32, "2026-11-03T08:20Z", "kit", "11-03 04:1x kit groom (user: kit keeps drifting; groom so it catches up). Related, not a duplicate: KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS is kit's local guard, refusing baseline rows for new code (git HEAD comparison). This item is the cross-repo CI ratchet; it can reuse that check once it lands.")
inl typed_link_sota () = Task ("TYPED-LINK-SOTA", "Typed links at SOTA: linking costs no typefeatureset expressiveness. Boundaries between crates/modules/units are as type-rich as one mega-sample compilation unit and as iggy's GADT message model, while the compiled ABI stays concrete. DoD: LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE reach 100% with byte-equal outputs on the 5 mega samples; LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH's verdict applied to the Cells, iggy and x pilots; TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET green in every repo's CI", Epic, P0, D7, 0u32, Planned, "LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE,LINK-GADT-FACADE,LINK-GENERIC-INTERFACE,LINK-BOUNDARY-BENCH,TYPED-BOUNDARY-RATCHET", "team:compiler,compiler,kit,x,linked-units,typefeatureset,sota,all-repos", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_typed_link_sota () = Planning ("TYPED-LINK-SOTA", Minutes 1800u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_typed_link_sota_1 () = Note ("TYPED-LINK-SOTA", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:26Z", "x", "2026-11-02 10:25 x: epic filed from user 11-02 to x: 'shouldn't the typed boundaries between crates/modules be as type rich as iggy's (and the mega samples' reach)? would it be hacky or a stretch to allow gadts to work through somehow? try reaching a sota model ... this can't be forgotten otherwise kit will drift forever, all projects actually'. Not hacky: GADTs cross at compile time (M2 shared inline model unit, or M3 interface-shipped generic definitions), while only concrete ABI code crosses at run time, which is what the monomorphic rule protects.")
inl agile_epic_dep_lint () = Task ("AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT", "kit agile check flags a dep on an unfinished Epic (an epic is a container: a child names its parent in a note, it never depends on it), and agile next explains when an item is hidden only by an epic dep", TaskKind, P1, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:kit,kit,agile,backlog-hygiene", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_agile_epic_dep_lint () = Planning ("AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_agile_epic_dep_lint_1 () = Note ("AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:34Z", "main", "main 11-02: found twice in one morning (the Lean/CIC agent on SPS-NOTEBOOKS, the regex agent on 23 of its own items), then swept backlog-wide: 67 open items depended on an unfinished Epic (no team tag 31, tibia 13, main 10, kit 6, fiscal 4, compiler 2, x 1). An epic depending on its children is fine; the reverse silently hides ready work from agile next. main cleared its own 10 (parent recorded in a note). List: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\GROOM-1102-MAIN\\epic-deps.csv. DoD: agile check reports each epic dep with the fix; a ratchet keeps the count at the current floor and lanes drive it to 0.")
inl note_of_agile_epic_dep_lint_2 () = Note ("AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT", 2u32, "2026-11-02T14:46Z", "main", "main 11-02 lesson for the lint: an epic dep cannot be classified mechanically here, because the parent link is recorded ONLY as the child dep (epics do not list their children, and the JSON has no note text). main cleared 19 parent-only deps (clear children by filing and name) and restored 5 that may be real prerequisites (BEND2-IN-SPIRAL, TREE-PAGES-EVERY-REPO, CI-COMPILER-FULL-SUITE, KINO-WITHOUT-ELIXIR, FSX-FROM-SPI). So the lint should separate the two meanings: a parent field (or :parent note) for membership, deps only for real ordering; then agile next can ignore membership.")
inl note_of_agile_epic_dep_lint_3 () = Note ("AGILE-EPIC-DEP-LINT", 3u32, "2026-11-02T14:59Z", "main", "main 11-02 related trap from the star exchange (fiscal #9): kit agile edit <id> deps X REPLACES the dep list (same for tags), so a 'fix' can silently drop real prerequisites. agile show first, then pass the full list. The lint should warn when an edit drops a dep that is not Done.")
inl lib_durable_append () = Task ("LIB-DURABLE-APPEND", "lib file_system: durable_append (append + sync_all) and replace_atomic (temp + sync + rename) with Result errors, Rust first", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:fiscal,lib,spiral,file-system", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_durable_append () = Planning ("LIB-DURABLE-APPEND", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_durable_append_1 () = Note ("LIB-DURABLE-APPEND", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:41Z", "fiscal", "fiscal 11-02 10:41 filed from main's epic-deps sweep (GROOM-1102-MAIN). Child of WORKSPACE-PRIMITIVES-LIB (parent named here, not as a dep). Today lib/spiral/file_system.spi has append_all_text / try_append_all_text (:1853/:1900) and rename (:303), but no sync_all/fsync anywhere in lib. Slice: durable_append (append + sync_all) and replace_atomic (write temp, sync, rename) with Result errors; Rust arm first, the other backends fail loudly; tests: append twice and read back, replace leaves no temp file. Consumer: FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG (outbox durability from lib, never from fiscal).")
inl note_of_lib_durable_append_2 () = Note ("LIB-DURABLE-APPEND", 2u32, "2026-11-03T17:20Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 13:20 fiscal: LANDED UNSTAGED in spiral: NEW module lib/spiral/durable_file.spi B9108D09 + one package.spiproj line after file_system_operators (next to peers' unstaged occupancy/pickler/markup/nameof_heal lines, untouched). A new module, not file_system.spi: that file is 2,183 lines (over the 1k gate) and carries another lane's 219-line unstaged C read_region WIP. API: 'durable_append path text : result () string' (OpenOptions append, write_all, sync_all) and 'replace_atomic path text : result () string' (File::create of path.tmp, write_all, sync_all, std::fs::rename over the target; the temp is deleted on any failure). Errors: 'the file could not be opened' / 'the write failed' / 'the sync failed' / 'the rename failed'. Other backends failwith loudly ('only the Rust backend syncs today'). Reuses file_system's public Rust handle types and helpers (rust_append_opened, rust_written_all, rust_io_ok). Tests (///> rust): durable_append_appends_twice_and_reads_back, replace_atomic_replaces_and_leaves_no_temp_file, durable_writes_report_a_missing_folder. PROOF on vultr (pack24): --check exit 0 (+ test bodies), non-vacuity probe exit 5 ETY-TermError; compiled --backend Rust (25,067 bytes, 5 sync_all sites), rustc -O builds, the binary runs all 3 bodies exit 0 with no probe or .tmp left in /tmp; MUTATION (expected 'ab' -> 'abc') exits 1 with 'the appends read back in order'. NOT YET: a Cells run (CI's lib tests on the next spiral push cover it; verify then) and directory fsync after the rename (Linux-only nicety; Windows cannot open a directory as a File). Consumer: FISCAL-ERP-EVENT-LOG.")
inl note_of_lib_durable_append_3 () = Note ("LIB-DURABLE-APPEND", 3u32, "2026-11-03T22:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:03 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793732410948-fiscal-confirm-landed2, t1101, pinned compiler core 2ABF22D79E6B6943 start and end, the landed files placed over the mirror and restored after): money 3/3, ledger 9/9, event_log 7/7, durable_file 3/3, lifecycle 10/10, document 6/6, p2p 14/14, posting 2/2, reports 3/3 -- every prediction met, every 'fails' negative recognized by Cells.")
inl note_of_lib_durable_append_4 () = Note ("LIB-DURABLE-APPEND", 4u32, "2026-11-04T04:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 00:13 fiscal: DONE (groom 11-04): delivered as lib durable_file (sync + atomic replace; live since 11-03 13:14, main accepted) and used by event_log's append_durably; Cells-confirmed 3/3 (job-1793732410948). Unstaged by the user's choice.")
inl note_of_lib_durable_append_5 () = Note ("LIB-DURABLE-APPEND", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:03Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:01 fiscal: RE-CLOSED. My 11-04 00:15 'set 100 Done' answered ok, yet at 07:2x the record read 90% Active again: the lost-update pattern (agile-status-lost-updates). Evidence: the note written in the same minute survived, only the Task record's progress/status reverted; tags unchanged (team:fiscal,lib,spiral,file-system). Delivered as lib durable_file (live since 11-03 13:14), Cells-confirmed 3/3.")
