inl note_of_regex_1_0_dod_1 () = Note ("REGEX-1-0-DOD", 1u32, "2026-11-02T14:45Z", "regex", "regex 10:2x FILED to follow the org convention (ORG-VERSIONING, adopted provisionally by x on 11-02; <REPO>-1-0-DOD per lane, cf. FISCAL-1-0-DOD, TIBIA-1-0-DOD, SPIRAL-COMPILER-1-0-DOD). REGEX 1.0 = (1) BRZOZOWSKI-PRODUCT n5 D1-D12 all met on one pushed commit (typed domain incl. the cell budget, engines, certificates, agreement, XSD front end with the fiscal oracle, test cells, 1000-line gate as a throw, CI benchmarks on the Pages site, CI green on ubuntu + windows, thin scripts, README/license/name, deletion plan); (2) the legacy mega sample ARCHIVED under the MIGRATION DONE RULE (REGEX-LEGACY-ABSORB n4); (3) REGEX-SOTA's throughput tables at or below the regex crate, or the gap and the cut decision recorded on the page; (4) on typed-units/1 (TEMPLATE-TYPED-UNITS-1) with its gates green; (5) the user's tag (a git action). Crate name candidate regex-typed (REGEX-PUBLISH n4). NEXT STEP: each criterion linked to its owning item so `agile next --prefix REGEX-` hands them out.")
inl train_on_node () = Task ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", "release trains run regen, crate gate, candidate and notebooks on the node and only the release build, smoke and guarded copy-back on the box", Story, P0, D4, 0u32, Planned, "", "team:kit,kit,remote,node,train,perf", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_train_on_node () = Planning ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", Minutes 300u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_train_on_node_1 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 1u32, "2026-11-02T15:05Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 11:2x filed. USER (via resilience 10:4x): the box is oversubscribed (905% of 800%) while the nodes idle; \"the user wants the nodes used\". DESIGN (code written, unstaged, parses; not yet run): launch-train.ps1 -Node <machine> re-launches itself as a PLAIN kit job (-NodeStage) so the box's heavy slot is only taken for the release. Steps: (1) parity: box vs node SpiralCompiler.dll hash + rustc --version, refuse on mismatch; (2) robocopy snapshot + lib copy, then remote.ps1 sync spiral+kit -Mirror <Name> (REMOTE-SYNC-OK required), then the live tree's manifest (src, scripts, compiler-contracts: spi/spir/rs/toml/spiproj/ps1/lock hashes) must still equal the snapshot's, else re-snapshot once, else refuse; (3) node: installed kit.exe at the mirror root, release-train.ps1 -NotebooksOnly in the mirror (regen, crate gate, candidate, notebooks); (4) fetch: node .rs hashes before/after the run; every changed .rs scp'd into the box snapshot and hash-checked; copy-back to the live tree only where the live file is unchanged since the snapshot (the existing guard); node verdicts fetched; (5) box: release-train.ps1 -Resume -Verdicts <node-verdicts> (new param: refuses unless every notebook of the box-computed set has a pass line) under the heavy gate: box candidate + release build + smoke. WHY THE SPLIT: kit bakes env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\") in 5 sites (rust_std_fs, rust_std_fs_mutation, kit_process, contracts_entry), so installed binaries build at the box path; live-tree writes stay on the box by rule; cross-machine compile determinism was proven 10-25 (0 diffs / 7,352 jobs). EXPECTED: box heavy time per train ~3.5 h -> ~40 min. ACCEPTANCE RULE (fixed before the run): TRAIN12 runs -Node; -Node becomes the default only if (a) its fetched .rs equal a box regen of a sample of owners byte for byte and (b) node wall time <= TRAIN10's box times (regen 75 min, notebooks 94 min). Box remains the fallback when the node is unreachable. Successor (Spiral-native, typed): EOIE-REMOTE-EXECUTOR / IGGY-MULTI-MACHINE event log.")
inl note_of_train_on_node_2 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 2u32, "2026-11-02T15:26Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 11:3x FOUND in TRAIN11's log: \"notebook set: 39 (39 use the binary; module notebooks of 1 changed packages)\" vs 69 in TRAIN10. release-train.ps1 derives the module-notebook set from `git status --porcelain -- src` = UNCOMMITTED changes, so a user commit between trains silently drops the module notebooks of every package changed since the last installed train (TRAIN11 carries kit_os_launch's breakaway fix and kit_jobs' message fix). FIX (to do with -Node, same scripts): each train writes a hash manifest of the tree it shipped (.cache/release-train/<Name>/shipped-manifest.txt); the next train's changed set = packages whose files differ from the LAST INSTALLED train's manifest, committed or not; fall back to git status only when no manifest exists. Rule: a test-selection input must not depend on the user's commit timing.")
inl note_of_train_on_node_3 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 3u32, "2026-11-02T16:47Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 13:0x TRAIN11 STOPPED at notebooks 33/39, all six non-green ENVIRONMENTAL: (1) five *_cli notebooks (standards, style_census, table_logs, table_query, table_sequences) compiled against the LIVE c:/home/git/spiral/lib/spiral/json_schema.spi while another lane's `^` heal had broken it (`^` removed from a :& group opener -> ParserErrors; repaired 12:27:46) - despite the log line \"notebooks read the lib at ...TRAIN11-lib\": notebooks that drive the binary under test let that binary resolve the DEFAULT lib path, so the lib snapshot leaks for them; (2) kit_lint_model timed out under load (slowest 306 s > 300 s). Resumed as job-1793637984834 (reruns only those 6, then installs). FIX for TRAIN-ON-NODE / release-train: pass the lib snapshot to the binary under test too (SPIRAL_LIB / SPIRAL_CELLS_LIB into the child env of every notebook AND whatever env the kit binary reads for its own compiles), and add a check that greps every notebook log for a lib path outside the snapshot and fails the train as an ISOLATION error (not a candidate failure).")
inl note_of_train_on_node_4 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 4u32, "2026-11-02T18:39Z", "kit", "kit 11-02 14:45 TRAIN12 node half FAILED at 12:46, and the root cause was dangerous. The box-side lib manifest was rooted at Split-Path twice of the lib copy (=.cache\\release-tree\\TRAIN12-lib), with dir \"spiral\". That folder does not exist (the files sit in TRAIN12-lib\\lib\\spiral), so the box lib manifest was EMPTY, and the reconcile computed drop = the node's entire spiral lib mirror. The only thing that stopped the deletion was ssh's \"The command line is too long\" on the inline Remove-Item list. FIX (scripts/launch-train.ps1, unstaged): the root is Split-Path once (=...-lib\\lib) for both the manifest and the reconcile pair, plus two refusal guards before any push or drop. (1) An empty box manifest refuses (\"refusing to reconcile <node root> against nothing\"). (2) A drop of more than max(25, 10% of the node files) refuses (\"a manifest root is likely wrong\"). Proof: the old root Test-Path is False and the new one is True; the parse check is clean. NEXT: relaunch TRAIN12 with -Node laptop when the node is free (main's pack16c node ship is retrying on \"target in use\"). Use laptop-ts for scp: bare `laptop:` no longer resolves since 09:54 (main).")
inl note_of_train_on_node_5 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T04:15Z", "kit", "User 11-04 00:1x (relayed by main): long heavy runs go to the node (and vultr) first; the box is the LAST machine to fill. Dogfood the train that way: the TRAIN17b relaunch (TRAIN18) targets the node first. Raises this item from backlog to the next kit train.")
inl note_of_train_on_node_6 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T04:44Z", "kit", "11-04 00:43 FIRST DOGFOOD: TRAIN18 launched with launch-train.ps1 -Node node -NodeMirror train18 -SshHost laptop-ts. Parity ok (dll 6B30D2F5, rustc 1.101.0-nightly 2026-10-17). The node half runs regen, crate gate, candidate and notebooks; then the box fetches regenerated outputs by hash plus the node verdicts and runs only -Resume -Verdicts (release build + install). Job job-1793767381784-kit-TRAIN18-node. Pending.")
inl note_of_train_on_node_7 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:44Z", "kit", "11-04 01:38 TRAIN18 node half RED at the crate gate after a clean regen: 231 changed owners published, 64 unchanged, 53 min on the node (the box took 78 min for regen alone on TRAIN17b). 294/295 crates under 1000; the one over was the new kit_heal_nameof (2120). The node pipeline itself worked end to end (parity, hash reconcile 2176+167 files, node half, verdict fetch path), so the dogfood mechanics are proven; only content failed. TRAIN19 relaunches node-first on pack33 once the node swap is done.")
inl note_of_train_on_node_8 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 8u32, "2026-11-04T05:51Z", "kit", "11-04 01:50 TRAIN19 launched node-first (job-1793771410815-kit-TRAIN19-node, mirror train19). GAP FOUND in launch-train's parity check: it hashes only the single-flight HOST dll (SpiralCompiler.dll 6B30D2F5), which is identical across packs; the compiler CORE (pack32 A63F4C2A vs pack33 D1379FED) is what changes. TRAIN19 is safe only because main hand-checked node core = box core = D1379FED after the 01:45 swap. Fix: the parity string adds the core assembly's hash (and the Cells runner hash), and refuses on any mismatch.")
inl note_of_train_on_node_9 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 9u32, "2026-11-04T07:41Z", "kit", "11-04 03:34 TRAIN19 RED at node regen (70 min): kit_window_wait and kit_machine_crowding failed ETY-UnboundVariable (option_value, free_mb). My S2 dead-code sweep of kit_machine_windows/windows.spi removed helpers those packages use through `:< kit_machine_windows.windows`; I had checked references only inside the file. windows.spi was restored to TRAIN18 and the sweep parked. 03:5x TRAIN20 launched node-first (job-1793778024444-kit-TRAIN20-node, mirror train20). Every new or changed crate was sized on the node first: heal 531 + findings 857, agile_lock 390 + mutation 932, do_facts 955 + receipt 106, census 892 + scoreboard 388, probes 307, measure 755, announce 818, todo scan 937 / merge 942, start_args 676, mirror 874, task_notes 860. The crate-gate draft (1010) is held back.")
inl note_of_train_on_node_10 () = Note ("TRAIN-ON-NODE", 10u32, "2026-11-04T08:30Z", "kit", "11-04 04:3x TRAIN20 STOPPED on purpose 45 min into its node regen. A box notebook pre-run of today's 15 new or changed test files (kit-new-tests-1104: 11/15) found 4 reds in TRAIN20's snapshot: three files gained tests without the notebook header/static prelude (start_args, task_notes, census: ETY-UnboundModule) and my scoreboard test expected 50000.0 where 5000.0 is right. All fixed in the tree; the re-run is going. Stopping freed the node and box for main's pack34 + toml-lib switch; TRAIN21 carries everything on pack34 + the toml lib. Also proven on the node: kit regen against main's toml-only lib (5 owners green, sizes unchanged).")
inl tibia_map_grids_typed () = Task ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", "tibia: port apps/map/run.ps1's map checks (walkability dump vs the committed golden, live-client scan agreement) into Spiral in apps/map, with the two grids as typed .spi data instead of results/arena-region-r45.txt and results/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt, then delete the .txt files", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,data,drift,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_map_grids_typed () = Planning ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_map_grids_typed_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", 1u32, "2026-11-02T15:48Z", "tibia", "11-02 tibia, parent MIGRATE-TIBIA-TSV (named here, not as a dep). The .txt files are still read by run.ps1:39-49, so per the deletion rule they move to their real format with their reader first. The comparison logic is pwsh glue doing real work, which also breaks spiral-first tooling. The -Update rewrite path becomes a kit/Spiral regeneration of the typed grid module.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_grids_typed_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", 2u32, "2026-11-03T01:13Z", "tibia", "11-02 21:1x tibia, HALF DONE (unstaged in tibia): the live-scan agreement check moved from apps/map/run.ps1 to Spiral. New typed whole-table modules results/rows/arena_region_r45.spi and results/rows/arena_spot_scan_r12.spi (the grids as table_rows Table literals, generated one-off from the committed .txt), registered under rows/ in results/spiral.toml and package.spiproj, plus results/map_grids.spi: frame records (region 1933,1350 r45; scan 1932,1349 r12), line_at/marker_from, region_walkable, and agreement () as fixed-width row walks (dy = k - 12, marks from column 4), mirroring run.ps1's loop. Tests (rust): the_live_scan_agrees_with_the_server_map = (252, 251), the exact counts run.ps1 printed (252 cells, 251 agree, 1 disagree, recomputed today with run.ps1's own logic), and the_grids_carry_the_frames_the_check_assumes (headers and the -12 first row). Node mirror memo-off (tibia-gates3, job map-grids-2): 2/2 green. Then run.ps1's PowerShell agreement block was REMOVED (the test enforces it) and results/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt DELETED from the worktree, unstaged (its content stays in git and in the rows module; only backlog history mentions it across C:\\home\\git). LEFT: arena-region-r45.txt is still run.ps1's comparison target for the live map dump (needs map.spi to emit the typed form and a live map run on the box), then it goes too.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_grids_typed_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", 3u32, "2026-11-03T01:21Z", "tibia", "11-02 21:2x tibia, second half done in the tree (unstaged): apps/map/run.ps1 now compares the live walkability dump with the typed row module results/rows/arena_region_r<radius>.spi instead of results/arena-region-r45.txt: it renders the dump into the exact module text (///- --no-respell, open table_rows, inl table () = Table \"<lines with \\n>\"), refuses a dump with a quote or backslash, and -Update rewrites the .spi. Verified locally: rendering the committed .txt as the dump equals the committed module byte for byte (9,042 = 9,042), so a live dump that matched before matches now. results/arena-region-r45.txt DELETED from the worktree, unstaged (no reference left in the tibia tree; its content is in git and in the rows module). Both map text tables are gone. Deleted paths: results/arena-region-r45.txt, results/arena-spot-scan-r12.txt. LEFT for 100%: one live map run on the box (apps/map/run.ps1 against the Canary world, needs the box free of kit's train) to prove the new comparison end to end.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_grids_typed_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", 4u32, "2026-11-03T03:08Z", "tibia", "11-02 23:0x tibia: REGRESSION CHECK green over the whole results package with the two new row modules and the manifest edits (node job results-suite-3, tibia-gates3 mirror at the current tree, memo-off): arena_rows 4/4, map_grids 2/2, row_census 2/2 (the 1,075 arena + 284 arm row counts), table_rows 1/1, all 4 test files green, build exit 0. (Earlier attempts failed only because consumer3's [string] -Files joined the list with spaces; the runner now splits on spaces and commas.) Only the live map run on the box remains for 100%.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_grids_typed_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", 5u32, "2026-11-04T04:18Z", "tibia", "11-04 00:18 tibia GROOM: parked to Planned (no note in 12 h). The regression suite is green on the node. NEXT: one live apps/map/run.ps1 run against the Canary world on the box, when no train or heavy window holds it.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_grids_typed_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", 6u32, "2026-11-04T04:21Z", "tibia", "11-04 00:21 tibia: back to Active, percent kept. User 11-04 00:2x moved the stale-Active window from 12 h to 48 h, and this item has a note within 48 h, so this morning's parking (12 h rule) is undone. The next step in the 00:2x note still holds.")
inl note_of_tibia_map_grids_typed_7 () = Note ("TIBIA-MAP-GRIDS-TYPED", 7u32, "2026-11-04T07:39Z", "tibia", "11-04 03:39 tibia: DONE, LIVE MAP RUN GREEN. apps/map/run.ps1 in check mode (no -Update) in a box compile window, against the Canary world files (canary.otbm, appearances.dat, items.xml): map.spi compiled to Rust (113,043 bytes) and built with rustc 1.101.0-nightly; the server's walkability dump matches the typed row module results/rows/arena_region_r45.spi (91 rows), and src/terrain.spi matches the server map (308 definitions). With the node regression suite already green (map_grids 2/2, arena_rows 4/4, row_census 2/2, table_rows 1/1), the map checks run end to end on typed rows: the old run.ps1 text-table comparison is gone, and the .spi row module is the committed golden that the live dump is checked against.")
inl todo_vs_agile_bench () = Task ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", "Benchmark the decentralized TODO-in-source model against the single agile.spi file model (write latency, lost updates, lock races, rename cost, read/query speed, lane concurrency), then decide TODO-AS-SOURCE scope from the numbers", Story, P1, D5, 60u32, Planned, "KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS", "team:main,main,kit,todo,agile,bench", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_todo_vs_agile_bench () = Planning ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_1 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 1u32, "2026-11-02T16:01Z", "main", "main 11-02 (user: \"we also should review why the task about spreading todo comments everywhere is parked, we gotta benchmark this decentralized approach vs the agile.spi file model\"). WHY PARKED: TODO-AS-SOURCE (P1 epic, 50%) was Paused only by silence; kit moved it back to Planned on 10-31, noting it is \"a deliberate destructive migration ... not abandoned work\" that needs a fresh scope decision. Its prototype migrate-prototype.py is archived (kit\\archive\\20261030-232045). The scanner KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS is 80%. No benchmark existed, so the decision had nothing to stand on. TODAY'S EVIDENCE FOR AGILE.SPI'S COST: every write rewrites the whole 11.7 MB file (1-8 s per note under load); one `kit agile rename` ran 15 min and 424 s of CPU, then lost an optimistic-lock race (KIT-AGILE-RENAME-COST); lost updates re-opened at least 2 items (FISCAL-PACKAGE-COVERAGE, LIB-RESHAPE status); batch writes hit \"file changed since read\" (tibia #8). PRE-REGISTERED BENCH (fixed before running): on a scratch copy of the backlog plus a scratch tree with the same items as TODO markers, measure p50/p95 latency of note/add/edit/rename/list/next with 1, 4 and 8 concurrent writers; lost-update count over 1,000 interleaved writes; full-text query time; and the git diff size per change. A/A on each side first (ab-needs-in-job-aa). Run on the node, not the box. DECISION RULE: adopt the source model for a class of items (code TODOs) if it wins p95 write latency and lost updates with no loss of query ability; keep agile.spi for epics and cross-repo items either way.")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_2 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 2u32, "2026-11-02T18:20Z", "main", "main 11-02 14:4x FIRST RESULTS (node DESKTOP-6E8C14G at ~99% CPU from other lanes, so latencies are loaded-box numbers; kit TRAIN11 AD5A8A62; scratch copy of the 11.3 MB backlog + a 925-file .spi tree; scripts and raw output in kit\\drafts\\i574n.github\\TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH and on the node C:\\home\\remote-stage\\todo-bench).\nHARNESS LESSONS (two VOID runs before the valid one): (1) a copied backlog carries its LEASE record, so the scratch copy started 608 h expired and EVERY write was refused (\"lease authority blocked ... should_wrap=1\"); fix: `kit agile begin <root> '<3-7 words>'` on the copy. (2) `kit agile add` refuses `--as` without `--note`; the target item was never created and the first run's \"write latency\" was refusal latency. Every sample now checks ok/refused/stored.\nVALID: agile.spi note writes, 24 per row: 1 writer p50 1.5 s / p95 2.9 s; 4 writers p50 2.0 s / p95 10.2 s; 8 writers p50 4.3 s / p95 8.6 s; 24/24 stored, 0 LOST at every width (kit's write lock serializes correctly). TODO-in-source marker write: p50 1-2 ms, p95 3-18 ms (A/A B/B2), no shared file, so no contention by construction. QUERY: agile.spi list --words 8.4 s, show 3.1 s, next 5.8 s; `kit agile todos` over 925 files 17.4 s (SLOWER than list). Diff size: agile.spi rewrites 11.3 MB per note; a marker adds 1 line to 1 file.\nDECISION RULE (pre-registered): adopt source TODOs for code items if they win p95 write latency AND lost updates with no loss of query ability. Write latency: source wins about 1000x. Lost updates: tie (0 vs 0). Query: source LOSES (17.4 s vs 8.4 s). VERDICT: NOT YET. The blocker is the todos scanner, not the model. Gate to adopt: make `agile todos` answer within agile list's time (an index or prefilter over changed files; KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS), then re-run this bench. Open anomaly: the todos query found 80 BENCH markers where 40 were written (double count in the output or the scan); check before the re-run. Note: production lost updates today (2 items) did NOT reproduce for concurrent notes, so they come from another write path (status set / edit), worth its own probe.")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_3 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 3u32, "2026-11-03T03:12Z", "main", "main 11-02 23:1x RE-TIMED with kit AF229BEC (TRAIN13c, 22:21) on the box, same backlog root: 'agile todos' 114,435 ms then 94,407 ms (roots=6, files=14,076, scanned=4,707, todos=9; skipped generated 6,241 + syntax 3,123), vs 'agile list' 2,476 ms. The scan is SLOWER than the 17.4 s of n2 because it now walks 6 roots / 14k files. VERDICT: still NOT YET, the gate (todos fast enough to replace the parked TODO list) is further away. For kit: the 9 todos cost a 14k-file walk each call; an mtime-keyed cache per root (the agile_todo_cache crate exists) or an index written at commit time would bring it under the list's 2.5 s.")
inl note_of_todo_vs_agile_bench_4 () = Note ("TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH", 4u32, "2026-11-05T08:10Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:1x kit groom (WIP cap: Active means a note within 48 h): Active -> Planned, last note 2026-11-03T03:12Z (53 h ago), progress kept at 60%. Resume from that note; nothing was lost, it just isn't being worked.")
inl py_rewrite_all () = Task ("PY-REWRITE-ALL", "Rewrite every remaining hand-written .py script in the i574n repos in Spiral (or drop it), and archive the originals; generated Python-backend outputs are out of scope", Story, P0, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "team:main,main,python,spiral-first,cleanup", "current", "current")
