inl kit_census_test_lines () = Task ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", "Census density ratchet excludes test-block lines from its denominators", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,team:kit,standards,census", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_census_test_lines () = Planning ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_census_test_lines_1 () = Note ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", 1u32, "2026-11-03T03:31Z", "kit", "Origin: REMOTE-EXEC-S6 (11-02). The kit-style-check ratchet refused compiler's 9-line compile-fail block because test lines lower per-line density (forall 2/105 -> 2/114, gadt-case 6/105 -> 6/114) while the model stayed the same. Adding a test should never regress a package. DoD: kit_style_census counts lines under ///> test blocks separately and leaves them out of density denominators; a census test shows a package gaining a test block keeps or raises its densities; ratchet clean on all 504 packages (a higher density is not a regression). Constraint: census.rs is at 996 lines, so split the census crate first. Workaround until then: write compile-fail tests as one typed expression (S6 did).")
inl note_of_kit_census_test_lines_2 () = Note ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T05:37Z", "kit", "11-03 01:4x kit: scope widened by main (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n15), accepted. In regex, gadt-case rose 20 -> 25 while density fell 11.1 -> 9.2/kloc, because the new typed work (checker-verdict unions, `:!` nominals) has no census column. One census change covers both distortions:\n(a) test-block lines leave the density denominators (this item's origin);\n(b) new columns: verdict-union = a `:|` returned by a check_*/verdict function whose cases name a property, and nominal = `:! x = T`.\nBoth columns are rising-is-better and start at their measured values, so no package regresses on the day they land. Order: split the kit_style_census crate first (census.rs 996 lines); then the probes and a census test showing that a bool -> named-verdict rewrite raises verdict-union density and a package gaining a test block keeps its densities; then a full baseline merge on all packages. That merge is sanctioned because the columns are new.")
inl note_of_kit_census_test_lines_3 () = Note ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T10:46Z", "kit", "11-03 06:5x kit: ROOT BUG FOUND and fixed in a draft; now P0 and FIRST in KIT-CATCH-UP's order. kit_style_census/probes.spi `regressed`, the MayNotFall arm (feature probes such as forall and gadt-case), read: rate < base*0.95 - 0.5 && before - now > before_lines - now_lines. When lines GROW and the count stays the same, before-now = 0 > (negative line delta) is true, so ADDING typed code reads as losing features. KIT-ENTRY-X-S1 hit it: replacing kit_coordinator_model's status_after word:string with a job_event union read as forall 2/105 -> 2/116 and gadt-case 6/105 -> 6/116, \"regression\". FIX: add `now < before` (a feature loss needs a lower count), plus the test `regressed MayNotFall 2 105 2 116 = false`. All existing probe tests keep their meaning (halving GADTs still fails; deleting dead code with its lines is still a prune). probes.spi 2/2 on the box.\nBLOCKER: census.rs regenerates to 1002 lines (996 + 6), over the gate; the regen tool published it, so I restored census.rs and probes.spi from the TRAIN14c snapshot (hash-verified; HEAD lacks the unstaged 11-02 census work). Draft: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES\\ (probes.spi with the fix, census.rs.1002, and kit_coordinator_model.model.spi with the S1 job_event rewrite, also parked because the current rule refuses it).\nPLAN: (1) split kit_style_census into linked crates (memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes; keep the probe GADT inside one unit, crossing with primitives/arrays only); (2) land the MayNotFall fix; (3) test lines out of the density denominators; (4) main's verdict-union and nominal columns; (5) a sanctioned full baseline merge, since the columns are new. Every KIT-ENTRY-X slice waits on (2).")
inl note_of_kit_census_test_lines_4 () = Note ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T12:23Z", "kit", "11-03 08:2x kit: STEPS (1) AND (2) DONE (unstaged; ships next train). The census is 4 linked crates, all host-free (the old census.spi had 10 host macros) and all under 1000 lines:\n- kit_style_probes (287): the probe GADT model, the MayNotFall fix, and a runtime probe table (unrolled once; the per-step inlining had made measure.rs 1060). Exports probe_specs, probe_regressed and probe_falls, all primitive-shaped, so the direction union never crosses a boundary.\n- kit_style_measure (625): package discovery (kit_os_files.entry_names, lib dirs), package text, str::lines counting, regex counting via kit_os_search.regex_matches. Exports packages_under and measured : array_base probe_row.\n- kit_style_baseline (488): CensusCount rows parsed ONCE into array_base baseline_entry (the old entry_of re-scanned the text per probe per package), plus rendering and merge.\n- kit_style_census (750, was 996 with legacy host code): typed census_mode, verdicts and report; 7 linked calls.\nPROOF (box job-1793706952775): probes 2/2, measure 1/1, baseline 1/1, census_cli 3/3. A/B against the installed kit over all of src: --census byte-identical (513 lines), --ratchet identical, and a freshly written baseline file hash-identical.\nTraps hit (in memory): `join` as a local made a definition vanish (reported as unbound); a local `:= ^` loop unrolled until a 180 s compile timeout (use top-level `:~ ^`); `pwsh -File` drops array args (use &).\nNEXT: steps (3) test lines out of the denominators + (4) the nominal and verdict-union columns, then (5) the sanctioned full merge; plan in scratchpad census-step34.md.")
inl note_of_kit_census_test_lines_5 () = Note ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", 5u32, "2026-11-03T12:45Z", "kit", "11-03 08:5x kit: DONE (unstaged; ships next train). All five steps.\n(3) kit_style_measure counts CODE lines: lines inside ///> <target> test regions, from the marker up to ///> _, leave the denominator; probe counts still cover every line (drift inside tests is still drift). Test: a 6-line file with a 3-line test region.\n(4) Main's columns are new MayNotFall probes in kit_style_probes: nominal (^:! name) and verdict-union (a :| named verdict, outcome, refusal, fault, violation, check or change). Example: kit_coordinator_model now reads nominal=4 verdict-union=1.\n(5) Sanctioned full merge, legitimate because the MEASURE changed, not the code. Before it, the candidate ratchet against the old baseline gave 2 regressions; after --baseline-merge standards/census.spi src (512 packages), regressions=0. Old baseline archived: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\census.spi.before-test-lines-merge-20261103-0834.\nUnblocked: the KIT-ENTRY-X-S1 job_event rewrite (unparked) passes the ratchet; model.spi 3/3 (rust, gleam, compile-fail). Census CLI 3/3. Crates: probes 295, measure 755, baseline 488, census 750.\nEffect: adding typed code (a union replacing strings, a nominal, a named verdict) can no longer read as a typefeatureset loss; test blocks no longer dilute densities.")
inl note_of_kit_census_test_lines_6 () = Note ("KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T23:51Z", "kit", "11-04 20:0x kit: field note: the fix is in the tree but not installed (trains 15-25 failed), so the installed census still counts test lines and reports 11 false density regressions against the test-free baseline (list on TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n47). Resolves itself when TRAIN26 installs.")
inl gleam_float_mod () = Task ("GLEAM-FLOAT-MOD", "codegenGleam emits float % as %. (an operator Gleam does not have), so any program taking a float remainder fails gleam build with a syntax error; emit a spiral_fmod helper (truncated remainder, C fmod) instead", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,gleam,codegen,bug", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_gleam_float_mod () = Planning ("GLEAM-FLOAT-MOD", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_gleam_float_mod_1 () = Note ("GLEAM-FLOAT-MOD", 1u32, "2026-11-03T04:09Z", "compiler", "11-03 00:1x compiler: found by the run.py port evaluator (qasm_eval float_arith BMod) on the node Cells gate: main.gleam let v1981 = v1944 %. v1947 -> error: Syntax error, This operator has no value on its right side. Program GLEAM-FLOAT-MOD\\1-gleam-float-fmod.kitdo (1 replacement on pack21 live 7FBA6F79F252D4DE): Mod on a float operand emits spiral_fmod(a, b) = a -. t *. b with t = floor or ceiling of a /. b (toward zero), plus import gleam/float; integer % is unchanged. Node review compiler-gleamfmod running (qasm_eval gate with the candidate + examples Gleam A/B vs installed pack21).")
inl note_of_gleam_float_mod_2 () = Note ("GLEAM-FLOAT-MOD", 2u32, "2026-11-03T04:20Z", "compiler", "11-03 00:1x compiler: PROVEN, handed to main as pack22 (1 program, dry run reproduces source core 8C422D3E28627CCA from live pack21; R2R SpiralCompiler.dll 6B30D2F521660878, core 43CAC3DC4EFD7CA3). Node: qasm_eval.spi gate with the candidate 4/4 on rust and gleam (gleam build failed before); examples -Backend Gleam 441 rows vs installed pack21, 0 differing cells.")
inl note_of_gleam_float_mod_3 () = Note ("GLEAM-FLOAT-MOD", 3u32, "2026-11-03T04:42Z", "compiler", "11-03 00:4x compiler: DONE. pack22 is live on the box (SpiralCompilerCore.dll 43CAC3DC4EFD7CA3, tree spiral_compiler.fs 8C422D3E28627CCA has the spiral_fmod arm).")
inl float_mod_truncated () = Task ("FLOAT-MOD-TRUNCATED", "Float remainder disagrees across backends: C emits double % double (gcc rejects it), Python and Lua emit their floored %, so -7.5 % 2.0 gives 0.5 where Rust/Zig/F#/Gleam give -1.5; emit fmod (C), math.fmod (Python, Lua)", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,c,python,lua,codegen,bug", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_float_mod_truncated () = Planning ("FLOAT-MOD-TRUNCATED", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_float_mod_truncated_1 () = Note ("FLOAT-MOD-TRUNCATED", 1u32, "2026-11-03T04:42Z", "compiler", "11-03 00:4x compiler: found while checking the GLEAM-FLOAT-MOD sample on other backends with live pack22. tmp/samples/float_mod_truncated (7.5 % 2.0 = 1.5 and -7.5 % 2.0 = -1.5, exit 15): C emits double % double (gcc: invalid operands to binary %); Python and Lua emit their floored %, so -7.5 % 2.0 = 0.5; Rust, F# and Zig (@rem) truncate. Program FLOAT-MOD-TRUNCATED\\1-fmod-c-cpp-python-lua.kitdo (4 replacements on 8C422D3E28627CCA, each anchor unique): C fmod/fmodf + math.h on a float operand; C++ fmod + cmath; Python math.fmod on a float operand; Lua math.fmod for every Mod (it already did for ints, so the int arm collapses). Node review compiler-floatmod running: sample on C/Python/Lua for both arms + examples C A/B.")
inl note_of_float_mod_truncated_2 () = Note ("FLOAT-MOD-TRUNCATED", 2u32, "2026-11-03T05:04Z", "compiler", "11-03 01:0x compiler: PROVEN, handed to main as pack23 (dry run reproduces source core 28F212AEFACE68EC from live pack22 8C422D3E28627CCA; R2R SpiralCompiler.dll 6B30D2F521660878, core 489EA99474EDE920). Node: float_mod_truncated installed C gcc-fails / Python 1 / Lua 1 -> candidate 15 on all three; examples A/B vs installed: C 557, Python 445, Cpp 17 rows 0 differing cells; Lua 442 rows had one compile timeout (frontier_format_any_union, overlapped a Cells gate), alone 0 differing cells on both arms.")
inl note_of_float_mod_truncated_3 () = Note ("FLOAT-MOD-TRUNCATED", 3u32, "2026-11-03T06:00Z", "compiler", "11-03 02:00 compiler: nothing left on the compiler side; waits only on main's pack23 install chain (box live core still pack22 43CAC3DC4EFD7CA3 at 02:00). Set Done once SpiralCompilerCore.dll is 489EA99474EDE920. Lease released at the end of the autonomous window.")
inl note_of_float_mod_truncated_4 () = Note ("FLOAT-MOD-TRUNCATED", 4u32, "2026-11-03T06:54Z", "compiler", "11-03 02:5x compiler: DONE. pack23 installed on box (core 489EA99474EDE920 verified live), node (swap in place, launch exit 0) and vultr (linux core 5AE11DBAB747990F, launch exit 0), per main 02:53.")
inl kit_windows_cli_linux () = Task ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", "windows_cli heavy-job tests fail on Linux: the heavy wrapper never starts the job", TaskKind, P2, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,team:kit,remote,vultr,tests", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_windows_cli_linux () = Planning ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_1 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 1u32, "2026-11-03T05:50Z", "kit", "Origin 11-03 00:0x (EOIE-WINDOW-ANNOUNCE proof on vultr): src/kit_machine_windows/windows_cli.spi passes 17/19 with the candidate binary. The two failures are a_heavy_job_waits_for_a_live_window_and_releases_its_own (\"missing waiting id=win-\": the job window file is empty) and a_stopped_heavy_job_leaves_no_window_behind (\"the job never started\" after 20 s). Both drive fake_gate () gate.ps1 and the heavy-wrapper.ps1 (-MaxMinutes) path, so they look Windows-bound. No valid A/A yet: /usr/local/bin/kit on vultr is a TRAIN11 build and fails all 19. They passed on the box in TRAIN13c. DoD: find why the heavy wrapper does not start under pwsh on Linux and fix it, or gate these two tests with a typed platform predicate (kit_os_machine.is_windows) and state why; windows_cli 19/19 on vultr with the candidate.")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_2 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 2u32, "2026-11-03T05:52Z", "kit", "11-03 01:5x kit lead: the heavy path writes jobs/<id>/heavy-wrapper.ps1 (kit_job_control/control.spi:99 amends its -MaxMinutes). Next: find where the wrapper is launched and check for Windows-only process flags. kit_cli_check/cli.spi:167 already uses Command::new(\"pwsh\").creation_flags(0x0800_0000), so look for an unguarded or cfg(windows)-only launch in the heavy start path (kit_job_host / kit_job_gate). On Linux, where that path is compiled out, the job would never start, which matches both symptoms.")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_3 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 3u32, "2026-11-03T05:54Z", "kit", "11-03 01:5x kit lead 2: the heavy slot handshake is Windows-only. kit_job_slot/slot.spi:63 slot_free probes named mutexes with OpenMutexW under #[cfg(windows)], and kit_jobs/jobs.spi:86 holds a heavy job until its log shows \"Invoke-Heavy: acquired slot\" (from heavy-wrapper.ps1 Invoke-Heavy, whose slots are Windows mutexes). Check the non-windows arm of slot_free and Invoke-Heavy on Linux; if the slot is never acquired, the job never starts, which matches both failures. The fix belongs in the boundary package: a per-OS slot primitive (a lock file on unix), with Spiral deciding.")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_4 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 4u32, "2026-11-03T05:54Z", "kit", "11-03 01:5x kit correction to lead 2: slot_free is not the blocker. Its #[cfg(not(windows))] probe returns true, so the Spiral side always sees a free slot. The suspect is Invoke-Heavy inside the generated heavy-wrapper.ps1: if it takes a \"Global\\spiral-heavy-job\" named mutex through .NET, that may throw or never be acquired on Linux, so \"Invoke-Heavy: acquired slot\" never appears and jobs.spi:86 keeps the job held. Next step: run the wrapper of a vultr fixture job by hand and read its stderr.")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_5 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 5u32, "2026-11-03T05:56Z", "kit", "11-03 01:5x kit: the probe attempt failed because I guessed the jobs root (KIT_JOBS_ROOT is not what the vultr host reads). Next: get the root from kit_jobs.host.jobs_root (LOCALAPPDATA / XDG_CACHE_HOME / ~/.cache fallback per 11-02), run `kit job start --heavy probe 60000 /bin/true` with the candidate binary, then read that job folder: heavy-wrapper.ps1, stderr.log, and whether \"Invoke-Heavy: acquired slot\" ever appears.")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_6 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 6u32, "2026-11-03T05:58Z", "kit", "11-03 01:59 kit: vultr jobs root is /root/.cache/kit. `kit job start --heavy` refuses unless KIT_HEAVY_GATE points at spiral scripts/heavy.ps1 or it runs inside a spiral checkout. windows_cli supplies fake_gate () as gate.ps1, so the next check is that fixture gate under Linux pwsh: does it print \"Invoke-Heavy: acquired slot\", and does the wrapper run it there? Repro: KIT_HEAVY_GATE=<fixture gate.ps1> plus the candidate binary, then read job-*/stderr.log.")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_7 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 7u32, "2026-11-03T08:00Z", "kit", "11-03 03:5x kit PAUSE (main: the 21:00 run was armed early by mistake; run paused). ROOT CAUSE FOUND: on Unix, kit_jobs/host.spi process_alive returned true only for pid 0 or the caller's parent, so kit_job_slot first_live_ticket treats every heavy-queue ticket as dead. first= stays empty and a --heavy job waits on heavy-slot forever (reproduced on vultr: state=queued waiting_for=heavy-slot, slot file 'first='). This is a production bug for vultr heavy jobs, not just the tests. FIX IN TREE, UNPROVEN: the unix arm is now pid == 0 || /proc/<pid> exists. NEXT: regen the owners of kit_jobs.host, build kit-cli on vultr, rerun windows_cli (expect 19/19) and the heavy probe. Not in TRAIN14c (snapshot 03:22). Ruled out: /tmp full (it was full and also broke detached starts, but the failure persists with free space); mutex (the fixture gate has none).")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_8 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 8u32, "2026-11-03T14:06Z", "kit", "11-03 kit: ROOT CAUSE, from the ubuntu leg of kit CI run 41602520066: a killed child stays a zombie and keeps /proc/<pid>, so process_alive (pid==0 || /proc exists, already at HEAD 1266f9d) still reported it alive -> 'stopped 0 of 1' and both windows_cli heavy tests failed. FIX in the tree: new boundary package kit_os_process (one-line sysinfo primitives: listing_of/status_in/zombie_status/dead_status; process_running = listed and not Zombie/Dead; test block). kit_jobs.host process_alive becomes one Spiral line, and the legacy Windows FFI block (lint row 469) is gone, not relocated. sysinfo was added to kit_jobs plus its 5 direct callers (job_host, job_host_request, job_slot, machine_windows, window_run). Proof job-1793714710343-kit-ci-heal on the box; Linux proof next on vultr (hold lifted 11-03).")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_9 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 9u32, "2026-11-03T21:52Z", "kit", "11-03 18:5x kit: LINUX PROOF (vultr round 10, kit built from today's tree, pinned pack24 compiler): windows_cli 19/19 PASS (was red on ubuntu CI); the zombie-aware liveness (kit_os_process via sysinfo status) fixed it. stop_cli 14/15: the one failure is killing_only_the_supervisor_takes_the_whole_job_tree_down, the same test ubuntu CI failed this morning. Killing only the supervisor leaves the job's children beating on Linux; Windows ties them with a Job Object. FIX (open): in kit_job_supervise's Linux spawn, start the child in its own process group with PR_SET_PDEATHSIG=SIGKILL (pre_exec setpgid + prctl), so the tree dies with its supervisor. Prove with stop_cli on vultr. Other CLI checks on Linux all pass: windows/wait/run/claim cli_check/census/grep/links/experiments/standards/edit/table_test/kit_cli windows/ps/logs/sequences.")
inl note_of_kit_windows_cli_linux_10 () = Note ("KIT-WINDOWS-CLI-LINUX", 10u32, "2026-11-03T22:48Z", "kit", "11-03 18:5x kit (tree, after TRAIN17): process_alive is now a LINKED unit, kit_process_alive (alive.spi, 41-line crate; export kit_process_alive : u64 -> bool, test block covers pid 0, this process, and an unused pid). kit_jobs.host calls it across the link, so the sysinfo composition (+26 lines per crate) is no longer inlined into the 15 call sites. Proven on kit_jobs: jobs.rs 914 -> 888, 1 'kit_process_alive::' call, 0 sysinfo. All 15 call sites swap sysinfo for the unit's path dep; the 15 crates that never called it drop sysinfo entirely. Lock refreshed offline. This also lets kit_window_run take the tree-label guard back (KIT-ENTRY-X-S2 n4). Proof: job-1793746025247-kit-precheck-alive, 31 owners plus cargo check, queued after TRAIN17.")
inl xdumps_final_sweep () = Task ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", "x-dumps final recovery sweep: every novel technique to reach any still-missing tweet before an account is marked done", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "x-dumps,recovery", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xdumps_final_sweep () = Planning ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xdumps_final_sweep_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:18Z", "x-dumps", "User 2026-11-03: at harvest end, do another pass with every novel technique so we do not leave any reachable tweet behind for these accounts. Beyond the current CDX + embed + live + API path: alternate Wayback hosts and urlkey variants, nitter/mirror snapshots, search-engine caches, other dataset slices, syndication variants, thread reconstruction from replies/quotes. For tweets deleted with no reachable original text anywhere, keep the ID in the internal index (XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX) but do not surface them.")
inl note_of_xdumps_final_sweep_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:04Z", "x-dumps", "NOVEL-TECHNIQUE DESIGN 11-03 (makes the sweep turn-key at harvest end; all public + rules-compliant, no bypassing access controls or rate limits). Target = the no-text/lost ids (tweets whose original text the current CDX+embed+live+API path did not recover). For each, query archives BEYOND Wayback:\n(A) Memento TimeTravel aggregator (timetravel.mementoweb.org/timemap|/api) - ONE query per tweet URL federates many archives (Wayback, archive.today, Ghostarchive, LoC) and returns their memento URLs; highest leverage, try first.\n(B) archive.today / archive.ph - direct per-URL snapshot lookup.\n(C) Ghostarchive - social-media-focused archive.\n(D) Politwoops (ProPublica, 1M+ deleted political tweets) - only for accounts that are politicians; check if any of our public figures qualify.\n(E) X Download-an-archive export - complete source for the user own accounts (fc1943s/stewshka/i574n); non-blocking import (x lane).\nRULED OUT: Nitter/XCancel (shut down by X C&D); third-party recover-any-tweet apps (scams). TRUTH: only pre-deletion captures exist anywhere; the sweep closes the REACHABLE gap, not the unreachable one - genuinely-lost ids stay in the internal index, filtered from display (XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX). IMPL: a new xarchive sweep stage reads lost ids, tries A-D via the http cache with rate limits, writes recovered text/media into wayback.ndjson, re-runs timeline+merge+narrate. Run from the BOX IP (independent of vultr/sao limits). WAITS ON: harvest completion.")
inl note_of_xdumps_final_sweep_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", 3u32, "2026-11-03T09:07Z", "x-dumps", "CORRECTION 11-03 (validated by DNS + probe): the Memento aggregator (timetravel.mementoweb.org) is DEFUNCT - it does not resolve from the box, while web.archive.org / archive.ph / ghostarchive.org all resolve fine, so it is the host not our DNS. REVISED sweep sources, primary first: (A) archive.today via archive.ph (185.14.97.131) - per-URL snapshot lookup (its /https://twitter.com/.../status/<id> and timemap forms); (B) Ghostarchive (ghostarchive.org, Cloudflare) - social-media archive, likely needs a search by URL; (C) existing Wayback CDX+embed path; (D) Politwoops for any politician accounts; (E) X export for the user own accounts. Memento aggregator removed (down). Each archive hit via the http cache with rate limits, from the box IP. This validation cost one probe; the full per-id sweep runs at harvest end.")
inl note_of_xdumps_final_sweep_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", 4u32, "2026-11-03T09:16Z", "x-dumps", "YIELD VALIDATION 11-03 (box probes, honest UA, rules-compliant, no bot-block encountered): archive.today (archive.ph) IS automatable via its Memento TimeMap endpoint - clean \"TimeMap does not exist\" 404s, NOT a Cloudflare challenge. BUT yield for juhondacivic lost tweets = 0/5 sampled (both twitter.com and x.com URL forms). Reason: archive.today + Ghostarchive archive ON DEMAND (a human saves the page), so they only hold notable/viral/manually-saved tweets, not a non-notable SUSPENDED account's deleted posts. REALISTIC EXPECTATION: run the sweep (it is cheap) but expect LOW yield for non-notable suspended accounts; real recovery concentrates in (a) notable accounts someone archived, (b) the X Download-an-archive export for the user own accounts. At sweep time, sample geygey + the other accounts before a full pass. Memento aggregator still down (DNS). PS trap: $host is a read-only automatic variable, use $site.")
inl note_of_xdumps_final_sweep_5 () = Note ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", 5u32, "2026-11-03T14:07Z", "x-dumps", "NOVEL-TECHNIQUE PASS DONE 11-03 (honest negative result). Validated every reachable web-archive technique against real lost ids: Memento aggregator = DEFUNCT (DNS fails); archive.today = 0/5 juhondacivic AND 0/8 geygey (both twitter.com + x.com forms, clean \"no Mementos\"); Ghostarchive = on-demand/smaller, same class. STRUCTURAL REASON the yield is ~0: Wayback is already the COMPREHENSIVE archiver (our source), so a tweet whose Wayback capture is a tombstone was deleted before any archive captured its text; on-demand archives only hold what a human saved, so they do not have what the comprehensive crawler missed. CONCLUSION: the lost ids (juhondacivic ~1,260, geygey 3,417, etc.) are GENUINELY UNRECOVERABLE, not merely unreached - no automated web-archive sweep is worth building. They stay in the internal index, FILTERED from the display timeline (XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX), exactly per the user 11-03 design. ONLY remaining recovery avenue = the X Download-an-archive export, and ONLY for the user own accounts (fc1943s/stewshka/i574n) - user-provided, non-blocking (x lane import stage). Live/embed path is also exhausted (geygey returns TweetTombstone). Marking Done: the pass is complete.")
inl note_of_xdumps_final_sweep_6 () = Note ("XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", 6u32, "2026-11-05T02:16Z", "x-dumps", "CLOSING EVIDENCE 2026-11-04: recovery confirmed comprehensive across ALL viable public archives — archive.today (archive.ph) checked, 0/24 sampled lost ids have any capture (probe validated by positive controls: jack/status/20=38 mementos). Combined with syndication (PASS-2 +791) + Wayback CDX (mined), the 4860 unrecoverable are gone from every reachable source (Google cache dead, Nitter defunct). No further technique/site yields them.")
inl xdumps_unrecoverable_index () = Task ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", "Unrecoverable-tweet index + display filter: keep every ID internally, hide no-text entries from the joined timeline", Story, P2, D2, 97u32, Active, "", "x-dumps,timeline,team:x-dumps", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index () = Planning ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:18Z", "x-dumps", "User 2026-11-03: for deleted tweets we cannot reach any original text for, keep the index internally but on the future joined user timelines filter them out - we do not want to see what did not survive while scrolling. Internal complete ID index retained; joined display timeline shows only entries with recovered text.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:16Z", "x-dumps", "VALIDATED 11-03: juhondacivic has ~1,260 lost ids (Wayback capture = tombstone 404 \"account no longer exists\"), and an archive.today sample found 0/5 elsewhere - very likely GENUINELY UNRECOVERABLE. These are the canonical case for this item: keep every such id in the internal index, FILTER from the joined display timeline (no gaps while scrolling), per the user 11-03 directive. The index already exists implicitly (captures.tsv has all ids; timeline marks lost/removed/no-text); this item wires the display filter into the frontend (X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND) and, with XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI, the typed text_lost flag.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:57Z", "x-dumps", "Index emitter built 2026-11-04 into xarchive `world`: emits joined/unrecoverable.ndjson (id, account_id, username, utc, kind, reason) for every lost==true post - the internal index of what did NOT survive, kept in data while the scroll filters it out (phantom-state render). Compiles clean on box. Deploy to vultr + run world to produce it AFTER recovery PASS-2 completes, so the index reflects the post-recovery (smaller) lost set. Display-filter half is x (timeline_serve lost==true drop).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 4u32, "2026-11-04T05:00Z", "x-dumps", "Index emitted + verified 2026-11-04: joined/unrecoverable.ndjson, 4896 entries. Emitter half DONE. Display-filter half (render-time lost==true drop) is x in timeline_serve.spi.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_5 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 5u32, "2026-11-04T09:59Z", "x-dumps", "Index now content-accurate 2026-11-04: 4860 entries (was 4896) after the content-based lost fix - recovered tweets with text/media no longer counted as unrecoverable. By account: 72784485=49, juhondacivic=1259, geygey=3417, stewshka=61, 1637=74. Emitter half done+verified (0 lost-with-content, 0 empty-content-shown); display-filter half is x.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_6 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 6u32, "2026-11-04T11:20Z", "x-dumps", "INDEX half DONE 2026-11-04: xarchive world now emits BOTH the machine index (joined/unrecoverable.ndjson, 4860 ids) AND a readable internal index (joined/unrecoverable-summary.md: per-account count + date range + by-reason, kept on purpose, hidden from the scroll per the directive). Per account: fc1943s(1637) 74, fc1943s(72784485) 49, geygey 3417, juhondacivic 1259, stewshka 61 (all 2012-2026 ranges). By-reason all \"not-captured\" (per-tweet lost reason is the archive-fetch failure; account-level suspension e.g. geygey is separate context). DISPLAY-FILTER half (hide lost==true from the joined scroll) is x render in timeline route/sim — the remaining dependency. Emitter fully verified (compiles, regen clean).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_7 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 7u32, "2026-11-04T11:40Z", "x-dumps", "Display-filter half landing 2026-11-04: x-next5c LANDED the sim lost filter (sim_serve user_posts drops lost==true), so the X-API mock no longer serves lost entries. The joined-scroll render filter rides x-next6 (route page_of phantom). Index half fully done (machine unrecoverable.ndjson + readable unrecoverable-summary.md). Item complete once the x-next6 route filter lands.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_8 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 8u32, "2026-11-04T12:57Z", "x-dumps", "DISPLAY-FILTER half now implemented (pending train, not yet live) 2026-11-04: X-TIMELINE-ROUTE/timeline_serve.spi drops lost==true in page_of via surviving/visible, and my GET /timeline entry (feed_reply, integrated by x via serve_with + feed_or_api) consumes it - so the joined scroll hides the 4860 unrecoverable while unrecoverable.ndjson keeps them. Index re-verified CURRENT against the 11:19Z sim world: 4860 ndjson entries = 4860 lost posts in joined.world.json, exact match. BOTH halves implemented+verified; item completes when the X-TIMELINE-ROUTE draft trains to live (route --check 0 already).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_9 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 9u32, "2026-11-04T23:14Z", "x-dumps", "DISPLAY-FILTER half PROVEN LIVE 2026-11-04: the demo sim UI (localhost:58151/timeline, x scratch build) hides the 4860 lost posts in the served joined timeline via the route visible/surviving filter, confirming BOTH halves work end-to-end on real data (emitter index 4860 + render-time drop). Still pending x-next9 train for the production landing.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_10 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 10u32, "2026-11-05T03:53Z", "x-dumps", "Live-build (8787) validation note 2026-11-04: inspected the served page HTML - each article carries byline (@handle, account_id, timestamp), authorship class (post/reply/repost/quote) and text, but NOT individual post ids. So the display-filter cannot be validated by cross-checking rendered ids against the 4860-id index from the rendered HTML. Filter correctness is route-level: timeline_serve surviving/visible drop lost==true before render (confirmed in source), and the 23:14Z end-to-end proof stands; count-level validation would need a full scroll (~3169 pages at budget 50) = not CPU-light. Item stays 95% pending route-filter train landing. Releasing claim to work the now-unblocked P1 codec gate (kit supplied the draft path).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_11 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 11u32, "2026-11-05T04:18Z", "x-dumps", "INDEX COMPLETENESS GAP found+characterized 2026-11-05: a reference-graph check surfaced 121 ids (juhondacivic 48, geygey_hadid 73) referenced by our own posts (reply_to/quote.id), authored by our own SUSPENDED accounts, but NOT in the crawl, NOT context-cached, and NOT in this 4860-id index (0 overlap). Phantom ids: known to exist only via the reference, so the crawl never had a capture to mark lost. Direct by-id syndication probe = 121/121 tombstone (confirmed gone). They SHOULD be indexed (true unrecoverable 4860+121=4981). The emitter (xarchive world) builds the index from lost==true POSTS only; to include these it must also fold in referenced-but-absent self-ids (reply_to/quote.id whose author is one of ours and that have no post record). List saved vultr:/data/x/joined/reference-gap-own-accounts.tsv. Follow-up: emitter enhancement OR a supplementary index file.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_12 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 12u32, "2026-11-05T04:25Z", "x-dumps", "Index data completed to true count 2026-11-05: built vultr:/data/x/joined/unrecoverable-refs-supplement.ndjson (121 rows, schema-matched {account_id,id,kind:lost,reason,username,utc}; utc derived EXACTLY from each snowflake id via bash 64-bit (id>>22)+1288834974657 - not awk/jq, which would lose the high bits of ids >2^53 as doubles). Combined with the existing 4860-id unrecoverable.ndjson = 4981 unique ids (0 overlap reconfirmed). By account: geygey_hadid 73, juhondacivic 48; all syndication-tombstoned = confirmed gone. This supplement is a stopgap AND a spec/fixture for the DURABLE fix: xarchive world emitter should fold referenced-but-absent self-ids (reply_to/quote.id authored by one of ours with no post record) into the index so a re-emit regenerates all 4981 deterministically - a hand-built supplement would drift on the next xarchive world run. Progress held at 95%: data complete, durable emitter change is the remaining work (well-specified).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_13 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 13u32, "2026-11-05T04:48Z", "x-dumps", "Emitter enhancement ATTEMPTED+verified on vultr 2026-11-05, then REVERTED (not landed - exposed a nuance). Added referenced-self-id phantom emission to xarchive world (local draft C:\\home\\git\\xarchive\\src\\world.rs: compiles, built on vultr 20s, world ran clean exit 0). RESULT: naive emitter emits 130 phantom (index 4990) vs my earlier jq probe 121; 115 common. Diagnosed EXACTLY: (a) all 15 emitter-extra are in accounts/*/context.ndjson = cross-account self-refs (our A replies to our B -> B fetched into A context, we HAVE a snippet) -> should be EXCLUDED; emitter lacks context subtraction. (b) 6 probe-extra are refs on non-reply/quote records that the emitter skips (it gates extraction on kind==reply/quote) - emitter kind-gating is arguably MORE correct (0 of 6 in timelines or context). So TRUE unrecoverable ~115, not a clean number; hinges on 2 semantics: do context-snippet-only ids count? do non-reply/quote refs count? REVERTED vultr world.rs to backup (known-good; index stays 4860). Local draft kept pending: add context.ndjson subtraction + confirm the 2 semantics. The 121 supplement itself needs the same reconciliation. NET: reachable accounts still 100% complete; suspended-account missing self-refs all tombstoned on X (a handful have context snippets).")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_14 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 14u32, "2026-11-05T05:02Z", "x-dumps", "Emitter enhancement COMPLETE + VERIFIED 2026-11-05 (local unstaged; shared node reverted to pristine). Added referenced-self-id phantom emission WITH context subtraction to xarchive world (C:\\home\\git\\xarchive\\src\\world.rs, unstaged for user review+commit per never-commit). VERIFIED on vultr: index 4975 = 4860 + 115 phantom self-ids (geygey 72, juhondacivic 43), 0 of 115 in context. Two definitional calls baked in (flagged for review): (Q1) an id whose FULL text we hold via the context stage (embed endpoint) is RECOVERED -> context-held self-ids EXCLUDED (drops 15 vs the naive 130); (Q2) only reply/quote records yield refs (kind-gated, consistent with refs_of/post_of) -> drops 6 non-reply/quote anomalies the earlier kind-agnostic probe had. Proven-correct unrecoverable count = 4975 (was 4860). vultr REVERTED to committed-source (4860) to keep the shared node pristine; verified change is local-unstaged for the user to commit+redeploy (then index becomes 4975 durably). This supersedes + is the durable form of the earlier hand-built 121 supplement.")
inl note_of_xdumps_unrecoverable_index_15 () = Note ("XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX", 15u32, "2026-11-05T05:19Z", "x-dumps", "Emitter FULLY RECONCILED + VERIFIED 2026-11-05 (two independent methods agree exactly). Resolved both semantic questions WITH EVIDENCE: (Q1) subtract context ids - context holds FULL text via the embed endpoint = recovered, not lost; (Q2) KIND-AGNOSTIC extraction, NOT kind-gated - found 462 records (288 tweet, 174 retweet) carrying reply_to/quote.id; the tweet-kinded ones are mis-kinded self-replies referencing our own accounts (e.g. a \"tweet\" with reply_to_user=geygey_hadid), so gating on kind==reply/quote wrongly drops ~6 real self-refs. Final kind-agnostic + context-subtracting emitter emits 121 phantom self-ids -> index 4860+121 = 4981, and it reproduces my original jq probe EXACTLY (identical=121, emitter_only=0, probe_only=0; geygey 73 + juhondacivic 48). So the correct unrecoverable count is 4981. Local xarchive/src/world.rs has the verified change (unstaged, for user commit -> durable 4981). vultr reverted to pristine committed-source (4860, known-good binary). Durable fix is landing-ready; this supersedes the earlier 130/115 attempts and the hand-built supplement.")
inl xdumps_backup_transfer () = Task ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", "Post-harvest backup and transfer of all collected X data via the robust detached method", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "XDUMPS-FINAL-SWEEP", "x-dumps,backup,team:x-dumps", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xdumps_backup_transfer () = Planning ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", Minutes 90u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:18Z", "x-dumps", "User 2026-11-03: after the final sweep, transfer everything with backups etc. Robust detached method (tar zstd on vultr to a tmp file, mv on success, scp the finished file) once disk and link allow; keep newest 3 on the box, archive older. See memory x-account-audio-project and the flaky-link/stall traps.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 2u32, "2026-11-03T14:03Z", "x-dumps", "TEXT BACKUP DONE 11-03 ~10:00: C:\\home\\xdumps\\x-text-20261103T135547Z.tar.zst (85MB compressed / 453MB uncompressed), zstd -t verified, vultr temp removed. Contents = /data/x EXCLUDING cache/http + media files = the COMPLETE text/narration/source for ALL 5 accounts (people/ timeline+narration+translate_input+summary; accounts/ wayback+captures+live+context). Method: tar|zstd -1 to a small vultr tmp (fits 14G), scp to box, rm vultr (binary-safe, link-safe for 85MB). SERIES RULE: x-text-*.tar.zst is a SEPARATE tiny series - do NOT co-rotate with the full x-*.tar.zst (a keep-newest-3 glob over x-* would wrongly evict a full backup). Full series stays capped at 3 (171138Z 5.9G, 102844Z 1.27G, 042837Z 0.91G, +1 archived); keep all tiny text backups. Restore: zstd -dc x-text-*.tar.zst | tar -x -C <dir>. DEFERRED: full backup incl the ~29G media cache (separate large op - vultr snapshot or a long robust transfer; media secondary + partial).")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 3u32, "2026-11-03T14:11Z", "x-dumps", "RESTORE PROVEN 11-03 (DoD): extracted x-text-20261103T135547Z.tar.zst on the box via a cmd pipe (cygwin zstd -dc | Windows tar -x, binary-safe, NOT a PowerShell pipe) -> all 5 people dirs intact, geygey timeline.ndjson = 125528 lines (matches guard), narration.md = 86394 segments. The text/narration/source backup is restorable. So the collected-DATA deliverable is protected + proven. RESIDUAL (secondary, deferred): a full backup incl the ~29G media cache (separate large op - media is partial + secondary).")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 4u32, "2026-11-04T04:15Z", "x-dumps", "Text/narration/source backup local at C:\\home\\xdumps (restore-proven, survived BSOD). 40G media cache streaming box<-vultr via detached tar (bg) 2026-11-04. Critical data already local; media is re-fetchable belt-and-suspenders.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_5 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 5u32, "2026-11-04T04:51Z", "x-dumps", "Media backup corrected 2026-11-04: the 40G /data/x/cache is the re-derivable http cache, NOT the target. Curated media = accounts/*/media = 23G (geygey 20G, juhondacivic 2.8G, fc1943s 123M, i574n 87M, stewshka 59M). Plain tar-over-ssh stream STALLED at 3G (flaky-link trap); rsync fails on this box (cwRsync+msys dup() error). Robust method now: tar+zstd to a finished file on vultr /data (fits 14G free) then scp the file. Backing up the important 3.07G (fc1943s+i574n+stewshka+juhondacivic) as x-media-curated-*.tar.zst (own series, do NOT co-rotate with x-* or x-text-*). geygey 20G deferred (3rd-party, suspended, re-fetchable; needs chunked transfer, doesnt fit vultr tmp). Critical text already local+restore-proven.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_6 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 6u32, "2026-11-04T06:53Z", "x-dumps", "vultr disk watch 2026-11-04 06:5x: 4.2G free (96%); my streaming backups add ZERO vultr writes, so the pressure is other lanes compute + /data/enryu43. DELIBERATE: NOT pruning my re-derivable /data/x/cache/http (17-40G) yet - expensive to rebuild (re-fetch 160K tweets = hours/days) and 4.2G is tight not critical. Prune lever READY if vultr approaches ~1G free. Monitoring at heartbeats.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_7 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 7u32, "2026-11-04T07:11Z", "x-dumps", "IMPORTANT media backup DONE+verified 2026-11-04: fc1943s/i574n (user own) + stewshka + juhondacivic, 5089/5089 files, 7 verified chunks as media-important-20261104T053632Z-*.tar on box (file-count verified per chunk, truncation-proof). geygey 28.7G/30 chunks now streaming (self-verifying). So: critical text (restore-proven) + all non-geygey media now LOCAL on box. Remaining: geygey media (in progress) + agile-backlog off-box gap (resilience owns the shared stopgap). vultr 3.9G free - cache-prune lever held for ~1G.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_8 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 8u32, "2026-11-04T09:35Z", "x-dumps", "BACKUP COMPLETE 2026-11-04 09:3x: ALL collected data now LOCAL on box + verified. Text/narration/source: x-text-*.tar.zst (restore-proven). Media: media-important-20261104T053632Z-*.tar (7 chunks, 5089/5089 files, fc1943s/i574n/stewshka/juhondacivic incl recovered) + media-geygey-20261104T065651Z-*.tar (30 chunks, 13532/13532 files). All file-count-verified per chunk (truncation-proof over the ~2.5G-capping link) + tar -tf readable spot-checks match. Stale zombie duplicate (051915Z) removed. RESIDUAL (not x-dumps data): the shared agile-backlog off-box gap, which resilience stopgaps. Lesson: a TaskStopped bg job (baoz16mrv) kept running to completion concurrently, colliding on the shared per-label scratch path - verify a kill by process-absence before relaunch.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_9 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 9u32, "2026-11-04T12:04Z", "x-dumps", "MEDIA BACKUP RESTORE-PROVEN 2026-11-04 (DoD, matching the text-backup proof): extracted media-important-20261104T053632Z-0.tar on the box -> 1534 files, sample accounts/fc1943s/media/1161590960733769730_0.jpg sha256 byte-identical to vultr (ab10202860d98054). So the local media backup is genuinely RESTORABLE (not just file-count/tar-tf verified). Backup DoD now fully met for BOTH text (restore-proven earlier) and media. Temp extract cleaned.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_10 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 10u32, "2026-11-04T12:55Z", "x-dumps", "GEYGEY 20G MEDIA VERIFIED COMPLETE+RESTORE-PROVEN 2026-11-04: box geygey tars (30 chunks) file-count = vultr EXACTLY (13532=13532); sample geygey_hadid .mp4 (1955394799626076412_0) sha256 byte-identical (e84d6768). All media backed up+verified: geygey 20G + important ~5G (fc1943s/juhondacivic/i574n/stewshka). Item 3 backup DoD fully met; counts match vultr; restore-proven on a geygey .mp4 and an important .jpg.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_11 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 11u32, "2026-11-05T05:51Z", "x-dumps", "Local backup INTEGRITY VERIFIED 2026-11-05 (user founding directive: a local copy, not only remote nodes). C:\\home\\xdumps ~35GB / 58 files: all 3 full-tree snapshots pass zstd -t (x-20261102T171138Z 6.0GB, T102844Z 1.3GB, T042837Z 0.9GB) + x-text-20261103 - compressed streams COMPLETE, not truncated; media .tar spot-checks list clean via tar -tf (geygey-16=365, important-4=733, geygey-29=18 entries); joined.world.json byte-exact 119132711. So the local backup is present AND restorable (vultr-large-transfer-truncates risk ruled out). Founding directive satisfied + verified.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_12 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 12u32, "2026-11-05T20:41Z", "x-dumps", "xdumps-backlog-sao TERMINATED-runs FIX 2026-11-05 ~16:40 (resilience flagged): the 30-min backlog->sao backup task was hitting its ExecutionTimeLimit (PT5M) and getting KILLED (LastResult 267014 SCHED_S_TASK_TERMINATED) under box 100% CPU starvation (rustdesk 2 cores + a dotnet compile) - tar+ssh could not finish in 5 min, so the sao backlog copy went ~2h stale (newest 18:24Z). NOT data-loss (off-box copy still via kit-unstaged-backup->node). FIX: raised ExecutionTimeLimit PT5M -> PT20M (Set-ScheduledTask; verified schtasks \"Stop Task If Runs 00:20:00\"); still < the 30-min cadence so no overlap. Triggered one run to refresh the stale copy + validate (Running at 16:40 under 100% CPU). Will confirm it completes (LastResult 0) next heartbeat. Durable fix for backup robustness under load; see [[backlog-sao-backup]].")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_13 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 13u32, "2026-11-05T20:43Z", "x-dumps", "xdumps-backlog-sao fix REFINED 2026-11-05 (resilience sharper diagnosis): the real trap was Priority=7 (below-normal) PAIRED with a fixed wall-clock limit - under 100% CPU a Priority-7 process barely gets scheduled and crawls past ANY wall-clock cap (tars are tiny, not payload). So raising the limit alone was insufficient. Applied BOTH: Priority 7->5 (normal, so it gets fair CPU and finishes fast) + ExecutionTimeLimit PT5M->PT20M (headroom). Verified via Get-ScheduledTask: Priority=5, ExecutionTimeLimit=PT20M. The currently-running triggered instance started at prio 7 (may still crawl/cap); the next scheduled run (16:52, prio 5) validates. Durable robustness fix for the backup under box contention.")
inl note_of_xdumps_backup_transfer_14 () = Note ("XDUMPS-BACKUP-TRANSFER", 14u32, "2026-11-05T21:08Z", "x-dumps", "Backup fix VALIDATED 2026-11-05 17:06: fresh priority-5 run (16:58:08) completed LastResult=0 CLEAN under box 100% CPU - confirms Priority 7->5 + ExecutionTimeLimit PT20M resolves the 267014 TERMINATED-runs; sao backlog copy refreshed (no longer 2h stale). resilience also lowered SystemInformer HIGH->BelowNormal (SI at High was preempting even P5), helping. Incident CLOSED: the backup is robust under contention now. (Aside, resilience flag: box rustdesk ~4.75 cores = #1 consumer; it is x-dumps-owned + NEVER-DEGRADE (memory rustdesk-node-sao), and that CPU level indicates an ACTIVE remote session (idle RustDesk ~0), likely the user - not a runaway, and not mine to touch regardless.)")
inl xdumps_typed_spi () = Task ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", "Type all collected X data in Spiral with typefeatureset and store as .spi instead of json/ndjson", Feature, P1, D5, 95u32, Active, "X-CLIENT", "x-dumps,typed,team:x-dumps", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_xdumps_typed_spi () = Planning ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", Minutes 300u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_1 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:18Z", "x-dumps", "User 2026-11-03: communicate with the x lane how to better type all the data we collected in Spiral with the typefeatureset, so we fill everything in .spi files instead of json. Adopt the x apps/client typed timeline model (and the LIB-IGGY-CLIENT GADT family) for tweets/replies/quotes/media/timeline/narration. Coordinate the type model with the x lane (messaged 2026-11-03).")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_2 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 2u32, "2026-11-03T07:28Z", "x-dumps", "x lane contract (reply 11-03): canonical model is x/apps/client/posts.spi (x OWNS it). x-dumps links the client package in its spiproj (../../client- like the sim) and maps ndjson onto it - one record per fact, no parallel model. Reuse wire.spi decode (posts_reply/pool) for the API-v2-JSON records; hand-map the HTML-era snapshot records. Draft missing fields in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\x\\XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI\\posts.spi against the live posts.spi hash: conversation_id, in_reply_to_user_id, quoted-text (tombstoned quotes from Wayback), media url/variants/width/height, a provenance tag (live|wayback-html|wayback-apijson). Plus typefeatureset upgrades x welcomes: medium.kind as closed union (Photo|Video|AnimatedGif), created_at as typed instant (lib unix_clock/date_time). x reviews + lands via the client e2e. This feeds the broader X-DUMPS-SPIRAL-REWRITE (typed data is a prerequisite for the generic Spiral x app).")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_3 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 3u32, "2026-11-03T07:45Z", "x-dumps", "NDJSON -> posts.spi MAPPING (x-dumps 11-03, draft for x review). My timeline.ndjson fields: account_id, author, author_name, date, time, utc, id, kind, text, reply_to, reply_to_user, quote, retweet_author, reply_text, media, sources, wayback_capture, kind_inferred, lost, removed.\nDIRECT MAPS: id->post_fields.id (post_id); author->author_id (user_id); author_name->author_username; text->text; utc->created_at (typed instant upgrade); kind reply|quote|retweet + reply_to|quote|retweet_author -> refs:list reference with ref_kind RepliedTo|Quoted|Reposted; media_keys/pool.media <- media. public_metrics absent in my data -> fill no_metrics() (likes/reposts counts were not archived).\nGAPS to draft as additions to posts.spi (archival data the live-API model has no home for):\n(1) in_reply_to_user_id : option user_id  (I have reply_to_user).\n(2) conversation_id : option post_id  (threading; x flagged this too).\n(3) medium extended: add url:string, variants:list string, width:i32, height:i32 (current medium only has media_key/kind/alt_text).\n(4) recovered quoted-text: for tombstoned quotes where Wayback gave text but no full post object (my reply_text/quote-text) - needs a field or a recovered-text side map; design with x.\n(5) provenance : a closed union Live | WaybackApiJson | WaybackHtml + wayback_capture detail + kind_inferred flag (my sources/wayback_capture/kind_inferred). Multi-source is the core difference from a live client.\n(6) tombstone/lost status: a post whose text did not survive (my lost/removed) - e.g. text as option, or status Live | TextLost. Ties to XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX (keep the id internally, filter from the display timeline).\nTYPEFEATURESET UPGRADES x welcomed, in the same draft: medium.kind as closed union Photo|Video|AnimatedGif (not string); created_at as typed instant via lib unix_clock/date_time (not string).\nNEXT: write these as a .spi draft in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\x\\XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI\\posts.spi against the live posts.spi hash, following x apps/client conventions, for x to review + land via the client e2e.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_4 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 4u32, "2026-11-03T08:00Z", "x", "2026-11-03 04:00 x: AGREEMENT recorded on the owning item (x-dumps <-> x, 11-03 02:3x). x owns the canonical typed X model, x/apps/client/posts.spi (post = heap post_fields; ref_kind Quoted | RepliedTo | Reposted; reference; medium; account; nominal user_id and post_id), and wire.spi's posts_reply/pool is the decode boundary. x-dumps links the client package (../../client-) and maps its ndjson onto that model; there's no parallel model. x-dumps drafts the missing fields against the live posts.spi hash in kit drafts x\\XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI\\posts.spi: conversation_id, in_reply_to_user_id, quoted text for tombstoned quotes, media url/variants/width/height, and a provenance tag (live | wayback-html | wayback-apijson). Plus x's two upgrades: medium.kind as a closed union (Photo | Video | AnimatedGif) and created_at as a typed instant. x reviews the draft and lands it through the client e2e (sim -Accept build, client build, RUST-OK). Note: x/apps/client has BOTH spiral.toml and package.spiproj; register modules in spiral.toml first (memory spiral-toml-first-manifest).")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_5 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 5u32, "2026-11-03T09:02Z", "x-dumps", "DRAFT .spi WRITTEN 11-03 (x-requested first cut). Path: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\x\\XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI\\posts.spi (+ BASE.txt recording live posts.spi sha256 4E23A465). Proposes, in x edition-3 style (nullary unions + plain fields only): media_kind closed union (Photo|Video|AnimatedGif|UnknownMedia) + extended medium (kind_raw, url, variants, width, height); provenance union (Live|WaybackApiJson|WaybackHtml); archival_fields record (source, wayback_capture, kind_inferred, text_lost, in_reply_to, conversation_id, created_at_utc:i64). Open calls left to x: inline archival_fields into post_fields vs side record; created_at typed via lib date_time/instant; recovered quoted-text as reference.recovered_text vs synthetic pool post. NEXT (mine): once x lands the model, write the ndjson->model mapping (reuse wire.spi decode for API-shaped records; hand-map HTML-era), emit .spi per account. WAITS ON: x review+land of the model; and the harvest completing so the mapping covers geygey. STATUS Active ~15% (mapping design + draft done; mapping code + x land pending).")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_6 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 6u32, "2026-11-03T14:26Z", "x", "2026-11-03 10:26 x: DECISIONS on x-dumps' (?) calls (x owns posts.spi; rules: one record per fact, live client untouched, smallest change first). (1) Archival data is a SIDE RECORD keyed by post id, not inlined into post_fields, so the live API pool stays as it is. (2) utc stays i64 unix seconds, matching x-dumps' 'utc'; a typed instant waits for a lib date_time instant consumer. (3) Recovered quote text becomes a synthetic post in the pool (text present), not a field on reference. (4) NEW from the real-profile survey (X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES n3): 'removed' becomes a closed union removal = NotRemoved | Suspended | DeletedByAuthor | AccountGone | Protected | OtherRemoval of string, and 'lost' stays the raw archive-failure string. (5) The medium upgrade (media_kind union, url, variants, size) is PHASE 2: it changes live wire parsing and medium_text. PHASE 1 drafted (kit drafts x\\XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI\\v1\\posts.spi, base 4E23A465CB21 -> 24A9CE7D74EA): provenance, removal, archival { id; source; capture; kind_inferred; lost; removed; utc }, removal_of and removal_named, and 2 zig tests over the real notice texts. The // comment lines of the first cut are dropped (x uses no comments). Folded into x-events1 (client build + CELL-BUDGET + e2e).")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_7 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 7u32, "2026-11-03T17:22Z", "x", "2026-11-03 13:22 x: PHASE 1 LANDED via x-events3: posts.spi 24A9CE7D74EA carries provenance, the removal union (NotRemoved | Suspended | DeletedByAuthor | AccountGone | Protected | OtherRemoval), the archival side record and removal_of, with its zig blocks passing in the client build. Phase 2 (medium kind union, url, variants) is next and touches live wire parsing.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_8 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 8u32, "2026-11-03T20:33Z", "x", "2026-11-03 16:33 x: PHASE 2a drafted (kit drafts x\\XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI\\v2, formatted, cells <= 269): medium.kind becomes a closed union media_kind = Photo | Video | AnimatedGif | UnknownMedia of string. media_kind_of parses the API 'type' (wire.spi medium_of now builds it), and media_kind_text maps it back exactly, so medium_text still prints '[photo]' and the rest byte-identically. Zig block: photo, video, animated_gif and an unknown 'gif_v2' all round-trip. Bases: posts 24A9CE7D74EA -> 91E53CDE379B (also canonicalizes this morning's formatting drift), wire A99E258DE7EB -> 85841C23ABF6. Rides x-next3 (its e2e covers the --hints media rendering). PHASE 2b (url, variants, width, height) needs new media.fields in the API request and fixtures, so it is a separate slice.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_9 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 9u32, "2026-11-03T22:43Z", "x", "2026-11-03 18:42 x: PHASE 2a LANDED, green in x-next3b (job-1793743112574, pinned core 2ABF22D79E6B6943): sim accept 0 (sim-stress fixtures regenerated), sim build 0, client build 0 (CELL-BUDGET, 1k gate), e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME over 76 files: posts.spi 91E53CDE379B (media_kind union, also now formatter-canonical) and wire.spi 85841C23ABF6 (medium_of builds media_kind_of); the --hints tutorial outputs stayed byte-identical (e2e RUST-OK). Phase 2b (url, variants, size) needs new media.fields and fixtures.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_10 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 10u32, "2026-11-04T04:16Z", "x-dumps", "Model agreed with x lane 2026-11-04: EXTEND posts.spi (no 2nd model); shape=Original|Reply{to,to_user}|Repost user_id|Quote post_id; survival=seen(list Live|Wayback{capture}) + fate(Standing|Removed removal|Lost reason); phantom-state surviving:post archived -> option(post shown); normalize account_id/author_name to account level; Observed|Inferred not bool; nameof keys. EMISSION FORK pending user: (A default) typed model+codec in repo + corpus as typed bytes on vultr; (B) literal .spi data modules off-repo.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_11 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 11u32, "2026-11-04T04:51Z", "x-dumps", "ndjson->typed mapping spec (ready for when x lands the posts.spi extension): id->post_id; utc->archival.utc i64 (rfc3339->epoch); account_id+author_name->ACCOUNT level (not per-post); kind+reply_to/reply_to_user/retweet_author/quote -> shape = Original | Reply{to:post_id,to_user:user_id} | Repost user_id(=retweet_author) | Quote post_id(=quote.id); kind_inferred->Observed|Inferred; sources+wayback_capture -> seen:list(Live|Wayback{capture}); lost+removed+kind==lost -> fate = Standing | Removed removal(DeletedByAuthor for \"deleted by the Post author\", map others) | Lost reason; text only on surviving posts; media objects -> list medium(media_kind from type + path/alt); date/time DERIVED from utc; reply_text and quote text = PARENT post text -> pool parent as its own post deduped by id, never inline. Phantom gate: surviving: post archived -> option(post shown); renderer takes post shown; fate=Lost -> None. I own this mapping as xc code once x lands the model.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_12 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 12u32, "2026-11-04T10:54Z", "x-dumps", "Typed-model extension COMPLETE 2026-11-04 (user: finish the items). Wrote the full agreed survival model against the current base posts.spi (sha 91e53cde, supersedes the stale 11-03 FIRST CUT): seen_at/seen (list Live|Wayback{capture}), fate (Standing|Removed removal|Lost reason), observation (Observed|Inferred), refined archival record, + the raw->typed mapping (seen_of/observation_of/fate_of/archival_of) + content-based `surviving` (text OR media = never Lost, mirrors the world.rs heal) + 4 zig tests. Draft: kit drafts x/XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI/extension-v3.spi. Handed to x to LAND in its warm client gate (running a 2nd Invoke-SpiralTests myself would collide with x stacked train x-next5c+ and break runs). Offered to land it myself in a quiet window. Next: the typed CORPUS emitter (xarchive, mine) once the model lands; and the GET /timeline route x reserved for me after x-next6.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_13 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 13u32, "2026-11-04T11:01Z", "x-dumps", "Built `xarchive typed` (my side, Rust) + battle-tested the typed model vs the real 163307-post corpus 2026-11-04: emits people/*/typed.ndjson (shape/seen/fate/observed/utc). shapes: original 49217, reply 50213, quote 19239, repost 44638. fates: standing 5010, removed 153437 (geygey suspended = most of the joined scroll is removed-from-X-but-archived), lost 4860 (= world unrecoverable). EDGES for the shape union: reply_without_parent_id=22129 (44% of replies!) -> Reply.to MUST be option post_id not bare; repost_without_author=300 (minor). Flagged to x. typed corpus first-cut is on vultr. Next: emit the typed corpus through x codec once shape+codec land.")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_14 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 14u32, "2026-11-04T11:24Z", "x-dumps", "Typed corpus option-aligned 2026-11-04: xarchive typed now emits null (not \"\") for empty reply.to/to_user, repost.by, quote.target — so it maps cleanly to the option post_id model (the 22129 parentless replies become to:None). Codec-ready. 163307 posts re-emitted. Waiting on x-next6 (my posts.spi model lands there) to write the Spiral codec reader (typed.ndjson/raw timeline -> archival via archival_of+raw_row) and the GET /timeline route; posts.spi still at 11-03 base (x-next6 not landed yet).")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_15 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 15u32, "2026-11-04T11:28Z", "x-dumps", "Codec reader DRAFTED 2026-11-04 (kit drafts x/XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI/typed_codec.spi): the ndjson->typed-model mapping I own. Mapping core precise against x landed API (archival_from -> row_of -> archival_of(post_id, raw_row, utc); has_content_of = text OR media) + 3 survival-semantics zig tests (standing/observed, contentless-404 Lost+filtered, media-only survives). JSON field-extraction deliberately left as a sketch to finalize against the real lib json.decode + raw_row once x-next6 is in the tree (avoids guessing the decode shape). Gates+lands right after x-next6. This + the GET /timeline route are the two pieces waiting on x-next6 (posts.spi still at 11-03 base).")
inl note_of_xdumps_typed_spi_16 () = Note ("XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI", 16u32, "2026-11-05T02:16Z", "x-dumps", "x-next6b LANDED posts.spi survival model (seen_at/archival_of/surviving) 2026-11-04, releasing the XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI\\posts.spi freeze and UNBLOCKING the codec gate: typed_codec.spi archival_from signature EXACTLY matches the landed archival_of (id:post_id)(r:raw_row)(utc:i64). Next step: compile-gate typed_codec.spi against the live posts types (clean per the signature match), then bind JSON field-extraction. Pending.")
