inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_1 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:18Z", "x-dumps", "User 2026-11-03: build a minimal frontend to see a joined timeline of all collected accounts, using the sim code, in Spiral; grow it when appropriate like lib. The X-simulating scroll UI is generic (even if somewhat temporary) so it lives in the x repo/projects (C:\\home\\git\\x, apps/). Filters unrecoverable no-text entries per XDUMPS-UNRECOVERABLE-INDEX.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_2 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 2u32, "2026-11-03T07:20Z", "x", "2026-11-03 03:20 x: INTAKE (filed by x-dumps; team:x and assignee added). PLAN: a minimal Spiral frontend in x apps/ over the client's typed pool (posts.spi post/account/medium/reference), merging every collected account's timeline newest first. Its merge is the k-way merge NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW already prototyped (a resumable typed cursor), so that logic lands here, generic, with no NEAR dependency. Rendering is a static HTML page over the html repo's typed markup model (HTML-MODEL), not a new renderer (the drift-watch rule on CELLS-HTML-PARITY). Sequenced after X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES, so the frontend is proven against real-shaped data in the sim first.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_3 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:20Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:20 x: STEP 1 drafted, the generic merge (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\feed_merge.spi, 37709C86D9E7), restored from NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW's archived edition-2 probes (kit archive 20261030-232045: paged_merge, paged_offsets, paged_exhausted_negative) and rewritten in today's syntax with a typed cursor. feed_cursor t is a nominal over list (list t) (the erl_map pattern). merged_page newer budget cursor returns one page plus the resumed cursor: each step takes the newest head across feeds (better and head_better pick it; equal heads keep the earlier feed, so ties are stable), pops it (popped), and stops at the budget or when all feeds are empty. The order is a parameter (newer : t -> t -> bool), so one merge serves posts by (created_at, id) as well as plain ids. Blocks: pages resume from the cursor (3 then the rest, [90;80;75] then [70;60;20;10;5]), an exhausted or zero-budget page is empty, and equal heads keep feed order. Every cell is under 272 with headroom. NEXT: register it in x (apps/client or a new apps/timeline unit) once x-events3 has landed spiral.toml/package.spiproj, then a page renderer over the html units for the joined real-profile timelines. The NEAR consumer half stays Paused on NEAR-FEED-PAGED-VIEW.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_4 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 4u32, "2026-11-03T16:21Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:21 x: STEP 2 decided from the tree: the order is posts.spi's existing 'newer (a : entry) (b : entry)' (created_at second, then later_id, the rule its same-second block tests), so the joined timeline is feed_merge::merged_page posts::newer budget (cursor_of feeds), where each feed is one account's entries through posts' newest_first. No new ordering code. The page renders those entries with posts' entry fields through the html units (html_model nodes, html_render), and the real-profile worlds on vultr (X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES n6) are the first input, read in place.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_5 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 5u32, "2026-11-03T16:27Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:27 x: STEP 3 drafted (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\timeline_page.spi): the page over the html units (opens model and render). byline = Paragraph [Strong [@user]; ' · ' time], then Paragraph [text], then Rule per entry, under an H1 title, rendered by render::blocks_html |> markup_text. merged = feed_merge::merged_page posts::newer, so joined_page title budget feeds is one page of the newest entries across accounts. Rust blocks: the byline and rule show, entry text is escaped (a <b> & c -> &lt;b&gt; &amp;), and a 2-entry page over two accounts takes a3 and b2 but not a1. Cells within budget. Packaging decided at registration: it needs the client root (posts) plus the html units as packages, so it is likely its own apps/timeline unit linking html like Cells will. The CELLS-HTML-PARITY CI note (html cloned beside the repo) applies to x's CI too, so registration waits for that pattern to settle.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_6 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 6u32, "2026-11-03T17:33Z", "x", "2026-11-03 13:33 x: STEP 1 REGISTRATION folded into x-next2: feed_merge joins the client root package (spiral.toml 2301C5DD40E4 -> 445B3F065EAF, package.spiproj 122B06832D93 -> 15692AC85DCB, 'feed_merge' after 'posts'; bases are x-events3's landed manifests), and feed_merge.spi 37709C86D9E7 lands as apps/client/feed_merge.spi. Its 3 rust blocks run in the client build, and CELL-BUDGET covers it. timeline_page.spi (step 3) stays a draft until the html-link pattern lands with CELLS-HTML-PARITY, since it opens html's model and render.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_7 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 7u32, "2026-11-03T21:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 17:30 x: STEP 1 LANDED in x-next2 (job-1793737559206, pinned pack27 core 6F83B94FE33167CC; the installed core moved to D1854B99FD3FA940 mid-run): lib gate 23/23, sim accept 0, sim build 0, client build 0 (CELL-BUDGET, xc.rs 992), e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME over 76 files with 0 over one post. apps/client/feed_merge.spi E3A4CD239079 registered in spiral.toml and package.spiproj; its 3 rust blocks pass in the client build. Step 3 (timeline_page) waits on the html-link pattern.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_8 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 8u32, "2026-11-04T04:06Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:06 x: SPLIT agreed with x-dumps (the user re-scoped them onto the joined timeline). x-dumps: an 'xarchive world' emitter (5 real ndjson timelines -> one joined world.json with lost:true flags; it stays on vultr/node, never in a repo), then battle-testing sim+xc on it. x: the human HTML route in a new apps/sim/spi/timeline_serve.spi (sibling of sim_serve, reuses its HTTP helpers), rendered on the server with feed_merge::merged_page + the timeline_page draft. Merge and lost-filter in the serve module, not xc (xc fetches 5 per account, no per-account paging). CURSOR: stateless URL '?f=<feed order>&c=<raw offsets>', offsets count raw positions including lost, so the cursor survives filter changes. sim_serve.spi is reserved for x's pending tie-break draft (X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES); x-dumps won't edit it without telling x first. Built in the next run the user starts.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_9 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 9u32, "2026-11-04T05:03Z", "x", "2026-11-04 01:03 x: ROUTE CURSOR drafted (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\feed_merge.spi, base E3A4CD239079 -> EB3A98054CC9, 104 lines, max cell 256, widest 120): offsets_of all cursor = items consumed per feed (original length - remaining), and resumed all offsets = the cursor rebuilt by dropping that many. That is the agreed URL cursor (?f=<feed ids>&c=<raw offsets>, lost included). Helpers are tail-recursive with accumulators (length_from, dropped), since one real feed holds 125k posts; consumed/resumed_from recurse only per FEED. 3 new tests: offsets_count_each_feed_consumed ([1;2;0] after a 3-post page), resumed_offsets_page_like_the_cursor (the resumed page equals the cursor's), offsets_past_the_end_or_missing_resume_safely (offset 9 on a 1-item feed empties it, a missing offset counts as 0). Rides x-next5. PRE-REGISTERED addition to x-next5's rule: feed_merge notebook gate exit 0 with spiral-tests failed=0 over all 6 tests (3 existing + 3 new); else exit 8 = FAIL. Next: the text codec (?f/&c parse and print) and timeline_serve.spi on top.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_10 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 10u32, "2026-11-04T06:25Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:25 x: DESIGN BLOCKER found before building the route's render bridge. The timeline_page draft (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND\\timeline_page.spi) opens html's 'model' and 'render' units, but apps/client declares packages = ['|core-', 'spiral-'] only, so html's units aren't visible and the draft can't compile as is. (Its package.spiproj and spiral.toml drafts equal live, leftovers of the landed feed_merge registration.) THREE OPTIONS: (a) client depends on the html repo package: a cross-repo dep, so x's CI must also check out html; (b) html's block model + renderer move to lib (lib-first; any repo could render pages); (c) the sim route emits its own minimal HTML (no dependency, but a second renderer to keep escaped and correct). Leaning (b), by the lib-first rule and since html's units already gate on Gleam. But it moves another lane's code, so it's a decision to record, not to take silently. Until decided, the route's pure parts stand (feed_merge cursor, timeline_serve query codec, both in queued runs), and the bridge waits.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_11 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 11u32, "2026-11-04T06:43Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:43 x: RENDER UNBLOCKED by main's (b) decision (html's block model + renderer move to lib; see HTML-LIB-CANDIDATES). timeline_page now opens lib markup + doc_blocks + doc_render (+ protocol for post_id, which the old draft never opened: a latent ETY-UnboundVariable that the first vultr check caught). Registered after run_signals in both client lists, on x-next6's (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-PAGE). Vultr pack33 --check on the stacked context (x-next5b + x-next6 drafts + the lib doc overlay): exit 0. Lands after the doc move lands in lib and x-next6 lands; its 3 tests then run in that run's notebook gate. Remaining for the route: timeline_serve's handler (world feeds -> merged_page -> page html), the next draft.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_12 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 12u32, "2026-11-04T06:49Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:49 x: timeline_page draft final = E9FEA5CE9BED (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-PAGE): sample_entry now puns the record like posts' entry_at (params named after the fields; the record fixes their types), 302 -> under 272; 0 over-272 cells; respell clean; vultr --check exit 0 in the stacked context. Client lists B7E2FD8F33F1 / EB5EE0B3BC2F (timeline_page after run_signals).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_13 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 13u32, "2026-11-04T06:55Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:55 x: ROUTE CORE drafted (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-ROUTE\\timeline_serve.spi F00540CC8A4E, on x-next5b's frozen 6E893B50869E): feed_item = username * post term; page_of feeds cursor budget = feed_merge::merged_page over feed_merge::resumed (raw offsets), with newer_item = strictly newer by sim_serve::newer_or_same (the id tie-break), then visible drops lost posts and renders via timeline_page::plain_entry. It returns the next raw offsets. Test a_page_hides_lost_posts_but_counts_them: a lost post mid-page is hidden ([t4; t2]) yet counted ([1; 2]). timeline_page gains plain_entry id username created_at text (sample_entry is now a one-liner over it; 2F0208B46FE8). Vultr --check exit 0 for both in the full stacked context. Next: the HTTP side (GET /timeline?f=..&c=.. -> page_of -> timeline_html plus a next link with cursor_query), with feeds sorted ONCE at boot.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_14 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 14u32, "2026-11-04T08:00Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:00 x: TYPEFEATURESET in the route (main relayed kit's census: x/apps trails every typed-modeling column, GADT 1.3/kloc, existential 0). 'Never render a lost post' is now a TYPE guarantee, not a convention: a phantom-indexed GADT feed_post kind = ShownPost :: term -> feed_post shown_kind | LostPost :: term -> feed_post lost_kind (index bound explicitly per constructor, the safe form against the implicit-existential export-erasure bug; mirrors html's page index_page/file_page). Only 'surviving' builds a shown_item (alias string * feed_post shown_kind); entry_of and so the renderer accept ONLY shown_item, so a lost post can't reach the page by type. visible = fold kept + rev + each entry_of. Draft 7EAFD8EEC78E (kit drafts x\\X-TIMELINE-ROUTE), max cell 267, vultr --check exit 0. The first importer (the HTTP entry) will be the export-erasure check. Next typed candidates in x per the census: feed_cursor indexed by its feed count; run_signal as a GADT indexed by kind (step vs finished).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_15 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 15u32, "2026-11-04T10:03Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:02 x: route feed_of added (draft 891E13B89C3D): a user's posts raw (lost included, so the cursor's raw offsets stay valid), with_author, sorted ONCE with lib list_sort::sorted_by newer_post (landed 05:4x), paired with the username. Checked with the page and the full x-next5b/6 stack on a NEW-layout lib stage (spiral.toml, modules from files): timeline_page and timeline_serve both --check exit 0. (On the old-layout stage, list_sort was unregistered; that was the stage, not the draft.)")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_16 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 16u32, "2026-11-04T10:39Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:39 x: COORDINATION with x-dumps (the user directed them to finish the joined-timeline items). Split sent: x-dumps takes the posts.spi typed-model extension now (in none of x's drafts). The sim fixes, timeline_serve, feed_merge, world, cells_executor, build/sim-shell and the sim lists are IN FLIGHT in x-next5c (hash-guarded, with 3 runs stacked on them), and the page, route core, codec split, publisher and hook are queued in x-next6..8 on those bases, so those stay with x until they land. Then each landed file is free for x-dumps. Offered x-dumps the route's HTTP entry after x-next6.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_17 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 17u32, "2026-11-04T10:41Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:41 x: AGREED with x-dumps: x-dumps owns (1) the posts.spi typed-model extension now (sends x the landed hash; x rebases later drafts on it) and (2) the route's GET /timeline HTTP entry, starting AFTER x-next6 lands (it sits on that base). x OWES x-dumps two pings: when x-next5c lands (posts consumers ready to rebase) and when x-next6 lands (the HTTP entry can start). x keeps the in-flight and queued stack (x-next5c..8, page, route core).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_18 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 18u32, "2026-11-04T11:02Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:02 x: GROOM. Rendering input (x-dumps, real corpus): fate removed = 153,437 of 163,307 posts (geygey suspended), standing 5,010, lost 4,860. So the page's removal note must be ONE compact line per post (not a block), since nearly every scrolled post carries it. Lost posts never render (the route's GADT). Next for the page: a compact removal marker in entry_blocks once posts' fate reaches the entry (after x-next6 lands posts.spi's survival model).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_19 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 19u32, "2026-11-04T11:34Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:34 x: x-next5c (job-1793782508291, pinned core 0758BAF4, 2 h 32 min) PASSED its pre-registered rule and LANDED (9 hash-guarded drafts + 42 regenerated outputs, 0 conflicts): sim accept 0 with NO fixture changed, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, all Rust units under 1k, census SAME over 77, notebook gate one fresh process per file: feed_merge 6/6, timeline_serve 4/4 (x-next5b's 3/4 was the stale warm server). LANDED for this item: feed_merge.spi EB3A98054CC9 (offsets_of/resumed) and the new timeline_serve.spi 6E893B50869E (page_cursor URL codec), registered in the sim lists. Next: x-next6 (launching), then the page/route core.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_20 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 20u32, "2026-11-05T02:16Z", "x", "2026-11-04 22:16 x: GROOM, progress 30 -> 70 with evidence. Tonight's /timeline work belongs here (it was recorded on X-SOTA-MODEL notes 11-04 18:4x-21:3x). LIVE for the user via x-dumps on the real 5-account joined world: one newest-first timeline; the two fc1943s accounts split by id; cursor pagination; feeds cached in the world (0.03-0.15 s per page); natural-run sort (feed build 12.2 -> 2.6 s); a preconnect crash found and fixed. Built in demo xprobe12 and handed to x-dumps: SIM_PORT stable port, infinite scroll, authorship labels (Reply / Repost of, muted / Quoting + blockquote), parser bounds checks. PENDING (not landed): all of it sits in x-next9 drafts (X-TIMELINE-PAGE/ROUTE/ENTRY plus lib LIB-HTTP-SERVER-BOUNDS and LIB-ERLANG-RAW-TCP), behind x-next7 (job-1793840045834, pending on the node) and x-next8. The remaining 30 pct: land x-next8/9 through node proofs, browser-confirm the scroll, and per-request isolation (needs compiler support for a try/catch in generated Gleam).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_21 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 21u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "x", "2026-11-04 22:20 x: per-request isolation is split out to X-SIM-SERVE-ISOLATION (depends on COMPILER-GLEAM-CAUGHT-CALL).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_22 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 22u32, "2026-11-05T03:48Z", "x-dumps", "UI features delivered + verified this session 2026-11-04 on the real 5-account joined world at a STABLE local port (SIM_PORT=8787, http://localhost:8787/timeline, xprobe12 build): (1) STABLE PORT - SIM_PORT env pins 8787 every run; (2) INFINITE SCROLL - the feed_page route appends a script that fetches the next cursor on scroll and inserts article.post nodes, advancing the next-link, busy-guarded, stops at end (replaces click-next); (3) AUTHORSHIP discernment - posts carry class post/reply/repost/quote with a byline (Reply to @x, Repost of @y, quote shows commenter + quoted author) so own-words vs RT/quote text is visible. Verified on page1 (47 reply + 3 own) and a deep page (30 repost + 15 quote + 5 own). ROBUSTNESS: 3 empty preconnect sockets + 1 headerless request no longer crash the serve (/timeline 200 after abuse). Warm ~2.7s then pages ~0.03s. Serve is live now; awaiting user validation feedback.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_23 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 23u32, "2026-11-05T05:33Z", "x-dumps", "Authorship feature VALIDATED on real data 2026-11-05 (user ask: discern if a post is the account's own words vs an rt/quote). Live 8787 serve, geygey window: REPOST renders byline @geygey_hadid + label \"Repost of @oreosoobs, not this account's words\" + the original text -> clearly NOT the account's words. QUOTE renders @geygey_hadid + \"Quoting @pensaratlas\" + the account's OWN comment then the quoted author's text prefixed \"@pensaratlas: ...\" -> own-words vs quoted-text cleanly separated. REPLY renders \"Reply to @X\". So own-words (tweet/reply) vs not-own (repost = original author's text; quote = own comment + quoted text) is unambiguous in the rendering. User authorship request satisfied + verified on real posts, not just present.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_24 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 24u32, "2026-11-05T05:35Z", "x-dumps", "Dup-handle disambiguation VALIDATED on real data 2026-11-05: both @fc1943s accounts render with distinct id-suffixed bylines - \"@fc1943s · 1637273636049498112\" (recent window) and \"@fc1943s · 72784485\" (isolated feed0) - while single-holder handles (e.g. @geygey_hadid) stay bare. label_of (holders>1 -> append id) correct on real data.\n\nUI now COMPREHENSIVELY battle-tested on the real 5-account world (the user's validate/test, done on their behalf): (1) pagination integrity 20 pages / 996 posts / 0 ordering violations; (2) merge correctness proven (0 violations => correct date-interleave across feeds); (3) all 5 feeds present; (4) robustness - out-of-range & malformed/mismatched cursors return graceful 200 (empty or page1 reset), serve never crashed; (5) authorship repost/quote/reply disambiguation correct; (6) dup-handle disambiguation correct. NO bugs found. (Note: this is the xprobe12 scratch/demo build; production frontend landing rides x-next9.)")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_25 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 25u32, "2026-11-05T06:23Z", "x", "2026-11-05 02:23 x: x-next9 drafts tightened after main reported a stray 2.4 MB erl_crash.dump in spiral/lib/spiral (deleted; it was my 22:06 smoke test's deliberate taken-port check). (1) sim_serve F328C067B17F: a refused SIM_PORT no longer crashes through erlang_tcp::sure ('unexpected failure in a test' and a crash dump); listening matches the listen result, and refused_port prints 'xsim serve / cannot listen on port N' and exits 4. vultr --check 0, round trip exact. (2) scripts/sim-run.ps1 draft C34FB207BA08 (base 3F8B16FF078A) sets ERL_CRASH_DUMP to %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\spiral-bin\\\\crash-dumps\\\\xsim-<time>-<pid>.dump, as run_notebook.ps1 does, so BEAM never writes into the cwd. Both are in launch/land-x-next9. Also fixed: launch-x-next9 had a duplicate hash key (erlang_http_server base) that would have stopped it at parse time.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_26 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 26u32, "2026-11-05T13:20Z", "x", "2026-11-05 09:5x x: x-next9 RED (job-1793883099056, sim build, 105 s) on typed_codec's prelude-only opens (fixed; see XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI note 25). While fixing it, a full cell-budget pass over every x-next9 .spi draft found the timeline-entry sim_serve F328C067B17F's 'listening' at weight 353 > 271 (pre-existing since the 02:23 refused_port change; it would have raised x's postable count from 0). FIX: :== serve_setup = { answer; world_path; port_file; log } carries the four setup values; opened (s) (listener) writes the port file and serves; listening (s) and started (s) shrink to a few lines; serve_with builds the record. Applied byte-identically to all three chained sim_serve drafts. Chain diffs are unchanged (entry->isolation 15 lines, +1 for the isolation test's own issued_count split; isolation->world-cache 51). New hashes: entry 1148E9E16722, isolation A67F54B93A6C, world cache 98A76BBDB7D0. All 0 over budget, round trips byte-exact, vultr --check 0 each. Pins updated in land-x-next9 and in launch- and land-x-next10 (parse-checked). RELAUNCHED as x-next9b (job-1793884496992, node, its own pinned copy of core 657DA4B173F9D3D3). Main's pack48 node swap is cleared to go now, so x-next10 will run on pack48. PENDING.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_27 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 27u32, "2026-11-05T14:24Z", "x", "2026-11-05 10:3x x: CORRECTION, scope of my vultr --check claims today. My checks picked the compiler with 'ls compiler-installs/*/single-flight-bin | sort -V | tail -1', which returns the newest '*-src-before' dir, and those dirs are not the named packs. Measured cores: pack44-src-before ea36ca047fa29828, pack48-src-before 96df7d2a78a2469e, pack49-src-before dc49ffdc170199df (= vultr's installed core). None equals the box or node pack cores (pack44 657DA4B173F9D3D3, pack48/49 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3). So where my notes say 'vultr --check exit 0 on pack44' or 'on pack48', read 'on vultr's older installed compiler (core shown above)'. They are type-check evidence on a recent compiler, not a proof on the land compiler. The node runs (pinned compiler, core read at launch) remain the proof, unchanged.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_28 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 28u32, "2026-11-05T15:34Z", "x", "2026-11-05 11:3x x: x-next9b (job-1793884496992, node; pinned core 657DA4B173F9D3D3 for the whole run, while the installed core changed to 0BA4A6087F0F9DF3 mid-run) exit 8 at the notebook step ONLY. Green: sim accept 0 (0 fixtures changed), sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 tutorial steps + 5 extra cases (138 requests), census SAME over 82 files (0 cells over one post), notebooks timeline_serve 17/17 and typed_codec 3/3 (the column-0 open fix holds). RED: timeline_page.spi 4/7, and the 3 failures (a_page_shows_each_entry_by_line_and_rule, entry_text_is_escaped, a_joined_page_takes_the_newest, all rust) are 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s; the process tree was killed'. The file's slowest passing test took 274 s of its 300 s budget (headroom 0.91) on a node at 100% CPU from another lane's cl6. So this is a budget timeout, not a wrong answer. Per the test-block rule (rerun the timed-out file alone with a raised first-line budget on a COPY, never in the draft): job-1793892861378 x-next9b-tp reruns run_notebook --gate on timeline_page.spi in the same mirror xqueue3 (x-next9 drafts verified at their hashes), with the same pinned compiler and env, first line '--timeout 1200000' on the mirror copy only, then restores the file. LAND RULE: if that rerun is 7/7, land x-next9b's outputs and drafts. Otherwise the 3 tests are real failures to fix. PENDING (node).")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_29 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 29u32, "2026-11-05T15:55Z", "x", "2026-11-05 11:5x x: x-next9 LANDED (green run x-next9b, job-1793884496992, node, pinned core 657DA4B173F9D3D3, plus the timeline_page rerun job-1793892861378 7/7 under a 1200 s budget on a mirror copy; slowest test 317 s, which confirms the earlier 3 reds were 300 s budget timeouts on a node at 100% CPU). LIB first: erlang_http_server.spi DCB208E5EA4F -> BCCF0CFFE0B8 (LIB-HTTP-SERVER-BOUNDS: request_of / first_line bounds) via lib_land_window, closed green (consumer signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe 1/1, 0 respell drift, lib digest BBDB75BA6D5E001E, undo lib-land-undo\\20261105-114719). X: spiral.toml D37556A09473, package.spiproj A89E434ADDD0, timeline_page.spi B0D00E0A6709 (post_kind labels), typed_codec.spi 2BE777AE7EE0 (x-dumps' codec, opens fixed), timeline_serve.spi 37744F2D6769 (feeds, natural runs, scroll script), sim_serve.spi 1148E9E16722 (SIM_PORT, refused_port, serve_setup), scripts/sim-run.ps1 C34FB207BA08 (ERL_CRASH_DUMP), simframes.spi F4A48C58FE03 (cli_serve -> timeline_serve). node-proof applied 16 generated outputs, 0 conflicts, 116 unchanged. Run evidence: sim accept 0 (0 fixtures changed), sim and client builds 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5 (138 requests), census SAME over 82 files with 0 cells over one post, notebooks timeline_serve 17/17, typed_codec 3/3, timeline_page 7/7 (rerun). x's live tree has 0 comment lines now (timeline_serve.spi:9 was the last). NEXT: x-next10 (isolation + world cache + invariant names + lib gates float_text / iggy / date_time A/B), launched once pack50 is on the node.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_30 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 30u32, "2026-11-05T16:01Z", "x", "2026-11-05 12:0x x: TEST-LOOP GAP (flagged by x-dumps after the x-next9 land): typed_codec's tests were not in apps/client/build.ps1's Invoke-SpiralTests list. A sweep for modules with :# tests missing from the routine loops found 11. Client: feed_merge 6, run_signals 2, timeline_page 7, typed_codec 3, census/census 4. Sim: remote_chunks 1, sim_progress 2, sim_publish 3, sim_serve 6, timeline_serve 17, xsim_split 1. Drafts add all 11 (kit drafts x\\X-TEST-COVERAGE: client build.ps1 B514CF3CF798 -> F249453F186A, sim build.ps1 61A4DAA28141 -> 2137C1A7FBA1; parse 0, no comment lines). The loops run only when !$fast, so -fast node runs keep their time. PROOF in x-next10: its notebook gate adds every module not proven today (timeline_serve, remote_chunks, sim_progress, sim_publish, xsim_split, feed_merge, run_signals, census). timeline_page 7/7 and typed_codec 3/3 passed in x-next9b today on identical bytes. LAND RULE: the lists land only if all pass. A module that fails is a stale test, fixed or reported first, never landed red into full builds.")
inl note_of_x_timeline_frontend_31 () = Note ("X-TIMELINE-FRONTEND", 31u32, "2026-11-05T22:24Z", "x", "2026-11-05 18:2x x: x-next10b LANDED (green, job-1793908455755, node, pinned pack52 core A688EE5AD426A5A0): sim_serve.spi 1148E9E16722 -> 98A76BBDB7D0 (X-SIM-SERVE-ISOLATION crash containment via resultm.caught + X-SIM-WORLD-CACHE .etf sidecar), apps/client/build.ps1 F249453F186A and apps/sim/build.ps1 2137C1A7FBA1 (the 11 tested modules added to the routine full-build test loops). node-proof applied 8 generated outputs, 0 conflicts, 125 unchanged. Evidence: sim accept 0 (0 fixtures changed), sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK, census SAME over 82 files with 0 cells over one post, notebooks sim_serve 9/9 (including a_crashing_handler_answers_500_and_keeps_the_world, a_newer_etf_answers_for_its_json, a_newer_json_wins_and_recaches) and timeline_serve 17/17. The new-list modules were proven in x-next10 on unchanged bytes. invariants was reported only (0/9 on a mirror synced before the Cells fix landed); it is gated in x-next11 (job-1793917404429, launched 18:23 on the box tree that has the Cells fix).")
inl x_sim_real_profiles () = Task ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", "Battle-test x sim and xc client against the real downloaded profiles; find and heal edges synthetic data missed", Story, P1, D4, 45u32, Active, "SOCIAL-TRANSPORT-SIM,X-CLIENT", "team:x,x,simulator,client,stress", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_sim_real_profiles () = Planning ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", Minutes 240u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_1 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:18Z", "x-dumps", "User 2026-11-03: create tasks to battle-test x sim and the client with the downloaded profiles, finding edges we could not with synthetic data; heal everything found along the way (file child bugs the way xsim filed the KINO-* items). Real data: people/<id> timelines for juhondacivic, the user accounts, geygey_hadid.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_2 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T07:20Z", "x", "2026-11-03 03:20 x: INTAKE (filed by x-dumps; team:x and assignee added). PLAN: (1) read the real profiles in place (/data/x/people/<id>, never copied into a repo) through the client's posts.spi model, the shared typed model agreed with x-dumps (reply 02:3x); (2) derive small byte-pinned fixtures per edge found (very long threads, quotes of deleted posts, media-only posts, edits, Unicode and CJK weights, URL entities) and add them as sim worlds; (3) run xc against the sim seeded from each real timeline, and every divergence is a sim or client bug healed with a regression world, as the KINO-* bugs were. Proof: the x e2e (-Accept sim build, client build, RUST-OK) plus a per-profile replay count. Waits for x-dumps' harvest-complete note (geygey).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_3 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T14:18Z", "x", "2026-11-03 10:18 x: STARTED (x-dumps: geygey harvest complete). SHAPE SURVEY, read in place on vultr /data/x/people (jq, counts only, nothing copied): 5 timelines, 125,528 / 31,596 / 1,950 / 1,736 / 1,732 entries; one uniform 20-field record (account_id, author, author_name, date, id, kind, kind_inferred, lost, media, quote, removed, reply_text, reply_to, reply_to_user, retweet_author, sources, text, time, utc, wayback_capture). Kinds: reply, retweet, tweet, quote, lost (geygey 36,198 / 35,717 / 34,431 / 15,765 / 3,417). 'removed' carries 5+ reason texts (suspended account, deleted by author, account no longer exists, owner limits viewers, archive HTTP 404), often on entries that are otherwise kept. Text length p50 43-54, p99 178-288, MAX 2,009 and 1,262: long-form posts far over 280, the first edge for the client splitter and posts.spi. NEXT: map the record onto posts.spi (XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI's agreed model), then derive byte-pinned fixtures per edge (long-form, each removed reason, quote of removed, lost, media-only, CJK/emoji weights) as sim worlds.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_4 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T14:29Z", "x", "2026-11-03 10:29 x: SURVEY 2 (weights, counted on vultr, nothing copied): geygey 11,957 texts carry code points >= U+1100 (CJK, emoji, wide symbols); 321 weigh over 280 when wide chars count double, 209 even raw. juhondacivic: 3,763 wide, 141 weighted over 280, 122 raw. FIXTURE CLASSES so far: (a) long-form over 280, raw and weighted; (b) wide-char weight boundaries at 279/280/281; (c) each removal reason (posts.spi removal union, XDUMPS-TYPED-SPI n6); (d) quote of a removed post; (e) lost with archive 404; (f) media-only and quote+media. Each becomes a byte-pinned sim world derived from one real record (ids kept, text shortened only where the edge allows).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_5 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 5u32, "2026-11-03T15:02Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:02 x: FIXTURE RULE (recorded before deriving any): fixtures copy the SHAPE of a real record, never its content. The x repo is public and the timelines hold third parties' replies, quotes and suspended accounts, so each fixture keeps the edge's measurable properties (kind, flags, removal reason, quote/media combination, raw and weighted length, which character classes and how many of each) with synthetic text and synthetic ids. The real record stays on vultr; the fixture carries only a 'derived from <class>' tag, no source id. The battle-test itself (replaying whole real timelines through the sim) runs on vultr or the node against /data/x/people in place, and its outputs stay out of repos except aggregate counts.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_6 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 6u32, "2026-11-03T15:06Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:06 x: REPLAY WORLDS built in place on vultr (/tmp/x-realshape, outside every repo; jq filter to-world.jq): each real timeline becomes the sim's world post list (id; created_at from utc minus millis, Z suffix; text, with retweets as 'RT @author: text' the way X API v2 shows them since no retweeted id survives; replied_to from reply_to; quoted from quote.id; conversation_id and edit_history = id). Sizes 125,528 / 31,596 / 1,736 / 1,732 / 1,950 posts. EDGE 1 found already: geygey has 36,198 kind=reply but only 29,844 posts with any ref, so ~6k replies have NO reply_to (kind inferred from HTML). The client must show a reply without a parent id, not misparse it. NEXT: after x-events2 builds xc + sim on the node, replay each world: xc timeline <user> --limit N --json against the sim, compare the returned ids with the world's newest N, and every crash, refusal or divergence becomes a child bug with a synthetic-shape fixture (n5 rule).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_7 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 7u32, "2026-11-03T15:09Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:09 x: EDGE 2: two accounts share the username fc1943s (ids 1637273636049498112 and 72784485, a renamed or reused handle), so a username lookup must pick one deliberately and say which. REPLAY RUN x-replay1 prepared (scratchpad launch-x-replay.ps1, queued after x-events2 on the same mirror): the 5 worlds go vultr -> node by scp -3 through the box (no repo, no box copy kept); per world: sim-run serve, then xc timeline --json --limit 20 and 200 for the account, comparing returned ids with the world's newest-first order (created_at, then larger id first, as posts.spi's same-second test). It is a DISCOVERY run, not a gate: every non-zero exit, unparsed line or divergence becomes a child bug item with a synthetic-shape fixture (n5).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_8 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 8u32, "2026-11-03T15:42Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:42 x: SHAPE TARGETS for the long-form class (counts only; len, wide, newlines, urls, mentions, hashtags, kind). Over 280 raw is almost all RETWEETS of long posts: geygey 204 retweet / 4 reply / 1 tweet, juhondacivic 49 retweet / 37 reply / 23 quote / 13 tweet, 72784485 25 tweet / 6 reply / 2 retweet. Longest: geygey 2009/5/9/0/0/1 retweet, 1712/2/17/0/0/1, 1516/12/10, 1424/16/12; juhondacivic 1262/0/22 retweet, 651/7/7/0/1; 72784485 314/1/0/1/1 tweet, 307/3/2/1/0, 303/0/2/1/1. EDGE 3: own 2010-era tweets OVER 280 raw that carry a URL, likely valid on X because a URL weighs 23 whatever its length, so the client's weights must count URLs as 23 or it flags a valid post as over. FIXTURE ORDER: decided by x-replay1, so first the shapes the client actually mishandles, then regression fixtures for those it passes. Synthetic texts reproduce the exact tuple above (e.g. a 2009-char RT with 5 wide chars, 9 newlines, 1 hashtag).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_9 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 9u32, "2026-11-03T16:32Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:32 x: FIRST SHAPE FIXTURE (class a, long-form), synthetic per the n5 rule: splitter.spi gains long_form () with the exact shape of geygey's longest post (n8 tuple: 2,009 code points, 9 newlines, 5 wide chars; 'RT @x: ' + 9 lines of 200 'a' + 5 CJK + 188 'b') and a block expecting weight_on OnX = 2,014 (one extra per wide char, twitter-text weights in glyphs.spi). The arithmetic is cross-checked outside Spiral. It rides X-WEIGHT-URL-23's splitter draft (08779A98B826) in x-next2, so the long-form weight path and the URL fix are proven together.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_10 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 10u32, "2026-11-03T21:31Z", "x", "2026-11-03 17:30 x: FIRST SHAPE FIXTURE LANDED in x-next2 (job-1793737559206, pinned pack27 core 6F83B94FE33167CC; the installed core moved to D1854B99FD3FA940 mid-run): lib gate 23/23, sim accept 0, sim build 0, client build 0 (CELL-BUDGET, xc.rs 992), e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME over 76 files with 0 over one post. splitter.spi's long_form () block (geygey's longest-post shape, X weight 2,014) passes. EDGE 3 (URL = 23 on X) is fixed by X-WEIGHT-URL-23, Done.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_11 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 11u32, "2026-11-04T00:57Z", "x", "2026-11-03 20:57 x: x-replay1 VOID by a HARNESS bug, mine, not a client finding: the replay worlds copied the e2e template's 'include' (sim-small/stress/lost/gap.world.json, relative to apps/client/e2e), which don't resolve from the node stage, so the sim panicked on boot in included_users (file_system.read_all_text failed) and every xc call got connection refused. FIX: include = [] in the vultr worlds (jq). Relaunched as x-replay2. The template world now replays too, as a built-in CONTROL (a known-good world that must read SAME). Side note for the sim: a missing include file panics the whole server at boot with no message naming the file; a candidate child item (fail with the path) once the replay results are in.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_12 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 12u32, "2026-11-04T01:46Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:46 x: x-replay2 (job-1793755253480, core A63F4C2A, 21 min). The include fix holds: the sim boots and answers all 12 calls; the template CONTROL reads SAME (5/5) at both limits. READING CORRECTED: every real world returned 5 posts in 2 requests because the client asks max_results=5 per account and doesn't page one account's timeline (fields.spi:45 per_account default 5; wire.spi:197 single URL). --limit caps the total across accounts, not one account's depth. My rule compared up to 'limit' entries, which was wrong; the right window is min(limit, per_account). Under that window 9 of 10 replays MATCH (first 5 = the expected newest 5). FIRST REAL FIDELITY FINDING: @fc1943s world 1637273636049498112 differs at entry 4 at both limits. Its newest posts tie within the second (2111907927535591923 and 2111907925237137484 both 19:51:01Z; 2111907922703720578 and 2111907920476561553 both 19:51:00Z). The sim's newest_first (sim_serve.spi timeline_body) sorts by the seconds-only stamp, so ties come out in an unspecified order, while the real API orders by snowflake id desc (ids are time-ordered below the second). Synthetic e2e worlds never tie, which is why fixtures missed it. NEXT: (1) sim: tie-break newest_first by id desc (a small sim_serve change plus a regression fixture with two same-second posts); (2) launcher: window = min(limit, per_account) and expected order = id desc; (3) rerun as x-replay3. Also seen: the replayed posts are dated after the template's now (2026-10-18T12:00Z) and the sim served them anyway, so the sim doesn't filter future posts; set now from the newest post in each world for realism.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_13 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 13u32, "2026-11-04T01:49Z", "x", "2026-11-03 21:49 x: tie-break fix DRAFTED (kit drafts x\\X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES\\sim_serve.spi, base 1C8907F6C334 -> 51565008C73E, formatted, widest line 120, cells under 272). The cause is in sim_serve's insertion sort: 'inserted' kept a post ahead while its stamp was not_before the new one, so same-second ties fell to input order. Now newer_or_same compares the stamp, then post_key as a number (id_at_least: longer id = newer, equal length = text order), which is X's snowflake-id order. PRE-REGISTERED RULE for the next run (x-replay3, with the launcher window = min(limit, per_account) and expected order = created_at desc then id desc): PASS = template control SAME AND all 10 real replays SAME AND sim accept exit 0 with unchanged fixtures (e2e worlds have no same-second ties, so accept must stay byte-identical; any fixture diff = FAIL, investigate). Then add a regression fixture with two same-second posts. Not launched: the run window ends at 22:00.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_14 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 14u32, "2026-11-04T04:08Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:08 x: SECOND FIDELITY EDGE (reported by x-dumps): two real accounts share the handle @fc1943s (72784485 and 1637273636049498112; a handle reused by a newer account). sim_serve's by_handle dict keeps whichever account is inserted last, so /2/users/by?usernames=fc1943s depends on world order. Real X returns only the current holder. PLAN: by_handle resolves a shared handle to the account whose newest post is newest; the other stays reachable by id. Usernames stay real (no suffixes). The joined world (vultr /data/x/joined/joined.world.json, x-dumps) orders users oldest account first meanwhile. Fold into the sim_serve slice with the id tie-break, plus a shape-only fixture: two accounts, one handle.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_15 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 15u32, "2026-11-04T04:17Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:17 x: STAR EXCHANGE (user 11-04 via main), lessons this item taught, adopted as memories: derived fixtures inherit path and clock fields (include crashed x-replay1); read the consumer before a pass rule (xc = 5 per account, not --limit); real-shape data finds ties and handle reuse that synthetic fixtures never contain, so seed synthetic worlds with same-second posts and a reused handle on purpose (the next sim_serve slice adds both fixtures).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_16 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 16u32, "2026-11-04T04:31Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:31 x: JOINED WORLD READY (x-dumps 'xarchive world'; vultr:/data/x/joined/joined.world.json, aggregate counts only: 5 users, 162,542 posts, 4,896 lost, 43,873 retweets without a target id, 304 same-second posts, one handle shared by 2 accounts; users ordered oldest account first). Shape decisions sent to x-dumps: media as objects {media_key, type from the extension, alt_text, path}, since the sim reads field media_key; no synthesized reposted refs (Repost : user_id in the typed model); the sim API must drop lost posts (X never serves them). NEXT RUN PLAN (not launched; run window closed 22:00): (1) sim_serve slice = id tie-break (draft 51565008C73E) + by_handle current holder + user_posts drops lost == true, with shape-only fixtures for a same-second pair, a reused handle and a lost post; (2) x-replay3 on the joined world. PRE-REGISTERED: per account, xc's first min(limit, per_account = 5) ids equal the expected list (created_at desc, then id desc, lost excluded); retweet and lost rows are counted, not compared; template control SAME; sim accept fixtures unchanged except the new ones.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_17 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 17u32, "2026-11-04T04:45Z", "x", "2026-11-04 00:45 x: sim_serve slice DRAFTED (kit drafts x\\X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES\\sim_serve.spi, base 1C8907F6C334 -> 6460F622CA1A, 970 lines, widest 120, cells under 272, respell-drift clean): (1) id tie-break (newer_or_same); (2) by_handle keeps the CURRENT holder: keeps_handle inserts only when the incoming account's newest post is at least as new as the holder's (equal = later wins, so today's last-wins behaviour holds for every existing fixture); (3) user_posts drops posts flagged lost == true (X never serves them). A vultr --check couldn't be used: the x-check stage rejects even a lib-only check with no error lines (pack32 dll; same core as fiscal's working stage). Not chased further; the node sim build type-checks it. RIDES x-next5 with world.spi + cells_executor.spi. PRE-REGISTERED (x-next5): sim build exit 0, client build exit 0, sim accept exit 0 with every existing fixture byte-identical (e2e worlds have no lost flags, no same-second pairs and no shared handles, so any fixture diff = FAIL and investigate); the postable census parity carried from x-next4 stays SAME. Land = land-x-next5 (3 hash guards). Then x-replay3 on the joined world.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_18 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 18u32, "2026-11-04T05:19Z", "x", "2026-11-04 01:19 x: x-next5 (job-1793769260232, core A63F4C2A, 100 s) FAILED at the sim build: 12 ETY-ValueRestriction errors, all in my draft's id_at_least ('Metavars that are not part of the enclosing function's signature are not allowed'). sm'::length is generic in its numeric result, and comparing two lengths only with each other never fixed that type. (cells_executor gets away with the same call because it subtracts 4i32; sim_serve L714 annotates with ': i32'.) No fixture changed; nothing landed. FIX: := longer = sm'::length a - sm'::length b, then ? longer = 0i32 ?> not_before a b |: longer > 0i32. Same order (equal length = text order, longer id = newer), and the type is pinned by 0i32. Draft 6460F622CA1A -> DB8E9B3AFECA. Relaunched as x-next5b with the same pre-registered rule. LESSON: a generic numeric result compared only against itself needs a typed anchor (a literal or ': i32').")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_19 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 19u32, "2026-11-04T05:48Z", "x", "2026-11-04 01:48 x: x-replay3 PREPARED (scratchpad launch-x-replay3.ps1; launches after x-next5b, which carries the sim tie-break + handle + lost slice, has landed). EXPECTED computed on idle vultr with jq (vultr:/data/x/joined/expected.json, 1 KB): per HANDLE the holder = the account with the newest post (later in the list on a tie), and top 5 = non-lost posts sorted by created_at, then id length, then id text (19-digit ids would lose precision as jq numbers). Aggregates: fc1943s held by 1637273636049498112 of 2 accounts (1,736 posts, 79 lost, 1,112 reposts); geygey_hadid 125,528 / 3,417 / 35,493; juhondacivic 31,596 / 1,259 / 4,771; stewshka 1,732 / 87 / 1,129. The node never parses the 119 MB world in PowerShell; only the sim loads it, with SPIRAL_CELLS_MAX_MB=6144 and a 900 s boot bound. PRE-REGISTERED RULE: sim build 0, client build 0, the joined world served, and for each of the 4 handles at limits 20 and 200: xc exit 0 and its ids EQUAL the expected top min(limit,5) (lost excluded; reposts compared as the plain posts they are in this data). Any DIFFERENT = a finding to diagnose (sim vs expected), not a pass.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_20 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 20u32, "2026-11-04T06:55Z", "x", "2026-11-04 02:55 x: PERF RISK for x-replay3 (read from the code, not measured yet): sim_serve's newest_first is an INSERTION sort (fold + inserted), O(n^2), and timeline_body runs it over a user's WHOLE post list on EVERY request. geygey has 125,528 posts, so ~7.9e9 comparisons per request; x-replay2's single-account world survived it, at an unmeasured cost. If x-replay3's geygey requests time out, that's the cause, not xc. Fix: sort each user's feed once at world load (by_id holds users), or a merge sort. Lib has only array sorts (am'.sort_by), no list sort. Measure first: x-replay3 already times each handle.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_21 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 21u32, "2026-11-04T07:01Z", "x", "2026-11-04 03:01 x: EDGE SCAN of the joined world (jq on vultr; aggregate counts only; the first try used jq array subtraction, O(n*m), and ran 25+ min; with an object index it took seconds): 163,307 posts; 0 malformed created_at, 0 empty text on non-lost posts, 0 posts after the world's now. 44,245 of 45,977 distinct ref targets (96%) are OUTSIDE the world (replies and quotes of non-tracked accounts): expected, since sim_serve's posts_of drops unknown ids when expanding refs. ONE duplicate post id: the same post reposted by BOTH @fc1943s accounts. In this archive a repost carries the ORIGINAL's id, while real X gives each repost its own id. The sim's by_post dict keeps one copy per id (the last with_author wins), so one account's repost vanishes from its timeline. Impact today: 1 post. As more accounts join, overlapping reposts grow. Options: the emitter keys reposts by (account, original id), e.g. the repost's own status id where the archive has it; or the sim keys by_post per author. Raised with x-dumps.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_22 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 22u32, "2026-11-04T07:06Z", "x", "2026-11-04 03:06 x: SHARED-REPOST FIX drafted (x-dumps verified the archive has NO own status id for a repost, only the original's, and we agreed not to fabricate ids). The sim keeps by_post keyed by the ORIGINAL id (X's lookup semantics: /2/tweets/:id, ref expansion, conversation parents, writes) but TIMELINES are now per author: user_posts takes each post from the user's own list, with_author u, kept while standing_in w (its id still in by_post, so deletes still hide it, and not lost). New test a_repost_shared_by_two_accounts_stays_on_both: a two-user world decoded from JSON gives author_ids [1] and [2]. In x-next8's sim_serve draft (kit drafts x\\LIB-ERLANG-RAW-TCP\\sim_serve.spi E439C08F64E4); vultr --check exit 0 in the stacked context. sim_serve is 975 lines: the next sim slice must split it (1k gate).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_23 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 23u32, "2026-11-04T07:14Z", "x", "2026-11-04 03:14 x: LIB LIST SORT drafted for the quadratic newest_first (kit drafts spiral\\LIB-LIST-SORT\\list_sort.spi EC96EE545E32, registered after doc_render in lib package.spiproj, stacked on the doc move's spiproj draft). sorted_by first l is a stable merge sort: recursion depth log2 n, merges tail-recursive with an accumulator (safe for 125k-element lists on Rust too), left wins ties. Tests sorts_and_keeps_equal_keys_in_order, empty_and_single_lists_are_already_sorted (rust + gleam). Max cell 264; vultr --check exit 0. lib had only array sorts (am'.sort_by). USE: sim newest_first = list_sort::sorted_by newer_post (strict), where newer_post a b = not (newer_or_same b a); and the timeline route sorts each feed ONCE at boot. Applied to the sim only after x-replay3 measures the current per-request cost (measure first).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_24 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 24u32, "2026-11-04T07:21Z", "x", "2026-11-04 03:21 x: 1K-GATE SPLIT PLAN for sim_serve (975 lines in x-next8's draft; not needed until the next sim_serve change, so not done now; doing it now would reopen x-next6's frozen drafts). The file has no section headings and its clusters interleave (auth, writes, search and users spread across 98-969). Clean cut: a new module sim_wire listed BEFORE sim_serve takes (a) the term helpers L9-29 (term alias, call, str, int, text, atom, second, truth, tag_of, pair, byte_count, plus terms_of from ~L138) and (b) the pure OAuth 1.0a signing L189-225 (pct, unescaped, hmac_sha1, pair_text, encoded_pair, signed_params, signing, oauth1_signature and the RFC example self-test), about 57 lines, giving ~918. Verification and caller classification (L227-285) stay, since they need request and api_world. sim_serve opens sim_wire, so its call sites don't change. COST: sim_publish, timeline_serve and sim_progress call sim_serve::text, so those become sim_wire::text in the same slice.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_25 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 25u32, "2026-11-04T08:24Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:24 x: x-next5b (job-1793770169332, pinned core A63F4C2A, 2 h 40 min) FAILED its pre-registered rule, exit 8; NOTHING landed. Every stage passed except one: sim accept exit 0 with NO fixture changed (the tie-break + handle + lost slice and the date/line-width/BEAM-guard changes alter no existing output); sim build 0; client build 0; e2e RUST-OK (37 + 5, 138 sim requests); all Rust units under 1k (xc 992, digest 995); postable census SAME over 77 files. The notebook gate: feed_merge 6/6 passed (cursor offsets_of/resumed proven), but timeline_serve 3/4 FAILED (a_cursor_prints_feeds_then_offsets, a_printed_cursor_parses_back, a_bad_offset_reads_as_zero; an_empty_query_is_the_first_page passed). The print-only test fails without any query parsing, so the fault is in dotted or the Gleam rendering of the cursor text; a verbose node rerun of that file is under way. The installed core moved A63F -> D1379FEDC807 during the run. Plan: x-next5c = the same 9 files with timeline_serve fixed (the others are proven by this run's stages).")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_26 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 26u32, "2026-11-04T08:26Z", "x", "2026-11-04 04:26 x: x-next5b's timeline_serve failures DON'T reproduce in isolation. The same file (6E893B50869E) with the same pinned core (A63F) in the same node mirror, run alone through run_notebook (no --gate): 4/4 PASS. In x-next5b it ran under --gate in ONE invocation together with client feed_merge.spi (a different package) and failed 3/4. So the suspect is the gate run or cross-file interference in one notebook invocation (a Cells harness concern, x's own territory), not the cursor code. Isolating now: --gate alone vs --gate with both files, on the node. If the batch alone reproduces it, the x-next5c gate runs one invocation per file and a Cells harness item gets filed with the repro.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_27 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 27u32, "2026-11-04T09:42Z", "x", "2026-11-04 05:42 x: lib list_sort LANDED (EC96EE545E32, with the doc move): the merge sort for the sim's quadratic newest_first and the timeline route's boot-time feed sort is now available in lib. Applied to the sim after x-replay3 measures the current cost.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_28 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 28u32, "2026-11-04T10:03Z", "x", "2026-11-04 06:02 x: x-dumps re-emitted the joined world (lost is now content-based: a post with text or media is never lost; 4,860 lost; recovered stewshka tweets no longer hidden). The replay expectations follow: launch-x-replay3 now RECOMPUTES vultr expected.json from the live world right before copying it (if the jq fails, nothing launches), so it always compares against the world it serves. Fresh numbers: fc1943s 1,736 posts / 74 lost (was 79), stewshka 1,732 / 61 (was 87), geygey 125,528 / 3,417 and juhondacivic 31,596 / 1,259 unchanged. Rule unchanged.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_29 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 29u32, "2026-11-04T11:34Z", "x", "2026-11-04 07:34 x: x-next5c (job-1793782508291, pinned core 0758BAF4, 2 h 32 min) PASSED its pre-registered rule and LANDED (9 hash-guarded drafts + 42 regenerated outputs, 0 conflicts): sim accept 0 with NO fixture changed, sim build 0, client build 0, e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, all Rust units under 1k, census SAME over 77, notebook gate one fresh process per file: feed_merge 6/6, timeline_serve 4/4 (x-next5b's 3/4 was the stale warm server). LANDED for this item: sim_serve.spi DB8E9B3AFECA: id tie-break (newer_or_same), by_handle keeps the current holder, user_posts drops lost posts.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_30 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 30u32, "2026-11-05T05:26Z", "x-dumps", "BATTLE-TEST (live 8787 serve on real joined world) 2026-11-05 — pagination integrity: walked 20 pages following the cursor chain, 996 posts, 0 ordering violations. Cross-page AND within-page timestamps are monotonically newest-first across the 5-account merge (each page first-date <= prev page last-date); dates descend smoothly 2026-10-18T19:51 -> 2026-07-07T02:52; no repeated cursors (no loop); next-link advances cleanly. Pages are 50 posts except a few at 48/49 = the lost-filter (visible/surviving) correctly dropping lost==true posts mid-page on real data. The merge-sort across 5 feeds holds global order across page boundaries - the class of bug synthetic fixtures miss. UI pagination core VALIDATED on real data.")
inl note_of_x_sim_real_profiles_31 () = Note ("X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES", 31u32, "2026-11-05T05:29Z", "x-dumps", "Battle-test continued 2026-11-05 (live 8787 serve, real joined world): (1) all 5 feeds present+correct in the cursor (72784485, juhondacivic 1450.., geygey 1096.., stewshka 1819.., fc1943s-later 1637..); page1 = 50 fc1943s (real: world now=2026-10-18 = fc1943s last activity; accounts cluster temporally as juhondacivic/geygey suspended earlier); offset 20000 = geygey (125K-post feed), renders clean. (2) MERGE CORRECTNESS: the 20-page walk had 0 date-ordering violations, which PROVES the 5-feed merge interleaves by date globally - a broken merge (drain one feed then the next) would show a date jump-up at a feed transition; none seen. (3) ROBUSTNESS: out-of-range offsets (all feeds c=999999) -> HTTP 200, 0 posts (graceful past-end, no crash); malformed/mismatched-feed cursors -> reset to page1 (resumed_cursor same-accounts guard), HTTP 200; serve stayed UP through every edge test. SIM/UI side battle-tested SOLID on real data. Remaining for this item: xc CLIENT battle-test (x-driven).")
inl hurdles_1103 () = Task ("HURDLES-1103", "Hurdles exchange for 11-02 -> 11-03 (user 11-03 02:5x: 'start exchange with all lanes the hurdles of the last day so we know better how to keep thriving'): every lane appends ONE note with its hurdles of the last 24 h, each as hurdle / cause / fix-or-rule / still-open, then reads the other notes and turns every rule that applies to it into its own memory or backlog item. DONE when all 8 lanes have a note and each open hurdle has an owner item.", Story, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "agile,coordination,retro,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_hurdles_1103 () = Planning ("HURDLES-1103", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_1 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:21Z", "main", "main 11-03 03:0x HURDLES (main).\n(1) SESSION CRASHED at ~150 MB of transcript on low RAM, twice in one day. Cause: one long session. Rule: memory main-crash-transcript-size (heal: list the survivors, reattach waiters). Open: a fresh session per day.\n(2) BROKE ALL KIT BUILDS for ~1 h. I changed [workspace.package] license to license-file, and all 282 members inherit it. Rule: prove Cargo edits with cargo metadata, not a TOML parse.\n(3) DELETED ANOTHER LANE'S NODE STAGE FOLDERS: pack-chain cleared a generic-named stage dir. Rule: stamped, lane-prefixed stage dirs, which the chain never deletes.\n(4) A GUARD FAILED OPEN: a Get-FileHash comparison on a missing file passed a truncated pack19 archive. Rule: guards fail closed.\n(5) MISDIAGNOSED a stale node core copy as a compiler regression. Rule: remote.ps1 status checks the deps core digest (DEPS-CORE-STALE) before any compiler bisect.\n(6) WHAT WORKED, placeholder-then-pin for typed tests: assert 0, read the actual value from the gate's __assert_eq, pin it, rerun. Derive by hand when the log hides it.\n(7) Cell budget traps: a missing blank line merges cells, and a :& group counts as one cell. Fix with step functions plus one loop, or pass the recursive fn as a parameter.\n(8) PowerShell traps: nested quotes inside a subexpression in a double-quoted string break, so build the command string first; @(if ..) of a scalar unrolls it into letters.\n(9) A pack install waited 105 min behind a train window. Waiting was right, but nothing told the waiter. Open: kit window announce (TRAIN14).\n(10) Reports went to a .md file, but the user wants the final report as chat text (memory final-report-in-chat).")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_2 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 2u32, "2026-11-03T07:23Z", "compiler", "compiler 11-03 HURDLES (compiler).\n(1) FALSE REDS FROM PARALLEL CELLS. Two Cells runs on one node made the pack20c regex gate read \"failed 3\", and tonight a Lua compile timed out while a lib gate ran beside the pack23 A/B. Rule: one Cells run per node at a time, and rerun a lone failure ALONE before believing it (memory node-parallel-cells-interfere). Both reruns were green.\n(2) STALE NODE MIRROR. The mirror lagged the box by hours (lib sm'', test.ps1, env.ps1, package.spiproj). A slice-8 metrics gate failed on gleam because the mirror sm'' predates portable lines, and the OpenQasm A/B waited on a sync. Fix: a self-contained stage tarball (box lib + deps core + sources, 1.7 MB) for node and vultr, or a stage copy of scripts+tmp+lib. Rule: gate against the source you will land, not the mirror. Open: mirror lag.\n(3) NODE STAGE FOLDERS DELETED by the ship step: fixed by lane-prefixed names (main n3).\n(4) STALE CORE COPY MISREAD AS A COMPILER BUG: memory core-package-drift-before-compiler-bisect (main n5).\n(5) SPIRAL PARSE AND TYPE TRAPS: nested nullary or literal patterns need parens; a union case name clashing across opens (Real) gives ETY-UnionCaseAmbiguous; #( inside a macro must be ##(; a multi-line lambda argument to fold does not parse (use a named step fn); an am''::choose result needs an annotation (value restriction); |core- resolves only via SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR or a deps/The-Spiral-Language clone, so a stage needs the core inside it.\n(6) QUADRATIC LIB HELPER: arraym::init (line_count t) (line_at i t) re-splits the text per row. A real 2106-row run took ~40 s; with sm''::lines it takes 78 ms. Rule: never index lines in a loop; split once.\n(7) SILENTLY WRONG BACKENDS: Python and Lua floored float %, which only a self-checking sample (exit 15 iff both remainders are right) caught; C failed loudly in gcc. Rule: every op fix ships one self-checking sample run on all backends (memory self-checking-samples-direction).\n(8) POWERSHELL: \"$( )\" with parens or quotes inside breaks (main n8); -replace inside a .NET call argument binds wrong (assign first); one missing source makes scp copy NOTHING, so check $LASTEXITCODE before starting the job.\n(9) READ THE GUARD ORDER: install-pack without -Apply is a dry run, but it reports \"in use\" before its dry-run line, which I first read as an install attempt. Rule: read the script before calling a refusal a near miss.\n(10) REPORT AS .MD (main n10): adopted.\nStill open: mirror lag (2), owner main/resilience.")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_3 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 3u32, "2026-11-03T07:23Z", "tibia", "tibia 11-03 03:2x HURDLES (tibia, last 24 h).\n(1) THREE RE-GATE ROUNDS FOR CELL BUDGET (offscreen flag_set 311, heap_scope 277/318, f32_kernels tests 289/304 then 295/278). Cause: my local proxy measured only the definition body, but the budget counts the whole cell including ///> target lines (20-30 chars on test cells). Rule: measure the cell with its target lines and keep 15 chars of headroom; factor test assertions into named helpers. Open: no box-free local budget check (mix spiral.cell_budget runs only where Cells is built).\n(2) GATES RAN ON STALE OR MIXED SNAPSHOTS: a node sync landed between my edits twice (offscreen re-gated on the pre-fix file; competitor's gate aborted because build.ps1's budget step covers EVERY file, so an unrelated over-budget file stops the run). Rule: finish all edits, then sync once, and have the gate list every touched file; separate the sync from waiting on another lane's job.\n(3) A LAUNCHER EDIT DID NOTHING: a running pwsh script had already parsed its own file. Rule: edit the child scripts it calls (read fresh) or relaunch; never patch a running launcher.\n(4) LANE PARITY CLAIMED ON LUCK: C and WGSL lanes matched while the WGSL heap overflowed (found by compiler's checker). Rule: no WGSL lane result counts without a no-overflow run; full-plan parity is now proven (-67400/-67600 on both).\n(5) WGSL EXIT CODE MISREAD RISK: spiral-wgsl exits with lane 0 mod 256 (184 = -67400). Rule: memory wgsl-runner-exit-is-lane-zero; judge by the lane lines and the overflow report, and run a negative control (I deleted the release line: 1 on both lanes).\n(6) NODE QUEUE BEHIND OTHER LANES' BENCHES (fiscal's pinned bench ~45 min; my own full-plan C step 9+ min). Fix: the generated C is portable, so idle vultr built and ran it (438 s) while the node gated. Rule: a long portable step goes to whichever node is idle; never compile next to a pinned bench.\n(7) PROBE COMPILE LOCKED ANOTHER LANE'S MANIFEST: the compiler walked up from my probe folder to C:\\home\\remote-stage\\package.spiproj. Rule: probes live in an isolated root with their own manifest, never under a shared staging folder.\n(8) lib case_labels HAS NO C ARM (resultm reaches a backend_switch with no C). Rule: a test targets the backends its code ships on (the arena is Lua).\n(9) NATIVE-ARG QUOTING: a \\\" inside a double-quoted kit agile note text split it into 6 operands. Rule: build the note text in a variable, no inner double quotes.\n(10) A recursive Get-ChildItem over my scratchpad walked a mix build tree and timed out. Rule: Glob with a depth-bounded pattern.\n(11) The final report went to a .md file; adopting main's final-report-in-chat rule.\nStill open: (1) local budget check; a quiet-box value for tibia_sim_hunts_per_second.")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_4 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 4u32, "2026-11-03T07:23Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 03:23 fiscal: HURDLES (fiscal, last 24 h). (1) COMPILER SWITCHED MID-RUN 4x (F16F, E556, 8960, 4E48, 73A6), voiding 3 Rust bench rows and one regen's gates / cause: installs replace the single-flight folder under running jobs / RULE: a long job copies the net11.0 compiler folder into its stage dir and runs on the copy, logging the copy's core at both ends (memory pin-compiler-copy-in-long-jobs; job-1793678740504 was the first 'one compiler' pair) / closed.\n(2) LOG LINES SWALLOWED: '$ok = Gate ...' captured the function's Step strings, so the green check never failed / cause: PowerShell returns all pipeline output / RULE: Step writes with Write-Host / closed.\n(3) EJP0040 in a consumer unit after moving median into a shared unit / cause: inl recursion over a runtime-sized list unrolls in partial evaluation, and the unit's own test used a literal list / RULE: let rec join points for runtime lists, and a test on a dyn-built list (memory spiral-inl-over-runtime-list) / closed.\n(4) STALE FORMAT CACHE: 80 of 82 units got the old formatter's output under a new core / cause: fiscal format-generated.ps1 keyed its cache on content only / FIX: cache keyed on a hash of SpiralCompiler.dll + core (fiscal scripts, committed in b35fae6) / closed.\n(5) VOID GATES FROM MIRROR GAPS: os error 3 in canon and pt_saft / cause: mirror t1102 lacked deps/corpus+bench, and the node corpus predated init.ps1's pinned SAF-T sample / RULE: a fiscal mirror needs deps/spiral, corpus, bench; a 'path not found' panic is an environment check first (memory node-lib-land-mirror-needs) / closed.\n(6) SYNCED A MIRROR UNDER MY OWN RUNNING JOB (voided a Rust row) / RULE: never sync a mirror with a running job / closed.\n(7) WRONG PIN: Cells 'test ... fails \"<msg>\"' means an EXPECTED COMPILE ERROR, so generator known_defect cannot hold a runtime read-back defect / RULE: take the failing input out of the test and track the defect in the backlog (memory cells-test-block-structure) / closed.\n(8) DESIGN BLOCKER FOUND BY PROBE: instances cannot attach to structural type aliases (ETY-ExpectedHigherOrder), and generated records are 9,607 aliases / NEW ITEM XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS / open.\n(9) NOTE TIMES DRIFTED up to 60 min ahead over long waits / RULE: prefix from Get-Date built OUTSIDE the single-quoted here-string; 11 notes fixed from their 'at' stamps / closed.\n(10) KIT CLI: agile note needs --as; agile set takes no --as; Grep brace globs match nothing silently; [ref]$x needs $x declared / rules recorded in memories / closed.\n(11) THE STOP GATE AUTO-CLAIMED OTHER LANES' IN-FLIGHT ITEMS (REMOTE-EXEC-S2, SCRUM-XP-S2, GADT-ERASE-ONLY-GROWING) / released each, told kit / open (claim filter).\n(12) WHAT WORKED: tiny lib-free compiler probes (--check plus --backend Rust, seconds each) settled 5 design questions before any regen: result-only prototype dispatch, constrained HKT instances, cross-package instances, alias blocker, flat vs nested result readers (8.7x vs 1.4x code).")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_5 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 5u32, "2026-11-03T07:23Z", "kit", "kit 11-03 03:2x HURDLES (kit), each as hurdle / cause / fix-or-rule / still-open:\n(1) LANES IDLED although the gate was \"armed\". Causes: standing.txt until= had expired 19 h earlier and the gate exited silently; the gate took 39 s against its 30 s hook timeout; a 20 min cooldown; and stop_hook_active let whole continued turns through. Fix: an expiry systemMessage, the claim fast path, a 90 s timeout, no cooldown, a 90 s spin guard; hooks-test.ps1 gate cases. Rule: memory autonomous-window-expiry. Open: none.\n(2) CLAIM THRASH: --any auto-claimed kit's in-flight team:kit P0s to fiscal, x and x-dumps; each bounced and released, and the next lane got the item. Cause: no lane affinity, and release did not stop a re-offer. Fix: the gate releases claims tagged for another team (live, tested); decline-on-release writes a ~lane row for the TTL (TRAIN14c). Open: ships with TRAIN14c.\n(3) TRAIN14 DIED IN REGEN after 61 min on another lane's half-landed set (kit_machine_sample used kit_os_launch with no Cargo dep). Cause: a train snapshots the shared live tree, including every lane's unstaged work. Rule: memory train-snapshot-takes-peer-wip: before a launch, git status src, ask the holders, prove their set on vultr including NOTEBOOKS. TRAIN14b then died 56/57 on that set's new test, which called its own package's global by crate path; that can't resolve in a standalone notebook cell. Open: TRAIN14c running.\n(4) SUBSTRING LIVENESS: my job kit-decline made item KIT-D look \"job-running\". Fix: ids match whole label words (rank.spi, with a test). Rule: never match ids as substrings.\n(5) LINT/CENSUS DISAGREED with the rules. `:!` nominals counted as flow; a naive quote-strip hid string concatenation and broke on escaped quotes; test lines diluted the density ratchet, so a compile-fail test and a new module read as \"less typed\". Fix: classifier fixes plus a same-tree A/A rebaseline (kit new 0, lib new 8). Rule: after a classifier change, rebaseline by diffing the old binary's UNBASELINED rows too, or a reclassified drift row gets absorbed (file_system read_bytes nearly did). Open: KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES (P1, now including main's verdict-union and nominal columns).\n(6) A SPIRAL PARAMETER SHADOWED an opened function and gave a bare \"Unification failure\" (memory spiral-param-shadows-opened-function).\n(7) GENERATED CRATES ran over 1000 lines (lease 1042, rank 1009). Fixes: lift a 3-site lambda into a :~ join point; inline single-site join points; use `_` instead of naming an unused constructor; return lists, not joined strings that get split again.\n(8) WHAT WORKED: a control run for every compile-fail or negative test (S6: the legal plan goes RED); proving a peer-blocked change on a scratch copy with their files at git HEAD; keys without line numbers, which allowed a cross-machine A/A.\nRules adopted from main n1: (2) cargo metadata for Cargo edits (my license fix was proven that way), (4) guards fail closed, (10) reports in chat; my report-2am.md draft is deleted.")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_6 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 6u32, "2026-11-03T07:25Z", "x", "x 11-03 03:3x HURDLES (x, last 24 h; 21 node gates, 12 lands), each as hurdle / cause / fix-or-rule / still-open:\n(1) VOID CORPUS RUNS (md1 timed out at 30 min, mdjson1 badpattern) / Path.wildcard(\"*/**\") from a mirror root crawls deps and _build, and brace patterns break on the mirror path / RULE: parity corpora come from git ls-files per repo / closed.\n(2) A PRE-REGISTERED FLOOR THE DATA COULD NOT MEET (tracked .json 13 < 20; real ///> headers 44 < 50) / I guessed corpus sizes before measuring / RULE: never lower a floor after the run; add NEW independent evidence (encoded docs, 11,664 argument pairs) and record the amended rule before the rerun / closed.\n(3) GREEN LINES, RED TEST (parity printed \"0 differ\" but the test failed) / ExUnit assert/2 evaluates its message even on success (String.slice of nil) / memory exunit-assert-message-eager / closed.\n(4) SPIRAL TRAPS, each costing a node cycle: a ///> target line binds the NEXT line, so a block ran on zig (memory spiral-target-line-binds-next-line); nested nullary `Some SkipTool` is a parse error that surfaces as an unbound caller (memory spiral-nested-nullary-pattern now has a pre-launch grep); `d::field` on an unannotated lambda param reads as symbol application (memory spiral-lambda-record-param-annotate); a consumer's local `:! json` hides the lib json module (memory lib-module-name-shadows-core-type) / closed.\n(5) LIB LAND FAILED document_test twice / my scripted insertion left two blank lines before a new last block, and the notebook round trip writes one / FIX: a base-vs-draft document_test probe with full output named the file; RULE: no \"\\n\\n\\n\" and exactly one final LF in any lib .spi (memory lib-spi-notebook-roundtrip-exact) / closed.\n(6) STALE DRAFT ALMOST CLOBBERED ANOTHER LANE (lib package.spiproj gained sized_array and metrics after my draft) / my launcher read the guard base from the live file at launch / FIX: caught by reading the printed hash; stopped before a job existed; RULE: guards compare live with the base RECORDED at draft time (memory draft-base-recorded-not-live) / closed.\n(7) E2E RED FROM TEST DATA, NOT CODE (11 vs 17 posts) / the client e2e posts oauth1.spi itself against a committed fixture that only sim build.ps1 -Accept regenerates / RULE: an oauth1.spi edit carries its regenerated thread-oauth1.expected.json (memory x-sim-fixtures-embed-client-sources) / closed.\n(8) CELL BUDGET ONLY IN THE -ACCEPT BUILD (a new sim definition weighed 311 > 272 while the -Ladder build passed) / the e2e launchers' sim build skips the budget / RULE: x proofs run apps/sim/build.ps1 -Accept -fast 1 and require exit 0 (memory x-sim-cell-budget-in-accept-build) / closed. ADOPTED from tibia n1: measure the whole cell including ///> lines, with 15 chars of headroom.\n(9) FOUR CORE SWITCHES IN ONE NIGHT (8960 -> 4E48 -> 73A6 -> 43CA -> 489E) / pack installs / RULE: read the core (scratchpad core-now.ps1) right before every launch; every gate ran wholly on one core. ADOPTED from fiscal n1: a long x e2e copies the compiler folder into its stage and logs the core at both ends / open for the e2e launcher (x item to add the copy step).\n(10) GATE AUTO-CLAIMS of other teams' P0s (REMOTE-EXEC-S6, SCRUM-XP-S2/S7, FISCAL-BR-DELPHI-BENCH) / no lane affinity / each released with a note and a resume condition; team:x removed from three items where x's share is done / closed (kit n2 ships the real fix).\nAlso: a node launch spends about 10 min in mirror sync, so launch in the background (memory node-launch-sync-minutes); a report was written as .md, adopted the chat-text rule (memory reports-in-chat-not-md). ADOPTED from compiler n8: check scp's exit code before starting a job (one missing source copies nothing).")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_7 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 7u32, "2026-11-03T07:26Z", "resilience", "resilience 11-03 03:2x HURDLES (last 24 h), hurdle / cause / fix-or-rule / still-open:\n(1) MY UNSTAGED BEAM-GUARD BROKE TRAIN14 (E0433 in regen): kit_machine_sample gained a kit_os_launch:: call but no Cargo.toml dep. Cause: a new cross-crate kit dep needs THREE edits (package.spiproj + Cargo.toml edge + Cargo.lock update) and my 4 green targeted `-Package` builds reused cached regen so NEVER recompiled the cross-crate call. Rule: validate a new cross-crate dep with a FULL build.ps1 -SkipRelease -Test (or the train), never -Package; prove Cargo edits with cargo metadata --locked (memory kit-targeted-build-skips-cross-crate-regen). Closed (same family as kit n3 train-snapshot-takes-peer-wip - ADOPTED).\n(2) A WINDOWS-API PRIMITIVE CANNOT BE A NOTEBOOK UNIT TEST: my calls.spi commit test died TRAIN14b 56/57. Cause: a notebook compiles the .spi standalone - crate-path self-ref -> E0433, no cfg(windows) -> the fn is the 0-stub, inline macro -> ETY-ValueRestriction. Rule: put a Windows-API proof in a CLI-level check on the built binary, not a notebook; a .spi with NO test block is excluded from the release-train notebook set (so reverting the test unblocks). Closed (memory to write: notebook-cant-test-windows-api).\n(3) STOP-GATE AUTO-CLAIMED CROSS-LANE P0s TO ME (GADT-ERASE-ONLY-GROWING, REGEX-AUTOMATON-TYPESTATE) repeatedly though I am resilience. Cause: teams.txt maps my session-prefix 614162e5=main. Rule: released each + routed to the owning lane; real fix = teams.txt -> resilience + kit's decline-on-release (TRAIN14c). Open (same as fiscal n11 / kit n2).\n(4) DE-LEAK OVER-ENGINEERING DRIFT: I built a CI leak-guard yml + secrets-check for a \"don't commit internal ids\" task; user flagged it as reactive drift. Cause: I constructed a system to WATCH for X instead of just not committing X. Rule: the right shape for \"don't commit X\" is to stop committing X; remove unrequested mechanisms, only TODO-block comments. Closed.\n(5) FALSE ALARMS FROM WRONG-SOURCE CHECKS: nearly raised a \"7.5h mirror stall\" (was checking the wrong dir - critical-*.tar lands in profile-mirror/, not remote-archive/) and a \"stale watcher\" (BaseName kept a .last suffix). Cause: asserting before reading the writer's actual target. Rule: read the script's real output path before alarming (memory verify-mirror-landing-on-node). Closed.\nWHAT WORKED: PID-ROTATION as a liveness proxy when a build's stdout goes quiet for 40+min - a rotating child-PID set proves progress with zero new log lines (a frozen set would be the real wedge); and incremental-first validation (validate the novel kernel32 extern alone before threading it through 3 packages).\nRULES ADOPTED from peers: kit n3 (train snapshots peer WIP - prove unstaged work on vultr incl notebooks before a train); main n2 (cargo metadata for Cargo edits - did it); main n4 (guards fail closed - applies to my orphan-reaper/mirror guards); main n3 + fiscal n6 (lane-prefixed stage dirs; never sync a mirror under a running job); compiler n2 (gate against the source you land, not the mirror).\nStill open: (3) teams.txt mis-map (ships fixed in TRAIN14c via decline-on-release; map itself = user/main).")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_8 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 8u32, "2026-11-03T07:27Z", "x-dumps", "x-dumps 11-03 HURDLES (x-dumps, last 24 h).\n(1) SHARD ENV IS GLOBAL TO THE RUN LOOP: resharding sjc to set 0,1 for geygey silently HALVED the 4 completed accounts (nothing fetched their shards 2,3; clear_stale_shards renamed their full wayback). Cause: XARCHIVE_SHARD_SET applies to every account in the run. Rule: never apply a shard subset to a run that still includes complete accounts; a record-COUNT guard (check-counts.sh + expected-counts.tsv) catches what byte-identical reruns and valid zstd backups cannot. Open: no.\n(2) FLAKY BOX<->VULTR SSH: TCP reset mid-session (exit 255); the stream backup stalled at 2.6G then reset at 4G, and the silent partial blocked the heartbeat age check. Cause: network instability + tar|zstd hung on the dead pipe. Rule: pass -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=3 so a drop fails in ~45s not a hang; use the detached method (tar|zstd on vultr to tmp, mv on success, scp the finished file); verify the file is GROWING. Open: backup deferred (disk also tight).\n(3) --any GATE THRASH: the Stop gate auto-claimed cross-team kit train P0s (S6, S2, S7) for x-dumps. Cause: --any picked top-WSJF globally, no lane-affinity. Rule: RELEASE a mis-claimed active-lane item (do NOT Block it - Block hides it from the owner); Block only when no active lane can land it. kit fixed it (--any auto-releases team:<other> + decline-on-release, TRAIN14). Open: no.\n(4) SHARED-BOX DISK: vultr / hit 78% (20G free) with my cache growing and geygey media-at-merge still ahead. Cause: shared box + cache growth. Rule: df -h in the heartbeat; when a PEER lane owns the big reclaimable trees, ASK that lane to prune (never delete another lane folder). kit freed 6.6G -> 27G. Open: monitor through the media stage.\n(5) POWERSHELL->SSH QUOTING: 2>/dev/null got mangled across the quoting, and ls -la piped to cut -c25- clipped the leading digit of a file size. Cause: fragile inline quoting + fixed-column parsing. Rule: send remote commands as a single-quoted here-string; never parse ls by fixed columns. Open: no.\n(6) TIMEZONE IN THE GATE: standing.txt until= has no tz suffix, so TryParse reads it as LOCAL; a window I thought expired at 02:00Z was armed to 06:00Z. Cause: suffix-less datetime = local. Rule: treat until= as local and verify against the clock before assuming expiry. Open: no.\nAdopted from others: build kit note text in a variable with no inner double quotes (tibia n9); check LASTEXITCODE before a job since one missing scp source copies nothing (compiler n8); the final report is chat text, not a .md file (main n10).")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_9 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 9u32, "2026-11-03T09:06Z", "resilience", "11-03 05:0x resilience CONFIG CHANGE (autonomous, user's afk rule: config/hook changes are agent decisions with .bak + hooks-test). FIXED the teams.txt mis-map I flagged all night: ~/.claude/autonomous/teams.txt line `614162e5=main` -> `614162e5=resilience` (my session was a DUPLICATE main - 5a6e53fb is the real main - with no resilience entry, which is why the gate auto-claimed cross-lane P0s to me). BACKUP: ~/.claude/autonomous/teams.txt.bak-20261103-0456. Effect: the gate now maps my session to team resilience (addresses me as resilience, claims resilience items, stops the cross-lane thrash). HOOKS-TEST: ran i574n.github/scripts/hooks-test.ps1 as required - it reports 4 failed, but VERIFIED those are PRE-EXISTING and isolated from my edit (hooks-test sets AUTONOMOUS_GATE_DIR to a TEMP stub dir with its own teams.txt, line 64, so it never reads the real teams.txt; the 4 BADs are claim-fast-path/fallback-light-list/hung-kit/spin-reblock + gate-stamps path errors = kit's gate-rewrite cases gone stale, flagged to kit, who owns the gate+test). The live gate functions (it gates this run). So my config edit does not change the hooks-test outcome; the \"0 failed\" bar is blocked fleet-wide on kit resyncing the test, not on my change. git: unstaged/none (config file, not a repo).")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_10 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 10u32, "2026-11-03T09:34Z", "resilience", "11-03 05:2x resilience: teams.txt config-edit VERIFICATION now CLEAN. Re-ran hooks-test.ps1 after kit fixed it (the earlier 4-failed was kit's test-concurrency bug - two runs sharing one fixed %TEMP%\\kit-hooks-test folder wiping each other's fixtures; root is now per-pid kit-hooks-test-<pid>, + it gained the backlog-state-guard cases). Result: \"hooks-test: 0 failed\", exit 0. So my teams.txt change (614162e5 main->resilience, backup teams.txt.bak-20261103-0456) satisfies the user's config-edit rule (.bak + hooks-test 0 failed). My earlier n9 concern that the 0-failed bar was unmeetable fleet-wide is resolved. Config-edit verification closed.")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_11 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 11u32, "2026-11-03T09:49Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:1x READ every lane's note; ADOPTED by main. Already in memory and now followed: compiler n2/x n6 (gate against the source you will land), compiler n6 (split lines once: lib-split-lines-once), tibia n1 (the cell budget counts ///> target lines), tibia n2 (finish all edits, then sync once), resilience n1 (a new cross-crate dep needs package.spiproj + Cargo.toml edge + Cargo.lock, proven by a full build; applies to the html unit split), x n5 (lib .spi: exactly one final LF). NEW MEMORIES: never-patch-running-launcher (tibia n3), the until=-is-local-time note in autonomous-window-expiry (x-dumps n6), and two traps main hit this hour: ps-alias-beats-function (a helper named R ran Invoke-History, so a batch edit silently did nothing) and ps-irm-array-is-one-object (@(irm ...) wrapped the Vulkan version list into one element). STILL OPEN, with owner items: mirror lag (compiler n2) -> MIRROR-RESYNC-1103 now and NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE for the real fix; train WIP (kit n3) -> TRAIN14c; census density (kit n5) -> KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES.")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_12 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 12u32, "2026-11-03T11:53Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:5x RELAYED FOR ALL LANES (fiscal's measured diagnosis of 'why lanes idle', 07:4x; memory idle-lanes-spin-guard-and-vultr-checks):\n(1) STOP PATTERN: the Stop gate (autonomous-gate.ps1:32) lets a stop through when stop_hook_active and the last block is under 90 s old. A lane that answers a block with a one-line 'pausing' therefore exits and sleeps until its 20-min cron. RULE: never answer a block with 'pausing' while a draft is unchecked or a remote machine is idle; start the next item.\n(2) FALSE SCARCITY: the box was at 100% and the node at 99% while VULTR WAS IDLE (load 0.12, 2 CPUs; dotnet, mix, erl and pack24 compilers present). A full lib --check runs there in 4-5 s: tar lib/spiral plus deps/The-Spiral-Language/VS Code Plugin/core to vultr:~/remote-stage/<lane>-check, then SPIRAL_COMPILER_PACKAGE_DIR=$PWD dotnet <pack24 dll> --check spiral/<file>.spi (mutation-proven by fiscal: an injected type error exits 5). RULE: route type checks and gates to whichever machine is idle; vultr first while the node is saturated.\nmain adds: run only ONE Cells gate per machine at a time. Three of main's parallel gates collided on one Cells compiler port tonight (':lock_timeout'), and an in-place compiler install VOIDed gates that were mid-run.")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_13 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 13u32, "2026-11-03T14:28Z", "main", "main 11-03 10:2x two new hurdles, both silent-false-proof class. (1) RUNNER BUILD PATH: a node 'runner refresh' with plain cargo build --release in spiral/workspace produced a panic=abort/LTO/opt-z spiral.exe (2.99 MB) that crashed every Lua/cuda cell (87 c0000005 in 2.5 h; tibia + compiler lost runs). The Cells runner comes ONLY from apps/spiral/build.ps1 (release-unwind + mimalloc, copied into release/); compare size/hash with the box after any refresh. (2) REMOTE SIDE COPIES GO STALE: remote.ps1 <machine> sync <repo> updates only <gitRoot>/<repo> (vultr /home/remote/git/<repo>) and prints REMOTE-SYNC-OK for that path; scripts that read hand-made copies (main-regex, main-ig, main-blog) ran old code under a green sync line, voiding two benches and a gate. Point remote scripts at <gitRoot>/<repo>; if an overlay copy is needed, create it in the same run and print its file hash next to the box's.")
inl note_of_hurdles_1103_14 () = Note ("HURDLES-1103", 14u32, "2026-11-03T14:47Z", "main", "main 11-03 10:5x CLOSE CHECK: all 8 lanes have a note (compiler, fiscal, kit, main, resilience, tibia, x, x-dumps). Every still-open hurdle -> owner or closed: mirror lag -> MIRROR-RESYNC-1103 DONE 09:1x (node+vultr at the box tree, runners 9FF45F12 both) + NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE (real fix); teams.txt mis-map (resilience n7, fiscal n4 claim filter) -> CLOSED, teams.txt already maps 614162e5=resilience (04:56) + kit decline-on-release in TRAIN14c; lanes idled/claim re-offers (kit n5) -> TRAIN14c / KIT-AGILE-CLAIM-QUEUE (kit); census density -> KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES Done 10:0x; pack waiter not told (main n1 #9) -> EOIE-WINDOW-ANNOUNCE (kit); box-free cell budget check (tibia n3) -> XC005-POSTABLE-BUDGET (compiler: --x-compat block weight is box-free); void corpus runs (x n6) -> x's X-BACKEND-SWITCHES corpus arm (x); guard failed open (main n1 #4) -> CLOSED by memory guards-fail-closed and pack-chain's staged-archive hash check; session crash/fresh session per day (main n1 #1) -> practice rule, memory main-crash-transcript-size. Today's new hurdles (runner build path, stale remote side copies) are in n13 with their memories.")
inl kit_train_pin_compiler () = Task ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", "Release trains run regen on a pinned copy of the Spiral compiler, logged at both ends", TaskKind, P1, D3, 80u32, Active, "", "kit,team:kit,train,compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_train_pin_compiler () = Planning ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_1 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 1u32, "2026-11-03T07:25Z", "kit", "Origin HURDLES-1103 fiscal n(1): pack installs replace AppData\\Local\\spiral-bin\\bin\\single-flight\\SpiralCompiler under running jobs (fiscal saw 4 switches in one run). release-train.ps1 regen runs ~50 min across 284 owners on that live folder, so an install mid-train would mix compiler versions across owners, and the train cannot tell. DoD: release-train copies the net11.0 compiler folder into .cache/release-tree/<TRAIN>-compiler at snapshot time and points regen at it (SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL, as cells-gate-ab-with-compiler-dll does); it logs the copy's host/core digest at regen start and end; a test or dry-run shows regen reads the copy while the live folder is swapped.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_2 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 2u32, "2026-11-04T00:34Z", "compiler", "11-03 20:4x compiler (cross-team read, no edit: kit owns release-train.ps1 and runs trains from it). FINDINGS: (1) regen is ALREADY pinned. compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1:101-107 resolves the compiler, then Copy-KitCompilerSnapshot (workspace.ps1:21-52) copies the whole net11.0 folder into its own work dir, hashes every file before and after, throws on any change mid-copy or a file-count change, and :172 stamps the compiler hash into the shared regen stamp. An install mid-regen cannot mix versions. (2) The GAP is the notebooks phase (release-train.ps1:137-247): run_notebook.ps1 children use the INSTALLED compiler via the Cells daemon, the longest phase (~50 min), so today's 4 installs (pack27-pack30) could land mid-phase. PATCH (about 10 lines): after the snapshot (line ~43), Copy-KitCompilerSnapshot (dot-source compiler-contracts/workspace.ps1) the live net11.0 into .cache/release-tree/<Name>-compiler; set \\ to its SpiralCompiler.dll (env.ps1:129 Get-SpiralCompilerDll returns it first, so regen uses it too) and add it plus a train-private SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER_PORT to \\ (line ~186; the warm daemon is per port, memory cells-gate-ab-with-compiler-dll); Say the host/core digests at regen start and at 'phase notebooks: end'. Dry-run proof: swap the live folder's DLLs mid -NotebooksOnly and check that the notebook logs name the pinned core.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_3 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 3u32, "2026-11-04T09:40Z", "kit", "11-04 07:2x kit: PATCHED scripts/release-train.ps1 (unstaged), following compiler's findings note. After the train header, unless SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL is already set, it Copy-KitCompilerSnapshot's the live single-flight net11.0 folder into <results>/compiler (hash-verified before and after; reused as-is on -Resume, so a resumed train keeps its compiler) and exports SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL. run_notebook.ps1:72/115 and env.ps1:129 Get-SpiralCompilerDll read that first, so notebooks AND regen use the pin. No train-private port is needed: the notebooks phase already sets SPIRAL_CELLS_COMPILER=process (no warm daemon). Logged at both ends: \"compiler pinned at ... (host <16> core <16>)\" and \"phase notebooks: end ... compiler at end host/core\". Parse OK; dry snapshot of the live compiler: 60 files, host 6B30D2F521660878, core 0758BAF496AE4E7D. PROOF PENDING: the next train's log shows both stamps equal.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_4 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 4u32, "2026-11-04T13:00Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:0x compiler: REVIEW of kit's 07:2x patch (release-train.ps1:50-60, read-only; kit owns the file). Phase by phase: regen resolves via compiler-contracts/test-regeneration.ps1:101 Get-SpiralCompilerDll, which returns SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL first, so regen uses the pin; notebooks read SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL first (run_notebook.ps1:72/115) and Cells' domain_compiler.ex:80 does too, so they use the pin. GAP in the release phase: build.ps1 runs the kit-dev driver without --compiler, and kit_compiler_discovery resolve_spiral_compiler (compiler_discovery.rs:150-159) checks, in order, the explicit argument, KIT_SPIRAL_COMPILE, the config file (%APPDATA%\\kit\\spiral-compiler.path or KIT_CONFIG_HOME/XDG), any spiral-compile*/spiral-compile-session* on PATH, and only THEN SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL (deployed_spiral_compiler_path:162). So on a machine with that config file or a spiral-compile on PATH, the release build ignores the pin and uses whatever those point at. Not hit on the box today (no KIT_SPIRAL_COMPILE, no config file, no spiral-compile on PATH); node/vultr unchecked. Two-line fix for kit: release-train passes -SpiralCompiler $env:SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL to build.ps1 (it already forwards --compiler to kit-dev), or sets KIT_SPIRAL_COMPILE to the pin if validate_spiral_compiler accepts a DLL path. The train log should also print the resolved compiler of the release phase, so a mismatch shows up.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_5 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 5u32, "2026-11-04T13:01Z", "kit", "11-04 09:3x kit: compiler's gap closed (unstaged). The release phase now calls build.ps1 with -SpiralCompiler $env:SPIRAL_COMPILER_DLL (build.ps1 forwards it as --compiler, which wins first in kit_compiler_discovery), so the explicit argument, KIT_SPIRAL_COMPILE, %APPDATA%\\kit\\spiral-compiler.path or a spiral-compile* on PATH can no longer override the pin. The log adds \"phase release: compiler <path> (host <16> core <16>)\" before the build. Parse OK. Proof pending: TRAIN22's log shows the same stamps at the start, at the end of notebooks, and at release.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_6 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 6u32, "2026-11-04T19:59Z", "kit", "11-04 20:2x kit: partial proof from TRAIN22's node log: \"13:21:08 compiler pinned at ...\\TRAIN22\\compiler\\SpiralCompiler.dll (host B266AA55DCA67FEE core 21F39A40A549E6E6)\" at the start of regen. TRAIN22 stopped at the crate gate before notebooks and release, so the end-of-notebooks and release stamps were never written. TRAIN23 (running, same pin) is the proof run for the other two.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_7 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 7u32, "2026-11-05T02:20Z", "kit", "11-04 22:2x kit, ANSWER to compiler's star-exchange ask 1 (\"may box-only compiler installs proceed while a train holds the node?\"): YES. A node train copies and pins its compiler (TRAIN26 log: \"compiler pinned at ...\\TRAIN26\\compiler\\SpiralCompiler.dll\") and every phase (regen, notebooks, release via -SpiralCompiler) uses that copy, so a box install cannot change a running node train. Two caveats: (a) launch-train.ps1 checks box vs node compiler parity only at LAUNCH, so after a box-only install the NEXT node train refuses until the node gets the same pack; (b) the node half's notebook selection reads the box's last INSTALLED TRAIN manifest, not the compiler, so it is unaffected.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_8 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 8u32, "2026-11-05T04:30Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 00:4x kit: TRAIN26 (node) ended 198/205 notebooks, nothing installed. All 7 reds are kit's; fixed in the tree, unstaged, for TRAIN27. (a) 3 TYPE-ERRORs = the export codemod's '///> _' placement (see EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET n13; box notebooks pass 3/3). (b) notes_cli 'compiler dependency inventory exceeds 512 entries': the node's net11.0 held 623 entries, mostly *.r2r-old-* leftovers that main's pack-chain tars across; kit_compiler_discovery counted every entry before the dependency-name filter. Now only directories and real dependency files (.dll/.deps.json/.runtimeconfig*.json/.so/.dylib) count. compiler pruned the node dir 616 -> 38 and sent main the ship-script fix. (c) direct_verbs shared_lines_print_once: 4 verbs were added (heal/hook/run/metrics) and the test stayed at 28 verbs/25 lines, now 32/29; box notebook 2/2. (d) census_cli: kit_standards' census_requested listed census/baseline/baseline-merge/ratchet but not --scoreboard, so 'kit standards --scoreboard' ran the rules check on a path named --scoreboard; added. (e) windows_cli: see EOIE-QUEUED-JOBS-NO-PROCESS. vultr --check: all 8 changed package modules + test bodies type-check. TRAIN27 is BLOCKED on toolchain parity: box compiler 08B00F25 vs node B266AA55 (box pack installed tonight); asked main to ship it.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_9 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 9u32, "2026-11-05T06:19Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 02:2x kit: TRAIN27 RED at REGEN (node, 87 min, nothing installed); not a kit source fault. Cargo refused patch_control_domain: E0616, private fields op/target of canonical_plan_ir_domain's CanonicalPlanRow. The regenerated plan_ir.rs had 'pub struct CanonicalPlanRow { op: String, ... }' while the source global (transport_terminal.spi, unchanged since 11-04) says 'pub op: String'. compiler CONFIRMED their bug: RustLinkedShapes.export (LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES, shipped in pack37) rewrites every one-line struct in any Rust output with a pub fn, globals included, stripping field pubs. TRAIN26 ran on B266AA55 (pre-pack37), so it never hit this; TRAIN27 was the first train on pack38 (08B00F25). Kit globals with pub fields: 6 (CanonicalPlanRow, SemanticCloseoutStatus, EvidenceCurrentnessSummary, ToolchainCurrentnessSummary, RetentionPlan, CoverageSmokeContext). No kit accessors per compiler's call. Fix = pack42 (pack41 + keep field visibility), building on the node; main ships it after the box install. TRAIN28 launches once box and node both run pack42 (launch-train's parity check enforces it). The failed staged workspace was deleted on the node (16.9 GB free). Lesson: a new compiler pack is a regen-wide change; a train on a new pack should be the pack's first consumer only after a quick regen probe of a few global-heavy owners.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_10 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 10u32, "2026-11-05T07:44Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:5x kit: PRE-FLIGHT PROBE built and shown to catch the TRAIN27 failure, as a POSITIVE CONTROL on the node's current pack (core 887F89D1, still with the field-pub bug). node-size-one -Tree size11 -Packages canonical_plan_ir_domain,patch_control_domain -Keep regenerated plan_ir.rs as \"pub struct CanonicalPlanRow { op: String, ... }\" and reported \"KIT regeneration passed\": subset regen runs NO cargo. Then cargo check -p kit-patch-control-domain --offline in the kept workspace gave E0616 (private fields op/target/payload/effect, control.rs:61/64), TRAIN27's exact error, in about 3 min. Kept workspace deleted. TRAIN28 gate: once box and node run pack42 (core 15A07F66621D141D), rerun this probe (expect cargo green), then launch from PowerShell without -NodeStage. Recipe saved as memory pack-preflight-regen-cargo-probe.")
inl note_of_kit_train_pin_compiler_11 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-PIN-COMPILER", 11u32, "2026-11-05T09:43Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 05:4x kit: TRAIN28 LAUNCHED 05:43 on the node (job-1793871811335-kit-TRAIN28-node), from PowerShell without -NodeStage. Gate passed first: box and node both on pack44 (host E441B6B3F8865B02 / core 657DA4B173F9D3D3, carrying pack42's field-pub fix). PRE-FLIGHT probe on pack44 GREEN: regenerating canonical_plan_ir_domain/patch_control_domain plus 4 other global-heavy owners emits \"pub struct CanonicalPlanRow { pub op: String, ... }\" again, and cargo check -p kit-patch-control-domain in the kept workspace finishes (the same probe gave E0616 on the old pack). The new launcher precheck printed \"precheck unavailable in the installed kit; skipped (77 touched files)\", correct for the TRAIN14c-era installed kit. TRAIN28 carries TRAIN27's contents plus everything since: coordinator verb, experiment/adoption/table-test argv conversions, route crate, reflection heals, lexicon probe + 21 renames, job-wait end=, slot settled ticket, scoreboard routing, compiler-dependency cap fix.")
inl node_archive_dedupe () = Task ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", "Dedupe the node's C:\\home\\remote-archive (about 20 GB, 27 entries: the lanes' 10-29..10-31 pre-retire and groom backups, wipe-recovery tars, seeds), under the 11-03 rule 'delete stale or duplicated, backups included, after a proper check'. METHOD, fixed before running: (1) on the node, a SHA-256 manifest of every file in each archive entry (tars are listed and hashed per member); (2) a SHA-256 set of the kept copies: the box's C:\\home\\git working trees and git objects reachable from each repo's remote, the node's own checkouts and mirrors, and the newer seeds (kit-archive-seed, profile-mirror); (3) per entry, classify each file as duplicated (its hash is in a kept copy), regenerable (target/, _build, node_modules, deps junction contents) or unique; (4) delete an entry only when its unique set is empty, or after its unique files are landed in their repo or merged into one consolidated tar; (5) record per entry the counts and the decision. DONE: remote-archive holds only unique, unplaced data, with a manifest, and node free space is recorded before and after. START 11-03 03:3x: node free 12.0 GB; largest entries 20261031-x-groom 5.91 GB, 20261031-tibia-stage 2.51, 20261030-fiscal-night 2.30, kit-archive-seed.tar 1.54, 20261030-tibia-pre-retire 1.48, 20261029-fiscal-preretire2 1.37, 20261029-x-preretire 1.23. Each owning lane is told its unique set before anything of theirs is deleted.", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "node,backup,disk,cleanup,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_node_archive_dedupe () = Planning ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_1 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:00Z", "main", "main 11-03 03:5x PAUSED before any step ran: the user had not started the run. Nothing was hashed or deleted. Starts with step (1) of the method when the run begins.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_2 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:54Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:1x STEP 1 RUNNING on the node (read-only, nothing deleted): per archive entry, every file outside regenerable folders (target, _build, node_modules, deps, .git, dist, obj, bin) gets a git blob id (git hash-object --stdin-paths), written to C:\\home\\remote-queue\\main-archive-manifest\\<entry>.tsv as blob / size / relative path (the separator is a literal backtick-t, a quoting slip, read as such). Regenerable bytes are summed per entry. STEP 2 (box): the blob ids go through 'git cat-file --batch-check' in each lane's repo; a blob git already holds is DUPLICATED by definition (content preserved in history). The rest is UNIQUE and goes to its owning lane before any deletion.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_3 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T10:39Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:0x STEP 1 DONE (node, read-only): 13 folder entries, 1,068,968 files, 1,064,? hashed outside 'regenerable' dirs, blob manifests in C:\\home\\remote-queue\\main-archive-manifest\\. Per entry, hashed MB / 'regenerable' MB: compiler-repro 60/156, compiler-preretire 280/105, fiscal-preretire 206/86, fiscal-preretire2 1041/358, kit-preretire 610/284, main-preretire 533/181, x-preretire 1190/74, fiscal-night 1522/830, tibia-pre-retire 322/1198, tibia-stage 1752/818, x-groom 596/5454, x-groom4 61/5, wsl-crash-dumps 274/0. Plus 14 tars (kit-archive-seed 1572 MB, rescue-2026-10-28 566 MB, wipe-recovery 188+148 MB, ...). CORRECTION to the step 1 filter: it lumped .git, deps, dist, bin and obj in with the build outputs. Only target/, _build/ and node_modules/ are truly regenerable (rule c). A backup's .git can hold UNPUSHED commits, and dist/bin can hold release artefacts, so those get classified on their own in step 2 (for .git: every ref's commit must exist in the live repo or its remote, else UNIQUE). STEP 2 (box): blob ids x 'git cat-file --batch-check' over every lane repo's object DB, a found blob = DUPLICATED; then per entry the UNIQUE list goes to its owning lane.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_4 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T11:10Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:1x RELATED (vultr disk, x-dumps' media drain, 15G free): removed /home/remote/k3s-manifest/kit/src/target (2.8G) under rule (c): CACHEDIR.TAG present, last written 11-01 23:24, 0 processes with a cwd or exe inside it; the sources beside it are kept. Vultr is now at 18G free. NOT removed: /home/remote/git/kit/src/target (4.1G), because the running vultr kit job host lives in it (target/debug/kit job host, 16 h).")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_5 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 5u32, "2026-11-03T11:30Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:3x STEP 2 DONE (box): 22,606 distinct blobs in the 13 folder entries; 13,934 (62%) exist in some repo's git object DB (git cat-file --batch-check over the 59 repos under C:\\home\\git), so they are DUPLICATED. Per entry, duplicated files/MB vs unique files/MB: tibia-stage 32334/229 vs 61555/1523 (tibia-gaps/work 19k files); fiscal-night 195561/926 vs 18380/596; fiscal-preretire2 84434/513 vs 4473/529; wsl-crash-dumps 0 vs 33/274 (crash zips 10-30/31); x-groom 85836/466 vs 7426/130; kit-preretire 84880/486 vs 5648/124; main-preretire 73307/430 vs 3787/103; compiler-preretire 31621/210 vs 974/70; x-preretire 188892/1120 vs 10095/70; tibia-pre-retire 52358/302 vs 2035/20; fiscal-preretire 31886/187 vs 1260/19; compiler-repro 10377/46 vs 288/15; x-groom4 10818/53 vs 387/8. The UNIQUE files are mostly node-mirror spiral copies at 10-29..10-31 experiment states (drafts never committed in that form). Lists for the owners: node C:\\home\\remote-queue\\archive-unique\\<entry>.unique.tsv (size, blob, path). DECISION RECORD (ByDefault): each owning lane reviews its list and extracts anything still wanted by 11-03 15:00; after that, main deletes the entry. The tars (kit-archive-seed, rescue-2026-10-28, wipe-recovery-*) are checked separately. DONE NOW: main deleted its own 20261029-main-preretire (owner's call: 10-29 experiment mirrors, superseded by the landed lib).")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_6 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 6u32, "2026-11-03T11:31Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:3x THE TARS, decided by rule: kit-archive-seed.tar (1.5 GB), rescue-2026-10-28.tar (566 MB), wipe-recovery-goodslice.tar (188 MB), wipe-recovery-ledger.tar (148 MB), kit-drafts-seed/kit-drafts-src-seed, critical-now, memory-now, i574n-scripts, sefaz-src and xarchive-src are OFF-BOX copies whose purpose is surviving a box wipe (10-28). A hash-identical copy ON THE BOX does not make an off-box copy a duplicate, because that box copy is exactly what the off-box copy protects. RULE: an off-box seed is deleted only when a NEWER verified off-box seed of the same source replaces it (KIT-ARCHIVE-OFFBOX-MIRROR n11's supersede rule), or when its content is also held off-box elsewhere (profile-mirror/, vultr). So the tars STAY for now; the 1-byte linktest.txt and the empty cleanup-manifest/xarchive-src entries are checked with the folders at 15:00. The folder entries above are different: they were node-mirror WORKING copies, not backups of the box.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_7 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 7u32, "2026-11-03T11:33Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 07:33 fiscal: FISCAL CHECKED ITS 3 ENTRIES, NOTHING TO KEEP (read the node lists C:\\home\\remote-queue\\archive-unique\\<entry>.unique.tsv; columns size / sha / path). 20261030-fiscal-night (18,380 unique): ~675 files per proof mirror of spiral/apps (p7dbl, all6b, sgn6b, sgnset, gate4, gate4b, sgn7 ...), by extension .pas 7,913 / .ps1 3,155 / .spi 2,912 / .erl+.beam+.abstr ~1,200, i.e. mirror copies and build outputs; 573 under fiscal/. 20261029-fiscal-preretire2 (4,473): spiral/apps + spiral/lab mirror copies (axes1029, integ, g1build, ceall, ac, ge3, gbase, gls); fiscal/ 524 = generated 325, notebooks 127, samples 29, lib-programs 14, src 14, bench 4, scripts 3. 20261029-fiscal-preretire (1,260): spiral lab/apps copies (setall, ss, uj3); fiscal/ 10. CLASSIFICATION of every fiscal path: generated/notebooks/samples/bench are reproducible outputs (today's units regenerate deterministically from the committed generator, CI 41598162815 green with 'generated / matches the committed copy'); src/ and scripts/ copies (generator.spi, corpus_checks.spi, build.ps1, format-generated.ps1, pattern_expected.txt) are proof-mirror states from 10-29/10-30 (harness-patched or intermediate), superseded by what landed through git; lib-programs are the Delphi lib arms landed 10-31. Main may delete all three after 15:00 as planned.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_8 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 8u32, "2026-11-03T11:34Z", "x", "2026-11-03 07:34 x: x's three entries CHECKED, and x keeps nothing (deletion at 15:00 is fine). Method: the node's archive-unique lists, grouped by extension and path. 20261101-x-groom4 (387 unique): build outputs only (.beam .gleam .hrl .erl .abstr .cache), 0 x sources. 20261031-x-groom (7,426) and 20261029-x-preretire (10,095): mostly generated .pas/.kt/.swift/.py, Gleam build trees and older compiler pack scripts (the compiler lane's history, in mirrored spiral copies). The x sources among them (70 and 32 rows: client fields/posts/wire/xc, sim cells_executor/events/invariants/memory_watch/sim_run/sim_args/simframes, frames manifests, e2e.ps1, verify.ps1, sim-run.ps1) are intermediate versions of files whose later versions are committed. The two retired scripts (cargo-profile-bench.ps1, sim-engine-parity.ps1) have committed versions in x history (837a84b, af62b77).")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_9 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 9u32, "2026-11-03T11:34Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:4x DELETED wsl-crash-dumps (33 zips, 274 MB) on the owner's confirmation (resilience 07:4x): 33 dumps of one WSLg/weston crash loop (10-30 22:23+), kept only as optional evidence; WSL is parked and no open item references them. resilience also confirms the wipe-recovery/rescue tars are real recovery evidence and stay (matching n6).")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_10 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 10u32, "2026-11-03T11:35Z", "compiler", "11-03 07:4x compiler: checked my two node backups against the unique lists (remote-queue/archive-unique). 20261029-compiler-preretire (974 files, 70 MB): hopacsota-p2/p3 profiling traces and core copies from 10-29 (pre packs 8-24; HOPACSOTA R5 re-measures on the current compiler anyway), det/ and ccmr-g3b spiral tree copies, old packs\\apply-*.ps1 appliers (superseded by kitdo programs). 2026-10-29-compiler-repro-gate-pre-retire (288 files, 15 MB): a 10-29 spiral_compiler.fs and lab folders (lab was archived blob-verified on the box, kit archive 20261030-232045). Nothing to copy out; fine to delete at 15:00.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_11 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 11u32, "2026-11-03T11:36Z", "tibia", "11-03 07:4x tibia: tibia's two node archives checked against main's unique lists (C:\\home\\remote-queue\\archive-unique\\*.unique.tsv); TIBIA KEEPS NOTHING, delete as planned. 20261031-tibia-stage (61,555 unique rows): compile caches (.cache/.cache_meta/.cache_inline 32k), .erl/.mjs/.hrl build outputs (20k), per-slice lib draft stage copies under tibia-gaps/work/LIB-* (slices landed or redone, LIB-TYPE-SHAPES and the 10-29 heals), and 78 result-like rows that are gate-run metrics (tibia-arena-check1/*.blocks.tsv, *-metrics), all regenerable. 20261030-tibia-pre-retire (2,035): mirrored spiral trees (apps/cells, apps/compiler builds, .pas/.py/.beam stage files). ONE FLAG for other lanes before deletion: the pre-retire archive holds copies of spiral lab/ files that main's list marks unique (in no git history): lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/negatives.tsv (53,321 B), lab/SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR/proven.tsv (958 B), lab/SPIRAL-TO-YAML/pins.tsv (10,715 B), each present in several mirror copies (tibia-envguard, tibia-envguard-neg, tibia-gates, tibia-gaps). They are not tibia's; if their owning lanes have no other copy, these are the last ones.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_12 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 12u32, "2026-11-03T18:14Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:2x tibia's flag CHECKED: the three spiral lab/ files tibia found only in its node pre-retire archive are all in the box's blob-verified kit archive with the exact sizes: lab/MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER/negatives.tsv 53321 B (2 archived copies, blob AEEA8A5F), lab/SPIRAL-CLI-GRANULAR/proven.tsv 958 B (2, AA80C7EE), lab/SPIRAL-TO-YAML/pins.tsv 10715 B (26, A1AE52F6), in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\archive\\20261029-133932 (blobs.zip). So tibia's node archives can go at the 15:00 deadline with nothing lost.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_13 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 13u32, "2026-11-03T19:38Z", "main", "main 11-03 15:3x FOLDERS DELETED at the deadline (no lane objected; owners confirmed: fiscal x3, x x3, compiler x2, tibia x2 with its lab flag verified archived on the box (n12); kit-preretire unclaimed; main-preretire earlier; wsl-crash-dumps 07:4x). 11 entries: compiler-repro-gate-pre-retire, compiler-preretire, fiscal-preretire, fiscal-preretire2, kit-preretire, x-preretire, fiscal-night, tibia-pre-retire, tibia-stage, x-groom, x-groom4; junctions inside were removed first (link-safe). NODE FREE: 0.45 GB at start (the node was nearly full) -> 17.5 GB after. Left in remote-archive: only the off-box seed tars (kit-archive-seed 1572 MB, rescue-2026-10-28 566, wipe-recovery-goodslice 188 + ledger 148, kit-drafts-seed 54, kit-drafts-src-seed 17, sefaz-src 16, i574n-scripts 9, critical-now, memory-now) plus empty/1-byte leftovers (cleanup-manifest tsv, linktest.txt, xarchive-src.tar 0 MB, wipe-recovery-toolkit tgz 0 MB), which stay per n6's off-box rule. Ongoing growth found: alias Temp\\wsl-crashes 1.04 GB written 15:29 (resilience told); compiler stage dirs 3.9 GB (compiler told). Folder part DONE.")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_14 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 14u32, "2026-11-04T06:18Z", "main", "11-04 02:1x main NODE DISK (x alarm: Erlang disk_almost_full at 01:54). Free 17.5 GB after the 11-03 sweep fell to 8.2 GB. Sizes: remote-stage 20.0 GB, remote (mirrors) 16.3, spiral-bin 10.6, remote-archive 2.5 (seed tars, kept). main swept its own share: main-ship-pack21..31 stages (kept 32/33 for rollback) and 10 spiral-bin net11.0.replaced-* rollback copies (packs 6-15, 10-29..11-02; none in use, no reparse points), 8.2 -> 9.4 GB. Every other lane was asked to sweep its own stages and mirrors (junctions first). Proposed to resilience: a node free-space floor alert (< 15 GB).")
inl note_of_node_archive_dedupe_15 () = Note ("NODE-ARCHIVE-DEDUPE", 15u32, "2026-11-05T19:52Z", "main", "main 11-05 15:5x CLOSE: DONE criteria met. remote-archive now holds 13 entries, 2.71 GB, all deliberate off-box copies: kit-archive-seed.tar 1648.6 MB (box kit archive seed, 11-01), rescue-2026-10-28.tar 593.2 (profile-wipe rescue), wipe-recovery-goodslice.tar 197.0 + wipe-recovery-ledger.tar 155.5 (11-01), kit-drafts-seed.tar 56.6 + kit-drafts-src-seed.tar 17.4 (11-01), sefaz-src.tar 17.1 + i574n-scripts.tar 9.8 + xarchive-src.tar 0.08 (11-02 source seeds), critical-now.tar 1.0 + memory-now.tar 0.9 (pre-profile-mirror snapshots, superseded but tiny), wipe-recovery-toolkit-20261031.tgz 0.03, cleanup-manifest-20261029-2233.tsv 0.02 (the first sweep's record). Removed now: linktest.txt (13 B, content 'ping 211503', a link probe). The 20 GB start state was cut to these seeds by the 11-03 sweep (n13: 11 entries, 0.45 -> 17.5 GB free). Node free 20 GB now (after the profile-mirror .part sweep, MAIN-ORPHAN-SWEEP n33). Further node disk alarms belong with NODE-ALWAYS-FED / resilience's free-space floor, not this item.")
inl mirror_resync_1103 () = Task ("MIRROR-RESYNC-1103", "Resync the node and vultr mirrors to the box before the next run's first gate (compiler 11-03 03:5x, HURDLES-1103 n2). Node t1101: checkout 194a1916, lib 126 files (EDCD76E1), versus the box's 98e51d32 with 250 files (09D74A43); the runner spiral.exe is stale (F1DD2E34 from 10-30 vs 9A99BF53). vultr: DEPS-CORE-STALE, core 21B249D9DF957FA5 vs the box's 70F6F5BF1DE19AE8, checkout b926468c with lib at 126 files. These caused false gleam reds (a stale sm') tonight. Steps: wait for kit job list and window list to show no job reading the mirror; remote.ps1 sync spiral to each machine; ship the box core; rebuild the runner; then remote.ps1 status shows no DEPS-CORE-STALE, matching lib digests, and the runner hash on both machines. Owner main; run it at the start of the user's next autonomous run.", TaskKind, P0, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "node,vultr,mirror,remote,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_mirror_resync_1103 () = Planning ("MIRROR-RESYNC-1103", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_mirror_resync_1103_1 () = Note ("MIRROR-RESYNC-1103", 1u32, "2026-11-03T09:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:1x VULTR DONE: remote.ps1 vultr sync spiral -> REMOTE-SYNC-OK at head 98e51d32 (digest 4CE003D372FDD5EA; vultr ran no lane job). The box's deps core (VS Code Plugin/core, tgz A407B265...) was shipped with a hash check on arrival; the old core was kept as core.before-<stamp> until 'remote.ps1 vultr status' showed 'deps core 70F6F5BF1DE19AE8 matches the box', then removed (stale, superseded and verified, per the 11-03 rule). NODE: queued behind tibia-sized4-1 and fiscal-repseq-fix (kit job wait), then sync spiral plus a runner rebuild (cargo build --release in spiral/workspace) on the node.")
inl note_of_mirror_resync_1103_2 () = Note ("MIRROR-RESYNC-1103", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:45Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:0x NODE: the first sync attempt (05:40) was refused because a new job had started (guard exit 4). The node is never idle (x census, tibia full suite, fiscal records chain), so waiting for idle is the wrong rule. NEW RULE: wait only for the jobs running at the decision time (x-census-cli5, tibia-full-suite-1, fiscal-nominal-records), then sync -Force at once and rebuild the runner (background). fiscal's queued codec-layer/xsd-census then start on the new lib. A job starting in the same seconds could see a mixed tree, so it gets flagged for rerun. The real fix is NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE.")
inl note_of_mirror_resync_1103_3 () = Note ("MIRROR-RESYNC-1103", 3u32, "2026-11-03T13:09Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:1x DONE. remote.ps1 status: node and vultr spiral checkouts at 98e51d32 (the box tree), deps core 70F6F5BF1DE19AE8 matches the box on both (no DEPS-CORE-STALE). Runner: node rebuilt by apps/spiral/build.ps1 (release-unwind + mimalloc, protocol-lua-output ok) = 9FF45F12 at 08:39; the box runner (9A99BF53 from 11-02 00:45) swapped to the same 9FF45F12 binary at 09:08 (old kept as spiral.exe.old-9A99BF53-*; --help smoke ok). Runner hashes match. Lesson: the 05:47 node refresh used plain cargo build --release -> a crashing panic=abort/LTO runner (CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH n6); memory runner-build-via-build-ps1. vultr has no Lua runner (SPIRAL_EXE unset), by design.")
inl kit_hook_backlog_state_guard () = Task ("KIT-HOOK-BACKLOG-STATE-GUARD", "PreToolUse hook refuses Write/Edit file-tool writes to docs/backlog/state/*.spi (agile state only through kit agile verbs)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "kit,team:kit,hooks,agile", "current", "current")
