inl note_of_kit_hook_backlog_state_guard_1 () = Note ("KIT-HOOK-BACKLOG-STATE-GUARD", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:01Z", "kit", "11-03 03:5x kit PAUSE (main: the 21:00 run was armed early by mistake; run paused). PLAN, proposed by kit and waiting for the run AND a direct user yes for hook config: a PreToolUse hook on Write|Edit|MultiEdit whose file_path matches docs[/\\\\]backlog[/\\\\]state[/\\\\].*\\.spi returns a deny pointing at kit agile note/set/edit. It fails open on parse errors (memory hooks-fast-and-fail-open). Before activation, hooks-test.ps1 cases: refused path, allowed sibling path, a malformed payload is allowed. Take a .bak of settings.json. Why: hand edits to agile.spi bypass the store's ordering and lost updates (memory agile-status-lost-updates).")
inl note_of_kit_hook_backlog_state_guard_2 () = Note ("KIT-HOOK-BACKLOG-STATE-GUARD", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:25Z", "kit", "11-03 05:2x kit DONE under the user's direct order ('config and hook changes need to be autonomous with backups etc'). ~/.claude/hooks/kit-backlog-state-guard.ps1: a PreToolUse hook on Edit|Write|MultiEdit, timeout 15 s, that denies file_path matching docs[/\\\\]backlog[/\\\\]state[/\\\\]*.spi and points at the kit agile verbs; a malformed payload fails open. settings.json backup: C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\settings.json.bak-state-guard-20261103-0519. hooks-test.ps1 has 6 new cases (deny, message, forward-slash path, sibling path allowed, a source file named state allowed, malformed payload). hooks-test: 0 failed after the settings edit. LIVE PROOF: a Write to a decoy scratchpad\\docs\\backlog\\state\\probe.spi was denied by the hook, with nothing written. Also fixed in hooks-test (resilience reported 4 failed): the fixture root is now unique per run (kit-hooks-test-<pid>), so concurrent runs from two lanes no longer clobber each other (two simultaneous runs: 0 failed each); the parallel-fallback check now proves overlap from per-call spans instead of a 30 s wall clock (a loaded run took 32.7 s and still overlapped), with 60 s kept as the hook-budget bound.")
