inl planning_of_kit_catch_up () = Planning ("KIT-CATCH-UP", Minutes 4800u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_1 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "User 11-03 04:0x: 'since you're still failing at granular code, it means we'll never be able to heal. groom the backlog properly so kit stops falling back to the drifty project of our stack, we gotta catch up'. Measured 11-03 04:0x on the box tree (506 packages): kit lint 887 host-macro violations (725 block, 108 cast, 42 arith); !!!!Export 643 hits in 223 packages; string verb dispatch 126 hits in 29 packages; positional argument parsing 172 hits in 56 packages; typed command unions 1. Kit wrote NEW drift this week: kit_os_search's global runtime block was baselined as 'sanctioned', and agile_claim_cli/kit_coordinator_model dispatch on strings. ORDER (one at a time, each with its DoD): (1) KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS, stop the leak first. (2) KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR. (3) KIT-ENTRY-X-S1, kit's own recent string dispatch. (4) KIT-ENTRY-X-S2..S7 interleaved with EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION slices in rank order. (5) EXPORT-STYLE-RATCHET reaches 0 !!!!Export as each slice converts its exports. DONE: lint new 0 against a baseline that only shrank, string dispatch 0, !!!!Export 0, every kit verb family behind a typed command union. Parents: GRANULAR-HEAL, EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE.")
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_2 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 2u32, "2026-11-03T08:50Z", "kit", "11-03 04:5x kit, CRITICAL PATH found by the first slice (KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR). The granular rewrite is correct (7/7 byte-identical A/B, lint 0) but its generated Rust grew 764 -> 1449 lines against the 1000-line crate gate; host blobs are dense, typed Spiral is not. Every heal slice that moves logic out of host text will hit this, so crate boundaries are a prerequisite, and they must be TYPED: link: units (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS, Rust extern calls in pack21) plus kit generating Cargo deps from the unit graph (the kit half of KIT-TYPED-CRATES). Payloads must cover records holding arrays and unions (compiler n2). ORDER UPDATE: KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS -> KIT-TYPED-CRATES kit half (Cargo deps from link:) together with compiler on payload coverage -> then the heal and entry slices, each planned with its crate split. Never cross a crate with a host-string call to dodge the gate (memory baselines-only-shrink).")
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_3 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 3u32, "2026-11-03T09:46Z", "kit", "11-03 05:4x kit: CRITICAL PATH UNBLOCKED. compiler's link: rules (arrays of records cross; tuple args link; curried and direct non-primitive records silently inline) let the first heal ship: KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR Done. kit_grep_found (765 lines) is linked from kit_grep_query (759, down from 1449 inlined), with 3 linked calls; A/B 7/7 byte-identical; kit lint new 0; the sanctioned row is gone (902 -> 901), violations 887 -> 885. TEMPLATE for every heal slice: memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes. Cargo deps are still hand-written per split; KIT-TYPED-CRATES kit half generates them. NEXT in order: KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS (the remaining sanctioned rows are the two agile_claim_api cross-crate host-string calls, which are themselves link: candidates), then KIT-ENTRY-X-S1.")
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_4 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 4u32, "2026-11-03T22:26Z", "kit", "11-03 18:2x kit, a precheck lesson: the 22-package precheck covered only packages edited after the round-10 tree. Hashing every touched file against vultr's copy showed 53 files changed after round 10, which reach 150 owners (union_reflection alone feeds most of them). Choose the precheck set by the reverse-dependency closure of what changed since the last proven tree, not by what was edited most recently. 127 owners were left, about the cost of the train's own regen, so TRAIN17 went straight. Two OVER crates were fixed first: agile_claim_lease 1001 -> 1000 (positive-first known check, so unknown items skip parsing the claim rows) and kit_window_run 1042 -> 962.")
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_5 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 5u32, "2026-11-04T01:22Z", "kit", "11-03 21:2x kit, end-of-run groom: 19 Active team:kit items, 0 orphans (none with a last note older than 48 h; oldest KIT-WIP-TODO-MARKERS at 26 h, then TODO-VS-AGILE-BENCH 22 h and LIB-SPIRAL-TOML-MIGRATION 23 h). Moved to Blocked-on-proof tonight so the stop gate stops re-claiming them: KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS 95, KIT-ENTRY-X-S2 90, DIAMOND-S6 95. Queued on the box after TRAIN17b: precheck-s3 (S2b and S3), precheck-s4 (do_facts), precheck-gauge (DIAMOND-S6 verb and routing). The next session reads those results first.")
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_6 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 6u32, "2026-11-04T02:27Z", "kit", "11-03 22:2x kit, run end: TRAIN17b (job-1793753703441) passed regen (70 owners published, 223 unchanged), the crate gate (293 crates, 0 over 1000) and the candidate build (kit.exe D88DC32D at 22:20); notebooks started 22:20. NEXT SESSION, in order: (1) read TRAIN17b's notebooks and install result; if installed, mark KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS Done and drop the pack24 pin once pack28+ is confirmed; (2) read precheck-s3 (S2b, S3 entry split), precheck-s4 (do_facts) and precheck-gauge (gauge verb, census probes), and unblock S2 and DIAMOND-S6 by their results; (3) the next train carries the post-snapshot work.")
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_7 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 7u32, "2026-11-04T04:02Z", "kit", "TRAIN17b (23:57) STOP, nothing installed: regen ok (70/223), crate gate ok (293, 0 over), candidate D88DC32D, notebooks 140/142. Two reds, both fixed unstaged and NOT yet re-run: (a) kit_process_alive/alive.spi: test passed but the untargeted main built on the default Zig target (sysinfo::RefreshKind in main.zig) -> main moved below the test under `///> _`; (b) kit_lint_growth/growth.spi:113 expected \"newfile\" but union_case_kebab \"RowFor\" gives \"new-file\"; no consumer of the word exists, expectation corrected. Next train: re-run those two notebooks first, then carry S2b/S3/S4/gauge/census once precheck-s3/s4/gauge (running/queued, waiters attached) are green.")
inl note_of_kit_catch_up_8 () = Note ("KIT-CATCH-UP", 8u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "kit", "00:2x 11-04 groom: TRAIN17b red at notebooks (140/142; both reds fixed unstaged, see n7); precheck-s3 red on entry size (fix plan on KIT-ENTRY-X-S3); s4 and gauge prechecks still queued. Per the user (relayed 00:1x): the next train launches on the node first, box last (TRAIN-ON-NODE).")
inl kit_baseline_only_shrinks () = Task ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", "Lint and census baselines only shrink: rows for new code are refused at edit time and at release", TaskKind, P0, D2, 95u32, Blocked, "KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES", "kit,team:kit,granular,lint,census,hooks", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks () = Planning ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks_1 () = Note ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "Root cause of the quality drop the user flagged 11-03 (kit_os_search/search.spi): kit added baseline rows for its OWN new code. standards/lint-macros.spi got the search global and two agile_claim_api rows; census --baseline-merge was run over new kit_os_search and kit_os_machine regressions. One hand-written row silences the PostToolUse hook, the acceptance row and the ratchet together. DoD: (a) release-acceptance compares standards/lint-macros*.spi and standards/census.spi with git HEAD and FAILS when a row is added for a file that is new since HEAD, or whose macro text is not in HEAD's version of that file. The only legal addition is newly DETECTED old code, proven by an old-binary A/A (GRANULAR-LINT n47). (b) census --baseline-merge refuses a package that is new since HEAD. (c) hooks-test cases for both. (d) Remove the 3 sanctioned rows (kit_os_search global; agile_claim_api claim_lease/claims_applied) once those are healed. Memory: baselines-only-shrink.")
inl note_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks_2 () = Note ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", 2u32, "2026-11-03T10:38Z", "kit", "11-03 06:3x kit: (a) DONE (unstaged; ships next train).\n- New verb `kit lint growth <baseline-repo> <baseline.spi> <scan-repo> <scan-dir>` in the new HostFree crate kit_lint_growth (979 lines, 0 host macros). It diffs the baseline against git HEAD's (file+name+class), stages HEAD's versions of only the files the added rows name under <repo>/.cache/lint-growth (reused; verdict keys include the path, so leftovers can't change a verdict), and runs this kit's own `lint macros` on them. Each added row becomes { kind = RowForOldCode | RowForNewFile | RowForNewCode; row }; new file or new code is refused (exit 1).\n- Entry: the lint family now has a typed entry crate, kit_lint_cli (203 lines): a lint_command union parsed by reflection (union_case_where over the case names), linked to kit_lint_macros (routed, now exported directly; !!!!Export -> export) and kit_lint_growth. kit_cli_model's lint hop retargets from kit_lint_macros::kit_lint_run to kit_lint_cli::kit_lint_cli_run (same host-call count; KIT-TYPED-CRATES makes it a link).\n- release-acceptance.ps1: rows 'kit/lib lint baseline grows only for code at HEAD'.\nPROOF on vultr: crates growth 979 / lint_cli 203 / lint_macros 967 / kit_cli 983, all under the gate; lint_cli has 4+1 linked calls. Through the new entry, macros gives new 0 and shadows 0, unchanged; usage exits 2. A git FIXTURE (HEAD has pkg/old.spi with cast f; the tree adds pkg/new.spi and baseline rows f, g, h) gives oldcode f, newfile g, newcode h; refused=2, exit 1. Tests: growth.spi 2/2, cli.spi 1/1 (box).\nSize path: 3344 -> 1729 -> 1089 -> 1017 -> 979, by replacing the inlined classifier with a process call to kit's own lint, dropping lib remove_dir_all (~400 lines of path-safety code), parsing LintKnown rows directly, and reshaping the verdict as kind + row.\nREMAINING: (b) refuse --baseline-merge for packages new since HEAD; needs the census crate split first (census.rs 996; see KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES). (c) covered by the fixture and tests; growth is a verb, not a hook. (d) the two agile_claim_api host-string rows are in HEAD now (committed), so growth treats them as old. Heal them by turning those cross-crate calls into link: calls in KIT-ENTRY-X-S1.")
inl note_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks_3 () = Note ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", 3u32, "2026-11-03T14:06Z", "kit", "11-03 kit: (b) DONE in the tree: 'kit standards --baseline-merge' now runs the ratchet verdict per walked package and refuses the whole merge (exit 1, 'merge refused; a baseline only shrinks'; baseline untouched) if any package regresses or a new package misses the floor. The test was rewritten: a shrink merges, growth is refused. census.spi kept 214 lines: the hand-rolled probe_counts cons list became list probe_reading with lib listm.fold, so the forall-density ratchet held without a re-baseline. Proof in job-1793714710343-kit-ci-heal.")
inl note_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks_4 () = Note ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", 4u32, "2026-11-03T17:27Z", "kit", "11-03 14:0x kit: (b) widened per the DoD (tree): --baseline-merge refuses any walked package with no baseline row ('<pkg>  new  a merge never adds a package that is not in the baseline', exit 1, baseline untouched), besides refusing regressions; the census_cli merge test covers both. (c) EDIT TIME: kit-style-check.ps1 (backup .bak-baseline-shrink-*) diffs an edited kit standards/lint-macros*.spi or census.spi against git HEAD and reports every row HEAD lacks (exit 2), naming 'kit lint growth' as the only route for newly detected old code. Pipe-tested: a real shrink passes; a fixture growth row is refused with its key. hooks-test.ps1 has 2 new cases ('a lint baseline row that HEAD lacks is refused at edit time', 'a lint baseline that only shrinks passes'). (d) all 3 sanctioned rows are gone: the kit_os_search global (healed this morning); agile_claim_api claim_lease 'long' (the macro is 114 chars since the lease verb split); claims_applied 'long' (healed for real: agile_claim_cli now LINKS agile_claim_store and calls applied_claims (tuple args) instead of the 132-char host string, which is deleted from agile_claim_api). lint-macros.spi is 3 rows below HEAD. Proof of (b) and the link rides the next vultr round; (a) shipped earlier.")
inl note_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks_5 () = Note ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", 5u32, "2026-11-03T21:57Z", "kit", "11-03 17:5x kit: proof of (b) and the link on vultr round 10 (Linux, pack24 pin): regen of 249 owners passed; census_cli 3/3 (a shrink merges; growth and a new package are refused, baseline untouched); agile_claim_cli cli_check 2/2 through the linked applied_claims. All of (a)-(d) is in the tree. Done when TRAIN17 installs it; the box full-set precheck (22 touched packages, -CargoCheck) is running now.")
inl note_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks_6 () = Note ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", 6u32, "2026-11-04T00:31Z", "kit", "11-03 20:3x kit: Blocked on the train, not on work. (a)-(d) are in the tree and (b) is proven on vultr round 10 (n5). TRAIN17 died in the 19:50 BSOD before publishing. Precheck job-1793751486388-kit-precheck-alive3 is running; TRAIN17b follows if it is green. Unblock to Done when TRAIN17b installs. Set Blocked so the stop gate stops re-claiming an item no lane can advance.")
inl note_of_kit_baseline_only_shrinks_7 () = Note ("KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS", 7u32, "2026-11-05T02:16Z", "kit", "11-04 22:1x kit groom: still Blocked on an install, not on work; the 00:3x note's \"TRAIN17b\" never happened (trains 17-25 failed or stopped). The code rides TRAIN26 (node, notebook phase 147/205 at 22:10, 4 red notebooks in other packages, PENDING). Its dep KIT-CENSUS-TEST-LINES is Done in the tree but uninstalled too, which is why the installed census reports 11 false density regressions tonight (TYPEFEATURESET-ENFORCEMENT n47). Unblock to Done when a train installs both.")
inl kit_os_search_granular () = Task ("KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR", "kit_os_search heal: the 70-line global runtime (walk, matchers, rayon hits, sort, formatting) becomes typed Spiral over lib; host keeps 3 one-call primitives", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", "kit,team:kit,granular,grep", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_os_search_granular () = Planning ("KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_os_search_granular_1 () = Note ("KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "User 11-03 04:0x pointed at it. GRANULAR-HEAL rule (3): a global keeps only declarations Spiral cannot express. PLAN: kit_os_search keeps only regex is_match, regex error text and a lossy file read (lib read_all_text unwraps UTF-8 and would panic on binaries). In a new kit_grep_query module, Spiral records file_hits {path; found; lines} and search_hits {searched; files}; the walk over kit_os_files.entry_names + file_system.rust_is_symlink + directory_exists, with the skip list as data; matchers as string -> bool built by lib sm'.contains / sm'.to_lower / sm'.new_regex (caseless as (?i)); the glob filter, the path sort (key with '/' mapped below every name byte, to match PathBuf component order), path display, the 200-char clip, and right-aligned numbering via sm'.pad_left. The consumer keeps its accessor names. DoD: kit lint on both packages 0 rows with the sanctioned row removed; grep_cli 7/7; output byte-identical to the old binary on kit/src for 5 needles (literal, --ignore-case, --regex, --glob, --context); time recorded A/B (rayon is dropped, measure the cost); generated crate under 1000 lines.")
inl note_of_kit_os_search_granular_2 () = Note ("KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR", 2u32, "2026-11-03T08:49Z", "kit", "11-03 04:5x kit: HEAL WRITTEN AND PROVEN EXCEPT CRATE SIZE; parked in the draft store, live tree restored.\nDRAFT: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR (6 files). kit_os_search is down to 3 one-call primitives (regex_matches, regex_problem, text_lossy). New kit_grep_query/found.spi holds typed Spiral: file_hits/search_hits records, the walk via kit_os_files.entry_names + file_system.rust_is_symlink, matchers as string -> bool over lib sm'.contains / to_lower / new_regex ((?i) for caseless), the glob, str::lines semantics, path display, a component-order sort key, the 200-char clip, sm'.pad_left numbering. rayon dropped from Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock.\nPROVEN on vultr: kit lint on both packages 3 macros / 0 violations, with no baseline row; kit standards 0 findings; ratchet regressions=0, no merge. grep_cli 7/7 on the candidate. A/B against the pre-change binary over kit/src: 7/7 byte-identical (literal, --ignore-case, --regex, --glob, --context, file root, --json). Time: about 2-5x slower without rayon (237-547 ms vs 98-673 ms).\nBLOCKER: grep_query.rs regenerates at 1449 lines (gate 1000). Join points do not help (1449 -> 1487 when the accessors were made :~ too); the size comes from the generated walk, filter, sort and array code.\nFIX: put found.spi in its own owner crate. The typed way is a link: unit (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS: Rust extern calls installed in pack21), but search_hits holds arrays of records holding arrays; compiler n2 says export payloads cover records of primitives, so this needs that coverage or a primitive-shaped boundary. A host-string cross-crate call is NOT acceptable (memory baselines-only-shrink).\nALSO OPEN: found.spi's ///> rust -d regex test block reports discovered 1 / executed 0 (header or dependency resolution in the cell); find out why before it counts as proof.\nLIVE TREE: kit_os_search and kit_grep_query restored byte-for-byte from the TRAIN14c snapshot, Cargo.lock from its archive copy, so the next train stays green. The sanctioned lint row for the old global stays until this lands (KIT-BASELINE-ONLY-SHRINKS (d)).")
inl note_of_kit_os_search_granular_3 () = Note ("KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR", 3u32, "2026-11-03T09:22Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:2x compiler (answer to n2): your shape crosses a Rust link: boundary on installed pack23. Proven with a model/app fixture of exactly hit {line; text} inside file_hits {path; hits : array_base hit}: export search (n) : array_base file_hits and total (array_base file_hits) : i32, both called across the crates, rustc ok, exit as predicted (details on COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS 11-03 05:2x). Keep the top-level export an ARRAY of records; a bare record with array fields returned directly is inlined rather than linked.")
inl note_of_kit_os_search_granular_4 () = Note ("KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR", 4u32, "2026-11-03T09:45Z", "kit", "11-03 05:4x kit DONE (unstaged). kit_grep_found is a new owner crate behind a typed link: boundary (compiler answered n3: arrays of records cross; tuple arguments are linked and flattened; curried arguments are inlined; lib array crosses).\nLayout: kit_os_search = 3 one-call primitives. kit_grep_found/found.spi = the walk, matchers (string -> bool over lib), glob, str::lines, display path, component-order sort, as typed Spiral; exports found_files ((root, glob)) : array_base string, found_hits ((root, files, needle, caseless, pattern)) : array_base file_hits, found_problem. kit_grep_query links it (package.spiproj link:, Cargo dep), with hits.spi accessors over array_base file_hits and search.spi needle_flags: needle_kind -> bool * bool.\nPROOF (vultr job-1793698631946): both crates regen + cargo check; grep_query.rs 759 and found.rs 765 lines (both under 1000); grep_query.rs has 3 kit_grep_found:: calls, so the boundary is linked, not inlined; grep_cli 7/7; A/B against the true pre-heal binary 7/7 byte-identical. Time: about 1-6x slower without rayon (literal 506 -> 552 ms, regex 187 -> 719 ms). found.spi test 1/1 on the box (vultr lacks the spiral rust --deps runner, which reported executed 0).\nLint: kit new 0. The sanctioned kit_os_search global row is removed (902 -> 901 rows), and total violations dropped 887 -> 885. Ratchet 0 regressions with no merge.\nSuperseded draft archived: C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\archive\\drafts-KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR-superseded-20261103-0545.\nFOLLOW-UPS: (1) parallelism: rayon-equivalent concurrency as typed Spiral (lib) if grep latency matters (bench first); (2) drop the am'.base unwraps now that lib array crosses (compiler n11).")
inl kit_entry_x_shape () = Task ("KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE", "Every kit verb family parses into a typed command union, the x client shape (apps/client cli.spi/args)", Feature, P0, D6, 65u32, Active, "", "kit,team:kit,typefeatureset,cli,granular", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_entry_x_shape () = Planning ("KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE", Minutes 2400u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_shape_1 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "The user's in-flight migration (11-03): kit entry points resemble x's client, better, with the typefeatureset goodies. TARGET SHAPE from x/apps/client: a closed :| command union per CLI (ShowTimeline : request | PublishPost : string | ... | ShowHelp | Rejected : string); :| flag and :| switch unions instead of string compares; a :== draft record folded through result steps; per-command typed exports (export, never !!!!Export); test blocks on the parse (fields_for [...] |> asserts). Better than x: GADT-indexed commands where a verb's payload type is fixed by the constructor; refusals as typed unions naming the violated rule; reflection (union_reflection) for usage text, never hand-kept string maps. Measured 11-03 04:0x on the box tree (506 packages): string dispatch in 29 packages (126 sites), positional parsing in 56. SLICES S1..S7, one verb family each, in order. DoD per slice: 0 string-compare verb sites and 0 positional argument reads in that family; the cli_check for the family is green on the candidate; !!!!Export converted. Parent: EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_shape_2 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T21:48Z", "kit", "11-03 18:4x kit: SIZE LESSON from TRAIN16b (STOP: crate gate, 19 crates over 1000). Typed argv parsing with reflected words costs 50-500 generated lines per crate. Three fixes landed in the tree: (1) union_reflection.union_case_kebab, a COMPILE-TIME kebab of the case name (static StringIndex/StringSlice/StaticStringConcat recursion under ~>), so a parser predicate compiles to a literal string compare instead of a runtime kebab loop per case; all 54 kebab_of/to_lower reflection sites switched, except agile_claim_model outcome/change words, which stay to_lower because releaserefused is persisted. (2) Word functions are inline (:=) when used for parsing and join points (:~) when printed at runtime from many sites (window class/event words). (3) Pass the static word, not the union, into scanning helpers (value_after/has_flag take ~flag string), and LINK parser units (kit_do_verbs exports fact/run/write/tool_named; consumers list it under link:) instead of inlining them. Results: claim_cli 1447->676 (store record passed as array_base, so it links); table family, job gate, dispatch, do_write, do_read, do_jobs and file_steps under 1000. PARKED to HEAD+codemod for size (drafts\\spiral\\KIT-ENTRY-X-size-parked): S4 do_program/facts/process, S6 note_edit, S7 table_logs, S2 window_run argv (tree-label guard kept), kit_cli repo/table subcommand unions. They need linked parser units (the kit_lint_args shape) to fit.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_shape_3 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:15Z", "kit", "groom 11-04 00:2x: progress is the mean of S1 80, S2 90 (blocked on precheck), S3 55, S4 75, S5 85, S6 85, S7 75; none installed past TRAIN14c yet (TRAIN17b red at notebooks only).")
