inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_1 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "Slice of KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE (shape and DoD there). kit_machine_windows windows.spi verb chain, kit_window_announce_verb, kit_window_query (legacy, migrate on touch). DoD: the slice's packages have 0 string verb dispatch and 0 positional argument reads; a typed command union with parse tests; exports via export; lint on those packages shrinks; cli_check green on the candidate.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_2 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 2u32, "2026-11-03T13:19Z", "kit", "11-03 09:3x kit: prerequisite found: the window router has the kebab verb wait-clear, so reflected words need a lib PascalCase -> kebab helper (sm'); land it in lib first (shared with KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF). EOIE-WINDOW-ANNOUNCE's check --minutes rides on this slice.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_3 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 3u32, "2026-11-03T15:23Z", "kit", "11-03 11:1x kit: router migrated in the tree (unproven). window_model: closed window_verb union (VerbRequest..VerbRemote), whose words come from reflection + lib sm'.kebab_of (landed 10:49), so 'wait-clear' is derived, not typed; verb_of/verb_words, plus test window_verbs_read_and_print_by_reflection. class_word and window_event_word now use the same reflection+kebab path, replacing 16 hand-typed string arms; the existing exact-word tests pin both lists. windows.spi: window_run matches verb_of on the argv list and verb_ran dispatches per case. window_released takes its id; window_requested takes class/minutes from kit_window_request's request_run, which pattern-matches the argv list. 0 positional argument reads and 0 string verb compares remain in kit_machine_windows. Left for this slice: the announce/check/query entry packages (kit_window_announce_verb, kit_window_query). Proof is queued with the CI-heal set.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_4 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 4u32, "2026-11-03T22:26Z", "kit", "11-03 18:2x kit: the tree-label guard on 'window run' is PARKED (KIT-ENTRY-X-size-parked\\kit_window_run.run.tree-label-guard.spi). Inlined it costs run.rs about 54 lines (rooted_path 18, tree_access 13, window_ran +23), and with process_alive's sysinfo composition (+26) run.rs reached 1042. Every real tree window (lib_land_window, cells_land_window) uses 'window request', which keeps the guard, and no script runs a tree class through 'window run'. Unpark it once window_model is a linked unit: run then calls tree_label_problem across the link, about 1 line. TRAIN17 carries run.rs at 962.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_5 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 5u32, "2026-11-04T00:36Z", "kit", "11-03 20:5x kit: S2's last string sites are DRAFTED in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-ENTRY-X-S2b\\src (tree frozen for TRAIN17b). The announce packages' remaining hits are test fixtures (holder names), not dispatch.\n(1) window_model: state_word is union_case_kebab \"\" over window_state (Held|Waiting), replacing the hand-written map, and row_of compares against state_word Held instead of the literal \"held\".\n(2) kit_window_query: shown_rows and shared_with parse each row ONCE with row_of and match on the typed row (state, kind, label, start_ms, until_ms) instead of six tab_field reads and two \"waiting\"/\"held\" compares. Behavior change: a row whose class doesn't parse is now skipped instead of printed raw.\nSide finding: 'kit window list' prints heavy_slots=N as the number of HOLDERS, not free capacity.\nLand with the S3 draft after the TRAIN17b snapshot. Proof: windows_cli 19/19 and wait_cli; the list output must be byte-identical for live rows.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_6 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 6u32, "2026-11-04T00:59Z", "kit", "11-03 21:0x kit: S2b LANDED in the tree after the TRAIN17b snapshot: window_model state_word via kebab, and kit_window_query reading typed rows through row_of. Proof rides job-1793753944565-kit-precheck-s3 (all window owners are in its 37).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_7 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 7u32, "2026-11-04T01:00Z", "kit", "11-03 21:0x kit: Blocked on proof, not on work. Every S2 site is in the tree: router typed, tree-label guard on request and run, S2b state and query. Unblock when job-1793753944565-kit-precheck-s3 is green and the next train's windows_cli and wait_cli pass on the candidate.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_8 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 8u32, "2026-11-04T05:45Z", "kit", "11-04 01:5x: S2b (typed window rows: state_word by reflection; shown_rows/shared_with match RowKnown/RowUnknown) passed TRAIN18's full node regen and crate gate (kit_window_query 951, kit_window_run 1000, window_model ok). Only the unrelated heal crate stopped that train. parked: waiting on TRAIN19 (node, ~02:15) for notebooks + install.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_9 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 9u32, "2026-11-04T06:04Z", "kit", "11-04 02:0x kit_machine_windows router: the request path in windows.spi was DEAD (VerbRequest routes to the kit_window_request crate, which has its own copy). Removed window_requested, announce_refusal, requested, request_head, request_row and the request record, then the helpers only they used (lock_taken, lock_released, free_mb, process_number, verdict_text) and the unused own_executable: windows.spi 323 -> 161 lines. That took 8 of the 9 string flag sites with it. The last (--bin, read twice) is a typed window_option union; its word is the compile-time `union_case_kebab \"Option\"` literal, bound once. No link: was added (this package has many consumers; a link: there leaks). vultr --check exit 0 (windows.spi, window_model.spi). Unproven: rides TRAIN20. 13 concat5 calls remain in windows.spi (next touch).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_10 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 10u32, "2026-11-04T07:00Z", "kit", "11-04 03:0x: the announce verb options are typed (announce_option AnnounceLabel/AnnounceWork; words via compile-time union_case_kebab; test updated). windows.spi has no concat5 left. Node size run: kit_machine_windows 722, kit_window_announce_verb 818 (both under 1000; vultr --check exit 0). The check/query entry packages had no string flag sites. All S2 code is in the tree. parked: waiting on TRAIN20 (notebooks + install).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_11 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 11u32, "2026-11-04T07:41Z", "kit", "11-04 03:5x: the windows.spi router sweep is REVERTED (it broke TRAIN19: kit_window_wait/kit_machine_crowding use option_value/free_mb via the module open) and parked at drafts\\kit\\KIT-ENTRY-X-S2-router-1104\\windows.spi. Redo it with a whole-tree grep per removed name, keeping option_value and free_mb (or moving them to window_model for their users). The announce verb options ride TRAIN20.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s2_12 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S2", 12u32, "2026-11-04T08:00Z", "kit", "11-04 04:3x: the windows.spi \"dead code\" sweep is ABANDONED. A whole-tree grep (build dirs excluded) shows windows.spi is a shared helper module: kit_job_gate references lock_taken, free_mb, process_number, verdict_text and request_row; kit_window_wait uses option_value; kit_machine_crowding uses free_mb. Only own_executable, announce_refusal and request_head are unused anywhere, too little to justify the risk. The parked copy stays in drafts as a record. S2 scope that remains: the announce verb (in TRAIN20) and the --bin typed option (re-apply alone on top of the TRAIN18 windows.spi if wanted).")
inl kit_entry_x_s3 () = Task ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", "Entry points in the x-client shape, job verbs: kit_jobs (16), kit_job_after_model (3), kit_job_launch_model (1), kit_process_kill (2), kit_process_table (1)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 75u32, Active, "", "kit,team:kit,typefeatureset,cli,granular", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_entry_x_s3 () = Planning ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_1 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "Slice of KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE (shape and DoD there). The largest dispatch site, and the top of the lint rank (kit_jobs 27 rows), so the heal and the shape ship together. DoD: the slice's packages have 0 string verb dispatch and 0 positional argument reads; a typed command union with parse tests; exports via export; lint on those packages shrinks; cli_check green on the candidate.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_2 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 2u32, "2026-11-03T22:55Z", "kit", "11-03 19:0x kit, S3 started (tree): kit_jobs/model.spi had the job-state word map twice, in state_of_parts and inline in job_state_of. job_state_of now calls state_of_parts (exit records only ever hold settled words, so its Live arms can't fire there): one map instead of two. NEXT, the typed half: union_reflection builds cases with a () payload, so it can only parse NULLARY unions. Split job_settled into JobFinished : i32 | JobSpawnFailed : string | JobSkipped : string | JobEnded : job_end, with job_end = JobTimedOut | JobStopped | JobLost | JobMemoryCapped | JobExpiredInQueue. The map then becomes union_case_where over job_end plus three payload arms. Sites: 15 across kit_jobs model/jobs, kit_job_after, kit_job_slot, kit_job_launch, kit_job_host queue, kit_job_gate (exit_line takes job_settled). Measure kit_job_gate's size with it, since it was 1060 on 11-03. Then jobs.spi's positional reads (argument 3/4 at lines 150-222) become an argv-list parse like kit_window_request's.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_3 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 3u32, "2026-11-03T23:16Z", "kit", "11-03 19:2x kit, S3 typed half done in the tree. (1) job_settled is split: JobFinished : i32 | JobSpawnFailed : string | JobSkipped : string | JobEnded : job_end (5 nullary endings). state_of_parts parses live and ending words through union_case_where, comparing literals at compile time; finished and skipped are named by union_case_kebab on the case, so no hand-written word strings remain. The model's three copies of the halt words and codes (halt_code and halt_word, both dead, plus halt_terms) collapse into halt_ending : job_halt -> job_end; halt_line and kit_job_supervise read end_exit and end_word from it. 11 sites in 7 crates wrap JobEnded. The round-trip test now folds over EVERY job_end case. (2) jobs.spi reads argv once: job_run matches env.command_line_arguments (_ :: verb :: first :: second) and job_ran (command, first, second) passes operands down; argument 3 and 4 are gone. (3) kit_jobs LINKS kit_job_dispatch (dispatch_run, a tuple-arg forward_run, list_on_run), replacing three host strings, including the list --on string kit added this morning; kit_jobs' host macros are now below HEAD. Proof: job-1793746025247-kit-precheck-alive (32 owners plus cargo check, queued after TRAIN17); watch whether list_on_run's () export links or inlines.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_4 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 4u32, "2026-11-03T23:43Z", "kit", "11-03 19:4x kit: probed on the box (pack24 pin). kit_jobs plus kit_job_launch compile; jobs.rs is 972 lines (under the gate) with 6 linked calls: kit_process_alive, kit_job_dispatch x3 (the () export of list_on_run links too), kit_job_chain, kit_job_serial (chain and serial now export their functions directly). Two traps were fixed on the way: Settled (JobEnded JobLost) is a nested nullary pattern, a parse error, so it became '| Settled (JobEnded ending) ?& end_lost ending =>' (jobs.spi, launch.spi); and three list-pattern arms that each called the inline job_command_of had copied the reflection pick 3x (jobs.rs 1247), so it is now matched once ('_ :: verb :: operands') with a job_operands join point. LEFT: kit_job_control, rechain, doctor, supervise, launch and host include kit_jobs as a PACKAGE, so kit_jobs can't link them (cycle). They need kit_jobs' model split into its own linked model unit first (KIT-TYPED-CRATES shape).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_5 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 5u32, "2026-11-04T00:20Z", "kit", "11-03 20:2x kit, post-BSOD. TRAIN17 was lost in the crash (nothing published); the tree is intact. The precheck is re-queued as job-1793751486388-kit-precheck-alive3, behind main's pack31 compiler-install window; TRAIN17b follows if it is green. PLAN for the remaining host strings (corrects n4): 34 packages include kit_jobs, using model, host and the jobs.spi helpers as a module LIBRARY. The link cycle comes only from kit_jobs ALSO being the entry crate (job_ran, job_run, main). So: move the entry into a new small owner crate (kit_job_entry: job_operands, job_ran, job_run, export kit_job_run) that links kit_job_control, rechain, doctor, supervise, launch, host, dispatch, chain and serial; kit_jobs becomes a plain package again; kit_cli's hop retargets to the entry crate. The 34 consumers don't change. Each linked crate exports its run fn directly (export 'name' fn; unit-arg exports link, proven tonight). No model split is needed.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_6 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 6u32, "2026-11-04T00:28Z", "kit", "11-03 20:4x kit: the S3 entry split is DRAFTED in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-ENTRY-X-S3\\src (mirrors src; not in the tree, so the precheck and TRAIN17b stay as proven). Contents:\n- New owner kit_job_entry (entry.spi, package.spiproj, Cargo.toml, standards.spi): job_status, job_waited, dispatched, placed, started_code, job_ran, job_operands, job_run, export kit_job_run. It LINKS process_alive, dispatch, chain, serial, control, rechain, doctor, supervise, launch and host, so jobs' 9 host strings become typed calls.\n- kit_jobs/jobs.spi keeps only the shared library (158 lines); its spiproj links only kit_process_alive.\n- Each target exports its function directly: control (4), rechain, supervise, host_run, and doctor via a new doctor_checked ().\n- kit_job_launch returns a primitive record start_answer { code : i32; id : string } from start_answered instead of a 'code<TAB>id' string. That removes 3 host macros, the to_string and the two split parses.\n- kit_cli_model's hop retargets to kit_job_entry::kit_job_run.\n- Workspace member kit_jobs is replaced by kit_job_entry; kit_cli and kit_do_jobs depend on kit-job-entry.\nLAND STEPS (after the TRAIN17b snapshot):\n1. Copy the draft over src.\n2. Archive kit_jobs/Cargo.toml and jobs.rs; kit_jobs stays a package for its 34 consumers.\n3. Run cargo update --offline --workspace in src.\n4. Precheck kit_job_entry, the 9 targets, kit_cli and kit_do_jobs with -CargoCheck. Grep entry.rs for each '<crate>::' call; every crate must be under 1000 lines.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_7 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 7u32, "2026-11-04T00:43Z", "kit", "11-03 20:4x kit: the job_end split is PARKED in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-ENTRY-X-S3-ending-split. Precheck alive3 (34 owners, cargo check clean, all links real) found kit_job_gate at 1031 lines and kit_job_state at 1023. Both inline kit_jobs' model, and the split's extra join points cost gate +27 lines (end_word 24, end_exit 19, settled_word -16) and state +85 (end_named 33, live_named 15, state_of_parts 35). Kept in the tree: job_state_of calls state_of_parts (one word map); the dead halt_code and halt_word are deleted; live_word via kebab; argv read once; the dispatch, chain and serial links. Unpark it WITH the entry split, once the state parse can sit behind a link instead of being inlined into every model consumer.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_8 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 8u32, "2026-11-04T00:59Z", "kit", "11-03 21:0x kit: LANDED in the tree after the TRAIN17b snapshot (20:55:30). TRAIN17b carries the proven state: links, argv once, sysinfo prune, kit_process_alive. NOT in TRAIN17b:\n- the entry split: kit_job_entry is new; kit_jobs/jobs.spi is the shared library only; the kit_jobs crate's Cargo.toml and jobs.rs are archived in the session scratchpad and recoverable from git HEAD;\n- direct exports in control, rechain, doctor (doctor_checked), supervise and host_run;\n- launch's start_answer record;\n- the kit_cli_model hop retargeted to kit_job_entry;\n- the workspace member swap and the kit_cli and kit_do_jobs deps;\n- three test-registry rows relabelled kit-jobs -> kit-job-entry.\nThe draft's jobs, launch and supervise copies predated the job_end-split revert, so those edits were RE-APPLIED to the current files instead of copied. Proof: job-1793753944565-kit-precheck-s3 (37 owners from the dependency closure, -CargoCheck), queued after TRAIN17b. Check that kit_job_entry has 10 linked calls and that every crate is <= 1000 lines (the gate fails only above 1000).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_9 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 9u32, "2026-11-04T04:14Z", "kit", "00:2x 11-04 precheck-s3 RED (job-1793753944565): kit_job_entry/entry.rs 1350 lines (gate 1000) plus E0433 kit_job_create and kit_job_start_args missing. Cause: launch.start_answered returned a record with a string field directly, which silently INLINES (records cross only inside arrays or with primitive fields), so job_started (227 lines) and its create/start_args calls landed in entry. Fixed unstaged: start_answered returns `array start_answer`, entry takes `am'.index 0i32`. Still ~1120 lines after that: next move job_status/job_waited (+ settle helpers, ~200 lines) and the placement route out of entry into a linked unit (control is 810, dispatch 959, so a new kit_job_query crate), then re-precheck. Linked calls proven in entry: 19 (chain, control x4, dispatch x3, host, rechain, serial, supervise x2, doctor, alive, state x2, host_request x2).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_10 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 10u32, "2026-11-04T04:44Z", "kit", "11-04 00:3x node precheck GREEN (job-1793766561602 on the node, pinned pack24, 7.4 min for 56 owners + cargo check; the box took ~3 h for 37). kit_job_entry 407 lines (was 1350), 16 linked calls. The new crate kit_job_query (587 lines, 8 linked calls) took job_status, job_waited and placed; it exports status_placed, wait_placed (tuple arg), tail_placed and stop_placed. launch.start_answered now returns `array start_answer`, so it links. Rides TRAIN18 (00:43, node first).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_11 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 11u32, "2026-11-05T08:28Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:3x kit: the slice's remaining string maps HEALED to reflection (unstaged). (1) kit_job_launch_model: start_shape cases renamed StartPlain|StartHeavy|StartCompile; shape_word = union_case_kebab \"Start\" (was a 3-arm case->own-name map), shape_of_word = union_case_where (plain by default), start_shape_of strips -- and reuses it. Consumers renamed: kit_job_create, kit_job_launch, kit_job_start_args. Notebook header + test shape_words_come_from_the_case_names added. (2) kit_process_table: ListProcesses/StopProcesses -> ProcessPs/ProcessKill; process_command_of = union_case_where over process_word = union_case_kebab \"Process\" (was word = \"ps\"/\"kill\"); test process_verbs_are_their_case_names. (3) kit_job_after_model: mode_word = union_case_kebab \"After\"; mode_of_flag reflects --ok (empty stays AfterAny); head_from's three string flags became a reflected chain_switch (SwitchOk|SwitchSerial|SwitchRunSerial -> --ok/--serial/--run-serial) applied by switched. union_reflection added to every consumer package. Box --check ok: launch_model, create, launch, start_args, process_table (model + run), after_model, chain, rechain, serial. Pending: box notebooks (job-1793867210054) and node size (job-1793867279683; kit_job_chain was at 949, the one to watch).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_12 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 12u32, "2026-11-05T08:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:4x kit: kit ps entry typed too (unstaged). kit_process_table/model.spi: ps_args { pattern; tree; mine; rejected } read by reflected switches PsTree|PsMine (--tree/--mine). The first other word is the pattern; an unknown --switch or a second pattern is refused (exit 2, with usage), where before a stray word silently became or replaced the pattern. run.spi: pattern_from and the argument/flag_present scans are gone; process_run matches the argv list (verb :: rest) and passes ps_of rest. Test ps_words_read_the_pattern_and_the_reflected_switches. Box --check ok. The host-string call into kit_process_kill stays on purpose: kit_process_kill opens kit_process_table, so a typed call would be a package cycle.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s3_13 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S3", 13u32, "2026-11-05T08:43Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:5x kit: SIZE results (node kit-size-0105f). kit_job_chain came out 1002, OVER, because the after-model heal (reflected mode_word/mode_of_flag/chain_switch) inlines into it at 949 + 53. That heal is REVERTED, git-clean: kit_job_after_model and the union_reflection lines in chain/rechain/serial are back to HEAD. It needs a kit_job_chain split first (e.g. the head/segment parsing into a linked crate). The other heals sized fine: kit_job_create 376, kit_job_launch 719, kit_job_start_args 696, kit_process_table 681, kit_job_rechain 903, kit_job_serial 668. Box notebooks: shapes 1/1, after model 5/5 (before the revert), process_table model 4/4 (verb reflection + ps args). Left in this slice: the after-model maps behind the chain split.")
inl kit_entry_x_s4 () = Task ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", "Entry points in the x-client shape, do verbs: kit_do_facts (11), kit_do_jobs (8), kit_do_process (7), kit_do_program (7), kit_do_write (4), kit_do_verbs (4), kit_do_file_steps (3), kit_do_read (2)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 75u32, Active, "", "kit,team:kit,typefeatureset,cli,granular", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_entry_x_s4 () = Planning ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_1 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "Slice of KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE (shape and DoD there). kit do is the program runner (EOIE-ONE-CALL); its step language becomes a GADT step algebra. DoD: the slice's packages have 0 string verb dispatch and 0 positional argument reads; a typed command union with parse tests; exports via export; lint on those packages shrinks; cli_check green on the candidate.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_2 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 2u32, "2026-11-03T16:27Z", "kit", "11-03 13:0x kit: first pass in the tree (unproven). kit_do_verbs is now the closed step vocabulary in prefix form: fact_verb FactHash..FactDiff, run_verb StepRun..StepStop, write_verb FileAppend..FileWrite, and a new tool_verb ToolGit/ToolJob/ToolLab. Their words come from reflection + sm'.kebab_of (4 hand maps removed; a test pins every list), and *_named parses them through union_case_where. Consumers now dispatch on these unions instead of string chains: kit_do_write grammar (file_step_parsed), kit_do_file_steps previews (step_previewed/append_previewed), kit_do_facts (fact_step_parsed + query_fact_parsed; messages use fact_word), kit_do_process (run_step_parsed + query_step_parsed on query_verb Tail/Search), and kit_do_jobs (closed job_action ActionStart/Wait/Stop with reflected words and a test, plus job_tool via tool_verb). LEFT: kit_do_model.query_verb_word (ReadAround->read and ListFiles->files are not kebab; renaming the cases touches every kit_do package), kit_do_jobs/run.spi state words (should share kit_jobs' settled union), kit_do_program keywords (edit/show/except/expect), and kit_do_read options (literal/paths, q kind).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_3 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:37Z", "kit", "11-03 13:2x kit: second pass (tree). kit_do_program: statement keywords are a closed keyword union (KeywordEdit/Show/Replace/Patch, read via keyword_at), and header options are header_option (OptionDryRun -> 'dry-run', Except, Expect); rules_at, header_options and step_at dispatch on them, keeping the inner matches inside the recursive functions (no mutual recursion); a test pins both word lists. kit_do_read: query_option is now ValuedIn..ValuedTimeout with a reflected word; the new query_flag (FlagLiteral/FlagPaths) with query_flag_applied replaces the 'literal'/'paths' compares; query_filler is FillerAround..FillerStatus, and '~' is an explicit tilde symbol, not a fake case; a test pins all three lists. Proof: job-1793723538573-kit-do-s4 (box) covers verbs/write/file_steps/facts/process/jobs/program plus kit_do_edit and kit_do_git CLI checks; kit_do_read rides the next batch.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_4 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 4u32, "2026-11-04T00:33Z", "kit", "11-03 20:4x kit, unpark lead for the size-parked do_facts slice (KIT-ENTRY-X-size-parked\\kit_do_facts__*). It already LINKS kit_do_verbs (fact_named crosses), yet do_facts.rs was 1305 at TRAIN16b (largest outcome_merged 142). Suspect: fact_word step at 3 sites (listed_fact, detail_fact, ...). On a runtime fact_verb, union_case_kebab expands an 11-arm match at each site. Try: kit_do_verbs exports fact_word directly (export 'kit_do_fact_word' fact_word, made :~), so the sites become linked one-liners. Proven tonight: unit and single-primitive exports link, and unions cross when the unit is linked and an export mentions them. Measure with a per-function delta against HEAD's do_facts.rs before parking or unparking anything else.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_5 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 5u32, "2026-11-04T01:03Z", "kit", "11-03 21:0x kit: do_facts slice UNPARKED into the tree after the TRAIN17b snapshot: the typed grammar from KIT-ENTRY-X-size-parked (fact_named across the kit_do_verbs link), plus a new linked fact_word_shown. kit_do_verbs exports it directly as kit_do_fact_word, and the 4 'fact_word step' display sites in grammar.spi call it. fact_word itself stays inline (:=) so fact_named's predicates still compare literals at compile time. Proof: job-1793754138918-kit-precheck-s4 (kit_do_facts, file_steps, jobs, verbs, write; -CargoCheck), queued after precheck-s3. If do_facts.rs is still over 1000, read the per-function delta against HEAD and re-park the grammar rather than baseline it.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_6 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 6u32, "2026-11-04T04:44Z", "kit", "11-04 00:4x RE-PARKED: kit_do_facts generated 1038 lines on the node precheck (gate 1000). Parked copies are in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\kit\\KIT-ENTRY-X-S4-parked-1104 (grammar.spi, package.spiproj, Cargo.toml); the tree is back to TRAIN17b's versions. The biggest function is outcome_merged (142 generated lines): a 27-field fact_tally is rebuilt in every one of the 10 fact arms (nested match, one 27-tuple per arm). Plan: tally counters as one `array u64` indexed by a per-fact slot, then one arm-free update (3 slot adds), so the 10 tuple rebuilds go; expected well under 1000. Then a node precheck (7 min).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_7 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 7u32, "2026-11-04T05:02Z", "kit", "11-04 01:0x UNPARKED AGAIN with the size fix (unstaged; vultr pack31 --check exit 0 for run.spi and grammar.spi). The 27-field fact_tally is now { report; failed; counts : array u64 }, indexed by a 25-case `counter` union (CountFiles .. CountDirSteps) through one `:~ counter_slot` (union_case_index, emitted once). fact_moves maps each fact kind to a counter_moves record (first, second, optional third, step), and counts_moved is one runtime loop, so the 10 nested 27-tuple rebuilds (142 generated lines) go. receipt_counts reads `n CountX`. Also every concat5 in run.spi is now ++# (7 calls; the file opens sm'_operators). Node precheck kit-precheck-s4b (job-1793768380344) is queued behind TRAIN18's node half; it sizes do_facts and checks the do family, kit_agile_mutation and kit_cli.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_8 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 8u32, "2026-11-04T07:41Z", "kit", "11-04 03:5x: do_facts 955 lines on the node with the parked typed grammar (fits). The fix: the receipt moved to the new linked crate kit_do_facts_receipt (106 lines), which exports receipt_of (array_base fact_counts) and is called with a one-element array. A DIRECT 25-u64 record argument did not link (it was inlined; 1044 lines). Rides TRAIN20.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_9 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 9u32, "2026-11-04T20:52Z", "kit", "11-04 22:3x kit: checked the parked kit_do_program keyword/option unions (drafts\\spiral\\KIT-ENTRY-X-size-parked\\kit_do_program__program.spi) for an unpark like note_edit/table_logs today: NOT yet, do_program.rs is 996 lines in the tree, so even the reflected keyword match would cross 1000. It needs the program grammar split first (rules_at/patch_at into a linked kit_do_grammar crate exporting a parse over the token array), then the unions fit.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_10 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 10u32, "2026-11-05T08:46Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 04:5x kit: re-scoped what blocks this slice (no code change). kit_do_program 996: the grammar split needs kit_do_model, a source-only package opened by 10 packages, to become a LINKED model unit (Cargo crate + link: in every crate on the path + one anchor export per crossing union: rule_list, step, steps), because the parse result types must cross the link (memory spiral-link-boundary-shapes). kit_do_jobs 978 and kit_do_process 936 also sit too near 1000 to absorb reflected unions; each needs its own split first. Next session: promote kit_do_model to a linked unit, then move tokens_of..program_of into kit_do_grammar.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_11 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 11u32, "2026-11-05T08:47Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 05:0x kit: design notes for promoting kit_do_model to a linked unit (not started; it needs node sizing + cargo checks that a draft cannot get before TRAIN28). It would likely SHRINK the four near-gate users (kit_do_program 996, kit_do_edit 986, kit_do_jobs 978, kit_do_read 977), since each now inlines its own copy of the model's 12 types and helpers. Hazards from the link rules: (1) rule, edit_block and query are records with union fields, and a record returned directly with non-primitive fields silently inlines, so anchors must wrap them in arrays (array_base rule, etc.) or each consumer keeps its own copy and rustc fails E0308 across crates; (2) every crate on each path (kit_do, kit_do_program, kit_do_edit, kit_do_facts, kit_do_file_steps, kit_do_jobs, kit_do_read, kit_do_verbs, kit_do_write, kit_do_write_host) must list kit_do_model under link:; (3) one anchor export per crossing union (rule_list, step, steps, query_verb, program_family, replace_count, rule_matcher, expectation, write_mode). Also seen: query_verb_word is a 6-arm map where 4 arms are the case name (Search/Head/Tail/Wait) and 2 are not (ReadAround -> read, ListFiles -> files); renaming those two cases to Read/Files would make it reflection.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_12 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 12u32, "2026-11-05T09:58Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 06:0x kit: kit_do_model PROMOTED to a linked unit (unstaged, started after the TRAIN28 snapshot, so it targets TRAIN29). The package gets its own crate (Cargo.toml + main) with one anchor export per union (replace_count, rule_matcher, rule_list, expectation, write_mode, query_verb, program_family, step, steps) plus query_verb_word/program_family_word. Records stay unanchored: they lower to tuples and so match across crates. All 10 users list it under link:; 9 crate users carry a kit-do-model Cargo dep; workspace member + Cargo.lock (awk insert, 0 removed lines, sorted). Box --check ok: model + all 10 users. NODE SIZE (kit-size-domodel): kit_do_model 335; kit_do_program 996 -> 960, kit_do_edit 986 -> 950, kit_do_verbs 920 -> 849, kit_do_facts 955 -> 935, kit_do_read 977 -> 981, kit_do_jobs 979, kit_do_write 938, kit_do_file_steps 739, kit_do 463. Generated consumers import kit_do_model::{query_verb} and call kit_do_model::kit_do_model_query_verb_word, so the link is real. A cargo check is pending: the first attempt could not compile, because kit_remote_activity (committed without its generated activity.rs) is outside the subset; rerunning with it in the regen set (job-1793872700191).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_13 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 13u32, "2026-11-05T10:09Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 06:1x kit: (1) the parked kit_do_program keyword/option unions are UNPARKED now that the model link freed 36 lines (996 -> 960). The draft (drafts\\spiral\\KIT-ENTRY-X-size-parked\\kit_do_program__program.spi) differed from live by exactly its own hunks, so it applied as-is: keyword (KeywordEdit|Show|Replace|Patch) and header_option (OptionDryRun|Except|Expect) read by reflection instead of word = \"replace\"/\"dry-run\"/... chains; union_reflection added. Box notebook program.spi 9/9 incl. keywords_and_header_options_read_by_reflection; box --check ok (program, kit_do). Re-size pending. (2) kit_do_process step verbs HEALED (unstaged): run_verb union (StepRun|Tail|Search|Errors|Processes|Stop, kebab \"Step\") with verb_parsed replaces the six-arm verb = \"run\"/\"tail\"/... chain; the unknown-verb refusal uses ++#. (3) The model-link CARGO probe is VOID, not failed: the subset workspace cannot compile because 56 crates created since the last install (kit_flag_words, kit_remote_activity, ...) have no generated .rs committed. Only a full regen (TRAIN29) runs that cargo gate; the evidence so far is box --check, node sizes and generated code calling kit_do_model::.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_14 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 14u32, "2026-11-05T10:15Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 06:2x kit: SIZE says no to the unpark: with the keyword/option unions, kit_do_program regenerates to 1076 (OVER). The reflected unions cost ~116 generated lines against the 36 the model link freed. REVERTED: program.spi is back at HEAD content (960 sized with the model link) and union_reflection is gone from its package. The grammar split into a linked kit_do_grammar crate is still the way to fit those unions. kit_do_process step verbs heal KEPT: sized 987 (was 936), box notebook grammar.spi 2/2.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s4_15 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S4", 15u32, "2026-11-05T10:18Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 06:2x kit: grammar-split scoping, for whoever picks this up. kit_do_program exports one thing, kit_do_program_compiled (string -> string), and builds the query_verb_known closure inside (host call into kit_do_verbs), so no closure has to cross. To get its keyword/option unions under 1000, the grammar (tokens_of .. program_of, ~495 source lines) must split across crates. The crossing types are then (a) token_list, a host Rc<Vec<(i32, Rc<str>)>> that can cross verbatim only if declared through a nominal shared by both crates, and (b) the generic parsed a (Rejected | Parsed : a * i32), which would have to move into the linked kit_do_model with an anchor per instantiation (parsed rule_list, parsed edit_block, parsed steps). A cheaper alternative: export edit_header_at/rules_at from a kit_do_edit_grammar crate that takes the program text plus a token index and re-tokenizes, trading a second tokenize for no host-type crossing.")
inl kit_entry_x_s5 () = Task ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S5", "Entry points in the x-client shape, read/grep verbs: kit_grep_query (6), kit_read_query (4)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 85u32, Active, "KIT-OS-SEARCH-GRANULAR", "kit,team:kit,typefeatureset,cli,granular", "current", "current")
