inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s6_1 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S6", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "Slice of KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE (shape and DoD there). agile is the most-used family; its cli_checks cover it. DoD: the slice's packages have 0 string verb dispatch and 0 positional argument reads; a typed command union with parse tests; exports via export; lint on those packages shrinks; cli_check green on the candidate.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s6_2 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S6", 2u32, "2026-11-03T17:34Z", "kit", "11-03 14:2x kit: in the tree (unproven except where noted). agile_note_edit: edit_switch (--append) and edit_valued (--as/--expect-at/--expect-prefix) unions with reflected words; options_read folds the argv list, keeping the old edge rules (blank value invalid; an empty word ends parsing); note_edit_entry matches '_ :: _ :: root :: id :: seq :: text :: flags'; argument_owned and the rust_std_env dep are gone; test note_edit_flags_read_by_reflection (registered). agile_memory_links: memory kinds are MemoryUser..MemoryUntyped with a reflected memory_kind_word (the unknown-word fallback stays MemoryUntyped); the links entry reads '--memory'/'--json' through links_switch/links_valued over the argv list. Deleted: the option_value host block that scanned std::env::args, flag_present, the argument helpers, the rust_std_env dep, and a trim_end host macro (now lib sm'.trim_end). agile_task_listing.sort_of_word parses through union_case_where on the reflected sort_word. LEFT: kit_cli_model's subcommand string chain (affected/accept-review/logs/sequences/test). Also proven today: kit_os_process liveness passes on Windows (box).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s6_3 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S6", 3u32, "2026-11-03T17:42Z", "kit", "11-03 14:4x kit: kit_cli_model done in the tree. repo/table subcommands are closed unions (RepoAffected/RepoAcceptReview, TableLogs/TableSequences/TableTest) with reflected kebab words, parsed into an option and matched, so a fallback like repo_run () never runs eagerly as a union_case_where default. Direct verb words come from sm'.kebab_of on the case suffix; the lowercase_named and to_ascii_lowercase host macros are deleted (all 28 direct verbs are single words, so the words are unchanged; the existing tests pin them). Found while proving S5/S6: a cons inside a tuple pattern needs parens ('| _, Some f, (v :: rest) =>'); fixed in 3 flag folds and saved as memory spiral-cons-in-tuple-pattern-needs-parens. Proof: vultr round 5 (248 crates + export A/B + 15 tests + 14 CLI checks).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s6_4 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S6", 4u32, "2026-11-04T16:10Z", "kit", "11-04 14:4x kit: UNPARKING note_edit (parked 11-03 for size in drafts\\spiral\\KIT-ENTRY-X-size-parked) in the kit_lint_args shape: NEW linked crate agile_note_edit_args owns argv (note_args_read skipped -> array_base note_args_row with root/id/seq/text/editor/append/expect_at/expect_prefix/valid, all primitive so it links), the reflected edit_switch/edit_valued unions and flags_read (old edge rules kept: blank value invalid, empty word ends parsing, last guard wins); test note_edit_flags_read_by_reflection moved there (+ last-guard-wins, short argv). agile_note_edit drops rust_std_env/argument_owned, links the args crate and maps the row to edit_options in options_of. Workspace member + Cargo.lock entry, cargo metadata --offline --locked ok. vultr --check: both ok (args with bodies). Pending: node size (job-1793808592934-kit-size-noteedit, queued behind TRAIN22) and the box notebook for the args crate. Still parked: S4 do_program/facts/process, S7 table_logs, S2 window_run, kit_cli subcommand unions.")
