inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_1 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 1u32, "2026-11-03T08:19Z", "kit", "Slice of KIT-ENTRY-X-SHAPE (shape and DoD there). Last slice; closes string dispatch at 0. DoD: the slice's packages have 0 string verb dispatch and 0 positional argument reads; a typed command union with parse tests; exports via export; lint on those packages shrinks; cli_check green on the candidate.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_2 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 2u32, "2026-11-03T17:46Z", "kit", "11-03 14:5x kit: first pass in the tree (unproven). kit_experiments: a closed experiment_verb union (VerbRegister..VerbRecordVerdict, 'record-verdict' via kebab_of) routes the 7 verbs, replacing the string chain; ledger/id come from the argv list; registered/shown take them as parameters; test experiment_verbs_read_by_reflection (static header, registered). kit_table_logs: logs_switch (--quiet) and logs_valued (--glob/--since/--out) unions; options_read folds the argv list, keeping the original order of checks (switch, bare path, 'has no value', valued, measure kinds via kind_of); the argument helpers are deleted. kit_table_sections: a column_pick union (--first/--last) folded by columns_read over the argv list. The tab-encoded column spec for the kit_log_sections host call is unchanged (a separate encoded-row heal). The shared kit_table_sequence_args helpers (argument/paths_from/value_after) are still index-based; that's the next step with kit_table_sequences. LEFT: kit_log_counts, kit_adoption, kit_lint_model sites. Proof: next vultr round.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_3 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 3u32, "2026-11-03T17:54Z", "kit", "11-03 15:0x kit: kit_log_counts flags are a count_flag union (--count/--in-set/--count-in) with reflected words, the index loop words_from is replaced by the argv list, and kit_lint_model.class_spelled is derived from macro_class via the reflected class_word (no hand-typed list). FOLLOW-UP FOUND (sized, not started): 11 packages carry their own index-based argv helpers (value_after/paths_from/has_counts/has_columns/known_flag): kit_table_sequence_args (shared by sequences/sections/sequence_measures), kit_lint_macros, kit_crate_gate, kit_lint_shadows, kit_process_kill, kit_mirror, kit_table_counts, kit_style_measure. known_flag is a pipe-joined string list of 18 flags. Plan: one typed flag union per verb family with reflected words, list folds as in grep/read/logs today, and a lib helper only if 3+ families still need a name-keyed lookup. Count: 54 call sites.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_4 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 4u32, "2026-11-03T18:02Z", "kit", "11-03 15:2x kit: argv-helper follow-up underway (tree, unproven). Done: kit_table_sequence_args (a sequence_flag union of 18 flags with reflected words replaces the pipe-joined known_flag string; value_after/has_flag/paths_from are list folds; consumers kit_table_sequence_measures, kit_table_sections, kit_table_sequences, kit_table_counts migrated, and counts' counted_names/stray_name are list folds); kit_crate_gate (gate_switch --enforce, gate_valued --limit; '_ :: _ :: root :: words'); kit_process_kill (kill_switch --tree/--mine, kill_valued --theirs; a kill_flags fold collects targets in order, and stops_from walks targets instead of indexes); kit_mirror (a mirror_command union for 'check', list-based paths_from, the argument helper deleted). Compile proof of the table family: box job-1793728709846. LEFT: the lint family (kit_lint_macros helpers also used by kit_lint_shadows) and kit_style_measure.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_5 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 5u32, "2026-11-03T18:39Z", "kit", "11-03 16:0x kit: the lint and crate-gate argv migrations are PARKED as drafts (drafts\\spiral\\KIT-ENTRY-X-S7-argv-split\\): the box proof (job-1793729119161) compiled them, but the typed flag parsing put crates over the 1000-line gate: lint 967->1185, shadows 852->1075, crate gate 944->1085, and growth 979->1060 from the inlined kebab loop. Restored to HEAD, keeping only kit_lint_macros' two exports (lint_run, shadows_run) that kit_lint_cli routes to directly; the second-level 'shadows' string router is gone. kit_lint_model.class_word uses sm'.to_lower (all 5 cases are single words, so the words are identical) to drop the inlined kebab loop. RESUME: put the flag parsing in a small linked unit (kit_lint_args exporting an array_base row of primitives + array_base string paths, the agile_claim_request shape) so macros/shadows link it instead of inlining ~245 lines each; same for crate gate.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_6 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 6u32, "2026-11-04T05:08Z", "kit", "11-04 01:1x RESUMED the crate-gate half. The lint half is already in the tree (kit_lint_args is a linked unit, and macros and shadows link it). The size cause of the parked gate draft (944 -> 1085) was a separately inlined sm'.kebab_of loop per flag union. New linked crate kit_flag_words exports kit_flag_word (~suffix : string -> string, \"--\" + kebab; a single-string arg links). The gate's switch_word/valued_word call it, so no kebab loop is inlined. The draft gate.spi (gate_switch/gate_valued unions, gate_flags record, reflected words, a list fold over argv) is unparked into the tree. vultr pack31 --check gate.spi exit 0; words.spi timed out at attestation under vultr load 16, but it's checked as the gate's dependency. Node precheck kit-precheck-s7 (job-1793768889526) is queued after s4b and sizes kit_crate_gate. Any crate over the gate on a flag union can reuse kit_flag_words.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_7 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 7u32, "2026-11-04T07:41Z", "kit", "11-04 03:5x: the crate-gate argv draft measured 1044 -> 1008 -> 1010 on the node (one gate_flag union with guarded patterns; then outcome_text with a single write). It is still over, so it is held out of TRAIN20 (tree = TRAIN18 gate). Next: move gate_checked's usage/limit messages or the measure walk into a small linked unit, then size again.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_8 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 8u32, "2026-11-04T08:36Z", "kit", "11-04 04:4x: the crate-gate argv migration FITS now. A new linked crate kit_crate_walk took the directory walk, the per-crate measure, the manifest parsing (spiral_manifest/manifest_read/crate_measure, section_fields, manifest_of, line_count) and their tests, and exports kit_crate_measures (root -> array_base crate_measure; records in an array cross). kit_crate_gate keeps the flags (one gate_flag union, guarded patterns, compile-time kebab words), the verdict model and outcome_text with a single write. Node size run: kit_crate_gate 552, kit_crate_walk 564 (was 1010 in one crate). vultr --check exit 0 for walk.spi, model.spi and gate.spi, as-is and bodies. Notebook pre-run queued; rides TRAIN21.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_9 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 9u32, "2026-11-04T16:42Z", "kit", "11-04 15:5x kit: UNPARKING table_logs (parked 11-03 for size) in the linked-args shape: NEW crate kit_table_logs_args owns argv (logs_args_read 2 -> array_base logs_args_row: paths/glob/since/out/quiet/rejected plus measure_words/measure_values as two parallel string arrays, all linkable), the reflected logs_switch/logs_valued unions and words_read (a missing value rejects; non-flag words are paths). kit_table_logs keeps kind_of/spec_applied and applies the measure pairs in order in measures_applied, so the typed measure specs never cross the link; argument/argument_count/options_from are gone. One behavior shift, invalid input only: an unknown --flag is now reported after a later missing-value error instead of before it. argv base: `kit table logs a.log` -> the list after dropping 2 starts at a.log (same as the old argument 3). Workspace member + Cargo.lock, cargo metadata --locked ok; vultr --check ok for both (args with bodies). Pending: box notebook job-1793810251862-kit-logs-args-tests, node size job-1793810518390-kit-size-tablelogs (behind TRAIN22).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_10 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 10u32, "2026-11-04T18:20Z", "kit", "11-04 20:0x kit: kit_table_logs_args PROVEN on the box (logs_flags_read_by_reflection 1/1). The node size job I queued at 15:5x spawn-failed after its queue wait (my start line passed -File as the program and a box path; memory node-job-start-program-first). Re-queued correctly with every changed crate: job-1793816314352-kit-size-all6 (behind TRAIN22).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_11 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 11u32, "2026-11-05T06:37Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 02:4x kit: TWO MORE ENTRIES CONVERTED (unstaged), and the remainder re-scoped. (1) kit_adoption: new module args.spi with reflected unions (SwitchHabits; ValuedDaysBack|ValuedDays|ValuedOut) parsed from the argv list after 'adoption' into a typed adoption_args record. run.spi lost argument/argument_count/option_value/flag_present/decimal_u64, and its three host print macros moved to lib console.write_error_line / console.write while touching the function. Behavior change on invalid input only: an unknown word or a flag without a value now exits 2 with 'kit error: adoption: ...' instead of being ignored. Test adoption_flags_read_by_reflection: box notebook 1/1; box --check ok (scratch tree; vultr was thrashing). (2) kit_experiments register: NEW linked crate kit_experiment_args (register_valued, 10 reflected flags -> array_base register_row of strings, confidence defaults 0.95, unknown flag refused). registered split into registration_text / registered_as / registered with ++# instead of concat5, and option_value calls are gone from experiments.spi. Workspace member + Cargo.lock wired; box --check ok for both packages. RE-SCOPE: kit_log_counts and kit_table_sections already read argv as a list with reflected flags, and kit_lint_model has no crate. What is left is kit_experiment_amend (10 reads), kit_experiment_import (26), kit_experiment_analysis (6, crate at 991 lines), all through ledger_host's argument/option_value/where_clauses, which stay until those three are converted. Pending: node size run job-1793860610864-kit-size-0105 (8 crates) and the box notebook for kit_experiment_args.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_12 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 12u32, "2026-11-05T06:44Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 02:5x kit: kit_experiment_amend CONVERTED (unstaged). kit_experiment_args gains amend_valued (AmendField|AmendReason|AmendValue, reflected --field/--reason/--value) and amend_row. Positional words fill ledger, id, note in order; a fourth word or a register-only flag is refused; export kit_experiment_amend_args. amend.spi: both amended and addended read the typed row (one am'.index_base call), refuse a rejected row first, and no longer call argument or option_value. Package link, Cargo dep and Cargo.lock wired. Box --check ok (args, amend); box notebook args.spi 2/2 (register + amend tests). NODE SIZE (kit-size-0105, before the amend parser): kit_adoption 801, kit_experiments 898, kit_experiment_args 330, plus this session's other changes: kit_job_query 663, kit_style_probes 312, kit_compiler_discovery 182, kit_job_slot 802, kit_standards 922, all under 1000. Left: kit_experiment_import (26 reads) and kit_experiment_analysis (6, crate 991); then ledger_host's argument/option_value/where_clauses can go; re-size args + amend.")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_13 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 13u32, "2026-11-05T07:36Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:3x kit: experiment family DONE in the tree (unstaged), plus kit_table_test. Every positional/flag read in kit_experiments, kit_experiment_amend, kit_experiment_analysis, kit_experiment_import and kit_table_test now comes from one typed linked row. SIZE forced a split: kit_experiment_args had reached 989 generated lines, so it keeps register + import + table_test (they share register_of; table test pulls the table and every --where, then hands the rest to register_of; one-case union TableWhere), and NEW linked crate kit_experiment_verb_args (verbs.spi) holds amend, analyze and record-verdict (reflected unions AmendX, AnalyzeX with repeatable --where, RecordX; positional ledger/id/note|table). ledger_host lost argument, option_value and the where_clauses host block (no callers left in the tree), and kit_experiments dropped its now-unused rust_std_env package. Consumers that got smaller from the conversion: analysis 991 -> 936, amend 777 -> 732. Workspace members + Cargo.lock (sorted, additions only) wired. Box --check ok for all 8 family packages (args, verb_args, experiments, amend, analysis, import, table_test, stats); box notebooks args 4/4 earlier. Pending: box notebooks args + verbs (job-1793864062717), node size of the 8 crates (job-1793864089910).")
inl note_of_kit_entry_x_s7_14 () = Note ("KIT-ENTRY-X-S7", 14u32, "2026-11-05T07:40Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 03:4x kit: family PROVEN. Box notebooks: kit_experiment_args 3/3 (register, import, table test), kit_experiment_verb_args 3/3 (amend, analyze, verdict). Node size (kit-size-0105d, regen passed for all 8): kit_experiment_args 601, kit_experiment_verb_args 574, kit_experiments 898, kit_experiment_amend 732, kit_experiment_analysis 936, kit_experiment_import 704, kit_table_test 720, kit_experiment_stats 795; every one under 1000. With kit_adoption (801, args 1/1) the slice is done in the tree; it closes when an install carries it (CLI checks on the candidate). Remaining positional reads elsewhere in kit (kit_job_host, kit_machine_windows, kit_do and others with their own local argument helpers) belong to other KIT-ENTRY-X slices, not S7.")
inl org_exit_fallout () = Task ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", "CI and link fallout from the user moving dir-tree-html and polyglot out of the i574n org (11-03: 'this way we can eventually finish all tasks til the end while fixing errors while they appear, in ci etc'). dir-tree-html is now fc1943s/dir-tree-html (the i574n URL redirects); polyglot is fc1943s/polyglot (NO redirect from i574n/polyglot). Local copies stay at C:\\home\\git\\dir-tree-html and C:\\home\\git\\polyglot as sources until their absorption items close. SITES (git grep 11-03, tracked files): (a) clones through the redirect: spiral/scripts/dir-tree-html.ps1 (used by publish-tree.ps1 for every gh-pages run, and directly by alphabet init, dice init/publish-bin, tapas2 init/publish, mechahaze-album1 publish) and i574n.github scripts/init.ps1 + build.ps1. They work while the redirect holds; the real fix is HTML-ADOPT-REPOS (the shim switches to html's release); if a run fails first, pin the clone to fc1943s/dir-tree-html at a643950e. (b) dead link: i574n.github profile/README.md -> i574n.github.io/polyglot/lib/math/math.spi.html; point it at zeta's page in spiral once ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE lands, or drop the line. (c) docs: i574n.github docs/agents/agent-sync.md lists polyglot as a core repo. (d) workspaces: i574n.code-workspace and i574n-deps.code-workspace include ../polyglot. (e) inventory scripts that still list polyglot: spiral apps/compiler/scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1, parser-corpus-gate.ps1, apps/compiler/tmp/formatter/extract-corpus.ps1; i574n.github pins.ps1, pages-sweep.ps1, recovered-drafts-census.ps1. (f) spiral apps/compiler/scripts/env.ps1:141 falls back to polyglot/deps for the VS Code plugin; apps/compiler/AGENTS.md says 'the polyglot builder'. (g) dotfiles dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1 calls polyglot's Supervisor (dead). (h) watch each repo's next CI run (gh run list) after the user's pushes; every red caused by the move is fixed here. OUT OF SCOPE: the fc1943s and fc1943s.github repos (dump org, polyglot is theirs now), singularity's data, the upstream fork's conditional fsproj path, and compiler source comments that record history. DONE: (a)-(g) fixed or ruled out with a reason, and one green CI run per affected repo.", Story, P0, D3, 90u32, Blocked, "", "ci,org,polyglot,dir-tree-html,drift,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_org_exit_fallout () = Planning ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_1 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 1u32, "2026-11-03T09:30Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:3x FIXED (unstaged), from reading each red CI run:\n(1) i574n/.github CI RED since the user's 23:17 push (runs at 23:17 and 07:43): scripts/workflow.ps1:13 dot-sourced ../../polyglot/scripts/core.ps1 ('The term ... is not recognized'). That was main's own 11-02 regression: init.ps1 stopped cloning polyglot, but workflow.ps1 still read it. Now '. ../../spiral/scripts/core.ps1', like build/outdated/publish.ps1 (init clones spiral first). Parses.\n(2) d: i574n.code-workspace drops the polyglot folder and polyglot/workspace/Cargo.toml from rust-analyzer.linkedProjects; i574n-deps.code-workspace points at ../spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language. Both parse as JSON.\n(3) c: docs/agents/agent-sync.md no longer lists polyglot as a core repo or a deps clone.\n(4) b: profile/README.md's math link now points to https://fc1943s.github.io/polyglot/lib/math/math.dib.html (HEAD 200; the old i574n URL and math.spi.html are 404). It moves to zeta's page under ZETA-NUMERIC-CORE.\n(5) e (i574n.github half): pins/pins.ps1 orgRepos now matches the org (gh repo list i574n): dir-tree-html and polyglot out, html and regex in. pins/workflows.spi drops the dir_tree_html and polyglot workflow definitions plus their 7 target rows (306 -> 275 lines; backup %TEMP%\\workflows.spi.before-org-exit). Node compile: RUST-FAILED for workflows AND the untouched pins_check, so it is the node's stale spiral checkout (MIRROR-RESYNC-1103), not this edit; it is re-run after the resync. html's gh-pages.yml is not modelled in pins yet (add with HTML-CI-RELEASE).\nSTILL OPEN: e (pages-sweep.ps1 and recovered-drafts-census.ps1 default repo lists; spiral apps/compiler scripts lib-usage-census, parser-corpus-gate, extract-corpus, env.ps1:141 and AGENTS.md, which are compiler's tree); g (dotfiles' appdata build uses polyglot's Supervisor); scripts/spiral-independent/rewrite-deps.ps1 (a finished one-off, deletion candidate after a stem grep).\nOTHER REDS, NOT FROM THE MOVE: html (the 1000-line gate, markdown/entry.rs 2339 lines; HTML-CI-RELEASE) and tibia (LunarG 'latest' = 1.4.363.1 has no Windows runtime zip, 404). The tibia one is fixed in spiral/scripts/init-wgsl-run.ps1: it tries 'latest', then the published versions newest first (vulkan.lunarg.com/sdk/versions/windows.json). Tested end to end on the box: it picks 1.4.363.0, and the zip carries x64/vulkan-1.dll. Lands when the user pushes spiral.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_2 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:34Z", "main", "main 11-03 05:4x MORE FIXED (unstaged): e, i574n.github half: scripts/pages-sweep.ps1 and recovered-drafts-census.ps1 default repo lists match the org (polyglot and dir-tree-html out, html and regex in; both parse). scripts/spiral-independent/rewrite-deps.ps1 DELETED: a finished one-off migration (SPIRAL-INDEPENDENT Done), referenced only by backlog notes and itself (stem grep over every repo); git history keeps it. g: dotfiles dist/appdata/spiral/build.ps1 now builds appdata.spi -> appdata.py through spiral's BuildSpiral -Backend Python instead of polyglot's Supervisor (parses). Its PROOF (compile + python run + same .appdata.toml.txt as before) runs after MIRROR-RESYNC-1103, on the node, or on the box once kit's TRAIN14c heavy window ends. e/f in spiral apps/compiler (5 sites) are handed to compiler (its tree). LEFT: the dotfiles proof, the pins compile re-run, compiler's 5 sites, and green runs after the user's pushes (.github: the workflow.ps1 fix; tibia: the Vulkan fallback in spiral).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_3 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 3u32, "2026-11-03T09:38Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:4x compiler: apps/compiler sites FIXED (unstaged, each .ps1 parse-checked). scripts/lib-usage-census.ps1 default repos: polyglot dropped, eoie -> kit. scripts/parser-corpus-gate.ps1 repo loop: polyglot -> kit. scripts/env.ps1 Get-SpiralPackageDir: the polyglot/deps fallback is gone; it still resolves spiral's deps/The-Spiral-Language (checked). tmp/formatter/extract-corpus.ps1 'user' corpus: now read from a bare cache clone of https://github.com/fc1943s/polyglot (LOCALAPPDATA/spiral-bin/corpus-src/polyglot.git, cloned on first use) at the same pinned bb856d13, which is on fc1943s/main (checked with branch -r --contains), so it survives POLYGLOT-RETIRE without vendoring 86 files / 577 KB. AGENTS.md: the stale 'build.ps1 in this directory packages ... with the polyglot builder' line is removed (no such file; the build is scripts/build.ps1). Also fixed beyond the five: tmp/AGENTS.md (core fallback wording) and tmp/README.md Upstream (the fork lives at spiral's deps/The-Spiral-Language). Left as history: tmp/AGENTS.md formatter note about dice's deps\\polyglot loop, and the contract sample name contract_cross_abi_polyglot_lowering.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_4 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 4u32, "2026-11-03T10:18Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:4x .github CI, second blocker found and FIXED (unstaged): workflow.ps1 also runs pins/pins.ps1, which now compiles (it had been failing on the node only because of the stale lib) and reported 3 workflow files differing from the typed source (scripts/pins/workflows.spi). The lanes had edited committed workflows without the model: i574n.github gh-pages.yml (an apps/graphs/build.ps1 step, if ubuntu, continue-on-error), spiral gh-pages.yml (the cells-gate job's transformer model cache step plus ci_gate -Roots lib/spiral,apps/transformer), and kit gh-pages.yml (env CARGO_PROFILE_DEV_DEBUG=0). Modelled all three: workflow.spi run_step gained continue_on_error (rendered after the body) plus a soft_run_if constructor; workflows.spi has the graphs step, a transformer_model_cache step and the kit env. pins.ps1 on the box: 'workflows: 0 workflow files differ from the typed source', exit 0. Backups %TEMP%\\pins-workflow.spi.bak, pins-workflows.spi.bak2. RULE for lanes: a workflow edit goes through scripts/pins/workflows.spi, or .github CI turns red.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_5 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 5u32, "2026-11-03T10:19Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:5x g RESOLVED BY DELETION, not a port. The box proof of the ported dotfiles build failed in the compiler, not the port: appdata.spi is edition-2 Spiral against an old lib backend union (ETY-UnionsCannotBeApplied on 'Rust None' / 'Rust (Wasm |> Some)', and ETY-UnboundVariable 'Python'). CHECK before deleting: nothing reads its output .appdata.toml.txt (git grep over dotfiles, spiral, kit, i574n.github, x and tibia; the only mention was main's own note), its builder was polyglot's dead Supervisor, it was last touched 2025-11-28, and it carried tracked .py files (no-py rule). So it is STALE by the 11-03 rule: DELETED dist/appdata/spiral (5 tracked files, unstaged; git history keeps them). The rest of dist/appdata (FancyZones, rider, vscode, read by src/windows/install-sudo.ps1) is untouched.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_6 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 6u32, "2026-11-03T17:50Z", "tibia", "11-03 13:5x tibia: one more fallout site of the polyglot exit, found in tibia CI and FIXED by main in spiral (unstaged, lands with the user spiral push): polyglot scripts/init.ps1 line 151 built the Spiral CLI (deps/spiral/apps/spiral/build.ps1), and spiral scripts/init-app-build.ps1, which every app switched to, did not. Cells runs every lua target through that CLI (spiral lua --lua-path), so on CI every lua target became unavailable; files whose only target is lua turned unsupported and the gate went red (tibia Ubuntu since d4ad52ad: combat_text, game_calls, samples, ground_trace, competitor). Fix: init-app-build.ps1 builds the CLI with apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1 when workspace/target/release/spiral[.exe] is missing (main). Affects every app on init-app-build (fiscal, blog, kit, x, dir-tree-html, html, regex, tibia). Proof = the first app CI run after the push with 0 unsupported lua rows. Details: TIBIA-1-0-DOD n5, POLYGLOT-RETIRE n25-n26.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_7 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 7u32, "2026-11-03T18:31Z", "main", "main 11-03 14:5x BLOCKED (not idle): every site from the move is fixed in the tree (i574n.github workflow.ps1/pins/workspaces/README/scripts, compiler's apps/compiler sites, dotfiles' dead build deleted, spiral init-wgsl-run fallback for tibia, init-app-build CLI build; i574n.github init/build no longer clone dir-tree-html; no workflow references either repo). Remaining: confirm CI green after the user's pushes of i574n.github, spiral and html. RESUME WHEN: any of those HEADs moves (i574n.github 5245678, spiral 98e51d32, html 05a1a436).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_8 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 8u32, "2026-11-05T04:13Z", "main", "11-05 00:13 main CI RED from main's own init-app-build CLI step (n7), found from fiscal's report. spiral faf422c9 (user push 11-04 23:18, run 41960731928) and fiscal bb1ebad (run 41960782740) are both red, with two causes and no change in the CLI itself (apps/spiral and its committed spiral.rs are identical to the last green, 98e51d32). (1) Ordering: init.ps1 line 14 runs init-app-build.ps1, which now builds the CLI and its run check, but sccache was only installed at init.ps1:78, while the CLI hard-sets RUSTC_WRAPPER=sccache (spiral.spi:256). Result: \"could not execute process sccache ... rustc -vV\" on ubuntu (rust, protocol-rust-build). (2) Layout: fiscal clones spiral to deps/spiral and runs init-app-build. file_system.get_workspace_root maps .../deps to its parent and then needs a sibling spiral/workspace checkout (the old polyglot layout), which a runner lacks, so every backend panics \"Option does not have a value\" (spiral.rs 19405/20376/20669/21359). FIX (unstaged; scripts only, no CLI regen): init-app-build.ps1 installs cargo-binstall and sccache BEFORE the CLI build (the block moved out of init.ps1, which still installs trunk after it), and sets SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT to its own checkout when unset, which get_workspace_root honors before any walk. Both parse clean. PENDING: CI on the user's next spiral push, then fiscal's. Follow-up: later CLI uses in a deps layout (fiscal's Cells lua runs) need SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT in the job env too, or a lib fallback in get_workspace_root (deps search fails -> use the deps/spiral checkout itself).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_9 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 9u32, "2026-11-05T04:48Z", "main", "11-05 00:48 main LIB FALLBACK (fiscal's choice over a per-step env var): draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-WORKSPACE-ROOT-DEPS\\file_system.spi (AB1B2AFC5F06, base A981A5951BF8). New deps_workspace_root: a found root named deps still prefers an outer spiral/workspace checkout (unchanged), else it returns the deps dir itself, so the root becomes deps/spiral instead of panicking; SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT still wins first. Test a_deps_root_without_an_outer_checkout_keeps_its_own_spiral. Round trip clean (lib_land_window dry run). First notebook gate VOID twice: once in a bare lib copy (packages unbound outside a repo), once cgroup-killed during mix setup while another lane's 1.5 GB rustc ran on vultr; it is re-armed to start after that build, in a -Mirror main-ws copy. Then the two-step land (node proof + box -ProvenLog). Ships with the user's next spiral push, together with the init-app-build sccache/SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT fix (n8).")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_10 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 10u32, "2026-11-05T06:42Z", "main", "11-05 02:42 main LANDED (unstaged, rides the user's next spiral push): lib/spiral/file_system.spi A981A5951BF8 -> AB1B2AFC5F06 (deps_workspace_root: a found root named deps still prefers an outer spiral/workspace checkout, else uses deps/spiral itself instead of panicking; SPIRAL_REPO_ROOT still wins first). Two-step land: node proof (mirror main-proven, Windows) control 40/42 with the 2 failures being 300 s cell TIMEOUTS (VOID, node at 100% under TRAIN27), draft 43/43; node close green (signatures 13 unchanged, spiral.spi compiles, document_test 26/26, type_probe 43 typed 0 errors, 0 respell drift); box close green from -ProvenLog (lib had moved, so fast checks reran; document_test taken from the proof), undo C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-023639. With the init-app-build fix (n8), the fiscal deps-layout panic and the sccache ordering are both fixed in the tree; a fresh-runner test of init on a codespace is running now.")
inl note_of_org_exit_fallout_11 () = Note ("ORG-EXIT-FALLOUT", 11u32, "2026-11-05T06:50Z", "main", "11-05 02:50 main FRESH-RUNNER PROOF of the init fix (before the user's push): codespace miniature-meme-x7jqqp6pp3v957 (Ubuntu 24.04, 4 cores, no Rust, no sccache, no cargo-binstall), spiral HEAD faf422c9 cloned with the box's fixed scripts/init-app-build.ps1 (886B46344C30) and init.ps1 dropped in; rustup + nightly-2026-10-18 minimal installed first, as setup-rust does in CI. init.ps1 -> init-app-build: cargo-binstall --self-install, then \"cargo binstall sccache\" (sccache v0.19.0 -> ~/.cargo/bin, 2.7 s), THEN apps/spiral/build.ps1 -fast 1: run check rust exit 0 \"spiral-check-rust 42\" (the CI red case), cuda/lua/gleam 42, protocol cases as expected, no FAILED / RUST-FAILED line; init continued (trunk via binstall). So the sccache-ordering red is fixed for every repo whose CI runs spiral init. The deps/spiral panic fix is the file_system.spi land (n10). PENDING: CI on the user's next push.")
inl scheduler_model_move () = Task ("SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE", "Move polyglot's scheduler model (apps/scheduler/Tasks.spi, 214 lines, last edited 10-25) to i574n.github/apps/scheduler, as decided by POLYGLOT-RETIRE n21 (polyglot left the org 11-03; the local copy is the source). It is a typed task-scheduling model: task_id/task_name nominals, manual_scheduling, recurrency_offset, fixed_recurrency and scheduling unions over date_time, action events, plus a terminal calendar printer. STEPS: (1) respell to edition 3: 'test x =' becomes ':# x =' with distinct names; the '/// ##' heading comments go (no-comment rule); field access becomes '::'; module calls follow the current lib spelling; (2) keep its 4 tests (get_actions, get_actions_2, cols, lines) on their zig target, adding rust; (3) a package.spiproj next to it, the way apps/graphs has one; (4) gate it on the node with memo off (after MIRROR-RESYNC-1103); (5) then rule out the polyglot copy. DONE: every test is green on the node, the file follows kit standards, and POLYGLOT-RETIRE notes the move.", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "MIRROR-RESYNC-1103", "polyglot,migration,typefeatureset,i574n.github,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_scheduler_model_move () = Planning ("SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_scheduler_model_move_1 () = Note ("SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE", 1u32, "2026-11-03T11:37Z", "main", "main 11-03 07:4x STARTED (unstaged): i574n.github/apps/scheduler/scheduler.spi + package.spiproj (edition 3, packageDir ../../../spiral/lib, like apps/graphs). Port: an edition-3 static test header, the '/// ##' heading comments dropped (no-comment rule), and the 4 tests renamed so they do not collide with their functions (the_actions_mention_task_00003, the_fourth_action_adds_task_00003, three_columns_print_side_by_side, the_calendar_lines_print). The body was already edition-3 compatible: it COMPILES on the box (pack24, Rust backend, first try). NEXT: gate its zig tests (plus rust) with Cells, then rule out the polyglot copy.")
inl note_of_scheduler_model_move_2 () = Note ("SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T12:13Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:1x DONE. Vultr Cells gate (pack24, memo off): i574n.github/apps/scheduler/scheduler.spi 4/4 on its original zig target (the_actions_mention_task_00003, the_fourth_action_adds_task_00003, three_columns_print_side_by_side, the_calendar_lines_print). It lives at i574n.github/apps/scheduler (unstaged; git add the folder). The polyglot copy is ruled out and goes with the local polyglot deletion (POLYGLOT-RETIRE n22).")
inl note_of_scheduler_model_move_3 () = Note ("SCHEDULER-MODEL-MOVE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T12:41Z", "main", "main 11-03 08:5x CORRECTION: apps/scheduler duplicated examples/scheduler (the 10-30 R4 examples-lab slice had already copied Tasks.spi there, tracked, byte-identical to polyglot's). R4 (examples lab = i574n.github/examples/<name>/) wins over n21's apps/ path. Folded (unstaged): examples/scheduler now holds scheduler.spi (the gated edition-3 port, 4/4) + package.spiproj (packageDir ../../../spiral/lib, same depth); Tasks.spi deleted (D); build.ps1 points at scheduler.spi. apps/scheduler removed (never tracked). Backup %TEMP%\\scheduler-fold-1103. Nothing referenced either path.")
inl node_versioned_spiral_source () = Task ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", "Versioned spiral source on the nodes, so the shared lib can be updated while lanes' jobs run (memory deploys-never-wait-for-idle). TODAY: every node mirror links deps to the node's C:\\home\\git\\<repo>\\deps, and those link spiral to the ONE mutable checkout C:\\home\\git\\spiral. A sync either waits for a node that is never idle (MIRROR-RESYNC-1103 waited 2 h behind 5+ jobs) or swaps files under running jobs. DESIGN: sync spiral into C:\\home\\remote\\spiral-src\\<head-digest> (immutable once built, runner included); remote.ps1 sync links each NEW mirror's spiral to the current version directory, so a job keeps the version it started with; a 'current' pointer moves atomically; old versions are deleted when no running job's mirror links them (kit job list plus a junction scan). The same on vultr. DONE: a sync under 3 running jobs changes none of their inputs (proven by hashing their mirror's lib before and after), and new jobs see the new head.", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "node,vultr,mirror,remote,deploy,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_node_versioned_spiral_source () = Planning ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_node_versioned_spiral_source_1 () = Note ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", 1u32, "2026-11-03T10:11Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:3x RELATED GAP, seen twice tonight: a repo synced to a machine where it was never initialized has no deps/spiral link, so its mirror's deps is empty and every gate fails before compiling (regex on vultr: 'deps/spiral/scripts/core.ps1 is not recognized'; html on the node: 'Cannot find path ...\\deps\\spiral\\apps\\cells'). Fixed by hand: /home/remote/git/regex/deps/spiral -> /home/remote/git/spiral on vultr, and C:\\home\\git\\html\\deps\\spiral -> C:\\home\\git\\spiral (junction) on the node. FIX IN remote.ps1 sync, with this item: when the repo's package.spiproj has packageDir ../deps/spiral/lib and the source lacks deps/spiral, create it (junction or symlink) to the machine's spiral checkout, which becomes the versioned source once this item lands.")
inl note_of_node_versioned_spiral_source_2 () = Note ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T10:18Z", "main", "main 11-03 06:4x DEPS BOOTSTRAP LANDED in remote.ps1 sync (unstaged): for a non-spiral repo, when a package.spiproj in the MIRROR (the source of a fresh machine has no working files, only objects) references deps/spiral, the source lacks deps/spiral, and the machine has a spiral checkout, it links deps/spiral -> <gitRoot>/spiral (Junction on Windows, SymbolicLink on Linux) and prints DEPS-SPIRAL-LINKED; the existing mirror step then links the mirror's deps. Proven on vultr with html, which had never been there: DEPS-SPIRAL-LINKED /home/remote/git/html/deps/spiral, MIRROR-DEPS-OK, and the mirror lists spiral's lib. Parses.")
inl note_of_node_versioned_spiral_source_3 () = Note ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", 3u32, "2026-11-04T14:07Z", "main", "11-04 10:1x main STEP 1 LANDED (unstaged i574n.github scripts/remote.ps1, parses): sync <repo> -Mirror <m> -SpiralMirror <s> links the non-spiral mirror's deps/spiral to <mirrorBase>/<s>/spiral instead of the node's ONE mutable base clone. The mirror's old deps link is removed with link-only .Delete() (never a recursive delete through a junction); a missing spiral mirror prints SPIRAL-MIRROR-MISSING and exits 8; success prints MIRROR-SPIRAL-LINKED. PROVEN on the node: html -Mirror main-html -SpiralMirror main-kernel -> REMOTE-SYNC-OK; the base C:\\home\\git\\html\\deps\\spiral is intact; the mirror's lib has doc_blocks.spi while the base clone does NOT (the 11-04 ETY-Unbound cause). So a gate of any repo can pin the spiral version it runs against (sync spiral -Mirror <s> first) without waiting for an idle node or touching other jobs' inputs. LEFT for the full item: content-addressed spiral-src/<digest> dirs with an atomic current pointer, and GC of versions no running job links.")
inl note_of_node_versioned_spiral_source_4 () = Note ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", 4u32, "2026-11-04T14:30Z", "main", "11-04 10:3x main STEP 2 LANDED (unstaged remote.ps1, parses): VERSIONED SOURCE + CURRENT POINTER. sync spiral -Publish (sync spiral only, no -Mirror) syncs into a mirror NAMED BY THE TREE, spiral-<head8>-<digest8>, so a version is never rewritten under a running job (the same tree reuses the same mirror), and after REMOTE-SYNC-OK writes <mirrorBase>/spiral-current.txt and prints SPIRAL-PUBLISHED. Any repo's mirror then takes -SpiralMirror current (resolved on the node from the pointer) or a named version. PROVEN on the node: SPIRAL-PUBLISHED spiral-98e51d32-28229005; html -Mirror main-html -SpiralMirror current -> MIRROR-SPIRAL-LINKED C:\\home\\remote\\spiral-98e51d32-28229005\\spiral, with doc_blocks and fin_vector present (the base clone has neither). The DONE test (3 running jobs keep their inputs) holds by construction: publishing creates a new directory and only moves the pointer, and no existing mirror is touched. LEFT: GC of versions no running mirror links and that aren't current; vultr uses the same code (not yet exercised there).")
inl note_of_node_versioned_spiral_source_5 () = Note ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", 5u32, "2026-11-04T14:33Z", "main", "11-04 10:4x main STEP 3 (GC, report-only by design): -Publish now prints SPIRAL-VERSION-STALE <dir> for every spiral-<head>-<digest> version that is not the one just published, is not the target of any mirror's deps/spiral link, and appears in no running process's command line. It does NOT delete: a version mirror holds junctions into shared deps, and a recursive delete through a junction is the one deletion that can destroy the shared tree (guards fail closed). Removal stays a reviewed step: .Delete() the junctions, then git worktree remove. Re-publish of the unchanged tree reused spiral-98e51d32-28229005 and reported nothing stale, as expected. On vultr the process check is empty (no Win32_Process), so the report is more conservative there.")
inl note_of_node_versioned_spiral_source_6 () = Note ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", 6u32, "2026-11-04T15:21Z", "main", "11-04 11:2x main VULTR exercised: -Publish created spiral-98e51d32-6EB06A80 and moved the pointer, but the stale scan crashed on Linux (Get-CimInstance does not exist there, and a missing command is not suppressed by -ErrorAction). Fixed: the process list comes from Get-CimInstance where it exists, else from ps -eo args, so the in-use check is real on Linux too. Re-publish: SPIRAL-PUBLISHED + REMOTE-SYNC-OK on vultr. Both machines now run the same code path.")
inl note_of_node_versioned_spiral_source_7 () = Note ("NODE-VERSIONED-SPIRAL-SOURCE", 7u32, "2026-11-05T07:34Z", "main", "11-05 03:34 main DoD PROVEN on the node: a stand-in job mirror (html -Mirror main-vtest1 -SpiralMirror current) linked spiral-98e51d32-28229005 (146 lib files, lib fingerprint AAF3555BCD3361A0, file_system 76CA7B4D). Then `sync spiral -Publish` of the box tree ran while tibia-cl2-cem-lanes-2 and fiscal-decode-one were RUNNING: SPIRAL-PUBLISHED spiral-faf422c9-1D12221C, REMOTE-SYNC-OK, and no SPIRAL-VERSION-STALE for the old version (correct: it was still linked). After: the old version byte-identical (same 146 files, same fingerprint), the stand-in still linked to it, the pointer on spiral-faf422c9-1D12221C; a mirror created after the publish (main-vtest2) links the new version (147 files, file_system AB1B2AFC5F06 = tonight's land). So publishing never rewrites a running job's inputs, and new jobs see the new head. Test mirrors removed junction-first (both versions intact after). Old versions stay report-only GC by design (deleting a version means unlinking its junctions first).")
inl linked_units_shared_instances () = Task ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", "Linked units re-emit generic union instantiations per crate: a core list (or option) instantiated over a linked unit's union (list inline, list block) is emitted as its own enum in every crate that uses it, so a list crossing a link: boundary fails rustc E0308. The defining linked unit should own the instantiation (pub) and every linking crate should import it, like the user unions it already imports", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS", "team:compiler,compiler,linked-units,rust,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_linked_units_shared_instances () = Planning ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_linked_units_shared_instances_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", 1u32, "2026-11-03T09:53Z", "compiler", "11-03 05:5x compiler: found by lu9 (COMPILER-LINKED-UNITS-EXTERN-CALLS n12). Repro: node remote-stage/compiler-lu9 (model unions inline/block over list, parse returns list block, render takes it): model.rs, parse.rs and render.rs each define pub enum list_inline/list_block/...; parse.rs and render.rs import only model::{inline, block}. Workaround in use: array_base at boundaries (lu9a, builds and runs).")
inl note_of_linked_units_shared_instances_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", 2u32, "2026-11-03T09:56Z", "compiler", "11-03 06:0x compiler: on html's critical path (main n10 on HTML-CI-RELEASE keeps list in the model; array_base fallback if this misses 11-04 06:00). Program LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES\\1-import-instances-by-shape.kitdo (1 replacement on pack23 live 28F212AEFACE68EC): linkedUnionName, when a union's declaring package is not a linked unit (core list/option), takes it from the first linked unit whose graph reached the same (source name, shape), so import_rust_unions and the Gleam importer import it like the unit's own unions. Rule that remains: the model unit's exports must reach every container instantiation crossing the boundary (lu9's model gains wrap (b : block) : list block for list block). Node review compiler-lu9fix running: lu9 (list) and lu9a (array) under installed and candidate, plus examples Rust and Gleam A/B.")
inl note_of_linked_units_shared_instances_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", 3u32, "2026-11-03T10:17Z", "compiler", "11-03 06:1x compiler: PROVEN, handed to main as pack24 (dry run reproduces source core C1D78AAEB261EB74 from live pack23; R2R SpiralCompiler.dll 6B30D2F521660878, core 21D5992EDB80D270). Node t1101 compiler-lu9fix: lu9 (list model + wrap) installed rustc E0308 -> candidate use model::{list_inline, list_list_inline, list_string, list_list_string, list_block, ...} in parse, render and app, 4 crates build, exit 108 (correct html length); lu9a (array) unchanged, exit 108 both arms; examples Rust 515 and Gleam 441 rows vs installed: 0 differing cells. Done when installed.")
inl note_of_linked_units_shared_instances_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-SHARED-INSTANCES", 4u32, "2026-11-03T10:27Z", "compiler", "11-03 06:3x compiler: DONE. pack24 installed on box (core 21D5992EDB80D270 verified live), node (swap, launch exit 0) and vultr (linux core D7577C480AAAF35A), per main 06:23. html's split (list model + wrap export) starts on it.")
inl html_lint_heal () = Task ("HTML-LINT-HEAL", "Heal html's kit standards findings (73 on 11-03, after kit's new lint rule). 64 x rec-outside-cycle ('^ on a definition in no recursion cycle'; '^' means rec, not join point): inline_parse 15, markdown 15, render 12, tree 8, model 7, pages 4, file_views 3. HTML-MODEL wrote ':~ ^' on non-recursive helpers, believing '^' marked join points. 9 x line-width (file_views 61/63, inline_parse 112, markdown 145, pages 82/84, tree 30/112/119), all predating 11-03. RULE for each '^' removal: html src stays green, and the generated markdown/entry.rs and cli/html.rs line counts must not grow (a '^' change can alter inlining). Measure before and after on the node. Do it after HTML-MARKDOWN's raw-item fix lands and before the unit split, so each file churns once. DONE: kit standards on html/src reports 0.", Story, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "html,lint,standards,team:main,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_html_lint_heal () = Planning ("HTML-LINT-HEAL", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_html_lint_heal_1 () = Note ("HTML-LINT-HEAL", 1u32, "2026-11-03T13:03Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:0x HEALED (unstaged) on the split layout: kit standards over the 8 html packages 79 -> 0. 64 x ':~ ^' -> ':~ ' on the flagged non-recursive defs only (38 truly recursive '^' kept); 15 line-width rewraps (bodies onto the next line, the lib's multi-line signature form for cli nodes_of, leading ++#/&&/?> continuations, two test strings split). GENERATED RUST BYTE-IDENTICAL for all 8 crates (model 586, inline 596, table 230, parse 837, render 480, pages 887, entry 12, cli 901); one literal split that added 2 lines to pages.rs was reverted to a single literal. Backup %TEMP%\\html-lint-heal-1103. NEXT: Cells gate of the unit notebooks on vultr, then Done.")
inl note_of_html_lint_heal_2 () = Note ("HTML-LINT-HEAL", 2u32, "2026-11-03T13:43Z", "main", "main 11-03 09:4x GATE: vultr Cells on the synced tree (/home/remote/git/html, memo off): 49/49 across model 5, inline_parse 7, table 2, markdown 10, render 10, file_views 4, pages_api 1, pages 5, tree 5 (same 49 as the box build). cli/html.spi is a test-free entry, not a notebook (excluded by build.ps1 too). DONE.")
inl cells_lua_host_crash () = Task ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", "Cells: 'spiral lua' host exits 0xC0000005 (access violation) intermittently under node load; plus compiler port lock_timeout", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "cells,lua,flaky,node,team:compiler,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_cells_lua_host_crash () = Planning ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_1 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 1u32, "2026-11-03T11:23Z", "tibia", "11-03 07:2x tibia, FILED from a full memo-off tibia suite on the node (job-1793697609391-tibia-full-suite-1, tibia-gates3, 7,200 s, timed out at 37 of ~60 files while fiscal and compiler jobs shared the node). The Cells runner's 'spiral lua --lua-path <tmp>/main.lua' exited -1073741819 (0xC0000005, a native access violation, no Lua error text) in 4 files: apps/canary/lead_trace.spi, apps/arena/measure.spi (0/4), apps/arena/observer.spi (0/2), apps/offscreen/offscreen.spi (1/9). The same offscreen file passed 9/9 an hour earlier in its own gate (job offscreen-2/chain4), so the crash is intermittent, not a test failure. Two other files failed to start the compiler at all: 'could not start the compiler on port 13969: :lock_timeout' (src/network.spi, src/pack_sim.spi 29/39). Next evidence: solo reruns of lead_trace, map, measure and network are queued on the node (tibia-load-chain-1, first step); a crash dump (WER LocalDumps for the spiral/lua host) would give the faulting module. Owner guess: the spiral CLI's Lua host, built by the compiler lane.")
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_2 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 2u32, "2026-11-03T11:45Z", "tibia", "11-03 07:4x tibia: the compiler-port half recurs. Job tibia-sized5-1 (lib gate of sized_array on tibia-gates3) aborted with 'could not start the compiler on port 13969: :lock_timeout' after 6/12 cells; a probe of the 5 'failed' tests passes on C and Rust on vultr, so the cells failed for lack of the compiler, not code. That makes 3 tibia jobs today (network, pack_sim, sized_array) hitting the same port lock while other lanes' Cells jobs shared the node. Suggestion: per-job compiler ports (or a queue on the daemon) so concurrent Cells runs wait for the lock rather than failing; until then, gates on a shared node can report false reds.")
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_3 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 3u32, "2026-11-03T12:18Z", "tibia", "11-03 08:1x tibia: the crash REPRODUCES in solo reruns (node job tibia-load-chain-1, whose first step ran only lead_trace, map, measure and network, with x-census and fiscal jobs also on the node): lead_trace 0/1 and measure 0/4 again exit -1073741819 from spiral lua --lua-path ...main.lua, while map 5/5 and network 7/7 (+1 wgsl unsupported) passed alone, so those two were contention. The same crash then aborted the file_system lib gate mid-batch (path_join_without_a_native_arm lua, lua_files_write_read_append_and_delete lua). So the Lua host crash is now reproducible on the node for lead_trace and measure, not only intermittent; measure passed 4/4 in tibia chain4 at about 05:5x local, so something in the node state since then (temp dir, memory, a Lua runtime update) may be involved. A WER LocalDumps capture for the spiral process on the node would give the faulting module.")
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_4 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 4u32, "2026-11-03T12:23Z", "tibia", "11-03 08:2x tibia, ROOT CAUSE LOCATED (node Application event log, read-only): every crash is spiral.exe itself, path C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\workspace\\target\\release\\spiral.exe on the node, exception c0000005 at the SAME offset 0x1dcbf9 (module spiral.exe 0.0.1.0). Timeline: that binary was REBUILT at 2026-11-03 05:47:05 (size 2,992,128); the first crash is 05:50; there are ZERO spiral.exe crashes in the 3 days before; since then 85 (05h 1, 06h 15, 07h 17, 08h 52, rising as more lanes run Lua cells). So this is a regression introduced by the 05:47 rebuild of the node's spiral CLI, deterministic at one code site, not a flaky Lua interpreter (it also explains why apps/arena/measure passed 4/4 in tibia chain4 just before and crashes now). It is not the compiler-port lock_timeout, which is separate. NEXT for the owner: identify who rebuilt workspace/target/release/spiral.exe at 05:47 and from which commit; rebuild from the last good state or bisect; a debug build or the PDB maps offset 0x1dcbf9 to the function. Every lane running Lua-target Cells on the node is affected until then.")
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_5 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 5u32, "2026-11-03T12:25Z", "tibia", "11-03 08:3x tibia, BUILD ORIGIN: the crashing node binary was built from the node checkout C:\\home\\git\\spiral at HEAD 194a1916 (tests, 2026-11-02 10:47; reflog: checked out 11-02 12:19), clean working tree (0 dirty files under workspace/ and apps/spiral), no other spiral.exe build on the node. compiler (direct message) confirms independently: their reflection lib gate crashed the same way on the node at 07:22 (spiral lua and spiral cuda --py-path both -1073741819) while the identical gate on the box with runner 9A99BF53 passed 12/12 on lua, rust, gleam, typescript and fsharp; compiler did not build it and points to main's run-start runner refresh (~04:53-05:47). So: a runner rebuilt at 05:47 from a day-old commit crashes, and the box's current runner works. Asked main (direct message) to rebuild the node runner from current spiral. Owner is main for the fix; the backlog tag team:compiler is kept for the runner code.")
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_6 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 6u32, "2026-11-03T12:32Z", "main", "main 08:4x: cause found - main's 05:47 node runner refresh used plain cargo build --release (opt z, LTO, panic=abort, 2.99 MB 45C8253E) instead of apps/spiral/build.ps1 (release-unwind + mimalloc, 6.1 MB). Node spiral synced to box tree 98e51d32 at 08:26; build.ps1 rebuild running on the node.")
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_7 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 7u32, "2026-11-03T12:38Z", "tibia", "11-03 08:4x tibia, FIX IN PROGRESS (main, direct messages): the bad node runner came from main's 05:47 run-start refresh, which ran a plain cargo build --release in workspace (45C8253E, 2.99 MB) instead of apps/spiral/build.ps1's release-unwind profile (panic=unwind, opt 3, no LTO, mimalloc appended). At 08:37 main copied the box's 9A99BF53 (6,109,696 B) over it, verified by tibia on the node (hash 9A99BF53, mtime 08:37:22); the bad binary is kept aside as spiral.exe.bad-45C8253E-*. build.ps1 is rebuilding the canonical runner from the synced tree (98e51d32) and will replace it. Crash count before the swap: 56 in the 30 min to 08:3x (other lanes kept running Lua cells). VERIFY NEXT: tibia's requeue job (tibia-suite-requeue-1) logs the runner hash at start and reruns the Lua-target files that crashed (lead_trace, measure, observer, offscreen, path, probe, random, samples, scan, scenario, scoreboard, policy); clean results there plus no new Application Error events for spiral.exe close this item.")
inl note_of_cells_lua_host_crash_8 () = Note ("CELLS-LUA-HOST-CRASH", 8u32, "2026-11-03T12:58Z", "tibia", "11-03 08:5x tibia, CLOSED, both closing conditions met: (1) on the canonical runner 9FF45F12 (6,083,072 B, apps/spiral/build.ps1 release-unwind, 08:39:29) the Lua files that crashed all morning pass in tibia-suite-requeue-1 batch 1: lead_trace 1/1, measure 4/4, observer 2/2, offscreen 9/9 (the batch started on main's interim copy 9A99BF53 and finished on 9FF45F12, both good); (2) the node Application log has 0 spiral.exe crashes since 08:39:30 (last crash overall 08:31:05, on the bad binary). Cause and fix are in n4-n7 (bad runner: a plain cargo build --release at 05:47; rule now: refresh the runner only via build.ps1, per main). The compiler-port lock_timeout half seen under contention is separate and did not recur in today's later jobs; reopen or file it if it returns.")
inl spiral_nameof_typed () = Task ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", "Typed names beyond the met nameof DoD: case_name returns a phantom-tagged name t (not a bare string) so names of different unions do not mix, name styles (exact/lower/snake/kebab) applied at compile time, qualified module::case names, and a GADT-indexed case table whose length is known at compile time", Story, P2, D5, 100u32, Done, "SPIRAL-NAMEOF", "team:compiler,compiler,typefeatureset,nameof", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_spiral_nameof_typed () = Planning ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 1u32, "2026-11-03T12:14Z", "compiler", "11-03 08:1x compiler: split from SPIRAL-NAMEOF (closed on its DoD: lib reflection case_name/case_of_name round-trip on rust/gleam/lua/typescript/fsharp and fold statically). Start from the call sites SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL finds, so the typed API is shaped by real users.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 2u32, "2026-11-04T08:03Z", "compiler", "11-04 03:5x compiler: SLICE 1 LANDED (closed green on the second close). lib reflection.spi gains a phantom-tagged name: ':! typed_name t = string', typed_case_name (x : t) : typed_name t, typed_name_text, and case_of_typed_name (typed_name t) : option t. case_name keeps returning string, so its users (lib metrics, the nameof-heal rewrites) are untouched. Test typed_case_name_round_trips (///> gleam, lua, rust, typescript): lib_gate 1/1 on a scratch lib. Type safety proven on the box: in a separate module, reflection::case_of_typed_name (typed_case_name Green) = Some Green compiles, and the same name compared with Some Circle (another union) fails with ETY-TermError: Unification failure. First close FAILED at document_test (the notebook round trip: one missing blank line between cells), was undone automatically, and the canonical form from lib_roundtrip.exs then landed: reflection.spi EA0F566D -> F525120D, document_test 22, type_probe 13 typed, undo 20261104-035524. Left on the story: name styles (lower/snake/kebab at compile time), qualified module::case names, and a GADT-indexed case table.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_3 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 3u32, "2026-11-04T08:11Z", "compiler", "11-04 04:0x compiler: SLICE 2 LANDED (name styles), closed green first time (round trip run BEFORE the window: canonical true). reflection.spi F525120D -> 3704C624, document_test 22, type_probe 14 typed, undo 20261104-040757. Adds styled_name separator text (lowercase, with the separator before each inner capital; a named fold step, since multi-line lambda arguments do not parse), typed_name_snake, typed_name_kebab and typed_name_lower. Test typed_name_styles (gleam, rust): HostMacro -> host_macro, GadtCase -> gadt-case, Contract -> contract, typed Browser -> browser (kebab, lower); lib_gate 1/1. Styles run at run time; compile-time folding is not guaranteed. Left: qualified module::case names and a GADT-indexed case table whose length is known at compile time.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_4 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 4u32, "2026-11-04T09:59Z", "compiler", "11-04 06:0x compiler: SCOPED the qualified-name slice. Lib cannot get a union's own nominal name today: real_core::type_to_symbol works only on symbol types (sm'_real symbol_to_string_real), and the compiler has show_nominal (TopEnv nominals_aux names) but no op exposing it to real code. NEXT CONCRETE STEP (compiler): an op like !!!!NominalName(`t) that peval folds to the nominal's name as a literal string (parser op table, typer arity, peval case reading nominals_aux), then lib typed_case_qualified_name = nominal name ++ '::' ++ case_name. Left after that: the GADT-indexed case table.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_5 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 5u32, "2026-11-04T10:00Z", "compiler", "11-04 06:0x compiler: COMPILER OP DRAFTED: kit drafts SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED\\3-nominal-name-op.kitdo (3 replacements). A new Op case NominalName, registered automatically by the reflection-built string_to_op_dict, and a peval arm: !!!!NominalName(`t) walks YApply to the head and folds a YNominal to its name as a string literal, otherwise 'Expected a nominal type'. It joins the TypeToVar/TypeToSymbol 'Expected a type' arm. Stacks on pack35 plus split-units. Planned for pack36 with split-units; after the install, lib gains case_qualified_name x = !!!!NominalName(`t) ++# '::' ++# case_name x (test: Contract -> reflection_test_target::Contract).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_6 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 6u32, "2026-11-04T15:56Z", "compiler", "11-04 11:5x compiler: SLICE 3 LANDED (qualified names) on installed pack36 (which brought !!!!NominalName). lib reflection.spi 3704C624 -> 94FB2F11: case_qualified_name x = !!!!NominalName(`t) ++# '::' ++# case_name x, plus test case_qualified_name (gleam, rust): Contract -> reflection_test_target::Contract, Browser -> reflection_test_target::Browser. Round trip canonical and a fixpoint first; lib_land_window closed green: 3 consumer-used signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22, type_probe pass (15 tests typed), 0 respell drift, lib digest 55569F48, undo 20261104-112115. The box lib_gate run was INCONCLUSIVE: under 100% box load a cell hit the 300 s timeout and the run aborted, reporting 10 of 15 targets 'failed', including targets green this morning (typed_name_styles rust), and the case_qualified_name cell has no output at all. Rerun on the node (job compiler-reflgate) with the landed file copied over (hash 94FB2F11). Left after that: the GADT-indexed case table.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_7 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 7u32, "2026-11-04T17:39Z", "compiler", "11-04 13:4x compiler: case_qualified_name PASSES on both targets (box lib_gate rerun at lower load: case_qualified_name gleam passed, rust passed). The same run reported 5 other targets failed (union_cases_fold typescript, union_cases_find rust, case_name cuda, nameof_cases_round_trip lua, typed_case_name_round_trips rust) with a 'timed out' cell and slowest cell 175 s. The failing set differs from the first, overloaded run (e.g. typed_name_styles rust failed there, passes here) and the land only ADDED a definition and a test, so these are load flakes in the Cells harness, not this change; the node gate (job compiler-reflgate) gives the clean full run. Slice 3 done; left: the GADT-indexed case table.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_8 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 8u32, "2026-11-04T18:14Z", "compiler", "11-04 14:1x compiler: NODE GATE (job compiler-reflgate, installed pack36, landed reflection.spi 94FB2F11): case_qualified_name gleam PASSED and rust PASSED (2 of 2 runs now), typed_name_styles gleam/rust passed. The run again hit 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s' and reported 6 other targets failed, a THIRD different set (now mostly typescript: get_union_fields_untag, union_try_pick, union_try_pick_2, union_cases_find; plus case_name rust, nameof_cases_round_trip fsharp). Three runs on two machines, three disjoint-ish failing sets, each with a cell timeout: reflection.spi's gate sits at the edge of the 300 s Cells cell budget under load, so whichever targets the timeout kills are reported failed. Not this change (the land only added a definition and a test). Worth its own fix: split reflection.spi's test cells or raise its cell budget, so the gate is deterministic.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_9 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 9u32, "2026-11-04T19:54Z", "compiler", "11-04 15:5x compiler: slice 3 (case_qualified_name) CONFIRMED in a clean full gate: reflection.spi lib_gate on the node, 15 of 15 tests passed, no cell timeout (after LIB-REFLECTION-GATE-TIMEOUT's per-test budgets). Left: the GADT-indexed case table.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_10 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 10u32, "2026-11-04T20:05Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:1x compiler: SLICE 4 STARTED (GADT and payload case names). Why: lib case_name compares x against constructed nullary cases (get_union_fields_untag), so it cannot name a payload case (Circle 1.5) or a GADT-indexed case (cells daemon request_line, the one spiral nameof-heal site left). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED\\5-union-case-name-op.kitdo (2 replacements, applies on pack38's source): op !!!!UnionCaseName(x). peval folds a known case (static DUnion, or a dyn value whose case is in s.unions) to a string literal; a dyn union becomes ArrayIndex over a string array literal of the case names placed by the union's own tag dictionary (declaration index, so GADT-pruned cases keep their slot and the table matches UnionTag on every backend), indexed by UnionTag. No backend change: both ops already exist everywhere. Probe (payload, nullary, GADT, static and dyn; exit 42 iff all names match) runs on the node in job compiler-casename, with installed pack36 as the negative control. After it lands in a pack: lib case_name = !!!!UnionCaseName(x), then the request_line heal.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_11 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 11u32, "2026-11-04T20:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:2x compiler: slice 4 LIB + HEAL DRAFTED (frozen; lands only after the op is in an installed pack). Dir %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED\\6-case-name-op: (a) reflection.spi on base F689F0385A602FFE: case_name x = !!!!UnionCaseName(x) (one line, replaces the nullary compare over get_union_fields_untag), and the case_name test adds a payload case (Some 3i32 -> 'Some') and a dyn one (~ None -> 'None'). (b) apps/cells/spi/daemon.spi on base D843CD7206331689: request_line becomes '| Compile a => tabbed (sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q) :: ask_fields a) | _ => sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q)' (four nullary arms -> one; the existing test pins 'compile\\\\trust\\\\t...'). Order: op probe green (job compiler-casename) -> op joins the pack after pack38 -> install -> round trip both files -> lib_land_window for reflection.spi -> cells test for daemon.spi.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_12 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 12u32, "2026-11-04T20:48Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:4x compiler: op v1 probe (node compiler-casename2, candidate core 74BFB8EC): installed pack36 rejects !!!!UnionCaseName with a parser error (negative control OK); candidate compiles Zig, Rust and C, static calls fold to string literals; Rust native exits 42 (all five names right), Zig native exits 1. CAUSE: for a GADT-specialized union, peval's static UnionTag and Rust's tag() use the DECLARED index (request i32: Count => 1), while Zig (and most backends: they emit the raw .tag their constructors store, the dense position over surviving cases) stores Count as tag 0. v2 of the draft (same file, 2 replacements): one surviving case folds to that case's literal (request_line's specializations are all single-case); an unpruned union keeps the tag table (dense = declared there); a partially pruned GADT with 2+ cases left is a compile error naming UnionTag. Probe v2 + negative (pick i32 keeps First and Second) in node job compiler-casename3. Filed the UnionTag numbering bug separately.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_13 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 13u32, "2026-11-04T20:57Z", "compiler", "11-04 16:5x compiler: op v2 PROVEN (node compiler-casename3, candidate core C5F72697 = pack38 source + 5-union-case-name-op v2): probe compiles on Zig, Rust and C; Zig native exit 42 and Rust native exit 42 (payload Circle/Square, nullary Dot, GADT Hello/Count, static Square all named right); the negative (pick i32 keeps First and Second) fails to compile with 'UnionCaseName cannot name a dynamic value of a GADT-specialized union that keeps more than one case...'. Draft frozen; it joins the pack after pack38 together with COMPILER-UNIONTAG-PRUNED-GADT's Zig fix, after which the guard can be lifted for the surveyed backends.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_14 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 14u32, "2026-11-04T21:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 17:1x compiler: held samples staged (land after the pack with the op is installed): %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED\\sample\\union_case_name_probe (exit 42 = payload, nullary, GADT, static names all right) and union_case_name_pruned_negative (+ matrix-row.psd1 Contains 'UnionCaseName cannot name a dynamic value of a GADT-specialized union'); COMPILER-UNIONTAG-PRUNED-GADT\\sample\\gadt_pruned_union_tag (exit 22). PLAN: if node job compiler-uniontag2 shows 22 on all 11 native backends, op v3 drops the 2+-surviving-case guard (the tag table then holds on every backend), and the negative sample becomes a positive one (pick i32 keeps First and Second; exit 42).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_15 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 15u32, "2026-11-04T21:27Z", "compiler", "11-04 17:2x compiler: op program 7 drafted, to follow COMPILER-UNIONTAG-PRUNED-GADT programs 1-3: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED\\7-case-name-any-pruned.kitdo (1 replacement on top of program 5) drops the 'more than one case left' guard; every dyn union then uses the declared-index name table (pruned slots hold ''). It is valid once UnionTag returns the declared index on every backend (programs 1-3: 10 backends proven, Gleam in node job compiler-uniontag4). Positive sample staged in sample7\\union_case_name_pruned (Third :: pick string declared first and pruned, so the table really shifts; First/Second/Third named dyn; exit 42). The negative sample is dropped if 7 lands.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_16 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 16u32, "2026-11-04T21:48Z", "compiler", "11-04 17:5x compiler: SLICE 4 OP PROVEN on 11 backends (node compiler-uniontag5, candidate core DDCA7897 = pack38 + programs 5 and 7 + COMPILER-UNIONTAG-PRUNED-GADT 1-3, native examples harness on a scratch copy): union_case_name_pruned (Third :: pick string declared first and pruned; First, Second and Third named from dyn values) exits 42 on C, Rust, Delphi, Zig, Wasm, Lean, TypeScript, Gleam, Lua and Python; union_case_name_probe (payload, nullary, single-case GADT, static) 42 on the same ten; Cpp cannot compile either probe because the CUDA C++ backend has no string compare (probe limit). gadt_pruned_union_tag 22 on all 11. Pack order for the next pack: SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED 5-union-case-name-op, COMPILER-UNIONTAG-PRUNED-GADT 1, 2, 3, then SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED 7-case-name-any-pruned (stacks on pack38's source). Held samples: sample\\union_case_name_probe, sample7\\union_case_name_pruned, UNIONTAG sample\\gadt_pruned_union_tag; the negative sample is dropped (program 7 makes that shape legal). Then the lib case_name draft (6-case-name-op) and the cells request_line heal.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_17 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 17u32, "2026-11-04T21:57Z", "compiler", "11-04 18:0x compiler: PACK39 candidate staged at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack39 (source core C1F448821ACDAE60 / host 5D4516B8 = pack38's source + SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED 5, COMPILER-UNIONTAG-PRUNED-GADT 1, 2, 3, SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED 7; byte-identical to the stack proven natively on 11 backends in compiler-uniontag5). Review on the node: job compiler-pack39rev, one build, examples -Native A/B vs the pack38 candidate bin (15FD51D7) on Zig, Delphi, Lean, Wasm and Gleam, the five backends whose emitters changed. Installs after pack38.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_18 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 18u32, "2026-11-04T23:11Z", "compiler", "11-04 19:2x compiler: PACK39 REVIEWED and handed to main (install after pack38). Node job compiler-pack39rev, one build (core DDCA7897 = the proof builds), examples -Native A/B vs the pack38 candidate bin: Zig 470 ran / 0 differing cells, Delphi 430 / 0, Wasm 438 / 0, Gleam 440 / 0 (2 build-fail on both arms, pre-existing), Lean 453 / 1 residual cell (a pruned union's spiralTag def) and 0 behavior; 0 DISAGREE everywhere. Unpruned unions are byte-identical as predicted.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_19 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 19u32, "2026-11-05T00:57Z", "compiler", "11-04 20:5x compiler: PENDING INSTALL. main's pack38 install-when-clear gave up at 20:56 after 110 min: it waits for running trains as well as an idle compiler, and kit's TRAIN26 ran on the node the whole window. The box stays on pack37 (host 08B00F25 / core 5F6F6E73). pack38 (reviewed; candidate %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack38) installs first in the next run, then pack39 (reviewed; needs live = pack38). The handover commands are in main's inbox from 15:3x (pack38) and 19:2x (pack39).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_20 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 20u32, "2026-11-05T04:51Z", "compiler", "11-05 00:5x compiler: ROUND TRIP DONE ahead of the land (CPU-light, does not need the op): drafts 6-case-name-op\\reflection.spi (lib, case_name = !!!!UnionCaseName(x) plus its Some/None test) and 6-case-name-op\\daemon.spi (cells request_line: the four nullary arms become one default arm over sm'::to_lower (reflection::case_name q); Compile stays explicit). apps/cells spi/lib_roundtrip.exs: reflection.spi canonical true fixpoint true; daemon.spi canonical true fixpoint true. Both drafts sit on the current live files (live reflection.spi 11-04 14:22, live daemon.spi 11-02 14:07, both older than the 11-04 16:07 drafts); the diffs are exactly the intended edits (reflection +6 lines, daemon 5 arms -> 2). Order unchanged: pack39 box install (its programs 5 and 7 carry the op) -> lib_land_window for reflection.spi -> cells test for daemon.spi. PENDING the install, which is waiting for the installed compiler to go idle (x, kit and tibia notebooks are running).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_21 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 21u32, "2026-11-05T05:04Z", "compiler", "11-05 00:5x compiler: INSTALLED on the BOX in pack39 (00:47, compiler's chain; it waited 69 min for x/kit/tibia notebooks to release the installed compiler). Dry run: the 5 pack39 programs (SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED 5-union-case-name-op and 7-case-name-any-pruned; COMPILER-UNIONTAG-PRUNED-GADT 1-zig-declared-tag, 2-pascal-lean-wasm-declared-tag, 3-gleam-tag-by-case) on live = pack38 reproduce candidate source core C1F44882 / host 5D4516B8. After install: SpiralCompilerCore.dll DDCA78971B4EAB36 and SpiralCompiler.dll 08B00F25C65C5283, both equal=True to the reviewed candidate; system dotnet launches it. Undo: spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack39-20261105-004718. Node and vultr ship: main's waiter (pack-chain -SkipInstall, now excluding *.r2r-old-*/*.replaced-*).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_22 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 22u32, "2026-11-05T05:27Z", "compiler", "11-05 01:2x compiler: LIB LANDED (unstaged): reflection.spi case_name = !!!!UnionCaseName(x), plus test lines for Some 3i32 -> \"Some\" and a None payload -> \"None\". lib_land_window closed GREEN at 01:1x: 3 consumer-used signatures unchanged, apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (15 tests typed, 0 errors), 0 respell drift. Live reflection.spi A2DCD3479A7D = the draft; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-010934. Behaviour run: `lib_gate -File reflection.spi -Test case_name -Compiler process` was VOID: 'Spiral cell timed out after 300s' (box at 82-100% CPU), although the block carries ///- --timeout 900000. The 300 s is cells' default budget, which suggests the -Test filter path loses the block's budget (to be checked). The full-file gate (how LIB-REFLECTION-GATE-TIMEOUT was proven) is running now on the box. The node can't run it: it is on pack38 under TRAIN27, without the op. SAMPLES LANDED (unstaged): tmp/samples/union_case_name_probe, union_case_name_pruned, gadt_pruned_union_tag. matrix.psd1 rows only on the backends where node job compiler-uniontag5 proved them on the same core bytes (DDCA7897): the two case-name samples on C,Rust,Pascal,Python + Zig, Wasm, Lean, Gleam, Lua, AlsoTypeScript (no Cpp: the CUDA C++ backend has no string compare); gadt_pruned_union_tag on the same plus Cpp. Box compile-only check on installed pack40: examples, 31 jobs, 31 ok (baseline new 31; -Accept comes with the next full native run). Next: the cells daemon request_line heal (daemon.spi draft, canonical) after the reflection gate is green.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_23 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 23u32, "2026-11-05T06:15Z", "compiler", "11-05 02:1x compiler: reflection.spi BEHAVIOUR GREEN on the box: lib_gate -File reflection.spi (daemon compiler, installed pack40, which carries the op) 'tests: passed 15 failed 0 of 15', including case_name (Contract / Some 3i32 -> 'Some' / None payload -> 'None' on gleam, lua, cuda, rust, typescript). The two earlier VOIDs were -Compiler process runs on a box at 100% CPU: each compile starts a fresh process, and one of the 3 single-target tests (nameof, get_record_fields, get_functions_types; default 300 s budget) passed 300 s and aborted the run. Daemon mode stays inside every budget. Next: the cells daemon request_line heal (daemon.spi draft, canonical).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_24 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 24u32, "2026-11-05T14:26Z", "compiler", "11-05 10:2x compiler: SLICE 'name styles at compile time' DRAFTED. Probe on installed pack49: reflection::typed_name_snake/kebab (styled_name = to_char_list |> listm::fold |> rev |> concat_list) on a STATIC case emits a run-time char-list fold (Rust 386 lines) and does not build on C at all ('backend_switch has no C arm', listm'.spi:770). Program 8 (drafts\\spiral\\SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED\\8-case-name-styles.kitdo, 1 replacement): !!!!UnionCaseName(x, style) takes an optional style literal: exact (default), lower, snake or kebab. peval styles the name in F#, both for the static fold and in the declared-index name table it already builds for dyn values, so styled names cost the same as plain ones on every backend that has the op (no run-time string code). Same rule as lib styled_step: separator before each uppercase char after the first, then lowercase. A non-literal or unknown style is a type error. Sample (scratch harness50 until install, since pack49 rejects the 2-arg form): union_case_name_styled (dyn LightGreen -> light_green / lightgreen, DeepBlue -> deep-blue, static DeepBlue snake -> deep_blue, exact; exit 42), rows mirroring union_case_name_probe. pack50 = pack49 + 8 building on the box. After install: lib case_name_snake/kebab/lower over the op (lib land window).")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_25 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 25u32, "2026-11-05T14:38Z", "compiler", "11-05 10:4x compiler: program 8 (styled UnionCaseName) PROVEN NATIVELY on pack50 (= pack49 + 8; bin core D3FD5378A74EAE2F, host A1BF06EB unchanged), box scratch harness50: union_case_name_styled exits 42 on C, Rust, Pascal, Python, Zig, Wasm, Lean, Gleam, Lua and TypeScript (10 ran, 0 build-fail, DISAGREE 0). Negative control, installed pack49: 'Compiler error: UnionCaseName with 2 args not implemented', exit 5. Parity review vs pack49 (linked + smoke) running. Lib program 9 drafted (9-lib-case-name-styles.kitdo: case_name_lower/snake/kebab over the op), to land after the install.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_26 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 26u32, "2026-11-05T15:01Z", "compiler", "11-05 11:0x compiler: INSTALLED on the BOX in pack50 (10:54-10:58): SpiralCompilerCore.dll D3FD5378A74EAE2F, SpiralCompiler.dll A1BF06EB9AD87F00, both equal=True; undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack50-20261105-105454. Parity vs pack49: linked 13/13, smoke 159 rows, 0 compile/residual diffs. Repo (unstaged): tmp/samples/union_case_name_styled + its 7 matrix rows (beside union_case_name_probe); on installed pack50, C/Rust/Python/Lua/Gleam -Native: styled + probe 10 ran, exit 42, DISAGREE 0. Handed to main for the node (no urgency). Next: lib program 9 (case_name_lower/snake/kebab) through lib_land_window once the node has pack50.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_27 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 27u32, "2026-11-05T16:20Z", "compiler", "11-05 12:1x compiler: LIB LANDED (unstaged): reflection.spi gains case_name_lower / case_name_snake / case_name_kebab over !!!!UnionCaseName(x, style) (pack51 on box + node), plus a case_style_probe union (HostMacro | GadtCase) and test case_name_styles (dyn HostMacro -> host_macro / hostmacro; GadtCase -> gadt-case / gadt_case) on gleam, lua, rust, typescript. Draft round-tripped canonical + fixpoint (lib_roundtrip.exs); lib copy gate 'tests: passed 1 failed 0', type errors 0. lib_land_window closed GREEN at 12:1x after waiting out a live reader (kit notebook pid 19208, exited 12:14): 3 consumer-used signatures unchanged, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 26 passed, type_probe PASS (16 tests typed), 0 respell drift. Live reflection.spi BC60005C7FCF -> 0F02B35BC118, lib digest 8E645B60FC634A17, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261105-121810. The compile-time styles slice is done; the remaining typed slices (phantom name t, qualified names) already exist as typed_name / case_qualified_name.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_28 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 28u32, "2026-11-05T16:21Z", "compiler", "11-05 12:2x compiler: DONE, every slice in the title is in place. (1) phantom-tagged name: typed_name t / typed_case_name / case_of_typed_name (names of different unions cannot mix). (2) name styles at compile time: !!!!UnionCaseName(x, exact|lower|snake|kebab) folded in peval (pack50/51, box + node), with lib case_name_lower/snake/kebab (landed 12:1x). (3) qualified module::case names: case_qualified_name via !!!!NominalName. (4) GADT-indexed case table: UnionCaseName's declared-index table works on GADT-specialized and pruned unions (union_case_name_pruned, gadt_pruned_union_tag; the cells daemon request_line over the GADT request healed with it on 11-05). Samples: union_case_name_probe, union_case_name_pruned, union_case_name_styled; lib tests case_name, typed_name_styles, case_name_styles, case_qualified_name.")
inl note_of_spiral_nameof_typed_29 () = Note ("SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED", 29u32, "2026-11-05T17:47Z", "compiler", "11-05 13:4x compiler (post-close evidence): ALL-BACKEND compile-only examples parity, pack49 vs installed pack51 (= programs 8 + derive retirement), box: 6825 rows each arm; compile-status differences 10, residual differences 10, ALL TEN on samples/union_case_name_styled (pack49 rejects the 2-arg form: error -> ok on C, Rust, Pascal, Python, Zig, Wasm, Lean, Gleam, Lua, TypeScript). The other 6815 rows are byte-identical on every backend, so the styled op and the derive retirement change no existing output.")
inl kit_heal_nameof () = Task ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", "kit heal nameof <repo>...: drive lib nameof_heal over git-tracked .spi and heal kit's hand-kept case<->string maps by reflection", TaskKind, P1, D3, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,team:kit,granular,typefeatureset,reflection", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_heal_nameof () = Planning ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_heal_nameof_1 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", 1u32, "2026-11-03T12:50Z", "kit", "Filed 11-03 09:0x from compiler (SPIRAL-NAMEOF-HEAL n5): lib/spiral/nameof_heal.spi has findings (source) (tokens) : list finding {kind ToName|OfName; first_line; arms; cases}. Census: 30 findings / 144 arms across 7 repos, 20 of them (108 arms) in kit (kit_adoption_habits 17, window_model 9, command_spec_domain 8, toolchain receipt 8), plus kit's own new kit_style_probes probe_word (19 arms; it was untracked at census time). PLAN: (1) the verb kit heal nameof <repo>... in a typed entry crate (x shape): list git-tracked .spi (skip samples/state/deps), run SpiralCompiler tokens <file> through lib process, call nameof_heal.findings, print typed rows file/line/kind/arms and a count per repo; (2) heal kit's rows with reflection (union_case_suffix + sm'.to_lower or a kebab helper), probe_word first (its words are kebab: gadt-case, wide-host-macro). Parent: KIT-CATCH-UP.")
inl note_of_kit_heal_nameof_2 () = Note ("KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF", 2u32, "2026-11-03T16:02Z", "kit", "11-03 11:5x kit: HEALED in the tree (unproven) now that lib sm'.kebab_of has landed. A scan found every match whose arms all return kebab(case name minus a shared prefix), checked CASE-SENSITIVELY: the first pass was case-insensitive and passed rust_tool_environment's RUSTC wrongly. 16 maps became 'sm'.kebab_of (union_reflection.cases.union_case_suffix PREFIX x)': kit_style_probes.probe_word (21 arms), lease_phase_text, legacy_word, sort_word, effect_name, toolchain_action_name, rust_tool_identity, ceremony_word, program_family_word, amendable_word, settled_word (payload cases too), lint class_word, verdict_word, standard_word, toolchain_action_name_label; plus window_model class_word/window_event_word under S2. rust_tool_environment is now to_upper (rust_tool_identity tool), not a second map. Kept as-is: query_filter_text (computed strings), phase_word (snake_case output). Proof: probes.spi 2/2 on vultr; the healed packages' 10 test files and the regen of their 86-package consumer closure run in the vultr round-2 job.")
inl lib_kebab_case () = Task ("LIB-KEBAB-CASE", "lib sm' kebab_of: PascalCase case names to kebab words (WaitClear -> wait-clear), so reflected union words replace hand-kept string maps", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "lib,team:kit,reflection,granular", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_kebab_case () = Planning ("LIB-KEBAB-CASE", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_kebab_case_1 () = Note ("LIB-KEBAB-CASE", 1u32, "2026-11-03T13:20Z", "kit", "Filed 11-03 09:3x by kit. Needed by KIT-ENTRY-X-S2 (window router verb wait-clear) and KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF (kit_style_probes probe_word: gadt-case, wide-host-macro, ...); compiler's nameof rewrite also uses one ('reflection::case_name plus sm'::to_lower or a kebab helper'). DoD: sm'.kebab_of (text) inserts '-' before each upper-case letter after the first and lower-cases; a lib test block (GadtCase -> gadt-case, WaitClear -> wait-clear, X -> x, ABC -> a-b-c is documented); backend_switch shape where hosts differ; landed through the lib gate (memory lanes-land-lib-directly).")
inl note_of_lib_kebab_case_2 () = Note ("LIB-KEBAB-CASE", 2u32, "2026-11-03T13:23Z", "kit", "11-03 09:4x kit: DRAFT written (not landed): C:\\Users\\i574n\\AppData\\Local\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\LIB-KEBAB-CASE\\kebab_of.spi.part. kebab_from (a top-level :~ ^ join point, never inl recursion over runtime text) walks substring/to_lower and puts '-' before each capital after the first; 3 lib tests (WaitClear -> wait-clear, Gadt -> gadt, ABC -> a-b-c). It uses only portable sm' ops, so no backend_switch is needed. NEXT, per memory lanes-land-lib-directly: insert into lib/spiral/sm'.spi beside to_lower on a node or vultr lib mirror, run lib_gate.ps1 -File sm'.spi on it (one Cells job per node), round-trip, then lib_land_window.ps1 -Draft ... -Apply. WAITS ON: a free gate machine (vultr is held for x-dumps' media stage, and the node is saturated).")
inl note_of_lib_kebab_case_3 () = Note ("LIB-KEBAB-CASE", 3u32, "2026-11-03T14:51Z", "kit", "11-03 10:5x kit: GATED on vultr against a staged lib copy. --check exit 0, and the injected type-error mutant exits 5. lib_gate -Test kebab_of_splits_pascal_case_words passed 1/1 and the mutant expectation fails, so the gate is real. Round trip: fixpoint; canonical differs from the candidate by one blank line, and the canonical bytes are the draft (drafts\\spiral\\LIB-KEBAB-CASE\\sm'.spi.canonical, base DA64EBB24582B655). The first -Apply undid itself: its type_probe hit file_system.spi:1050 (array_base vs array u8), from tibia's uncommitted TRANSFORMER-CHECKPOINT-LOAD block written at 10:42, mid-wait. The same failure reproduces on live without this change; main routed it to tibia. The reapply is running, and the break now counts as a base failure. Consumers waiting: KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF (probe_word draft in drafts\\spiral\\KIT-HEAL-NAMEOF) and KIT-ENTRY-X-S2 (verb_word/class_word/window_event_word by reflection + kebab_of; drafts in drafts\\spiral\\KIT-ENTRY-X-S2).")
inl note_of_lib_kebab_case_4 () = Note ("LIB-KEBAB-CASE", 4u32, "2026-11-03T15:06Z", "kit", "11-03 10:49 kit: LANDED and closed green (lib_land_window): sm'.spi 25191F00112C; 30 consumer-used signatures unchanged; apps/spiral compiles; document_test 22 passed; type_probe pass; 0 respell drift; undo at spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261103-104911. The file_system break was fixed by tibia before the reapply. DONE.")
inl backend_switch_missing_arm () = Task ("BACKEND-SWITCH-MISSING-ARM", "A lib backend_switch with no arm for the current backend compiled silently on Gleam (Nil), F# (()) and C++ (nullptr), surfacing later as an unrelated type error; emit the backend_switch_has_no_<Backend>_arm_in_lib_spiral marker for non-unit types, which the compiler's guard turns into a compile error naming the backend and call chain", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,lib,backends,typefeatureset", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_backend_switch_missing_arm () = Planning ("BACKEND-SWITCH-MISSING-ARM", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_backend_switch_missing_arm_1 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-MISSING-ARM", 1u32, "2026-11-03T14:06Z", "compiler", "11-03 10:0x compiler: reported by x (x-html-gleam2: sm'.char_code has no Gleam arm; domain.gleam got let v2 = Nil, then gleam Type mismatch at domain.gleam:25165). Program BACKEND-SWITCH-MISSING-ARM\\1-name-missing-arm.kitdo (3 replacements on lib backend.spi 308AFF49EBAC3F34 -> 4298BC925B9B0B3A): Gleam, Fsharp and Cpp arms use the ?: t typed fallback like C/Lean/Pascal (unit keeps Nil / () / ((void)0)). PROOF: a Gleam main calling sm'::char_code now fails at compile time: \"This program reaches a lib/spiral backend_switch that has no arm for the Gleam backend ... Macro: backend_switch_has_no_Gleam_arm_in_lib_spiral, Reached from: sm'.spi:1046 < main.spi:3\" (the existing guard). Box lib gate backend.spi 3/3, round trip canonical; landing queued (job compiler-lib-land-bsw). Left: Python (None) and Lua (print) fallbacks, which change runtime behavior and need an A/B over lib-using samples first.")
inl note_of_backend_switch_missing_arm_2 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-MISSING-ARM", 2u32, "2026-11-03T14:16Z", "compiler", "11-03 10:1x compiler: LANDED (closed green: document_test 22 passed, type_probe backend.spi 3 typed tests; backend.spi 4298BC925B9B0B3A; undo 20261103-100416). Gleam, F# and C++ now name a missing lib arm at compile time through the existing guard. Left: Python/Lua fallbacks (runtime behavior change, needs an A/B over lib-using samples).")
inl note_of_backend_switch_missing_arm_3 () = Note ("BACKEND-SWITCH-MISSING-ARM", 3u32, "2026-11-03T18:03Z", "compiler", "11-03 13:5x compiler: Python/Lua LANDED green 13:59 (backend.spi 4298BC92 -> F9DF904E; program BACKEND-SWITCH-MISSING-ARM\\2-python-lua-typed-fallbacks.kitdo). Both use the ?: t typed fallback; unit keeps 'None ## ...' / the Lua print, so a unit gap compiles as before. A/B (same compiler, core 7C49B7A6; lib copy A = live, B = live + draft): every lib-using matrix row on Python/Lua (frontier_format_any_union, frontier_join_format_any, frontier_static_list_eq on both; portable_console_lines, portable_convert_parse, portable_math_rounding on Lua) emits byte-identical output on A and B (9/9), so no matrix sample reached a non-unit Python/Lua gap and runtime behavior is unchanged. Positive control: a main calling am'::to_le_bytes (Rust-only arm) compiled silently on A for both Python and Lua (Lua: a 118-byte program around the print) and fails on B with 'This program reaches a lib/spiral backend_switch that has no arm for the Python/Lua backend ... Reached from: am'.spi:405 < main.spi:3'. Every backend in backend.spi now names a missing non-unit arm at compile time except CppHost (nullptr) and TypeScript/Rust/Zig, which already raise in the target language. DoD met.")
inl granular_split_xpath_eval () = Task ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", "Split lib xpath_eval.spi's eval recursion group (14292 chars, 1st largest lib definition, 11-03 measure) into named per-family helpers under the 280 budget", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "team:fiscal,fiscal,granular,lib,xpath", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_granular_split_xpath_eval () = Planning ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_1 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 1u32, "2026-11-03T15:11Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:2x (GRANULAR-STATS): eval (xpath_eval.spi:912) is a 30-arm match over xpath plus its mutual-recursion tail. PLAN: one :~ ^ helper per arm family in the same recursive group (literals/variables, path steps and axes, comparisons and arithmetic, function calls by family), each under 280 chars; eval keeps only the dispatch. Proof: lib xpath_eval notebook + fiscal's schematron corpus unchanged; land through drafts + lib_land; coordinate names with LIB-RESHAPE.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_2 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:45Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 11:45 fiscal: STEP 1 DRAFTED, proof queued. MEASURE NOTE: GRANULAR-STATS counts chars per block INCLUDING its recursion group, so adding helpers inside the :& group (the plan's wording) cannot shrink it; the group must be broken. Dependency map of the 20 group members (xpath_eval.spi:912-1199): the CALL FAMILY never calls back into eval (call -> call_bool, call_value -> numeric_value, node_name_value, namespace_uri_value, substring_value) and node_values only recurses on itself. STEP 1 (pure move, no semantic change): those 8 definitions become standalone blocks before eval, in define-before-use order (call_bool, numeric_value, node_name_value, namespace_uri_value, substring_value, call_value, call; node_values keeps '^', the others lose it per REC-MARKER-HEAL). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL\\lib\\spiral\\xpath_eval.spi (5C718539, base 734F0463); by trimmed chars the moved blocks are ~51% of the group, so the measured 14,292 should fall to ~7k (largest standalone: call_value ~2.3k). Type-checks on vultr incl. all 12 test bodies. PROOF queued: job-1793720688543-fiscal-xpath-split (after the census rerun): xpath_eval notebook + fiscal corpus_checks 26/26 (the schematron corpus) on the draft. STEP 2 (next): thread eval as a parameter through each_bound, evaluated, quantified, step_nodes/kept_by/kept_at, values_kept, mapped_each, binary/bool_binary/evaluated_binary so eval's group is the dispatch alone; then split eval's arms by family.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_3 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 3u32, "2026-11-03T15:56Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 11:56 fiscal: CODEGEN IDENTITY PROOFS on idle vultr (pack24; probe = read_xml + xpath.parse 'count(//a) = 2' + xpath_eval.evaluate from dyn input, compiled to Rust against each lib). STEP 1 (5C718539, the call family + node_values moved out as standalone blocks): Rust BYTE-IDENTICAL to the live lib (1,591,578 bytes both), so the move is a pure reorganization down to generated code; its Cells proof (xpath_eval notebook + corpus_checks) is queued as job-1793720688543. STEP 2 (9A5AD742, eval passed as an 'ev' parameter so the group is eval alone): type-checks incl. test bodies, BUT codegen changes: 1,597,681 bytes, 3,687 differing lines (345 after normalizing generated names), 178 vs 176 fns (bool_binary_42 and evaluated_binary_43 become standalone), and a NEW CLOSURE ('CLOSURE.with(|closure| closure.clone())', closureN calls), the eta/first-class-function hazard of memory spiral-eta-reduction-makes-closures, here in the evaluator every schematron check runs. DECISION: step 2 REJECTED as written; keep step 1 (identity-proven). Further shrinking of the eval group must stay codegen-identical, e.g. moving more non-recursive pure helpers out, or splitting eval's arm bodies into non-recursive value helpers that take already-evaluated xvalues (no function arguments).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_4 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 4u32, "2026-11-03T16:02Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:2x SIZE CORRECTION (GRANULAR-STATS n14): 14292 was eval's whole :& group; eval alone is 2535 chars (~9x the budget, still worth its per-family helpers). The file's largest single block is regional_functions_follow_their_definitions (6829), a test/data block: split it into per-region named cases first.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_5 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 5u32, "2026-11-03T21:43Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 17:43 fiscal: STEP 1 LANDED through lib_land_window (label fiscal-xpath-split, closed green, undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261103-172909, lib digest AD7A2C458C32D068): xpath_eval.spi 734F0463 -> 5C718539 (the call family call / call_bool / call_value + 4 value helpers + node_values moved out of eval's :& recursion group as standalone blocks; the split script re-run on today's live file reproduces 5C718539, so the base matched). Proof before landing: generated Rust byte-identical to the live module (1,591,578 bytes, 11:4x); vultr pack27 --check with bodies exit 0; ALL 12 xpath_eval test bodies compiled to Rust, run exit 0; respell 0 findings. Window close: signatures 0 changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22, type_probe PASS (12 tests typed), respell 0. Step 2 (passing eval as a parameter) stays rejected: it adds a closure (spiral-eta-reduction-makes-closures). The queued node job fiscal-xpath-split3 now serves as a Cells confirmation incl. corpus_checks.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_6 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 6u32, "2026-11-03T22:35Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:34 fiscal: NODE CELLS CONFIRMATION (job-1793732448229-fiscal-xpath-split3, t1101, core 2ABF22D79E6B6943, one compiler): xpath_eval 12/12 with the landed split. corpus_checks 24/26: models_the_corpus_census and resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet failed with a Rust panic 'Os { code: 2, kind: NotFound }' (a corpus file missing on the mirror) -- an ENVIRONMENT failure, VOID for those 2 rows, not a verdict on the split: neither test calls xpath_eval (they read and resolve the whole XSD corpus), and all 24 schematron/xpath-using rows pass. To settle it: rerun those 2 on a mirror whose deps/corpus matches the box (the t1101 corpus has drifted since its last init).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_7 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 7u32, "2026-11-03T22:40Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 18:40 fiscal: ROOT CAUSE of the 2 VOID corpus_checks rows (correcting n6's 'corpus drift' guess): both read fiscal src/corpus.txt, a gitignored file that scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write generates and build.ps1 runs before any test file (build.ps1:96). My standalone lib_gate job never ran it, so the file is absent on the box AND the mirror -> NotFound. A harness gap of my job, not a defect: CI runs build.ps1, so CI is unaffected. Fix for future direct corpus_checks gates: run pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write first.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_8 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 8u32, "2026-11-04T00:48Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 20:48 fiscal: MEASURED AFTER STEP 1 (live 5C718539): eval's :& group is 151 lines / 12 members / about 6,500 chars (trimmed), down from 14,292; still far over 280 because the measure counts the whole recursion group. The 12 members are genuinely mutually recursive with eval (each evaluates sub-expressions), and the one way to break the group tried so far (eval as a parameter, step 2) makes a heap closure and is rejected. REMAINING OPTIONS, for a decision: (1) defunctionalize: a work-list/union of pending evaluations driven by one loop, so helpers return data instead of calling eval (real rewrite, needs the Rust identity + xpath/schematron gates); (2) accept a recursion group as the unit and have GRANULAR measure members individually when every member is under the bar (a measure change, kit's); (3) stop here (the 1st-largest lib definition halved). Recommend (2) as the standards question it is, then (1) only if the measure stays group-wide.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_9 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 9u32, "2026-11-04T01:38Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 21:37 fiscal: CELLS CONFIRMED (node job-1793754211554-fiscal-corpus-checks, core A63F4C2A8E8029C2, one compiler): with scripts/pattern-oracle.ps1 -Write run first (src/corpus.txt 580 lines) and the box manifests, the live corpus_checks.spi is 28/28 -- incl. every_myinvois_sample_reaches_the_ubl_invoice_unit_in_both_syntaxes, every_sunat_homologation_case_reaches_its_ubl_unit, and models_the_corpus_census / resolves_the_corpus_like_dotnet (the 2 rows VOID this afternoon; the NotFound root cause is confirmed).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_10 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 10u32, "2026-11-04T06:18Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 02:18 fiscal: OPTION (2) MEASURED, and it does not settle the item alone: measured per member (trimmed chars, live 5C718539), eval 2,198, call_value 2,337, call 953, call_bool 934, arithmetic 839 are each far over 280 by themselves, so a per-member measure still flags them. What remains is the shape: eval and call are the recursion (only option 1, defunctionalizing, shrinks them); call_value / call_bool are FLAT one-line-per-case dispatchers over the builtin GADT (about 40 arms; one concept, no recursion) -- splitting them by category would re-match the same GADT twice, worse for reading. DONE NOW (real duplication, not a bar chase): call_value's Round/Floor/Abs arms shared 'empty -> (), number_of -> op | None -> VError' -> number_function name op first + named floored/absolute (inline helpers, so the passed op inlines; not the rejected eval-as-parameter closure). Draft %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL\\lib\\spiral\\xpath_eval.spi CA3D167F (base copy xpath_eval.base-5C718539.spi): vultr pack27 --check exit 0, bodies exit 0, no new >120 lines (one removed); all xpath_eval bodies to Rust QUEUED on vultr. STANDARDS QUESTION for kit's GRANULAR measure: exempt (or measure per arm) a flat '?=' dispatch over a closed union whose arms are one line each, as the stats already exempt declarations (term_value, purchase).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_11 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 11u32, "2026-11-04T07:14Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 03:14 fiscal: LANDED (unstaged) lib xpath_eval.spi 5C718539 -> D5246ED9 through lib_land_window (label fiscal-xpath-dedup, closed green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22/22, type_probe PASS 12 tests typed, 0 respell drift; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261104-025845). Content: call_value's Round/Floor/Abs -> number_function + floored/absolute, plus the abs coverage that was missing ('abs(-2.5) = 2.5 and abs(3) = 3 and abs(0) = 0'). PROOF before landing, vultr pack27: check + bodies exit 0, all 12 xpath_eval bodies to Rust exit 0; MUTATION (absolute returns n) fails 'abs' as predicted. What remains on this item is the standards question (n10) and option (1) for eval/call.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_12 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 12u32, "2026-11-04T11:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:36 fiscal: KIT RULED (11-04 07:3x) on the n10 standards question -- two checkable rules, shipping in kit_style_measure through a train: (1) FLAT DISPATCH measured per arm (one match over a closed union, every arm a single line <=120 chars with no nested match/?/:=/lambda; measured as its longest arm + the match header; one multi-line arm puts the definition back on the full count); (2) the forall binders, prototype-constraint record and parameter list are excluded, the body counts from the first line after '='. No defunctionalize rewrite. Until the rule ships, call_value and call_bool are recorded as 'pending GRANULAR rule (1)', not baseline rows (baselines only shrink). CHECK against rule (1): call_value now has one-line arms except where an arm calls a helper (number_function etc., already one line); any remaining multi-line arm moves to a named helper when the rule ships. eval and call stay the recursion (measured in full).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_13 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 13u32, "2026-11-04T11:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:41 fiscal: MEASURED UNDER kit's GRANULAR rules (GRANULAR-STATS note 11-04 08:2x; they apply now, no train): call_value under rule (1) = 32 one-line arms, longest arm 96 + match header 7 = 103 (passes 280); call_bool had 2 arms with inline matches (FnExists, FnEmpty), which would put it back on the full count -> drafted on live D5246ED9: FnEmpty => is_empty_value first (the identical existing helper), FnExists => has_items first (its old inline expression moved verbatim), plus the missing coverage 'empty(cbc:Missing) and not(empty(cbc:ID)) and not(exists(cbc:Missing))'; under rule (1) call_bool = 20 one-line arms, longest 59 + 7 = 66. Proof (format, check, all bodies to Rust, mutation FnEmpty -> has_items) running on vultr. eval and call remain the recursion, measured in full.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_14 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 14u32, "2026-11-04T12:22Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:22 fiscal: LANDED (unstaged) lib xpath_eval.spi D5246ED9 -> 49EE88FB through lib_land_window (label fiscal-xpath-call-bool; it waited ~20 min for box memory, then closed green: 0 consumer-used signatures changed, apps/spiral compiles, document_test 22/22, type_probe PASS 12 tests typed, 0 respell drift; undo spiral-bin\\lib-land-undo\\20261104-081706). Content: call_bool's FnExists/FnEmpty inline matches -> has_items / is_empty_value (call_bool now 20 one-line arms: rule (1) 66), plus the missing empty() coverage. Proven before landing: vultr check + bodies, all 12 bodies to Rust exit 0, mutation FnEmpty -> has_items fails 'empty'. NEXT: the call split (call -> function_value / bool_function_value / value_function_value + current_date_value / current_datetime_value; also removes the formatter's mis-indented None arm, the file's layout diff 56 -> ~24 lines), drafted in xpath_eval.call-split.spi (kept OUT of the window's draft path while it was open), proof running.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_15 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 15u32, "2026-11-04T12:30Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:30 fiscal: call split PROVEN on vultr pack27 (91704DDx: check + bodies exit 0, all xpath_eval bodies to Rust, rustc 207 s, run exit 0). Draft then made formatter-canonical (34D87D0x: the formatter's own output, 22 layout-only lines -- a record literal and two test assertions), final-bytes proof running. NEXT STEP drafted in a separate file (xpath_eval.eval.spi, so the draft path stays frozen for the coming window): eval's 7 multi-line arms -> step_value / filter_value / apply_value / conditional_value / domain_items (in eval's :& group) + number_literal / negate_value / member_holds (plain, defined before eval; deps checked defined earlier). eval is now a flat one-line dispatch: longest arm 99 (rule 1 passes), body 2154 -> 1062. --check exit 0, format clean first try; Rust-bodies proof queued behind the final-bytes run. Land order: 34D87D0x, then the eval split on top.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_16 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 16u32, "2026-11-04T12:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:41 fiscal: LANDED (unstaged) the call split, 49EE88FB -> 34D87D08 (call -> function_value / bool_function_value / value_function_value + current_date/datetime_value, whole file formatter-canonical): window closed green -- consumers, document_test 22/22, type_probe PASS 12, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo\\20261104-083236. Proven layers stacked on it (vultr pack27: check + bodies + ALL bodies to Rust, run exit 0; formatter 0 each): eval split (flat dispatch, longest arm 99, body 2154 -> 1062), arithmetic (number_arithmetic flat, quotient/remainder keep the zero guard lazy without lambdas), datetime_seconds (shape/zone/day/clock; days_from_civil checked total before computing it early). Landing these three as ONE window now (file 0304B926, base 34D87D08). Next layer proving: element_axis_nodes lambdas -> is_after/is_before, binary/bool_binary lambdas -> number_binary / nodes_binary / compared_value partial applications + or_value/and_value (ACA420D7).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_17 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 17u32, "2026-11-04T12:53Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 08:53 fiscal: layer stack (each layer's vultr pack27 proof = check + bodies + ALL bodies to Rust run exit 0, formatter 0; each re-proves the layers below): L2 0304B926 eval/arithmetic/datetime -- in a land window waiting for a box slot; L3 ACA420D7 axis predicates named (is_after/is_before) + binary/bool_binary lambdas -> number_binary/nodes_binary/compared_value partial applications + or_value/and_value -- PROVEN; L4 7BB41173 zone_after shared by datetime + xs:time, matches_value flattened (matches_flags/compiled_search/pattern_matches) -- PROVEN; L5 A565FD0B scanners as step function + 2-line tail loop (duration_step/designator_seconds, greedy_step/piece_to) -- PROVEN; L6 7B90D4B4 search_pattern anchors, name_matches_in (own_namespace/prefixed_name_matches), castable_text table -- proving; L7 1CCEA84F substring_start/count, is_date_shaped/is_valid_day, offset_seconds (hh_mm_offset/signed_offset) -- proving; L8 E2843FD1 step_nodes axis_found (also removes a found/found shadowing), kept_at arms collapsed via is_kept -- proving. After L2 lands, the next window lands the deepest proven layer in one swap.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_18 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 18u32, "2026-11-04T13:15Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:15 fiscal: L2 window (0304B926) REFUSED safely at its start: 'live lib readers still present: not landing' -- another lane's erl.exe (Cells) was reading the live lib; nothing changed, live stays 34D87D08. Not retried as L2: the retry lands the DEEPEST proven layer in one window (L9 6D1F36E0 proven now; L10 619F6483 validators/digits_at, L11 BEEF814B, L12 3C7AB34F search_pattern are proving on vultr). After L12 the only non-dispatch body over 280 is greedy_step (ruling asked on GRANULAR-STATS note 31).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_19 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 19u32, "2026-11-04T13:49Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 09:49 fiscal: SPLIT LIVE. Two windows, both closed green (consumers compile, document_test 22/22, type_probe PASS 12, 0 respell drift): (a) L2-L10 34D87D08 -> 619F6483 (undo lib-land-undo\\20261104-091653); (b) L11-L12 619F6483 -> 3C7AB34F (undo lib-land-undo\\20261104-093354). The first L2 attempt refused at start on another lane's live Cells reader and changed nothing; landing the deepest proven layer instead of retrying L2 saved a window. Every layer was proven before landing on vultr pack27 (check + bodies + all bodies to Rust, run exit 0, formatter 0). Remaining over 280 by the plain measure: call_value, eval, call_bool, element_axis_nodes (all rule (1) flat dispatches) and greedy_step (one-line conditional chain; ruling asked GRANULAR-STATS note 31). Closing this item when that ruling lands; if chains do not qualify, one more layer turns greedy_step into a classifier + ?= dispatch.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_20 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 20u32, "2026-11-04T14:21Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 10:21 fiscal: DONE. Last layer L13 LANDED (unstaged) 3C7AB34F -> C77D611B, closed green (consumers, document_test 22/22, type_probe PASS 12, 0 respell drift; undo lib-land-undo\\20261104-101319): greedy_step is now a greedy_token classifier (6 cases) + a flat ?= dispatch, since kit's rule (1) text names ONE match over a closed union (the chain ruling asked in GRANULAR-STATS note 31 is moot for this file). Final measure of live xpath_eval (rules 1+2 applied): 254+ top-level defs, every body over 280 is a rule-(1) flat dispatch (call_value, eval, call_bool, element_axis_nodes, greedy_step); 0 non-dispatch bodies over 280. Four land windows in total today (call_bool, call split, L2-L10, L11-L12, L13), all green; every layer proven on vultr pack27 first (check + bodies + all bodies to Rust).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_21 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 21u32, "2026-11-04T15:01Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:01 fiscal: CORRECTION -- REOPENED. I closed this at 10:21 on MY approximation of the measure (trimmed body chars, tests excluded, kit's 11-04 rules (1) flat-dispatch and (2) header-exclusion applied by hand): 0 non-dispatch bodies over 280. kit's ACTUAL counter (Spiral.Cells.CellBudget.over_budget with the default profile, run on vultr against live xpath_eval C77D611B) reports 75 of 247 top-level blocks over budget = 30.4%. The counter differs in kind: its blocks are blank-line-separated and include test blocks, its weights differ (header subtracted, defused dots), and it does not (yet) implement rules (1)/(2). The landed splits stand -- every layer was proven before landing, and they halved the outliers -- but 'Done' is not established against the real counter. Next: split the 75 by test vs code (running) and ask kit whether the ruled rules (1)/(2) will be implemented in CellBudget or the DoD is the raw counter.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_22 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 22u32, "2026-11-04T15:07Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:07 fiscal: kit RULED (b) at ~11:0x by message: the DoD is the counter WITH rules (1)/(2); signature-only and flat-dispatch overages count as compliant until kit's CellBudget change lands in apps/cells, then re-measure. Ruled measure meanwhile via my draft Spiral.Cells.CellBudgetRuled (kit drafts cells\\CELLBUDGET-RULES, real weights incl. indentation, tests excluded, run on vultr): live xpath_eval 21/235 = 8.9% (under 10%). Keeping this Active until the re-measure with kit's landed counter.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_23 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 23u32, "2026-11-04T15:50Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:50 fiscal: RE-MEASURED with kit's ADOPTED module (Spiral.Cells.CellBudgetRuled in vultr's synced apps/cells, also 'mix spiral.cell_budget --granular'): live xpath_eval C77D611B = 21 of 235 code blocks over = 8.94% (identical to my draft's figure); with test blocks included 33 of 247 = 13.4%. Asked kit whether test blocks count; if they do, the 12 multi-assert test blocks get split into one test per behavior (lib change, so through the land window). Status stays Active until that answer.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xpath_eval_24 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL", 24u32, "2026-11-04T15:51Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 11:51 fiscal: DONE (kit ruling by message: GRANULAR counts code blocks only, tests excluded, as GRANULAR-STATS does). Live xpath_eval C77D611B under kit's adopted CellBudgetRuled: 21 of 235 code blocks over = 8.94% (with test blocks: 33 of 247 = 13.4%). Splitting the multi-assert test blocks is filed as its own follow-up, not a gate.")
