inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_1 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 1u32, "2026-11-03T15:11Z", "main", "main 11-03 11:2x (GRANULAR-STATS): XSD is the user's #1 priority and xsd_emit holds 3 of the 10 largest lib definitions. PLAN: emit_named_type -> one helper per type_def case (Simple enum / Simple restriction / Complex sequence / choice / extension); named_type_walk -> a walker step plus a visitor per node kind; is_staged_signature -> named predicates per stage. Proof: generated emitter output byte-identical over fiscal's XSD corpus (DFe.NET schemas) before/after; land via drafts + lib_land; coordinate with the open XSD-* items to avoid churn on the same lines.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_2 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:58Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-03 11:58 fiscal: SEQUENCED, not started (decided per this item's own 'avoid churn' clause): three fiscal xsd_emit drafts are in flight on the same file, XSD-NOMINAL-RECORDS (EF61AD94, output-exact, 70%), XSD-CODEC-PROTOTYPES (9F2CA353, proven in generated units, 60%) and FISCAL-PT-SAFT-3 (group_part 325E10F1, proof running in job-1793700298985). Splitting xsd_emit's groups now would force a rebase of all three. ORDER: after those land. METHOD, proven on GRANULAR-SPLIT-XPATH-EVAL n3: map each recursion group's members, move only NON-recursive helpers out as standalone blocks (never pass the recursive function as a parameter: that introduced a closure in xpath), and gate every step on byte-identical output, both the Rust of a probe program on idle vultr (cmp .rs) and the generated emitter text over fiscal's XSD corpus (DFe.NET schemas) via one node regen with 0 generated diff.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_3 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 3u32, "2026-11-03T16:02Z", "main", "main 11-03 12:2x SIZE CORRECTION (GRANULAR-STATS n14): emit_named_type and named_type_walk were measured with their :& groups; with members as boundaries the file's real outlier is is_staged_signature (6361 chars, 4th largest lib block). Start there; the other two get re-measured per member before splitting.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_4 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 4u32, "2026-11-04T11:19Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:19 fiscal: STARTED (claimed). LAYERED ON the XSD-DECODE-RESULT draft (base copy xsd_emit.base-E8F660ED.spi), since the decode draft rewrites most reader emitters; this lands right after decode. Re-measured per definition on that base (trimmed chars): content_walk 1,751, collect_content 1,667, emit_named_type 1,590, pattern_checks 1,491 (left for FISCAL-XSD-PATTERNS-LARGE), staging_prelude 1,459 (a string template), union_text 1,339. DONE in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\kit\\drafts\\spiral\\GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT\\lib\\spiral\\xsd_emit.spi (51A73F02): (1) emit_named_type's whole Simple/no-enumeration branch -> emit_simple_text name base facets + simple_text_example (emit_named_type is now a 4-arm dispatch); (2) collect_content's 5 arms each built the same 'collected' record (push a field, add references, append extra) -> collected_with field references extra acc, every arm a binding or two plus one call (it also removes a record literal and the next arm crammed onto one 300-char line). Both outside the recursion group's dependencies (defined before the group head). vultr pack27: --check exit 0, format clean. PROOF: output identity -- regenerate all 36 families with the split draft and diff -r against the decode draft's generated tree (run 1 for change (1) running; run 2 for (1)+(2) next).")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_5 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 5u32, "2026-11-04T11:36Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:36 fiscal: OUTPUT IDENTITY PROVEN for changes (1)-(3) (vultr pack27, same inputs on both sides): every family regenerated with the decode xsd_emit and with the split draft -- 69 unit dirs each, 0 differing files. (The first run's single difference, UBL CreditNote's real-document list, came from staging the UBL manifests between snapshot and regen -- input skew, not the split; the rerun generates both sides in one script.) Change (4), the complement text constants, is running against the same decode reference. KIT RULED on the standards question: content_walk falls under rule (2) (its 15-prototype header excluded; the body still counts), so it is recorded as 'pending GRANULAR rule (2)', not a baseline row.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_6 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 6u32, "2026-11-04T11:41Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:41 fiscal: MEASURED UNDER kit's rule (2) (GRANULAR-STATS note 11-04 08:2x): content_walk's BODY alone (after the 15-prototype header) is 1,396 > 280, so it splits; with the header excluded, extracting its arms into :& helpers that repeat the header costs nothing in the measure. Next in the draft.")
inl note_of_granular_split_xsd_emit_7 () = Note ("GRANULAR-SPLIT-XSD-EMIT", 7u32, "2026-11-04T11:44Z", "fiscal", "2026-11-04 07:44 fiscal: content_walk SPLIT under rule (2) (draft 7AB34830): its repeated-group, choice and element arms -> :& members repeated_group_walk / choice_content_walk / element_content_walk (each repeats the 15-prototype header, excluded by rule 2); content_walk is now a 6-arm dispatch. vultr pack27: --check exit 0, format clean (only the 216-char constraint headers exceed 120, as before). Rule-(2) BODY sizes now: content_walk 469 (was 1,396; its first arm keeps a ?& guard, so rule (1) does not apply), repeated_group_walk 484, choice_content_walk 366, element_content_walk 204. Still over 280: the two arm walks, each a straight run of named bindings (first, name, field, part, witness, push) -- the next cut would pass tuples around for little gain; left for a decision with the rest of the item. Output-identity run for this step queued after change (4)'s run.")
