inl x_weight_url_23 () = Task ("X-WEIGHT-URL-23", "x: X weighs every URL as 23 (t.co) but splitter's on_x padding is the identity, so the sim refuses valid posts with long URLs", Story, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "-", "team:x,x,splitter,sim,real-profiles,weights", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_x_weight_url_23 () = Planning ("X-WEIGHT-URL-23", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_x_weight_url_23_1 () = Note ("X-WEIGHT-URL-23", 1u32, "2026-11-03T15:44Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:43 x: FOUND by X-SIM-REAL-PROFILES (EDGE 3, n8): the user's own 2010-era tweets in 72784485 run to 314 raw chars with one URL, which X accepted because a URL counts 23 whatever its length. In x, splitter.spi:149 ':+ padded_as on_x = \\ _ us => us' applies no link padding (only on_mastodon uses 'linked', at mastodon_link_weight 23), and the sim's POST /2/tweets validates with splitter::x_weight (sim_serve.spi:865 too_heavy), so the sim answers 400 'text must be 1 to 280 characters' where X answers 201. xc post itself sends text unchanged and lets the server decide, so the client has no separate check. FIX: on_x pads links like Mastodon (one shared link_weight 23). IMPACT to measure, pre-registered: the thread splitter also weighs cells on OnX, so program cells that contain http(s):// URLs (comments, README-style docs) weigh less and may split into fewer posts. The proof re-runs the census (postable-report equality on x, and the cross-repo report) and lists every file whose post count changes; sim-stress fixtures regenerate under -Accept. A regression block: a 314-char text with one 60-char URL weighs 277 on X.")
inl note_of_x_weight_url_23_2 () = Note ("X-WEIGHT-URL-23", 2u32, "2026-11-03T15:48Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:48 x: DRAFTED (kit drafts x\\X-WEIGHT-URL-23\\splitter.spi, base 8EB7531B6F56 -> B4C81B0571A0). SECOND FINDING while reading: Mastodon's padded_link only RAISED short links to 23 ('at least 23') and never lowered long ones, but both X and Mastodon count every URL as exactly 23. New model: a link's first unit weighs link_weight () = 23 and its other units 0 (next_inside counts down the link, link_weighed sets each unit; linked recurses), shared by on_x and on_mastodon; Bluesky unchanged (bytes). mastodon_link_weight is renamed link_weight (no other user). Tests: the Mastodon block keeps 23/31; new block: 'x ' + a 60-char URL weighs 25 on X, the URL alone 23 on Mastodon. Folded into x-next1. RULE additions: client build CELL-BUDGET passes; e2e RUST-OK (its Mastodon step still holds 'Mastodon's split <= X's'); x census equality SAME with 'cells over one post 0' kept, which bounds the increase side (a URL shorter than 23 now weighs 23). Per-file post-count changes are listed in the cross-repo census after landing.")
inl note_of_x_weight_url_23_3 () = Note ("X-WEIGHT-URL-23", 3u32, "2026-11-03T15:49Z", "x", "2026-11-03 11:49 x: CORRECTION to n2's 'folded into x-next1': moved to its OWN run x-next2 (scratchpad launch-x-next2.ps1). splitter.spi is inlined into several client crates, so in x-next1 it would confound X-JSON-COLLECT-DEDUP's pre-registered A/B ('no crate grows > 5'), which must change one thing. Order: x-next1 (dedup, oauth1, world) then x-next2 (this). Same rule as n2.")
inl note_of_x_weight_url_23_4 () = Note ("X-WEIGHT-URL-23", 4u32, "2026-11-03T16:45Z", "x", "2026-11-03 12:45 x: IMPACT PREDICTED before x-next2 (raw regex count of http(s):// links in tracked .spi). Across repos: fiscal 45 files / 572 links (104 shorter than 23, 468 longer), i574n.github 5 / 128, spiral 18 / 35, x 5 / 14, Spiral-s-ML-Library 9 / 9, tictactoe 5 / 9, blog 3 / 8, dice 2 / 4, alphabet, dir-tree-html, eoie, kit, polyglot 1 each. x: 10 of 14 links are SHORTER than 23 (api.x.com 17, 127.0.0.1:9 18-19, bsky.social 19, console.x.com 21, a.co 11), so their cells get heavier; the 4 long sim problem URLs get lighter. Every affected x cell under the fix: cli usage_environment 119->125, wire tests 148->157 / 154->159 / 182->186 / 207->213, xc base_url 69->75 / write_base 199->203 / missing_bearer 143->145, splitter mastodon test 191->203, sim_serve example_signing 245->226 / problem_kind 81->57 / protected_entry 221->188 / unsupported_kind 93->61. Max 213 < 272, so PREDICTION: x-next2 keeps CELL-BUDGET passing and 'cells over one post 0'. A spill there would mean the model is wrong, not the budget. Fiscal's 468 long links get lighter (fewer posts), which the cross-repo census will show.")
inl note_of_x_weight_url_23_5 () = Note ("X-WEIGHT-URL-23", 5u32, "2026-11-03T21:30Z", "x", "2026-11-03 17:30 x: DONE. GREEN in x-next2 (job-1793737559206, pinned pack27 core 6F83B94FE33167CC; the installed core moved to D1854B99FD3FA940 mid-run): lib gate 23/23, sim accept 0, sim build 0, client build 0 (CELL-BUDGET, xc.rs 992), e2e RUST-OK 37 + 5, census SAME over 76 files with 0 over one post. The prediction held: CELL-BUDGET passed and x keeps 0 cells over one post. Visible effect: the e2e made 139 requests instead of 141, because it posts oauth1.spi as a thread and its long api.x.com URLs now weigh 23, so the thread needs fewer posts; thread-oauth1.expected.json regenerated under -Accept accordingly. The long-form shape block (weight 2,014) passed too. LANDED unstaged: splitter.spi EC590CC5C413 (formatted) plus outputs.")
inl compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export () = Task ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", "compiler: a GADT case whose type variable appears only in its payload (an implicit existential) type-checks in its module but silently erases the module exported types for consumers (ETY-ValueRestriction with _ in place of the type constructor, or ModuleIndexFailed: no key pick)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,gadt,existential,team:compiler", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export () = Planning ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", Minutes 120u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", 1u32, "2026-11-03T16:40Z", "tibia", "11-03 12:5x tibia, found while drafting lib pickler v3 (LIB-PICKLER-GADT). Isolation on vultr (single-flight compiler, same lib), one variable per step, consumer main calls pickler::round_trips (pickler::sample ()): (1) v2 as landed: compiles. (2) leaf t marked recursive (:| ^ leaf t): compiles. (3) + case LeafIso :: \\* a b. (a -> b) * (b -> a) * leaf b -> leaf a with matching arms: the MODULE reports no error, but the consumer gets ETY-ValueRestriction Got: _ (option i32 * bool) -> bool, and with an annotation pickler::pick ... gives ETY-ModuleIndexFailed: The module does not have the key: pick; a probe IN the module file then shows Unbound type variable: pick / Unbound term variable: PPair, LeafBelow from bits3 onward. (4) same case without function fields, LeafIso :: \\* a. leaf a -> leaf a: compiles. (5) function field but no existential, LeafIso :: \\* a. (a -> a) * leaf a -> leaf a: compiles. So the trigger is a case type variable (b) absent from the result type: expected either acceptance or a diagnostic at the case, never a silent loss of the module exports. The supported spelling is an explicit existential in a separate union (xsd_certificate.spi PackedMoves : (\\? n. ...), unpacked with := \\? n. x = packed). Tibia worked around it (LeafEnum fixes b = i32). Repro files: vultr /root/tibia-probes/stage pickler_exp*.spi are not kept; rebuild from the cases above.")
inl note_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", 2u32, "2026-11-04T04:19Z", "compiler", "11-04 00:2x compiler groom (star exchange, tibia #3): raised P2 -> P1. The failure is SILENT: every export of the module disappears, consumers see unbound names, and there is no error at the GADT. tibia lost about an hour bisecting it on 11-03. A loud error is the first step (name the case and the implicit existential variable, and suggest an explicit exists); then make the export work. Next step: a regression sample, a module with one such case plus one plain export, that a consumer imports.")
inl note_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", 3u32, "2026-11-04T04:46Z", "compiler", "11-04 00:5x compiler: REPRODUCED, AND THE CAUSE IS NOT WHAT THE TITLE SAYS. Repro (box, pack32/pack33 compilers; also pack15c, pack20 and pack25 backups): model leaf t with LeafInt :: i32 -> leaf i32 and LeafIso :: \\* a b. (a -> b) * (b -> a) * leaf b -> leaf a, plus a consumer. Every compiler REPORTS it, in all 4 layouts (same package or dependency package; consumer calling a plain export or the GADT; --check of the module or the consumer): ETY-UnusedTypeVariable 'The type variable b is unused in the function's type signature. In the definition: leaf', then the cascade (Unbound type variable: leaf, CasePatternNotFound, consumer ModuleIndexFailed). Two real defects explain why it looked silent: (1) in a dependency-package layout the ENTRY package's errors print FIRST (states = tc :: dependencies), so the consumer's ModuleIndexFailed tops the list and the root cause sits below it; (2) the message speaks of a function's type signature for a union case and never mentions existentials. Fix drafted: kit drafts COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT\\1-name-the-case-root-cause-first.kitdo (5 replacements). It adds a new error, ETY-GadtImplicitExistential, at the GADT result-type check, naming the case and variables and pointing to the explicit (\\? b. ...) spelling, and lists dependency packages' errors before the entry package's (topological order, deepest first). Node review job compiler-gadtx running (control = pack33 build).")
inl note_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", 4u32, "2026-11-04T05:03Z", "compiler", "11-04 01:1x compiler: REVIEWED node-first (job compiler-gadtx, node, control = pack33 build). Base D00B41EE -> source DB6F930D1C1343FE, candidate core 91B04B53D050A50E, host 6B30D2F5 unchanged. The repro rows behave as predicted: gx-bad and gx-bad-pkg now lead with ETY-GadtImplicitExistential ('The GADT case LeafIso binds b, which its result type does not mention ... pack it explicitly in the payload: (\\? b. ...)'). In gx-bad-pkg the consumer's ModuleIndexFailed used to print first; it now comes after the root cause. gx-ok arms are unchanged. Contracts Rust 8 rows and Zig 620 rows: 0 differing cells, 0 behavior, 0 DISAGREE. Noted anomaly: the node's candidate gx-bad printed 11 ETY lines against control's 6. Box rerun of the same core: 6 = 6 on both arms. The extra 5 were the host's timing-dependent 'TypeErrors (uri): %A' dump of model.spi's errors (Program.fs diagnosticForOther). That race exists on control too and is not from this patch. Regression sample drafted at kit drafts COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT\\sample\\gadt_implicit_existential_negative. Its matrix ExpectedErrors entry is Contains 'ETY-GadtImplicitExistential: The GADT case LeafIso binds b' (verified on the candidate). It lands WITH the install, since live pack33 would mark it WRONG-ERROR. Bundled as pack34 with COMPILER-LINK-INLINE-DIAGNOSTIC once that review passes.")
inl note_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", 5u32, "2026-11-04T05:45Z", "tibia", "11-04 01:45 tibia: dropped the plain tibia tag I added when filing this item (tags now compiler,gadt,existential,team:compiler). It made the stop gate's --team tibia routing offer compiler's in-flight fix back to tibia. Tibia still consumes the result: LIB-PICKLER-GADT v8 uses a record-of-operations wrap instead of an existential, so it no longer waits on this item.")
inl note_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", 6u32, "2026-11-04T08:11Z", "compiler", "11-04 04:1x compiler: HANDED TO MAIN as pack34 (5 programs: GADT, link v4, forall hint, format --respell, Zig fast), with the exact -Programs command. Final node review compiler-pack34f: source B33D213B29D2757D, core dll 0758BAF496AE4E7D, host 6B30D2F5; contracts Rust 8 and Zig 620: 0 differing cells; examples F#: only load-timeout flips, verified on a 180 s rerun. Box dry run ok. Staged at spiral-bin-candidates\\pack34. Done when installed; regression samples land right after the install.")
inl note_of_compiler_gadt_implicit_existential_export_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-GADT-IMPLICIT-EXISTENTIAL-EXPORT", 7u32, "2026-11-04T08:47Z", "compiler", "11-04 04:5x compiler: DONE. pack34 installed by main at 04:4x on the box (core 0758BAF496AE4E7D, equal to the reviewed candidate; undo compiler-installs\\pack34-20261104-043420), the node (in-place swap, stale shadow dirs removed) and vultr (built from B33D source). Regression samples landed with it (unstaged): samples/gadt_implicit_existential_negative and samples/forall_real_block_operator_negative, plus their matrix ExpectedErrors entries. Box run on pack34: both rows compile=error with the expected text (no WRONG-ERROR).")
