inl compiler_zig_linked_struct_types () = Task ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", "compiler Zig linked units: generated struct types (Mut, Tuple, heap structs) are per unit, so an export passing one fails to build; alias them to the exporting unit like unions", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,zig,linked-units", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types () = Planning ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 1u32, "2026-11-04T10:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 06:1x compiler: FOUND by the split-invariance oracle (box v6, class zig-build-fail; both units compile, linked Zig does not build). The linked Zig app sees its own copy of a generated structural type: main.zig 'expected type []*main.Mut0, found []*model.Mut0' (array_mut_f32 cut 2: model.create returns an array of mut { value : f32 * string }; model.zig 'const Mut0 = struct { l0: f32, l1: []const u8 }'). Same class on array_union_heap_pair_heaps and array_heap_heap_heap (heap structs in arrays). Unions already cross: import_zig_unions aliases the importer's union to the model's ('const USn = model.<name>'), but Mut/Tuple/heap-union structs and closure Fun types get no such alias. Fix direction: extend the alias step to every generated type reachable from an export's signature (the unit graph already lists unions by shape; add mut layouts, tuples and heap structs), so the importer writes 'const Mut0 = model.Mut0' instead of declaring its own. Gleam has the same problem for SpiralArray (LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-ARRAYS). Not a wrong program (it fails to build), so lower urgency than COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-ALLOCATOR.")
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 2u32, "2026-11-04T10:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 06:2x compiler: DESIGN (from reading import_zig_unions ~16508). Unions cross because the unit graph lists them by source name and the importer replaces its 'const USn = struct{...}' with 'const USn = model.<name>'. Generated structs are numbered per unit (the model's Mut0 need not be the app's Mut0), so they must be matched by SHAPE. (1) unitGraphJson adds 'structs': the show_ty shape strings of every YLayout, YPair-tuple and heap-union type reachable from the export signatures (a walk over each export's domain and range, codegen-independent like the unions list). (2) The exporting unit's codegenZig emits 'pub const SpiralShape_<hash> = <its generated name>;' for each listed shape (hash = the first 16 hex chars of SHA-256 of the shape text). (3) The importer's codegenZig, for each struct it declares whose shape is in a linked unit's list, replaces its declaration with 'const <local name> = <unit>.SpiralShape_<hash>;' (the same regex replace as import_zig_unions). Gleam's SpiralArray is the same class (LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-ARRAYS); an analogous shape alias on Gleam would close both. Acceptance: the oracle's 3 zig-build-fail samples (array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_heap_heap_heap) become LEGAL with 0 DIFFERS.")
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 3u32, "2026-11-04T10:45Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:1x compiler: ZIG FIX PROVEN ON BOX (draft COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES\\1-shape-aliases.kitdo, stacked on the pack35 allocator program). Instead of extending the unit graph it works purely in Zig text, after codegen: every 'const X = struct {...};' gets a canonical shape hash, iterated 6 rounds so that names of other generated structs are replaced by their own hashes and union aliases (const USn = model.Name) by their target; a unit with exports appends 'pub const SpiralShape_<h> = X;' per distinct shape; an importing unit rewrites each struct as 'const X = if (@hasDecl(model, \"SpiralShape_<h>\")) model.SpiralShape_<h> else struct {...};', a comptime choice, so a shape the model never declared falls back to the local struct. Single-unit programs: no imports, no exports, body unchanged. First version (hash of the raw field text) fixed array_mut_f32 but not heap structs whose fields name Heap1 vs Heap1__struct_3; the canonical-hash version fixed them. Evidence (box, candidate = live + allocator + splitter + this): the 6 oracle cuts that failed with 'expected []*main.Mut0, found []*model.Mut0' or '*model.Heap1 vs *main.Heap1__struct_3' (array_mut_f32 cut2, array_cell cut2, array_union_heap_pair_heaps cuts 3 and 5, array_heap_heap_heap cut2, array_union_pair_heaps cut3) now build and exit 0 like the single build; contracts Zig 620 rows 0 differing cells vs pack34 control; test.ps1 -Suite linked 9/9 pass. Next: the full Zig oracle on node with this stacked (expect the 17 struct build-fails to go LEGAL), then a Rust counterpart (17 E0308 on the Rust oracle, same samples).")
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T12:16Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:1x compiler: NODE ORACLE PROOF (job compiler-splitu8, v8): with 1-shape-aliases.kitdo the struct-identity build failures go 17 -> 0 across all 30 Zig samples and every cut, REACH 214/227, 0 DIFFERS. Together with the box evidence (contracts Zig 620 rows 0 differing cells, linked 9/9), the program is ready for a pack: it stacks on COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-ALLOCATOR (pack35). Slot: pack37, after pack36.")
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T13:24Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:2x compiler: PACK37 COMPOSITION, stack-checked on live (box): every program below applies in this order on top of pack35 (COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-ALLOCATOR\\1) and pack36 (LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE\\1, SPIRAL-NAMEOF-TYPED\\3): COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES\\1 (node oracle 214/227, contracts Zig 0 cells), LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES\\1 (oracle 62/66, examples Rust 0 cells), LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT\\1 (examples Rust 0 cells), COMPILER-REAL-CLOSURE-HINT\\1 (message only; its negative sample lands after), LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE\\4 and \\5 (splitter only); CONDITIONAL on their node reviews: BEND-UNSAFE-MINIMIZE\\1+\\2 (v5 green for \\1; v6 with \\2 running) and DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY\\1 (review running). Held for x's window: LINKED-UNITS-GLEAM-ARRAYS\\1 (also stacks cleanly). Per DOTNET-ORACLE-COST's lesson, pack37 gets ONE candidate build and one combined review (contracts + examples on every touched backend + linked + split) rather than per-program rebuilds.")
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T16:39Z", "compiler", "11-04 12:3x compiler: PACK37 REVIEW, partial (node job compiler-pack37rev, ONE build: source BFD1DB5F/5D4516B8 -> candidate core 5F6F6E73 / host 08B00F25; control = installed pack36 core 21F39A40): contracts Zig 620 rows 0 differing cells; examples Rust -Native 518 rows (494 ran) 0 differing cells; linked suite 10/10. families and split suites still running in the same job.")
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 7u32, "2026-11-04T19:34Z", "compiler", "11-04 15:3x compiler: PACK37 REVIEW RESULT (node job compiler-pack37rev; stopped in its split phase, see LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE): contracts Zig 620 rows 0 differing cells; examples Rust -Native 518 rows (494 ran) 0 differing cells; linked suite 10/10; families exit 0 (all agree). Candidate core 5F6F6E73 / host 08B00F25 from source BFD1DB5F / 5D4516B8. The strided split suite on the candidate runs in node job compiler-splitsuite2; once green, pack37 goes to main.")
inl note_of_compiler_zig_linked_struct_types_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES", 8u32, "2026-11-04T23:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 19:1x compiler: pack37 INSTALLED on the box 19:01 by main (core 5F6F6E73 / host 08B00F25 = the reviewed candidate; undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack37-20261104-190103). Node ship and vultr source build deferred until kit's TRAIN26 regen finishes (after 21:00). The 6 held Split samples landed in matrix.psd1's Split list (program 7, unstaged): array_cell, array_heap_heap_heap, array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_union_pair_heaps, while_control.")
