inl linked_units_rust_struct_types () = Task ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", "compiler Rust linked units: generated structs (Mut, heap structs) are private per crate, so an export passing one fails rustc E0308; alias them to the exporting crate by canonical shape hash like the Zig fix", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "", "team:compiler,compiler,rust,linked-units", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types () = Planning ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_1 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 1u32, "2026-11-04T11:00Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:2x compiler: FOUND by the split-invariance oracle (node v6 Rust: 17 of 66 cuts rustc E0308, the same array samples as Zig's COMPILER-ZIG-LINKED-STRUCT-TYPES). array_mut_f32 cut 2: both model.rs and main.rs declare a private 'struct Mut0 { l0: f32, l1: Rc<str> }'; main calls model::model_create, which returns Rc<RefCell<Vec<Rc<RefCell<model::Mut0>>>>>. Rust has no comptime @hasDecl, so the Zig trick (importer chooses at compile time) does not carry over. Design: the exporting crate's codegenRust makes generated structs pub with pub fields and emits 'pub type SpiralShape_<h> = X;' (same canonical 6-round shape hash as the Zig program); unitGraphJson adds a 'shapes' array of those hashes; readUnitGraph and LinkedUnit carry it; the importer's codegenRust drops each struct whose canonical hash is in a linked unit's shapes and emits 'use <unit>::SpiralShape_<h> as X;'. Acceptance: the Rust oracle's 17 E0308 cuts become LEGAL with 0 DIFFERS, contracts Rust 0 differing cells, linked suite green.")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_2 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 2u32, "2026-11-04T11:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 07:1x compiler: DRAFTED LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES\\1-rust-shape-aliases.kitdo (applies stacked on allocator + splitter + Zig shapes; 4 replacements). LinkedUnit gains 'shapes : Set<string>'. A RustLinkedShapes module is added before readUnitGraph: the same canonical 6-round shape hash as the Zig program, over 'struct X { ... }' lines. Exporter (code has a 'pub fn'): structs and their l<i> fields become pub, 'pub type SpiralShape_<h> = X;' is appended, and the hashes go to <unitGraphDir>/<stem>.rust-shapes.json (deleted when there are none). Importer: for each struct whose hash a linked unit owns, it drops the struct, its #[derive] line and its impl Default, and appends 'use <unit>::SpiralShape_<h> as X;' at the end of the file (prepending could land before a #![...] inner attribute). Proof is queued on the node (box and node both at 100% CPU; vultr reserved for tibia's quiet bench): node job compiler-splitu9r, the full v6r Rust oracle with this stacked, starts when compiler-bendsafe4 finishes. A residual change is expected on single-unit samples that have a 'pub fn' (pub struct plus aliases); contracts Rust compare is next.")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_3 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 3u32, "2026-11-04T12:17Z", "compiler", "11-04 08:2x compiler: NODE ORACLE PROOF (job compiler-splitu9r; pack34 + allocator + splitter + this program): Rust REACH 62 of 66 cuts LEGAL (v6r: 45), 0 DIFFERS. The 17 rustc E0308 struct-identity failures are gone (array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_heap_heap_heap and the rest now link through 'use model::SpiralShape_<h> as X'). Remaining 4: 2 EJP0040 (frontier spin, deliberate) and 2 while_control cuts exporting break' (E0267 'break inside of a closure', the macro-body class that LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE\\4-macro-bodies-by-source.kitdo moves to source). Still pending before a pack: the contracts Rust -Native residual check (node job compiler-rustrev, control pack34 vs this + LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT\\1), where single-unit rows with a 'pub fn' are expected to change residual only.")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_4 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 4u32, "2026-11-04T13:04Z", "compiler", "11-04 09:1x compiler: SINGLE-UNIT REGRESSION CHECK GREEN (node job compiler-rustrev2, the node git-root copy; control pack34 vs candidate = this + LINKED-UNITS-DERIVE-OUT\\1): examples Rust -Native 518 rows, 494 ran natively on both arms, 0 build-fail; compare: 0 differing cells (not even residual), 0 behavior cells, 0 DISAGREE. So no single-unit example emits a top-level pub fn, and the shape aliasing is invisible outside linked builds. With the v9r oracle (62/66, 0 DIFFERS) the program is ready for pack37.")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_5 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 5u32, "2026-11-04T23:08Z", "compiler", "11-04 19:1x compiler: pack37 INSTALLED on the box 19:01 by main (core 5F6F6E73 / host 08B00F25 = the reviewed candidate; undo spiral-bin\\compiler-installs\\pack37-20261104-190103). Node ship and vultr source build deferred until kit's TRAIN26 regen finishes (after 21:00). The 6 held Split samples landed in matrix.psd1's Split list (program 7, unstaged): array_cell, array_heap_heap_heap, array_mut_f32, array_union_heap_pair_heaps, array_union_pair_heaps, while_control.")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_6 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 6u32, "2026-11-04T23:11Z", "compiler", "11-04 19:2x compiler: DONE (installed is done): the program rode pack37, installed on the box at 19:01 with the reviewed bytes; node/vultr follow after kit's TRAIN26. Proof chain in the notes above: oracle 0 DIFFERS, struct-identity build failures gone, single-unit examples unchanged. The cuts still not legal are the deliberate frontier/EJP0040 class and the macro-body class handled by LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE's by-source programs (also in pack37).")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_7 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 7u32, "2026-11-05T06:21Z", "compiler", "11-05 02:2x compiler: REGRESSION from this item's program 1 (shipped in pack37, so in every core since 5F6F6E73), found by kit: TRAIN27 (the first train on 08B00F25 / pack38) died at regen. RustLinkedShapes.export (spiral_compiler.fs:35041-35046) runs on every Rust output that has a `pub fn` line. Its decl regex rewrites EVERY one-line `struct X { ... }`, including hand-written !!!!Global text: it strips all field `pub `s, then re-adds `pub` only before Spiral-generated `lN:` fields. kit src/canonical_plan_ir_domain/transport_terminal.spi's global `pub struct CanonicalPlanRow { pub op: String, pub target: String, ... }` came out as `{ op: String, target: String, ... }`, and patch_control_domain (another crate) failed with E0616 private field. `pub struct` / `pub fn` lines survive; only field pubs go. FIX (one replacement): 2-keep-field-visibility.kitdo keeps the existing field pubs. The lN regex `(?<=^ |, )(?=l\\d+: )` already skips a field that has `pub ` before it, so generated fields still open and nothing doubles. (shapes() still ignores `pub` when hashing, as it should.) pack42 = pack41 + this fix: source core 63B37773 / host 92849440. Review on the node (job compiler-pack42rev, control = pack41 bin core 887F89D1): kit's transport_terminal package compiled on both arms (expect `pub op: String` back), linked suite, Rust examples parity. PENDING. Regression sample (cross-unit read of a hand-written pub field) to follow.")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_8 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 8u32, "2026-11-05T06:43Z", "compiler", "11-05 02:4x compiler: FIX PROVEN; PACK42 READY. Node review (compiler-pack42rev, control = pack41 bin core 887F89D1, candidate = pack41 + 2-keep-field-visibility: source core 63B37773 / host 92849440, bin host 89530093 / core 15A07F66621D141D): linked suite 10/10 both arms; examples -Backend Rust 518 rows (494 ok, 24 expected errors) both arms, compile-status differences 0, residual differences 0, so no Spiral-generated struct changes. The kit-package compile was VOID on the node: canonical_plan_ir_domain's package.spiproj needs C:/home/git/eoie/src/spiral, which isn't there. Decisive proof instead: REGRESSION SAMPLE apps/compiler/tmp/samples/linked_rust_global_pub_fields (unstaged; Linked row 'Backends = Rust; Exit = 13; Calls = model_make'). model unit: global 'pub struct Row { pub op: i32, pub target: i32 }' plus an export; app unit reads r.op + r.target across the crate boundary. Installed pack40 (bug): 'rustc app: error[E0616]: field `op` of struct `Row` is private', linked 11 rows 10 pass 1 FAIL. pack42 candidate bin: ran, exit 13, linked 11 rows 11 pass. Candidate %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin-candidates\\pack42. Box install follows pack41 (mid-apply now); main ships to the node after TRAIN27 and tells x first. Node stage deleted.")
