inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_10 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 10u32, "2026-11-05T11:23Z", "compiler", "11-05 07:1x compiler: SECOND REGRESSION from program 1, reported by kit (TRAIN28 on pack44 went red at cargo, kit_agile_sprint_show show.rs:250 E0308 'expected agile_note_listing::UH0, found UH0'). Cause: shapes() hashes a field's TYPE NAME literally when that type is not one of the hashed structs (an enum such as a list-string union UH0). Both crates inline lib sm'.split_list, so each has its own UH0 enum and its own loop-state struct Mut1 { l0: i32, l1: UH0 } with the same text. B's Mut1 hashed equal to A's, import replaced it with A's (field = A's UH0), and B's code still builds B's UH0. REPRODUCED: new sample tmp/samples/linked_rust_local_union_loop (both units call sm'.split_list; the app links the model's second_line export; packages '../../../../../../lib/spiral-'); Linked row 'Backends = Rust; Exit = 5; Calls = model_second_line'. Installed pack44: 'rustc app: error[E0308]: mismatched types', linked 12 rows 11 pass 1 FAIL. FIX drafted: 3-import-only-closed-shapes.kitdo. A struct is imported only if every LOCALLY defined type its fields mention (enum/struct/type/union declared in this crate) is itself imported, settled to a fixpoint. Candidate (pack44 + 3) building on the box; then the linked suite on it. PENDING.")
