inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_12 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 12u32, "2026-11-05T12:29Z", "compiler", "11-05 08:3x compiler: PACK47 REVIEWED on the box (scratchpad pack47\\review.ps1). pack47 = pack44 + this item's 3-import-only-closed-shapes + UNIONTAG-PARITY 1 (Kotlin/Swift) + 2 (Bend); source core 12A9B02940923093, bin core 1DC33DD0CD113196 / host E441B6B3F8865B02 (host unchanged from pack44). Control = pack44 candidate bin core 657DA4B173F9D3D3. Linked: control 11/12 (linked_rust_local_union_loop E0308), draft 12/12. Examples -Backend Rust,Kotlin,Swift: 1414 shared rows (1387 ok + 27 expected errors on both arms), compile-status differences 0, residual differences 0. The draft's one extra row is the new tmp/samples/union_tag_nullary (added mid-run; ok). Split suite (LINK-SPLIT-INVARIANCE's oracle, which every link change keeps) RUNNING on the box now; install after it is green.")
inl note_of_linked_units_rust_struct_types_13 () = Note ("LINKED-UNITS-RUST-STRUCT-TYPES", 13u32, "2026-11-05T12:48Z", "compiler", "11-05 08:5x compiler: THIRD REGRESSION from program 1, export side (main relayed TRAIN29, red at regen 08:44 on pack44): cargo E0425 in kit_ingest_frontier/ingest_frontier.rs:317 'pub type SpiralShape_bd785a8b4651 = IngestTarget;' cannot find type IngestTarget. CONFIRMED in the node regen tree (kit-regeneration\\dbc0f5f9...): a hand-written global opens 'mod ingest_runtime {' at line 5, and its 'pub struct IngestTarget { workspace: String, ... }' sits at COLUMN 0 at line 12. export's shape regex takes every column-0 one-line struct, so it aliased a mod-nested user struct at the crate root. pack46fix/pack47 have the same export. FIX 4 drafted: 4-generated-structs-only.kitdo. RustLinkedShapes.decl matches only Spiral-generated structs (lookahead: first field '(pub )?l0: '), so shapes, import's candidates and export's pub-opening never see user globals. Corpus census: all 298 one-line structs in tmp/samples' Rust outputs start with l0:, so generated behaviour is unchanged. Regression sample tmp/samples/linked_rust_global_in_mod (global 'pub mod inner { pub struct Row {...} }' + export; app reads r.op + r.target through model::inner::Row), Linked row 'Backends = Rust; Exit = 13; Calls = model_make'. pack48 = pack47 + 4 building on the box; review vs pack47 next.")
