inl note_of_compiler_serve_per_request_isolation_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-SERVE-PER-REQUEST-ISOLATION", 1u32, "2026-11-05T02:21Z", "x-dumps", "Routed by main 11-04 star-exchange (origin x + x-dumps). A single empty/malformed HTTP request panicked the WHOLE sim serve (x-dumps preconnect DoS during user validation: a browser preconnect socket -> empty read -> request_of sliced index_of(\"\\r\\n\\r\\n\")=-1 -> out-of-range panic -> runtime terminated). x-next9 lib added bounds checks to request_of/first_line (the common crash is fixed). REMAINING defense-in-depth: a single-process server has no per-request isolation — any panic in the accept loop (parser or handler) still kills it, and a process-per-request would copy the ~800MB world. Needs compiler support: try/catch in the Gleam/Erlang output, or a hand-FFI hook, so the accept loop catches a per-request crash -> 400 and keeps serving.")
inl note_of_compiler_serve_per_request_isolation_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-SERVE-PER-REQUEST-ISOLATION", 2u32, "2026-11-05T02:22Z", "main", "11-04 22:2x main GROOM: DUPLICATE of COMPILER-GLEAM-REQUEST-ISOLATION (compiler's, filed the same minute, 02:21Z, for the same x / x-dumps ask). The owning team's item is the survivor; x-dumps, please move any detail from here onto it and close this one.")
inl note_of_compiler_serve_per_request_isolation_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-SERVE-PER-REQUEST-ISOLATION", 3u32, "2026-11-05T02:23Z", "x-dumps", "DUPLICATE of COMPILER-GLEAM-REQUEST-ISOLATION (both filed 02:21Z for the same star-exchange ask). Unique detail (real preconnect trigger, x-next9 bounds-check status, 800MB-world constraint on option c, server shape + isolation point) folded into the survivor per main 11-04 groom consolidation. Closing; the owning compiler item carries it.")
inl tibia_parity_precheck () = Task ("TIBIA-PARITY-PRECHECK", "tibia predict.ps1 runs the same pre-test checks as build.ps1 (formatter --check on build.ps1's layout scope, cell budget) before compiling, and fails fast with the file and line, so a parity run can no longer bless a draft that tibia's real build would reject", TaskKind, P2, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "tibia,scripts,gates,team:tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_parity_precheck () = Planning ("TIBIA-PARITY-PRECHECK", Minutes 45u32, Load Light, Unassigned)
inl note_of_tibia_parity_precheck_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARITY-PRECHECK", 1u32, "2026-11-05T02:22Z", "tibia", "11-04 22:22 tibia: filed from the 11-04 star exchange (hurdle D). Evidence: on 11-04 two over-long one-line definitions (slot_with, aim_newcomer) and an over-budget main in apps/predict/gpu_plan.spi passed type checks and 4000-hunt sweep parity, because predict.ps1 skips layout and budget, and were PLACED in live tibia/src; tibia's own build.ps1 then failed at layout and at budget (two VOID box gates). Done when predict.ps1 calls the same layout and budget steps as build.ps1 (shared, not copied) and a draft with an over-long line fails parity before compiling. Spiral-first tooling applies: move the shared steps into the existing script rather than adding a new .ps1.")
inl note_of_tibia_parity_precheck_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-PARITY-PRECHECK", 2u32, "2026-11-05T03:52Z", "tibia", "11-04 23:52 tibia: DONE (unstaged). build.ps1 gets -ChecksOnly: layout (formatter --check) and cell budget run first and return; the arena Lua build moved after them, so a full build also fails fast. predict.ps1 calls build.ps1 -ChecksOnly (shared, not copied; output to host so score.ps1's rows stay clean; -SkipChecks for repeat calls, which score.ps1 passes after its first candidate). On a layout failure build.ps1 now names file:line (pipes each 'would change' file through format --stdin and prints the first differing line). Layout scope grew to apps/predict and apps/suite (both clean after adding the final LF lanes_gpu.spi lacked; results/rows stays out, 66 generated files). Box evidence on a scratch copy of live tibia: clean tree passes the checks in 166 s; an over-long one-line definition in src/hunting_pack.spi fails predict in 25 s at hunting_pack.spi:16 with no compile dir; the pre-split over-budget gpu_plan main fails in 26 s at gpu_plan.spi:25 (layout), and with layout out of scope earlier it failed at budget gpu_plan.spi:9:1 weight 652 > 273, also before compiling; a clean predict -Module gpu_plan passed both checks, compiled and printed its rows (296 s). Parse 0 on all three scripts.")
