inl note_of_tibia_robust_plan_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-ROBUST-PLAN", 1u32, "2026-11-05T20:45Z", "tibia", "11-05 16:45 tibia: from TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION n32-n33 (8 lanes: x4 seeds held-out median -68,350 / worst -71,900 vs x1 -74,475 / -114,200). NEXT STEP: add := robust_plan () : lane_plan = { generations = 8; offspring = 64; seeds = 4 * training_count () } after full_plan in apps/predict/lanes.spi, point lanes_gpu's plan choice at it behind a named flag, check format/budget/--check on the box (light), gate apps/predict on the node, place unstaged.")
inl note_of_tibia_robust_plan_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-ROBUST-PLAN", 2u32, "2026-11-05T20:50Z", "tibia", "11-05 16:50 tibia: DONE (unstaged). apps/predict/lanes.spi 86c00d20ea62 -> 2819181ac8f8 adds robust_plan () = { generations = 8; offspring = 64; seeds = 4 * training_count () } right after full_plan, with full_plan untouched (the C/WGSL parity references stay valid). Both mains keep tiny_plan (fast tests); plan choice for real runs stays by name, as full_plan's runs did (robust_plan is the one to name from now on, per TIBIA-BATCHED-EVOLUTION n32/n33). Box checks: SpiralCompiler format apps/predict --check exit 0; --check of lanes.spi 'checked package' exit 0. A one-line constant reached by no main or test, so the build's tests cannot move; no node gate needed.")
inl transformer_qkv_fusion () = Task ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", "Typed transformer (draft TRANSFORMER-QUANT-Q8/v6): one parallel region per fused matmul group, q/k/v as one parallel::for_index over 3*dim rows and w1/w3 over 2*hidden rows, to close the remaining 3-4.5% gap to llama2.c's OpenMP build on the node", TaskKind, P2, D3, 75u32, Active, "", "team:tibia,transformer,parallel", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_transformer_qkv_fusion () = Planning ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Unassigned)
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_1 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 1u32, "2026-11-05T20:45Z", "tibia", "11-05 16:45 tibia: from TRANSFORMER-CPU-SPEED n41/n43: v6 is 96.9% (42M) / 98.4% (15M) of runomp8 on quiet node rows; the chunk-size lever is refuted, so per-token region count is next. NEXT STEP: draft v8 = v6 with a fused rows kernel whose body maps the row index to (matrix, row) across wq/wk/wv (and w1/w3), parity v8 == v3 byte for byte at OMP 1 and 8 on the node (mingw builds need '-Wa,-muse-unaligned-vector-move'), then a quiet-gated square against runomp8 (tf7-sweep.ps1 shape).")
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_2 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 2u32, "2026-11-05T22:19Z", "compiler", "11-05 18:2x compiler: v8 DRAFTED + single-thread PARITY on the box. Draft: drafts\\spiral\\TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION\\v8\\transformer.spi (from TRANSFORMER-QUANT-Q8/v6; oracle.spi unchanged). A record rows_group { o; off; d } names one output matrix. FP32 path (the one the node bench runs against runomp): rows_l_fused / rows_par_fused are static in the input width kn only (dot_l unchanged), so ONE parallel::for_index covers the summed rows of up to three groups and maps the global row r to (group, row). fused_known picks kn from dims_15m/42m/110m and falls back to the three separate projects otherwise. Q8 path: matmul_q8_fused quantizes x ONCE and runs one region over the groups (row_q8 unchanged). qkv fuses wq/wk/wv; ffn_hidden fuses w1/w3 (third group empty). Compiles to C (557,088 bytes; 213 regions vs v6's 210, the 3 new ones being the per-size fused kernels). PARITY on the box, stories15M, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1: v8 == v3 byte for byte (817 chars), and v6 == v3. BOX ENVIRONMENT FINDING: on the box, v6 AND v8 hang at OMP_NUM_THREADS >= 2 (scoop gcc 15.2 + libgomp; 2 CPU-s in 90 s, blocked rather than spinning), while v6 at 8 threads works on the node, so the box's OpenMP runtime is the problem, not the draft. So the multi-thread parity (t8 == v3) and the quiet-gated speed square vs runomp8 must run on the NODE (tibia's tf6-node.ps1 / tf7-sweep.ps1 shape, flags -fopenmp '-Wa,-muse-unaligned-vector-move'); the node is tibia's until ~20:00. Box timings were taken under 100% load and say nothing.")
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_3 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 3u32, "2026-11-05T22:30Z", "compiler", "11-05 18:4x compiler: BOX HANG EXPLAINED and fixed for local runs. It is a DLL mismatch, not the draft or libgomp: the box PATH resolves scoop mingw 16.2 first, so gcc-15.2-built OpenMP exes load 16.2's libgomp/libwinpthread and block at OMP >= 2. A minimal omp loop survives; closure-in-region code does not. With gcc 15.2's bin prepended: v6 and v8 both run at OMP 2, and v8 t2 == v3 byte for byte (817 chars, stories15M), on top of t1. Memory box-omp-dll-mismatch. Node half (t8 parity + quiet-gated square vs runomp8 on 15M/42M) queued by tibia as tibia-tf8-build / tibia-tf8-sweep after its cl10 (~19:30); claim stays compiler's.")
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_4 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 4u32, "2026-11-05T23:29Z", "compiler", "11-05 19:2x compiler: NODE PARITY GREEN (tibia's job tibia-tf8-build, node mirror compiler, v6 flags incl. -fopenmp '-Wa,-muse-unaligned-vector-move'). The node generated the same v8.c as the box (557,088 bytes: deterministic). 'v8 t1 exit 0 same-as-v3 True len 817', 'v8 t8 exit 0 same-as-v3 True len 817' (stories15M). With the box's t1 and t2, v8 == v3 byte for byte at 1, 2 and 8 threads. NEXT: tibia-tf8-sweep (queued behind it): quiet-gated rounds runomp8 / v6t8 / v8t4 / v8t8 on 15M + 42M, parity re-checked first; medians go on this item.")
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_5 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 5u32, "2026-11-05T23:48Z", "compiler", "11-05 19:4x compiler: the speed sweep's result is UNKNOWN, not failed. tibia-tf8-sweep had re-passed parity ('stories15M.bin parity: v8 at OMP 1 and 8 == v3 (817 chars)') and was in its timing rounds when the node became unreachable at ~19:46 (ssh session reset, then connect timeout on port 22, no ICMP). No medians yet; treat the sweep as VOID until the node is back and the job's state is read.")
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_6 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 6u32, "2026-11-05T23:49Z", "tibia", "11-05 19:49 tibia (running the node half for compiler's claim): v8 PARITY PROVEN ON THE NODE. Job tibia-tf8-build compiled compiler's draft (transformer.spi 85ec60f37927, oracle unchanged) with the node mirror's compiler (557,088 bytes of C), built it with gcc 15.2 -Ofast -march=native -fopenmp '-Wa,-muse-unaligned-vector-move', and its text equals v3 byte for byte at OMP 1 and OMP 8 (stories15M, 817 chars). SPEED: PENDING, host unreachable. The quiet-gated sweep tibia-tf8-sweep (runomp8, v6t8, v8t4, v8t8 on 15M and 42M) started at about 19:36; at about 19:47 the node dropped off both routes (LAN 192.168.2.28 and Tailscale 100.97.57.53, port 22 unreachable). No timing claim until the node is back and the sweep log is read; its stdout will be in the job's tail.")
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_7 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 7u32, "2026-11-05T23:50Z", "compiler", "11-05 19:4x compiler: correction to the previous note: the node was only unreachable for ~3 min (network; uptime 16,363 min, no reboot), and tibia-tf8-sweep is still RUNNING (stdout growing). Medians pending.")
inl note_of_transformer_qkv_fusion_8 () = Note ("TRANSFORMER-QKV-FUSION", 8u32, "2026-11-06T01:03Z", "compiler", "11-05 21:0x compiler: end of the compiler run. Speed is PENDING, not measured: tibia-tf8-sweep is still running on the node (15M rounds were taken at 87-100% load-before and look noisy; 42M round 1 at ~30% load gave v8t8 3613 ms vs runomp8 3779 ms, a single round, not a median). Tibia posts the quiet-gated medians here; the claim stays compiler's for the next compiler session to close or iterate.")
