inl note_of_lib_parallel_map_index_1 () = Note ("LIB-PARALLEL-MAP-INDEX", 1u32, "2026-11-05T20:45Z", "tibia", "11-05 16:45 tibia: map-shaped bodies only read shared data, so a Rust arm needs no &mut aliasing; tibia's scores_by is already this shape. NEXT STEP: draft map_index in lib/spiral/parallel.spi beside for_index (C arm via c_for_index writing into a fresh array; others via each_index), a test map_index_matches_sequential (c, rust) plus a mutant, round-trip with lib_land_window dry run (main's 11-05 precheck), node proof, then land; switch network.spi scores_by to it after.")
inl note_of_lib_parallel_map_index_2 () = Note ("LIB-PARALLEL-MAP-INDEX", 2u32, "2026-11-05T21:06Z", "tibia", "11-05 17:06 tibia: DRAFTED (kit drafts LIB-PARALLEL-MAP-INDEX/v1/parallel.spi 642e9c2c445d, base BEEEAB18B7B7): map_index count fn = allocate the output array, then for_index count (\\ i => set out i (fn i)); C runs it as for_index's omp loop, other backends sequentially. Test map_index_puts_each_result_at_its_index (c, rust): squares of 0..99 weighted by position must sum to 24,830,850, so a result in the wrong slot fails. ROUND TRIP: lib_land_window dry run says '1 drafts round-trip as document_test requires', nothing written. The only over-120 lines are 2 that predate the draft. PROOF queued: node gate tibia-mapidx-gate-1 runs parallel.spi's notebook on the spiral mirror tibia-np1s (base equal), draft then a mutant that writes each result to slot count-1-i, restoring the file after; it runs after cl10 frees the node.")
inl note_of_lib_parallel_map_index_3 () = Note ("LIB-PARALLEL-MAP-INDEX", 3u32, "2026-11-05T21:32Z", "tibia", "11-05 17:32 tibia: PROVEN on the node (job tibia-mapidx-gate-2, 1011 s; parallel.spi's notebook on spiral mirror tibia-np1s, draft swapped in and restored to BEEEAB18B7B7). Draft 642e9c2c445d: discovered 8, executed 8, passed 8 on every target (chunks zig x2; for_index c, rust; map_index_puts_each_result_at_its_index c, rust; map_workers rust; map_keeps_order gleam, rust; map_empty gleam, rust; map_strings gleam). Mutant c9764fb80021 (writes each result to slot count-1-i) fails exactly map_index_puts_each_result_at_its_index (actual 8,332,500, expected 24,830,850). LANDING now: lib_land_window -Apply on the live lib with base BEEEAB18B7B7 and its close checks; the result follows.")
inl note_of_lib_parallel_map_index_4 () = Note ("LIB-PARALLEL-MAP-INDEX", 4u32, "2026-11-05T22:19Z", "tibia", "11-05 18:19 tibia: LANDED and closed green (lib_land_window, live lib parallel.spi BEEEAB18B7B7 -> 642E9C2C445D, lib digest 8829B9266D318C60, undo lib-land-undo\\20261105-175352). Close: round trip ok; 0 consumer-used signatures changed; apps/spiral/spiral.spi compiles; document_test 26 passed; type_probe PASS (8 tests typed, 0 errors, control ok); 0 respell drift. Node proof before the land: draft 8/8 on every target; the mutant failed exactly the new test. parallel::map_index count fn : array a is now in the lib for every lane: omp-threaded on C, sequential elsewhere, and map-shaped so a sound threaded Rust arm can follow (COMPILER-EMIT-PARALLEL-LOOPS n9). Next consumer: tibia network.spi scores_by can become map_index count (\\ child => judge j (mutate r child)).")
inl note_of_lib_parallel_map_index_5 () = Note ("LIB-PARALLEL-MAP-INDEX", 5u32, "2026-11-05T23:30Z", "tibia", "11-05 19:30 tibia: FIRST CONSUMER PLACED: tibia/src/network.spi scores_by is now parallel::map_index r::s::offspring (\\ child => judge j (mutate r child)) (live 4c3abc8069dc -> b46fe9f2d44b, unstaged; one line replaces create + for_index + set). Node gate tibia-np5-gate-2 (tibia build.ps1 -Files network on mirror tibia-np1 with the landed parallel.spi 642E9C2C445D in the spiral mirror): layout and budget clean, 14/14 tests on every target (c, rust, wgsl), including parallel_climb_keeps_the_sequential_winner (c, rust), which checks scores_by directly; the mirror was restored to its original network.spi.")
inl kit_train_watcher_retry () = Task ("KIT-TRAIN-WATCHER-RETRY", "launch-train's box-side watcher retries a lost ssh route instead of ending the train's install step", TaskKind, P1, D2, 0u32, Planned, "", "kit,team:kit,train,remote", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kit_train_watcher_retry () = Planning ("KIT-TRAIN-WATCHER-RETRY", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kit_train_watcher_retry_1 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-WATCHER-RETRY", 1u32, "2026-11-05T23:50Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 19:4x kit FILED from TRAIN32: the box job (job-1793906232412-kit-TRAIN32-node) ended exit 1 after 4.5 h because remote.ps1 found no route to the node (port 22 unreachable on both LAN and tailscale, sshd starved at 100 pct CPU); both ports answered a minute later and the node half kept running notebooks. A green train would have lost its install step to this blip. DoD: the box-side poll treats a no-route error as transient (retry with backoff for up to ~10 min before giving up), logs each retry, and a forced one-poll ssh failure in a test still ends with the node half's real verdict.")
inl note_of_kit_train_watcher_retry_2 () = Note ("KIT-TRAIN-WATCHER-RETRY", 2u32, "2026-11-05T23:52Z", "kit-fc1568a6", "11-05 19:5x kit: BUILT (unstaged) in scripts/launch-train.ps1: the node-half wait is now a loop. It breaks on the real verdict line (kit job wait ok ...); any other output (a lost route, a dropped ssh session) is logged as 'node wait lost its route (n of 10): <last line>' and retried after 60 s, up to 10 straight misses, then the existing exit=0 check decides as before. Parse 0, CRLF kept (live hash now 81841578748EB2B8). Not yet exercised: proves itself on the next train that hits a blip; a forced-failure test needs a fake remote, not done.")
